完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","textEn":"Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估去膠與清潔造成的二次改變」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess secondary changes from stripping and cleaning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","後清潔可能改變已形成圖形。"],"optionsEn":["Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.","RIE is purely physical bombardment.","Post-cleaning can modify completed patterns."],"answer":2,"explanation":"後清潔可能改變已形成圖形。 完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","explanationEn":"Post-cleaning can modify completed patterns. Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}},{"id":"a051-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-21"],"title":"將截面尺寸與電阻載具對照","titleEn":"Relate cross-sectional dimensions to resistance vehicles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何與電性應共同驗證。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Geometry and electrical behavior need joint verification.","instruction":"將截面尺寸與電阻載具對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「幾何與電性應共同驗證。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate cross-sectional dimensions to resistance vehicles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Geometry and electrical behavior need joint verification.","observation":"幾何與電性應共同驗證。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Geometry and electrical behavior need joint verification. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將截面尺寸與電阻載具對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何與電性應共同驗證。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate cross-sectional dimensions to resistance vehicles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Geometry and electrical behavior need joint verification.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何與電性應共同驗證。","textEn":"Geometry and electrical behavior need joint verification."},{"id":"a051-v8-22-k2","title":"損傷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Damage and transfer: principle and limits","text":"完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","textEn":"Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將截面尺寸與電阻載具對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate cross-sectional dimensions to resistance vehicles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["幾何與電性應共同驗證。","側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。"],"optionsEn":["Geometry and electrical behavior need joint verification.","Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.","RIE is purely physical bombardment."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何與電性應共同驗證。 完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","explanationEn":"Geometry and electrical behavior need joint verification. Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}},{"id":"a051-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-22"],"title":"比較不同樣品材料對腔體的污染風險","titleEn":"Compare chamber-contamination risks of sample materials","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共用設備需要材料相容性規則。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Shared equipment needs material-compatibility rules.","instruction":"比較不同樣品材料對腔體的污染風險。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「共用設備需要材料相容性規則。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare chamber-contamination risks of sample materials. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Shared equipment needs material-compatibility rules.","observation":"共用設備需要材料相容性規則。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Shared equipment needs material-compatibility rules. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同樣品材料對腔體的污染風險」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共用設備需要材料相容性規則。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare chamber-contamination risks of sample materials\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Shared equipment needs material-compatibility rules.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共用設備需要材料相容性規則。","textEn":"Shared equipment needs material-compatibility rules."},{"id":"a051-v8-23-k2","title":"損傷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Damage and transfer: principle and limits","text":"完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","textEn":"Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同樣品材料對腔體的污染風險」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare chamber-contamination risks of sample materials\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。","共用設備需要材料相容性規則。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。"],"optionsEn":["Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.","Shared equipment needs material-compatibility rules.","RIE is purely physical bombardment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共用設備需要材料相容性規則。 完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","explanationEn":"Shared equipment needs material-compatibility rules. Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}},{"id":"a051-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-rie","v8b-lametch","v8b-endpoint","v8b-nisttools"],"prerequisiteIds":["a051-v8-23"],"title":"交付速率、輪廓、選擇性與損傷報告","titleEn":"Report rate, profile, selectivity and damage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：RIE 合格判準必須是多維度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: RIE acceptance criteria must be multidimensional.","instruction":"交付速率、輪廓、選擇性與損傷報告。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「RIE 合格判準必須是多維度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Report rate, profile, selectivity and damage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: RIE acceptance criteria must be multidimensional.","observation":"RIE 合格判準必須是多維度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"RIE acceptance criteria must be multidimensional. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付速率、輪廓、選擇性與損傷報告」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「RIE 合格判準必須是多維度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Report rate, profile, selectivity and damage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"RIE acceptance criteria must be multidimensional.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a051-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"RIE 合格判準必須是多維度。","textEn":"RIE acceptance criteria must be multidimensional."},{"id":"a051-v8-24-k2","title":"損傷與轉移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Damage and transfer: principle and limits","text":"完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","textEn":"Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付速率、輪廓、選擇性與損傷報告」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Report rate, profile, selectivity and damage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["側壁筆直就可排除電性損傷。","RIE 完全只有物理撞擊。","RIE 合格判準必須是多維度。"],"optionsEn":["Straight sidewalls rule out electrical damage.","RIE is purely physical bombardment.","RIE acceptance criteria must be multidimensional."],"answer":2,"explanation":"RIE 合格判準必須是多維度。 完成圖案仍需檢查表面、電性與污染。","explanationEn":"RIE acceptance criteria must be multidimensional. Completed patterns still need surface, electrical and contamination checks."}}]}]},{"id":"a052","title":"原子層蝕刻","titleEn":"Atomic layer etching","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究自限制反應、循環與視窗、三維與選擇性、電性與效率；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: self-limiting reactions, cycles and windows, 3d and selectivity, electrical quality and efficiency. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["自限制反應","循環與視窗","三維與選擇性","電性與效率"],"labelsEn":["Self-limiting reactions","Cycles and windows","3D and selectivity","Electrical quality and efficiency"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"etch","subcategoryTitle":"蝕刻與電漿","subcategoryTitleEn":"Etch and plasma","stages":[{"id":"a052-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"自限制反應","titleEn":"Self-limiting reactions","description":"ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","descriptionEn":"ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient.","steps":[{"id":"a052-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出表面改質與移除兩個半循環","titleEn":"Draw surface-modification and removal half-cycles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反應分離是循環控制的核心。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Separated reactions enable cycle control.","instruction":"畫出表面改質與移除兩個半循環。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「反應分離是循環控制的核心。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw surface-modification and removal half-cycles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Separated reactions enable cycle control.","observation":"反應分離是循環控制的核心。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Separated reactions enable cycle control. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出表面改質與移除兩個半循環」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反應分離是循環控制的核心。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw surface-modification and removal half-cycles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Separated reactions enable cycle control.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反應分離是循環控制的核心。","textEn":"Separated reactions enable cycle control."},{"id":"a052-v8-01-k2","title":"自限制反應的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-limiting reactions: principle and limits","text":"ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","textEn":"ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出表面改質與移除兩個半循環」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw surface-modification and removal half-cycles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["反應分離是循環控制的核心。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。"],"optionsEn":["Separated reactions enable cycle control.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane."],"answer":0,"explanation":"反應分離是循環控制的核心。 ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","explanationEn":"Separated reactions enable cycle control. ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}},{"id":"a052-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-01"],"title":"比較連續 RIE 與循環 ALE","titleEn":"Compare continuous RIE with cyclic ALE","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：時間分離改變控制方式而非消除所有反應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Temporal separation changes control without eliminating all reactions.","instruction":"比較連續 RIE 與循環 ALE。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「時間分離改變控制方式而非消除所有反應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare continuous RIE with cyclic ALE. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Temporal separation changes control without eliminating all reactions.","observation":"時間分離改變控制方式而非消除所有反應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Temporal separation changes control without eliminating all reactions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較連續 RIE 與循環 ALE」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「時間分離改變控制方式而非消除所有反應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare continuous RIE with cyclic ALE\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Temporal separation changes control without eliminating all reactions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"時間分離改變控制方式而非消除所有反應。","textEn":"Temporal separation changes control without eliminating all reactions."},{"id":"a052-v8-02-k2","title":"自限制反應的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-limiting reactions: principle and limits","text":"ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","textEn":"ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較連續 RIE 與循環 ALE」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare continuous RIE with cyclic ALE\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","時間分離改變控制方式而非消除所有反應。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。"],"optionsEn":["Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Temporal separation changes control without eliminating all reactions.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間分離改變控制方式而非消除所有反應。 ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","explanationEn":"Temporal separation changes control without eliminating all reactions. ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}},{"id":"a052-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-02"],"title":"設計只有改質步驟的對照","titleEn":"Design a modification-only control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單一步驟對照可檢查非預期移除。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Single-step controls test unintended removal.","instruction":"設計只有改質步驟的對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「單一步驟對照可檢查非預期移除。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Design a modification-only control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Single-step controls test unintended removal.","observation":"單一步驟對照可檢查非預期移除。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Single-step controls test unintended removal. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計只有改質步驟的對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單一步驟對照可檢查非預期移除。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Design a modification-only control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Single-step controls test unintended removal.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單一步驟對照可檢查非預期移除。","textEn":"Single-step controls test unintended removal."},{"id":"a052-v8-03-k2","title":"自限制反應的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-limiting reactions: principle and limits","text":"ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","textEn":"ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計只有改質步驟的對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Design a modification-only control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","單一步驟對照可檢查非預期移除。"],"optionsEn":["Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","Single-step controls test unintended removal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一步驟對照可檢查非預期移除。 ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","explanationEn":"Single-step controls test unintended removal. ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}},{"id":"a052-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-03"],"title":"設計只有移除步驟的對照","titleEn":"Design a removal-only control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：未改質表面的移除量影響協同性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Removal of unmodified surfaces affects synergy.","instruction":"設計只有移除步驟的對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「未改質表面的移除量影響協同性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Design a removal-only control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Removal of unmodified surfaces affects synergy.","observation":"未改質表面的移除量影響協同性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Removal of unmodified surfaces affects synergy. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計只有移除步驟的對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「未改質表面的移除量影響協同性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Design a removal-only control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Removal of unmodified surfaces affects synergy.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"未改質表面的移除量影響協同性。","textEn":"Removal of unmodified surfaces affects synergy."},{"id":"a052-v8-04-k2","title":"自限制反應的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-limiting reactions: principle and limits","text":"ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","textEn":"ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計只有移除步驟的對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Design a removal-only control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["未改質表面的移除量影響協同性。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。"],"optionsEn":["Removal of unmodified surfaces affects synergy.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未改質表面的移除量影響協同性。 ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","explanationEn":"Removal of unmodified surfaces affects synergy. ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}},{"id":"a052-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-04"],"title":"計算完整循環與對照的協同程度","titleEn":"Compare full-cycle removal with controls","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：完整循環需優於獨立步驟的非選擇性效果。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Full cycles must be distinguished from independent nonspecific removal.","instruction":"計算完整循環與對照的協同程度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「完整循環需優於獨立步驟的非選擇性效果。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：設完整循環移除量 0.20 nm；僅改質對照 0.02 nm；僅移除對照 0.03 nm。本例定義協同分率 S=[E_full-(E_mod+E_remove)]/E_full，得到 S=0.75。即使 S 高，仍必須另畫暴露時間飽和曲線，因為協同性不單獨證明自限制；0.20 nm 也不代表恰好一個晶格層。","instructionEn":"Compare full-cycle removal with controls. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Full cycles must be distinguished from independent nonspecific removal.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Let full-cycle removal be 0.20 nm, modification-only removal 0.02 nm and removal-only control 0.03 nm. Define synergy S=[E_full-(E_mod+E_remove)]/E_full; S=0.75. High synergy still requires exposure-time saturation curves because synergy alone does not establish self-limitation. Nor does 0.20 nm necessarily equal one lattice plane.","observation":"完整循環需優於獨立步驟的非選擇性效果。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n以明示定義得到 75%，並保留飽和性尚需驗證的結論。","observationEn":"Full cycles must be distinguished from independent nonspecific removal. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nObtain 75% using the stated definition and retain the need for saturation verification.","failure":"若報告假設「任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算完整循環與對照的協同程度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「完整循環需優於獨立步驟的非選擇性效果。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：以明示定義得到 75%，並保留飽和性尚需驗證的結論。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare full-cycle removal with controls\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Full cycles must be distinguished from independent nonspecific removal.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Obtain 75% using the stated definition and retain the need for saturation verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"完整循環需優於獨立步驟的非選擇性效果。","textEn":"Full cycles must be distinguished from independent nonspecific removal."},{"id":"a052-v8-05-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"設完整循環移除量 0.20 nm；僅改質對照 0.02 nm；僅移除對照 0.03 nm。本例定義協同分率 S=[E_full-(E_mod+E_remove)]/E_full，得到 S=0.75。即使 S 高，仍必須另畫暴露時間飽和曲線，因為協同性不單獨證明自限制；0.20 nm 也不代表恰好一個晶格層。","textEn":"Let full-cycle removal be 0.20 nm, modification-only removal 0.02 nm and removal-only control 0.03 nm. Define synergy S=[E_full-(E_mod+E_remove)]/E_full; S=0.75. High synergy still requires exposure-time saturation curves because synergy alone does not establish self-limitation. Nor does 0.20 nm necessarily equal one lattice plane."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算完整循環與對照的協同程度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare full-cycle removal with controls\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","完整循環需優於獨立步驟的非選擇性效果。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。"],"optionsEn":["Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Full cycles must be distinguished from independent nonspecific removal.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane."],"answer":1,"explanation":"完整循環需優於獨立步驟的非選擇性效果。 ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","explanationEn":"Full cycles must be distinguished from independent nonspecific removal. ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"設完整循環移除量 0.20 nm；僅改質對照 0.02 nm；僅移除對照 0.03 nm。本例定義協同分率 S=[E_full-(E_mod+E_remove)]/E_full，得到 S=0.75。即使 S 高，仍必須另畫暴露時間飽和曲線，因為協同性不單獨證明自限制；0.20 nm 也不代表恰好一個晶格層。","textEn":"Let full-cycle removal be 0.20 nm, modification-only removal 0.02 nm and removal-only control 0.03 nm. Define synergy S=[E_full-(E_mod+E_remove)]/E_full; S=0.75. High synergy still requires exposure-time saturation curves because synergy alone does not establish self-limitation. Nor does 0.20 nm necessarily equal one lattice plane.","check":"以明示定義得到 75%，並保留飽和性尚需驗證的結論。","checkEn":"Obtain 75% using the stated definition and retain the need for saturation verification."}},{"id":"a052-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-05"],"title":"列出熱式與電漿式 ALE 的差異","titleEn":"Distinguish thermal and plasma ALE","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：能量來源會改變方向性與材料適用性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Energy source changes directionality and material applicability.","instruction":"列出熱式與電漿式 ALE 的差異。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「能量來源會改變方向性與材料適用性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish thermal and plasma ALE. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Energy source changes directionality and material applicability.","observation":"能量來源會改變方向性與材料適用性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Energy source changes directionality and material applicability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出熱式與電漿式 ALE 的差異」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「能量來源會改變方向性與材料適用性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish thermal and plasma ALE\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Energy source changes directionality and material applicability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"能量來源會改變方向性與材料適用性。","textEn":"Energy source changes directionality and material applicability."},{"id":"a052-v8-06-k2","title":"自限制反應的原理與限制","titleEn":"Self-limiting reactions: principle and limits","text":"ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","textEn":"ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出熱式與電漿式 ALE 的差異」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish thermal and plasma ALE\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","能量來源會改變方向性與材料適用性。"],"optionsEn":["Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","Energy source changes directionality and material applicability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"能量來源會改變方向性與材料適用性。 ALE 必須以飽和與對照證據確認自限制性，不能只因製程循環就稱為原子層蝕刻。","explanationEn":"Energy source changes directionality and material applicability. ALE requires saturation and control evidence of self-limitation; cycling alone is insufficient."}}]},{"id":"a052-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"循環與視窗","titleEn":"Cycles and windows","description":"每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","descriptionEn":"Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior.","steps":[{"id":"a052-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-06"],"title":"繪製改質暴露時間的飽和曲線","titleEn":"Plot modification saturation against exposure time","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平台區才支持自限制解釋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A plateau supports self-limiting interpretation.","instruction":"繪製改質暴露時間的飽和曲線。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「平台區才支持自限制解釋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plot modification saturation against exposure time. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A plateau supports self-limiting interpretation.","observation":"平台區才支持自限制解釋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A plateau supports self-limiting interpretation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製改質暴露時間的飽和曲線」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平台區才支持自限制解釋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plot modification saturation against exposure time\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A plateau supports self-limiting interpretation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平台區才支持自限制解釋。","textEn":"A plateau supports self-limiting interpretation."},{"id":"a052-v8-07-k2","title":"循環與視窗的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycles and windows: principle and limits","text":"每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","textEn":"Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製改質暴露時間的飽和曲線」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plot modification saturation against exposure time\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平台區才支持自限制解釋。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。"],"optionsEn":["A plateau supports self-limiting interpretation.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平台區才支持自限制解釋。 每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","explanationEn":"A plateau supports self-limiting interpretation. Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}},{"id":"a052-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-07"],"title":"繪製移除能量的允許視窗","titleEn":"Plot a permissible removal-energy window","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：過低可能不移除，過高可能直接濺射。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Too little energy may not remove; too much may sputter directly.","instruction":"繪製移除能量的允許視窗。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「過低可能不移除，過高可能直接濺射。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plot a permissible removal-energy window. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Too little energy may not remove; too much may sputter directly.","observation":"過低可能不移除，過高可能直接濺射。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Too little energy may not remove; too much may sputter directly. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製移除能量的允許視窗」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「過低可能不移除，過高可能直接濺射。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plot a permissible removal-energy window\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Too little energy may not remove; too much may sputter directly.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"過低可能不移除，過高可能直接濺射。","textEn":"Too little energy may not remove; too much may sputter directly."},{"id":"a052-v8-08-k2","title":"循環與視窗的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycles and windows: principle and limits","text":"每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","textEn":"Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製移除能量的允許視窗」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plot a permissible removal-energy window\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","過低可能不移除，過高可能直接濺射。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。"],"optionsEn":["Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","Too little energy may not remove; too much may sputter directly.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"過低可能不移除，過高可能直接濺射。 每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","explanationEn":"Too little energy may not remove; too much may sputter directly. Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}},{"id":"a052-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-08"],"title":"檢查吹除不足造成的混合反應","titleEn":"Assess mixed reactions from insufficient purging","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：半循環重疊會破壞理想分離。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Overlapping half-cycles undermine ideal separation.","instruction":"檢查吹除不足造成的混合反應。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「半循環重疊會破壞理想分離。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess mixed reactions from insufficient purging. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Overlapping half-cycles undermine ideal separation.","observation":"半循環重疊會破壞理想分離。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Overlapping half-cycles undermine ideal separation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查吹除不足造成的混合反應」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「半循環重疊會破壞理想分離。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess mixed reactions from insufficient purging\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Overlapping half-cycles undermine ideal separation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"半循環重疊會破壞理想分離。","textEn":"Overlapping half-cycles undermine ideal separation."},{"id":"a052-v8-09-k2","title":"循環與視窗的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycles and windows: principle and limits","text":"每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","textEn":"Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查吹除不足造成的混合反應」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess mixed reactions from insufficient purging\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","半循環重疊會破壞理想分離。"],"optionsEn":["Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Overlapping half-cycles undermine ideal separation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"半循環重疊會破壞理想分離。 每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","explanationEn":"Overlapping half-cycles undermine ideal separation. Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}},{"id":"a052-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-09"],"title":"比較前幾循環與穩態循環","titleEn":"Compare initial cycles with steady cycles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面初始狀態可造成暫態。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Initial surface state can cause transients.","instruction":"比較前幾循環與穩態循環。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「表面初始狀態可造成暫態。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare initial cycles with steady cycles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Initial surface state can cause transients.","observation":"表面初始狀態可造成暫態。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Initial surface state can cause transients. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較前幾循環與穩態循環」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面初始狀態可造成暫態。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare initial cycles with steady cycles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Initial surface state can cause transients.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面初始狀態可造成暫態。","textEn":"Initial surface state can cause transients."},{"id":"a052-v8-10-k2","title":"循環與視窗的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycles and windows: principle and limits","text":"每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","textEn":"Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較前幾循環與穩態循環」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare initial cycles with steady cycles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面初始狀態可造成暫態。","每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。"],"optionsEn":["Initial surface state can cause transients.","Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面初始狀態可造成暫態。 每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","explanationEn":"Initial surface state can cause transients. Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}},{"id":"a052-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-10"],"title":"以厚度對循環數求每循環移除量","titleEn":"Fit removal per cycle from thickness versus cycles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：線性區間應明確標示。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The fitted linear range must be stated.","instruction":"以厚度對循環數求每循環移除量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「線性區間應明確標示。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Fit removal per cycle from thickness versus cycles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: The fitted linear range must be stated.","observation":"線性區間應明確標示。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The fitted linear range must be stated. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以厚度對循環數求每循環移除量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「線性區間應明確標示。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Fit removal per cycle from thickness versus cycles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The fitted linear range must be stated.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"線性區間應明確標示。","textEn":"The fitted linear range must be stated."},{"id":"a052-v8-11-k2","title":"循環與視窗的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycles and windows: principle and limits","text":"每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","textEn":"Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以厚度對循環數求每循環移除量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Fit removal per cycle from thickness versus cycles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","線性區間應明確標示。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。"],"optionsEn":["Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","The fitted linear range must be stated.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"線性區間應明確標示。 每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","explanationEn":"The fitted linear range must be stated. Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}},{"id":"a052-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-11"],"title":"計算剩餘薄膜的量測不確定度","titleEn":"Calculate uncertainty in remaining thickness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：移除量接近噪聲時需增加可辨識性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Removal near the noise floor needs improved identifiability.","instruction":"計算剩餘薄膜的量測不確定度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「移除量接近噪聲時需增加可辨識性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Calculate uncertainty in remaining thickness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Removal near the noise floor needs improved identifiability.","observation":"移除量接近噪聲時需增加可辨識性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Removal near the noise floor needs improved identifiability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算剩餘薄膜的量測不確定度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「移除量接近噪聲時需增加可辨識性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Calculate uncertainty in remaining thickness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Removal near the noise floor needs improved identifiability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"移除量接近噪聲時需增加可辨識性。","textEn":"Removal near the noise floor needs improved identifiability."},{"id":"a052-v8-12-k2","title":"循環與視窗的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycles and windows: principle and limits","text":"每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","textEn":"Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算剩餘薄膜的量測不確定度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Calculate uncertainty in remaining thickness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每個循環必定精確移除一個完整晶格層。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","移除量接近噪聲時需增加可辨識性。"],"optionsEn":["Each cycle necessarily removes exactly one complete lattice plane.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Removal near the noise floor needs improved identifiability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除量接近噪聲時需增加可辨識性。 每循環移除量與循環數的關係可能有成核或暫態階段。","explanationEn":"Removal near the noise floor needs improved identifiability. Removal per cycle can include nucleation or transient behavior."}}]},{"id":"a052-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"三維與選擇性","titleEn":"3D and selectivity","description":"方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","descriptionEn":"Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives.","steps":[{"id":"a052-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-12"],"title":"比較水平與垂直表面的移除","titleEn":"Compare removal on horizontal and vertical surfaces","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：方向性取決於活化機制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Directionality depends on the activation mechanism.","instruction":"比較水平與垂直表面的移除。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「方向性取決於活化機制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare removal on horizontal and vertical surfaces. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Directionality depends on the activation mechanism.","observation":"方向性取決於活化機制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Directionality depends on the activation mechanism. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較水平與垂直表面的移除」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「方向性取決於活化機制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare removal on horizontal and vertical surfaces\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Directionality depends on the activation mechanism.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"方向性取決於活化機制。","textEn":"Directionality depends on the activation mechanism."},{"id":"a052-v8-13-k2","title":"三維與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","textEn":"Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較水平與垂直表面的移除」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare removal on horizontal and vertical surfaces\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["方向性取決於活化機制。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Directionality depends on the activation mechanism.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"方向性取決於活化機制。 方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","explanationEn":"Directionality depends on the activation mechanism. Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}},{"id":"a052-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-13"],"title":"檢查高深寬比區的反應物到達","titleEn":"Assess reactant access in high-aspect-ratio features","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：自限制不代表所有位置即時飽和。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Self-limitation does not imply immediate saturation everywhere.","instruction":"檢查高深寬比區的反應物到達。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「自限制不代表所有位置即時飽和。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess reactant access in high-aspect-ratio features. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Self-limitation does not imply immediate saturation everywhere.","observation":"自限制不代表所有位置即時飽和。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Self-limitation does not imply immediate saturation everywhere. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查高深寬比區的反應物到達」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「自限制不代表所有位置即時飽和。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess reactant access in high-aspect-ratio features\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Self-limitation does not imply immediate saturation everywhere.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"自限制不代表所有位置即時飽和。","textEn":"Self-limitation does not imply immediate saturation everywhere."},{"id":"a052-v8-14-k2","title":"三維與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","textEn":"Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查高深寬比區的反應物到達」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess reactant access in high-aspect-ratio features\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","自限制不代表所有位置即時飽和。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Self-limitation does not imply immediate saturation everywhere.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"自限制不代表所有位置即時飽和。 方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","explanationEn":"Self-limitation does not imply immediate saturation everywhere. Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}},{"id":"a052-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-14"],"title":"測試不同材料的飽和與移除","titleEn":"Compare saturation and removal across materials","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料選擇性需實際對照證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material selectivity needs comparative evidence.","instruction":"測試不同材料的飽和與移除。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「材料選擇性需實際對照證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare saturation and removal across materials. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material selectivity needs comparative evidence.","observation":"材料選擇性需實際對照證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material selectivity needs comparative evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「測試不同材料的飽和與移除」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料選擇性需實際對照證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare saturation and removal across materials\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material selectivity needs comparative evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料選擇性需實際對照證據。","textEn":"Material selectivity needs comparative evidence."},{"id":"a052-v8-15-k2","title":"三維與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","textEn":"Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「測試不同材料的飽和與移除」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare saturation and removal across materials\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","材料選擇性需實際對照證據。"],"optionsEn":["Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","Material selectivity needs comparative evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料選擇性需實際對照證據。 方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","explanationEn":"Material selectivity needs comparative evidence. Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}},{"id":"a052-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-15"],"title":"將粗糙度頻譜前後疊合","titleEn":"Overlay roughness spectra before and after etching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平均平滑可能掩蓋特定尺度粗糙化。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mean smoothing can hide roughening at particular scales.","instruction":"將粗糙度頻譜前後疊合。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「平均平滑可能掩蓋特定尺度粗糙化。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Overlay roughness spectra before and after etching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mean smoothing can hide roughening at particular scales.","observation":"平均平滑可能掩蓋特定尺度粗糙化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mean smoothing can hide roughening at particular scales. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將粗糙度頻譜前後疊合」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平均平滑可能掩蓋特定尺度粗糙化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Overlay roughness spectra before and after etching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mean smoothing can hide roughening at particular scales.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平均平滑可能掩蓋特定尺度粗糙化。","textEn":"Mean smoothing can hide roughening at particular scales."},{"id":"a052-v8-16-k2","title":"三維與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","textEn":"Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將粗糙度頻譜前後疊合」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Overlay roughness spectra before and after etching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均平滑可能掩蓋特定尺度粗糙化。","自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Mean smoothing can hide roughening at particular scales.","Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均平滑可能掩蓋特定尺度粗糙化。 方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","explanationEn":"Mean smoothing can hide roughening at particular scales. Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}},{"id":"a052-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-16"],"title":"檢查表面改質層是否殘留","titleEn":"Check for residual modified surface layers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何完成不等於化學狀態恢復。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Geometric completion does not imply restored chemistry.","instruction":"檢查表面改質層是否殘留。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「幾何完成不等於化學狀態恢復。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check for residual modified surface layers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Geometric completion does not imply restored chemistry.","observation":"幾何完成不等於化學狀態恢復。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Geometric completion does not imply restored chemistry. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查表面改質層是否殘留」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何完成不等於化學狀態恢復。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check for residual modified surface layers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Geometric completion does not imply restored chemistry.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何完成不等於化學狀態恢復。","textEn":"Geometric completion does not imply restored chemistry."},{"id":"a052-v8-17-k2","title":"三維與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","textEn":"Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查表面改質層是否殘留」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check for residual modified surface layers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","幾何完成不等於化學狀態恢復。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Geometric completion does not imply restored chemistry.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"幾何完成不等於化學狀態恢復。 方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","explanationEn":"Geometric completion does not imply restored chemistry. Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}},{"id":"a052-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-17"],"title":"分析循環中的再沉積可能性","titleEn":"Assess redeposition during cycles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：移除產物仍須有效排出。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Removed products must still be evacuated effectively.","instruction":"分析循環中的再沉積可能性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「移除產物仍須有效排出。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess redeposition during cycles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Removed products must still be evacuated effectively.","observation":"移除產物仍須有效排出。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Removed products must still be evacuated effectively. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分析循環中的再沉積可能性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「移除產物仍須有效排出。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess redeposition during cycles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Removed products must still be evacuated effectively.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"移除產物仍須有效排出。","textEn":"Removed products must still be evacuated effectively."},{"id":"a052-v8-18-k2","title":"三維與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","textEn":"Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分析循環中的再沉積可能性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess redeposition during cycles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["自限制就表示所有材料完全不受影響。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","移除產物仍須有效排出。"],"optionsEn":["Self-limitation means all other materials are completely unaffected.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","Removed products must still be evacuated effectively."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除產物仍須有效排出。 方向性、材料選擇性與損傷是不同控制目標。","explanationEn":"Removed products must still be evacuated effectively. Directionality, material selectivity and damage are separate control objectives."}}]},{"id":"a052-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性與效率","titleEn":"Electrical quality and efficiency","description":"小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","descriptionEn":"Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency.","steps":[{"id":"a052-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-18"],"title":"比較閘極凹槽深度與電性","titleEn":"Compare gate-recess depth with electrical behavior","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：薄層深度差可改變元件特性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Small depth changes can alter device behavior.","instruction":"比較閘極凹槽深度與電性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「薄層深度差可改變元件特性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare gate-recess depth with electrical behavior. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Small depth changes can alter device behavior.","observation":"薄層深度差可改變元件特性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Small depth changes can alter device behavior. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較閘極凹槽深度與電性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「薄層深度差可改變元件特性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare gate-recess depth with electrical behavior\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Small depth changes can alter device behavior.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"薄層深度差可改變元件特性。","textEn":"Small depth changes can alter device behavior."},{"id":"a052-v8-19-k2","title":"電性與效率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and efficiency: principle and limits","text":"小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","textEn":"Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較閘極凹槽深度與電性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare gate-recess depth with electrical behavior\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["薄層深度差可改變元件特性。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。"],"optionsEn":["Small depth changes can alter device behavior.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE."],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄層深度差可改變元件特性。 小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","explanationEn":"Small depth changes can alter device behavior. Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}},{"id":"a052-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-19"],"title":"以漏電或介面量測檢查損傷","titleEn":"Check damage through leakage or interface measurements","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低能量處理仍需電性證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low-energy processing still needs electrical evidence.","instruction":"以漏電或介面量測檢查損傷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「低能量處理仍需電性證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check damage through leakage or interface measurements. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low-energy processing still needs electrical evidence.","observation":"低能量處理仍需電性證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low-energy processing still needs electrical evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以漏電或介面量測檢查損傷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低能量處理仍需電性證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check damage through leakage or interface measurements\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low-energy processing still needs electrical evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低能量處理仍需電性證據。","textEn":"Low-energy processing still needs electrical evidence."},{"id":"a052-v8-20-k2","title":"電性與效率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and efficiency: principle and limits","text":"小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","textEn":"Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以漏電或介面量測檢查損傷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check damage through leakage or interface measurements\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","低能量處理仍需電性證據。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。"],"optionsEn":["Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","Low-energy processing still needs electrical evidence.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低能量處理仍需電性證據。 小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","explanationEn":"Low-energy processing still needs electrical evidence. Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}},{"id":"a052-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-20"],"title":"比較 ALE 與 RIE 的總處理時間","titleEn":"Compare total ALE and RIE processing time","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：循環精度可能犧牲吞吐量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cyclic precision can trade against throughput.","instruction":"比較 ALE 與 RIE 的總處理時間。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「循環精度可能犧牲吞吐量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare total ALE and RIE processing time. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cyclic precision can trade against throughput.","observation":"循環精度可能犧牲吞吐量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cyclic precision can trade against throughput. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 ALE 與 RIE 的總處理時間」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「循環精度可能犧牲吞吐量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare total ALE and RIE processing time\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cyclic precision can trade against throughput.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"循環精度可能犧牲吞吐量。","textEn":"Cyclic precision can trade against throughput."},{"id":"a052-v8-21-k2","title":"電性與效率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and efficiency: principle and limits","text":"小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","textEn":"Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 ALE 與 RIE 的總處理時間」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare total ALE and RIE processing time\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","循環精度可能犧牲吞吐量。"],"optionsEn":["Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Cyclic precision can trade against throughput."],"answer":2,"explanation":"循環精度可能犧牲吞吐量。 小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","explanationEn":"Cyclic precision can trade against throughput. Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}},{"id":"a052-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-21"],"title":"建立端點與循環數共同控制","titleEn":"Combine endpoint and cycle-count control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：循環計數不能補償所有初始厚度差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cycle counting cannot compensate every initial-thickness difference.","instruction":"建立端點與循環數共同控制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「循環計數不能補償所有初始厚度差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Combine endpoint and cycle-count control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cycle counting cannot compensate every initial-thickness difference.","observation":"循環計數不能補償所有初始厚度差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cycle counting cannot compensate every initial-thickness difference. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立端點與循環數共同控制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「循環計數不能補償所有初始厚度差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Combine endpoint and cycle-count control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cycle counting cannot compensate every initial-thickness difference.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"循環計數不能補償所有初始厚度差。","textEn":"Cycle counting cannot compensate every initial-thickness difference."},{"id":"a052-v8-22-k2","title":"電性與效率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and efficiency: principle and limits","text":"小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","textEn":"Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立端點與循環數共同控制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Combine endpoint and cycle-count control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["循環計數不能補償所有初始厚度差。","蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。"],"optionsEn":["Cycle counting cannot compensate every initial-thickness difference.","Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE."],"answer":0,"explanation":"循環計數不能補償所有初始厚度差。 小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","explanationEn":"Cycle counting cannot compensate every initial-thickness difference. Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}},{"id":"a052-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-22"],"title":"記錄材料適用範圍與未驗證條件","titleEn":"Record material scope and untested conditions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：一種材料的視窗不能直接移植。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A window for one material cannot be transferred directly.","instruction":"記錄材料適用範圍與未驗證條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「一種材料的視窗不能直接移植。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Record material scope and untested conditions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: A window for one material cannot be transferred directly.","observation":"一種材料的視窗不能直接移植。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A window for one material cannot be transferred directly. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「記錄材料適用範圍與未驗證條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「一種材料的視窗不能直接移植。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Record material scope and untested conditions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A window for one material cannot be transferred directly.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"一種材料的視窗不能直接移植。","textEn":"A window for one material cannot be transferred directly."},{"id":"a052-v8-23-k2","title":"電性與效率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and efficiency: principle and limits","text":"小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","textEn":"Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記錄材料適用範圍與未驗證條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Record material scope and untested conditions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","一種材料的視窗不能直接移植。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。"],"optionsEn":["Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","A window for one material cannot be transferred directly.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一種材料的視窗不能直接移植。 小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","explanationEn":"A window for one material cannot be transferred directly. Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}},{"id":"a052-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-ale","v8b-atomic","v8b-lamale","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a052-v8-23"],"title":"交付飽和、選擇性及電性證據包","titleEn":"Deliver saturation, selectivity and electrical evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：自限制主張需要可重現實驗支持。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Self-limitation claims need reproducible experimental support.","instruction":"交付飽和、選擇性及電性證據包。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「自限制主張需要可重現實驗支持。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver saturation, selectivity and electrical evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Self-limitation claims need reproducible experimental support.","observation":"自限制主張需要可重現實驗支持。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Self-limitation claims need reproducible experimental support. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付飽和、選擇性及電性證據包」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「自限制主張需要可重現實驗支持。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver saturation, selectivity and electrical evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Self-limitation claims need reproducible experimental support.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a052-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"自限制主張需要可重現實驗支持。","textEn":"Self-limitation claims need reproducible experimental support."},{"id":"a052-v8-24-k2","title":"電性與效率的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and efficiency: principle and limits","text":"小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","textEn":"Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付飽和、選擇性及電性證據包」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver saturation, selectivity and electrical evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻量很小就完全不需要電性驗證。","任何分段電漿都可直接稱為 ALE。","自限制主張需要可重現實驗支持。"],"optionsEn":["Tiny removal eliminates the need for electrical validation.","Any segmented plasma process is automatically ALE.","Self-limitation claims need reproducible experimental support."],"answer":2,"explanation":"自限制主張需要可重現實驗支持。 小移除量不自動代表無損傷或高效率。","explanationEn":"Self-limitation claims need reproducible experimental support. Small removal per cycle does not automatically mean no damage or high efficiency."}}]}]},{"id":"a053","title":"深反應式離子蝕刻","titleEn":"Deep reactive-ion etching","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究深矽幾何、循環與低溫、深度與輪廓、整合與可靠度；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: deep-silicon geometry, cycling and cryogenics, depth and profile, integration and reliability. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["深矽幾何","循環與低溫","深度與輪廓","整合與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Deep-silicon geometry","Cycling and cryogenics","Depth and profile","Integration and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"etch","subcategoryTitle":"蝕刻與電漿","subcategoryTitleEn":"Etch and plasma","stages":[{"id":"a053-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"深矽幾何","titleEn":"Deep-silicon geometry","description":"DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","descriptionEn":"DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together.","steps":[{"id":"a053-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"用孔深除以孔寬定義深寬比","titleEn":"Define aspect ratio from depth and width","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：深寬比需註明採用的橫向尺度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Aspect ratio needs a stated lateral dimension.","instruction":"用孔深除以孔寬定義深寬比。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「深寬比需註明採用的橫向尺度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define aspect ratio from depth and width. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Aspect ratio needs a stated lateral dimension.","observation":"深寬比需註明採用的橫向尺度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Aspect ratio needs a stated lateral dimension. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用孔深除以孔寬定義深寬比」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「深寬比需註明採用的橫向尺度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define aspect ratio from depth and width\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Aspect ratio needs a stated lateral dimension.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"深寬比需註明採用的橫向尺度。","textEn":"Aspect ratio needs a stated lateral dimension."},{"id":"a053-v8-01-k2","title":"深矽幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deep-silicon geometry: principle and limits","text":"DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","textEn":"DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用孔深除以孔寬定義深寬比」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define aspect ratio from depth and width\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["深寬比需註明採用的橫向尺度。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Aspect ratio needs a stated lateral dimension.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical."],"answer":0,"explanation":"深寬比需註明採用的橫向尺度。 DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","explanationEn":"Aspect ratio needs a stated lateral dimension. DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}},{"id":"a053-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-01"],"title":"比較 MEMS 溝槽與 TSV 孔用途","titleEn":"Compare MEMS trenches with TSV holes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：機械釋放與電性連接有不同要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mechanical release and electrical connection have different requirements.","instruction":"比較 MEMS 溝槽與 TSV 孔用途。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「機械釋放與電性連接有不同要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare MEMS trenches with TSV holes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mechanical release and electrical connection have different requirements.","observation":"機械釋放與電性連接有不同要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mechanical release and electrical connection have different requirements. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 MEMS 溝槽與 TSV 孔用途」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「機械釋放與電性連接有不同要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare MEMS trenches with TSV holes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mechanical release and electrical connection have different requirements.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"機械釋放與電性連接有不同要求。","textEn":"Mechanical release and electrical connection have different requirements."},{"id":"a053-v8-02-k2","title":"深矽幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deep-silicon geometry: principle and limits","text":"DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","textEn":"DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 MEMS 溝槽與 TSV 孔用途」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare MEMS trenches with TSV holes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","機械釋放與電性連接有不同要求。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","Mechanical release and electrical connection have different requirements.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"機械釋放與電性連接有不同要求。 DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","explanationEn":"Mechanical release and electrical connection have different requirements. DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}},{"id":"a053-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-02"],"title":"估算硬罩消耗所允許的深度","titleEn":"Estimate mask-limited achievable depth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：高選擇比仍需保留厚度裕量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: High selectivity still needs thickness margin.","instruction":"估算硬罩消耗所允許的深度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「高選擇比仍需保留厚度裕量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設溝槽目標深度 100 μm、孔寬 5 μm，深寬比為 20。若矽對硬罩選擇比為 50，理想硬罩消耗為 2 μm；初始 2.5 μm 僅剩 0.5 μm。若另需 20% 等效過蝕刻，硬罩總消耗為 2.4 μm，只剩 0.1 μm。數值是假想預算，未包含均勻性與側向侵蝕。","instructionEn":"Estimate mask-limited achievable depth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: High selectivity still needs thickness margin.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a 100 μm target depth and 5 μm width: aspect ratio is 20. At silicon-to-mask selectivity 50, ideal mask loss is 2 μm, leaving 0.5 μm from an initial 2.5 μm. Adding 20% equivalent overetch raises loss to 2.4 μm and leaves only 0.1 μm. These are hypothetical budgets excluding nonuniformity and lateral erosion.","observation":"高選擇比仍需保留厚度裕量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n須報告 AR=20、剩餘 0.5/0.1 μm，並指出小裕量風險。","observationEn":"High selectivity still needs thickness margin. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport AR=20 and 0.5/0.1 μm remainder, identifying the small-margin risk.","failure":"若報告假設「只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算硬罩消耗所允許的深度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「高選擇比仍需保留厚度裕量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：須報告 AR=20、剩餘 0.5/0.1 μm，並指出小裕量風險。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate mask-limited achievable depth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"High selectivity still needs thickness margin.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report AR=20 and 0.5/0.1 μm remainder, identifying the small-margin risk.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"高選擇比仍需保留厚度裕量。","textEn":"High selectivity still needs thickness margin."},{"id":"a053-v8-03-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設溝槽目標深度 100 μm、孔寬 5 μm，深寬比為 20。若矽對硬罩選擇比為 50，理想硬罩消耗為 2 μm；初始 2.5 μm 僅剩 0.5 μm。若另需 20% 等效過蝕刻，硬罩總消耗為 2.4 μm，只剩 0.1 μm。數值是假想預算，未包含均勻性與側向侵蝕。","textEn":"Assume a 100 μm target depth and 5 μm width: aspect ratio is 20. At silicon-to-mask selectivity 50, ideal mask loss is 2 μm, leaving 0.5 μm from an initial 2.5 μm. Adding 20% equivalent overetch raises loss to 2.4 μm and leaves only 0.1 μm. These are hypothetical budgets excluding nonuniformity and lateral erosion."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算硬罩消耗所允許的深度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate mask-limited achievable depth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","高選擇比仍需保留厚度裕量。"],"optionsEn":["Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","High selectivity still needs thickness margin."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高選擇比仍需保留厚度裕量。 DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","explanationEn":"High selectivity still needs thickness margin. DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設溝槽目標深度 100 μm、孔寬 5 μm，深寬比為 20。若矽對硬罩選擇比為 50，理想硬罩消耗為 2 μm；初始 2.5 μm 僅剩 0.5 μm。若另需 20% 等效過蝕刻，硬罩總消耗為 2.4 μm，只剩 0.1 μm。數值是假想預算，未包含均勻性與側向侵蝕。","textEn":"Assume a 100 μm target depth and 5 μm width: aspect ratio is 20. At silicon-to-mask selectivity 50, ideal mask loss is 2 μm, leaving 0.5 μm from an initial 2.5 μm. Adding 20% equivalent overetch raises loss to 2.4 μm and leaves only 0.1 μm. These are hypothetical budgets excluding nonuniformity and lateral erosion.","check":"須報告 AR=20、剩餘 0.5/0.1 μm，並指出小裕量風險。","checkEn":"Report AR=20 and 0.5/0.1 μm remainder, identifying the small-margin risk."}},{"id":"a053-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-03"],"title":"畫出頂部、側壁與底部的輸運路徑","titleEn":"Draw transport paths to top, walls and bottom","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：深部表面接收的通量不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Deep surfaces receive different fluxes.","instruction":"畫出頂部、側壁與底部的輸運路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「深部表面接收的通量不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw transport paths to top, walls and bottom. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Deep surfaces receive different fluxes.","observation":"深部表面接收的通量不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Deep surfaces receive different fluxes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出頂部、側壁與底部的輸運路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「深部表面接收的通量不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw transport paths to top, walls and bottom\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Deep surfaces receive different fluxes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"深部表面接收的通量不同。","textEn":"Deep surfaces receive different fluxes."},{"id":"a053-v8-04-k2","title":"深矽幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deep-silicon geometry: principle and limits","text":"DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","textEn":"DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出頂部、側壁與底部的輸運路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw transport paths to top, walls and bottom\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["深部表面接收的通量不同。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Deep surfaces receive different fluxes.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical."],"answer":0,"explanation":"深部表面接收的通量不同。 DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","explanationEn":"Deep surfaces receive different fluxes. DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}},{"id":"a053-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-04"],"title":"標記晶圓背面散熱與支撐","titleEn":"Mark backside cooling and support","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：深蝕刻熱負載會影響鈍化。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thermal load affects passivation during deep etching.","instruction":"標記晶圓背面散熱與支撐。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「深蝕刻熱負載會影響鈍化。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark backside cooling and support. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thermal load affects passivation during deep etching.","observation":"深蝕刻熱負載會影響鈍化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thermal load affects passivation during deep etching. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記晶圓背面散熱與支撐」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「深蝕刻熱負載會影響鈍化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark backside cooling and support\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thermal load affects passivation during deep etching.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"深蝕刻熱負載會影響鈍化。","textEn":"Thermal load affects passivation during deep etching."},{"id":"a053-v8-05-k2","title":"深矽幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deep-silicon geometry: principle and limits","text":"DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","textEn":"DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記晶圓背面散熱與支撐」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark backside cooling and support\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","深蝕刻熱負載會影響鈍化。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","Thermal load affects passivation during deep etching.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"深蝕刻熱負載會影響鈍化。 DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","explanationEn":"Thermal load affects passivation during deep etching. DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}},{"id":"a053-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-05"],"title":"規畫開放面積與局部密度取樣","titleEn":"Plan sampling of open area and local density","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：圖形密度會影響速率與均勻性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pattern density affects rate and uniformity.","instruction":"規畫開放面積與局部密度取樣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「圖形密度會影響速率與均勻性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plan sampling of open area and local density. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pattern density affects rate and uniformity.","observation":"圖形密度會影響速率與均勻性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pattern density affects rate and uniformity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「規畫開放面積與局部密度取樣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「圖形密度會影響速率與均勻性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan sampling of open area and local density\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pattern density affects rate and uniformity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"圖形密度會影響速率與均勻性。","textEn":"Pattern density affects rate and uniformity."},{"id":"a053-v8-06-k2","title":"深矽幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deep-silicon geometry: principle and limits","text":"DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","textEn":"DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「規畫開放面積與局部密度取樣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan sampling of open area and local density\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","圖形密度會影響速率與均勻性。"],"optionsEn":["Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","Pattern density affects rate and uniformity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"圖形密度會影響速率與均勻性。 DRIE 的深度與方向性須同時考慮掩膜、反應物運輸及側壁保護。","explanationEn":"Pattern density affects rate and uniformity. DRIE depth and directionality depend on mask, transport and sidewall protection together."}}]},{"id":"a053-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"循環與低溫","titleEn":"Cycling and cryogenics","description":"Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","descriptionEn":"Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe.","steps":[{"id":"a053-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-06"],"title":"畫出 Bosch 蝕刻與鈍化交替","titleEn":"Sketch alternating Bosch etch and passivation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：交替作用產生方向性也可能形成扇貝紋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Alternation enables anisotropy and can produce scallops.","instruction":"畫出 Bosch 蝕刻與鈍化交替。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「交替作用產生方向性也可能形成扇貝紋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch alternating Bosch etch and passivation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Alternation enables anisotropy and can produce scallops.","observation":"交替作用產生方向性也可能形成扇貝紋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Alternation enables anisotropy and can produce scallops. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出 Bosch 蝕刻與鈍化交替」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「交替作用產生方向性也可能形成扇貝紋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch alternating Bosch etch and passivation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Alternation enables anisotropy and can produce scallops.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"交替作用產生方向性也可能形成扇貝紋。","textEn":"Alternation enables anisotropy and can produce scallops."},{"id":"a053-v8-07-k2","title":"循環與低溫的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycling and cryogenics: principle and limits","text":"Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","textEn":"Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出 Bosch 蝕刻與鈍化交替」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch alternating Bosch etch and passivation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["交替作用產生方向性也可能形成扇貝紋。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。"],"optionsEn":["Alternation enables anisotropy and can produce scallops.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交替作用產生方向性也可能形成扇貝紋。 Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","explanationEn":"Alternation enables anisotropy and can produce scallops. Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}},{"id":"a053-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-07"],"title":"比較長短循環的輪廓代價","titleEn":"Compare profile costs of long and short cycles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：循環時間會影響粗糙度與效率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cycle timing affects roughness and efficiency.","instruction":"比較長短循環的輪廓代價。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「循環時間會影響粗糙度與效率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare profile costs of long and short cycles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cycle timing affects roughness and efficiency.","observation":"循環時間會影響粗糙度與效率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cycle timing affects roughness and efficiency. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較長短循環的輪廓代價」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「循環時間會影響粗糙度與效率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare profile costs of long and short cycles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cycle timing affects roughness and efficiency.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"循環時間會影響粗糙度與效率。","textEn":"Cycle timing affects roughness and efficiency."},{"id":"a053-v8-08-k2","title":"循環與低溫的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycling and cryogenics: principle and limits","text":"Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","textEn":"Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較長短循環的輪廓代價」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare profile costs of long and short cycles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","循環時間會影響粗糙度與效率。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。"],"optionsEn":["Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","Cycle timing affects roughness and efficiency.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"循環時間會影響粗糙度與效率。 Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","explanationEn":"Cycle timing affects roughness and efficiency. Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}},{"id":"a053-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-08"],"title":"解釋低溫側壁保護的角色","titleEn":"Explain cryogenic sidewall protection","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低溫改變表面反應與鈍化平衡。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low temperature changes surface reaction and passivation balance.","instruction":"解釋低溫側壁保護的角色。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「低溫改變表面反應與鈍化平衡。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Explain cryogenic sidewall protection. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low temperature changes surface reaction and passivation balance.","observation":"低溫改變表面反應與鈍化平衡。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low temperature changes surface reaction and passivation balance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「解釋低溫側壁保護的角色」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低溫改變表面反應與鈍化平衡。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Explain cryogenic sidewall protection\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low temperature changes surface reaction and passivation balance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低溫改變表面反應與鈍化平衡。","textEn":"Low temperature changes surface reaction and passivation balance."},{"id":"a053-v8-09-k2","title":"循環與低溫的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycling and cryogenics: principle and limits","text":"Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","textEn":"Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「解釋低溫側壁保護的角色」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Explain cryogenic sidewall protection\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","低溫改變表面反應與鈍化平衡。"],"optionsEn":["Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","Low temperature changes surface reaction and passivation balance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低溫改變表面反應與鈍化平衡。 Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","explanationEn":"Low temperature changes surface reaction and passivation balance. Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}},{"id":"a053-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-09"],"title":"比較兩種製程的溫度敏感性","titleEn":"Compare temperature sensitivity of both processes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：熱接觸差異可造成輪廓差異。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thermal-contact differences can alter profiles.","instruction":"比較兩種製程的溫度敏感性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「熱接觸差異可造成輪廓差異。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare temperature sensitivity of both processes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thermal-contact differences can alter profiles.","observation":"熱接觸差異可造成輪廓差異。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thermal-contact differences can alter profiles. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較兩種製程的溫度敏感性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「熱接觸差異可造成輪廓差異。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare temperature sensitivity of both processes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thermal-contact differences can alter profiles.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"熱接觸差異可造成輪廓差異。","textEn":"Thermal-contact differences can alter profiles."},{"id":"a053-v8-10-k2","title":"循環與低溫的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycling and cryogenics: principle and limits","text":"Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","textEn":"Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較兩種製程的溫度敏感性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare temperature sensitivity of both processes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["熱接觸差異可造成輪廓差異。","Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thermal-contact differences can alter profiles.","Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱接觸差異可造成輪廓差異。 Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","explanationEn":"Thermal-contact differences can alter profiles. Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}},{"id":"a053-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-10"],"title":"檢查鈍化過多與不足的截面","titleEn":"Inspect profiles with excessive and insufficient passivation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：過量可阻塞，過少可造成側蝕。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Excess can block etching; deficiency can cause lateral erosion.","instruction":"檢查鈍化過多與不足的截面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「過量可阻塞，過少可造成側蝕。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect profiles with excessive and insufficient passivation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Excess can block etching; deficiency can cause lateral erosion.","observation":"過量可阻塞，過少可造成側蝕。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Excess can block etching; deficiency can cause lateral erosion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查鈍化過多與不足的截面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「過量可阻塞，過少可造成側蝕。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect profiles with excessive and insufficient passivation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Excess can block etching; deficiency can cause lateral erosion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"過量可阻塞，過少可造成側蝕。","textEn":"Excess can block etching; deficiency can cause lateral erosion."},{"id":"a053-v8-11-k2","title":"循環與低溫的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycling and cryogenics: principle and limits","text":"Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","textEn":"Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查鈍化過多與不足的截面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect profiles with excessive and insufficient passivation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","過量可阻塞，過少可造成側蝕。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。"],"optionsEn":["Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","Excess can block etching; deficiency can cause lateral erosion.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"過量可阻塞，過少可造成側蝕。 Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","explanationEn":"Excess can block etching; deficiency can cause lateral erosion. Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}},{"id":"a053-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-11"],"title":"追蹤循環參數隨深度的控制概念","titleEn":"Track the concept of depth-dependent cycle control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：深度增加時輸運條件會改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Transport conditions change as depth increases.","instruction":"追蹤循環參數隨深度的控制概念。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「深度增加時輸運條件會改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track the concept of depth-dependent cycle control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Transport conditions change as depth increases.","observation":"深度增加時輸運條件會改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Transport conditions change as depth increases. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤循環參數隨深度的控制概念」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「深度增加時輸運條件會改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track the concept of depth-dependent cycle control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Transport conditions change as depth increases.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"深度增加時輸運條件會改變。","textEn":"Transport conditions change as depth increases."},{"id":"a053-v8-12-k2","title":"循環與低溫的原理與限制","titleEn":"Cycling and cryogenics: principle and limits","text":"Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","textEn":"Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤循環參數隨深度的控制概念」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track the concept of depth-dependent cycle control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["Bosch 與低溫蝕刻的鈍化完全相同。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","深度增加時輸運條件會改變。"],"optionsEn":["Bosch and cryogenic passivation are identical.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","Transport conditions change as depth increases."],"answer":2,"explanation":"深度增加時輸運條件會改變。 Bosch 循環與低溫製程採用不同鈍化控制，不應混成一組配方。","explanationEn":"Transport conditions change as depth increases. Bosch and cryogenic processes use different passivation control and must not be combined into one recipe."}}]},{"id":"a053-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"深度與輪廓","titleEn":"Depth and profile","description":"深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","descriptionEn":"Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom.","steps":[{"id":"a053-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-12"],"title":"比較不同孔徑的蝕刻延遲","titleEn":"Compare etch lag at different opening sizes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：深寬比相依速率可能造成深度差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Aspect-ratio-dependent rate can create depth differences.","instruction":"比較不同孔徑的蝕刻延遲。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「深寬比相依速率可能造成深度差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare etch lag at different opening sizes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Aspect-ratio-dependent rate can create depth differences.","observation":"深寬比相依速率可能造成深度差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Aspect-ratio-dependent rate can create depth differences. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同孔徑的蝕刻延遲」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「深寬比相依速率可能造成深度差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare etch lag at different opening sizes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Aspect-ratio-dependent rate can create depth differences.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"深寬比相依速率可能造成深度差。","textEn":"Aspect-ratio-dependent rate can create depth differences."},{"id":"a053-v8-13-k2","title":"深度與輪廓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Depth and profile: principle and limits","text":"深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","textEn":"Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同孔徑的蝕刻延遲」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare etch lag at different opening sizes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["深寬比相依速率可能造成深度差。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。"],"optionsEn":["Aspect-ratio-dependent rate can create depth differences.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","An open hole means a completed TSV."],"answer":0,"explanation":"深寬比相依速率可能造成深度差。 深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","explanationEn":"Aspect-ratio-dependent rate can create depth differences. Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}},{"id":"a053-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-13"],"title":"量測頂寬、底寬與側壁角","titleEn":"Measure top width, bottom width and wall angle","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：只量測孔口不能描述截面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Opening width alone cannot describe the section.","instruction":"量測頂寬、底寬與側壁角。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「只量測孔口不能描述截面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure top width, bottom width and wall angle. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Opening width alone cannot describe the section.","observation":"只量測孔口不能描述截面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Opening width alone cannot describe the section. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測頂寬、底寬與側壁角」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「只量測孔口不能描述截面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure top width, bottom width and wall angle\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Opening width alone cannot describe the section.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"只量測孔口不能描述截面。","textEn":"Opening width alone cannot describe the section."},{"id":"a053-v8-14-k2","title":"深度與輪廓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Depth and profile: principle and limits","text":"深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","textEn":"Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測頂寬、底寬與側壁角」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure top width, bottom width and wall angle\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","只量測孔口不能描述截面。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。"],"optionsEn":["Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","Opening width alone cannot describe the section.","An open hole means a completed TSV."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只量測孔口不能描述截面。 深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","explanationEn":"Opening width alone cannot describe the section. Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}},{"id":"a053-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-14"],"title":"計算扇貝紋的振幅與週期","titleEn":"Measure scallop amplitude and period","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：扇貝紋會影響後續覆蓋與應力。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Scallops affect subsequent coverage and stress.","instruction":"計算扇貝紋的振幅與週期。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「扇貝紋會影響後續覆蓋與應力。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure scallop amplitude and period. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Scallops affect subsequent coverage and stress.","observation":"扇貝紋會影響後續覆蓋與應力。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Scallops affect subsequent coverage and stress. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「計算扇貝紋的振幅與週期」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「扇貝紋會影響後續覆蓋與應力。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure scallop amplitude and period\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Scallops affect subsequent coverage and stress.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"扇貝紋會影響後續覆蓋與應力。","textEn":"Scallops affect subsequent coverage and stress."},{"id":"a053-v8-15-k2","title":"深度與輪廓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Depth and profile: principle and limits","text":"深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","textEn":"Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「計算扇貝紋的振幅與週期」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure scallop amplitude and period\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","扇貝紋會影響後續覆蓋與應力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","An open hole means a completed TSV.","Scallops affect subsequent coverage and stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"扇貝紋會影響後續覆蓋與應力。 深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","explanationEn":"Scallops affect subsequent coverage and stress. Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}},{"id":"a053-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-15"],"title":"辨識底部缺口與介電停止層充電","titleEn":"Identify notching near a dielectric stop","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：底部電場改變可能導致側向異常。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Changed bottom fields can cause lateral anomalies.","instruction":"辨識底部缺口與介電停止層充電。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「底部電場改變可能導致側向異常。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify notching near a dielectric stop. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Changed bottom fields can cause lateral anomalies.","observation":"底部電場改變可能導致側向異常。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Changed bottom fields can cause lateral anomalies. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「辨識底部缺口與介電停止層充電」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「底部電場改變可能導致側向異常。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify notching near a dielectric stop\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Changed bottom fields can cause lateral anomalies.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"底部電場改變可能導致側向異常。","textEn":"Changed bottom fields can cause lateral anomalies."},{"id":"a053-v8-16-k2","title":"深度與輪廓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Depth and profile: principle and limits","text":"深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","textEn":"Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「辨識底部缺口與介電停止層充電」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify notching near a dielectric stop\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["底部電場改變可能導致側向異常。","孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。"],"optionsEn":["Changed bottom fields can cause lateral anomalies.","Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","An open hole means a completed TSV."],"answer":0,"explanation":"底部電場改變可能導致側向異常。 深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","explanationEn":"Changed bottom fields can cause lateral anomalies. Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}},{"id":"a053-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-16"],"title":"檢查晶圓中心與邊緣的深度圖","titleEn":"Inspect center-to-edge depth maps","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：全片均勻性與局部深寬比效應不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Wafer uniformity differs from local aspect-ratio effects.","instruction":"檢查晶圓中心與邊緣的深度圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「全片均勻性與局部深寬比效應不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect center-to-edge depth maps. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Wafer uniformity differs from local aspect-ratio effects.","observation":"全片均勻性與局部深寬比效應不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Wafer uniformity differs from local aspect-ratio effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查晶圓中心與邊緣的深度圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「全片均勻性與局部深寬比效應不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect center-to-edge depth maps\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Wafer uniformity differs from local aspect-ratio effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"全片均勻性與局部深寬比效應不同。","textEn":"Wafer uniformity differs from local aspect-ratio effects."},{"id":"a053-v8-17-k2","title":"深度與輪廓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Depth and profile: principle and limits","text":"深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","textEn":"Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查晶圓中心與邊緣的深度圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect center-to-edge depth maps\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","全片均勻性與局部深寬比效應不同。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。"],"optionsEn":["Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","Wafer uniformity differs from local aspect-ratio effects.","An open hole means a completed TSV."],"answer":1,"explanation":"全片均勻性與局部深寬比效應不同。 深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","explanationEn":"Wafer uniformity differs from local aspect-ratio effects. Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}},{"id":"a053-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-17"],"title":"比較時間控制與光學端點證據","titleEn":"Compare timed control with optical endpoint evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：端點訊號需能辨識實際停止層。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Endpoint signals must identify the actual stop layer.","instruction":"比較時間控制與光學端點證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「端點訊號需能辨識實際停止層。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare timed control with optical endpoint evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Endpoint signals must identify the actual stop layer.","observation":"端點訊號需能辨識實際停止層。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Endpoint signals must identify the actual stop layer. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較時間控制與光學端點證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「端點訊號需能辨識實際停止層。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare timed control with optical endpoint evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Endpoint signals must identify the actual stop layer.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"端點訊號需能辨識實際停止層。","textEn":"Endpoint signals must identify the actual stop layer."},{"id":"a053-v8-18-k2","title":"深度與輪廓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Depth and profile: principle and limits","text":"深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","textEn":"Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較時間控制與光學端點證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare timed control with optical endpoint evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口寬度相同就代表底部速率相同。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","端點訊號需能辨識實際停止層。"],"optionsEn":["Equal opening width proves equal bottom etch rate.","An open hole means a completed TSV.","Endpoint signals must identify the actual stop layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"端點訊號需能辨識實際停止層。 深寬比增加會改變離子與中性物種到達底部的機會。","explanationEn":"Endpoint signals must identify the actual stop layer. Increasing aspect ratio changes ion and neutral access to the bottom."}}]},{"id":"a053-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合與可靠度","titleEn":"Integration and reliability","description":"深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","descriptionEn":"Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality.","steps":[{"id":"a053-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-18"],"title":"評估側壁殘留去除的需求","titleEn":"Assess removal of sidewall residue","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘留會影響絕緣與黏著。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residue affects insulation and adhesion.","instruction":"評估側壁殘留去除的需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「殘留會影響絕緣與黏著。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess removal of sidewall residue. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residue affects insulation and adhesion.","observation":"殘留會影響絕緣與黏著。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residue affects insulation and adhesion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An open hole means a completed TSV.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估側壁殘留去除的需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘留會影響絕緣與黏著。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess removal of sidewall residue\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residue affects insulation and adhesion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘留會影響絕緣與黏著。","textEn":"Residue affects insulation and adhesion."},{"id":"a053-v8-19-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","textEn":"Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估側壁殘留去除的需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess removal of sidewall residue\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["殘留會影響絕緣與黏著。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。"],"optionsEn":["Residue affects insulation and adhesion.","An open hole means a completed TSV.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘留會影響絕緣與黏著。 深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","explanationEn":"Residue affects insulation and adhesion. Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}},{"id":"a053-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-19"],"title":"畫出深孔絕緣層的覆蓋困難","titleEn":"Sketch insulation-coverage challenges in deep holes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：蝕刻輪廓決定後續可沉積性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Etch profile determines later depositability.","instruction":"畫出深孔絕緣層的覆蓋困難。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「蝕刻輪廓決定後續可沉積性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch insulation-coverage challenges in deep holes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Etch profile determines later depositability.","observation":"蝕刻輪廓決定後續可沉積性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Etch profile determines later depositability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An open hole means a completed TSV.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出深孔絕緣層的覆蓋困難」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「蝕刻輪廓決定後續可沉積性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch insulation-coverage challenges in deep holes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Etch profile determines later depositability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"蝕刻輪廓決定後續可沉積性。","textEn":"Etch profile determines later depositability."},{"id":"a053-v8-20-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","textEn":"Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出深孔絕緣層的覆蓋困難」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch insulation-coverage challenges in deep holes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","蝕刻輪廓決定後續可沉積性。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。"],"optionsEn":["An open hole means a completed TSV.","Etch profile determines later depositability.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"蝕刻輪廓決定後續可沉積性。 深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","explanationEn":"Etch profile determines later depositability. Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}},{"id":"a053-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-20"],"title":"比較深孔金屬填充與機械釋放驗收","titleEn":"Compare metal-fill and mechanical-release acceptance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：用途不同會改變允許粗糙度與殘留。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Application changes acceptable roughness and residue.","instruction":"比較深孔金屬填充與機械釋放驗收。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「用途不同會改變允許粗糙度與殘留。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare metal-fill and mechanical-release acceptance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Application changes acceptable roughness and residue.","observation":"用途不同會改變允許粗糙度與殘留。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Application changes acceptable roughness and residue. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An open hole means a completed TSV.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較深孔金屬填充與機械釋放驗收」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「用途不同會改變允許粗糙度與殘留。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare metal-fill and mechanical-release acceptance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Application changes acceptable roughness and residue.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"用途不同會改變允許粗糙度與殘留。","textEn":"Application changes acceptable roughness and residue."},{"id":"a053-v8-21-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","textEn":"Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較深孔金屬填充與機械釋放驗收」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare metal-fill and mechanical-release acceptance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","用途不同會改變允許粗糙度與殘留。"],"optionsEn":["An open hole means a completed TSV.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","Application changes acceptable roughness and residue."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用途不同會改變允許粗糙度與殘留。 深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","explanationEn":"Application changes acceptable roughness and residue. Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}},{"id":"a053-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-21"],"title":"檢查薄結構翹曲與破裂","titleEn":"Inspect warpage and fracture of thin structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何深度之外還需機械穩定性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Mechanical stability matters beyond geometric depth.","instruction":"檢查薄結構翹曲與破裂。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「幾何深度之外還需機械穩定性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect warpage and fracture of thin structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Mechanical stability matters beyond geometric depth.","observation":"幾何深度之外還需機械穩定性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Mechanical stability matters beyond geometric depth. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An open hole means a completed TSV.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查薄結構翹曲與破裂」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何深度之外還需機械穩定性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect warpage and fracture of thin structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Mechanical stability matters beyond geometric depth.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何深度之外還需機械穩定性。","textEn":"Mechanical stability matters beyond geometric depth."},{"id":"a053-v8-22-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","textEn":"Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查薄結構翹曲與破裂」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect warpage and fracture of thin structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["幾何深度之外還需機械穩定性。","孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。"],"optionsEn":["Mechanical stability matters beyond geometric depth.","An open hole means a completed TSV.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何深度之外還需機械穩定性。 深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","explanationEn":"Mechanical stability matters beyond geometric depth. Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}},{"id":"a053-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-22"],"title":"建立對照截面與功能量測","titleEn":"Pair cross sections with functional measurements","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：形貌合格不自動證明功能合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Acceptable morphology does not automatically prove function.","instruction":"建立對照截面與功能量測。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「形貌合格不自動證明功能合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Pair cross sections with functional measurements. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Acceptable morphology does not automatically prove function.","observation":"形貌合格不自動證明功能合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Acceptable morphology does not automatically prove function. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An open hole means a completed TSV.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立對照截面與功能量測」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「形貌合格不自動證明功能合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Pair cross sections with functional measurements\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Acceptable morphology does not automatically prove function.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"形貌合格不自動證明功能合格。","textEn":"Acceptable morphology does not automatically prove function."},{"id":"a053-v8-23-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","textEn":"Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立對照截面與功能量測」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Pair cross sections with functional measurements\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","形貌合格不自動證明功能合格。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。"],"optionsEn":["An open hole means a completed TSV.","Acceptable morphology does not automatically prove function.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"形貌合格不自動證明功能合格。 深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","explanationEn":"Acceptable morphology does not automatically prove function. Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}},{"id":"a053-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v8b-caltechdrie","v8b-rie","v8b-endpoint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a053-v8-23"],"title":"交付深度、側壁與後續相容性報告","titleEn":"Report depth, walls and downstream compatibility","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：DRIE 應作為整合流程的一部分驗收。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: DRIE should be accepted as part of an integrated flow.","instruction":"交付深度、側壁與後續相容性報告。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「DRIE 應作為整合流程的一部分驗收。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Report depth, walls and downstream compatibility. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: DRIE should be accepted as part of an integrated flow.","observation":"DRIE 應作為整合流程的一部分驗收。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"DRIE should be accepted as part of an integrated flow. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An open hole means a completed TSV.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付深度、側壁與後續相容性報告」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「DRIE 應作為整合流程的一部分驗收。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Report depth, walls and downstream compatibility\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"DRIE should be accepted as part of an integrated flow.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a053-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"DRIE 應作為整合流程的一部分驗收。","textEn":"DRIE should be accepted as part of an integrated flow."},{"id":"a053-v8-24-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","textEn":"Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付深度、側壁與後續相容性報告」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Report depth, walls and downstream compatibility\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔洞已打通就等於 TSV 已完成。","只延長時間就能維持相同輪廓無限加深。","DRIE 應作為整合流程的一部分驗收。"],"optionsEn":["An open hole means a completed TSV.","Longer time preserves the same profile at unlimited depth.","DRIE should be accepted as part of an integrated flow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"DRIE 應作為整合流程的一部分驗收。 深孔完成後的清潔、絕緣與金屬化會決定最終功能。","explanationEn":"DRIE should be accepted as part of an integrated flow. Cleaning, insulation and metallization after etching determine final functionality."}}]}]},{"id":"a054","title":"高深寬比介電層蝕刻","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究介電堆疊、輸運與充電、輪廓控制、端點與功能；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: dielectric stacks, transport and charging, profile control, endpoint and function. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["介電堆疊","輸運與充電","輪廓控制","端點與功能"],"labelsEn":["Dielectric stacks","Transport and charging","Profile control","Endpoint and function"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"etch","subcategoryTitle":"蝕刻與電漿","subcategoryTitleEn":"Etch and plasma","stages":[{"id":"a054-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"介電堆疊","titleEn":"Dielectric stacks","description":"高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","descriptionEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport.","steps":[{"id":"a054-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出交替介電層與目標通道","titleEn":"Draw alternating dielectric layers and the target channel","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同材料層可能有不同移除速率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different layers can have different removal rates.","instruction":"畫出交替介電層與目標通道。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「不同材料層可能有不同移除速率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw alternating dielectric layers and the target channel. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different layers can have different removal rates.","observation":"不同材料層可能有不同移除速率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different layers can have different removal rates. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出交替介電層與目標通道」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同材料層可能有不同移除速率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw alternating dielectric layers and the target channel\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different layers can have different removal rates.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同材料層可能有不同移除速率。","textEn":"Different layers can have different removal rates."},{"id":"a054-v8-01-k2","title":"介電堆疊的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric stacks: principle and limits","text":"高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","textEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出交替介電層與目標通道」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw alternating dielectric layers and the target channel\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同材料層可能有不同移除速率。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。"],"optionsEn":["Different layers can have different removal rates.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同材料層可能有不同移除速率。 高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","explanationEn":"Different layers can have different removal rates. High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}},{"id":"a054-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-01"],"title":"定義深度、最小孔徑與偏斜量","titleEn":"Define depth, minimum diameter and deviation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：輪廓需要多個幾何指標。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Profiles require multiple geometric metrics.","instruction":"定義深度、最小孔徑與偏斜量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「輪廓需要多個幾何指標。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define depth, minimum diameter and deviation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Profiles require multiple geometric metrics.","observation":"輪廓需要多個幾何指標。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Profiles require multiple geometric metrics. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「定義深度、最小孔徑與偏斜量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「輪廓需要多個幾何指標。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define depth, minimum diameter and deviation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Profiles require multiple geometric metrics.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"輪廓需要多個幾何指標。","textEn":"Profiles require multiple geometric metrics."},{"id":"a054-v8-02-k2","title":"介電堆疊的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric stacks: principle and limits","text":"高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","textEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「定義深度、最小孔徑與偏斜量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define depth, minimum diameter and deviation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","輪廓需要多個幾何指標。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。"],"optionsEn":["Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","Profiles require multiple geometric metrics.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons."],"answer":1,"explanation":"輪廓需要多個幾何指標。 高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","explanationEn":"Profiles require multiple geometric metrics. High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}},{"id":"a054-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-02"],"title":"估算硬罩厚度與孔口縮窄","titleEn":"Estimate mask thickness and opening narrowing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：厚硬罩也會增加入口輸運限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thick masks can also restrict entrance transport.","instruction":"估算硬罩厚度與孔口縮窄。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「厚硬罩也會增加入口輸運限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate mask thickness and opening narrowing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thick masks can also restrict entrance transport.","observation":"厚硬罩也會增加入口輸運限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thick masks can also restrict entrance transport. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算硬罩厚度與孔口縮窄」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「厚硬罩也會增加入口輸運限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate mask thickness and opening narrowing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thick masks can also restrict entrance transport.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"厚硬罩也會增加入口輸運限制。","textEn":"Thick masks can also restrict entrance transport."},{"id":"a054-v8-03-k2","title":"介電堆疊的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric stacks: principle and limits","text":"高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","textEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算硬罩厚度與孔口縮窄」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate mask thickness and opening narrowing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","厚硬罩也會增加入口輸運限制。"],"optionsEn":["Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","Thick masks can also restrict entrance transport."],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚硬罩也會增加入口輸運限制。 高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","explanationEn":"Thick masks can also restrict entrance transport. High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}},{"id":"a054-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-03"],"title":"比較單層與多層堆疊模型","titleEn":"Compare single-layer and multilayer models","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單一平均材料不能捕捉層間反應差異。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: An average material misses layer-specific reactions.","instruction":"比較單層與多層堆疊模型。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「單一平均材料不能捕捉層間反應差異。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare single-layer and multilayer models. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: An average material misses layer-specific reactions.","observation":"單一平均材料不能捕捉層間反應差異。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"An average material misses layer-specific reactions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較單層與多層堆疊模型」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單一平均材料不能捕捉層間反應差異。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare single-layer and multilayer models\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"An average material misses layer-specific reactions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單一平均材料不能捕捉層間反應差異。","textEn":"An average material misses layer-specific reactions."},{"id":"a054-v8-04-k2","title":"介電堆疊的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric stacks: principle and limits","text":"高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","textEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較單層與多層堆疊模型」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare single-layer and multilayer models\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單一平均材料不能捕捉層間反應差異。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。"],"optionsEn":["An average material misses layer-specific reactions.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一平均材料不能捕捉層間反應差異。 高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","explanationEn":"An average material misses layer-specific reactions. High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}},{"id":"a054-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-04"],"title":"標記開口密度與全片負載","titleEn":"Mark open-area density and wafer loading","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：圖形布局會影響反應物供應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Layout influences reactant supply.","instruction":"標記開口密度與全片負載。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「圖形布局會影響反應物供應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark open-area density and wafer loading. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Layout influences reactant supply.","observation":"圖形布局會影響反應物供應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Layout influences reactant supply. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記開口密度與全片負載」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「圖形布局會影響反應物供應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark open-area density and wafer loading\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Layout influences reactant supply.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"圖形布局會影響反應物供應。","textEn":"Layout influences reactant supply."},{"id":"a054-v8-05-k2","title":"介電堆疊的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric stacks: principle and limits","text":"高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","textEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記開口密度與全片負載」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark open-area density and wafer loading\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","圖形布局會影響反應物供應。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。"],"optionsEn":["Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","Layout influences reactant supply.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons."],"answer":1,"explanation":"圖形布局會影響反應物供應。 高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","explanationEn":"Layout influences reactant supply. High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}},{"id":"a054-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-05"],"title":"建立孔底允許損傷的功能需求","titleEn":"Define allowable bottom damage from function","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：停止位置需連結後續接觸或儲存功能。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Stop position must relate to later contact or storage function.","instruction":"建立孔底允許損傷的功能需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「停止位置需連結後續接觸或儲存功能。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define allowable bottom damage from function. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Stop position must relate to later contact or storage function.","observation":"停止位置需連結後續接觸或儲存功能。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Stop position must relate to later contact or storage function. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立孔底允許損傷的功能需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「停止位置需連結後續接觸或儲存功能。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define allowable bottom damage from function\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Stop position must relate to later contact or storage function.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"停止位置需連結後續接觸或儲存功能。","textEn":"Stop position must relate to later contact or storage function."},{"id":"a054-v8-06-k2","title":"介電堆疊的原理與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric stacks: principle and limits","text":"高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","textEn":"High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立孔底允許損傷的功能需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define allowable bottom damage from function\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","停止位置需連結後續接觸或儲存功能。"],"optionsEn":["Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","Stop position must relate to later contact or storage function."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停止位置需連結後續接觸或儲存功能。 高深寬比介電蝕刻要同時管理硬罩消耗、帶電粒子與反應物輸運。","explanationEn":"Stop position must relate to later contact or storage function. High-aspect-ratio dielectric etching jointly manages mask consumption, charged particles and reactant transport."}}]},{"id":"a054-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"輸運與充電","titleEn":"Transport and charging","description":"絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","descriptionEn":"Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories.","steps":[{"id":"a054-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-06"],"title":"畫出離子與自由基的不同入孔路徑","titleEn":"Draw distinct ion and radical entry paths","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：方向性物種與中性物種傳輸不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Directional and neutral species travel differently.","instruction":"畫出離子與自由基的不同入孔路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「方向性物種與中性物種傳輸不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw distinct ion and radical entry paths. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Directional and neutral species travel differently.","observation":"方向性物種與中性物種傳輸不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Directional and neutral species travel differently. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出離子與自由基的不同入孔路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「方向性物種與中性物種傳輸不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw distinct ion and radical entry paths\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Directional and neutral species travel differently.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"方向性物種與中性物種傳輸不同。","textEn":"Directional and neutral species travel differently."},{"id":"a054-v8-07-k2","title":"輸運與充電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and charging: principle and limits","text":"絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","textEn":"Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出離子與自由基的不同入孔路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw distinct ion and radical entry paths\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["方向性物種與中性物種傳輸不同。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。"],"optionsEn":["Directional and neutral species travel differently.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole."],"answer":0,"explanation":"方向性物種與中性物種傳輸不同。 絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","explanationEn":"Directional and neutral species travel differently. Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}},{"id":"a054-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-07"],"title":"比較高深寬比下的反應物耗盡","titleEn":"Assess reactant depletion at high aspect ratio","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：孔底反應可能受輸運而非源端濃度限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bottom reactions can be transport-limited rather than source-limited.","instruction":"比較高深寬比下的反應物耗盡。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「孔底反應可能受輸運而非源端濃度限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess reactant depletion at high aspect ratio. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bottom reactions can be transport-limited rather than source-limited.","observation":"孔底反應可能受輸運而非源端濃度限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bottom reactions can be transport-limited rather than source-limited. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較高深寬比下的反應物耗盡」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「孔底反應可能受輸運而非源端濃度限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess reactant depletion at high aspect ratio\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bottom reactions can be transport-limited rather than source-limited.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"孔底反應可能受輸運而非源端濃度限制。","textEn":"Bottom reactions can be transport-limited rather than source-limited."},{"id":"a054-v8-08-k2","title":"輸運與充電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and charging: principle and limits","text":"絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","textEn":"Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較高深寬比下的反應物耗盡」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess reactant depletion at high aspect ratio\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","孔底反應可能受輸運而非源端濃度限制。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。"],"optionsEn":["Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","Bottom reactions can be transport-limited rather than source-limited.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole."],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔底反應可能受輸運而非源端濃度限制。 絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","explanationEn":"Bottom reactions can be transport-limited rather than source-limited. Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}},{"id":"a054-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-08"],"title":"分析電子與離子到達不對稱","titleEn":"Analyze unequal electron and ion access","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：到達差異可形成局部電位。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Unequal access can create local potentials.","instruction":"分析電子與離子到達不對稱。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「到達差異可形成局部電位。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Analyze unequal electron and ion access. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Unequal access can create local potentials.","observation":"到達差異可形成局部電位。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Unequal access can create local potentials. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分析電子與離子到達不對稱」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「到達差異可形成局部電位。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Analyze unequal electron and ion access\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Unequal access can create local potentials.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"到達差異可形成局部電位。","textEn":"Unequal access can create local potentials."},{"id":"a054-v8-09-k2","title":"輸運與充電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and charging: principle and limits","text":"絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","textEn":"Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分析電子與離子到達不對稱」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Analyze unequal electron and ion access\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","到達差異可形成局部電位。"],"optionsEn":["Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Unequal access can create local potentials."],"answer":2,"explanation":"到達差異可形成局部電位。 絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","explanationEn":"Unequal access can create local potentials. Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}},{"id":"a054-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-09"],"title":"畫出充電偏折造成的孔道彎曲","titleEn":"Sketch charging-induced channel deflection","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部電場可能使孔道偏離垂直。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local fields can deflect channels from vertical.","instruction":"畫出充電偏折造成的孔道彎曲。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「局部電場可能使孔道偏離垂直。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch charging-induced channel deflection. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local fields can deflect channels from vertical.","observation":"局部電場可能使孔道偏離垂直。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local fields can deflect channels from vertical. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出充電偏折造成的孔道彎曲」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部電場可能使孔道偏離垂直。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch charging-induced channel deflection\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local fields can deflect channels from vertical.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部電場可能使孔道偏離垂直。","textEn":"Local fields can deflect channels from vertical."},{"id":"a054-v8-10-k2","title":"輸運與充電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and charging: principle and limits","text":"絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","textEn":"Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出充電偏折造成的孔道彎曲」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch charging-induced channel deflection\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["局部電場可能使孔道偏離垂直。","介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。"],"optionsEn":["Local fields can deflect channels from vertical.","Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole."],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部電場可能使孔道偏離垂直。 絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","explanationEn":"Local fields can deflect channels from vertical. Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}},{"id":"a054-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-10"],"title":"比較連續與脈衝控制的研究目標","titleEn":"Compare goals of continuous and pulsed control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：脈衝設計可影響充電與反應歷程。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pulsing can alter charging and reaction history.","instruction":"比較連續與脈衝控制的研究目標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「脈衝設計可影響充電與反應歷程。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare goals of continuous and pulsed control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pulsing can alter charging and reaction history.","observation":"脈衝設計可影響充電與反應歷程。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pulsing can alter charging and reaction history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較連續與脈衝控制的研究目標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「脈衝設計可影響充電與反應歷程。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare goals of continuous and pulsed control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pulsing can alter charging and reaction history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"脈衝設計可影響充電與反應歷程。","textEn":"Pulsing can alter charging and reaction history."},{"id":"a054-v8-11-k2","title":"輸運與充電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and charging: principle and limits","text":"絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","textEn":"Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較連續與脈衝控制的研究目標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare goals of continuous and pulsed control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","脈衝設計可影響充電與反應歷程。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。"],"optionsEn":["Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","Pulsing can alter charging and reaction history.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole."],"answer":1,"explanation":"脈衝設計可影響充電與反應歷程。 絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","explanationEn":"Pulsing can alter charging and reaction history. Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}},{"id":"a054-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-11"],"title":"檢查孔內副產物排出的限制","titleEn":"Assess byproduct-removal limitations","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：產物滯留可能抑制反應或再沉積。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Retained products can inhibit reaction or redeposit.","instruction":"檢查孔內副產物排出的限制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「產物滯留可能抑制反應或再沉積。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess byproduct-removal limitations. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Retained products can inhibit reaction or redeposit.","observation":"產物滯留可能抑制反應或再沉積。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Retained products can inhibit reaction or redeposit. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查孔內副產物排出的限制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「產物滯留可能抑制反應或再沉積。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess byproduct-removal limitations\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Retained products can inhibit reaction or redeposit.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"產物滯留可能抑制反應或再沉積。","textEn":"Retained products can inhibit reaction or redeposit."},{"id":"a054-v8-12-k2","title":"輸運與充電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and charging: principle and limits","text":"絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","textEn":"Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查孔內副產物排出的限制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess byproduct-removal limitations\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["介電層沒有自由電子，所以不會充電。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","產物滯留可能抑制反應或再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Dielectrics cannot charge because they lack free electrons.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Retained products can inhibit reaction or redeposit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"產物滯留可能抑制反應或再沉積。 絕緣側壁可能累積電荷並改變離子路徑。","explanationEn":"Retained products can inhibit reaction or redeposit. Insulating walls can accumulate charge and alter ion trajectories."}}]},{"id":"a054-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"輪廓控制","titleEn":"Profile control","description":"孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","descriptionEn":"Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths.","steps":[{"id":"a054-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-12"],"title":"量測孔口、最大膨脹處與孔底","titleEn":"Measure opening, maximum bow and bottom","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單一截面寬度不足以描述弓形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One width cannot characterize bowing.","instruction":"量測孔口、最大膨脹處與孔底。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「單一截面寬度不足以描述弓形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設介電孔深 1000 nm，孔口 100 nm，中段最大孔徑 120 nm，孔底最小孔徑 60 nm。以孔口計 AR=10，但以最小孔徑計有效幾何比為 16.7；中段相對孔口膨脹 20%。在同一截面標出三個量測位置，不能只用孔口照片宣告全孔垂直與等寬。","instructionEn":"Measure opening, maximum bow and bottom. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: One width cannot characterize bowing.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a 1000 nm deep dielectric hole with 100 nm opening, 120 nm maximum mid-depth diameter and 60 nm minimum bottom diameter. Opening-based AR is 10, while the minimum-diameter ratio is 16.7; mid-depth bow is 20% relative to the opening. Mark all three sites in one section rather than declaring a straight, uniform hole from an opening image.","observation":"單一截面寬度不足以描述弓形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 10、16.7、20% 與三位置截面標記。","observationEn":"One width cannot characterize bowing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 10, 16.7 and 20% with three labeled cross-sectional sites.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測孔口、最大膨脹處與孔底」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單一截面寬度不足以描述弓形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 10、16.7、20% 與三位置截面標記。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure opening, maximum bow and bottom\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One width cannot characterize bowing.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 10, 16.7 and 20% with three labeled cross-sectional sites.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單一截面寬度不足以描述弓形。","textEn":"One width cannot characterize bowing."},{"id":"a054-v8-13-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設介電孔深 1000 nm，孔口 100 nm，中段最大孔徑 120 nm，孔底最小孔徑 60 nm。以孔口計 AR=10，但以最小孔徑計有效幾何比為 16.7；中段相對孔口膨脹 20%。在同一截面標出三個量測位置，不能只用孔口照片宣告全孔垂直與等寬。","textEn":"Assume a 1000 nm deep dielectric hole with 100 nm opening, 120 nm maximum mid-depth diameter and 60 nm minimum bottom diameter. Opening-based AR is 10, while the minimum-diameter ratio is 16.7; mid-depth bow is 20% relative to the opening. Mark all three sites in one section rather than declaring a straight, uniform hole from an opening image."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測孔口、最大膨脹處與孔底」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure opening, maximum bow and bottom\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單一截面寬度不足以描述弓形。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。"],"optionsEn":["One width cannot characterize bowing.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一截面寬度不足以描述弓形。 孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","explanationEn":"One width cannot characterize bowing. Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設介電孔深 1000 nm，孔口 100 nm，中段最大孔徑 120 nm，孔底最小孔徑 60 nm。以孔口計 AR=10，但以最小孔徑計有效幾何比為 16.7；中段相對孔口膨脹 20%。在同一截面標出三個量測位置，不能只用孔口照片宣告全孔垂直與等寬。","textEn":"Assume a 1000 nm deep dielectric hole with 100 nm opening, 120 nm maximum mid-depth diameter and 60 nm minimum bottom diameter. Opening-based AR is 10, while the minimum-diameter ratio is 16.7; mid-depth bow is 20% relative to the opening. Mark all three sites in one section rather than declaring a straight, uniform hole from an opening image.","check":"交付 10、16.7、20% 與三位置截面標記。","checkEn":"Report 10, 16.7 and 20% with three labeled cross-sectional sites."}},{"id":"a054-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-13"],"title":"比較側壁保護不足與過量","titleEn":"Compare insufficient and excess wall protection","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：保護不足會側蝕，過量會使孔收窄。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Insufficient protection erodes walls; excess narrows holes.","instruction":"比較側壁保護不足與過量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「保護不足會側蝕，過量會使孔收窄。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare insufficient and excess wall protection. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Insufficient protection erodes walls; excess narrows holes.","observation":"保護不足會側蝕，過量會使孔收窄。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Insufficient protection erodes walls; excess narrows holes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較側壁保護不足與過量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「保護不足會側蝕，過量會使孔收窄。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare insufficient and excess wall protection\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Insufficient protection erodes walls; excess narrows holes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"保護不足會側蝕，過量會使孔收窄。","textEn":"Insufficient protection erodes walls; excess narrows holes."},{"id":"a054-v8-14-k2","title":"輪廓控制的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile control: principle and limits","text":"孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","textEn":"Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較側壁保護不足與過量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare insufficient and excess wall protection\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","保護不足會側蝕，過量會使孔收窄。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。"],"optionsEn":["A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Insufficient protection erodes walls; excess narrows holes.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護不足會側蝕，過量會使孔收窄。 孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","explanationEn":"Insufficient protection erodes walls; excess narrows holes. Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}},{"id":"a054-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-14"],"title":"檢查局部材料層造成的條紋","titleEn":"Inspect striations associated with local layers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：層間速率差可能留在側壁形貌中。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Layer-rate differences can remain in wall morphology.","instruction":"檢查局部材料層造成的條紋。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「層間速率差可能留在側壁形貌中。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect striations associated with local layers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Layer-rate differences can remain in wall morphology.","observation":"層間速率差可能留在側壁形貌中。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Layer-rate differences can remain in wall morphology. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查局部材料層造成的條紋」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「層間速率差可能留在側壁形貌中。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect striations associated with local layers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Layer-rate differences can remain in wall morphology.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"層間速率差可能留在側壁形貌中。","textEn":"Layer-rate differences can remain in wall morphology."},{"id":"a054-v8-15-k2","title":"輪廓控制的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile control: principle and limits","text":"孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","textEn":"Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查局部材料層造成的條紋」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect striations associated with local layers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","層間速率差可能留在側壁形貌中。"],"optionsEn":["A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Layer-rate differences can remain in wall morphology."],"answer":2,"explanation":"層間速率差可能留在側壁形貌中。 孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","explanationEn":"Layer-rate differences can remain in wall morphology. Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}},{"id":"a054-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-15"],"title":"追蹤孔道扭曲與設計落點","titleEn":"Trace channel twist against the intended landing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：孔底偏移會破壞層間連接。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bottom displacement can disrupt interlayer connection.","instruction":"追蹤孔道扭曲與設計落點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「孔底偏移會破壞層間連接。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace channel twist against the intended landing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bottom displacement can disrupt interlayer connection.","observation":"孔底偏移會破壞層間連接。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bottom displacement can disrupt interlayer connection. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤孔道扭曲與設計落點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「孔底偏移會破壞層間連接。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace channel twist against the intended landing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bottom displacement can disrupt interlayer connection.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"孔底偏移會破壞層間連接。","textEn":"Bottom displacement can disrupt interlayer connection."},{"id":"a054-v8-16-k2","title":"輪廓控制的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile control: principle and limits","text":"孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","textEn":"Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤孔道扭曲與設計落點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace channel twist against the intended landing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔底偏移會破壞層間連接。","孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。"],"optionsEn":["Bottom displacement can disrupt interlayer connection.","A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient."],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔底偏移會破壞層間連接。 孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","explanationEn":"Bottom displacement can disrupt interlayer connection. Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}},{"id":"a054-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-16"],"title":"比較不同孔徑的深度延遲","titleEn":"Compare depth lag across diameters","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：尺寸差異會造成完成時間分散。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Size differences spread completion times.","instruction":"比較不同孔徑的深度延遲。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「尺寸差異會造成完成時間分散。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare depth lag across diameters. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Size differences spread completion times.","observation":"尺寸差異會造成完成時間分散。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Size differences spread completion times. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同孔徑的深度延遲」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「尺寸差異會造成完成時間分散。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare depth lag across diameters\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Size differences spread completion times.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"尺寸差異會造成完成時間分散。","textEn":"Size differences spread completion times."},{"id":"a054-v8-17-k2","title":"輪廓控制的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile control: principle and limits","text":"孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","textEn":"Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同孔徑的深度延遲」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare depth lag across diameters\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","尺寸差異會造成完成時間分散。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。"],"optionsEn":["A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Size differences spread completion times.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient."],"answer":1,"explanation":"尺寸差異會造成完成時間分散。 孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","explanationEn":"Size differences spread completion times. Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}},{"id":"a054-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-17"],"title":"評估遮罩侵蝕造成的孔口擴大","titleEn":"Assess opening growth caused by mask erosion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：早期遮罩變化會傳入深部輪廓。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Early mask changes propagate into deep profiles.","instruction":"評估遮罩侵蝕造成的孔口擴大。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「早期遮罩變化會傳入深部輪廓。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess opening growth caused by mask erosion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Early mask changes propagate into deep profiles.","observation":"早期遮罩變化會傳入深部輪廓。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Early mask changes propagate into deep profiles. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估遮罩侵蝕造成的孔口擴大」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「早期遮罩變化會傳入深部輪廓。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess opening growth caused by mask erosion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Early mask changes propagate into deep profiles.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"早期遮罩變化會傳入深部輪廓。","textEn":"Early mask changes propagate into deep profiles."},{"id":"a054-v8-18-k2","title":"輪廓控制的原理與限制","titleEn":"Profile control: principle and limits","text":"孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","textEn":"Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估遮罩侵蝕造成的孔口擴大」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess opening growth caused by mask erosion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口圓形可保證整孔筆直。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","早期遮罩變化會傳入深部輪廓。"],"optionsEn":["A circular opening guarantees a straight hole.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Early mask changes propagate into deep profiles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"早期遮罩變化會傳入深部輪廓。 孔形狀由不同深度的局部反應平衡決定。","explanationEn":"Early mask changes propagate into deep profiles. Hole shape follows local reaction balances at different depths."}}]},{"id":"a054-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"端點與功能","titleEn":"Endpoint and function","description":"完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","descriptionEn":"Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage.","steps":[{"id":"a054-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-18"],"title":"選擇能辨識堆疊底部的端點證據","titleEn":"Choose endpoint evidence for the stack bottom","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：發光訊號需對應特定材料轉換。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Emission signals must map to a specific material transition.","instruction":"選擇能辨識堆疊底部的端點證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「發光訊號需對應特定材料轉換。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Choose endpoint evidence for the stack bottom. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Emission signals must map to a specific material transition.","observation":"發光訊號需對應特定材料轉換。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Emission signals must map to a specific material transition. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只檢查是否打通即可驗收。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「選擇能辨識堆疊底部的端點證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「發光訊號需對應特定材料轉換。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Choose endpoint evidence for the stack bottom\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Emission signals must map to a specific material transition.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"發光訊號需對應特定材料轉換。","textEn":"Emission signals must map to a specific material transition."},{"id":"a054-v8-19-k2","title":"端點與功能的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and function: principle and limits","text":"完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","textEn":"Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「選擇能辨識堆疊底部的端點證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Choose endpoint evidence for the stack bottom\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["發光訊號需對應特定材料轉換。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。"],"optionsEn":["Emission signals must map to a specific material transition.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"發光訊號需對應特定材料轉換。 完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","explanationEn":"Emission signals must map to a specific material transition. Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}},{"id":"a054-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-19"],"title":"為最慢孔與最快孔分配過蝕刻裕量","titleEn":"Budget overetch for the slowest and fastest holes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：補足慢孔會增加快孔損傷風險。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Finishing slow holes increases damage risk in fast holes.","instruction":"為最慢孔與最快孔分配過蝕刻裕量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「補足慢孔會增加快孔損傷風險。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Budget overetch for the slowest and fastest holes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Finishing slow holes increases damage risk in fast holes.","observation":"補足慢孔會增加快孔損傷風險。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Finishing slow holes increases damage risk in fast holes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只檢查是否打通即可驗收。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「為最慢孔與最快孔分配過蝕刻裕量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「補足慢孔會增加快孔損傷風險。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Budget overetch for the slowest and fastest holes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Finishing slow holes increases damage risk in fast holes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"補足慢孔會增加快孔損傷風險。","textEn":"Finishing slow holes increases damage risk in fast holes."},{"id":"a054-v8-20-k2","title":"端點與功能的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and function: principle and limits","text":"完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","textEn":"Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「為最慢孔與最快孔分配過蝕刻裕量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Budget overetch for the slowest and fastest holes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","補足慢孔會增加快孔損傷風險。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。"],"optionsEn":["Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Finishing slow holes increases damage risk in fast holes.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"補足慢孔會增加快孔損傷風險。 完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","explanationEn":"Finishing slow holes increases damage risk in fast holes. Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}},{"id":"a054-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-20"],"title":"檢查孔底殘留與局部表面化學","titleEn":"Inspect bottom residue and surface chemistry","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何打通可能仍有絕緣殘留。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Geometric breakthrough can still leave insulating residue.","instruction":"檢查孔底殘留與局部表面化學。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「幾何打通可能仍有絕緣殘留。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect bottom residue and surface chemistry. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Geometric breakthrough can still leave insulating residue.","observation":"幾何打通可能仍有絕緣殘留。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Geometric breakthrough can still leave insulating residue. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只檢查是否打通即可驗收。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查孔底殘留與局部表面化學」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何打通可能仍有絕緣殘留。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect bottom residue and surface chemistry\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Geometric breakthrough can still leave insulating residue.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何打通可能仍有絕緣殘留。","textEn":"Geometric breakthrough can still leave insulating residue."},{"id":"a054-v8-21-k2","title":"端點與功能的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and function: principle and limits","text":"完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","textEn":"Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查孔底殘留與局部表面化學」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect bottom residue and surface chemistry\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","幾何打通可能仍有絕緣殘留。"],"optionsEn":["Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","Geometric breakthrough can still leave insulating residue."],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何打通可能仍有絕緣殘留。 完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","explanationEn":"Geometric breakthrough can still leave insulating residue. Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}},{"id":"a054-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-21"],"title":"比較後續共形膜的覆蓋品質","titleEn":"Compare subsequent conformal-film coverage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：蝕刻輪廓會限制沉積和填孔。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Etch profiles constrain deposition and fill.","instruction":"比較後續共形膜的覆蓋品質。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「蝕刻輪廓會限制沉積和填孔。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare subsequent conformal-film coverage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Etch profiles constrain deposition and fill.","observation":"蝕刻輪廓會限制沉積和填孔。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Etch profiles constrain deposition and fill. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只檢查是否打通即可驗收。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較後續共形膜的覆蓋品質」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「蝕刻輪廓會限制沉積和填孔。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare subsequent conformal-film coverage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Etch profiles constrain deposition and fill.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"蝕刻輪廓會限制沉積和填孔。","textEn":"Etch profiles constrain deposition and fill."},{"id":"a054-v8-22-k2","title":"端點與功能的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and function: principle and limits","text":"完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","textEn":"Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較後續共形膜的覆蓋品質」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare subsequent conformal-film coverage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["蝕刻輪廓會限制沉積和填孔。","只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。"],"optionsEn":["Etch profiles constrain deposition and fill.","Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth."],"answer":0,"explanation":"蝕刻輪廓會限制沉積和填孔。 完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","explanationEn":"Etch profiles constrain deposition and fill. Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}},{"id":"a054-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-22"],"title":"將孔道形貌與電性分布連結","titleEn":"Relate channel morphology to electrical distributions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部幾何差異可造成元件散布。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local geometric differences can cause device variation.","instruction":"將孔道形貌與電性分布連結。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「局部幾何差異可造成元件散布。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate channel morphology to electrical distributions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local geometric differences can cause device variation.","observation":"局部幾何差異可造成元件散布。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local geometric differences can cause device variation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只檢查是否打通即可驗收。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將孔道形貌與電性分布連結」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部幾何差異可造成元件散布。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate channel morphology to electrical distributions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local geometric differences can cause device variation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部幾何差異可造成元件散布。","textEn":"Local geometric differences can cause device variation."},{"id":"a054-v8-23-k2","title":"端點與功能的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and function: principle and limits","text":"完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","textEn":"Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將孔道形貌與電性分布連結」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate channel morphology to electrical distributions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","局部幾何差異可造成元件散布。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。"],"optionsEn":["Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Local geometric differences can cause device variation.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部幾何差異可造成元件散布。 完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","explanationEn":"Local geometric differences can cause device variation. Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}},{"id":"a054-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lametch","v8b-lamemory","v8b-endpoint","v8b-rie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a054-v8-23"],"title":"交付含深度剖面的整合風險圖","titleEn":"Deliver an integration-risk map with depth profiles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：高深寬比驗證必須涵蓋整個深度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: High-aspect-ratio validation must cover the full depth.","instruction":"交付含深度剖面的整合風險圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「高深寬比驗證必須涵蓋整個深度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver an integration-risk map with depth profiles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: High-aspect-ratio validation must cover the full depth.","observation":"高深寬比驗證必須涵蓋整個深度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"High-aspect-ratio validation must cover the full depth. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只檢查是否打通即可驗收。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付含深度剖面的整合風險圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「高深寬比驗證必須涵蓋整個深度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver an integration-risk map with depth profiles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"High-aspect-ratio validation must cover the full depth.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a054-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"高深寬比驗證必須涵蓋整個深度。","textEn":"High-aspect-ratio validation must cover the full depth."},{"id":"a054-v8-24-k2","title":"端點與功能的原理與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint and function: principle and limits","text":"完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","textEn":"Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付含深度剖面的整合風險圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver an integration-risk map with depth profiles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只檢查是否打通即可驗收。","開口相同就代表所有深度的通量相同。","高深寬比驗證必須涵蓋整個深度。"],"optionsEn":["Checking breakthrough alone is sufficient.","Equal openings imply equal flux at every depth.","High-aspect-ratio validation must cover the full depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高深寬比驗證必須涵蓋整個深度。 完整貫穿不等於孔底損傷、殘留與後續覆蓋合格。","explanationEn":"High-aspect-ratio validation must cover the full depth. Complete penetration does not prove acceptable bottom damage, residue or later coverage."}}]}]},{"id":"a055","title":"選擇性矽鍺蝕刻","titleEn":"Selective silicon-germanium etching","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究材料與選擇性、反應與幾何、釋放與表面、元件整合；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: materials and selectivity, reaction and geometry, release and surfaces, device integration. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["材料與選擇性","反應與幾何","釋放與表面","元件整合"],"labelsEn":["Materials and selectivity","Reaction and geometry","Release and surfaces","Device integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"etch","subcategoryTitle":"蝕刻與電漿","subcategoryTitleEn":"Etch and plasma","stages":[{"id":"a055-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"材料與選擇性","titleEn":"Materials and selectivity","description":"選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","descriptionEn":"Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere.","steps":[{"id":"a055-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出交替矽與矽鍺奈米片","titleEn":"Draw alternating Si and SiGe nanosheets","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：犧牲層與保留通道的角色不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sacrificial layers and retained channels serve different roles.","instruction":"畫出交替矽與矽鍺奈米片。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「犧牲層與保留通道的角色不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw alternating Si and SiGe nanosheets. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sacrificial layers and retained channels serve different roles.","observation":"犧牲層與保留通道的角色不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sacrificial layers and retained channels serve different roles. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出交替矽與矽鍺奈米片」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「犧牲層與保留通道的角色不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw alternating Si and SiGe nanosheets\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sacrificial layers and retained channels serve different roles.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"犧牲層與保留通道的角色不同。","textEn":"Sacrificial layers and retained channels serve different roles."},{"id":"a055-v8-01-k2","title":"材料與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","textEn":"Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出交替矽與矽鍺奈米片」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw alternating Si and SiGe nanosheets\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["犧牲層與保留通道的角色不同。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。"],"optionsEn":["Sacrificial layers and retained channels serve different roles.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"犧牲層與保留通道的角色不同。 選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","explanationEn":"Sacrificial layers and retained channels serve different roles. Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}},{"id":"a055-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-01"],"title":"比較通道釋放與背面停止層移除","titleEn":"Compare channel release with backside stop removal","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩用途有不同幾何與終點要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The two uses have different geometries and endpoints.","instruction":"比較通道釋放與背面停止層移除。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「兩用途有不同幾何與終點要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare channel release with backside stop removal. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The two uses have different geometries and endpoints.","observation":"兩用途有不同幾何與終點要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The two uses have different geometries and endpoints. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較通道釋放與背面停止層移除」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩用途有不同幾何與終點要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare channel release with backside stop removal\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The two uses have different geometries and endpoints.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩用途有不同幾何與終點要求。","textEn":"The two uses have different geometries and endpoints."},{"id":"a055-v8-02-k2","title":"材料與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","textEn":"Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較通道釋放與背面停止層移除」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare channel release with backside stop removal\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","兩用途有不同幾何與終點要求。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。"],"optionsEn":["High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","The two uses have different geometries and endpoints.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩用途有不同幾何與終點要求。 選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","explanationEn":"The two uses have different geometries and endpoints. Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}},{"id":"a055-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-02"],"title":"用兩材料損失定義選擇比","titleEn":"Define selectivity from loss of both materials","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：極小分母需要量測偵測限。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A very small denominator requires a detection limit.","instruction":"用兩材料損失定義選擇比。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「極小分母需要量測偵測限。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設同一處理後 SiGe 損失 100 nm，Si 損失 2.0 nm，選擇比為 50。若另一測試的 Si 損失低於 0.20 nm 偵測限，只能在量測前提下說明選擇比大於 500，不能報告無限大或矽零損失。另指出平面試片結果仍需在奈米間隙幾何重新驗證。","instructionEn":"Define selectivity from loss of both materials. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: A very small denominator requires a detection limit.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume 100 nm SiGe loss and 2.0 nm Si loss in the same treatment: selectivity is 50. If another test has Si loss below a 0.20 nm detection limit, the measurement supports a lower bound above 500, not infinite selectivity or zero silicon loss. Blanket-sample results still need revalidation in nanogap geometry.","observation":"極小分母需要量測偵測限。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n分別報告 50 與 >500，清楚標出偵測限。","observationEn":"A very small denominator requires a detection limit. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 50 and >500 separately and state the detection limit.","failure":"若報告假設「高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用兩材料損失定義選擇比」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「極小分母需要量測偵測限。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：分別報告 50 與 >500，清楚標出偵測限。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define selectivity from loss of both materials\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A very small denominator requires a detection limit.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 50 and >500 separately and state the detection limit.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"極小分母需要量測偵測限。","textEn":"A very small denominator requires a detection limit."},{"id":"a055-v8-03-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設同一處理後 SiGe 損失 100 nm，Si 損失 2.0 nm，選擇比為 50。若另一測試的 Si 損失低於 0.20 nm 偵測限，只能在量測前提下說明選擇比大於 500，不能報告無限大或矽零損失。另指出平面試片結果仍需在奈米間隙幾何重新驗證。","textEn":"Assume 100 nm SiGe loss and 2.0 nm Si loss in the same treatment: selectivity is 50. If another test has Si loss below a 0.20 nm detection limit, the measurement supports a lower bound above 500, not infinite selectivity or zero silicon loss. Blanket-sample results still need revalidation in nanogap geometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用兩材料損失定義選擇比」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define selectivity from loss of both materials\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","極小分母需要量測偵測限。"],"optionsEn":["High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","A very small denominator requires a detection limit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"極小分母需要量測偵測限。 選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","explanationEn":"A very small denominator requires a detection limit. Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設同一處理後 SiGe 損失 100 nm，Si 損失 2.0 nm，選擇比為 50。若另一測試的 Si 損失低於 0.20 nm 偵測限，只能在量測前提下說明選擇比大於 500，不能報告無限大或矽零損失。另指出平面試片結果仍需在奈米間隙幾何重新驗證。","textEn":"Assume 100 nm SiGe loss and 2.0 nm Si loss in the same treatment: selectivity is 50. If another test has Si loss below a 0.20 nm detection limit, the measurement supports a lower bound above 500, not infinite selectivity or zero silicon loss. Blanket-sample results still need revalidation in nanogap geometry.","check":"分別報告 50 與 >500，清楚標出偵測限。","checkEn":"Report 50 and >500 separately and state the detection limit."}},{"id":"a055-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-03"],"title":"標明 SiGe 組成與應變狀態","titleEn":"State SiGe composition and strain","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料標籤不足以描述反應條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A material label is insufficient to describe reaction conditions.","instruction":"標明 SiGe 組成與應變狀態。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「材料標籤不足以描述反應條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"State SiGe composition and strain. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: A material label is insufficient to describe reaction conditions.","observation":"材料標籤不足以描述反應條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A material label is insufficient to describe reaction conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標明 SiGe 組成與應變狀態」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料標籤不足以描述反應條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"State SiGe composition and strain\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A material label is insufficient to describe reaction conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料標籤不足以描述反應條件。","textEn":"A material label is insufficient to describe reaction conditions."},{"id":"a055-v8-04-k2","title":"材料與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","textEn":"Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標明 SiGe 組成與應變狀態」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"State SiGe composition and strain\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料標籤不足以描述反應條件。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。"],"optionsEn":["A material label is insufficient to describe reaction conditions.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料標籤不足以描述反應條件。 選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","explanationEn":"A material label is insufficient to describe reaction conditions. Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}},{"id":"a055-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-04"],"title":"建立保留矽厚度損失預算","titleEn":"Budget allowable retained-silicon loss","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：通道厚度損失可能改變電性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Channel-thickness loss can alter electrical behavior.","instruction":"建立保留矽厚度損失預算。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「通道厚度損失可能改變電性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Budget allowable retained-silicon loss. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Channel-thickness loss can alter electrical behavior.","observation":"通道厚度損失可能改變電性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Channel-thickness loss can alter electrical behavior. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立保留矽厚度損失預算」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「通道厚度損失可能改變電性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Budget allowable retained-silicon loss\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Channel-thickness loss can alter electrical behavior.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"通道厚度損失可能改變電性。","textEn":"Channel-thickness loss can alter electrical behavior."},{"id":"a055-v8-05-k2","title":"材料與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","textEn":"Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立保留矽厚度損失預算」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Budget allowable retained-silicon loss\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","通道厚度損失可能改變電性。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。"],"optionsEn":["High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","Channel-thickness loss can alter electrical behavior.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"通道厚度損失可能改變電性。 選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","explanationEn":"Channel-thickness loss can alter electrical behavior. Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}},{"id":"a055-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-05"],"title":"列出不同晶面與摻雜的可能影響","titleEn":"List possible orientation and doping effects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料微觀狀態可影響表面反應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Microscopic material state can affect surface reactions.","instruction":"列出不同晶面與摻雜的可能影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「材料微觀狀態可影響表面反應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List possible orientation and doping effects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Microscopic material state can affect surface reactions.","observation":"材料微觀狀態可影響表面反應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Microscopic material state can affect surface reactions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出不同晶面與摻雜的可能影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料微觀狀態可影響表面反應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List possible orientation and doping effects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Microscopic material state can affect surface reactions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料微觀狀態可影響表面反應。","textEn":"Microscopic material state can affect surface reactions."},{"id":"a055-v8-06-k2","title":"材料與選擇性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and selectivity: principle and limits","text":"選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","textEn":"Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出不同晶面與摻雜的可能影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List possible orientation and doping effects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","材料微觀狀態可影響表面反應。"],"optionsEn":["High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","Microscopic material state can affect surface reactions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料微觀狀態可影響表面反應。 選擇性蝕刻是材料對的相對速率，不是目標外材料絕對零損失。","explanationEn":"Microscopic material state can affect surface reactions. Selective etching is a relative rate for a material pair, not necessarily zero loss elsewhere."}}]},{"id":"a055-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"反應與幾何","titleEn":"Reaction and geometry","description":"SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","descriptionEn":"SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior.","steps":[{"id":"a055-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-06"],"title":"分開表面反應與反應物輸運","titleEn":"Separate surface reaction from reactant transport","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：狹窄間隙可能由輸運限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Narrow gaps can be transport-limited.","instruction":"分開表面反應與反應物輸運。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「狹窄間隙可能由輸運限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate surface reaction from reactant transport. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Narrow gaps can be transport-limited.","observation":"狹窄間隙可能由輸運限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Narrow gaps can be transport-limited. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開表面反應與反應物輸運」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「狹窄間隙可能由輸運限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate surface reaction from reactant transport\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Narrow gaps can be transport-limited.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"狹窄間隙可能由輸運限制。","textEn":"Narrow gaps can be transport-limited."},{"id":"a055-v8-07-k2","title":"反應與幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reaction and geometry: principle and limits","text":"SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","textEn":"SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開表面反應與反應物輸運」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate surface reaction from reactant transport\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["狹窄間隙可能由輸運限制。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。"],"optionsEn":["Narrow gaps can be transport-limited.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","A clean opening proves complete internal release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"狹窄間隙可能由輸運限制。 SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","explanationEn":"Narrow gaps can be transport-limited. SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}},{"id":"a055-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-07"],"title":"比較各向同性移除與方向性蝕刻","titleEn":"Compare isotropic removal with directional etching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：通道側向釋放通常需要側向進入。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Lateral channel release requires lateral access.","instruction":"比較各向同性移除與方向性蝕刻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「通道側向釋放通常需要側向進入。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare isotropic removal with directional etching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Lateral channel release requires lateral access.","observation":"通道側向釋放通常需要側向進入。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Lateral channel release requires lateral access. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較各向同性移除與方向性蝕刻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「通道側向釋放通常需要側向進入。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare isotropic removal with directional etching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Lateral channel release requires lateral access.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"通道側向釋放通常需要側向進入。","textEn":"Lateral channel release requires lateral access."},{"id":"a055-v8-08-k2","title":"反應與幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reaction and geometry: principle and limits","text":"SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","textEn":"SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較各向同性移除與方向性蝕刻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare isotropic removal with directional etching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","通道側向釋放通常需要側向進入。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。"],"optionsEn":["Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","Lateral channel release requires lateral access.","A clean opening proves complete internal release."],"answer":1,"explanation":"通道側向釋放通常需要側向進入。 SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","explanationEn":"Lateral channel release requires lateral access. SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}},{"id":"a055-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-08"],"title":"畫出反應物到達中間層的路徑","titleEn":"Trace reactant access to middle layers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：最外層完成不代表中間層完成。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Outer-layer completion does not prove middle-layer completion.","instruction":"畫出反應物到達中間層的路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「最外層完成不代表中間層完成。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace reactant access to middle layers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Outer-layer completion does not prove middle-layer completion.","observation":"最外層完成不代表中間層完成。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Outer-layer completion does not prove middle-layer completion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出反應物到達中間層的路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「最外層完成不代表中間層完成。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace reactant access to middle layers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Outer-layer completion does not prove middle-layer completion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"最外層完成不代表中間層完成。","textEn":"Outer-layer completion does not prove middle-layer completion."},{"id":"a055-v8-09-k2","title":"反應與幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reaction and geometry: principle and limits","text":"SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","textEn":"SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出反應物到達中間層的路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace reactant access to middle layers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","最外層完成不代表中間層完成。"],"optionsEn":["Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Outer-layer completion does not prove middle-layer completion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"最外層完成不代表中間層完成。 SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","explanationEn":"Outer-layer completion does not prove middle-layer completion. SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}},{"id":"a055-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-09"],"title":"檢查原生氧化層對反應起始的影響","titleEn":"Assess native-oxide effects on reaction initiation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：起始延遲可造成層間差異。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Initiation delays can create layer-to-layer differences.","instruction":"檢查原生氧化層對反應起始的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「起始延遲可造成層間差異。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess native-oxide effects on reaction initiation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Initiation delays can create layer-to-layer differences.","observation":"起始延遲可造成層間差異。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Initiation delays can create layer-to-layer differences. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查原生氧化層對反應起始的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「起始延遲可造成層間差異。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess native-oxide effects on reaction initiation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Initiation delays can create layer-to-layer differences.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"起始延遲可造成層間差異。","textEn":"Initiation delays can create layer-to-layer differences."},{"id":"a055-v8-10-k2","title":"反應與幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reaction and geometry: principle and limits","text":"SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","textEn":"SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查原生氧化層對反應起始的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess native-oxide effects on reaction initiation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["起始延遲可造成層間差異。","所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。"],"optionsEn":["Initiation delays can create layer-to-layer differences.","Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","A clean opening proves complete internal release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"起始延遲可造成層間差異。 SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","explanationEn":"Initiation delays can create layer-to-layer differences. SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}},{"id":"a055-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-10"],"title":"以空白矽與 SiGe 試片建立對照","titleEn":"Use blanket Si and SiGe controls","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平面對照有助於分離材料因素。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Blanket controls help isolate material effects.","instruction":"以空白矽與 SiGe 試片建立對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「平面對照有助於分離材料因素。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use blanket Si and SiGe controls. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Blanket controls help isolate material effects.","observation":"平面對照有助於分離材料因素。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Blanket controls help isolate material effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以空白矽與 SiGe 試片建立對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平面對照有助於分離材料因素。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use blanket Si and SiGe controls\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Blanket controls help isolate material effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平面對照有助於分離材料因素。","textEn":"Blanket controls help isolate material effects."},{"id":"a055-v8-11-k2","title":"反應與幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reaction and geometry: principle and limits","text":"SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","textEn":"SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以空白矽與 SiGe 試片建立對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use blanket Si and SiGe controls\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","平面對照有助於分離材料因素。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。"],"optionsEn":["Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","Blanket controls help isolate material effects.","A clean opening proves complete internal release."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平面對照有助於分離材料因素。 SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","explanationEn":"Blanket controls help isolate material effects. SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}},{"id":"a055-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-11"],"title":"比較平面速率與奈米間隙有效速率","titleEn":"Compare blanket rates with nanogap effective rates","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平面速率不能無條件代入三維結構。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Blanket rates cannot be inserted unconditionally into 3D structures.","instruction":"比較平面速率與奈米間隙有效速率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「平面速率不能無條件代入三維結構。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare blanket rates with nanogap effective rates. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Blanket rates cannot be inserted unconditionally into 3D structures.","observation":"平面速率不能無條件代入三維結構。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Blanket rates cannot be inserted unconditionally into 3D structures. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較平面速率與奈米間隙有效速率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平面速率不能無條件代入三維結構。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare blanket rates with nanogap effective rates\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Blanket rates cannot be inserted unconditionally into 3D structures.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平面速率不能無條件代入三維結構。","textEn":"Blanket rates cannot be inserted unconditionally into 3D structures."},{"id":"a055-v8-12-k2","title":"反應與幾何的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reaction and geometry: principle and limits","text":"SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","textEn":"SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較平面速率與奈米間隙有效速率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare blanket rates with nanogap effective rates\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有鍺比例的 SiGe 都有相同反應速率。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","平面速率不能無條件代入三維結構。"],"optionsEn":["Every SiGe composition has the same reaction rate.","A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Blanket rates cannot be inserted unconditionally into 3D structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平面速率不能無條件代入三維結構。 SiGe 組成、應變、表面與幾何都可能改變反應。","explanationEn":"Blanket rates cannot be inserted unconditionally into 3D structures. SiGe composition, strain, surfaces and geometry can change reaction behavior."}}]},{"id":"a055-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"釋放與表面","titleEn":"Release and surfaces","description":"側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","descriptionEn":"Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity.","steps":[{"id":"a055-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-12"],"title":"由截面辨識未移除的 SiGe 殘留","titleEn":"Identify residual SiGe in sections","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部殘留會阻礙後續閘極包覆。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local residue can obstruct later gate wrapping.","instruction":"由截面辨識未移除的 SiGe 殘留。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「局部殘留會阻礙後續閘極包覆。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify residual SiGe in sections. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local residue can obstruct later gate wrapping.","observation":"局部殘留會阻礙後續閘極包覆。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local residue can obstruct later gate wrapping. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A clean opening proves complete internal release.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「由截面辨識未移除的 SiGe 殘留」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部殘留會阻礙後續閘極包覆。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify residual SiGe in sections\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local residue can obstruct later gate wrapping.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部殘留會阻礙後續閘極包覆。","textEn":"Local residue can obstruct later gate wrapping."},{"id":"a055-v8-13-k2","title":"釋放與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Release and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","textEn":"Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「由截面辨識未移除的 SiGe 殘留」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify residual SiGe in sections\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["局部殘留會阻礙後續閘極包覆。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Local residue can obstruct later gate wrapping.","A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部殘留會阻礙後續閘極包覆。 側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","explanationEn":"Local residue can obstruct later gate wrapping. Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}},{"id":"a055-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-13"],"title":"檢查通道頂底的厚度差","titleEn":"Inspect thickness differences across channels","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：選擇性損失可能隨位置不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Selective loss can vary by location.","instruction":"檢查通道頂底的厚度差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「選擇性損失可能隨位置不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect thickness differences across channels. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Selective loss can vary by location.","observation":"選擇性損失可能隨位置不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Selective loss can vary by location. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A clean opening proves complete internal release.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查通道頂底的厚度差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「選擇性損失可能隨位置不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect thickness differences across channels\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Selective loss can vary by location.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"選擇性損失可能隨位置不同。","textEn":"Selective loss can vary by location."},{"id":"a055-v8-14-k2","title":"釋放與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Release and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","textEn":"Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查通道頂底的厚度差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect thickness differences across channels\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","選擇性損失可能隨位置不同。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Selective loss can vary by location.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇性損失可能隨位置不同。 側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","explanationEn":"Selective loss can vary by location. Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}},{"id":"a055-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-14"],"title":"比較釋放前後的粗糙度","titleEn":"Compare roughness before and after release","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：小平均損失仍可能增加粗糙度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Small average loss can still increase roughness.","instruction":"比較釋放前後的粗糙度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「小平均損失仍可能增加粗糙度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare roughness before and after release. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Small average loss can still increase roughness.","observation":"小平均損失仍可能增加粗糙度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Small average loss can still increase roughness. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A clean opening proves complete internal release.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較釋放前後的粗糙度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「小平均損失仍可能增加粗糙度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare roughness before and after release\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Small average loss can still increase roughness.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"小平均損失仍可能增加粗糙度。","textEn":"Small average loss can still increase roughness."},{"id":"a055-v8-15-k2","title":"釋放與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Release and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","textEn":"Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較釋放前後的粗糙度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare roughness before and after release\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","小平均損失仍可能增加粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","Small average loss can still increase roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"小平均損失仍可能增加粗糙度。 側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","explanationEn":"Small average loss can still increase roughness. Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}},{"id":"a055-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-15"],"title":"評估釋放後奈米片的機械穩定","titleEn":"Assess released-sheet mechanical stability","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：薄片可能因應力或表面力變形。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thin sheets can deform under stress or surface forces.","instruction":"評估釋放後奈米片的機械穩定。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「薄片可能因應力或表面力變形。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess released-sheet mechanical stability. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thin sheets can deform under stress or surface forces.","observation":"薄片可能因應力或表面力變形。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thin sheets can deform under stress or surface forces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A clean opening proves complete internal release.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估釋放後奈米片的機械穩定」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「薄片可能因應力或表面力變形。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess released-sheet mechanical stability\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thin sheets can deform under stress or surface forces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"薄片可能因應力或表面力變形。","textEn":"Thin sheets can deform under stress or surface forces."},{"id":"a055-v8-16-k2","title":"釋放與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Release and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","textEn":"Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估釋放後奈米片的機械穩定」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess released-sheet mechanical stability\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["薄片可能因應力或表面力變形。","孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Thin sheets can deform under stress or surface forces.","A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄片可能因應力或表面力變形。 側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","explanationEn":"Thin sheets can deform under stress or surface forces. Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}},{"id":"a055-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-16"],"title":"檢查清潔後的元素與氧化狀態","titleEn":"Inspect elements and oxidation states after cleaning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：清潔度需以化學量測支持。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cleanliness needs chemical measurement evidence.","instruction":"檢查清潔後的元素與氧化狀態。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「清潔度需以化學量測支持。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect elements and oxidation states after cleaning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cleanliness needs chemical measurement evidence.","observation":"清潔度需以化學量測支持。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cleanliness needs chemical measurement evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A clean opening proves complete internal release.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查清潔後的元素與氧化狀態」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「清潔度需以化學量測支持。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect elements and oxidation states after cleaning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cleanliness needs chemical measurement evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"清潔度需以化學量測支持。","textEn":"Cleanliness needs chemical measurement evidence."},{"id":"a055-v8-17-k2","title":"釋放與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Release and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","textEn":"Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查清潔後的元素與氧化狀態」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect elements and oxidation states after cleaning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","清潔度需以化學量測支持。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Cleanliness needs chemical measurement evidence.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔度需以化學量測支持。 側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","explanationEn":"Cleanliness needs chemical measurement evidence. Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}},{"id":"a055-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-17"],"title":"標出內間隔層需保留的區域","titleEn":"Mark inner-spacer regions to preserve","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：選擇性需涵蓋完整周邊材料集合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Selectivity must cover the full surrounding material set.","instruction":"標出內間隔層需保留的區域。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「選擇性需涵蓋完整周邊材料集合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark inner-spacer regions to preserve. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Selectivity must cover the full surrounding material set.","observation":"選擇性需涵蓋完整周邊材料集合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Selectivity must cover the full surrounding material set. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A clean opening proves complete internal release.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標出內間隔層需保留的區域」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「選擇性需涵蓋完整周邊材料集合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark inner-spacer regions to preserve\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Selectivity must cover the full surrounding material set.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"選擇性需涵蓋完整周邊材料集合。","textEn":"Selectivity must cover the full surrounding material set."},{"id":"a055-v8-18-k2","title":"釋放與表面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Release and surfaces: principle and limits","text":"側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","textEn":"Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標出內間隔層需保留的區域」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark inner-spacer regions to preserve\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口乾淨就表示內部完全釋放。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","選擇性需涵蓋完整周邊材料集合。"],"optionsEn":["A clean opening proves complete internal release.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","Selectivity must cover the full surrounding material set."],"answer":2,"explanation":"選擇性需涵蓋完整周邊材料集合。 側向釋放需要檢查深部移除與保留矽的完整性。","explanationEn":"Selectivity must cover the full surrounding material set. Lateral release needs checks of deep removal and retained-silicon integrity."}}]},{"id":"a055-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"元件整合","titleEn":"Device integration","description":"通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","descriptionEn":"Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation.","steps":[{"id":"a055-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-18"],"title":"比較閘極共形沉積前的表面條件","titleEn":"Compare surfaces before conformal gate deposition","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：釋放表面直接影響介面品質。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Released surfaces directly affect interface quality.","instruction":"比較閘極共形沉積前的表面條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「釋放表面直接影響介面品質。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare surfaces before conformal gate deposition. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Released surfaces directly affect interface quality.","observation":"釋放表面直接影響介面品質。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Released surfaces directly affect interface quality. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較閘極共形沉積前的表面條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「釋放表面直接影響介面品質。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare surfaces before conformal gate deposition\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Released surfaces directly affect interface quality.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"釋放表面直接影響介面品質。","textEn":"Released surfaces directly affect interface quality."},{"id":"a055-v8-19-k2","title":"元件整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Device integration: principle and limits","text":"通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","textEn":"Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較閘極共形沉積前的表面條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare surfaces before conformal gate deposition\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["釋放表面直接影響介面品質。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。"],"optionsEn":["Released surfaces directly affect interface quality.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss."],"answer":0,"explanation":"釋放表面直接影響介面品質。 通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","explanationEn":"Released surfaces directly affect interface quality. Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}},{"id":"a055-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-19"],"title":"用漏電與臨界電壓檢查後果","titleEn":"Assess consequences through leakage and threshold voltage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何差異可能表現在電性散布。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Geometric differences can appear as electrical variation.","instruction":"用漏電與臨界電壓檢查後果。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「幾何差異可能表現在電性散布。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess consequences through leakage and threshold voltage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Geometric differences can appear as electrical variation.","observation":"幾何差異可能表現在電性散布。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Geometric differences can appear as electrical variation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用漏電與臨界電壓檢查後果」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何差異可能表現在電性散布。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess consequences through leakage and threshold voltage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Geometric differences can appear as electrical variation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何差異可能表現在電性散布。","textEn":"Geometric differences can appear as electrical variation."},{"id":"a055-v8-20-k2","title":"元件整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Device integration: principle and limits","text":"通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","textEn":"Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用漏電與臨界電壓檢查後果」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess consequences through leakage and threshold voltage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","幾何差異可能表現在電性散布。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。"],"optionsEn":["Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","Geometric differences can appear as electrical variation.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"幾何差異可能表現在電性散布。 通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","explanationEn":"Geometric differences can appear as electrical variation. Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}},{"id":"a055-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-20"],"title":"追蹤三維堆疊中各層的性能","titleEn":"Track performance across layers in a 3D stack","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平均元件值可能掩蓋單層異常。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Average device values can hide one-layer anomalies.","instruction":"追蹤三維堆疊中各層的性能。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「平均元件值可能掩蓋單層異常。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track performance across layers in a 3D stack. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Average device values can hide one-layer anomalies.","observation":"平均元件值可能掩蓋單層異常。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Average device values can hide one-layer anomalies. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤三維堆疊中各層的性能」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平均元件值可能掩蓋單層異常。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track performance across layers in a 3D stack\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Average device values can hide one-layer anomalies.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平均元件值可能掩蓋單層異常。","textEn":"Average device values can hide one-layer anomalies."},{"id":"a055-v8-21-k2","title":"元件整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Device integration: principle and limits","text":"通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","textEn":"Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤三維堆疊中各層的性能」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track performance across layers in a 3D stack\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","平均元件值可能掩蓋單層異常。"],"optionsEn":["Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","Average device values can hide one-layer anomalies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均元件值可能掩蓋單層異常。 通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","explanationEn":"Average device values can hide one-layer anomalies. Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}},{"id":"a055-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-21"],"title":"比較選擇性提升與總時間代價","titleEn":"Compare improved selectivity with total-time cost","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：更溫和移除可能延長製程。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Gentler removal can lengthen processing.","instruction":"比較選擇性提升與總時間代價。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「更溫和移除可能延長製程。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare improved selectivity with total-time cost. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Gentler removal can lengthen processing.","observation":"更溫和移除可能延長製程。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Gentler removal can lengthen processing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較選擇性提升與總時間代價」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「更溫和移除可能延長製程。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare improved selectivity with total-time cost\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Gentler removal can lengthen processing.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"更溫和移除可能延長製程。","textEn":"Gentler removal can lengthen processing."},{"id":"a055-v8-22-k2","title":"元件整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Device integration: principle and limits","text":"通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","textEn":"Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較選擇性提升與總時間代價」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare improved selectivity with total-time cost\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["更溫和移除可能延長製程。","釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。"],"optionsEn":["Gentler removal can lengthen processing.","Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更溫和移除可能延長製程。 通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","explanationEn":"Gentler removal can lengthen processing. Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}},{"id":"a055-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-22"],"title":"記錄不能跨組成外推的條件","titleEn":"Document conditions not transferable across compositions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：特定材料對的結果不是通用配方。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A result for one material pair is not a universal recipe.","instruction":"記錄不能跨組成外推的條件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「特定材料對的結果不是通用配方。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Document conditions not transferable across compositions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: A result for one material pair is not a universal recipe.","observation":"特定材料對的結果不是通用配方。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A result for one material pair is not a universal recipe. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「記錄不能跨組成外推的條件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「特定材料對的結果不是通用配方。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Document conditions not transferable across compositions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A result for one material pair is not a universal recipe.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"特定材料對的結果不是通用配方。","textEn":"A result for one material pair is not a universal recipe."},{"id":"a055-v8-23-k2","title":"元件整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Device integration: principle and limits","text":"通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","textEn":"Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記錄不能跨組成外推的條件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Document conditions not transferable across compositions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","特定材料對的結果不是通用配方。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。"],"optionsEn":["Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","A result for one material pair is not a universal recipe.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss."],"answer":1,"explanation":"特定材料對的結果不是通用配方。 通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","explanationEn":"A result for one material pair is not a universal recipe. Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}},{"id":"a055-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-selective","v8b-shape","v8b-backside","v8b-ale"],"prerequisiteIds":["a055-v8-23"],"title":"交付釋放、表面與元件的證據鏈","titleEn":"Deliver release, surface and device evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：成功整合需要形貌與功能共同支持。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Successful integration needs morphological and functional support.","instruction":"交付釋放、表面與元件的證據鏈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「成功整合需要形貌與功能共同支持。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver release, surface and device evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Successful integration needs morphological and functional support.","observation":"成功整合需要形貌與功能共同支持。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Successful integration needs morphological and functional support. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付釋放、表面與元件的證據鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「成功整合需要形貌與功能共同支持。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver release, surface and device evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Successful integration needs morphological and functional support.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a055-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"成功整合需要形貌與功能共同支持。","textEn":"Successful integration needs morphological and functional support."},{"id":"a055-v8-24-k2","title":"元件整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Device integration: principle and limits","text":"通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","textEn":"Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付釋放、表面與元件的證據鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver release, surface and device evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["釋放完成即可省略閘極介面驗證。","高選擇比表示矽完全沒有任何損失。","成功整合需要形貌與功能共同支持。"],"optionsEn":["Completed release removes the need for gate-interface checks.","High selectivity means absolutely no silicon loss.","Successful integration needs morphological and functional support."],"answer":2,"explanation":"成功整合需要形貌與功能共同支持。 通道釋放或停止層移除都需與後續介面品質聯動。","explanationEn":"Successful integration needs morphological and functional support. Channel release and stop-layer removal both require downstream interface validation."}}]}]},{"id":"a056","title":"電漿端點偵測","titleEn":"Plasma endpoint detection","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究訊號來源、訊號處理、停止邏輯、驗證與漂移；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: signal origins, signal processing, stop logic, validation and drift. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["訊號來源","訊號處理","停止邏輯","驗證與漂移"],"labelsEn":["Signal origins","Signal processing","Stop logic","Validation and drift"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"etch","subcategoryTitle":"蝕刻與電漿","subcategoryTitleEn":"Etch and plasma","stages":[{"id":"a056-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"訊號來源","titleEn":"Signal origins","description":"端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","descriptionEn":"Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals.","steps":[{"id":"a056-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"把 OES 發光峰對應至可能物種","titleEn":"Associate OES peaks with candidate species","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：峰值指認需排除重疊與背景。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Peak assignments need overlap and background checks.","instruction":"把 OES 發光峰對應至可能物種。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「峰值指認需排除重疊與背景。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Associate OES peaks with candidate species. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Peak assignments need overlap and background checks.","observation":"峰值指認需排除重疊與背景。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Peak assignments need overlap and background checks. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every brightness change means etching is complete.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把 OES 發光峰對應至可能物種」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「峰值指認需排除重疊與背景。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Associate OES peaks with candidate species\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Peak assignments need overlap and background checks.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"峰值指認需排除重疊與背景。","textEn":"Peak assignments need overlap and background checks."},{"id":"a056-v8-01-k2","title":"訊號來源的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal origins: principle and limits","text":"端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","textEn":"Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把 OES 發光峰對應至可能物種」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Associate OES peaks with candidate species\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["峰值指認需排除重疊與背景。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。"],"optionsEn":["Peak assignments need overlap and background checks.","Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Longer filtering is always better."],"answer":0,"explanation":"峰值指認需排除重疊與背景。 端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","explanationEn":"Peak assignments need overlap and background checks. Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}},{"id":"a056-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-01"],"title":"比較反應物消耗與產物生成訊號","titleEn":"Compare reactant depletion with product-generation signals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同訊號可能在端點反向變化。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Signals can change in opposite directions at endpoint.","instruction":"比較反應物消耗與產物生成訊號。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「不同訊號可能在端點反向變化。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare reactant depletion with product-generation signals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Signals can change in opposite directions at endpoint.","observation":"不同訊號可能在端點反向變化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Signals can change in opposite directions at endpoint. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every brightness change means etching is complete.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較反應物消耗與產物生成訊號」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同訊號可能在端點反向變化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare reactant depletion with product-generation signals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Signals can change in opposite directions at endpoint.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同訊號可能在端點反向變化。","textEn":"Signals can change in opposite directions at endpoint."},{"id":"a056-v8-02-k2","title":"訊號來源的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal origins: principle and limits","text":"端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","textEn":"Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較反應物消耗與產物生成訊號」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare reactant depletion with product-generation signals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","不同訊號可能在端點反向變化。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。"],"optionsEn":["Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Signals can change in opposite directions at endpoint.","Longer filtering is always better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同訊號可能在端點反向變化。 端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","explanationEn":"Signals can change in opposite directions at endpoint. Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}},{"id":"a056-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-02"],"title":"畫出薄膜反射干涉的訊號","titleEn":"Sketch thin-film reflection-interference signals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：條紋與光學厚度有關。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Fringes depend on optical thickness.","instruction":"畫出薄膜反射干涉的訊號。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「條紋與光學厚度有關。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch thin-film reflection-interference signals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Fringes depend on optical thickness.","observation":"條紋與光學厚度有關。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Fringes depend on optical thickness. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every brightness change means etching is complete.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出薄膜反射干涉的訊號」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「條紋與光學厚度有關。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch thin-film reflection-interference signals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Fringes depend on optical thickness.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"條紋與光學厚度有關。","textEn":"Fringes depend on optical thickness."},{"id":"a056-v8-03-k2","title":"訊號來源的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal origins: principle and limits","text":"端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","textEn":"Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出薄膜反射干涉的訊號」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch thin-film reflection-interference signals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","條紋與光學厚度有關。"],"optionsEn":["Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Longer filtering is always better.","Fringes depend on optical thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"條紋與光學厚度有關。 端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","explanationEn":"Fringes depend on optical thickness. Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}},{"id":"a056-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-03"],"title":"區分界面端點與指定深度端點","titleEn":"Distinguish interface endpoints from target-depth endpoints","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者需要不同判讀模型。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: They require different interpretation models.","instruction":"區分界面端點與指定深度端點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「兩者需要不同判讀模型。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish interface endpoints from target-depth endpoints. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: They require different interpretation models.","observation":"兩者需要不同判讀模型。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"They require different interpretation models. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every brightness change means etching is complete.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分界面端點與指定深度端點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者需要不同判讀模型。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish interface endpoints from target-depth endpoints\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"They require different interpretation models.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者需要不同判讀模型。","textEn":"They require different interpretation models."},{"id":"a056-v8-04-k2","title":"訊號來源的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal origins: principle and limits","text":"端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","textEn":"Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分界面端點與指定深度端點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish interface endpoints from target-depth endpoints\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩者需要不同判讀模型。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。"],"optionsEn":["They require different interpretation models.","Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Longer filtering is always better."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩者需要不同判讀模型。 端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","explanationEn":"They require different interpretation models. Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}},{"id":"a056-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-04"],"title":"標示量測視野與實際開口區","titleEn":"Mark the viewing area and actual open regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：感測訊號可能平均多個位置。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sensor signals can average multiple locations.","instruction":"標示量測視野與實際開口區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「感測訊號可能平均多個位置。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark the viewing area and actual open regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sensor signals can average multiple locations.","observation":"感測訊號可能平均多個位置。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sensor signals can average multiple locations. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every brightness change means etching is complete.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標示量測視野與實際開口區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「感測訊號可能平均多個位置。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark the viewing area and actual open regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sensor signals can average multiple locations.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"感測訊號可能平均多個位置。","textEn":"Sensor signals can average multiple locations."},{"id":"a056-v8-05-k2","title":"訊號來源的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal origins: principle and limits","text":"端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","textEn":"Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標示量測視野與實際開口區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark the viewing area and actual open regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","感測訊號可能平均多個位置。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。"],"optionsEn":["Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Sensor signals can average multiple locations.","Longer filtering is always better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測訊號可能平均多個位置。 端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","explanationEn":"Sensor signals can average multiple locations. Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}},{"id":"a056-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-05"],"title":"比較大開口與小開口訊號強度","titleEn":"Compare large- and small-open-area signals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：小開口可能降低可偵測性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low open area can reduce detectability.","instruction":"比較大開口與小開口訊號強度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「小開口可能降低可偵測性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare large- and small-open-area signals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low open area can reduce detectability.","observation":"小開口可能降低可偵測性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low open area can reduce detectability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every brightness change means etching is complete.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較大開口與小開口訊號強度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「小開口可能降低可偵測性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare large- and small-open-area signals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low open area can reduce detectability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"小開口可能降低可偵測性。","textEn":"Low open area can reduce detectability."},{"id":"a056-v8-06-k2","title":"訊號來源的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal origins: principle and limits","text":"端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","textEn":"Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較大開口與小開口訊號強度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare large- and small-open-area signals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","小開口可能降低可偵測性。"],"optionsEn":["Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Longer filtering is always better.","Low open area can reduce detectability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"小開口可能降低可偵測性。 端點偵測是從間接光學或電性訊號推斷製程狀態。","explanationEn":"Low open area can reduce detectability. Endpoint detection infers process state from indirect optical or electrical signals."}}]},{"id":"a056-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"訊號處理","titleEn":"Signal processing","description":"訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","descriptionEn":"Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective.","steps":[{"id":"a056-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-06"],"title":"建立曝光前背景與暗訊號","titleEn":"Establish background and dark signals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：背景扣除需要穩定的參考。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Background subtraction needs a stable reference.","instruction":"建立曝光前背景與暗訊號。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「背景扣除需要穩定的參考。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Establish background and dark signals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Background subtraction needs a stable reference.","observation":"背景扣除需要穩定的參考。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Background subtraction needs a stable reference. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer filtering is always better.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立曝光前背景與暗訊號」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「背景扣除需要穩定的參考。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Establish background and dark signals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Background subtraction needs a stable reference.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"背景扣除需要穩定的參考。","textEn":"Background subtraction needs a stable reference."},{"id":"a056-v8-07-k2","title":"訊號處理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal processing: principle and limits","text":"訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","textEn":"Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立曝光前背景與暗訊號」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Establish background and dark signals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["背景扣除需要穩定的參考。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。"],"optionsEn":["Background subtraction needs a stable reference.","Longer filtering is always better.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"背景扣除需要穩定的參考。 訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","explanationEn":"Background subtraction needs a stable reference. Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}},{"id":"a056-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-07"],"title":"比較單一波長與峰值比值","titleEn":"Compare one wavelength with peak ratios","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：比值可減少部分共同強度漂移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Ratios can reduce some common intensity drift.","instruction":"比較單一波長與峰值比值。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「比值可減少部分共同強度漂移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare one wavelength with peak ratios. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Ratios can reduce some common intensity drift.","observation":"比值可減少部分共同強度漂移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Ratios can reduce some common intensity drift. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer filtering is always better.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較單一波長與峰值比值」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「比值可減少部分共同強度漂移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare one wavelength with peak ratios\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Ratios can reduce some common intensity drift.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"比值可減少部分共同強度漂移。","textEn":"Ratios can reduce some common intensity drift."},{"id":"a056-v8-08-k2","title":"訊號處理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal processing: principle and limits","text":"訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","textEn":"Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較單一波長與峰值比值」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare one wavelength with peak ratios\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","比值可減少部分共同強度漂移。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。"],"optionsEn":["Longer filtering is always better.","Ratios can reduce some common intensity drift.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比值可減少部分共同強度漂移。 訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","explanationEn":"Ratios can reduce some common intensity drift. Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}},{"id":"a056-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-08"],"title":"以合成資料測試移動平均延遲","titleEn":"Test moving-average delay using synthetic data","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平滑會把轉折向後移。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Smoothing delays apparent transitions.","instruction":"以合成資料測試移動平均延遲。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「平滑會把轉折向後移。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Test moving-average delay using synthetic data. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Smoothing delays apparent transitions.","observation":"平滑會把轉折向後移。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Smoothing delays apparent transitions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer filtering is always better.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以合成資料測試移動平均延遲」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平滑會把轉折向後移。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Test moving-average delay using synthetic data\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Smoothing delays apparent transitions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平滑會把轉折向後移。","textEn":"Smoothing delays apparent transitions."},{"id":"a056-v8-09-k2","title":"訊號處理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal processing: principle and limits","text":"訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","textEn":"Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以合成資料測試移動平均延遲」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Test moving-average delay using synthetic data\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","平滑會把轉折向後移。"],"optionsEn":["Longer filtering is always better.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","Smoothing delays apparent transitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平滑會把轉折向後移。 訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","explanationEn":"Smoothing delays apparent transitions. Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}},{"id":"a056-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-09"],"title":"比較斜率與絕對強度判準","titleEn":"Compare slope and absolute-intensity criteria","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩種判準對背景漂移敏感度不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The criteria differ in sensitivity to baseline drift.","instruction":"比較斜率與絕對強度判準。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「兩種判準對背景漂移敏感度不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare slope and absolute-intensity criteria. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The criteria differ in sensitivity to baseline drift.","observation":"兩種判準對背景漂移敏感度不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The criteria differ in sensitivity to baseline drift. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer filtering is always better.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較斜率與絕對強度判準」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩種判準對背景漂移敏感度不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare slope and absolute-intensity criteria\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The criteria differ in sensitivity to baseline drift.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩種判準對背景漂移敏感度不同。","textEn":"The criteria differ in sensitivity to baseline drift."},{"id":"a056-v8-10-k2","title":"訊號處理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal processing: principle and limits","text":"訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","textEn":"Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較斜率與絕對強度判準」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare slope and absolute-intensity criteria\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩種判準對背景漂移敏感度不同。","把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。"],"optionsEn":["The criteria differ in sensitivity to baseline drift.","Longer filtering is always better.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種判準對背景漂移敏感度不同。 訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","explanationEn":"The criteria differ in sensitivity to baseline drift. Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}},{"id":"a056-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-10"],"title":"辨識脈衝或點火暫態的假端點","titleEn":"Identify false endpoints from pulses or ignition","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：初期暫態應與材料轉換分離。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Startup transients need separation from material transitions.","instruction":"辨識脈衝或點火暫態的假端點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「初期暫態應與材料轉換分離。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify false endpoints from pulses or ignition. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Startup transients need separation from material transitions.","observation":"初期暫態應與材料轉換分離。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Startup transients need separation from material transitions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer filtering is always better.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「辨識脈衝或點火暫態的假端點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「初期暫態應與材料轉換分離。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify false endpoints from pulses or ignition\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Startup transients need separation from material transitions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"初期暫態應與材料轉換分離。","textEn":"Startup transients need separation from material transitions."},{"id":"a056-v8-11-k2","title":"訊號處理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal processing: principle and limits","text":"訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","textEn":"Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「辨識脈衝或點火暫態的假端點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify false endpoints from pulses or ignition\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","初期暫態應與材料轉換分離。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。"],"optionsEn":["Longer filtering is always better.","Startup transients need separation from material transitions.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初期暫態應與材料轉換分離。 訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","explanationEn":"Startup transients need separation from material transitions. Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}},{"id":"a056-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-11"],"title":"記錄訊號飽和與資料缺失","titleEn":"Record saturation and missing data","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：無效訊號不能直接視為合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Invalid signals must not be treated as acceptance.","instruction":"記錄訊號飽和與資料缺失。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「無效訊號不能直接視為合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Record saturation and missing data. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Invalid signals must not be treated as acceptance.","observation":"無效訊號不能直接視為合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Invalid signals must not be treated as acceptance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Longer filtering is always better.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「記錄訊號飽和與資料缺失」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「無效訊號不能直接視為合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Record saturation and missing data\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Invalid signals must not be treated as acceptance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"無效訊號不能直接視為合格。","textEn":"Invalid signals must not be treated as acceptance."},{"id":"a056-v8-12-k2","title":"訊號處理的原理與限制","titleEn":"Signal processing: principle and limits","text":"訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","textEn":"Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記錄訊號飽和與資料缺失」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Record saturation and missing data\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["把濾波時間拉長永遠更好。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","無效訊號不能直接視為合格。"],"optionsEn":["Longer filtering is always better.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","Invalid signals must not be treated as acceptance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"無效訊號不能直接視為合格。 訊號濾波會影響噪聲與延遲，不能只追求平滑。","explanationEn":"Invalid signals must not be treated as acceptance. Filtering affects noise and latency, so smoothness is not the sole objective."}}]},{"id":"a056-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"停止邏輯","titleEn":"Stop logic","description":"停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","descriptionEn":"Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency.","steps":[{"id":"a056-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-12"],"title":"設計持續時間確認以避免誤觸發","titleEn":"Require persistence to reduce false triggers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：確認時間也增加停止延遲。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Persistence confirmation adds stop delay.","instruction":"設計持續時間確認以避免誤觸發。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「確認時間也增加停止延遲。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Require persistence to reduce false triggers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Persistence confirmation adds stop delay.","observation":"確認時間也增加停止延遲。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Persistence confirmation adds stop delay. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計持續時間確認以避免誤觸發」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「確認時間也增加停止延遲。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Require persistence to reduce false triggers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Persistence confirmation adds stop delay.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"確認時間也增加停止延遲。","textEn":"Persistence confirmation adds stop delay."},{"id":"a056-v8-13-k2","title":"停止邏輯的原理與限制","titleEn":"Stop logic: principle and limits","text":"停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","textEn":"Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計持續時間確認以避免誤觸發」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Require persistence to reduce false triggers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["確認時間也增加停止延遲。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。"],"optionsEn":["Persistence confirmation adds stop delay.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"確認時間也增加停止延遲。 停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","explanationEn":"Persistence confirmation adds stop delay. Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}},{"id":"a056-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-13"],"title":"將感測、判讀與機台停止延遲分帳","titleEn":"Separate sensing, decision and tool-stop delays","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：總延遲決定額外移除量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Total latency determines extra removal.","instruction":"將感測、判讀與機台停止延遲分帳。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「總延遲決定額外移除量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate sensing, decision and tool-stop delays. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Total latency determines extra removal.","observation":"總延遲決定額外移除量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Total latency determines extra removal. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將感測、判讀與機台停止延遲分帳」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「總延遲決定額外移除量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate sensing, decision and tool-stop delays\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Total latency determines extra removal.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"總延遲決定額外移除量。","textEn":"Total latency determines extra removal."},{"id":"a056-v8-14-k2","title":"停止邏輯的原理與限制","titleEn":"Stop logic: principle and limits","text":"停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","textEn":"Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將感測、判讀與機台停止延遲分帳」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate sensing, decision and tool-stop delays\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","總延遲決定額外移除量。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。"],"optionsEn":["All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","Total latency determines extra removal.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"總延遲決定額外移除量。 停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","explanationEn":"Total latency determines extra removal. Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}},{"id":"a056-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-14"],"title":"以速率估算延遲造成的過蝕刻","titleEn":"Estimate overetch caused by latency","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：速率不確定度會傳入深度誤差。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rate uncertainty propagates into depth error.","instruction":"以速率估算延遲造成的過蝕刻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「速率不確定度會傳入深度誤差。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設穩態速率 2.0 nm/s，感測延遲 0.20 s、濾波判讀 0.50 s、停止反應延遲 0.30 s。總延遲 1.00 s，額外移除量約 2.0 nm。若實際速率介於 1.8–2.2 nm/s，延遲所致移除量也介於 1.8–2.2 nm。忽略化學反應停止後的殘餘效應，並把此限制寫入報告。","instructionEn":"Estimate overetch caused by latency. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rate uncertainty propagates into depth error.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume steady removal 2.0 nm/s, sensing delay 0.20 s, filtering/decision delay 0.50 s and process-stop delay 0.30 s. Total latency is 1.00 s, causing about 2.0 nm extra removal. A rate range of 1.8–2.2 nm/s gives 1.8–2.2 nm extra removal. State that residual post-stop chemistry is excluded.","observation":"速率不確定度會傳入深度誤差。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n必須把三種延遲相加，得到 1.00 s 與 1.8–2.2 nm 範圍。","observationEn":"Rate uncertainty propagates into depth error. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nSum all three delays to obtain 1.00 s and the 1.8–2.2 nm range.","failure":"若報告假設「偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以速率估算延遲造成的過蝕刻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「速率不確定度會傳入深度誤差。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：必須把三種延遲相加，得到 1.00 s 與 1.8–2.2 nm 範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate overetch caused by latency\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rate uncertainty propagates into depth error.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Sum all three delays to obtain 1.00 s and the 1.8–2.2 nm range.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"速率不確定度會傳入深度誤差。","textEn":"Rate uncertainty propagates into depth error."},{"id":"a056-v8-15-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設穩態速率 2.0 nm/s，感測延遲 0.20 s、濾波判讀 0.50 s、停止反應延遲 0.30 s。總延遲 1.00 s，額外移除量約 2.0 nm。若實際速率介於 1.8–2.2 nm/s，延遲所致移除量也介於 1.8–2.2 nm。忽略化學反應停止後的殘餘效應，並把此限制寫入報告。","textEn":"Assume steady removal 2.0 nm/s, sensing delay 0.20 s, filtering/decision delay 0.50 s and process-stop delay 0.30 s. Total latency is 1.00 s, causing about 2.0 nm extra removal. A rate range of 1.8–2.2 nm/s gives 1.8–2.2 nm extra removal. State that residual post-stop chemistry is excluded."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以速率估算延遲造成的過蝕刻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate overetch caused by latency\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","速率不確定度會傳入深度誤差。"],"optionsEn":["All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","Rate uncertainty propagates into depth error."],"answer":2,"explanation":"速率不確定度會傳入深度誤差。 停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","explanationEn":"Rate uncertainty propagates into depth error. Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設穩態速率 2.0 nm/s，感測延遲 0.20 s、濾波判讀 0.50 s、停止反應延遲 0.30 s。總延遲 1.00 s，額外移除量約 2.0 nm。若實際速率介於 1.8–2.2 nm/s，延遲所致移除量也介於 1.8–2.2 nm。忽略化學反應停止後的殘餘效應，並把此限制寫入報告。","textEn":"Assume steady removal 2.0 nm/s, sensing delay 0.20 s, filtering/decision delay 0.50 s and process-stop delay 0.30 s. Total latency is 1.00 s, causing about 2.0 nm extra removal. A rate range of 1.8–2.2 nm/s gives 1.8–2.2 nm extra removal. State that residual post-stop chemistry is excluded.","check":"必須把三種延遲相加，得到 1.00 s 與 1.8–2.2 nm 範圍。","checkEn":"Sum all three delays to obtain 1.00 s and the 1.8–2.2 nm range."}},{"id":"a056-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-15"],"title":"設計端點未出現時的逾時分流","titleEn":"Define timeout handling when no endpoint appears","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：逾時是異常而非正常完工證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Timeout is an anomaly, not proof of completion.","instruction":"設計端點未出現時的逾時分流。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「逾時是異常而非正常完工證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define timeout handling when no endpoint appears. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Timeout is an anomaly, not proof of completion.","observation":"逾時是異常而非正常完工證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Timeout is an anomaly, not proof of completion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計端點未出現時的逾時分流」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「逾時是異常而非正常完工證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define timeout handling when no endpoint appears\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Timeout is an anomaly, not proof of completion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"逾時是異常而非正常完工證據。","textEn":"Timeout is an anomaly, not proof of completion."},{"id":"a056-v8-16-k2","title":"停止邏輯的原理與限制","titleEn":"Stop logic: principle and limits","text":"停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","textEn":"Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計端點未出現時的逾時分流」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define timeout handling when no endpoint appears\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["逾時是異常而非正常完工證據。","偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。"],"optionsEn":["Timeout is an anomaly, not proof of completion.","All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逾時是異常而非正常完工證據。 停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","explanationEn":"Timeout is an anomaly, not proof of completion. Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}},{"id":"a056-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-16"],"title":"比較最快與最慢區域的停止需求","titleEn":"Compare stop needs of the fastest and slowest regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：全片完成度可能需要有限過蝕刻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Whole-wafer completion may need bounded overetch.","instruction":"比較最快與最慢區域的停止需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「全片完成度可能需要有限過蝕刻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare stop needs of the fastest and slowest regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Whole-wafer completion may need bounded overetch.","observation":"全片完成度可能需要有限過蝕刻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Whole-wafer completion may need bounded overetch. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較最快與最慢區域的停止需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「全片完成度可能需要有限過蝕刻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare stop needs of the fastest and slowest regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Whole-wafer completion may need bounded overetch.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"全片完成度可能需要有限過蝕刻。","textEn":"Whole-wafer completion may need bounded overetch."},{"id":"a056-v8-17-k2","title":"停止邏輯的原理與限制","titleEn":"Stop logic: principle and limits","text":"停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","textEn":"Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較最快與最慢區域的停止需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare stop needs of the fastest and slowest regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","全片完成度可能需要有限過蝕刻。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。"],"optionsEn":["All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","Whole-wafer completion may need bounded overetch.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"全片完成度可能需要有限過蝕刻。 停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","explanationEn":"Whole-wafer completion may need bounded overetch. Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}},{"id":"a056-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-17"],"title":"區分腔體清潔端點與晶圓端點","titleEn":"Distinguish chamber-cleaning and wafer endpoints","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同物種訊號可代表不同反應狀態。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The same species signal can indicate different process states.","instruction":"區分腔體清潔端點與晶圓端點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「相同物種訊號可代表不同反應狀態。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish chamber-cleaning and wafer endpoints. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: The same species signal can indicate different process states.","observation":"相同物種訊號可代表不同反應狀態。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The same species signal can indicate different process states. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分腔體清潔端點與晶圓端點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同物種訊號可代表不同反應狀態。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish chamber-cleaning and wafer endpoints\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The same species signal can indicate different process states.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同物種訊號可代表不同反應狀態。","textEn":"The same species signal can indicate different process states."},{"id":"a056-v8-18-k2","title":"停止邏輯的原理與限制","titleEn":"Stop logic: principle and limits","text":"停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","textEn":"Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分腔體清潔端點與晶圓端點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish chamber-cleaning and wafer endpoints\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["偵測到端點後所有反應立即停止。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","相同物種訊號可代表不同反應狀態。"],"optionsEn":["All reactions stop instantly when endpoint is detected.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","The same species signal can indicate different process states."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同物種訊號可代表不同反應狀態。 停止邏輯需兼顧誤觸發、漏檢及控制延遲。","explanationEn":"The same species signal can indicate different process states. Stop logic must balance false triggers, misses and control latency."}}]},{"id":"a056-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗證與漂移","titleEn":"Validation and drift","description":"端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","descriptionEn":"Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history.","steps":[{"id":"a056-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-18"],"title":"以截面膜厚驗證端點判讀","titleEn":"Validate endpoint decisions using cross-sectional thickness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：直接量測提供外部參考。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Direct measurements provide an external reference.","instruction":"以截面膜厚驗證端點判讀。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「直接量測提供外部參考。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Validate endpoint decisions using cross-sectional thickness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Direct measurements provide an external reference.","observation":"直接量測提供外部參考。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Direct measurements provide an external reference. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以截面膜厚驗證端點判讀」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「直接量測提供外部參考。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Validate endpoint decisions using cross-sectional thickness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Direct measurements provide an external reference.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"直接量測提供外部參考。","textEn":"Direct measurements provide an external reference."},{"id":"a056-v8-19-k2","title":"驗證與漂移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Validation and drift: principle and limits","text":"端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","textEn":"Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以截面膜厚驗證端點判讀」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Validate endpoint decisions using cross-sectional thickness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["直接量測提供外部參考。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。"],"optionsEn":["Direct measurements provide an external reference.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","Every brightness change means etching is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"直接量測提供外部參考。 端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","explanationEn":"Direct measurements provide an external reference. Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}},{"id":"a056-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-19"],"title":"用盲測批次檢驗判讀門檻","titleEn":"Test thresholds on held-out lots","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：門檻需在未調整資料上驗證。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thresholds need validation on untuned data.","instruction":"用盲測批次檢驗判讀門檻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「門檻需在未調整資料上驗證。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Test thresholds on held-out lots. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thresholds need validation on untuned data.","observation":"門檻需在未調整資料上驗證。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thresholds need validation on untuned data. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用盲測批次檢驗判讀門檻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「門檻需在未調整資料上驗證。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Test thresholds on held-out lots\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thresholds need validation on untuned data.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"門檻需在未調整資料上驗證。","textEn":"Thresholds need validation on untuned data."},{"id":"a056-v8-20-k2","title":"驗證與漂移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Validation and drift: principle and limits","text":"端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","textEn":"Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用盲測批次檢驗判讀門檻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Test thresholds on held-out lots\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","門檻需在未調整資料上驗證。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。"],"optionsEn":["One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","Thresholds need validation on untuned data.","Every brightness change means etching is complete."],"answer":1,"explanation":"門檻需在未調整資料上驗證。 端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","explanationEn":"Thresholds need validation on untuned data. Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}},{"id":"a056-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-20"],"title":"追蹤視窗污染造成的光學漂移","titleEn":"Track optical drift from window contamination","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：透光變化會改變量測基線。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Transmission changes alter the measurement baseline.","instruction":"追蹤視窗污染造成的光學漂移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「透光變化會改變量測基線。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track optical drift from window contamination. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Transmission changes alter the measurement baseline.","observation":"透光變化會改變量測基線。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Transmission changes alter the measurement baseline. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤視窗污染造成的光學漂移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「透光變化會改變量測基線。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track optical drift from window contamination\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Transmission changes alter the measurement baseline.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"透光變化會改變量測基線。","textEn":"Transmission changes alter the measurement baseline."},{"id":"a056-v8-21-k2","title":"驗證與漂移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Validation and drift: principle and limits","text":"端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","textEn":"Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤視窗污染造成的光學漂移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track optical drift from window contamination\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","透光變化會改變量測基線。"],"optionsEn":["One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Transmission changes alter the measurement baseline."],"answer":2,"explanation":"透光變化會改變量測基線。 端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","explanationEn":"Transmission changes alter the measurement baseline. Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}},{"id":"a056-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-21"],"title":"比較清潔前後的模型可用性","titleEn":"Compare model validity before and after cleaning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：腔體重置可能改變訊號特徵。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Chamber reset can change signal features.","instruction":"比較清潔前後的模型可用性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「腔體重置可能改變訊號特徵。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare model validity before and after cleaning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Chamber reset can change signal features.","observation":"腔體重置可能改變訊號特徵。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Chamber reset can change signal features. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較清潔前後的模型可用性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「腔體重置可能改變訊號特徵。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare model validity before and after cleaning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Chamber reset can change signal features.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"腔體重置可能改變訊號特徵。","textEn":"Chamber reset can change signal features."},{"id":"a056-v8-22-k2","title":"驗證與漂移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Validation and drift: principle and limits","text":"端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","textEn":"Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較清潔前後的模型可用性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare model validity before and after cleaning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["腔體重置可能改變訊號特徵。","一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。"],"optionsEn":["Chamber reset can change signal features.","One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","Every brightness change means etching is complete."],"answer":0,"explanation":"腔體重置可能改變訊號特徵。 端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","explanationEn":"Chamber reset can change signal features. Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}},{"id":"a056-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-22"],"title":"建立誤停與漏停的成本矩陣","titleEn":"Build a cost matrix for early and missed stops","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩種失敗的後果可能不對稱。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The consequences of the two failures can be asymmetric.","instruction":"建立誤停與漏停的成本矩陣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「兩種失敗的後果可能不對稱。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a cost matrix for early and missed stops. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: The consequences of the two failures can be asymmetric.","observation":"兩種失敗的後果可能不對稱。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The consequences of the two failures can be asymmetric. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立誤停與漏停的成本矩陣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩種失敗的後果可能不對稱。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a cost matrix for early and missed stops\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The consequences of the two failures can be asymmetric.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩種失敗的後果可能不對稱。","textEn":"The consequences of the two failures can be asymmetric."},{"id":"a056-v8-23-k2","title":"驗證與漂移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Validation and drift: principle and limits","text":"端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","textEn":"Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立誤停與漏停的成本矩陣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a cost matrix for early and missed stops\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","兩種失敗的後果可能不對稱。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。"],"optionsEn":["One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","The consequences of the two failures can be asymmetric.","Every brightness change means etching is complete."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩種失敗的後果可能不對稱。 端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","explanationEn":"The consequences of the two failures can be asymmetric. Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}},{"id":"a056-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-endpoint","v8b-endpointblog","v8b-ale","v8b-lametch"],"prerequisiteIds":["a056-v8-23"],"title":"交付具回溯資料的端點控制計畫","titleEn":"Deliver an endpoint plan with traceable data","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：每次停止應能對應訊號與膜厚證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Each stop should link to signal and thickness evidence.","instruction":"交付具回溯資料的端點控制計畫。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「每次停止應能對應訊號與膜厚證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver an endpoint plan with traceable data. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Each stop should link to signal and thickness evidence.","observation":"每次停止應能對應訊號與膜厚證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Each stop should link to signal and thickness evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付具回溯資料的端點控制計畫」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「每次停止應能對應訊號與膜厚證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver an endpoint plan with traceable data\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Each stop should link to signal and thickness evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a056-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"每次停止應能對應訊號與膜厚證據。","textEn":"Each stop should link to signal and thickness evidence."},{"id":"a056-v8-24-k2","title":"驗證與漂移的原理與限制","titleEn":"Validation and drift: principle and limits","text":"端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","textEn":"Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付具回溯資料的端點控制計畫」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver an endpoint plan with traceable data\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次校準後不需要再量膜厚。","所有亮度變化都等於材料已蝕刻完。","每次停止應能對應訊號與膜厚證據。"],"optionsEn":["One calibration removes the need for further thickness measurement.","Every brightness change means etching is complete.","Each stop should link to signal and thickness evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每次停止應能對應訊號與膜厚證據。 端點模型需要以實際剩餘膜厚與腔體歷程持續驗證。","explanationEn":"Each stop should link to signal and thickness evidence. Endpoint models need validation against remaining thickness and chamber history."}}]}]},{"id":"a057","title":"電漿增強化學氣相沉積","titleEn":"Plasma-enhanced chemical vapor deposition","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究電漿與成膜、膜性與應力、三維覆蓋、整合與可靠度；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: plasma and growth, film properties and stress, 3d coverage, integration and reliability. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電漿與成膜","膜性與應力","三維覆蓋","整合與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Plasma and growth","Film properties and stress","3D coverage","Integration and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"deposition","subcategoryTitle":"薄膜沉積","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thin-film deposition","stages":[{"id":"a057-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"電漿與成膜","titleEn":"Plasma and growth","description":"PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","descriptionEn":"PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage.","steps":[{"id":"a057-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出電漿活化到表面反應路徑","titleEn":"Trace plasma activation into surface growth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氣相與表面反應共同參與沉積。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Gas-phase and surface reactions both contribute to deposition.","instruction":"畫出電漿活化到表面反應路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「氣相與表面反應共同參與沉積。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace plasma activation into surface growth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Gas-phase and surface reactions both contribute to deposition.","observation":"氣相與表面反應共同參與沉積。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Gas-phase and surface reactions both contribute to deposition. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出電漿活化到表面反應路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氣相與表面反應共同參與沉積。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace plasma activation into surface growth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Gas-phase and surface reactions both contribute to deposition.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氣相與表面反應共同參與沉積。","textEn":"Gas-phase and surface reactions both contribute to deposition."},{"id":"a057-v8-01-k2","title":"電漿與成膜的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and growth: principle and limits","text":"PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","textEn":"PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出電漿活化到表面反應路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace plasma activation into surface growth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣相與表面反應共同參與沉積。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。"],"optionsEn":["Gas-phase and surface reactions both contribute to deposition.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氣相與表面反應共同參與沉積。 PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","explanationEn":"Gas-phase and surface reactions both contribute to deposition. PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}},{"id":"a057-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-01"],"title":"比較熱 CVD 與 PECVD 能量來源","titleEn":"Compare energy sources in thermal CVD and PECVD","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電漿可降低部分熱活化需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Plasma can reduce some thermal-activation requirements.","instruction":"比較熱 CVD 與 PECVD 能量來源。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「電漿可降低部分熱活化需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare energy sources in thermal CVD and PECVD. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Plasma can reduce some thermal-activation requirements.","observation":"電漿可降低部分熱活化需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Plasma can reduce some thermal-activation requirements. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較熱 CVD 與 PECVD 能量來源」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電漿可降低部分熱活化需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare energy sources in thermal CVD and PECVD\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Plasma can reduce some thermal-activation requirements.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電漿可降低部分熱活化需求。","textEn":"Plasma can reduce some thermal-activation requirements."},{"id":"a057-v8-02-k2","title":"電漿與成膜的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and growth: principle and limits","text":"PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","textEn":"PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較熱 CVD 與 PECVD 能量來源」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare energy sources in thermal CVD and PECVD\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","電漿可降低部分熱活化需求。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。"],"optionsEn":["Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","Plasma can reduce some thermal-activation requirements.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電漿可降低部分熱活化需求。 PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","explanationEn":"Plasma can reduce some thermal-activation requirements. PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}},{"id":"a057-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-02"],"title":"列出基板可接受的熱預算","titleEn":"List the substrate thermal budget","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低溫整合仍需評估累積熱史。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low-temperature integration still needs cumulative thermal history.","instruction":"列出基板可接受的熱預算。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「低溫整合仍需評估累積熱史。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List the substrate thermal budget. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low-temperature integration still needs cumulative thermal history.","observation":"低溫整合仍需評估累積熱史。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low-temperature integration still needs cumulative thermal history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出基板可接受的熱預算」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低溫整合仍需評估累積熱史。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List the substrate thermal budget\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low-temperature integration still needs cumulative thermal history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低溫整合仍需評估累積熱史。","textEn":"Low-temperature integration still needs cumulative thermal history."},{"id":"a057-v8-03-k2","title":"電漿與成膜的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and growth: principle and limits","text":"PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","textEn":"PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出基板可接受的熱預算」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List the substrate thermal budget\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","低溫整合仍需評估累積熱史。"],"optionsEn":["Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Low-temperature integration still needs cumulative thermal history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低溫整合仍需評估累積熱史。 PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","explanationEn":"Low-temperature integration still needs cumulative thermal history. PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}},{"id":"a057-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-03"],"title":"分開沉積與離子轟擊的作用","titleEn":"Separate deposition from ion-bombardment effects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：轟擊可能改變密度與損傷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bombardment can alter density and damage.","instruction":"分開沉積與離子轟擊的作用。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「轟擊可能改變密度與損傷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate deposition from ion-bombardment effects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bombardment can alter density and damage.","observation":"轟擊可能改變密度與損傷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bombardment can alter density and damage. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開沉積與離子轟擊的作用」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「轟擊可能改變密度與損傷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate deposition from ion-bombardment effects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bombardment can alter density and damage.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"轟擊可能改變密度與損傷。","textEn":"Bombardment can alter density and damage."},{"id":"a057-v8-04-k2","title":"電漿與成膜的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and growth: principle and limits","text":"PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","textEn":"PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開沉積與離子轟擊的作用」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate deposition from ion-bombardment effects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["轟擊可能改變密度與損傷。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。"],"optionsEn":["Bombardment can alter density and damage.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"轟擊可能改變密度與損傷。 PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","explanationEn":"Bombardment can alter density and damage. PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}},{"id":"a057-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-04"],"title":"建立基板前處理的對照組","titleEn":"Create controls for substrate pretreatment","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：初始表面影響成核與黏著。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Initial surfaces affect nucleation and adhesion.","instruction":"建立基板前處理的對照組。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「初始表面影響成核與黏著。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Create controls for substrate pretreatment. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Initial surfaces affect nucleation and adhesion.","observation":"初始表面影響成核與黏著。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Initial surfaces affect nucleation and adhesion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立基板前處理的對照組」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「初始表面影響成核與黏著。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Create controls for substrate pretreatment\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Initial surfaces affect nucleation and adhesion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"初始表面影響成核與黏著。","textEn":"Initial surfaces affect nucleation and adhesion."},{"id":"a057-v8-05-k2","title":"電漿與成膜的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and growth: principle and limits","text":"PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","textEn":"PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立基板前處理的對照組」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Create controls for substrate pretreatment\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","初始表面影響成核與黏著。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。"],"optionsEn":["Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","Initial surfaces affect nucleation and adhesion.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始表面影響成核與黏著。 PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","explanationEn":"Initial surfaces affect nucleation and adhesion. PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}},{"id":"a057-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-05"],"title":"選擇絕緣、保護或側壁用途","titleEn":"Choose insulation, passivation or spacer use","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同用途需要不同膜性目標。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different uses require different film-property targets.","instruction":"選擇絕緣、保護或側壁用途。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「不同用途需要不同膜性目標。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Choose insulation, passivation or spacer use. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different uses require different film-property targets.","observation":"不同用途需要不同膜性目標。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different uses require different film-property targets. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「選擇絕緣、保護或側壁用途」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同用途需要不同膜性目標。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Choose insulation, passivation or spacer use\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different uses require different film-property targets.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同用途需要不同膜性目標。","textEn":"Different uses require different film-property targets."},{"id":"a057-v8-06-k2","title":"電漿與成膜的原理與限制","titleEn":"Plasma and growth: principle and limits","text":"PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","textEn":"PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「選擇絕緣、保護或側壁用途」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Choose insulation, passivation or spacer use\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","不同用途需要不同膜性目標。"],"optionsEn":["Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Different uses require different film-property targets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同用途需要不同膜性目標。 PECVD 利用電漿活化反應，較低基板溫度不代表所有損傷都較低。","explanationEn":"Different uses require different film-property targets. PECVD activates reactions with plasma; lower substrate temperature does not guarantee lower total damage."}}]},{"id":"a057-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"膜性與應力","titleEn":"Film properties and stress","description":"膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","descriptionEn":"Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics.","steps":[{"id":"a057-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-06"],"title":"量測膜厚與折射率並檢查模型","titleEn":"Measure thickness and index while checking the model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：橢圓偏光擬合參數可能相關。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Ellipsometric fit parameters can be correlated.","instruction":"量測膜厚與折射率並檢查模型。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「橢圓偏光擬合參數可能相關。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure thickness and index while checking the model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Ellipsometric fit parameters can be correlated.","observation":"橢圓偏光擬合參數可能相關。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Ellipsometric fit parameters can be correlated. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測膜厚與折射率並檢查模型」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「橢圓偏光擬合參數可能相關。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure thickness and index while checking the model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Ellipsometric fit parameters can be correlated.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"橢圓偏光擬合參數可能相關。","textEn":"Ellipsometric fit parameters can be correlated."},{"id":"a057-v8-07-k2","title":"膜性與應力的原理與限制","titleEn":"Film properties and stress: principle and limits","text":"膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","textEn":"Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測膜厚與折射率並檢查模型」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure thickness and index while checking the model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["橢圓偏光擬合參數可能相關。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。"],"optionsEn":["Ellipsometric fit parameters can be correlated.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"橢圓偏光擬合參數可能相關。 膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","explanationEn":"Ellipsometric fit parameters can be correlated. Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}},{"id":"a057-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-07"],"title":"用光譜辨識氫相關鍵結","titleEn":"Identify hydrogen-related bonds spectroscopically","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氫可影響後續熱穩定與電性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Hydrogen can affect later thermal stability and electrical behavior.","instruction":"用光譜辨識氫相關鍵結。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「氫可影響後續熱穩定與電性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify hydrogen-related bonds spectroscopically. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Hydrogen can affect later thermal stability and electrical behavior.","observation":"氫可影響後續熱穩定與電性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Hydrogen can affect later thermal stability and electrical behavior. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用光譜辨識氫相關鍵結」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氫可影響後續熱穩定與電性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify hydrogen-related bonds spectroscopically\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Hydrogen can affect later thermal stability and electrical behavior.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氫可影響後續熱穩定與電性。","textEn":"Hydrogen can affect later thermal stability and electrical behavior."},{"id":"a057-v8-08-k2","title":"膜性與應力的原理與限制","titleEn":"Film properties and stress: principle and limits","text":"膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","textEn":"Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用光譜辨識氫相關鍵結」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify hydrogen-related bonds spectroscopically\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","氫可影響後續熱穩定與電性。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Hydrogen can affect later thermal stability and electrical behavior.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"氫可影響後續熱穩定與電性。 膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","explanationEn":"Hydrogen can affect later thermal stability and electrical behavior. Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}},{"id":"a057-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-08"],"title":"以晶圓曲率估算薄膜應力","titleEn":"Estimate film stress from wafer curvature","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：Stoney 近似需滿足薄膜與基板條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The Stoney approximation requires suitable film and substrate conditions.","instruction":"以晶圓曲率估算薄膜應力。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「Stoney 近似需滿足薄膜與基板條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate film stress from wafer curvature. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: The Stoney approximation requires suitable film and substrate conditions.","observation":"Stoney 近似需滿足薄膜與基板條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The Stoney approximation requires suitable film and substrate conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以晶圓曲率估算薄膜應力」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「Stoney 近似需滿足薄膜與基板條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate film stress from wafer curvature\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The Stoney approximation requires suitable film and substrate conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"Stoney 近似需滿足薄膜與基板條件。","textEn":"The Stoney approximation requires suitable film and substrate conditions."},{"id":"a057-v8-09-k2","title":"膜性與應力的原理與限制","titleEn":"Film properties and stress: principle and limits","text":"膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","textEn":"Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以晶圓曲率估算薄膜應力」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate film stress from wafer curvature\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","Stoney 近似需滿足薄膜與基板條件。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","The Stoney approximation requires suitable film and substrate conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Stoney 近似需滿足薄膜與基板條件。 膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","explanationEn":"The Stoney approximation requires suitable film and substrate conditions. Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}},{"id":"a057-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-09"],"title":"比較拉伸與壓縮應力的失效","titleEn":"Compare tensile- and compressive-stress failures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩種應力可能導致裂紋或剝離等不同結果。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The stress signs can produce different cracking or delamination outcomes.","instruction":"比較拉伸與壓縮應力的失效。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「兩種應力可能導致裂紋或剝離等不同結果。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare tensile- and compressive-stress failures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The stress signs can produce different cracking or delamination outcomes.","observation":"兩種應力可能導致裂紋或剝離等不同結果。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The stress signs can produce different cracking or delamination outcomes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較拉伸與壓縮應力的失效」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩種應力可能導致裂紋或剝離等不同結果。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare tensile- and compressive-stress failures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The stress signs can produce different cracking or delamination outcomes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩種應力可能導致裂紋或剝離等不同結果。","textEn":"The stress signs can produce different cracking or delamination outcomes."},{"id":"a057-v8-10-k2","title":"膜性與應力的原理與限制","titleEn":"Film properties and stress: principle and limits","text":"膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","textEn":"Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較拉伸與壓縮應力的失效」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare tensile- and compressive-stress failures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩種應力可能導致裂紋或剝離等不同結果。","厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。"],"optionsEn":["The stress signs can produce different cracking or delamination outcomes.","Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種應力可能導致裂紋或剝離等不同結果。 膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","explanationEn":"The stress signs can produce different cracking or delamination outcomes. Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}},{"id":"a057-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-10"],"title":"將濕蝕刻速率作為輔助膜性指標","titleEn":"Use wet-etch rate as a supplementary film metric","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：速率不是膜密度或電性的唯一證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rate is not sole evidence of density or electrical quality.","instruction":"將濕蝕刻速率作為輔助膜性指標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「速率不是膜密度或電性的唯一證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use wet-etch rate as a supplementary film metric. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rate is not sole evidence of density or electrical quality.","observation":"速率不是膜密度或電性的唯一證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rate is not sole evidence of density or electrical quality. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將濕蝕刻速率作為輔助膜性指標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「速率不是膜密度或電性的唯一證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use wet-etch rate as a supplementary film metric\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rate is not sole evidence of density or electrical quality.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"速率不是膜密度或電性的唯一證據。","textEn":"Rate is not sole evidence of density or electrical quality."},{"id":"a057-v8-11-k2","title":"膜性與應力的原理與限制","titleEn":"Film properties and stress: principle and limits","text":"膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","textEn":"Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將濕蝕刻速率作為輔助膜性指標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use wet-etch rate as a supplementary film metric\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","速率不是膜密度或電性的唯一證據。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Rate is not sole evidence of density or electrical quality.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"速率不是膜密度或電性的唯一證據。 膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","explanationEn":"Rate is not sole evidence of density or electrical quality. Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}},{"id":"a057-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-11"],"title":"比較沉積後與熱處理後的膜性","titleEn":"Compare as-deposited and annealed properties","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：後續熱史可能改變氫與應力。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Later thermal history can change hydrogen and stress.","instruction":"比較沉積後與熱處理後的膜性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「後續熱史可能改變氫與應力。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare as-deposited and annealed properties. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Later thermal history can change hydrogen and stress.","observation":"後續熱史可能改變氫與應力。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Later thermal history can change hydrogen and stress. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較沉積後與熱處理後的膜性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「後續熱史可能改變氫與應力。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare as-deposited and annealed properties\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Later thermal history can change hydrogen and stress.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"後續熱史可能改變氫與應力。","textEn":"Later thermal history can change hydrogen and stress."},{"id":"a057-v8-12-k2","title":"膜性與應力的原理與限制","titleEn":"Film properties and stress: principle and limits","text":"膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","textEn":"Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較沉積後與熱處理後的膜性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare as-deposited and annealed properties\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["厚度相同就表示介電品質相同。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","後續熱史可能改變氫與應力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal thickness proves equal dielectric quality.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","Later thermal history can change hydrogen and stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"後續熱史可能改變氫與應力。 膜厚、化學組成、氫含量與應力是不同材料指標。","explanationEn":"Later thermal history can change hydrogen and stress. Thickness, composition, hydrogen content and stress are distinct film metrics."}}]},{"id":"a057-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"三維覆蓋","titleEn":"3D coverage","description":"頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","descriptionEn":"Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality.","steps":[{"id":"a057-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-12"],"title":"畫出溝槽頂部、側壁與底部厚度","titleEn":"Map thickness at trench top, walls and bottom","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共形性需以位置比值表達。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Conformality needs location-dependent ratios.","instruction":"畫出溝槽頂部、側壁與底部厚度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「共形性需以位置比值表達。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Map thickness at trench top, walls and bottom. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Conformality needs location-dependent ratios.","observation":"共形性需以位置比值表達。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Conformality needs location-dependent ratios. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出溝槽頂部、側壁與底部厚度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共形性需以位置比值表達。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Map thickness at trench top, walls and bottom\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Conformality needs location-dependent ratios.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共形性需以位置比值表達。","textEn":"Conformality needs location-dependent ratios."},{"id":"a057-v8-13-k2","title":"三維覆蓋的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D coverage: principle and limits","text":"頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","textEn":"Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出溝槽頂部、側壁與底部厚度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Map thickness at trench top, walls and bottom\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["共形性需以位置比值表達。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。"],"optionsEn":["Conformality needs location-dependent ratios.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共形性需以位置比值表達。 頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","explanationEn":"Conformality needs location-dependent ratios. Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}},{"id":"a057-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-13"],"title":"比較高黏著機率與反應物耗盡","titleEn":"Compare high sticking probability with reactant depletion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：入口消耗會限制深部覆蓋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Entrance consumption can limit deep coverage.","instruction":"比較高黏著機率與反應物耗盡。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「入口消耗會限制深部覆蓋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare high sticking probability with reactant depletion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Entrance consumption can limit deep coverage.","observation":"入口消耗會限制深部覆蓋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Entrance consumption can limit deep coverage. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較高黏著機率與反應物耗盡」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「入口消耗會限制深部覆蓋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare high sticking probability with reactant depletion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Entrance consumption can limit deep coverage.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"入口消耗會限制深部覆蓋。","textEn":"Entrance consumption can limit deep coverage."},{"id":"a057-v8-14-k2","title":"三維覆蓋的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D coverage: principle and limits","text":"頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","textEn":"Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較高黏著機率與反應物耗盡」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare high sticking probability with reactant depletion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","入口消耗會限制深部覆蓋。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。"],"optionsEn":["Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","Entrance consumption can limit deep coverage.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口消耗會限制深部覆蓋。 頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","explanationEn":"Entrance consumption can limit deep coverage. Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}},{"id":"a057-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-14"],"title":"辨識夾縫封口與內部空洞","titleEn":"Identify pinch-off and internal voids","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面閉合不能證明內部填滿。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Surface closure does not prove internal fill.","instruction":"辨識夾縫封口與內部空洞。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「表面閉合不能證明內部填滿。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Identify pinch-off and internal voids. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Surface closure does not prove internal fill.","observation":"表面閉合不能證明內部填滿。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Surface closure does not prove internal fill. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「辨識夾縫封口與內部空洞」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面閉合不能證明內部填滿。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Identify pinch-off and internal voids\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Surface closure does not prove internal fill.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面閉合不能證明內部填滿。","textEn":"Surface closure does not prove internal fill."},{"id":"a057-v8-15-k2","title":"三維覆蓋的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D coverage: principle and limits","text":"頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","textEn":"Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「辨識夾縫封口與內部空洞」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Identify pinch-off and internal voids\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","表面閉合不能證明內部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Surface closure does not prove internal fill."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面閉合不能證明內部填滿。 頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","explanationEn":"Surface closure does not prove internal fill. Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}},{"id":"a057-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-15"],"title":"量測晶圓邊緣與中心膜厚","titleEn":"Measure edge and center thickness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：晶圓內均勻性需要空間統計。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Within-wafer uniformity needs spatial statistics.","instruction":"量測晶圓邊緣與中心膜厚。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「晶圓內均勻性需要空間統計。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure edge and center thickness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Within-wafer uniformity needs spatial statistics.","observation":"晶圓內均勻性需要空間統計。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Within-wafer uniformity needs spatial statistics. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測晶圓邊緣與中心膜厚」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「晶圓內均勻性需要空間統計。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure edge and center thickness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Within-wafer uniformity needs spatial statistics.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"晶圓內均勻性需要空間統計。","textEn":"Within-wafer uniformity needs spatial statistics."},{"id":"a057-v8-16-k2","title":"三維覆蓋的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D coverage: principle and limits","text":"頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","textEn":"Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測晶圓邊緣與中心膜厚」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure edge and center thickness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["晶圓內均勻性需要空間統計。","平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。"],"optionsEn":["Within-wafer uniformity needs spatial statistics.","Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶圓內均勻性需要空間統計。 頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","explanationEn":"Within-wafer uniformity needs spatial statistics. Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}},{"id":"a057-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-16"],"title":"檢查顆粒與腔壁沉積關聯","titleEn":"Relate particles to chamber-wall deposition","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：腔壁膜可能形成顆粒來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Wall films can become particle sources.","instruction":"檢查顆粒與腔壁沉積關聯。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「腔壁膜可能形成顆粒來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate particles to chamber-wall deposition. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Wall films can become particle sources.","observation":"腔壁膜可能形成顆粒來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Wall films can become particle sources. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查顆粒與腔壁沉積關聯」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「腔壁膜可能形成顆粒來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate particles to chamber-wall deposition\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Wall films can become particle sources.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"腔壁膜可能形成顆粒來源。","textEn":"Wall films can become particle sources."},{"id":"a057-v8-17-k2","title":"三維覆蓋的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D coverage: principle and limits","text":"頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","textEn":"Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查顆粒與腔壁沉積關聯」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate particles to chamber-wall deposition\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","腔壁膜可能形成顆粒來源。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。"],"optionsEn":["Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","Wall films can become particle sources.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"腔壁膜可能形成顆粒來源。 頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","explanationEn":"Wall films can become particle sources. Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}},{"id":"a057-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-17"],"title":"比較腔體清潔前後的成膜漂移","titleEn":"Compare deposition drift around chamber cleaning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：腔壁狀態可能改變製程再現性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Wall condition can alter process repeatability.","instruction":"比較腔體清潔前後的成膜漂移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「腔壁狀態可能改變製程再現性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare deposition drift around chamber cleaning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Wall condition can alter process repeatability.","observation":"腔壁狀態可能改變製程再現性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Wall condition can alter process repeatability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較腔體清潔前後的成膜漂移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「腔壁狀態可能改變製程再現性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare deposition drift around chamber cleaning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Wall condition can alter process repeatability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"腔壁狀態可能改變製程再現性。","textEn":"Wall condition can alter process repeatability."},{"id":"a057-v8-18-k2","title":"三維覆蓋的原理與限制","titleEn":"3D coverage: principle and limits","text":"頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","textEn":"Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較腔體清潔前後的成膜漂移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare deposition drift around chamber cleaning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面均勻就表示所有側壁等厚。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","腔壁狀態可能改變製程再現性。"],"optionsEn":["Planar uniformity proves equal sidewall thickness.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Wall condition can alter process repeatability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"腔壁狀態可能改變製程再現性。 頂部沉積均勻性不代表三維側壁共形性。","explanationEn":"Wall condition can alter process repeatability. Uniform top-surface deposition does not establish 3D conformality."}}]},{"id":"a057-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合與可靠度","titleEn":"Integration and reliability","description":"介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","descriptionEn":"Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index.","steps":[{"id":"a057-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-18"],"title":"以電容結構估算介電常數","titleEn":"Estimate permittivity using capacitor structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：面積、厚度與邊緣效應需分辨。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Area, thickness and fringe effects need separation.","instruction":"以電容結構估算介電常數。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「面積、厚度與邊緣效應需分辨。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：使用假想平行板電容 A=1.00 mm²、膜厚 t=1.00 μm、C=35.416 pF，忽略邊緣與寄生電容。由 εr=Ct/(ε0A)，ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m，得到 εr=4.00。若未扣除 5 pF 寄生，表觀值約 4.565；這說明量測寄生不能直接歸因於膜成分。","instructionEn":"Estimate permittivity using capacitor structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Area, thickness and fringe effects need separation.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Use a hypothetical parallel-plate capacitor with A=1.00 mm², t=1.00 μm and C=35.416 pF, initially neglecting fringing and parasitics. εr=Ct/(ε0A), with ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m, gives 4.00. An unremoved 5 pF parasitic gives an apparent 4.565, showing why parasitics cannot be attributed directly to film composition.","observation":"面積、厚度與邊緣效應需分辨。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 SI 單位換算、4.00 與約 4.565，並明示寄生假設。","observationEn":"Area, thickness and fringe effects need separation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nShow SI conversions, 4.00 and about 4.565, stating parasitic assumptions.","failure":"若報告假設「折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以電容結構估算介電常數」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「面積、厚度與邊緣效應需分辨。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 SI 單位換算、4.00 與約 4.565，並明示寄生假設。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate permittivity using capacitor structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Area, thickness and fringe effects need separation.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Show SI conversions, 4.00 and about 4.565, stating parasitic assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"面積、厚度與邊緣效應需分辨。","textEn":"Area, thickness and fringe effects need separation."},{"id":"a057-v8-19-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"使用假想平行板電容 A=1.00 mm²、膜厚 t=1.00 μm、C=35.416 pF，忽略邊緣與寄生電容。由 εr=Ct/(ε0A)，ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m，得到 εr=4.00。若未扣除 5 pF 寄生，表觀值約 4.565；這說明量測寄生不能直接歸因於膜成分。","textEn":"Use a hypothetical parallel-plate capacitor with A=1.00 mm², t=1.00 μm and C=35.416 pF, initially neglecting fringing and parasitics. εr=Ct/(ε0A), with ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m, gives 4.00. An unremoved 5 pF parasitic gives an apparent 4.565, showing why parasitics cannot be attributed directly to film composition."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以電容結構估算介電常數」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate permittivity using capacitor structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["面積、厚度與邊緣效應需分辨。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Area, thickness and fringe effects need separation.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"面積、厚度與邊緣效應需分辨。 介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","explanationEn":"Area, thickness and fringe effects need separation. Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"使用假想平行板電容 A=1.00 mm²、膜厚 t=1.00 μm、C=35.416 pF，忽略邊緣與寄生電容。由 εr=Ct/(ε0A)，ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m，得到 εr=4.00。若未扣除 5 pF 寄生，表觀值約 4.565；這說明量測寄生不能直接歸因於膜成分。","textEn":"Use a hypothetical parallel-plate capacitor with A=1.00 mm², t=1.00 μm and C=35.416 pF, initially neglecting fringing and parasitics. εr=Ct/(ε0A), with ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m, gives 4.00. An unremoved 5 pF parasitic gives an apparent 4.565, showing why parasitics cannot be attributed directly to film composition.","check":"交付 SI 單位換算、4.00 與約 4.565，並明示寄生假設。","checkEn":"Show SI conversions, 4.00 and about 4.565, stating parasitic assumptions."}},{"id":"a057-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-19"],"title":"量測漏電隨電場的關係","titleEn":"Measure leakage versus electric field","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同電壓在不同厚度有不同電場。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Equal voltage gives different fields at different thicknesses.","instruction":"量測漏電隨電場的關係。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「相同電壓在不同厚度有不同電場。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure leakage versus electric field. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Equal voltage gives different fields at different thicknesses.","observation":"相同電壓在不同厚度有不同電場。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Equal voltage gives different fields at different thicknesses. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測漏電隨電場的關係」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同電壓在不同厚度有不同電場。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure leakage versus electric field\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Equal voltage gives different fields at different thicknesses.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同電壓在不同厚度有不同電場。","textEn":"Equal voltage gives different fields at different thicknesses."},{"id":"a057-v8-20-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","textEn":"Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測漏電隨電場的關係」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure leakage versus electric field\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","相同電壓在不同厚度有不同電場。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Equal voltage gives different fields at different thicknesses.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同電壓在不同厚度有不同電場。 介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","explanationEn":"Equal voltage gives different fields at different thicknesses. Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}},{"id":"a057-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-20"],"title":"比較介面陷阱與體材料缺陷","titleEn":"Distinguish interface traps from bulk defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：介面與體材料需要不同量測解釋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Interface and bulk behavior need different interpretations.","instruction":"比較介面陷阱與體材料缺陷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「介面與體材料需要不同量測解釋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish interface traps from bulk defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Interface and bulk behavior need different interpretations.","observation":"介面與體材料需要不同量測解釋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Interface and bulk behavior need different interpretations. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較介面陷阱與體材料缺陷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「介面與體材料需要不同量測解釋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish interface traps from bulk defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Interface and bulk behavior need different interpretations.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"介面與體材料需要不同量測解釋。","textEn":"Interface and bulk behavior need different interpretations."},{"id":"a057-v8-21-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","textEn":"Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較介面陷阱與體材料缺陷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish interface traps from bulk defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","介面與體材料需要不同量測解釋。"],"optionsEn":["Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","Interface and bulk behavior need different interpretations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介面與體材料需要不同量測解釋。 介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","explanationEn":"Interface and bulk behavior need different interpretations. Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}},{"id":"a057-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-21"],"title":"檢查膜層與金屬接觸的黏著","titleEn":"Assess adhesion to metal-contact regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：介面污染可降低附著與可靠度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Interface contamination can weaken adhesion and reliability.","instruction":"檢查膜層與金屬接觸的黏著。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「介面污染可降低附著與可靠度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess adhesion to metal-contact regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Interface contamination can weaken adhesion and reliability.","observation":"介面污染可降低附著與可靠度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Interface contamination can weaken adhesion and reliability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查膜層與金屬接觸的黏著」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「介面污染可降低附著與可靠度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess adhesion to metal-contact regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Interface contamination can weaken adhesion and reliability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"介面污染可降低附著與可靠度。","textEn":"Interface contamination can weaken adhesion and reliability."},{"id":"a057-v8-22-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","textEn":"Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查膜層與金屬接觸的黏著」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess adhesion to metal-contact regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["介面污染可降低附著與可靠度。","折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Interface contamination can weaken adhesion and reliability.","Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面污染可降低附著與可靠度。 介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","explanationEn":"Interface contamination can weaken adhesion and reliability. Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}},{"id":"a057-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-22"],"title":"追蹤濕度或熱循環後的變化","titleEn":"Track changes after humidity or thermal cycling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：初始合格不代表長期穩定。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Initial acceptance does not prove long-term stability.","instruction":"追蹤濕度或熱循環後的變化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「初始合格不代表長期穩定。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track changes after humidity or thermal cycling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Initial acceptance does not prove long-term stability.","observation":"初始合格不代表長期穩定。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Initial acceptance does not prove long-term stability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤濕度或熱循環後的變化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「初始合格不代表長期穩定。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track changes after humidity or thermal cycling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Initial acceptance does not prove long-term stability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"初始合格不代表長期穩定。","textEn":"Initial acceptance does not prove long-term stability."},{"id":"a057-v8-23-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","textEn":"Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤濕度或熱循環後的變化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track changes after humidity or thermal cycling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","初始合格不代表長期穩定。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Initial acceptance does not prove long-term stability.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始合格不代表長期穩定。 介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","explanationEn":"Initial acceptance does not prove long-term stability. Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}},{"id":"a057-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-oxpecvd","v8b-nisttools","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a057-v8-23"],"title":"交付膜性、覆蓋與可靠度矩陣","titleEn":"Deliver a property–coverage–reliability matrix","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：PECVD 材料需按整合用途驗收。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: PECVD films need application-specific acceptance.","instruction":"交付膜性、覆蓋與可靠度矩陣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「PECVD 材料需按整合用途驗收。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver a property–coverage–reliability matrix. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: PECVD films need application-specific acceptance.","observation":"PECVD 材料需按整合用途驗收。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"PECVD films need application-specific acceptance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付膜性、覆蓋與可靠度矩陣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「PECVD 材料需按整合用途驗收。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver a property–coverage–reliability matrix\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"PECVD films need application-specific acceptance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a057-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"PECVD 材料需按整合用途驗收。","textEn":"PECVD films need application-specific acceptance."},{"id":"a057-v8-24-k2","title":"整合與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and reliability: principle and limits","text":"介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","textEn":"Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付膜性、覆蓋與可靠度矩陣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver a property–coverage–reliability matrix\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["折射率合格即可取代漏電測試。","較低溫度就能保證完全無電漿損傷。","PECVD 材料需按整合用途驗收。"],"optionsEn":["Passing refractive index replaces leakage testing.","Lower temperature guarantees no plasma damage.","PECVD films need application-specific acceptance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"PECVD 材料需按整合用途驗收。 介電與機械驗證需依用途制定，不能只測折射率。","explanationEn":"PECVD films need application-specific acceptance. Electrical and mechanical validation must match application, not rely only on index."}}]}]},{"id":"a058","title":"低壓化學氣相沉積","titleEn":"Low-pressure chemical vapor deposition","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究熱反應與低壓、批次與均勻性、材料與膜性、整合與品質；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: thermal reaction and low pressure, batch and uniformity, materials and film properties, integration and quality. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["熱反應與低壓","批次與均勻性","材料與膜性","整合與品質"],"labelsEn":["Thermal reaction and low pressure","Batch and uniformity","Materials and film properties","Integration and quality"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"deposition","subcategoryTitle":"薄膜沉積","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thin-film deposition","stages":[{"id":"a058-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"熱反應與低壓","titleEn":"Thermal reaction and low pressure","description":"LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","descriptionEn":"LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport.","steps":[{"id":"a058-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出進氣、熱區與排氣的流程","titleEn":"Draw inlet, heated zone and exhaust","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氣體歷程會影響基板反應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Gas history affects substrate reaction.","instruction":"畫出進氣、熱區與排氣的流程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「氣體歷程會影響基板反應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw inlet, heated zone and exhaust. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Gas history affects substrate reaction.","observation":"氣體歷程會影響基板反應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Gas history affects substrate reaction. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出進氣、熱區與排氣的流程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氣體歷程會影響基板反應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw inlet, heated zone and exhaust\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Gas history affects substrate reaction.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氣體歷程會影響基板反應。","textEn":"Gas history affects substrate reaction."},{"id":"a058-v8-01-k2","title":"熱反應與低壓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Thermal reaction and low pressure: principle and limits","text":"LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","textEn":"LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出進氣、熱區與排氣的流程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw inlet, heated zone and exhaust\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣體歷程會影響基板反應。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Gas history affects substrate reaction.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","Every batch position is inherently identical."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氣體歷程會影響基板反應。 LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","explanationEn":"Gas history affects substrate reaction. LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}},{"id":"a058-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-01"],"title":"比較反應限制與輸運限制區","titleEn":"Compare reaction-limited and transport-limited regimes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同區域有不同溫度與流量敏感性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Regimes differ in temperature and flow sensitivity.","instruction":"比較反應限制與輸運限制區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「不同區域有不同溫度與流量敏感性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare reaction-limited and transport-limited regimes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Regimes differ in temperature and flow sensitivity.","observation":"不同區域有不同溫度與流量敏感性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Regimes differ in temperature and flow sensitivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較反應限制與輸運限制區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同區域有不同溫度與流量敏感性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare reaction-limited and transport-limited regimes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Regimes differ in temperature and flow sensitivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同區域有不同溫度與流量敏感性。","textEn":"Regimes differ in temperature and flow sensitivity."},{"id":"a058-v8-02-k2","title":"熱反應與低壓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Thermal reaction and low pressure: principle and limits","text":"LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","textEn":"LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較反應限制與輸運限制區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare reaction-limited and transport-limited regimes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","不同區域有不同溫度與流量敏感性。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","Regimes differ in temperature and flow sensitivity.","Every batch position is inherently identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同區域有不同溫度與流量敏感性。 LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","explanationEn":"Regimes differ in temperature and flow sensitivity. LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}},{"id":"a058-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-02"],"title":"用概念 Arrhenius 圖辨識熱活化","titleEn":"Use a conceptual Arrhenius plot to identify activation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：斜率解釋需限於相同反應機制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Slope interpretation requires the same reaction mechanism.","instruction":"用概念 Arrhenius 圖辨識熱活化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「斜率解釋需限於相同反應機制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use a conceptual Arrhenius plot to identify activation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Slope interpretation requires the same reaction mechanism.","observation":"斜率解釋需限於相同反應機制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Slope interpretation requires the same reaction mechanism. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用概念 Arrhenius 圖辨識熱活化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「斜率解釋需限於相同反應機制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use a conceptual Arrhenius plot to identify activation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Slope interpretation requires the same reaction mechanism.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"斜率解釋需限於相同反應機制。","textEn":"Slope interpretation requires the same reaction mechanism."},{"id":"a058-v8-03-k2","title":"熱反應與低壓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Thermal reaction and low pressure: principle and limits","text":"LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","textEn":"LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用概念 Arrhenius 圖辨識熱活化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use a conceptual Arrhenius plot to identify activation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","斜率解釋需限於相同反應機制。"],"optionsEn":["Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","Every batch position is inherently identical.","Slope interpretation requires the same reaction mechanism."],"answer":2,"explanation":"斜率解釋需限於相同反應機制。 LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","explanationEn":"Slope interpretation requires the same reaction mechanism. LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}},{"id":"a058-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-03"],"title":"分開總壓與前驅物分壓","titleEn":"Separate total pressure from precursor partial pressure","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同總壓可能有不同反應物供應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Equal total pressure can have different reactant supply.","instruction":"分開總壓與前驅物分壓。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「相同總壓可能有不同反應物供應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate total pressure from precursor partial pressure. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Equal total pressure can have different reactant supply.","observation":"相同總壓可能有不同反應物供應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Equal total pressure can have different reactant supply. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開總壓與前驅物分壓」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同總壓可能有不同反應物供應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate total pressure from precursor partial pressure\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Equal total pressure can have different reactant supply.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同總壓可能有不同反應物供應。","textEn":"Equal total pressure can have different reactant supply."},{"id":"a058-v8-04-k2","title":"熱反應與低壓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Thermal reaction and low pressure: principle and limits","text":"LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","textEn":"LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開總壓與前驅物分壓」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate total pressure from precursor partial pressure\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同總壓可能有不同反應物供應。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Equal total pressure can have different reactant supply.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","Every batch position is inherently identical."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同總壓可能有不同反應物供應。 LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","explanationEn":"Equal total pressure can have different reactant supply. LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}},{"id":"a058-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-04"],"title":"列出晶圓間距與表面積負載","titleEn":"List wafer spacing and exposed surface load","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：批次裝載會改變耗盡程度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Batch loading changes depletion.","instruction":"列出晶圓間距與表面積負載。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「批次裝載會改變耗盡程度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List wafer spacing and exposed surface load. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Batch loading changes depletion.","observation":"批次裝載會改變耗盡程度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Batch loading changes depletion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出晶圓間距與表面積負載」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「批次裝載會改變耗盡程度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List wafer spacing and exposed surface load\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Batch loading changes depletion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"批次裝載會改變耗盡程度。","textEn":"Batch loading changes depletion."},{"id":"a058-v8-05-k2","title":"熱反應與低壓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Thermal reaction and low pressure: principle and limits","text":"LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","textEn":"LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出晶圓間距與表面積負載」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List wafer spacing and exposed surface load\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","批次裝載會改變耗盡程度。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","Batch loading changes depletion.","Every batch position is inherently identical."],"answer":1,"explanation":"批次裝載會改變耗盡程度。 LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","explanationEn":"Batch loading changes depletion. LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}},{"id":"a058-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-05"],"title":"建立已加工元件的熱預算清單","titleEn":"Build a thermal-budget list for processed devices","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可沉積溫度受前段歷程限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Allowable temperature is constrained by earlier processing.","instruction":"建立已加工元件的熱預算清單。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可沉積溫度受前段歷程限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a thermal-budget list for processed devices. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Allowable temperature is constrained by earlier processing.","observation":"可沉積溫度受前段歷程限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Allowable temperature is constrained by earlier processing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立已加工元件的熱預算清單」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可沉積溫度受前段歷程限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a thermal-budget list for processed devices\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Allowable temperature is constrained by earlier processing.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可沉積溫度受前段歷程限制。","textEn":"Allowable temperature is constrained by earlier processing."},{"id":"a058-v8-06-k2","title":"熱反應與低壓的原理與限制","titleEn":"Thermal reaction and low pressure: principle and limits","text":"LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","textEn":"LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立已加工元件的熱預算清單」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a thermal-budget list for processed devices\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","可沉積溫度受前段歷程限制。"],"optionsEn":["Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","Every batch position is inherently identical.","Allowable temperature is constrained by earlier processing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可沉積溫度受前段歷程限制。 LPCVD 的速率受表面反應與氣體輸運共同限制。","explanationEn":"Allowable temperature is constrained by earlier processing. LPCVD rate is jointly constrained by surface reactions and gas transport."}}]},{"id":"a058-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"批次與均勻性","titleEn":"Batch and uniformity","description":"批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","descriptionEn":"Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity.","steps":[{"id":"a058-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-06"],"title":"規畫沿爐管方向的見證片","titleEn":"Plan witness wafers along the furnace","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：軸向取樣可揭露反應物與溫度梯度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Axial sampling reveals reactant and temperature gradients.","instruction":"規畫沿爐管方向的見證片。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「軸向取樣可揭露反應物與溫度梯度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設三個爐管位置的見證片膜厚為 50、55、60 nm。平均值為 55 nm；本例定義半範圍不均勻度 U=(max-min)/(2mean)=9.09%。若另一批三片皆 55 nm，平均仍相同但 U=0。只用批次平均無法判斷軸向均勻性；三片也不足以證明所有晶圓位置。","instructionEn":"Plan witness wafers along the furnace. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Axial sampling reveals reactant and temperature gradients.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Three hypothetical furnace witness wafers measure 50, 55 and 60 nm. Mean is 55 nm; define half-range nonuniformity U=(max-min)/(2mean)=9.09%. Another batch with three 55 nm values has the same mean but U=0. Batch means cannot establish axial uniformity, and three wafers cannot establish every position.","observation":"軸向取樣可揭露反應物與溫度梯度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 55 nm、9.09% 與取樣限制，明確定義均勻度公式。","observationEn":"Axial sampling reveals reactant and temperature gradients. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 55 nm, 9.09% and sampling limits with the uniformity formula stated.","failure":"若報告假設「同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every batch position is inherently identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「規畫沿爐管方向的見證片」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「軸向取樣可揭露反應物與溫度梯度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 55 nm、9.09% 與取樣限制，明確定義均勻度公式。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plan witness wafers along the furnace\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Axial sampling reveals reactant and temperature gradients.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 55 nm, 9.09% and sampling limits with the uniformity formula stated.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"軸向取樣可揭露反應物與溫度梯度。","textEn":"Axial sampling reveals reactant and temperature gradients."},{"id":"a058-v8-07-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設三個爐管位置的見證片膜厚為 50、55、60 nm。平均值為 55 nm；本例定義半範圍不均勻度 U=(max-min)/(2mean)=9.09%。若另一批三片皆 55 nm，平均仍相同但 U=0。只用批次平均無法判斷軸向均勻性；三片也不足以證明所有晶圓位置。","textEn":"Three hypothetical furnace witness wafers measure 50, 55 and 60 nm. Mean is 55 nm; define half-range nonuniformity U=(max-min)/(2mean)=9.09%. Another batch with three 55 nm values has the same mean but U=0. Batch means cannot establish axial uniformity, and three wafers cannot establish every position."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「規畫沿爐管方向的見證片」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plan witness wafers along the furnace\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["軸向取樣可揭露反應物與溫度梯度。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Axial sampling reveals reactant and temperature gradients.","Every batch position is inherently identical.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"軸向取樣可揭露反應物與溫度梯度。 批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","explanationEn":"Axial sampling reveals reactant and temperature gradients. Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設三個爐管位置的見證片膜厚為 50、55、60 nm。平均值為 55 nm；本例定義半範圍不均勻度 U=(max-min)/(2mean)=9.09%。若另一批三片皆 55 nm，平均仍相同但 U=0。只用批次平均無法判斷軸向均勻性；三片也不足以證明所有晶圓位置。","textEn":"Three hypothetical furnace witness wafers measure 50, 55 and 60 nm. Mean is 55 nm; define half-range nonuniformity U=(max-min)/(2mean)=9.09%. Another batch with three 55 nm values has the same mean but U=0. Batch means cannot establish axial uniformity, and three wafers cannot establish every position.","check":"交付 55 nm、9.09% 與取樣限制，明確定義均勻度公式。","checkEn":"Report 55 nm, 9.09% and sampling limits with the uniformity formula stated."}},{"id":"a058-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-07"],"title":"比較單片中心與邊緣膜厚","titleEn":"Compare within-wafer center and edge thickness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：批間與片內不均勻需分開。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Batch and within-wafer nonuniformity need separation.","instruction":"比較單片中心與邊緣膜厚。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「批間與片內不均勻需分開。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare within-wafer center and edge thickness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Batch and within-wafer nonuniformity need separation.","observation":"批間與片內不均勻需分開。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Batch and within-wafer nonuniformity need separation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every batch position is inherently identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較單片中心與邊緣膜厚」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「批間與片內不均勻需分開。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare within-wafer center and edge thickness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Batch and within-wafer nonuniformity need separation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"批間與片內不均勻需分開。","textEn":"Batch and within-wafer nonuniformity need separation."},{"id":"a058-v8-08-k2","title":"批次與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Batch and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","textEn":"Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較單片中心與邊緣膜厚」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare within-wafer center and edge thickness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","批間與片內不均勻需分開。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every batch position is inherently identical.","Batch and within-wafer nonuniformity need separation.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"批間與片內不均勻需分開。 批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","explanationEn":"Batch and within-wafer nonuniformity need separation. Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}},{"id":"a058-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-08"],"title":"檢查入氣端到出氣端的耗盡","titleEn":"Inspect depletion from inlet to outlet","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：上游沉積會改變下游供應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Upstream deposition changes downstream supply.","instruction":"檢查入氣端到出氣端的耗盡。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「上游沉積會改變下游供應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect depletion from inlet to outlet. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Upstream deposition changes downstream supply.","observation":"上游沉積會改變下游供應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Upstream deposition changes downstream supply. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every batch position is inherently identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查入氣端到出氣端的耗盡」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「上游沉積會改變下游供應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect depletion from inlet to outlet\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Upstream deposition changes downstream supply.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"上游沉積會改變下游供應。","textEn":"Upstream deposition changes downstream supply."},{"id":"a058-v8-09-k2","title":"批次與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Batch and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","textEn":"Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查入氣端到出氣端的耗盡」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect depletion from inlet to outlet\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","上游沉積會改變下游供應。"],"optionsEn":["Every batch position is inherently identical.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","Upstream deposition changes downstream supply."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上游沉積會改變下游供應。 批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","explanationEn":"Upstream deposition changes downstream supply. Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}},{"id":"a058-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-09"],"title":"以空載與滿載假設比較成膜","titleEn":"Compare hypothetical lightly and fully loaded growth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：裝載差異需要一致的對照條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Loading differences require controlled comparisons.","instruction":"以空載與滿載假設比較成膜。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「裝載差異需要一致的對照條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical lightly and fully loaded growth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Loading differences require controlled comparisons.","observation":"裝載差異需要一致的對照條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Loading differences require controlled comparisons. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every batch position is inherently identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以空載與滿載假設比較成膜」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「裝載差異需要一致的對照條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare hypothetical lightly and fully loaded growth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Loading differences require controlled comparisons.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"裝載差異需要一致的對照條件。","textEn":"Loading differences require controlled comparisons."},{"id":"a058-v8-10-k2","title":"批次與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Batch and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","textEn":"Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以空載與滿載假設比較成膜」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare hypothetical lightly and fully loaded growth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["裝載差異需要一致的對照條件。","同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Loading differences require controlled comparisons.","Every batch position is inherently identical.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"裝載差異需要一致的對照條件。 批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","explanationEn":"Loading differences require controlled comparisons. Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}},{"id":"a058-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-10"],"title":"追蹤爐管清潔前後的膜厚變化","titleEn":"Track thickness around tube cleaning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：管壁狀態可改變再現性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Tube-wall state can alter repeatability.","instruction":"追蹤爐管清潔前後的膜厚變化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「管壁狀態可改變再現性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track thickness around tube cleaning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Tube-wall state can alter repeatability.","observation":"管壁狀態可改變再現性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Tube-wall state can alter repeatability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every batch position is inherently identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤爐管清潔前後的膜厚變化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「管壁狀態可改變再現性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track thickness around tube cleaning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Tube-wall state can alter repeatability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"管壁狀態可改變再現性。","textEn":"Tube-wall state can alter repeatability."},{"id":"a058-v8-11-k2","title":"批次與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Batch and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","textEn":"Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤爐管清潔前後的膜厚變化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track thickness around tube cleaning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","管壁狀態可改變再現性。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every batch position is inherently identical.","Tube-wall state can alter repeatability.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管壁狀態可改變再現性。 批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","explanationEn":"Tube-wall state can alter repeatability. Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}},{"id":"a058-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-11"],"title":"比較升溫與穩溫階段的貢獻","titleEn":"Compare ramp and soak contributions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：有效熱史不只有名目沉積時間。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Effective thermal history extends beyond nominal deposition time.","instruction":"比較升溫與穩溫階段的貢獻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「有效熱史不只有名目沉積時間。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare ramp and soak contributions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Effective thermal history extends beyond nominal deposition time.","observation":"有效熱史不只有名目沉積時間。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Effective thermal history extends beyond nominal deposition time. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every batch position is inherently identical.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較升溫與穩溫階段的貢獻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「有效熱史不只有名目沉積時間。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare ramp and soak contributions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Effective thermal history extends beyond nominal deposition time.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"有效熱史不只有名目沉積時間。","textEn":"Effective thermal history extends beyond nominal deposition time."},{"id":"a058-v8-12-k2","title":"批次與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Batch and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","textEn":"Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較升溫與穩溫階段的貢獻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare ramp and soak contributions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["同一批次所有位置自然完全相同。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","有效熱史不只有名目沉積時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every batch position is inherently identical.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","Effective thermal history extends beyond nominal deposition time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"有效熱史不只有名目沉積時間。 批次位置、溫度分布與前驅物耗盡會造成不均勻。","explanationEn":"Effective thermal history extends beyond nominal deposition time. Batch position, temperature distribution and precursor depletion cause nonuniformity."}}]},{"id":"a058-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"材料與膜性","titleEn":"Materials and film properties","description":"不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","descriptionEn":"Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements.","steps":[{"id":"a058-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-12"],"title":"比較非晶矽與多晶矽的結構證據","titleEn":"Compare evidence for amorphous and polycrystalline silicon","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同元素不代表相同微結構。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The same element does not imply the same microstructure.","instruction":"比較非晶矽與多晶矽的結構證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「相同元素不代表相同微結構。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare evidence for amorphous and polycrystalline silicon. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: The same element does not imply the same microstructure.","observation":"相同元素不代表相同微結構。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The same element does not imply the same microstructure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較非晶矽與多晶矽的結構證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同元素不代表相同微結構。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare evidence for amorphous and polycrystalline silicon\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The same element does not imply the same microstructure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同元素不代表相同微結構。","textEn":"The same element does not imply the same microstructure."},{"id":"a058-v8-13-k2","title":"材料與膜性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and film properties: principle and limits","text":"不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","textEn":"Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較非晶矽與多晶矽的結構證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare evidence for amorphous and polycrystalline silicon\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同元素不代表相同微結構。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。"],"optionsEn":["The same element does not imply the same microstructure.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同元素不代表相同微結構。 不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","explanationEn":"The same element does not imply the same microstructure. Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}},{"id":"a058-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-13"],"title":"分開化學計量氮化矽與低應力氮化矽","titleEn":"Distinguish stoichiometric and low-stress silicon nitride","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低應力命名不保證所有膜性一致。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A low-stress label does not guarantee identical properties.","instruction":"分開化學計量氮化矽與低應力氮化矽。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「低應力命名不保證所有膜性一致。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish stoichiometric and low-stress silicon nitride. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: A low-stress label does not guarantee identical properties.","observation":"低應力命名不保證所有膜性一致。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A low-stress label does not guarantee identical properties. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開化學計量氮化矽與低應力氮化矽」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低應力命名不保證所有膜性一致。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish stoichiometric and low-stress silicon nitride\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A low-stress label does not guarantee identical properties.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低應力命名不保證所有膜性一致。","textEn":"A low-stress label does not guarantee identical properties."},{"id":"a058-v8-14-k2","title":"材料與膜性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and film properties: principle and limits","text":"不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","textEn":"Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開化學計量氮化矽與低應力氮化矽」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish stoichiometric and low-stress silicon nitride\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","低應力命名不保證所有膜性一致。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。"],"optionsEn":["Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","A low-stress label does not guarantee identical properties.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低應力命名不保證所有膜性一致。 不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","explanationEn":"A low-stress label does not guarantee identical properties. Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}},{"id":"a058-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-14"],"title":"比較 LTO 與其他氧化層的整合用途","titleEn":"Compare LTO with other oxide uses","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：成膜方式會影響密度、雜質與熱史。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Growth method affects density, impurities and thermal history.","instruction":"比較 LTO 與其他氧化層的整合用途。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「成膜方式會影響密度、雜質與熱史。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare LTO with other oxide uses. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Growth method affects density, impurities and thermal history.","observation":"成膜方式會影響密度、雜質與熱史。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Growth method affects density, impurities and thermal history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 LTO 與其他氧化層的整合用途」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「成膜方式會影響密度、雜質與熱史。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare LTO with other oxide uses\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Growth method affects density, impurities and thermal history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"成膜方式會影響密度、雜質與熱史。","textEn":"Growth method affects density, impurities and thermal history."},{"id":"a058-v8-15-k2","title":"材料與膜性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and film properties: principle and limits","text":"不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","textEn":"Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 LTO 與其他氧化層的整合用途」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare LTO with other oxide uses\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","成膜方式會影響密度、雜質與熱史。"],"optionsEn":["Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","Growth method affects density, impurities and thermal history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"成膜方式會影響密度、雜質與熱史。 不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","explanationEn":"Growth method affects density, impurities and thermal history. Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}},{"id":"a058-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-15"],"title":"量測膜厚、折射率與化學鍵結","titleEn":"Measure thickness, index and chemical bonds","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多種量測可減少單一模型歧義。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Multiple measurements reduce single-model ambiguity.","instruction":"量測膜厚、折射率與化學鍵結。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「多種量測可減少單一模型歧義。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure thickness, index and chemical bonds. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Multiple measurements reduce single-model ambiguity.","observation":"多種量測可減少單一模型歧義。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Multiple measurements reduce single-model ambiguity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測膜厚、折射率與化學鍵結」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多種量測可減少單一模型歧義。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure thickness, index and chemical bonds\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Multiple measurements reduce single-model ambiguity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多種量測可減少單一模型歧義。","textEn":"Multiple measurements reduce single-model ambiguity."},{"id":"a058-v8-16-k2","title":"材料與膜性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and film properties: principle and limits","text":"不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","textEn":"Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測膜厚、折射率與化學鍵結」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure thickness, index and chemical bonds\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["多種量測可減少單一模型歧義。","所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。"],"optionsEn":["Multiple measurements reduce single-model ambiguity.","Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多種量測可減少單一模型歧義。 不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","explanationEn":"Multiple measurements reduce single-model ambiguity. Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}},{"id":"a058-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-16"],"title":"由曲率變化估算應力符號","titleEn":"Infer stress sign from curvature change","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：應力估算依賴基板與薄膜假設。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Stress estimation depends on substrate and film assumptions.","instruction":"由曲率變化估算應力符號。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「應力估算依賴基板與薄膜假設。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Infer stress sign from curvature change. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Stress estimation depends on substrate and film assumptions.","observation":"應力估算依賴基板與薄膜假設。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Stress estimation depends on substrate and film assumptions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「由曲率變化估算應力符號」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「應力估算依賴基板與薄膜假設。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Infer stress sign from curvature change\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Stress estimation depends on substrate and film assumptions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"應力估算依賴基板與薄膜假設。","textEn":"Stress estimation depends on substrate and film assumptions."},{"id":"a058-v8-17-k2","title":"材料與膜性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and film properties: principle and limits","text":"不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","textEn":"Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「由曲率變化估算應力符號」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Infer stress sign from curvature change\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","應力估算依賴基板與薄膜假設。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。"],"optionsEn":["Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","Stress estimation depends on substrate and film assumptions.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應力估算依賴基板與薄膜假設。 不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","explanationEn":"Stress estimation depends on substrate and film assumptions. Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}},{"id":"a058-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-17"],"title":"檢查厚膜裂紋與邊緣剝離","titleEn":"Inspect thick-film cracks and edge delamination","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：累積應力能量可能超過介面耐受。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Accumulated strain energy can exceed interface resistance.","instruction":"檢查厚膜裂紋與邊緣剝離。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「累積應力能量可能超過介面耐受。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect thick-film cracks and edge delamination. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Accumulated strain energy can exceed interface resistance.","observation":"累積應力能量可能超過介面耐受。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Accumulated strain energy can exceed interface resistance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查厚膜裂紋與邊緣剝離」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「累積應力能量可能超過介面耐受。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect thick-film cracks and edge delamination\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Accumulated strain energy can exceed interface resistance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"累積應力能量可能超過介面耐受。","textEn":"Accumulated strain energy can exceed interface resistance."},{"id":"a058-v8-18-k2","title":"材料與膜性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Materials and film properties: principle and limits","text":"不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","textEn":"Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查厚膜裂紋與邊緣剝離」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect thick-film cracks and edge delamination\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有 LPCVD 膜都具有相同低應力。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","累積應力能量可能超過介面耐受。"],"optionsEn":["Every LPCVD film has the same low stress.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","Accumulated strain energy can exceed interface resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"累積應力能量可能超過介面耐受。 不同 LPCVD 材料有不同結構、應力與熱預算要求。","explanationEn":"Accumulated strain energy can exceed interface resistance. Different LPCVD materials have different structure, stress and thermal-budget requirements."}}]},{"id":"a058-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合與品質","titleEn":"Integration and quality","description":"高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","descriptionEn":"High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals.","steps":[{"id":"a058-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-18"],"title":"評估側壁覆蓋與狹窄溝槽封口","titleEn":"Assess sidewall coverage and trench pinch-off","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共形沉積仍可能封口留下空洞。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Conformal growth can still pinch off and leave voids.","instruction":"評估側壁覆蓋與狹窄溝槽封口。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「共形沉積仍可能封口留下空洞。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess sidewall coverage and trench pinch-off. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Conformal growth can still pinch off and leave voids.","observation":"共形沉積仍可能封口留下空洞。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Conformal growth can still pinch off and leave voids. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估側壁覆蓋與狹窄溝槽封口」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共形沉積仍可能封口留下空洞。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess sidewall coverage and trench pinch-off\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Conformal growth can still pinch off and leave voids.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共形沉積仍可能封口留下空洞。","textEn":"Conformal growth can still pinch off and leave voids."},{"id":"a058-v8-19-k2","title":"整合與品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and quality: principle and limits","text":"高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","textEn":"High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估側壁覆蓋與狹窄溝槽封口」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess sidewall coverage and trench pinch-off\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["共形沉積仍可能封口留下空洞。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。"],"optionsEn":["Conformal growth can still pinch off and leave voids.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"共形沉積仍可能封口留下空洞。 高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","explanationEn":"Conformal growth can still pinch off and leave voids. High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}},{"id":"a058-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-19"],"title":"比較沉積前後的摻雜分布需求","titleEn":"Assess dopant-profile constraints before and after growth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：高溫可能改變摻雜擴散。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: High temperature can alter dopant diffusion.","instruction":"比較沉積前後的摻雜分布需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「高溫可能改變摻雜擴散。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess dopant-profile constraints before and after growth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: High temperature can alter dopant diffusion.","observation":"高溫可能改變摻雜擴散。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"High temperature can alter dopant diffusion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較沉積前後的摻雜分布需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「高溫可能改變摻雜擴散。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess dopant-profile constraints before and after growth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"High temperature can alter dopant diffusion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"高溫可能改變摻雜擴散。","textEn":"High temperature can alter dopant diffusion."},{"id":"a058-v8-20-k2","title":"整合與品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and quality: principle and limits","text":"高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","textEn":"High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較沉積前後的摻雜分布需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess dopant-profile constraints before and after growth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","高溫可能改變摻雜擴散。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。"],"optionsEn":["Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","High temperature can alter dopant diffusion.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高溫可能改變摻雜擴散。 高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","explanationEn":"High temperature can alter dopant diffusion. High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}},{"id":"a058-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-20"],"title":"檢查既有金屬的材料相容性","titleEn":"Check compatibility of existing metals","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共用爐管通常有嚴格材料限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Shared furnaces commonly have strict material restrictions.","instruction":"檢查既有金屬的材料相容性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「共用爐管通常有嚴格材料限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check compatibility of existing metals. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Shared furnaces commonly have strict material restrictions.","observation":"共用爐管通常有嚴格材料限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Shared furnaces commonly have strict material restrictions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查既有金屬的材料相容性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共用爐管通常有嚴格材料限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check compatibility of existing metals\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Shared furnaces commonly have strict material restrictions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共用爐管通常有嚴格材料限制。","textEn":"Shared furnaces commonly have strict material restrictions."},{"id":"a058-v8-21-k2","title":"整合與品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and quality: principle and limits","text":"高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","textEn":"High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查既有金屬的材料相容性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check compatibility of existing metals\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","共用爐管通常有嚴格材料限制。"],"optionsEn":["Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","Shared furnaces commonly have strict material restrictions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共用爐管通常有嚴格材料限制。 高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","explanationEn":"Shared furnaces commonly have strict material restrictions. High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}},{"id":"a058-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-21"],"title":"以電性載具驗證介電或導電用途","titleEn":"Verify insulating or conducting function electrically","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：外觀均勻不代表功能符合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Uniform appearance does not establish function.","instruction":"以電性載具驗證介電或導電用途。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「外觀均勻不代表功能符合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Verify insulating or conducting function electrically. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Uniform appearance does not establish function.","observation":"外觀均勻不代表功能符合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Uniform appearance does not establish function. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以電性載具驗證介電或導電用途」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「外觀均勻不代表功能符合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Verify insulating or conducting function electrically\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Uniform appearance does not establish function.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"外觀均勻不代表功能符合。","textEn":"Uniform appearance does not establish function."},{"id":"a058-v8-22-k2","title":"整合與品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and quality: principle and limits","text":"高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","textEn":"High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以電性載具驗證介電或導電用途」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Verify insulating or conducting function electrically\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["外觀均勻不代表功能符合。","膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform appearance does not establish function.","Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外觀均勻不代表功能符合。 高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","explanationEn":"Uniform appearance does not establish function. High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}},{"id":"a058-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-22"],"title":"建立批次位置與最終良率對照","titleEn":"Relate batch position to final yield","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：位置相關性可提供製程來源線索。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Position dependence can identify process-origin clues.","instruction":"建立批次位置與最終良率對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「位置相關性可提供製程來源線索。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate batch position to final yield. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Position dependence can identify process-origin clues.","observation":"位置相關性可提供製程來源線索。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Position dependence can identify process-origin clues. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立批次位置與最終良率對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「位置相關性可提供製程來源線索。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate batch position to final yield\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Position dependence can identify process-origin clues.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"位置相關性可提供製程來源線索。","textEn":"Position dependence can identify process-origin clues."},{"id":"a058-v8-23-k2","title":"整合與品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and quality: principle and limits","text":"高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","textEn":"High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立批次位置與最終良率對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate batch position to final yield\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","位置相關性可提供製程來源線索。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。"],"optionsEn":["Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","Position dependence can identify process-origin clues.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate."],"answer":1,"explanation":"位置相關性可提供製程來源線索。 高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","explanationEn":"Position dependence can identify process-origin clues. High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}},{"id":"a058-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lpcvd","v8b-nistpoly","v8b-nistnitride","v8b-nistlto"],"prerequisiteIds":["a058-v8-23"],"title":"交付熱史、均勻性與材料驗收","titleEn":"Deliver thermal history, uniformity and material acceptance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：LPCVD 需將批次管理納入整合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: LPCVD integration must include batch management.","instruction":"交付熱史、均勻性與材料驗收。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「LPCVD 需將批次管理納入整合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver thermal history, uniformity and material acceptance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: LPCVD integration must include batch management.","observation":"LPCVD 需將批次管理納入整合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"LPCVD integration must include batch management. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付熱史、均勻性與材料驗收」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「LPCVD 需將批次管理納入整合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver thermal history, uniformity and material acceptance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"LPCVD integration must include batch management.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a058-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"LPCVD 需將批次管理納入整合。","textEn":"LPCVD integration must include batch management."},{"id":"a058-v8-24-k2","title":"整合與品質的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration and quality: principle and limits","text":"高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","textEn":"High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付熱史、均勻性與材料驗收」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver thermal history, uniformity and material acceptance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["膜質好就可以忽略元件熱預算。","降低壓力必定增加所有材料的沉積速率。","LPCVD 需將批次管理納入整合。"],"optionsEn":["Good film quality removes device thermal-budget concerns.","Lower pressure necessarily increases every deposition rate.","LPCVD integration must include batch management."],"answer":2,"explanation":"LPCVD 需將批次管理納入整合。 高溫成膜必須與已有元件、摻雜及金屬相容。","explanationEn":"LPCVD integration must include batch management. High-temperature growth must remain compatible with existing devices, dopants and metals."}}]}]},{"id":"a059","title":"金屬有機化學氣相沉積","titleEn":"Metal-organic chemical vapor deposition","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究前驅物與磊晶、反應器與均勻性、結構與光電性、界面與整合；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: precursors and epitaxy, reactor and uniformity, structure and optoelectronics, interfaces and integration. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["前驅物與磊晶","反應器與均勻性","結構與光電性","界面與整合"],"labelsEn":["Precursors and epitaxy","Reactor and uniformity","Structure and optoelectronics","Interfaces and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"deposition","subcategoryTitle":"薄膜沉積","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thin-film deposition","stages":[{"id":"a059-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"前驅物與磊晶","titleEn":"Precursors and epitaxy","description":"MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","descriptionEn":"MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization.","steps":[{"id":"a059-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出金屬有機源到晶體薄膜的路徑","titleEn":"Trace metal-organic sources into crystalline films","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氣相分解與表面反應不是同一階段。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Gas decomposition and surface reaction are different stages.","instruction":"畫出金屬有機源到晶體薄膜的路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「氣相分解與表面反應不是同一階段。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace metal-organic sources into crystalline films. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Gas decomposition and surface reaction are different stages.","observation":"氣相分解與表面反應不是同一階段。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Gas decomposition and surface reaction are different stages. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出金屬有機源到晶體薄膜的路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氣相分解與表面反應不是同一階段。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace metal-organic sources into crystalline films\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Gas decomposition and surface reaction are different stages.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氣相分解與表面反應不是同一階段。","textEn":"Gas decomposition and surface reaction are different stages."},{"id":"a059-v8-01-k2","title":"前驅物與磊晶的原理與限制","titleEn":"Precursors and epitaxy: principle and limits","text":"MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","textEn":"MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出金屬有機源到晶體薄膜的路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace metal-organic sources into crystalline films\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣相分解與表面反應不是同一階段。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Gas decomposition and surface reaction are different stages.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氣相分解與表面反應不是同一階段。 MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","explanationEn":"Gas decomposition and surface reaction are different stages. MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}},{"id":"a059-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-01"],"title":"區分同質與異質磊晶","titleEn":"Distinguish homoepitaxy from heteroepitaxy","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：基板與薄膜晶格關系影響缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Film–substrate lattice relations affect defects.","instruction":"區分同質與異質磊晶。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「基板與薄膜晶格關系影響缺陷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish homoepitaxy from heteroepitaxy. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Film–substrate lattice relations affect defects.","observation":"基板與薄膜晶格關系影響缺陷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Film–substrate lattice relations affect defects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分同質與異質磊晶」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「基板與薄膜晶格關系影響缺陷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish homoepitaxy from heteroepitaxy\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Film–substrate lattice relations affect defects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"基板與薄膜晶格關系影響缺陷。","textEn":"Film–substrate lattice relations affect defects."},{"id":"a059-v8-02-k2","title":"前驅物與磊晶的原理與限制","titleEn":"Precursors and epitaxy: principle and limits","text":"MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","textEn":"MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分同質與異質磊晶」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish homoepitaxy from heteroepitaxy\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","基板與薄膜晶格關系影響缺陷。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Film–substrate lattice relations affect defects.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"基板與薄膜晶格關系影響缺陷。 MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","explanationEn":"Film–substrate lattice relations affect defects. MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}},{"id":"a059-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-02"],"title":"比較 III–V 材料不同元素來源的角色","titleEn":"Compare precursor roles in III–V materials","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：元素供應比不直接等於固體組成比。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Supply ratio does not directly equal solid composition.","instruction":"比較 III–V 材料不同元素來源的角色。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「元素供應比不直接等於固體組成比。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare precursor roles in III–V materials. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Supply ratio does not directly equal solid composition.","observation":"元素供應比不直接等於固體組成比。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Supply ratio does not directly equal solid composition. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 III–V 材料不同元素來源的角色」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「元素供應比不直接等於固體組成比。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare precursor roles in III–V materials\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Supply ratio does not directly equal solid composition.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"元素供應比不直接等於固體組成比。","textEn":"Supply ratio does not directly equal solid composition."},{"id":"a059-v8-03-k2","title":"前驅物與磊晶的原理與限制","titleEn":"Precursors and epitaxy: principle and limits","text":"MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","textEn":"MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 III–V 材料不同元素來源的角色」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare precursor roles in III–V materials\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","元素供應比不直接等於固體組成比。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Supply ratio does not directly equal solid composition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"元素供應比不直接等於固體組成比。 MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","explanationEn":"Supply ratio does not directly equal solid composition. MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}},{"id":"a059-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-03"],"title":"繪製反應限制與輸運限制示意","titleEn":"Sketch reaction- and transport-limited regimes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：速率控制機制可隨條件改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Rate-control mechanisms can change with conditions.","instruction":"繪製反應限制與輸運限制示意。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「速率控制機制可隨條件改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch reaction- and transport-limited regimes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Rate-control mechanisms can change with conditions.","observation":"速率控制機制可隨條件改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Rate-control mechanisms can change with conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製反應限制與輸運限制示意」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「速率控制機制可隨條件改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch reaction- and transport-limited regimes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Rate-control mechanisms can change with conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"速率控制機制可隨條件改變。","textEn":"Rate-control mechanisms can change with conditions."},{"id":"a059-v8-04-k2","title":"前驅物與磊晶的原理與限制","titleEn":"Precursors and epitaxy: principle and limits","text":"MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","textEn":"MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製反應限制與輸運限制示意」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch reaction- and transport-limited regimes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["速率控制機制可隨條件改變。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Rate-control mechanisms can change with conditions.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers."],"answer":0,"explanation":"速率控制機制可隨條件改變。 MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","explanationEn":"Rate-control mechanisms can change with conditions. MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}},{"id":"a059-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-04"],"title":"標記氣體隔離、監測與排放介面","titleEn":"Mark gas isolation, monitoring and exhaust interfaces","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反應器分析需包含設施介面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reactor analysis must include facility interfaces.","instruction":"標記氣體隔離、監測與排放介面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「反應器分析需包含設施介面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark gas isolation, monitoring and exhaust interfaces. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reactor analysis must include facility interfaces.","observation":"反應器分析需包含設施介面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reactor analysis must include facility interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記氣體隔離、監測與排放介面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反應器分析需包含設施介面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark gas isolation, monitoring and exhaust interfaces\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reactor analysis must include facility interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反應器分析需包含設施介面。","textEn":"Reactor analysis must include facility interfaces."},{"id":"a059-v8-05-k2","title":"前驅物與磊晶的原理與限制","titleEn":"Precursors and epitaxy: principle and limits","text":"MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","textEn":"MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記氣體隔離、監測與排放介面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark gas isolation, monitoring and exhaust interfaces\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","反應器分析需包含設施介面。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Reactor analysis must include facility interfaces.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反應器分析需包含設施介面。 MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","explanationEn":"Reactor analysis must include facility interfaces. MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}},{"id":"a059-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-05"],"title":"建立不含操作配方的材料需求表","titleEn":"Build a material-requirement table without recipes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：公開材料目標與現場操作授權不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Public material targets differ from operational authorization.","instruction":"建立不含操作配方的材料需求表。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「公開材料目標與現場操作授權不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build a material-requirement table without recipes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Public material targets differ from operational authorization.","observation":"公開材料目標與現場操作授權不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Public material targets differ from operational authorization. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立不含操作配方的材料需求表」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「公開材料目標與現場操作授權不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a material-requirement table without recipes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Public material targets differ from operational authorization.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"公開材料目標與現場操作授權不同。","textEn":"Public material targets differ from operational authorization."},{"id":"a059-v8-06-k2","title":"前驅物與磊晶的原理與限制","titleEn":"Precursors and epitaxy: principle and limits","text":"MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","textEn":"MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立不含操作配方的材料需求表」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a material-requirement table without recipes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","公開材料目標與現場操作授權不同。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Public material targets differ from operational authorization."],"answer":2,"explanation":"公開材料目標與現場操作授權不同。 MOCVD 的氣相輸運、前驅物分解與表面結晶須共同分析。","explanationEn":"Public material targets differ from operational authorization. MOCVD requires joint analysis of gas transport, precursor decomposition and surface crystallization."}}]},{"id":"a059-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"反應器與均勻性","titleEn":"Reactor and uniformity","description":"反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","descriptionEn":"Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness.","steps":[{"id":"a059-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-06"],"title":"比較行星式與近距離淋浴式反應器","titleEn":"Compare planetary and close-coupled showerhead reactors","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氣體導入與基板運動方式不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Gas delivery and substrate motion differ.","instruction":"比較行星式與近距離淋浴式反應器。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「氣體導入與基板運動方式不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare planetary and close-coupled showerhead reactors. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Gas delivery and substrate motion differ.","observation":"氣體導入與基板運動方式不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Gas delivery and substrate motion differ. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較行星式與近距離淋浴式反應器」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氣體導入與基板運動方式不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare planetary and close-coupled showerhead reactors\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Gas delivery and substrate motion differ.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氣體導入與基板運動方式不同。","textEn":"Gas delivery and substrate motion differ."},{"id":"a059-v8-07-k2","title":"反應器與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reactor and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","textEn":"Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較行星式與近距離淋浴式反應器」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare planetary and close-coupled showerhead reactors\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣體導入與基板運動方式不同。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Gas delivery and substrate motion differ.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氣體導入與基板運動方式不同。 反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","explanationEn":"Gas delivery and substrate motion differ. Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}},{"id":"a059-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-07"],"title":"畫出邊界層與表面物種耗盡","titleEn":"Sketch boundary layers and surface-species depletion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面供應不等於入口濃度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Surface supply differs from inlet concentration.","instruction":"畫出邊界層與表面物種耗盡。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「表面供應不等於入口濃度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch boundary layers and surface-species depletion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Surface supply differs from inlet concentration.","observation":"表面供應不等於入口濃度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Surface supply differs from inlet concentration. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出邊界層與表面物種耗盡」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面供應不等於入口濃度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch boundary layers and surface-species depletion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Surface supply differs from inlet concentration.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面供應不等於入口濃度。","textEn":"Surface supply differs from inlet concentration."},{"id":"a059-v8-08-k2","title":"反應器與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reactor and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","textEn":"Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出邊界層與表面物種耗盡」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch boundary layers and surface-species depletion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","表面供應不等於入口濃度。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Surface supply differs from inlet concentration.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面供應不等於入口濃度。 反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","explanationEn":"Surface supply differs from inlet concentration. Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}},{"id":"a059-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-08"],"title":"檢查晶圓溫度與載盤溫度差","titleEn":"Assess wafer–susceptor temperature differences","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：控制器溫度不必然等於表面溫度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Controller temperature need not equal surface temperature.","instruction":"檢查晶圓溫度與載盤溫度差。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「控制器溫度不必然等於表面溫度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess wafer–susceptor temperature differences. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Controller temperature need not equal surface temperature.","observation":"控制器溫度不必然等於表面溫度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Controller temperature need not equal surface temperature. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查晶圓溫度與載盤溫度差」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「控制器溫度不必然等於表面溫度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess wafer–susceptor temperature differences\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Controller temperature need not equal surface temperature.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"控制器溫度不必然等於表面溫度。","textEn":"Controller temperature need not equal surface temperature."},{"id":"a059-v8-09-k2","title":"反應器與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reactor and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","textEn":"Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查晶圓溫度與載盤溫度差」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess wafer–susceptor temperature differences\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","控制器溫度不必然等於表面溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","Controller temperature need not equal surface temperature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制器溫度不必然等於表面溫度。 反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","explanationEn":"Controller temperature need not equal surface temperature. Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}},{"id":"a059-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-09"],"title":"比較中心與邊緣的成分地圖","titleEn":"Compare center-to-edge composition maps","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：厚度均勻不保證成分均勻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thickness uniformity does not guarantee composition uniformity.","instruction":"比較中心與邊緣的成分地圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「厚度均勻不保證成分均勻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare center-to-edge composition maps. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thickness uniformity does not guarantee composition uniformity.","observation":"厚度均勻不保證成分均勻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thickness uniformity does not guarantee composition uniformity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較中心與邊緣的成分地圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「厚度均勻不保證成分均勻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare center-to-edge composition maps\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thickness uniformity does not guarantee composition uniformity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"厚度均勻不保證成分均勻。","textEn":"Thickness uniformity does not guarantee composition uniformity."},{"id":"a059-v8-10-k2","title":"反應器與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reactor and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","textEn":"Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較中心與邊緣的成分地圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare center-to-edge composition maps\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["厚度均勻不保證成分均勻。","每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Thickness uniformity does not guarantee composition uniformity.","Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality."],"answer":0,"explanation":"厚度均勻不保證成分均勻。 反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","explanationEn":"Thickness uniformity does not guarantee composition uniformity. Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}},{"id":"a059-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-10"],"title":"分析晶圓翹曲對熱接觸的影響","titleEn":"Analyze bow effects on thermal contact","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：翹曲可改變溫度與成長分布。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bow can alter temperature and growth distribution.","instruction":"分析晶圓翹曲對熱接觸的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「翹曲可改變溫度與成長分布。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Analyze bow effects on thermal contact. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bow can alter temperature and growth distribution.","observation":"翹曲可改變溫度與成長分布。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bow can alter temperature and growth distribution. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分析晶圓翹曲對熱接觸的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「翹曲可改變溫度與成長分布。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Analyze bow effects on thermal contact\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bow can alter temperature and growth distribution.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"翹曲可改變溫度與成長分布。","textEn":"Bow can alter temperature and growth distribution."},{"id":"a059-v8-11-k2","title":"反應器與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reactor and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","textEn":"Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分析晶圓翹曲對熱接觸的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Analyze bow effects on thermal contact\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","翹曲可改變溫度與成長分布。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Bow can alter temperature and growth distribution.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"翹曲可改變溫度與成長分布。 反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","explanationEn":"Bow can alter temperature and growth distribution. Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}},{"id":"a059-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-11"],"title":"以見證片追蹤反應器歷程","titleEn":"Use witness samples to track reactor history","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：腔壁沉積可能帶來記憶效應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Wall deposits can create memory effects.","instruction":"以見證片追蹤反應器歷程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「腔壁沉積可能帶來記憶效應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use witness samples to track reactor history. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Wall deposits can create memory effects.","observation":"腔壁沉積可能帶來記憶效應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Wall deposits can create memory effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以見證片追蹤反應器歷程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「腔壁沉積可能帶來記憶效應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use witness samples to track reactor history\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Wall deposits can create memory effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"腔壁沉積可能帶來記憶效應。","textEn":"Wall deposits can create memory effects."},{"id":"a059-v8-12-k2","title":"反應器與均勻性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reactor and uniformity: principle and limits","text":"反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","textEn":"Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以見證片追蹤反應器歷程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use witness samples to track reactor history\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["每片晶圓只需相同轉速即可均勻。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","腔壁沉積可能帶來記憶效應。"],"optionsEn":["Equal rotation speed alone ensures uniform wafers.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","Wall deposits can create memory effects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"腔壁沉積可能帶來記憶效應。 反應器流場與溫度場共同影響成分與厚度。","explanationEn":"Wall deposits can create memory effects. Reactor flow and temperature jointly affect composition and thickness."}}]},{"id":"a059-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"結構與光電性","titleEn":"Structure and optoelectronics","description":"厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","descriptionEn":"Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior.","steps":[{"id":"a059-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-12"],"title":"用 XRD 概念分開晶格常數與應變","titleEn":"Use XRD concepts to distinguish lattice parameter and strain","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：峰位改變可能有多種來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Peak shifts can have multiple origins.","instruction":"用 XRD 概念分開晶格常數與應變。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「峰位改變可能有多種來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use XRD concepts to distinguish lattice parameter and strain. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Peak shifts can have multiple origins.","observation":"峰位改變可能有多種來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Peak shifts can have multiple origins. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用 XRD 概念分開晶格常數與應變」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「峰位改變可能有多種來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use XRD concepts to distinguish lattice parameter and strain\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Peak shifts can have multiple origins.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"峰位改變可能有多種來源。","textEn":"Peak shifts can have multiple origins."},{"id":"a059-v8-13-k2","title":"結構與光電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Structure and optoelectronics: principle and limits","text":"厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","textEn":"Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用 XRD 概念分開晶格常數與應變」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use XRD concepts to distinguish lattice parameter and strain\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["峰位改變可能有多種來源。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。"],"optionsEn":["Peak shifts can have multiple origins.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor."],"answer":0,"explanation":"峰位改變可能有多種來源。 厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","explanationEn":"Peak shifts can have multiple origins. Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}},{"id":"a059-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-13"],"title":"比較光激發光峰位與線寬","titleEn":"Compare photoluminescence peak position and width","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：光譜需要結合厚度、成分與缺陷解釋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Spectra need interpretation with thickness, composition and defects.","instruction":"比較光激發光峰位與線寬。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「光譜需要結合厚度、成分與缺陷解釋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設兩片磊晶樣品的 PL 峰位為 450 與 460 nm，以 E≈1240/λ(nm) eV 換算為 2.756 與 2.696 eV，能量下降約 0.060 eV。這個紅移可能牽涉組成、應變、溫度或量子井厚度，不能只由峰位反推唯一材料組成；提出 XRD 或厚度對照以區分。","instructionEn":"Compare photoluminescence peak position and width. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Spectra need interpretation with thickness, composition and defects.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Hypothetical epitaxial samples have PL peaks at 450 and 460 nm. E≈1240/λ(nm) eV gives 2.756 and 2.696 eV, a decrease of about 0.060 eV. Composition, strain, temperature or well thickness can cause such a redshift; peak position alone cannot uniquely determine composition. Propose XRD or thickness controls to distinguish causes.","observation":"光譜需要結合厚度、成分與缺陷解釋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n算出約 60 meV 紅移，並保留至少兩種可能原因。","observationEn":"Spectra need interpretation with thickness, composition and defects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nCalculate an approximately 60 meV redshift and retain at least two possible causes.","failure":"若報告假設「發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較光激發光峰位與線寬」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「光譜需要結合厚度、成分與缺陷解釋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：算出約 60 meV 紅移，並保留至少兩種可能原因。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare photoluminescence peak position and width\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Spectra need interpretation with thickness, composition and defects.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Calculate an approximately 60 meV redshift and retain at least two possible causes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"光譜需要結合厚度、成分與缺陷解釋。","textEn":"Spectra need interpretation with thickness, composition and defects."},{"id":"a059-v8-14-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設兩片磊晶樣品的 PL 峰位為 450 與 460 nm，以 E≈1240/λ(nm) eV 換算為 2.756 與 2.696 eV，能量下降約 0.060 eV。這個紅移可能牽涉組成、應變、溫度或量子井厚度，不能只由峰位反推唯一材料組成；提出 XRD 或厚度對照以區分。","textEn":"Hypothetical epitaxial samples have PL peaks at 450 and 460 nm. E≈1240/λ(nm) eV gives 2.756 and 2.696 eV, a decrease of about 0.060 eV. Composition, strain, temperature or well thickness can cause such a redshift; peak position alone cannot uniquely determine composition. Propose XRD or thickness controls to distinguish causes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較光激發光峰位與線寬」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare photoluminescence peak position and width\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","光譜需要結合厚度、成分與缺陷解釋。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。"],"optionsEn":["Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","Spectra need interpretation with thickness, composition and defects.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光譜需要結合厚度、成分與缺陷解釋。 厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","explanationEn":"Spectra need interpretation with thickness, composition and defects. Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設兩片磊晶樣品的 PL 峰位為 450 與 460 nm，以 E≈1240/λ(nm) eV 換算為 2.756 與 2.696 eV，能量下降約 0.060 eV。這個紅移可能牽涉組成、應變、溫度或量子井厚度，不能只由峰位反推唯一材料組成；提出 XRD 或厚度對照以區分。","textEn":"Hypothetical epitaxial samples have PL peaks at 450 and 460 nm. E≈1240/λ(nm) eV gives 2.756 and 2.696 eV, a decrease of about 0.060 eV. Composition, strain, temperature or well thickness can cause such a redshift; peak position alone cannot uniquely determine composition. Propose XRD or thickness controls to distinguish causes.","check":"算出約 60 meV 紅移，並保留至少兩種可能原因。","checkEn":"Calculate an approximately 60 meV redshift and retain at least two possible causes."}},{"id":"a059-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-14"],"title":"畫出量子井與障壁的能帶示意","titleEn":"Sketch quantum-well and barrier band profiles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：能階也依賴井寬與材料參數。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Levels depend on well width and material parameters.","instruction":"畫出量子井與障壁的能帶示意。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「能階也依賴井寬與材料參數。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch quantum-well and barrier band profiles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Levels depend on well width and material parameters.","observation":"能階也依賴井寬與材料參數。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Levels depend on well width and material parameters. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出量子井與障壁的能帶示意」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「能階也依賴井寬與材料參數。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch quantum-well and barrier band profiles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Levels depend on well width and material parameters.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"能階也依賴井寬與材料參數。","textEn":"Levels depend on well width and material parameters."},{"id":"a059-v8-15-k2","title":"結構與光電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Structure and optoelectronics: principle and limits","text":"厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","textEn":"Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出量子井與障壁的能帶示意」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch quantum-well and barrier band profiles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","能階也依賴井寬與材料參數。"],"optionsEn":["Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Levels depend on well width and material parameters."],"answer":2,"explanation":"能階也依賴井寬與材料參數。 厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","explanationEn":"Levels depend on well width and material parameters. Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}},{"id":"a059-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-15"],"title":"檢查界面漸變對量子井的影響","titleEn":"Assess graded interfaces in quantum wells","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氣體切換不一定形成瞬間銳利界面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Gas switching need not create instantly sharp interfaces.","instruction":"檢查界面漸變對量子井的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「氣體切換不一定形成瞬間銳利界面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess graded interfaces in quantum wells. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Gas switching need not create instantly sharp interfaces.","observation":"氣體切換不一定形成瞬間銳利界面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Gas switching need not create instantly sharp interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查界面漸變對量子井的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氣體切換不一定形成瞬間銳利界面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess graded interfaces in quantum wells\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Gas switching need not create instantly sharp interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氣體切換不一定形成瞬間銳利界面。","textEn":"Gas switching need not create instantly sharp interfaces."},{"id":"a059-v8-16-k2","title":"結構與光電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Structure and optoelectronics: principle and limits","text":"厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","textEn":"Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查界面漸變對量子井的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess graded interfaces in quantum wells\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣體切換不一定形成瞬間銳利界面。","發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。"],"optionsEn":["Gas switching need not create instantly sharp interfaces.","Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氣體切換不一定形成瞬間銳利界面。 厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","explanationEn":"Gas switching need not create instantly sharp interfaces. Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}},{"id":"a059-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-16"],"title":"比較缺陷密度與發光效率證據","titleEn":"Compare defect-density and emission-efficiency evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單一光譜指標不能唯一決定缺陷密度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One spectral metric cannot uniquely determine defect density.","instruction":"比較缺陷密度與發光效率證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「單一光譜指標不能唯一決定缺陷密度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare defect-density and emission-efficiency evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: One spectral metric cannot uniquely determine defect density.","observation":"單一光譜指標不能唯一決定缺陷密度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One spectral metric cannot uniquely determine defect density. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較缺陷密度與發光效率證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單一光譜指標不能唯一決定缺陷密度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare defect-density and emission-efficiency evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One spectral metric cannot uniquely determine defect density.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單一光譜指標不能唯一決定缺陷密度。","textEn":"One spectral metric cannot uniquely determine defect density."},{"id":"a059-v8-17-k2","title":"結構與光電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Structure and optoelectronics: principle and limits","text":"厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","textEn":"Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較缺陷密度與發光效率證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare defect-density and emission-efficiency evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","單一光譜指標不能唯一決定缺陷密度。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。"],"optionsEn":["Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","One spectral metric cannot uniquely determine defect density.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一光譜指標不能唯一決定缺陷密度。 厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","explanationEn":"One spectral metric cannot uniquely determine defect density. Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}},{"id":"a059-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-17"],"title":"以霍爾量測概念分開濃度與遷移率","titleEn":"Separate carrier density and mobility through Hall concepts","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：導電率同時依賴兩者。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Conductivity depends on both.","instruction":"以霍爾量測概念分開濃度與遷移率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「導電率同時依賴兩者。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate carrier density and mobility through Hall concepts. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Conductivity depends on both.","observation":"導電率同時依賴兩者。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Conductivity depends on both. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以霍爾量測概念分開濃度與遷移率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「導電率同時依賴兩者。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate carrier density and mobility through Hall concepts\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Conductivity depends on both.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"導電率同時依賴兩者。","textEn":"Conductivity depends on both."},{"id":"a059-v8-18-k2","title":"結構與光電性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Structure and optoelectronics: principle and limits","text":"厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","textEn":"Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以霍爾量測概念分開濃度與遷移率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate carrier density and mobility through Hall concepts\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["發光強度相同就代表晶體品質完全相同。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","導電率同時依賴兩者。"],"optionsEn":["Equal emission intensity proves identical crystal quality.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Conductivity depends on both."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導電率同時依賴兩者。 厚度、合金組成、應變與缺陷都會影響光電性能。","explanationEn":"Conductivity depends on both. Thickness, alloy composition, strain and defects all affect optoelectronic behavior."}}]},{"id":"a059-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"界面與整合","titleEn":"Interfaces and integration","description":"本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","descriptionEn":"This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors.","steps":[{"id":"a059-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-18"],"title":"追蹤摻雜切換與記憶效應","titleEn":"Track dopant switching and memory effects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：先前成長歷程可能污染後續層。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Previous growth history can affect later layers.","instruction":"追蹤摻雜切換與記憶效應。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「先前成長歷程可能污染後續層。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track dopant switching and memory effects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Previous growth history can affect later layers.","observation":"先前成長歷程可能污染後續層。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Previous growth history can affect later layers. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤摻雜切換與記憶效應」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「先前成長歷程可能污染後續層。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track dopant switching and memory effects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Previous growth history can affect later layers.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"先前成長歷程可能污染後續層。","textEn":"Previous growth history can affect later layers."},{"id":"a059-v8-19-k2","title":"界面與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and integration: principle and limits","text":"本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","textEn":"This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤摻雜切換與記憶效應」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track dopant switching and memory effects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["先前成長歷程可能污染後續層。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Previous growth history can affect later layers.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先前成長歷程可能污染後續層。 本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","explanationEn":"Previous growth history can affect later layers. This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}},{"id":"a059-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-19"],"title":"比較緩衝層與主動層的功能","titleEn":"Compare buffer and active-layer functions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：緩衝層可能處理應變與缺陷傳遞。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Buffers can manage strain and defect propagation.","instruction":"比較緩衝層與主動層的功能。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「緩衝層可能處理應變與缺陷傳遞。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare buffer and active-layer functions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Buffers can manage strain and defect propagation.","observation":"緩衝層可能處理應變與缺陷傳遞。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Buffers can manage strain and defect propagation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較緩衝層與主動層的功能」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「緩衝層可能處理應變與缺陷傳遞。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare buffer and active-layer functions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Buffers can manage strain and defect propagation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"緩衝層可能處理應變與缺陷傳遞。","textEn":"Buffers can manage strain and defect propagation."},{"id":"a059-v8-20-k2","title":"界面與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and integration: principle and limits","text":"本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","textEn":"This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較緩衝層與主動層的功能」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare buffer and active-layer functions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","緩衝層可能處理應變與缺陷傳遞。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Buffers can manage strain and defect propagation.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals."],"answer":1,"explanation":"緩衝層可能處理應變與缺陷傳遞。 本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","explanationEn":"Buffers can manage strain and defect propagation. This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}},{"id":"a059-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-20"],"title":"檢查成長後冷卻造成的熱應力","titleEn":"Assess thermal stress during cooldown","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：熱膨脹不匹配可能造成裂紋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thermal-expansion mismatch can cause cracking.","instruction":"檢查成長後冷卻造成的熱應力。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「熱膨脹不匹配可能造成裂紋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess thermal stress during cooldown. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thermal-expansion mismatch can cause cracking.","observation":"熱膨脹不匹配可能造成裂紋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thermal-expansion mismatch can cause cracking. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查成長後冷卻造成的熱應力」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「熱膨脹不匹配可能造成裂紋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess thermal stress during cooldown\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thermal-expansion mismatch can cause cracking.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"熱膨脹不匹配可能造成裂紋。","textEn":"Thermal-expansion mismatch can cause cracking."},{"id":"a059-v8-21-k2","title":"界面與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and integration: principle and limits","text":"本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","textEn":"This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查成長後冷卻造成的熱應力」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess thermal stress during cooldown\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","熱膨脹不匹配可能造成裂紋。"],"optionsEn":["A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Thermal-expansion mismatch can cause cracking."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱膨脹不匹配可能造成裂紋。 本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","explanationEn":"Thermal-expansion mismatch can cause cracking. This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}},{"id":"a059-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-21"],"title":"建立跨片厚度與光電性能對照","titleEn":"Relate wafer thickness maps to optoelectronic maps","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：多圖疊合有助於辨識共同來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Map overlays help identify shared origins.","instruction":"建立跨片厚度與光電性能對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「多圖疊合有助於辨識共同來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate wafer thickness maps to optoelectronic maps. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Map overlays help identify shared origins.","observation":"多圖疊合有助於辨識共同來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Map overlays help identify shared origins. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立跨片厚度與光電性能對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「多圖疊合有助於辨識共同來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate wafer thickness maps to optoelectronic maps\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Map overlays help identify shared origins.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"多圖疊合有助於辨識共同來源。","textEn":"Map overlays help identify shared origins."},{"id":"a059-v8-22-k2","title":"界面與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and integration: principle and limits","text":"本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","textEn":"This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立跨片厚度與光電性能對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate wafer thickness maps to optoelectronic maps\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["多圖疊合有助於辨識共同來源。","研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Map overlays help identify shared origins.","A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多圖疊合有助於辨識共同來源。 本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","explanationEn":"Map overlays help identify shared origins. This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}},{"id":"a059-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-22"],"title":"區分研究磊晶片與產品製程資格","titleEn":"Distinguish research epitaxy from product qualification","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：研究性能不等於產品可靠度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Research performance is not product reliability.","instruction":"區分研究磊晶片與產品製程資格。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「研究性能不等於產品可靠度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish research epitaxy from product qualification. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Research performance is not product reliability.","observation":"研究性能不等於產品可靠度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Research performance is not product reliability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分研究磊晶片與產品製程資格」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「研究性能不等於產品可靠度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish research epitaxy from product qualification\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Research performance is not product reliability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"研究性能不等於產品可靠度。","textEn":"Research performance is not product reliability."},{"id":"a059-v8-23-k2","title":"界面與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and integration: principle and limits","text":"本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","textEn":"This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分研究磊晶片與產品製程資格」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish research epitaxy from product qualification\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","研究性能不等於產品可靠度。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Research performance is not product reliability.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals."],"answer":1,"explanation":"研究性能不等於產品可靠度。 本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","explanationEn":"Research performance is not product reliability. This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}},{"id":"a059-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-mocvd","v8b-planetary","v8b-showerhead","v8b-aixhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a059-v8-23"],"title":"交付反應器、結構與性能的證據鏈","titleEn":"Deliver reactor, structure and performance evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可重現成長需要完整條件與量測範圍。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reproducible growth needs complete conditions and measurement scope.","instruction":"交付反應器、結構與性能的證據鏈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「可重現成長需要完整條件與量測範圍。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver reactor, structure and performance evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reproducible growth needs complete conditions and measurement scope.","observation":"可重現成長需要完整條件與量測範圍。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reproducible growth needs complete conditions and measurement scope. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付反應器、結構與性能的證據鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可重現成長需要完整條件與量測範圍。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver reactor, structure and performance evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reproducible growth needs complete conditions and measurement scope.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a059-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可重現成長需要完整條件與量測範圍。","textEn":"Reproducible growth needs complete conditions and measurement scope."},{"id":"a059-v8-24-k2","title":"界面與整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and integration: principle and limits","text":"本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","textEn":"This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付反應器、結構與性能的證據鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver reactor, structure and performance evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["研究配方可直接搬到任意反應器。","氣相混合均勻就能保證晶體完全無缺陷。","可重現成長需要完整條件與量測範圍。"],"optionsEn":["A research recipe transfers directly to any reactor.","Uniform gas mixing guarantees defect-free crystals.","Reproducible growth needs complete conditions and measurement scope."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可重現成長需要完整條件與量測範圍。 本課程以公開原理和模擬資料分析，不提供有毒或自燃前驅物操作配方。","explanationEn":"Reproducible growth needs complete conditions and measurement scope. This course analyzes public principles and simulated data, not operating recipes for toxic or pyrophoric precursors."}}]}]},{"id":"a060","title":"濺鍍薄膜製程","titleEn":"Sputtered thin-film processing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究動量與輸運、靶材與電漿、薄膜與介面、圖案與驗收；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: momentum and transport, targets and plasma, films and interfaces, patterns and acceptance. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["動量與輸運","靶材與電漿","薄膜與介面","圖案與驗收"],"labelsEn":["Momentum and transport","Targets and plasma","Films and interfaces","Patterns and acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"deposition","subcategoryTitle":"薄膜沉積","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thin-film deposition","stages":[{"id":"a060-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"動量與輸運","titleEn":"Momentum and transport","description":"濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","descriptionEn":"Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition.","steps":[{"id":"a060-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出離子撞擊靶材與原子逸出","titleEn":"Sketch ion impact and target-atom ejection","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：濺鍍產率依入射與材料條件改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sputter yield depends on incidence and material conditions.","instruction":"畫出離子撞擊靶材與原子逸出。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「濺鍍產率依入射與材料條件改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch ion impact and target-atom ejection. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sputter yield depends on incidence and material conditions.","observation":"濺鍍產率依入射與材料條件改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sputter yield depends on incidence and material conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Sputtering simply boils the target.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出離子撞擊靶材與原子逸出」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「濺鍍產率依入射與材料條件改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch ion impact and target-atom ejection\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sputter yield depends on incidence and material conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"濺鍍產率依入射與材料條件改變。","textEn":"Sputter yield depends on incidence and material conditions."},{"id":"a060-v8-01-k2","title":"動量與輸運的原理與限制","titleEn":"Momentum and transport: principle and limits","text":"濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","textEn":"Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出離子撞擊靶材與原子逸出」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch ion impact and target-atom ejection\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["濺鍍產率依入射與材料條件改變。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。"],"optionsEn":["Sputter yield depends on incidence and material conditions.","Sputtering simply boils the target.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"濺鍍產率依入射與材料條件改變。 濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","explanationEn":"Sputter yield depends on incidence and material conditions. Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}},{"id":"a060-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-01"],"title":"比較濺鍍、蒸發與 CVD 的物質來源","titleEn":"Compare material sources in sputtering, evaporation and CVD","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同來源造成不同覆蓋與污染議題。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sources create different coverage and contamination issues.","instruction":"比較濺鍍、蒸發與 CVD 的物質來源。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「不同來源造成不同覆蓋與污染議題。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare material sources in sputtering, evaporation and CVD. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sources create different coverage and contamination issues.","observation":"不同來源造成不同覆蓋與污染議題。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sources create different coverage and contamination issues. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Sputtering simply boils the target.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較濺鍍、蒸發與 CVD 的物質來源」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同來源造成不同覆蓋與污染議題。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare material sources in sputtering, evaporation and CVD\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sources create different coverage and contamination issues.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同來源造成不同覆蓋與污染議題。","textEn":"Sources create different coverage and contamination issues."},{"id":"a060-v8-02-k2","title":"動量與輸運的原理與限制","titleEn":"Momentum and transport: principle and limits","text":"濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","textEn":"Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較濺鍍、蒸發與 CVD 的物質來源」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare material sources in sputtering, evaporation and CVD\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","不同來源造成不同覆蓋與污染議題。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。"],"optionsEn":["Sputtering simply boils the target.","Sources create different coverage and contamination issues.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同來源造成不同覆蓋與污染議題。 濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","explanationEn":"Sources create different coverage and contamination issues. Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}},{"id":"a060-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-02"],"title":"繪製靶到晶圓的角度分布","titleEn":"Sketch target-to-wafer angular distributions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：到達方向會影響陰影區覆蓋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Arrival direction affects shadowed coverage.","instruction":"繪製靶到晶圓的角度分布。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「到達方向會影響陰影區覆蓋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch target-to-wafer angular distributions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Arrival direction affects shadowed coverage.","observation":"到達方向會影響陰影區覆蓋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Arrival direction affects shadowed coverage. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Sputtering simply boils the target.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製靶到晶圓的角度分布」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「到達方向會影響陰影區覆蓋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch target-to-wafer angular distributions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Arrival direction affects shadowed coverage.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"到達方向會影響陰影區覆蓋。","textEn":"Arrival direction affects shadowed coverage."},{"id":"a060-v8-03-k2","title":"動量與輸運的原理與限制","titleEn":"Momentum and transport: principle and limits","text":"濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","textEn":"Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製靶到晶圓的角度分布」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch target-to-wafer angular distributions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","到達方向會影響陰影區覆蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Sputtering simply boils the target.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Arrival direction affects shadowed coverage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"到達方向會影響陰影區覆蓋。 濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","explanationEn":"Arrival direction affects shadowed coverage. Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}},{"id":"a060-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-03"],"title":"以平均自由程概念比較碰撞","titleEn":"Compare collisions using mean-free-path concepts","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：壓力會改變粒子輸運與能量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pressure changes particle transport and energy.","instruction":"以平均自由程概念比較碰撞。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「壓力會改變粒子輸運與能量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare collisions using mean-free-path concepts. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pressure changes particle transport and energy.","observation":"壓力會改變粒子輸運與能量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pressure changes particle transport and energy. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Sputtering simply boils the target.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以平均自由程概念比較碰撞」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「壓力會改變粒子輸運與能量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare collisions using mean-free-path concepts\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pressure changes particle transport and energy.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"壓力會改變粒子輸運與能量。","textEn":"Pressure changes particle transport and energy."},{"id":"a060-v8-04-k2","title":"動量與輸運的原理與限制","titleEn":"Momentum and transport: principle and limits","text":"濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","textEn":"Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以平均自由程概念比較碰撞」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare collisions using mean-free-path concepts\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["壓力會改變粒子輸運與能量。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。"],"optionsEn":["Pressure changes particle transport and energy.","Sputtering simply boils the target.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge."],"answer":0,"explanation":"壓力會改變粒子輸運與能量。 濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","explanationEn":"Pressure changes particle transport and energy. Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}},{"id":"a060-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-04"],"title":"分開基壓與製程壓力","titleEn":"Separate base pressure from working pressure","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘餘氣體與工作氣體有不同角色。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residual and working gases have different roles.","instruction":"分開基壓與製程壓力。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「殘餘氣體與工作氣體有不同角色。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate base pressure from working pressure. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residual and working gases have different roles.","observation":"殘餘氣體與工作氣體有不同角色。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residual and working gases have different roles. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Sputtering simply boils the target.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開基壓與製程壓力」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘餘氣體與工作氣體有不同角色。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate base pressure from working pressure\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residual and working gases have different roles.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘餘氣體與工作氣體有不同角色。","textEn":"Residual and working gases have different roles."},{"id":"a060-v8-05-k2","title":"動量與輸運的原理與限制","titleEn":"Momentum and transport: principle and limits","text":"濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","textEn":"Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開基壓與製程壓力」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate base pressure from working pressure\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","殘餘氣體與工作氣體有不同角色。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。"],"optionsEn":["Sputtering simply boils the target.","Residual and working gases have different roles.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘餘氣體與工作氣體有不同角色。 濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","explanationEn":"Residual and working gases have different roles. Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}},{"id":"a060-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-05"],"title":"建立靶材、基板與污染相容性表","titleEn":"Build target–substrate contamination compatibility","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：共用設備需要追蹤材料交叉污染。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Shared equipment needs cross-contamination tracking.","instruction":"建立靶材、基板與污染相容性表。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「共用設備需要追蹤材料交叉污染。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build target–substrate contamination compatibility. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Shared equipment needs cross-contamination tracking.","observation":"共用設備需要追蹤材料交叉污染。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Shared equipment needs cross-contamination tracking. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Sputtering simply boils the target.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立靶材、基板與污染相容性表」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「共用設備需要追蹤材料交叉污染。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build target–substrate contamination compatibility\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Shared equipment needs cross-contamination tracking.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"共用設備需要追蹤材料交叉污染。","textEn":"Shared equipment needs cross-contamination tracking."},{"id":"a060-v8-06-k2","title":"動量與輸運的原理與限制","titleEn":"Momentum and transport: principle and limits","text":"濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","textEn":"Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立靶材、基板與污染相容性表」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build target–substrate contamination compatibility\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","共用設備需要追蹤材料交叉污染。"],"optionsEn":["Sputtering simply boils the target.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Shared equipment needs cross-contamination tracking."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共用設備需要追蹤材料交叉污染。 濺鍍以粒子動量移除靶原子並沉積，與蒸發及化學沉積不同。","explanationEn":"Shared equipment needs cross-contamination tracking. Sputtering ejects target atoms by momentum transfer and differs from evaporation and chemical deposition."}}]},{"id":"a060-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"靶材與電漿","titleEn":"Targets and plasma","description":"放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","descriptionEn":"Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other.","steps":[{"id":"a060-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-06"],"title":"比較 DC 與 RF 濺鍍適用性","titleEn":"Compare DC and RF sputtering applicability","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：導電性影響穩定放電方式。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Conductivity affects stable discharge modes.","instruction":"比較 DC 與 RF 濺鍍適用性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「導電性影響穩定放電方式。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare DC and RF sputtering applicability. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Conductivity affects stable discharge modes.","observation":"導電性影響穩定放電方式。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Conductivity affects stable discharge modes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 DC 與 RF 濺鍍適用性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「導電性影響穩定放電方式。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare DC and RF sputtering applicability\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Conductivity affects stable discharge modes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"導電性影響穩定放電方式。","textEn":"Conductivity affects stable discharge modes."},{"id":"a060-v8-07-k2","title":"靶材與電漿的原理與限制","titleEn":"Targets and plasma: principle and limits","text":"放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","textEn":"Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 DC 與 RF 濺鍍適用性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare DC and RF sputtering applicability\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["導電性影響穩定放電方式。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Conductivity affects stable discharge modes.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"導電性影響穩定放電方式。 放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","explanationEn":"Conductivity affects stable discharge modes. Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}},{"id":"a060-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-07"],"title":"畫出磁控場對電子路徑的影響","titleEn":"Sketch magnetron effects on electron paths","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：磁控可增加近靶區電離效率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Magnetron confinement can improve ionization near the target.","instruction":"畫出磁控場對電子路徑的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「磁控可增加近靶區電離效率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch magnetron effects on electron paths. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Magnetron confinement can improve ionization near the target.","observation":"磁控可增加近靶區電離效率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Magnetron confinement can improve ionization near the target. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出磁控場對電子路徑的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「磁控可增加近靶區電離效率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch magnetron effects on electron paths\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Magnetron confinement can improve ionization near the target.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"磁控可增加近靶區電離效率。","textEn":"Magnetron confinement can improve ionization near the target."},{"id":"a060-v8-08-k2","title":"靶材與電漿的原理與限制","titleEn":"Targets and plasma: principle and limits","text":"放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","textEn":"Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出磁控場對電子路徑的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch magnetron effects on electron paths\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","磁控可增加近靶區電離效率。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Magnetron confinement can improve ionization near the target.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"磁控可增加近靶區電離效率。 放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","explanationEn":"Magnetron confinement can improve ionization near the target. Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}},{"id":"a060-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-08"],"title":"檢查靶面侵蝕區與使用歷程","titleEn":"Inspect target erosion tracks and use history","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：靶面狀態可能改變均勻性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Target condition can change uniformity.","instruction":"檢查靶面侵蝕區與使用歷程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「靶面狀態可能改變均勻性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect target erosion tracks and use history. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Target condition can change uniformity.","observation":"靶面狀態可能改變均勻性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Target condition can change uniformity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查靶面侵蝕區與使用歷程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「靶面狀態可能改變均勻性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect target erosion tracks and use history\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Target condition can change uniformity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"靶面狀態可能改變均勻性。","textEn":"Target condition can change uniformity."},{"id":"a060-v8-09-k2","title":"靶材與電漿的原理與限制","titleEn":"Targets and plasma: principle and limits","text":"放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","textEn":"Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查靶面侵蝕區與使用歷程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect target erosion tracks and use history\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","靶面狀態可能改變均勻性。"],"optionsEn":["Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Target condition can change uniformity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"靶面狀態可能改變均勻性。 放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","explanationEn":"Target condition can change uniformity. Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}},{"id":"a060-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-09"],"title":"比較預濺鍍與正式沉積的目的","titleEn":"Compare pre-sputter and deposition purposes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：靶面清理不等於基板清理。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Target cleaning is not substrate cleaning.","instruction":"比較預濺鍍與正式沉積的目的。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「靶面清理不等於基板清理。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare pre-sputter and deposition purposes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Target cleaning is not substrate cleaning.","observation":"靶面清理不等於基板清理。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Target cleaning is not substrate cleaning. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較預濺鍍與正式沉積的目的」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「靶面清理不等於基板清理。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare pre-sputter and deposition purposes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Target cleaning is not substrate cleaning.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"靶面清理不等於基板清理。","textEn":"Target cleaning is not substrate cleaning."},{"id":"a060-v8-10-k2","title":"靶材與電漿的原理與限制","titleEn":"Targets and plasma: principle and limits","text":"放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","textEn":"Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較預濺鍍與正式沉積的目的」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare pre-sputter and deposition purposes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["靶面清理不等於基板清理。","所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Target cleaning is not substrate cleaning.","Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress."],"answer":0,"explanation":"靶面清理不等於基板清理。 放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","explanationEn":"Target cleaning is not substrate cleaning. Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}},{"id":"a060-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-10"],"title":"以反應式濺鍍概念畫靶中毒迴圈","titleEn":"Sketch target-poisoning hysteresis in reactive sputtering","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：反應氣體可改變靶面與放電。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reactive gas can change target surfaces and discharge.","instruction":"以反應式濺鍍概念畫靶中毒迴圈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「反應氣體可改變靶面與放電。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch target-poisoning hysteresis in reactive sputtering. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reactive gas can change target surfaces and discharge.","observation":"反應氣體可改變靶面與放電。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reactive gas can change target surfaces and discharge. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以反應式濺鍍概念畫靶中毒迴圈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「反應氣體可改變靶面與放電。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch target-poisoning hysteresis in reactive sputtering\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reactive gas can change target surfaces and discharge.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"反應氣體可改變靶面與放電。","textEn":"Reactive gas can change target surfaces and discharge."},{"id":"a060-v8-11-k2","title":"靶材與電漿的原理與限制","titleEn":"Targets and plasma: principle and limits","text":"放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","textEn":"Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以反應式濺鍍概念畫靶中毒迴圈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch target-poisoning hysteresis in reactive sputtering\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","反應氣體可改變靶面與放電。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Reactive gas can change target surfaces and discharge.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress."],"answer":1,"explanation":"反應氣體可改變靶面與放電。 放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","explanationEn":"Reactive gas can change target surfaces and discharge. Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}},{"id":"a060-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-11"],"title":"分開離子束沉積與偏壓靶沉積","titleEn":"Distinguish ion-beam and biased-target deposition","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：能量控制方式會影響介面混合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Energy-control methods affect interface mixing.","instruction":"分開離子束沉積與偏壓靶沉積。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「能量控制方式會影響介面混合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish ion-beam and biased-target deposition. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Energy-control methods affect interface mixing.","observation":"能量控制方式會影響介面混合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Energy-control methods affect interface mixing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開離子束沉積與偏壓靶沉積」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「能量控制方式會影響介面混合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish ion-beam and biased-target deposition\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Energy-control methods affect interface mixing.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"能量控制方式會影響介面混合。","textEn":"Energy-control methods affect interface mixing."},{"id":"a060-v8-12-k2","title":"靶材與電漿的原理與限制","titleEn":"Targets and plasma: principle and limits","text":"放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","textEn":"Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開離子束沉積與偏壓靶沉積」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish ion-beam and biased-target deposition\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["所有絕緣靶都能直接使用相同 DC 放電。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","能量控制方式會影響介面混合。"],"optionsEn":["Every insulating target can use the same DC discharge.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Energy-control methods affect interface mixing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"能量控制方式會影響介面混合。 放電方式與靶材導電性相互限制。","explanationEn":"Energy-control methods affect interface mixing. Discharge mode and target conductivity constrain each other."}}]},{"id":"a060-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"薄膜與介面","titleEn":"Films and interfaces","description":"薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","descriptionEn":"Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility.","steps":[{"id":"a060-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-12"],"title":"量測厚度地圖並計算均勻性","titleEn":"Map thickness and calculate uniformity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：均勻性公式與取樣範圍需明示。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Uniformity definition and sampling range must be stated.","instruction":"量測厚度地圖並計算均勻性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「均勻性公式與取樣範圍需明示。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Map thickness and calculate uniformity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Uniformity definition and sampling range must be stated.","observation":"均勻性公式與取樣範圍需明示。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Uniformity definition and sampling range must be stated. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較厚薄膜一定較低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測厚度地圖並計算均勻性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「均勻性公式與取樣範圍需明示。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Map thickness and calculate uniformity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Uniformity definition and sampling range must be stated.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"均勻性公式與取樣範圍需明示。","textEn":"Uniformity definition and sampling range must be stated."},{"id":"a060-v8-13-k2","title":"薄膜與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Films and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","textEn":"Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測厚度地圖並計算均勻性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Map thickness and calculate uniformity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["均勻性公式與取樣範圍需明示。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。"],"optionsEn":["Uniformity definition and sampling range must be stated.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均勻性公式與取樣範圍需明示。 薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","explanationEn":"Uniformity definition and sampling range must be stated. Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}},{"id":"a060-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-13"],"title":"比較沉積速率與時間的線性","titleEn":"Test linearity of thickness with time","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：起始與靶面變化可能造成非線性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Startup and target changes can cause nonlinearity.","instruction":"比較沉積速率與時間的線性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「起始與靶面變化可能造成非線性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Test linearity of thickness with time. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Startup and target changes can cause nonlinearity.","observation":"起始與靶面變化可能造成非線性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Startup and target changes can cause nonlinearity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較厚薄膜一定較低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較沉積速率與時間的線性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「起始與靶面變化可能造成非線性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Test linearity of thickness with time\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Startup and target changes can cause nonlinearity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"起始與靶面變化可能造成非線性。","textEn":"Startup and target changes can cause nonlinearity."},{"id":"a060-v8-14-k2","title":"薄膜與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Films and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","textEn":"Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較沉積速率與時間的線性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Test linearity of thickness with time\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","起始與靶面變化可能造成非線性。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Startup and target changes can cause nonlinearity.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall."],"answer":1,"explanation":"起始與靶面變化可能造成非線性。 薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","explanationEn":"Startup and target changes can cause nonlinearity. Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}},{"id":"a060-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-14"],"title":"用曲率檢查應力符號","titleEn":"Check stress sign through curvature","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：應力需與膜厚和基板條件一起解釋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Stress needs interpretation with thickness and substrate conditions.","instruction":"用曲率檢查應力符號。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「應力需與膜厚和基板條件一起解釋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check stress sign through curvature. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Stress needs interpretation with thickness and substrate conditions.","observation":"應力需與膜厚和基板條件一起解釋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Stress needs interpretation with thickness and substrate conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較厚薄膜一定較低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用曲率檢查應力符號」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「應力需與膜厚和基板條件一起解釋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check stress sign through curvature\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Stress needs interpretation with thickness and substrate conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"應力需與膜厚和基板條件一起解釋。","textEn":"Stress needs interpretation with thickness and substrate conditions."},{"id":"a060-v8-15-k2","title":"薄膜與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Films and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","textEn":"Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用曲率檢查應力符號」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check stress sign through curvature\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","應力需與膜厚和基板條件一起解釋。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Stress needs interpretation with thickness and substrate conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應力需與膜厚和基板條件一起解釋。 薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","explanationEn":"Stress needs interpretation with thickness and substrate conditions. Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}},{"id":"a060-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-15"],"title":"比較 AFM 粗糙度與密度指標","titleEn":"Compare AFM roughness with density measures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面平滑不能單獨證明高密度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Smoothness alone does not prove high density.","instruction":"比較 AFM 粗糙度與密度指標。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「表面平滑不能單獨證明高密度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare AFM roughness with density measures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Smoothness alone does not prove high density.","observation":"表面平滑不能單獨證明高密度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Smoothness alone does not prove high density. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較厚薄膜一定較低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 AFM 粗糙度與密度指標」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面平滑不能單獨證明高密度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare AFM roughness with density measures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Smoothness alone does not prove high density.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面平滑不能單獨證明高密度。","textEn":"Smoothness alone does not prove high density."},{"id":"a060-v8-16-k2","title":"薄膜與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Films and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","textEn":"Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 AFM 粗糙度與密度指標」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare AFM roughness with density measures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面平滑不能單獨證明高密度。","較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。"],"optionsEn":["Smoothness alone does not prove high density.","Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面平滑不能單獨證明高密度。 薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","explanationEn":"Smoothness alone does not prove high density. Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}},{"id":"a060-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-16"],"title":"檢查介面氧化與黏著問題","titleEn":"Inspect interface oxidation and adhesion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：真空中轉移可減少部分再氧化。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Vacuum transfer can reduce some reoxidation.","instruction":"檢查介面氧化與黏著問題。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「真空中轉移可減少部分再氧化。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect interface oxidation and adhesion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Vacuum transfer can reduce some reoxidation.","observation":"真空中轉移可減少部分再氧化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Vacuum transfer can reduce some reoxidation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「較厚薄膜一定較低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查介面氧化與黏著問題」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「真空中轉移可減少部分再氧化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect interface oxidation and adhesion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Vacuum transfer can reduce some reoxidation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"真空中轉移可減少部分再氧化。","textEn":"Vacuum transfer can reduce some reoxidation."},{"id":"a060-v8-17-k2","title":"薄膜與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Films and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","textEn":"Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查介面氧化與黏著問題」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect interface oxidation and adhesion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","真空中轉移可減少部分再氧化。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Vacuum transfer can reduce some reoxidation.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall."],"answer":1,"explanation":"真空中轉移可減少部分再氧化。 薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","explanationEn":"Vacuum transfer can reduce some reoxidation. Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."}},{"id":"a060-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-17"],"title":"量測薄膜片電阻與連續性","titleEn":"Measure sheet resistance and continuity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：超薄膜可能未形成連續導電路徑。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Ultrathin films may lack continuous conducting paths.","instruction":"量測薄膜片電阻與連續性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「超薄膜可能未形成連續導電路徑。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設均勻且連續的濺鍍膜厚 50 nm，片電阻 20 Ω/□。由 ρ=Rs t 得 ρ=1.0×10⁻⁶ Ω·m=100 μΩ·cm。若厚度估計偏高 10%，推算電阻率也偏高 10%。此關係假設連續膜與適當幾何修正；不連續島狀膜不能直接用同一塊材模型解釋。","instructionEn":"Measure sheet resistance and continuity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Ultrathin films may lack continuous conducting paths.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a uniform continuous sputtered film 50 nm thick with sheet resistance 20 Ω/□. ρ=Rs t gives 1.0×10⁻⁶ Ω·m=100 μΩ·cm. A 10% high thickness estimate makes inferred resistivity 10% high. The relation assumes a continuous film and proper geometry correction; disconnected islands cannot be interpreted with the same bulk-film model.","observation":"超薄膜可能未形成連續導電路徑。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 100 μΩ·cm、誤差傳遞與連續膜假設。","observationEn":"Ultrathin films may lack continuous conducting paths. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 100 μΩ·cm, error propagation and the continuous-film assumption.","failure":"若報告假設「較厚薄膜一定較低應力。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測薄膜片電阻與連續性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「超薄膜可能未形成連續導電路徑。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 100 μΩ·cm、誤差傳遞與連續膜假設。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure sheet resistance and continuity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Ultrathin films may lack continuous conducting paths.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 100 μΩ·cm, error propagation and the continuous-film assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"超薄膜可能未形成連續導電路徑。","textEn":"Ultrathin films may lack continuous conducting paths."},{"id":"a060-v8-18-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設均勻且連續的濺鍍膜厚 50 nm，片電阻 20 Ω/□。由 ρ=Rs t 得 ρ=1.0×10⁻⁶ Ω·m=100 μΩ·cm。若厚度估計偏高 10%，推算電阻率也偏高 10%。此關係假設連續膜與適當幾何修正；不連續島狀膜不能直接用同一塊材模型解釋。","textEn":"Assume a uniform continuous sputtered film 50 nm thick with sheet resistance 20 Ω/□. ρ=Rs t gives 1.0×10⁻⁶ Ω·m=100 μΩ·cm. A 10% high thickness estimate makes inferred resistivity 10% high. The relation assumes a continuous film and proper geometry correction; disconnected islands cannot be interpreted with the same bulk-film model."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測薄膜片電阻與連續性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure sheet resistance and continuity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["較厚薄膜一定較低應力。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","超薄膜可能未形成連續導電路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker films necessarily have lower stress.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Ultrathin films may lack continuous conducting paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超薄膜可能未形成連續導電路徑。 薄膜密度、應力與粗糙度取決於到達粒子與表面遷移。","explanationEn":"Ultrathin films may lack continuous conducting paths. Film density, stress and roughness depend on arriving particles and surface mobility."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設均勻且連續的濺鍍膜厚 50 nm，片電阻 20 Ω/□。由 ρ=Rs t 得 ρ=1.0×10⁻⁶ Ω·m=100 μΩ·cm。若厚度估計偏高 10%，推算電阻率也偏高 10%。此關係假設連續膜與適當幾何修正；不連續島狀膜不能直接用同一塊材模型解釋。","textEn":"Assume a uniform continuous sputtered film 50 nm thick with sheet resistance 20 Ω/□. ρ=Rs t gives 1.0×10⁻⁶ Ω·m=100 μΩ·cm. A 10% high thickness estimate makes inferred resistivity 10% high. The relation assumes a continuous film and proper geometry correction; disconnected islands cannot be interpreted with the same bulk-film model.","check":"交付 100 μΩ·cm、誤差傳遞與連續膜假設。","checkEn":"Report 100 μΩ·cm, error propagation and the continuous-film assumption."}}]},{"id":"a060-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"圖案與驗收","titleEn":"Patterns and acceptance","description":"平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","descriptionEn":"Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality.","steps":[{"id":"a060-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-18"],"title":"比較階梯頂部與側壁覆蓋","titleEn":"Compare coverage on step tops and sidewalls","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：方向性輸運可造成陰影。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Directional transport can create shadows.","instruction":"比較階梯頂部與側壁覆蓋。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「方向性輸運可造成陰影。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare coverage on step tops and sidewalls. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Directional transport can create shadows.","observation":"方向性輸運可造成陰影。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Directional transport can create shadows. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar thickness represents every sidewall.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較階梯頂部與側壁覆蓋」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「方向性輸運可造成陰影。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare coverage on step tops and sidewalls\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Directional transport can create shadows.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"方向性輸運可造成陰影。","textEn":"Directional transport can create shadows."},{"id":"a060-v8-19-k2","title":"圖案與驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterns and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","textEn":"Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較階梯頂部與側壁覆蓋」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare coverage on step tops and sidewalls\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["方向性輸運可造成陰影。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。"],"optionsEn":["Directional transport can create shadows.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Sputtering simply boils the target."],"answer":0,"explanation":"方向性輸運可造成陰影。 平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","explanationEn":"Directional transport can create shadows. Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}},{"id":"a060-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-19"],"title":"評估深孔入口懸垂與底部覆蓋","titleEn":"Assess overhang and bottom coverage in deep holes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：入口增厚可能阻礙後續填孔。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Entrance thickening can obstruct later fill.","instruction":"評估深孔入口懸垂與底部覆蓋。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「入口增厚可能阻礙後續填孔。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess overhang and bottom coverage in deep holes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Entrance thickening can obstruct later fill.","observation":"入口增厚可能阻礙後續填孔。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Entrance thickening can obstruct later fill. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar thickness represents every sidewall.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估深孔入口懸垂與底部覆蓋」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「入口增厚可能阻礙後續填孔。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess overhang and bottom coverage in deep holes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Entrance thickening can obstruct later fill.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"入口增厚可能阻礙後續填孔。","textEn":"Entrance thickening can obstruct later fill."},{"id":"a060-v8-20-k2","title":"圖案與驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterns and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","textEn":"Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估深孔入口懸垂與底部覆蓋」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess overhang and bottom coverage in deep holes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","入口增厚可能阻礙後續填孔。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。"],"optionsEn":["Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Entrance thickening can obstruct later fill.","Sputtering simply boils the target."],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口增厚可能阻礙後續填孔。 平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","explanationEn":"Entrance thickening can obstruct later fill. Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}},{"id":"a060-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-20"],"title":"檢查抬離圖形的側壁金屬連接","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall metal bridges in lift-off patterns","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：過度側壁覆蓋可能妨礙抬離。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Excess sidewall coating can hinder lift-off.","instruction":"檢查抬離圖形的側壁金屬連接。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「過度側壁覆蓋可能妨礙抬離。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect sidewall metal bridges in lift-off patterns. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Excess sidewall coating can hinder lift-off.","observation":"過度側壁覆蓋可能妨礙抬離。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Excess sidewall coating can hinder lift-off. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar thickness represents every sidewall.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查抬離圖形的側壁金屬連接」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「過度側壁覆蓋可能妨礙抬離。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect sidewall metal bridges in lift-off patterns\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Excess sidewall coating can hinder lift-off.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"過度側壁覆蓋可能妨礙抬離。","textEn":"Excess sidewall coating can hinder lift-off."},{"id":"a060-v8-21-k2","title":"圖案與驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterns and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","textEn":"Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查抬離圖形的側壁金屬連接」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect sidewall metal bridges in lift-off patterns\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","過度側壁覆蓋可能妨礙抬離。"],"optionsEn":["Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Sputtering simply boils the target.","Excess sidewall coating can hinder lift-off."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過度側壁覆蓋可能妨礙抬離。 平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","explanationEn":"Excess sidewall coating can hinder lift-off. Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}},{"id":"a060-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-21"],"title":"比較多層連續沉積與中途曝氣","titleEn":"Compare continuous multilayers with air breaks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：曝氣可能增加介面污染。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Air breaks can increase interface contamination.","instruction":"比較多層連續沉積與中途曝氣。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「曝氣可能增加介面污染。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare continuous multilayers with air breaks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Air breaks can increase interface contamination.","observation":"曝氣可能增加介面污染。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Air breaks can increase interface contamination. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar thickness represents every sidewall.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較多層連續沉積與中途曝氣」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「曝氣可能增加介面污染。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare continuous multilayers with air breaks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Air breaks can increase interface contamination.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"曝氣可能增加介面污染。","textEn":"Air breaks can increase interface contamination."},{"id":"a060-v8-22-k2","title":"圖案與驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterns and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","textEn":"Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較多層連續沉積與中途曝氣」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare continuous multilayers with air breaks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["曝氣可能增加介面污染。","平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。"],"optionsEn":["Air breaks can increase interface contamination.","Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Sputtering simply boils the target."],"answer":0,"explanation":"曝氣可能增加介面污染。 平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","explanationEn":"Air breaks can increase interface contamination. Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}},{"id":"a060-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-22"],"title":"追蹤熱處理後電阻與應力","titleEn":"Track resistance and stress after annealing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：後續熱史可能改變晶粒與介面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Later heating can change grains and interfaces.","instruction":"追蹤熱處理後電阻與應力。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「後續熱史可能改變晶粒與介面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track resistance and stress after annealing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Later heating can change grains and interfaces.","observation":"後續熱史可能改變晶粒與介面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Later heating can change grains and interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar thickness represents every sidewall.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤熱處理後電阻與應力」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「後續熱史可能改變晶粒與介面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track resistance and stress after annealing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Later heating can change grains and interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"後續熱史可能改變晶粒與介面。","textEn":"Later heating can change grains and interfaces."},{"id":"a060-v8-23-k2","title":"圖案與驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterns and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","textEn":"Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤熱處理後電阻與應力」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track resistance and stress after annealing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","後續熱史可能改變晶粒與介面。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。"],"optionsEn":["Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Later heating can change grains and interfaces.","Sputtering simply boils the target."],"answer":1,"explanation":"後續熱史可能改變晶粒與介面。 平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","explanationEn":"Later heating can change grains and interfaces. Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}},{"id":"a060-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-sputter","v8b-nistpaper","v8b-lamdep","v8b-plating"],"prerequisiteIds":["a060-v8-23"],"title":"交付厚度、介面、電性與覆蓋證據","titleEn":"Deliver thickness, interface, electrical and coverage evidence","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：薄膜用途決定驗收指標組合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Film application determines the acceptance metrics.","instruction":"交付厚度、介面、電性與覆蓋證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「薄膜用途決定驗收指標組合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver thickness, interface, electrical and coverage evidence. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Film application determines the acceptance metrics.","observation":"薄膜用途決定驗收指標組合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Film application determines the acceptance metrics. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Planar thickness represents every sidewall.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付厚度、介面、電性與覆蓋證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「薄膜用途決定驗收指標組合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver thickness, interface, electrical and coverage evidence\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Film application determines the acceptance metrics.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a060-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"薄膜用途決定驗收指標組合。","textEn":"Film application determines the acceptance metrics."},{"id":"a060-v8-24-k2","title":"圖案與驗收的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterns and acceptance: principle and limits","text":"平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","textEn":"Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付厚度、介面、電性與覆蓋證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver thickness, interface, electrical and coverage evidence\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平面膜厚可代表所有側壁。","濺鍍就是把靶材煮沸。","薄膜用途決定驗收指標組合。"],"optionsEn":["Planar thickness represents every sidewall.","Sputtering simply boils the target.","Film application determines the acceptance metrics."],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄膜用途決定驗收指標組合。 平面膜質合格不保證深孔覆蓋或抬離品質。","explanationEn":"Film application determines the acceptance metrics. Acceptable planar films do not guarantee deep-hole coverage or lift-off quality."}}]}]},{"id":"a061","title":"鎢插塞製作","titleEn":"Tungsten plug fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究接點與材料、成核與填充、平坦化與介面、電性與可靠度；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: contacts and materials, nucleation and fill, planarization and interfaces, electrical quality and reliability. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["接點與材料","成核與填充","平坦化與介面","電性與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Contacts and materials","Nucleation and fill","Planarization and interfaces","Electrical quality and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability","stages":[{"id":"a061-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"接點與材料","titleEn":"Contacts and materials","description":"鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","descriptionEn":"Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes.","steps":[{"id":"a061-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出元件到第一層金屬的接點","titleEn":"Draw a contact from device to first metal","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：垂直接點包含多個材料介面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A vertical contact includes multiple material interfaces.","instruction":"畫出元件到第一層金屬的接點。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「垂直接點包含多個材料介面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw a contact from device to first metal. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A vertical contact includes multiple material interfaces.","observation":"垂直接點包含多個材料介面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A vertical contact includes multiple material interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出元件到第一層金屬的接點」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「垂直接點包含多個材料介面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw a contact from device to first metal\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A vertical contact includes multiple material interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"垂直接點包含多個材料介面。","textEn":"A vertical contact includes multiple material interfaces."},{"id":"a061-v8-01-k2","title":"接點與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and materials: principle and limits","text":"鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","textEn":"Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出元件到第一層金屬的接點」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw a contact from device to first metal\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["垂直接點包含多個材料介面。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["A vertical contact includes multiple material interfaces.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","A closed opening proves full internal fill."],"answer":0,"explanation":"垂直接點包含多個材料介面。 鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","explanationEn":"A vertical contact includes multiple material interfaces. Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}},{"id":"a061-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-01"],"title":"比較鎢插塞與銅通孔的角色","titleEn":"Compare tungsten plugs with copper vias","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料選擇受到整合位置與熱史影響。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material choice depends on integration level and thermal history.","instruction":"比較鎢插塞與銅通孔的角色。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「材料選擇受到整合位置與熱史影響。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare tungsten plugs with copper vias. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material choice depends on integration level and thermal history.","observation":"材料選擇受到整合位置與熱史影響。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material choice depends on integration level and thermal history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較鎢插塞與銅通孔的角色」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料選擇受到整合位置與熱史影響。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare tungsten plugs with copper vias\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material choice depends on integration level and thermal history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料選擇受到整合位置與熱史影響。","textEn":"Material choice depends on integration level and thermal history."},{"id":"a061-v8-02-k2","title":"接點與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and materials: principle and limits","text":"鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","textEn":"Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較鎢插塞與銅通孔的角色」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare tungsten plugs with copper vias\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","材料選擇受到整合位置與熱史影響。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","Material choice depends on integration level and thermal history.","A closed opening proves full internal fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料選擇受到整合位置與熱史影響。 鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","explanationEn":"Material choice depends on integration level and thermal history. Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}},{"id":"a061-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-02"],"title":"估算孔徑縮小對電阻的影響","titleEn":"Estimate resistance changes as diameter shrinks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：導電截面縮小會增加幾何電阻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A smaller conducting section increases geometric resistance.","instruction":"估算孔徑縮小對電阻的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「導電截面縮小會增加幾何電阻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Estimate resistance changes as diameter shrinks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: A smaller conducting section increases geometric resistance.","observation":"導電截面縮小會增加幾何電阻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A smaller conducting section increases geometric resistance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算孔徑縮小對電阻的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「導電截面縮小會增加幾何電阻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate resistance changes as diameter shrinks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A smaller conducting section increases geometric resistance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"導電截面縮小會增加幾何電阻。","textEn":"A smaller conducting section increases geometric resistance."},{"id":"a061-v8-03-k2","title":"接點與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and materials: principle and limits","text":"鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","textEn":"Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算孔徑縮小對電阻的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate resistance changes as diameter shrinks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","導電截面縮小會增加幾何電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","A closed opening proves full internal fill.","A smaller conducting section increases geometric resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導電截面縮小會增加幾何電阻。 鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","explanationEn":"A smaller conducting section increases geometric resistance. Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}},{"id":"a061-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-03"],"title":"分開體電阻與接觸電阻","titleEn":"Separate bulk and interface resistance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：介面可在小尺寸下占重要比例。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Interfaces can dominate at small dimensions.","instruction":"分開體電阻與接觸電阻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「介面可在小尺寸下占重要比例。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設圓柱插塞長 100 nm、直徑 20 nm、有效電阻率 2.0×10⁻⁷ Ω·m。R=ρL/[π(d/2)²]≈63.7 Ω；上下介面各 10 Ω 時總計約 83.7 Ω。直徑減半時主體電阻變為約 254.6 Ω，總計 274.6 Ω，而不是 83.7 的四倍；介面在此簡化例中假設固定。","instructionEn":"Separate bulk and interface resistance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Interfaces can dominate at small dimensions.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a cylindrical plug with length 100 nm, diameter 20 nm and effective resistivity 2.0×10⁻⁷ Ω·m. R=ρL/[π(d/2)²]≈63.7 Ω. With 10 Ω at each interface, total is about 83.7 Ω. Halving diameter raises bulk resistance to about 254.6 Ω and total to 274.6 Ω, not four times 83.7; interfaces are held constant in this simplified model.","observation":"介面可在小尺寸下占重要比例。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n分開主體 63.7 Ω 與總值 83.7 Ω，並說明介面固定假設。","observationEn":"Interfaces can dominate at small dimensions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nSeparate 63.7 Ω bulk from 83.7 Ω total and state the fixed-interface assumption.","failure":"若報告假設「鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開體電阻與接觸電阻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「介面可在小尺寸下占重要比例。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：分開主體 63.7 Ω 與總值 83.7 Ω，並說明介面固定假設。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate bulk and interface resistance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Interfaces can dominate at small dimensions.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Separate 63.7 Ω bulk from 83.7 Ω total and state the fixed-interface assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"介面可在小尺寸下占重要比例。","textEn":"Interfaces can dominate at small dimensions."},{"id":"a061-v8-04-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設圓柱插塞長 100 nm、直徑 20 nm、有效電阻率 2.0×10⁻⁷ Ω·m。R=ρL/[π(d/2)²]≈63.7 Ω；上下介面各 10 Ω 時總計約 83.7 Ω。直徑減半時主體電阻變為約 254.6 Ω，總計 274.6 Ω，而不是 83.7 的四倍；介面在此簡化例中假設固定。","textEn":"Assume a cylindrical plug with length 100 nm, diameter 20 nm and effective resistivity 2.0×10⁻⁷ Ω·m. R=ρL/[π(d/2)²]≈63.7 Ω. With 10 Ω at each interface, total is about 83.7 Ω. Halving diameter raises bulk resistance to about 254.6 Ω and total to 274.6 Ω, not four times 83.7; interfaces are held constant in this simplified model."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開體電阻與接觸電阻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate bulk and interface resistance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["介面可在小尺寸下占重要比例。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Interfaces can dominate at small dimensions.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","A closed opening proves full internal fill."],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面可在小尺寸下占重要比例。 鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","explanationEn":"Interfaces can dominate at small dimensions. Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設圓柱插塞長 100 nm、直徑 20 nm、有效電阻率 2.0×10⁻⁷ Ω·m。R=ρL/[π(d/2)²]≈63.7 Ω；上下介面各 10 Ω 時總計約 83.7 Ω。直徑減半時主體電阻變為約 254.6 Ω，總計 274.6 Ω，而不是 83.7 的四倍；介面在此簡化例中假設固定。","textEn":"Assume a cylindrical plug with length 100 nm, diameter 20 nm and effective resistivity 2.0×10⁻⁷ Ω·m. R=ρL/[π(d/2)²]≈63.7 Ω. With 10 Ω at each interface, total is about 83.7 Ω. Halving diameter raises bulk resistance to about 254.6 Ω and total to 274.6 Ω, not four times 83.7; interfaces are held constant in this simplified model.","check":"分開主體 63.7 Ω 與總值 83.7 Ω，並說明介面固定假設。","checkEn":"Separate 63.7 Ω bulk from 83.7 Ω total and state the fixed-interface assumption."}},{"id":"a061-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-04"],"title":"標記前清潔與原生氧化層","titleEn":"Mark preclean and native oxide","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘留氧化層可能增加接觸電阻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residual oxide can increase contact resistance.","instruction":"標記前清潔與原生氧化層。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「殘留氧化層可能增加接觸電阻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark preclean and native oxide. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residual oxide can increase contact resistance.","observation":"殘留氧化層可能增加接觸電阻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residual oxide can increase contact resistance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記前清潔與原生氧化層」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘留氧化層可能增加接觸電阻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark preclean and native oxide\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residual oxide can increase contact resistance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘留氧化層可能增加接觸電阻。","textEn":"Residual oxide can increase contact resistance."},{"id":"a061-v8-05-k2","title":"接點與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and materials: principle and limits","text":"鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","textEn":"Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記前清潔與原生氧化層」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark preclean and native oxide\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","殘留氧化層可能增加接觸電阻。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。"],"optionsEn":["Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","Residual oxide can increase contact resistance.","A closed opening proves full internal fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘留氧化層可能增加接觸電阻。 鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","explanationEn":"Residual oxide can increase contact resistance. Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}},{"id":"a061-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-05"],"title":"建立孔底與側壁的材料清單","titleEn":"List materials at the bottom and sidewalls","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相容性需涵蓋整個接點堆疊。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Compatibility must cover the full contact stack.","instruction":"建立孔底與側壁的材料清單。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「相容性需涵蓋整個接點堆疊。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List materials at the bottom and sidewalls. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Compatibility must cover the full contact stack.","observation":"相容性需涵蓋整個接點堆疊。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Compatibility must cover the full contact stack. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立孔底與側壁的材料清單」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相容性需涵蓋整個接點堆疊。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List materials at the bottom and sidewalls\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Compatibility must cover the full contact stack.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相容性需涵蓋整個接點堆疊。","textEn":"Compatibility must cover the full contact stack."},{"id":"a061-v8-06-k2","title":"接點與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and materials: principle and limits","text":"鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","textEn":"Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立孔底與側壁的材料清單」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List materials at the bottom and sidewalls\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","相容性需涵蓋整個接點堆疊。"],"optionsEn":["Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","A closed opening proves full internal fill.","Compatibility must cover the full contact stack."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相容性需涵蓋整個接點堆疊。 鎢插塞需同時提供低阻連接與相容介面，不只是填滿洞。","explanationEn":"Compatibility must cover the full contact stack. Tungsten plugs need low-resistance connections and compatible interfaces, not merely filled holes."}}]},{"id":"a061-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"成核與填充","titleEn":"Nucleation and fill","description":"成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","descriptionEn":"Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids.","steps":[{"id":"a061-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-06"],"title":"畫出成核層與主體鎢的生長","titleEn":"Draw nucleation and bulk tungsten growth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：成核與主體沉積可有不同機制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Nucleation and bulk growth can have different mechanisms.","instruction":"畫出成核層與主體鎢的生長。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「成核與主體沉積可有不同機制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw nucleation and bulk tungsten growth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Nucleation and bulk growth can have different mechanisms.","observation":"成核與主體沉積可有不同機制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Nucleation and bulk growth can have different mechanisms. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A closed opening proves full internal fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出成核層與主體鎢的生長」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「成核與主體沉積可有不同機制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw nucleation and bulk tungsten growth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Nucleation and bulk growth can have different mechanisms.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"成核與主體沉積可有不同機制。","textEn":"Nucleation and bulk growth can have different mechanisms."},{"id":"a061-v8-07-k2","title":"成核與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Nucleation and fill: principle and limits","text":"成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","textEn":"Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出成核層與主體鎢的生長」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw nucleation and bulk tungsten growth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["成核與主體沉積可有不同機制。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Nucleation and bulk growth can have different mechanisms.","A closed opening proves full internal fill.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"成核與主體沉積可有不同機制。 成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","explanationEn":"Nucleation and bulk growth can have different mechanisms. Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}},{"id":"a061-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-07"],"title":"比較 ALD 成核與 CVD 主體填充","titleEn":"Compare ALD nucleation with CVD bulk fill","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：薄層精度與高產率可由不同步驟分工。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thin-layer precision and productivity can be split across steps.","instruction":"比較 ALD 成核與 CVD 主體填充。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「薄層精度與高產率可由不同步驟分工。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare ALD nucleation with CVD bulk fill. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thin-layer precision and productivity can be split across steps.","observation":"薄層精度與高產率可由不同步驟分工。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thin-layer precision and productivity can be split across steps. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A closed opening proves full internal fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 ALD 成核與 CVD 主體填充」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「薄層精度與高產率可由不同步驟分工。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare ALD nucleation with CVD bulk fill\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thin-layer precision and productivity can be split across steps.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"薄層精度與高產率可由不同步驟分工。","textEn":"Thin-layer precision and productivity can be split across steps."},{"id":"a061-v8-08-k2","title":"成核與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Nucleation and fill: principle and limits","text":"成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","textEn":"Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 ALD 成核與 CVD 主體填充」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare ALD nucleation with CVD bulk fill\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","薄層精度與高產率可由不同步驟分工。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。"],"optionsEn":["A closed opening proves full internal fill.","Thin-layer precision and productivity can be split across steps.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄層精度與高產率可由不同步驟分工。 成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","explanationEn":"Thin-layer precision and productivity can be split across steps. Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}},{"id":"a061-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-08"],"title":"檢查不同表面的成核延遲","titleEn":"Assess nucleation delay on different surfaces","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：非均勻起始可造成局部空隙。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Nonuniform initiation can create local gaps.","instruction":"檢查不同表面的成核延遲。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「非均勻起始可造成局部空隙。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess nucleation delay on different surfaces. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Nonuniform initiation can create local gaps.","observation":"非均勻起始可造成局部空隙。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Nonuniform initiation can create local gaps. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A closed opening proves full internal fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查不同表面的成核延遲」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「非均勻起始可造成局部空隙。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess nucleation delay on different surfaces\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Nonuniform initiation can create local gaps.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"非均勻起始可造成局部空隙。","textEn":"Nonuniform initiation can create local gaps."},{"id":"a061-v8-09-k2","title":"成核與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Nucleation and fill: principle and limits","text":"成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","textEn":"Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查不同表面的成核延遲」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess nucleation delay on different surfaces\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","非均勻起始可造成局部空隙。"],"optionsEn":["A closed opening proves full internal fill.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","Nonuniform initiation can create local gaps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"非均勻起始可造成局部空隙。 成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","explanationEn":"Nonuniform initiation can create local gaps. Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}},{"id":"a061-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-09"],"title":"比較共形生長的中央接縫","titleEn":"Inspect central seams from conformal growth","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：側壁相向生長可能留下接縫。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Opposing sidewall growth can leave a seam.","instruction":"比較共形生長的中央接縫。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「側壁相向生長可能留下接縫。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect central seams from conformal growth. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Opposing sidewall growth can leave a seam.","observation":"側壁相向生長可能留下接縫。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Opposing sidewall growth can leave a seam. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A closed opening proves full internal fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較共形生長的中央接縫」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「側壁相向生長可能留下接縫。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect central seams from conformal growth\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Opposing sidewall growth can leave a seam.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"側壁相向生長可能留下接縫。","textEn":"Opposing sidewall growth can leave a seam."},{"id":"a061-v8-10-k2","title":"成核與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Nucleation and fill: principle and limits","text":"成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","textEn":"Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較共形生長的中央接縫」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect central seams from conformal growth\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["側壁相向生長可能留下接縫。","洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Opposing sidewall growth can leave a seam.","A closed opening proves full internal fill.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"側壁相向生長可能留下接縫。 成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","explanationEn":"Opposing sidewall growth can leave a seam. Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}},{"id":"a061-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-10"],"title":"追蹤孔口懸垂到封口","titleEn":"Trace entrance overhang into pinch-off","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：過早封口可能包住空洞。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Early closure can trap voids.","instruction":"追蹤孔口懸垂到封口。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「過早封口可能包住空洞。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace entrance overhang into pinch-off. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Early closure can trap voids.","observation":"過早封口可能包住空洞。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Early closure can trap voids. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A closed opening proves full internal fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤孔口懸垂到封口」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「過早封口可能包住空洞。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace entrance overhang into pinch-off\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Early closure can trap voids.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"過早封口可能包住空洞。","textEn":"Early closure can trap voids."},{"id":"a061-v8-11-k2","title":"成核與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Nucleation and fill: principle and limits","text":"成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","textEn":"Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤孔口懸垂到封口」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace entrance overhang into pinch-off\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","過早封口可能包住空洞。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。"],"optionsEn":["A closed opening proves full internal fill.","Early closure can trap voids.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"過早封口可能包住空洞。 成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","explanationEn":"Early closure can trap voids. Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}},{"id":"a061-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-11"],"title":"對照截面與沉積厚度的填充狀態","titleEn":"Compare fill state with deposition thickness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：外部厚度不能唯一代表孔內填充。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: External thickness does not uniquely establish internal fill.","instruction":"對照截面與沉積厚度的填充狀態。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「外部厚度不能唯一代表孔內填充。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare fill state with deposition thickness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: External thickness does not uniquely establish internal fill.","observation":"外部厚度不能唯一代表孔內填充。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"External thickness does not uniquely establish internal fill. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A closed opening proves full internal fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「對照截面與沉積厚度的填充狀態」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「外部厚度不能唯一代表孔內填充。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare fill state with deposition thickness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"External thickness does not uniquely establish internal fill.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"外部厚度不能唯一代表孔內填充。","textEn":"External thickness does not uniquely establish internal fill."},{"id":"a061-v8-12-k2","title":"成核與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Nucleation and fill: principle and limits","text":"成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","textEn":"Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對照截面與沉積厚度的填充狀態」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare fill state with deposition thickness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["洞口封閉就能證明內部填滿。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","外部厚度不能唯一代表孔內填充。"],"optionsEn":["A closed opening proves full internal fill.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","External thickness does not uniquely establish internal fill."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外部厚度不能唯一代表孔內填充。 成核延遲與共形生長會影響接縫及空洞。","explanationEn":"External thickness does not uniquely establish internal fill. Nucleation delay and conformal growth affect seams and voids."}}]},{"id":"a061-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"平坦化與介面","titleEn":"Planarization and interfaces","description":"阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","descriptionEn":"Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area.","steps":[{"id":"a061-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-12"],"title":"檢查阻障與襯層的連續性","titleEn":"Inspect barrier and liner continuity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部破口可能造成化學或擴散問題。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local gaps can cause chemical or diffusion problems.","instruction":"檢查阻障與襯層的連續性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「局部破口可能造成化學或擴散問題。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect barrier and liner continuity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local gaps can cause chemical or diffusion problems.","observation":"局部破口可能造成化學或擴散問題。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local gaps can cause chemical or diffusion problems. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層越厚一定越低電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查阻障與襯層的連續性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部破口可能造成化學或擴散問題。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect barrier and liner continuity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local gaps can cause chemical or diffusion problems.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部破口可能造成化學或擴散問題。","textEn":"Local gaps can cause chemical or diffusion problems."},{"id":"a061-v8-13-k2","title":"平坦化與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Planarization and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","textEn":"Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查阻障與襯層的連續性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect barrier and liner continuity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["局部破口可能造成化學或擴散問題。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Local gaps can cause chemical or diffusion problems.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部破口可能造成化學或擴散問題。 阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","explanationEn":"Local gaps can cause chemical or diffusion problems. Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}},{"id":"a061-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-13"],"title":"比較襯層厚度對有效孔徑的影響","titleEn":"Assess liner thickness against effective diameter","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：襯層占用導電截面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Liners consume conducting area.","instruction":"比較襯層厚度對有效孔徑的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「襯層占用導電截面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess liner thickness against effective diameter. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Liners consume conducting area.","observation":"襯層占用導電截面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Liners consume conducting area. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層越厚一定越低電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較襯層厚度對有效孔徑的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「襯層占用導電截面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess liner thickness against effective diameter\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Liners consume conducting area.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"襯層占用導電截面。","textEn":"Liners consume conducting area."},{"id":"a061-v8-14-k2","title":"平坦化與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Planarization and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","textEn":"Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較襯層厚度對有效孔徑的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess liner thickness against effective diameter\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","襯層占用導電截面。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。"],"optionsEn":["A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","Liners consume conducting area.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"襯層占用導電截面。 阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","explanationEn":"Liners consume conducting area. Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}},{"id":"a061-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-14"],"title":"畫出 CMP 移除頂部多餘鎢","titleEn":"Sketch CMP removal of excess top tungsten","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平坦化需停止在適當介電層。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Planarization needs an appropriate dielectric stop.","instruction":"畫出 CMP 移除頂部多餘鎢。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「平坦化需停止在適當介電層。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch CMP removal of excess top tungsten. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Planarization needs an appropriate dielectric stop.","observation":"平坦化需停止在適當介電層。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Planarization needs an appropriate dielectric stop. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層越厚一定越低電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出 CMP 移除頂部多餘鎢」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平坦化需停止在適當介電層。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch CMP removal of excess top tungsten\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Planarization needs an appropriate dielectric stop.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平坦化需停止在適當介電層。","textEn":"Planarization needs an appropriate dielectric stop."},{"id":"a061-v8-15-k2","title":"平坦化與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Planarization and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","textEn":"Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出 CMP 移除頂部多餘鎢」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch CMP removal of excess top tungsten\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","平坦化需停止在適當介電層。"],"optionsEn":["A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Planarization needs an appropriate dielectric stop."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平坦化需停止在適當介電層。 阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","explanationEn":"Planarization needs an appropriate dielectric stop. Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}},{"id":"a061-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-15"],"title":"量測凹陷與殘留金屬","titleEn":"Measure recess and residual metal","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：過度與不足移除造成不同失效。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Over- and under-removal cause different failures.","instruction":"量測凹陷與殘留金屬。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「過度與不足移除造成不同失效。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure recess and residual metal. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Over- and under-removal cause different failures.","observation":"過度與不足移除造成不同失效。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Over- and under-removal cause different failures. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層越厚一定越低電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測凹陷與殘留金屬」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「過度與不足移除造成不同失效。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure recess and residual metal\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Over- and under-removal cause different failures.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"過度與不足移除造成不同失效。","textEn":"Over- and under-removal cause different failures."},{"id":"a061-v8-16-k2","title":"平坦化與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Planarization and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","textEn":"Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測凹陷與殘留金屬」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure recess and residual metal\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["過度與不足移除造成不同失效。","襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Over- and under-removal cause different failures.","A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"過度與不足移除造成不同失效。 阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","explanationEn":"Over- and under-removal cause different failures. Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}},{"id":"a061-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-16"],"title":"檢查 CMP 後清潔的顆粒與腐蝕","titleEn":"Inspect post-CMP particles and corrosion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：清潔可能改善顆粒也改變表面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cleaning can reduce particles while changing surfaces.","instruction":"檢查 CMP 後清潔的顆粒與腐蝕。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「清潔可能改善顆粒也改變表面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect post-CMP particles and corrosion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cleaning can reduce particles while changing surfaces.","observation":"清潔可能改善顆粒也改變表面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cleaning can reduce particles while changing surfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層越厚一定越低電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查 CMP 後清潔的顆粒與腐蝕」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「清潔可能改善顆粒也改變表面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect post-CMP particles and corrosion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cleaning can reduce particles while changing surfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"清潔可能改善顆粒也改變表面。","textEn":"Cleaning can reduce particles while changing surfaces."},{"id":"a061-v8-17-k2","title":"平坦化與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Planarization and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","textEn":"Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查 CMP 後清潔的顆粒與腐蝕」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect post-CMP particles and corrosion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","清潔可能改善顆粒也改變表面。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。"],"optionsEn":["A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","Cleaning can reduce particles while changing surfaces.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔可能改善顆粒也改變表面。 阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","explanationEn":"Cleaning can reduce particles while changing surfaces. Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}},{"id":"a061-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-17"],"title":"比較熱處理前後的界面狀態","titleEn":"Compare interfaces before and after heating","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：熱史可能改變反應層與應力。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Thermal history can alter reaction layers and stress.","instruction":"比較熱處理前後的界面狀態。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「熱史可能改變反應層與應力。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare interfaces before and after heating. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Thermal history can alter reaction layers and stress.","observation":"熱史可能改變反應層與應力。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Thermal history can alter reaction layers and stress. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層越厚一定越低電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較熱處理前後的界面狀態」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「熱史可能改變反應層與應力。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare interfaces before and after heating\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Thermal history can alter reaction layers and stress.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"熱史可能改變反應層與應力。","textEn":"Thermal history can alter reaction layers and stress."},{"id":"a061-v8-18-k2","title":"平坦化與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Planarization and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","textEn":"Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較熱處理前後的界面狀態」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare interfaces before and after heating\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層越厚一定越低電阻。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","熱史可能改變反應層與應力。"],"optionsEn":["A thicker liner necessarily lowers resistance.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Thermal history can alter reaction layers and stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱史可能改變反應層與應力。 阻障、襯層與前清潔會改變接觸電阻與有效導電面積。","explanationEn":"Thermal history can alter reaction layers and stress. Barriers, liners and preclean change contact resistance and conducting area."}}]},{"id":"a061-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性與可靠度","titleEn":"Electrical quality and reliability","description":"總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","descriptionEn":"Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces.","steps":[{"id":"a061-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-18"],"title":"以 Kelvin 結構分離接觸電阻","titleEn":"Separate contact resistance using Kelvin structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：量測設計可減少導線電阻混入。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Measurement design can reduce lead-resistance contamination.","instruction":"以 Kelvin 結構分離接觸電阻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「量測設計可減少導線電阻混入。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate contact resistance using Kelvin structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Measurement design can reduce lead-resistance contamination.","observation":"量測設計可減少導線電阻混入。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Measurement design can reduce lead-resistance contamination. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以 Kelvin 結構分離接觸電阻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「量測設計可減少導線電阻混入。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate contact resistance using Kelvin structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Measurement design can reduce lead-resistance contamination.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"量測設計可減少導線電阻混入。","textEn":"Measurement design can reduce lead-resistance contamination."},{"id":"a061-v8-19-k2","title":"電性與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and reliability: principle and limits","text":"總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","textEn":"Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以 Kelvin 結構分離接觸電阻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate contact resistance using Kelvin structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["量測設計可減少導線電阻混入。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Measurement design can reduce lead-resistance contamination.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測設計可減少導線電阻混入。 總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","explanationEn":"Measurement design can reduce lead-resistance contamination. Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}},{"id":"a061-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-19"],"title":"以接點鏈放大稀有開路事件","titleEn":"Use contact chains to reveal rare opens","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：長鏈增加觀察機會也需對應樣本數。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Long chains increase opportunities and require defined sample counts.","instruction":"以接點鏈放大稀有開路事件。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「長鏈增加觀察機會也需對應樣本數。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use contact chains to reveal rare opens. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Long chains increase opportunities and require defined sample counts.","observation":"長鏈增加觀察機會也需對應樣本數。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Long chains increase opportunities and require defined sample counts. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以接點鏈放大稀有開路事件」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「長鏈增加觀察機會也需對應樣本數。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use contact chains to reveal rare opens\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Long chains increase opportunities and require defined sample counts.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"長鏈增加觀察機會也需對應樣本數。","textEn":"Long chains increase opportunities and require defined sample counts."},{"id":"a061-v8-20-k2","title":"電性與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and reliability: principle and limits","text":"總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","textEn":"Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以接點鏈放大稀有開路事件」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use contact chains to reveal rare opens\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","長鏈增加觀察機會也需對應樣本數。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。"],"optionsEn":["One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Long chains increase opportunities and require defined sample counts.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長鏈增加觀察機會也需對應樣本數。 總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","explanationEn":"Long chains increase opportunities and require defined sample counts. Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}},{"id":"a061-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-20"],"title":"比較電阻尾端與平均值","titleEn":"Compare resistance tails with the mean","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：少數高阻接點可能主導產品失效。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A few high-resistance contacts can dominate failures.","instruction":"比較電阻尾端與平均值。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「少數高阻接點可能主導產品失效。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare resistance tails with the mean. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: A few high-resistance contacts can dominate failures.","observation":"少數高阻接點可能主導產品失效。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A few high-resistance contacts can dominate failures. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較電阻尾端與平均值」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「少數高阻接點可能主導產品失效。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare resistance tails with the mean\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A few high-resistance contacts can dominate failures.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"少數高阻接點可能主導產品失效。","textEn":"A few high-resistance contacts can dominate failures."},{"id":"a061-v8-21-k2","title":"電性與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and reliability: principle and limits","text":"總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","textEn":"Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較電阻尾端與平均值」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare resistance tails with the mean\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","少數高阻接點可能主導產品失效。"],"optionsEn":["One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","A few high-resistance contacts can dominate failures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"少數高阻接點可能主導產品失效。 總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","explanationEn":"A few high-resistance contacts can dominate failures. Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}},{"id":"a061-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-21"],"title":"將空洞位置與電阻異常對應","titleEn":"Relate void locations to resistance anomalies","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：形貌因果需用同位置證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Morphological causality needs co-located evidence.","instruction":"將空洞位置與電阻異常對應。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「形貌因果需用同位置證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate void locations to resistance anomalies. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Morphological causality needs co-located evidence.","observation":"形貌因果需用同位置證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Morphological causality needs co-located evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將空洞位置與電阻異常對應」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「形貌因果需用同位置證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate void locations to resistance anomalies\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Morphological causality needs co-located evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"形貌因果需用同位置證據。","textEn":"Morphological causality needs co-located evidence."},{"id":"a061-v8-22-k2","title":"電性與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and reliability: principle and limits","text":"總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","textEn":"Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將空洞位置與電阻異常對應」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate void locations to resistance anomalies\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["形貌因果需用同位置證據。","單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Morphological causality needs co-located evidence.","One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"形貌因果需用同位置證據。 總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","explanationEn":"Morphological causality needs co-located evidence. Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}},{"id":"a061-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-22"],"title":"檢查熱循環後的接點穩定度","titleEn":"Assess contact stability after thermal cycling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：初始導通不等於長期穩定。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Initial continuity is not long-term stability.","instruction":"檢查熱循環後的接點穩定度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「初始導通不等於長期穩定。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess contact stability after thermal cycling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Initial continuity is not long-term stability.","observation":"初始導通不等於長期穩定。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Initial continuity is not long-term stability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查熱循環後的接點穩定度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「初始導通不等於長期穩定。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess contact stability after thermal cycling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Initial continuity is not long-term stability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"初始導通不等於長期穩定。","textEn":"Initial continuity is not long-term stability."},{"id":"a061-v8-23-k2","title":"電性與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and reliability: principle and limits","text":"總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","textEn":"Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查熱循環後的接點穩定度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess contact stability after thermal cycling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","初始導通不等於長期穩定。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。"],"optionsEn":["One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Initial continuity is not long-term stability.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始導通不等於長期穩定。 總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","explanationEn":"Initial continuity is not long-term stability. Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}},{"id":"a061-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-lamdep","v8b-lamale","v8b-interconnect","v8b-lamemory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a061-v8-23"],"title":"交付填充、平坦化與接觸電阻審查","titleEn":"Review fill, planarization and contact resistance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：插塞驗證需跨越幾何與介面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Plug validation must cover geometry and interfaces.","instruction":"交付填充、平坦化與接觸電阻審查。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「插塞驗證需跨越幾何與介面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Review fill, planarization and contact resistance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Plug validation must cover geometry and interfaces.","observation":"插塞驗證需跨越幾何與介面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Plug validation must cover geometry and interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付填充、平坦化與接觸電阻審查」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「插塞驗證需跨越幾何與介面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Review fill, planarization and contact resistance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Plug validation must cover geometry and interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a061-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"插塞驗證需跨越幾何與介面。","textEn":"Plug validation must cover geometry and interfaces."},{"id":"a061-v8-24-k2","title":"電性與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrical quality and reliability: principle and limits","text":"總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","textEn":"Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付填充、平坦化與接觸電阻審查」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Review fill, planarization and contact resistance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["單一接點導通即可證明整批可靠。","鎢體電阻率即可決定所有接點電阻。","插塞驗證需跨越幾何與介面。"],"optionsEn":["One conducting contact proves whole-lot reliability.","Bulk tungsten resistivity determines every contact resistance.","Plug validation must cover geometry and interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"插塞驗證需跨越幾何與介面。 總電阻包含體材料、幾何與上下介面。","explanationEn":"Plug validation must cover geometry and interfaces. Total resistance includes bulk material, geometry and both interfaces."}}]}]},{"id":"a062","title":"銅雙鑲嵌互連","titleEn":"Copper dual-damascene interconnects","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究線孔整合、蝕刻與襯層、填銅與平坦化、RC 與可靠度；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: line–via integration, etch and liners, copper fill and planarization, rc and reliability. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["線孔整合","蝕刻與襯層","填銅與平坦化","RC 與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Line–via integration","Etch and liners","Copper fill and planarization","RC and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability","stages":[{"id":"a062-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"線孔整合","titleEn":"Line–via integration","description":"雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","descriptionEn":"Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling.","steps":[{"id":"a062-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出兩金屬層之間的通孔與線槽","titleEn":"Draw a via and trench between metal levels","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：垂直與水平連接具有不同幾何。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Vertical and horizontal connections have different geometry.","instruction":"畫出兩金屬層之間的通孔與線槽。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「垂直與水平連接具有不同幾何。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw a via and trench between metal levels. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Vertical and horizontal connections have different geometry.","observation":"垂直與水平連接具有不同幾何。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Vertical and horizontal connections have different geometry. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出兩金屬層之間的通孔與線槽」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「垂直與水平連接具有不同幾何。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw a via and trench between metal levels\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Vertical and horizontal connections have different geometry.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"垂直與水平連接具有不同幾何。","textEn":"Vertical and horizontal connections have different geometry."},{"id":"a062-v8-01-k2","title":"線孔整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Line–via integration: principle and limits","text":"雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","textEn":"Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出兩金屬層之間的通孔與線槽」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw a via and trench between metal levels\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["垂直與水平連接具有不同幾何。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Vertical and horizontal connections have different geometry.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"垂直與水平連接具有不同幾何。 雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","explanationEn":"Vertical and horizontal connections have different geometry. Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}},{"id":"a062-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-01"],"title":"比較 via-first 與 trench-first 流程","titleEn":"Compare via-first and trench-first flows","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：順序改變保護、清潔與對位需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Sequence changes protection, cleaning and alignment needs.","instruction":"比較 via-first 與 trench-first 流程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「順序改變保護、清潔與對位需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare via-first and trench-first flows. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Sequence changes protection, cleaning and alignment needs.","observation":"順序改變保護、清潔與對位需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Sequence changes protection, cleaning and alignment needs. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 via-first 與 trench-first 流程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「順序改變保護、清潔與對位需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare via-first and trench-first flows\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Sequence changes protection, cleaning and alignment needs.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"順序改變保護、清潔與對位需求。","textEn":"Sequence changes protection, cleaning and alignment needs."},{"id":"a062-v8-02-k2","title":"線孔整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Line–via integration: principle and limits","text":"雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","textEn":"Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 via-first 與 trench-first 流程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare via-first and trench-first flows\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","順序改變保護、清潔與對位需求。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Sequence changes protection, cleaning and alignment needs.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"順序改變保護、清潔與對位需求。 雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","explanationEn":"Sequence changes protection, cleaning and alignment needs. Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}},{"id":"a062-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-02"],"title":"標記蝕刻停止層與低介電層","titleEn":"Mark etch-stop and low-k layers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同介電層具有不同功能。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different dielectric layers serve different functions.","instruction":"標記蝕刻停止層與低介電層。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「不同介電層具有不同功能。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark etch-stop and low-k layers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different dielectric layers serve different functions.","observation":"不同介電層具有不同功能。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different dielectric layers serve different functions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記蝕刻停止層與低介電層」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同介電層具有不同功能。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark etch-stop and low-k layers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different dielectric layers serve different functions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同介電層具有不同功能。","textEn":"Different dielectric layers serve different functions."},{"id":"a062-v8-03-k2","title":"線孔整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Line–via integration: principle and limits","text":"雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","textEn":"Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記蝕刻停止層與低介電層」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark etch-stop and low-k layers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","不同介電層具有不同功能。"],"optionsEn":["Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","Different dielectric layers serve different functions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同介電層具有不同功能。 雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","explanationEn":"Different dielectric layers serve different functions. Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}},{"id":"a062-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-03"],"title":"規畫通孔落在下層線上的裕量","titleEn":"Budget via landing on the lower line","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：套刻偏差會降低接觸面積或形成短路。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Overlay error can reduce contact area or cause shorts.","instruction":"規畫通孔落在下層線上的裕量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「套刻偏差會降低接觸面積或形成短路。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Budget via landing on the lower line. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Overlay error can reduce contact area or cause shorts.","observation":"套刻偏差會降低接觸面積或形成短路。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Overlay error can reduce contact area or cause shorts. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「規畫通孔落在下層線上的裕量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「套刻偏差會降低接觸面積或形成短路。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Budget via landing on the lower line\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Overlay error can reduce contact area or cause shorts.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"套刻偏差會降低接觸面積或形成短路。","textEn":"Overlay error can reduce contact area or cause shorts."},{"id":"a062-v8-04-k2","title":"線孔整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Line–via integration: principle and limits","text":"雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","textEn":"Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「規畫通孔落在下層線上的裕量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Budget via landing on the lower line\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["套刻偏差會降低接觸面積或形成短路。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Overlay error can reduce contact area or cause shorts.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns."],"answer":0,"explanation":"套刻偏差會降低接觸面積或形成短路。 雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","explanationEn":"Overlay error can reduce contact area or cause shorts. Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}},{"id":"a062-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-04"],"title":"比較線寬與線距對 RC 的影響","titleEn":"Compare width and spacing effects on RC","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：加寬降阻可能增加耦合電容。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Widening can lower resistance while increasing coupling capacitance.","instruction":"比較線寬與線距對 RC 的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「加寬降阻可能增加耦合電容。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare width and spacing effects on RC. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Widening can lower resistance while increasing coupling capacitance.","observation":"加寬降阻可能增加耦合電容。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Widening can lower resistance while increasing coupling capacitance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較線寬與線距對 RC 的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「加寬降阻可能增加耦合電容。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare width and spacing effects on RC\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Widening can lower resistance while increasing coupling capacitance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"加寬降阻可能增加耦合電容。","textEn":"Widening can lower resistance while increasing coupling capacitance."},{"id":"a062-v8-05-k2","title":"線孔整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Line–via integration: principle and limits","text":"雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","textEn":"Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較線寬與線距對 RC 的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare width and spacing effects on RC\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","加寬降阻可能增加耦合電容。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Widening can lower resistance while increasing coupling capacitance.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns."],"answer":1,"explanation":"加寬降阻可能增加耦合電容。 雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","explanationEn":"Widening can lower resistance while increasing coupling capacitance. Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}},{"id":"a062-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-05"],"title":"建立跨兩層的連通性圖","titleEn":"Build connectivity across two metal levels","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：幾何疊合需符合網路意圖。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Geometric overlap must match network intent.","instruction":"建立跨兩層的連通性圖。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「幾何疊合需符合網路意圖。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Build connectivity across two metal levels. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Geometric overlap must match network intent.","observation":"幾何疊合需符合網路意圖。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Geometric overlap must match network intent. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立跨兩層的連通性圖」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「幾何疊合需符合網路意圖。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build connectivity across two metal levels\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Geometric overlap must match network intent.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"幾何疊合需符合網路意圖。","textEn":"Geometric overlap must match network intent."},{"id":"a062-v8-06-k2","title":"線孔整合的原理與限制","titleEn":"Line–via integration: principle and limits","text":"雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","textEn":"Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立跨兩層的連通性圖」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build connectivity across two metal levels\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","幾何疊合需符合網路意圖。"],"optionsEn":["Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","Geometric overlap must match network intent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何疊合需符合網路意圖。 雙鑲嵌先在介電層形成線槽與通孔，再以金屬填入。","explanationEn":"Geometric overlap must match network intent. Dual damascene forms trenches and vias in dielectric before metal filling."}}]},{"id":"a062-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"蝕刻與襯層","titleEn":"Etch and liners","description":"線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","descriptionEn":"Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability.","steps":[{"id":"a062-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-06"],"title":"追蹤通孔蝕刻到停止層","titleEn":"Trace via etching to the stop layer","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：停止層保護下層但也需適時開啟。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A stop protects the lower layer but must later be opened.","instruction":"追蹤通孔蝕刻到停止層。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「停止層保護下層但也需適時開啟。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace via etching to the stop layer. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A stop protects the lower layer but must later be opened.","observation":"停止層保護下層但也需適時開啟。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A stop protects the lower layer but must later be opened. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤通孔蝕刻到停止層」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「停止層保護下層但也需適時開啟。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace via etching to the stop layer\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A stop protects the lower layer but must later be opened.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"停止層保護下層但也需適時開啟。","textEn":"A stop protects the lower layer but must later be opened."},{"id":"a062-v8-07-k2","title":"蝕刻與襯層的原理與限制","titleEn":"Etch and liners: principle and limits","text":"線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","textEn":"Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤通孔蝕刻到停止層」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace via etching to the stop layer\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["停止層保護下層但也需適時開啟。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。"],"optionsEn":["A stop protects the lower layer but must later be opened.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","A planar surface rules out internal voids."],"answer":0,"explanation":"停止層保護下層但也需適時開啟。 線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","explanationEn":"A stop protects the lower layer but must later be opened. Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}},{"id":"a062-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-07"],"title":"檢查線槽深度與通孔肩部","titleEn":"Inspect trench depth and via shoulders","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：肩部形狀會影響襯層與填充。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Shoulder geometry affects lining and fill.","instruction":"檢查線槽深度與通孔肩部。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「肩部形狀會影響襯層與填充。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect trench depth and via shoulders. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Shoulder geometry affects lining and fill.","observation":"肩部形狀會影響襯層與填充。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Shoulder geometry affects lining and fill. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查線槽深度與通孔肩部」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「肩部形狀會影響襯層與填充。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect trench depth and via shoulders\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Shoulder geometry affects lining and fill.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"肩部形狀會影響襯層與填充。","textEn":"Shoulder geometry affects lining and fill."},{"id":"a062-v8-08-k2","title":"蝕刻與襯層的原理與限制","titleEn":"Etch and liners: principle and limits","text":"線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","textEn":"Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查線槽深度與通孔肩部」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect trench depth and via shoulders\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","肩部形狀會影響襯層與填充。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","Shoulder geometry affects lining and fill.","A planar surface rules out internal voids."],"answer":1,"explanation":"肩部形狀會影響襯層與填充。 線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","explanationEn":"Shoulder geometry affects lining and fill. Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}},{"id":"a062-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-08"],"title":"評估光阻去除對低 k 的損傷","titleEn":"Assess low-k damage during resist removal","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：去膠可能改變表面組成與介電性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Stripping can change surface composition and permittivity.","instruction":"評估光阻去除對低 k 的損傷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「去膠可能改變表面組成與介電性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess low-k damage during resist removal. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Stripping can change surface composition and permittivity.","observation":"去膠可能改變表面組成與介電性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Stripping can change surface composition and permittivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估光阻去除對低 k 的損傷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「去膠可能改變表面組成與介電性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess low-k damage during resist removal\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Stripping can change surface composition and permittivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"去膠可能改變表面組成與介電性。","textEn":"Stripping can change surface composition and permittivity."},{"id":"a062-v8-09-k2","title":"蝕刻與襯層的原理與限制","titleEn":"Etch and liners: principle and limits","text":"線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","textEn":"Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估光阻去除對低 k 的損傷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess low-k damage during resist removal\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","去膠可能改變表面組成與介電性。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","A planar surface rules out internal voids.","Stripping can change surface composition and permittivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去膠可能改變表面組成與介電性。 線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","explanationEn":"Stripping can change surface composition and permittivity. Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}},{"id":"a062-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-09"],"title":"檢查下層銅表面氧化與殘留","titleEn":"Inspect lower-copper oxidation and residue","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：接點介面污染可能增加通孔電阻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Interface contamination can increase via resistance.","instruction":"檢查下層銅表面氧化與殘留。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「接點介面污染可能增加通孔電阻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect lower-copper oxidation and residue. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Interface contamination can increase via resistance.","observation":"接點介面污染可能增加通孔電阻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Interface contamination can increase via resistance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查下層銅表面氧化與殘留」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「接點介面污染可能增加通孔電阻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect lower-copper oxidation and residue\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Interface contamination can increase via resistance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"接點介面污染可能增加通孔電阻。","textEn":"Interface contamination can increase via resistance."},{"id":"a062-v8-10-k2","title":"蝕刻與襯層的原理與限制","titleEn":"Etch and liners: principle and limits","text":"線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","textEn":"Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查下層銅表面氧化與殘留」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect lower-copper oxidation and residue\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["接點介面污染可能增加通孔電阻。","阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Interface contamination can increase via resistance.","Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","A planar surface rules out internal voids."],"answer":0,"explanation":"接點介面污染可能增加通孔電阻。 線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","explanationEn":"Interface contamination can increase via resistance. Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}},{"id":"a062-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-10"],"title":"畫出阻障層與種子層的位置","titleEn":"Draw barrier and seed-layer locations","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：阻擴散與供電鍍起始是不同功能。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Diffusion blocking and plating initiation are different functions.","instruction":"畫出阻障層與種子層的位置。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「阻擴散與供電鍍起始是不同功能。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw barrier and seed-layer locations. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Diffusion blocking and plating initiation are different functions.","observation":"阻擴散與供電鍍起始是不同功能。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Diffusion blocking and plating initiation are different functions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出阻障層與種子層的位置」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「阻擴散與供電鍍起始是不同功能。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw barrier and seed-layer locations\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Diffusion blocking and plating initiation are different functions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"阻擴散與供電鍍起始是不同功能。","textEn":"Diffusion blocking and plating initiation are different functions."},{"id":"a062-v8-11-k2","title":"蝕刻與襯層的原理與限制","titleEn":"Etch and liners: principle and limits","text":"線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","textEn":"Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出阻障層與種子層的位置」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw barrier and seed-layer locations\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","阻擴散與供電鍍起始是不同功能。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","Diffusion blocking and plating initiation are different functions.","A planar surface rules out internal voids."],"answer":1,"explanation":"阻擴散與供電鍍起始是不同功能。 線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","explanationEn":"Diffusion blocking and plating initiation are different functions. Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}},{"id":"a062-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-11"],"title":"比較側壁與孔底覆蓋比例","titleEn":"Compare wall and bottom coverage ratios","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：最薄位置可能決定失效。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The thinnest region can determine failure.","instruction":"比較側壁與孔底覆蓋比例。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「最薄位置可能決定失效。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare wall and bottom coverage ratios. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: The thinnest region can determine failure.","observation":"最薄位置可能決定失效。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The thinnest region can determine failure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較側壁與孔底覆蓋比例」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「最薄位置可能決定失效。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare wall and bottom coverage ratios\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The thinnest region can determine failure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"最薄位置可能決定失效。","textEn":"The thinnest region can determine failure."},{"id":"a062-v8-12-k2","title":"蝕刻與襯層的原理與限制","titleEn":"Etch and liners: principle and limits","text":"線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","textEn":"Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較側壁與孔底覆蓋比例」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare wall and bottom coverage ratios\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["阻障層越厚越不需要考慮電阻。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","最薄位置可能決定失效。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker barriers remove resistance concerns.","A planar surface rules out internal voids.","The thinnest region can determine failure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"最薄位置可能決定失效。 線槽、通孔、停止層與阻障之間的介面決定可填充性。","explanationEn":"The thinnest region can determine failure. Interfaces among trenches, vias, stops and barriers determine fillability."}}]},{"id":"a062-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"填銅與平坦化","titleEn":"Copper fill and planarization","description":"填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","descriptionEn":"Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts.","steps":[{"id":"a062-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-12"],"title":"用截面追蹤自底向上的銅填充","titleEn":"Trace bottom-up copper fill in sections","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：超共形填充可避免過早封口。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Superconformal fill can avoid premature closure.","instruction":"用截面追蹤自底向上的銅填充。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「超共形填充可避免過早封口。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace bottom-up copper fill in sections. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Superconformal fill can avoid premature closure.","observation":"超共形填充可避免過早封口。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Superconformal fill can avoid premature closure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面平坦可排除內部空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A planar surface rules out internal voids.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用截面追蹤自底向上的銅填充」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「超共形填充可避免過早封口。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace bottom-up copper fill in sections\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Superconformal fill can avoid premature closure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"超共形填充可避免過早封口。","textEn":"Superconformal fill can avoid premature closure."},{"id":"a062-v8-13-k2","title":"填銅與平坦化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Copper fill and planarization: principle and limits","text":"填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","textEn":"Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用截面追蹤自底向上的銅填充」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace bottom-up copper fill in sections\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["超共形填充可避免過早封口。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。"],"optionsEn":["Superconformal fill can avoid premature closure.","A planar surface rules out internal voids.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"超共形填充可避免過早封口。 填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","explanationEn":"Superconformal fill can avoid premature closure. Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}},{"id":"a062-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-13"],"title":"辨識接縫、空洞與未連續種子","titleEn":"Distinguish seams, voids and seed discontinuity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相似高阻結果可能有不同起因。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Similar high resistance can have different causes.","instruction":"辨識接縫、空洞與未連續種子。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「相似高阻結果可能有不同起因。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish seams, voids and seed discontinuity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Similar high resistance can have different causes.","observation":"相似高阻結果可能有不同起因。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Similar high resistance can have different causes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面平坦可排除內部空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A planar surface rules out internal voids.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「辨識接縫、空洞與未連續種子」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相似高阻結果可能有不同起因。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish seams, voids and seed discontinuity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Similar high resistance can have different causes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相似高阻結果可能有不同起因。","textEn":"Similar high resistance can have different causes."},{"id":"a062-v8-14-k2","title":"填銅與平坦化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Copper fill and planarization: principle and limits","text":"填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","textEn":"Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「辨識接縫、空洞與未連續種子」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish seams, voids and seed discontinuity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","相似高阻結果可能有不同起因。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。"],"optionsEn":["A planar surface rules out internal voids.","Similar high resistance can have different causes.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相似高阻結果可能有不同起因。 填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","explanationEn":"Similar high resistance can have different causes. Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}},{"id":"a062-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-14"],"title":"比較電鍍厚度與頂部過鍍","titleEn":"Compare plated thickness with overburden","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：填孔與表面過鍍需共同控制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Feature fill and overburden need joint control.","instruction":"比較電鍍厚度與頂部過鍍。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「填孔與表面過鍍需共同控制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare plated thickness with overburden. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Feature fill and overburden need joint control.","observation":"填孔與表面過鍍需共同控制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Feature fill and overburden need joint control. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面平坦可排除內部空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A planar surface rules out internal voids.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較電鍍厚度與頂部過鍍」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「填孔與表面過鍍需共同控制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare plated thickness with overburden\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Feature fill and overburden need joint control.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"填孔與表面過鍍需共同控制。","textEn":"Feature fill and overburden need joint control."},{"id":"a062-v8-15-k2","title":"填銅與平坦化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Copper fill and planarization: principle and limits","text":"填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","textEn":"Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較電鍍厚度與頂部過鍍」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare plated thickness with overburden\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","填孔與表面過鍍需共同控制。"],"optionsEn":["A planar surface rules out internal voids.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Feature fill and overburden need joint control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"填孔與表面過鍍需共同控制。 填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","explanationEn":"Feature fill and overburden need joint control. Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}},{"id":"a062-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-15"],"title":"畫出 CMP 先去銅再處理阻障","titleEn":"Sketch copper and barrier CMP stages","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同材料移除需避免相對高度失控。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Removing different materials requires height control.","instruction":"畫出 CMP 先去銅再處理阻障。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「不同材料移除需避免相對高度失控。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch copper and barrier CMP stages. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Removing different materials requires height control.","observation":"不同材料移除需避免相對高度失控。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Removing different materials requires height control. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面平坦可排除內部空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A planar surface rules out internal voids.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出 CMP 先去銅再處理阻障」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同材料移除需避免相對高度失控。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch copper and barrier CMP stages\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Removing different materials requires height control.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同材料移除需避免相對高度失控。","textEn":"Removing different materials requires height control."},{"id":"a062-v8-16-k2","title":"填銅與平坦化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Copper fill and planarization: principle and limits","text":"填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","textEn":"Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出 CMP 先去銅再處理阻障」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch copper and barrier CMP stages\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同材料移除需避免相對高度失控。","表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。"],"optionsEn":["Removing different materials requires height control.","A planar surface rules out internal voids.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同材料移除需避免相對高度失控。 填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","explanationEn":"Removing different materials requires height control. Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}},{"id":"a062-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-16"],"title":"量測線寬相關凹陷與圖形密度侵蝕","titleEn":"Measure width-dependent dishing and density-dependent erosion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部版圖影響平坦化結果。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local layout affects planarization.","instruction":"量測線寬相關凹陷與圖形密度侵蝕。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「局部版圖影響平坦化結果。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure width-dependent dishing and density-dependent erosion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local layout affects planarization.","observation":"局部版圖影響平坦化結果。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local layout affects planarization. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面平坦可排除內部空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A planar surface rules out internal voids.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測線寬相關凹陷與圖形密度侵蝕」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部版圖影響平坦化結果。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure width-dependent dishing and density-dependent erosion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local layout affects planarization.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部版圖影響平坦化結果。","textEn":"Local layout affects planarization."},{"id":"a062-v8-17-k2","title":"填銅與平坦化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Copper fill and planarization: principle and limits","text":"填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","textEn":"Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測線寬相關凹陷與圖形密度侵蝕」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure width-dependent dishing and density-dependent erosion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","局部版圖影響平坦化結果。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。"],"optionsEn":["A planar surface rules out internal voids.","Local layout affects planarization.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部版圖影響平坦化結果。 填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","explanationEn":"Local layout affects planarization. Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}},{"id":"a062-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-17"],"title":"檢查金屬殘留與後清潔腐蝕","titleEn":"Inspect metal residue and post-clean corrosion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：清潔與平坦化共同影響短路與可靠度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cleaning and planarization jointly affect shorts and reliability.","instruction":"檢查金屬殘留與後清潔腐蝕。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「清潔與平坦化共同影響短路與可靠度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect metal residue and post-clean corrosion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cleaning and planarization jointly affect shorts and reliability.","observation":"清潔與平坦化共同影響短路與可靠度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cleaning and planarization jointly affect shorts and reliability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面平坦可排除內部空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A planar surface rules out internal voids.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查金屬殘留與後清潔腐蝕」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「清潔與平坦化共同影響短路與可靠度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect metal residue and post-clean corrosion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cleaning and planarization jointly affect shorts and reliability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"清潔與平坦化共同影響短路與可靠度。","textEn":"Cleaning and planarization jointly affect shorts and reliability."},{"id":"a062-v8-18-k2","title":"填銅與平坦化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Copper fill and planarization: principle and limits","text":"填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","textEn":"Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查金屬殘留與後清潔腐蝕」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect metal residue and post-clean corrosion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面平坦可排除內部空洞。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","清潔與平坦化共同影響短路與可靠度。"],"optionsEn":["A planar surface rules out internal voids.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Cleaning and planarization jointly affect shorts and reliability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"清潔與平坦化共同影響短路與可靠度。 填滿與平坦化需避免空洞、凹陷及殘留短路。","explanationEn":"Cleaning and planarization jointly affect shorts and reliability. Fill and planarization must avoid voids, dishing and residual shorts."}}]},{"id":"a062-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"RC 與可靠度","titleEn":"RC and reliability","description":"互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","descriptionEn":"Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together.","steps":[{"id":"a062-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-18"],"title":"以線電阻分離幾何與材料貢獻","titleEn":"Separate geometric and material contributions to line resistance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：有效截面包括襯層占用。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Effective cross section accounts for liner occupancy.","instruction":"以線電阻分離幾何與材料貢獻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「有效截面包括襯層占用。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設線槽寬 40 nm、高 60 nm，兩側與底部各由 3 nm 非銅襯層占用，不計頂部帽層。銅截面為 (40-6)(60-3)=1938 nm²，而外部截面為 2400 nm²。若銅電阻率與長度固定，襯層占用使電阻相對理想全銅增加 2400/1938-1≈23.8%。這尚未計入尺寸散射與接觸電阻。","instructionEn":"Separate geometric and material contributions to line resistance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Effective cross section accounts for liner occupancy.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a 40 nm wide, 60 nm tall trench with 3 nm non-copper liners on both sides and bottom, excluding a top cap. Copper area is (40-6)(60-3)=1938 nm² versus 2400 nm² external area. With fixed copper resistivity and length, liner occupancy raises resistance by 2400/1938-1≈23.8% over ideal all-copper. Size scattering and contact resistance are excluded.","observation":"有效截面包括襯層占用。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 1938 nm² 與 23.8%，標出襯層位於兩側和底部。","observationEn":"Effective cross section accounts for liner occupancy. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 1938 nm² and 23.8%, marking liners on both sides and bottom.","failure":"若報告假設「只有直流電阻決定互連效能。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以線電阻分離幾何與材料貢獻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「有效截面包括襯層占用。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 1938 nm² 與 23.8%，標出襯層位於兩側和底部。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate geometric and material contributions to line resistance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Effective cross section accounts for liner occupancy.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 1938 nm² and 23.8%, marking liners on both sides and bottom.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"有效截面包括襯層占用。","textEn":"Effective cross section accounts for liner occupancy."},{"id":"a062-v8-19-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設線槽寬 40 nm、高 60 nm，兩側與底部各由 3 nm 非銅襯層占用，不計頂部帽層。銅截面為 (40-6)(60-3)=1938 nm²，而外部截面為 2400 nm²。若銅電阻率與長度固定，襯層占用使電阻相對理想全銅增加 2400/1938-1≈23.8%。這尚未計入尺寸散射與接觸電阻。","textEn":"Assume a 40 nm wide, 60 nm tall trench with 3 nm non-copper liners on both sides and bottom, excluding a top cap. Copper area is (40-6)(60-3)=1938 nm² versus 2400 nm² external area. With fixed copper resistivity and length, liner occupancy raises resistance by 2400/1938-1≈23.8% over ideal all-copper. Size scattering and contact resistance are excluded."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以線電阻分離幾何與材料貢獻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate geometric and material contributions to line resistance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["有效截面包括襯層占用。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。"],"optionsEn":["Effective cross section accounts for liner occupancy.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"有效截面包括襯層占用。 互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","explanationEn":"Effective cross section accounts for liner occupancy. Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設線槽寬 40 nm、高 60 nm，兩側與底部各由 3 nm 非銅襯層占用，不計頂部帽層。銅截面為 (40-6)(60-3)=1938 nm²，而外部截面為 2400 nm²。若銅電阻率與長度固定，襯層占用使電阻相對理想全銅增加 2400/1938-1≈23.8%。這尚未計入尺寸散射與接觸電阻。","textEn":"Assume a 40 nm wide, 60 nm tall trench with 3 nm non-copper liners on both sides and bottom, excluding a top cap. Copper area is (40-6)(60-3)=1938 nm² versus 2400 nm² external area. With fixed copper resistivity and length, liner occupancy raises resistance by 2400/1938-1≈23.8% over ideal all-copper. Size scattering and contact resistance are excluded.","check":"交付 1938 nm² 與 23.8%，標出襯層位於兩側和底部。","checkEn":"Report 1938 nm² and 23.8%, marking liners on both sides and bottom."}},{"id":"a062-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-19"],"title":"以 Kelvin 通孔量測分離接觸損失","titleEn":"Use Kelvin via structures to separate contact loss","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：四端量測降低引線影響。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Four-terminal measurement reduces lead effects.","instruction":"以 Kelvin 通孔量測分離接觸損失。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「四端量測降低引線影響。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use Kelvin via structures to separate contact loss. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Four-terminal measurement reduces lead effects.","observation":"四端量測降低引線影響。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Four-terminal measurement reduces lead effects. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有直流電阻決定互連效能。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以 Kelvin 通孔量測分離接觸損失」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「四端量測降低引線影響。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use Kelvin via structures to separate contact loss\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Four-terminal measurement reduces lead effects.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"四端量測降低引線影響。","textEn":"Four-terminal measurement reduces lead effects."},{"id":"a062-v8-20-k2","title":"RC 與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"RC and reliability: principle and limits","text":"互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","textEn":"Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以 Kelvin 通孔量測分離接觸損失」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use Kelvin via structures to separate contact loss\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","四端量測降低引線影響。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。"],"optionsEn":["DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Four-terminal measurement reduces lead effects.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"四端量測降低引線影響。 互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","explanationEn":"Four-terminal measurement reduces lead effects. Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}},{"id":"a062-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-20"],"title":"以梳狀結構量測線間漏電","titleEn":"Measure interline leakage using comb structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：介電損傷可能在電性上才明顯。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Dielectric damage may become clear only electrically.","instruction":"以梳狀結構量測線間漏電。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「介電損傷可能在電性上才明顯。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure interline leakage using comb structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Dielectric damage may become clear only electrically.","observation":"介電損傷可能在電性上才明顯。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Dielectric damage may become clear only electrically. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有直流電阻決定互連效能。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以梳狀結構量測線間漏電」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「介電損傷可能在電性上才明顯。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure interline leakage using comb structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Dielectric damage may become clear only electrically.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"介電損傷可能在電性上才明顯。","textEn":"Dielectric damage may become clear only electrically."},{"id":"a062-v8-21-k2","title":"RC 與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"RC and reliability: principle and limits","text":"互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","textEn":"Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以梳狀結構量測線間漏電」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure interline leakage using comb structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","介電損傷可能在電性上才明顯。"],"optionsEn":["DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Dielectric damage may become clear only electrically."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電損傷可能在電性上才明顯。 互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","explanationEn":"Dielectric damage may become clear only electrically. Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}},{"id":"a062-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-21"],"title":"評估電遷移的電流密度與溫度","titleEn":"Assess current density and temperature in electromigration","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：壽命比較需一致應力條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Lifetime comparisons need matching stress conditions.","instruction":"評估電遷移的電流密度與溫度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「壽命比較需一致應力條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess current density and temperature in electromigration. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Lifetime comparisons need matching stress conditions.","observation":"壽命比較需一致應力條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Lifetime comparisons need matching stress conditions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有直流電阻決定互連效能。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估電遷移的電流密度與溫度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「壽命比較需一致應力條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess current density and temperature in electromigration\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Lifetime comparisons need matching stress conditions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"壽命比較需一致應力條件。","textEn":"Lifetime comparisons need matching stress conditions."},{"id":"a062-v8-22-k2","title":"RC 與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"RC and reliability: principle and limits","text":"互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","textEn":"Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估電遷移的電流密度與溫度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess current density and temperature in electromigration\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["壽命比較需一致應力條件。","只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。"],"optionsEn":["Lifetime comparisons need matching stress conditions.","DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias."],"answer":0,"explanation":"壽命比較需一致應力條件。 互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","explanationEn":"Lifetime comparisons need matching stress conditions. Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}},{"id":"a062-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-22"],"title":"比較銅雙鑲嵌與釕半鑲嵌","titleEn":"Compare copper dual damascene with ruthenium semi-damascene","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同金屬可能搭配不同圖案形成方式。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different metals can use different patterning schemes.","instruction":"比較銅雙鑲嵌與釕半鑲嵌。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「不同金屬可能搭配不同圖案形成方式。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare copper dual damascene with ruthenium semi-damascene. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different metals can use different patterning schemes.","observation":"不同金屬可能搭配不同圖案形成方式。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different metals can use different patterning schemes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有直流電阻決定互連效能。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較銅雙鑲嵌與釕半鑲嵌」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同金屬可能搭配不同圖案形成方式。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare copper dual damascene with ruthenium semi-damascene\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different metals can use different patterning schemes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同金屬可能搭配不同圖案形成方式。","textEn":"Different metals can use different patterning schemes."},{"id":"a062-v8-23-k2","title":"RC 與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"RC and reliability: principle and limits","text":"互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","textEn":"Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較銅雙鑲嵌與釕半鑲嵌」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare copper dual damascene with ruthenium semi-damascene\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","不同金屬可能搭配不同圖案形成方式。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。"],"optionsEn":["DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Different metals can use different patterning schemes.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同金屬可能搭配不同圖案形成方式。 互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","explanationEn":"Different metals can use different patterning schemes. Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}},{"id":"a062-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-copperhistory","v8b-plating","v8b-semidam","v8b-wiring"],"prerequisiteIds":["a062-v8-23"],"title":"交付兩層互連的 RC 與失效審查","titleEn":"Deliver a two-level RC and failure review","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部製程合格仍需跨層功能驗證。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local process acceptance still needs cross-layer functional validation.","instruction":"交付兩層互連的 RC 與失效審查。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「局部製程合格仍需跨層功能驗證。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver a two-level RC and failure review. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local process acceptance still needs cross-layer functional validation.","observation":"局部製程合格仍需跨層功能驗證。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local process acceptance still needs cross-layer functional validation. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只有直流電阻決定互連效能。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付兩層互連的 RC 與失效審查」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部製程合格仍需跨層功能驗證。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver a two-level RC and failure review\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local process acceptance still needs cross-layer functional validation.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a062-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部製程合格仍需跨層功能驗證。","textEn":"Local process acceptance still needs cross-layer functional validation."},{"id":"a062-v8-24-k2","title":"RC 與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"RC and reliability: principle and limits","text":"互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","textEn":"Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付兩層互連的 RC 與失效審查」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver a two-level RC and failure review\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只有直流電阻決定互連效能。","雙鑲嵌就是直接蝕刻厚銅形成所有線孔。","局部製程合格仍需跨層功能驗證。"],"optionsEn":["DC resistance alone determines interconnect performance.","Dual damascene directly etches thick copper into all lines and vias.","Local process acceptance still needs cross-layer functional validation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部製程合格仍需跨層功能驗證。 互連效能同時受電阻、電容與可靠度限制。","explanationEn":"Local process acceptance still needs cross-layer functional validation. Interconnect performance is constrained by resistance, capacitance and reliability together."}}]}]},{"id":"a063","title":"鈷與釕互連研究","titleEn":"Cobalt and ruthenium interconnect research","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究尺度與材料、整合路線、電阻與介面、可靠度比較；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: scaling and materials, integration routes, resistance and interfaces, reliability comparison. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["尺度與材料","整合路線","電阻與介面","可靠度比較"],"labelsEn":["Scaling and materials","Integration routes","Resistance and interfaces","Reliability comparison"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability","stages":[{"id":"a063-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"尺度與材料","titleEn":"Scaling and materials","description":"奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","descriptionEn":"Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter.","steps":[{"id":"a063-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"比較塊材與奈米線的電阻率概念","titleEn":"Compare bulk and nanoscale-wire resistivity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：尺寸效應會改變材料排序。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Size effects can change material rankings.","instruction":"比較塊材與奈米線的電阻率概念。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「尺寸效應會改變材料排序。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare bulk and nanoscale-wire resistivity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Size effects can change material rankings.","observation":"尺寸效應會改變材料排序。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Size effects can change material rankings. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較塊材與奈米線的電阻率概念」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「尺寸效應會改變材料排序。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare bulk and nanoscale-wire resistivity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Size effects can change material rankings.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"尺寸效應會改變材料排序。","textEn":"Size effects can change material rankings."},{"id":"a063-v8-01-k2","title":"尺度與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scaling and materials: principle and limits","text":"奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","textEn":"Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較塊材與奈米線的電阻率概念」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare bulk and nanoscale-wire resistivity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["尺寸效應會改變材料排序。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。"],"optionsEn":["Size effects can change material rankings.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Changing metal requires no process changes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"尺寸效應會改變材料排序。 奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","explanationEn":"Size effects can change material rankings. Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}},{"id":"a063-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-01"],"title":"畫出阻障占比隨線寬縮小的變化","titleEn":"Plot barrier fraction as linewidth shrinks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：非導電或高阻襯層會占用截面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Nonconducting or resistive liners consume cross section.","instruction":"畫出阻障占比隨線寬縮小的變化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「非導電或高阻襯層會占用截面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Plot barrier fraction as linewidth shrinks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Nonconducting or resistive liners consume cross section.","observation":"非導電或高阻襯層會占用截面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Nonconducting or resistive liners consume cross section. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出阻障占比隨線寬縮小的變化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「非導電或高阻襯層會占用截面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Plot barrier fraction as linewidth shrinks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Nonconducting or resistive liners consume cross section.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"非導電或高阻襯層會占用截面。","textEn":"Nonconducting or resistive liners consume cross section."},{"id":"a063-v8-02-k2","title":"尺度與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scaling and materials: principle and limits","text":"奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","textEn":"Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出阻障占比隨線寬縮小的變化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Plot barrier fraction as linewidth shrinks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","非導電或高阻襯層會占用截面。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。"],"optionsEn":["The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Nonconducting or resistive liners consume cross section.","Changing metal requires no process changes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"非導電或高阻襯層會占用截面。 奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","explanationEn":"Nonconducting or resistive liners consume cross section. Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}},{"id":"a063-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-02"],"title":"分開表面散射與晶界散射","titleEn":"Separate surface and grain-boundary scattering","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩者對微結構的依賴不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: They depend differently on microstructure.","instruction":"分開表面散射與晶界散射。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「兩者對微結構的依賴不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate surface and grain-boundary scattering. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: They depend differently on microstructure.","observation":"兩者對微結構的依賴不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"They depend differently on microstructure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開表面散射與晶界散射」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩者對微結構的依賴不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate surface and grain-boundary scattering\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"They depend differently on microstructure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩者對微結構的依賴不同。","textEn":"They depend differently on microstructure."},{"id":"a063-v8-03-k2","title":"尺度與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scaling and materials: principle and limits","text":"奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","textEn":"Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開表面散射與晶界散射」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate surface and grain-boundary scattering\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","兩者對微結構的依賴不同。"],"optionsEn":["The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Changing metal requires no process changes.","They depend differently on microstructure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩者對微結構的依賴不同。 奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","explanationEn":"They depend differently on microstructure. Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}},{"id":"a063-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-03"],"title":"比較 Cu、Co 與 Ru 的整合問題","titleEn":"Compare integration issues for Cu, Co and Ru","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料優勢與可製造性必須共同評估。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material advantages and manufacturability need joint assessment.","instruction":"比較 Cu、Co 與 Ru 的整合問題。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「材料優勢與可製造性必須共同評估。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare integration issues for Cu, Co and Ru. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material advantages and manufacturability need joint assessment.","observation":"材料優勢與可製造性必須共同評估。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material advantages and manufacturability need joint assessment. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 Cu、Co 與 Ru 的整合問題」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料優勢與可製造性必須共同評估。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare integration issues for Cu, Co and Ru\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material advantages and manufacturability need joint assessment.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料優勢與可製造性必須共同評估。","textEn":"Material advantages and manufacturability need joint assessment."},{"id":"a063-v8-04-k2","title":"尺度與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scaling and materials: principle and limits","text":"奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","textEn":"Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 Cu、Co 與 Ru 的整合問題」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare integration issues for Cu, Co and Ru\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料優勢與可製造性必須共同評估。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。"],"optionsEn":["Material advantages and manufacturability need joint assessment.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Changing metal requires no process changes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料優勢與可製造性必須共同評估。 奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","explanationEn":"Material advantages and manufacturability need joint assessment. Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}},{"id":"a063-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-04"],"title":"選定線、通孔或接點的研究範圍","titleEn":"Choose a line, via or contact study scope","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同位置不能直接套用同一比較。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different locations cannot share an unqualified comparison.","instruction":"選定線、通孔或接點的研究範圍。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「不同位置不能直接套用同一比較。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Choose a line, via or contact study scope. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different locations cannot share an unqualified comparison.","observation":"不同位置不能直接套用同一比較。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different locations cannot share an unqualified comparison. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「選定線、通孔或接點的研究範圍」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同位置不能直接套用同一比較。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Choose a line, via or contact study scope\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different locations cannot share an unqualified comparison.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同位置不能直接套用同一比較。","textEn":"Different locations cannot share an unqualified comparison."},{"id":"a063-v8-05-k2","title":"尺度與材料的原理與限制","titleEn":"Scaling and materials: principle and limits","text":"奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","textEn":"Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「選定線、通孔或接點的研究範圍」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Choose a line, via or contact study scope\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","不同位置不能直接套用同一比較。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。"],"optionsEn":["The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Different locations cannot share an unqualified comparison.","Changing metal requires no process changes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同位置不能直接套用同一比較。 奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","explanationEn":"Different locations cannot share an unqualified comparison. Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."}},{"id":"a063-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-05"],"title":"建立相同有效截面的公平基準","titleEn":"Build a fair benchmark at matched conducting area","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：名目線寬相同未必導電面積相同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Equal nominal width need not mean equal conducting area.","instruction":"建立相同有效截面的公平基準。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「名目線寬相同未必導電面積相同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：以同一外框 20×30 nm² 比較假想材料。Cu 有兩側與底部 3 nm 襯層，導電面積 14×27=378 nm²，有效ρ=4 μΩ·cm；無襯層候選金屬面積600 nm²、有效ρ=6 μΩ·cm。相同線長下比較 ρ/A，比例為 (6/600)/(4/378)=0.945；較高ρ的候選反而低阻約5.5%。這不證明無襯層可靠，須另驗證擴散與附著。","instructionEn":"Build a fair benchmark at matched conducting area. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Equal nominal width need not mean equal conducting area.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Compare hypothetical materials in the same 20×30 nm² footprint. Cu has 3 nm side/bottom liners, conducting area 14×27=378 nm² and effective ρ=4 μΩ·cm. A linerless candidate has area 600 nm² and effective ρ=6 μΩ·cm. At equal length, resistance ratio is (6/600)/(4/378)=0.945: the higher-ρ candidate is about 5.5% lower in resistance. This does not prove linerless reliability; diffusion and adhesion need separate tests.","observation":"名目線寬相同未必導電面積相同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n算出 0.945 並指出材料數字為假設、外框相同但有效截面不同。","observationEn":"Equal nominal width need not mean equal conducting area. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nCalculate 0.945 and state that values are hypothetical and footprints match while conducting areas differ.","failure":"若報告假設「塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立相同有效截面的公平基準」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「名目線寬相同未必導電面積相同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：算出 0.945 並指出材料數字為假設、外框相同但有效截面不同。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a fair benchmark at matched conducting area\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Equal nominal width need not mean equal conducting area.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Calculate 0.945 and state that values are hypothetical and footprints match while conducting areas differ.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"名目線寬相同未必導電面積相同。","textEn":"Equal nominal width need not mean equal conducting area."},{"id":"a063-v8-06-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"以同一外框 20×30 nm² 比較假想材料。Cu 有兩側與底部 3 nm 襯層，導電面積 14×27=378 nm²，有效ρ=4 μΩ·cm；無襯層候選金屬面積600 nm²、有效ρ=6 μΩ·cm。相同線長下比較 ρ/A，比例為 (6/600)/(4/378)=0.945；較高ρ的候選反而低阻約5.5%。這不證明無襯層可靠，須另驗證擴散與附著。","textEn":"Compare hypothetical materials in the same 20×30 nm² footprint. Cu has 3 nm side/bottom liners, conducting area 14×27=378 nm² and effective ρ=4 μΩ·cm. A linerless candidate has area 600 nm² and effective ρ=6 μΩ·cm. At equal length, resistance ratio is (6/600)/(4/378)=0.945: the higher-ρ candidate is about 5.5% lower in resistance. This does not prove linerless reliability; diffusion and adhesion need separate tests."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立相同有效截面的公平基準」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a fair benchmark at matched conducting area\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","名目線寬相同未必導電面積相同。"],"optionsEn":["The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Changing metal requires no process changes.","Equal nominal width need not mean equal conducting area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"名目線寬相同未必導電面積相同。 奈米線電阻不能只依塊材電阻率排名，表面散射與有效截面很重要。","explanationEn":"Equal nominal width need not mean equal conducting area. Nanoscale line resistance cannot be ranked by bulk resistivity alone; surface scattering and effective area matter."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"以同一外框 20×30 nm² 比較假想材料。Cu 有兩側與底部 3 nm 襯層，導電面積 14×27=378 nm²，有效ρ=4 μΩ·cm；無襯層候選金屬面積600 nm²、有效ρ=6 μΩ·cm。相同線長下比較 ρ/A，比例為 (6/600)/(4/378)=0.945；較高ρ的候選反而低阻約5.5%。這不證明無襯層可靠，須另驗證擴散與附著。","textEn":"Compare hypothetical materials in the same 20×30 nm² footprint. Cu has 3 nm side/bottom liners, conducting area 14×27=378 nm² and effective ρ=4 μΩ·cm. A linerless candidate has area 600 nm² and effective ρ=6 μΩ·cm. At equal length, resistance ratio is (6/600)/(4/378)=0.945: the higher-ρ candidate is about 5.5% lower in resistance. This does not prove linerless reliability; diffusion and adhesion need separate tests.","check":"算出 0.945 並指出材料數字為假設、外框相同但有效截面不同。","checkEn":"Calculate 0.945 and state that values are hypothetical and footprints match while conducting areas differ."}}]},{"id":"a063-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"整合路線","titleEn":"Integration routes","description":"替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","descriptionEn":"Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration.","steps":[{"id":"a063-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-06"],"title":"比較鑲嵌填充與減法金屬蝕刻","titleEn":"Compare damascene fill with subtractive metal etch","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料可蝕刻性影響路線選擇。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Metal etchability influences integration choice.","instruction":"比較鑲嵌填充與減法金屬蝕刻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「材料可蝕刻性影響路線選擇。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare damascene fill with subtractive metal etch. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Metal etchability influences integration choice.","observation":"材料可蝕刻性影響路線選擇。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Metal etchability influences integration choice. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「更換金屬不需要改任何製程。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Changing metal requires no process changes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較鑲嵌填充與減法金屬蝕刻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料可蝕刻性影響路線選擇。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare damascene fill with subtractive metal etch\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Metal etchability influences integration choice.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料可蝕刻性影響路線選擇。","textEn":"Metal etchability influences integration choice."},{"id":"a063-v8-07-k2","title":"整合路線的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration routes: principle and limits","text":"替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","textEn":"Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較鑲嵌填充與減法金屬蝕刻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare damascene fill with subtractive metal etch\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料可蝕刻性影響路線選擇。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。"],"optionsEn":["Metal etchability influences integration choice.","Changing metal requires no process changes.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料可蝕刻性影響路線選擇。 替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","explanationEn":"Metal etchability influences integration choice. Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}},{"id":"a063-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-07"],"title":"畫出半鑲嵌的通孔與上層線","titleEn":"Draw vias and upper lines in semi-damascene","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：通孔填充與上層金屬可在相關步驟形成。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Via fill and upper metal can be formed in related steps.","instruction":"畫出半鑲嵌的通孔與上層線。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「通孔填充與上層金屬可在相關步驟形成。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw vias and upper lines in semi-damascene. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Via fill and upper metal can be formed in related steps.","observation":"通孔填充與上層金屬可在相關步驟形成。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Via fill and upper metal can be formed in related steps. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「更換金屬不需要改任何製程。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Changing metal requires no process changes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出半鑲嵌的通孔與上層線」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「通孔填充與上層金屬可在相關步驟形成。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw vias and upper lines in semi-damascene\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Via fill and upper metal can be formed in related steps.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"通孔填充與上層金屬可在相關步驟形成。","textEn":"Via fill and upper metal can be formed in related steps."},{"id":"a063-v8-08-k2","title":"整合路線的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration routes: principle and limits","text":"替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","textEn":"Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出半鑲嵌的通孔與上層線」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw vias and upper lines in semi-damascene\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","通孔填充與上層金屬可在相關步驟形成。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。"],"optionsEn":["Changing metal requires no process changes.","Via fill and upper metal can be formed in related steps.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"通孔填充與上層金屬可在相關步驟形成。 替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","explanationEn":"Via fill and upper metal can be formed in related steps. Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}},{"id":"a063-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-08"],"title":"評估自對準通孔的落點保護","titleEn":"Assess landing protection from self-aligned vias","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：自對準仍有材料選擇性與形貌要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Self-alignment still needs material selectivity and profile control.","instruction":"評估自對準通孔的落點保護。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「自對準仍有材料選擇性與形貌要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess landing protection from self-aligned vias. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Self-alignment still needs material selectivity and profile control.","observation":"自對準仍有材料選擇性與形貌要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Self-alignment still needs material selectivity and profile control. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「更換金屬不需要改任何製程。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Changing metal requires no process changes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估自對準通孔的落點保護」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「自對準仍有材料選擇性與形貌要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess landing protection from self-aligned vias\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Self-alignment still needs material selectivity and profile control.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"自對準仍有材料選擇性與形貌要求。","textEn":"Self-alignment still needs material selectivity and profile control."},{"id":"a063-v8-09-k2","title":"整合路線的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration routes: principle and limits","text":"替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","textEn":"Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估自對準通孔的落點保護」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess landing protection from self-aligned vias\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","自對準仍有材料選擇性與形貌要求。"],"optionsEn":["Changing metal requires no process changes.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","Self-alignment still needs material selectivity and profile control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"自對準仍有材料選擇性與形貌要求。 替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","explanationEn":"Self-alignment still needs material selectivity and profile control. Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}},{"id":"a063-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-09"],"title":"比較有襯層與無襯層的材料風險","titleEn":"Compare lined and linerless material risks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：省去襯層需證明擴散與黏著相容。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Removing liners requires diffusion and adhesion evidence.","instruction":"比較有襯層與無襯層的材料風險。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「省去襯層需證明擴散與黏著相容。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare lined and linerless material risks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Removing liners requires diffusion and adhesion evidence.","observation":"省去襯層需證明擴散與黏著相容。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Removing liners requires diffusion and adhesion evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「更換金屬不需要改任何製程。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Changing metal requires no process changes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較有襯層與無襯層的材料風險」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「省去襯層需證明擴散與黏著相容。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare lined and linerless material risks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Removing liners requires diffusion and adhesion evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"省去襯層需證明擴散與黏著相容。","textEn":"Removing liners requires diffusion and adhesion evidence."},{"id":"a063-v8-10-k2","title":"整合路線的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration routes: principle and limits","text":"替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","textEn":"Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較有襯層與無襯層的材料風險」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare lined and linerless material risks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["省去襯層需證明擴散與黏著相容。","更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。"],"optionsEn":["Removing liners requires diffusion and adhesion evidence.","Changing metal requires no process changes.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"省去襯層需證明擴散與黏著相容。 替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","explanationEn":"Removing liners requires diffusion and adhesion evidence. Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}},{"id":"a063-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-10"],"title":"檢查金屬成核與連續膜形成","titleEn":"Assess nucleation and continuous-film formation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：薄膜早期可能是不連續島狀。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Early films can consist of disconnected islands.","instruction":"檢查金屬成核與連續膜形成。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「薄膜早期可能是不連續島狀。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess nucleation and continuous-film formation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Early films can consist of disconnected islands.","observation":"薄膜早期可能是不連續島狀。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Early films can consist of disconnected islands. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「更換金屬不需要改任何製程。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Changing metal requires no process changes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查金屬成核與連續膜形成」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「薄膜早期可能是不連續島狀。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess nucleation and continuous-film formation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Early films can consist of disconnected islands.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"薄膜早期可能是不連續島狀。","textEn":"Early films can consist of disconnected islands."},{"id":"a063-v8-11-k2","title":"整合路線的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration routes: principle and limits","text":"替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","textEn":"Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查金屬成核與連續膜形成」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess nucleation and continuous-film formation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","薄膜早期可能是不連續島狀。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。"],"optionsEn":["Changing metal requires no process changes.","Early films can consist of disconnected islands.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄膜早期可能是不連續島狀。 替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","explanationEn":"Early films can consist of disconnected islands. Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}},{"id":"a063-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-11"],"title":"評估直接蝕刻後的側壁殘留","titleEn":"Assess residues after direct metal etching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：殘留可改變電性與介電整合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Residues can affect electrical and dielectric integration.","instruction":"評估直接蝕刻後的側壁殘留。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「殘留可改變電性與介電整合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess residues after direct metal etching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Residues can affect electrical and dielectric integration.","observation":"殘留可改變電性與介電整合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Residues can affect electrical and dielectric integration. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「更換金屬不需要改任何製程。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Changing metal requires no process changes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估直接蝕刻後的側壁殘留」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「殘留可改變電性與介電整合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess residues after direct metal etching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Residues can affect electrical and dielectric integration.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"殘留可改變電性與介電整合。","textEn":"Residues can affect electrical and dielectric integration."},{"id":"a063-v8-12-k2","title":"整合路線的原理與限制","titleEn":"Integration routes: principle and limits","text":"替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","textEn":"Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估直接蝕刻後的側壁殘留」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess residues after direct metal etching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["更換金屬不需要改任何製程。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","殘留可改變電性與介電整合。"],"optionsEn":["Changing metal requires no process changes.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","Residues can affect electrical and dielectric integration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"殘留可改變電性與介電整合。 替代金屬研究需比較沉積、蝕刻、襯層與介電整合。","explanationEn":"Residues can affect electrical and dielectric integration. Alternative-metal research must compare deposition, etch, liners and dielectric integration."}}]},{"id":"a063-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"電阻與介面","titleEn":"Resistance and interfaces","description":"線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","descriptionEn":"Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations.","steps":[{"id":"a063-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-12"],"title":"量測電阻對導電面積的關係","titleEn":"Measure resistance versus conducting area","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：面積量測誤差會影響材料比較。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Area-measurement errors affect material comparison.","instruction":"量測電阻對導電面積的關係。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「面積量測誤差會影響材料比較。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure resistance versus conducting area. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Area-measurement errors affect material comparison.","observation":"面積量測誤差會影響材料比較。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Area-measurement errors affect material comparison. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測電阻對導電面積的關係」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「面積量測誤差會影響材料比較。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure resistance versus conducting area\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Area-measurement errors affect material comparison.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"面積量測誤差會影響材料比較。","textEn":"Area-measurement errors affect material comparison."},{"id":"a063-v8-13-k2","title":"電阻與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Resistance and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","textEn":"Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測電阻對導電面積的關係」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure resistance versus conducting area\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["面積量測誤差會影響材料比較。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。"],"optionsEn":["Area-measurement errors affect material comparison.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"面積量測誤差會影響材料比較。 線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","explanationEn":"Area-measurement errors affect material comparison. Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}},{"id":"a063-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-13"],"title":"把線長掃描分解成斜率與截距","titleEn":"Use length scaling to separate slope and intercept","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：截距可包含接觸與引線貢獻。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The intercept can contain contact and lead contributions.","instruction":"把線長掃描分解成斜率與截距。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「截距可包含接觸與引線貢獻。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Use length scaling to separate slope and intercept. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The intercept can contain contact and lead contributions.","observation":"截距可包含接觸與引線貢獻。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The intercept can contain contact and lead contributions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把線長掃描分解成斜率與截距」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「截距可包含接觸與引線貢獻。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Use length scaling to separate slope and intercept\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The intercept can contain contact and lead contributions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"截距可包含接觸與引線貢獻。","textEn":"The intercept can contain contact and lead contributions."},{"id":"a063-v8-14-k2","title":"電阻與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Resistance and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","textEn":"Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把線長掃描分解成斜率與截距」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Use length scaling to separate slope and intercept\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","截距可包含接觸與引線貢獻。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。"],"optionsEn":["Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","The intercept can contain contact and lead contributions.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"截距可包含接觸與引線貢獻。 線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","explanationEn":"The intercept can contain contact and lead contributions. Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}},{"id":"a063-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-14"],"title":"比較不同晶粒結構的電阻","titleEn":"Compare resistance across grain structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：微結構是電阻模型的一部分。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Microstructure is part of the resistance model.","instruction":"比較不同晶粒結構的電阻。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「微結構是電阻模型的一部分。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare resistance across grain structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Microstructure is part of the resistance model.","observation":"微結構是電阻模型的一部分。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Microstructure is part of the resistance model. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同晶粒結構的電阻」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「微結構是電阻模型的一部分。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare resistance across grain structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Microstructure is part of the resistance model.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"微結構是電阻模型的一部分。","textEn":"Microstructure is part of the resistance model."},{"id":"a063-v8-15-k2","title":"電阻與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Resistance and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","textEn":"Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同晶粒結構的電阻」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare resistance across grain structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","微結構是電阻模型的一部分。"],"optionsEn":["Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","Microstructure is part of the resistance model."],"answer":2,"explanation":"微結構是電阻模型的一部分。 線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","explanationEn":"Microstructure is part of the resistance model. Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}},{"id":"a063-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-15"],"title":"量測通孔分布而非只看平均","titleEn":"Measure via distributions rather than only means","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：高阻尾端可能決定電路風險。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: High-resistance tails can determine circuit risk.","instruction":"量測通孔分布而非只看平均。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「高阻尾端可能決定電路風險。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure via distributions rather than only means. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: High-resistance tails can determine circuit risk.","observation":"高阻尾端可能決定電路風險。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"High-resistance tails can determine circuit risk. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測通孔分布而非只看平均」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「高阻尾端可能決定電路風險。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure via distributions rather than only means\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"High-resistance tails can determine circuit risk.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"高阻尾端可能決定電路風險。","textEn":"High-resistance tails can determine circuit risk."},{"id":"a063-v8-16-k2","title":"電阻與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Resistance and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","textEn":"Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測通孔分布而非只看平均」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure via distributions rather than only means\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["高阻尾端可能決定電路風險。","線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。"],"optionsEn":["High-resistance tails can determine circuit risk.","Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"高阻尾端可能決定電路風險。 線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","explanationEn":"High-resistance tails can determine circuit risk. Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}},{"id":"a063-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-16"],"title":"比較高深寬比線對電容的影響","titleEn":"Assess capacitance of tall narrow lines","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：加高可降阻但可能增加側壁耦合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Greater height can lower resistance but increase sidewall coupling.","instruction":"比較高深寬比線對電容的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「加高可降阻但可能增加側壁耦合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess capacitance of tall narrow lines. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Greater height can lower resistance but increase sidewall coupling.","observation":"加高可降阻但可能增加側壁耦合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Greater height can lower resistance but increase sidewall coupling. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較高深寬比線對電容的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「加高可降阻但可能增加側壁耦合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess capacitance of tall narrow lines\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Greater height can lower resistance but increase sidewall coupling.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"加高可降阻但可能增加側壁耦合。","textEn":"Greater height can lower resistance but increase sidewall coupling."},{"id":"a063-v8-17-k2","title":"電阻與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Resistance and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","textEn":"Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較高深寬比線對電容的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess capacitance of tall narrow lines\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","加高可降阻但可能增加側壁耦合。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。"],"optionsEn":["Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","Greater height can lower resistance but increase sidewall coupling.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"加高可降阻但可能增加側壁耦合。 線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","explanationEn":"Greater height can lower resistance but increase sidewall coupling. Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}},{"id":"a063-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-17"],"title":"將空氣間隙加入 RC 比較","titleEn":"Include air gaps in RC comparisons","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低電容方案也有機械與封口要求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low-capacitance schemes also need mechanical and sealing control.","instruction":"將空氣間隙加入 RC 比較。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「低電容方案也有機械與封口要求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Include air gaps in RC comparisons. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low-capacitance schemes also need mechanical and sealing control.","observation":"低電容方案也有機械與封口要求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low-capacitance schemes also need mechanical and sealing control. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將空氣間隙加入 RC 比較」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低電容方案也有機械與封口要求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Include air gaps in RC comparisons\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low-capacitance schemes also need mechanical and sealing control.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低電容方案也有機械與封口要求。","textEn":"Low-capacitance schemes also need mechanical and sealing control."},{"id":"a063-v8-18-k2","title":"電阻與介面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Resistance and interfaces: principle and limits","text":"線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","textEn":"Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將空氣間隙加入 RC 比較」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Include air gaps in RC comparisons\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["線電阻較低就保證通孔電阻較低。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","低電容方案也有機械與封口要求。"],"optionsEn":["Lower line resistance guarantees lower via resistance.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","Low-capacitance schemes also need mechanical and sealing control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"低電容方案也有機械與封口要求。 線、通孔與接觸的限制可能不同。","explanationEn":"Low-capacitance schemes also need mechanical and sealing control. Lines, vias and contacts can have different limitations."}}]},{"id":"a063-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"可靠度比較","titleEn":"Reliability comparison","description":"研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","descriptionEn":"Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product.","steps":[{"id":"a063-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-18"],"title":"設計線間介電崩潰對照","titleEn":"Design interline dielectric-breakdown comparisons","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：可靠度取決於金屬與介電介面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Reliability depends on metal–dielectric interfaces.","instruction":"設計線間介電崩潰對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「可靠度取決於金屬與介電介面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Design interline dielectric-breakdown comparisons. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Reliability depends on metal–dielectric interfaces.","observation":"可靠度取決於金屬與介電介面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Reliability depends on metal–dielectric interfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One demonstration proves universal production replacement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「設計線間介電崩潰對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「可靠度取決於金屬與介電介面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Design interline dielectric-breakdown comparisons\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Reliability depends on metal–dielectric interfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"可靠度取決於金屬與介電介面。","textEn":"Reliability depends on metal–dielectric interfaces."},{"id":"a063-v8-19-k2","title":"可靠度比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reliability comparison: principle and limits","text":"研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","textEn":"Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「設計線間介電崩潰對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Design interline dielectric-breakdown comparisons\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["可靠度取決於金屬與介電介面。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Reliability depends on metal–dielectric interfaces.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可靠度取決於金屬與介電介面。 研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","explanationEn":"Reliability depends on metal–dielectric interfaces. Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}},{"id":"a063-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-19"],"title":"比較相同溫度與電流密度下的壽命","titleEn":"Compare lifetime at matched temperature and current density","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同應力條件不能直接排名。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different stress conditions cannot be ranked directly.","instruction":"比較相同溫度與電流密度下的壽命。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「不同應力條件不能直接排名。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare lifetime at matched temperature and current density. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different stress conditions cannot be ranked directly.","observation":"不同應力條件不能直接排名。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different stress conditions cannot be ranked directly. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One demonstration proves universal production replacement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較相同溫度與電流密度下的壽命」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同應力條件不能直接排名。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare lifetime at matched temperature and current density\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different stress conditions cannot be ranked directly.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同應力條件不能直接排名。","textEn":"Different stress conditions cannot be ranked directly."},{"id":"a063-v8-20-k2","title":"可靠度比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reliability comparison: principle and limits","text":"研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","textEn":"Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較相同溫度與電流密度下的壽命」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare lifetime at matched temperature and current density\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","不同應力條件不能直接排名。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","Different stress conditions cannot be ranked directly.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best."],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同應力條件不能直接排名。 研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","explanationEn":"Different stress conditions cannot be ranked directly. Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}},{"id":"a063-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-20"],"title":"檢查熱處理後的擴散與黏著","titleEn":"Assess diffusion and adhesion after heating","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：初始電阻低不保證熱穩定。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low initial resistance does not prove thermal stability.","instruction":"檢查熱處理後的擴散與黏著。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「初始電阻低不保證熱穩定。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess diffusion and adhesion after heating. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low initial resistance does not prove thermal stability.","observation":"初始電阻低不保證熱穩定。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low initial resistance does not prove thermal stability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One demonstration proves universal production replacement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查熱處理後的擴散與黏著」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「初始電阻低不保證熱穩定。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess diffusion and adhesion after heating\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low initial resistance does not prove thermal stability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"初始電阻低不保證熱穩定。","textEn":"Low initial resistance does not prove thermal stability."},{"id":"a063-v8-21-k2","title":"可靠度比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reliability comparison: principle and limits","text":"研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","textEn":"Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查熱處理後的擴散與黏著」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess diffusion and adhesion after heating\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","初始電阻低不保證熱穩定。"],"optionsEn":["One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Low initial resistance does not prove thermal stability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"初始電阻低不保證熱穩定。 研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","explanationEn":"Low initial resistance does not prove thermal stability. Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}},{"id":"a063-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-21"],"title":"區分模擬改善與實驗展示","titleEn":"Distinguish simulated gains from demonstrations","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同證據層次支持不同主張。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different evidence levels support different claims.","instruction":"區分模擬改善與實驗展示。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「不同證據層次支持不同主張。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish simulated gains from demonstrations. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different evidence levels support different claims.","observation":"不同證據層次支持不同主張。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different evidence levels support different claims. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One demonstration proves universal production replacement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分模擬改善與實驗展示」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同證據層次支持不同主張。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish simulated gains from demonstrations\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different evidence levels support different claims.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同證據層次支持不同主張。","textEn":"Different evidence levels support different claims."},{"id":"a063-v8-22-k2","title":"可靠度比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reliability comparison: principle and limits","text":"研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","textEn":"Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分模擬改善與實驗展示」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish simulated gains from demonstrations\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同證據層次支持不同主張。","一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Different evidence levels support different claims.","One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同證據層次支持不同主張。 研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","explanationEn":"Different evidence levels support different claims. Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}},{"id":"a063-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-22"],"title":"比較研究節點名稱與實際測試尺寸","titleEn":"Compare node labels with measured test dimensions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：節點名稱不是完整幾何規格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A node label is not a complete geometry specification.","instruction":"比較研究節點名稱與實際測試尺寸。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「節點名稱不是完整幾何規格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare node labels with measured test dimensions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: A node label is not a complete geometry specification.","observation":"節點名稱不是完整幾何規格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A node label is not a complete geometry specification. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One demonstration proves universal production replacement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較研究節點名稱與實際測試尺寸」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「節點名稱不是完整幾何規格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare node labels with measured test dimensions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A node label is not a complete geometry specification.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"節點名稱不是完整幾何規格。","textEn":"A node label is not a complete geometry specification."},{"id":"a063-v8-23-k2","title":"可靠度比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reliability comparison: principle and limits","text":"研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","textEn":"Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較研究節點名稱與實際測試尺寸」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare node labels with measured test dimensions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","節點名稱不是完整幾何規格。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。"],"optionsEn":["One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","A node label is not a complete geometry specification.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best."],"answer":1,"explanation":"節點名稱不是完整幾何規格。 研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","explanationEn":"A node label is not a complete geometry specification. Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}},{"id":"a063-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-altmetals","v8b-metals2018","v8b-semidam","v8b-beoltoolbox"],"prerequisiteIds":["a063-v8-23"],"title":"提交材料、流程、RC 與可靠度取捨","titleEn":"Review material, flow, RC and reliability tradeoffs","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：替代金屬選擇是整合問題。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Alternative-metal selection is an integration problem.","instruction":"提交材料、流程、RC 與可靠度取捨。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「替代金屬選擇是整合問題。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Review material, flow, RC and reliability tradeoffs. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Alternative-metal selection is an integration problem.","observation":"替代金屬選擇是整合問題。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Alternative-metal selection is an integration problem. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"One demonstration proves universal production replacement.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「提交材料、流程、RC 與可靠度取捨」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「替代金屬選擇是整合問題。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Review material, flow, RC and reliability tradeoffs\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Alternative-metal selection is an integration problem.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a063-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"替代金屬選擇是整合問題。","textEn":"Alternative-metal selection is an integration problem."},{"id":"a063-v8-24-k2","title":"可靠度比較的原理與限制","titleEn":"Reliability comparison: principle and limits","text":"研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","textEn":"Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「提交材料、流程、RC 與可靠度取捨」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Review material, flow, RC and reliability tradeoffs\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["一次研究展示即可宣布全面量產替代。","塊材電阻率最低的金屬永遠最佳。","替代金屬選擇是整合問題。"],"optionsEn":["One demonstration proves universal production replacement.","The lowest bulk-resistivity metal is always best.","Alternative-metal selection is an integration problem."],"answer":2,"explanation":"替代金屬選擇是整合問題。 研究測試結構的優勢不代表所有金屬層或所有產品皆適用。","explanationEn":"Alternative-metal selection is an integration problem. Test-structure benefits do not imply suitability for every level or product."}}]}]},{"id":"a064","title":"低介電常數互連介電層","titleEn":"Low-k interconnect dielectrics","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究電容與孔隙、成膜與固化、圖案化損傷、機械與可靠度；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: capacitance and porosity, growth and curing, patterning damage, mechanics and reliability. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電容與孔隙","成膜與固化","圖案化損傷","機械與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Capacitance and porosity","Growth and curing","Patterning damage","Mechanics and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability","stages":[{"id":"a064-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"電容與孔隙","titleEn":"Capacitance and porosity","description":"降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","descriptionEn":"Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance.","steps":[{"id":"a064-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"用平行板模型分開 k、面積與厚度","titleEn":"Separate k, area and thickness in a plate model","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電容改變不一定來自材料 k 改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A capacitance change need not originate from k.","instruction":"用平行板模型分開 k、面積與厚度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「電容改變不一定來自材料 k 改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate k, area and thickness in a plate model. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A capacitance change need not originate from k.","observation":"電容改變不一定來自材料 k 改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A capacitance change need not originate from k. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More porosity always improves integration.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用平行板模型分開 k、面積與厚度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電容改變不一定來自材料 k 改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate k, area and thickness in a plate model\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A capacitance change need not originate from k.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電容改變不一定來自材料 k 改變。","textEn":"A capacitance change need not originate from k."},{"id":"a064-v8-01-k2","title":"電容與孔隙的原理與限制","titleEn":"Capacitance and porosity: principle and limits","text":"降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","textEn":"Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用平行板模型分開 k、面積與厚度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate k, area and thickness in a plate model\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電容改變不一定來自材料 k 改變。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。"],"optionsEn":["A capacitance change need not originate from k.","More porosity always improves integration.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電容改變不一定來自材料 k 改變。 降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","explanationEn":"A capacitance change need not originate from k. Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}},{"id":"a064-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-01"],"title":"畫出線間與上下層耦合電容","titleEn":"Draw lateral and vertical coupling capacitances","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：實際互連有多種電場路徑。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Real interconnects have multiple field paths.","instruction":"畫出線間與上下層耦合電容。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「實際互連有多種電場路徑。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw lateral and vertical coupling capacitances. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Real interconnects have multiple field paths.","observation":"實際互連有多種電場路徑。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Real interconnects have multiple field paths. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More porosity always improves integration.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出線間與上下層耦合電容」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「實際互連有多種電場路徑。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw lateral and vertical coupling capacitances\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Real interconnects have multiple field paths.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"實際互連有多種電場路徑。","textEn":"Real interconnects have multiple field paths."},{"id":"a064-v8-02-k2","title":"電容與孔隙的原理與限制","titleEn":"Capacitance and porosity: principle and limits","text":"降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","textEn":"Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出線間與上下層耦合電容」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw lateral and vertical coupling capacitances\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","實際互連有多種電場路徑。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。"],"optionsEn":["More porosity always improves integration.","Real interconnects have multiple field paths.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"實際互連有多種電場路徑。 降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","explanationEn":"Real interconnects have multiple field paths. Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}},{"id":"a064-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-02"],"title":"比較緻密低 k 與多孔低 k","titleEn":"Compare dense and porous low-k","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：孔隙降低平均極化也改變強度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Porosity reduces average polarization and alters strength.","instruction":"比較緻密低 k 與多孔低 k。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「孔隙降低平均極化也改變強度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare dense and porous low-k. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Porosity reduces average polarization and alters strength.","observation":"孔隙降低平均極化也改變強度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Porosity reduces average polarization and alters strength. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More porosity always improves integration.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較緻密低 k 與多孔低 k」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「孔隙降低平均極化也改變強度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare dense and porous low-k\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Porosity reduces average polarization and alters strength.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"孔隙降低平均極化也改變強度。","textEn":"Porosity reduces average polarization and alters strength."},{"id":"a064-v8-03-k2","title":"電容與孔隙的原理與限制","titleEn":"Capacitance and porosity: principle and limits","text":"降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","textEn":"Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較緻密低 k 與多孔低 k」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare dense and porous low-k\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","孔隙降低平均極化也改變強度。"],"optionsEn":["More porosity always improves integration.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Porosity reduces average polarization and alters strength."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔隙降低平均極化也改變強度。 降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","explanationEn":"Porosity reduces average polarization and alters strength. Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}},{"id":"a064-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-03"],"title":"建立 RC 延遲的簡化比較","titleEn":"Build a simplified RC-delay comparison","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低 k 的收益需與導線電阻共同評估。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low-k benefits need evaluation with line resistance.","instruction":"建立 RC 延遲的簡化比較。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「低 k 的收益需與導線電阻共同評估。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設幾何不變，介電常數從 4.0 降為 2.8，電容比 C₂/C₁=0.70。若電阻保持不變，RC 降低30%；但若新整合使電阻增加50%，RC 比值變為 1.5×0.70=1.05，反而增加5%。本例以集中參數 RC 說明取捨，不等於完整訊號時序模擬。","instructionEn":"Build a simplified RC-delay comparison. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low-k benefits need evaluation with line resistance.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): At fixed geometry, lowering permittivity from 4.0 to 2.8 gives capacitance ratio 0.70. With unchanged resistance, RC falls 30%; if the new integration raises resistance by 50%, RC ratio becomes 1.5×0.70=1.05, a 5% increase. This lumped-RC example illustrates tradeoffs rather than full timing simulation.","observation":"低 k 的收益需與導線電阻共同評估。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n須同時給出 0.70 與 1.05，避免把低 k 等同更低延遲。","observationEn":"Low-k benefits need evaluation with line resistance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport both 0.70 and 1.05 rather than equating lower k with lower delay.","failure":"若報告假設「只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More porosity always improves integration.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立 RC 延遲的簡化比較」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低 k 的收益需與導線電阻共同評估。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：須同時給出 0.70 與 1.05，避免把低 k 等同更低延遲。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Build a simplified RC-delay comparison\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low-k benefits need evaluation with line resistance.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report both 0.70 and 1.05 rather than equating lower k with lower delay.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低 k 的收益需與導線電阻共同評估。","textEn":"Low-k benefits need evaluation with line resistance."},{"id":"a064-v8-04-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設幾何不變，介電常數從 4.0 降為 2.8，電容比 C₂/C₁=0.70。若電阻保持不變，RC 降低30%；但若新整合使電阻增加50%，RC 比值變為 1.5×0.70=1.05，反而增加5%。本例以集中參數 RC 說明取捨，不等於完整訊號時序模擬。","textEn":"At fixed geometry, lowering permittivity from 4.0 to 2.8 gives capacitance ratio 0.70. With unchanged resistance, RC falls 30%; if the new integration raises resistance by 50%, RC ratio becomes 1.5×0.70=1.05, a 5% increase. This lumped-RC example illustrates tradeoffs rather than full timing simulation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立 RC 延遲的簡化比較」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Build a simplified RC-delay comparison\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["低 k 的收益需與導線電阻共同評估。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。"],"optionsEn":["Low-k benefits need evaluation with line resistance.","More porosity always improves integration.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低 k 的收益需與導線電阻共同評估。 降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","explanationEn":"Low-k benefits need evaluation with line resistance. Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設幾何不變，介電常數從 4.0 降為 2.8，電容比 C₂/C₁=0.70。若電阻保持不變，RC 降低30%；但若新整合使電阻增加50%，RC 比值變為 1.5×0.70=1.05，反而增加5%。本例以集中參數 RC 說明取捨，不等於完整訊號時序模擬。","textEn":"At fixed geometry, lowering permittivity from 4.0 to 2.8 gives capacitance ratio 0.70. With unchanged resistance, RC falls 30%; if the new integration raises resistance by 50%, RC ratio becomes 1.5×0.70=1.05, a 5% increase. This lumped-RC example illustrates tradeoffs rather than full timing simulation.","check":"須同時給出 0.70 與 1.05，避免把低 k 等同更低延遲。","checkEn":"Report both 0.70 and 1.05 rather than equating lower k with lower delay."}},{"id":"a064-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-04"],"title":"分開材料 k 與有效堆疊 k","titleEn":"Separate material k from effective-stack k","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：襯層與停止層也貢獻電容。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Liners and stops also contribute capacitance.","instruction":"分開材料 k 與有效堆疊 k。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「襯層與停止層也貢獻電容。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate material k from effective-stack k. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Liners and stops also contribute capacitance.","observation":"襯層與停止層也貢獻電容。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Liners and stops also contribute capacitance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More porosity always improves integration.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開材料 k 與有效堆疊 k」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「襯層與停止層也貢獻電容。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate material k from effective-stack k\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Liners and stops also contribute capacitance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"襯層與停止層也貢獻電容。","textEn":"Liners and stops also contribute capacitance."},{"id":"a064-v8-05-k2","title":"電容與孔隙的原理與限制","titleEn":"Capacitance and porosity: principle and limits","text":"降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","textEn":"Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開材料 k 與有效堆疊 k」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate material k from effective-stack k\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","襯層與停止層也貢獻電容。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。"],"optionsEn":["More porosity always improves integration.","Liners and stops also contribute capacitance.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"襯層與停止層也貢獻電容。 降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","explanationEn":"Liners and stops also contribute capacitance. Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}},{"id":"a064-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-05"],"title":"列出封裝載荷與附著需求","titleEn":"List packaging loads and adhesion needs","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：晶片後段機械負載會傳入低 k。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Back-end mechanical loads reach low-k layers.","instruction":"列出封裝載荷與附著需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「晶片後段機械負載會傳入低 k。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"List packaging loads and adhesion needs. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Back-end mechanical loads reach low-k layers.","observation":"晶片後段機械負載會傳入低 k。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Back-end mechanical loads reach low-k layers. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More porosity always improves integration.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「列出封裝載荷與附著需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「晶片後段機械負載會傳入低 k。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"List packaging loads and adhesion needs\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Back-end mechanical loads reach low-k layers.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"晶片後段機械負載會傳入低 k。","textEn":"Back-end mechanical loads reach low-k layers."},{"id":"a064-v8-06-k2","title":"電容與孔隙的原理與限制","titleEn":"Capacitance and porosity: principle and limits","text":"降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","textEn":"Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「列出封裝載荷與附著需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"List packaging loads and adhesion needs\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","晶片後段機械負載會傳入低 k。"],"optionsEn":["More porosity always improves integration.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Back-end mechanical loads reach low-k layers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶片後段機械負載會傳入低 k。 降低介電常數可減少耦合電容，但孔隙可能降低機械與化學耐受性。","explanationEn":"Back-end mechanical loads reach low-k layers. Lower permittivity reduces coupling but porosity can weaken mechanical and chemical resistance."}}]},{"id":"a064-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"成膜與固化","titleEn":"Growth and curing","description":"材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","descriptionEn":"Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k.","steps":[{"id":"a064-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-06"],"title":"比較沉積前驅物與造孔概念","titleEn":"Compare film-precursor and porogen concepts","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：造孔需要控制孔隙形成與移除。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Porosity generation needs controlled formation and removal.","instruction":"比較沉積前驅物與造孔概念。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「造孔需要控制孔隙形成與移除。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare film-precursor and porogen concepts. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Porosity generation needs controlled formation and removal.","observation":"造孔需要控制孔隙形成與移除。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Porosity generation needs controlled formation and removal. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較沉積前驅物與造孔概念」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「造孔需要控制孔隙形成與移除。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare film-precursor and porogen concepts\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Porosity generation needs controlled formation and removal.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"造孔需要控制孔隙形成與移除。","textEn":"Porosity generation needs controlled formation and removal."},{"id":"a064-v8-07-k2","title":"成膜與固化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Growth and curing: principle and limits","text":"材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","textEn":"Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較沉積前驅物與造孔概念」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare film-precursor and porogen concepts\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["造孔需要控制孔隙形成與移除。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。"],"optionsEn":["Porosity generation needs controlled formation and removal.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k."],"answer":0,"explanation":"造孔需要控制孔隙形成與移除。 材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","explanationEn":"Porosity generation needs controlled formation and removal. Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}},{"id":"a064-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-07"],"title":"畫出固化前後的網路結構","titleEn":"Sketch network structure before and after curing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：固化可改變鍵結、應力與孔隙。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Curing can alter bonding, stress and porosity.","instruction":"畫出固化前後的網路結構。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「固化可改變鍵結、應力與孔隙。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch network structure before and after curing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Curing can alter bonding, stress and porosity.","observation":"固化可改變鍵結、應力與孔隙。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Curing can alter bonding, stress and porosity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出固化前後的網路結構」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「固化可改變鍵結、應力與孔隙。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch network structure before and after curing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Curing can alter bonding, stress and porosity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"固化可改變鍵結、應力與孔隙。","textEn":"Curing can alter bonding, stress and porosity."},{"id":"a064-v8-08-k2","title":"成膜與固化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Growth and curing: principle and limits","text":"材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","textEn":"Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出固化前後的網路結構」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch network structure before and after curing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","固化可改變鍵結、應力與孔隙。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。"],"optionsEn":["Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Curing can alter bonding, stress and porosity.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k."],"answer":1,"explanation":"固化可改變鍵結、應力與孔隙。 材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","explanationEn":"Curing can alter bonding, stress and porosity. Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}},{"id":"a064-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-08"],"title":"用光譜追蹤碳相關鍵結","titleEn":"Track carbon-related bonds spectroscopically","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：鍵結變化可提示材料損傷。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bond changes can indicate material damage.","instruction":"用光譜追蹤碳相關鍵結。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「鍵結變化可提示材料損傷。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track carbon-related bonds spectroscopically. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bond changes can indicate material damage.","observation":"鍵結變化可提示材料損傷。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bond changes can indicate material damage. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用光譜追蹤碳相關鍵結」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「鍵結變化可提示材料損傷。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track carbon-related bonds spectroscopically\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bond changes can indicate material damage.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"鍵結變化可提示材料損傷。","textEn":"Bond changes can indicate material damage."},{"id":"a064-v8-09-k2","title":"成膜與固化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Growth and curing: principle and limits","text":"材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","textEn":"Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用光譜追蹤碳相關鍵結」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track carbon-related bonds spectroscopically\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","鍵結變化可提示材料損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Bond changes can indicate material damage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鍵結變化可提示材料損傷。 材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","explanationEn":"Bond changes can indicate material damage. Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}},{"id":"a064-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-09"],"title":"比較孔徑分布與總孔隙率","titleEn":"Compare pore-size distribution with total porosity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相同孔隙率可能有不同連通性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Equal porosity can have different connectivity.","instruction":"比較孔徑分布與總孔隙率。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「相同孔隙率可能有不同連通性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare pore-size distribution with total porosity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Equal porosity can have different connectivity.","observation":"相同孔隙率可能有不同連通性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Equal porosity can have different connectivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較孔徑分布與總孔隙率」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相同孔隙率可能有不同連通性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare pore-size distribution with total porosity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Equal porosity can have different connectivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相同孔隙率可能有不同連通性。","textEn":"Equal porosity can have different connectivity."},{"id":"a064-v8-10-k2","title":"成膜與固化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Growth and curing: principle and limits","text":"材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","textEn":"Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較孔徑分布與總孔隙率」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare pore-size distribution with total porosity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["相同孔隙率可能有不同連通性。","材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。"],"optionsEn":["Equal porosity can have different connectivity.","Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同孔隙率可能有不同連通性。 材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","explanationEn":"Equal porosity can have different connectivity. Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}},{"id":"a064-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-10"],"title":"量測膜厚與應力的固化變化","titleEn":"Measure thickness and stress changes during curing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：收縮會改變幾何及機械狀態。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Shrinkage changes geometry and mechanics.","instruction":"量測膜厚與應力的固化變化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「收縮會改變幾何及機械狀態。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure thickness and stress changes during curing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Shrinkage changes geometry and mechanics.","observation":"收縮會改變幾何及機械狀態。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Shrinkage changes geometry and mechanics. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測膜厚與應力的固化變化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「收縮會改變幾何及機械狀態。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure thickness and stress changes during curing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Shrinkage changes geometry and mechanics.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"收縮會改變幾何及機械狀態。","textEn":"Shrinkage changes geometry and mechanics."},{"id":"a064-v8-11-k2","title":"成膜與固化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Growth and curing: principle and limits","text":"材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","textEn":"Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測膜厚與應力的固化變化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure thickness and stress changes during curing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","收縮會改變幾何及機械狀態。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。"],"optionsEn":["Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Shrinkage changes geometry and mechanics.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k."],"answer":1,"explanation":"收縮會改變幾何及機械狀態。 材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","explanationEn":"Shrinkage changes geometry and mechanics. Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}},{"id":"a064-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-11"],"title":"建立吸濕前後的電容對照","titleEn":"Compare capacitance before and after moisture exposure","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：水分可提高有效介電反應。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Moisture can increase effective dielectric response.","instruction":"建立吸濕前後的電容對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「水分可提高有效介電反應。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare capacitance before and after moisture exposure. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Moisture can increase effective dielectric response.","observation":"水分可提高有效介電反應。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Moisture can increase effective dielectric response. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立吸濕前後的電容對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「水分可提高有效介電反應。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare capacitance before and after moisture exposure\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Moisture can increase effective dielectric response.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"水分可提高有效介電反應。","textEn":"Moisture can increase effective dielectric response."},{"id":"a064-v8-12-k2","title":"成膜與固化的原理與限制","titleEn":"Growth and curing: principle and limits","text":"材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","textEn":"Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立吸濕前後的電容對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare capacitance before and after moisture exposure\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["材料標稱 k 值就等於整個互連有效 k。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","水分可提高有效介電反應。"],"optionsEn":["Nominal k equals the effective k of the entire interconnect.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Moisture can increase effective dielectric response."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水分可提高有效介電反應。 材料名目 k 值與整合後有效 k 值不同。","explanationEn":"Moisture can increase effective dielectric response. Nominal material k differs from integrated effective k."}}]},{"id":"a064-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"圖案化損傷","titleEn":"Patterning damage","description":"蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","descriptionEn":"Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores.","steps":[{"id":"a064-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-12"],"title":"檢查蝕刻後側壁的化學改變","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall chemistry after etching","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：損傷層可能比本體有更高 k。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A damaged layer can have higher k than the bulk.","instruction":"檢查蝕刻後側壁的化學改變。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「損傷層可能比本體有更高 k。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect sidewall chemistry after etching. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: A damaged layer can have higher k than the bulk.","observation":"損傷層可能比本體有更高 k。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A damaged layer can have higher k than the bulk. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Stripping affects resist but never low-k.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查蝕刻後側壁的化學改變」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「損傷層可能比本體有更高 k。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect sidewall chemistry after etching\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A damaged layer can have higher k than the bulk.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"損傷層可能比本體有更高 k。","textEn":"A damaged layer can have higher k than the bulk."},{"id":"a064-v8-13-k2","title":"圖案化損傷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterning damage: principle and limits","text":"蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","textEn":"Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查蝕刻後側壁的化學改變」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect sidewall chemistry after etching\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["損傷層可能比本體有更高 k。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。"],"optionsEn":["A damaged layer can have higher k than the bulk.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"損傷層可能比本體有更高 k。 蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","explanationEn":"A damaged layer can have higher k than the bulk. Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}},{"id":"a064-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-13"],"title":"比較不同去膠路線的材料保留","titleEn":"Compare material preservation in stripping routes","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：去除效率與低 k 保護需兼顧。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Removal efficiency and low-k preservation need balancing.","instruction":"比較不同去膠路線的材料保留。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「去除效率與低 k 保護需兼顧。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare material preservation in stripping routes. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Removal efficiency and low-k preservation need balancing.","observation":"去除效率與低 k 保護需兼顧。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Removal efficiency and low-k preservation need balancing. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Stripping affects resist but never low-k.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同去膠路線的材料保留」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「去除效率與低 k 保護需兼顧。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare material preservation in stripping routes\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Removal efficiency and low-k preservation need balancing.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"去除效率與低 k 保護需兼顧。","textEn":"Removal efficiency and low-k preservation need balancing."},{"id":"a064-v8-14-k2","title":"圖案化損傷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterning damage: principle and limits","text":"蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","textEn":"Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同去膠路線的材料保留」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare material preservation in stripping routes\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","去除效率與低 k 保護需兼顧。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。"],"optionsEn":["Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Removal efficiency and low-k preservation need balancing.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"去除效率與低 k 保護需兼顧。 蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","explanationEn":"Removal efficiency and low-k preservation need balancing. Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}},{"id":"a064-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-14"],"title":"評估濕清潔液進入開放孔隙","titleEn":"Assess cleaning-liquid entry into open pores","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：開放孔隙會改變污染與乾燥歷程。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Open pores change contamination and drying history.","instruction":"評估濕清潔液進入開放孔隙。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「開放孔隙會改變污染與乾燥歷程。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess cleaning-liquid entry into open pores. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Open pores change contamination and drying history.","observation":"開放孔隙會改變污染與乾燥歷程。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Open pores change contamination and drying history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Stripping affects resist but never low-k.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估濕清潔液進入開放孔隙」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「開放孔隙會改變污染與乾燥歷程。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess cleaning-liquid entry into open pores\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Open pores change contamination and drying history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"開放孔隙會改變污染與乾燥歷程。","textEn":"Open pores change contamination and drying history."},{"id":"a064-v8-15-k2","title":"圖案化損傷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterning damage: principle and limits","text":"蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","textEn":"Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估濕清潔液進入開放孔隙」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess cleaning-liquid entry into open pores\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","開放孔隙會改變污染與乾燥歷程。"],"optionsEn":["Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","Open pores change contamination and drying history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開放孔隙會改變污染與乾燥歷程。 蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","explanationEn":"Open pores change contamination and drying history. Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}},{"id":"a064-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-15"],"title":"畫出側壁封孔對有效尺寸的影響","titleEn":"Sketch pore-sealing effects on effective dimensions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：封孔可能改善保護但占用空間。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Pore sealing can protect surfaces while consuming space.","instruction":"畫出側壁封孔對有效尺寸的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「封孔可能改善保護但占用空間。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch pore-sealing effects on effective dimensions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Pore sealing can protect surfaces while consuming space.","observation":"封孔可能改善保護但占用空間。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Pore sealing can protect surfaces while consuming space. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Stripping affects resist but never low-k.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出側壁封孔對有效尺寸的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「封孔可能改善保護但占用空間。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch pore-sealing effects on effective dimensions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Pore sealing can protect surfaces while consuming space.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"封孔可能改善保護但占用空間。","textEn":"Pore sealing can protect surfaces while consuming space."},{"id":"a064-v8-16-k2","title":"圖案化損傷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterning damage: principle and limits","text":"蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","textEn":"Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出側壁封孔對有效尺寸的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch pore-sealing effects on effective dimensions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["封孔可能改善保護但占用空間。","去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。"],"optionsEn":["Pore sealing can protect surfaces while consuming space.","Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant."],"answer":0,"explanation":"封孔可能改善保護但占用空間。 蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","explanationEn":"Pore sealing can protect surfaces while consuming space. Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}},{"id":"a064-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-16"],"title":"比較圖形化前後的有效 k","titleEn":"Compare effective k before and after patterning","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：整合過程可能抵銷材料原始優勢。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Integration can offset the material's original benefit.","instruction":"比較圖形化前後的有效 k。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「整合過程可能抵銷材料原始優勢。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare effective k before and after patterning. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Integration can offset the material's original benefit.","observation":"整合過程可能抵銷材料原始優勢。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Integration can offset the material's original benefit. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Stripping affects resist but never low-k.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較圖形化前後的有效 k」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「整合過程可能抵銷材料原始優勢。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare effective k before and after patterning\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Integration can offset the material's original benefit.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"整合過程可能抵銷材料原始優勢。","textEn":"Integration can offset the material's original benefit."},{"id":"a064-v8-17-k2","title":"圖案化損傷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterning damage: principle and limits","text":"蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","textEn":"Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較圖形化前後的有效 k」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare effective k before and after patterning\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","整合過程可能抵銷材料原始優勢。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。"],"optionsEn":["Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Integration can offset the material's original benefit.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"整合過程可能抵銷材料原始優勢。 蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","explanationEn":"Integration can offset the material's original benefit. Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}},{"id":"a064-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-17"],"title":"檢查銅阻障在多孔側壁的連續性","titleEn":"Inspect barrier continuity on porous sidewalls","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面孔隙可能妨礙完整覆蓋。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Surface pores can obstruct continuous coverage.","instruction":"檢查銅阻障在多孔側壁的連續性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「表面孔隙可能妨礙完整覆蓋。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect barrier continuity on porous sidewalls. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Surface pores can obstruct continuous coverage.","observation":"表面孔隙可能妨礙完整覆蓋。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Surface pores can obstruct continuous coverage. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Stripping affects resist but never low-k.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查銅阻障在多孔側壁的連續性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面孔隙可能妨礙完整覆蓋。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect barrier continuity on porous sidewalls\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Surface pores can obstruct continuous coverage.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面孔隙可能妨礙完整覆蓋。","textEn":"Surface pores can obstruct continuous coverage."},{"id":"a064-v8-18-k2","title":"圖案化損傷的原理與限制","titleEn":"Patterning damage: principle and limits","text":"蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","textEn":"Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查銅阻障在多孔側壁的連續性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect barrier continuity on porous sidewalls\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["去膠只影響光阻，不影響低 k。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","表面孔隙可能妨礙完整覆蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Stripping affects resist but never low-k.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","Surface pores can obstruct continuous coverage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面孔隙可能妨礙完整覆蓋。 蝕刻、去膠、清潔與吸水會改變低 k 表面與孔隙。","explanationEn":"Surface pores can obstruct continuous coverage. Etch, strip, clean and moisture can change low-k surfaces and pores."}}]},{"id":"a064-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"機械與可靠度","titleEn":"Mechanics and reliability","description":"低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","descriptionEn":"Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together.","steps":[{"id":"a064-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-18"],"title":"以梳狀結構評估漏電與崩潰","titleEn":"Assess leakage and breakdown with comb structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低電容不保證高介電可靠度。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low capacitance does not guarantee dielectric reliability.","instruction":"以梳狀結構評估漏電與崩潰。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「低電容不保證高介電可靠度。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess leakage and breakdown with comb structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low capacitance does not guarantee dielectric reliability.","observation":"低電容不保證高介電可靠度。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low capacitance does not guarantee dielectric reliability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以梳狀結構評估漏電與崩潰」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低電容不保證高介電可靠度。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess leakage and breakdown with comb structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low capacitance does not guarantee dielectric reliability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低電容不保證高介電可靠度。","textEn":"Low capacitance does not guarantee dielectric reliability."},{"id":"a064-v8-19-k2","title":"機械與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mechanics and reliability: principle and limits","text":"低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","textEn":"Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以梳狀結構評估漏電與崩潰」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess leakage and breakdown with comb structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["低電容不保證高介電可靠度。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。"],"optionsEn":["Low capacitance does not guarantee dielectric reliability.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","More porosity always improves integration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低電容不保證高介電可靠度。 低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","explanationEn":"Low capacitance does not guarantee dielectric reliability. Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}},{"id":"a064-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-19"],"title":"比較不同應力下的裂紋路徑","titleEn":"Compare crack paths under different stresses","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：最弱介面可能決定整體機械失效。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The weakest interface can control mechanical failure.","instruction":"比較不同應力下的裂紋路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「最弱介面可能決定整體機械失效。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare crack paths under different stresses. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The weakest interface can control mechanical failure.","observation":"最弱介面可能決定整體機械失效。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The weakest interface can control mechanical failure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較不同應力下的裂紋路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「最弱介面可能決定整體機械失效。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare crack paths under different stresses\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The weakest interface can control mechanical failure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"最弱介面可能決定整體機械失效。","textEn":"The weakest interface can control mechanical failure."},{"id":"a064-v8-20-k2","title":"機械與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mechanics and reliability: principle and limits","text":"低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","textEn":"Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較不同應力下的裂紋路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare crack paths under different stresses\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","最弱介面可能決定整體機械失效。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。"],"optionsEn":["Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","The weakest interface can control mechanical failure.","More porosity always improves integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"最弱介面可能決定整體機械失效。 低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","explanationEn":"The weakest interface can control mechanical failure. Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}},{"id":"a064-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-20"],"title":"檢查 CMP 與接合載荷的後果","titleEn":"Assess consequences of CMP and bonding loads","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：加工載荷需納入低 k 整合。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Processing loads belong in low-k integration analysis.","instruction":"檢查 CMP 與接合載荷的後果。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「加工載荷需納入低 k 整合。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess consequences of CMP and bonding loads. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Processing loads belong in low-k integration analysis.","observation":"加工載荷需納入低 k 整合。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Processing loads belong in low-k integration analysis. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查 CMP 與接合載荷的後果」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「加工載荷需納入低 k 整合。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess consequences of CMP and bonding loads\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Processing loads belong in low-k integration analysis.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"加工載荷需納入低 k 整合。","textEn":"Processing loads belong in low-k integration analysis."},{"id":"a064-v8-21-k2","title":"機械與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mechanics and reliability: principle and limits","text":"低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","textEn":"Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查 CMP 與接合載荷的後果」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess consequences of CMP and bonding loads\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","加工載荷需納入低 k 整合。"],"optionsEn":["Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","More porosity always improves integration.","Processing loads belong in low-k integration analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"加工載荷需納入低 k 整合。 低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","explanationEn":"Processing loads belong in low-k integration analysis. Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}},{"id":"a064-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-21"],"title":"比較空氣間隙與多孔介電層","titleEn":"Compare air gaps with porous dielectrics","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：兩種低電容策略有不同支撐需求。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The two low-capacitance strategies need different support.","instruction":"比較空氣間隙與多孔介電層。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「兩種低電容策略有不同支撐需求。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare air gaps with porous dielectrics. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: The two low-capacitance strategies need different support.","observation":"兩種低電容策略有不同支撐需求。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The two low-capacitance strategies need different support. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較空氣間隙與多孔介電層」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「兩種低電容策略有不同支撐需求。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare air gaps with porous dielectrics\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The two low-capacitance strategies need different support.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"兩種低電容策略有不同支撐需求。","textEn":"The two low-capacitance strategies need different support."},{"id":"a064-v8-22-k2","title":"機械與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mechanics and reliability: principle and limits","text":"低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","textEn":"Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較空氣間隙與多孔介電層」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare air gaps with porous dielectrics\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["兩種低電容策略有不同支撐需求。","電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。"],"optionsEn":["The two low-capacitance strategies need different support.","Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","More porosity always improves integration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種低電容策略有不同支撐需求。 低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","explanationEn":"The two low-capacitance strategies need different support. Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}},{"id":"a064-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-22"],"title":"將電容、漏電與機械強度放入取捨表","titleEn":"Tabulate capacitance, leakage and strength tradeoffs","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：單一 k 數字不足以決定材料選擇。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: One k value is insufficient for material selection.","instruction":"將電容、漏電與機械強度放入取捨表。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「單一 k 數字不足以決定材料選擇。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Tabulate capacitance, leakage and strength tradeoffs. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: One k value is insufficient for material selection.","observation":"單一 k 數字不足以決定材料選擇。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"One k value is insufficient for material selection. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將電容、漏電與機械強度放入取捨表」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「單一 k 數字不足以決定材料選擇。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Tabulate capacitance, leakage and strength tradeoffs\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"One k value is insufficient for material selection.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"單一 k 數字不足以決定材料選擇。","textEn":"One k value is insufficient for material selection."},{"id":"a064-v8-23-k2","title":"機械與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mechanics and reliability: principle and limits","text":"低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","textEn":"Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將電容、漏電與機械強度放入取捨表」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Tabulate capacitance, leakage and strength tradeoffs\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","單一 k 數字不足以決定材料選擇。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。"],"optionsEn":["Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","One k value is insufficient for material selection.","More porosity always improves integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一 k 數字不足以決定材料選擇。 低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","explanationEn":"One k value is insufficient for material selection. Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}},{"id":"a064-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-beoltoolbox","v8b-wiring","v8b-semidam","v8b-lowkbarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a064-v8-23"],"title":"交付整合後低 k 的性能證據","titleEn":"Deliver evidence for integrated low-k performance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料驗收需跨越成膜與後續圖案化。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Acceptance must span growth and subsequent patterning.","instruction":"交付整合後低 k 的性能證據。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「材料驗收需跨越成膜與後續圖案化。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver evidence for integrated low-k performance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Acceptance must span growth and subsequent patterning.","observation":"材料驗收需跨越成膜與後續圖案化。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Acceptance must span growth and subsequent patterning. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付整合後低 k 的性能證據」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料驗收需跨越成膜與後續圖案化。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver evidence for integrated low-k performance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Acceptance must span growth and subsequent patterning.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a064-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料驗收需跨越成膜與後續圖案化。","textEn":"Acceptance must span growth and subsequent patterning."},{"id":"a064-v8-24-k2","title":"機械與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Mechanics and reliability: principle and limits","text":"低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","textEn":"Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付整合後低 k 的性能證據」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver evidence for integrated low-k performance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電容下降即可忽略機械裂紋。","只要孔隙越多就一定更適合整合。","材料驗收需跨越成膜與後續圖案化。"],"optionsEn":["Lower capacitance makes mechanical cracks irrelevant.","More porosity always improves integration.","Acceptance must span growth and subsequent patterning."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料驗收需跨越成膜與後續圖案化。 低 k 成功需同時滿足 RC、漏電、附著與封裝機械要求。","explanationEn":"Acceptance must span growth and subsequent patterning. Successful low-k integration needs RC, leakage, adhesion and packaging mechanics together."}}]}]},{"id":"a065","title":"阻障層與種子層沉積","titleEn":"Barrier and seed-layer deposition","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究功能與截面、沉積與連續性、介面與填充、擴散與可靠度；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: functions and sections, deposition and continuity, interfaces and filling, diffusion and reliability. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["功能與截面","沉積與連續性","介面與填充","擴散與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Functions and sections","Deposition and continuity","Interfaces and filling","Diffusion and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability","stages":[{"id":"a065-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"功能與截面","titleEn":"Functions and sections","description":"阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","descriptionEn":"Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ.","steps":[{"id":"a065-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出介電層、阻障、種子與銅主體","titleEn":"Draw dielectric, barrier, seed and bulk copper","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同層負責不同物理功能。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different layers serve different physical functions.","instruction":"畫出介電層、阻障、種子與銅主體。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「不同層負責不同物理功能。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw dielectric, barrier, seed and bulk copper. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different layers serve different physical functions.","observation":"不同層負責不同物理功能。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different layers serve different physical functions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出介電層、阻障、種子與銅主體」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同層負責不同物理功能。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw dielectric, barrier, seed and bulk copper\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different layers serve different physical functions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同層負責不同物理功能。","textEn":"Different layers serve different physical functions."},{"id":"a065-v8-01-k2","title":"功能與截面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Functions and sections: principle and limits","text":"阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","textEn":"Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出介電層、阻障、種子與銅主體」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw dielectric, barrier, seed and bulk copper\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同層負責不同物理功能。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。"],"optionsEn":["Different layers serve different physical functions.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同層負責不同物理功能。 阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","explanationEn":"Different layers serve different physical functions. Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}},{"id":"a065-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-01"],"title":"比較擴散阻擋與電性導通需求","titleEn":"Compare diffusion blocking with electrical continuity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：良好阻擴散不一定是良好電鍍表面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A good diffusion barrier need not be a good plating surface.","instruction":"比較擴散阻擋與電性導通需求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「良好阻擴散不一定是良好電鍍表面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare diffusion blocking with electrical continuity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: A good diffusion barrier need not be a good plating surface.","observation":"良好阻擴散不一定是良好電鍍表面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A good diffusion barrier need not be a good plating surface. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較擴散阻擋與電性導通需求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「良好阻擴散不一定是良好電鍍表面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare diffusion blocking with electrical continuity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A good diffusion barrier need not be a good plating surface.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"良好阻擴散不一定是良好電鍍表面。","textEn":"A good diffusion barrier need not be a good plating surface."},{"id":"a065-v8-02-k2","title":"功能與截面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Functions and sections: principle and limits","text":"阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","textEn":"Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較擴散阻擋與電性導通需求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare diffusion blocking with electrical continuity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","良好阻擴散不一定是良好電鍍表面。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。"],"optionsEn":["A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","A good diffusion barrier need not be a good plating surface.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"良好阻擴散不一定是良好電鍍表面。 阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","explanationEn":"A good diffusion barrier need not be a good plating surface. Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}},{"id":"a065-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-02"],"title":"估算襯層占用的導電截面","titleEn":"Estimate conducting area consumed by liners","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：尺度縮小時占比會提高。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The fractional occupancy grows as dimensions shrink.","instruction":"估算襯層占用的導電截面。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「尺度縮小時占比會提高。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：假設矩形溝槽外框 20×40 nm²，襯層只占兩側與底部。厚度 2 nm 時導電截面為 16×38=608 nm²；厚度 3 nm 時為14×37=518 nm²。固定ρ與長度後，電阻比為608/518≈1.174，增加17.4%。但較薄層若有針孔，不能只憑低電阻選用；補上擴散可靠度關卡。","instructionEn":"Estimate conducting area consumed by liners. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: The fractional occupancy grows as dimensions shrink.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): Assume a 20×40 nm² trench with liners on both sides and bottom. At 2 nm thickness, conducting area is 16×38=608 nm²; at 3 nm it is 14×37=518 nm². With fixed ρ and length, resistance ratio is 608/518≈1.174, a 17.4% increase. A thinner layer with pinholes cannot be selected on resistance alone; add diffusion-reliability gates.","observation":"尺度縮小時占比會提高。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 608、518 nm²與17.4%，且不得省略阻障完整性。","observationEn":"The fractional occupancy grows as dimensions shrink. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 608 and 518 nm² and 17.4%, retaining barrier-integrity requirements.","failure":"若報告假設「有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算襯層占用的導電截面」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「尺度縮小時占比會提高。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 608、518 nm²與17.4%，且不得省略阻障完整性。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate conducting area consumed by liners\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The fractional occupancy grows as dimensions shrink.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 608 and 518 nm² and 17.4%, retaining barrier-integrity requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"尺度縮小時占比會提高。","textEn":"The fractional occupancy grows as dimensions shrink."},{"id":"a065-v8-03-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"假設矩形溝槽外框 20×40 nm²，襯層只占兩側與底部。厚度 2 nm 時導電截面為 16×38=608 nm²；厚度 3 nm 時為14×37=518 nm²。固定ρ與長度後，電阻比為608/518≈1.174，增加17.4%。但較薄層若有針孔，不能只憑低電阻選用；補上擴散可靠度關卡。","textEn":"Assume a 20×40 nm² trench with liners on both sides and bottom. At 2 nm thickness, conducting area is 16×38=608 nm²; at 3 nm it is 14×37=518 nm². With fixed ρ and length, resistance ratio is 608/518≈1.174, a 17.4% increase. A thinner layer with pinholes cannot be selected on resistance alone; add diffusion-reliability gates."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算襯層占用的導電截面」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate conducting area consumed by liners\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","尺度縮小時占比會提高。"],"optionsEn":["A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","The fractional occupancy grows as dimensions shrink."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尺度縮小時占比會提高。 阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","explanationEn":"The fractional occupancy grows as dimensions shrink. Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"假設矩形溝槽外框 20×40 nm²，襯層只占兩側與底部。厚度 2 nm 時導電截面為 16×38=608 nm²；厚度 3 nm 時為14×37=518 nm²。固定ρ與長度後，電阻比為608/518≈1.174，增加17.4%。但較薄層若有針孔，不能只憑低電阻選用；補上擴散可靠度關卡。","textEn":"Assume a 20×40 nm² trench with liners on both sides and bottom. At 2 nm thickness, conducting area is 16×38=608 nm²; at 3 nm it is 14×37=518 nm². With fixed ρ and length, resistance ratio is 608/518≈1.174, a 17.4% increase. A thinner layer with pinholes cannot be selected on resistance alone; add diffusion-reliability gates.","check":"交付 608、518 nm²與17.4%，且不得省略阻障完整性。","checkEn":"Report 608 and 518 nm² and 17.4%, retaining barrier-integrity requirements."}},{"id":"a065-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-03"],"title":"標記側壁、孔底與轉角的要求","titleEn":"Mark wall, bottom and corner requirements","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：各位置的覆蓋難度不同。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Coverage difficulty differs by location.","instruction":"標記側壁、孔底與轉角的要求。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「各位置的覆蓋難度不同。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark wall, bottom and corner requirements. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Coverage difficulty differs by location.","observation":"各位置的覆蓋難度不同。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Coverage difficulty differs by location. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記側壁、孔底與轉角的要求」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「各位置的覆蓋難度不同。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark wall, bottom and corner requirements\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Coverage difficulty differs by location.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"各位置的覆蓋難度不同。","textEn":"Coverage difficulty differs by location."},{"id":"a065-v8-04-k2","title":"功能與截面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Functions and sections: principle and limits","text":"阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","textEn":"Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記側壁、孔底與轉角的要求」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark wall, bottom and corner requirements\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["各位置的覆蓋難度不同。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。"],"optionsEn":["Coverage difficulty differs by location.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"各位置的覆蓋難度不同。 阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","explanationEn":"Coverage difficulty differs by location. Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}},{"id":"a065-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-04"],"title":"建立基板表面污染的影響鏈","titleEn":"Trace effects of surface contamination","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：污染可破壞成核與附著。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Contamination can disrupt nucleation and adhesion.","instruction":"建立基板表面污染的影響鏈。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「污染可破壞成核與附著。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace effects of surface contamination. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Contamination can disrupt nucleation and adhesion.","observation":"污染可破壞成核與附著。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Contamination can disrupt nucleation and adhesion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立基板表面污染的影響鏈」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「污染可破壞成核與附著。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace effects of surface contamination\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Contamination can disrupt nucleation and adhesion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"污染可破壞成核與附著。","textEn":"Contamination can disrupt nucleation and adhesion."},{"id":"a065-v8-05-k2","title":"功能與截面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Functions and sections: principle and limits","text":"阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","textEn":"Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立基板表面污染的影響鏈」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace effects of surface contamination\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","污染可破壞成核與附著。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。"],"optionsEn":["A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","Contamination can disrupt nucleation and adhesion.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"污染可破壞成核與附著。 阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","explanationEn":"Contamination can disrupt nucleation and adhesion. Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}},{"id":"a065-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-05"],"title":"比較多層阻障與整合襯層概念","titleEn":"Compare multilayer barriers with integrated liners","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：新材料需重新驗證每項功能。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: New materials require revalidation of every function.","instruction":"比較多層阻障與整合襯層概念。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「新材料需重新驗證每項功能。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare multilayer barriers with integrated liners. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: New materials require revalidation of every function.","observation":"新材料需重新驗證每項功能。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"New materials require revalidation of every function. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較多層阻障與整合襯層概念」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「新材料需重新驗證每項功能。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare multilayer barriers with integrated liners\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"New materials require revalidation of every function.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"新材料需重新驗證每項功能。","textEn":"New materials require revalidation of every function."},{"id":"a065-v8-06-k2","title":"功能與截面的原理與限制","titleEn":"Functions and sections: principle and limits","text":"阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","textEn":"Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較多層阻障與整合襯層概念」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare multilayer barriers with integrated liners\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","新材料需重新驗證每項功能。"],"optionsEn":["A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","New materials require revalidation of every function."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新材料需重新驗證每項功能。 阻障層阻擋擴散，種子層提供電鍍起始與導電路徑，功能不可混同。","explanationEn":"New materials require revalidation of every function. Barriers block diffusion; seeds enable plating and electrical continuity; the roles differ."}}]},{"id":"a065-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"沉積與連續性","titleEn":"Deposition and continuity","description":"最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","descriptionEn":"The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity.","steps":[{"id":"a065-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-06"],"title":"比較 PVD、CVD 與 ALD 覆蓋機制","titleEn":"Compare PVD, CVD and ALD coverage","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同沉積機制有不同深部可達性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Deposition mechanisms differ in deep-feature access.","instruction":"比較 PVD、CVD 與 ALD 覆蓋機制。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「不同沉積機制有不同深部可達性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare PVD, CVD and ALD coverage. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Deposition mechanisms differ in deep-feature access.","observation":"不同沉積機制有不同深部可達性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Deposition mechanisms differ in deep-feature access. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 PVD、CVD 與 ALD 覆蓋機制」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同沉積機制有不同深部可達性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare PVD, CVD and ALD coverage\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Deposition mechanisms differ in deep-feature access.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同沉積機制有不同深部可達性。","textEn":"Deposition mechanisms differ in deep-feature access."},{"id":"a065-v8-07-k2","title":"沉積與連續性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deposition and continuity: principle and limits","text":"最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","textEn":"The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 PVD、CVD 與 ALD 覆蓋機制」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare PVD, CVD and ALD coverage\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不同沉積機制有不同深部可達性。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。"],"optionsEn":["Deposition mechanisms differ in deep-feature access.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同沉積機制有不同深部可達性。 最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","explanationEn":"Deposition mechanisms differ in deep-feature access. The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}},{"id":"a065-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-07"],"title":"量測頂部與側壁厚度比","titleEn":"Measure top-to-sidewall thickness ratios","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平面厚度不能替代共形性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Planar thickness does not substitute for conformality.","instruction":"量測頂部與側壁厚度比。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「平面厚度不能替代共形性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure top-to-sidewall thickness ratios. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Planar thickness does not substitute for conformality.","observation":"平面厚度不能替代共形性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Planar thickness does not substitute for conformality. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「量測頂部與側壁厚度比」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平面厚度不能替代共形性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure top-to-sidewall thickness ratios\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Planar thickness does not substitute for conformality.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平面厚度不能替代共形性。","textEn":"Planar thickness does not substitute for conformality."},{"id":"a065-v8-08-k2","title":"沉積與連續性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deposition and continuity: principle and limits","text":"最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","textEn":"The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「量測頂部與側壁厚度比」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure top-to-sidewall thickness ratios\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","平面厚度不能替代共形性。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","Planar thickness does not substitute for conformality.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平面厚度不能替代共形性。 最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","explanationEn":"Planar thickness does not substitute for conformality. The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}},{"id":"a065-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-08"],"title":"檢查孔底最薄點的連續性","titleEn":"Inspect continuity at the thinnest bottom region","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部破口可能支配擴散失效。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local gaps can dominate diffusion failure.","instruction":"檢查孔底最薄點的連續性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「局部破口可能支配擴散失效。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect continuity at the thinnest bottom region. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local gaps can dominate diffusion failure.","observation":"局部破口可能支配擴散失效。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local gaps can dominate diffusion failure. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查孔底最薄點的連續性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部破口可能支配擴散失效。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect continuity at the thinnest bottom region\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local gaps can dominate diffusion failure.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部破口可能支配擴散失效。","textEn":"Local gaps can dominate diffusion failure."},{"id":"a065-v8-09-k2","title":"沉積與連續性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deposition and continuity: principle and limits","text":"最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","textEn":"The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查孔底最薄點的連續性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect continuity at the thinnest bottom region\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","局部破口可能支配擴散失效。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","Local gaps can dominate diffusion failure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部破口可能支配擴散失效。 最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","explanationEn":"Local gaps can dominate diffusion failure. The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}},{"id":"a065-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-09"],"title":"比較成核島連結成膜的階段","titleEn":"Compare nucleation islands merging into a film","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：名目沉積量不一定代表連續薄膜。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Nominal deposited amount need not imply a continuous film.","instruction":"比較成核島連結成膜的階段。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「名目沉積量不一定代表連續薄膜。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare nucleation islands merging into a film. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Nominal deposited amount need not imply a continuous film.","observation":"名目沉積量不一定代表連續薄膜。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Nominal deposited amount need not imply a continuous film. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較成核島連結成膜的階段」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「名目沉積量不一定代表連續薄膜。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare nucleation islands merging into a film\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Nominal deposited amount need not imply a continuous film.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"名目沉積量不一定代表連續薄膜。","textEn":"Nominal deposited amount need not imply a continuous film."},{"id":"a065-v8-10-k2","title":"沉積與連續性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deposition and continuity: principle and limits","text":"最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","textEn":"The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較成核島連結成膜的階段」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare nucleation islands merging into a film\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["名目沉積量不一定代表連續薄膜。","平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。"],"optionsEn":["Nominal deposited amount need not imply a continuous film.","Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating."],"answer":0,"explanation":"名目沉積量不一定代表連續薄膜。 最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","explanationEn":"Nominal deposited amount need not imply a continuous film. The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}},{"id":"a065-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-10"],"title":"評估 PVD 孔口懸垂與遮蔽","titleEn":"Assess PVD entrance overhang and shadowing","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：入口沉積可阻擋深部通量。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Entrance deposition can block deep flux.","instruction":"評估 PVD 孔口懸垂與遮蔽。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「入口沉積可阻擋深部通量。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess PVD entrance overhang and shadowing. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Entrance deposition can block deep flux.","observation":"入口沉積可阻擋深部通量。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Entrance deposition can block deep flux. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估 PVD 孔口懸垂與遮蔽」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「入口沉積可阻擋深部通量。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess PVD entrance overhang and shadowing\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Entrance deposition can block deep flux.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"入口沉積可阻擋深部通量。","textEn":"Entrance deposition can block deep flux."},{"id":"a065-v8-11-k2","title":"沉積與連續性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deposition and continuity: principle and limits","text":"最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","textEn":"The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估 PVD 孔口懸垂與遮蔽」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess PVD entrance overhang and shadowing\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","入口沉積可阻擋深部通量。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","Entrance deposition can block deep flux.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口沉積可阻擋深部通量。 最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","explanationEn":"Entrance deposition can block deep flux. The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}},{"id":"a065-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-11"],"title":"追蹤層間曝氣造成的表面氧化","titleEn":"Track oxidation caused by interlayer air breaks","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：曝氣歷程會改變接觸與潤濕。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Air-break history changes contact and wetting.","instruction":"追蹤層間曝氣造成的表面氧化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「曝氣歷程會改變接觸與潤濕。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track oxidation caused by interlayer air breaks. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Air-break history changes contact and wetting.","observation":"曝氣歷程會改變接觸與潤濕。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Air-break history changes contact and wetting. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤層間曝氣造成的表面氧化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「曝氣歷程會改變接觸與潤濕。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track oxidation caused by interlayer air breaks\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Air-break history changes contact and wetting.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"曝氣歷程會改變接觸與潤濕。","textEn":"Air-break history changes contact and wetting."},{"id":"a065-v8-12-k2","title":"沉積與連續性的原理與限制","titleEn":"Deposition and continuity: principle and limits","text":"最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","textEn":"The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤層間曝氣造成的表面氧化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track oxidation caused by interlayer air breaks\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["平均厚度合格就能保證沒有針孔。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","曝氣歷程會改變接觸與潤濕。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptable average thickness proves no pinholes.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","Air-break history changes contact and wetting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"曝氣歷程會改變接觸與潤濕。 最薄側壁或孔底可能決定整體阻障完整性。","explanationEn":"Air-break history changes contact and wetting. The thinnest wall or bottom region can determine barrier integrity."}}]},{"id":"a065-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"介面與填充","titleEn":"Interfaces and filling","description":"種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","descriptionEn":"Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation.","steps":[{"id":"a065-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-12"],"title":"以片電阻地圖檢查種子連續性","titleEn":"Map sheet resistance to assess seed continuity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：低平均電阻仍可能伴隨局部斷點。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Low mean resistance can coexist with local discontinuities.","instruction":"以片電阻地圖檢查種子連續性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「低平均電阻仍可能伴隨局部斷點。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Map sheet resistance to assess seed continuity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Low mean resistance can coexist with local discontinuities.","observation":"低平均電阻仍可能伴隨局部斷點。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Low mean resistance can coexist with local discontinuities. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以片電阻地圖檢查種子連續性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「低平均電阻仍可能伴隨局部斷點。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Map sheet resistance to assess seed continuity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Low mean resistance can coexist with local discontinuities.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"低平均電阻仍可能伴隨局部斷點。","textEn":"Low mean resistance can coexist with local discontinuities."},{"id":"a065-v8-13-k2","title":"介面與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and filling: principle and limits","text":"種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","textEn":"Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以片電阻地圖檢查種子連續性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Map sheet resistance to assess seed continuity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["低平均電阻仍可能伴隨局部斷點。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean resistance can coexist with local discontinuities.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低平均電阻仍可能伴隨局部斷點。 種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","explanationEn":"Low mean resistance can coexist with local discontinuities. Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}},{"id":"a065-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-13"],"title":"比較氧化前後的電鍍起始","titleEn":"Compare plating initiation before and after oxidation","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：表面化學影響成核過電位。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Surface chemistry affects nucleation overpotential.","instruction":"比較氧化前後的電鍍起始。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「表面化學影響成核過電位。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare plating initiation before and after oxidation. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Surface chemistry affects nucleation overpotential.","observation":"表面化學影響成核過電位。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Surface chemistry affects nucleation overpotential. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較氧化前後的電鍍起始」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「表面化學影響成核過電位。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare plating initiation before and after oxidation\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Surface chemistry affects nucleation overpotential.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"表面化學影響成核過電位。","textEn":"Surface chemistry affects nucleation overpotential."},{"id":"a065-v8-14-k2","title":"介面與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and filling: principle and limits","text":"種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","textEn":"Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較氧化前後的電鍍起始」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare plating initiation before and after oxidation\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","表面化學影響成核過電位。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","Surface chemistry affects nucleation overpotential.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面化學影響成核過電位。 種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","explanationEn":"Surface chemistry affects nucleation overpotential. Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}},{"id":"a065-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-14"],"title":"畫出邊緣接點到孔底的供電路徑","titleEn":"Trace current from edge contacts to feature bottoms","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：種子層提供電流分布的路徑。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The seed provides current-distribution paths.","instruction":"畫出邊緣接點到孔底的供電路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「種子層提供電流分布的路徑。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace current from edge contacts to feature bottoms. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: The seed provides current-distribution paths.","observation":"種子層提供電流分布的路徑。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The seed provides current-distribution paths. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出邊緣接點到孔底的供電路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「種子層提供電流分布的路徑。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace current from edge contacts to feature bottoms\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The seed provides current-distribution paths.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"種子層提供電流分布的路徑。","textEn":"The seed provides current-distribution paths."},{"id":"a065-v8-15-k2","title":"介面與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and filling: principle and limits","text":"種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","textEn":"Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出邊緣接點到孔底的供電路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace current from edge contacts to feature bottoms\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。","種子層提供電流分布的路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","The seed provides current-distribution paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"種子層提供電流分布的路徑。 種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","explanationEn":"The seed provides current-distribution paths. Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}},{"id":"a065-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-15"],"title":"檢查浸潤不足與孔底氣泡","titleEn":"Inspect poor wetting and trapped bottom bubbles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：未潤濕區域可能無法正常電鍍。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Unwetted regions may not plate normally.","instruction":"檢查浸潤不足與孔底氣泡。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「未潤濕區域可能無法正常電鍍。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect poor wetting and trapped bottom bubbles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Unwetted regions may not plate normally.","observation":"未潤濕區域可能無法正常電鍍。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Unwetted regions may not plate normally. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查浸潤不足與孔底氣泡」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「未潤濕區域可能無法正常電鍍。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect poor wetting and trapped bottom bubbles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Unwetted regions may not plate normally.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"未潤濕區域可能無法正常電鍍。","textEn":"Unwetted regions may not plate normally."},{"id":"a065-v8-16-k2","title":"介面與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and filling: principle and limits","text":"種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","textEn":"Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查浸潤不足與孔底氣泡」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect poor wetting and trapped bottom bubbles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["未潤濕區域可能無法正常電鍍。","種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Unwetted regions may not plate normally.","Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未潤濕區域可能無法正常電鍍。 種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","explanationEn":"Unwetted regions may not plate normally. Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}},{"id":"a065-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-16"],"title":"比較前清潔強度與種子損失","titleEn":"Compare preclean intensity with seed loss","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：清潔過程可能同時消耗薄種子。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Cleaning can also consume a thin seed.","instruction":"比較前清潔強度與種子損失。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「清潔過程可能同時消耗薄種子。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare preclean intensity with seed loss. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Cleaning can also consume a thin seed.","observation":"清潔過程可能同時消耗薄種子。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Cleaning can also consume a thin seed. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較前清潔強度與種子損失」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「清潔過程可能同時消耗薄種子。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare preclean intensity with seed loss\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Cleaning can also consume a thin seed.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"清潔過程可能同時消耗薄種子。","textEn":"Cleaning can also consume a thin seed."},{"id":"a065-v8-17-k2","title":"介面與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and filling: principle and limits","text":"種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","textEn":"Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較前清潔強度與種子損失」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare preclean intensity with seed loss\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","清潔過程可能同時消耗薄種子。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。"],"optionsEn":["Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","Cleaning can also consume a thin seed.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔過程可能同時消耗薄種子。 種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","explanationEn":"Cleaning can also consume a thin seed. Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}},{"id":"a065-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-17"],"title":"把填孔空洞回溯至覆蓋缺陷","titleEn":"Trace fill voids back to coverage defects","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電鍍失敗可能源自更早沉積。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Plating failures can originate in earlier deposition.","instruction":"把填孔空洞回溯至覆蓋缺陷。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「電鍍失敗可能源自更早沉積。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Trace fill voids back to coverage defects. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Plating failures can originate in earlier deposition.","observation":"電鍍失敗可能源自更早沉積。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Plating failures can originate in earlier deposition. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「把填孔空洞回溯至覆蓋缺陷」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電鍍失敗可能源自更早沉積。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Trace fill voids back to coverage defects\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Plating failures can originate in earlier deposition.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電鍍失敗可能源自更早沉積。","textEn":"Plating failures can originate in earlier deposition."},{"id":"a065-v8-18-k2","title":"介面與填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Interfaces and filling: principle and limits","text":"種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","textEn":"Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「把填孔空洞回溯至覆蓋缺陷」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Trace fill voids back to coverage defects\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["種子表面氧化不會影響電鍍。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。","電鍍失敗可能源自更早沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Seed oxidation cannot affect plating.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","Plating failures can originate in earlier deposition."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電鍍失敗可能源自更早沉積。 種子連續性、氧化與潤濕會影響後續銅成核。","explanationEn":"Plating failures can originate in earlier deposition. Seed continuity, oxidation and wetting affect subsequent copper nucleation."}}]},{"id":"a065-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"擴散與可靠度","titleEn":"Diffusion and reliability","description":"減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","descriptionEn":"Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability.","steps":[{"id":"a065-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-18"],"title":"以熱處理後元素剖面檢查擴散","titleEn":"Check diffusion using post-anneal elemental profiles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：阻障驗證需要時間與溫度條件。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Barrier validation needs stated time and temperature.","instruction":"以熱處理後元素剖面檢查擴散。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「阻障驗證需要時間與溫度條件。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check diffusion using post-anneal elemental profiles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Barrier validation needs stated time and temperature.","observation":"阻障驗證需要時間與溫度條件。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Barrier validation needs stated time and temperature. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層無限薄一定最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以熱處理後元素剖面檢查擴散」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「阻障驗證需要時間與溫度條件。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check diffusion using post-anneal elemental profiles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Barrier validation needs stated time and temperature.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"阻障驗證需要時間與溫度條件。","textEn":"Barrier validation needs stated time and temperature."},{"id":"a065-v8-19-k2","title":"擴散與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Diffusion and reliability: principle and limits","text":"減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","textEn":"Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以熱處理後元素剖面檢查擴散」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check diffusion using post-anneal elemental profiles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["阻障驗證需要時間與溫度條件。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。"],"optionsEn":["Barrier validation needs stated time and temperature.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻障驗證需要時間與溫度條件。 減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","explanationEn":"Barrier validation needs stated time and temperature. Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}},{"id":"a065-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-19"],"title":"以漏電結構檢查銅污染影響","titleEn":"Assess copper-contamination effects using leakage structures","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：微量擴散可能先表現在電性。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Small diffusion can first appear electrically.","instruction":"以漏電結構檢查銅污染影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「微量擴散可能先表現在電性。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess copper-contamination effects using leakage structures. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Small diffusion can first appear electrically.","observation":"微量擴散可能先表現在電性。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Small diffusion can first appear electrically. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層無限薄一定最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以漏電結構檢查銅污染影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「微量擴散可能先表現在電性。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess copper-contamination effects using leakage structures\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Small diffusion can first appear electrically.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"微量擴散可能先表現在電性。","textEn":"Small diffusion can first appear electrically."},{"id":"a065-v8-20-k2","title":"擴散與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Diffusion and reliability: principle and limits","text":"減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","textEn":"Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以漏電結構檢查銅污染影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess copper-contamination effects using leakage structures\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層無限薄一定最佳。","微量擴散可能先表現在電性。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。"],"optionsEn":["An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","Small diffusion can first appear electrically.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier."],"answer":1,"explanation":"微量擴散可能先表現在電性。 減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","explanationEn":"Small diffusion can first appear electrically. Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}},{"id":"a065-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-20"],"title":"比較附著與熱循環的介面耐受","titleEn":"Compare adhesion and thermal-cycle interface resistance","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：阻擴散合格不代表附著合格。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Passing diffusion control does not prove adequate adhesion.","instruction":"比較附著與熱循環的介面耐受。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「阻擴散合格不代表附著合格。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare adhesion and thermal-cycle interface resistance. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Passing diffusion control does not prove adequate adhesion.","observation":"阻擴散合格不代表附著合格。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Passing diffusion control does not prove adequate adhesion. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層無限薄一定最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較附著與熱循環的介面耐受」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「阻擴散合格不代表附著合格。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare adhesion and thermal-cycle interface resistance\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Passing diffusion control does not prove adequate adhesion.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"阻擴散合格不代表附著合格。","textEn":"Passing diffusion control does not prove adequate adhesion."},{"id":"a065-v8-21-k2","title":"擴散與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Diffusion and reliability: principle and limits","text":"減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","textEn":"Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較附著與熱循環的介面耐受」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare adhesion and thermal-cycle interface resistance\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層無限薄一定最佳。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","阻擴散合格不代表附著合格。"],"optionsEn":["An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","Passing diffusion control does not prove adequate adhesion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"阻擴散合格不代表附著合格。 減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","explanationEn":"Passing diffusion control does not prove adequate adhesion. Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}},{"id":"a065-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-21"],"title":"評估薄襯層的電阻收益與風險","titleEn":"Evaluate resistance benefit and risk of thin liners","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：面積收益需與最薄點可靠度相衡。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Area gains must be balanced against weakest-point reliability.","instruction":"評估薄襯層的電阻收益與風險。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「面積收益需與最薄點可靠度相衡。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Evaluate resistance benefit and risk of thin liners. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Area gains must be balanced against weakest-point reliability.","observation":"面積收益需與最薄點可靠度相衡。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Area gains must be balanced against weakest-point reliability. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層無限薄一定最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「評估薄襯層的電阻收益與風險」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「面積收益需與最薄點可靠度相衡。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Evaluate resistance benefit and risk of thin liners\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Area gains must be balanced against weakest-point reliability.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"面積收益需與最薄點可靠度相衡。","textEn":"Area gains must be balanced against weakest-point reliability."},{"id":"a065-v8-22-k2","title":"擴散與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Diffusion and reliability: principle and limits","text":"減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","textEn":"Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「評估薄襯層的電阻收益與風險」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Evaluate resistance benefit and risk of thin liners\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["面積收益需與最薄點可靠度相衡。","襯層無限薄一定最佳。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。"],"optionsEn":["Area gains must be balanced against weakest-point reliability.","An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier."],"answer":0,"explanation":"面積收益需與最薄點可靠度相衡。 減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","explanationEn":"Area gains must be balanced against weakest-point reliability. Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}},{"id":"a065-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-22"],"title":"比較單一截面與統計取樣結論","titleEn":"Compare one cross section with statistical sampling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部影像不能代表全片缺陷率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: A local image cannot establish wafer defect rate.","instruction":"比較單一截面與統計取樣結論。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「局部影像不能代表全片缺陷率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare one cross section with statistical sampling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: A local image cannot establish wafer defect rate.","observation":"局部影像不能代表全片缺陷率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"A local image cannot establish wafer defect rate. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層無限薄一定最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較單一截面與統計取樣結論」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部影像不能代表全片缺陷率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare one cross section with statistical sampling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"A local image cannot establish wafer defect rate.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部影像不能代表全片缺陷率。","textEn":"A local image cannot establish wafer defect rate."},{"id":"a065-v8-23-k2","title":"擴散與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Diffusion and reliability: principle and limits","text":"減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","textEn":"Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較單一截面與統計取樣結論」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare one cross section with statistical sampling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層無限薄一定最佳。","局部影像不能代表全片缺陷率。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。"],"optionsEn":["An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","A local image cannot establish wafer defect rate.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier."],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部影像不能代表全片缺陷率。 減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","explanationEn":"A local image cannot establish wafer defect rate. Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}},{"id":"a065-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-sputter","v8b-wiring","v8b-copperhistory"],"prerequisiteIds":["a065-v8-23"],"title":"交付覆蓋、導通、擴散與附著評審","titleEn":"Review coverage, continuity, diffusion and adhesion","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：阻障種子整合需要四類證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Barrier–seed integration needs four classes of evidence.","instruction":"交付覆蓋、導通、擴散與附著評審。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「阻障種子整合需要四類證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Review coverage, continuity, diffusion and adhesion. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Barrier–seed integration needs four classes of evidence.","observation":"阻障種子整合需要四類證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Barrier–seed integration needs four classes of evidence. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「襯層無限薄一定最佳。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付覆蓋、導通、擴散與附著評審」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「阻障種子整合需要四類證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Review coverage, continuity, diffusion and adhesion\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Barrier–seed integration needs four classes of evidence.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a065-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"阻障種子整合需要四類證據。","textEn":"Barrier–seed integration needs four classes of evidence."},{"id":"a065-v8-24-k2","title":"擴散與可靠度的原理與限制","titleEn":"Diffusion and reliability: principle and limits","text":"減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","textEn":"Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付覆蓋、導通、擴散與附著評審」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Review coverage, continuity, diffusion and adhesion\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["襯層無限薄一定最佳。","有種子層就不需要任何擴散阻障。","阻障種子整合需要四類證據。"],"optionsEn":["An arbitrarily thin liner is always best.","A seed layer eliminates all need for a diffusion barrier.","Barrier–seed integration needs four classes of evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"阻障種子整合需要四類證據。 減薄襯層增加導電面積，但需保持擴散與附著可靠度。","explanationEn":"Barrier–seed integration needs four classes of evidence. Thinner liners increase conducting area but must retain diffusion and adhesion reliability."}}]}]},{"id":"a066","title":"晶圓電化學銅填孔","titleEn":"Electrochemical copper via filling","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 個工程判讀工作包，逐步研究電化學與供電、傳質與添加劑、超共形填充、缺陷與後段；每步交付圖表、對照、計算或驗證紀錄。","summaryEn":"Work through 24 engineering investigations in four stages: electrochemistry and current, transport and additives, superconformal filling, defects and downstream processing. Each step produces a diagram, comparison, calculation or verification record.","sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"curriculumVersion":8,"scope":"依公開原理編寫的教學課程；24 步是研究與工程判讀任務，不是完整晶圓廠配方或設備操作指令。自訂數據須標示假設，數值不代表任何廠商製程。課程內容完整提供繁體中文與英文。","scopeEn":"Educational investigations based on public principles. These 24 steps are research and engineering-review tasks, not complete fab recipes or equipment operating instructions. Hypothetical data must be labeled and do not represent any vendor process. Full content is supplied in Traditional Chinese and English.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電化學與供電","傳質與添加劑","超共形填充","缺陷與後段"],"labelsEn":["Electrochemistry and current","Transport and additives","Superconformal filling","Defects and downstream processing"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability","stages":[{"id":"a066-v8-stage01","order":1,"title":"電化學與供電","titleEn":"Electrochemistry and current","description":"電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","descriptionEn":"Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area.","steps":[{"id":"a066-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"畫出陽極、陰極與電解液的電流路徑","titleEn":"Draw anode, cathode and electrolyte current paths","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電子與離子在不同路徑傳輸。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Electrons and ions travel through different paths.","instruction":"畫出陽極、陰極與電解液的電流路徑。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「電子與離子在不同路徑傳輸。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Draw anode, cathode and electrolyte current paths. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Electrons and ions travel through different paths.","observation":"電子與離子在不同路徑傳輸。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Electrons and ions travel through different paths. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出陽極、陰極與電解液的電流路徑」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電子與離子在不同路徑傳輸。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Draw anode, cathode and electrolyte current paths\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Electrons and ions travel through different paths.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-01-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電子與離子在不同路徑傳輸。","textEn":"Electrons and ions travel through different paths."},{"id":"a066-v8-01-k2","title":"電化學與供電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrochemistry and current: principle and limits","text":"電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","textEn":"Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出陽極、陰極與電解液的電流路徑」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Draw anode, cathode and electrolyte current paths\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電子與離子在不同路徑傳輸。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。"],"optionsEn":["Electrons and ions travel through different paths.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","More additive always improves fill."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電子與離子在不同路徑傳輸。 電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","explanationEn":"Electrons and ions travel through different paths. Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}},{"id":"a066-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-01"],"title":"用法拉第定律估算理想沉積質量","titleEn":"Estimate ideal deposited mass with Faraday's law","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：實際質量還依賴電流效率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Actual mass also depends on current efficiency.","instruction":"用法拉第定律估算理想沉積質量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「實際質量還依賴電流效率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。\n\n具體演算（全部數據為教學假設）：用純粹教學電荷帳本：Cu²⁺還原為 Cu，假設 Q=0.10 C，M=63.546 g/mol，F=96485 C/mol，z=2。理想質量 m=MQ/(zF)=32.93 μg；若電流效率90%，則為29.64 μg。這不包含任何鍍液組成或操作條件；需再用截面體積與銅密度檢查電荷、體積及損失是否一致。","instructionEn":"Estimate ideal deposited mass with Faraday's law. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Actual mass also depends on current efficiency.\n\nWorked example (all values are teaching assumptions): For an educational charge ledger, reduce Cu²⁺ to Cu with Q=0.10 C, M=63.546 g/mol, F=96485 C/mol and z=2. Ideal mass m=MQ/(zF)=32.93 μg; at 90% current efficiency it is 29.64 μg. No bath composition or operating conditions are supplied. Check consistency against cross-sectional volume and copper density to account for charge, volume and losses.","observation":"實際質量還依賴電流效率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。\n交付 32.93 與29.64 μg，不能把電流效率假設成自動100%。","observationEn":"Actual mass also depends on current efficiency. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.\nReport 32.93 and 29.64 μg without automatically assuming 100% efficiency.","failure":"若報告假設「通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「用法拉第定律估算理想沉積質量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「實際質量還依賴電流效率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。\n本例驗收：交付 32.93 與29.64 μg，不能把電流效率假設成自動100%。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Estimate ideal deposited mass with Faraday's law\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Actual mass also depends on current efficiency.\" and retain one limitation.\nExample acceptance: Report 32.93 and 29.64 μg without automatically assuming 100% efficiency.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-02-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"實際質量還依賴電流效率。","textEn":"Actual mass also depends on current efficiency."},{"id":"a066-v8-02-k2","title":"具體案例、推導與適用限制","titleEn":"Worked case, derivation and applicability","text":"用純粹教學電荷帳本：Cu²⁺還原為 Cu，假設 Q=0.10 C，M=63.546 g/mol，F=96485 C/mol，z=2。理想質量 m=MQ/(zF)=32.93 μg；若電流效率90%，則為29.64 μg。這不包含任何鍍液組成或操作條件；需再用截面體積與銅密度檢查電荷、體積及損失是否一致。","textEn":"For an educational charge ledger, reduce Cu²⁺ to Cu with Q=0.10 C, M=63.546 g/mol, F=96485 C/mol and z=2. Ideal mass m=MQ/(zF)=32.93 μg; at 90% current efficiency it is 29.64 μg. No bath composition or operating conditions are supplied. Check consistency against cross-sectional volume and copper density to account for charge, volume and losses."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「用法拉第定律估算理想沉積質量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Estimate ideal deposited mass with Faraday's law\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","實際質量還依賴電流效率。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。"],"optionsEn":["All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","Actual mass also depends on current efficiency.","More additive always improves fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"實際質量還依賴電流效率。 電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","explanationEn":"Actual mass also depends on current efficiency. Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."},"workedExample":{"hypothetical":true,"text":"用純粹教學電荷帳本：Cu²⁺還原為 Cu，假設 Q=0.10 C，M=63.546 g/mol，F=96485 C/mol，z=2。理想質量 m=MQ/(zF)=32.93 μg；若電流效率90%，則為29.64 μg。這不包含任何鍍液組成或操作條件；需再用截面體積與銅密度檢查電荷、體積及損失是否一致。","textEn":"For an educational charge ledger, reduce Cu²⁺ to Cu with Q=0.10 C, M=63.546 g/mol, F=96485 C/mol and z=2. Ideal mass m=MQ/(zF)=32.93 μg; at 90% current efficiency it is 29.64 μg. No bath composition or operating conditions are supplied. Check consistency against cross-sectional volume and copper density to account for charge, volume and losses.","check":"交付 32.93 與29.64 μg，不能把電流效率假設成自動100%。","checkEn":"Report 32.93 and 29.64 μg without automatically assuming 100% efficiency."}},{"id":"a066-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-02"],"title":"分開總電流與局部電流密度","titleEn":"Separate total current from local current density","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：局部沉積速率由局部條件決定。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Local conditions determine local deposition rate.","instruction":"分開總電流與局部電流密度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「局部沉積速率由局部條件決定。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate total current from local current density. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Local conditions determine local deposition rate.","observation":"局部沉積速率由局部條件決定。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Local conditions determine local deposition rate. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「分開總電流與局部電流密度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「局部沉積速率由局部條件決定。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate total current from local current density\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Local conditions determine local deposition rate.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-03-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"局部沉積速率由局部條件決定。","textEn":"Local conditions determine local deposition rate."},{"id":"a066-v8-03-k2","title":"電化學與供電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrochemistry and current: principle and limits","text":"電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","textEn":"Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「分開總電流與局部電流密度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate total current from local current density\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","局部沉積速率由局部條件決定。"],"optionsEn":["All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","More additive always improves fill.","Local conditions determine local deposition rate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部沉積速率由局部條件決定。 電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","explanationEn":"Local conditions determine local deposition rate. Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}},{"id":"a066-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-03"],"title":"檢查種子層的供電連續性","titleEn":"Check seed-layer electrical continuity","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電化學填充需要可到達的導電表面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Electrochemical fill needs accessible conducting surfaces.","instruction":"檢查種子層的供電連續性。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「電化學填充需要可到達的導電表面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check seed-layer electrical continuity. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Electrochemical fill needs accessible conducting surfaces.","observation":"電化學填充需要可到達的導電表面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Electrochemical fill needs accessible conducting surfaces. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查種子層的供電連續性」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電化學填充需要可到達的導電表面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check seed-layer electrical continuity\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Electrochemical fill needs accessible conducting surfaces.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-04-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電化學填充需要可到達的導電表面。","textEn":"Electrochemical fill needs accessible conducting surfaces."},{"id":"a066-v8-04-k2","title":"電化學與供電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrochemistry and current: principle and limits","text":"電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","textEn":"Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查種子層的供電連續性」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check seed-layer electrical continuity\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電化學填充需要可到達的導電表面。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。"],"optionsEn":["Electrochemical fill needs accessible conducting surfaces.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","More additive always improves fill."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電化學填充需要可到達的導電表面。 電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","explanationEn":"Electrochemical fill needs accessible conducting surfaces. Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}},{"id":"a066-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-04"],"title":"標記阻障與介電層不應鍍銅的區域","titleEn":"Mark regions that should not plate copper","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：材料選擇與遮蔽影響沉積位置。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Material choice and masking affect deposition location.","instruction":"標記阻障與介電層不應鍍銅的區域。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「材料選擇與遮蔽影響沉積位置。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Mark regions that should not plate copper. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Material choice and masking affect deposition location.","observation":"材料選擇與遮蔽影響沉積位置。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Material choice and masking affect deposition location. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「標記阻障與介電層不應鍍銅的區域」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「材料選擇與遮蔽影響沉積位置。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Mark regions that should not plate copper\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Material choice and masking affect deposition location.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-05-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"材料選擇與遮蔽影響沉積位置。","textEn":"Material choice and masking affect deposition location."},{"id":"a066-v8-05-k2","title":"電化學與供電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrochemistry and current: principle and limits","text":"電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","textEn":"Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「標記阻障與介電層不應鍍銅的區域」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Mark regions that should not plate copper\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","材料選擇與遮蔽影響沉積位置。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。"],"optionsEn":["All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","Material choice and masking affect deposition location.","More additive always improves fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料選擇與遮蔽影響沉積位置。 電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","explanationEn":"Material choice and masking affect deposition location. Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}},{"id":"a066-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-05"],"title":"建立假設鍍液與量測資料的邊界","titleEn":"Define the scope of hypothetical electrolyte data","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：教學電化學模型不是商用鍍液配方。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Educational electrochemical models are not commercial bath recipes.","instruction":"建立假設鍍液與量測資料的邊界。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「教學電化學模型不是商用鍍液配方。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Define the scope of hypothetical electrolyte data. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Educational electrochemical models are not commercial bath recipes.","observation":"教學電化學模型不是商用鍍液配方。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Educational electrochemical models are not commercial bath recipes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立假設鍍液與量測資料的邊界」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「教學電化學模型不是商用鍍液配方。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Define the scope of hypothetical electrolyte data\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Educational electrochemical models are not commercial bath recipes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-06-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"教學電化學模型不是商用鍍液配方。","textEn":"Educational electrochemical models are not commercial bath recipes."},{"id":"a066-v8-06-k2","title":"電化學與供電的原理與限制","titleEn":"Electrochemistry and current: principle and limits","text":"電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","textEn":"Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立假設鍍液與量測資料的邊界」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Define the scope of hypothetical electrolyte data\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","教學電化學模型不是商用鍍液配方。"],"optionsEn":["All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","More additive always improves fill.","Educational electrochemical models are not commercial bath recipes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學電化學模型不是商用鍍液配方。 電鍍總電荷與沉積量相關，但需考慮電流效率與實際有效面積。","explanationEn":"Educational electrochemical models are not commercial bath recipes. Plating charge relates to deposited mass but requires current efficiency and effective area."}}]},{"id":"a066-v8-stage02","order":2,"title":"傳質與添加劑","titleEn":"Transport and additives","description":"添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","descriptionEn":"Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates.","steps":[{"id":"a066-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-06"],"title":"畫出孔口到孔底的濃度梯度","titleEn":"Sketch concentration gradients into a feature","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：深部供應可能受傳質限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Deep supply can be mass-transfer-limited.","instruction":"畫出孔口到孔底的濃度梯度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「深部供應可能受傳質限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch concentration gradients into a feature. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Deep supply can be mass-transfer-limited.","observation":"深部供應可能受傳質限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Deep supply can be mass-transfer-limited. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「添加劑越多一定填孔越好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More additive always improves fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「畫出孔口到孔底的濃度梯度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「深部供應可能受傳質限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch concentration gradients into a feature\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Deep supply can be mass-transfer-limited.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-07-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"深部供應可能受傳質限制。","textEn":"Deep supply can be mass-transfer-limited."},{"id":"a066-v8-07-k2","title":"傳質與添加劑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and additives: principle and limits","text":"添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","textEn":"Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「畫出孔口到孔底的濃度梯度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch concentration gradients into a feature\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["深部供應可能受傳質限制。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。"],"optionsEn":["Deep supply can be mass-transfer-limited.","More additive always improves fill.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill."],"answer":0,"explanation":"深部供應可能受傳質限制。 添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","explanationEn":"Deep supply can be mass-transfer-limited. Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}},{"id":"a066-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-07"],"title":"比較擴散、對流與電遷移","titleEn":"Compare diffusion, convection and migration","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：三種輸運機制依條件有不同權重。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The three mechanisms have condition-dependent importance.","instruction":"比較擴散、對流與電遷移。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「三種輸運機制依條件有不同權重。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare diffusion, convection and migration. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The three mechanisms have condition-dependent importance.","observation":"三種輸運機制依條件有不同權重。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The three mechanisms have condition-dependent importance. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「添加劑越多一定填孔越好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More additive always improves fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較擴散、對流與電遷移」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「三種輸運機制依條件有不同權重。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare diffusion, convection and migration\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The three mechanisms have condition-dependent importance.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-08-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"三種輸運機制依條件有不同權重。","textEn":"The three mechanisms have condition-dependent importance."},{"id":"a066-v8-08-k2","title":"傳質與添加劑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and additives: principle and limits","text":"添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","textEn":"Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較擴散、對流與電遷移」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare diffusion, convection and migration\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","三種輸運機制依條件有不同權重。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。"],"optionsEn":["More additive always improves fill.","The three mechanisms have condition-dependent importance.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"三種輸運機制依條件有不同權重。 添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","explanationEn":"The three mechanisms have condition-dependent importance. Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}},{"id":"a066-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-08"],"title":"區分抑制劑、促進劑與整平劑功能","titleEn":"Distinguish suppressor, accelerator and leveler roles","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：添加劑會改變表面反應而非只改導電率。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Additives change surface reactions, not merely conductivity.","instruction":"區分抑制劑、促進劑與整平劑功能。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「添加劑會改變表面反應而非只改導電率。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish suppressor, accelerator and leveler roles. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Additives change surface reactions, not merely conductivity.","observation":"添加劑會改變表面反應而非只改導電率。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Additives change surface reactions, not merely conductivity. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「添加劑越多一定填孔越好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More additive always improves fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「區分抑制劑、促進劑與整平劑功能」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「添加劑會改變表面反應而非只改導電率。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Distinguish suppressor, accelerator and leveler roles\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Additives change surface reactions, not merely conductivity.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-09-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"添加劑會改變表面反應而非只改導電率。","textEn":"Additives change surface reactions, not merely conductivity."},{"id":"a066-v8-09-k2","title":"傳質與添加劑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and additives: principle and limits","text":"添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","textEn":"Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「區分抑制劑、促進劑與整平劑功能」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Distinguish suppressor, accelerator and leveler roles\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","添加劑會改變表面反應而非只改導電率。"],"optionsEn":["More additive always improves fill.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","Additives change surface reactions, not merely conductivity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"添加劑會改變表面反應而非只改導電率。 添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","explanationEn":"Additives change surface reactions, not merely conductivity. Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}},{"id":"a066-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-09"],"title":"比較旋轉或流動對邊界層的影響","titleEn":"Compare flow effects on boundary layers","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：外部流動改善不一定完全解除孔內限制。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: External flow improvements need not remove internal transport limits.","instruction":"比較旋轉或流動對邊界層的影響。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「外部流動改善不一定完全解除孔內限制。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare flow effects on boundary layers. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: External flow improvements need not remove internal transport limits.","observation":"外部流動改善不一定完全解除孔內限制。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"External flow improvements need not remove internal transport limits. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「添加劑越多一定填孔越好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More additive always improves fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較旋轉或流動對邊界層的影響」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「外部流動改善不一定完全解除孔內限制。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare flow effects on boundary layers\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"External flow improvements need not remove internal transport limits.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-10-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"外部流動改善不一定完全解除孔內限制。","textEn":"External flow improvements need not remove internal transport limits."},{"id":"a066-v8-10-k2","title":"傳質與添加劑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and additives: principle and limits","text":"添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","textEn":"Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較旋轉或流動對邊界層的影響」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare flow effects on boundary layers\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["外部流動改善不一定完全解除孔內限制。","添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。"],"optionsEn":["External flow improvements need not remove internal transport limits.","More additive always improves fill.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外部流動改善不一定完全解除孔內限制。 添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","explanationEn":"External flow improvements need not remove internal transport limits. Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}},{"id":"a066-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-10"],"title":"檢查添加劑消耗與鍍液歷程","titleEn":"Assess additive depletion and bath history","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：鍍液狀態會隨使用時間改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bath condition changes with use history.","instruction":"檢查添加劑消耗與鍍液歷程。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「鍍液狀態會隨使用時間改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess additive depletion and bath history. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bath condition changes with use history.","observation":"鍍液狀態會隨使用時間改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bath condition changes with use history. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「添加劑越多一定填孔越好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More additive always improves fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查添加劑消耗與鍍液歷程」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「鍍液狀態會隨使用時間改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess additive depletion and bath history\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bath condition changes with use history.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-11-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"鍍液狀態會隨使用時間改變。","textEn":"Bath condition changes with use history."},{"id":"a066-v8-11-k2","title":"傳質與添加劑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and additives: principle and limits","text":"添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","textEn":"Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查添加劑消耗與鍍液歷程」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess additive depletion and bath history\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","鍍液狀態會隨使用時間改變。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。"],"optionsEn":["More additive always improves fill.","Bath condition changes with use history.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鍍液狀態會隨使用時間改變。 添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","explanationEn":"Bath condition changes with use history. Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}},{"id":"a066-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-11"],"title":"比較定電流與定電位的觀測量","titleEn":"Compare observables under current and potential control","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：控制一個量時另一個量提供狀態資訊。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: When one is controlled, the other provides state information.","instruction":"比較定電流與定電位的觀測量。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「控制一個量時另一個量提供狀態資訊。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare observables under current and potential control. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: When one is controlled, the other provides state information.","observation":"控制一個量時另一個量提供狀態資訊。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"When one is controlled, the other provides state information. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「添加劑越多一定填孔越好。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"More additive always improves fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較定電流與定電位的觀測量」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「控制一個量時另一個量提供狀態資訊。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare observables under current and potential control\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"When one is controlled, the other provides state information.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-12-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"控制一個量時另一個量提供狀態資訊。","textEn":"When one is controlled, the other provides state information."},{"id":"a066-v8-12-k2","title":"傳質與添加劑的原理與限制","titleEn":"Transport and additives: principle and limits","text":"添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","textEn":"Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較定電流與定電位的觀測量」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare observables under current and potential control\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["添加劑越多一定填孔越好。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","控制一個量時另一個量提供狀態資訊。"],"optionsEn":["More additive always improves fill.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","When one is controlled, the other provides state information."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制一個量時另一個量提供狀態資訊。 添加劑、流場與電位共同影響不同位置的沉積速率。","explanationEn":"When one is controlled, the other provides state information. Additives, flow and potential jointly affect local deposition rates."}}]},{"id":"a066-v8-stage03","order":3,"title":"超共形填充","titleEn":"Superconformal filling","description":"自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","descriptionEn":"Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate.","steps":[{"id":"a066-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-12"],"title":"繪製共形填充與自底向上填充","titleEn":"Sketch conformal and bottom-up filling","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：底部較快成長可減少封口空洞。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Faster bottom growth can reduce pinch-off voids.","instruction":"繪製共形填充與自底向上填充。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「底部較快成長可減少封口空洞。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Sketch conformal and bottom-up filling. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Faster bottom growth can reduce pinch-off voids.","observation":"底部較快成長可減少封口空洞。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Faster bottom growth can reduce pinch-off voids. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「繪製共形填充與自底向上填充」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「底部較快成長可減少封口空洞。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Sketch conformal and bottom-up filling\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Faster bottom growth can reduce pinch-off voids.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-13-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"底部較快成長可減少封口空洞。","textEn":"Faster bottom growth can reduce pinch-off voids."},{"id":"a066-v8-13-k2","title":"超共形填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Superconformal filling: principle and limits","text":"自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","textEn":"Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「繪製共形填充與自底向上填充」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Sketch conformal and bottom-up filling\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["底部較快成長可減少封口空洞。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Faster bottom growth can reduce pinch-off voids.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","A shiny surface proves void-free features."],"answer":0,"explanation":"底部較快成長可減少封口空洞。 自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","explanationEn":"Faster bottom growth can reduce pinch-off voids. Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}},{"id":"a066-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-13"],"title":"追蹤填充前緣與孔口剩餘空間","titleEn":"Track fill fronts and remaining opening","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：孔口必須保持足夠傳輸通道。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: The opening must retain sufficient transport access.","instruction":"追蹤填充前緣與孔口剩餘空間。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「孔口必須保持足夠傳輸通道。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Track fill fronts and remaining opening. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: The opening must retain sufficient transport access.","observation":"孔口必須保持足夠傳輸通道。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"The opening must retain sufficient transport access. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「追蹤填充前緣與孔口剩餘空間」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「孔口必須保持足夠傳輸通道。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Track fill fronts and remaining opening\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"The opening must retain sufficient transport access.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-14-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"孔口必須保持足夠傳輸通道。","textEn":"The opening must retain sufficient transport access."},{"id":"a066-v8-14-k2","title":"超共形填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Superconformal filling: principle and limits","text":"自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","textEn":"Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「追蹤填充前緣與孔口剩餘空間」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Track fill fronts and remaining opening\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","孔口必須保持足夠傳輸通道。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","The opening must retain sufficient transport access.","A shiny surface proves void-free features."],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔口必須保持足夠傳輸通道。 自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","explanationEn":"The opening must retain sufficient transport access. Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}},{"id":"a066-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-14"],"title":"比較窄孔與寬槽的填充演化","titleEn":"Compare filling of narrow vias and wide trenches","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不同幾何需要不同局部速率分布。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Different geometries require different local rate distributions.","instruction":"比較窄孔與寬槽的填充演化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「不同幾何需要不同局部速率分布。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare filling of narrow vias and wide trenches. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Different geometries require different local rate distributions.","observation":"不同幾何需要不同局部速率分布。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Different geometries require different local rate distributions. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較窄孔與寬槽的填充演化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不同幾何需要不同局部速率分布。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare filling of narrow vias and wide trenches\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Different geometries require different local rate distributions.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-15-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不同幾何需要不同局部速率分布。","textEn":"Different geometries require different local rate distributions."},{"id":"a066-v8-15-k2","title":"超共形填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Superconformal filling: principle and limits","text":"自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","textEn":"Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較窄孔與寬槽的填充演化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare filling of narrow vias and wide trenches\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","不同幾何需要不同局部速率分布。"],"optionsEn":["Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","A shiny surface proves void-free features.","Different geometries require different local rate distributions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同幾何需要不同局部速率分布。 自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","explanationEn":"Different geometries require different local rate distributions. Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}},{"id":"a066-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-15"],"title":"檢查底部氣泡與未潤濕區","titleEn":"Inspect bottom bubbles and unwetted regions","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：氣泡可隔斷電解液與表面。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Bubbles can isolate the surface from electrolyte.","instruction":"檢查底部氣泡與未潤濕區。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「氣泡可隔斷電解液與表面。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect bottom bubbles and unwetted regions. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Bubbles can isolate the surface from electrolyte.","observation":"氣泡可隔斷電解液與表面。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Bubbles can isolate the surface from electrolyte. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查底部氣泡與未潤濕區」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「氣泡可隔斷電解液與表面。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Inspect bottom bubbles and unwetted regions\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Bubbles can isolate the surface from electrolyte.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-16-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"氣泡可隔斷電解液與表面。","textEn":"Bubbles can isolate the surface from electrolyte."},{"id":"a066-v8-16-k2","title":"超共形填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Superconformal filling: principle and limits","text":"自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","textEn":"Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查底部氣泡與未潤濕區」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Inspect bottom bubbles and unwetted regions\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["氣泡可隔斷電解液與表面。","孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Bubbles can isolate the surface from electrolyte.","Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","A shiny surface proves void-free features."],"answer":0,"explanation":"氣泡可隔斷電解液與表面。 自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","explanationEn":"Bubbles can isolate the surface from electrolyte. Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}},{"id":"a066-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-16"],"title":"將種子斷裂與接縫空洞分開","titleEn":"Separate seed discontinuity from seam voids","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相似空洞可能有不同上游來源。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Similar voids can have different upstream origins.","instruction":"將種子斷裂與接縫空洞分開。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「相似空洞可能有不同上游來源。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Separate seed discontinuity from seam voids. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Similar voids can have different upstream origins.","observation":"相似空洞可能有不同上游來源。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Similar voids can have different upstream origins. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「將種子斷裂與接縫空洞分開」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相似空洞可能有不同上游來源。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Separate seed discontinuity from seam voids\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Similar voids can have different upstream origins.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-17-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相似空洞可能有不同上游來源。","textEn":"Similar voids can have different upstream origins."},{"id":"a066-v8-17-k2","title":"超共形填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Superconformal filling: principle and limits","text":"自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","textEn":"Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「將種子斷裂與接縫空洞分開」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Separate seed discontinuity from seam voids\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","相似空洞可能有不同上游來源。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","Similar voids can have different upstream origins.","A shiny surface proves void-free features."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相似空洞可能有不同上游來源。 自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","explanationEn":"Similar voids can have different upstream origins. Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}},{"id":"a066-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-17"],"title":"比較過鍍厚度與填孔完成度","titleEn":"Compare overburden thickness with fill completeness","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：大量過鍍不能補救所有內部空洞。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Heavy overplating cannot repair every internal void.","instruction":"比較過鍍厚度與填孔完成度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「大量過鍍不能補救所有內部空洞。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare overburden thickness with fill completeness. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Heavy overplating cannot repair every internal void.","observation":"大量過鍍不能補救所有內部空洞。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Heavy overplating cannot repair every internal void. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較過鍍厚度與填孔完成度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「大量過鍍不能補救所有內部空洞。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare overburden thickness with fill completeness\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Heavy overplating cannot repair every internal void.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-18-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"大量過鍍不能補救所有內部空洞。","textEn":"Heavy overplating cannot repair every internal void."},{"id":"a066-v8-18-k2","title":"超共形填充的原理與限制","titleEn":"Superconformal filling: principle and limits","text":"自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","textEn":"Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較過鍍厚度與填孔完成度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare overburden thickness with fill completeness\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["孔口沉積最快就是最佳填孔。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","大量過鍍不能補救所有內部空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Fastest opening deposition is the best fill.","A shiny surface proves void-free features.","Heavy overplating cannot repair every internal void."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大量過鍍不能補救所有內部空洞。 自底向上填充需要抑制過早封口，不能只提高整體沉積速度。","explanationEn":"Heavy overplating cannot repair every internal void. Bottom-up fill requires avoiding early closure, not merely increasing overall deposition rate."}}]},{"id":"a066-v8-stage04","order":4,"title":"缺陷與後段","titleEn":"Defects and downstream processing","description":"填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","descriptionEn":"Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior.","steps":[{"id":"a066-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-18"],"title":"估算電荷與截面體積是否一致","titleEn":"Check consistency between charge and filled volume","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：不一致可能來自效率或面積估算錯誤。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Disagreement can reflect efficiency or area-estimation errors.","instruction":"估算電荷與截面體積是否一致。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。附上帶材料、方向與尺度標記的示意圖，圈出一處不能由圖單獨推論的量。最後以「不一致可能來自效率或面積估算錯誤。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Check consistency between charge and filled volume. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Attach a diagram labeled with materials, directions and scales; circle one quantity not inferable from the drawing alone. Finally check your inference against this principle: Disagreement can reflect efficiency or area-estimation errors.","observation":"不一致可能來自效率或面積估算錯誤。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Disagreement can reflect efficiency or area-estimation errors. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A shiny surface proves void-free features.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「估算電荷與截面體積是否一致」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「不一致可能來自效率或面積估算錯誤。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Check consistency between charge and filled volume\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Disagreement can reflect efficiency or area-estimation errors.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-19-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"不一致可能來自效率或面積估算錯誤。","textEn":"Disagreement can reflect efficiency or area-estimation errors."},{"id":"a066-v8-19-k2","title":"缺陷與後段的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and downstream processing: principle and limits","text":"填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","textEn":"Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「估算電荷與截面體積是否一致」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Check consistency between charge and filled volume\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["不一致可能來自效率或面積估算錯誤。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。"],"optionsEn":["Disagreement can reflect efficiency or area-estimation errors.","A shiny surface proves void-free features.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不一致可能來自效率或面積估算錯誤。 填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","explanationEn":"Disagreement can reflect efficiency or area-estimation errors. Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}},{"id":"a066-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-19"],"title":"檢查沉積後應力與晶粒演化","titleEn":"Assess post-deposition stress and grain evolution","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：銅組織可能隨時間或熱處理改變。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Copper microstructure can evolve with time or heating.","instruction":"檢查沉積後應力與晶粒演化。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立兩種條件的對照表，分別寫出固定量、改變量與可量測的輸出。最後以「銅組織可能隨時間或熱處理改變。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Assess post-deposition stress and grain evolution. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a two-condition comparison table listing fixed quantities, changed quantities and measurable outputs. Finally check your inference against this principle: Copper microstructure can evolve with time or heating.","observation":"銅組織可能隨時間或熱處理改變。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Copper microstructure can evolve with time or heating. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A shiny surface proves void-free features.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「檢查沉積後應力與晶粒演化」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「銅組織可能隨時間或熱處理改變。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Assess post-deposition stress and grain evolution\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Copper microstructure can evolve with time or heating.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-20-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"銅組織可能隨時間或熱處理改變。","textEn":"Copper microstructure can evolve with time or heating."},{"id":"a066-v8-20-k2","title":"缺陷與後段的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and downstream processing: principle and limits","text":"填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","textEn":"Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「檢查沉積後應力與晶粒演化」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Assess post-deposition stress and grain evolution\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","銅組織可能隨時間或熱處理改變。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。"],"optionsEn":["A shiny surface proves void-free features.","Copper microstructure can evolve with time or heating.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper."],"answer":1,"explanation":"銅組織可能隨時間或熱處理改變。 填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","explanationEn":"Copper microstructure can evolve with time or heating. Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}},{"id":"a066-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-20"],"title":"比較 CMP 前後的缺陷可見度","titleEn":"Compare defect visibility before and after CMP","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：平坦化可能暴露原先埋藏空洞。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Planarization can expose previously buried voids.","instruction":"比較 CMP 前後的缺陷可見度。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。用自訂並標明的假設資料做一個計算或分類例，保留單位、分母與中間結果。最後以「平坦化可能暴露原先埋藏空洞。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Compare defect visibility before and after CMP. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Use explicitly hypothetical data for one calculation or classification; retain units, denominators and intermediate results. Finally check your inference against this principle: Planarization can expose previously buried voids.","observation":"平坦化可能暴露原先埋藏空洞。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Planarization can expose previously buried voids. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A shiny surface proves void-free features.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「比較 CMP 前後的缺陷可見度」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「平坦化可能暴露原先埋藏空洞。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Compare defect visibility before and after CMP\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Planarization can expose previously buried voids.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-21-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"平坦化可能暴露原先埋藏空洞。","textEn":"Planarization can expose previously buried voids."},{"id":"a066-v8-21-k2","title":"缺陷與後段的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and downstream processing: principle and limits","text":"填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","textEn":"Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「比較 CMP 前後的缺陷可見度」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Compare defect visibility before and after CMP\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","平坦化可能暴露原先埋藏空洞。"],"optionsEn":["A shiny surface proves void-free features.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","Planarization can expose previously buried voids."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平坦化可能暴露原先埋藏空洞。 填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","explanationEn":"Planarization can expose previously buried voids. Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}},{"id":"a066-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-21"],"title":"以通孔鏈量測高阻與開路","titleEn":"Measure high resistance and opens using via chains","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：電性量測可放大稀有填充失敗。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Electrical measurements can reveal rare fill failures.","instruction":"以通孔鏈量測高阻與開路。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。建立因果與量測對照表，區分直接觀測、模型推論與尚需額外證據的結論。最後以「電性量測可放大稀有填充失敗。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Measure high resistance and opens using via chains. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Build a cause–measurement table separating direct observations, model inferences and conclusions needing more evidence. Finally check your inference against this principle: Electrical measurements can reveal rare fill failures.","observation":"電性量測可放大稀有填充失敗。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Electrical measurements can reveal rare fill failures. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A shiny surface proves void-free features.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「以通孔鏈量測高阻與開路」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「電性量測可放大稀有填充失敗。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Measure high resistance and opens using via chains\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Electrical measurements can reveal rare fill failures.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-22-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"電性量測可放大稀有填充失敗。","textEn":"Electrical measurements can reveal rare fill failures."},{"id":"a066-v8-22-k2","title":"缺陷與後段的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and downstream processing: principle and limits","text":"填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","textEn":"Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「以通孔鏈量測高阻與開路」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Measure high resistance and opens using via chains\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["電性量測可放大稀有填充失敗。","表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical measurements can reveal rare fill failures.","A shiny surface proves void-free features.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性量測可放大稀有填充失敗。 填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","explanationEn":"Electrical measurements can reveal rare fill failures. Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}},{"id":"a066-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-22"],"title":"建立鍍液監控與缺陷趨勢對照","titleEn":"Relate bath monitoring to defect trends","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：相關趨勢需對照材料與設備變動。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Correlations need controls for material and equipment changes.","instruction":"建立鍍液監控與缺陷趨勢對照。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。列出一個可能混淆原因，提出能區分兩個解釋的對照或額外量測。最後以「相關趨勢需對照材料與設備變動。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Relate bath monitoring to defect trends. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. List one plausible confounder and propose a control or measurement distinguishing two explanations. Finally check your inference against this principle: Correlations need controls for material and equipment changes.","observation":"相關趨勢需對照材料與設備變動。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Correlations need controls for material and equipment changes. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A shiny surface proves void-free features.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「建立鍍液監控與缺陷趨勢對照」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「相關趨勢需對照材料與設備變動。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Relate bath monitoring to defect trends\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Correlations need controls for material and equipment changes.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-23-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"相關趨勢需對照材料與設備變動。","textEn":"Correlations need controls for material and equipment changes."},{"id":"a066-v8-23-k2","title":"缺陷與後段的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and downstream processing: principle and limits","text":"填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","textEn":"Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「建立鍍液監控與缺陷趨勢對照」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Relate bath monitoring to defect trends\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","相關趨勢需對照材料與設備變動。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。"],"optionsEn":["A shiny surface proves void-free features.","Correlations need controls for material and equipment changes.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相關趨勢需對照材料與設備變動。 填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","explanationEn":"Correlations need controls for material and equipment changes. Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}},{"id":"a066-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-plating","v8b-lamdep","v8b-copperhistory","v8b-interconnect"],"prerequisiteIds":["a066-v8-23"],"title":"交付電荷、截面與電性一致性報告","titleEn":"Deliver charge, cross-section and electrical consistency","objective":"透過本步證據判讀：填孔成功需要多種相互支持的證據。","objectiveEn":"Use this investigation to assess the following principle: Successful fill needs mutually supporting evidence types.","instruction":"交付電荷、截面與電性一致性報告。先讀本步來源，標出其實際材料、圖形或工具適用範圍，再以教學草圖或明確假設資料完成任務。完成一頁審查紀錄，列出接受條件、證據缺口與不應外推的範圍。最後以「填孔成功需要多種相互支持的證據。」檢查推論是否超出證據。","instructionEn":"Deliver charge, cross-section and electrical consistency. Read the step sources and identify their actual material, pattern or tool scope. Complete the task using an educational sketch or explicitly hypothetical data. Complete a one-page review listing acceptance criteria, evidence gaps and limits on extrapolation. Finally check your inference against this principle: Successful fill needs mutually supporting evidence types.","observation":"填孔成功需要多種相互支持的證據。 本步須保留至少一項直接觀測與一項推論的區別。","observationEn":"Successful fill needs mutually supporting evidence types. Preserve the distinction between at least one direct observation and one inference.","failure":"若報告假設「表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。」，回到本階段原理重畫因果鏈，並補上反例或未量測項。","failureEn":"If the report assumes \"A shiny surface proves void-free features.\", revisit the stage principle, redraw the causal chain and add a counterexample or unmeasured quantity.","check":"交付「交付電荷、截面與電性一致性報告」的圖表或計算、採用來源、假設與單位；說明本步結論「填孔成功需要多種相互支持的證據。」可由哪些證據支持，並保留一項限制。","checkEn":"Submit the diagram, table or calculation for \"Deliver charge, cross-section and electrical consistency\", with sources, assumptions and units. Identify evidence supporting \"Successful fill needs mutually supporting evidence types.\" and retain one limitation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a066-v8-24-k1","title":"本步技術判讀","titleEn":"Step-specific technical interpretation","text":"填孔成功需要多種相互支持的證據。","textEn":"Successful fill needs mutually supporting evidence types."},{"id":"a066-v8-24-k2","title":"缺陷與後段的原理與限制","titleEn":"Defects and downstream processing: principle and limits","text":"填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","textEn":"Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「交付電荷、截面與電性一致性報告」後，哪項判讀可靠？","questionEn":"After \"Deliver charge, cross-section and electrical consistency\", which interpretation is defensible?","options":["表面光亮就證明孔內沒有空洞。","通過多少電荷就保證全部都變成銅。","填孔成功需要多種相互支持的證據。"],"optionsEn":["A shiny surface proves void-free features.","All passed charge is guaranteed to become copper.","Successful fill needs mutually supporting evidence types."],"answer":2,"explanation":"填孔成功需要多種相互支持的證據。 填銅驗收需連結空洞、應力、晶粒、平坦化與電性。","explanationEn":"Successful fill needs mutually supporting evidence types. Copper-fill acceptance links voids, stress, grains, planarization and electrical behavior."}}]}]},{"id":"a067","title":"化學機械平坦化","titleEn":"Chemical mechanical planarization","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從移除量與平坦度、碟陷與侵蝕到整合驗收：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Removal versus planarity and Dishing and erosion to Integration acceptance: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["移除量與平坦度","圖形密度","研磨墊狀態","研磨後潔淨"],"labelsEn":["Removal versus planarity","Pattern density","Pad condition","Post-CMP cleanliness"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a067-stage01","order":1,"title":"移除量與平坦度 → 晶圓徑向控制","titleEn":"Removal versus planarity to Radial wafer control","description":"把「移除量與平坦度」「Preston 近似」「晶圓徑向控制」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Removal versus planarity, Preston approximation, Radial wafer control.","steps":[{"id":"a067-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"移除量與平坦度：建立模型","titleEn":"Removal versus planarity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography.","instruction":"畫三點研磨前後高度並分算移除量和剩餘高差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設同一高度基準下三個配對測點研磨前為 110、100、90 nm，研磨後為 75、70、65 nm。逐點移除量為 35、30、25 nm，平均 30 nm；表面高度極差由 20 降為 10 nm。請分別畫高度與移除量，不把平均移除量當成平坦度；三點不足以代表整片晶圓。","instructionEn":"Draw before/after heights at three sites and calculate removal separately from residual height difference. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume three matched sites share one height datum: before polishing 110, 100 and 90 nm; after 75, 70 and 65 nm. Removal is 35, 30 and 25 nm, averaging 30 nm; surface-height range falls from 20 to 10 nm. Plot height and removal separately. Mean removal is not flatness, and three sites do not characterize a wafer.","observation":"均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化；配對測點可降低空間錯配誤差。","observationEn":"Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography; Matched sites reduce spatial mismatch error.","failure":"若採用「把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「移除量與平坦度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化。\n算例驗收：驗算平均移除 30 nm、殘餘高度極差 10 nm，並標出配對測點與共同基準。","checkEn":"Submit the Removal versus planarity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 30 nm mean removal and 10 nm residual height range; identify matched sites and the common datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-01-k1","title":"移除量與平坦度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Removal versus planarity / Physics and model","text":"機制：均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography."},{"id":"a067-v8-01-k2","title":"移除量與平坦度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Removal versus planarity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦」。\n假設數值與推算：假設同一高度基準下三個配對測點研磨前為 110、100、90 nm，研磨後為 75、70、65 nm。逐點移除量為 35、30、25 nm，平均 30 nm；表面高度極差由 20 降為 10 nm。請分別畫高度與移除量，不把平均移除量當成平坦度；三點不足以代表整片晶圓。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume three matched sites share one height datum: before polishing 110, 100 and 90 nm; after 75, 70 and 65 nm. Removal is 35, 30 and 25 nm, averaging 30 nm; surface-height range falls from 20 to 10 nm. Plot height and removal separately. Mean removal is not flatness, and three sites do not characterize a wafer."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「移除量與平坦度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Removal versus planarity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化","把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦","把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料"],"optionsEn":["Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography","Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization","Using one k for every film and slurry"],"answer":0,"explanation":"均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-01"],"title":"移除量與平坦度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Removal versus planarity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization.","instruction":"接續前一步「移除量與平坦度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：配對測點可降低空間錯配誤差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Removal versus planarity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Matched sites reduce spatial mismatch error. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化；配對測點可降低空間錯配誤差。","observationEn":"Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography; Matched sites reduce spatial mismatch error.","failure":"若採用「把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「移除量與平坦度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「配對測點可降低空間錯配誤差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Removal versus planarity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Matched sites reduce spatial mismatch error\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-02-k1","title":"移除量與平坦度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Removal versus planarity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：配對測點可降低空間錯配誤差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Matched sites reduce spatial mismatch error."},{"id":"a067-v8-02-k2","title":"移除量與平坦度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Removal versus planarity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦」與「均勻移除不保證原有地形被平坦化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization\" is not equivalent to \"Uniform removal need not flatten existing topography\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「移除量與平坦度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Removal versus planarity?","options":["把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料","配對測點可降低空間錯配誤差","把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦"],"optionsEn":["Using one k for every film and slurry","Matched sites reduce spatial mismatch error","Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization"],"answer":1,"explanation":"配對測點可降低空間錯配誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Matched sites reduce spatial mismatch error. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-02"],"title":"Preston 近似：建立模型","titleEn":"Preston approximation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range.","instruction":"自訂壓力與相對速度矩陣，以 R=kPV 比較相對速率並註明 k 固定假設。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Choose hypothetical pressure and speed pairs; compare R=kPV with a stated constant-k assumption. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用；摩擦熱可能改變經驗係數。","observationEn":"A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range; Frictional heating can change the empirical coefficient.","failure":"若採用「把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one k for every film and slurry\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「Preston 近似」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用。","checkEn":"Submit the Preston approximation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-03-k1","title":"Preston 近似／物理與模型","titleEn":"Preston approximation / Physics and model","text":"機制：線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用。","textEn":"Mechanism: A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range."},{"id":"a067-v8-03-k2","title":"Preston 近似／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Preston approximation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one k for every film and slurry."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「Preston 近似」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Preston approximation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料","用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜","線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用"],"optionsEn":["Using one k for every film and slurry","Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean","A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range"],"answer":2,"explanation":"線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-03"],"title":"Preston 近似：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Preston approximation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one k for every film and slurry.","instruction":"接續前一步「Preston 近似」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：摩擦熱可能改變經驗係數。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Preston approximation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one k for every film and slurry\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Frictional heating can change the empirical coefficient. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用；摩擦熱可能改變經驗係數。","observationEn":"A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range; Frictional heating can change the empirical coefficient.","failure":"若採用「把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one k for every film and slurry\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「Preston 近似」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「摩擦熱可能改變經驗係數」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Preston approximation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Frictional heating can change the empirical coefficient\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-04-k1","title":"Preston 近似／物理與模型","titleEn":"Preston approximation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：摩擦熱可能改變經驗係數。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Frictional heating can change the empirical coefficient."},{"id":"a067-v8-04-k2","title":"Preston 近似／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Preston approximation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料」與「線性經驗式只在校正範圍內可用」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one k for every film and slurry\" is not equivalent to \"A linear empirical law is valid only in its calibrated range\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「Preston 近似」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Preston approximation?","options":["摩擦熱可能改變經驗係數","把同一 k 套用所有膜材與漿料","用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜"],"optionsEn":["Frictional heating can change the empirical coefficient","Using one k for every film and slurry","Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean"],"answer":0,"explanation":"摩擦熱可能改變經驗係數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Frictional heating can change the empirical coefficient. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-04"],"title":"晶圓徑向控制：建立模型","titleEn":"Radial wafer control: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「區域控制需要保留空間資料」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Zonal control requires spatial data.","instruction":"畫中心、中圈與邊緣厚度偏差，指定各區壓力修正方向。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plot center, middle and edge thickness errors and assign pressure-correction directions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"區域控制需要保留空間資料；邊緣排除寬度會改變均勻度指標。","observationEn":"Zonal control requires spatial data; Edge exclusion changes uniformity metrics.","failure":"若採用「用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶圓徑向控制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：區域控制需要保留空間資料。","checkEn":"Submit the Radial wafer control diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Zonal control requires spatial data.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-05-k1","title":"晶圓徑向控制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Radial wafer control / Physics and model","text":"機制：區域控制需要保留空間資料。","textEn":"Mechanism: Zonal control requires spatial data."},{"id":"a067-v8-05-k2","title":"晶圓徑向控制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Radial wafer control / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶圓徑向控制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Radial wafer control, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率","區域控制需要保留空間資料","用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜"],"optionsEn":["Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate","Zonal control requires spatial data","Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean"],"answer":1,"explanation":"區域控制需要保留空間資料；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Zonal control requires spatial data. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-05"],"title":"晶圓徑向控制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Radial wafer control: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶圓徑向控制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：邊緣排除寬度會改變均勻度指標。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Radial wafer control artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Edge exclusion changes uniformity metrics. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"區域控制需要保留空間資料；邊緣排除寬度會改變均勻度指標。","observationEn":"Zonal control requires spatial data; Edge exclusion changes uniformity metrics.","failure":"若採用「用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶圓徑向控制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「邊緣排除寬度會改變均勻度指標」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Radial wafer control, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Edge exclusion changes uniformity metrics\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-06-k1","title":"晶圓徑向控制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Radial wafer control / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：邊緣排除寬度會改變均勻度指標。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Edge exclusion changes uniformity metrics."},{"id":"a067-v8-06-k2","title":"晶圓徑向控制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Radial wafer control / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜」與「區域控制需要保留空間資料」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean\" is not equivalent to \"Zonal control requires spatial data\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶圓徑向控制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Radial wafer control?","options":["用全片平均遮住邊緣殘膜","把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率","邊緣排除寬度會改變均勻度指標"],"optionsEn":["Hiding edge residue behind the wafer mean","Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate","Edge exclusion changes uniformity metrics"],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣排除寬度會改變均勻度指標；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edge exclusion changes uniformity metrics. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a067-stage02","order":2,"title":"圖形密度 → 停止層選擇性","titleEn":"Pattern density to Stop-layer selectivity","description":"把「圖形密度」「碟陷與侵蝕」「停止層選擇性」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pattern density, Dishing and erosion, Stop-layer selectivity.","steps":[{"id":"a067-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-06"],"title":"圖形密度：建立模型","titleEn":"Pattern density: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Pattern density changes local contact and removal.","instruction":"並列密線與孤立線截面，標記相同研磨時間後的局部形貌。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare dense and isolated lines and mark local topography after equal polishing time. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除；密度視窗大小也是模型條件。","observationEn":"Pattern density changes local contact and removal; Density-window size is a model condition.","failure":"若採用「把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「圖形密度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除。","checkEn":"Submit the Pattern density diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Pattern density changes local contact and removal.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-07-k1","title":"圖形密度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pattern density / Physics and model","text":"機制：圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除。","textEn":"Mechanism: Pattern density changes local contact and removal."},{"id":"a067-v8-07-k2","title":"圖形密度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pattern density / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「圖形密度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pattern density, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除","把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率","只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者"],"optionsEn":["Pattern density changes local contact and removal","Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate","Using one roughness number to identify both"],"answer":0,"explanation":"圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pattern density changes local contact and removal. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-07"],"title":"圖形密度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pattern density: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate.","instruction":"接續前一步「圖形密度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：密度視窗大小也是模型條件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pattern density artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Density-window size is a model condition. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除；密度視窗大小也是模型條件。","observationEn":"Pattern density changes local contact and removal; Density-window size is a model condition.","failure":"若採用「把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「圖形密度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「密度視窗大小也是模型條件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pattern density, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Density-window size is a model condition\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-08-k1","title":"圖形密度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pattern density / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：密度視窗大小也是模型條件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Density-window size is a model condition."},{"id":"a067-v8-08-k2","title":"圖形密度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pattern density / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率」與「圖形密度改變局部接觸與材料移除」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate\" is not equivalent to \"Pattern density changes local contact and removal\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「圖形密度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pattern density?","options":["只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者","密度視窗大小也是模型條件","把裸膜速率直接當成圖形晶圓速率"],"optionsEn":["Using one roughness number to identify both","Density-window size is a model condition","Equating blanket-film rate with patterned-wafer rate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"密度視窗大小也是模型條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Density-window size is a model condition. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-08"],"title":"碟陷與侵蝕：建立模型","titleEn":"Dishing and erosion: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities.","instruction":"分別畫寬金屬線中央凹陷及密集區整體下沉，標示量測基準。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw wide-line center recess and dense-area lowering with measurement datums. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量；凹陷基準要連到鄰近介質高度。","observationEn":"Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities; Recess references need adjacent dielectric height.","failure":"若採用「只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one roughness number to identify both\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「碟陷與侵蝕」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量。","checkEn":"Submit the Dishing and erosion diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-09-k1","title":"碟陷與侵蝕／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dishing and erosion / Physics and model","text":"機制：碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量。","textEn":"Mechanism: Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities."},{"id":"a067-v8-09-k2","title":"碟陷與侵蝕／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dishing and erosion / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one roughness number to identify both."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「碟陷與侵蝕」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dishing and erosion, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者","把選擇性當成無限停止能力","碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量"],"optionsEn":["Using one roughness number to identify both","Treating selectivity as an infinite stop","Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities"],"answer":2,"explanation":"碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-09"],"title":"碟陷與侵蝕：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dishing and erosion: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one roughness number to identify both.","instruction":"接續前一步「碟陷與侵蝕」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：凹陷基準要連到鄰近介質高度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dishing and erosion artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one roughness number to identify both\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Recess references need adjacent dielectric height. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量；凹陷基準要連到鄰近介質高度。","observationEn":"Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities; Recess references need adjacent dielectric height.","failure":"若採用「只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one roughness number to identify both\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「碟陷與侵蝕」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「凹陷基準要連到鄰近介質高度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dishing and erosion, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Recess references need adjacent dielectric height\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-10-k1","title":"碟陷與侵蝕／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dishing and erosion / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：凹陷基準要連到鄰近介質高度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Recess references need adjacent dielectric height."},{"id":"a067-v8-10-k2","title":"碟陷與侵蝕／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dishing and erosion / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者」與「碟陷與侵蝕是不同的幾何量」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one roughness number to identify both\" is not equivalent to \"Dishing and erosion are different geometric quantities\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「碟陷與侵蝕」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dishing and erosion?","options":["凹陷基準要連到鄰近介質高度","只給一個粗糙度數字判斷兩者","把選擇性當成無限停止能力"],"optionsEn":["Recess references need adjacent dielectric height","Using one roughness number to identify both","Treating selectivity as an infinite stop"],"answer":0,"explanation":"凹陷基準要連到鄰近介質高度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Recess references need adjacent dielectric height. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-10"],"title":"停止層選擇性：建立模型","titleEn":"Stop-layer selectivity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss.","instruction":"假設兩膜移除速率，算選擇比並追蹤過研磨後停止層厚度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Assume two removal rates, compute selectivity and track stop-layer loss during overpolish. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失；過研磨時間和停止層損失共同評估。","observationEn":"High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss; Assess overpolish time with stop-layer loss.","failure":"若採用「把選擇性當成無限停止能力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating selectivity as an infinite stop\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「停止層選擇性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失。","checkEn":"Submit the Stop-layer selectivity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-11-k1","title":"停止層選擇性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stop-layer selectivity / Physics and model","text":"機制：高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失。","textEn":"Mechanism: High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss."},{"id":"a067-v8-11-k2","title":"停止層選擇性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stop-layer selectivity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把選擇性當成無限停止能力」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating selectivity as an infinite stop."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「停止層選擇性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Stop-layer selectivity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態","高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失","把選擇性當成無限停止能力"],"optionsEn":["Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state","High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss","Treating selectivity as an infinite stop"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-11"],"title":"停止層選擇性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Stop-layer selectivity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把選擇性當成無限停止能力」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating selectivity as an infinite stop.","instruction":"接續前一步「停止層選擇性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把選擇性當成無限停止能力」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：過研磨時間和停止層損失共同評估。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Stop-layer selectivity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating selectivity as an infinite stop\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Assess overpolish time with stop-layer loss. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失；過研磨時間和停止層損失共同評估。","observationEn":"High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss; Assess overpolish time with stop-layer loss.","failure":"若採用「把選擇性當成無限停止能力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating selectivity as an infinite stop\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「停止層選擇性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「過研磨時間和停止層損失共同評估」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Stop-layer selectivity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Assess overpolish time with stop-layer loss\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-12-k1","title":"停止層選擇性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stop-layer selectivity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：過研磨時間和停止層損失共同評估。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Assess overpolish time with stop-layer loss."},{"id":"a067-v8-12-k2","title":"停止層選擇性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stop-layer selectivity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把選擇性當成無限停止能力」與「高選擇性不代表停止層完全不損失」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating selectivity as an infinite stop\" is not equivalent to \"High selectivity does not imply zero stop-layer loss\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「停止層選擇性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Stop-layer selectivity?","options":["把選擇性當成無限停止能力","只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態","過研磨時間和停止層損失共同評估"],"optionsEn":["Treating selectivity as an infinite stop","Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state","Assess overpolish time with stop-layer loss"],"answer":2,"explanation":"過研磨時間和停止層損失共同評估；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Assess overpolish time with stop-layer loss. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a067-stage03","order":3,"title":"研磨墊狀態 → 漿料輸送","titleEn":"Pad condition to Slurry delivery","description":"把「研磨墊狀態」「終點訊號」「漿料輸送」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pad condition, Endpoint signal, Slurry delivery.","steps":[{"id":"a067-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-12"],"title":"研磨墊狀態：建立模型","titleEn":"Pad condition: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity.","instruction":"畫新墊、釉化墊與修整後接觸分布，規劃監測磨耗的試片。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch contact distributions for new, glazed and conditioned pads and specify a wear monitor. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度；修整器磨耗也會改變墊狀態。","observationEn":"Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity; Conditioner wear also changes pad state.","failure":"若採用「只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「研磨墊狀態」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度。","checkEn":"Submit the Pad condition diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-13-k1","title":"研磨墊狀態／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pad condition / Physics and model","text":"機制：墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity."},{"id":"a067-v8-13-k2","title":"研磨墊狀態／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pad condition / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「研磨墊狀態」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pad condition, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度","只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態","把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成"],"optionsEn":["Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity","Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state","Calling every signal jump complete clearing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-13"],"title":"研磨墊狀態：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pad condition: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state.","instruction":"接續前一步「研磨墊狀態」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：修整器磨耗也會改變墊狀態。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pad condition artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Conditioner wear also changes pad state. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度；修整器磨耗也會改變墊狀態。","observationEn":"Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity; Conditioner wear also changes pad state.","failure":"若採用「只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「研磨墊狀態」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「修整器磨耗也會改變墊狀態」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pad condition, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Conditioner wear also changes pad state\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-14-k1","title":"研磨墊狀態／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pad condition / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：修整器磨耗也會改變墊狀態。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Conditioner wear also changes pad state."},{"id":"a067-v8-14-k2","title":"研磨墊狀態／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pad condition / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態」與「墊表面演化會改變移除與均勻度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state\" is not equivalent to \"Pad evolution changes removal and uniformity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「研磨墊狀態」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pad condition?","options":["把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成","修整器磨耗也會改變墊狀態","只記累積片數而忽略墊狀態"],"optionsEn":["Calling every signal jump complete clearing","Conditioner wear also changes pad state","Recording wafer count while ignoring pad state"],"answer":1,"explanation":"修整器磨耗也會改變墊狀態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Conditioner wear also changes pad state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-14"],"title":"終點訊號：建立模型","titleEn":"Endpoint signal: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Endpoint signals require material and pattern context.","instruction":"自製有基線漂移的反射訊號，標出候選終點及獨立厚度查核。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Create a reflectance trace with baseline drift and mark endpoint candidates and independent thickness checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋；反射訊號可同時受濕膜影響。","observationEn":"Endpoint signals require material and pattern context; Wet films can also alter reflectance.","failure":"若採用「把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling every signal jump complete clearing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「終點訊號」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋。","checkEn":"Submit the Endpoint signal diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Endpoint signals require material and pattern context.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-15-k1","title":"終點訊號／物理與模型","titleEn":"Endpoint signal / Physics and model","text":"機制：終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋。","textEn":"Mechanism: Endpoint signals require material and pattern context."},{"id":"a067-v8-15-k2","title":"終點訊號／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint signal / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling every signal jump complete clearing."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「終點訊號」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Endpoint signal, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成","用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新","終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋"],"optionsEn":["Calling every signal jump complete clearing","Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere","Endpoint signals require material and pattern context"],"answer":2,"explanation":"終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Endpoint signals require material and pattern context. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-15"],"title":"終點訊號：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Endpoint signal: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling every signal jump complete clearing.","instruction":"接續前一步「終點訊號」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：反射訊號可同時受濕膜影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Endpoint signal artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling every signal jump complete clearing\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Wet films can also alter reflectance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋；反射訊號可同時受濕膜影響。","observationEn":"Endpoint signals require material and pattern context; Wet films can also alter reflectance.","failure":"若採用「把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling every signal jump complete clearing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「終點訊號」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「反射訊號可同時受濕膜影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Endpoint signal, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Wet films can also alter reflectance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-16-k1","title":"終點訊號／物理與模型","titleEn":"Endpoint signal / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：反射訊號可同時受濕膜影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Wet films can also alter reflectance."},{"id":"a067-v8-16-k2","title":"終點訊號／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Endpoint signal / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成」與「終點訊號需要材料與圖形背景解釋」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling every signal jump complete clearing\" is not equivalent to \"Endpoint signals require material and pattern context\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「終點訊號」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Endpoint signal?","options":["反射訊號可同時受濕膜影響","把任何訊號突變都當成清除完成","用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新"],"optionsEn":["Wet films can also alter reflectance","Calling every signal jump complete clearing","Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere"],"answer":0,"explanation":"反射訊號可同時受濕膜影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Wet films can also alter reflectance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-16"],"title":"漿料輸送：建立模型","titleEn":"Slurry delivery: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry.","instruction":"畫入口、旋轉接觸區與排液，辨識停滯區和供液中斷。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map inlet, rotating contact and drainage; identify stagnant areas and delivery interruptions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件；氣泡可能遮蔽局部接觸。","observationEn":"Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry; Bubbles can mask local contact.","failure":"若採用「用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「漿料輸送」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件。","checkEn":"Submit the Slurry delivery diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-17-k1","title":"漿料輸送／物理與模型","titleEn":"Slurry delivery / Physics and model","text":"機制：入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry."},{"id":"a067-v8-17-k2","title":"漿料輸送／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Slurry delivery / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漿料輸送」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Slurry delivery, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只用光學外觀核准表面","入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件","用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新"],"optionsEn":["Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone","Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry","Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere"],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-17"],"title":"漿料輸送：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Slurry delivery: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere.","instruction":"接續前一步「漿料輸送」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：氣泡可能遮蔽局部接觸。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Slurry delivery artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bubbles can mask local contact. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件；氣泡可能遮蔽局部接觸。","observationEn":"Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry; Bubbles can mask local contact.","failure":"若採用「用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「漿料輸送」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「氣泡可能遮蔽局部接觸」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Slurry delivery, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bubbles can mask local contact\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-18-k1","title":"漿料輸送／物理與模型","titleEn":"Slurry delivery / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：氣泡可能遮蔽局部接觸。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bubbles can mask local contact."},{"id":"a067-v8-18-k2","title":"漿料輸送／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Slurry delivery / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新」與「入口流量不等於每一位置都得到相同化學條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere\" is not equivalent to \"Inlet flow does not guarantee identical local chemistry\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「漿料輸送」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Slurry delivery?","options":["用總流量證明所有接觸區充分更新","只用光學外觀核准表面","氣泡可能遮蔽局部接觸"],"optionsEn":["Using total flow to prove renewal everywhere","Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone","Bubbles can mask local contact"],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣泡可能遮蔽局部接觸；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bubbles can mask local contact. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a067-stage04","order":4,"title":"研磨後潔淨 → 整合驗收","titleEn":"Post-CMP cleanliness to Integration acceptance","description":"把「研磨後潔淨」「量測誤差帳本」「整合驗收」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Post-CMP cleanliness, Measurement-error ledger, Integration acceptance.","steps":[{"id":"a067-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-18"],"title":"研磨後潔淨：建立模型","titleEn":"Post-CMP cleanliness: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness.","instruction":"將殘留磨粒、金屬污染與水痕分開，為各類選擇檢查證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate residual abrasive, metal contamination and watermarks and assign evidence for each. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨；乾燥造成的水痕是不同缺陷族群。","observationEn":"Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness; Drying watermarks form a distinct defect population.","failure":"若採用「只用光學外觀核准表面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「研磨後潔淨」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨。","checkEn":"Submit the Post-CMP cleanliness diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-19-k1","title":"研磨後潔淨／物理與模型","titleEn":"Post-CMP cleanliness / Physics and model","text":"機制：低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨。","textEn":"Mechanism: Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness."},{"id":"a067-v8-19-k2","title":"研磨後潔淨／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Post-CMP cleanliness / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用光學外觀核准表面」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「研磨後潔淨」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Post-CMP cleanliness, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨","只用光學外觀核准表面","將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除"],"optionsEn":["Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness","Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone","Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-19"],"title":"研磨後潔淨：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Post-CMP cleanliness: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用光學外觀核准表面」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「研磨後潔淨」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用光學外觀核准表面」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：乾燥造成的水痕是不同缺陷族群。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Post-CMP cleanliness artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Drying watermarks form a distinct defect population. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨；乾燥造成的水痕是不同缺陷族群。","observationEn":"Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness; Drying watermarks form a distinct defect population.","failure":"若採用「只用光學外觀核准表面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「研磨後潔淨」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「乾燥造成的水痕是不同缺陷族群」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Post-CMP cleanliness, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Drying watermarks form a distinct defect population\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-20-k1","title":"研磨後潔淨／物理與模型","titleEn":"Post-CMP cleanliness / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：乾燥造成的水痕是不同缺陷族群。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Drying watermarks form a distinct defect population."},{"id":"a067-v8-20-k2","title":"研磨後潔淨／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Post-CMP cleanliness / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用光學外觀核准表面」與「低刮傷數不能證明表面化學潔淨」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone\" is not equivalent to \"Few scratches do not prove chemical cleanliness\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「研磨後潔淨」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Post-CMP cleanliness?","options":["將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除","乾燥造成的水痕是不同缺陷族群","只用光學外觀核准表面"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal","Drying watermarks form a distinct defect population","Accepting the surface from optical appearance alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"乾燥造成的水痕是不同缺陷族群；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Drying watermarks form a distinct defect population. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-20"],"title":"量測誤差帳本：建立模型","titleEn":"Measurement-error ledger: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Removal differences contain errors from both measurements.","instruction":"對同一片前後測點配對，估算厚度差的不確定度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Pair pre/post sites and estimate uncertainty of the thickness difference. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差；共同校正偏差不一定在差值完全抵消。","observationEn":"Removal differences contain errors from both measurements; Shared calibration bias may not fully cancel.","failure":"若採用「將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「量測誤差帳本」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差。","checkEn":"Submit the Measurement-error ledger diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Removal differences contain errors from both measurements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-21-k1","title":"量測誤差帳本／物理與模型","titleEn":"Measurement-error ledger / Physics and model","text":"機制：移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差。","textEn":"Mechanism: Removal differences contain errors from both measurements."},{"id":"a067-v8-21-k2","title":"量測誤差帳本／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Measurement-error ledger / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測誤差帳本」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Measurement-error ledger, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除","只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求","移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal","Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness","Removal differences contain errors from both measurements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Removal differences contain errors from both measurements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-21"],"title":"量測誤差帳本：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Measurement-error ledger: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal.","instruction":"接續前一步「量測誤差帳本」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：共同校正偏差不一定在差值完全抵消。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Measurement-error ledger artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Shared calibration bias may not fully cancel. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差；共同校正偏差不一定在差值完全抵消。","observationEn":"Removal differences contain errors from both measurements; Shared calibration bias may not fully cancel.","failure":"若採用「將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「量測誤差帳本」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「共同校正偏差不一定在差值完全抵消」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Measurement-error ledger, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Shared calibration bias may not fully cancel\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-22-k1","title":"量測誤差帳本／物理與模型","titleEn":"Measurement-error ledger / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：共同校正偏差不一定在差值完全抵消。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Shared calibration bias may not fully cancel."},{"id":"a067-v8-22-k2","title":"量測誤差帳本／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Measurement-error ledger / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除」與「移除量差值包含兩次量測誤差」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal\" is not equivalent to \"Removal differences contain errors from both measurements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「量測誤差帳本」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Measurement-error ledger?","options":["共同校正偏差不一定在差值完全抵消","將不同位置量測相減當成真實移除","只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求"],"optionsEn":["Shared calibration bias may not fully cancel","Subtracting unmatched locations as true removal","Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"共同校正偏差不一定在差值完全抵消；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shared calibration bias may not fully cancel. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-22"],"title":"整合驗收：建立模型","titleEn":"Integration acceptance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration.","instruction":"將殘膜、碟陷、刮傷和下一層微影焦距需求放入同一驗收表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine residual film, dishing, scratches and next-layer focus needs in one acceptance table. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求；微影焦深需求與局部地形有關。","observationEn":"CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration; Lithographic focus needs depend on local topography.","failure":"若採用「只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「整合驗收」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求。","checkEn":"Submit the Integration acceptance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-23-k1","title":"整合驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Integration acceptance / Physics and model","text":"機制：CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求。","textEn":"Mechanism: CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration."},{"id":"a067-v8-23-k2","title":"整合驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Integration acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「整合驗收」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Integration acceptance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦","CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求","只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求"],"optionsEn":["Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization","CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration","Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a067-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cmp","v8-c-cmp-endpoint","v8-c-vm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a067-v8-23"],"title":"整合驗收：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Integration acceptance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness.","instruction":"接續前一步「整合驗收」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：微影焦深需求與局部地形有關。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Integration acceptance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Lithographic focus needs depend on local topography. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求；微影焦深需求與局部地形有關。","observationEn":"CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration; Lithographic focus needs depend on local topography.","failure":"若採用「只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「整合驗收」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「微影焦深需求與局部地形有關」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Integration acceptance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Lithographic focus needs depend on local topography\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a067-v8-24-k1","title":"整合驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Integration acceptance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：微影焦深需求與局部地形有關。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Lithographic focus needs depend on local topography."},{"id":"a067-v8-24-k2","title":"整合驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Integration acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求」與「CMP 驗收必須連到後續整合要求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness\" is not equivalent to \"CMP acceptance must connect to downstream integration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「整合驗收」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Integration acceptance?","options":["只追求最快移除而取消後續平坦度要求","把所有位置厚度同減視為已平坦","微影焦深需求與局部地形有關"],"optionsEn":["Optimizing removal speed while discarding downstream flatness","Treating equal thickness reduction everywhere as planarization","Lithographic focus needs depend on local topography"],"answer":2,"explanation":"微影焦深需求與局部地形有關；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Lithographic focus needs depend on local topography. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability"},{"id":"a068","title":"CMP 漿料與磨粒控制","titleEn":"CMP slurry and abrasive control","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從磨粒族群、化學與機械分工到批次放行：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Abrasive populations and Chemical and mechanical roles to Lot release: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["磨粒族群","膠體穩定性","過濾取捨","氧化劑老化"],"labelsEn":["Abrasive populations","Colloidal stability","Filtration tradeoff","Oxidizer aging"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a068-stage01","order":1,"title":"磨粒族群 → 稀釋代表性","titleEn":"Abrasive populations to Dilution representativeness","description":"把「磨粒族群」「數目與強度分布」「稀釋代表性」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Abrasive populations, Number versus intensity distributions, Dilution representativeness.","steps":[{"id":"a068-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"磨粒族群：建立模型","titleEn":"Abrasive populations: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Rare large particles can dominate scratching.","instruction":"比較相同平均粒徑但不同大粒尾端的兩個假設分布。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設漿料 A 的離散計數為 9,999 顆直徑 100 nm 加 1 顆 1,000 nm，B 為 10,000 顆直徑 100.09 nm。兩者數目加權平均均為 100.09 nm；大於 500 nm 的顆數卻為 A=1、B=0。畫出尾端計數，說明平均值相同仍可能有不同大粒子風險；這不是實際漿料規格，亦不能單由粒徑斷定刮傷。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical distributions with equal means but different large-particle tails. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume slurry A contains 9,999 particles of diameter 100 nm and one of 1,000 nm; B contains 10,000 particles of 100.09 nm. Both number-weighted means are 100.09 nm, but counts above 500 nm are A=1 and B=0. Plot tail counts and explain how equal means conceal large-particle differences. These are not slurry specifications, and diameter alone does not establish scratching.","observation":"稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷；尾端估計需足夠取樣體積。","observationEn":"Rare large particles can dominate scratching; Tail estimates require sufficient sampled volume.","failure":"若採用「只用平均粒徑核准漿料」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「磨粒族群」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷。\n算例驗收：列出平均值計算及 500 nm 門檻計數；不得把數目加權平均和體積加權平均混用。","checkEn":"Submit the Abrasive populations diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Rare large particles can dominate scratching.\nWorked-example acceptance: Show both mean calculations and the 500 nm threshold counts; do not interchange number- and volume-weighted means.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-01-k1","title":"磨粒族群／物理與模型","titleEn":"Abrasive populations / Physics and model","text":"機制：稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Rare large particles can dominate scratching."},{"id":"a068-v8-01-k2","title":"磨粒族群／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Abrasive populations / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用平均粒徑核准漿料」。\n假設數值與推算：假設漿料 A 的離散計數為 9,999 顆直徑 100 nm 加 1 顆 1,000 nm，B 為 10,000 顆直徑 100.09 nm。兩者數目加權平均均為 100.09 nm；大於 500 nm 的顆數卻為 A=1、B=0。畫出尾端計數，說明平均值相同仍可能有不同大粒子風險；這不是實際漿料規格，亦不能單由粒徑斷定刮傷。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume slurry A contains 9,999 particles of diameter 100 nm and one of 1,000 nm; B contains 10,000 particles of 100.09 nm. Both number-weighted means are 100.09 nm, but counts above 500 nm are A=1 and B=0. Plot tail counts and explain how equal means conceal large-particle differences. These are not slurry specifications, and diameter alone does not establish scratching."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「磨粒族群」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Abrasive populations, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷","只用平均粒徑核准漿料","直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度"],"optionsEn":["Rare large particles can dominate scratching","Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone","Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Rare large particles can dominate scratching. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-01"],"title":"磨粒族群：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Abrasive populations: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用平均粒徑核准漿料」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「磨粒族群」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用平均粒徑核准漿料」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：尾端估計需足夠取樣體積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Abrasive populations artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Tail estimates require sufficient sampled volume. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷；尾端估計需足夠取樣體積。","observationEn":"Rare large particles can dominate scratching; Tail estimates require sufficient sampled volume.","failure":"若採用「只用平均粒徑核准漿料」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「磨粒族群」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「尾端估計需足夠取樣體積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Abrasive populations, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Tail estimates require sufficient sampled volume\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-02-k1","title":"磨粒族群／物理與模型","titleEn":"Abrasive populations / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：尾端估計需足夠取樣體積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Tail estimates require sufficient sampled volume."},{"id":"a068-v8-02-k2","title":"磨粒族群／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Abrasive populations / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用平均粒徑核准漿料」與「稀少大顆粒可能主導刮傷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone\" is not equivalent to \"Rare large particles can dominate scratching\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「磨粒族群」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Abrasive populations?","options":["直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度","尾端估計需足夠取樣體積","只用平均粒徑核准漿料"],"optionsEn":["Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions","Tail estimates require sufficient sampled volume","Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"尾端估計需足夠取樣體積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Tail estimates require sufficient sampled volume. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-02"],"title":"數目與強度分布：建立模型","titleEn":"Number versus intensity distributions: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings.","instruction":"為 DLS 與單粒計數各畫輸出座標，說明何者強調散射大顆粒。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch DLS and single-particle-count outputs and explain large-particle scattering weighting. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同；折射率也影響光學粒徑換算。","observationEn":"Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings; Refractive index affects optical sizing.","failure":"若採用「直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「數目與強度分布」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Number versus intensity distributions diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-03-k1","title":"數目與強度分布／物理與模型","titleEn":"Number versus intensity distributions / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings."},{"id":"a068-v8-03-k2","title":"數目與強度分布／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Number versus intensity distributions / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「數目與強度分布」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Number versus intensity distributions, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度","假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群","不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同"],"optionsEn":["Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions","Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations","Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-03"],"title":"數目與強度分布：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Number versus intensity distributions: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions.","instruction":"接續前一步「數目與強度分布」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：折射率也影響光學粒徑換算。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Number versus intensity distributions artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Refractive index affects optical sizing. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同；折射率也影響光學粒徑換算。","observationEn":"Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings; Refractive index affects optical sizing.","failure":"若採用「直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「數目與強度分布」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「折射率也影響光學粒徑換算」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Number versus intensity distributions, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Refractive index affects optical sizing\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-04-k1","title":"數目與強度分布／物理與模型","titleEn":"Number versus intensity distributions / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：折射率也影響光學粒徑換算。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Refractive index affects optical sizing."},{"id":"a068-v8-04-k2","title":"數目與強度分布／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Number versus intensity distributions / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度」與「不同粒徑方法的分布權重不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions\" is not equivalent to \"Particle-sizing methods use different distribution weightings\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「數目與強度分布」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Number versus intensity distributions?","options":["折射率也影響光學粒徑換算","直接疊合強度分布和數目分布比較濃度","假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群"],"optionsEn":["Refractive index affects optical sizing","Comparing concentration by overlaying intensity and number distributions","Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations"],"answer":0,"explanation":"折射率也影響光學粒徑換算；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Refractive index affects optical sizing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-04"],"title":"稀釋代表性：建立模型","titleEn":"Dilution representativeness: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「稀釋可能改變團聚平衡」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium.","instruction":"設計原液與兩個稀釋倍數的測試帳本並回算每毫升顆粒數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plan stock and two dilution measurements and back-calculate counts per milliliter. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"稀釋可能改變團聚平衡；濃度回算需傳播稀釋倍數誤差。","observationEn":"Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium; Concentration uncertainty includes dilution error.","failure":"若採用「假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「稀釋代表性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：稀釋可能改變團聚平衡。","checkEn":"Submit the Dilution representativeness diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-05-k1","title":"稀釋代表性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dilution representativeness / Physics and model","text":"機制：稀釋可能改變團聚平衡。","textEn":"Mechanism: Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium."},{"id":"a068-v8-05-k2","title":"稀釋代表性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dilution representativeness / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「稀釋代表性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dilution representativeness, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定","稀釋可能改變團聚平衡","假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群"],"optionsEn":["Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution","Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium","Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations"],"answer":1,"explanation":"稀釋可能改變團聚平衡；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-05"],"title":"稀釋代表性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dilution representativeness: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations.","instruction":"接續前一步「稀釋代表性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：濃度回算需傳播稀釋倍數誤差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dilution representativeness artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Concentration uncertainty includes dilution error. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"稀釋可能改變團聚平衡；濃度回算需傳播稀釋倍數誤差。","observationEn":"Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium; Concentration uncertainty includes dilution error.","failure":"若採用「假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「稀釋代表性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「濃度回算需傳播稀釋倍數誤差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dilution representativeness, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Concentration uncertainty includes dilution error\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-06-k1","title":"稀釋代表性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dilution representativeness / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：濃度回算需傳播稀釋倍數誤差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Concentration uncertainty includes dilution error."},{"id":"a068-v8-06-k2","title":"稀釋代表性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dilution representativeness / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群」與「稀釋可能改變團聚平衡」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations\" is not equivalent to \"Dilution can alter aggregation equilibrium\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「稀釋代表性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dilution representativeness?","options":["假定稀釋只改濃度完全不改族群","認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定","濃度回算需傳播稀釋倍數誤差"],"optionsEn":["Assuming dilution changes concentration but never populations","Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution","Concentration uncertainty includes dilution error"],"answer":2,"explanation":"濃度回算需傳播稀釋倍數誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Concentration uncertainty includes dilution error. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a068-stage02","order":2,"title":"膠體穩定性 → 選擇性矩陣","titleEn":"Colloidal stability to Selectivity matrix","description":"把「膠體穩定性」「化學與機械分工」「選擇性矩陣」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Colloidal stability, Chemical and mechanical roles, Selectivity matrix.","steps":[{"id":"a068-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-06"],"title":"膠體穩定性：建立模型","titleEn":"Colloidal stability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「靜電排斥受溶液條件影響」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions.","instruction":"畫表面電荷、離子屏蔽和碰撞，比較鹽度改變後的團聚趨勢。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch surface charge, ionic screening and collisions; compare aggregation after ionic-strength changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"靜電排斥受溶液條件影響；測得 zeta 電位不等同表面真實電位。","observationEn":"Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions; Zeta potential is not the exact surface potential.","failure":"若採用「認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「膠體穩定性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：靜電排斥受溶液條件影響。","checkEn":"Submit the Colloidal stability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-07-k1","title":"膠體穩定性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Colloidal stability / Physics and model","text":"機制：靜電排斥受溶液條件影響。","textEn":"Mechanism: Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions."},{"id":"a068-v8-07-k2","title":"膠體穩定性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Colloidal stability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「膠體穩定性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Colloidal stability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["靜電排斥受溶液條件影響","認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定","只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高"],"optionsEn":["Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions","Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution","Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"靜電排斥受溶液條件影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-07"],"title":"膠體穩定性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Colloidal stability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution.","instruction":"接續前一步「膠體穩定性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：測得 zeta 電位不等同表面真實電位。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Colloidal stability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Zeta potential is not the exact surface potential. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"靜電排斥受溶液條件影響；測得 zeta 電位不等同表面真實電位。","observationEn":"Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions; Zeta potential is not the exact surface potential.","failure":"若採用「認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「膠體穩定性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「測得 zeta 電位不等同表面真實電位」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Colloidal stability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Zeta potential is not the exact surface potential\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-08-k1","title":"膠體穩定性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Colloidal stability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：測得 zeta 電位不等同表面真實電位。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Zeta potential is not the exact surface potential."},{"id":"a068-v8-08-k2","title":"膠體穩定性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Colloidal stability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定」與「靜電排斥受溶液條件影響」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution\" is not equivalent to \"Electrostatic repulsion depends on solution conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「膠體穩定性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Colloidal stability?","options":["只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高","測得 zeta 電位不等同表面真實電位","認為同一磨粒在任何溶液都穩定"],"optionsEn":["Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance","Zeta potential is not the exact surface potential","Assuming one abrasive is stable in every solution"],"answer":1,"explanation":"測得 zeta 電位不等同表面真實電位；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Zeta potential is not the exact surface potential. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-08"],"title":"化學與機械分工：建立模型","titleEn":"Chemical and mechanical roles: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP.","instruction":"用兩色標示膜表面反應與磨粒移除，再列出速率和缺陷兩個響應。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Color-code surface reaction and abrasive removal and list rate and defect responses. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP；化學鈍化膜可改變接觸移除。","observationEn":"Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP; Chemical passivation can change contact removal.","failure":"若採用「只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「化學與機械分工」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP。","checkEn":"Submit the Chemical and mechanical roles diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-09-k1","title":"化學與機械分工／物理與模型","titleEn":"Chemical and mechanical roles / Physics and model","text":"機制：化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP。","textEn":"Mechanism: Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP."},{"id":"a068-v8-09-k2","title":"化學與機械分工／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Chemical and mechanical roles / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「化學與機械分工」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Chemical and mechanical roles, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高","只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性","化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP"],"optionsEn":["Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance","Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone","Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP"],"answer":2,"explanation":"化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-09"],"title":"化學與機械分工：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Chemical and mechanical roles: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance.","instruction":"接續前一步「化學與機械分工」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：化學鈍化膜可改變接觸移除。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Chemical and mechanical roles artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Chemical passivation can change contact removal. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP；化學鈍化膜可改變接觸移除。","observationEn":"Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP; Chemical passivation can change contact removal.","failure":"若採用「只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「化學與機械分工」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「化學鈍化膜可改變接觸移除」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Chemical and mechanical roles, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Chemical passivation can change contact removal\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-10-k1","title":"化學與機械分工／物理與模型","titleEn":"Chemical and mechanical roles / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：化學鈍化膜可改變接觸移除。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Chemical passivation can change contact removal."},{"id":"a068-v8-10-k2","title":"化學與機械分工／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Chemical and mechanical roles / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高」與「化學反應與接觸摩擦共同決定 CMP」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance\" is not equivalent to \"Surface chemistry and mechanical contact jointly determine CMP\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「化學與機械分工」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Chemical and mechanical roles?","options":["化學鈍化膜可改變接觸移除","只增加磨粒硬度就推定整體性能提高","只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性"],"optionsEn":["Chemical passivation can change contact removal","Assuming harder abrasive always improves overall performance","Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"化學鈍化膜可改變接觸移除；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Chemical passivation can change contact removal. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-10"],"title":"選擇性矩陣：建立模型","titleEn":"Selectivity matrix: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes.","instruction":"對目標膜與阻擋膜填寫假設速率矩陣，區分速率增益和選擇性增益。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Build hypothetical target/barrier removal matrices and separate rate gain from selectivity gain. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算；停止層速率接近零時比值很不穩定。","observationEn":"Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes; Ratios become unstable near zero stop-layer rate.","failure":"若採用「只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「選擇性矩陣」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算。","checkEn":"Submit the Selectivity matrix diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-11-k1","title":"選擇性矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Selectivity matrix / Physics and model","text":"機制：分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算。","textEn":"Mechanism: Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes."},{"id":"a068-v8-11-k2","title":"選擇性矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Selectivity matrix / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「選擇性矩陣」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Selectivity matrix, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好","分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算","只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性"],"optionsEn":["Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better","Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes","Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-11"],"title":"選擇性矩陣：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Selectivity matrix: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「選擇性矩陣」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：停止層速率接近零時比值很不穩定。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Selectivity matrix artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Ratios become unstable near zero stop-layer rate. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算；停止層速率接近零時比值很不穩定。","observationEn":"Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes; Ratios become unstable near zero stop-layer rate.","failure":"若採用「只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「選擇性矩陣」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「停止層速率接近零時比值很不穩定」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Selectivity matrix, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Ratios become unstable near zero stop-layer rate\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-12-k1","title":"選擇性矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Selectivity matrix / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：停止層速率接近零時比值很不穩定。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Ratios become unstable near zero stop-layer rate."},{"id":"a068-v8-12-k2","title":"選擇性矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Selectivity matrix / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性」與「分子與分母都變動時選擇比需重算」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone\" is not equivalent to \"Selectivity must be recalculated when either rate changes\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「選擇性矩陣」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Selectivity matrix?","options":["只看目標膜速率判斷選擇性","把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好","停止層速率接近零時比值很不穩定"],"optionsEn":["Judging selectivity from the target-film rate alone","Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better","Ratios become unstable near zero stop-layer rate"],"answer":2,"explanation":"停止層速率接近零時比值很不穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Ratios become unstable near zero stop-layer rate. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a068-stage03","order":3,"title":"過濾取捨 → 取樣污染","titleEn":"Filtration tradeoff to Sampling contamination","description":"把「過濾取捨」「循環剪切」「取樣污染」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Filtration tradeoff, Recirculation shear, Sampling contamination.","steps":[{"id":"a068-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-12"],"title":"過濾取捨：建立模型","titleEn":"Filtration tradeoff: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations.","instruction":"畫進出濾器的尾端粒數和有效磨粒濃度，計算兩者回收率。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plot tail counts and useful abrasive concentrations before/after filtration and calculate recovery. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群；濾壓差可能提示堵塞與旁通。","observationEn":"Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations; Pressure drop may reveal clogging or bypass.","failure":"若採用「把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「過濾取捨」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群。","checkEn":"Submit the Filtration tradeoff diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-13-k1","title":"過濾取捨／物理與模型","titleEn":"Filtration tradeoff / Physics and model","text":"機制：去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群。","textEn":"Mechanism: Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations."},{"id":"a068-v8-13-k2","title":"過濾取捨／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Filtration tradeoff / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「過濾取捨」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Filtration tradeoff, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群","把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好","用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間"],"optionsEn":["Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations","Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better","Using a factory measurement for the entire use period"],"answer":0,"explanation":"去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-13"],"title":"過濾取捨：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Filtration tradeoff: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better.","instruction":"接續前一步「過濾取捨」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：濾壓差可能提示堵塞與旁通。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Filtration tradeoff artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pressure drop may reveal clogging or bypass. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群；濾壓差可能提示堵塞與旁通。","observationEn":"Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations; Pressure drop may reveal clogging or bypass.","failure":"若採用「把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「過濾取捨」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「濾壓差可能提示堵塞與旁通」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Filtration tradeoff, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pressure drop may reveal clogging or bypass\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-14-k1","title":"過濾取捨／物理與模型","titleEn":"Filtration tradeoff / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：濾壓差可能提示堵塞與旁通。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pressure drop may reveal clogging or bypass."},{"id":"a068-v8-14-k2","title":"過濾取捨／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Filtration tradeoff / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好」與「去除團聚物也可能改變有效磨粒族群」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better\" is not equivalent to \"Removing agglomerates can also change useful abrasive populations\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「過濾取捨」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Filtration tradeoff?","options":["用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間","濾壓差可能提示堵塞與旁通","把濾後越少顆粒一律視為越好"],"optionsEn":["Using a factory measurement for the entire use period","Pressure drop may reveal clogging or bypass","Treating fewer particles after filtration as universally better"],"answer":1,"explanation":"濾壓差可能提示堵塞與旁通；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pressure drop may reveal clogging or bypass. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-14"],"title":"循環剪切：建立模型","titleEn":"Recirculation shear: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Delivery history can affect particle state.","instruction":"設計循環前後及停機後的取樣時間線，分辨剪切與靜置效應。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plan samples before/after circulation and after stoppage to separate shear from aging. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態；停滯死角可累積老化漿料。","observationEn":"Delivery history can affect particle state; Dead legs accumulate aged slurry.","failure":"若採用「用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using a factory measurement for the entire use period\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「循環剪切」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態。","checkEn":"Submit the Recirculation shear diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Delivery history can affect particle state.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-15-k1","title":"循環剪切／物理與模型","titleEn":"Recirculation shear / Physics and model","text":"機制：輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態。","textEn":"Mechanism: Delivery history can affect particle state."},{"id":"a068-v8-15-k2","title":"循環剪切／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Recirculation shear / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using a factory measurement for the entire use period."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「循環剪切」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Recirculation shear, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間","未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次","輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態"],"optionsEn":["Using a factory measurement for the entire use period","Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks","Delivery history can affect particle state"],"answer":2,"explanation":"輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Delivery history can affect particle state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-15"],"title":"循環剪切：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Recirculation shear: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using a factory measurement for the entire use period.","instruction":"接續前一步「循環剪切」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：停滯死角可累積老化漿料。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Recirculation shear artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using a factory measurement for the entire use period\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dead legs accumulate aged slurry. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態；停滯死角可累積老化漿料。","observationEn":"Delivery history can affect particle state; Dead legs accumulate aged slurry.","failure":"若採用「用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using a factory measurement for the entire use period\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「循環剪切」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「停滯死角可累積老化漿料」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Recirculation shear, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dead legs accumulate aged slurry\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-16-k1","title":"循環剪切／物理與模型","titleEn":"Recirculation shear / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：停滯死角可累積老化漿料。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dead legs accumulate aged slurry."},{"id":"a068-v8-16-k2","title":"循環剪切／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Recirculation shear / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間」與「輸送歷史會影響顆粒狀態」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using a factory measurement for the entire use period\" is not equivalent to \"Delivery history can affect particle state\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「循環剪切」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Recirculation shear?","options":["停滯死角可累積老化漿料","用出廠一次量測代表整個使用期間","未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次"],"optionsEn":["Dead legs accumulate aged slurry","Using a factory measurement for the entire use period","Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"停滯死角可累積老化漿料；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dead legs accumulate aged slurry. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-16"],"title":"取樣污染：建立模型","titleEn":"Sampling contamination: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals.","instruction":"畫容器空白、管線空白和真樣品三條流程，辨識外加顆粒。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map bottle blank, line blank and real-sample flows to identify added particles. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號；容器清洗也需要空白驗證。","observationEn":"Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals; Container cleaning needs blank validation.","failure":"若採用「未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「取樣污染」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號。","checkEn":"Submit the Sampling contamination diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-17-k1","title":"取樣污染／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sampling contamination / Physics and model","text":"機制：容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號。","textEn":"Mechanism: Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals."},{"id":"a068-v8-17-k2","title":"取樣污染／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sampling contamination / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「取樣污染」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Sampling contamination, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變","容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號","未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次"],"optionsEn":["Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry","Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals","Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-17"],"title":"取樣污染：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Sampling contamination: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks.","instruction":"接續前一步「取樣污染」成果，先指出錯誤主張「未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：容器清洗也需要空白驗證。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Sampling contamination artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Container cleaning needs blank validation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號；容器清洗也需要空白驗證。","observationEn":"Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals; Container cleaning needs blank validation.","failure":"若採用「未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「取樣污染」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「容器清洗也需要空白驗證」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Sampling contamination, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Container cleaning needs blank validation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-18-k1","title":"取樣污染／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sampling contamination / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：容器清洗也需要空白驗證。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Container cleaning needs blank validation."},{"id":"a068-v8-18-k2","title":"取樣污染／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sampling contamination / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次」與「容器與取樣管本身會引入訊號」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks\" is not equivalent to \"Containers and sampling lines can introduce signals\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「取樣污染」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Sampling contamination?","options":["未扣除空白就歸咎漿料批次","以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變","容器清洗也需要空白驗證"],"optionsEn":["Blaming slurry lots without checking blanks","Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry","Container cleaning needs blank validation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"容器清洗也需要空白驗證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Container cleaning needs blank validation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a068-stage04","order":4,"title":"氧化劑老化 → 批次放行","titleEn":"Oxidizer aging to Lot release","description":"把「氧化劑老化」「缺陷對位」「批次放行」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Oxidizer aging, Defect registration, Lot release.","steps":[{"id":"a068-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-18"],"title":"氧化劑老化：建立模型","titleEn":"Oxidizer aging: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size.","instruction":"用假設活性隨時間曲線規劃配製時間、使用時間和化學檢查欄位。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Use a hypothetical activity-time curve to plan preparation, use and chemistry checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑；混合順序可影響短期膠體狀態。","observationEn":"Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size; Mixing order can affect transient colloidal state.","failure":"若採用「以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「氧化劑老化」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑。","checkEn":"Submit the Oxidizer aging diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-19-k1","title":"氧化劑老化／物理與模型","titleEn":"Oxidizer aging / Physics and model","text":"機制：化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑。","textEn":"Mechanism: Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size."},{"id":"a068-v8-19-k2","title":"氧化劑老化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Oxidizer aging / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氧化劑老化」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Oxidizer aging, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑","以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變","一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立"],"optionsEn":["Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size","Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry","Declaring causation from one coincidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-19"],"title":"氧化劑老化：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Oxidizer aging: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry.","instruction":"接續前一步「氧化劑老化」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：混合順序可影響短期膠體狀態。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Oxidizer aging artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mixing order can affect transient colloidal state. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑；混合順序可影響短期膠體狀態。","observationEn":"Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size; Mixing order can affect transient colloidal state.","failure":"若採用「以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「氧化劑老化」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「混合順序可影響短期膠體狀態」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Oxidizer aging, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mixing order can affect transient colloidal state\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-20-k1","title":"氧化劑老化／物理與模型","titleEn":"Oxidizer aging / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：混合順序可影響短期膠體狀態。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mixing order can affect transient colloidal state."},{"id":"a068-v8-20-k2","title":"氧化劑老化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Oxidizer aging / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變」與「化學活性變化不一定反映在粒徑」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry\" is not equivalent to \"Chemical activity changes need not appear in particle size\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「氧化劑老化」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Oxidizer aging?","options":["一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立","混合順序可影響短期膠體狀態","以粒徑未變證明全部化學性質未變"],"optionsEn":["Declaring causation from one coincidence","Mixing order can affect transient colloidal state","Treating stable size as proof of unchanged chemistry"],"answer":1,"explanation":"混合順序可影響短期膠體狀態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mixing order can affect transient colloidal state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-20"],"title":"缺陷對位：建立模型","titleEn":"Defect registration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders.","instruction":"將大粒事件時間與晶圓刮傷位置配對，保留未對上的樣本。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Align large-particle event times with scratch maps and retain unmatched samples. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素；量測時間戳需對齊實際取樣延遲。","observationEn":"Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders; Timestamps must account for sampling delay.","failure":"若採用「一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring causation from one coincidence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「缺陷對位」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素。","checkEn":"Submit the Defect registration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-21-k1","title":"缺陷對位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect registration / Physics and model","text":"機制：相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素。","textEn":"Mechanism: Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders."},{"id":"a068-v8-21-k2","title":"缺陷對位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect registration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Declaring causation from one coincidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷對位」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Defect registration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立","只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效","相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素"],"optionsEn":["Declaring causation from one coincidence","Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name","Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders"],"answer":2,"explanation":"相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-21"],"title":"缺陷對位：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Defect registration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Declaring causation from one coincidence.","instruction":"接續前一步「缺陷對位」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：量測時間戳需對齊實際取樣延遲。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Defect registration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Declaring causation from one coincidence\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Timestamps must account for sampling delay. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素；量測時間戳需對齊實際取樣延遲。","observationEn":"Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders; Timestamps must account for sampling delay.","failure":"若採用「一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring causation from one coincidence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「缺陷對位」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「量測時間戳需對齊實際取樣延遲」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Defect registration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Timestamps must account for sampling delay\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-22-k1","title":"缺陷對位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect registration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：量測時間戳需對齊實際取樣延遲。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Timestamps must account for sampling delay."},{"id":"a068-v8-22-k2","title":"缺陷對位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect registration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立」與「相關性需排除墊與清洗等混雜因素」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Declaring causation from one coincidence\" is not equivalent to \"Correlation must account for pad and cleaning confounders\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「缺陷對位」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Defect registration?","options":["量測時間戳需對齊實際取樣延遲","一次同時出現就宣稱因果確立","只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效"],"optionsEn":["Timestamps must account for sampling delay","Declaring causation from one coincidence","Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name"],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測時間戳需對齊實際取樣延遲；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Timestamps must account for sampling delay. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-22"],"title":"批次放行：建立模型","titleEn":"Lot release: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types.","instruction":"建立粒徑尾端、濃度、化學活性與試片缺陷的共同放行表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Build a joint release record for distribution tails, concentration, activity and coupon defects. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據；保存條件也是批次追溯欄位。","observationEn":"Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types; Storage conditions belong in lot traceability.","failure":"若採用「只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「批次放行」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據。","checkEn":"Submit the Lot release diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-23-k1","title":"批次放行／物理與模型","titleEn":"Lot release / Physics and model","text":"機制：放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據。","textEn":"Mechanism: Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types."},{"id":"a068-v8-23-k2","title":"批次放行／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Lot release / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「批次放行」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Lot release, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只用平均粒徑核准漿料","放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據","只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone","Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types","Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name"],"answer":1,"explanation":"放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a068-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-slurry","v8-c-filter","v8-c-cmp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a068-v8-23"],"title":"批次放行：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Lot release: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name.","instruction":"接續前一步「批次放行」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：保存條件也是批次追溯欄位。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Lot release artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Storage conditions belong in lot traceability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據；保存條件也是批次追溯欄位。","observationEn":"Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types; Storage conditions belong in lot traceability.","failure":"若採用「只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「批次放行」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「保存條件也是批次追溯欄位」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Lot release, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Storage conditions belong in lot traceability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a068-v8-24-k1","title":"批次放行／物理與模型","titleEn":"Lot release / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：保存條件也是批次追溯欄位。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Storage conditions belong in lot traceability."},{"id":"a068-v8-24-k2","title":"批次放行／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Lot release / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效」與「放行應使用多項與失效相關的證據」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name\" is not equivalent to \"Release requires several failure-relevant evidence types\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「批次放行」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Lot release?","options":["只以供應商品名相同視為批次等效","只用平均粒徑核准漿料","保存條件也是批次追溯欄位"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equivalent lots from the same product name","Qualifying slurry from mean particle size alone","Storage conditions belong in lot traceability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"保存條件也是批次追溯欄位；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Storage conditions belong in lot traceability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability"},{"id":"a069","title":"互連電遷移可靠度","titleEn":"Interconnect electromigration reliability","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從電子流與原子遷移、加速模型到使用情境：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Electron flow and atomic transport and Acceleration model to Use-condition transfer: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電子流與原子遷移","焦耳熱","微結構","失效分析"],"labelsEn":["Electron flow and atomic transport","Joule heating","Microstructure","Failure analysis"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a069-stage01","order":1,"title":"電子流與原子遷移 → 通孔擁擠","titleEn":"Electron flow and atomic transport to Via current crowding","description":"把「電子流與原子遷移」「電流密度」「通孔擁擠」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Electron flow and atomic transport, Current density, Via current crowding.","steps":[{"id":"a069-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"電子流與原子遷移：建立模型","titleEn":"Electron flow and atomic transport: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「原子通量與通量散度不是同一量」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities.","instruction":"畫導線的電子流、傳統電流及可能原子通量，分清方向定義。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw electron flow, conventional current and possible atomic flux with explicit conventions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"原子通量與通量散度不是同一量；通量散度對應局部堆積與耗空。","observationEn":"Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities; Flux divergence tracks accumulation or depletion.","failure":"若採用「只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Locating every void from a current arrow alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電子流與原子遷移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：原子通量與通量散度不是同一量。","checkEn":"Submit the Electron flow and atomic transport diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-01-k1","title":"電子流與原子遷移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electron flow and atomic transport / Physics and model","text":"機制：原子通量與通量散度不是同一量。","textEn":"Mechanism: Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities."},{"id":"a069-v8-01-k2","title":"電子流與原子遷移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electron flow and atomic transport / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Locating every void from a current arrow alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電子流與原子遷移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Electron flow and atomic transport, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["原子通量與通量散度不是同一量","只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置","用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命"],"optionsEn":["Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities","Locating every void from a current arrow alone","Comparing different widths by rated current alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原子通量與通量散度不是同一量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-01"],"title":"電子流與原子遷移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Electron flow and atomic transport: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Locating every void from a current arrow alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「電子流與原子遷移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：通量散度對應局部堆積與耗空。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Electron flow and atomic transport artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Locating every void from a current arrow alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Flux divergence tracks accumulation or depletion. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"原子通量與通量散度不是同一量；通量散度對應局部堆積與耗空。","observationEn":"Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities; Flux divergence tracks accumulation or depletion.","failure":"若採用「只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Locating every void from a current arrow alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電子流與原子遷移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「通量散度對應局部堆積與耗空」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Electron flow and atomic transport, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Flux divergence tracks accumulation or depletion\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-02-k1","title":"電子流與原子遷移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electron flow and atomic transport / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：通量散度對應局部堆積與耗空。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Flux divergence tracks accumulation or depletion."},{"id":"a069-v8-02-k2","title":"電子流與原子遷移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electron flow and atomic transport / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置」與「原子通量與通量散度不是同一量」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Locating every void from a current arrow alone\" is not equivalent to \"Atomic flux and its divergence are different quantities\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電子流與原子遷移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Electron flow and atomic transport?","options":["用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命","通量散度對應局部堆積與耗空","只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置"],"optionsEn":["Comparing different widths by rated current alone","Flux divergence tracks accumulation or depletion","Locating every void from a current arrow alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"通量散度對應局部堆積與耗空；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Flux divergence tracks accumulation or depletion. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-02"],"title":"電流密度：建立模型","titleEn":"Current density: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相同電流不代表相同電流密度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Equal current does not imply equal current density.","instruction":"對兩種截面計算 J=I/A，並分別記錄總電流與截面。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設矩形互連寬 100 nm、厚 50 nm，電流 1 mA，均勻截面 A=5×10⁻¹⁵ m²；J=I/A=2×10¹¹ A/m²=2×10⁷ A/cm²，即 20 MA/cm²。再把厚度改為 40 nm，J 升為 25 MA/cm²。此例只練習單位與幾何敏感度，不是允許電流或可靠度門檻，也忽略局部電流擁擠。","instructionEn":"Calculate J=I/A for two cross-sections while recording current and area separately. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a rectangular line 100 nm wide and 50 nm thick carrying 1 mA uniformly. A=5×10⁻¹⁵ m²; J=I/A=2×10¹¹ A/m²=2×10⁷ A/cm², or 20 MA/cm². At 40 nm thickness J becomes 25 MA/cm². This exercises units and geometry sensitivity, not permitted current or a reliability limit; it ignores local current crowding.","observation":"相同電流不代表相同電流密度；膜厚誤差直接傳到電流密度。","observationEn":"Equal current does not imply equal current density; Thickness error propagates into current density.","failure":"若採用「用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing different widths by rated current alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電流密度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相同電流不代表相同電流密度。\n算例驗收：驗算 20 與 25 MA/cm²，註明 A/m² 轉 A/cm² 要除以 10,000。","checkEn":"Submit the Current density diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Equal current does not imply equal current density.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 20 and 25 MA/cm², noting that A/m² converts to A/cm² by division by 10,000.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-03-k1","title":"電流密度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Current density / Physics and model","text":"機制：相同電流不代表相同電流密度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Equal current does not imply equal current density."},{"id":"a069-v8-03-k2","title":"電流密度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Current density / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命」。\n假設數值與推算：假設矩形互連寬 100 nm、厚 50 nm，電流 1 mA，均勻截面 A=5×10⁻¹⁵ m²；J=I/A=2×10¹¹ A/m²=2×10⁷ A/cm²，即 20 MA/cm²。再把厚度改為 40 nm，J 升為 25 MA/cm²。此例只練習單位與幾何敏感度，不是允許電流或可靠度門檻，也忽略局部電流擁擠。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing different widths by rated current alone.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a rectangular line 100 nm wide and 50 nm thick carrying 1 mA uniformly. A=5×10⁻¹⁵ m²; J=I/A=2×10¹¹ A/m²=2×10⁷ A/cm², or 20 MA/cm². At 40 nm thickness J becomes 25 MA/cm². This exercises units and geometry sensitivity, not permitted current or a reliability limit; it ignores local current crowding."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電流密度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Current density, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命","把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值","相同電流不代表相同電流密度"],"optionsEn":["Comparing different widths by rated current alone","Using uniform line J as the worst via value","Equal current does not imply equal current density"],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同電流不代表相同電流密度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Equal current does not imply equal current density. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-03"],"title":"電流密度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Current density: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing different widths by rated current alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「電流密度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：膜厚誤差直接傳到電流密度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Current density artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing different widths by rated current alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thickness error propagates into current density. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相同電流不代表相同電流密度；膜厚誤差直接傳到電流密度。","observationEn":"Equal current does not imply equal current density; Thickness error propagates into current density.","failure":"若採用「用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing different widths by rated current alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電流密度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「膜厚誤差直接傳到電流密度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Current density, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thickness error propagates into current density\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-04-k1","title":"電流密度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Current density / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：膜厚誤差直接傳到電流密度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thickness error propagates into current density."},{"id":"a069-v8-04-k2","title":"電流密度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Current density / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命」與「相同電流不代表相同電流密度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing different widths by rated current alone\" is not equivalent to \"Equal current does not imply equal current density\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電流密度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Current density?","options":["膜厚誤差直接傳到電流密度","用額定電流直接比較不同線寬壽命","把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值"],"optionsEn":["Thickness error propagates into current density","Comparing different widths by rated current alone","Using uniform line J as the worst via value"],"answer":0,"explanation":"膜厚誤差直接傳到電流密度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thickness error propagates into current density. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-04"],"title":"通孔擁擠：建立模型","titleEn":"Via current crowding: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「平均 J 可能低估局部應力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Average J can underestimate local stress.","instruction":"畫線轉通孔轉角的等流線，圈出幾何擁擠和局部熱點。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw streamlines at a line-to-via turn and identify crowding and hotspots. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"平均 J 可能低估局部應力；平行通孔不一定平均分流。","observationEn":"Average J can underestimate local stress; Parallel vias need not share current equally.","failure":"若採用「把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using uniform line J as the worst via value\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「通孔擁擠」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：平均 J 可能低估局部應力。","checkEn":"Submit the Via current crowding diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Average J can underestimate local stress.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-05-k1","title":"通孔擁擠／物理與模型","titleEn":"Via current crowding / Physics and model","text":"機制：平均 J 可能低估局部應力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Average J can underestimate local stress."},{"id":"a069-v8-05-k2","title":"通孔擁擠／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Via current crowding / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using uniform line J as the worst via value."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通孔擁擠」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Via current crowding, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度","平均 J 可能低估局部應力","把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值"],"optionsEn":["Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint","Average J can underestimate local stress","Using uniform line J as the worst via value"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均 J 可能低估局部應力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Average J can underestimate local stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-05"],"title":"通孔擁擠：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Via current crowding: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using uniform line J as the worst via value.","instruction":"接續前一步「通孔擁擠」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：平行通孔不一定平均分流。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Via current crowding artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using uniform line J as the worst via value\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Parallel vias need not share current equally. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"平均 J 可能低估局部應力；平行通孔不一定平均分流。","observationEn":"Average J can underestimate local stress; Parallel vias need not share current equally.","failure":"若採用「把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using uniform line J as the worst via value\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「通孔擁擠」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「平行通孔不一定平均分流」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Via current crowding, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Parallel vias need not share current equally\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-06-k1","title":"通孔擁擠／物理與模型","titleEn":"Via current crowding / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：平行通孔不一定平均分流。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Parallel vias need not share current equally."},{"id":"a069-v8-06-k2","title":"通孔擁擠／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Via current crowding / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值」與「平均 J 可能低估局部應力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using uniform line J as the worst via value\" is not equivalent to \"Average J can underestimate local stress\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「通孔擁擠」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Via current crowding?","options":["把整段均勻 J 當成通孔最壞值","以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度","平行通孔不一定平均分流"],"optionsEn":["Using uniform line J as the worst via value","Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint","Parallel vias need not share current equally"],"answer":2,"explanation":"平行通孔不一定平均分流；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Parallel vias need not share current equally. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a069-stage02","order":2,"title":"焦耳熱 → 長度效應","titleEn":"Joule heating to Length effect","description":"把「焦耳熱」「加速模型」「長度效應」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Joule heating, Acceleration model, Length effect.","steps":[{"id":"a069-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-06"],"title":"焦耳熱：建立模型","titleEn":"Joule heating: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「試件溫度可能高於載台溫度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature.","instruction":"自訂電阻及電流算 I²R，畫電熱回授並要求獨立溫度量測。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Calculate hypothetical I²R, sketch electrothermal feedback and require temperature evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"試件溫度可能高於載台溫度；電阻溫度係數會混入損傷訊號。","observationEn":"Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature; Temperature coefficients contaminate damage signals.","failure":"若採用「以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「焦耳熱」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：試件溫度可能高於載台溫度。","checkEn":"Submit the Joule heating diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-07-k1","title":"焦耳熱／物理與模型","titleEn":"Joule heating / Physics and model","text":"機制：試件溫度可能高於載台溫度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature."},{"id":"a069-v8-07-k2","title":"焦耳熱／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Joule heating / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焦耳熱」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Joule heating, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["試件溫度可能高於載台溫度","以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度","把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數"],"optionsEn":["Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature","Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint","Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent"],"answer":0,"explanation":"試件溫度可能高於載台溫度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-07"],"title":"焦耳熱：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Joule heating: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint.","instruction":"接續前一步「焦耳熱」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電阻溫度係數會混入損傷訊號。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Joule heating artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Temperature coefficients contaminate damage signals. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"試件溫度可能高於載台溫度；電阻溫度係數會混入損傷訊號。","observationEn":"Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature; Temperature coefficients contaminate damage signals.","failure":"若採用「以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「焦耳熱」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電阻溫度係數會混入損傷訊號」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Joule heating, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Temperature coefficients contaminate damage signals\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-08-k1","title":"焦耳熱／物理與模型","titleEn":"Joule heating / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電阻溫度係數會混入損傷訊號。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Temperature coefficients contaminate damage signals."},{"id":"a069-v8-08-k2","title":"焦耳熱／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Joule heating / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度」與「試件溫度可能高於載台溫度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint\" is not equivalent to \"Specimen temperature may exceed chuck temperature\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「焦耳熱」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Joule heating?","options":["把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數","電阻溫度係數會混入損傷訊號","以載台設定值取代導線實際溫度"],"optionsEn":["Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent","Temperature coefficients contaminate damage signals","Replacing conductor temperature with the chuck setpoint"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電阻溫度係數會混入損傷訊號；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Temperature coefficients contaminate damage signals. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-08"],"title":"加速模型：建立模型","titleEn":"Acceleration model: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「外推需要機制及參數適用性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters.","instruction":"以假設 n 與活化能比較 Black 模型壽命比，所有溫度轉為 K。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare Black-model life ratios with hypothetical n and activation energy using kelvin. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"外推需要機制及參數適用性；活化能需以能量一致單位處理。","observationEn":"Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters; Activation energies need consistent energy units.","failure":"若採用「把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「加速模型」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：外推需要機制及參數適用性。","checkEn":"Submit the Acceleration model diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-09-k1","title":"加速模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Acceleration model / Physics and model","text":"機制：外推需要機制及參數適用性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters."},{"id":"a069-v8-09-k2","title":"加速模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Acceleration model / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「加速模型」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Acceleration model, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數","認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效","外推需要機制及參數適用性"],"optionsEn":["Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent","Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low","Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters"],"answer":2,"explanation":"外推需要機制及參數適用性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-09"],"title":"加速模型：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Acceleration model: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent.","instruction":"接續前一步「加速模型」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：活化能需以能量一致單位處理。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Acceleration model artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Activation energies need consistent energy units. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"外推需要機制及參數適用性；活化能需以能量一致單位處理。","observationEn":"Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters; Activation energies need consistent energy units.","failure":"若採用「把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「加速模型」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「活化能需以能量一致單位處理」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Acceleration model, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Activation energies need consistent energy units\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-10-k1","title":"加速模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Acceleration model / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：活化能需以能量一致單位處理。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Activation energies need consistent energy units."},{"id":"a069-v8-10-k2","title":"加速模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Acceleration model / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數」與「外推需要機制及參數適用性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent\" is not equivalent to \"Extrapolation requires valid mechanisms and parameters\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「加速模型」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Acceleration model?","options":["活化能需以能量一致單位處理","把攝氏值直接放入 Arrhenius 指數","認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效"],"optionsEn":["Activation energies need consistent energy units","Putting Celsius directly into an Arrhenius exponent","Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low"],"answer":0,"explanation":"活化能需以能量一致單位處理；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Activation energies need consistent energy units. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-10"],"title":"長度效應：建立模型","titleEn":"Length effect: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport.","instruction":"畫短線兩端受限的背應力，比較不同 J×L 教學案例。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw back stress in a constrained short line and compare hypothetical J×L cases. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移；端點原子阻擋條件會改變背應力。","observationEn":"Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport; Atomic blocking boundaries alter back stress.","failure":"若採用「認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「長度效應」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移。","checkEn":"Submit the Length effect diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-11-k1","title":"長度效應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Length effect / Physics and model","text":"機制：機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移。","textEn":"Mechanism: Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport."},{"id":"a069-v8-11-k2","title":"長度效應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Length effect / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長度效應」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Length effect, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導","機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移","認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效"],"optionsEn":["Assigning the same dominant path to all metals","Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport","Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low"],"answer":1,"explanation":"機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-11"],"title":"長度效應：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Length effect: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low.","instruction":"接續前一步「長度效應」成果，先指出錯誤主張「認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：端點原子阻擋條件會改變背應力。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Length effect artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Atomic blocking boundaries alter back stress. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移；端點原子阻擋條件會改變背應力。","observationEn":"Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport; Atomic blocking boundaries alter back stress.","failure":"若採用「認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「長度效應」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「端點原子阻擋條件會改變背應力」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Length effect, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Atomic blocking boundaries alter back stress\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-12-k1","title":"長度效應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Length effect / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：端點原子阻擋條件會改變背應力。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Atomic blocking boundaries alter back stress."},{"id":"a069-v8-12-k2","title":"長度效應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Length effect / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效」與「機械邊界會影響淨原子遷移」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low\" is not equivalent to \"Mechanical boundaries affect net atomic transport\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「長度效應」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Length effect?","options":["認為短線只因電阻低而必然不失效","宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導","端點原子阻擋條件會改變背應力"],"optionsEn":["Assuming short lines never fail merely because resistance is low","Assigning the same dominant path to all metals","Atomic blocking boundaries alter back stress"],"answer":2,"explanation":"端點原子阻擋條件會改變背應力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Atomic blocking boundaries alter back stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a069-stage03","order":3,"title":"微結構 → 截尾樣本","titleEn":"Microstructure to Censored specimens","description":"把「微結構」「失效準則」「截尾樣本」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Microstructure, Failure criterion, Censored specimens.","steps":[{"id":"a069-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-12"],"title":"微結構：建立模型","titleEn":"Microstructure: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure.","instruction":"比較晶界、介面與晶粒內路徑，為各路徑標記可觀察證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare grain-boundary, interface and bulk paths with observable evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異；介面黏著會改變機械約束。","observationEn":"The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure; Interface adhesion changes mechanical constraint.","failure":"若採用「宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning the same dominant path to all metals\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「微結構」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異。","checkEn":"Submit the Microstructure diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-13-k1","title":"微結構／物理與模型","titleEn":"Microstructure / Physics and model","text":"機制：最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異。","textEn":"Mechanism: The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure."},{"id":"a069-v8-13-k2","title":"微結構／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Microstructure / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assigning the same dominant path to all metals."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「微結構」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Microstructure, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異","宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導","看完數據才挑最有利的門檻"],"optionsEn":["The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure","Assigning the same dominant path to all metals","Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data"],"answer":0,"explanation":"最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-13"],"title":"微結構：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Microstructure: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assigning the same dominant path to all metals.","instruction":"接續前一步「微結構」成果，先指出錯誤主張「宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：介面黏著會改變機械約束。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Microstructure artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assigning the same dominant path to all metals\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Interface adhesion changes mechanical constraint. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異；介面黏著會改變機械約束。","observationEn":"The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure; Interface adhesion changes mechanical constraint.","failure":"若採用「宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning the same dominant path to all metals\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「微結構」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「介面黏著會改變機械約束」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Microstructure, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Interface adhesion changes mechanical constraint\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-14-k1","title":"微結構／物理與模型","titleEn":"Microstructure / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：介面黏著會改變機械約束。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Interface adhesion changes mechanical constraint."},{"id":"a069-v8-14-k2","title":"微結構／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Microstructure / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導」與「最快擴散路徑依材料與結構而異」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assigning the same dominant path to all metals\" is not equivalent to \"The fastest diffusion path depends on material and structure\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「微結構」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Microstructure?","options":["看完數據才挑最有利的門檻","介面黏著會改變機械約束","宣稱所有金屬都由同一擴散路徑主導"],"optionsEn":["Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data","Interface adhesion changes mechanical constraint","Assigning the same dominant path to all metals"],"answer":1,"explanation":"介面黏著會改變機械約束；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Interface adhesion changes mechanical constraint. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-14"],"title":"失效準則：建立模型","titleEn":"Failure criterion: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「門檻改變會改變報告壽命」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime.","instruction":"在假設電阻時間曲線標出噪聲、漂移與事先定義的失效門檻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark noise, drift and a predeclared failure threshold on resistance-time traces. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"門檻改變會改變報告壽命；初始電阻歸一化仍需保留原值。","observationEn":"Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime; Normalization should retain original resistance.","failure":"若採用「看完數據才挑最有利的門檻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「失效準則」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：門檻改變會改變報告壽命。","checkEn":"Submit the Failure criterion diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-15-k1","title":"失效準則／物理與模型","titleEn":"Failure criterion / Physics and model","text":"機制：門檻改變會改變報告壽命。","textEn":"Mechanism: Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime."},{"id":"a069-v8-15-k2","title":"失效準則／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Failure criterion / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「看完數據才挑最有利的門檻」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「失效準則」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Failure criterion, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["看完數據才挑最有利的門檻","把未失效樣本從統計中刪除","門檻改變會改變報告壽命"],"optionsEn":["Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data","Deleting surviving samples from statistics","Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime"],"answer":2,"explanation":"門檻改變會改變報告壽命；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-15"],"title":"失效準則：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Failure criterion: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「看完數據才挑最有利的門檻」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data.","instruction":"接續前一步「失效準則」成果，先指出錯誤主張「看完數據才挑最有利的門檻」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：初始電阻歸一化仍需保留原值。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Failure criterion artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Normalization should retain original resistance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"門檻改變會改變報告壽命；初始電阻歸一化仍需保留原值。","observationEn":"Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime; Normalization should retain original resistance.","failure":"若採用「看完數據才挑最有利的門檻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「失效準則」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「初始電阻歸一化仍需保留原值」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Failure criterion, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Normalization should retain original resistance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-16-k1","title":"失效準則／物理與模型","titleEn":"Failure criterion / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：初始電阻歸一化仍需保留原值。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Normalization should retain original resistance."},{"id":"a069-v8-16-k2","title":"失效準則／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Failure criterion / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「看完數據才挑最有利的門檻」與「門檻改變會改變報告壽命」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data\" is not equivalent to \"Changing the threshold changes reported lifetime\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「失效準則」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Failure criterion?","options":["初始電阻歸一化仍需保留原值","看完數據才挑最有利的門檻","把未失效樣本從統計中刪除"],"optionsEn":["Normalization should retain original resistance","Selecting a favorable threshold after viewing data","Deleting surviving samples from statistics"],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始電阻歸一化仍需保留原值；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Normalization should retain original resistance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-16"],"title":"截尾樣本：建立模型","titleEn":"Censored specimens: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life.","instruction":"建立失效及到期未失效樣本表，保留應力時間與狀態。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Tabulate failed and still-surviving specimens with stress time and status. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命；測試中止原因也需記錄。","observationEn":"Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life; Record why each test was stopped.","failure":"若採用「把未失效樣本從統計中刪除」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Deleting surviving samples from statistics\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「截尾樣本」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命。","checkEn":"Submit the Censored specimens diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-17-k1","title":"截尾樣本／物理與模型","titleEn":"Censored specimens / Physics and model","text":"機制：未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命。","textEn":"Mechanism: Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life."},{"id":"a069-v8-17-k2","title":"截尾樣本／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Censored specimens / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把未失效樣本從統計中刪除」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Deleting surviving samples from statistics."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「截尾樣本」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Censored specimens, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有開路都直接分類為電遷移","未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命","把未失效樣本從統計中刪除"],"optionsEn":["Classifying every open circuit as electromigration","Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life","Deleting surviving samples from statistics"],"answer":1,"explanation":"未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-17"],"title":"截尾樣本：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Censored specimens: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把未失效樣本從統計中刪除」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Deleting surviving samples from statistics.","instruction":"接續前一步「截尾樣本」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把未失效樣本從統計中刪除」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：測試中止原因也需記錄。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Censored specimens artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Deleting surviving samples from statistics\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Record why each test was stopped. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命；測試中止原因也需記錄。","observationEn":"Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life; Record why each test was stopped.","failure":"若採用「把未失效樣本從統計中刪除」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Deleting surviving samples from statistics\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「截尾樣本」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「測試中止原因也需記錄」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Censored specimens, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Record why each test was stopped\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-18-k1","title":"截尾樣本／物理與模型","titleEn":"Censored specimens / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：測試中止原因也需記錄。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Record why each test was stopped."},{"id":"a069-v8-18-k2","title":"截尾樣本／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Censored specimens / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把未失效樣本從統計中刪除」與「未失效樣本提供壽命下界而非無限壽命」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Deleting surviving samples from statistics\" is not equivalent to \"Survivors give lower bounds rather than infinite life\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「截尾樣本」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Censored specimens?","options":["把未失效樣本從統計中刪除","所有開路都直接分類為電遷移","測試中止原因也需記錄"],"optionsEn":["Deleting surviving samples from statistics","Classifying every open circuit as electromigration","Record why each test was stopped"],"answer":2,"explanation":"測試中止原因也需記錄；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Record why each test was stopped. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a069-stage04","order":4,"title":"失效分析 → 使用情境","titleEn":"Failure analysis to Use-condition transfer","description":"把「失效分析」「設計修正」「使用情境」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Failure analysis, Design revision, Use-condition transfer.","steps":[{"id":"a069-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-18"],"title":"失效分析：建立模型","titleEn":"Failure analysis: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration.","instruction":"將電阻突變對應空洞、裂紋和接觸異常三種假說，列出區分影像。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare void, crack and contact-fault hypotheses for a resistance jump and specify discriminating images. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制；裂紋可來自熱機械疲勞。","observationEn":"Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration; Cracks can arise from thermomechanical fatigue.","failure":"若採用「所有開路都直接分類為電遷移」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Classifying every open circuit as electromigration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「失效分析」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制。","checkEn":"Submit the Failure analysis diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-19-k1","title":"失效分析／物理與模型","titleEn":"Failure analysis / Physics and model","text":"機制：電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration."},{"id":"a069-v8-19-k2","title":"失效分析／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Failure analysis / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有開路都直接分類為電遷移」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Classifying every open circuit as electromigration."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「失效分析」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Failure analysis, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制","所有開路都直接分類為電遷移","通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍"],"optionsEn":["Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration","Classifying every open circuit as electromigration","Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-19"],"title":"失效分析：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Failure analysis: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有開路都直接分類為電遷移」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Classifying every open circuit as electromigration.","instruction":"接續前一步「失效分析」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有開路都直接分類為電遷移」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：裂紋可來自熱機械疲勞。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Failure analysis artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Classifying every open circuit as electromigration\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cracks can arise from thermomechanical fatigue. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制；裂紋可來自熱機械疲勞。","observationEn":"Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration; Cracks can arise from thermomechanical fatigue.","failure":"若採用「所有開路都直接分類為電遷移」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Classifying every open circuit as electromigration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「失效分析」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「裂紋可來自熱機械疲勞」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Failure analysis, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cracks can arise from thermomechanical fatigue\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-20-k1","title":"失效分析／物理與模型","titleEn":"Failure analysis / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：裂紋可來自熱機械疲勞。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cracks can arise from thermomechanical fatigue."},{"id":"a069-v8-20-k2","title":"失效分析／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Failure analysis / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有開路都直接分類為電遷移」與「電性失效不能獨自證明電遷移機制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Classifying every open circuit as electromigration\" is not equivalent to \"Electrical failure alone does not prove electromigration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「失效分析」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Failure analysis?","options":["通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍","裂紋可來自熱機械疲勞","所有開路都直接分類為電遷移"],"optionsEn":["Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime","Cracks can arise from thermomechanical fatigue","Classifying every open circuit as electromigration"],"answer":1,"explanation":"裂紋可來自熱機械疲勞；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cracks can arise from thermomechanical fatigue. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-20"],"title":"設計修正：建立模型","titleEn":"Design revision: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension.","instruction":"比較加寬線、增加通孔與改善散熱對 J、R、溫度的共同影響。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare widening, extra vias and cooling for effects on J, R and temperature. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸；設計改動也可能增加寄生電容。","observationEn":"Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension; Design revisions may increase parasitic capacitance.","failure":"若採用「通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「設計修正」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸。","checkEn":"Submit the Design revision diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-21-k1","title":"設計修正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Design revision / Physics and model","text":"機制：改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸。","textEn":"Mechanism: Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension."},{"id":"a069-v8-21-k2","title":"設計修正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Design revision / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設計修正」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Design revision, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍","只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效","改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸"],"optionsEn":["Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime","Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone","Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension"],"answer":2,"explanation":"改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-21"],"title":"設計修正：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Design revision: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime.","instruction":"接續前一步「設計修正」成果，先指出錯誤主張「通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：設計改動也可能增加寄生電容。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Design revision artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Design revisions may increase parasitic capacitance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸；設計改動也可能增加寄生電容。","observationEn":"Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension; Design revisions may increase parasitic capacitance.","failure":"若採用「通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「設計修正」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「設計改動也可能增加寄生電容」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Design revision, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Design revisions may increase parasitic capacitance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-22-k1","title":"設計修正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Design revision / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：設計改動也可能增加寄生電容。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Design revisions may increase parasitic capacitance."},{"id":"a069-v8-22-k2","title":"設計修正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Design revision / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍」與「改善須連到實際瓶頸而非單一尺寸」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime\" is not equivalent to \"Improvements must target the actual bottleneck, not one dimension\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「設計修正」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Design revision?","options":["設計改動也可能增加寄生電容","通孔加倍就假定壽命固定加倍","只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效"],"optionsEn":["Design revisions may increase parasitic capacitance","Assuming twice the vias always doubles lifetime","Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"設計改動也可能增加寄生電容；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Design revisions may increase parasitic capacitance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-22"],"title":"使用情境：建立模型","titleEn":"Use-condition transfer: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable.","instruction":"將測試直流負載與產品脈衝工作週期分開，列出不能直接外推的部分。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate DC stress from pulsed duty cycles and list unsupported extrapolations. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換；脈衝期間的熱峰值可能高於平均。","observationEn":"Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable; Pulsed thermal peaks can exceed averages.","failure":"若採用「只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「使用情境」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換。","checkEn":"Submit the Use-condition transfer diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-23-k1","title":"使用情境／物理與模型","titleEn":"Use-condition transfer / Physics and model","text":"機制：峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換。","textEn":"Mechanism: Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable."},{"id":"a069-v8-23-k2","title":"使用情境／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Use-condition transfer / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「使用情境」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Use-condition transfer, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置","峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換","只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效"],"optionsEn":["Locating every void from a current arrow alone","Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable","Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a069-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-em-model","v8-c-em-tsv","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a069-v8-23"],"title":"使用情境：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Use-condition transfer: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「使用情境」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：脈衝期間的熱峰值可能高於平均。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Use-condition transfer artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pulsed thermal peaks can exceed averages. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換；脈衝期間的熱峰值可能高於平均。","observationEn":"Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable; Pulsed thermal peaks can exceed averages.","failure":"若採用「只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「使用情境」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「脈衝期間的熱峰值可能高於平均」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Use-condition transfer, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pulsed thermal peaks can exceed averages\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a069-v8-24-k1","title":"使用情境／物理與模型","titleEn":"Use-condition transfer / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：脈衝期間的熱峰值可能高於平均。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pulsed thermal peaks can exceed averages."},{"id":"a069-v8-24-k2","title":"使用情境／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Use-condition transfer / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效」與「峰值、平均值與熱時間尺度不能互換」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone\" is not equivalent to \"Peak, average and thermal time scale are not interchangeable\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「使用情境」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Use-condition transfer?","options":["只匹配平均電流就宣稱情境等效","只畫電流箭頭便確定所有空洞位置","脈衝期間的熱峰值可能高於平均"],"optionsEn":["Declaring equivalent conditions from average current alone","Locating every void from a current arrow alone","Pulsed thermal peaks can exceed averages"],"answer":2,"explanation":"脈衝期間的熱峰值可能高於平均；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pulsed thermal peaks can exceed averages. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability"},{"id":"a070","title":"時間相依介電崩潰量測","titleEn":"Time-dependent dielectric breakdown measurement","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v10-media-9d48e1bc39c5"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從電場與厚度、時間解析度到可靠度報告：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Field and thickness and Time resolution to Reliability report: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電場與厚度","軟硬崩潰","面積縮放","量測回路"],"labelsEn":["Field and thickness","Soft and hard breakdown","Area scaling","Measurement circuit"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a070-stage01","order":1,"title":"電場與厚度 → 初始漏電","titleEn":"Field and thickness to Initial leakage","description":"把「電場與厚度」「應力模式」「初始漏電」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Field and thickness, Stress modes, Initial leakage.","steps":[{"id":"a070-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"電場與厚度：建立模型","titleEn":"Field and thickness: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Edge and multilayer local fields may differ.","instruction":"用假設 V、t 算 E=V/t 並標註均勻平板近似。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設單一均勻介質厚 5 nm、實際介質壓降 1 V，E=V/t=2×10⁸ V/m=2 MV/cm；厚度若為 4 nm 而電壓不變，場增為 2.5 MV/cm。用圖標明壓降與厚度。這不是 TDDB 壽命預測；多層介質、固定電荷與局部場增強未納入。","instructionEn":"Calculate E=V/t from hypothetical values and state the uniform planar approximation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a uniform 5 nm dielectric with an actual 1 V drop: E=V/t=2×10⁸ V/m=2 MV/cm. At 4 nm and the same voltage the field becomes 2.5 MV/cm. Label voltage drop and thickness on a sketch. This is not a TDDB lifetime prediction; multilayers, fixed charge and local field enhancement are excluded.","observation":"端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同；多層介質分壓依介電常數而變。","observationEn":"Edge and multilayer local fields may differ; Multilayer voltage division depends on permittivity.","failure":"若採用「直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電場與厚度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同。\n算例驗收：驗算兩個電場並說明為何單憑電場不能給出崩潰時間。","checkEn":"Submit the Field and thickness diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Edge and multilayer local fields may differ.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both fields and explain why field alone does not determine time to breakdown.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-01-k1","title":"電場與厚度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field and thickness / Physics and model","text":"機制：端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Edge and multilayer local fields may differ."},{"id":"a070-v8-01-k2","title":"電場與厚度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field and thickness / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場」。\n假設數值與推算：假設單一均勻介質厚 5 nm、實際介質壓降 1 V，E=V/t=2×10⁸ V/m=2 MV/cm；厚度若為 4 nm 而電壓不變，場增為 2.5 MV/cm。用圖標明壓降與厚度。這不是 TDDB 壽命預測；多層介質、固定電荷與局部場增強未納入。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a uniform 5 nm dielectric with an actual 1 V drop: E=V/t=2×10⁸ V/m=2 MV/cm. At 4 nm and the same voltage the field becomes 2.5 MV/cm. Label voltage drop and thickness on a sketch. This is not a TDDB lifetime prediction; multilayers, fixed charge and local field enhancement are excluded."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電場與厚度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Field and thickness, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同","直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場","將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布"],"optionsEn":["Edge and multilayer local fields may differ","Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness","Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times"],"answer":0,"explanation":"端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edge and multilayer local fields may differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-01"],"title":"電場與厚度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Field and thickness: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness.","instruction":"接續前一步「電場與厚度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：多層介質分壓依介電常數而變。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Field and thickness artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Multilayer voltage division depends on permittivity. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同；多層介質分壓依介電常數而變。","observationEn":"Edge and multilayer local fields may differ; Multilayer voltage division depends on permittivity.","failure":"若採用「直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電場與厚度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「多層介質分壓依介電常數而變」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Field and thickness, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Multilayer voltage division depends on permittivity\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-02-k1","title":"電場與厚度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field and thickness / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：多層介質分壓依介電常數而變。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Multilayer voltage division depends on permittivity."},{"id":"a070-v8-02-k2","title":"電場與厚度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field and thickness / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場」與「端點及多層介質的局部場可能不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness\" is not equivalent to \"Edge and multilayer local fields may differ\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電場與厚度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Field and thickness?","options":["將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布","多層介質分壓依介電常數而變","直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場"],"optionsEn":["Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times","Multilayer voltage division depends on permittivity","Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多層介質分壓依介電常數而變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multilayer voltage division depends on permittivity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-02"],"title":"應力模式：建立模型","titleEn":"Stress modes: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Different stress modes produce different energy histories.","instruction":"並列定電壓與定電流應力的控制量、響應及失效判準。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare controlled variables, responses and failure criteria for voltage and current stress. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史；恆流下電壓歷史需同步保存。","observationEn":"Different stress modes produce different energy histories; Constant-current tests need voltage histories.","failure":"若採用「將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「應力模式」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史。","checkEn":"Submit the Stress modes diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Different stress modes produce different energy histories.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-03-k1","title":"應力模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stress modes / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史。","textEn":"Mechanism: Different stress modes produce different energy histories."},{"id":"a070-v8-03-k2","title":"應力模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stress modes / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「應力模式」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Stress modes, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布","用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷","不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史"],"optionsEn":["Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times","Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric","Different stress modes produce different energy histories"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Different stress modes produce different energy histories. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-03"],"title":"應力模式：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Stress modes: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times.","instruction":"接續前一步「應力模式」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：恆流下電壓歷史需同步保存。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Stress modes artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Constant-current tests need voltage histories. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史；恆流下電壓歷史需同步保存。","observationEn":"Different stress modes produce different energy histories; Constant-current tests need voltage histories.","failure":"若採用「將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「應力模式」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「恆流下電壓歷史需同步保存」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Stress modes, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Constant-current tests need voltage histories\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-04-k1","title":"應力模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stress modes / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：恆流下電壓歷史需同步保存。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Constant-current tests need voltage histories."},{"id":"a070-v8-04-k2","title":"應力模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stress modes / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布」與「不同應力模式會產生不同能量歷史」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times\" is not equivalent to \"Different stress modes produce different energy histories\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「應力模式」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Stress modes?","options":["恆流下電壓歷史需同步保存","將定電流和定電壓時間直接混為同分布","用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Constant-current tests need voltage histories","Pooling constant-current and constant-voltage times","Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric"],"answer":0,"explanation":"恆流下電壓歷史需同步保存；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Constant-current tests need voltage histories. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-04"],"title":"初始漏電：建立模型","titleEn":"Initial leakage: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Below-floor current is not zero leakage.","instruction":"畫初始 I-V 並加入量測地板，區分漏電數值與低於解析度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw initial I-V with a measurement floor and separate measured leakage from unresolved values. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電；漏電測試需包含守衛與等待時間。","observationEn":"Below-floor current is not zero leakage; Leakage tests require guarding and settling.","failure":"若採用「用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「初始漏電」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電。","checkEn":"Submit the Initial leakage diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Below-floor current is not zero leakage.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-05-k1","title":"初始漏電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Initial leakage / Physics and model","text":"機制：低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電。","textEn":"Mechanism: Below-floor current is not zero leakage."},{"id":"a070-v8-05-k2","title":"初始漏電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Initial leakage / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「初始漏電」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Initial leakage, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰","低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電","用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown","Below-floor current is not zero leakage","Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric"],"answer":1,"explanation":"低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Below-floor current is not zero leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-05"],"title":"初始漏電：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Initial leakage: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric.","instruction":"接續前一步「初始漏電」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：漏電測試需包含守衛與等待時間。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Initial leakage artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Leakage tests require guarding and settling. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電；漏電測試需包含守衛與等待時間。","observationEn":"Below-floor current is not zero leakage; Leakage tests require guarding and settling.","failure":"若採用「用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「初始漏電」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「漏電測試需包含守衛與等待時間」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Initial leakage, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Leakage tests require guarding and settling\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-06-k1","title":"初始漏電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Initial leakage / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：漏電測試需包含守衛與等待時間。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Leakage tests require guarding and settling."},{"id":"a070-v8-06-k2","title":"初始漏電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Initial leakage / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷」與「低於儀器地板不能寫成零漏電」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric\" is not equivalent to \"Below-floor current is not zero leakage\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「初始漏電」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Initial leakage?","options":["用顯示零值證明介電層無缺陷","把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰","漏電測試需包含守衛與等待時間"],"optionsEn":["Treating a displayed zero as a defect-free dielectric","Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown","Leakage tests require guarding and settling"],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏電測試需包含守衛與等待時間；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Leakage tests require guarding and settling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a070-stage02","order":2,"title":"軟硬崩潰 → Weibull 座標","titleEn":"Soft and hard breakdown to Weibull coordinates","description":"把「軟硬崩潰」「時間解析度」「Weibull 座標」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Soft and hard breakdown, Time resolution, Weibull coordinates.","steps":[{"id":"a070-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-06"],"title":"軟硬崩潰：建立模型","titleEn":"Soft and hard breakdown: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled.","instruction":"比較有階躍但仍限流與低阻短路曲線，提出兩套判準。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare stepped leakage with current limiting against low-resistance shorting and define criteria. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併；限流可能掩蔽硬崩潰後導通。","observationEn":"Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled; Compliance can conceal post-breakdown conduction.","failure":"若採用「把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「軟硬崩潰」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併。","checkEn":"Submit the Soft and hard breakdown diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-07-k1","title":"軟硬崩潰／物理與模型","titleEn":"Soft and hard breakdown / Physics and model","text":"機制：軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併。","textEn":"Mechanism: Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled."},{"id":"a070-v8-07-k2","title":"軟硬崩潰／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Soft and hard breakdown / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「軟硬崩潰」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Soft and hard breakdown, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併","把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰","在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數"],"optionsEn":["Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled","Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown","Inventing an exact time between sparse samples"],"answer":0,"explanation":"軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-07"],"title":"軟硬崩潰：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Soft and hard breakdown: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown.","instruction":"接續前一步「軟硬崩潰」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：限流可能掩蔽硬崩潰後導通。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Soft and hard breakdown artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Compliance can conceal post-breakdown conduction. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併；限流可能掩蔽硬崩潰後導通。","observationEn":"Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled; Compliance can conceal post-breakdown conduction.","failure":"若採用「把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「軟硬崩潰」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「限流可能掩蔽硬崩潰後導通」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Soft and hard breakdown, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Compliance can conceal post-breakdown conduction\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-08-k1","title":"軟硬崩潰／物理與模型","titleEn":"Soft and hard breakdown / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：限流可能掩蔽硬崩潰後導通。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Compliance can conceal post-breakdown conduction."},{"id":"a070-v8-08-k2","title":"軟硬崩潰／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Soft and hard breakdown / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰」與「軟崩潰與硬崩潰不應任意合併」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown\" is not equivalent to \"Soft and hard breakdown should not be arbitrarily pooled\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「軟硬崩潰」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Soft and hard breakdown?","options":["在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數","限流可能掩蔽硬崩潰後導通","把第一次任何電流波動都算硬崩潰"],"optionsEn":["Inventing an exact time between sparse samples","Compliance can conceal post-breakdown conduction","Calling the first current fluctuation hard breakdown"],"answer":1,"explanation":"限流可能掩蔽硬崩潰後導通；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Compliance can conceal post-breakdown conduction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-08"],"title":"時間解析度：建立模型","titleEn":"Time resolution: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Event timing is limited by sampling interval.","instruction":"給兩個取樣間隔判讀同一模擬崩潰事件，報告區間而非假精確時刻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Analyze one simulated event with two sampling intervals and report an interval. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制；量測積分時間會平滑快速事件。","observationEn":"Event timing is limited by sampling interval; Integration time smooths rapid events.","failure":"若採用「在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inventing an exact time between sparse samples\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「時間解析度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制。","checkEn":"Submit the Time resolution diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Event timing is limited by sampling interval.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-09-k1","title":"時間解析度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Time resolution / Physics and model","text":"機制：事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Event timing is limited by sampling interval."},{"id":"a070-v8-09-k2","title":"時間解析度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Time resolution / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inventing an exact time between sparse samples."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間解析度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Time resolution, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數","把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能","事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制"],"optionsEn":["Inventing an exact time between sparse samples","Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy","Event timing is limited by sampling interval"],"answer":2,"explanation":"事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Event timing is limited by sampling interval. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-09"],"title":"時間解析度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Time resolution: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inventing an exact time between sparse samples.","instruction":"接續前一步「時間解析度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：量測積分時間會平滑快速事件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Time resolution artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inventing an exact time between sparse samples\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Integration time smooths rapid events. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制；量測積分時間會平滑快速事件。","observationEn":"Event timing is limited by sampling interval; Integration time smooths rapid events.","failure":"若採用「在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inventing an exact time between sparse samples\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「時間解析度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「量測積分時間會平滑快速事件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Time resolution, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Integration time smooths rapid events\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-10-k1","title":"時間解析度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Time resolution / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：量測積分時間會平滑快速事件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Integration time smooths rapid events."},{"id":"a070-v8-10-k2","title":"時間解析度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Time resolution / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數」與「事件時刻受到採樣間隔限制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inventing an exact time between sparse samples\" is not equivalent to \"Event timing is limited by sampling interval\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「時間解析度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Time resolution?","options":["量測積分時間會平滑快速事件","在稀疏採樣間填入沒有量測的精確秒數","把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能"],"optionsEn":["Integration time smooths rapid events","Inventing an exact time between sparse samples","Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測積分時間會平滑快速事件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Integration time smooths rapid events. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-10"],"title":"Weibull 座標：建立模型","titleEn":"Weibull coordinates: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy.","instruction":"對假設失效時間排序，繪製 ln[-ln(1-F)] 對 ln t 並標出排名法。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Rank hypothetical failures and plot ln[-ln(1-F)] against ln t with the ranking method. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能；排名估計對小樣本有偏差。","observationEn":"Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy; Rank estimates are uncertain in small samples.","failure":"若採用「把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「Weibull 座標」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能。","checkEn":"Submit the Weibull coordinates diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-11-k1","title":"Weibull 座標／物理與模型","titleEn":"Weibull coordinates / Physics and model","text":"機制：Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能。","textEn":"Mechanism: Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy."},{"id":"a070-v8-11-k2","title":"Weibull 座標／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Weibull coordinates / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「Weibull 座標」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Weibull coordinates, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應","Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能","把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能"],"optionsEn":["Using different materials to establish a pure area effect","Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy","Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-11"],"title":"Weibull 座標：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Weibull coordinates: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy.","instruction":"接續前一步「Weibull 座標」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：排名估計對小樣本有偏差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Weibull coordinates artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Rank estimates are uncertain in small samples. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能；排名估計對小樣本有偏差。","observationEn":"Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy; Rank estimates are uncertain in small samples.","failure":"若採用「把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「Weibull 座標」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「排名估計對小樣本有偏差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Weibull coordinates, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Rank estimates are uncertain in small samples\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-12-k1","title":"Weibull 座標／物理與模型","titleEn":"Weibull coordinates / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：排名估計對小樣本有偏差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Rank estimates are uncertain in small samples."},{"id":"a070-v8-12-k2","title":"Weibull 座標／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Weibull coordinates / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能」與「Weibull 斜率反映分布形狀而非直接等於活化能」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy\" is not equivalent to \"Weibull slope describes distribution shape, not activation energy\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「Weibull 座標」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Weibull coordinates?","options":["把斜率直接當成 Arrhenius 活化能","用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應","排名估計對小樣本有偏差"],"optionsEn":["Interpreting the slope as Arrhenius activation energy","Using different materials to establish a pure area effect","Rank estimates are uncertain in small samples"],"answer":2,"explanation":"排名估計對小樣本有偏差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Rank estimates are uncertain in small samples. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a070-stage03","order":3,"title":"面積縮放 → 電壓加速","titleEn":"Area scaling to Voltage acceleration","description":"把「面積縮放」「溫度加速」「電壓加速」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Area scaling, Thermal acceleration, Voltage acceleration.","steps":[{"id":"a070-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-12"],"title":"面積縮放：建立模型","titleEn":"Area scaling: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism.","instruction":"用相同製程不同面積電容比較弱點統計，註明獨立缺陷假設。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare capacitor areas under identical processing and state independent-defect assumptions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制；缺陷聚集會破壞獨立面積假設。","observationEn":"Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism; Defect clustering breaks independent-area assumptions.","failure":"若採用「用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using different materials to establish a pure area effect\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「面積縮放」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制。","checkEn":"Submit the Area scaling diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-13-k1","title":"面積縮放／物理與模型","titleEn":"Area scaling / Physics and model","text":"機制：面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism."},{"id":"a070-v8-13-k2","title":"面積縮放／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Area scaling / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using different materials to establish a pure area effect."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「面積縮放」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Area scaling, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制","用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應","所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線"],"optionsEn":["Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism","Using different materials to establish a pure area effect","Forcing all temperatures onto one line"],"answer":0,"explanation":"面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-13"],"title":"面積縮放：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Area scaling: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using different materials to establish a pure area effect.","instruction":"接續前一步「面積縮放」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：缺陷聚集會破壞獨立面積假設。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Area scaling artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using different materials to establish a pure area effect\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Defect clustering breaks independent-area assumptions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制；缺陷聚集會破壞獨立面積假設。","observationEn":"Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism; Defect clustering breaks independent-area assumptions.","failure":"若採用「用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using different materials to establish a pure area effect\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「面積縮放」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「缺陷聚集會破壞獨立面積假設」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Area scaling, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Defect clustering breaks independent-area assumptions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-14-k1","title":"面積縮放／物理與模型","titleEn":"Area scaling / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：缺陷聚集會破壞獨立面積假設。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Defect clustering breaks independent-area assumptions."},{"id":"a070-v8-14-k2","title":"面積縮放／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Area scaling / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應」與「面積縮放需同一缺陷族群及機制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using different materials to establish a pure area effect\" is not equivalent to \"Area scaling requires the same defect population and mechanism\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「面積縮放」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Area scaling?","options":["所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線","缺陷聚集會破壞獨立面積假設","用不同材料電容驗證純面積效應"],"optionsEn":["Forcing all temperatures onto one line","Defect clustering breaks independent-area assumptions","Using different materials to establish a pure area effect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺陷聚集會破壞獨立面積假設；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Defect clustering breaks independent-area assumptions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-14"],"title":"溫度加速：建立模型","titleEn":"Thermal acceleration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions.","instruction":"固定電場比較兩溫度壽命，分辨機制轉換與熱加速。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare life at two temperatures and fixed field, checking for mechanism changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換；接面自熱可能偏離載台溫度。","observationEn":"Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions; Junction self-heating differs from chuck temperature.","failure":"若採用「所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Forcing all temperatures onto one line\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「溫度加速」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換。","checkEn":"Submit the Thermal acceleration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-15-k1","title":"溫度加速／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal acceleration / Physics and model","text":"機制：溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換。","textEn":"Mechanism: Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions."},{"id":"a070-v8-15-k2","title":"溫度加速／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal acceleration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Forcing all temperatures onto one line."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度加速」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thermal acceleration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線","只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型","溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換"],"optionsEn":["Forcing all temperatures onto one line","Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²","Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-15"],"title":"溫度加速：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal acceleration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Forcing all temperatures onto one line.","instruction":"接續前一步「溫度加速」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接面自熱可能偏離載台溫度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thermal acceleration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Forcing all temperatures onto one line\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Junction self-heating differs from chuck temperature. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換；接面自熱可能偏離載台溫度。","observationEn":"Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions; Junction self-heating differs from chuck temperature.","failure":"若採用「所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Forcing all temperatures onto one line\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「溫度加速」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接面自熱可能偏離載台溫度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thermal acceleration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Junction self-heating differs from chuck temperature\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-16-k1","title":"溫度加速／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal acceleration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接面自熱可能偏離載台溫度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Junction self-heating differs from chuck temperature."},{"id":"a070-v8-16-k2","title":"溫度加速／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal acceleration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線」與「溫度外推不能跨越未知機制轉換」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Forcing all temperatures onto one line\" is not equivalent to \"Temperature extrapolation cannot ignore mechanism transitions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「溫度加速」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thermal acceleration?","options":["接面自熱可能偏離載台溫度","所有溫度點強迫共用一條直線","只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型"],"optionsEn":["Junction self-heating differs from chuck temperature","Forcing all temperatures onto one line","Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接面自熱可能偏離載台溫度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Junction self-heating differs from chuck temperature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-16"],"title":"電壓加速：建立模型","titleEn":"Voltage acceleration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike.","instruction":"比較兩種候選電場加速模型在測試區和使用區的預測差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare two field-acceleration models within test and use ranges. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同；模型選擇不確定度需納入外推。","observationEn":"Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike; Include model-selection uncertainty in extrapolation.","failure":"若採用「只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電壓加速」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同。","checkEn":"Submit the Voltage acceleration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-17-k1","title":"電壓加速／物理與模型","titleEn":"Voltage acceleration / Physics and model","text":"機制：測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike."},{"id":"a070-v8-17-k2","title":"電壓加速／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Voltage acceleration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電壓加速」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Voltage acceleration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調","測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同","只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型"],"optionsEn":["Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot","Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike","Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²"],"answer":1,"explanation":"測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-17"],"title":"電壓加速：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Voltage acceleration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R².","instruction":"接續前一步「電壓加速」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：模型選擇不確定度需納入外推。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Voltage acceleration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Include model-selection uncertainty in extrapolation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同；模型選擇不確定度需納入外推。","observationEn":"Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike; Include model-selection uncertainty in extrapolation.","failure":"若採用「只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電壓加速」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「模型選擇不確定度需納入外推」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Voltage acceleration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Include model-selection uncertainty in extrapolation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-18-k1","title":"電壓加速／物理與模型","titleEn":"Voltage acceleration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：模型選擇不確定度需納入外推。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Include model-selection uncertainty in extrapolation."},{"id":"a070-v8-18-k2","title":"電壓加速／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Voltage acceleration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型」與「測試區擬合接近不代表遠端外推相同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²\" is not equivalent to \"Similar in-range fits need not extrapolate alike\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電壓加速」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Voltage acceleration?","options":["只以最大 R² 選定終身壽命模型","把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調","模型選擇不確定度需納入外推"],"optionsEn":["Choosing a lifetime model solely by maximum R²","Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot","Include model-selection uncertainty in extrapolation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"模型選擇不確定度需納入外推；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Include model-selection uncertainty in extrapolation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a070-stage04","order":4,"title":"量測回路 → 可靠度報告","titleEn":"Measurement circuit to Reliability report","description":"把「量測回路」「缺陷與製程」「可靠度報告」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Measurement circuit, Defects and processing, Reliability report.","steps":[{"id":"a070-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-18"],"title":"量測回路：建立模型","titleEn":"Measurement circuit: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy.","instruction":"畫寄生電容、串聯電阻及限流，辨識崩潰瞬間能量來源。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw parasitic capacitance, resistance and compliance and identify transient energy sources. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能；寄生儲能可放大局部損傷。","observationEn":"Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy; Parasitic stored energy can amplify damage.","failure":"若採用「把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「量測回路」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能。","checkEn":"Submit the Measurement circuit diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-19-k1","title":"量測回路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Measurement circuit / Physics and model","text":"機制：儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能。","textEn":"Mechanism: Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy."},{"id":"a070-v8-19-k2","title":"量測回路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Measurement circuit / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測回路」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Measurement circuit, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能","把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調","所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命"],"optionsEn":["Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy","Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot","Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime"],"answer":0,"explanation":"儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-19"],"title":"量測回路：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Measurement circuit: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot.","instruction":"接續前一步「量測回路」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：寄生儲能可放大局部損傷。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Measurement circuit artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Parasitic stored energy can amplify damage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能；寄生儲能可放大局部損傷。","observationEn":"Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy; Parasitic stored energy can amplify damage.","failure":"若採用「把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「量測回路」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「寄生儲能可放大局部損傷」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Measurement circuit, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Parasitic stored energy can amplify damage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-20-k1","title":"量測回路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Measurement circuit / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：寄生儲能可放大局部損傷。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Parasitic stored energy can amplify damage."},{"id":"a070-v8-20-k2","title":"量測回路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Measurement circuit / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調」與「儀器限流不會立即消除已儲存電能」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot\" is not equivalent to \"Compliance does not instantly remove stored electrical energy\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「量測回路」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Measurement circuit?","options":["所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命","寄生儲能可放大局部損傷","把限流設定當成任何瞬間都無超調"],"optionsEn":["Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime","Parasitic stored energy can amplify damage","Assuming compliance guarantees no transient overshoot"],"answer":1,"explanation":"寄生儲能可放大局部損傷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Parasitic stored energy can amplify damage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-20"],"title":"缺陷與製程：建立模型","titleEn":"Defects and processing: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures.","instruction":"將粒子、厚度薄點與電極邊緣列為假說，規劃分組電容版圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"List particles, thin spots and electrode edges as hypotheses and design split structures. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效；早失效尾端可能是不同族群。","observationEn":"Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures; Early-failure tails may form a separate population.","failure":"若採用「所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「缺陷與製程」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效。","checkEn":"Submit the Defects and processing diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-21-k1","title":"缺陷與製程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defects and processing / Physics and model","text":"機制：幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效。","textEn":"Mechanism: Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures."},{"id":"a070-v8-21-k2","title":"缺陷與製程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defects and processing / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷與製程」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Defects and processing, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命","只報最長未失效時間作為保證","幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效"],"optionsEn":["Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime","Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee","Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures"],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-21"],"title":"缺陷與製程：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Defects and processing: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime.","instruction":"接續前一步「缺陷與製程」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：早失效尾端可能是不同族群。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Defects and processing artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Early-failure tails may form a separate population. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效；早失效尾端可能是不同族群。","observationEn":"Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures; Early-failure tails may form a separate population.","failure":"若採用「所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「缺陷與製程」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「早失效尾端可能是不同族群」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Defects and processing, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Early-failure tails may form a separate population\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-22-k1","title":"缺陷與製程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defects and processing / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：早失效尾端可能是不同族群。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Early-failure tails may form a separate population."},{"id":"a070-v8-22-k2","title":"缺陷與製程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defects and processing / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命」與「幾何及污染會混合內在與外在失效」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime\" is not equivalent to \"Geometry and contamination mix intrinsic and extrinsic failures\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「缺陷與製程」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Defects and processing?","options":["早失效尾端可能是不同族群","所有早期失效都視為材料本徵壽命","只報最長未失效時間作為保證"],"optionsEn":["Early-failure tails may form a separate population","Calling all early failures intrinsic material lifetime","Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee"],"answer":0,"explanation":"早失效尾端可能是不同族群；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Early-failure tails may form a separate population. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-22"],"title":"可靠度報告：建立模型","titleEn":"Reliability report: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence.","instruction":"整合樣本數、截尾、失效定義、模型和不確定區間的審查表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine sample count, censoring, criterion, model and uncertainty in a review sheet. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度；信賴區間應說明樣本與假設。","observationEn":"One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence; Confidence intervals need sample and assumption context.","failure":"若採用「只報最長未失效時間作為保證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「可靠度報告」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度。","checkEn":"Submit the Reliability report diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-23-k1","title":"可靠度報告／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reliability report / Physics and model","text":"機制：單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度。","textEn":"Mechanism: One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence."},{"id":"a070-v8-23-k2","title":"可靠度報告／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reliability report / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只報最長未失效時間作為保證」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「可靠度報告」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Reliability report, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場","單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度","只報最長未失效時間作為保證"],"optionsEn":["Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness","One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence","Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee"],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a070-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-td-db","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a070-v8-23"],"title":"可靠度報告：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Reliability report: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只報最長未失效時間作為保證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee.","instruction":"接續前一步「可靠度報告」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只報最長未失效時間作為保證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：信賴區間應說明樣本與假設。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Reliability report artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Confidence intervals need sample and assumption context. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度；信賴區間應說明樣本與假設。","observationEn":"One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence; Confidence intervals need sample and assumption context.","failure":"若採用「只報最長未失效時間作為保證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「可靠度報告」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「信賴區間應說明樣本與假設」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Reliability report, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Confidence intervals need sample and assumption context\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a070-v8-24-k1","title":"可靠度報告／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reliability report / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：信賴區間應說明樣本與假設。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Confidence intervals need sample and assumption context."},{"id":"a070-v8-24-k2","title":"可靠度報告／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reliability report / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只報最長未失效時間作為保證」與「單一最佳估計不足以表達壽命可信度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee\" is not equivalent to \"One best estimate does not express lifetime confidence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「可靠度報告」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Reliability report?","options":["只報最長未失效時間作為保證","直接用總堆疊厚度推斷每層相同電場","信賴區間應說明樣本與假設"],"optionsEn":["Reporting only the longest survivor as a guarantee","Inferring equal field in every layer from total thickness","Confidence intervals need sample and assumption context"],"answer":2,"explanation":"信賴區間應說明樣本與假設；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Confidence intervals need sample and assumption context. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"interconnect","subcategoryTitle":"互連、平坦化與可靠度","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interconnect, planarization and reliability"},{"id":"a071","title":"動態隨機存取記憶體電容製作","titleEn":"DRAM capacitor fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從1T1C 儲存、側壁共形性到電容整合審查：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From One-transistor one-capacitor storage and Sidewall conformality to Capacitor integration review: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["1T1C 儲存","高深寬比開口","機械支撐","寄生耦合"],"labelsEn":["One-transistor one-capacitor storage","High-aspect-ratio openings","Mechanical support","Parasitic coupling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a071-stage01","order":1,"title":"1T1C 儲存 → 立體表面","titleEn":"One-transistor one-capacitor storage to Three-dimensional surface","description":"把「1T1C 儲存」「電容預算」「立體表面」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for One-transistor one-capacitor storage, Capacitance budget, Three-dimensional surface.","steps":[{"id":"a071-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"1T1C 儲存：建立模型","titleEn":"One-transistor one-capacitor storage: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration.","instruction":"畫存取電晶體、儲存電容與位元線並追蹤寫入讀出。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw access transistor, capacitor and bitline and trace write/read paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復；位元線電容影響電荷共享電壓。","observationEn":"Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration; Bitline capacitance affects charge-sharing voltage.","failure":"若採用「把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「1T1C 儲存」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復。","checkEn":"Submit the One-transistor one-capacitor storage diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-01-k1","title":"1T1C 儲存／物理與模型","titleEn":"One-transistor one-capacitor storage / Physics and model","text":"機制：讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復。","textEn":"Mechanism: Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration."},{"id":"a071-v8-01-k2","title":"1T1C 儲存／驗證與限制","titleEn":"One-transistor one-capacitor storage / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「1T1C 儲存」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For One-transistor one-capacitor storage, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復","把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷","只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解"],"optionsEn":["Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration","Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing","Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization"],"answer":0,"explanation":"讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-01"],"title":"1T1C 儲存：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"One-transistor one-capacitor storage: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing.","instruction":"接續前一步「1T1C 儲存」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：位元線電容影響電荷共享電壓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding One-transistor one-capacitor storage artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bitline capacitance affects charge-sharing voltage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復；位元線電容影響電荷共享電壓。","observationEn":"Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration; Bitline capacitance affects charge-sharing voltage.","failure":"若採用「把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「1T1C 儲存」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「位元線電容影響電荷共享電壓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for One-transistor one-capacitor storage, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bitline capacitance affects charge-sharing voltage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-02-k1","title":"1T1C 儲存／物理與模型","titleEn":"One-transistor one-capacitor storage / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：位元線電容影響電荷共享電壓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bitline capacitance affects charge-sharing voltage."},{"id":"a071-v8-02-k2","title":"1T1C 儲存／驗證與限制","titleEn":"One-transistor one-capacitor storage / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷」與「讀出擾動儲存電荷並需要恢復」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing\" is not equivalent to \"Readout disturbs stored charge and requires restoration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「1T1C 儲存」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of One-transistor one-capacitor storage?","options":["只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解","位元線電容影響電荷共享電壓","把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷"],"optionsEn":["Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization","Bitline capacitance affects charge-sharing voltage","Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing"],"answer":1,"explanation":"位元線電容影響電荷共享電壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bitline capacitance affects charge-sharing voltage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-02"],"title":"電容預算：建立模型","titleEn":"Capacitance budget: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment.","instruction":"用 C=εA/t 比較面積、介電常數與厚度三種假設改善。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設理想平板電容 εr=20、A=1 µm²、t=10 nm，取 ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m，C=ε0εrA/t=17.708 fF。厚度不變而面積加倍時為 35.416 fF。這是幾何練習；未含邊緣場、死層、漏電與位元線負載，不是量產 DRAM 單元規格。","instructionEn":"Use C=εA/t to compare hypothetical area, permittivity and thickness changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume an ideal parallel-plate capacitor with εr=20, A=1 µm² and t=10 nm. Using ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m gives C=ε0εrA/t=17.708 fF; doubling area at fixed thickness gives 35.416 fF. This geometry exercise excludes fringing, dead layers, leakage and bitline loading and is not a production DRAM-cell specification.","observation":"薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估；邊緣場使平板公式成為近似。","observationEn":"Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment; Fringing makes the parallel-plate formula approximate.","failure":"若採用「只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電容預算」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估。\n算例驗收：將 µm² 換算為 10⁻¹² m²，驗算 17.708 fF，另列一項公式未包含的影響。","checkEn":"Submit the Capacitance budget diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment.\nWorked-example acceptance: Convert µm² to 10⁻¹² m², verify 17.708 fF and list one excluded effect.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-03-k1","title":"電容預算／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capacitance budget / Physics and model","text":"機制：薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估。","textEn":"Mechanism: Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment."},{"id":"a071-v8-03-k2","title":"電容預算／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capacitance budget / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解」。\n假設數值與推算：假設理想平板電容 εr=20、A=1 µm²、t=10 nm，取 ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m，C=ε0εrA/t=17.708 fF。厚度不變而面積加倍時為 35.416 fF。這是幾何練習；未含邊緣場、死層、漏電與位元線負載，不是量產 DRAM 單元規格。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume an ideal parallel-plate capacitor with εr=20, A=1 µm² and t=10 nm. Using ε0=8.854×10⁻¹² F/m gives C=ε0εrA/t=17.708 fF; doubling area at fixed thickness gives 35.416 fF. This geometry exercise excludes fringing, dead layers, leakage and bitline loading and is not a production DRAM-cell specification."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電容預算」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Capacitance budget, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解","以平面占地直接等同電極面積","薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估"],"optionsEn":["Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization","Equating footprint directly with electrode area","Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment"],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-03"],"title":"電容預算：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Capacitance budget: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization.","instruction":"接續前一步「電容預算」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：邊緣場使平板公式成為近似。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Capacitance budget artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Fringing makes the parallel-plate formula approximate. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估；邊緣場使平板公式成為近似。","observationEn":"Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment; Fringing makes the parallel-plate formula approximate.","failure":"若採用「只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電容預算」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「邊緣場使平板公式成為近似」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Capacitance budget, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Fringing makes the parallel-plate formula approximate\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-04-k1","title":"電容預算／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capacitance budget / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：邊緣場使平板公式成為近似。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Fringing makes the parallel-plate formula approximate."},{"id":"a071-v8-04-k2","title":"電容預算／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capacitance budget / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解」與「薄介電層的電容收益必須和漏電一起評估」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization\" is not equivalent to \"Capacitance gains from thinning require leakage assessment\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電容預算」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Capacitance budget?","options":["邊緣場使平板公式成為近似","只把介電層無限變薄當成可行最佳解","以平面占地直接等同電極面積"],"optionsEn":["Fringing makes the parallel-plate formula approximate","Treating unlimited dielectric thinning as feasible optimization","Equating footprint directly with electrode area"],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣場使平板公式成為近似；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Fringing makes the parallel-plate formula approximate. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-04"],"title":"立體表面：建立模型","titleEn":"Three-dimensional surface: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「垂直結構以高度換取表面面積」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Vertical structures exchange height for surface area.","instruction":"畫杯狀電容的內外表面，計算可利用面積而非只算底面。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch inner/outer cup surfaces and count usable area rather than footprint alone. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"垂直結構以高度換取表面面積；支撐接點可能減少有效面積。","observationEn":"Vertical structures exchange height for surface area; Support contacts may reduce effective area.","failure":"若採用「以平面占地直接等同電極面積」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating footprint directly with electrode area\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「立體表面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：垂直結構以高度換取表面面積。","checkEn":"Submit the Three-dimensional surface diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Vertical structures exchange height for surface area.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-05-k1","title":"立體表面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Three-dimensional surface / Physics and model","text":"機制：垂直結構以高度換取表面面積。","textEn":"Mechanism: Vertical structures exchange height for surface area."},{"id":"a071-v8-05-k2","title":"立體表面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Three-dimensional surface / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以平面占地直接等同電極面積」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating footprint directly with electrode area."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「立體表面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Three-dimensional surface, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格","垂直結構以高度換取表面面積","以平面占地直接等同電極面積"],"optionsEn":["Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD","Vertical structures exchange height for surface area","Equating footprint directly with electrode area"],"answer":1,"explanation":"垂直結構以高度換取表面面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Vertical structures exchange height for surface area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-05"],"title":"立體表面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Three-dimensional surface: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以平面占地直接等同電極面積」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating footprint directly with electrode area.","instruction":"接續前一步「立體表面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以平面占地直接等同電極面積」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：支撐接點可能減少有效面積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Three-dimensional surface artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating footprint directly with electrode area\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Support contacts may reduce effective area. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"垂直結構以高度換取表面面積；支撐接點可能減少有效面積。","observationEn":"Vertical structures exchange height for surface area; Support contacts may reduce effective area.","failure":"若採用「以平面占地直接等同電極面積」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating footprint directly with electrode area\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「立體表面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「支撐接點可能減少有效面積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Three-dimensional surface, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Support contacts may reduce effective area\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-06-k1","title":"立體表面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Three-dimensional surface / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：支撐接點可能減少有效面積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Support contacts may reduce effective area."},{"id":"a071-v8-06-k2","title":"立體表面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Three-dimensional surface / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以平面占地直接等同電極面積」與「垂直結構以高度換取表面面積」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating footprint directly with electrode area\" is not equivalent to \"Vertical structures exchange height for surface area\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「立體表面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Three-dimensional surface?","options":["以平面占地直接等同電極面積","量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格","支撐接點可能減少有效面積"],"optionsEn":["Equating footprint directly with electrode area","Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD","Support contacts may reduce effective area"],"answer":2,"explanation":"支撐接點可能減少有效面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Support contacts may reduce effective area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a071-stage02","order":2,"title":"高深寬比開口 → 下電極連續性","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio openings to Bottom-electrode continuity","description":"把「高深寬比開口」「側壁共形性」「下電極連續性」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for High-aspect-ratio openings, Sidewall conformality, Bottom-electrode continuity.","steps":[{"id":"a071-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-06"],"title":"高深寬比開口：建立模型","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio openings: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature.","instruction":"將頂部、中部和底部寬度標在假設剖面，計算各段收縮。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark top, middle and bottom widths on a hypothetical section and quantify narrowing. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌；蝕刻停止可發生在孔底而孔口正常。","observationEn":"Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature; Bottom etch stop can coexist with normal openings.","failure":"若採用「量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「高深寬比開口」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌。","checkEn":"Submit the High-aspect-ratio openings diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-07-k1","title":"高深寬比開口／物理與模型","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio openings / Physics and model","text":"機制：孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌。","textEn":"Mechanism: Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature."},{"id":"a071-v8-07-k2","title":"高深寬比開口／驗證與限制","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio openings / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高深寬比開口」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For High-aspect-ratio openings, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌","量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格","把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證"],"optionsEn":["Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature","Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD","Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-07"],"title":"高深寬比開口：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio openings: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD.","instruction":"接續前一步「高深寬比開口」成果，先指出錯誤主張「量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：蝕刻停止可發生在孔底而孔口正常。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding High-aspect-ratio openings artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bottom etch stop can coexist with normal openings. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌；蝕刻停止可發生在孔底而孔口正常。","observationEn":"Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature; Bottom etch stop can coexist with normal openings.","failure":"若採用「量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「高深寬比開口」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「蝕刻停止可發生在孔底而孔口正常」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for High-aspect-ratio openings, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bottom etch stop can coexist with normal openings\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-08-k1","title":"高深寬比開口／物理與模型","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio openings / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：蝕刻停止可發生在孔底而孔口正常。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bottom etch stop can coexist with normal openings."},{"id":"a071-v8-08-k2","title":"高深寬比開口／驗證與限制","titleEn":"High-aspect-ratio openings / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格」與「孔口尺寸不能完整描述深孔形貌」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD\" is not equivalent to \"Opening CD does not fully describe a deep feature\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「高深寬比開口」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of High-aspect-ratio openings?","options":["把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證","蝕刻停止可發生在孔底而孔口正常","量到孔口正確就判定整孔合格"],"optionsEn":["Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity","Bottom etch stop can coexist with normal openings","Accepting the whole hole from the opening CD"],"answer":1,"explanation":"蝕刻停止可發生在孔底而孔口正常；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bottom etch stop can coexist with normal openings. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-08"],"title":"側壁共形性：建立模型","titleEn":"Sidewall conformality: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth.","instruction":"比較入口與底部膜厚，定義覆蓋率並標出量測位置。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare entrance/bottom thickness, define coverage and mark measurement sites. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處；深孔反應物耗盡可造成厚度梯度。","observationEn":"Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth; Reactant depletion can cause depth gradients.","failure":"若採用「把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「側壁共形性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處。","checkEn":"Submit the Sidewall conformality diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-09-k1","title":"側壁共形性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sidewall conformality / Physics and model","text":"機制：表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處。","textEn":"Mechanism: Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth."},{"id":"a071-v8-09-k2","title":"側壁共形性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sidewall conformality / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「側壁共形性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Sidewall conformality, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證","只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整","表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處"],"optionsEn":["Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity","Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance","Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth"],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-09"],"title":"側壁共形性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Sidewall conformality: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity.","instruction":"接續前一步「側壁共形性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：深孔反應物耗盡可造成厚度梯度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Sidewall conformality artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reactant depletion can cause depth gradients. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處；深孔反應物耗盡可造成厚度梯度。","observationEn":"Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth; Reactant depletion can cause depth gradients.","failure":"若採用「把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「側壁共形性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「深孔反應物耗盡可造成厚度梯度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Sidewall conformality, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reactant depletion can cause depth gradients\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-10-k1","title":"側壁共形性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sidewall conformality / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：深孔反應物耗盡可造成厚度梯度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reactant depletion can cause depth gradients."},{"id":"a071-v8-10-k2","title":"側壁共形性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sidewall conformality / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證」與「表面限制反應仍需足夠前驅物流入深處」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity\" is not equivalent to \"Surface-limited reactions still need precursor access to depth\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「側壁共形性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Sidewall conformality?","options":["深孔反應物耗盡可造成厚度梯度","把 ALD 名稱當成百分百深孔均勻的保證","只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整"],"optionsEn":["Reactant depletion can cause depth gradients","Treating the ALD label as guaranteed deep-hole uniformity","Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"深孔反應物耗盡可造成厚度梯度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reactant depletion can cause depth gradients. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-10"],"title":"下電極連續性：建立模型","titleEn":"Bottom-electrode continuity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A film break can isolate useful area.","instruction":"畫斷裂與完整電極兩種路徑，規劃電阻與截面交叉檢查。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw broken/continuous electrodes and plan resistance plus cross-sectional checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積；電極粗糙也會改變局部電場。","observationEn":"A film break can isolate useful area; Electrode roughness alters local electric fields.","failure":"若採用「只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「下電極連續性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積。","checkEn":"Submit the Bottom-electrode continuity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A film break can isolate useful area.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-11-k1","title":"下電極連續性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bottom-electrode continuity / Physics and model","text":"機制：局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積。","textEn":"Mechanism: A film break can isolate useful area."},{"id":"a071-v8-11-k2","title":"下電極連續性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bottom-electrode continuity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下電極連續性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Bottom-electrode continuity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只加高電容而忽略結構支撐","局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積","只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整"],"optionsEn":["Increasing height without considering support","A film break can isolate useful area","Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A film break can isolate useful area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-11"],"title":"下電極連續性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Bottom-electrode continuity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance.","instruction":"接續前一步「下電極連續性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電極粗糙也會改變局部電場。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Bottom-electrode continuity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electrode roughness alters local electric fields. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積；電極粗糙也會改變局部電場。","observationEn":"A film break can isolate useful area; Electrode roughness alters local electric fields.","failure":"若採用「只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「下電極連續性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電極粗糙也會改變局部電場」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Bottom-electrode continuity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electrode roughness alters local electric fields\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-12-k1","title":"下電極連續性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bottom-electrode continuity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電極粗糙也會改變局部電場。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electrode roughness alters local electric fields."},{"id":"a071-v8-12-k2","title":"下電極連續性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bottom-electrode continuity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整」與「局部斷膜可能隔離部分有效面積」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance\" is not equivalent to \"A film break can isolate useful area\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「下電極連續性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Bottom-electrode continuity?","options":["只看外觀連續便推定電流路徑完整","只加高電容而忽略結構支撐","電極粗糙也會改變局部電場"],"optionsEn":["Assuming electrical continuity from exterior appearance","Increasing height without considering support","Electrode roughness alters local electric fields"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電極粗糙也會改變局部電場；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrode roughness alters local electric fields. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a071-stage03","order":3,"title":"機械支撐 → 漏電保持","titleEn":"Mechanical support to Leakage and retention","description":"把「機械支撐」「高介電界面」「漏電保持」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Mechanical support, High-k interfaces, Leakage and retention.","steps":[{"id":"a071-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-12"],"title":"機械支撐：建立模型","titleEn":"Mechanical support: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高度增加同時提高機械整合難度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty.","instruction":"畫高柱電容與支撐層，判斷移除犧牲層後的倒塌風險。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch tall capacitors and supports and assess collapse after sacrificial removal. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高度增加同時提高機械整合難度；乾燥表面力可拉倒高柱結構。","observationEn":"Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty; Drying forces can collapse tall structures.","failure":"若採用「只加高電容而忽略結構支撐」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Increasing height without considering support\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「機械支撐」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高度增加同時提高機械整合難度。","checkEn":"Submit the Mechanical support diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-13-k1","title":"機械支撐／物理與模型","titleEn":"Mechanical support / Physics and model","text":"機制：高度增加同時提高機械整合難度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty."},{"id":"a071-v8-13-k2","title":"機械支撐／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Mechanical support / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只加高電容而忽略結構支撐」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Increasing height without considering support."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「機械支撐」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Mechanical support, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["高度增加同時提高機械整合難度","只加高電容而忽略結構支撐","把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ"],"optionsEn":["Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty","Increasing height without considering support","Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa"],"answer":0,"explanation":"高度增加同時提高機械整合難度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-13"],"title":"機械支撐：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Mechanical support: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只加高電容而忽略結構支撐」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Increasing height without considering support.","instruction":"接續前一步「機械支撐」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只加高電容而忽略結構支撐」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：乾燥表面力可拉倒高柱結構。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Mechanical support artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Increasing height without considering support\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Drying forces can collapse tall structures. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高度增加同時提高機械整合難度；乾燥表面力可拉倒高柱結構。","observationEn":"Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty; Drying forces can collapse tall structures.","failure":"若採用「只加高電容而忽略結構支撐」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Increasing height without considering support\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「機械支撐」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「乾燥表面力可拉倒高柱結構」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Mechanical support, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Drying forces can collapse tall structures\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-14-k1","title":"機械支撐／物理與模型","titleEn":"Mechanical support / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：乾燥表面力可拉倒高柱結構。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Drying forces can collapse tall structures."},{"id":"a071-v8-14-k2","title":"機械支撐／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Mechanical support / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只加高電容而忽略結構支撐」與「高度增加同時提高機械整合難度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Increasing height without considering support\" is not equivalent to \"Greater height also raises mechanical integration difficulty\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「機械支撐」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Mechanical support?","options":["把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ","乾燥表面力可拉倒高柱結構","只加高電容而忽略結構支撐"],"optionsEn":["Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa","Drying forces can collapse tall structures","Increasing height without considering support"],"answer":1,"explanation":"乾燥表面力可拉倒高柱結構；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Drying forces can collapse tall structures. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-14"],"title":"高介電界面：建立模型","titleEn":"High-k interfaces: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低電容介面層可限制整體電容」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack.","instruction":"畫電極與高介電膜間串聯介面層，計算等效電容。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw interfacial layers in series with high-k and calculate effective capacitance. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"低電容介面層可限制整體電容；串聯中最小電容貢獻最大阻抗。","observationEn":"A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack; The smallest series capacitance dominates impedance.","failure":"若採用「把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「高介電界面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低電容介面層可限制整體電容。","checkEn":"Submit the High-k interfaces diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-15-k1","title":"高介電界面／物理與模型","titleEn":"High-k interfaces / Physics and model","text":"機制：低電容介面層可限制整體電容。","textEn":"Mechanism: A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack."},{"id":"a071-v8-15-k2","title":"高介電界面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"High-k interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高介電界面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For High-k interfaces, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ","只比較電容大小而忽略漏電","低電容介面層可限制整體電容"],"optionsEn":["Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa","Comparing retention by capacitance alone","A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack"],"answer":2,"explanation":"低電容介面層可限制整體電容；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-15"],"title":"高介電界面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"High-k interfaces: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa.","instruction":"接續前一步「高介電界面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：串聯中最小電容貢獻最大阻抗。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding High-k interfaces artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: The smallest series capacitance dominates impedance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低電容介面層可限制整體電容；串聯中最小電容貢獻最大阻抗。","observationEn":"A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack; The smallest series capacitance dominates impedance.","failure":"若採用「把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「高介電界面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「串聯中最小電容貢獻最大阻抗」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for High-k interfaces, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"The smallest series capacitance dominates impedance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-16-k1","title":"高介電界面／物理與模型","titleEn":"High-k interfaces / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：串聯中最小電容貢獻最大阻抗。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: The smallest series capacitance dominates impedance."},{"id":"a071-v8-16-k2","title":"高介電界面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"High-k interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ」與「低電容介面層可限制整體電容」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa\" is not equivalent to \"A low-capacitance interface can limit the whole stack\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「高介電界面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of High-k interfaces?","options":["串聯中最小電容貢獻最大阻抗","把材料本體 κ 直接當作元件有效 κ","只比較電容大小而忽略漏電"],"optionsEn":["The smallest series capacitance dominates impedance","Equating bulk kappa with device-effective kappa","Comparing retention by capacitance alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"串聯中最小電容貢獻最大阻抗；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The smallest series capacitance dominates impedance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-16"],"title":"漏電保持：建立模型","titleEn":"Leakage and retention: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage.","instruction":"以假設 Q=CV 和漏電 I 估算 Δt=ΔQ/I 的理想化保持時間。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Estimate idealized Δt=ΔQ/I using hypothetical Q=CV and leakage. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電；漏電通常依電壓與溫度而變。","observationEn":"Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage; Leakage depends on voltage and temperature.","failure":"若採用「只比較電容大小而忽略漏電」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing retention by capacitance alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「漏電保持」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電。","checkEn":"Submit the Leakage and retention diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-17-k1","title":"漏電保持／物理與模型","titleEn":"Leakage and retention / Physics and model","text":"機制：保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電。","textEn":"Mechanism: Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage."},{"id":"a071-v8-17-k2","title":"漏電保持／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Leakage and retention / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只比較電容大小而忽略漏電」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing retention by capacitance alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漏電保持」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Leakage and retention, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立","保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電","只比較電容大小而忽略漏電"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every array capacitor is isolated","Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage","Comparing retention by capacitance alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-17"],"title":"漏電保持：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Leakage and retention: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只比較電容大小而忽略漏電」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing retention by capacitance alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「漏電保持」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只比較電容大小而忽略漏電」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：漏電通常依電壓與溫度而變。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Leakage and retention artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing retention by capacitance alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Leakage depends on voltage and temperature. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電；漏電通常依電壓與溫度而變。","observationEn":"Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage; Leakage depends on voltage and temperature.","failure":"若採用「只比較電容大小而忽略漏電」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing retention by capacitance alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「漏電保持」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「漏電通常依電壓與溫度而變」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Leakage and retention, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Leakage depends on voltage and temperature\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-18-k1","title":"漏電保持／物理與模型","titleEn":"Leakage and retention / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：漏電通常依電壓與溫度而變。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Leakage depends on voltage and temperature."},{"id":"a071-v8-18-k2","title":"漏電保持／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Leakage and retention / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只比較電容大小而忽略漏電」與「保持時間取決於可容許電荷損失與漏電」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing retention by capacitance alone\" is not equivalent to \"Retention depends on allowable charge loss and leakage\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「漏電保持」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Leakage and retention?","options":["只比較電容大小而忽略漏電","假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立","漏電通常依電壓與溫度而變"],"optionsEn":["Comparing retention by capacitance alone","Assuming every array capacitor is isolated","Leakage depends on voltage and temperature"],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏電通常依電壓與溫度而變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Leakage depends on voltage and temperature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a071-stage04","order":4,"title":"寄生耦合 → 電容整合審查","titleEn":"Parasitic coupling to Capacitor integration review","description":"把「寄生耦合」「分布尾端」「電容整合審查」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Parasitic coupling, Distribution tails, Capacitor integration review.","steps":[{"id":"a071-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-18"],"title":"寄生耦合：建立模型","titleEn":"Parasitic coupling: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage.","instruction":"畫相鄰儲存節點，對一次位元線切換標示可能耦合路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw neighboring storage nodes and coupling during a bitline transition. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響；耦合瞬態受節點阻抗影響。","observationEn":"Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage; Coupling transients depend on node impedance.","failure":"若採用「假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every array capacitor is isolated\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「寄生耦合」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響。","checkEn":"Submit the Parasitic coupling diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-19-k1","title":"寄生耦合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Parasitic coupling / Physics and model","text":"機制：鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響。","textEn":"Mechanism: Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage."},{"id":"a071-v8-19-k2","title":"寄生耦合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Parasitic coupling / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming every array capacitor is isolated."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「寄生耦合」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Parasitic coupling, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響","假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立","用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新"],"optionsEn":["Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage","Assuming every array capacitor is isolated","Setting array refresh from mean retention alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-19"],"title":"寄生耦合：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Parasitic coupling: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming every array capacitor is isolated.","instruction":"接續前一步「寄生耦合」成果，先指出錯誤主張「假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：耦合瞬態受節點阻抗影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Parasitic coupling artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming every array capacitor is isolated\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Coupling transients depend on node impedance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響；耦合瞬態受節點阻抗影響。","observationEn":"Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage; Coupling transients depend on node impedance.","failure":"若採用「假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every array capacitor is isolated\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「寄生耦合」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「耦合瞬態受節點阻抗影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Parasitic coupling, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Coupling transients depend on node impedance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-20-k1","title":"寄生耦合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Parasitic coupling / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：耦合瞬態受節點阻抗影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Coupling transients depend on node impedance."},{"id":"a071-v8-20-k2","title":"寄生耦合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Parasitic coupling / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立」與「鄰近導體使節點電位受到非預期影響」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming every array capacitor is isolated\" is not equivalent to \"Neighboring conductors can perturb node voltage\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「寄生耦合」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Parasitic coupling?","options":["用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新","耦合瞬態受節點阻抗影響","假定每顆電容在陣列中完全孤立"],"optionsEn":["Setting array refresh from mean retention alone","Coupling transients depend on node impedance","Assuming every array capacitor is isolated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"耦合瞬態受節點阻抗影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Coupling transients depend on node impedance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-20"],"title":"分布尾端：建立模型","titleEn":"Distribution tails: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements.","instruction":"比較同平均保持時間但不同短保持尾端的兩批假設資料。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical lots with equal mean retention but different short-retention tails. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求；刷新功耗會隨刷新頻率增加。","observationEn":"Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements; Refresh power increases with refresh frequency.","failure":"若採用「用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Setting array refresh from mean retention alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「分布尾端」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求。","checkEn":"Submit the Distribution tails diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-21-k1","title":"分布尾端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Distribution tails / Physics and model","text":"機制：最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements."},{"id":"a071-v8-21-k2","title":"分布尾端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Distribution tails / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Setting array refresh from mean retention alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分布尾端」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Distribution tails, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新","只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格","最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求"],"optionsEn":["Setting array refresh from mean retention alone","Claiming functional memory from an attractive section","Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-21"],"title":"分布尾端：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Distribution tails: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Setting array refresh from mean retention alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「分布尾端」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：刷新功耗會隨刷新頻率增加。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Distribution tails artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Setting array refresh from mean retention alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Refresh power increases with refresh frequency. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求；刷新功耗會隨刷新頻率增加。","observationEn":"Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements; Refresh power increases with refresh frequency.","failure":"若採用「用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Setting array refresh from mean retention alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「分布尾端」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「刷新功耗會隨刷新頻率增加」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Distribution tails, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Refresh power increases with refresh frequency\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-22-k1","title":"分布尾端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Distribution tails / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：刷新功耗會隨刷新頻率增加。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Refresh power increases with refresh frequency."},{"id":"a071-v8-22-k2","title":"分布尾端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Distribution tails / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新」與「最弱儲存單元可能支配刷新要求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Setting array refresh from mean retention alone\" is not equivalent to \"Weak cells can dominate refresh requirements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「分布尾端」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Distribution tails?","options":["刷新功耗會隨刷新頻率增加","用平均保持時間設定全陣列刷新","只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格"],"optionsEn":["Refresh power increases with refresh frequency","Setting array refresh from mean retention alone","Claiming functional memory from an attractive section"],"answer":0,"explanation":"刷新功耗會隨刷新頻率增加；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Refresh power increases with refresh frequency. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-22"],"title":"電容整合審查：建立模型","titleEn":"Capacitor integration review: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電性與結構證據需相互對應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Electrical and structural evidence must correspond.","instruction":"把電容、漏電、深孔形貌、電極連通與機械支撐放入證據矩陣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine capacitance, leakage, profile, continuity and support in an evidence matrix. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電性與結構證據需相互對應；電容結構合格不等於整個感測放大器合格。","observationEn":"Electrical and structural evidence must correspond; Capacitor quality does not qualify sense amplifiers.","failure":"若採用「只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming functional memory from an attractive section\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電容整合審查」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電性與結構證據需相互對應。","checkEn":"Submit the Capacitor integration review diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Electrical and structural evidence must correspond.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-23-k1","title":"電容整合審查／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capacitor integration review / Physics and model","text":"機制：電性與結構證據需相互對應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Electrical and structural evidence must correspond."},{"id":"a071-v8-23-k2","title":"電容整合審查／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capacitor integration review / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Claiming functional memory from an attractive section."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電容整合審查」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Capacitor integration review, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷","電性與結構證據需相互對應","只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格"],"optionsEn":["Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing","Electrical and structural evidence must correspond","Claiming functional memory from an attractive section"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電性與結構證據需相互對應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrical and structural evidence must correspond. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a071-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-dram","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a071-v8-23"],"title":"電容整合審查：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Capacitor integration review: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Claiming functional memory from an attractive section.","instruction":"接續前一步「電容整合審查」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電容結構合格不等於整個感測放大器合格。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Capacitor integration review artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Claiming functional memory from an attractive section\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Capacitor quality does not qualify sense amplifiers. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電性與結構證據需相互對應；電容結構合格不等於整個感測放大器合格。","observationEn":"Electrical and structural evidence must correspond; Capacitor quality does not qualify sense amplifiers.","failure":"若採用「只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming functional memory from an attractive section\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電容整合審查」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電容結構合格不等於整個感測放大器合格」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Capacitor integration review, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Capacitor quality does not qualify sense amplifiers\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a071-v8-24-k1","title":"電容整合審查／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capacitor integration review / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電容結構合格不等於整個感測放大器合格。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Capacitor quality does not qualify sense amplifiers."},{"id":"a071-v8-24-k2","title":"電容整合審查／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capacitor integration review / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格」與「電性與結構證據需相互對應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Claiming functional memory from an attractive section\" is not equivalent to \"Electrical and structural evidence must correspond\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電容整合審查」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Capacitor integration review?","options":["只展示漂亮截面就宣稱記憶體功能合格","把 DRAM 讀取當成完全不改變電容電荷","電容結構合格不等於整個感測放大器合格"],"optionsEn":["Claiming functional memory from an attractive section","Treating DRAM read as entirely nondisturbing","Capacitor quality does not qualify sense amplifiers"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電容結構合格不等於整個感測放大器合格；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Capacitor quality does not qualify sense amplifiers. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"},{"id":"a072","title":"垂直 NAND 記憶體堆疊","titleEn":"Vertical NAND memory stacking","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從垂直字串、階梯接點到良率地圖：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Vertical strings and Staircase contacts to Yield map: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["垂直字串","深孔輪廓","通道連續","擾動路徑"],"labelsEn":["Vertical strings","Deep-hole profile","Channel continuity","Disturb pathways"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a072-stage01","order":1,"title":"垂直字串 → 晶圓彎曲","titleEn":"Vertical strings to Wafer bow","description":"把「垂直字串」「交替薄膜」「晶圓彎曲」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Vertical strings, Alternating films, Wafer bow.","steps":[{"id":"a072-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"垂直字串：建立模型","titleEn":"Vertical strings: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Layer count differs from bits stored per cell.","instruction":"畫穿過多層字線的通道並標示選擇閘和每層記憶單元。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設一條 NAND 串有 64 個可儲存單元，每單元用 TLC 編碼 3 bit，原始容量為 64×3=192 bit。另有兩個選擇閘，不能計入儲存單元數；若編碼改為每單元 2 bit，則為 128 bit。未扣 ECC、備援與壞單元，也不由此推算整顆晶片密度。","instructionEn":"Draw a channel through stacked wordlines with select gates and per-layer cells. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume one NAND string has 64 storage cells, each encoded as TLC with 3 bits: raw capacity is 64×3=192 bits. Two additional select gates are not storage cells. At 2 bits per cell the string has 128 raw bits. ECC, redundancy and bad cells are not deducted, and this does not determine whole-chip density.","observation":"堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數；選擇閘與儲存單元的功能不同。","observationEn":"Layer count differs from bits stored per cell; Select gates differ from storage cells.","failure":"若採用「把 3D 層數當成單元位元數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating stack layers with bits per cell\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「垂直字串」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數。\n算例驗收：圖上分開 64 個儲存單元與兩個選擇閘，驗算 192 與 128 bit，說明層數與每單元位元數不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Vertical strings diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Layer count differs from bits stored per cell.\nWorked-example acceptance: Separate 64 storage cells from two select gates; verify 192 and 128 bits and distinguish layer count from bits per cell.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-01-k1","title":"垂直字串／物理與模型","titleEn":"Vertical strings / Physics and model","text":"機制：堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數。","textEn":"Mechanism: Layer count differs from bits stored per cell."},{"id":"a072-v8-01-k2","title":"垂直字串／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Vertical strings / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把 3D 層數當成單元位元數」。\n假設數值與推算：假設一條 NAND 串有 64 個可儲存單元，每單元用 TLC 編碼 3 bit，原始容量為 64×3=192 bit。另有兩個選擇閘，不能計入儲存單元數；若編碼改為每單元 2 bit，則為 128 bit。未扣 ECC、備援與壞單元，也不由此推算整顆晶片密度。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating stack layers with bits per cell.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume one NAND string has 64 storage cells, each encoded as TLC with 3 bits: raw capacity is 64×3=192 bits. Two additional select gates are not storage cells. At 2 bits per cell the string has 128 raw bits. ECC, redundancy and bad cells are not deducted, and this does not determine whole-chip density."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂直字串」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Vertical strings, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數","把 3D 層數當成單元位元數","只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效"],"optionsEn":["Layer count differs from bits stored per cell","Equating stack layers with bits per cell","Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Layer count differs from bits stored per cell. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-01"],"title":"垂直字串：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Vertical strings: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把 3D 層數當成單元位元數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating stack layers with bits per cell.","instruction":"接續前一步「垂直字串」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把 3D 層數當成單元位元數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：選擇閘與儲存單元的功能不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Vertical strings artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating stack layers with bits per cell\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Select gates differ from storage cells. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數；選擇閘與儲存單元的功能不同。","observationEn":"Layer count differs from bits stored per cell; Select gates differ from storage cells.","failure":"若採用「把 3D 層數當成單元位元數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating stack layers with bits per cell\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「垂直字串」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「選擇閘與儲存單元的功能不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Vertical strings, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Select gates differ from storage cells\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-02-k1","title":"垂直字串／物理與模型","titleEn":"Vertical strings / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：選擇閘與儲存單元的功能不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Select gates differ from storage cells."},{"id":"a072-v8-02-k2","title":"垂直字串／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Vertical strings / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把 3D 層數當成單元位元數」與「堆疊層數不同於每顆單元可儲存位元數」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating stack layers with bits per cell\" is not equivalent to \"Layer count differs from bits stored per cell\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「垂直字串」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Vertical strings?","options":["只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效","選擇閘與儲存單元的功能不同","把 3D 層數當成單元位元數"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer","Select gates differ from storage cells","Equating stack layers with bits per cell"],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇閘與儲存單元的功能不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Select gates differ from storage cells. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-02"],"title":"交替薄膜：建立模型","titleEn":"Alternating films: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Small per-layer errors can accumulate.","instruction":"畫兩材料交替堆疊，追蹤累積厚度誤差與應力方向。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw alternating films and track accumulated thickness error and stress. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差；層間粗糙可沿堆疊複製或放大。","observationEn":"Small per-layer errors can accumulate; Roughness can propagate through stacked layers.","failure":"若採用「只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「交替薄膜」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差。","checkEn":"Submit the Alternating films diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Small per-layer errors can accumulate.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-03-k1","title":"交替薄膜／物理與模型","titleEn":"Alternating films / Physics and model","text":"機制：小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差。","textEn":"Mechanism: Small per-layer errors can accumulate."},{"id":"a072-v8-03-k2","title":"交替薄膜／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Alternating films / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「交替薄膜」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Alternating films, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效","晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力","小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer","Calling every layer stress-free after flattening","Small per-layer errors can accumulate"],"answer":2,"explanation":"小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small per-layer errors can accumulate. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-03"],"title":"交替薄膜：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Alternating films: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer.","instruction":"接續前一步「交替薄膜」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：層間粗糙可沿堆疊複製或放大。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Alternating films artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Roughness can propagate through stacked layers. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差；層間粗糙可沿堆疊複製或放大。","observationEn":"Small per-layer errors can accumulate; Roughness can propagate through stacked layers.","failure":"若採用「只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「交替薄膜」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「層間粗糙可沿堆疊複製或放大」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Alternating films, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Roughness can propagate through stacked layers\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-04-k1","title":"交替薄膜／物理與模型","titleEn":"Alternating films / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：層間粗糙可沿堆疊複製或放大。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Roughness can propagate through stacked layers."},{"id":"a072-v8-04-k2","title":"交替薄膜／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Alternating films / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效」與「小的每層偏差可能累積成整體偏差」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer\" is not equivalent to \"Small per-layer errors can accumulate\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「交替薄膜」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Alternating films?","options":["層間粗糙可沿堆疊複製或放大","只驗第一層就視為整堆疊等效","晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力"],"optionsEn":["Roughness can propagate through stacked layers","Qualifying an entire stack from the first layer","Calling every layer stress-free after flattening"],"answer":0,"explanation":"層間粗糙可沿堆疊複製或放大；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Roughness can propagate through stacked layers. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-04"],"title":"晶圓彎曲：建立模型","titleEn":"Wafer bow: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress.","instruction":"對稱與非對稱應力堆疊各畫曲率，加入背面補償的假设。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch bow for symmetric/asymmetric stress stacks and a hypothetical backside compensation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失；局部彎曲也影響對準與聚焦。","observationEn":"Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress; Local bow affects alignment and focus.","failure":"若採用「晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling every layer stress-free after flattening\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶圓彎曲」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失。","checkEn":"Submit the Wafer bow diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-05-k1","title":"晶圓彎曲／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wafer bow / Physics and model","text":"機制：補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失。","textEn":"Mechanism: Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress."},{"id":"a072-v8-05-k2","title":"晶圓彎曲／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wafer bow / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling every layer stress-free after flattening."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶圓彎曲」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Wafer bow, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述","補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失","晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力"],"optionsEn":["Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone","Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress","Calling every layer stress-free after flattening"],"answer":1,"explanation":"補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-05"],"title":"晶圓彎曲：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Wafer bow: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling every layer stress-free after flattening.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶圓彎曲」成果，先指出錯誤主張「晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：局部彎曲也影響對準與聚焦。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Wafer bow artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling every layer stress-free after flattening\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Local bow affects alignment and focus. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失；局部彎曲也影響對準與聚焦。","observationEn":"Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress; Local bow affects alignment and focus.","failure":"若採用「晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling every layer stress-free after flattening\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶圓彎曲」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「局部彎曲也影響對準與聚焦」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Wafer bow, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Local bow affects alignment and focus\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-06-k1","title":"晶圓彎曲／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wafer bow / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：局部彎曲也影響對準與聚焦。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Local bow affects alignment and focus."},{"id":"a072-v8-06-k2","title":"晶圓彎曲／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wafer bow / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力」與「補償平均曲率不能保證局部應力消失」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling every layer stress-free after flattening\" is not equivalent to \"Compensating mean curvature does not remove all local stress\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶圓彎曲」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Wafer bow?","options":["晶圓外觀變平就宣稱每層無應力","所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述","局部彎曲也影響對準與聚焦"],"optionsEn":["Calling every layer stress-free after flattening","Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone","Local bow affects alignment and focus"],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部彎曲也影響對準與聚焦；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Local bow affects alignment and focus. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a072-stage02","order":2,"title":"深孔輪廓 → 閘極取代","titleEn":"Deep-hole profile to Replacement gates","description":"把「深孔輪廓」「階梯接點」「閘極取代」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Deep-hole profile, Staircase contacts, Replacement gates.","steps":[{"id":"a072-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-06"],"title":"深孔輪廓：建立模型","titleEn":"Deep-hole profile: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures.","instruction":"比較理想、彎曲與扭轉孔剖面，標出頂中底 CD。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare ideal, bowed and twisted hole sections with top/middle/bottom CD. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常；孔底材料殘留可造成整串中斷。","observationEn":"High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures; Bottom residue can interrupt an entire string.","failure":"若採用「所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「深孔輪廓」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常。","checkEn":"Submit the Deep-hole profile diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-07-k1","title":"深孔輪廓／物理與模型","titleEn":"Deep-hole profile / Physics and model","text":"機制：高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常。","textEn":"Mechanism: High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures."},{"id":"a072-v8-07-k2","title":"深孔輪廓／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Deep-hole profile / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「深孔輪廓」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Deep-hole profile, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常","所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述","認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度"],"optionsEn":["High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures","Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone","Assuming more layers add no connection complexity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-07"],"title":"深孔輪廓：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Deep-hole profile: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「深孔輪廓」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：孔底材料殘留可造成整串中斷。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Deep-hole profile artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bottom residue can interrupt an entire string. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常；孔底材料殘留可造成整串中斷。","observationEn":"High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures; Bottom residue can interrupt an entire string.","failure":"若採用「所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「深孔輪廓」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「孔底材料殘留可造成整串中斷」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Deep-hole profile, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bottom residue can interrupt an entire string\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-08-k1","title":"深孔輪廓／物理與模型","titleEn":"Deep-hole profile / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：孔底材料殘留可造成整串中斷。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bottom residue can interrupt an entire string."},{"id":"a072-v8-08-k2","title":"深孔輪廓／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Deep-hole profile / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述」與「高深寬比蝕刻可能出現多種形貌異常」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone\" is not equivalent to \"High-aspect-ratio etching can produce different profile failures\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「深孔輪廓」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Deep-hole profile?","options":["認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度","孔底材料殘留可造成整串中斷","所有深孔異常只用深度一項描述"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more layers add no connection complexity","Bottom residue can interrupt an entire string","Describing all deep-hole failures by depth alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔底材料殘留可造成整串中斷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bottom residue can interrupt an entire string. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-08"],"title":"階梯接點：建立模型","titleEn":"Staircase contacts: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections.","instruction":"畫每層字線露出的階梯與接點，檢查是否唯一連到目標層。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw exposed staircase wordlines and verify unique contacts to target layers. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口；階梯版圖也占用晶片面積。","observationEn":"Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections; Staircases consume die area.","failure":"若採用「認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more layers add no connection complexity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「階梯接點」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口。","checkEn":"Submit the Staircase contacts diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-09-k1","title":"階梯接點／物理與模型","titleEn":"Staircase contacts / Physics and model","text":"機制：垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口。","textEn":"Mechanism: Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections."},{"id":"a072-v8-09-k2","title":"階梯接點／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Staircase contacts / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more layers add no connection complexity."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「階梯接點」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Staircase contacts, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度","移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層","垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more layers add no connection complexity","Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers","Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections"],"answer":2,"explanation":"垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-09"],"title":"階梯接點：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Staircase contacts: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more layers add no connection complexity.","instruction":"接續前一步「階梯接點」成果，先指出錯誤主張「認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：階梯版圖也占用晶片面積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Staircase contacts artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more layers add no connection complexity\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Staircases consume die area. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口；階梯版圖也占用晶片面積。","observationEn":"Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections; Staircases consume die area.","failure":"若採用「認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more layers add no connection complexity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「階梯接點」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「階梯版圖也占用晶片面積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Staircase contacts, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Staircases consume die area\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-10-k1","title":"階梯接點／物理與模型","titleEn":"Staircase contacts / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：階梯版圖也占用晶片面積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Staircases consume die area."},{"id":"a072-v8-10-k2","title":"階梯接點／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Staircase contacts / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度」與「垂直層仍需可尋址的電性出口」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more layers add no connection complexity\" is not equivalent to \"Vertical layers still need addressable electrical connections\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「階梯接點」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Staircase contacts?","options":["階梯版圖也占用晶片面積","認為只加堆疊便不需增加連接複雜度","移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層"],"optionsEn":["Staircases consume die area","Assuming more layers add no connection complexity","Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers"],"answer":0,"explanation":"階梯版圖也占用晶片面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Staircases consume die area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-10"],"title":"閘極取代：建立模型","titleEn":"Replacement gates: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity.","instruction":"紙上依序移除犧牲材料和填入導體，圈出需保留的絕緣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"On paper remove sacrificial material and add conductor while preserving required insulation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性；金屬填充空洞可能形成高電阻。","observationEn":"Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity; Metal-fill voids can produce high resistance.","failure":"若採用「移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閘極取代」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性。","checkEn":"Submit the Replacement gates diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-11-k1","title":"閘極取代／物理與模型","titleEn":"Replacement gates / Physics and model","text":"機制：選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity."},{"id":"a072-v8-11-k2","title":"閘極取代／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Replacement gates / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘極取代」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Replacement gates, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通","選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性","移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness","Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity","Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-11"],"title":"閘極取代：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Replacement gates: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers.","instruction":"接續前一步「閘極取代」成果，先指出錯誤主張「移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：金屬填充空洞可能形成高電阻。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Replacement gates artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Metal-fill voids can produce high resistance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性；金屬填充空洞可能形成高電阻。","observationEn":"Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity; Metal-fill voids can produce high resistance.","failure":"若採用「移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閘極取代」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「金屬填充空洞可能形成高電阻」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Replacement gates, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Metal-fill voids can produce high resistance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-12-k1","title":"閘極取代／物理與模型","titleEn":"Replacement gates / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：金屬填充空洞可能形成高電阻。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Metal-fill voids can produce high resistance."},{"id":"a072-v8-12-k2","title":"閘極取代／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Replacement gates / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層」與「選擇性移除和填充共同限制字線連續性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers\" is not equivalent to \"Selective removal and fill jointly limit wordline continuity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閘極取代」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Replacement gates?","options":["移除越徹底就一定不傷其餘層","只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通","金屬填充空洞可能形成高電阻"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more aggressive removal cannot damage other layers","Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness","Metal-fill voids can produce high resistance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"金屬填充空洞可能形成高電阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Metal-fill voids can produce high resistance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a072-stage03","order":3,"title":"通道連續 → 臨界電壓窗","titleEn":"Channel continuity to Threshold windows","description":"把「通道連續」「多堆疊接合」「臨界電壓窗」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Channel continuity, Multiple-deck junctions, Threshold windows.","steps":[{"id":"a072-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-12"],"title":"通道連續：建立模型","titleEn":"Channel continuity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path.","instruction":"畫通道膜沿深孔側壁的接續並辨識底部與接合區缺口。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Trace channel film down a hole and identify bottom/junction gaps. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑；通道晶界可能影響傳輸變異。","observationEn":"Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path; Channel grain boundaries can affect transport variability.","failure":"若採用「只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「通道連續」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑。","checkEn":"Submit the Channel continuity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-13-k1","title":"通道連續／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel continuity / Physics and model","text":"機制：垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑。","textEn":"Mechanism: Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path."},{"id":"a072-v8-13-k2","title":"通道連續／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel continuity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通道連續」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Channel continuity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑","只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通","兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面"],"optionsEn":["Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path","Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness","Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces"],"answer":0,"explanation":"垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-13"],"title":"通道連續：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Channel continuity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness.","instruction":"接續前一步「通道連續」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：通道晶界可能影響傳輸變異。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Channel continuity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Channel grain boundaries can affect transport variability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑；通道晶界可能影響傳輸變異。","observationEn":"Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path; Channel grain boundaries can affect transport variability.","failure":"若採用「只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「通道連續」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「通道晶界可能影響傳輸變異」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Channel continuity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Channel grain boundaries can affect transport variability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-14-k1","title":"通道連續／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel continuity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：通道晶界可能影響傳輸變異。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Channel grain boundaries can affect transport variability."},{"id":"a072-v8-14-k2","title":"通道連續／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel continuity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通」與「垂直導通需要整段連續的通道路徑」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness\" is not equivalent to \"Vertical conduction requires a continuous channel path\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「通道連續」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Channel continuity?","options":["兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面","通道晶界可能影響傳輸變異","只測頂部膜厚就保證整串導通"],"optionsEn":["Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces","Channel grain boundaries can affect transport variability","Guaranteeing string conduction from top thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"通道晶界可能影響傳輸變異；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Channel grain boundaries can affect transport variability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-14"],"title":"多堆疊接合：建立模型","titleEn":"Multiple-deck junctions: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error.","instruction":"畫上下兩疊孔的偏移與縮頸，追蹤最窄通道位置。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw offset and necking between two decks and locate the narrowest passage. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差；接合處局部場可能不同於層內。","observationEn":"Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error; Junction fields can differ from in-deck fields.","failure":"若採用「兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「多堆疊接合」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差。","checkEn":"Submit the Multiple-deck junctions diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-15-k1","title":"多堆疊接合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multiple-deck junctions / Physics and model","text":"機制：分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差。","textEn":"Mechanism: Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error."},{"id":"a072-v8-15-k2","title":"多堆疊接合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multiple-deck junctions / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多堆疊接合」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Multiple-deck junctions, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面","位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變","分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差"],"optionsEn":["Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces","Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin","Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error"],"answer":2,"explanation":"分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-15"],"title":"多堆疊接合：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Multiple-deck junctions: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces.","instruction":"接續前一步「多堆疊接合」成果，先指出錯誤主張「兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接合處局部場可能不同於層內。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Multiple-deck junctions artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Junction fields can differ from in-deck fields. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差；接合處局部場可能不同於層內。","observationEn":"Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error; Junction fields can differ from in-deck fields.","failure":"若採用「兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「多堆疊接合」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接合處局部場可能不同於層內」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Multiple-deck junctions, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Junction fields can differ from in-deck fields\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-16-k1","title":"多堆疊接合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multiple-deck junctions / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接合處局部場可能不同於層內。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Junction fields can differ from in-deck fields."},{"id":"a072-v8-16-k2","title":"多堆疊接合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multiple-deck junctions / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面」與「分段堆疊降低單次深度但新增接合誤差」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces\" is not equivalent to \"Deck splitting lowers per-etch depth but adds junction error\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「多堆疊接合」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Multiple-deck junctions?","options":["接合處局部場可能不同於層內","兩疊技術只增加層數而沒有新介面","位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變"],"optionsEn":["Junction fields can differ from in-deck fields","Assuming two decks add layers without new interfaces","Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接合處局部場可能不同於層內；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Junction fields can differ from in-deck fields. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-16"],"title":"臨界電壓窗：建立模型","titleEn":"Threshold windows: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: More states reduce the margin allocated to each state.","instruction":"畫多位元單元的假設電壓分布與讀取門檻，檢查重疊。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw hypothetical multi-bit threshold distributions and read thresholds and inspect overlap. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量；讀取門檻需考慮老化後分布。","observationEn":"More states reduce the margin allocated to each state; Read thresholds need aged distributions.","failure":"若採用「位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「臨界電壓窗」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量。","checkEn":"Submit the Threshold windows diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: More states reduce the margin allocated to each state.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-17-k1","title":"臨界電壓窗／物理與模型","titleEn":"Threshold windows / Physics and model","text":"機制：多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量。","textEn":"Mechanism: More states reduce the margin allocated to each state."},{"id":"a072-v8-17-k2","title":"臨界電壓窗／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Threshold windows / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「臨界電壓窗」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Threshold windows, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["未選中就完全不受讀寫影響","多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量","位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變"],"optionsEn":["Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes","More states reduce the margin allocated to each state","Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"More states reduce the margin allocated to each state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-17"],"title":"臨界電壓窗：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Threshold windows: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin.","instruction":"接續前一步「臨界電壓窗」成果，先指出錯誤主張「位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：讀取門檻需考慮老化後分布。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Threshold windows artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Read thresholds need aged distributions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量；讀取門檻需考慮老化後分布。","observationEn":"More states reduce the margin allocated to each state; Read thresholds need aged distributions.","failure":"若採用「位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「臨界電壓窗」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「讀取門檻需考慮老化後分布」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Threshold windows, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Read thresholds need aged distributions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-18-k1","title":"臨界電壓窗／物理與模型","titleEn":"Threshold windows / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：讀取門檻需考慮老化後分布。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Read thresholds need aged distributions."},{"id":"a072-v8-18-k2","title":"臨界電壓窗／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Threshold windows / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變」與「多狀態儲存壓縮單一狀態的容許裕量」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin\" is not equivalent to \"More states reduce the margin allocated to each state\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「臨界電壓窗」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Threshold windows?","options":["位元數增加而每個狀態裕量保持不變","未選中就完全不受讀寫影響","讀取門檻需考慮老化後分布"],"optionsEn":["Increasing bits while assuming unchanged per-state margin","Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes","Read thresholds need aged distributions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"讀取門檻需考慮老化後分布；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Read thresholds need aged distributions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a072-stage04","order":4,"title":"擾動路徑 → 良率地圖","titleEn":"Disturb pathways to Yield map","description":"把「擾動路徑」「陣列與周邊」「良率地圖」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Disturb pathways, Array and periphery, Yield map.","steps":[{"id":"a072-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-18"],"title":"擾動路徑：建立模型","titleEn":"Disturb pathways: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Unselected cells can still experience electric fields.","instruction":"分開選定字線、通過字線與鄰近字線的偏壓角色。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate selected, pass and neighboring wordline bias roles. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場；通過偏壓可能累積讀取擾動。","observationEn":"Unselected cells can still experience electric fields; Pass bias can accumulate read disturb.","failure":"若採用「未選中就完全不受讀寫影響」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「擾動路徑」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場。","checkEn":"Submit the Disturb pathways diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Unselected cells can still experience electric fields.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-19-k1","title":"擾動路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Disturb pathways / Physics and model","text":"機制：未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場。","textEn":"Mechanism: Unselected cells can still experience electric fields."},{"id":"a072-v8-19-k2","title":"擾動路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Disturb pathways / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「未選中就完全不受讀寫影響」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「擾動路徑」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Disturb pathways, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場","未選中就完全不受讀寫影響","所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置"],"optionsEn":["Unselected cells can still experience electric fields","Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes","Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND"],"answer":0,"explanation":"未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Unselected cells can still experience electric fields. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-19"],"title":"擾動路徑：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Disturb pathways: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「未選中就完全不受讀寫影響」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes.","instruction":"接續前一步「擾動路徑」成果，先指出錯誤主張「未選中就完全不受讀寫影響」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：通過偏壓可能累積讀取擾動。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Disturb pathways artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pass bias can accumulate read disturb. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場；通過偏壓可能累積讀取擾動。","observationEn":"Unselected cells can still experience electric fields; Pass bias can accumulate read disturb.","failure":"若採用「未選中就完全不受讀寫影響」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「擾動路徑」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「通過偏壓可能累積讀取擾動」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Disturb pathways, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pass bias can accumulate read disturb\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-20-k1","title":"擾動路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Disturb pathways / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：通過偏壓可能累積讀取擾動。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pass bias can accumulate read disturb."},{"id":"a072-v8-20-k2","title":"擾動路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Disturb pathways / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「未選中就完全不受讀寫影響」與「未被選中的單元仍可能承受電場」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes\" is not equivalent to \"Unselected cells can still experience electric fields\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「擾動路徑」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Disturb pathways?","options":["所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置","通過偏壓可能累積讀取擾動","未選中就完全不受讀寫影響"],"optionsEn":["Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND","Pass bias can accumulate read disturb","Assuming unselected means unaffected by reads/writes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"通過偏壓可能累積讀取擾動；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pass bias can accumulate read disturb. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-20"],"title":"陣列與周邊：建立模型","titleEn":"Array and periphery: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects.","instruction":"比較陣列下 CMOS 與分層接合架構，畫訊號與熱預算依賴。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare CMOS-under-array and bonded tiers with signal and thermal dependencies. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連；周邊熱預算會限制陣列加工順序。","observationEn":"Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects; Peripheral thermal budgets constrain array sequencing.","failure":"若採用「所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「陣列與周邊」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連。","checkEn":"Submit the Array and periphery diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-21-k1","title":"陣列與周邊／物理與模型","titleEn":"Array and periphery / Physics and model","text":"機制：周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連。","textEn":"Mechanism: Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects."},{"id":"a072-v8-21-k2","title":"陣列與周邊／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Array and periphery / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「陣列與周邊」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Array and periphery, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置","只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標","周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連"],"optionsEn":["Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND","Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die","Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects"],"answer":2,"explanation":"周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-21"],"title":"陣列與周邊：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Array and periphery: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND.","instruction":"接續前一步「陣列與周邊」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：周邊熱預算會限制陣列加工順序。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Array and periphery artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Peripheral thermal budgets constrain array sequencing. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連；周邊熱預算會限制陣列加工順序。","observationEn":"Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects; Peripheral thermal budgets constrain array sequencing.","failure":"若採用「所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「陣列與周邊」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「周邊熱預算會限制陣列加工順序」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Array and periphery, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Peripheral thermal budgets constrain array sequencing\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-22-k1","title":"陣列與周邊／物理與模型","titleEn":"Array and periphery / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：周邊熱預算會限制陣列加工順序。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Peripheral thermal budgets constrain array sequencing."},{"id":"a072-v8-22-k2","title":"陣列與周邊／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Array and periphery / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置」與「周邊電路位置影響整合順序及互連」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND\" is not equivalent to \"Peripheral placement affects process order and interconnects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「陣列與周邊」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Array and periphery?","options":["周邊熱預算會限制陣列加工順序","所有 3D NAND 都有相同周邊配置","只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標"],"optionsEn":["Peripheral thermal budgets constrain array sequencing","Assuming identical periphery in every 3D NAND","Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die"],"answer":0,"explanation":"周邊熱預算會限制陣列加工順序；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Peripheral thermal budgets constrain array sequencing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-22"],"title":"良率地圖：建立模型","titleEn":"Yield map: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information.","instruction":"以層號與字串位置建立失效熱圖，分辨層相關與孔相關模式。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Build a failure map by layer and string location to separate layer and hole patterns. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊；層選擇失效和通道失效有不同圖樣。","observationEn":"A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information; Layer-select and channel faults have different patterns.","failure":"若採用「只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「良率地圖」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊。","checkEn":"Submit the Yield map diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-23-k1","title":"良率地圖／物理與模型","titleEn":"Yield map / Physics and model","text":"機制：單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊。","textEn":"Mechanism: A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information."},{"id":"a072-v8-23-k2","title":"良率地圖／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Yield map / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「良率地圖」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Yield map, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把 3D 層數當成單元位元數","單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊","只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標"],"optionsEn":["Equating stack layers with bits per cell","A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information","Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die"],"answer":1,"explanation":"單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a072-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand","v8-c-har","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a072-v8-23"],"title":"良率地圖：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Yield map: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die.","instruction":"接續前一步「良率地圖」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：層選擇失效和通道失效有不同圖樣。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Yield map artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Layer-select and channel faults have different patterns. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊；層選擇失效和通道失效有不同圖樣。","observationEn":"A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information; Layer-select and channel faults have different patterns.","failure":"若採用「只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「良率地圖」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「層選擇失效和通道失效有不同圖樣」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Yield map, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Layer-select and channel faults have different patterns\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a072-v8-24-k1","title":"良率地圖／物理與模型","titleEn":"Yield map / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：層選擇失效和通道失效有不同圖樣。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Layer-select and channel faults have different patterns."},{"id":"a072-v8-24-k2","title":"良率地圖／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Yield map / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標」與「單一晶圓二維圖可能隱藏深度資訊」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die\" is not equivalent to \"A two-dimensional wafer map can hide depth information\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「良率地圖」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Yield map?","options":["只保留每顆晶片一個合格旗標","把 3D 層數當成單元位元數","層選擇失效和通道失效有不同圖樣"],"optionsEn":["Retaining only one pass/fail flag per die","Equating stack layers with bits per cell","Layer-select and channel faults have different patterns"],"answer":2,"explanation":"層選擇失效和通道失效有不同圖樣；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Layer-select and channel faults have different patterns. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"},{"id":"a073","title":"電荷捕捉記憶體閘極工程","titleEn":"Charge-trap memory gate engineering","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從電荷儲存層、能階深度到記憶窗驗收：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Charge-storage layer and Trap depth to Memory-window acceptance: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["電荷儲存層","捕捉位置","阻擋層","循環損傷"],"labelsEn":["Charge-storage layer","Trap location","Blocking layer","Cycling damage"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a073-stage01","order":1,"title":"電荷儲存層 → 注入與釋放","titleEn":"Charge-storage layer to Injection and release","description":"把「電荷儲存層」「閘極耦合」「注入與釋放」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Charge-storage layer, Gate coupling, Injection and release.","steps":[{"id":"a073-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"電荷儲存層：建立模型","titleEn":"Charge-storage layer: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates.","instruction":"畫通道、穿隧層、捕捉層、阻擋層及閘極，標示電荷位置。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw channel, tunnel, trap, blocking layers and gate with charge locations. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同；局域捕捉電荷可具有不同能階。","observationEn":"Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates; Localized trapped charges occupy different energies.","failure":"若採用「把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電荷儲存層」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Charge-storage layer diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-01-k1","title":"電荷儲存層／物理與模型","titleEn":"Charge-storage layer / Physics and model","text":"機制：電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates."},{"id":"a073-v8-01-k2","title":"電荷儲存層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Charge-storage layer / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電荷儲存層」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Charge-storage layer, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同","把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘","以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場"],"optionsEn":["Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates","Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate","Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-01"],"title":"電荷儲存層：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Charge-storage layer: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate.","instruction":"接續前一步「電荷儲存層」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：局域捕捉電荷可具有不同能階。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Charge-storage layer artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Localized trapped charges occupy different energies. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同；局域捕捉電荷可具有不同能階。","observationEn":"Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates; Localized trapped charges occupy different energies.","failure":"若採用「把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電荷儲存層」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「局域捕捉電荷可具有不同能階」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Charge-storage layer, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Localized trapped charges occupy different energies\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-02-k1","title":"電荷儲存層／物理與模型","titleEn":"Charge-storage layer / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：局域捕捉電荷可具有不同能階。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Localized trapped charges occupy different energies."},{"id":"a073-v8-02-k2","title":"電荷儲存層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Charge-storage layer / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘」與「電荷捕捉層和導電浮閘的儲存方式不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate\" is not equivalent to \"Charge-trap layers store charge differently from conductive floating gates\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電荷儲存層」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Charge-storage layer?","options":["以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場","局域捕捉電荷可具有不同能階","把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘"],"optionsEn":["Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division","Localized trapped charges occupy different energies","Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局域捕捉電荷可具有不同能階；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Localized trapped charges occupy different energies. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-02"],"title":"閘極耦合：建立模型","titleEn":"Gate coupling: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer.","instruction":"以串聯電容圖分配各層電壓，標註面積與介電常數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設兩層介質的面積電容相等、串聯且沒有固定或捕獲電荷，總壓降 4 V 時各分得 2 V。若其中穿隧層厚 5 nm，其平均場為 2 V/5 nm=4 MV/cm。加入捕獲電荷後原分壓模型需重算；這不是寫入電壓建議，也未計算穿隧率。","instructionEn":"Use a series-capacitor diagram to divide voltage across layers with area and permittivity. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume two dielectric layers have equal areal capacitance in series with no fixed or trapped charge. A total 4 V divides into 2 V per layer. If the tunnel layer is 5 nm thick, its average field is 2 V/5 nm=4 MV/cm. Trapped charge requires recalculating voltage division. This is not a programming-voltage recommendation and does not calculate tunneling rate.","observation":"外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層；介面電荷也會改變分壓。","observationEn":"Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer; Interface charge also changes voltage division.","failure":"若採用「以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閘極耦合」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層。\n算例驗收：驗算 2 V 與 4 MV/cm，指出等分壓依賴等電容而非只看等厚度。","checkEn":"Submit the Gate coupling diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 2 V and 4 MV/cm; explain that equal division requires equal capacitance, not merely equal thickness.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-03-k1","title":"閘極耦合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate coupling / Physics and model","text":"機制：外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層。","textEn":"Mechanism: Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer."},{"id":"a073-v8-03-k2","title":"閘極耦合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate coupling / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場」。\n假設數值與推算：假設兩層介質的面積電容相等、串聯且沒有固定或捕獲電荷，總壓降 4 V 時各分得 2 V。若其中穿隧層厚 5 nm，其平均場為 2 V/5 nm=4 MV/cm。加入捕獲電荷後原分壓模型需重算；這不是寫入電壓建議，也未計算穿隧率。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume two dielectric layers have equal areal capacitance in series with no fixed or trapped charge. A total 4 V divides into 2 V per layer. If the tunnel layer is 5 nm thick, its average field is 2 V/5 nm=4 MV/cm. Trapped charge requires recalculating voltage division. This is not a programming-voltage recommendation and does not calculate tunneling rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘極耦合」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Gate coupling, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場","只改文字標籤不改電場方向","外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層"],"optionsEn":["Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division","Changing labels without changing field direction","Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer"],"answer":2,"explanation":"外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-03"],"title":"閘極耦合：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Gate coupling: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division.","instruction":"接續前一步「閘極耦合」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：介面電荷也會改變分壓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Gate coupling artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Interface charge also changes voltage division. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層；介面電荷也會改變分壓。","observationEn":"Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer; Interface charge also changes voltage division.","failure":"若採用「以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閘極耦合」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「介面電荷也會改變分壓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Gate coupling, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Interface charge also changes voltage division\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-04-k1","title":"閘極耦合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate coupling / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：介面電荷也會改變分壓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Interface charge also changes voltage division."},{"id":"a073-v8-04-k2","title":"閘極耦合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate coupling / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場」與「外加閘壓不全部降在穿隧層」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division\" is not equivalent to \"Not all gate voltage falls across the tunnel layer\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閘極耦合」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Gate coupling?","options":["介面電荷也會改變分壓","以總閘壓除穿隧層厚度直接算電場","只改文字標籤不改電場方向"],"optionsEn":["Interface charge also changes voltage division","Dividing total gate voltage by tunnel thickness without voltage division","Changing labels without changing field direction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面電荷也會改變分壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Interface charge also changes voltage division. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-04"],"title":"注入與釋放：建立模型","titleEn":"Injection and release: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Program and erase must be tied to band conditions.","instruction":"畫編程和抹除時的載子方向，保留能障與極性定義。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch carrier direction during program/erase with barrier and polarity conventions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件；穿隧機率對能障高度很敏感。","observationEn":"Program and erase must be tied to band conditions; Tunneling depends strongly on barrier height.","failure":"若採用「只改文字標籤不改電場方向」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Changing labels without changing field direction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「注入與釋放」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件。","checkEn":"Submit the Injection and release diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Program and erase must be tied to band conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-05-k1","title":"注入與釋放／物理與模型","titleEn":"Injection and release / Physics and model","text":"機制：編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Program and erase must be tied to band conditions."},{"id":"a073-v8-05-k2","title":"注入與釋放／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Injection and release / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只改文字標籤不改電場方向」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Changing labels without changing field direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「注入與釋放」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Injection and release, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同","編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件","只改文字標籤不改電場方向"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt","Program and erase must be tied to band conditions","Changing labels without changing field direction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Program and erase must be tied to band conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-05"],"title":"注入與釋放：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Injection and release: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只改文字標籤不改電場方向」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Changing labels without changing field direction.","instruction":"接續前一步「注入與釋放」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只改文字標籤不改電場方向」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：穿隧機率對能障高度很敏感。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Injection and release artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Changing labels without changing field direction\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Tunneling depends strongly on barrier height. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件；穿隧機率對能障高度很敏感。","observationEn":"Program and erase must be tied to band conditions; Tunneling depends strongly on barrier height.","failure":"若採用「只改文字標籤不改電場方向」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Changing labels without changing field direction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「注入與釋放」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「穿隧機率對能障高度很敏感」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Injection and release, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Tunneling depends strongly on barrier height\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-06-k1","title":"注入與釋放／物理與模型","titleEn":"Injection and release / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：穿隧機率對能障高度很敏感。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Tunneling depends strongly on barrier height."},{"id":"a073-v8-06-k2","title":"注入與釋放／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Injection and release / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只改文字標籤不改電場方向」與「編程與抹除須連到實際能帶條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Changing labels without changing field direction\" is not equivalent to \"Program and erase must be tied to band conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「注入與釋放」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Injection and release?","options":["只改文字標籤不改電場方向","假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同","穿隧機率對能障高度很敏感"],"optionsEn":["Changing labels without changing field direction","Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt","Tunneling depends strongly on barrier height"],"answer":2,"explanation":"穿隧機率對能障高度很敏感；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Tunneling depends strongly on barrier height. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a073-stage02","order":2,"title":"捕捉位置 → 穿隧層厚度","titleEn":"Trap location to Tunnel thickness","description":"把「捕捉位置」「能階深度」「穿隧層厚度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Trap location, Trap depth, Tunnel thickness.","steps":[{"id":"a073-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-06"],"title":"捕捉位置：建立模型","titleEn":"Trap location: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Equal charge at different positions can couple differently.","instruction":"比較靠近通道與靠近閘極的捕捉電荷對臨界電壓影響。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare near-channel and near-gate trapped charge effects on threshold. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合；鄰近電極會改變電荷耦合係數。","observationEn":"Equal charge at different positions can couple differently; Nearby electrodes change charge coupling.","failure":"若採用「假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「捕捉位置」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合。","checkEn":"Submit the Trap location diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Equal charge at different positions can couple differently.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-07-k1","title":"捕捉位置／物理與模型","titleEn":"Trap location / Physics and model","text":"機制：同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合。","textEn":"Mechanism: Equal charge at different positions can couple differently."},{"id":"a073-v8-07-k2","title":"捕捉位置／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Trap location / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「捕捉位置」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Trap location, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合","假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同","只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端"],"optionsEn":["Equal charge at different positions can couple differently","Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt","Using one trap level for all retention tails"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Equal charge at different positions can couple differently. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-07"],"title":"捕捉位置：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Trap location: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt.","instruction":"接續前一步「捕捉位置」成果，先指出錯誤主張「假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：鄰近電極會改變電荷耦合係數。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Trap location artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Nearby electrodes change charge coupling. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合；鄰近電極會改變電荷耦合係數。","observationEn":"Equal charge at different positions can couple differently; Nearby electrodes change charge coupling.","failure":"若採用「假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「捕捉位置」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「鄰近電極會改變電荷耦合係數」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Trap location, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Nearby electrodes change charge coupling\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-08-k1","title":"捕捉位置／物理與模型","titleEn":"Trap location / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：鄰近電極會改變電荷耦合係數。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Nearby electrodes change charge coupling."},{"id":"a073-v8-08-k2","title":"捕捉位置／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Trap location / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同」與「同樣電荷量不同位置可能有不同耦合」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt\" is not equivalent to \"Equal charge at different positions can couple differently\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「捕捉位置」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Trap location?","options":["只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端","鄰近電極會改變電荷耦合係數","假定只要總電荷相同 ΔVt 必相同"],"optionsEn":["Using one trap level for all retention tails","Nearby electrodes change charge coupling","Assuming equal total charge always gives equal ΔVt"],"answer":1,"explanation":"鄰近電極會改變電荷耦合係數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Nearby electrodes change charge coupling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-08"],"title":"能階深度：建立模型","titleEn":"Trap depth: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Trap distributions affect time and temperature response.","instruction":"畫淺與深捕捉能階的釋放路徑，分開快速暫態與長期保持。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw release paths for shallow/deep traps and separate transients from retention. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應；不同釋放時間會造成非單指數衰減。","observationEn":"Trap distributions affect time and temperature response; Distributed times produce non-single-exponential decay.","failure":"若採用「只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one trap level for all retention tails\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「能階深度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應。","checkEn":"Submit the Trap depth diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Trap distributions affect time and temperature response.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-09-k1","title":"能階深度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Trap depth / Physics and model","text":"機制：捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Trap distributions affect time and temperature response."},{"id":"a073-v8-09-k2","title":"能階深度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Trap depth / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one trap level for all retention tails."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「能階深度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Trap depth, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端","穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好","捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應"],"optionsEn":["Using one trap level for all retention tails","Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric","Trap distributions affect time and temperature response"],"answer":2,"explanation":"捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Trap distributions affect time and temperature response. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-09"],"title":"能階深度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Trap depth: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one trap level for all retention tails.","instruction":"接續前一步「能階深度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：不同釋放時間會造成非單指數衰減。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Trap depth artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one trap level for all retention tails\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Distributed times produce non-single-exponential decay. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應；不同釋放時間會造成非單指數衰減。","observationEn":"Trap distributions affect time and temperature response; Distributed times produce non-single-exponential decay.","failure":"若採用「只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one trap level for all retention tails\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「能階深度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「不同釋放時間會造成非單指數衰減」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Trap depth, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Distributed times produce non-single-exponential decay\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-10-k1","title":"能階深度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Trap depth / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：不同釋放時間會造成非單指數衰減。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Distributed times produce non-single-exponential decay."},{"id":"a073-v8-10-k2","title":"能階深度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Trap depth / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端」與「捕捉態分布影響時間與溫度響應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one trap level for all retention tails\" is not equivalent to \"Trap distributions affect time and temperature response\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「能階深度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Trap depth?","options":["不同釋放時間會造成非單指數衰減","只用單一捕捉能階代表所有保持尾端","穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好"],"optionsEn":["Distributed times produce non-single-exponential decay","Using one trap level for all retention tails","Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同釋放時間會造成非單指數衰減；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Distributed times produce non-single-exponential decay. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-10"],"title":"穿隧層厚度：建立模型","titleEn":"Tunnel thickness: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands.","instruction":"比較薄層編程便利與保持障壁，列出待量測的兩項結果。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare programming access versus retention barrier and specify both measurements. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力；薄點可主導整片漏電。","observationEn":"Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands; Thin spots can dominate total leakage.","failure":"若採用「穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「穿隧層厚度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力。","checkEn":"Submit the Tunnel thickness diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-11-k1","title":"穿隧層厚度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Tunnel thickness / Physics and model","text":"機制：讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands."},{"id":"a073-v8-11-k2","title":"穿隧層厚度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Tunnel thickness / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「穿隧層厚度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Tunnel thickness, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變","讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力","穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好"],"optionsEn":["Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands","Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands","Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric"],"answer":1,"explanation":"讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-11"],"title":"穿隧層厚度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Tunnel thickness: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric.","instruction":"接續前一步「穿隧層厚度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：薄點可主導整片漏電。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Tunnel thickness artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thin spots can dominate total leakage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力；薄點可主導整片漏電。","observationEn":"Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands; Thin spots can dominate total leakage.","failure":"若採用「穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「穿隧層厚度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「薄點可主導整片漏電」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Tunnel thickness, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thin spots can dominate total leakage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-12-k1","title":"穿隧層厚度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Tunnel thickness / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：薄點可主導整片漏電。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thin spots can dominate total leakage."},{"id":"a073-v8-12-k2","title":"穿隧層厚度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Tunnel thickness / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好」與「讀寫速度與保持常有相反設計壓力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric\" is not equivalent to \"Write speed and retention often impose opposing demands\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「穿隧層厚度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Tunnel thickness?","options":["穿隧層越薄一定在所有指標更好","互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變","薄點可主導整片漏電"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a thinner tunnel layer improves every metric","Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands","Thin spots can dominate total leakage"],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄點可主導整片漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thin spots can dominate total leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a073-stage03","order":3,"title":"阻擋層 → 增量編程","titleEn":"Blocking layer to Incremental programming","description":"把「阻擋層」「橫向遷移」「增量編程」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Blocking layer, Lateral migration, Incremental programming.","steps":[{"id":"a073-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-12"],"title":"阻擋層：建立模型","titleEn":"Blocking layer: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer.","instruction":"畫往閘極的非預期漏電路徑，與通道注入路徑分色。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Distinguish unwanted gate-side leakage from channel injection. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層；閘極注入可和通道注入競爭。","observationEn":"The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer; Gate injection can compete with channel injection.","failure":"若採用「互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「阻擋層」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層。","checkEn":"Submit the Blocking layer diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-13-k1","title":"阻擋層／物理與模型","titleEn":"Blocking layer / Physics and model","text":"機制：阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層。","textEn":"Mechanism: The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer."},{"id":"a073-v8-13-k2","title":"阻擋層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Blocking layer / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「阻擋層」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Blocking layer, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層","互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變","只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合"],"optionsEn":["The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer","Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands","Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-13"],"title":"阻擋層：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Blocking layer: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands.","instruction":"接續前一步「阻擋層」成果，先指出錯誤主張「互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：閘極注入可和通道注入競爭。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Blocking layer artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Gate injection can compete with channel injection. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層；閘極注入可和通道注入競爭。","observationEn":"The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer; Gate injection can compete with channel injection.","failure":"若採用「互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「阻擋層」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「閘極注入可和通道注入競爭」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Blocking layer, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Gate injection can compete with channel injection\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-14-k1","title":"阻擋層／物理與模型","titleEn":"Blocking layer / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：閘極注入可和通道注入競爭。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Gate injection can compete with channel injection."},{"id":"a073-v8-14-k2","title":"阻擋層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Blocking layer / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變」與「阻擋層服務的界面不同於穿隧層」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands\" is not equivalent to \"The blocking layer serves a different interface from the tunnel layer\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「阻擋層」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Blocking layer?","options":["只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合","閘極注入可和通道注入競爭","互換兩層而假定能帶條件不變"],"optionsEn":["Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions","Gate injection can compete with channel injection","Swapping the layers while assuming unchanged bands"],"answer":1,"explanation":"閘極注入可和通道注入競爭；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Gate injection can compete with channel injection. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-14"],"title":"橫向遷移：建立模型","titleEn":"Lateral migration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport.","instruction":"畫相鄰單元沿連續捕捉層的電荷再分布，比較隔離假說。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw possible charge redistribution along a continuous trap layer and compare isolation hypotheses. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸；幾何不連續可能限制橫向傳輸。","observationEn":"Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport; Geometric discontinuities can limit lateral transport.","failure":"若採用「只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「橫向遷移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸。","checkEn":"Submit the Lateral migration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-15-k1","title":"橫向遷移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Lateral migration / Physics and model","text":"機制：局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸。","textEn":"Mechanism: Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport."},{"id":"a073-v8-15-k2","title":"橫向遷移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Lateral migration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橫向遷移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Lateral migration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合","單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異","局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸"],"optionsEn":["Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions","Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation","Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport"],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-15"],"title":"橫向遷移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral migration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions.","instruction":"接續前一步「橫向遷移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：幾何不連續可能限制橫向傳輸。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Lateral migration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Geometric discontinuities can limit lateral transport. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸；幾何不連續可能限制橫向傳輸。","observationEn":"Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport; Geometric discontinuities can limit lateral transport.","failure":"若採用「只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「橫向遷移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「幾何不連續可能限制橫向傳輸」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Lateral migration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Geometric discontinuities can limit lateral transport\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-16-k1","title":"橫向遷移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Lateral migration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：幾何不連續可能限制橫向傳輸。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Geometric discontinuities can limit lateral transport."},{"id":"a073-v8-16-k2","title":"橫向遷移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Lateral migration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合」與「局部儲存不代表完全沒有橫向傳輸」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions\" is not equivalent to \"Localized storage does not imply zero lateral transport\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「橫向遷移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Lateral migration?","options":["幾何不連續可能限制橫向傳輸","只要叫電荷捕捉便不存在鄰近耦合","單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異"],"optionsEn":["Geometric discontinuities can limit lateral transport","Assuming charge trapping eliminates all neighbor interactions","Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何不連續可能限制橫向傳輸；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Geometric discontinuities can limit lateral transport. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-16"],"title":"增量編程：建立模型","titleEn":"Incremental programming: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Verification feedback trades time for state control.","instruction":"對自訂目標窗模擬小步脈衝與驗證，計算過衝與迭代次數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Simulate small programming increments and verification for a hypothetical target window. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制；每次驗證也會消耗時間和讀取應力。","observationEn":"Verification feedback trades time for state control; Verification adds time and read stress.","failure":"若採用「單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「增量編程」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制。","checkEn":"Submit the Incremental programming diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Verification feedback trades time for state control.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-17-k1","title":"增量編程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Incremental programming / Physics and model","text":"機制：驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Verification feedback trades time for state control."},{"id":"a073-v8-17-k2","title":"增量編程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Incremental programming / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「增量編程」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Incremental programming, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["抹除能回復全部材料損傷","驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制","單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異"],"optionsEn":["Assuming erase reverses all material damage","Verification feedback trades time for state control","Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Verification feedback trades time for state control. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-17"],"title":"增量編程：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Incremental programming: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation.","instruction":"接續前一步「增量編程」成果，先指出錯誤主張「單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：每次驗證也會消耗時間和讀取應力。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Incremental programming artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Verification adds time and read stress. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制；每次驗證也會消耗時間和讀取應力。","observationEn":"Verification feedback trades time for state control; Verification adds time and read stress.","failure":"若採用「單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「增量編程」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「每次驗證也會消耗時間和讀取應力」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Incremental programming, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Verification adds time and read stress\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-18-k1","title":"增量編程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Incremental programming / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：每次驗證也會消耗時間和讀取應力。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Verification adds time and read stress."},{"id":"a073-v8-18-k2","title":"增量編程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Incremental programming / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異」與「驗證回授以時間成本換取狀態控制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation\" is not equivalent to \"Verification feedback trades time for state control\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「增量編程」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Incremental programming?","options":["單次固定脈衝可忽略單元差異","抹除能回復全部材料損傷","每次驗證也會消耗時間和讀取應力"],"optionsEn":["Assuming one fixed pulse eliminates cell variation","Assuming erase reverses all material damage","Verification adds time and read stress"],"answer":2,"explanation":"每次驗證也會消耗時間和讀取應力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Verification adds time and read stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a073-stage04","order":4,"title":"循環損傷 → 記憶窗驗收","titleEn":"Cycling damage to Memory-window acceptance","description":"把「循環損傷」「讀擾與保持」「記憶窗驗收」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Cycling damage, Read disturb and retention, Memory-window acceptance.","steps":[{"id":"a073-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-18"],"title":"循環損傷：建立模型","titleEn":"Cycling damage: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge.","instruction":"比較循環前後漏電與電壓窗，將新缺陷和原始捕捉態分開。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare leakage/windows before and after cycling, distinguishing generated defects. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷；循環後陷阱也可能提高讀擾敏感度。","observationEn":"Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge; Cycling can increase read-disturb sensitivity.","failure":"若採用「抹除能回復全部材料損傷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming erase reverses all material damage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「循環損傷」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷。","checkEn":"Submit the Cycling damage diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-19-k1","title":"循環損傷／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cycling damage / Physics and model","text":"機制：操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge."},{"id":"a073-v8-19-k2","title":"循環損傷／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cycling damage / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「抹除能回復全部材料損傷」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming erase reverses all material damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「循環損傷」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Cycling damage, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷","抹除能回復全部材料損傷","將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間"],"optionsEn":["Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge","Assuming erase reverses all material damage","Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time"],"answer":0,"explanation":"操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-19"],"title":"循環損傷：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Cycling damage: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「抹除能回復全部材料損傷」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming erase reverses all material damage.","instruction":"接續前一步「循環損傷」成果，先指出錯誤主張「抹除能回復全部材料損傷」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：循環後陷阱也可能提高讀擾敏感度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Cycling damage artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming erase reverses all material damage\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cycling can increase read-disturb sensitivity. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷；循環後陷阱也可能提高讀擾敏感度。","observationEn":"Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge; Cycling can increase read-disturb sensitivity.","failure":"若採用「抹除能回復全部材料損傷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming erase reverses all material damage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「循環損傷」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「循環後陷阱也可能提高讀擾敏感度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Cycling damage, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cycling can increase read-disturb sensitivity\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-20-k1","title":"循環損傷／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cycling damage / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：循環後陷阱也可能提高讀擾敏感度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cycling can increase read-disturb sensitivity."},{"id":"a073-v8-20-k2","title":"循環損傷／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cycling damage / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「抹除能回復全部材料損傷」與「操作累積可能改變介電層而非只改儲存電荷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming erase reverses all material damage\" is not equivalent to \"Cycling can alter the dielectric, not only stored charge\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「循環損傷」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Cycling damage?","options":["將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間","循環後陷阱也可能提高讀擾敏感度","抹除能回復全部材料損傷"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time","Cycling can increase read-disturb sensitivity","Assuming erase reverses all material damage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"循環後陷阱也可能提高讀擾敏感度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cycling can increase read-disturb sensitivity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-20"],"title":"讀擾與保持：建立模型","titleEn":"Read disturb and retention: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Time aging and read disturbance require different controls.","instruction":"設計相同等待時間但不同讀次數的對照，隔離讀擾。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare equal waiting times with different read counts to isolate read disturb. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照；比較組要使用相同溫度歷史。","observationEn":"Time aging and read disturbance require different controls; Controls need matching thermal histories.","failure":"若採用「將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「讀擾與保持」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照。","checkEn":"Submit the Read disturb and retention diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Time aging and read disturbance require different controls.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-21-k1","title":"讀擾與保持／物理與模型","titleEn":"Read disturb and retention / Physics and model","text":"機制：時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照。","textEn":"Mechanism: Time aging and read disturbance require different controls."},{"id":"a073-v8-21-k2","title":"讀擾與保持／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Read disturb and retention / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「讀擾與保持」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Read disturb and retention, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間","只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤","時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time","Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages","Time aging and read disturbance require different controls"],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Time aging and read disturbance require different controls. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-21"],"title":"讀擾與保持：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Read disturb and retention: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time.","instruction":"接續前一步「讀擾與保持」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：比較組要使用相同溫度歷史。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Read disturb and retention artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Controls need matching thermal histories. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照；比較組要使用相同溫度歷史。","observationEn":"Time aging and read disturbance require different controls; Controls need matching thermal histories.","failure":"若採用「將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「讀擾與保持」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「比較組要使用相同溫度歷史」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Read disturb and retention, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Controls need matching thermal histories\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-22-k1","title":"讀擾與保持／物理與模型","titleEn":"Read disturb and retention / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：比較組要使用相同溫度歷史。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Controls need matching thermal histories."},{"id":"a073-v8-22-k2","title":"讀擾與保持／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Read disturb and retention / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間」與「時間老化與讀取擾動需要不同對照」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time\" is not equivalent to \"Time aging and read disturbance require different controls\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「讀擾與保持」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Read disturb and retention?","options":["比較組要使用相同溫度歷史","將所有 ΔVt 漂移歸因於等待時間","只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤"],"optionsEn":["Controls need matching thermal histories","Attributing every threshold shift to elapsed time","Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較組要使用相同溫度歷史；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Controls need matching thermal histories. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-22"],"title":"記憶窗驗收：建立模型","titleEn":"Memory-window acceptance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin.","instruction":"以初始、循環後及保持後三組分布設定有證據的讀取裕量。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Set evidence-based read margins using initial, cycled and retained distributions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量；錯誤更正能力不能取代元件量測。","observationEn":"Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin; Error correction does not replace device measurements.","failure":"若採用「只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「記憶窗驗收」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量。","checkEn":"Submit the Memory-window acceptance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-23-k1","title":"記憶窗驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Memory-window acceptance / Physics and model","text":"機制：平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量。","textEn":"Mechanism: Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin."},{"id":"a073-v8-23-k2","title":"記憶窗驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Memory-window acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「記憶窗驗收」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Memory-window acceptance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘","平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量","只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤"],"optionsEn":["Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate","Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin","Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a073-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-nand","v8-c-td-stat"],"prerequisiteIds":["a073-v8-23"],"title":"記憶窗驗收：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Memory-window acceptance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages.","instruction":"接續前一步「記憶窗驗收」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：錯誤更正能力不能取代元件量測。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Memory-window acceptance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Error correction does not replace device measurements. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量；錯誤更正能力不能取代元件量測。","observationEn":"Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin; Error correction does not replace device measurements.","failure":"若採用「只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「記憶窗驗收」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「錯誤更正能力不能取代元件量測」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Memory-window acceptance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Error correction does not replace device measurements\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a073-v8-24-k1","title":"記憶窗驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Memory-window acceptance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：錯誤更正能力不能取代元件量測。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Error correction does not replace device measurements."},{"id":"a073-v8-24-k2","title":"記憶窗驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Memory-window acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤」與「平均記憶窗不能代表最弱單元裕量」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages\" is not equivalent to \"Mean window does not represent weakest-cell margin\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「記憶窗驗收」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Memory-window acceptance?","options":["只用兩個平均電壓差證明零錯誤","把捕捉層畫成等電位金屬浮閘","錯誤更正能力不能取代元件量測"],"optionsEn":["Claiming zero errors from two mean voltages","Drawing a trap layer as an equipotential metallic floating gate","Error correction does not replace device measurements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"錯誤更正能力不能取代元件量測；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Error correction does not replace device measurements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"},{"id":"a074","title":"相變化記憶體製作","titleEn":"Phase-change memory fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從相態與電阻、脈衝能量到陣列耐久度：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Phase and resistance and Pulse energy to Array endurance: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["相態與電阻","熱阻網路","受限相變體積","選擇器與偷流"],"labelsEn":["Phase and resistance","Thermal network","Confined active volume","Selector and sneak paths"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a074-stage01","order":1,"title":"相態與電阻 → 加熱器幾何","titleEn":"Phase and resistance to Heater geometry","description":"把「相態與電阻」「SET 與 RESET」「加熱器幾何」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Phase and resistance, SET and RESET, Heater geometry.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"相態與電阻：建立模型","titleEn":"Phase and resistance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture.","instruction":"畫晶態及非晶態原子示意，連結到兩組假設電阻分布。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch crystalline/amorphous arrangements and connect them to resistance distributions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路；電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。","observationEn":"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture; Read bias should avoid reheating the state.","failure":"若採用「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「相態與電阻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路。","checkEn":"Submit the Phase and resistance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-01-k1","title":"相態與電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Physics and model","text":"機制：電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路。","textEn":"Mechanism: Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture."},{"id":"a074-v8-01-k2","title":"相態與電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「相態與電阻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Phase and resistance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路","把高阻態都視為燒斷導線","只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態"],"optionsEn":["Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture","Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire","Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-01"],"title":"相態與電阻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Phase and resistance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire.","instruction":"接續前一步「相態與電阻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Phase and resistance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Read bias should avoid reheating the state. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路；電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。","observationEn":"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture; Read bias should avoid reheating the state.","failure":"若採用「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「相態與電阻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Phase and resistance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Read bias should avoid reheating the state\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-02-k1","title":"相態與電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Read bias should avoid reheating the state."},{"id":"a074-v8-02-k2","title":"相態與電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and resistance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把高阻態都視為燒斷導線」與「電阻對比來自材料狀態而非永久斷路」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire\" is not equivalent to \"Resistance contrast reflects material state, not necessarily permanent rupture\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「相態與電阻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Phase and resistance?","options":["只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態","電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態","把高阻態都視為燒斷導線"],"optionsEn":["Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone","Read bias should avoid reheating the state","Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電阻讀取應避免再次加熱改態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Read bias should avoid reheating the state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-02"],"title":"SET 與 RESET：建立模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase.","instruction":"畫結晶保溫與熔融後快冷的概念溫度時間曲線。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw conceptual crystallizing dwell and melt-quench temperature trajectories. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態；冷卻速率會影響非晶化。","observationEn":"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase; Cooling rate affects amorphization.","failure":"若採用「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「SET 與 RESET」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態。","checkEn":"Submit the SET and RESET diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-03-k1","title":"SET 與 RESET／物理與模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Physics and model","text":"機制：峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態。","textEn":"Mechanism: Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase."},{"id":"a074-v8-03-k2","title":"SET 與 RESET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「SET 與 RESET」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For SET and RESET, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態","只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量","峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態"],"optionsEn":["Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone","Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone","Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase"],"answer":2,"explanation":"峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-03"],"title":"SET 與 RESET：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"SET and RESET: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「SET 與 RESET」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：冷卻速率會影響非晶化。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding SET and RESET artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cooling rate affects amorphization. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態；冷卻速率會影響非晶化。","observationEn":"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase; Cooling rate affects amorphization.","failure":"若採用「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「SET 與 RESET」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「冷卻速率會影響非晶化」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for SET and RESET, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cooling rate affects amorphization\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-04-k1","title":"SET 與 RESET／物理與模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：冷卻速率會影響非晶化。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cooling rate affects amorphization."},{"id":"a074-v8-04-k2","title":"SET 與 RESET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態」與「峰值溫度與冷卻歷史共同決定相態」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone\" is not equivalent to \"Peak temperature and cooling history jointly determine phase\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「SET 與 RESET」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of SET and RESET?","options":["冷卻速率會影響非晶化","只比較最大脈衝幅度判斷最終相態","只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量"],"optionsEn":["Cooling rate affects amorphization","Judging final phase from maximum pulse amplitude alone","Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"冷卻速率會影響非晶化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cooling rate affects amorphization. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-04"],"title":"加熱器幾何：建立模型","titleEn":"Heater geometry: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「加熱效率與有效相變體積相關」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume.","instruction":"比較小接觸與大接觸的熱集中位置並標示電流路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare heat localization for small/large contacts and mark current paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"加熱效率與有效相變體積相關；接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。","observationEn":"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume; Contact resistance changes local heating.","failure":"若採用「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「加熱器幾何」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：加熱效率與有效相變體積相關。","checkEn":"Submit the Heater geometry diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-05-k1","title":"加熱器幾何／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Physics and model","text":"機制：加熱效率與有效相變體積相關。","textEn":"Mechanism: Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume."},{"id":"a074-v8-05-k2","title":"加熱器幾何／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「加熱器幾何」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Heater geometry, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易","加熱效率與有效相變體積相關","只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET","Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume","Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"加熱效率與有效相變體積相關；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-05"],"title":"加熱器幾何：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Heater geometry: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「加熱器幾何」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Heater geometry artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Contact resistance changes local heating. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"加熱效率與有效相變體積相關；接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。","observationEn":"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume; Contact resistance changes local heating.","failure":"若採用「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「加熱器幾何」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸電阻也影響局部發熱」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Heater geometry, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Contact resistance changes local heating\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-06-k1","title":"加熱器幾何／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸電阻也影響局部發熱。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Contact resistance changes local heating."},{"id":"a074-v8-06-k2","title":"加熱器幾何／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heater geometry / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量」與「加熱效率與有效相變體積相關」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone\" is not equivalent to \"Heating efficiency relates to active phase-change volume\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「加熱器幾何」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Heater geometry?","options":["只以整顆元件體積計算切換能量","熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易","接觸電阻也影響局部發熱"],"optionsEn":["Estimating switching energy from total device volume alone","Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET","Contact resistance changes local heating"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸電阻也影響局部發熱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance changes local heating. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a074-stage02","order":2,"title":"熱阻網路 → 材料組成","titleEn":"Thermal network to Material composition","description":"把「熱阻網路」「脈衝能量」「材料組成」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Thermal network, Pulse energy, Material composition.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-06"],"title":"熱阻網路：建立模型","titleEn":"Thermal network: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling.","instruction":"畫相變層到電極及基板的熱阻，計算假設穩態溫升。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw thermal paths to electrodes/substrate and estimate hypothetical steady rise. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻；多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。","observationEn":"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling; Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel.","failure":"若採用「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱阻網路」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻。","checkEn":"Submit the Thermal network diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-07-k1","title":"熱阻網路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal network / Physics and model","text":"機制：熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling."},{"id":"a074-v8-07-k2","title":"熱阻網路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal network / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱阻網路」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thermal network, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻","熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易","相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態"],"optionsEn":["Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling","Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET","Equating joules with identical material states"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-07"],"title":"熱阻網路：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal network: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱阻網路」成果，先指出錯誤主張「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thermal network artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻；多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。","observationEn":"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling; Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel.","failure":"若採用「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱阻網路」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「多條熱路徑需要並聯組合」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thermal network, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-08-k1","title":"熱阻網路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal network / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：多條熱路徑需要並聯組合。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel."},{"id":"a074-v8-08-k2","title":"熱阻網路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal network / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易」與「熱侷限有助加熱但也影響冷卻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET\" is not equivalent to \"Thermal confinement aids heating but also affects cooling\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱阻網路」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thermal network?","options":["相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態","多條熱路徑需要並聯組合","熱阻越高就保證 RESET 越容易"],"optionsEn":["Equating joules with identical material states","Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel","Assuming higher thermal resistance always simplifies RESET"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多條熱路徑需要並聯組合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multiple thermal paths combine in parallel. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-08"],"title":"脈衝能量：建立模型","titleEn":"Pulse energy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories.","instruction":"對假設 V(t)、I(t) 做能量積分，分辨峰值功率與總能量。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設在 PCM 元件端量到理想矩形脈衝，V=2 V、I=0.5 mA、持續 20 ns，電能 E=VIt=20 pJ。保持 V、I 不變而時間加倍，電能為 40 pJ。這不等於材料吸收熱量，亦不能證明 RESET；熱損失、脈衝邊緣及動態電阻另需量測。","instructionEn":"Integrate hypothetical V(t)I(t) and distinguish peak power from total energy. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume an ideal rectangular pulse measured at a PCM device: V=2 V, I=0.5 mA for 20 ns. Electrical energy E=VIt=20 pJ; doubling duration at fixed V and I gives 40 pJ. This is not absorbed material heat and does not prove RESET; thermal loss, pulse edges and dynamic resistance need separate evidence.","observation":"相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡；波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。","observationEn":"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories; Cable loss changes the actual die pulse.","failure":"若採用「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating joules with identical material states\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「脈衝能量」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡。\n算例驗收：以瓦特與秒核對 20 pJ，區分電能、溫度與相態三個不同量。","checkEn":"Submit the Pulse energy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories.\nWorked-example acceptance: Check 20 pJ using watts and seconds and distinguish electrical energy, temperature and phase.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-09-k1","title":"脈衝能量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Physics and model","text":"機制：相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡。","textEn":"Mechanism: Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories."},{"id":"a074-v8-09-k2","title":"脈衝能量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」。\n假設數值與推算：假設在 PCM 元件端量到理想矩形脈衝，V=2 V、I=0.5 mA、持續 20 ns，電能 E=VIt=20 pJ。保持 V、I 不變而時間加倍，電能為 40 pJ。這不等於材料吸收熱量，亦不能證明 RESET；熱損失、脈衝邊緣及動態電阻另需量測。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating joules with identical material states.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume an ideal rectangular pulse measured at a PCM device: V=2 V, I=0.5 mA for 20 ns. Electrical energy E=VIt=20 pJ; doubling duration at fixed V and I gives 40 pJ. This is not absorbed material heat and does not prove RESET; thermal loss, pulse edges and dynamic resistance need separate evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「脈衝能量」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pulse energy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態","只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持","相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡"],"optionsEn":["Equating joules with identical material states","Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention","Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories"],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-09"],"title":"脈衝能量：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pulse energy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating joules with identical material states.","instruction":"接續前一步「脈衝能量」成果，先指出錯誤主張「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pulse energy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating joules with identical material states\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cable loss changes the actual die pulse. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡；波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。","observationEn":"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories; Cable loss changes the actual die pulse.","failure":"若採用「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating joules with identical material states\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「脈衝能量」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pulse energy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cable loss changes the actual die pulse\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-10-k1","title":"脈衝能量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cable loss changes the actual die pulse."},{"id":"a074-v8-10-k2","title":"脈衝能量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pulse energy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態」與「相同能量不同時間形狀可形成不同溫度軌跡」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating joules with identical material states\" is not equivalent to \"Equal energies with different shapes can yield different thermal histories\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「脈衝能量」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pulse energy?","options":["波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝","相同焦耳數就必有相同材料狀態","只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持"],"optionsEn":["Cable loss changes the actual die pulse","Equating joules with identical material states","Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention"],"answer":0,"explanation":"波形線纜損失會改變晶片實際脈衝；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cable loss changes the actual die pulse. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-10"],"title":"材料組成：建立模型","titleEn":"Material composition: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Materials are constrained by switching and stability together.","instruction":"比較兩種假設組成的結晶速度、保持與漂移需求表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical compositions for crystallization speed, retention and drift. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束；材料偏析可能累積造成失效。","observationEn":"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together; Segregation can accumulate into failure.","failure":"若採用「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「材料組成」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束。","checkEn":"Submit the Material composition diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Materials are constrained by switching and stability together.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-11-k1","title":"材料組成／物理與模型","titleEn":"Material composition / Physics and model","text":"機制：材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束。","textEn":"Mechanism: Materials are constrained by switching and stability together."},{"id":"a074-v8-11-k2","title":"材料組成／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Material composition / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料組成」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Material composition, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔","材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束","只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持"],"optionsEn":["Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle","Materials are constrained by switching and stability together","Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-11"],"title":"材料組成：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Material composition: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention.","instruction":"接續前一步「材料組成」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：材料偏析可能累積造成失效。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Material composition artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Segregation can accumulate into failure. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束；材料偏析可能累積造成失效。","observationEn":"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together; Segregation can accumulate into failure.","failure":"若採用「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「材料組成」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「材料偏析可能累積造成失效」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Material composition, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Segregation can accumulate into failure\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-12-k1","title":"材料組成／物理與模型","titleEn":"Material composition / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：材料偏析可能累積造成失效。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Segregation can accumulate into failure."},{"id":"a074-v8-12-k2","title":"材料組成／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Material composition / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持」與「材料選擇同時受切換與穩定性約束」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention\" is not equivalent to \"Materials are constrained by switching and stability together\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「材料組成」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Material composition?","options":["只追求最快結晶而忽略非晶保持","把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔","材料偏析可能累積造成失效"],"optionsEn":["Optimizing crystallization speed while ignoring amorphous retention","Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle","Segregation can accumulate into failure"],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料偏析可能累積造成失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Segregation can accumulate into failure. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a074-stage03","order":3,"title":"受限相變體積 → 多位準","titleEn":"Confined active volume to Multilevel states","description":"把「受限相變體積」「電阻漂移」「多位準」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Confined active volume, Resistance drift, Multilevel states.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-12"],"title":"受限相變體積：建立模型","titleEn":"Confined active volume: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「外圍材料未必每次都完成相變」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Surrounding material need not transform each cycle.","instruction":"畫蘑菇型與受限結構的熱區，將有效區和外圍材料分色。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw mushroom/confined thermal regions and separate active from surrounding material. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"外圍材料未必每次都完成相變；有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。","observationEn":"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle; Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area.","failure":"若採用「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「受限相變體積」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：外圍材料未必每次都完成相變。","checkEn":"Submit the Confined active volume diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Surrounding material need not transform each cycle.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-13-k1","title":"受限相變體積／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Physics and model","text":"機制：外圍材料未必每次都完成相變。","textEn":"Mechanism: Surrounding material need not transform each cycle."},{"id":"a074-v8-13-k2","title":"受限相變體積／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「受限相變體積」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Confined active volume, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["外圍材料未必每次都完成相變","把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔","用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性"],"optionsEn":["Surrounding material need not transform each cycle","Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle","Comparing write consistency at different read delays"],"answer":0,"explanation":"外圍材料未必每次都完成相變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-13"],"title":"受限相變體積：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Confined active volume: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle.","instruction":"接續前一步「受限相變體積」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Confined active volume artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"外圍材料未必每次都完成相變；有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。","observationEn":"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle; Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area.","failure":"若採用「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「受限相變體積」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Confined active volume, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-14-k1","title":"受限相變體積／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area."},{"id":"a074-v8-14-k2","title":"受限相變體積／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confined active volume / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔」與「外圍材料未必每次都完成相變」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle\" is not equivalent to \"Surrounding material need not transform each cycle\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「受限相變體積」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Confined active volume?","options":["用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性","有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積","把全部沉積材料當成每次都重熔"],"optionsEn":["Comparing write consistency at different read delays","Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area","Assuming all deposited material remelts each cycle"],"answer":1,"explanation":"有效熱區可小於電極覆蓋面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Active thermal volume can be smaller than electrode area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-14"],"title":"電阻漂移：建立模型","titleEn":"Resistance drift: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states.","instruction":"用自訂 R=R0(t/t0)^ν 比較兩個 ν，標明模型及時間窗。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare two hypothetical drift exponents using R=R0(t/t0)^ν with a time window. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻；漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。","observationEn":"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states; Drift depends on temperature and initial state.","failure":"若採用「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電阻漂移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻。","checkEn":"Submit the Resistance drift diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-15-k1","title":"電阻漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Physics and model","text":"機制：讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states."},{"id":"a074-v8-15-k2","title":"電阻漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing write consistency at different read delays."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電阻漂移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Resistance drift, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性","初始分開就保證長期不重疊","讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻"],"optionsEn":["Comparing write consistency at different read delays","Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation","Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states"],"answer":2,"explanation":"讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-15"],"title":"電阻漂移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Resistance drift: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing write consistency at different read delays.","instruction":"接續前一步「電阻漂移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Resistance drift artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Drift depends on temperature and initial state. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻；漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。","observationEn":"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states; Drift depends on temperature and initial state.","failure":"若採用「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電阻漂移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Resistance drift, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Drift depends on temperature and initial state\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-16-k1","title":"電阻漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Drift depends on temperature and initial state."},{"id":"a074-v8-16-k2","title":"電阻漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resistance drift / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性」與「讀取時間不同會影響相同初態的電阻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing write consistency at different read delays\" is not equivalent to \"Read timing affects resistance even for identical initial states\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電阻漂移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Resistance drift?","options":["漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變","用不同延遲電阻比較寫入一致性","初始分開就保證長期不重疊"],"optionsEn":["Drift depends on temperature and initial state","Comparing write consistency at different read delays","Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"漂移參數依溫度和初始態而變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Drift depends on temperature and initial state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-16"],"title":"多位準：建立模型","titleEn":"Multilevel states: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability.","instruction":"畫部分結晶的三個假設電阻窗，加入漂移和讀取雜訊。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw three partial-crystallization windows including drift and read noise. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制；狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。","observationEn":"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability; Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis.","failure":"若採用「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「多位準」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制。","checkEn":"Submit the Multilevel states diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-17-k1","title":"多位準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Physics and model","text":"機制：可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability."},{"id":"a074-v8-17-k2","title":"多位準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多位準」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Multilevel states, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變","可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制","初始分開就保證長期不重疊"],"optionsEn":["Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change","Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability","Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-17"],"title":"多位準：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Multilevel states: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation.","instruction":"接續前一步「多位準」成果，先指出錯誤主張「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Multilevel states artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制；狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。","observationEn":"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability; Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis.","failure":"若採用「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「多位準」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Multilevel states, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-18-k1","title":"多位準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis."},{"id":"a074-v8-18-k2","title":"多位準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multilevel states / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「初始分開就保證長期不重疊」與「可分辨狀態數受漂移與變異共同限制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation\" is not equivalent to \"Distinguishable states are limited by drift and variability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「多位準」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Multilevel states?","options":["初始分開就保證長期不重疊","將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變","狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端"],"optionsEn":["Assuming initial separation guarantees permanent separation","Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change","Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis"],"answer":2,"explanation":"狀態間相鄰重疊需看分布尾端；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Neighbor-state overlap requires tail analysis. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a074-stage04","order":4,"title":"選擇器與偷流 → 陣列耐久度","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths to Array endurance","description":"把「選擇器與偷流」「過度編程」「陣列耐久度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Selector and sneak paths, Over-programming, Array endurance.","steps":[{"id":"a074-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-18"],"title":"選擇器與偷流：建立模型","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Selectors and storage material serve different roles.","instruction":"畫一個交叉點陣列，追蹤選中路徑與未選中旁路。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw a cross-point array and trace selected and sneak paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同；選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。","observationEn":"Selectors and storage material serve different roles; Selector voltage drop consumes write energy.","failure":"若採用「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「選擇器與偷流」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Selector and sneak paths diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Selectors and storage material serve different roles.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-19-k1","title":"選擇器與偷流／物理與模型","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Physics and model","text":"機制：選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Selectors and storage material serve different roles."},{"id":"a074-v8-19-k2","title":"選擇器與偷流／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「選擇器與偷流」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Selector and sneak paths, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同","將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變","高阻態越高就一定壽命越長"],"optionsEn":["Selectors and storage material serve different roles","Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change","Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life"],"answer":0,"explanation":"選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Selectors and storage material serve different roles. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-19"],"title":"選擇器與偷流：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change.","instruction":"接續前一步「選擇器與偷流」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Selector and sneak paths artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Selector voltage drop consumes write energy. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同；選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。","observationEn":"Selectors and storage material serve different roles; Selector voltage drop consumes write energy.","failure":"若採用「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「選擇器與偷流」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Selector and sneak paths, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Selector voltage drop consumes write energy\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-20-k1","title":"選擇器與偷流／物理與模型","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Selector voltage drop consumes write energy."},{"id":"a074-v8-20-k2","title":"選擇器與偷流／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Selector and sneak paths / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變」與「選擇器與記憶材料的職責不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change\" is not equivalent to \"Selectors and storage material serve different roles\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「選擇器與偷流」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Selector and sneak paths?","options":["高阻態越高就一定壽命越長","選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量","將 OTS 閾值切換直接等同 PCM 相變"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life","Selector voltage drop consumes write energy","Equating OTS threshold switching directly with PCM phase change"],"answer":1,"explanation":"選擇器導通壓降消耗部分寫入能量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Selector voltage drop consumes write energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-20"],"title":"過度編程：建立模型","titleEn":"Over-programming: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation.","instruction":"比較達標即停與過強 RESET 的假設循環圖，列出偏析證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare stop-on-target and excessive RESET cycling and specify segregation evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化；更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。","observationEn":"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation; Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy.","failure":"若採用「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「過度編程」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化。","checkEn":"Submit the Over-programming diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-21-k1","title":"過度編程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Over-programming / Physics and model","text":"機制：更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation."},{"id":"a074-v8-21-k2","title":"過度編程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Over-programming / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「過度編程」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Over-programming, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["高阻態越高就一定壽命越長","挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元","更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life","Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit","Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-21"],"title":"過度編程：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Over-programming: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life.","instruction":"接續前一步「過度編程」成果，先指出錯誤主張「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Over-programming artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化；更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。","observationEn":"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation; Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy.","failure":"若採用「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「過度編程」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「更短脈衝未必有較低總能量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Over-programming, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-22-k1","title":"過度編程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Over-programming / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：更短脈衝未必有較低總能量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy."},{"id":"a074-v8-22-k2","title":"過度編程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Over-programming / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「高阻態越高就一定壽命越長」與「更大寫入能量可能加速材料劣化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life\" is not equivalent to \"Greater write energy can accelerate material degradation\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「過度編程」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Over-programming?","options":["更短脈衝未必有較低總能量","高阻態越高就一定壽命越長","挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元"],"optionsEn":["Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy","Assuming higher RESET resistance guarantees longer life","Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"更短脈衝未必有較低總能量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shorter pulses need not have lower total energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-22"],"title":"陣列耐久度：建立模型","titleEn":"Array endurance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence.","instruction":"將平均值、早失效尾端和測試中未失效樣本同時報告。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Report means, early-failure tails and surviving array cells together. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同；耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。","observationEn":"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence; Endurance and retention need different test sequences.","failure":"若採用「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「陣列耐久度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Array endurance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-23-k1","title":"陣列耐久度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Array endurance / Physics and model","text":"機制：單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence."},{"id":"a074-v8-23-k2","title":"陣列耐久度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Array endurance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「陣列耐久度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Array endurance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把高阻態都視為燒斷導線","單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同","挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元"],"optionsEn":["Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire","Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence","Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a074-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pcm","v8-c-pcm-selector","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a074-v8-23"],"title":"陣列耐久度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Array endurance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit.","instruction":"接續前一步「陣列耐久度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Array endurance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Endurance and retention need different test sequences. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同；耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。","observationEn":"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence; Endurance and retention need different test sequences.","failure":"若採用「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「陣列耐久度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Array endurance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Endurance and retention need different test sequences\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a074-v8-24-k1","title":"陣列耐久度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Array endurance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Endurance and retention need different test sequences."},{"id":"a074-v8-24-k2","title":"陣列耐久度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Array endurance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元」與「單元展示和整陣列可靠度證據不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit\" is not equivalent to \"Single-cell demonstrations and array reliability are different evidence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「陣列耐久度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Array endurance?","options":["挑最佳單元的次數代表所有位元","把高阻態都視為燒斷導線","耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列"],"optionsEn":["Using the best cell's cycle count for every bit","Treating every high-resistance state as a burnt wire","Endurance and retention need different test sequences"],"answer":2,"explanation":"耐久與保持通常需不同測試序列；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Endurance and retention need different test sequences. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"},{"id":"a075","title":"磁阻式記憶體磁穿隧接面","titleEn":"MRAM magnetic tunnel junctions","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從MTJ 分層、STT 路徑到記憶體用途：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From MTJ stack and STT pathway to Memory application: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["MTJ 分層","熱穩定因子","障壁均勻度","寫錯機率"],"labelsEn":["MTJ stack","Thermal stability factor","Barrier uniformity","Write-error probability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a075-stage01","order":1,"title":"MTJ 分層 → 磁各向異性","titleEn":"MTJ stack to Magnetic anisotropy","description":"把「MTJ 分層」「TMR 定義」「磁各向異性」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for MTJ stack, TMR definition, Magnetic anisotropy.","steps":[{"id":"a075-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"MTJ 分層：建立模型","titleEn":"MTJ stack: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization.","instruction":"畫參考層、穿隧障壁及自由層，標出讀寫端點。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw reference layer, barrier and free layer with read/write terminals. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態；參考層穩定性也是讀值條件。","observationEn":"Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization; Reference-layer stability also conditions readout.","failure":"若採用「只標自由層方向而不定義參考層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「MTJ 分層」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態。","checkEn":"Submit the MTJ stack diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-01-k1","title":"MTJ 分層／物理與模型","titleEn":"MTJ stack / Physics and model","text":"機制：穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態。","textEn":"Mechanism: Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization."},{"id":"a075-v8-01-k2","title":"MTJ 分層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"MTJ stack / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只標自由層方向而不定義參考層」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「MTJ 分層」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For MTJ stack, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態","只標自由層方向而不定義參考層","不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比"],"optionsEn":["Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization","Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer","Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-01"],"title":"MTJ 分層：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"MTJ stack: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只標自由層方向而不定義參考層」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer.","instruction":"接續前一步「MTJ 分層」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只標自由層方向而不定義參考層」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：參考層穩定性也是讀值條件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding MTJ stack artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reference-layer stability also conditions readout. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態；參考層穩定性也是讀值條件。","observationEn":"Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization; Reference-layer stability also conditions readout.","failure":"若採用「只標自由層方向而不定義參考層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「MTJ 分層」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「參考層穩定性也是讀值條件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for MTJ stack, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reference-layer stability also conditions readout\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-02-k1","title":"MTJ 分層／物理與模型","titleEn":"MTJ stack / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：參考層穩定性也是讀值條件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reference-layer stability also conditions readout."},{"id":"a075-v8-02-k2","title":"MTJ 分層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"MTJ stack / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只標自由層方向而不定義參考層」與「穿隧電阻取決於相對磁化狀態」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer\" is not equivalent to \"Tunnel resistance depends on relative magnetization\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「MTJ 分層」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of MTJ stack?","options":["不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比","參考層穩定性也是讀值條件","只標自由層方向而不定義參考層"],"optionsEn":["Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions","Reference-layer stability also conditions readout","Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"參考層穩定性也是讀值條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reference-layer stability also conditions readout. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-02"],"title":"TMR 定義：建立模型","titleEn":"TMR definition: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電阻比的分母必須一致」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent.","instruction":"以假設 RP、RAP 計算 (RAP-RP)/RP 並註明慣例。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設同一偏壓與溫度下 MTJ 平行電阻 RP=5 kΩ、反平行 RAP=10 kΩ，TMR=(RAP−RP)/RP=100%。若錯用 RAP 當分母會得到 50%。本例不含讀取電路雜訊或電阻分布，不能由平均 TMR 直接宣告可靠讀取。","instructionEn":"Compute (RAP-RP)/RP from hypothetical values with the convention stated. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume MTJ resistances measured at the same bias and temperature are RP=5 kΩ and RAP=10 kΩ. TMR=(RAP−RP)/RP=100%; incorrectly using RAP as denominator gives 50%. Noise and resistance distributions are absent, so mean TMR does not establish reliable reading.","observation":"電阻比的分母必須一致；RA 需註明有效接面面積。","observationEn":"The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent; Resistance-area values need effective junction area.","failure":"若採用「不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「TMR 定義」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電阻比的分母必須一致。\n算例驗收：驗算 100%，標示分母 RP，並畫出兩態分布可能重疊的情況。","checkEn":"Submit the TMR definition diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 100%, label RP as denominator and sketch a possible overlap of the two state distributions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-03-k1","title":"TMR 定義／物理與模型","titleEn":"TMR definition / Physics and model","text":"機制：電阻比的分母必須一致。","textEn":"Mechanism: The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent."},{"id":"a075-v8-03-k2","title":"TMR 定義／驗證與限制","titleEn":"TMR definition / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比」。\n假設數值與推算：假設同一偏壓與溫度下 MTJ 平行電阻 RP=5 kΩ、反平行 RAP=10 kΩ，TMR=(RAP−RP)/RP=100%。若錯用 RAP 當分母會得到 50%。本例不含讀取電路雜訊或電阻分布，不能由平均 TMR 直接宣告可靠讀取。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume MTJ resistances measured at the same bias and temperature are RP=5 kΩ and RAP=10 kΩ. TMR=(RAP−RP)/RP=100%; incorrectly using RAP as denominator gives 50%. Noise and resistance distributions are absent, so mean TMR does not establish reliable reading."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「TMR 定義」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For TMR definition, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比","只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定","電阻比的分母必須一致"],"optionsEn":["Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions","Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability","The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電阻比的分母必須一致；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-03"],"title":"TMR 定義：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"TMR definition: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions.","instruction":"接續前一步「TMR 定義」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：RA 需註明有效接面面積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding TMR definition artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Resistance-area values need effective junction area. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電阻比的分母必須一致；RA 需註明有效接面面積。","observationEn":"The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent; Resistance-area values need effective junction area.","failure":"若採用「不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「TMR 定義」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「RA 需註明有效接面面積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for TMR definition, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Resistance-area values need effective junction area\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-04-k1","title":"TMR 定義／物理與模型","titleEn":"TMR definition / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：RA 需註明有效接面面積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Resistance-area values need effective junction area."},{"id":"a075-v8-04-k2","title":"TMR 定義／驗證與限制","titleEn":"TMR definition / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比」與「電阻比的分母必須一致」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions\" is not equivalent to \"The resistance-ratio denominator must be consistent\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「TMR 定義」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of TMR definition?","options":["RA 需註明有效接面面積","不註明分母便比較不同 TMR 百分比","只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定"],"optionsEn":["Resistance-area values need effective junction area","Comparing TMR percentages without denominator conventions","Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"RA 需註明有效接面面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Resistance-area values need effective junction area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-04"],"title":"磁各向異性：建立模型","titleEn":"Magnetic anisotropy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability.","instruction":"畫平面及垂直磁化的能量井，連結面積縮放需求。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw energy wells for in-plane/perpendicular magnetization and relate them to scaling. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定；形狀和介面都可貢獻各向異性。","observationEn":"Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability; Shape and interfaces both contribute anisotropy.","failure":"若採用「只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「磁各向異性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定。","checkEn":"Submit the Magnetic anisotropy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-05-k1","title":"磁各向異性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Magnetic anisotropy / Physics and model","text":"機制：易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability."},{"id":"a075-v8-05-k2","title":"磁各向異性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Magnetic anisotropy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「磁各向異性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Magnetic anisotropy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持","易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定","只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定"],"optionsEn":["Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write","Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability","Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-05"],"title":"磁各向異性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Magnetic anisotropy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability.","instruction":"接續前一步「磁各向異性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：形狀和介面都可貢獻各向異性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Magnetic anisotropy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Shape and interfaces both contribute anisotropy. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定；形狀和介面都可貢獻各向異性。","observationEn":"Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability; Shape and interfaces both contribute anisotropy.","failure":"若採用「只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「磁各向異性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「形狀和介面都可貢獻各向異性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Magnetic anisotropy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Shape and interfaces both contribute anisotropy\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-06-k1","title":"磁各向異性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Magnetic anisotropy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：形狀和介面都可貢獻各向異性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Shape and interfaces both contribute anisotropy."},{"id":"a075-v8-06-k2","title":"磁各向異性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Magnetic anisotropy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定」與「易軸方向與能障都影響狀態穩定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability\" is not equivalent to \"Easy-axis direction and barrier affect state stability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「磁各向異性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Magnetic anisotropy?","options":["只因磁層存在就假設狀態永久穩定","室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持","形狀和介面都可貢獻各向異性"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a magnetic film guarantees permanent stability","Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write","Shape and interfaces both contribute anisotropy"],"answer":2,"explanation":"形狀和介面都可貢獻各向異性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shape and interfaces both contribute anisotropy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a075-stage02","order":2,"title":"熱穩定因子 → SOT 路徑","titleEn":"Thermal stability factor to SOT pathway","description":"把「熱穩定因子」「STT 路徑」「SOT 路徑」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Thermal stability factor, STT pathway, SOT pathway.","steps":[{"id":"a075-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-06"],"title":"熱穩定因子：建立模型","titleEn":"Thermal stability factor: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success.","instruction":"用假設 Δ=Eb/(kBT) 比較體積及溫度改變。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical Δ=Eb/(kBT) under volume and temperature changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功；能障縮小也可能降低寫入門檻。","observationEn":"Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success; Lower barriers can also ease writing.","failure":"若採用「室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱穩定因子」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功。","checkEn":"Submit the Thermal stability factor diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-07-k1","title":"熱穩定因子／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal stability factor / Physics and model","text":"機制：保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功。","textEn":"Mechanism: Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success."},{"id":"a075-v8-07-k2","title":"熱穩定因子／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal stability factor / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱穩定因子」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thermal stability factor, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功","室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持","讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化"],"optionsEn":["Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success","Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write","Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization"],"answer":0,"explanation":"保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-07"],"title":"熱穩定因子：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal stability factor: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱穩定因子」成果，先指出錯誤主張「室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：能障縮小也可能降低寫入門檻。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thermal stability factor artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Lower barriers can also ease writing. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功；能障縮小也可能降低寫入門檻。","observationEn":"Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success; Lower barriers can also ease writing.","failure":"若採用「室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱穩定因子」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「能障縮小也可能降低寫入門檻」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thermal stability factor, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Lower barriers can also ease writing\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-08-k1","title":"熱穩定因子／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal stability factor / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：能障縮小也可能降低寫入門檻。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Lower barriers can also ease writing."},{"id":"a075-v8-08-k2","title":"熱穩定因子／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal stability factor / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持」與「保持與熱擾動相關，不能只看寫入成功」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write\" is not equivalent to \"Retention depends on thermal fluctuation, not just write success\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱穩定因子」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thermal stability factor?","options":["讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化","能障縮小也可能降低寫入門檻","室溫一次寫入成功就保證高溫保持"],"optionsEn":["Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization","Lower barriers can also ease writing","Inferring hot retention from one room-temperature write"],"answer":1,"explanation":"能障縮小也可能降低寫入門檻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Lower barriers can also ease writing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-08"],"title":"STT 路徑：建立模型","titleEn":"STT pathway: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control.","instruction":"畫穿過障壁的寫入電流與讀電流，分出各自應力。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw write and read currents through the barrier and distinguish stresses. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾；寫入脈寬會改變成功機率。","observationEn":"Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control; Write duration changes switching probability.","failure":"若採用「讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「STT 路徑」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾。","checkEn":"Submit the STT pathway diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-09-k1","title":"STT 路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"STT pathway / Physics and model","text":"機制：STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾。","textEn":"Mechanism: Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control."},{"id":"a075-v8-09-k2","title":"STT 路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"STT pathway / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「STT 路徑」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For STT pathway, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化","SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換","STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾"],"optionsEn":["Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization","Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes","Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control"],"answer":2,"explanation":"STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-09"],"title":"STT 路徑：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"STT pathway: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization.","instruction":"接續前一步「STT 路徑」成果，先指出錯誤主張「讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：寫入脈寬會改變成功機率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding STT pathway artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Write duration changes switching probability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾；寫入脈寬會改變成功機率。","observationEn":"Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control; Write duration changes switching probability.","failure":"若採用「讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「STT 路徑」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「寫入脈寬會改變成功機率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for STT pathway, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Write duration changes switching probability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-10-k1","title":"STT 路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"STT pathway / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：寫入脈寬會改變成功機率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Write duration changes switching probability."},{"id":"a075-v8-10-k2","title":"STT 路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"STT pathway / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化」與「STT 讀寫共享接面須處理讀擾」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization\" is not equivalent to \"Shared STT read/write junctions require read-disturb control\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「STT 路徑」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of STT pathway?","options":["寫入脈寬會改變成功機率","讀取電流永遠不可能擾動磁化","SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換"],"optionsEn":["Write duration changes switching probability","Assuming read current can never disturb magnetization","Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"寫入脈寬會改變成功機率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Write duration changes switching probability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-10"],"title":"SOT 路徑：建立模型","titleEn":"SOT pathway: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs.","instruction":"畫平面 SOT 軌和垂直讀路徑，計算假設足跡面積。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw lateral SOT track and vertical read path and calculate a hypothetical footprint. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求；SOT 軌電流擁擠影響局部熱。","observationEn":"Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs; SOT-track crowding affects local heating.","failure":"若採用「SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「SOT 路徑」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求。","checkEn":"Submit the SOT pathway diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-11-k1","title":"SOT 路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"SOT pathway / Physics and model","text":"機制：分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs."},{"id":"a075-v8-11-k2","title":"SOT 路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SOT pathway / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「SOT 路徑」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For SOT pathway, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效","分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求","SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers","Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs","Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-11"],"title":"SOT 路徑：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"SOT pathway: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes.","instruction":"接續前一步「SOT 路徑」成果，先指出錯誤主張「SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：SOT 軌電流擁擠影響局部熱。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding SOT pathway artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: SOT-track crowding affects local heating. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求；SOT 軌電流擁擠影響局部熱。","observationEn":"Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs; SOT-track crowding affects local heating.","failure":"若採用「SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「SOT 路徑」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「SOT 軌電流擁擠影響局部熱」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for SOT pathway, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"SOT-track crowding affects local heating\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-12-k1","title":"SOT 路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"SOT pathway / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：SOT 軌電流擁擠影響局部熱。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: SOT-track crowding affects local heating."},{"id":"a075-v8-12-k2","title":"SOT 路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SOT pathway / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換」與「分離讀寫可增加端點與佈線需求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes\" is not equivalent to \"Separated read/write can increase terminals and routing needs\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「SOT 路徑」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of SOT pathway?","options":["SOT 與 STT 可以不改版圖直接互換","平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效","SOT 軌電流擁擠影響局部熱"],"optionsEn":["Swapping SOT and STT without layout changes","Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers","SOT-track crowding affects local heating"],"answer":2,"explanation":"SOT 軌電流擁擠影響局部熱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"SOT-track crowding affects local heating. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a075-stage03","order":3,"title":"障壁均勻度 → 熱預算","titleEn":"Barrier uniformity to Thermal budget","description":"把「障壁均勻度」「圖形邊緣」「熱預算」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Barrier uniformity, Patterned edges, Thermal budget.","steps":[{"id":"a075-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-12"],"title":"障壁均勻度：建立模型","titleEn":"Barrier uniformity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown.","instruction":"比較均勻障壁和局部薄點的電流路徑，規劃 RA 分布量測。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare uniform barrier/local thin spots and plan resistance-area distributions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰；障壁缺口可形成平行漏電路徑。","observationEn":"Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown; Barrier defects can add parallel leakage.","failure":"若採用「平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「障壁均勻度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰。","checkEn":"Submit the Barrier uniformity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-13-k1","title":"障壁均勻度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Barrier uniformity / Physics and model","text":"機制：局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰。","textEn":"Mechanism: Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown."},{"id":"a075-v8-13-k2","title":"障壁均勻度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Barrier uniformity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「障壁均勻度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Barrier uniformity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰","平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效","只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質"],"optionsEn":["Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown","Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers","Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-13"],"title":"障壁均勻度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Barrier uniformity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers.","instruction":"接續前一步「障壁均勻度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：障壁缺口可形成平行漏電路徑。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Barrier uniformity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Barrier defects can add parallel leakage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰；障壁缺口可形成平行漏電路徑。","observationEn":"Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown; Barrier defects can add parallel leakage.","failure":"若採用「平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「障壁均勻度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「障壁缺口可形成平行漏電路徑」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Barrier uniformity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Barrier defects can add parallel leakage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-14-k1","title":"障壁均勻度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Barrier uniformity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：障壁缺口可形成平行漏電路徑。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Barrier defects can add parallel leakage."},{"id":"a075-v8-14-k2","title":"障壁均勻度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Barrier uniformity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效」與「局部薄點可能支配穿隧與崩潰」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers\" is not equivalent to \"Thin spots can dominate tunneling and breakdown\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「障壁均勻度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Barrier uniformity?","options":["只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質","障壁缺口可形成平行漏電路徑","平均厚度相同便推定障壁電性等效"],"optionsEn":["Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone","Barrier defects can add parallel leakage","Assuming equal average thickness means equivalent electrical barriers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"障壁缺口可形成平行漏電路徑；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Barrier defects can add parallel leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-14"],"title":"圖形邊緣：建立模型","titleEn":"Patterned edges: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation.","instruction":"畫蝕刻後柱壁損傷和金屬再沉積，區分磁性與漏電異常。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch sidewall damage/redeposition and separate magnetic from leakage faults. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣；再沉積可短接柱側壁。","observationEn":"Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation; Redeposition can short pillar sidewalls.","failure":"若採用「只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「圖形邊緣」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣。","checkEn":"Submit the Patterned edges diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-15-k1","title":"圖形邊緣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Patterned edges / Physics and model","text":"機制：柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣。","textEn":"Mechanism: Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation."},{"id":"a075-v8-15-k2","title":"圖形邊緣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Patterned edges / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「圖形邊緣」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Patterned edges, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質","初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟","柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣"],"optionsEn":["Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone","Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal","Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-15"],"title":"圖形邊緣：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Patterned edges: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「圖形邊緣」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：再沉積可短接柱側壁。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Patterned edges artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Redeposition can short pillar sidewalls. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣；再沉積可短接柱側壁。","observationEn":"Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation; Redeposition can short pillar sidewalls.","failure":"若採用「只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「圖形邊緣」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「再沉積可短接柱側壁」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Patterned edges, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Redeposition can short pillar sidewalls\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-16-k1","title":"圖形邊緣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Patterned edges / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：再沉積可短接柱側壁。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Redeposition can short pillar sidewalls."},{"id":"a075-v8-16-k2","title":"圖形邊緣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Patterned edges / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質」與「柱邊緣整合可能同時改變磁性和絕緣」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone\" is not equivalent to \"Pillar-edge processing can affect magnetism and insulation\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「圖形邊緣」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Patterned edges?","options":["再沉積可短接柱側壁","只量柱徑就證明 MTJ 品質","初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟"],"optionsEn":["Redeposition can short pillar sidewalls","Proving MTJ quality from pillar diameter alone","Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"再沉積可短接柱側壁；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Redeposition can short pillar sidewalls. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-16"],"title":"熱預算：建立模型","titleEn":"Thermal budget: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Later heating is part of MTJ integration.","instruction":"把磁堆疊退火與後續製程溫度排入流程，追蹤界面變化。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Place stack anneal and later heating in a sequence and track interface changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分；材料擴散可能降低界面磁性品質。","observationEn":"Later heating is part of MTJ integration; Interdiffusion can degrade magnetic interfaces.","failure":"若採用「初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱預算」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分。","checkEn":"Submit the Thermal budget diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Later heating is part of MTJ integration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-17-k1","title":"熱預算／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal budget / Physics and model","text":"機制：後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分。","textEn":"Mechanism: Later heating is part of MTJ integration."},{"id":"a075-v8-17-k2","title":"熱預算／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal budget / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱預算」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thermal budget, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率","後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分","初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟"],"optionsEn":["Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes","Later heating is part of MTJ integration","Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Later heating is part of MTJ integration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-17"],"title":"熱預算：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal budget: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱預算」成果，先指出錯誤主張「初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：材料擴散可能降低界面磁性品質。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thermal budget artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Interdiffusion can degrade magnetic interfaces. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分；材料擴散可能降低界面磁性品質。","observationEn":"Later heating is part of MTJ integration; Interdiffusion can degrade magnetic interfaces.","failure":"若採用「初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱預算」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「材料擴散可能降低界面磁性品質」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thermal budget, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Interdiffusion can degrade magnetic interfaces\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-18-k1","title":"熱預算／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal budget / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：材料擴散可能降低界面磁性品質。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Interdiffusion can degrade magnetic interfaces."},{"id":"a075-v8-18-k2","title":"熱預算／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal budget / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟」與「後續熱歷史也是 MTJ 整合的一部分」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal\" is not equivalent to \"Later heating is part of MTJ integration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱預算」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thermal budget?","options":["初次退火合格便忽略後續熱步驟","十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率","材料擴散可能降低界面磁性品質"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring later heating after an initial passing anneal","Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes","Interdiffusion can degrade magnetic interfaces"],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料擴散可能降低界面磁性品質；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Interdiffusion can degrade magnetic interfaces. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a075-stage04","order":4,"title":"寫錯機率 → 記憶體用途","titleEn":"Write-error probability to Memory application","description":"把「寫錯機率」「讀窗與擾動」「記憶體用途」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Write-error probability, Read window and disturb, Memory application.","steps":[{"id":"a075-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-18"],"title":"寫錯機率：建立模型","titleEn":"Write-error probability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability.","instruction":"對假設脈衝重複實驗計算錯誤率並報樣本數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compute errors from repeated hypothetical pulses with sample count. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零；零錯誤樣本只提供機率界限。","observationEn":"Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability; Zero-error samples give probability bounds.","failure":"若採用「十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「寫錯機率」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零。","checkEn":"Submit the Write-error probability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-19-k1","title":"寫錯機率／物理與模型","titleEn":"Write-error probability / Physics and model","text":"機制：未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零。","textEn":"Mechanism: Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability."},{"id":"a075-v8-19-k2","title":"寫錯機率／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Write-error probability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「寫錯機率」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Write-error probability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零","十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率","只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾"],"optionsEn":["Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability","Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes","Raising read current without checking disturb"],"answer":0,"explanation":"未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-19"],"title":"寫錯機率：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Write-error probability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes.","instruction":"接續前一步「寫錯機率」成果，先指出錯誤主張「十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：零錯誤樣本只提供機率界限。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Write-error probability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Zero-error samples give probability bounds. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零；零錯誤樣本只提供機率界限。","observationEn":"Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability; Zero-error samples give probability bounds.","failure":"若採用「十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「寫錯機率」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「零錯誤樣本只提供機率界限」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Write-error probability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Zero-error samples give probability bounds\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-20-k1","title":"寫錯機率／物理與模型","titleEn":"Write-error probability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：零錯誤樣本只提供機率界限。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Zero-error samples give probability bounds."},{"id":"a075-v8-20-k2","title":"寫錯機率／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Write-error probability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率」與「未觀察錯誤不等於錯誤機率為零」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes\" is not equivalent to \"Observing no errors does not imply zero error probability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「寫錯機率」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Write-error probability?","options":["只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾","零錯誤樣本只提供機率界限","十次成功就宣稱任意低錯誤率"],"optionsEn":["Raising read current without checking disturb","Zero-error samples give probability bounds","Claiming arbitrarily low error rates from ten successes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"零錯誤樣本只提供機率界限；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Zero-error samples give probability bounds. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-20"],"title":"讀窗與擾動：建立模型","titleEn":"Read window and disturb: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Increasing read signal can increase junction stress.","instruction":"比較兩阻態分布、放大器誤差及讀取幅度，找共同裕量。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare state distributions, amplifier error and read amplitude for joint margin. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力；感測放大器偏移縮小可用讀窗。","observationEn":"Increasing read signal can increase junction stress; Sense-amplifier offsets shrink read margins.","failure":"若採用「只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Raising read current without checking disturb\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「讀窗與擾動」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力。","checkEn":"Submit the Read window and disturb diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Increasing read signal can increase junction stress.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-21-k1","title":"讀窗與擾動／物理與模型","titleEn":"Read window and disturb / Physics and model","text":"機制：提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Increasing read signal can increase junction stress."},{"id":"a075-v8-21-k2","title":"讀窗與擾動／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Read window and disturb / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Raising read current without checking disturb."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「讀窗與擾動」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Read window and disturb, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾","一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳","提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力"],"optionsEn":["Raising read current without checking disturb","Treating one energy record as best for every use","Increasing read signal can increase junction stress"],"answer":2,"explanation":"提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Increasing read signal can increase junction stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-21"],"title":"讀窗與擾動：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Read window and disturb: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Raising read current without checking disturb.","instruction":"接續前一步「讀窗與擾動」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：感測放大器偏移縮小可用讀窗。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Read window and disturb artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Raising read current without checking disturb\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sense-amplifier offsets shrink read margins. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力；感測放大器偏移縮小可用讀窗。","observationEn":"Increasing read signal can increase junction stress; Sense-amplifier offsets shrink read margins.","failure":"若採用「只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Raising read current without checking disturb\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「讀窗與擾動」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「感測放大器偏移縮小可用讀窗」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Read window and disturb, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sense-amplifier offsets shrink read margins\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-22-k1","title":"讀窗與擾動／物理與模型","titleEn":"Read window and disturb / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：感測放大器偏移縮小可用讀窗。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sense-amplifier offsets shrink read margins."},{"id":"a075-v8-22-k2","title":"讀窗與擾動／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Read window and disturb / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾」與「提高讀訊號也可能提高接面應力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Raising read current without checking disturb\" is not equivalent to \"Increasing read signal can increase junction stress\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「讀窗與擾動」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Read window and disturb?","options":["感測放大器偏移縮小可用讀窗","只放大讀電流而不檢查讀擾","一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳"],"optionsEn":["Sense-amplifier offsets shrink read margins","Raising read current without checking disturb","Treating one energy record as best for every use"],"answer":0,"explanation":"感測放大器偏移縮小可用讀窗；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sense-amplifier offsets shrink read margins. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-22"],"title":"記憶體用途：建立模型","titleEn":"Memory application: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use.","instruction":"對快取與長期儲存分別列出速度、保持、耐久與面積權重。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Weight speed, retention, endurance and area separately for cache and storage. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同；快取保持需求可不同於長期儲存。","observationEn":"The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use; Cache retention needs differ from archival storage.","failure":"若採用「一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one energy record as best for every use\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「記憶體用途」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Memory application diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-23-k1","title":"記憶體用途／物理與模型","titleEn":"Memory application / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use."},{"id":"a075-v8-23-k2","title":"記憶體用途／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Memory application / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating one energy record as best for every use."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「記憶體用途」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Memory application, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只標自由層方向而不定義參考層","不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同","一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳"],"optionsEn":["Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer","The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use","Treating one energy record as best for every use"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a075-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mram","v8-c-sot","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a075-v8-23"],"title":"記憶體用途：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Memory application: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating one energy record as best for every use.","instruction":"接續前一步「記憶體用途」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：快取保持需求可不同於長期儲存。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Memory application artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating one energy record as best for every use\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cache retention needs differ from archival storage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同；快取保持需求可不同於長期儲存。","observationEn":"The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use; Cache retention needs differ from archival storage.","failure":"若採用「一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one energy record as best for every use\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「記憶體用途」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「快取保持需求可不同於長期儲存」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Memory application, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cache retention needs differ from archival storage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a075-v8-24-k1","title":"記憶體用途／物理與模型","titleEn":"Memory application / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：快取保持需求可不同於長期儲存。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cache retention needs differ from archival storage."},{"id":"a075-v8-24-k2","title":"記憶體用途／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Memory application / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳」與「不同用途下最佳磁記憶體架構可不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating one energy record as best for every use\" is not equivalent to \"The best magnetic-memory architecture depends on use\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「記憶體用途」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Memory application?","options":["一項最低能量記錄證明所有用途最佳","只標自由層方向而不定義參考層","快取保持需求可不同於長期儲存"],"optionsEn":["Treating one energy record as best for every use","Specifying free-layer direction without a reference layer","Cache retention needs differ from archival storage"],"answer":2,"explanation":"快取保持需求可不同於長期儲存；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cache retention needs differ from archival storage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"},{"id":"a076","title":"電阻式記憶體製作","titleEn":"Resistive memory fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從阻變截面、SET 與 RESET到權重漂移：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Resistive-switching section and SET and RESET to Weight drift: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["阻變截面","氧空缺","循環與元件變異","寫入驗證"],"labelsEn":["Resistive-switching section","Oxygen vacancies","Cycle and device variability","Program and verify"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a076-stage01","order":1,"title":"阻變截面 → 電流限制","titleEn":"Resistive-switching section to Current compliance","description":"把「阻變截面」「形成步驟」「電流限制」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Resistive-switching section, Electroforming, Current compliance.","steps":[{"id":"a076-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"阻變截面：建立模型","titleEn":"Resistive-switching section: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism.","instruction":"畫兩電極與氧化物，標出細絲型假說及不適用的均勻模型。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw electrodes/oxide and label filamentary assumptions versus uniform switching. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制；電極活性會改變離子交換。","observationEn":"Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism; Electrode reactivity changes ion exchange.","failure":"若採用「把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「阻變截面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制。","checkEn":"Submit the Resistive-switching section diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-01-k1","title":"阻變截面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resistive-switching section / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism."},{"id":"a076-v8-01-k2","title":"阻變截面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resistive-switching section / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「阻變截面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Resistive-switching section, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制","把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷","把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態"],"optionsEn":["Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism","Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses","Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-01"],"title":"阻變截面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Resistive-switching section: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses.","instruction":"接續前一步「阻變截面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電極活性會改變離子交換。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Resistive-switching section artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electrode reactivity changes ion exchange. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制；電極活性會改變離子交換。","observationEn":"Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism; Electrode reactivity changes ion exchange.","failure":"若採用「把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「阻變截面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電極活性會改變離子交換」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Resistive-switching section, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electrode reactivity changes ion exchange\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-02-k1","title":"阻變截面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resistive-switching section / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電極活性會改變離子交換。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electrode reactivity changes ion exchange."},{"id":"a076-v8-02-k2","title":"阻變截面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resistive-switching section / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷」與「不同 RRAM 材料系統未必使用同一機制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses\" is not equivalent to \"Different RRAM material systems need not share one mechanism\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「阻變截面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Resistive-switching section?","options":["把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態","電極活性會改變離子交換","把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷"],"optionsEn":["Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically","Electrode reactivity changes ion exchange","Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電極活性會改變離子交換；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrode reactivity changes ion exchange. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-02"],"title":"形成步驟：建立模型","titleEn":"Electroforming: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「首次形成歷史會影響後續切換」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Initial forming history can influence later switching.","instruction":"畫初始形成與後續 SET 的差異，列出電流限制與初態證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Distinguish initial forming from later SET and specify current limits and initial-state evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"首次形成歷史會影響後續切換；形成失敗分布也須列入良率。","observationEn":"Initial forming history can influence later switching; Forming failures belong in yield statistics.","failure":"若採用「把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「形成步驟」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：首次形成歷史會影響後續切換。","checkEn":"Submit the Electroforming diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Initial forming history can influence later switching.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-03-k1","title":"形成步驟／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electroforming / Physics and model","text":"機制：首次形成歷史會影響後續切換。","textEn":"Mechanism: Initial forming history can influence later switching."},{"id":"a076-v8-03-k2","title":"形成步驟／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electroforming / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「形成步驟」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Electroforming, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態","只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致","首次形成歷史會影響後續切換"],"optionsEn":["Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically","Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone","Initial forming history can influence later switching"],"answer":2,"explanation":"首次形成歷史會影響後續切換；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Initial forming history can influence later switching. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-03"],"title":"形成步驟：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Electroforming: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically.","instruction":"接續前一步「形成步驟」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：形成失敗分布也須列入良率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Electroforming artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Forming failures belong in yield statistics. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"首次形成歷史會影響後續切換；形成失敗分布也須列入良率。","observationEn":"Initial forming history can influence later switching; Forming failures belong in yield statistics.","failure":"若採用「把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「形成步驟」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「形成失敗分布也須列入良率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Electroforming, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Forming failures belong in yield statistics\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-04-k1","title":"形成步驟／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electroforming / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：形成失敗分布也須列入良率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Forming failures belong in yield statistics."},{"id":"a076-v8-04-k2","title":"形成步驟／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electroforming / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態」與「首次形成歷史會影響後續切換」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically\" is not equivalent to \"Initial forming history can influence later switching\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「形成步驟」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Electroforming?","options":["形成失敗分布也須列入良率","把形成和所有後續寫入視為相同初態","只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致"],"optionsEn":["Forming failures belong in yield statistics","Assuming forming and subsequent writes start identically","Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"形成失敗分布也須列入良率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Forming failures belong in yield statistics. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-04"],"title":"電流限制：建立模型","titleEn":"Current compliance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A compliance setting does not replace transient verification.","instruction":"以假設串聯晶體管和寄生電容畫形成過衝路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw forming overshoot paths with a hypothetical transistor and parasitic capacitance. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證；線纜儲能可能繞過慢速限流。","observationEn":"A compliance setting does not replace transient verification; Cable stored energy can bypass slow compliance.","failure":"若採用「只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電流限制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證。","checkEn":"Submit the Current compliance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A compliance setting does not replace transient verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-05-k1","title":"電流限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Current compliance / Physics and model","text":"機制：設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證。","textEn":"Mechanism: A compliance setting does not replace transient verification."},{"id":"a076-v8-05-k2","title":"電流限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Current compliance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電流限制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Current compliance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒","設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證","只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致"],"optionsEn":["Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle","A compliance setting does not replace transient verification","Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A compliance setting does not replace transient verification. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-05"],"title":"電流限制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Current compliance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「電流限制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：線纜儲能可能繞過慢速限流。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Current compliance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cable stored energy can bypass slow compliance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證；線纜儲能可能繞過慢速限流。","observationEn":"A compliance setting does not replace transient verification; Cable stored energy can bypass slow compliance.","failure":"若採用「只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電流限制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「線纜儲能可能繞過慢速限流」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Current compliance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cable stored energy can bypass slow compliance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-06-k1","title":"電流限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Current compliance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：線纜儲能可能繞過慢速限流。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cable stored energy can bypass slow compliance."},{"id":"a076-v8-06-k2","title":"電流限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Current compliance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致」與「設定限流不能取代瞬態電流驗證」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone\" is not equivalent to \"A compliance setting does not replace transient verification\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電流限制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Current compliance?","options":["只記 SMU 限流值便保證細絲尺寸一致","把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒","線纜儲能可能繞過慢速限流"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing identical filaments from an SMU limit alone","Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle","Cable stored energy can bypass slow compliance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"線纜儲能可能繞過慢速限流；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cable stored energy can bypass slow compliance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a076-stage02","order":2,"title":"氧空缺 → 細絲侷部性","titleEn":"Oxygen vacancies to Filament locality","description":"把「氧空缺」「SET 與 RESET」「細絲侷部性」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Oxygen vacancies, SET and RESET, Filament locality.","steps":[{"id":"a076-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-06"],"title":"氧空缺：建立模型","titleEn":"Oxygen vacancies: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations.","instruction":"分色畫氧離子與空缺遷移，保持電荷與方向定義。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Color-code oxygen ions and vacancies with charge/direction conventions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群；氧空缺與金屬離子細絲模型不同。","observationEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations; Vacancy and metal-ion filaments are different models.","failure":"若採用「把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「氧空缺」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群。","checkEn":"Submit the Oxygen vacancies diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-07-k1","title":"氧空缺／物理與模型","titleEn":"Oxygen vacancies / Physics and model","text":"機制：氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群。","textEn":"Mechanism: Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations."},{"id":"a076-v8-07-k2","title":"氧空缺／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Oxygen vacancies / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氧空缺」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Oxygen vacancies, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群","把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒","只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性"],"optionsEn":["Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations","Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle","Inferring all switching polarity from material name"],"answer":0,"explanation":"氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-07"],"title":"氧空缺：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Oxygen vacancies: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle.","instruction":"接續前一步「氧空缺」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：氧空缺與金屬離子細絲模型不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Oxygen vacancies artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Vacancy and metal-ion filaments are different models. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群；氧空缺與金屬離子細絲模型不同。","observationEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations; Vacancy and metal-ion filaments are different models.","failure":"若採用「把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「氧空缺」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「氧空缺與金屬離子細絲模型不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Oxygen vacancies, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Vacancy and metal-ion filaments are different models\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-08-k1","title":"氧空缺／物理與模型","titleEn":"Oxygen vacancies / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：氧空缺與金屬離子細絲模型不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Vacancy and metal-ion filaments are different models."},{"id":"a076-v8-08-k2","title":"氧空缺／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Oxygen vacancies / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒」與「氧交換界面可改變可用缺陷族群」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle\" is not equivalent to \"Oxygen-exchange interfaces can change available defect populations\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「氧空缺」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Oxygen vacancies?","options":["只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性","氧空缺與金屬離子細絲模型不同","把空缺畫成與氧離子相同方向的同一顆粒"],"optionsEn":["Inferring all switching polarity from material name","Vacancy and metal-ion filaments are different models","Treating vacancies and oxygen ions as the same moving particle"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氧空缺與金屬離子細絲模型不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Vacancy and metal-ion filaments are different models. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-08"],"title":"SET 與 RESET：建立模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior.","instruction":"在假設 I-V 曲線標出高低阻態轉換和極性。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark high/low resistance transitions and polarity on hypothetical I-V. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為；極性定義需固定接地電極。","observationEn":"Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior; Polarity definitions require a fixed reference electrode.","failure":"若採用「只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring all switching polarity from material name\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「SET 與 RESET」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為。","checkEn":"Submit the SET and RESET diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-09-k1","title":"SET 與 RESET／物理與模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Physics and model","text":"機制：雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為。","textEn":"Mechanism: Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior."},{"id":"a076-v8-09-k2","title":"SET 與 RESET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring all switching polarity from material name."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「SET 與 RESET」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For SET and RESET, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性","一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化","雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為"],"optionsEn":["Inferring all switching polarity from material name","Inferring full localization from one area point","Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior"],"answer":2,"explanation":"雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-09"],"title":"SET 與 RESET：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"SET and RESET: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring all switching polarity from material name.","instruction":"接續前一步「SET 與 RESET」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：極性定義需固定接地電極。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding SET and RESET artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring all switching polarity from material name\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Polarity definitions require a fixed reference electrode. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為；極性定義需固定接地電極。","observationEn":"Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior; Polarity definitions require a fixed reference electrode.","failure":"若採用「只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring all switching polarity from material name\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「SET 與 RESET」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「極性定義需固定接地電極」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for SET and RESET, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Polarity definitions require a fixed reference electrode\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-10-k1","title":"SET 與 RESET／物理與模型","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：極性定義需固定接地電極。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Polarity definitions require a fixed reference electrode."},{"id":"a076-v8-10-k2","title":"SET 與 RESET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SET and RESET / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性」與「雙極性與單極性分類需依實際偏壓行為」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring all switching polarity from material name\" is not equivalent to \"Bipolar/unipolar classification requires actual bias behavior\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「SET 與 RESET」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of SET and RESET?","options":["極性定義需固定接地電極","只依材料名稱決定所有切換極性","一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化"],"optionsEn":["Polarity definitions require a fixed reference electrode","Inferring all switching polarity from material name","Inferring full localization from one area point"],"answer":0,"explanation":"極性定義需固定接地電極；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Polarity definitions require a fixed reference electrode. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-10"],"title":"細絲侷部性：建立模型","titleEn":"Filament locality: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism.","instruction":"比較面積縮放前後的假設電流，測試局部與均勻模型。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical area-scaled current to test local versus uniform models. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明；多條細絲可能改變面積依賴。","observationEn":"Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism; Multiple filaments can alter area dependence.","failure":"若採用「一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring full localization from one area point\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「細絲侷部性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明。","checkEn":"Submit the Filament locality diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-11-k1","title":"細絲侷部性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Filament locality / Physics and model","text":"機制：面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明。","textEn":"Mechanism: Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism."},{"id":"a076-v8-11-k2","title":"細絲侷部性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Filament locality / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring full localization from one area point."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「細絲侷部性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Filament locality, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件","面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明","一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化"],"optionsEn":["Counting repeated reads as independent devices","Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism","Inferring full localization from one area point"],"answer":1,"explanation":"面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-11"],"title":"細絲侷部性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Filament locality: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring full localization from one area point.","instruction":"接續前一步「細絲侷部性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：多條細絲可能改變面積依賴。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Filament locality artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring full localization from one area point\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Multiple filaments can alter area dependence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明；多條細絲可能改變面積依賴。","observationEn":"Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism; Multiple filaments can alter area dependence.","failure":"若採用「一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring full localization from one area point\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「細絲侷部性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「多條細絲可能改變面積依賴」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Filament locality, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Multiple filaments can alter area dependence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-12-k1","title":"細絲侷部性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Filament locality / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：多條細絲可能改變面積依賴。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Multiple filaments can alter area dependence."},{"id":"a076-v8-12-k2","title":"細絲侷部性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Filament locality / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化」與「面積依賴是機制證據之一但不是唯一證明」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring full localization from one area point\" is not equivalent to \"Area dependence is evidence, not sole proof, of mechanism\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「細絲侷部性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Filament locality?","options":["一個面積點就斷定電流完全局部化","把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件","多條細絲可能改變面積依賴"],"optionsEn":["Inferring full localization from one area point","Counting repeated reads as independent devices","Multiple filaments can alter area dependence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"多條細絲可能改變面積依賴；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multiple filaments can alter area dependence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a076-stage03","order":3,"title":"循環與元件變異 → 隨機電報雜訊","titleEn":"Cycle and device variability to Random telegraph noise","description":"把「循環與元件變異」「保持尾端」「隨機電報雜訊」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Cycle and device variability, Retention tails, Random telegraph noise.","steps":[{"id":"a076-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-12"],"title":"循環與元件變異：建立模型","titleEn":"Cycle and device variability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「兩種變異需不同的實驗層級」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: These variability sources require different experimental levels.","instruction":"將每元件多循環結果分成器件間和循環間分布。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate device-to-device and cycle-to-cycle distributions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"兩種變異需不同的實驗層級；讀取雜訊需先與狀態變異分開。","observationEn":"These variability sources require different experimental levels; Separate read noise from state variability.","failure":"若採用「把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Counting repeated reads as independent devices\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「循環與元件變異」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：兩種變異需不同的實驗層級。","checkEn":"Submit the Cycle and device variability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: These variability sources require different experimental levels.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-13-k1","title":"循環與元件變異／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cycle and device variability / Physics and model","text":"機制：兩種變異需不同的實驗層級。","textEn":"Mechanism: These variability sources require different experimental levels."},{"id":"a076-v8-13-k2","title":"循環與元件變異／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cycle and device variability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Counting repeated reads as independent devices."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「循環與元件變異」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Cycle and device variability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["兩種變異需不同的實驗層級","把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件","只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端"],"optionsEn":["These variability sources require different experimental levels","Counting repeated reads as independent devices","Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails"],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩種變異需不同的實驗層級；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"These variability sources require different experimental levels. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-13"],"title":"循環與元件變異：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Cycle and device variability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Counting repeated reads as independent devices.","instruction":"接續前一步「循環與元件變異」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：讀取雜訊需先與狀態變異分開。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Cycle and device variability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Counting repeated reads as independent devices\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Separate read noise from state variability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"兩種變異需不同的實驗層級；讀取雜訊需先與狀態變異分開。","observationEn":"These variability sources require different experimental levels; Separate read noise from state variability.","failure":"若採用「把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Counting repeated reads as independent devices\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「循環與元件變異」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「讀取雜訊需先與狀態變異分開」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Cycle and device variability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Separate read noise from state variability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-14-k1","title":"循環與元件變異／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cycle and device variability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：讀取雜訊需先與狀態變異分開。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Separate read noise from state variability."},{"id":"a076-v8-14-k2","title":"循環與元件變異／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cycle and device variability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件」與「兩種變異需不同的實驗層級」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Counting repeated reads as independent devices\" is not equivalent to \"These variability sources require different experimental levels\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「循環與元件變異」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Cycle and device variability?","options":["只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端","讀取雜訊需先與狀態變異分開","把同一元件多次讀取當成多顆獨立元件"],"optionsEn":["Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails","Separate read noise from state variability","Counting repeated reads as independent devices"],"answer":1,"explanation":"讀取雜訊需先與狀態變異分開；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Separate read noise from state variability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-14"],"title":"保持尾端：建立模型","titleEn":"Retention tails: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A small unstable population can dominate array retention.","instruction":"比較相同平均阻值但不同早衰細絲比例的兩組資料。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare equal-mean resistance populations with different early-decay tails. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持；編程歷史會改變早衰比例。","observationEn":"A small unstable population can dominate array retention; Programming history changes early-decay fractions.","failure":"若採用「只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「保持尾端」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持。","checkEn":"Submit the Retention tails diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A small unstable population can dominate array retention.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-15-k1","title":"保持尾端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Retention tails / Physics and model","text":"機制：少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持。","textEn":"Mechanism: A small unstable population can dominate array retention."},{"id":"a076-v8-15-k2","title":"保持尾端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Retention tails / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「保持尾端」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Retention tails, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端","把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗","少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持"],"optionsEn":["Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails","Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins","A small unstable population can dominate array retention"],"answer":2,"explanation":"少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A small unstable population can dominate array retention. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-15"],"title":"保持尾端：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Retention tails: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails.","instruction":"接續前一步「保持尾端」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：編程歷史會改變早衰比例。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Retention tails artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Programming history changes early-decay fractions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持；編程歷史會改變早衰比例。","observationEn":"A small unstable population can dominate array retention; Programming history changes early-decay fractions.","failure":"若採用「只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「保持尾端」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「編程歷史會改變早衰比例」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Retention tails, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Programming history changes early-decay fractions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-16-k1","title":"保持尾端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Retention tails / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：編程歷史會改變早衰比例。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Programming history changes early-decay fractions."},{"id":"a076-v8-16-k2","title":"保持尾端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Retention tails / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端」與「少數不穩定狀態可支配陣列保持」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails\" is not equivalent to \"A small unstable population can dominate array retention\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「保持尾端」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Retention tails?","options":["編程歷史會改變早衰比例","只追蹤典型位元而忽略尾端","把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗"],"optionsEn":["Programming history changes early-decay fractions","Tracking typical bits while ignoring tails","Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins"],"answer":0,"explanation":"編程歷史會改變早衰比例；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Programming history changes early-decay fractions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-16"],"title":"隨機電報雜訊：建立模型","titleEn":"Random telegraph noise: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation.","instruction":"畫兩電平跳動與緩慢漂移，設計取樣間隔和觀察窗。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw two-level switching versus slow drift and choose sampling/time windows. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀；帶寬限制可漏掉快速跳動。","observationEn":"Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation; Bandwidth limits can hide rapid switching.","failure":"若採用「把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「隨機電報雜訊」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀。","checkEn":"Submit the Random telegraph noise diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-17-k1","title":"隨機電報雜訊／物理與模型","titleEn":"Random telegraph noise / Physics and model","text":"機制：離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀。","textEn":"Mechanism: Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation."},{"id":"a076-v8-17-k2","title":"隨機電報雜訊／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Random telegraph noise / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隨機電報雜訊」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Random telegraph noise, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["無限重試而沒有失败出口","離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀","把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗"],"optionsEn":["Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit","Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation","Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins"],"answer":1,"explanation":"離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-17"],"title":"隨機電報雜訊：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Random telegraph noise: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins.","instruction":"接續前一步「隨機電報雜訊」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：帶寬限制可漏掉快速跳動。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Random telegraph noise artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bandwidth limits can hide rapid switching. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀；帶寬限制可漏掉快速跳動。","observationEn":"Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation; Bandwidth limits can hide rapid switching.","failure":"若採用「把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「隨機電報雜訊」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「帶寬限制可漏掉快速跳動」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Random telegraph noise, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bandwidth limits can hide rapid switching\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-18-k1","title":"隨機電報雜訊／物理與模型","titleEn":"Random telegraph noise / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：帶寬限制可漏掉快速跳動。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bandwidth limits can hide rapid switching."},{"id":"a076-v8-18-k2","title":"隨機電報雜訊／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Random telegraph noise / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗」與「離散跳動與連續漂移有不同判讀」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins\" is not equivalent to \"Discrete jumps and continuous drift need different interpretation\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「隨機電報雜訊」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Random telegraph noise?","options":["把所有電流波動平均掉再判斷讀窗","無限重試而沒有失败出口","帶寬限制可漏掉快速跳動"],"optionsEn":["Averaging away all fluctuations before checking read margins","Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit","Bandwidth limits can hide rapid switching"],"answer":2,"explanation":"帶寬限制可漏掉快速跳動；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bandwidth limits can hide rapid switching. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a076-stage04","order":4,"title":"寫入驗證 → 權重漂移","titleEn":"Program and verify to Weight drift","description":"把「寫入驗證」「交叉陣列」「權重漂移」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Program and verify, Crossbar array, Weight drift.","steps":[{"id":"a076-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-18"],"title":"寫入驗證：建立模型","titleEn":"Program and verify: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence.","instruction":"對自訂導電目標窗模擬逐次寫入與讀取，記錄不收斂情況。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Simulate write/read iterations toward a conductance window and record nonconvergence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂；最大重試次數影響能量及良率。","observationEn":"Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence; Retry bounds affect energy and yield.","failure":"若採用「無限重試而沒有失败出口」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「寫入驗證」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂。","checkEn":"Submit the Program and verify diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-19-k1","title":"寫入驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Program and verify / Physics and model","text":"機制：回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂。","textEn":"Mechanism: Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence."},{"id":"a076-v8-19-k2","title":"寫入驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Program and verify / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「無限重試而沒有失败出口」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「寫入驗證」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Program and verify, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂","無限重試而沒有失败出口","單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確"],"optionsEn":["Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence","Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit","Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication"],"answer":0,"explanation":"回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-19"],"title":"寫入驗證：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Program and verify: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「無限重試而沒有失败出口」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit.","instruction":"接續前一步「寫入驗證」成果，先指出錯誤主張「無限重試而沒有失败出口」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：最大重試次數影響能量及良率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Program and verify artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Retry bounds affect energy and yield. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂；最大重試次數影響能量及良率。","observationEn":"Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence; Retry bounds affect energy and yield.","failure":"若採用「無限重試而沒有失败出口」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「寫入驗證」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「最大重試次數影響能量及良率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Program and verify, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Retry bounds affect energy and yield\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-20-k1","title":"寫入驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Program and verify / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：最大重試次數影響能量及良率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Retry bounds affect energy and yield."},{"id":"a076-v8-20-k2","title":"寫入驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Program and verify / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「無限重試而沒有失败出口」與「回授可縮小誤差但不能保證每個位元都收斂」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit\" is not equivalent to \"Feedback reduces error but does not guarantee convergence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「寫入驗證」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Program and verify?","options":["單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確","最大重試次數影響能量及良率","無限重試而沒有失败出口"],"optionsEn":["Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication","Retry bounds affect energy and yield","Retrying indefinitely without a failure exit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"最大重試次數影響能量及良率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Retry bounds affect energy and yield. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-20"],"title":"交叉陣列：建立模型","titleEn":"Crossbar array: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Array output depends on more than cell conductance.","instruction":"用小型電阻矩陣計算理想列電流，再加入線阻和偷流。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設理想交叉陣列的一個求和節點具有 G1=10 µS、G2=20 µS，輸入 V1=0.1 V、V2=0.2 V。兩支路電流為 1 與 4 µA，總和 5 µA。請依 I=ΣGV 列式；線阻、非線性、偷漏路徑與 ADC 誤差均未納入，結果不是實際神經網路精度。","instructionEn":"Compute ideal column current for a small conductance matrix, then add line resistance/sneak paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume an ideal crossbar summing node with G1=10 µS, G2=20 µS and inputs V1=0.1 V, V2=0.2 V. Branch currents are 1 and 4 µA, totaling 5 µA by I=ΣGV. Line resistance, nonlinearity, sneak paths and ADC errors are excluded; the result is not real neural-network accuracy.","observation":"陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定；列電壓因線阻而沿線下降。","observationEn":"Array output depends on more than cell conductance; Line resistance changes local column voltages.","failure":"若採用「單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「交叉陣列」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定。\n算例驗收：驗算兩支路與 5 µA 總和，並在電路圖上加一個可能破壞理想求和的寄生元件。","checkEn":"Submit the Crossbar array diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Array output depends on more than cell conductance.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify the branch currents and 5 µA sum, then add a parasitic element that could break ideal summation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-21-k1","title":"交叉陣列／物理與模型","titleEn":"Crossbar array / Physics and model","text":"機制：陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Array output depends on more than cell conductance."},{"id":"a076-v8-21-k2","title":"交叉陣列／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Crossbar array / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確」。\n假設數值與推算：假設理想交叉陣列的一個求和節點具有 G1=10 µS、G2=20 µS，輸入 V1=0.1 V、V2=0.2 V。兩支路電流為 1 與 4 µA，總和 5 µA。請依 I=ΣGV 列式；線阻、非線性、偷漏路徑與 ADC 誤差均未納入，結果不是實際神經網路精度。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume an ideal crossbar summing node with G1=10 µS, G2=20 µS and inputs V1=0.1 V, V2=0.2 V. Branch currents are 1 and 4 µA, totaling 5 µA by I=ΣGV. Line resistance, nonlinearity, sneak paths and ADC errors are excluded; the result is not real neural-network accuracy."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「交叉陣列」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Crossbar array, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確","只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確","陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定"],"optionsEn":["Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication","Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states","Array output depends on more than cell conductance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Array output depends on more than cell conductance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-21"],"title":"交叉陣列：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Crossbar array: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication.","instruction":"接續前一步「交叉陣列」成果，先指出錯誤主張「單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：列電壓因線阻而沿線下降。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Crossbar array artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Line resistance changes local column voltages. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定；列電壓因線阻而沿線下降。","observationEn":"Array output depends on more than cell conductance; Line resistance changes local column voltages.","failure":"若採用「單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「交叉陣列」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「列電壓因線阻而沿線下降」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Crossbar array, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Line resistance changes local column voltages\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-22-k1","title":"交叉陣列／物理與模型","titleEn":"Crossbar array / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：列電壓因線阻而沿線下降。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Line resistance changes local column voltages."},{"id":"a076-v8-22-k2","title":"交叉陣列／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Crossbar array / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確」與「陣列輸出不只由單元導電值決定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication\" is not equivalent to \"Array output depends on more than cell conductance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「交叉陣列」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Crossbar array?","options":["列電壓因線阻而沿線下降","單元線性就假定整陣列乘法精確","只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確"],"optionsEn":["Line resistance changes local column voltages","Assuming linear cells guarantee exact array multiplication","Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states"],"answer":0,"explanation":"列電壓因線阻而沿線下降；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Line resistance changes local column voltages. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-22"],"title":"權重漂移：建立模型","titleEn":"Weight drift: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Analog-compute error needs system-level verification.","instruction":"比較儲存後權重與參考權重，設定由誤差觸發的校驗策略。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare aged/reference weights and define error-triggered verification. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證；更新策略需計入讀寫成本。","observationEn":"Analog-compute error needs system-level verification; Refresh policies must include read/write costs.","failure":"若採用「只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「權重漂移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證。","checkEn":"Submit the Weight drift diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Analog-compute error needs system-level verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-23-k1","title":"權重漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Weight drift / Physics and model","text":"機制：類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證。","textEn":"Mechanism: Analog-compute error needs system-level verification."},{"id":"a076-v8-23-k2","title":"權重漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Weight drift / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「權重漂移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Weight drift, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷","類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證","只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確"],"optionsEn":["Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses","Analog-compute error needs system-level verification","Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states"],"answer":1,"explanation":"類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Analog-compute error needs system-level verification. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a076-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-rram","v8-c-rram-relax","v8-c-memory-process"],"prerequisiteIds":["a076-v8-23"],"title":"權重漂移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Weight drift: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states.","instruction":"接續前一步「權重漂移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：更新策略需計入讀寫成本。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Weight drift artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Refresh policies must include read/write costs. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證；更新策略需計入讀寫成本。","observationEn":"Analog-compute error needs system-level verification; Refresh policies must include read/write costs.","failure":"若採用「只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「權重漂移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「更新策略需計入讀寫成本」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Weight drift, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Refresh policies must include read/write costs\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a076-v8-24-k1","title":"權重漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Weight drift / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：更新策略需計入讀寫成本。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Refresh policies must include read/write costs."},{"id":"a076-v8-24-k2","title":"權重漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Weight drift / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確」與「類比運算誤差需要系統層級驗證」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states\" is not equivalent to \"Analog-compute error needs system-level verification\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「權重漂移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Weight drift?","options":["只看元件阻態仍分開就保證推論準確","把所有阻變元件都視為金屬熔斷","更新策略需計入讀寫成本"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing inference accuracy from separated device states","Treating all resistive switches as metal fuses","Refresh policies must include read/write costs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"更新策略需計入讀寫成本；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Refresh policies must include read/write costs. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"},{"id":"a077","title":"鐵電記憶體氧化鉿薄膜","titleEn":"Hafnia thin films for ferroelectric memory","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v10-video-bf0998107592"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從晶相與鐵電性、摻雜與比例到整合證據：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Phase and ferroelectricity and Dopants and composition to Integration evidence: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["晶相與鐵電性","厚度與場","氧交換介面","FeCAP 與 FeFET"],"labelsEn":["Phase and ferroelectricity","Thickness and field","Oxygen-exchange interfaces","FeCAP and FeFET"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a077-stage01","order":1,"title":"晶相與鐵電性 → PUND 差分","titleEn":"Phase and ferroelectricity to PUND differencing","description":"把「晶相與鐵電性」「極化迴圈」「PUND 差分」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Phase and ferroelectricity, Polarization loops, PUND differencing.","steps":[{"id":"a077-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"晶相與鐵電性：建立模型","titleEn":"Phase and ferroelectricity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase.","instruction":"對單斜、四方及正交相畫分類表，分開結構證據與電性證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Classify monoclinic, tetragonal and orthorhombic phases with structural/electrical evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相；X 光相峰重疊可能使相判讀不唯一。","observationEn":"The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase; Overlapping diffraction peaks can obscure phase identity.","failure":"若採用「只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶相與鐵電性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相。","checkEn":"Submit the Phase and ferroelectricity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-01-k1","title":"晶相與鐵電性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and ferroelectricity / Physics and model","text":"機制：氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相。","textEn":"Mechanism: The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase."},{"id":"a077-v8-01-k2","title":"晶相與鐵電性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and ferroelectricity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶相與鐵電性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Phase and ferroelectricity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相","只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性","任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明"],"optionsEn":["The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase","Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone","Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof"],"answer":0,"explanation":"氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-01"],"title":"晶相與鐵電性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Phase and ferroelectricity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶相與鐵電性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：X 光相峰重疊可能使相判讀不唯一。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Phase and ferroelectricity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Overlapping diffraction peaks can obscure phase identity. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相；X 光相峰重疊可能使相判讀不唯一。","observationEn":"The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase; Overlapping diffraction peaks can obscure phase identity.","failure":"若採用「只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶相與鐵電性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「X 光相峰重疊可能使相判讀不唯一」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Phase and ferroelectricity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Overlapping diffraction peaks can obscure phase identity\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-02-k1","title":"晶相與鐵電性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and ferroelectricity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：X 光相峰重疊可能使相判讀不唯一。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Overlapping diffraction peaks can obscure phase identity."},{"id":"a077-v8-02-k2","title":"晶相與鐵電性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and ferroelectricity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性」與「氧化鉿存在不等於已形成鐵電相」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone\" is not equivalent to \"The presence of hafnia does not establish a ferroelectric phase\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶相與鐵電性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Phase and ferroelectricity?","options":["任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明","X 光相峰重疊可能使相判讀不唯一","只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性"],"optionsEn":["Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof","Overlapping diffraction peaks can obscure phase identity","Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"X 光相峰重疊可能使相判讀不唯一；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Overlapping diffraction peaks can obscure phase identity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-02"],"title":"極化迴圈：建立模型","titleEn":"Polarization loops: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis.","instruction":"畫理想極化與含漏電的積分電荷迴圈，比較可混淆訊號。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare ideal polarization with leakage-contaminated integrated-charge loops. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯；儀器串聯阻抗也會改變迴圈。","observationEn":"Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis; Series impedance can distort loops.","failure":"若採用「任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「極化迴圈」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯。","checkEn":"Submit the Polarization loops diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-03-k1","title":"極化迴圈／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization loops / Physics and model","text":"機制：漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯。","textEn":"Mechanism: Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis."},{"id":"a077-v8-03-k2","title":"極化迴圈／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization loops / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「極化迴圈」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Polarization loops, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明","不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷","漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯"],"optionsEn":["Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof","Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge","Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis"],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-03"],"title":"極化迴圈：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Polarization loops: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof.","instruction":"接續前一步「極化迴圈」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：儀器串聯阻抗也會改變迴圈。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Polarization loops artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Series impedance can distort loops. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯；儀器串聯阻抗也會改變迴圈。","observationEn":"Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis; Series impedance can distort loops.","failure":"若採用「任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「極化迴圈」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「儀器串聯阻抗也會改變迴圈」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Polarization loops, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Series impedance can distort loops\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-04-k1","title":"極化迴圈／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization loops / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：儀器串聯阻抗也會改變迴圈。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Series impedance can distort loops."},{"id":"a077-v8-04-k2","title":"極化迴圈／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization loops / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明」與「漏電可讓電荷迴圈看似有鐵電遲滯」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof\" is not equivalent to \"Leakage can make charge loops resemble ferroelectric hysteresis\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「極化迴圈」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Polarization loops?","options":["儀器串聯阻抗也會改變迴圈","任何封閉 I-V 積分迴圈都當鐵電證明","不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷"],"optionsEn":["Series impedance can distort loops","Treating every closed integrated loop as ferroelectric proof","Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"儀器串聯阻抗也會改變迴圈；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Series impedance can distort loops. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-04"],"title":"PUND 差分：建立模型","titleEn":"PUND differencing: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds.","instruction":"畫同極性切換與不切換脈衝，標示相減得到的切換電荷。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw switching/non-switching pulses and subtract their charges. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性；陷阱充放電仍可能殘留於差分。","observationEn":"Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds; Trapping can remain after pulse subtraction.","failure":"若採用「不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「PUND 差分」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性。","checkEn":"Submit the PUND differencing diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-05-k1","title":"PUND 差分／物理與模型","titleEn":"PUND differencing / Physics and model","text":"機制：差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds."},{"id":"a077-v8-05-k2","title":"PUND 差分／驗證與限制","titleEn":"PUND differencing / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「PUND 差分」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For PUND differencing, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平","差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性","不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷"],"optionsEn":["Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage","Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds","Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-05"],"title":"PUND 差分：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"PUND differencing: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge.","instruction":"接續前一步「PUND 差分」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：陷阱充放電仍可能殘留於差分。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding PUND differencing artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Trapping can remain after pulse subtraction. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性；陷阱充放電仍可能殘留於差分。","observationEn":"Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds; Trapping can remain after pulse subtraction.","failure":"若採用「不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「PUND 差分」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「陷阱充放電仍可能殘留於差分」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for PUND differencing, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Trapping can remain after pulse subtraction\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-06-k1","title":"PUND 差分／物理與模型","titleEn":"PUND differencing / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：陷阱充放電仍可能殘留於差分。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Trapping can remain after pulse subtraction."},{"id":"a077-v8-06-k2","title":"PUND 差分／驗證與限制","titleEn":"PUND differencing / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷」與「差分脈衝需控制非切換背景的可比性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge\" is not equivalent to \"Pulse subtraction requires comparable nonswitching backgrounds\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「PUND 差分」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of PUND differencing?","options":["不同脈寬仍直接相減當切換電荷","用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平","陷阱充放電仍可能殘留於差分"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting unmatched pulse widths as switching charge","Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage","Trapping can remain after pulse subtraction"],"answer":2,"explanation":"陷阱充放電仍可能殘留於差分；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Trapping can remain after pulse subtraction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a077-stage02","order":2,"title":"厚度與場 → 電極與應力","titleEn":"Thickness and field to Electrodes and stress","description":"把「厚度與場」「摻雜與比例」「電極與應力」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Thickness and field, Dopants and composition, Electrodes and stress.","steps":[{"id":"a077-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-06"],"title":"厚度與場：建立模型","titleEn":"Thickness and field: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress.","instruction":"將假設施加電壓轉為場，分開物理膜厚與介面分壓。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設均勻 HZO 薄膜厚 10 nm，真正跨薄膜電壓為 1 V，平均場 E=1 MV/cm；改為 20 nm 則為 0.5 MV/cm。這個換算不能證明鐵電性或矯頑場；介面層分壓、漏電和量測波形需另外檢查。","instructionEn":"Convert hypothetical voltage to field while separating film thickness/interface division. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a uniform 10 nm HZO film with an actual 1 V drop: average E=1 MV/cm; at 20 nm it is 0.5 MV/cm. This conversion does not demonstrate ferroelectricity or a coercive field; interface voltage division, leakage and the measurement waveform require separate checks.","observation":"相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力；局部薄點的電場高於平均。","observationEn":"Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress; Local thin spots have higher fields.","failure":"若採用「用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「厚度與場」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力。\n算例驗收：驗算兩個場值並指出要驗證可切換極化仍需要哪類對照量測。","checkEn":"Submit the Thickness and field diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both fields and identify a control measurement still needed to establish switchable polarization.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-07-k1","title":"厚度與場／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness and field / Physics and model","text":"機制：相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress."},{"id":"a077-v8-07-k2","title":"厚度與場／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness and field / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平」。\n假設數值與推算：假設均勻 HZO 薄膜厚 10 nm，真正跨薄膜電壓為 1 V，平均場 E=1 MV/cm；改為 20 nm 則為 0.5 MV/cm。這個換算不能證明鐵電性或矯頑場；介面層分壓、漏電和量測波形需另外檢查。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a uniform 10 nm HZO film with an actual 1 V drop: average E=1 MV/cm; at 20 nm it is 0.5 MV/cm. This conversion does not demonstrate ferroelectricity or a coercive field; interface voltage division, leakage and the measurement waveform require separate checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「厚度與場」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thickness and field, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力","用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平","只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電"],"optionsEn":["Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress","Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage","Maximizing remanence without examining leakage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-07"],"title":"厚度與場：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thickness and field: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage.","instruction":"接續前一步「厚度與場」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：局部薄點的電場高於平均。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thickness and field artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Local thin spots have higher fields. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力；局部薄點的電場高於平均。","observationEn":"Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress; Local thin spots have higher fields.","failure":"若採用「用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「厚度與場」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「局部薄點的電場高於平均」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thickness and field, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Local thin spots have higher fields\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-08-k1","title":"厚度與場／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness and field / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：局部薄點的電場高於平均。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Local thin spots have higher fields."},{"id":"a077-v8-08-k2","title":"厚度與場／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness and field / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平」與「相同電壓對不同膜厚並非相同應力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage\" is not equivalent to \"Equal voltage across different thicknesses is not equal stress\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「厚度與場」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thickness and field?","options":["只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電","局部薄點的電場高於平均","用電壓相同就宣稱不同厚度測試公平"],"optionsEn":["Maximizing remanence without examining leakage","Local thin spots have higher fields","Claiming fair thickness comparison from equal voltage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部薄點的電場高於平均；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Local thin spots have higher fields. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-08"],"title":"摻雜與比例：建立模型","titleEn":"Dopants and composition: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment.","instruction":"以假設 Hf/Zr 比例矩陣規劃結構、極化和漏電共同量測。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plan structural, polarization and leakage measurements over hypothetical Hf/Zr ratios. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估；晶粒尺寸也可能影響相穩定。","observationEn":"Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment; Grain size can affect phase stability.","failure":"若採用「只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Maximizing remanence without examining leakage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「摻雜與比例」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估。","checkEn":"Submit the Dopants and composition diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-09-k1","title":"摻雜與比例／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dopants and composition / Physics and model","text":"機制：相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估。","textEn":"Mechanism: Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment."},{"id":"a077-v8-09-k2","title":"摻雜與比例／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dopants and composition / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Maximizing remanence without examining leakage."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「摻雜與比例」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dopants and composition, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電","更換電極只計算片電阻變化","相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估"],"optionsEn":["Maximizing remanence without examining leakage","Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes","Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment"],"answer":2,"explanation":"相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-09"],"title":"摻雜與比例：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dopants and composition: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Maximizing remanence without examining leakage.","instruction":"接續前一步「摻雜與比例」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：晶粒尺寸也可能影響相穩定。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dopants and composition artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Maximizing remanence without examining leakage\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Grain size can affect phase stability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估；晶粒尺寸也可能影響相穩定。","observationEn":"Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment; Grain size can affect phase stability.","failure":"若採用「只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Maximizing remanence without examining leakage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「摻雜與比例」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「晶粒尺寸也可能影響相穩定」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dopants and composition, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Grain size can affect phase stability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-10-k1","title":"摻雜與比例／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dopants and composition / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：晶粒尺寸也可能影響相穩定。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Grain size can affect phase stability."},{"id":"a077-v8-10-k2","title":"摻雜與比例／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dopants and composition / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電」與「相穩定化和漏電必須共同評估」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Maximizing remanence without examining leakage\" is not equivalent to \"Phase stabilization and leakage need joint assessment\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「摻雜與比例」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dopants and composition?","options":["晶粒尺寸也可能影響相穩定","只最大化剩餘極化而不看漏電","更換電極只計算片電阻變化"],"optionsEn":["Grain size can affect phase stability","Maximizing remanence without examining leakage","Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒尺寸也可能影響相穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Grain size can affect phase stability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-10"],"title":"電極與應力：建立模型","titleEn":"Electrodes and stress: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries.","instruction":"畫上下電極夾持及熱膨脹差，列出退火前後量測。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw electrode constraint/thermal mismatch and specify before/after anneal checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界；電極反應可能產生額外介面層。","observationEn":"Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries; Electrode reactions can create interlayers.","failure":"若採用「更換電極只計算片電阻變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電極與應力」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界。","checkEn":"Submit the Electrodes and stress diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-11-k1","title":"電極與應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electrodes and stress / Physics and model","text":"機制：電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界。","textEn":"Mechanism: Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries."},{"id":"a077-v8-11-k2","title":"電極與應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electrodes and stress / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「更換電極只計算片電阻變化」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電極與應力」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Electrodes and stress, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能","電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界","更換電極只計算片電阻變化"],"optionsEn":["Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property","Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries","Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-11"],"title":"電極與應力：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Electrodes and stress: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「更換電極只計算片電阻變化」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes.","instruction":"接續前一步「電極與應力」成果，先指出錯誤主張「更換電極只計算片電阻變化」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電極反應可能產生額外介面層。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Electrodes and stress artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electrode reactions can create interlayers. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界；電極反應可能產生額外介面層。","observationEn":"Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries; Electrode reactions can create interlayers.","failure":"若採用「更換電極只計算片電阻變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電極與應力」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電極反應可能產生額外介面層」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Electrodes and stress, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electrode reactions can create interlayers\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-12-k1","title":"電極與應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electrodes and stress / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電極反應可能產生額外介面層。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electrode reactions can create interlayers."},{"id":"a077-v8-12-k2","title":"電極與應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electrodes and stress / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「更換電極只計算片電阻變化」與「電極不只是導線，也影響界面與機械邊界」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes\" is not equivalent to \"Electrodes also affect interfaces and mechanical boundaries\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電極與應力」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Electrodes and stress?","options":["更換電極只計算片電阻變化","所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能","電極反應可能產生額外介面層"],"optionsEn":["Considering only sheet resistance when changing electrodes","Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property","Electrode reactions can create interlayers"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電極反應可能產生額外介面層；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrode reactions can create interlayers. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a077-stage03","order":3,"title":"氧交換介面 → 疲勞與印記","titleEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces to Fatigue and imprint","description":"把「氧交換介面」「喚醒效應」「疲勞與印記」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Oxygen-exchange interfaces, Wake-up effect, Fatigue and imprint.","steps":[{"id":"a077-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-12"],"title":"氧交換介面：建立模型","titleEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects.","instruction":"畫電極與 HZO 間氧交換方向，提出相組成及缺陷兩種驗證。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw oxygen exchange across HZO/electrode interfaces and propose phase/defect checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷；氧移動可能伴隨循環歷史效應。","observationEn":"Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects; Oxygen migration can depend on cycling history.","failure":"若採用「所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「氧交換介面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷。","checkEn":"Submit the Oxygen-exchange interfaces diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-13-k1","title":"氧交換介面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces / Physics and model","text":"機制：改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects."},{"id":"a077-v8-13-k2","title":"氧交換介面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氧交換介面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Oxygen-exchange interfaces, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷","所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能","第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗"],"optionsEn":["Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects","Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property","Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-13"],"title":"氧交換介面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property.","instruction":"接續前一步「氧交換介面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：氧移動可能伴隨循環歷史效應。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Oxygen-exchange interfaces artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Oxygen migration can depend on cycling history. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷；氧移動可能伴隨循環歷史效應。","observationEn":"Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects; Oxygen migration can depend on cycling history.","failure":"若採用「所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「氧交換介面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「氧移動可能伴隨循環歷史效應」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Oxygen-exchange interfaces, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Oxygen migration can depend on cycling history\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-14-k1","title":"氧交換介面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：氧移動可能伴隨循環歷史效應。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Oxygen migration can depend on cycling history."},{"id":"a077-v8-14-k2","title":"氧交換介面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Oxygen-exchange interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能」與「改變氧環境可能同時改變晶相和缺陷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property\" is not equivalent to \"Oxygen conditions can alter both phase and defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「氧交換介面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Oxygen-exchange interfaces?","options":["第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗","氧移動可能伴隨循環歷史效應","所有氧空缺減少都必然改善全部性能"],"optionsEn":["Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure","Oxygen migration can depend on cycling history","Assuming fewer oxygen vacancies improve every property"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氧移動可能伴隨循環歷史效應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Oxygen migration can depend on cycling history. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-14"],"title":"喚醒效應：建立模型","titleEn":"Wake-up effect: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「喚醒與測量暫態需要區分」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients.","instruction":"畫前幾輪循環極化增加的假設曲線，和儀器穩定化對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw hypothetical early-cycle polarization growth and compare instrument settling. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"喚醒與測量暫態需要區分；喚醒改善不代表無後續疲勞。","observationEn":"Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients; Wake-up improvement does not prevent later fatigue.","failure":"若採用「第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「喚醒效應」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：喚醒與測量暫態需要區分。","checkEn":"Submit the Wake-up effect diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-15-k1","title":"喚醒效應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wake-up effect / Physics and model","text":"機制：喚醒與測量暫態需要區分。","textEn":"Mechanism: Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients."},{"id":"a077-v8-15-k2","title":"喚醒效應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wake-up effect / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「喚醒效應」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Wake-up effect, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗","用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊","喚醒與測量暫態需要區分"],"optionsEn":["Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure","Replacing all aging information with loop area","Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients"],"answer":2,"explanation":"喚醒與測量暫態需要區分；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-15"],"title":"喚醒效應：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Wake-up effect: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure.","instruction":"接續前一步「喚醒效應」成果，先指出錯誤主張「第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：喚醒改善不代表無後續疲勞。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Wake-up effect artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Wake-up improvement does not prevent later fatigue. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"喚醒與測量暫態需要區分；喚醒改善不代表無後續疲勞。","observationEn":"Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients; Wake-up improvement does not prevent later fatigue.","failure":"若採用「第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「喚醒效應」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「喚醒改善不代表無後續疲勞」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Wake-up effect, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Wake-up improvement does not prevent later fatigue\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-16-k1","title":"喚醒效應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wake-up effect / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：喚醒改善不代表無後續疲勞。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Wake-up improvement does not prevent later fatigue."},{"id":"a077-v8-16-k2","title":"喚醒效應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wake-up effect / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗」與「喚醒與測量暫態需要區分」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure\" is not equivalent to \"Wake-up must be distinguished from measurement transients\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「喚醒效應」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Wake-up effect?","options":["喚醒改善不代表無後續疲勞","第一次較小就當永久性製程失敗","用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊"],"optionsEn":["Wake-up improvement does not prevent later fatigue","Treating a small first cycle as permanent process failure","Replacing all aging information with loop area"],"answer":0,"explanation":"喚醒改善不代表無後續疲勞；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Wake-up improvement does not prevent later fatigue. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-16"],"title":"疲勞與印記：建立模型","titleEn":"Fatigue and imprint: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features.","instruction":"分開迴圈縮小和水平位移，量化極化幅度及中心偏移。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate loop shrinkage from horizontal shift and quantify both. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵；非對稱電極可能造成內建偏壓。","observationEn":"Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features; Asymmetric electrodes can create built-in bias.","failure":"若採用「用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing all aging information with loop area\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「疲勞與印記」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵。","checkEn":"Submit the Fatigue and imprint diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-17-k1","title":"疲勞與印記／物理與模型","titleEn":"Fatigue and imprint / Physics and model","text":"機制：疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵。","textEn":"Mechanism: Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features."},{"id":"a077-v8-17-k2","title":"疲勞與印記／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Fatigue and imprint / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Replacing all aging information with loop area."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疲勞與印記」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Fatigue and imprint, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗","疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵","用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊"],"optionsEn":["Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop","Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features","Replacing all aging information with loop area"],"answer":1,"explanation":"疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-17"],"title":"疲勞與印記：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Fatigue and imprint: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Replacing all aging information with loop area.","instruction":"接續前一步「疲勞與印記」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：非對稱電極可能造成內建偏壓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Fatigue and imprint artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Replacing all aging information with loop area\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Asymmetric electrodes can create built-in bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵；非對稱電極可能造成內建偏壓。","observationEn":"Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features; Asymmetric electrodes can create built-in bias.","failure":"若採用「用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing all aging information with loop area\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「疲勞與印記」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「非對稱電極可能造成內建偏壓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Fatigue and imprint, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Asymmetric electrodes can create built-in bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-18-k1","title":"疲勞與印記／物理與模型","titleEn":"Fatigue and imprint / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：非對稱電極可能造成內建偏壓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Asymmetric electrodes can create built-in bias."},{"id":"a077-v8-18-k2","title":"疲勞與印記／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Fatigue and imprint / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊」與「疲勞與印記描述不同退化特徵」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Replacing all aging information with loop area\" is not equivalent to \"Fatigue and imprint describe different degradation features\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「疲勞與印記」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Fatigue and imprint?","options":["用單一遲滯面積代替全部老化資訊","同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗","非對稱電極可能造成內建偏壓"],"optionsEn":["Replacing all aging information with loop area","Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop","Asymmetric electrodes can create built-in bias"],"answer":2,"explanation":"非對稱電極可能造成內建偏壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Asymmetric electrodes can create built-in bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a077-stage04","order":4,"title":"FeCAP 與 FeFET → 整合證據","titleEn":"FeCAP and FeFET to Integration evidence","description":"把「FeCAP 與 FeFET」「非破壞讀出」「整合證據」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for FeCAP and FeFET, Nondestructive readout, Integration evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a077-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-18"],"title":"FeCAP 與 FeFET：建立模型","titleEn":"FeCAP and FeFET: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ.","instruction":"畫獨立電容讀電荷與閘極控制通道讀電流的兩種回路。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw capacitor charge readout and ferroelectric-gated transistor current readout. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同；FeFET 通道捕捉也能移動閾值。","observationEn":"FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ; FeFET channel traps can also shift threshold.","failure":"若採用「同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「FeCAP 與 FeFET」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同。","checkEn":"Submit the FeCAP and FeFET diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-19-k1","title":"FeCAP 與 FeFET／物理與模型","titleEn":"FeCAP and FeFET / Physics and model","text":"機制：FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ."},{"id":"a077-v8-19-k2","title":"FeCAP 與 FeFET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"FeCAP and FeFET / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「FeCAP 與 FeFET」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For FeCAP and FeFET, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同","同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗","讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動"],"optionsEn":["FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ","Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop","Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current"],"answer":0,"explanation":"FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-19"],"title":"FeCAP 與 FeFET：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"FeCAP and FeFET: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop.","instruction":"接續前一步「FeCAP 與 FeFET」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：FeFET 通道捕捉也能移動閾值。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding FeCAP and FeFET artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: FeFET channel traps can also shift threshold. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同；FeFET 通道捕捉也能移動閾值。","observationEn":"FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ; FeFET channel traps can also shift threshold.","failure":"若採用「同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「FeCAP 與 FeFET」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「FeFET 通道捕捉也能移動閾值」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for FeCAP and FeFET, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"FeFET channel traps can also shift threshold\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-20-k1","title":"FeCAP 與 FeFET／物理與模型","titleEn":"FeCAP and FeFET / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：FeFET 通道捕捉也能移動閾值。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: FeFET channel traps can also shift threshold."},{"id":"a077-v8-20-k2","title":"FeCAP 與 FeFET／驗證與限制","titleEn":"FeCAP and FeFET / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗」與「FeCAP 與 FeFET 的讀取及介面要求不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop\" is not equivalent to \"FeCAP and FeFET readout/interface requirements differ\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「FeCAP 與 FeFET」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of FeCAP and FeFET?","options":["讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動","FeFET 通道捕捉也能移動閾值","同一電容迴圈便完整預測 FeFET 記憶窗"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current","FeFET channel traps can also shift threshold","Predicting a complete FeFET window from one capacitor loop"],"answer":1,"explanation":"FeFET 通道捕捉也能移動閾值；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"FeFET channel traps can also shift threshold. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-20"],"title":"非破壞讀出：建立模型","titleEn":"Nondestructive readout: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification.","instruction":"比較極化翻轉讀出與小訊號電容讀出，列出需驗證的擾動。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare polarization-switching and small-signal capacitive readout with disturb checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留；小訊號頻率會改變電容對比。","observationEn":"Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification; Small-signal frequency changes capacitive contrast.","failure":"若採用「讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「非破壞讀出」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留。","checkEn":"Submit the Nondestructive readout diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-21-k1","title":"非破壞讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Nondestructive readout / Physics and model","text":"機制：非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留。","textEn":"Mechanism: Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification."},{"id":"a077-v8-21-k2","title":"非破壞讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Nondestructive readout / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「非破壞讀出」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Nondestructive readout, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動","將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度","非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current","Treating best polarization as production reliability","Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification"],"answer":2,"explanation":"非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-21"],"title":"非破壞讀出：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Nondestructive readout: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current.","instruction":"接續前一步「非破壞讀出」成果，先指出錯誤主張「讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：小訊號頻率會改變電容對比。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Nondestructive readout artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Small-signal frequency changes capacitive contrast. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留；小訊號頻率會改變電容對比。","observationEn":"Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification; Small-signal frequency changes capacitive contrast.","failure":"若採用「讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「非破壞讀出」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「小訊號頻率會改變電容對比」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Nondestructive readout, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Small-signal frequency changes capacitive contrast\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-22-k1","title":"非破壞讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Nondestructive readout / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：小訊號頻率會改變電容對比。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Small-signal frequency changes capacitive contrast."},{"id":"a077-v8-22-k2","title":"非破壞讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Nondestructive readout / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動」與「非破壞讀取須驗證讀後狀態保留」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current\" is not equivalent to \"Nondestructive reading requires post-read state verification\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「非破壞讀出」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Nondestructive readout?","options":["小訊號頻率會改變電容對比","讀出電流小就直接保證不擾動","將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Small-signal frequency changes capacitive contrast","Guaranteeing nondisturbance from small read current","Treating best polarization as production reliability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"小訊號頻率會改變電容對比；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small-signal frequency changes capacitive contrast. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-22"],"title":"整合證據：建立模型","titleEn":"Integration evidence: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions.","instruction":"同時審查相鑑定、切換電荷、保持、循環和熱預算。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Review phase evidence, switched charge, retention, cycling and thermal budget together. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀；極化與漏電需在同條件下比較。","observationEn":"Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions; Compare polarization and leakage under matching conditions.","failure":"若採用「將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating best polarization as production reliability\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「整合證據」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀。","checkEn":"Submit the Integration evidence diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-23-k1","title":"整合證據／物理與模型","titleEn":"Integration evidence / Physics and model","text":"機制：研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀。","textEn":"Mechanism: Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions."},{"id":"a077-v8-23-k2","title":"整合證據／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Integration evidence / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating best polarization as production reliability."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「整合證據」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Integration evidence, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性","研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀","將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone","Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions","Treating best polarization as production reliability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a077-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-hzo","v8-c-hzo-endurance","v8-c-nand-roadmap"],"prerequisiteIds":["a077-v8-23"],"title":"整合證據：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Integration evidence: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating best polarization as production reliability.","instruction":"接續前一步「整合證據」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：極化與漏電需在同條件下比較。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Integration evidence artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating best polarization as production reliability\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Compare polarization and leakage under matching conditions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀；極化與漏電需在同條件下比較。","observationEn":"Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions; Compare polarization and leakage under matching conditions.","failure":"若採用「將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating best polarization as production reliability\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「整合證據」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「極化與漏電需在同條件下比較」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Integration evidence, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Compare polarization and leakage under matching conditions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a077-v8-24-k1","title":"整合證據／物理與模型","titleEn":"Integration evidence / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：極化與漏電需在同條件下比較。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Compare polarization and leakage under matching conditions."},{"id":"a077-v8-24-k2","title":"整合證據／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Integration evidence / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度」與「研究最佳值需連同條件與分布閱讀」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating best polarization as production reliability\" is not equivalent to \"Research best values must be read with conditions and distributions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「整合證據」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Integration evidence?","options":["將單次最佳極化當成量產可靠度","只量化學成分就宣稱鐵電性","極化與漏電需在同條件下比較"],"optionsEn":["Treating best polarization as production reliability","Claiming ferroelectricity from composition alone","Compare polarization and leakage under matching conditions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"極化與漏電需在同條件下比較；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Compare polarization and leakage under matching conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"memory","subcategoryTitle":"記憶體","subcategoryTitleEn":"Memory"},{"id":"a078","title":"CMOS 影像感測器製作","titleEn":"CMOS image-sensor fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從像素訊號鏈、完整電荷轉移到感測器驗收：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Pixel signal chain and Complete charge transfer to Sensor acceptance: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["像素訊號鏈","暗訊號","像素隔離","讀出時間"],"labelsEn":["Pixel signal chain","Dark signal","Pixel isolation","Readout timing"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a078-stage01","order":1,"title":"像素訊號鏈 → 光二極體深度","titleEn":"Pixel signal chain to Photodiode depth","description":"把「像素訊號鏈」「前照與背照」「光二極體深度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pixel signal chain, Front versus back illumination, Photodiode depth.","steps":[{"id":"a078-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"像素訊號鏈：建立模型","titleEn":"Pixel signal chain: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies.","instruction":"畫光子、光電荷、轉移閘、浮接擴散與讀出放大器。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw photons, photocharge, transfer gate, floating diffusion and amplifier. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率；轉移閘時序會影響可讀出的電荷。","observationEn":"Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies; Transfer timing affects readable charge.","failure":"若採用「把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「像素訊號鏈」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率。","checkEn":"Submit the Pixel signal chain diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-01-k1","title":"像素訊號鏈／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel signal chain / Physics and model","text":"機制：光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies."},{"id":"a078-v8-01-k2","title":"像素訊號鏈／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel signal chain / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「像素訊號鏈」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pixel signal chain, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率","把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標","背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾"],"optionsEn":["Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies","Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain","Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk"],"answer":0,"explanation":"光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-01"],"title":"像素訊號鏈：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pixel signal chain: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain.","instruction":"接續前一步「像素訊號鏈」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：轉移閘時序會影響可讀出的電荷。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pixel signal chain artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Transfer timing affects readable charge. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率；轉移閘時序會影響可讀出的電荷。","observationEn":"Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies; Transfer timing affects readable charge.","failure":"若採用「把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「像素訊號鏈」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「轉移閘時序會影響可讀出的電荷」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pixel signal chain, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Transfer timing affects readable charge\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-02-k1","title":"像素訊號鏈／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel signal chain / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：轉移閘時序會影響可讀出的電荷。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Transfer timing affects readable charge."},{"id":"a078-v8-02-k2","title":"像素訊號鏈／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel signal chain / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標」與「光學收集與電性讀出是不同效率」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain\" is not equivalent to \"Optical collection and electrical readout have different efficiencies\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「像素訊號鏈」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pixel signal chain?","options":["背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾","轉移閘時序會影響可讀出的電荷","把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標"],"optionsEn":["Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk","Transfer timing affects readable charge","Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain"],"answer":1,"explanation":"轉移閘時序會影響可讀出的電荷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Transfer timing affects readable charge. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-02"],"title":"前照與背照：建立模型","titleEn":"Front versus back illumination: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control.","instruction":"畫光穿過配線前照及由背面入射兩種截面。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw light paths through front wiring and through backside silicon. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度；背面表面態可能造成載子復合。","observationEn":"Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control; Backside states can cause recombination.","failure":"若採用「背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「前照與背照」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度。","checkEn":"Submit the Front versus back illumination diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-03-k1","title":"前照與背照／物理與模型","titleEn":"Front versus back illumination / Physics and model","text":"機制：背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control."},{"id":"a078-v8-03-k2","title":"前照與背照／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Front versus back illumination / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「前照與背照」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Front versus back illumination, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾","將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率","背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度"],"optionsEn":["Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk","Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency","Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control"],"answer":2,"explanation":"背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-03"],"title":"前照與背照：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Front versus back illumination: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk.","instruction":"接續前一步「前照與背照」成果，先指出錯誤主張「背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：背面表面態可能造成載子復合。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Front versus back illumination artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Backside states can cause recombination. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度；背面表面態可能造成載子復合。","observationEn":"Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control; Backside states can cause recombination.","failure":"若採用「背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「前照與背照」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「背面表面態可能造成載子復合」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Front versus back illumination, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Backside states can cause recombination\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-04-k1","title":"前照與背照／物理與模型","titleEn":"Front versus back illumination / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：背面表面態可能造成載子復合。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Backside states can cause recombination."},{"id":"a078-v8-04-k2","title":"前照與背照／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Front versus back illumination / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾」與「背照改善入射路徑仍需處理表面與厚度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk\" is not equivalent to \"Back illumination changes entry paths but still needs surface/thickness control\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「前照與背照」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Front versus back illumination?","options":["背面表面態可能造成載子復合","背照就自動消除暗電流與串擾","將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率"],"optionsEn":["Backside states can cause recombination","Assuming backside illumination eliminates dark current and crosstalk","Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency"],"answer":0,"explanation":"背面表面態可能造成載子復合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Backside states can cause recombination. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-04"],"title":"光二極體深度：建立模型","titleEn":"Photodiode depth: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection.","instruction":"比較不同波長吸收深度與收集區，標示復合損失。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare wavelength-dependent absorption depths and collection regions with recombination. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集；電荷擴散長度影響收集範圍。","observationEn":"Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection; Diffusion length affects collection range.","failure":"若採用「將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「光二極體深度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集。","checkEn":"Submit the Photodiode depth diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-05-k1","title":"光二極體深度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Photodiode depth / Physics and model","text":"機制：吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集。","textEn":"Mechanism: Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection."},{"id":"a078-v8-05-k2","title":"光二極體深度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Photodiode depth / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「光二極體深度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Photodiode depth, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率","吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集","將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率"],"optionsEn":["Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate","Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection","Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency"],"answer":1,"explanation":"吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-05"],"title":"光二極體深度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Photodiode depth: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency.","instruction":"接續前一步「光二極體深度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電荷擴散長度影響收集範圍。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Photodiode depth artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Diffusion length affects collection range. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集；電荷擴散長度影響收集範圍。","observationEn":"Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection; Diffusion length affects collection range.","failure":"若採用「將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「光二極體深度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電荷擴散長度影響收集範圍」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Photodiode depth, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Diffusion length affects collection range\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-06-k1","title":"光二極體深度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Photodiode depth / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電荷擴散長度影響收集範圍。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Diffusion length affects collection range."},{"id":"a078-v8-06-k2","title":"光二極體深度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Photodiode depth / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率」與「吸收光子不代表其電荷全部被收集」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency\" is not equivalent to \"Absorption does not guarantee complete charge collection\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「光二極體深度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Photodiode depth?","options":["將吸收率直接等同外部量子效率","用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率","電荷擴散長度影響收集範圍"],"optionsEn":["Equating absorption with external quantum efficiency","Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate","Diffusion length affects collection range"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電荷擴散長度影響收集範圍；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Diffusion length affects collection range. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a078-stage02","order":2,"title":"暗訊號 → 飽和與轉換增益","titleEn":"Dark signal to Saturation and conversion gain","description":"把「暗訊號」「完整電荷轉移」「飽和與轉換增益」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Dark signal, Complete charge transfer, Saturation and conversion gain.","steps":[{"id":"a078-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-06"],"title":"暗訊號：建立模型","titleEn":"Dark signal: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「暗電流通常隨積分時間累積」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time.","instruction":"對暗場自訂曝光時間及溫度矩陣，分辨固定偏移與暗電流。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Use a hypothetical exposure/temperature matrix to separate offset from dark current. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"暗電流通常隨積分時間累積；暗訊號非均勻與時間噪聲要分開。","observationEn":"Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time; Separate dark nonuniformity from temporal noise.","failure":"若採用「用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「暗訊號」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：暗電流通常隨積分時間累積。","checkEn":"Submit the Dark signal diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-07-k1","title":"暗訊號／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dark signal / Physics and model","text":"機制：暗電流通常隨積分時間累積。","textEn":"Mechanism: Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time."},{"id":"a078-v8-07-k2","title":"暗訊號／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dark signal / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「暗訊號」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dark signal, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["暗電流通常隨積分時間累積","用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率","把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體"],"optionsEn":["Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time","Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate","Attributing all lag to image software"],"answer":0,"explanation":"暗電流通常隨積分時間累積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-07"],"title":"暗訊號：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dark signal: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate.","instruction":"接續前一步「暗訊號」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：暗訊號非均勻與時間噪聲要分開。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dark signal artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Separate dark nonuniformity from temporal noise. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"暗電流通常隨積分時間累積；暗訊號非均勻與時間噪聲要分開。","observationEn":"Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time; Separate dark nonuniformity from temporal noise.","failure":"若採用「用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「暗訊號」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「暗訊號非均勻與時間噪聲要分開」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dark signal, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Separate dark nonuniformity from temporal noise\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-08-k1","title":"暗訊號／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dark signal / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：暗訊號非均勻與時間噪聲要分開。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Separate dark nonuniformity from temporal noise."},{"id":"a078-v8-08-k2","title":"暗訊號／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dark signal / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率」與「暗電流通常隨積分時間累積」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate\" is not equivalent to \"Dark-current charge accumulates with integration time\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「暗訊號」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dark signal?","options":["把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體","暗訊號非均勻與時間噪聲要分開","用單次黑畫面直接代表暗電流率"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all lag to image software","Separate dark nonuniformity from temporal noise","Treating one dark image as a dark-current rate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"暗訊號非均勻與時間噪聲要分開；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Separate dark nonuniformity from temporal noise. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-08"],"title":"完整電荷轉移：建立模型","titleEn":"Complete charge transfer: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information.","instruction":"畫轉移前後位勢井，檢查殘留電荷及影像延遲。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch potential wells before/after transfer and inspect residual charge and lag. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊；前一幀殘留可用亮暗交替測試。","observationEn":"Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information; Bright/dark alternation can expose lag.","failure":"若採用「把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all lag to image software\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「完整電荷轉移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊。","checkEn":"Submit the Complete charge transfer diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-09-k1","title":"完整電荷轉移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Complete charge transfer / Physics and model","text":"機制：電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊。","textEn":"Mechanism: Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information."},{"id":"a078-v8-09-k2","title":"完整電荷轉移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Complete charge transfer / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing all lag to image software."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「完整電荷轉移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Complete charge transfer, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體","用單一增益數值代表動態範圍","電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all lag to image software","Representing dynamic range by gain alone","Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-09"],"title":"完整電荷轉移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Complete charge transfer: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing all lag to image software.","instruction":"接續前一步「完整電荷轉移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：前一幀殘留可用亮暗交替測試。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Complete charge transfer artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing all lag to image software\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bright/dark alternation can expose lag. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊；前一幀殘留可用亮暗交替測試。","observationEn":"Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information; Bright/dark alternation can expose lag.","failure":"若採用「把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all lag to image software\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「完整電荷轉移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「前一幀殘留可用亮暗交替測試」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Complete charge transfer, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bright/dark alternation can expose lag\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-10-k1","title":"完整電荷轉移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Complete charge transfer / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：前一幀殘留可用亮暗交替測試。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bright/dark alternation can expose lag."},{"id":"a078-v8-10-k2","title":"完整電荷轉移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Complete charge transfer / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體」與「電荷轉移不完整會留下前一影像資訊」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing all lag to image software\" is not equivalent to \"Incomplete transfer can retain previous-image information\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「完整電荷轉移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Complete charge transfer?","options":["前一幀殘留可用亮暗交替測試","把延遲完全歸因於影像軟體","用單一增益數值代表動態範圍"],"optionsEn":["Bright/dark alternation can expose lag","Attributing all lag to image software","Representing dynamic range by gain alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"前一幀殘留可用亮暗交替測試；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bright/dark alternation can expose lag. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-10"],"title":"飽和與轉換增益：建立模型","titleEn":"Saturation and conversion gain: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well.","instruction":"用假設浮接電容算 ΔV=Q/C，比較訊號增益和容量需求。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設 1,000 個電子完整轉移到 10 fF 的感測節點，q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C，Q=1.602×10⁻¹⁶ C，電壓變化幅度 ΔV=Q/C=16.02 mV。若電容增為 20 fF，幅度為 8.01 mV。忽略寄生、漏失與放大器增益；這不是滿井容量或量子效率。","instructionEn":"Use hypothetical floating-node capacitance to compare ΔV=Q/C and capacity. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume 1,000 electrons transfer completely to a 10 fF sense node. With q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C, Q=1.602×10⁻¹⁶ C and voltage-change magnitude ΔV=Q/C=16.02 mV. At 20 fF it becomes 8.01 mV. Parasitics, charge loss and amplifier gain are excluded; this is neither full-well capacity nor quantum efficiency.","observation":"更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量；讀噪需換算到同一電子或電壓單位。","observationEn":"Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well; Read noise needs consistent electron or voltage units.","failure":"若採用「用單一增益數值代表動態範圍」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Representing dynamic range by gain alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「飽和與轉換增益」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量。\n算例驗收：驗算 16.02 與 8.01 mV，並說明為何電容加倍使電荷轉電壓增益減半。","checkEn":"Submit the Saturation and conversion gain diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 16.02 and 8.01 mV and explain why doubling capacitance halves charge-to-voltage gain.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-11-k1","title":"飽和與轉換增益／物理與模型","titleEn":"Saturation and conversion gain / Physics and model","text":"機制：更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量。","textEn":"Mechanism: Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well."},{"id":"a078-v8-11-k2","title":"飽和與轉換增益／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Saturation and conversion gain / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用單一增益數值代表動態範圍」。\n假設數值與推算：假設 1,000 個電子完整轉移到 10 fF 的感測節點，q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C，Q=1.602×10⁻¹⁶ C，電壓變化幅度 ΔV=Q/C=16.02 mV。若電容增為 20 fF，幅度為 8.01 mV。忽略寄生、漏失與放大器增益；這不是滿井容量或量子效率。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Representing dynamic range by gain alone.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume 1,000 electrons transfer completely to a 10 fF sense node. With q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C, Q=1.602×10⁻¹⁶ C and voltage-change magnitude ΔV=Q/C=16.02 mV. At 20 fF it becomes 8.01 mV. Parasitics, charge loss and amplifier gain are excluded; this is neither full-well capacity nor quantum efficiency."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「飽和與轉換增益」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Saturation and conversion gain, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾","更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量","用單一增益數值代表動態範圍"],"optionsEn":["Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation","Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well","Representing dynamic range by gain alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-11"],"title":"飽和與轉換增益：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Saturation and conversion gain: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用單一增益數值代表動態範圍」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Representing dynamic range by gain alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「飽和與轉換增益」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用單一增益數值代表動態範圍」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：讀噪需換算到同一電子或電壓單位。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Saturation and conversion gain artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Representing dynamic range by gain alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Read noise needs consistent electron or voltage units. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量；讀噪需換算到同一電子或電壓單位。","observationEn":"Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well; Read noise needs consistent electron or voltage units.","failure":"若採用「用單一增益數值代表動態範圍」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Representing dynamic range by gain alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「飽和與轉換增益」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「讀噪需換算到同一電子或電壓單位」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Saturation and conversion gain, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Read noise needs consistent electron or voltage units\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-12-k1","title":"飽和與轉換增益／物理與模型","titleEn":"Saturation and conversion gain / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：讀噪需換算到同一電子或電壓單位。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Read noise needs consistent electron or voltage units."},{"id":"a078-v8-12-k2","title":"飽和與轉換增益／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Saturation and conversion gain / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用單一增益數值代表動態範圍」與「更高電壓轉換增益不等於更高滿井容量」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Representing dynamic range by gain alone\" is not equivalent to \"Higher voltage conversion gain does not imply greater full well\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「飽和與轉換增益」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Saturation and conversion gain?","options":["用單一增益數值代表動態範圍","電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾","讀噪需換算到同一電子或電壓單位"],"optionsEn":["Representing dynamic range by gain alone","Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation","Read noise needs consistent electron or voltage units"],"answer":2,"explanation":"讀噪需換算到同一電子或電壓單位；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Read noise needs consistent electron or voltage units. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a078-stage03","order":3,"title":"像素隔離 → 堆疊接口","titleEn":"Pixel isolation to Stacked interfaces","description":"把「像素隔離」「微透鏡與濾色」「堆疊接口」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pixel isolation, Microlenses and filters, Stacked interfaces.","steps":[{"id":"a078-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-12"],"title":"像素隔離：建立模型","titleEn":"Pixel isolation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optical isolation and charge isolation differ.","instruction":"畫光學與載子兩種串擾路徑，為溝槽隔離指定對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw optical/carrier crosstalk paths and controls for trench isolation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事；深溝槽也可能引入新表面缺陷。","observationEn":"Optical isolation and charge isolation differ; Deep trenches can introduce new surface defects.","failure":"若採用「電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「像素隔離」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事。","checkEn":"Submit the Pixel isolation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optical isolation and charge isolation differ.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-13-k1","title":"像素隔離／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel isolation / Physics and model","text":"機制：光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optical isolation and charge isolation differ."},{"id":"a078-v8-13-k2","title":"像素隔離／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel isolation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「像素隔離」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pixel isolation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事","電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾","全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Optical isolation and charge isolation differ","Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation","Assuming identical optical conditions across the image"],"answer":0,"explanation":"光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optical isolation and charge isolation differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-13"],"title":"像素隔離：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pixel isolation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation.","instruction":"接續前一步「像素隔離」成果，先指出錯誤主張「電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：深溝槽也可能引入新表面缺陷。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pixel isolation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Deep trenches can introduce new surface defects. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事；深溝槽也可能引入新表面缺陷。","observationEn":"Optical isolation and charge isolation differ; Deep trenches can introduce new surface defects.","failure":"若採用「電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「像素隔離」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「深溝槽也可能引入新表面缺陷」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pixel isolation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Deep trenches can introduce new surface defects\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-14-k1","title":"像素隔離／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel isolation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：深溝槽也可能引入新表面缺陷。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Deep trenches can introduce new surface defects."},{"id":"a078-v8-14-k2","title":"像素隔離／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel isolation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾」與「光學隔離與電荷隔離不是同一件事」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation\" is not equivalent to \"Optical isolation and charge isolation differ\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「像素隔離」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pixel isolation?","options":["全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同","深溝槽也可能引入新表面缺陷","電性隔離合格便推定無光學串擾"],"optionsEn":["Assuming identical optical conditions across the image","Deep trenches can introduce new surface defects","Inferring no optical crosstalk from electrical isolation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"深溝槽也可能引入新表面缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Deep trenches can introduce new surface defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-14"],"title":"微透鏡與濾色：建立模型","titleEn":"Microlenses and filters: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光學堆疊對位要配合入射角」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle.","instruction":"畫斜入射在邊緣像素的光路，檢查微透鏡偏移與濾色對位。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Trace oblique rays at edge pixels and check microlens/filter registration. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"光學堆疊對位要配合入射角；濾色材料也有角度與光譜依賴。","observationEn":"Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle; Color filters have angular and spectral dependence.","failure":"若採用「全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming identical optical conditions across the image\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「微透鏡與濾色」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光學堆疊對位要配合入射角。","checkEn":"Submit the Microlenses and filters diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-15-k1","title":"微透鏡與濾色／物理與模型","titleEn":"Microlenses and filters / Physics and model","text":"機制：光學堆疊對位要配合入射角。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle."},{"id":"a078-v8-15-k2","title":"微透鏡與濾色／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Microlenses and filters / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming identical optical conditions across the image."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「微透鏡與濾色」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Microlenses and filters, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同","堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格","光學堆疊對位要配合入射角"],"optionsEn":["Assuming identical optical conditions across the image","Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification","Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle"],"answer":2,"explanation":"光學堆疊對位要配合入射角；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-15"],"title":"微透鏡與濾色：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Microlenses and filters: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming identical optical conditions across the image.","instruction":"接續前一步「微透鏡與濾色」成果，先指出錯誤主張「全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：濾色材料也有角度與光譜依賴。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Microlenses and filters artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming identical optical conditions across the image\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Color filters have angular and spectral dependence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光學堆疊對位要配合入射角；濾色材料也有角度與光譜依賴。","observationEn":"Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle; Color filters have angular and spectral dependence.","failure":"若採用「全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming identical optical conditions across the image\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「微透鏡與濾色」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「濾色材料也有角度與光譜依賴」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Microlenses and filters, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Color filters have angular and spectral dependence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-16-k1","title":"微透鏡與濾色／物理與模型","titleEn":"Microlenses and filters / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：濾色材料也有角度與光譜依賴。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Color filters have angular and spectral dependence."},{"id":"a078-v8-16-k2","title":"微透鏡與濾色／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Microlenses and filters / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同」與「光學堆疊對位要配合入射角」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming identical optical conditions across the image\" is not equivalent to \"Optical-stack registration depends on incidence angle\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「微透鏡與濾色」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Microlenses and filters?","options":["濾色材料也有角度與光譜依賴","全畫面所有像素光學條件完全相同","堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格"],"optionsEn":["Color filters have angular and spectral dependence","Assuming identical optical conditions across the image","Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"濾色材料也有角度與光譜依賴；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Color filters have angular and spectral dependence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-16"],"title":"堆疊接口：建立模型","titleEn":"Stacked interfaces: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements.","instruction":"分開像素、像素電晶體與邏輯層，追蹤一條跨層訊號。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate pixel, pixel-transistor and logic layers and trace an inter-tier signal. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求；跨層連接失效可表現為局部壞點。","observationEn":"Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements; Inter-tier faults can appear as local bad pixels.","failure":"若採用「堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「堆疊接口」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求。","checkEn":"Submit the Stacked interfaces diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-17-k1","title":"堆疊接口／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stacked interfaces / Physics and model","text":"機制：分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements."},{"id":"a078-v8-17-k2","title":"堆疊接口／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stacked interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堆疊接口」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Stacked interfaces, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同時輸出資料就等於全域快門","分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求","堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格"],"optionsEn":["Equating simultaneous output with global shutter","Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements","Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-17"],"title":"堆疊接口：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Stacked interfaces: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification.","instruction":"接續前一步「堆疊接口」成果，先指出錯誤主張「堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：跨層連接失效可表現為局部壞點。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Stacked interfaces artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Inter-tier faults can appear as local bad pixels. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求；跨層連接失效可表現為局部壞點。","observationEn":"Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements; Inter-tier faults can appear as local bad pixels.","failure":"若採用「堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「堆疊接口」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「跨層連接失效可表現為局部壞點」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Stacked interfaces, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Inter-tier faults can appear as local bad pixels\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-18-k1","title":"堆疊接口／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stacked interfaces / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：跨層連接失效可表現為局部壞點。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Inter-tier faults can appear as local bad pixels."},{"id":"a078-v8-18-k2","title":"堆疊接口／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stacked interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格」與「分層允許不同製程最佳化但增加互連要求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification\" is not equivalent to \"Separate tiers allow process optimization but add interconnect requirements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「堆疊接口」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Stacked interfaces?","options":["堆疊後所有層都可完全獨立不需介面規格","同時輸出資料就等於全域快門","跨層連接失效可表現為局部壞點"],"optionsEn":["Assuming stacked tiers require no interface specification","Equating simultaneous output with global shutter","Inter-tier faults can appear as local bad pixels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨層連接失效可表現為局部壞點；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Inter-tier faults can appear as local bad pixels. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a078-stage04","order":4,"title":"讀出時間 → 感測器驗收","titleEn":"Readout timing to Sensor acceptance","description":"把「讀出時間」「均勻場校正」「感測器驗收」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Readout timing, Flat-field calibration, Sensor acceptance.","steps":[{"id":"a078-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-18"],"title":"讀出時間：建立模型","titleEn":"Readout timing: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order.","instruction":"畫逐列與同時曝光的時間圖，預測移動物體形變。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw rolling/global exposure timing and predict moving-object distortion. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念；全域快門也有儲存節點限制。","observationEn":"Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order; Global shutters also have storage-node constraints.","failure":"若採用「同時輸出資料就等於全域快門」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating simultaneous output with global shutter\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「讀出時間」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念。","checkEn":"Submit the Readout timing diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-19-k1","title":"讀出時間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Readout timing / Physics and model","text":"機制：曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念。","textEn":"Mechanism: Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order."},{"id":"a078-v8-19-k2","title":"讀出時間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Readout timing / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同時輸出資料就等於全域快門」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating simultaneous output with global shutter."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「讀出時間」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Readout timing, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念","同時輸出資料就等於全域快門","一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異"],"optionsEn":["Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order","Equating simultaneous output with global shutter","Using one dark frame for all response variation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-19"],"title":"讀出時間：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Readout timing: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同時輸出資料就等於全域快門」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating simultaneous output with global shutter.","instruction":"接續前一步「讀出時間」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同時輸出資料就等於全域快門」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：全域快門也有儲存節點限制。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Readout timing artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating simultaneous output with global shutter\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Global shutters also have storage-node constraints. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念；全域快門也有儲存節點限制。","observationEn":"Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order; Global shutters also have storage-node constraints.","failure":"若採用「同時輸出資料就等於全域快門」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating simultaneous output with global shutter\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「讀出時間」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「全域快門也有儲存節點限制」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Readout timing, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Global shutters also have storage-node constraints\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-20-k1","title":"讀出時間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Readout timing / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：全域快門也有儲存節點限制。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Global shutters also have storage-node constraints."},{"id":"a078-v8-20-k2","title":"讀出時間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Readout timing / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同時輸出資料就等於全域快門」與「曝光同步與資料輸出順序是不同概念」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating simultaneous output with global shutter\" is not equivalent to \"Exposure synchronization differs from data-output order\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「讀出時間」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Readout timing?","options":["一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異","全域快門也有儲存節點限制","同時輸出資料就等於全域快門"],"optionsEn":["Using one dark frame for all response variation","Global shutters also have storage-node constraints","Equating simultaneous output with global shutter"],"answer":1,"explanation":"全域快門也有儲存節點限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Global shutters also have storage-node constraints. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-20"],"title":"均勻場校正：建立模型","titleEn":"Flat-field calibration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity.","instruction":"用假設均勻照明影像分離暗偏移與光響應非均勻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate dark offset from response nonuniformity in hypothetical flat fields. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均；光源不均須先與像素不均分離。","observationEn":"Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity; Separate illumination nonuniformity from sensor nonuniformity.","failure":"若採用「一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one dark frame for all response variation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「均勻場校正」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均。","checkEn":"Submit the Flat-field calibration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-21-k1","title":"均勻場校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Flat-field calibration / Physics and model","text":"機制：暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均。","textEn":"Mechanism: Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity."},{"id":"a078-v8-21-k2","title":"均勻場校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Flat-field calibration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one dark frame for all response variation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「均勻場校正」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Flat-field calibration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異","畫素越多就必然弱光越好","暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均"],"optionsEn":["Using one dark frame for all response variation","Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance","Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity"],"answer":2,"explanation":"暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-21"],"title":"均勻場校正：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Flat-field calibration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one dark frame for all response variation.","instruction":"接續前一步「均勻場校正」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：光源不均須先與像素不均分離。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Flat-field calibration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one dark frame for all response variation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Separate illumination nonuniformity from sensor nonuniformity. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均；光源不均須先與像素不均分離。","observationEn":"Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity; Separate illumination nonuniformity from sensor nonuniformity.","failure":"若採用「一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one dark frame for all response variation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「均勻場校正」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「光源不均須先與像素不均分離」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Flat-field calibration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Separate illumination nonuniformity from sensor nonuniformity\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-22-k1","title":"均勻場校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Flat-field calibration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：光源不均須先與像素不均分離。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Separate illumination nonuniformity from sensor nonuniformity."},{"id":"a078-v8-22-k2","title":"均勻場校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Flat-field calibration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異」與「暗場扣除不能單獨消除增益不均」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one dark frame for all response variation\" is not equivalent to \"Dark subtraction alone cannot remove gain nonuniformity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「均勻場校正」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Flat-field calibration?","options":["光源不均須先與像素不均分離","一張暗場可校正全部光響應差異","畫素越多就必然弱光越好"],"optionsEn":["Separate illumination nonuniformity from sensor nonuniformity","Using one dark frame for all response variation","Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"光源不均須先與像素不均分離；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Separate illumination nonuniformity from sensor nonuniformity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-22"],"title":"感測器驗收：建立模型","titleEn":"Sensor acceptance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count.","instruction":"整合 QE、讀噪、滿井、壞點和串擾，保留曝光及溫度條件。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine QE, read noise, full well, bad pixels and crosstalk with conditions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數；數位增益不會提高入射光子統計。","observationEn":"Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count; Digital gain does not improve incident-photon statistics.","failure":"若採用「畫素越多就必然弱光越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「感測器驗收」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數。","checkEn":"Submit the Sensor acceptance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-23-k1","title":"感測器驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sensor acceptance / Physics and model","text":"機制：影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數。","textEn":"Mechanism: Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count."},{"id":"a078-v8-23-k2","title":"感測器驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sensor acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「畫素越多就必然弱光越好」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「感測器驗收」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Sensor acceptance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標","影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數","畫素越多就必然弱光越好"],"optionsEn":["Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain","Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count","Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a078-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cis","v8-c-cis-two","v8-c-imaging"],"prerequisiteIds":["a078-v8-23"],"title":"感測器驗收：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Sensor acceptance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「畫素越多就必然弱光越好」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance.","instruction":"接續前一步「感測器驗收」成果，先指出錯誤主張「畫素越多就必然弱光越好」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：數位增益不會提高入射光子統計。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Sensor acceptance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Digital gain does not improve incident-photon statistics. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數；數位增益不會提高入射光子統計。","observationEn":"Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count; Digital gain does not improve incident-photon statistics.","failure":"若採用「畫素越多就必然弱光越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「感測器驗收」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「數位增益不會提高入射光子統計」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Sensor acceptance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Digital gain does not improve incident-photon statistics\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a078-v8-24-k1","title":"感測器驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sensor acceptance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：數位增益不會提高入射光子統計。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Digital gain does not improve incident-photon statistics."},{"id":"a078-v8-24-k2","title":"感測器驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sensor acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「畫素越多就必然弱光越好」與「影像品質需多條證據而非只看像素數」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance\" is not equivalent to \"Image quality needs more evidence than pixel count\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「感測器驗收」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Sensor acceptance?","options":["畫素越多就必然弱光越好","把量子效率和電壓增益當同一指標","數位增益不會提高入射光子統計"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more pixels guarantee better low-light performance","Equating quantum efficiency with voltage gain","Digital gain does not improve incident-photon statistics"],"answer":2,"explanation":"數位增益不會提高入射光子統計；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Digital gain does not improve incident-photon statistics. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"sensors","subcategoryTitle":"影像與光子感測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Image and photon sensors"},{"id":"a079","title":"雪崩光二極體製作","titleEn":"Avalanche photodiode fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-ham-place","v8-c-ham-history","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從吸收與倍增、暗電流來源到偵測系統：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Absorption and multiplication and Dark-current sources to Detection system: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["吸收與倍增","倍增雜訊","頻寬限制","接觸與封裝"],"labelsEn":["Absorption and multiplication","Multiplication noise","Bandwidth limits","Contacts and package"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a079-stage01","order":1,"title":"吸收與倍增 → 場形塑","titleEn":"Absorption and multiplication to Field shaping","description":"把「吸收與倍增」「線性模式」「場形塑」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Absorption and multiplication, Linear mode, Field shaping.","steps":[{"id":"a079-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"吸收與倍增：建立模型","titleEn":"Absorption and multiplication: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements.","instruction":"畫吸收區與高電場倍增區，追蹤一對光生載子。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw absorption/multiplication regions and track a photogenerated pair. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求；電子和電洞游離率可能不同。","observationEn":"Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements; Electron and hole ionization rates can differ.","failure":"若採用「把整個元件都畫成相同高場」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Drawing uniform high field throughout the device\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「吸收與倍增」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求。","checkEn":"Submit the Absorption and multiplication diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-01-k1","title":"吸收與倍增／物理與模型","titleEn":"Absorption and multiplication / Physics and model","text":"機制：光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements."},{"id":"a079-v8-01-k2","title":"吸收與倍增／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Absorption and multiplication / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把整個元件都畫成相同高場」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Drawing uniform high field throughout the device."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吸收與倍增」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Absorption and multiplication, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求","把整個元件都畫成相同高場","APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上"],"optionsEn":["Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements","Drawing uniform high field throughout the device","Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-01"],"title":"吸收與倍增：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Absorption and multiplication: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把整個元件都畫成相同高場」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Drawing uniform high field throughout the device.","instruction":"接續前一步「吸收與倍增」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把整個元件都畫成相同高場」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電子和電洞游離率可能不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Absorption and multiplication artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Drawing uniform high field throughout the device\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electron and hole ionization rates can differ. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求；電子和電洞游離率可能不同。","observationEn":"Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements; Electron and hole ionization rates can differ.","failure":"若採用「把整個元件都畫成相同高場」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Drawing uniform high field throughout the device\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「吸收與倍增」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電子和電洞游離率可能不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Absorption and multiplication, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electron and hole ionization rates can differ\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-02-k1","title":"吸收與倍增／物理與模型","titleEn":"Absorption and multiplication / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電子和電洞游離率可能不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electron and hole ionization rates can differ."},{"id":"a079-v8-02-k2","title":"吸收與倍增／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Absorption and multiplication / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把整個元件都畫成相同高場」與「光吸收與雪崩倍增可有不同空間要求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Drawing uniform high field throughout the device\" is not equivalent to \"Absorption and avalanche multiplication have different spatial requirements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「吸收與倍增」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Absorption and multiplication?","options":["APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上","電子和電洞游離率可能不同","把整個元件都畫成相同高場"],"optionsEn":["Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation","Electron and hole ionization rates can differ","Drawing uniform high field throughout the device"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電子和電洞游離率可能不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electron and hole ionization rates can differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-02"],"title":"線性模式：建立模型","titleEn":"Linear mode: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering.","instruction":"在增益對偏壓曲線標出崩潰前工作範圍。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark the pre-breakdown operating region on a gain-bias plot. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同；串聯電阻會改變接面實際偏壓。","observationEn":"Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering; Series resistance changes actual junction bias.","failure":"若採用「APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「線性模式」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Linear mode diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-03-k1","title":"線性模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Linear mode / Physics and model","text":"機制：線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering."},{"id":"a079-v8-03-k2","title":"線性模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Linear mode / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「線性模式」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Linear mode, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上","只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置","線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同"],"optionsEn":["Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation","Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone","Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering"],"answer":2,"explanation":"線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-03"],"title":"線性模式：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Linear mode: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation.","instruction":"接續前一步「線性模式」成果，先指出錯誤主張「APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：串聯電阻會改變接面實際偏壓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Linear mode artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Series resistance changes actual junction bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同；串聯電阻會改變接面實際偏壓。","observationEn":"Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering; Series resistance changes actual junction bias.","failure":"若採用「APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「線性模式」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「串聯電阻會改變接面實際偏壓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Linear mode, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Series resistance changes actual junction bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-04-k1","title":"線性模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Linear mode / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：串聯電阻會改變接面實際偏壓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Series resistance changes actual junction bias."},{"id":"a079-v8-04-k2","title":"線性模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Linear mode / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上」與「線性 APD 增益與 Geiger 觸發不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation\" is not equivalent to \"Linear APD gain differs from Geiger triggering\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「線性模式」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Linear mode?","options":["串聯電阻會改變接面實際偏壓","APD 有增益便必須工作在崩潰以上","只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置"],"optionsEn":["Series resistance changes actual junction bias","Assuming gain requires above-breakdown operation","Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"串聯電阻會改變接面實際偏壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Series resistance changes actual junction bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-04"],"title":"場形塑：建立模型","titleEn":"Field shaping: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Edges can break down before the central region.","instruction":"畫平面接面及邊緣曲率，說明護環如何改變局部場。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw planar and curved junction edges and explain guard-ring field shaping. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰；表面電荷也會扭曲邊緣電場。","observationEn":"Edges can break down before the central region; Surface charge distorts edge fields.","failure":"若採用「只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「場形塑」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰。","checkEn":"Submit the Field shaping diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Edges can break down before the central region.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-05-k1","title":"場形塑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field shaping / Physics and model","text":"機制：邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰。","textEn":"Mechanism: Edges can break down before the central region."},{"id":"a079-v8-05-k2","title":"場形塑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field shaping / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「場形塑」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Field shaping, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大","邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰","只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置"],"optionsEn":["Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification","Edges can break down before the central region","Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edges can break down before the central region. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-05"],"title":"場形塑：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Field shaping: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「場形塑」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：表面電荷也會扭曲邊緣電場。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Field shaping artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Surface charge distorts edge fields. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰；表面電荷也會扭曲邊緣電場。","observationEn":"Edges can break down before the central region; Surface charge distorts edge fields.","failure":"若採用「只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「場形塑」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「表面電荷也會扭曲邊緣電場」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Field shaping, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Surface charge distorts edge fields\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-06-k1","title":"場形塑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field shaping / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：表面電荷也會扭曲邊緣電場。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Surface charge distorts edge fields."},{"id":"a079-v8-06-k2","title":"場形塑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field shaping / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置」與「邊緣可能先於中央發生崩潰」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone\" is not equivalent to \"Edges can break down before the central region\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「場形塑」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Field shaping?","options":["只用平均接面電場判斷崩潰位置","把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大","表面電荷也會扭曲邊緣電場"],"optionsEn":["Locating breakdown from mean junction field alone","Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification","Surface charge distorts edge fields"],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面電荷也會扭曲邊緣電場；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface charge distorts edge fields. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a079-stage02","order":2,"title":"倍增雜訊 → 溫度補償","titleEn":"Multiplication noise to Temperature compensation","description":"把「倍增雜訊」「暗電流來源」「溫度補償」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Multiplication noise, Dark-current sources, Temperature compensation.","steps":[{"id":"a079-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-06"],"title":"倍增雜訊：建立模型","titleEn":"Multiplication noise: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Avalanche randomness adds signal variance.","instruction":"比較同均值不同脈衝電荷變異的資料，定義額外雜訊。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare equal-mean signals with different charge variance and define excess noise. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異；額外雜訊需在相同增益比較。","observationEn":"Avalanche randomness adds signal variance; Compare excess noise at matched gain.","failure":"若採用「把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「倍增雜訊」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異。","checkEn":"Submit the Multiplication noise diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Avalanche randomness adds signal variance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-07-k1","title":"倍增雜訊／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multiplication noise / Physics and model","text":"機制：雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異。","textEn":"Mechanism: Avalanche randomness adds signal variance."},{"id":"a079-v8-07-k2","title":"倍增雜訊／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multiplication noise / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「倍增雜訊」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Multiplication noise, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異","把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大","把全部暗電流一律乘以 M"],"optionsEn":["Avalanche randomness adds signal variance","Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification","Multiplying every dark-current component by M"],"answer":0,"explanation":"雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Avalanche randomness adds signal variance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-07"],"title":"倍增雜訊：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Multiplication noise: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification.","instruction":"接續前一步「倍增雜訊」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：額外雜訊需在相同增益比較。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Multiplication noise artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Compare excess noise at matched gain. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異；額外雜訊需在相同增益比較。","observationEn":"Avalanche randomness adds signal variance; Compare excess noise at matched gain.","failure":"若採用「把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「倍增雜訊」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「額外雜訊需在相同增益比較」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Multiplication noise, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Compare excess noise at matched gain\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-08-k1","title":"倍增雜訊／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multiplication noise / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：額外雜訊需在相同增益比較。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Compare excess noise at matched gain."},{"id":"a079-v8-08-k2","title":"倍增雜訊／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multiplication noise / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大」與「雪崩的隨機性會增加訊號變異」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification\" is not equivalent to \"Avalanche randomness adds signal variance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「倍增雜訊」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Multiplication noise?","options":["把全部暗電流一律乘以 M","額外雜訊需在相同增益比較","把內部增益當成完全無雜訊放大"],"optionsEn":["Multiplying every dark-current component by M","Compare excess noise at matched gain","Treating internal gain as noiseless amplification"],"answer":1,"explanation":"額外雜訊需在相同增益比較；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Compare excess noise at matched gain. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-08"],"title":"暗電流來源：建立模型","titleEn":"Dark-current sources: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Not all dark-current components share multiplication.","instruction":"分開表面漏電與經倍增區的體生成電流。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate surface leakage from multiplied bulk-generated current. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子；暗電流需要和量測帶寬一起解釋。","observationEn":"Not all dark-current components share multiplication; Interpret dark current with measurement bandwidth.","failure":"若採用「把全部暗電流一律乘以 M」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Multiplying every dark-current component by M\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「暗電流來源」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子。","checkEn":"Submit the Dark-current sources diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Not all dark-current components share multiplication.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-09-k1","title":"暗電流來源／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dark-current sources / Physics and model","text":"機制：並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子。","textEn":"Mechanism: Not all dark-current components share multiplication."},{"id":"a079-v8-09-k2","title":"暗電流來源／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dark-current sources / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把全部暗電流一律乘以 M」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Multiplying every dark-current component by M."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「暗電流來源」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dark-current sources, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把全部暗電流一律乘以 M","固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益","並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子"],"optionsEn":["Multiplying every dark-current component by M","Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures","Not all dark-current components share multiplication"],"answer":2,"explanation":"並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Not all dark-current components share multiplication. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-09"],"title":"暗電流來源：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dark-current sources: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把全部暗電流一律乘以 M」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Multiplying every dark-current component by M.","instruction":"接續前一步「暗電流來源」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把全部暗電流一律乘以 M」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：暗電流需要和量測帶寬一起解釋。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dark-current sources artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Multiplying every dark-current component by M\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Interpret dark current with measurement bandwidth. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子；暗電流需要和量測帶寬一起解釋。","observationEn":"Not all dark-current components share multiplication; Interpret dark current with measurement bandwidth.","failure":"若採用「把全部暗電流一律乘以 M」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Multiplying every dark-current component by M\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「暗電流來源」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「暗電流需要和量測帶寬一起解釋」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dark-current sources, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Interpret dark current with measurement bandwidth\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-10-k1","title":"暗電流來源／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dark-current sources / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：暗電流需要和量測帶寬一起解釋。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Interpret dark current with measurement bandwidth."},{"id":"a079-v8-10-k2","title":"暗電流來源／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dark-current sources / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把全部暗電流一律乘以 M」與「並非所有暗電流都乘上相同倍增因子」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Multiplying every dark-current component by M\" is not equivalent to \"Not all dark-current components share multiplication\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「暗電流來源」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dark-current sources?","options":["暗電流需要和量測帶寬一起解釋","把全部暗電流一律乘以 M","固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益"],"optionsEn":["Interpret dark current with measurement bandwidth","Multiplying every dark-current component by M","Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures"],"answer":0,"explanation":"暗電流需要和量測帶寬一起解釋；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Interpret dark current with measurement bandwidth. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-10"],"title":"溫度補償：建立模型","titleEn":"Temperature compensation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions.","instruction":"畫兩溫度的增益偏壓曲線，找保持相同增益的偏壓差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw gain-bias curves at two temperatures and find equal-gain bias differences. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件；偏壓補償需避免溫度感測延遲。","observationEn":"Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions; Bias compensation must consider thermal-sensor lag.","failure":"若採用「固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「溫度補償」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件。","checkEn":"Submit the Temperature compensation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-11-k1","title":"溫度補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Physics and model","text":"機制：溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions."},{"id":"a079-v8-11-k2","title":"溫度補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度補償」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Temperature compensation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度","溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件","固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益"],"optionsEn":["Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed","Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions","Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures"],"answer":1,"explanation":"溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-11"],"title":"溫度補償：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Temperature compensation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures.","instruction":"接續前一步「溫度補償」成果，先指出錯誤主張「固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：偏壓補償需避免溫度感測延遲。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Temperature compensation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bias compensation must consider thermal-sensor lag. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件；偏壓補償需避免溫度感測延遲。","observationEn":"Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions; Bias compensation must consider thermal-sensor lag.","failure":"若採用「固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「溫度補償」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「偏壓補償需避免溫度感測延遲」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Temperature compensation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bias compensation must consider thermal-sensor lag\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-12-k1","title":"溫度補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：偏壓補償需避免溫度感測延遲。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bias compensation must consider thermal-sensor lag."},{"id":"a079-v8-12-k2","title":"溫度補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益」與「溫度改變會移動增益與崩潰條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures\" is not equivalent to \"Temperature changes gain and breakdown conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「溫度補償」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Temperature compensation?","options":["固定偏壓即可保證全年固定增益","只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度","偏壓補償需避免溫度感測延遲"],"optionsEn":["Assuming fixed bias guarantees fixed gain across temperatures","Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed","Bias compensation must consider thermal-sensor lag"],"answer":2,"explanation":"偏壓補償需避免溫度感測延遲；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bias compensation must consider thermal-sensor lag. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a079-stage03","order":3,"title":"頻寬限制 → 面積與電容","titleEn":"Bandwidth limits to Area and capacitance","description":"把「頻寬限制」「光譜響應」「面積與電容」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Bandwidth limits, Spectral response, Area and capacitance.","steps":[{"id":"a079-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-12"],"title":"頻寬限制：建立模型","titleEn":"Bandwidth limits: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「最慢動態環節會限制響應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The slowest dynamic process limits response.","instruction":"並列 RC 時間、載子渡越與雪崩建立時間的時間常數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare RC, carrier transit and avalanche buildup time constants. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"最慢動態環節會限制響應；增益建立時間造成增益頻寬取捨。","observationEn":"The slowest dynamic process limits response; Avalanche buildup creates gain-bandwidth tradeoffs.","failure":"若採用「只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「頻寬限制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：最慢動態環節會限制響應。","checkEn":"Submit the Bandwidth limits diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The slowest dynamic process limits response.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-13-k1","title":"頻寬限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bandwidth limits / Physics and model","text":"機制：最慢動態環節會限制響應。","textEn":"Mechanism: The slowest dynamic process limits response."},{"id":"a079-v8-13-k2","title":"頻寬限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bandwidth limits / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「頻寬限制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Bandwidth limits, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["最慢動態環節會限制響應","只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度","用單一波長響應代表全光譜"],"optionsEn":["The slowest dynamic process limits response","Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed","Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum"],"answer":0,"explanation":"最慢動態環節會限制響應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The slowest dynamic process limits response. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-13"],"title":"頻寬限制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Bandwidth limits: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed.","instruction":"接續前一步「頻寬限制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：增益建立時間造成增益頻寬取捨。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Bandwidth limits artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Avalanche buildup creates gain-bandwidth tradeoffs. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"最慢動態環節會限制響應；增益建立時間造成增益頻寬取捨。","observationEn":"The slowest dynamic process limits response; Avalanche buildup creates gain-bandwidth tradeoffs.","failure":"若採用「只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「頻寬限制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「增益建立時間造成增益頻寬取捨」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Bandwidth limits, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Avalanche buildup creates gain-bandwidth tradeoffs\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-14-k1","title":"頻寬限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bandwidth limits / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：增益建立時間造成增益頻寬取捨。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Avalanche buildup creates gain-bandwidth tradeoffs."},{"id":"a079-v8-14-k2","title":"頻寬限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bandwidth limits / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度」與「最慢動態環節會限制響應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed\" is not equivalent to \"The slowest dynamic process limits response\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「頻寬限制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Bandwidth limits?","options":["用單一波長響應代表全光譜","增益建立時間造成增益頻寬取捨","只降低外部電阻就無限制提升速度"],"optionsEn":["Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum","Avalanche buildup creates gain-bandwidth tradeoffs","Assuming resistance reduction provides unlimited speed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"增益建立時間造成增益頻寬取捨；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Avalanche buildup creates gain-bandwidth tradeoffs. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-14"],"title":"光譜響應：建立模型","titleEn":"Spectral response: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength.","instruction":"將不同波長吸收深度與倍增區重疊比較。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare wavelength-dependent absorption depth with multiplication-region overlap. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴；表面反射會改變有效入射光通量。","observationEn":"Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength; Reflection changes effective incident flux.","failure":"若採用「用單一波長響應代表全光譜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「光譜響應」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴。","checkEn":"Submit the Spectral response diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-15-k1","title":"光譜響應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Spectral response / Physics and model","text":"機制：有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴。","textEn":"Mechanism: Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength."},{"id":"a079-v8-15-k2","title":"光譜響應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Spectral response / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用單一波長響應代表全光譜」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「光譜響應」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Spectral response, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用單一波長響應代表全光譜","大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳","有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴"],"optionsEn":["Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum","Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed","Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength"],"answer":2,"explanation":"有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-15"],"title":"光譜響應：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Spectral response: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用單一波長響應代表全光譜」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum.","instruction":"接續前一步「光譜響應」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用單一波長響應代表全光譜」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：表面反射會改變有效入射光通量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Spectral response artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reflection changes effective incident flux. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴；表面反射會改變有效入射光通量。","observationEn":"Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength; Reflection changes effective incident flux.","failure":"若採用「用單一波長響應代表全光譜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「光譜響應」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「表面反射會改變有效入射光通量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Spectral response, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reflection changes effective incident flux\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-16-k1","title":"光譜響應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Spectral response / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：表面反射會改變有效入射光通量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reflection changes effective incident flux."},{"id":"a079-v8-16-k2","title":"光譜響應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Spectral response / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用單一波長響應代表全光譜」與「有效增益與收集效率可能有光譜依賴」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum\" is not equivalent to \"Effective gain and collection can depend on wavelength\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「光譜響應」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Spectral response?","options":["表面反射會改變有效入射光通量","用單一波長響應代表全光譜","大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳"],"optionsEn":["Reflection changes effective incident flux","Using one wavelength for the entire spectrum","Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面反射會改變有效入射光通量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reflection changes effective incident flux. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-16"],"title":"面積與電容：建立模型","titleEn":"Area and capacitance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading.","instruction":"對兩個假設接面面積比較收光、電容與暗電流。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare collection, capacitance and dark current for two areas. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載；大面積也增加缺陷採樣機會。","observationEn":"Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading; Large area also samples more defects.","failure":"若採用「大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「面積與電容」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載。","checkEn":"Submit the Area and capacitance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-17-k1","title":"面積與電容／物理與模型","titleEn":"Area and capacitance / Physics and model","text":"機制：增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載。","textEn":"Mechanism: Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading."},{"id":"a079-v8-17-k2","title":"面積與電容／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Area and capacitance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「面積與電容」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Area and capacitance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看裸晶參數推定模組表現","增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載","大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳"],"optionsEn":["Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone","Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading","Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed"],"answer":1,"explanation":"增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-17"],"title":"面積與電容：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Area and capacitance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed.","instruction":"接續前一步「面積與電容」成果，先指出錯誤主張「大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：大面積也增加缺陷採樣機會。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Area and capacitance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Large area also samples more defects. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載；大面積也增加缺陷採樣機會。","observationEn":"Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading; Large area also samples more defects.","failure":"若採用「大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「面積與電容」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「大面積也增加缺陷採樣機會」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Area and capacitance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Large area also samples more defects\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-18-k1","title":"面積與電容／物理與模型","titleEn":"Area and capacitance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：大面積也增加缺陷採樣機會。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Large area also samples more defects."},{"id":"a079-v8-18-k2","title":"面積與電容／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Area and capacitance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳」與「增大面積會同時改變光學與電路負載」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed\" is not equivalent to \"Larger area changes both optical collection and circuit loading\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「面積與電容」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Area and capacitance?","options":["大面積在靈敏度和速度上都必然最佳","只看裸晶參數推定模組表現","大面積也增加缺陷採樣機會"],"optionsEn":["Assuming largest area is always best for sensitivity and speed","Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone","Large area also samples more defects"],"answer":2,"explanation":"大面積也增加缺陷採樣機會；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Large area also samples more defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a079-stage04","order":4,"title":"接觸與封裝 → 偵測系統","titleEn":"Contacts and package to Detection system","description":"把「接觸與封裝」「增益校正」「偵測系統」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Contacts and package, Gain calibration, Detection system.","steps":[{"id":"a079-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-18"],"title":"接觸與封裝：建立模型","titleEn":"Contacts and package: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「封裝可限制晶片原有響應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response.","instruction":"畫反射窗口、鍵合線與放大器輸入，列出寄生和遮光。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw window, bonds and amplifier input with parasitics and shading. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"封裝可限制晶片原有響應；接收窗污染可能造成靈敏度下降。","observationEn":"Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response; Window contamination can reduce sensitivity.","failure":"若採用「只看裸晶參數推定模組表現」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸與封裝」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：封裝可限制晶片原有響應。","checkEn":"Submit the Contacts and package diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-19-k1","title":"接觸與封裝／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contacts and package / Physics and model","text":"機制：封裝可限制晶片原有響應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response."},{"id":"a079-v8-19-k2","title":"接觸與封裝／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and package / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看裸晶參數推定模組表現」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸與封裝」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Contacts and package, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["封裝可限制晶片原有響應","只看裸晶參數推定模組表現","不同光強下的電流比直接當 M"],"optionsEn":["Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response","Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone","Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain"],"answer":0,"explanation":"封裝可限制晶片原有響應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-19"],"title":"接觸與封裝：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Contacts and package: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看裸晶參數推定模組表現」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸與封裝」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看裸晶參數推定模組表現」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接收窗污染可能造成靈敏度下降。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Contacts and package artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Window contamination can reduce sensitivity. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"封裝可限制晶片原有響應；接收窗污染可能造成靈敏度下降。","observationEn":"Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response; Window contamination can reduce sensitivity.","failure":"若採用「只看裸晶參數推定模組表現」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸與封裝」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接收窗污染可能造成靈敏度下降」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Contacts and package, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Window contamination can reduce sensitivity\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-20-k1","title":"接觸與封裝／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contacts and package / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接收窗污染可能造成靈敏度下降。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Window contamination can reduce sensitivity."},{"id":"a079-v8-20-k2","title":"接觸與封裝／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and package / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看裸晶參數推定模組表現」與「封裝可限制晶片原有響應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone\" is not equivalent to \"Packaging can limit intrinsic chip response\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸與封裝」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Contacts and package?","options":["不同光強下的電流比直接當 M","接收窗污染可能造成靈敏度下降","只看裸晶參數推定模組表現"],"optionsEn":["Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain","Window contamination can reduce sensitivity","Predicting module performance from bare-die parameters alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接收窗污染可能造成靈敏度下降；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Window contamination can reduce sensitivity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-20"],"title":"增益校正：建立模型","titleEn":"Gain calibration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光源漂移會混入增益估計」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Source drift contaminates gain estimates.","instruction":"用同光通量比較低倍增參考與工作偏壓電流並扣暗電流。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設相同光通量下，已扣暗電流的單位增益參考光電流為 10 nA，工作偏壓下為 200 nA，雪崩增益 M=200/10=20。若未扣暗電流便用總電流相除，可能偏差。此例假定參考確為 M=1，且不提供過剩雜訊或擊穿電壓資訊。","instructionEn":"Compare low-gain and operating currents at equal flux with dark subtraction. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume equal photon flux and dark-subtracted photocurrents of 10 nA at a unit-gain reference and 200 nA at operating bias. Avalanche gain M=200/10=20. Dividing total currents without dark subtraction can bias gain. The reference is assumed to have M=1; the example does not determine excess noise or breakdown voltage.","observation":"光源漂移會混入增益估計；低偏壓參考仍需確認收集效率。","observationEn":"Source drift contaminates gain estimates; Low-bias references still need collection checks.","failure":"若採用「不同光強下的電流比直接當 M」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「增益校正」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光源漂移會混入增益估計。\n算例驗收：驗算 M=20，寫出兩個必要條件：等光通量與暗電流扣除，另註明單位增益參考假設。","checkEn":"Submit the Gain calibration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Source drift contaminates gain estimates.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify M=20 and record equal flux, dark subtraction and the assumed unit-gain reference.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-21-k1","title":"增益校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gain calibration / Physics and model","text":"機制：光源漂移會混入增益估計。","textEn":"Mechanism: Source drift contaminates gain estimates."},{"id":"a079-v8-21-k2","title":"增益校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gain calibration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不同光強下的電流比直接當 M」。\n假設數值與推算：假設相同光通量下，已扣暗電流的單位增益參考光電流為 10 nA，工作偏壓下為 200 nA，雪崩增益 M=200/10=20。若未扣暗電流便用總電流相除，可能偏差。此例假定參考確為 M=1，且不提供過剩雜訊或擊穿電壓資訊。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume equal photon flux and dark-subtracted photocurrents of 10 nA at a unit-gain reference and 200 nA at operating bias. Avalanche gain M=200/10=20. Dividing total currents without dark subtraction can bias gain. The reference is assumed to have M=1; the example does not determine excess noise or breakdown voltage."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「增益校正」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Gain calibration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同光強下的電流比直接當 M","增益越高訊雜比永遠越好","光源漂移會混入增益估計"],"optionsEn":["Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain","Assuming SNR always increases with gain","Source drift contaminates gain estimates"],"answer":2,"explanation":"光源漂移會混入增益估計；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Source drift contaminates gain estimates. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-21"],"title":"增益校正：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Gain calibration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不同光強下的電流比直接當 M」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain.","instruction":"接續前一步「增益校正」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不同光強下的電流比直接當 M」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：低偏壓參考仍需確認收集效率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Gain calibration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Low-bias references still need collection checks. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光源漂移會混入增益估計；低偏壓參考仍需確認收集效率。","observationEn":"Source drift contaminates gain estimates; Low-bias references still need collection checks.","failure":"若採用「不同光強下的電流比直接當 M」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「增益校正」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「低偏壓參考仍需確認收集效率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Gain calibration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Low-bias references still need collection checks\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-22-k1","title":"增益校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gain calibration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：低偏壓參考仍需確認收集效率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Low-bias references still need collection checks."},{"id":"a079-v8-22-k2","title":"增益校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gain calibration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不同光強下的電流比直接當 M」與「光源漂移會混入增益估計」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain\" is not equivalent to \"Source drift contaminates gain estimates\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「增益校正」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Gain calibration?","options":["低偏壓參考仍需確認收集效率","不同光強下的電流比直接當 M","增益越高訊雜比永遠越好"],"optionsEn":["Low-bias references still need collection checks","Calling a ratio at different illumination the gain","Assuming SNR always increases with gain"],"answer":0,"explanation":"低偏壓參考仍需確認收集效率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low-bias references still need collection checks. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-22"],"title":"偵測系統：建立模型","titleEn":"Detection system: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget.","instruction":"合併光子雜訊、倍增雜訊與讀出雜訊，比較兩個假設增益。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine photon, multiplication and readout noise for two gains. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算；放大器輸入電容會影響最佳配置。","observationEn":"Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget; Amplifier input capacitance affects optimal configuration.","failure":"若採用「增益越高訊雜比永遠越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming SNR always increases with gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「偵測系統」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算。","checkEn":"Submit the Detection system diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-23-k1","title":"偵測系統／物理與模型","titleEn":"Detection system / Physics and model","text":"機制：最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget."},{"id":"a079-v8-23-k2","title":"偵測系統／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Detection system / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「增益越高訊雜比永遠越好」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming SNR always increases with gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偵測系統」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Detection system, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把整個元件都畫成相同高場","最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算","增益越高訊雜比永遠越好"],"optionsEn":["Drawing uniform high field throughout the device","Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget","Assuming SNR always increases with gain"],"answer":1,"explanation":"最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a079-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-apd","v8-c-sipm"],"prerequisiteIds":["a079-v8-23"],"title":"偵測系統：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Detection system: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「增益越高訊雜比永遠越好」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming SNR always increases with gain.","instruction":"接續前一步「偵測系統」成果，先指出錯誤主張「增益越高訊雜比永遠越好」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：放大器輸入電容會影響最佳配置。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Detection system artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming SNR always increases with gain\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Amplifier input capacitance affects optimal configuration. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算；放大器輸入電容會影響最佳配置。","observationEn":"Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget; Amplifier input capacitance affects optimal configuration.","failure":"若採用「增益越高訊雜比永遠越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming SNR always increases with gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「偵測系統」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「放大器輸入電容會影響最佳配置」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Detection system, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Amplifier input capacitance affects optimal configuration\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a079-v8-24-k1","title":"偵測系統／物理與模型","titleEn":"Detection system / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：放大器輸入電容會影響最佳配置。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Amplifier input capacitance affects optimal configuration."},{"id":"a079-v8-24-k2","title":"偵測系統／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Detection system / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「增益越高訊雜比永遠越好」與「最佳增益取決於整個雜訊預算」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming SNR always increases with gain\" is not equivalent to \"Optimal gain depends on the complete noise budget\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「偵測系統」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Detection system?","options":["增益越高訊雜比永遠越好","把整個元件都畫成相同高場","放大器輸入電容會影響最佳配置"],"optionsEn":["Assuming SNR always increases with gain","Drawing uniform high field throughout the device","Amplifier input capacitance affects optimal configuration"],"answer":2,"explanation":"放大器輸入電容會影響最佳配置；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Amplifier input capacitance affects optimal configuration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"sensors","subcategoryTitle":"影像與光子感測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Image and photon sensors"},{"id":"a080","title":"單光子雪崩二極體陣列","titleEn":"Single-photon avalanche-diode arrays","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof","v8-c-ham-place","v8-c-ham-history","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從Geiger 觸發、後脈衝到熱點像素：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Geiger triggering and Afterpulsing to Hot pixels: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["Geiger 觸發","暗計數","死時間","直接飛行時間"],"labelsEn":["Geiger triggering","Dark counts","Dead time","Direct time of flight"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a080-stage01","order":1,"title":"Geiger 觸發 → 偵測機率","titleEn":"Geiger triggering to Photon-detection probability","description":"把「Geiger 觸發」「淬熄復位」「偵測機率」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Geiger triggering, Quench and reset, Photon-detection probability.","steps":[{"id":"a080-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"Geiger 觸發：建立模型","titleEn":"Geiger triggering: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons.","instruction":"畫超額偏壓與雪崩觸發後的脈衝，分離光子數和脈衝幅度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw excess bias and triggered pulses and separate photon count from pulse height. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數；多像素數可擴展陣列動態範圍。","observationEn":"A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons; More microcells can extend array dynamic range.","failure":"若採用「用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「Geiger 觸發」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數。","checkEn":"Submit the Geiger triggering diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-01-k1","title":"Geiger 觸發／物理與模型","titleEn":"Geiger triggering / Physics and model","text":"機制：單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數。","textEn":"Mechanism: A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons."},{"id":"a080-v8-01-k2","title":"Geiger 觸發／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Geiger triggering / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「Geiger 觸發」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Geiger triggering, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數","用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數","只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測"],"optionsEn":["A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons","Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height","Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection"],"answer":0,"explanation":"單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-01"],"title":"Geiger 觸發：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Geiger triggering: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height.","instruction":"接續前一步「Geiger 觸發」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：多像素數可擴展陣列動態範圍。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Geiger triggering artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: More microcells can extend array dynamic range. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數；多像素數可擴展陣列動態範圍。","observationEn":"A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons; More microcells can extend array dynamic range.","failure":"若採用「用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「Geiger 觸發」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「多像素數可擴展陣列動態範圍」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Geiger triggering, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"More microcells can extend array dynamic range\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-02-k1","title":"Geiger 觸發／物理與模型","titleEn":"Geiger triggering / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：多像素數可擴展陣列動態範圍。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: More microcells can extend array dynamic range."},{"id":"a080-v8-02-k2","title":"Geiger 觸發／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Geiger triggering / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數」與「單像素飽和脈衝不直接量出同時光子數」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height\" is not equivalent to \"A saturated pixel pulse does not directly count simultaneous photons\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「Geiger 觸發」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Geiger triggering?","options":["只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測","多像素數可擴展陣列動態範圍","用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection","More microcells can extend array dynamic range","Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多像素數可擴展陣列動態範圍；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"More microcells can extend array dynamic range. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-02"],"title":"淬熄復位：建立模型","titleEn":"Quench and reset: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection.","instruction":"畫觸發、降至崩潰以下與恢復偏壓三段時間圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw trigger, below-breakdown quench and bias-recovery timing. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測；復位中的像素可能暫時低靈敏。","observationEn":"Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection; Recovering pixels may have reduced sensitivity.","failure":"若採用「只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「淬熄復位」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測。","checkEn":"Submit the Quench and reset diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-03-k1","title":"淬熄復位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Quench and reset / Physics and model","text":"機制：雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測。","textEn":"Mechanism: Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection."},{"id":"a080-v8-03-k2","title":"淬熄復位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Quench and reset / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「淬熄復位」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Quench and reset, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測","將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名","雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection","Ranking PDE values with different definitions","Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection"],"answer":2,"explanation":"雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-03"],"title":"淬熄復位：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Quench and reset: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection.","instruction":"接續前一步「淬熄復位」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：復位中的像素可能暫時低靈敏。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Quench and reset artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Recovering pixels may have reduced sensitivity. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測；復位中的像素可能暫時低靈敏。","observationEn":"Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection; Recovering pixels may have reduced sensitivity.","failure":"若採用「只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「淬熄復位」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「復位中的像素可能暫時低靈敏」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Quench and reset, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Recovering pixels may have reduced sensitivity\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-04-k1","title":"淬熄復位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Quench and reset / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：復位中的像素可能暫時低靈敏。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Recovering pixels may have reduced sensitivity."},{"id":"a080-v8-04-k2","title":"淬熄復位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Quench and reset / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測」與「雪崩需要淬熄後才能可靠重新偵測」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection\" is not equivalent to \"Avalanche must be quenched before reliable redetection\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「淬熄復位」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Quench and reset?","options":["復位中的像素可能暫時低靈敏","只加大偏壓就能不間斷偵測","將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名"],"optionsEn":["Recovering pixels may have reduced sensitivity","Assuming higher bias enables uninterrupted detection","Ranking PDE values with different definitions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"復位中的像素可能暫時低靈敏；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Recovering pixels may have reduced sensitivity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-04"],"title":"偵測機率：建立模型","titleEn":"Photon-detection probability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included.","instruction":"分拆吸收、收集及觸發機率並區分像素 PDE 與陣列填充因子。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate absorption, collection and trigger probabilities from array fill factor. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子；超額偏壓也影響暗計數和串擾。","observationEn":"Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included; Excess bias also affects dark counts and crosstalk.","failure":"若採用「將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ranking PDE values with different definitions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「偵測機率」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子。","checkEn":"Submit the Photon-detection probability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-05-k1","title":"偵測機率／物理與模型","titleEn":"Photon-detection probability / Physics and model","text":"機制：偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子。","textEn":"Mechanism: Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included."},{"id":"a080-v8-05-k2","title":"偵測機率／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Photon-detection probability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Ranking PDE values with different definitions."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偵測機率」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Photon-detection probability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["以暗電流單位報告暗計數率","偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子","將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名"],"optionsEn":["Reporting dark count in current units","Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included","Ranking PDE values with different definitions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-05"],"title":"偵測機率：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Photon-detection probability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Ranking PDE values with different definitions.","instruction":"接續前一步「偵測機率」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：超額偏壓也影響暗計數和串擾。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Photon-detection probability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Ranking PDE values with different definitions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Excess bias also affects dark counts and crosstalk. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子；超額偏壓也影響暗計數和串擾。","observationEn":"Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included; Excess bias also affects dark counts and crosstalk.","failure":"若採用「將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ranking PDE values with different definitions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「偵測機率」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「超額偏壓也影響暗計數和串擾」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Photon-detection probability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Excess bias also affects dark counts and crosstalk\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-06-k1","title":"偵測機率／物理與模型","titleEn":"Photon-detection probability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：超額偏壓也影響暗計數和串擾。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Excess bias also affects dark counts and crosstalk."},{"id":"a080-v8-06-k2","title":"偵測機率／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Photon-detection probability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名」與「偵測效率定義必須說明是否包含填充因子」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Ranking PDE values with different definitions\" is not equivalent to \"Efficiency definitions must state whether fill factor is included\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「偵測機率」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Photon-detection probability?","options":["將不同定義 PDE 數字直接排名","以暗電流單位報告暗計數率","超額偏壓也影響暗計數和串擾"],"optionsEn":["Ranking PDE values with different definitions","Reporting dark count in current units","Excess bias also affects dark counts and crosstalk"],"answer":2,"explanation":"超額偏壓也影響暗計數和串擾；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Excess bias also affects dark counts and crosstalk. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a080-stage02","order":2,"title":"暗計數 → 光學串擾","titleEn":"Dark counts to Optical crosstalk","description":"把「暗計數」「後脈衝」「光學串擾」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Dark counts, Afterpulsing, Optical crosstalk.","steps":[{"id":"a080-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-06"],"title":"暗計數：建立模型","titleEn":"Dark counts: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current.","instruction":"在遮光下建立每像素計數率地圖和溫度對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map per-pixel dark rates under shielding with temperature controls. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流；熱像素尾端不能只用全片平均表示。","observationEn":"Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current; Hot-pixel tails need more than a wafer mean.","failure":"若採用「以暗電流單位報告暗計數率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting dark count in current units\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「暗計數」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流。","checkEn":"Submit the Dark counts diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-07-k1","title":"暗計數／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dark counts / Physics and model","text":"機制：暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流。","textEn":"Mechanism: Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current."},{"id":"a080-v8-07-k2","title":"暗計數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dark counts / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以暗電流單位報告暗計數率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Reporting dark count in current units."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「暗計數」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dark counts, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流","以暗電流單位報告暗計數率","將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光"],"optionsEn":["Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current","Reporting dark count in current units","Treating all delayed events as independent background photons"],"answer":0,"explanation":"暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-07"],"title":"暗計數：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dark counts: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以暗電流單位報告暗計數率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Reporting dark count in current units.","instruction":"接續前一步「暗計數」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以暗電流單位報告暗計數率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：熱像素尾端不能只用全片平均表示。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dark counts artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Reporting dark count in current units\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Hot-pixel tails need more than a wafer mean. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流；熱像素尾端不能只用全片平均表示。","observationEn":"Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current; Hot-pixel tails need more than a wafer mean.","failure":"若採用「以暗電流單位報告暗計數率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting dark count in current units\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「暗計數」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「熱像素尾端不能只用全片平均表示」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dark counts, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Hot-pixel tails need more than a wafer mean\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-08-k1","title":"暗計數／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dark counts / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：熱像素尾端不能只用全片平均表示。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Hot-pixel tails need more than a wafer mean."},{"id":"a080-v8-08-k2","title":"暗計數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dark counts / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以暗電流單位報告暗計數率」與「暗計數是事件率而非連續暗電流」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Reporting dark count in current units\" is not equivalent to \"Dark count is an event rate, not continuous dark current\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「暗計數」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dark counts?","options":["將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光","熱像素尾端不能只用全片平均表示","以暗電流單位報告暗計數率"],"optionsEn":["Treating all delayed events as independent background photons","Hot-pixel tails need more than a wafer mean","Reporting dark count in current units"],"answer":1,"explanation":"熱像素尾端不能只用全片平均表示；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Hot-pixel tails need more than a wafer mean. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-08"],"title":"後脈衝：建立模型","titleEn":"Afterpulsing: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events.","instruction":"畫觸發後延遲事件直方圖，改變保持時間並比對背景。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Histogram delayed events and compare holdoff settings with background. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數；較長保持時間會降低最大計數率。","observationEn":"Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events; Longer holdoff reduces maximum count rate.","failure":"若採用「將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all delayed events as independent background photons\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「後脈衝」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數。","checkEn":"Submit the Afterpulsing diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-09-k1","title":"後脈衝／物理與模型","titleEn":"Afterpulsing / Physics and model","text":"機制：捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數。","textEn":"Mechanism: Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events."},{"id":"a080-v8-09-k2","title":"後脈衝／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Afterpulsing / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating all delayed events as independent background photons."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「後脈衝」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Afterpulsing, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光","同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子","捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數"],"optionsEn":["Treating all delayed events as independent background photons","Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons","Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events"],"answer":2,"explanation":"捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-09"],"title":"後脈衝：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Afterpulsing: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating all delayed events as independent background photons.","instruction":"接續前一步「後脈衝」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：較長保持時間會降低最大計數率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Afterpulsing artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating all delayed events as independent background photons\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Longer holdoff reduces maximum count rate. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數；較長保持時間會降低最大計數率。","observationEn":"Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events; Longer holdoff reduces maximum count rate.","failure":"若採用「將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all delayed events as independent background photons\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「後脈衝」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「較長保持時間會降低最大計數率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Afterpulsing, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Longer holdoff reduces maximum count rate\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-10-k1","title":"後脈衝／物理與模型","titleEn":"Afterpulsing / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：較長保持時間會降低最大計數率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Longer holdoff reduces maximum count rate."},{"id":"a080-v8-10-k2","title":"後脈衝／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Afterpulsing / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光」與「捕捉載子釋放可形成與前次事件相關的計數」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating all delayed events as independent background photons\" is not equivalent to \"Released trapped carriers can produce correlated events\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「後脈衝」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Afterpulsing?","options":["較長保持時間會降低最大計數率","將所有延遲事件當成獨立背景光","同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子"],"optionsEn":["Longer holdoff reduces maximum count rate","Treating all delayed events as independent background photons","Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons"],"answer":0,"explanation":"較長保持時間會降低最大計數率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Longer holdoff reduces maximum count rate. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-10"],"title":"光學串擾：建立模型","titleEn":"Optical crosstalk: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors.","instruction":"畫鄰像素同步事件矩陣，加入遮光及距離對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Build neighboring coincidence matrices with shielding/distance controls. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素；電性串擾也能造成相關事件。","observationEn":"Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors; Electrical crosstalk can also correlate events.","failure":"若採用「同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「光學串擾」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素。","checkEn":"Submit the Optical crosstalk diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-11-k1","title":"光學串擾／物理與模型","titleEn":"Optical crosstalk / Physics and model","text":"機制：雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素。","textEn":"Mechanism: Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors."},{"id":"a080-v8-11-k2","title":"光學串擾／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Optical crosstalk / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「光學串擾」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Optical crosstalk, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將低光強線性外推到任意高光強","雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素","同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子"],"optionsEn":["Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux","Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors","Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons"],"answer":1,"explanation":"雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-11"],"title":"光學串擾：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Optical crosstalk: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons.","instruction":"接續前一步「光學串擾」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電性串擾也能造成相關事件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Optical crosstalk artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electrical crosstalk can also correlate events. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素；電性串擾也能造成相關事件。","observationEn":"Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors; Electrical crosstalk can also correlate events.","failure":"若採用「同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「光學串擾」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電性串擾也能造成相關事件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Optical crosstalk, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electrical crosstalk can also correlate events\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-12-k1","title":"光學串擾／物理與模型","titleEn":"Optical crosstalk / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電性串擾也能造成相關事件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electrical crosstalk can also correlate events."},{"id":"a080-v8-12-k2","title":"光學串擾／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Optical crosstalk / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子」與「雪崩產生的光可能觸發鄰近像素」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons\" is not equivalent to \"Avalanche-generated light can trigger neighbors\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「光學串擾」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Optical crosstalk?","options":["同時多像素事件必然都是多個外來光子","將低光強線性外推到任意高光強","電性串擾也能造成相關事件"],"optionsEn":["Assuming coincidences always mean multiple incident photons","Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux","Electrical crosstalk can also correlate events"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電性串擾也能造成相關事件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrical crosstalk can also correlate events. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a080-stage03","order":3,"title":"死時間 → TDC 量化","titleEn":"Dead time to TDC quantization","description":"把「死時間」「時間抖動」「TDC 量化」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Dead time, Timing jitter, TDC quantization.","steps":[{"id":"a080-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-12"],"title":"死時間：建立模型","titleEn":"Dead time: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Measured count rate can become nonlinear.","instruction":"用假設固定死時間估算高計數壓縮，註明不可延長模型。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Estimate high-rate compression with a hypothetical nonparalyzable dead-time model. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性；不同死時間模型有不同飽和曲線。","observationEn":"Measured count rate can become nonlinear; Dead-time models predict different saturation curves.","failure":"若採用「將低光強線性外推到任意高光強」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「死時間」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性。","checkEn":"Submit the Dead time diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Measured count rate can become nonlinear.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-13-k1","title":"死時間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dead time / Physics and model","text":"機制：計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Measured count rate can become nonlinear."},{"id":"a080-v8-13-k2","title":"死時間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dead time / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將低光強線性外推到任意高光強」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「死時間」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dead time, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性","將低光強線性外推到任意高光強","將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程"],"optionsEn":["Measured count rate can become nonlinear","Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux","Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Measured count rate can become nonlinear. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-13"],"title":"死時間：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dead time: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將低光強線性外推到任意高光強」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux.","instruction":"接續前一步「死時間」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將低光強線性外推到任意高光強」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：不同死時間模型有不同飽和曲線。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dead time artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dead-time models predict different saturation curves. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性；不同死時間模型有不同飽和曲線。","observationEn":"Measured count rate can become nonlinear; Dead-time models predict different saturation curves.","failure":"若採用「將低光強線性外推到任意高光強」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「死時間」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「不同死時間模型有不同飽和曲線」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dead time, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dead-time models predict different saturation curves\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-14-k1","title":"死時間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dead time / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：不同死時間模型有不同飽和曲線。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dead-time models predict different saturation curves."},{"id":"a080-v8-14-k2","title":"死時間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dead time / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將低光強線性外推到任意高光強」與「計數率增加後量測可能偏離線性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux\" is not equivalent to \"Measured count rate can become nonlinear\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「死時間」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dead time?","options":["將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程","不同死時間模型有不同飽和曲線","將低光強線性外推到任意高光強"],"optionsEn":["Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing","Dead-time models predict different saturation curves","Extending low-flux linearity to arbitrary flux"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同死時間模型有不同飽和曲線；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dead-time models predict different saturation curves. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-14"],"title":"時間抖動：建立模型","titleEn":"Timing jitter: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter.","instruction":"畫到達時間直方圖並分拆雷射、偵測器與 TDC 貢獻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw arrival histograms and separate laser, detector and TDC contributions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動；抖動各項平方相加需獨立假設。","observationEn":"System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter; Quadrature jitter addition assumes independence.","failure":"若採用「將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「時間抖動」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動。","checkEn":"Submit the Timing jitter diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-15-k1","title":"時間抖動／物理與模型","titleEn":"Timing jitter / Physics and model","text":"機制：系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動。","textEn":"Mechanism: System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter."},{"id":"a080-v8-15-k2","title":"時間抖動／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Timing jitter / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間抖動」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Timing jitter, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程","插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度","系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動"],"optionsEn":["Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing","Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution","System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter"],"answer":2,"explanation":"系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-15"],"title":"時間抖動：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Timing jitter: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing.","instruction":"接續前一步「時間抖動」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：抖動各項平方相加需獨立假設。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Timing jitter artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Quadrature jitter addition assumes independence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動；抖動各項平方相加需獨立假設。","observationEn":"System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter; Quadrature jitter addition assumes independence.","failure":"若採用「將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「時間抖動」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「抖動各項平方相加需獨立假設」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Timing jitter, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Quadrature jitter addition assumes independence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-16-k1","title":"時間抖動／物理與模型","titleEn":"Timing jitter / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：抖動各項平方相加需獨立假設。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Quadrature jitter addition assumes independence."},{"id":"a080-v8-16-k2","title":"時間抖動／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Timing jitter / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程」與「系統抖動不完全等於 SPAD 本體抖動」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing\" is not equivalent to \"System jitter is not solely intrinsic SPAD jitter\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「時間抖動」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Timing jitter?","options":["抖動各項平方相加需獨立假設","將總脈寬全部歸因於半導體製程","插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度"],"optionsEn":["Quadrature jitter addition assumes independence","Attributing total timing width to semiconductor processing","Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution"],"answer":0,"explanation":"抖動各項平方相加需獨立假設；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Quadrature jitter addition assumes independence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-16"],"title":"TDC 量化：建立模型","titleEn":"TDC quantization: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Bin width limits resolvable timing detail.","instruction":"以假設分箱大小比較同一事件序列的直方圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Bin the same hypothetical event sequence at two TDC resolutions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節；TDC 非均勻分箱需校正。","observationEn":"Bin width limits resolvable timing detail; Nonuniform TDC bins need calibration.","failure":"若採用「插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「TDC 量化」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節。","checkEn":"Submit the TDC quantization diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Bin width limits resolvable timing detail.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-17-k1","title":"TDC 量化／物理與模型","titleEn":"TDC quantization / Physics and model","text":"機制：分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節。","textEn":"Mechanism: Bin width limits resolvable timing detail."},{"id":"a080-v8-17-k2","title":"TDC 量化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"TDC quantization / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「TDC 量化」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For TDC quantization, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離","分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節","插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度"],"optionsEn":["Using cΔt as one-way distance","Bin width limits resolvable timing detail","Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bin width limits resolvable timing detail. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-17"],"title":"TDC 量化：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"TDC quantization: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution.","instruction":"接續前一步「TDC 量化」成果，先指出錯誤主張「插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：TDC 非均勻分箱需校正。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding TDC quantization artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Nonuniform TDC bins need calibration. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節；TDC 非均勻分箱需校正。","observationEn":"Bin width limits resolvable timing detail; Nonuniform TDC bins need calibration.","failure":"若採用「插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「TDC 量化」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「TDC 非均勻分箱需校正」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for TDC quantization, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Nonuniform TDC bins need calibration\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-18-k1","title":"TDC 量化／物理與模型","titleEn":"TDC quantization / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：TDC 非均勻分箱需校正。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Nonuniform TDC bins need calibration."},{"id":"a080-v8-18-k2","title":"TDC 量化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"TDC quantization / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度」與「分箱寬度限制可辨識的時間細節」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution\" is not equivalent to \"Bin width limits resolvable timing detail\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「TDC 量化」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of TDC quantization?","options":["插值畫平滑曲線就代表新增時間解析度","直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離","TDC 非均勻分箱需校正"],"optionsEn":["Treating smooth interpolation as new time resolution","Using cΔt as one-way distance","Nonuniform TDC bins need calibration"],"answer":2,"explanation":"TDC 非均勻分箱需校正；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Nonuniform TDC bins need calibration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a080-stage04","order":4,"title":"直接飛行時間 → 熱點像素","titleEn":"Direct time of flight to Hot pixels","description":"把「直接飛行時間」「堆疊讀出」「熱點像素」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Direct time of flight, Stacked readout, Hot pixels.","steps":[{"id":"a080-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-18"],"title":"直接飛行時間：建立模型","titleEn":"Direct time of flight: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「往返飛行時間須除以二」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two.","instruction":"用 d=cΔt/2 算假設距離並扣除電子延遲。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設直接 ToF 系統已扣除電子延遲，測得往返時間 10 ns，取 c=3×10⁸ m/s，距離 d=ct/2=1.5 m。若時間誤差為 1 ns，對應距離誤差幅度 0.15 m。未處理多重路徑、光子統計及介質折射率；不可省略往返的二分之一。","instructionEn":"Compute hypothetical d=cΔt/2 after subtracting electronic delay. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a direct-ToF system has removed electronic delay and measures a 10 ns round trip. With c=3×10⁸ m/s, d=ct/2=1.5 m. A 1 ns timing-error magnitude corresponds to 0.15 m. Multipath, photon statistics and medium refractive index are excluded; the round-trip factor of one-half is essential.","observation":"往返飛行時間須除以二；多重反射會產生多個距離峰。","observationEn":"Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two; Multipath produces multiple range peaks.","failure":"若採用「直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using cΔt as one-way distance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「直接飛行時間」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：往返飛行時間須除以二。\n算例驗收：驗算 1.5 m 與 0.15 m，畫出發射及返回兩段光路。","checkEn":"Submit the Direct time of flight diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 1.5 m and 0.15 m and draw the outgoing and returning optical paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-19-k1","title":"直接飛行時間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Direct time of flight / Physics and model","text":"機制：往返飛行時間須除以二。","textEn":"Mechanism: Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two."},{"id":"a080-v8-19-k2","title":"直接飛行時間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Direct time of flight / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離」。\n假設數值與推算：假設直接 ToF 系統已扣除電子延遲，測得往返時間 10 ns，取 c=3×10⁸ m/s，距離 d=ct/2=1.5 m。若時間誤差為 1 ns，對應距離誤差幅度 0.15 m。未處理多重路徑、光子統計及介質折射率；不可省略往返的二分之一。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using cΔt as one-way distance.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a direct-ToF system has removed electronic delay and measures a 10 ns round trip. With c=3×10⁸ m/s, d=ct/2=1.5 m. A 1 ns timing-error magnitude corresponds to 0.15 m. Multipath, photon statistics and medium refractive index are excluded; the round-trip factor of one-half is essential."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「直接飛行時間」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Direct time of flight, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["往返飛行時間須除以二","直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離","偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出"],"optionsEn":["Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two","Using cΔt as one-way distance","Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported"],"answer":0,"explanation":"往返飛行時間須除以二；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-19"],"title":"直接飛行時間：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Direct time of flight: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using cΔt as one-way distance.","instruction":"接續前一步「直接飛行時間」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：多重反射會產生多個距離峰。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Direct time of flight artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using cΔt as one-way distance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Multipath produces multiple range peaks. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"往返飛行時間須除以二；多重反射會產生多個距離峰。","observationEn":"Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two; Multipath produces multiple range peaks.","failure":"若採用「直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using cΔt as one-way distance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「直接飛行時間」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「多重反射會產生多個距離峰」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Direct time of flight, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Multipath produces multiple range peaks\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-20-k1","title":"直接飛行時間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Direct time of flight / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：多重反射會產生多個距離峰。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Multipath produces multiple range peaks."},{"id":"a080-v8-20-k2","title":"直接飛行時間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Direct time of flight / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離」與「往返飛行時間須除以二」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using cΔt as one-way distance\" is not equivalent to \"Round-trip flight time requires a factor of two\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「直接飛行時間」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Direct time of flight?","options":["偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出","多重反射會產生多個距離峰","直接用 cΔt 作為單程距離"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported","Multipath produces multiple range peaks","Using cΔt as one-way distance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多重反射會產生多個距離峰；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multipath produces multiple range peaks. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-20"],"title":"堆疊讀出：建立模型","titleEn":"Stacked readout: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck.","instruction":"畫 SPAD 層、計數器層及連接，檢查填充率和資料吞吐。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw detector/counter tiers and links and check fill factor and throughput. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸；資料遺失會偏差時間直方圖。","observationEn":"Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck; Dropped data can bias time histograms.","failure":"若採用「偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「堆疊讀出」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸。","checkEn":"Submit the Stacked readout diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-21-k1","title":"堆疊讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stacked readout / Physics and model","text":"機制：堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸。","textEn":"Mechanism: Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck."},{"id":"a080-v8-21-k2","title":"堆疊讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stacked readout / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堆疊讀出」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Stacked readout, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出","只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素","堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported","Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels","Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck"],"answer":2,"explanation":"堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-21"],"title":"堆疊讀出：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Stacked readout: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported.","instruction":"接續前一步「堆疊讀出」成果，先指出錯誤主張「偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：資料遺失會偏差時間直方圖。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Stacked readout artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dropped data can bias time histograms. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸；資料遺失會偏差時間直方圖。","observationEn":"Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck; Dropped data can bias time histograms.","failure":"若採用「偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「堆疊讀出」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「資料遺失會偏差時間直方圖」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Stacked readout, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dropped data can bias time histograms\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-22-k1","title":"堆疊讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stacked readout / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：資料遺失會偏差時間直方圖。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dropped data can bias time histograms."},{"id":"a080-v8-22-k2","title":"堆疊讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stacked readout / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出」與「堆疊可改善面積配置但不消除讀出瓶頸」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported\" is not equivalent to \"Stacking improves area allocation but not every readout bottleneck\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「堆疊讀出」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Stacked readout?","options":["資料遺失會偏差時間直方圖","偵測器變多即保證事件資料全部送出","只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素"],"optionsEn":["Dropped data can bias time histograms","Assuming more pixels guarantee all events can be exported","Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels"],"answer":0,"explanation":"資料遺失會偏差時間直方圖；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dropped data can bias time histograms. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-22"],"title":"熱點像素：建立模型","titleEn":"Hot pixels: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling.","instruction":"制定遮罩前後影像與偵測率比較，保留被移除面積。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare images/detection before and after masking and retain excluded area. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣；遮罩版本應與影像同步保存。","observationEn":"Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling; Mask versions should accompany image records.","failure":"若採用「只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱點像素」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣。","checkEn":"Submit the Hot pixels diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-23-k1","title":"熱點像素／物理與模型","titleEn":"Hot pixels / Physics and model","text":"機制：移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣。","textEn":"Mechanism: Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling."},{"id":"a080-v8-23-k2","title":"熱點像素／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Hot pixels / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱點像素」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Hot pixels, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數","移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣","只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素"],"optionsEn":["Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height","Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling","Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels"],"answer":1,"explanation":"移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a080-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spad","v8-c-sipm","v8-c-tof"],"prerequisiteIds":["a080-v8-23"],"title":"熱點像素：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Hot pixels: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱點像素」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：遮罩版本應與影像同步保存。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Hot pixels artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mask versions should accompany image records. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣；遮罩版本應與影像同步保存。","observationEn":"Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling; Mask versions should accompany image records.","failure":"若採用「只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱點像素」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「遮罩版本應與影像同步保存」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Hot pixels, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mask versions should accompany image records\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a080-v8-24-k1","title":"熱點像素／物理與模型","titleEn":"Hot pixels / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：遮罩版本應與影像同步保存。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mask versions should accompany image records."},{"id":"a080-v8-24-k2","title":"熱點像素／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Hot pixels / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素」與「移除高暗計數像素也減少有效取樣」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels\" is not equivalent to \"Masking high-dark pixels reduces effective sampling\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱點像素」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Hot pixels?","options":["只報遮罩後最佳暗計數而不報失去像素","用單一雪崩脈衝高度精確判斷入射光子數","遮罩版本應與影像同步保存"],"optionsEn":["Reporting improved dark rate without lost pixels","Inferring exact photon number from one avalanche height","Mask versions should accompany image records"],"answer":2,"explanation":"遮罩版本應與影像同步保存；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mask versions should accompany image records. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"sensors","subcategoryTitle":"影像與光子感測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Image and photon sensors"},{"id":"a081","title":"碳化矽磊晶與缺陷控制","titleEn":"Silicon-carbide epitaxy and defect control","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從多型與基板、穿通差排到磊晶放行：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Polytype and substrate and Threading dislocations to Epitaxy release: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["多型與基板","基面差排","厚度均勻度","缺陷檢出率"],"labelsEn":["Polytype and substrate","Basal-plane dislocations","Thickness uniformity","Defect detectability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a081-stage01","order":1,"title":"多型與基板 → 差排傳承","titleEn":"Polytype and substrate to Dislocation inheritance","description":"把「多型與基板」「偏角與台階」「差排傳承」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Polytype and substrate, Miscut and steps, Dislocation inheritance.","steps":[{"id":"a081-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"多型與基板：建立模型","titleEn":"Polytype and substrate: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking.","instruction":"區分 4H 與其他多型，標記晶向及磊晶面。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Distinguish 4H from other polytypes and label orientation/epitaxial face. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同；相同多型仍可能有不同晶面。","observationEn":"Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking; The same polytype can have different crystal faces.","failure":"若採用「只看 Si:C 比就確認多型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「多型與基板」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同。","checkEn":"Submit the Polytype and substrate diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-01-k1","title":"多型與基板／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polytype and substrate / Physics and model","text":"機制：化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking."},{"id":"a081-v8-01-k2","title":"多型與基板／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polytype and substrate / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看 Si:C 比就確認多型」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多型與基板」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Polytype and substrate, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同","只看 Si:C 比就確認多型","認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差"],"optionsEn":["Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking","Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone","Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error"],"answer":0,"explanation":"化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-01"],"title":"多型與基板：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Polytype and substrate: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看 Si:C 比就確認多型」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「多型與基板」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看 Si:C 比就確認多型」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：相同多型仍可能有不同晶面。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Polytype and substrate artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: The same polytype can have different crystal faces. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同；相同多型仍可能有不同晶面。","observationEn":"Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking; The same polytype can have different crystal faces.","failure":"若採用「只看 Si:C 比就確認多型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「多型與基板」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「相同多型仍可能有不同晶面」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Polytype and substrate, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"The same polytype can have different crystal faces\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-02-k1","title":"多型與基板／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polytype and substrate / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：相同多型仍可能有不同晶面。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: The same polytype can have different crystal faces."},{"id":"a081-v8-02-k2","title":"多型與基板／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polytype and substrate / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看 Si:C 比就確認多型」與「化學成分相同不代表晶體堆疊相同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone\" is not equivalent to \"Equal chemistry does not imply identical stacking\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「多型與基板」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Polytype and substrate?","options":["認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差","相同多型仍可能有不同晶面","只看 Si:C 比就確認多型"],"optionsEn":["Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error","The same polytype can have different crystal faces","Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同多型仍可能有不同晶面；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The same polytype can have different crystal faces. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-02"],"title":"偏角與台階：建立模型","titleEn":"Miscut and steps: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth.","instruction":"畫偏角表面台階，比較台階流與二維成核的假說。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch miscut steps and compare step-flow and island-nucleation hypotheses. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長；台階聚集可能改變局部成長形貌。","observationEn":"Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth; Step bunching changes local morphology.","failure":"若採用「認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「偏角與台階」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長。","checkEn":"Submit the Miscut and steps diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-03-k1","title":"偏角與台階／物理與模型","titleEn":"Miscut and steps / Physics and model","text":"機制：偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長。","textEn":"Mechanism: Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth."},{"id":"a081-v8-03-k2","title":"偏角與台階／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Miscut and steps / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偏角與台階」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Miscut and steps, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差","所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生","偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長"],"optionsEn":["Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error","Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated","Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth"],"answer":2,"explanation":"偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-03"],"title":"偏角與台階：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Miscut and steps: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error.","instruction":"接續前一步「偏角與台階」成果，先指出錯誤主張「認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：台階聚集可能改變局部成長形貌。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Miscut and steps artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Step bunching changes local morphology. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長；台階聚集可能改變局部成長形貌。","observationEn":"Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth; Step bunching changes local morphology.","failure":"若採用「認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「偏角與台階」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「台階聚集可能改變局部成長形貌」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Miscut and steps, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Step bunching changes local morphology\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-04-k1","title":"偏角與台階／物理與模型","titleEn":"Miscut and steps / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：台階聚集可能改變局部成長形貌。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Step bunching changes local morphology."},{"id":"a081-v8-04-k2","title":"偏角與台階／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Miscut and steps / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差」與「偏角和表面動力學共同影響成長」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error\" is not equivalent to \"Miscut and surface kinetics jointly affect growth\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「偏角與台階」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Miscut and steps?","options":["台階聚集可能改變局部成長形貌","認為偏角是可忽略的幾何誤差","所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生"],"optionsEn":["Step bunching changes local morphology","Treating miscut as irrelevant geometric error","Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated"],"answer":0,"explanation":"台階聚集可能改變局部成長形貌；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Step bunching changes local morphology. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-04"],"title":"差排傳承：建立模型","titleEn":"Dislocation inheritance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects.","instruction":"對基板與磊晶缺陷圖配準，區分繼承與新增缺陷。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Register substrate/epilayer maps and separate inherited from new defects. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷；配準誤差會造成假新增缺陷。","observationEn":"Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects; Registration error produces false new defects.","failure":"若採用「所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「差排傳承」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷。","checkEn":"Submit the Dislocation inheritance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-05-k1","title":"差排傳承／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dislocation inheritance / Physics and model","text":"機制：磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects."},{"id":"a081-v8-05-k2","title":"差排傳承／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dislocation inheritance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「差排傳承」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dislocation inheritance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化","磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷","所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生"],"optionsEn":["Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change","Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects","Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-05"],"title":"差排傳承：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dislocation inheritance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated.","instruction":"接續前一步「差排傳承」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：配準誤差會造成假新增缺陷。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dislocation inheritance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Registration error produces false new defects. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷；配準誤差會造成假新增缺陷。","observationEn":"Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects; Registration error produces false new defects.","failure":"若採用「所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「差排傳承」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「配準誤差會造成假新增缺陷」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dislocation inheritance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Registration error produces false new defects\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-06-k1","title":"差排傳承／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dislocation inheritance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：配準誤差會造成假新增缺陷。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Registration error produces false new defects."},{"id":"a081-v8-06-k2","title":"差排傳承／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dislocation inheritance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生」與「磊晶品質需要追溯基板缺陷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated\" is not equivalent to \"Epitaxial quality must be traced to substrate defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「差排傳承」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dislocation inheritance?","options":["所有磊晶缺陷都由同一成長步驟新生","出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化","配準誤差會造成假新增缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Assuming all epilayer defects are newly generated","Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change","Registration error produces false new defects"],"answer":2,"explanation":"配準誤差會造成假新增缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Registration error produces false new defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a081-stage02","order":2,"title":"基面差排 → 表面台階聚集","titleEn":"Basal-plane dislocations to Step bunching","description":"把「基面差排」「穿通差排」「表面台階聚集」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Basal-plane dislocations, Threading dislocations, Step bunching.","steps":[{"id":"a081-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-06"],"title":"基面差排：建立模型","titleEn":"Basal-plane dislocations: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection.","instruction":"畫基面差排與可能堆疊錯擴展，連到雙極注入的驗證。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw basal dislocations and possible stacking-fault expansion with bipolar-injection checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化；注入條件決定堆疊錯擴展風險。","observationEn":"Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection; Injection conditions affect fault-expansion risk.","failure":"若採用「出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「基面差排」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化。","checkEn":"Submit the Basal-plane dislocations diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-07-k1","title":"基面差排／物理與模型","titleEn":"Basal-plane dislocations / Physics and model","text":"機制：某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection."},{"id":"a081-v8-07-k2","title":"基面差排／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Basal-plane dislocations / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基面差排」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Basal-plane dislocations, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化","出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化","所有暗點都標為相同差排類型"],"optionsEn":["Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection","Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change","Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-07"],"title":"基面差排：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Basal-plane dislocations: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change.","instruction":"接續前一步「基面差排」成果，先指出錯誤主張「出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：注入條件決定堆疊錯擴展風險。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Basal-plane dislocations artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Injection conditions affect fault-expansion risk. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化；注入條件決定堆疊錯擴展風險。","observationEn":"Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection; Injection conditions affect fault-expansion risk.","failure":"若採用「出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「基面差排」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「注入條件決定堆疊錯擴展風險」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Basal-plane dislocations, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Injection conditions affect fault-expansion risk\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-08-k1","title":"基面差排／物理與模型","titleEn":"Basal-plane dislocations / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：注入條件決定堆疊錯擴展風險。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Injection conditions affect fault-expansion risk."},{"id":"a081-v8-08-k2","title":"基面差排／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Basal-plane dislocations / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化」與「某些結構缺陷可在載子注入後演化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change\" is not equivalent to \"Some structural defects evolve after carrier injection\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「基面差排」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Basal-plane dislocations?","options":["所有暗點都標為相同差排類型","注入條件決定堆疊錯擴展風險","出廠缺陷圖能涵蓋所有操作後變化"],"optionsEn":["Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation","Injection conditions affect fault-expansion risk","Assuming as-grown maps capture every operational change"],"answer":1,"explanation":"注入條件決定堆疊錯擴展風險；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Injection conditions affect fault-expansion risk. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-08"],"title":"穿通差排：建立模型","titleEn":"Threading dislocations: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone.","instruction":"區分刃型與螺型差排的幾何，列出成像交叉證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Distinguish threading edge/screw geometry and list cross-imaging evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類；缺陷分類需校正檢查方法靈敏度。","observationEn":"Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone; Classification requires detection-sensitivity context.","failure":"若採用「所有暗點都標為相同差排類型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「穿通差排」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類。","checkEn":"Submit the Threading dislocations diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-09-k1","title":"穿通差排／物理與模型","titleEn":"Threading dislocations / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類。","textEn":"Mechanism: Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone."},{"id":"a081-v8-09-k2","title":"穿通差排／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Threading dislocations / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有暗點都標為相同差排類型」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「穿通差排」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Threading dislocations, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有暗點都標為相同差排類型","不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名","不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類"],"optionsEn":["Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation","Ranking RMS values from different scan areas","Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-09"],"title":"穿通差排：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Threading dislocations: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有暗點都標為相同差排類型」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation.","instruction":"接續前一步「穿通差排」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有暗點都標為相同差排類型」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：缺陷分類需校正檢查方法靈敏度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Threading dislocations artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Classification requires detection-sensitivity context. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類；缺陷分類需校正檢查方法靈敏度。","observationEn":"Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone; Classification requires detection-sensitivity context.","failure":"若採用「所有暗點都標為相同差排類型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「穿通差排」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「缺陷分類需校正檢查方法靈敏度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Threading dislocations, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Classification requires detection-sensitivity context\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-10-k1","title":"穿通差排／物理與模型","titleEn":"Threading dislocations / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：缺陷分類需校正檢查方法靈敏度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Classification requires detection-sensitivity context."},{"id":"a081-v8-10-k2","title":"穿通差排／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Threading dislocations / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有暗點都標為相同差排類型」與「不同差排不能只靠同一表面暗點分類」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation\" is not equivalent to \"Different dislocations cannot be classified from one dark spot alone\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「穿通差排」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Threading dislocations?","options":["缺陷分類需校正檢查方法靈敏度","所有暗點都標為相同差排類型","不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名"],"optionsEn":["Classification requires detection-sensitivity context","Labeling all dark spots the same dislocation","Ranking RMS values from different scan areas"],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷分類需校正檢查方法靈敏度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Classification requires detection-sensitivity context. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-10"],"title":"表面台階聚集：建立模型","titleEn":"Step bunching: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale.","instruction":"畫等距台階與聚集台階，計算相同掃描尺度的高度起伏。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare regular/bunched steps at the same scan scale. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀；AFM 尖端形狀會影響量測輪廓。","observationEn":"Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale; AFM-tip geometry affects measured profiles.","failure":"若採用「不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ranking RMS values from different scan areas\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「表面台階聚集」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀。","checkEn":"Submit the Step bunching diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-11-k1","title":"表面台階聚集／物理與模型","titleEn":"Step bunching / Physics and model","text":"機制：粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀。","textEn":"Mechanism: Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale."},{"id":"a081-v8-11-k2","title":"表面台階聚集／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Step bunching / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Ranking RMS values from different scan areas."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「表面台階聚集」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Step bunching, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致","粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀","不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名"],"optionsEn":["Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness","Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale","Ranking RMS values from different scan areas"],"answer":1,"explanation":"粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-11"],"title":"表面台階聚集：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Step bunching: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Ranking RMS values from different scan areas.","instruction":"接續前一步「表面台階聚集」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：AFM 尖端形狀會影響量測輪廓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Step bunching artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Ranking RMS values from different scan areas\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: AFM-tip geometry affects measured profiles. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀；AFM 尖端形狀會影響量測輪廓。","observationEn":"Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale; AFM-tip geometry affects measured profiles.","failure":"若採用「不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ranking RMS values from different scan areas\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「表面台階聚集」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「AFM 尖端形狀會影響量測輪廓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Step bunching, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"AFM-tip geometry affects measured profiles\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-12-k1","title":"表面台階聚集／物理與模型","titleEn":"Step bunching / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：AFM 尖端形狀會影響量測輪廓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: AFM-tip geometry affects measured profiles."},{"id":"a081-v8-12-k2","title":"表面台階聚集／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Step bunching / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名」與「粗糙度需連同空間尺度解讀」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Ranking RMS values from different scan areas\" is not equivalent to \"Roughness must be interpreted with spatial scale\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「表面台階聚集」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Step bunching?","options":["不同掃描面積的 RMS 可直接排名","中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致","AFM 尖端形狀會影響量測輪廓"],"optionsEn":["Ranking RMS values from different scan areas","Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness","AFM-tip geometry affects measured profiles"],"answer":2,"explanation":"AFM 尖端形狀會影響量測輪廓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"AFM-tip geometry affects measured profiles. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a081-stage03","order":3,"title":"厚度均勻度 → 表面污染","titleEn":"Thickness uniformity to Surface contamination","description":"把「厚度均勻度」「摻雜分布」「表面污染」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Thickness uniformity, Doping distribution, Surface contamination.","steps":[{"id":"a081-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-12"],"title":"厚度均勻度：建立模型","titleEn":"Thickness uniformity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer.","instruction":"建立徑向厚度圖並分開片內與片間偏差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設三個外延厚度測點為 99、100、101 µm，平均 100 µm、極差 2 µm。若僅描述這三點、使用母體定義，標準差 sqrt(2/3)=0.8165 µm，變異係數 0.8165%；若作樣本估計則標準差為 1 µm。必須寫明分母，且三點不能推論整片缺陷密度。","instructionEn":"Map radial thickness and separate within-wafer from wafer-to-wafer variation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume three epitaxial thickness readings of 99, 100 and 101 µm. Mean is 100 µm and range 2 µm. Describing just these points with the population definition gives standard deviation sqrt(2/3)=0.8165 µm and CV=0.8165%; the sample estimate instead gives 1 µm. State the denominator; three sites cannot establish wafer-wide defect density.","observation":"一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層；厚度與摻雜分布可能相互相關。","observationEn":"One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer; Thickness and doping variations may correlate.","failure":"若採用「中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「厚度均勻度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層。\n算例驗收：驗算平均、極差及兩種標準差，並在圖上註明取樣位置不足的限制。","checkEn":"Submit the Thickness uniformity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify mean, range and both standard-deviation definitions and mark the sampling limitation on the map.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-13-k1","title":"厚度均勻度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness uniformity / Physics and model","text":"機制：一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層。","textEn":"Mechanism: One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer."},{"id":"a081-v8-13-k2","title":"厚度均勻度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness uniformity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致」。\n假設數值與推算：假設三個外延厚度測點為 99、100、101 µm，平均 100 µm、極差 2 µm。若僅描述這三點、使用母體定義，標準差 sqrt(2/3)=0.8165 µm，變異係數 0.8165%；若作樣本估計則標準差為 1 µm。必須寫明分母，且三點不能推論整片缺陷密度。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume three epitaxial thickness readings of 99, 100 and 101 µm. Mean is 100 µm and range 2 µm. Describing just these points with the population definition gives standard deviation sqrt(2/3)=0.8165 µm and CV=0.8165%; the sample estimate instead gives 1 µm. State the denominator; three sites cannot establish wafer-wide defect density."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「厚度均勻度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thickness uniformity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層","中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致","只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓"],"optionsEn":["One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer","Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness","Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost"],"answer":0,"explanation":"一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-13"],"title":"厚度均勻度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thickness uniformity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness.","instruction":"接續前一步「厚度均勻度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：厚度與摻雜分布可能相互相關。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thickness uniformity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thickness and doping variations may correlate. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層；厚度與摻雜分布可能相互相關。","observationEn":"One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer; Thickness and doping variations may correlate.","failure":"若採用「中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「厚度均勻度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「厚度與摻雜分布可能相互相關」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thickness uniformity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thickness and doping variations may correlate\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-14-k1","title":"厚度均勻度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness uniformity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：厚度與摻雜分布可能相互相關。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thickness and doping variations may correlate."},{"id":"a081-v8-14-k2","title":"厚度均勻度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness uniformity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致」與「一個中心點無法代表全片漂移層」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness\" is not equivalent to \"One center point cannot represent the whole drift layer\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「厚度均勻度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thickness uniformity?","options":["只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓","厚度與摻雜分布可能相互相關","中心厚度合格就代表全片耐壓一致"],"optionsEn":["Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost","Thickness and doping variations may correlate","Inferring uniform blocking capability from center thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚度與摻雜分布可能相互相關；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thickness and doping variations may correlate. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-14"],"title":"摻雜分布：建立模型","titleEn":"Doping distribution: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「厚度與摻雜需共同設計」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Thickness and doping need joint design.","instruction":"對厚度和載子濃度建立雙圖，解釋阻斷與導通取捨。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map thickness/carrier concentration together and discuss blocking/conduction tradeoffs. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"厚度與摻雜需共同設計；電性濃度不一定等於化學總濃度。","observationEn":"Thickness and doping need joint design; Electrical concentration differs from total chemistry.","failure":"若採用「只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「摻雜分布」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：厚度與摻雜需共同設計。","checkEn":"Submit the Doping distribution diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Thickness and doping need joint design.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-15-k1","title":"摻雜分布／物理與模型","titleEn":"Doping distribution / Physics and model","text":"機制：厚度與摻雜需共同設計。","textEn":"Mechanism: Thickness and doping need joint design."},{"id":"a081-v8-15-k2","title":"摻雜分布／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Doping distribution / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「摻雜分布」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Doping distribution, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓","晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨","厚度與摻雜需共同設計"],"optionsEn":["Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost","Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality","Thickness and doping need joint design"],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚度與摻雜需共同設計；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thickness and doping need joint design. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-15"],"title":"摻雜分布：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Doping distribution: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost.","instruction":"接續前一步「摻雜分布」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電性濃度不一定等於化學總濃度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Doping distribution artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electrical concentration differs from total chemistry. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"厚度與摻雜需共同設計；電性濃度不一定等於化學總濃度。","observationEn":"Thickness and doping need joint design; Electrical concentration differs from total chemistry.","failure":"若採用「只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「摻雜分布」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電性濃度不一定等於化學總濃度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Doping distribution, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electrical concentration differs from total chemistry\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-16-k1","title":"摻雜分布／物理與模型","titleEn":"Doping distribution / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電性濃度不一定等於化學總濃度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electrical concentration differs from total chemistry."},{"id":"a081-v8-16-k2","title":"摻雜分布／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Doping distribution / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓」與「厚度與摻雜需共同設計」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost\" is not equivalent to \"Thickness and doping need joint design\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「摻雜分布」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Doping distribution?","options":["電性濃度不一定等於化學總濃度","只減少摻雜就無代價提升耐壓","晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨"],"optionsEn":["Electrical concentration differs from total chemistry","Assuming reduced doping improves blocking without cost","Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性濃度不一定等於化學總濃度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrical concentration differs from total chemistry. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-16"],"title":"表面污染：建立模型","titleEn":"Surface contamination: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues.","instruction":"把粒子、殘碳及刮傷分開，選擇各自靈敏的檢查。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate particles, carbon residue and scratches with suitable inspections. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題；清洗也可能改变表面終止態。","observationEn":"Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues; Cleaning can change surface termination.","failure":"若採用「晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「表面污染」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題。","checkEn":"Submit the Surface contamination diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-17-k1","title":"表面污染／物理與模型","titleEn":"Surface contamination / Physics and model","text":"機制：清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題。","textEn":"Mechanism: Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues."},{"id":"a081-v8-17-k2","title":"表面污染／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Surface contamination / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「表面污染」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Surface contamination, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在","清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題","晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨"],"optionsEn":["Taking non-detection by one method as absence","Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues","Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality"],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-17"],"title":"表面污染：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Surface contamination: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality.","instruction":"接續前一步「表面污染」成果，先指出錯誤主張「晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：清洗也可能改变表面終止態。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Surface contamination artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cleaning can change surface termination. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題；清洗也可能改变表面終止態。","observationEn":"Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues; Cleaning can change surface termination.","failure":"若採用「晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「表面污染」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「清洗也可能改变表面終止態」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Surface contamination, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cleaning can change surface termination\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-18-k1","title":"表面污染／物理與模型","titleEn":"Surface contamination / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：清洗也可能改变表面終止態。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cleaning can change surface termination."},{"id":"a081-v8-18-k2","title":"表面污染／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Surface contamination / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨」與「清潔度與晶體缺陷是不同問題」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality\" is not equivalent to \"Cleanliness and crystallographic defects are different issues\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「表面污染」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Surface contamination?","options":["晶體 X 光合格就證明表面潔淨","某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在","清洗也可能改变表面終止態"],"optionsEn":["Inferring surface cleanliness from crystal X-ray quality","Taking non-detection by one method as absence","Cleaning can change surface termination"],"answer":2,"explanation":"清洗也可能改变表面終止態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cleaning can change surface termination. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a081-stage04","order":4,"title":"缺陷檢出率 → 磊晶放行","titleEn":"Defect detectability to Epitaxy release","description":"把「缺陷檢出率」「晶粒接受區」「磊晶放行」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Defect detectability, Die acceptance regions, Epitaxy release.","steps":[{"id":"a081-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-18"],"title":"缺陷檢出率：建立模型","titleEn":"Defect detectability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Methods have different visibility for a given defect.","instruction":"將光致發光、表面影像與電性圖配對，記錄各法盲點。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Correlate photoluminescence, surface images and electrical maps with blind spots. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同；漏檢與誤檢都應量化。","observationEn":"Methods have different visibility for a given defect; Quantify misses as well as false detections.","failure":"若採用「某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Taking non-detection by one method as absence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「缺陷檢出率」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Defect detectability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Methods have different visibility for a given defect.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-19-k1","title":"缺陷檢出率／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect detectability / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Methods have different visibility for a given defect."},{"id":"a081-v8-19-k2","title":"缺陷檢出率／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect detectability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Taking non-detection by one method as absence."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷檢出率」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Defect detectability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同","某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在","每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒"],"optionsEn":["Methods have different visibility for a given defect","Taking non-detection by one method as absence","Assuming every defect kills every die equally"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Methods have different visibility for a given defect. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-19"],"title":"缺陷檢出率：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Defect detectability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Taking non-detection by one method as absence.","instruction":"接續前一步「缺陷檢出率」成果，先指出錯誤主張「某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：漏檢與誤檢都應量化。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Defect detectability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Taking non-detection by one method as absence\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Quantify misses as well as false detections. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同；漏檢與誤檢都應量化。","observationEn":"Methods have different visibility for a given defect; Quantify misses as well as false detections.","failure":"若採用「某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Taking non-detection by one method as absence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「缺陷檢出率」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「漏檢與誤檢都應量化」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Defect detectability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Quantify misses as well as false detections\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-20-k1","title":"缺陷檢出率／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect detectability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：漏檢與誤檢都應量化。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Quantify misses as well as false detections."},{"id":"a081-v8-20-k2","title":"缺陷檢出率／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect detectability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在」與「不同方法對同一缺陷的可見性不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Taking non-detection by one method as absence\" is not equivalent to \"Methods have different visibility for a given defect\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「缺陷檢出率」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Defect detectability?","options":["每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒","漏檢與誤檢都應量化","某法未看見就證明缺陷不存在"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every defect kills every die equally","Quantify misses as well as false detections","Taking non-detection by one method as absence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏檢與誤檢都應量化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Quantify misses as well as false detections. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-20"],"title":"晶粒接受區：建立模型","titleEn":"Die acceptance regions: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity.","instruction":"將缺陷座標覆到假設晶粒版圖，區分主動區與外圍。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Overlay defects on hypothetical dies and separate active regions from periphery. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度；元件終端區也可能對缺陷敏感。","observationEn":"Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity; Device termination can also be defect-sensitive.","failure":"若採用「每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every defect kills every die equally\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶粒接受區」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度。","checkEn":"Submit the Die acceptance regions diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-21-k1","title":"晶粒接受區／物理與模型","titleEn":"Die acceptance regions / Physics and model","text":"機制：缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity."},{"id":"a081-v8-21-k2","title":"晶粒接受區／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Die acceptance regions / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming every defect kills every die equally."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶粒接受區」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Die acceptance regions, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒","只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格","缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every defect kills every die equally","Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements","Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity"],"answer":2,"explanation":"缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-21"],"title":"晶粒接受區：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Die acceptance regions: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming every defect kills every die equally.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶粒接受區」成果，先指出錯誤主張「每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：元件終端區也可能對缺陷敏感。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Die acceptance regions artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming every defect kills every die equally\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Device termination can also be defect-sensitive. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度；元件終端區也可能對缺陷敏感。","observationEn":"Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity; Device termination can also be defect-sensitive.","failure":"若採用「每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every defect kills every die equally\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶粒接受區」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「元件終端區也可能對缺陷敏感」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Die acceptance regions, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Device termination can also be defect-sensitive\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-22-k1","title":"晶粒接受區／物理與模型","titleEn":"Die acceptance regions / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：元件終端區也可能對缺陷敏感。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Device termination can also be defect-sensitive."},{"id":"a081-v8-22-k2","title":"晶粒接受區／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Die acceptance regions / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒」與「缺陷風險取決於位置與元件敏感度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming every defect kills every die equally\" is not equivalent to \"Defect risk depends on location and device sensitivity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶粒接受區」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Die acceptance regions?","options":["元件終端區也可能對缺陷敏感","每顆缺陷都以同一方式殺死所有晶粒","只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格"],"optionsEn":["Device termination can also be defect-sensitive","Assuming every defect kills every die equally","Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements"],"answer":0,"explanation":"元件終端區也可能對缺陷敏感；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Device termination can also be defect-sensitive. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-22"],"title":"磊晶放行：建立模型","titleEn":"Epitaxy release: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs.","instruction":"整合厚度、摻雜、缺陷、粗糙與基板追溯表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine thickness, doping, defects, roughness and substrate traceability. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求；放行規格應固定所用缺陷定義。","observationEn":"Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs; Release specifications need fixed defect definitions.","failure":"若採用「只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「磊晶放行」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求。","checkEn":"Submit the Epitaxy release diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-23-k1","title":"磊晶放行／物理與模型","titleEn":"Epitaxy release / Physics and model","text":"機制：磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs."},{"id":"a081-v8-23-k2","title":"磊晶放行／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Epitaxy release / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「磊晶放行」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Epitaxy release, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看 Si:C 比就確認多型","磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求","只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格"],"optionsEn":["Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone","Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs","Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a081-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-sic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a081-v8-23"],"title":"磊晶放行：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Epitaxy release: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements.","instruction":"接續前一步「磊晶放行」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：放行規格應固定所用缺陷定義。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Epitaxy release artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Release specifications need fixed defect definitions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求；放行規格應固定所用缺陷定義。","observationEn":"Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs; Release specifications need fixed defect definitions.","failure":"若採用「只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「磊晶放行」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「放行規格應固定所用缺陷定義」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Epitaxy release, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Release specifications need fixed defect definitions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a081-v8-24-k1","title":"磊晶放行／物理與模型","titleEn":"Epitaxy release / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：放行規格應固定所用缺陷定義。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Release specifications need fixed defect definitions."},{"id":"a081-v8-24-k2","title":"磊晶放行／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Epitaxy release / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格」與「磊晶放行須連到後續元件需求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements\" is not equivalent to \"Epitaxy release must connect to downstream device needs\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「磊晶放行」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Epitaxy release?","options":["只選缺陷密度最低批次而忽略其他規格","只看 Si:C 比就確認多型","放行規格應固定所用缺陷定義"],"optionsEn":["Selecting minimum defect density while ignoring other requirements","Identifying polytype from Si:C ratio alone","Release specifications need fixed defect definitions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"放行規格應固定所用缺陷定義；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Release specifications need fixed defect definitions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"compound","subcategoryTitle":"化合物與新材料元件","subcategoryTitleEn":"Compound and emerging devices"},{"id":"a082","title":"碳化矽 MOSFET 製程","titleEn":"Silicon-carbide MOSFET processing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從垂直元件路徑、植入與活化到晶片到模組：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Vertical device path and Implantation and activation to Die-to-module validation: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["垂直元件路徑","閘氧電場","接觸電阻","閾值穩定"],"labelsEn":["Vertical device path","Gate-oxide field","Contact resistance","Threshold stability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a082-stage01","order":1,"title":"垂直元件路徑 → 通道界面","titleEn":"Vertical device path to Channel interface","description":"把「垂直元件路徑」「阻斷設計」「通道界面」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Vertical device path, Blocking design, Channel interface.","steps":[{"id":"a082-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"垂直元件路徑：建立模型","titleEn":"Vertical device path: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions.","instruction":"畫源極、通道、漂移層與背面汲極，追蹤導通。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw source, channel, drift region and backside drain and trace conduction. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成；封裝引線也貢獻量到的電阻。","observationEn":"Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions; Package leads contribute measured resistance.","failure":"若採用「把全部導通電阻都歸給通道」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all on-resistance to the channel\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「垂直元件路徑」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成。","checkEn":"Submit the Vertical device path diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-01-k1","title":"垂直元件路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Vertical device path / Physics and model","text":"機制：垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成。","textEn":"Mechanism: Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions."},{"id":"a082-v8-01-k2","title":"垂直元件路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Vertical device path / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把全部導通電阻都歸給通道」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing all on-resistance to the channel."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂直元件路徑」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Vertical device path, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成","把全部導通電阻都歸給通道","任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量"],"optionsEn":["Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions","Attributing all on-resistance to the channel","Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-01"],"title":"垂直元件路徑：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Vertical device path: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把全部導通電阻都歸給通道」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing all on-resistance to the channel.","instruction":"接續前一步「垂直元件路徑」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把全部導通電阻都歸給通道」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：封裝引線也貢獻量到的電阻。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Vertical device path artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing all on-resistance to the channel\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Package leads contribute measured resistance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成；封裝引線也貢獻量到的電阻。","observationEn":"Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions; Package leads contribute measured resistance.","failure":"若採用「把全部導通電阻都歸給通道」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all on-resistance to the channel\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「垂直元件路徑」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「封裝引線也貢獻量到的電阻」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Vertical device path, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Package leads contribute measured resistance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-02-k1","title":"垂直元件路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Vertical device path / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：封裝引線也貢獻量到的電阻。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Package leads contribute measured resistance."},{"id":"a082-v8-02-k2","title":"垂直元件路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Vertical device path / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把全部導通電阻都歸給通道」與「垂直 MOSFET 的電阻由多區域組成」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing all on-resistance to the channel\" is not equivalent to \"Vertical MOSFET resistance has multiple regional contributions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「垂直元件路徑」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Vertical device path?","options":["任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量","封裝引線也貢獻量到的電阻","把全部導通電阻都歸給通道"],"optionsEn":["Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin","Package leads contribute measured resistance","Attributing all on-resistance to the channel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"封裝引線也貢獻量到的電阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Package leads contribute measured resistance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-02"],"title":"阻斷設計：建立模型","titleEn":"Blocking design: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs.","instruction":"比較假設漂移厚度與摻雜，分開耐壓及電阻趨勢。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical drift thickness/doping for blocking and resistance trends. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨；終端設計可先限制理論漂移層能力。","observationEn":"Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs; Termination may limit ideal drift-layer capability.","failure":"若採用「任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「阻斷設計」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨。","checkEn":"Submit the Blocking design diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-03-k1","title":"阻斷設計／物理與模型","titleEn":"Blocking design / Physics and model","text":"機制：低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨。","textEn":"Mechanism: Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs."},{"id":"a082-v8-03-k2","title":"阻斷設計／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Blocking design / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「阻斷設計」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Blocking design, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量","只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道","低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨"],"optionsEn":["Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin","Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone","Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-03"],"title":"阻斷設計：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Blocking design: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin.","instruction":"接續前一步「阻斷設計」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：終端設計可先限制理論漂移層能力。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Blocking design artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Termination may limit ideal drift-layer capability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨；終端設計可先限制理論漂移層能力。","observationEn":"Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs; Termination may limit ideal drift-layer capability.","failure":"若採用「任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「阻斷設計」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「終端設計可先限制理論漂移層能力」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Blocking design, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Termination may limit ideal drift-layer capability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-04-k1","title":"阻斷設計／物理與模型","titleEn":"Blocking design / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：終端設計可先限制理論漂移層能力。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Termination may limit ideal drift-layer capability."},{"id":"a082-v8-04-k2","title":"阻斷設計／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Blocking design / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量」與「低電阻與高阻斷能力需要取捨」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin\" is not equivalent to \"Low resistance and high blocking require tradeoffs\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「阻斷設計」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Blocking design?","options":["終端設計可先限制理論漂移層能力","任意提高摻雜卻保持同樣阻斷裕量","只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道"],"optionsEn":["Termination may limit ideal drift-layer capability","Increasing doping arbitrarily while retaining blocking margin","Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"終端設計可先限制理論漂移層能力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Termination may limit ideal drift-layer capability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-04"],"title":"通道界面：建立模型","titleEn":"Channel interface: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold.","instruction":"畫 SiC/氧化層捕捉態與通道載子，定義遷移率量測條件。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw interface traps/carriers and define mobility-measurement conditions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值；場效遷移率抽取受到接觸電阻影響。","observationEn":"Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold; Field-effect mobility extraction includes contact effects.","failure":"若採用「只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「通道界面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值。","checkEn":"Submit the Channel interface diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-05-k1","title":"通道界面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel interface / Physics and model","text":"機制：界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值。","textEn":"Mechanism: Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold."},{"id":"a082-v8-05-k2","title":"通道界面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel interface / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通道界面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Channel interface, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓","界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值","只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道"],"optionsEn":["Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance","Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold","Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-05"],"title":"通道界面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Channel interface: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「通道界面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：場效遷移率抽取受到接觸電阻影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Channel interface artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Field-effect mobility extraction includes contact effects. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值；場效遷移率抽取受到接觸電阻影響。","observationEn":"Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold; Field-effect mobility extraction includes contact effects.","failure":"若採用「只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「通道界面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「場效遷移率抽取受到接觸電阻影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Channel interface, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Field-effect mobility extraction includes contact effects\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-06-k1","title":"通道界面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel interface / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：場效遷移率抽取受到接觸電阻影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Field-effect mobility extraction includes contact effects."},{"id":"a082-v8-06-k2","title":"通道界面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel interface / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道」與「界面捕捉態可影響通道與閾值」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone\" is not equivalent to \"Interface traps affect channel behavior and threshold\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「通道界面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Channel interface?","options":["只用體材料遷移率預測 MOS 通道","元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓","場效遷移率抽取受到接觸電阻影響"],"optionsEn":["Predicting the MOS channel from bulk mobility alone","Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance","Field-effect mobility extraction includes contact effects"],"answer":2,"explanation":"場效遷移率抽取受到接觸電阻影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Field-effect mobility extraction includes contact effects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a082-stage02","order":2,"title":"閘氧電場 → 平面與溝槽","titleEn":"Gate-oxide field to Planar versus trench","description":"把「閘氧電場」「植入與活化」「平面與溝槽」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Gate-oxide field, Implantation and activation, Planar versus trench.","steps":[{"id":"a082-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-06"],"title":"閘氧電場：建立模型","titleEn":"Gate-oxide field: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking.","instruction":"對截面標出 SiC 和氧化層的電位降，比較角落場集中。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark SiC/oxide voltage division and corner field crowding. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓；溝槽角落需要局部場分析。","observationEn":"Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking; Trench corners require local field analysis.","failure":"若採用「元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閘氧電場」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓。","checkEn":"Submit the Gate-oxide field diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-07-k1","title":"閘氧電場／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate-oxide field / Physics and model","text":"機制：氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓。","textEn":"Mechanism: Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking."},{"id":"a082-v8-07-k2","title":"閘氧電場／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate-oxide field / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘氧電場」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Gate-oxide field, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓","元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓","只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻"],"optionsEn":["Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking","Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance","Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-07"],"title":"閘氧電場：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Gate-oxide field: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance.","instruction":"接續前一步「閘氧電場」成果，先指出錯誤主張「元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：溝槽角落需要局部場分析。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Gate-oxide field artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Trench corners require local field analysis. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓；溝槽角落需要局部場分析。","observationEn":"Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking; Trench corners require local field analysis.","failure":"若採用「元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閘氧電場」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「溝槽角落需要局部場分析」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Gate-oxide field, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Trench corners require local field analysis\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-08-k1","title":"閘氧電場／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate-oxide field / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：溝槽角落需要局部場分析。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Trench corners require local field analysis."},{"id":"a082-v8-08-k2","title":"閘氧電場／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate-oxide field / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓」與「氧化層電場可靠度不同於漂移層耐壓」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance\" is not equivalent to \"Oxide-field reliability differs from drift blocking\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閘氧電場」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Gate-oxide field?","options":["只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻","溝槽角落需要局部場分析","元件耐壓高便代表閘極可承相同高壓"],"optionsEn":["Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone","Trench corners require local field analysis","Assuming high drain rating implies equal gate-voltage tolerance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"溝槽角落需要局部場分析；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Trench corners require local field analysis. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-08"],"title":"植入與活化：建立模型","titleEn":"Implantation and activation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Implanted dose is not identical to active doping.","instruction":"畫假設植入輪廓與電性活化輪廓，區分總雜質與有效載子。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare implanted and electrically active profiles. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜；活化熱處理同時影響表面形貌。","observationEn":"Implanted dose is not identical to active doping; Activation heating can alter surface morphology.","failure":"若採用「只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「植入與活化」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜。","checkEn":"Submit the Implantation and activation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Implanted dose is not identical to active doping.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-09-k1","title":"植入與活化／物理與模型","titleEn":"Implantation and activation / Physics and model","text":"機制：植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜。","textEn":"Mechanism: Implanted dose is not identical to active doping."},{"id":"a082-v8-09-k2","title":"植入與活化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Implantation and activation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「植入與活化」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Implantation and activation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻","溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面","植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜"],"optionsEn":["Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone","Assuming denser trenches are universally superior","Implanted dose is not identical to active doping"],"answer":2,"explanation":"植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Implanted dose is not identical to active doping. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-09"],"title":"植入與活化：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Implantation and activation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「植入與活化」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：活化熱處理同時影響表面形貌。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Implantation and activation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Activation heating can alter surface morphology. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜；活化熱處理同時影響表面形貌。","observationEn":"Implanted dose is not identical to active doping; Activation heating can alter surface morphology.","failure":"若採用「只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「植入與活化」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「活化熱處理同時影響表面形貌」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Implantation and activation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Activation heating can alter surface morphology\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-10-k1","title":"植入與活化／物理與模型","titleEn":"Implantation and activation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：活化熱處理同時影響表面形貌。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Activation heating can alter surface morphology."},{"id":"a082-v8-10-k2","title":"植入與活化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Implantation and activation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻」與「植入劑量不直接等於有效摻雜」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone\" is not equivalent to \"Implanted dose is not identical to active doping\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「植入與活化」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Implantation and activation?","options":["活化熱處理同時影響表面形貌","只看劑量就證明接觸區電阻","溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面"],"optionsEn":["Activation heating can alter surface morphology","Inferring contact-region resistance from dose alone","Assuming denser trenches are universally superior"],"answer":0,"explanation":"活化熱處理同時影響表面形貌；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Activation heating can alter surface morphology. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-10"],"title":"平面與溝槽：建立模型","titleEn":"Planar versus trench: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment.","instruction":"畫兩種通道及溝槽角落，列出面積、通道和場管理差別。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare channels/corners with area and field-management tradeoffs. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估；不同晶面通道性質可能不同。","observationEn":"Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment; Channel properties can depend on crystal face.","failure":"若採用「溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming denser trenches are universally superior\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「平面與溝槽」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估。","checkEn":"Submit the Planar versus trench diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-11-k1","title":"平面與溝槽／物理與模型","titleEn":"Planar versus trench / Physics and model","text":"機制：溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估。","textEn":"Mechanism: Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment."},{"id":"a082-v8-11-k2","title":"平面與溝槽／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Planar versus trench / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming denser trenches are universally superior."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平面與溝槽」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Planar versus trench, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻","溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估","溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面"],"optionsEn":["Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance","Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment","Assuming denser trenches are universally superior"],"answer":1,"explanation":"溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-11"],"title":"平面與溝槽：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Planar versus trench: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming denser trenches are universally superior.","instruction":"接續前一步「平面與溝槽」成果，先指出錯誤主張「溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：不同晶面通道性質可能不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Planar versus trench artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming denser trenches are universally superior\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Channel properties can depend on crystal face. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估；不同晶面通道性質可能不同。","observationEn":"Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment; Channel properties can depend on crystal face.","failure":"若採用「溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming denser trenches are universally superior\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「平面與溝槽」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「不同晶面通道性質可能不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Planar versus trench, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Channel properties can depend on crystal face\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-12-k1","title":"平面與溝槽／物理與模型","titleEn":"Planar versus trench / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：不同晶面通道性質可能不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Channel properties can depend on crystal face."},{"id":"a082-v8-12-k2","title":"平面與溝槽／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Planar versus trench / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面」與「溝槽面積利益需連同角落保護評估」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming denser trenches are universally superior\" is not equivalent to \"Trench density benefits require corner-field assessment\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「平面與溝槽」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Planar versus trench?","options":["溝槽較密就必然全面優於平面","把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻","不同晶面通道性質可能不同"],"optionsEn":["Assuming denser trenches are universally superior","Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance","Channel properties can depend on crystal face"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同晶面通道性質可能不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Channel properties can depend on crystal face. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a082-stage03","order":3,"title":"接觸電阻 → 體二極體","titleEn":"Contact resistance to Body diode","description":"把「接觸電阻」「邊緣終端」「體二極體」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Contact resistance, Edge termination, Body diode.","steps":[{"id":"a082-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-12"],"title":"接觸電阻：建立模型","titleEn":"Contact resistance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms.","instruction":"用假設 TLM 長度系列區分片電阻與接觸截距。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Use hypothetical TLM spacings to separate sheet resistance and contact intercept. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻；接觸模型需要確認線性工作範圍。","observationEn":"Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms; Contact models need verified linear ranges.","failure":"若採用「把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸電阻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻。","checkEn":"Submit the Contact resistance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-13-k1","title":"接觸電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact resistance / Physics and model","text":"機制：二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms."},{"id":"a082-v8-13-k2","title":"接觸電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact resistance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸電阻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Contact resistance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻","把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻","只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓"],"optionsEn":["Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms","Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance","Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model"],"answer":0,"explanation":"二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-13"],"title":"接觸電阻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Contact resistance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸電阻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸模型需要確認線性工作範圍。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Contact resistance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Contact models need verified linear ranges. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻；接觸模型需要確認線性工作範圍。","observationEn":"Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms; Contact models need verified linear ranges.","failure":"若採用「把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸電阻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸模型需要確認線性工作範圍」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Contact resistance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Contact models need verified linear ranges\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-14-k1","title":"接觸電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact resistance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸模型需要確認線性工作範圍。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Contact models need verified linear ranges."},{"id":"a082-v8-14-k2","title":"接觸電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact resistance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻」與「二端電阻含接觸和通道貢獻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance\" is not equivalent to \"Two-terminal resistance includes contact and channel terms\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸電阻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Contact resistance?","options":["只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓","接觸模型需要確認線性工作範圍","把二端總電阻直接當接觸電阻"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model","Contact models need verified linear ranges","Calling total two-terminal resistance contact resistance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸模型需要確認線性工作範圍；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact models need verified linear ranges. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-14"],"title":"邊緣終端：建立模型","titleEn":"Edge termination: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Die edges can limit blocking first.","instruction":"畫主接面、終端環與表面，指出場線擴展。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw main junction, termination rings and surface with field spreading. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力；表面污染會改變終端性能。","observationEn":"Die edges can limit blocking first; Surface contamination changes termination behavior.","failure":"若採用「只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「邊緣終端」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力。","checkEn":"Submit the Edge termination diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Die edges can limit blocking first.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-15-k1","title":"邊緣終端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Edge termination / Physics and model","text":"機制：晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Die edges can limit blocking first."},{"id":"a082-v8-15-k2","title":"邊緣終端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Edge termination / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「邊緣終端」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Edge termination, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓","所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體","晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model","Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode","Die edges can limit blocking first"],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Die edges can limit blocking first. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-15"],"title":"邊緣終端：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Edge termination: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model.","instruction":"接續前一步「邊緣終端」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：表面污染會改變終端性能。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Edge termination artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Surface contamination changes termination behavior. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力；表面污染會改變終端性能。","observationEn":"Die edges can limit blocking first; Surface contamination changes termination behavior.","failure":"若採用「只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「邊緣終端」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「表面污染會改變終端性能」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Edge termination, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Surface contamination changes termination behavior\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-16-k1","title":"邊緣終端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Edge termination / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：表面污染會改變終端性能。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Surface contamination changes termination behavior."},{"id":"a082-v8-16-k2","title":"邊緣終端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Edge termination / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓」與「晶片邊緣可能先限制阻斷能力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model\" is not equivalent to \"Die edges can limit blocking first\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「邊緣終端」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Edge termination?","options":["表面污染會改變終端性能","只模擬無限大單元就保證整顆耐壓","所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體"],"optionsEn":["Surface contamination changes termination behavior","Guaranteeing die blocking from an infinite-cell model","Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面污染會改變終端性能；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface contamination changes termination behavior. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-16"],"title":"體二極體：建立模型","titleEn":"Body diode: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior.","instruction":"畫反向導通的體二極體和受控通道路徑，分清載子。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Distinguish reverse body-diode and gated-channel paths with carrier types. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化；體二極體注入可影響結構缺陷。","observationEn":"Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior; Body-diode injection can affect structural defects.","failure":"若採用「所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「體二極體」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化。","checkEn":"Submit the Body diode diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-17-k1","title":"體二極體／物理與模型","titleEn":"Body diode / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior."},{"id":"a082-v8-17-k2","title":"體二極體／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Body diode / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「體二極體」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Body diode, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移","不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化","所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體"],"optionsEn":["Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay","Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior","Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-17"],"title":"體二極體：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Body diode: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode.","instruction":"接續前一步「體二極體」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：體二極體注入可影響結構缺陷。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Body diode artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Body-diode injection can affect structural defects. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化；體二極體注入可影響結構缺陷。","observationEn":"Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior; Body-diode injection can affect structural defects.","failure":"若採用「所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「體二極體」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「體二極體注入可影響結構缺陷」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Body diode, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Body-diode injection can affect structural defects\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-18-k1","title":"體二極體／物理與模型","titleEn":"Body diode / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：體二極體注入可影響結構缺陷。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Body-diode injection can affect structural defects."},{"id":"a082-v8-18-k2","title":"體二極體／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Body diode / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體」與「不同反向導通路徑有不同損耗及退化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode\" is not equivalent to \"Reverse paths have different loss and degradation behavior\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「體二極體」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Body diode?","options":["所有反向電流都只經同一理想二極體","忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移","體二極體注入可影響結構缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Sending all reverse current through one ideal diode","Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay","Body-diode injection can affect structural defects"],"answer":2,"explanation":"體二極體注入可影響結構缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Body-diode injection can affect structural defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a082-stage04","order":4,"title":"閾值穩定 → 晶片到模組","titleEn":"Threshold stability to Die-to-module validation","description":"把「閾值穩定」「動態損耗」「晶片到模組」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Threshold stability, Dynamic losses, Die-to-module validation.","steps":[{"id":"a082-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-18"],"title":"閾值穩定：建立模型","titleEn":"Threshold stability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects.","instruction":"比較正負閘應力後不同延遲的 Vth，保留恢復時間。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare post-stress Vth at different delays and retain recovery time. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應；掃描速度也會改變表觀 Vth。","observationEn":"Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects; Sweep speed changes apparent threshold.","failure":"若採用「忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閾值穩定」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應。","checkEn":"Submit the Threshold stability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-19-k1","title":"閾值穩定／物理與模型","titleEn":"Threshold stability / Physics and model","text":"機制：測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects."},{"id":"a082-v8-19-k2","title":"閾值穩定／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Threshold stability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閾值穩定」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Threshold stability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應","忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移","只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案"],"optionsEn":["Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects","Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay","Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-19"],"title":"閾值穩定：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Threshold stability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay.","instruction":"接續前一步「閾值穩定」成果，先指出錯誤主張「忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：掃描速度也會改變表觀 Vth。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Threshold stability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sweep speed changes apparent threshold. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應；掃描速度也會改變表觀 Vth。","observationEn":"Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects; Sweep speed changes apparent threshold.","failure":"若採用「忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閾值穩定」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「掃描速度也會改變表觀 Vth」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Threshold stability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sweep speed changes apparent threshold\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-20-k1","title":"閾值穩定／物理與模型","titleEn":"Threshold stability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：掃描速度也會改變表觀 Vth。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sweep speed changes apparent threshold."},{"id":"a082-v8-20-k2","title":"閾值穩定／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Threshold stability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移」與「測量延遲可改變觀察到的捕捉效應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay\" is not equivalent to \"Measurement delay changes observed trapping effects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閾值穩定」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Threshold stability?","options":["只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案","掃描速度也會改變表觀 Vth","忽略應力後延遲直接比較漂移"],"optionsEn":["Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone","Sweep speed changes apparent threshold","Comparing drift while ignoring post-stress delay"],"answer":1,"explanation":"掃描速度也會改變表觀 Vth；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sweep speed changes apparent threshold. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-20"],"title":"動態損耗：建立模型","titleEn":"Dynamic losses: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss.","instruction":"以假設 V(t)I(t) 積分比較切換損耗與導通損耗。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設功率開關在特定溫度的 RDS(on)=10 mΩ，導通電流 10 A、占空比先設為 100%，導通損耗 I²R=1 W。若熱態電阻加倍，損耗為 2 W。這不含切換、閘極驅動或反向恢復損耗；若占空比為 50% 且電流維持矩形 10 A，平均導通損耗才各減半。另假設每周期切換能量 Eon+Eoff=10 µJ、頻率 100 kHz，切換功率為 1 W，冷態 50% 導通加切換合計 1.5 W，仍未含驅動損耗。","instructionEn":"Integrate hypothetical V(t)I(t) and compare switching/conduction losses. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a power switch has RDS(on)=10 mΩ at a specified temperature and conducts 10 A continuously: I²R=1 W. Doubling hot-state resistance gives 2 W. Switching, gate-drive and reverse-recovery losses are excluded. At 50% duty with rectangular 10 A current, average conduction loss halves in each case. Also assume switching energy Eon+Eoff=10 µJ per cycle at 100 kHz: switching power is 1 W, so the cold 50%-duty conduction-plus-switching total is 1.5 W, still excluding drive losses.","observation":"低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗；電壓電流探棒時間偏移會誤算能量。","observationEn":"Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss; Probe timing mismatch biases switching energy.","failure":"若採用「只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「動態損耗」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗。\n算例驗收：驗算連續導通 1 W、熱態 2 W、50% 占空比下 0.5/1 W 及冷態含切換的 1.5 W，勿用平均電流直接平方取代 RMS。","checkEn":"Submit the Dynamic losses diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 1 W continuous, 2 W hot, 0.5/1 W at 50% duty and the cold 1.5 W total including switching; do not square average current instead of using RMS current.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-21-k1","title":"動態損耗／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dynamic losses / Physics and model","text":"機制：低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗。","textEn":"Mechanism: Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss."},{"id":"a082-v8-21-k2","title":"動態損耗／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dynamic losses / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案」。\n假設數值與推算：假設功率開關在特定溫度的 RDS(on)=10 mΩ，導通電流 10 A、占空比先設為 100%，導通損耗 I²R=1 W。若熱態電阻加倍，損耗為 2 W。這不含切換、閘極驅動或反向恢復損耗；若占空比為 50% 且電流維持矩形 10 A，平均導通損耗才各減半。另假設每周期切換能量 Eon+Eoff=10 µJ、頻率 100 kHz，切換功率為 1 W，冷態 50% 導通加切換合計 1.5 W，仍未含驅動損耗。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a power switch has RDS(on)=10 mΩ at a specified temperature and conducts 10 A continuously: I²R=1 W. Doubling hot-state resistance gives 2 W. Switching, gate-drive and reverse-recovery losses are excluded. At 50% duty with rectangular 10 A current, average conduction loss halves in each case. Also assume switching energy Eon+Eoff=10 µJ per cycle at 100 kHz: switching power is 1 W, so the cold 50%-duty conduction-plus-switching total is 1.5 W, still excluding drive losses."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「動態損耗」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dynamic losses, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案","裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證","低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗"],"optionsEn":["Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone","Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass","Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss"],"answer":2,"explanation":"低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-21"],"title":"動態損耗：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dynamic losses: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「動態損耗」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電壓電流探棒時間偏移會誤算能量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dynamic losses artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Probe timing mismatch biases switching energy. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗；電壓電流探棒時間偏移會誤算能量。","observationEn":"Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss; Probe timing mismatch biases switching energy.","failure":"若採用「只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「動態損耗」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電壓電流探棒時間偏移會誤算能量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dynamic losses, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Probe timing mismatch biases switching energy\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-22-k1","title":"動態損耗／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dynamic losses / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電壓電流探棒時間偏移會誤算能量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Probe timing mismatch biases switching energy."},{"id":"a082-v8-22-k2","title":"動態損耗／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dynamic losses / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案」與「低 RDS(on) 不保證最低總損耗」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone\" is not equivalent to \"Low on-resistance does not guarantee minimum total loss\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「動態損耗」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dynamic losses?","options":["電壓電流探棒時間偏移會誤算能量","只按室溫導通電阻選最高頻方案","裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證"],"optionsEn":["Probe timing mismatch biases switching energy","Selecting high-frequency devices by room-temperature resistance alone","Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電壓電流探棒時間偏移會誤算能量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Probe timing mismatch biases switching energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-22"],"title":"晶片到模組：建立模型","titleEn":"Die-to-module validation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress.","instruction":"合併閘氧、終端、接觸與封裝熱阻的驗收證據。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine gate, termination, contact and package thermal evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力；熱循環也會改變封裝界面。","observationEn":"Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress; Thermal cycling can alter package interfaces.","failure":"若採用「裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶片到模組」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力。","checkEn":"Submit the Die-to-module validation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-23-k1","title":"晶片到模組／物理與模型","titleEn":"Die-to-module validation / Physics and model","text":"機制：封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress."},{"id":"a082-v8-23-k2","title":"晶片到模組／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Die-to-module validation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶片到模組」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Die-to-module validation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把全部導通電阻都歸給通道","封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力","裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all on-resistance to the channel","Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress","Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass"],"answer":1,"explanation":"封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a082-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-sic","v8-c-sic-gate","v8-c-sic-life"],"prerequisiteIds":["a082-v8-23"],"title":"晶片到模組：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Die-to-module validation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶片到模組」成果，先指出錯誤主張「裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：熱循環也會改變封裝界面。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Die-to-module validation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thermal cycling can alter package interfaces. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力；熱循環也會改變封裝界面。","observationEn":"Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress; Thermal cycling can alter package interfaces.","failure":"若採用「裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶片到模組」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「熱循環也會改變封裝界面」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Die-to-module validation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thermal cycling can alter package interfaces\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a082-v8-24-k1","title":"晶片到模組／物理與模型","titleEn":"Die-to-module validation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：熱循環也會改變封裝界面。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thermal cycling can alter package interfaces."},{"id":"a082-v8-24-k2","title":"晶片到模組／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Die-to-module validation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證」與「封裝及驅動條件會改變元件實際應力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass\" is not equivalent to \"Package and drive conditions alter actual device stress\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶片到模組」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Die-to-module validation?","options":["裸晶測試合格就取消模組條件驗證","把全部導通電阻都歸給通道","熱循環也會改變封裝界面"],"optionsEn":["Skipping module-condition validation after a bare-die pass","Attributing all on-resistance to the channel","Thermal cycling can alter package interfaces"],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱循環也會改變封裝界面；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal cycling can alter package interfaces. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"compound","subcategoryTitle":"化合物與新材料元件","subcategoryTitleEn":"Compound and emerging devices"},{"id":"a083","title":"氮化鎵高電子遷移率電晶體","titleEn":"Gallium-nitride high-electron-mobility transistors","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從異質接面、緩衝層到整合驗證：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Heterojunction and Buffer layer to Integration verification: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["異質接面","p-GaN 與凹槽","場板","功率與 RF"],"labelsEn":["Heterojunction","p-GaN and recessed gates","Field plates","Power versus RF"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a083-stage01","order":1,"title":"異質接面 → 常開與常關","titleEn":"Heterojunction to Normally on/off","description":"把「異質接面」「極化電荷」「常開與常關」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Heterojunction, Polarization charge, Normally on/off.","steps":[{"id":"a083-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"異質接面：建立模型","titleEn":"Heterojunction: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer.","instruction":"畫 AlGaN/GaN 與能帶井，定位二維電子氣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw AlGaN/GaN and its band well and locate the 2DEG. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層；界面粗糙會影響通道散射。","observationEn":"A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer; Interface roughness affects channel scattering.","failure":"若採用「把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「異質接面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層。","checkEn":"Submit the Heterojunction diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-01-k1","title":"異質接面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heterojunction / Physics and model","text":"機制：異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層。","textEn":"Mechanism: A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer."},{"id":"a083-v8-01-k2","title":"異質接面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heterojunction / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「異質接面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Heterojunction, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層","把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜","將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流"],"optionsEn":["A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer","Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping","Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles"],"answer":0,"explanation":"異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-01"],"title":"異質接面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Heterojunction: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping.","instruction":"接續前一步「異質接面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：界面粗糙會影響通道散射。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Heterojunction artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Interface roughness affects channel scattering. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層；界面粗糙會影響通道散射。","observationEn":"A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer; Interface roughness affects channel scattering.","failure":"若採用「把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「異質接面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「界面粗糙會影響通道散射」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Heterojunction, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Interface roughness affects channel scattering\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-02-k1","title":"異質接面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heterojunction / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：界面粗糙會影響通道散射。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Interface roughness affects channel scattering."},{"id":"a083-v8-02-k2","title":"異質接面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heterojunction / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜」與「異質接面通道不同於矽 MOS 反轉層」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping\" is not equivalent to \"A heterojunction channel differs from a silicon inversion layer\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「異質接面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Heterojunction?","options":["將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流","界面粗糙會影響通道散射","把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜"],"optionsEn":["Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles","Interface roughness affects channel scattering","Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping"],"answer":1,"explanation":"界面粗糙會影響通道散射；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Interface roughness affects channel scattering. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-02"],"title":"極化電荷：建立模型","titleEn":"Polarization charge: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations.","instruction":"標出界面電荷及能帶彎曲，區分自由載子與固定電荷。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark interface charge/band bending and separate fixed charge from mobile carriers. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群；極化符號依晶向與應變定義。","observationEn":"Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations; Polarization signs depend on orientation and strain.","failure":"若採用「將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「極化電荷」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群。","checkEn":"Submit the Polarization charge diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-03-k1","title":"極化電荷／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization charge / Physics and model","text":"機制：極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群。","textEn":"Mechanism: Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations."},{"id":"a083-v8-03-k2","title":"極化電荷／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization charge / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「極化電荷」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Polarization charge, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流","只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關","極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群"],"optionsEn":["Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles","Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver","Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations"],"answer":2,"explanation":"極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-03"],"title":"極化電荷：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Polarization charge: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles.","instruction":"接續前一步「極化電荷」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：極化符號依晶向與應變定義。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Polarization charge artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Polarization signs depend on orientation and strain. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群；極化符號依晶向與應變定義。","observationEn":"Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations; Polarization signs depend on orientation and strain.","failure":"若採用「將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「極化電荷」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「極化符號依晶向與應變定義」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Polarization charge, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Polarization signs depend on orientation and strain\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-04-k1","title":"極化電荷／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization charge / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：極化符號依晶向與應變定義。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Polarization signs depend on orientation and strain."},{"id":"a083-v8-04-k2","title":"極化電荷／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization charge / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流」與「極化電荷和載流子不是相同族群」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles\" is not equivalent to \"Polarization charge and mobile carriers are different populations\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「極化電荷」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Polarization charge?","options":["極化符號依晶向與應變定義","將固定極化電荷當成直接流動電流","只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關"],"optionsEn":["Polarization signs depend on orientation and strain","Treating fixed polarization charge as current-carrying particles","Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver"],"answer":0,"explanation":"極化符號依晶向與應變定義；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Polarization signs depend on orientation and strain. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-04"],"title":"常開與常關：建立模型","titleEn":"Normally on/off: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias.","instruction":"比較零閘壓下通道是否耗盡的兩個能帶圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare zero-gate-bias band diagrams with/devoid of a channel. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道；閾值分布需保留溫度條件。","observationEn":"Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias; Threshold distributions need temperature context.","failure":"若採用「只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「常開與常關」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道。","checkEn":"Submit the Normally on/off diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-05-k1","title":"常開與常關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Normally on/off / Physics and model","text":"機制：常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道。","textEn":"Mechanism: Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias."},{"id":"a083-v8-05-k2","title":"常開與常關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Normally on/off / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「常開與常關」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Normally on/off, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格","常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道","只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關"],"optionsEn":["Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types","Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias","Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver"],"answer":1,"explanation":"常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-05"],"title":"常開與常關：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Normally on/off: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver.","instruction":"接續前一步「常開與常關」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：閾值分布需保留溫度條件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Normally on/off artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Threshold distributions need temperature context. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道；閾值分布需保留溫度條件。","observationEn":"Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias; Threshold distributions need temperature context.","failure":"若採用「只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「常開與常關」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「閾值分布需保留溫度條件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Normally on/off, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Threshold distributions need temperature context\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-06-k1","title":"常開與常關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Normally on/off / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：閾值分布需保留溫度條件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Threshold distributions need temperature context."},{"id":"a083-v8-06-k2","title":"常開與常關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Normally on/off / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關」與「常關需要在零閘壓抑制通道」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver\" is not equivalent to \"Normally-off operation requires channel suppression at zero gate bias\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「常開與常關」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Normally on/off?","options":["只把驅動器關掉就把常開元件變成常關","對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格","閾值分布需保留溫度條件"],"optionsEn":["Turning a normally-on device off merely by disabling its driver","Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types","Threshold distributions need temperature context"],"answer":2,"explanation":"閾值分布需保留溫度條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Threshold distributions need temperature context. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a083-stage02","order":2,"title":"p-GaN 與凹槽 → 歐姆接觸","titleEn":"p-GaN and recessed gates to Ohmic contacts","description":"把「p-GaN 與凹槽」「緩衝層」「歐姆接觸」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for p-GaN and recessed gates, Buffer layer, Ohmic contacts.","steps":[{"id":"a083-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-06"],"title":"p-GaN 與凹槽：建立模型","titleEn":"p-GaN and recessed gates: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同常關架構有不同閘極容限」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances.","instruction":"畫兩種閘極改造，分開材料移除和電性耗盡。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw gate alternatives and distinguish removal from electrical depletion. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同常關架構有不同閘極容限；凹槽蝕刻損傷可能增加陷阱。","observationEn":"Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances; Recess etch damage can add traps.","failure":"若採用「對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「p-GaN 與凹槽」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同常關架構有不同閘極容限。","checkEn":"Submit the p-GaN and recessed gates diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-07-k1","title":"p-GaN 與凹槽／物理與模型","titleEn":"p-GaN and recessed gates / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同常關架構有不同閘極容限。","textEn":"Mechanism: Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances."},{"id":"a083-v8-07-k2","title":"p-GaN 與凹槽／驗證與限制","titleEn":"p-GaN and recessed gates / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「p-GaN 與凹槽」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For p-GaN and recessed gates, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同常關架構有不同閘極容限","對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格","緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性"],"optionsEn":["Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances","Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types","Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同常關架構有不同閘極容限；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-07"],"title":"p-GaN 與凹槽：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"p-GaN and recessed gates: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types.","instruction":"接續前一步「p-GaN 與凹槽」成果，先指出錯誤主張「對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：凹槽蝕刻損傷可能增加陷阱。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding p-GaN and recessed gates artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Recess etch damage can add traps. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同常關架構有不同閘極容限；凹槽蝕刻損傷可能增加陷阱。","observationEn":"Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances; Recess etch damage can add traps.","failure":"若採用「對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「p-GaN 與凹槽」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「凹槽蝕刻損傷可能增加陷阱」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for p-GaN and recessed gates, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Recess etch damage can add traps\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-08-k1","title":"p-GaN 與凹槽／物理與模型","titleEn":"p-GaN and recessed gates / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：凹槽蝕刻損傷可能增加陷阱。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Recess etch damage can add traps."},{"id":"a083-v8-08-k2","title":"p-GaN 與凹槽／驗證與限制","titleEn":"p-GaN and recessed gates / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格」與「不同常關架構有不同閘極容限」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types\" is not equivalent to \"Normally-off architectures have different gate tolerances\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「p-GaN 與凹槽」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of p-GaN and recessed gates?","options":["緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性","凹槽蝕刻損傷可能增加陷阱","對所有 GaN 共用同一閘極電壓規格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property","Recess etch damage can add traps","Using one gate-voltage limit for all GaN types"],"answer":1,"explanation":"凹槽蝕刻損傷可能增加陷阱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Recess etch damage can add traps. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-08"],"title":"緩衝層：建立模型","titleEn":"Buffer layer: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration.","instruction":"畫基板、緩衝及通道，列出漏電與應力路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw substrate, buffer and channel and mark leakage/stress paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合；基板漏電與表面漏電需分離。","observationEn":"Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration; Separate substrate from surface leakage.","failure":"若採用「緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「緩衝層」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合。","checkEn":"Submit the Buffer layer diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-09-k1","title":"緩衝層／物理與模型","titleEn":"Buffer layer / Physics and model","text":"機制：緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合。","textEn":"Mechanism: Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration."},{"id":"a083-v8-09-k2","title":"緩衝層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Buffer layer / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「緩衝層」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Buffer layer, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性","只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失","緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property","Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone","Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration"],"answer":2,"explanation":"緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-09"],"title":"緩衝層：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Buffer layer: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property.","instruction":"接續前一步「緩衝層」成果，先指出錯誤主張「緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：基板漏電與表面漏電需分離。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Buffer layer artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Separate substrate from surface leakage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合；基板漏電與表面漏電需分離。","observationEn":"Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration; Separate substrate from surface leakage.","failure":"若採用「緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「緩衝層」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「基板漏電與表面漏電需分離」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Buffer layer, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Separate substrate from surface leakage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-10-k1","title":"緩衝層／物理與模型","titleEn":"Buffer layer / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：基板漏電與表面漏電需分離。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Separate substrate from surface leakage."},{"id":"a083-v8-10-k2","title":"緩衝層／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Buffer layer / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性」與「緩衝層同時關係絕緣、缺陷與機械整合」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property\" is not equivalent to \"Buffers affect isolation, defects and mechanical integration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「緩衝層」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Buffer layer?","options":["基板漏電與表面漏電需分離","緩衝越厚就無條件改善所有電性","只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失"],"optionsEn":["Separate substrate from surface leakage","Assuming thicker buffers improve every electrical property","Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"基板漏電與表面漏電需分離；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Separate substrate from surface leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-10"],"title":"歐姆接觸：建立模型","titleEn":"Ohmic contacts: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance.","instruction":"以假設 TLM 資料分離接觸電阻和接觸間通道電阻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設線性 TLM 回歸 Rtotal(L) 的零距離截距為 0.4 Ω，兩端接觸相同且寄生已扣除，截距=2Rc，所以每個接觸 Rc=0.2 Ω。未給接觸寬度，不能報成 Ω·mm；若 I-V 非線性或兩接觸不同，此抽取就需修改。","instructionEn":"Separate contact and channel resistance with hypothetical TLM data. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a linear TLM fit Rtotal(L) has a zero-spacing intercept of 0.4 Ω, with identical contacts and parasitics removed. The intercept is 2Rc, giving Rc=0.2 Ω per contact. Without width, do not report Ω·mm; nonlinear I-V or unequal contacts invalidates the simple extraction.","observation":"接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能；接觸正規化需註明單位寬度。","observationEn":"Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance; Contact normalization needs width conventions.","failure":"若採用「只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「歐姆接觸」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能。\n算例驗收：驗算 0.2 Ω，區分總截距、單接觸電阻與寬度歸一化電阻。","checkEn":"Submit the Ohmic contacts diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 0.2 Ω and distinguish total intercept, single-contact resistance and width-normalized resistance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-11-k1","title":"歐姆接觸／物理與模型","titleEn":"Ohmic contacts / Physics and model","text":"機制：接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能。","textEn":"Mechanism: Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance."},{"id":"a083-v8-11-k2","title":"歐姆接觸／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Ohmic contacts / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失」。\n假設數值與推算：假設線性 TLM 回歸 Rtotal(L) 的零距離截距為 0.4 Ω，兩端接觸相同且寄生已扣除，截距=2Rc，所以每個接觸 Rc=0.2 Ω。未給接觸寬度，不能報成 Ω·mm；若 I-V 非線性或兩接觸不同，此抽取就需修改。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a linear TLM fit Rtotal(L) has a zero-spacing intercept of 0.4 Ω, with identical contacts and parasitics removed. The intercept is 2Rc, giving Rc=0.2 Ω per contact. Without width, do not report Ω·mm; nonlinear I-V or unequal contacts invalidates the simple extraction."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「歐姆接觸」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Ohmic contacts, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價","接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能","只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失"],"optionsEn":["Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost","Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance","Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-11"],"title":"歐姆接觸：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Ohmic contacts: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「歐姆接觸」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸正規化需註明單位寬度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Ohmic contacts artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Contact normalization needs width conventions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能；接觸正規化需註明單位寬度。","observationEn":"Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance; Contact normalization needs width conventions.","failure":"若採用「只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「歐姆接觸」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸正規化需註明單位寬度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Ohmic contacts, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Contact normalization needs width conventions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-12-k1","title":"歐姆接觸／物理與模型","titleEn":"Ohmic contacts / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸正規化需註明單位寬度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Contact normalization needs width conventions."},{"id":"a083-v8-12-k2","title":"歐姆接觸／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Ohmic contacts / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失」與「接觸電阻影響導通和 RF 性能」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone\" is not equivalent to \"Contact resistance affects conduction and RF performance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「歐姆接觸」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Ohmic contacts?","options":["只提高通道遷移率就消除所有串聯損失","場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價","接觸正規化需註明單位寬度"],"optionsEn":["Eliminating all series loss by increasing mobility alone","Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost","Contact normalization needs width conventions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸正規化需註明單位寬度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact normalization needs width conventions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a083-stage03","order":3,"title":"場板 → 反向導通","titleEn":"Field plates to Reverse conduction","description":"把「場板」「動態導通電阻」「反向導通」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Field plates, Dynamic on-resistance, Reverse conduction.","steps":[{"id":"a083-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-12"],"title":"場板：建立模型","titleEn":"Field plates: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Field shaping may also increase capacitance.","instruction":"畫場板前後的場線和寄生電容，建立兩項取捨。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch field spreading and parasitic capacitance before/after a field plate. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容；增加寄生電容可能增加切換能量。","observationEn":"Field shaping may also increase capacitance; Added capacitance can increase switching energy.","failure":"若採用「場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「場板」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容。","checkEn":"Submit the Field plates diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Field shaping may also increase capacitance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-13-k1","title":"場板／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field plates / Physics and model","text":"機制：場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容。","textEn":"Mechanism: Field shaping may also increase capacitance."},{"id":"a083-v8-13-k2","title":"場板／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field plates / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「場板」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Field plates, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容","場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價","只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境"],"optionsEn":["Field shaping may also increase capacitance","Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost","Using DC resistance for every switching condition"],"answer":0,"explanation":"場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Field shaping may also increase capacitance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-13"],"title":"場板：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Field plates: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost.","instruction":"接續前一步「場板」成果，先指出錯誤主張「場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：增加寄生電容可能增加切換能量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Field plates artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Added capacitance can increase switching energy. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容；增加寄生電容可能增加切換能量。","observationEn":"Field shaping may also increase capacitance; Added capacitance can increase switching energy.","failure":"若採用「場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「場板」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「增加寄生電容可能增加切換能量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Field plates, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Added capacitance can increase switching energy\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-14-k1","title":"場板／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field plates / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：增加寄生電容可能增加切換能量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Added capacitance can increase switching energy."},{"id":"a083-v8-14-k2","title":"場板／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field plates / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價」與「場形塑可能同時增加寄生電容」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost\" is not equivalent to \"Field shaping may also increase capacitance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「場板」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Field plates?","options":["只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境","增加寄生電容可能增加切換能量","場板只提升耐壓而完全沒有動態代價"],"optionsEn":["Using DC resistance for every switching condition","Added capacitance can increase switching energy","Assuming field plates add blocking with no dynamic cost"],"answer":1,"explanation":"增加寄生電容可能增加切換能量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Added capacitance can increase switching energy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-14"],"title":"動態導通電阻：建立模型","titleEn":"Dynamic on-resistance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance.","instruction":"比較靜態與高壓休止後脈衝導通，記錄延遲與溫度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare static and post-blocking pulsed conduction with delay/temperature recorded. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻；量測延遲可掩蓋快速恢復。","observationEn":"Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance; Measurement delays hide fast recovery.","failure":"若採用「只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using DC resistance for every switching condition\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「動態導通電阻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻。","checkEn":"Submit the Dynamic on-resistance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-15-k1","title":"動態導通電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dynamic on-resistance / Physics and model","text":"機制：捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance."},{"id":"a083-v8-15-k2","title":"動態導通電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dynamic on-resistance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using DC resistance for every switching condition."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「動態導通電阻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dynamic on-resistance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境","把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上","捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻"],"optionsEn":["Using DC resistance for every switching condition","Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged","Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-15"],"title":"動態導通電阻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dynamic on-resistance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using DC resistance for every switching condition.","instruction":"接續前一步「動態導通電阻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：量測延遲可掩蓋快速恢復。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dynamic on-resistance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using DC resistance for every switching condition\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Measurement delays hide fast recovery. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻；量測延遲可掩蓋快速恢復。","observationEn":"Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance; Measurement delays hide fast recovery.","failure":"若採用「只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using DC resistance for every switching condition\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「動態導通電阻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「量測延遲可掩蓋快速恢復」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dynamic on-resistance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Measurement delays hide fast recovery\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-16-k1","title":"動態導通電阻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dynamic on-resistance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：量測延遲可掩蓋快速恢復。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Measurement delays hide fast recovery."},{"id":"a083-v8-16-k2","title":"動態導通電阻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dynamic on-resistance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境」與「捕捉與自熱可能共同影響動態電阻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using DC resistance for every switching condition\" is not equivalent to \"Trapping and self-heating can jointly affect dynamic resistance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「動態導通電阻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dynamic on-resistance?","options":["量測延遲可掩蓋快速恢復","只用直流電阻代表所有切換情境","把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上"],"optionsEn":["Measurement delays hide fast recovery","Using DC resistance for every switching condition","Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged"],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測延遲可掩蓋快速恢復；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Measurement delays hide fast recovery. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-16"],"title":"反向導通：建立模型","titleEn":"Reverse conduction: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure.","instruction":"畫橫向 HEMT 第三象限通道與矽體二極體差別。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare lateral-HEMT third-quadrant channel and silicon body diode. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構；反向導通壓降會受閘偏壓影響。","observationEn":"Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure; Reverse drop depends on gate bias.","failure":"若採用「把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「反向導通」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構。","checkEn":"Submit the Reverse conduction diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-17-k1","title":"反向導通／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reverse conduction / Physics and model","text":"機制：橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構。","textEn":"Mechanism: Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure."},{"id":"a083-v8-17-k2","title":"反向導通／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reverse conduction / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「反向導通」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Reverse conduction, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益","橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構","把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上"],"optionsEn":["Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain","Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure","Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged"],"answer":1,"explanation":"橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-17"],"title":"反向導通：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Reverse conduction: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged.","instruction":"接續前一步「反向導通」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：反向導通壓降會受閘偏壓影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Reverse conduction artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reverse drop depends on gate bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構；反向導通壓降會受閘偏壓影響。","observationEn":"Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure; Reverse drop depends on gate bias.","failure":"若採用「把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「反向導通」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「反向導通壓降會受閘偏壓影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Reverse conduction, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reverse drop depends on gate bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-18-k1","title":"反向導通／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reverse conduction / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：反向導通壓降會受閘偏壓影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reverse drop depends on gate bias."},{"id":"a083-v8-18-k2","title":"反向導通／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reverse conduction / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上」與「橫向 GaN HEMT 不靠同樣的矽體二極體結構」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged\" is not equivalent to \"Lateral GaN HEMTs do not use the same silicon body-diode structure\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「反向導通」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Reverse conduction?","options":["把矽二極體反向恢復模型原封套上","一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益","反向導通壓降會受閘偏壓影響"],"optionsEn":["Copying a silicon diode recovery model unchanged","Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain","Reverse drop depends on gate bias"],"answer":2,"explanation":"反向導通壓降會受閘偏壓影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reverse drop depends on gate bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a083-stage04","order":4,"title":"功率與 RF → 整合驗證","titleEn":"Power versus RF to Integration verification","description":"把「功率與 RF」「熱路徑」「整合驗證」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Power versus RF, Thermal paths, Integration verification.","steps":[{"id":"a083-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-18"],"title":"功率與 RF：建立模型","titleEn":"Power versus RF: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The best structure for one material depends on application.","instruction":"對切換電源及放大器各列出損耗、線性、頻寬要求。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"List loss, linearity and bandwidth needs for switches versus amplifiers. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異；RF 效率必須附頻率與輸出條件。","observationEn":"The best structure for one material depends on application; RF efficiency needs frequency and output conditions.","failure":"若採用「一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「功率與 RF」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異。","checkEn":"Submit the Power versus RF diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The best structure for one material depends on application.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-19-k1","title":"功率與 RF／物理與模型","titleEn":"Power versus RF / Physics and model","text":"機制：同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異。","textEn":"Mechanism: The best structure for one material depends on application."},{"id":"a083-v8-19-k2","title":"功率與 RF／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Power versus RF / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「功率與 RF」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Power versus RF, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異","一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益","只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率"],"optionsEn":["The best structure for one material depends on application","Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain","Determining allowable power from bandgap alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The best structure for one material depends on application. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-19"],"title":"功率與 RF：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Power versus RF: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain.","instruction":"接續前一步「功率與 RF」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：RF 效率必須附頻率與輸出條件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Power versus RF artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: RF efficiency needs frequency and output conditions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異；RF 效率必須附頻率與輸出條件。","observationEn":"The best structure for one material depends on application; RF efficiency needs frequency and output conditions.","failure":"若採用「一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「功率與 RF」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「RF 效率必須附頻率與輸出條件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Power versus RF, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"RF efficiency needs frequency and output conditions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-20-k1","title":"功率與 RF／物理與模型","titleEn":"Power versus RF / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：RF 效率必須附頻率與輸出條件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: RF efficiency needs frequency and output conditions."},{"id":"a083-v8-20-k2","title":"功率與 RF／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Power versus RF / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益」與「同一材料的最佳結構依用途而異」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain\" is not equivalent to \"The best structure for one material depends on application\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「功率與 RF」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Power versus RF?","options":["只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率","RF 效率必須附頻率與輸出條件","一顆最高耐壓元件就必然有最佳 RF 增益"],"optionsEn":["Determining allowable power from bandgap alone","RF efficiency needs frequency and output conditions","Assuming maximum voltage rating ensures best RF gain"],"answer":1,"explanation":"RF 效率必須附頻率與輸出條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"RF efficiency needs frequency and output conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-20"],"title":"熱路徑：建立模型","titleEn":"Thermal paths: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高臨界電場不代表容易散熱」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: High critical field does not imply easy heat removal.","instruction":"畫通道熱點經基板、界面到散熱器的路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Trace channel hotspots through substrate/interfaces to a heat sink. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高臨界電場不代表容易散熱；熱界面電阻可能主導局部溫升。","observationEn":"High critical field does not imply easy heat removal; Thermal-interface resistance may dominate heating.","failure":"若採用「只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Determining allowable power from bandgap alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱路徑」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高臨界電場不代表容易散熱。","checkEn":"Submit the Thermal paths diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: High critical field does not imply easy heat removal.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-21-k1","title":"熱路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal paths / Physics and model","text":"機制：高臨界電場不代表容易散熱。","textEn":"Mechanism: High critical field does not imply easy heat removal."},{"id":"a083-v8-21-k2","title":"熱路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal paths / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Determining allowable power from bandgap alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱路徑」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thermal paths, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率","以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格","高臨界電場不代表容易散熱"],"optionsEn":["Determining allowable power from bandgap alone","Treating one research record as a production specification","High critical field does not imply easy heat removal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"高臨界電場不代表容易散熱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"High critical field does not imply easy heat removal. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-21"],"title":"熱路徑：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal paths: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Determining allowable power from bandgap alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱路徑」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：熱界面電阻可能主導局部溫升。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thermal paths artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Determining allowable power from bandgap alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thermal-interface resistance may dominate heating. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高臨界電場不代表容易散熱；熱界面電阻可能主導局部溫升。","observationEn":"High critical field does not imply easy heat removal; Thermal-interface resistance may dominate heating.","failure":"若採用「只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Determining allowable power from bandgap alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱路徑」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「熱界面電阻可能主導局部溫升」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thermal paths, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thermal-interface resistance may dominate heating\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-22-k1","title":"熱路徑／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal paths / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：熱界面電阻可能主導局部溫升。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thermal-interface resistance may dominate heating."},{"id":"a083-v8-22-k2","title":"熱路徑／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal paths / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率」與「高臨界電場不代表容易散熱」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Determining allowable power from bandgap alone\" is not equivalent to \"High critical field does not imply easy heat removal\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱路徑」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thermal paths?","options":["熱界面電阻可能主導局部溫升","只看材料能隙就決定可容許功率","以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格"],"optionsEn":["Thermal-interface resistance may dominate heating","Determining allowable power from bandgap alone","Treating one research record as a production specification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱界面電阻可能主導局部溫升；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal-interface resistance may dominate heating. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-22"],"title":"整合驗證：建立模型","titleEn":"Integration verification: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification.","instruction":"合併閘極、緩衝、接觸、動態電阻與溫度的矩陣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine gate, buffer, contact, dynamic-resistance and thermal evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證；封裝寄生電感可能造成閘極過衝。","observationEn":"Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification; Package inductance can cause gate overshoot.","failure":"若採用「以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one research record as a production specification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「整合驗證」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證。","checkEn":"Submit the Integration verification diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-23-k1","title":"整合驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Integration verification / Physics and model","text":"機制：低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證。","textEn":"Mechanism: Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification."},{"id":"a083-v8-23-k2","title":"整合驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Integration verification / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating one research record as a production specification."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「整合驗證」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Integration verification, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜","低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證","以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格"],"optionsEn":["Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping","Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification","Treating one research record as a production specification"],"answer":1,"explanation":"低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a083-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gan","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a083-v8-23"],"title":"整合驗證：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Integration verification: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating one research record as a production specification.","instruction":"接續前一步「整合驗證」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：封裝寄生電感可能造成閘極過衝。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Integration verification artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating one research record as a production specification\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Package inductance can cause gate overshoot. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證；封裝寄生電感可能造成閘極過衝。","observationEn":"Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification; Package inductance can cause gate overshoot.","failure":"若採用「以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one research record as a production specification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「整合驗證」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「封裝寄生電感可能造成閘極過衝」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Integration verification, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Package inductance can cause gate overshoot\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a083-v8-24-k1","title":"整合驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Integration verification / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：封裝寄生電感可能造成閘極過衝。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Package inductance can cause gate overshoot."},{"id":"a083-v8-24-k2","title":"整合驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Integration verification / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格」與「低壓研究示範不可直接當高壓產品認證」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating one research record as a production specification\" is not equivalent to \"Low-voltage demonstrations are not high-voltage qualification\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「整合驗證」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Integration verification?","options":["以單一研究最佳值代表完整量產規格","把 2DEG 畫成整片均勻體摻雜","封裝寄生電感可能造成閘極過衝"],"optionsEn":["Treating one research record as a production specification","Drawing the 2DEG as uniform bulk doping","Package inductance can cause gate overshoot"],"answer":2,"explanation":"封裝寄生電感可能造成閘極過衝；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Package inductance can cause gate overshoot. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"compound","subcategoryTitle":"化合物與新材料元件","subcategoryTitleEn":"Compound and emerging devices"},{"id":"a084","title":"氮化鎵發光二極體磊晶","titleEn":"Gallium-nitride LED epitaxy","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize","v8-c-nagoya-place","v8-c-nagoya-history","v8-c-nagoya-map","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從直接能隙、組成與波長到磊晶驗收：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Direct bandgap and Composition and wavelength to Epitaxy acceptance: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["直接能隙","量子井","多重量子井","效率下降"],"labelsEn":["Direct bandgap","Quantum wells","Multiple quantum wells","Efficiency droop"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a084-stage01","order":1,"title":"直接能隙 → n 型與 p 型","titleEn":"Direct bandgap to n-type and p-type","description":"把「直接能隙」「基板失配」「n 型與 p 型」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Direct bandgap, Substrate mismatch, n-type and p-type.","steps":[{"id":"a084-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"直接能隙：建立模型","titleEn":"Direct bandgap: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電流不會全部轉換成出射光」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Not all current becomes emitted light.","instruction":"用能帶示意比較輻射和非輻射復合，標示能量出口。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare radiative/nonradiative recombination and energy destinations. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電流不會全部轉換成出射光；非輻射復合可轉為熱。","observationEn":"Not all current becomes emitted light; Nonradiative recombination produces heat.","failure":"若採用「以注入電流直接等同光子流」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating injected current with photon flux\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「直接能隙」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電流不會全部轉換成出射光。","checkEn":"Submit the Direct bandgap diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Not all current becomes emitted light.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-01-k1","title":"直接能隙／物理與模型","titleEn":"Direct bandgap / Physics and model","text":"機制：電流不會全部轉換成出射光。","textEn":"Mechanism: Not all current becomes emitted light."},{"id":"a084-v8-01-k2","title":"直接能隙／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Direct bandgap / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以注入電流直接等同光子流」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating injected current with photon flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「直接能隙」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Direct bandgap, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["電流不會全部轉換成出射光","以注入電流直接等同光子流","加緩衝層便完全消除失配"],"optionsEn":["Not all current becomes emitted light","Equating injected current with photon flux","Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電流不會全部轉換成出射光；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Not all current becomes emitted light. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-01"],"title":"直接能隙：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Direct bandgap: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以注入電流直接等同光子流」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating injected current with photon flux.","instruction":"接續前一步「直接能隙」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以注入電流直接等同光子流」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：非輻射復合可轉為熱。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Direct bandgap artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating injected current with photon flux\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Nonradiative recombination produces heat. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電流不會全部轉換成出射光；非輻射復合可轉為熱。","observationEn":"Not all current becomes emitted light; Nonradiative recombination produces heat.","failure":"若採用「以注入電流直接等同光子流」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating injected current with photon flux\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「直接能隙」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「非輻射復合可轉為熱」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Direct bandgap, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Nonradiative recombination produces heat\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-02-k1","title":"直接能隙／物理與模型","titleEn":"Direct bandgap / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：非輻射復合可轉為熱。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Nonradiative recombination produces heat."},{"id":"a084-v8-02-k2","title":"直接能隙／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Direct bandgap / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以注入電流直接等同光子流」與「電流不會全部轉換成出射光」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating injected current with photon flux\" is not equivalent to \"Not all current becomes emitted light\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「直接能隙」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Direct bandgap?","options":["加緩衝層便完全消除失配","非輻射復合可轉為熱","以注入電流直接等同光子流"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch","Nonradiative recombination produces heat","Equating injected current with photon flux"],"answer":1,"explanation":"非輻射復合可轉為熱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Nonradiative recombination produces heat. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-02"],"title":"基板失配：建立模型","titleEn":"Substrate mismatch: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material.","instruction":"畫藍寶石與 GaN 晶格失配，加入緩衝層角色。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw sapphire/GaN mismatch and the buffer role. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷；差排密度和出光效率非一對一。","observationEn":"Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material; Dislocation density is not one-to-one with efficiency.","failure":"若採用「加緩衝層便完全消除失配」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「基板失配」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷。","checkEn":"Submit the Substrate mismatch diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-03-k1","title":"基板失配／物理與模型","titleEn":"Substrate mismatch / Physics and model","text":"機制：緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material."},{"id":"a084-v8-03-k2","title":"基板失配／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Substrate mismatch / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「加緩衝層便完全消除失配」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基板失配」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Substrate mismatch, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["加緩衝層便完全消除失配","用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度","緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch","Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration","Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material"],"answer":2,"explanation":"緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-03"],"title":"基板失配：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Substrate mismatch: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「加緩衝層便完全消除失配」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch.","instruction":"接續前一步「基板失配」成果，先指出錯誤主張「加緩衝層便完全消除失配」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：差排密度和出光效率非一對一。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Substrate mismatch artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dislocation density is not one-to-one with efficiency. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷；差排密度和出光效率非一對一。","observationEn":"Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material; Dislocation density is not one-to-one with efficiency.","failure":"若採用「加緩衝層便完全消除失配」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「基板失配」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「差排密度和出光效率非一對一」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Substrate mismatch, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dislocation density is not one-to-one with efficiency\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-04-k1","title":"基板失配／物理與模型","titleEn":"Substrate mismatch / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：差排密度和出光效率非一對一。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dislocation density is not one-to-one with efficiency."},{"id":"a084-v8-04-k2","title":"基板失配／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Substrate mismatch / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「加緩衝層便完全消除失配」與「緩衝設計有助成長但不保證零缺陷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch\" is not equivalent to \"Buffers aid growth without guaranteeing defect-free material\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「基板失配」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Substrate mismatch?","options":["差排密度和出光效率非一對一","加緩衝層便完全消除失配","用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度"],"optionsEn":["Dislocation density is not one-to-one with efficiency","Assuming a buffer eliminates all mismatch","Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"差排密度和出光效率非一對一；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dislocation density is not one-to-one with efficiency. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-04"],"title":"n 型與 p 型：建立模型","titleEn":"n-type and p-type: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density.","instruction":"畫電子與電洞注入，區分 Mg 摻入與電性活化。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw electron/hole injection and distinguish Mg incorporation from activation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞；氫可影響 Mg 受體活化。","observationEn":"Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density; Hydrogen can influence Mg-acceptor activation.","failure":"若採用「用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「n 型與 p 型」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞。","checkEn":"Submit the n-type and p-type diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-05-k1","title":"n 型與 p 型／物理與模型","titleEn":"n-type and p-type / Physics and model","text":"機制：摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞。","textEn":"Mechanism: Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density."},{"id":"a084-v8-05-k2","title":"n 型與 p 型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"n-type and p-type / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「n 型與 p 型」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For n-type and p-type, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層","摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞","用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度"],"optionsEn":["Treating wells as colored layers without band effects","Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density","Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration"],"answer":1,"explanation":"摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-05"],"title":"n 型與 p 型：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"n-type and p-type: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration.","instruction":"接續前一步「n 型與 p 型」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：氫可影響 Mg 受體活化。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding n-type and p-type artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Hydrogen can influence Mg-acceptor activation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞；氫可影響 Mg 受體活化。","observationEn":"Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density; Hydrogen can influence Mg-acceptor activation.","failure":"若採用「用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「n 型與 p 型」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「氫可影響 Mg 受體活化」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for n-type and p-type, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Hydrogen can influence Mg-acceptor activation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-06-k1","title":"n 型與 p 型／物理與模型","titleEn":"n-type and p-type / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：氫可影響 Mg 受體活化。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Hydrogen can influence Mg-acceptor activation."},{"id":"a084-v8-06-k2","title":"n 型與 p 型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"n-type and p-type / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度」與「摻入受體不必然產生等量自由電洞」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration\" is not equivalent to \"Acceptor incorporation need not produce equal free-hole density\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「n 型與 p 型」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of n-type and p-type?","options":["用 Mg 原子數直接當電洞濃度","只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層","氫可影響 Mg 受體活化"],"optionsEn":["Equating Mg atoms with free-hole concentration","Treating wells as colored layers without band effects","Hydrogen can influence Mg-acceptor activation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"氫可影響 Mg 受體活化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Hydrogen can influence Mg-acceptor activation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a084-stage02","order":2,"title":"量子井 → 極化內建場","titleEn":"Quantum wells to Polarization field","description":"把「量子井」「組成與波長」「極化內建場」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Quantum wells, Composition and wavelength, Polarization field.","steps":[{"id":"a084-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-06"],"title":"量子井：建立模型","titleEn":"Quantum wells: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement.","instruction":"畫 InGaN 井與 GaN 障壁，定位電子與電洞。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw InGaN wells/GaN barriers and locate carriers. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合；井寬變異會改變量子侷限。","observationEn":"Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement; Well-width variation changes confinement.","failure":"若採用「只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating wells as colored layers without band effects\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「量子井」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合。","checkEn":"Submit the Quantum wells diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-07-k1","title":"量子井／物理與模型","titleEn":"Quantum wells / Physics and model","text":"機制：量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合。","textEn":"Mechanism: Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement."},{"id":"a084-v8-07-k2","title":"量子井／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Quantum wells / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating wells as colored layers without band effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量子井」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Quantum wells, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合","只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層","只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長"],"optionsEn":["Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement","Treating wells as colored layers without band effects","Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio"],"answer":0,"explanation":"量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-07"],"title":"量子井：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Quantum wells: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating wells as colored layers without band effects.","instruction":"接續前一步「量子井」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：井寬變異會改變量子侷限。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Quantum wells artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating wells as colored layers without band effects\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Well-width variation changes confinement. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合；井寬變異會改變量子侷限。","observationEn":"Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement; Well-width variation changes confinement.","failure":"若採用「只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating wells as colored layers without band effects\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「量子井」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「井寬變異會改變量子侷限」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Quantum wells, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Well-width variation changes confinement\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-08-k1","title":"量子井／物理與模型","titleEn":"Quantum wells / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：井寬變異會改變量子侷限。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Well-width variation changes confinement."},{"id":"a084-v8-08-k2","title":"量子井／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Quantum wells / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層」與「量子井透過能帶侷限改變復合」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating wells as colored layers without band effects\" is not equivalent to \"Quantum wells modify recombination through confinement\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「量子井」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Quantum wells?","options":["只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長","井寬變異會改變量子侷限","只把井當成沒有能带作用的色層"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio","Well-width variation changes confinement","Treating wells as colored layers without band effects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"井寬變異會改變量子侷限；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Well-width variation changes confinement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-08"],"title":"組成與波長：建立模型","titleEn":"Composition and wavelength: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain.","instruction":"比較假設銦組成及應變對能量的影響，避免只用單一因素。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設 LED 光子波長為 450 nm，用 hc≈1240 eV·nm 得光子能量 E≈2.756 eV；若為 500 nm，E≈2.480 eV。畫出能量隨波長反向變化。這是光子關係，不保證等於材料體能隙，也未處理量子侷限、應變與譜線寬。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical indium-content and strain effects on energy. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume an LED photon wavelength of 450 nm. Using hc≈1240 eV·nm gives E≈2.756 eV; at 500 nm E≈2.480 eV. Plot the inverse wavelength relation. Photon energy need not equal bulk bandgap; confinement, strain and spectral width are excluded.","observation":"發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響；溫度也會改變發光光譜。","observationEn":"Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain; Temperature also shifts emission spectra.","failure":"若採用「只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「組成與波長」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響。\n算例驗收：驗算兩個能量，並說明較長波長為何對應較低光子能量。","checkEn":"Submit the Composition and wavelength diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both energies and explain why longer wavelength corresponds to lower photon energy.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-09-k1","title":"組成與波長／物理與模型","titleEn":"Composition and wavelength / Physics and model","text":"機制：發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響。","textEn":"Mechanism: Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain."},{"id":"a084-v8-09-k2","title":"組成與波長／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Composition and wavelength / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長」。\n假設數值與推算：假設 LED 光子波長為 450 nm，用 hc≈1240 eV·nm 得光子能量 E≈2.756 eV；若為 500 nm，E≈2.480 eV。畫出能量隨波長反向變化。這是光子關係，不保證等於材料體能隙，也未處理量子侷限、應變與譜線寬。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume an LED photon wavelength of 450 nm. Using hc≈1240 eV·nm gives E≈2.756 eV; at 500 nm E≈2.480 eV. Plot the inverse wavelength relation. Photon energy need not equal bulk bandgap; confinement, strain and spectral width are excluded."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「組成與波長」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Composition and wavelength, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長","能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊","發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio","Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap","Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain"],"answer":2,"explanation":"發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-09"],"title":"組成與波長：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Composition and wavelength: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio.","instruction":"接續前一步「組成與波長」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：溫度也會改變發光光譜。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Composition and wavelength artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Temperature also shifts emission spectra. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響；溫度也會改變發光光譜。","observationEn":"Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain; Temperature also shifts emission spectra.","failure":"若採用「只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「組成與波長」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「溫度也會改變發光光譜」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Composition and wavelength, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Temperature also shifts emission spectra\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-10-k1","title":"組成與波長／物理與模型","titleEn":"Composition and wavelength / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：溫度也會改變發光光譜。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Temperature also shifts emission spectra."},{"id":"a084-v8-10-k2","title":"組成與波長／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Composition and wavelength / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長」與「發光波長受組成、侷限與應變影響」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio\" is not equivalent to \"Emission depends on composition, confinement and strain\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「組成與波長」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Composition and wavelength?","options":["溫度也會改變發光光譜","只看一個化學比例就保證精確波長","能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊"],"optionsEn":["Temperature also shifts emission spectra","Guaranteeing exact wavelength from one composition ratio","Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap"],"answer":0,"explanation":"溫度也會改變發光光譜；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Temperature also shifts emission spectra. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-10"],"title":"極化內建場：建立模型","titleEn":"Polarization field: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「內建場可能分離電子與電洞」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Internal fields can separate electrons and holes.","instruction":"畫井中傾斜能帶與波函重疊，比較平帶參考。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw tilted-well bands and wavefunction overlap versus a flat-band reference. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"內建場可能分離電子與電洞；注入載子可屏蔽部分內建場。","observationEn":"Internal fields can separate electrons and holes; Injected carriers can screen internal fields.","failure":"若採用「能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「極化內建場」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：內建場可能分離電子與電洞。","checkEn":"Submit the Polarization field diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Internal fields can separate electrons and holes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-11-k1","title":"極化內建場／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization field / Physics and model","text":"機制：內建場可能分離電子與電洞。","textEn":"Mechanism: Internal fields can separate electrons and holes."},{"id":"a084-v8-11-k2","title":"極化內建場／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization field / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「極化內建場」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Polarization field, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率","內建場可能分離電子與電洞","能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current","Internal fields can separate electrons and holes","Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap"],"answer":1,"explanation":"內建場可能分離電子與電洞；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Internal fields can separate electrons and holes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-11"],"title":"極化內建場：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Polarization field: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap.","instruction":"接續前一步「極化內建場」成果，先指出錯誤主張「能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：注入載子可屏蔽部分內建場。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Polarization field artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Injected carriers can screen internal fields. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"內建場可能分離電子與電洞；注入載子可屏蔽部分內建場。","observationEn":"Internal fields can separate electrons and holes; Injected carriers can screen internal fields.","failure":"若採用「能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「極化內建場」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「注入載子可屏蔽部分內建場」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Polarization field, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Injected carriers can screen internal fields\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-12-k1","title":"極化內建場／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization field / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：注入載子可屏蔽部分內建場。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Injected carriers can screen internal fields."},{"id":"a084-v8-12-k2","title":"極化內建場／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization field / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊」與「內建場可能分離電子與電洞」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap\" is not equivalent to \"Internal fields can separate electrons and holes\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「極化內建場」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Polarization field?","options":["能障越高就必然有最大波函重疊","將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率","注入載子可屏蔽部分內建場"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher barriers always maximize overlap","Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current","Injected carriers can screen internal fields"],"answer":2,"explanation":"注入載子可屏蔽部分內建場；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Injected carriers can screen internal fields. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a084-stage03","order":3,"title":"多重量子井 → 光取出","titleEn":"Multiple quantum wells to Light extraction","description":"把「多重量子井」「電流擴展」「光取出」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Multiple quantum wells, Current spreading, Light extraction.","steps":[{"id":"a084-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-12"],"title":"多重量子井：建立模型","titleEn":"Multiple quantum wells: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「多井不表示每井注入完全相等」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well.","instruction":"畫各井載子分配，檢查是否均勻及可能溢流。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch carrier distribution across wells and inspect nonuniformity/spillover. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"多井不表示每井注入完全相等；井間傳輸受障壁和捕捉影響。","observationEn":"Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well; Inter-well transport depends on barriers and capture.","failure":"若採用「將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「多重量子井」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：多井不表示每井注入完全相等。","checkEn":"Submit the Multiple quantum wells diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-13-k1","title":"多重量子井／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multiple quantum wells / Physics and model","text":"機制：多井不表示每井注入完全相等。","textEn":"Mechanism: Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well."},{"id":"a084-v8-13-k2","title":"多重量子井／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multiple quantum wells / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多重量子井」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Multiple quantum wells, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["多井不表示每井注入完全相等","將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率","只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻"],"optionsEn":["Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well","Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current","Inferring uniform emission from total flux"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多井不表示每井注入完全相等；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-13"],"title":"多重量子井：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Multiple quantum wells: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current.","instruction":"接續前一步「多重量子井」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：井間傳輸受障壁和捕捉影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Multiple quantum wells artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Inter-well transport depends on barriers and capture. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"多井不表示每井注入完全相等；井間傳輸受障壁和捕捉影響。","observationEn":"Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well; Inter-well transport depends on barriers and capture.","failure":"若採用「將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「多重量子井」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「井間傳輸受障壁和捕捉影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Multiple quantum wells, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Inter-well transport depends on barriers and capture\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-14-k1","title":"多重量子井／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multiple quantum wells / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：井間傳輸受障壁和捕捉影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Inter-well transport depends on barriers and capture."},{"id":"a084-v8-14-k2","title":"多重量子井／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multiple quantum wells / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率」與「多井不表示每井注入完全相等」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current\" is not equivalent to \"Multiple wells do not imply equal injection per well\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「多重量子井」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Multiple quantum wells?","options":["只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻","井間傳輸受障壁和捕捉影響","將總電流平均分配便宣稱每井同效率"],"optionsEn":["Inferring uniform emission from total flux","Inter-well transport depends on barriers and capture","Assuming equal per-well efficiency by dividing current"],"answer":1,"explanation":"井間傳輸受障壁和捕捉影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Inter-well transport depends on barriers and capture. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-14"],"title":"電流擴展：建立模型","titleEn":"Current spreading: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission.","instruction":"畫接觸附近與遠處注入路徑，預測亮度不均。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Trace near/far-contact current paths and predict brightness variation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光；接觸遮光會降低有效出光。","observationEn":"Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission; Contact shading reduces optical extraction.","failure":"若採用「只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring uniform emission from total flux\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電流擴展」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光。","checkEn":"Submit the Current spreading diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-15-k1","title":"電流擴展／物理與模型","titleEn":"Current spreading / Physics and model","text":"機制：片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光。","textEn":"Mechanism: Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission."},{"id":"a084-v8-15-k2","title":"電流擴展／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Current spreading / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring uniform emission from total flux."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電流擴展」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Current spreading, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻","量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強","片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光"],"optionsEn":["Inferring uniform emission from total flux","Equating strong well emission with packaged light output","Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission"],"answer":2,"explanation":"片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-15"],"title":"電流擴展：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Current spreading: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring uniform emission from total flux.","instruction":"接續前一步「電流擴展」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸遮光會降低有效出光。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Current spreading artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring uniform emission from total flux\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Contact shading reduces optical extraction. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光；接觸遮光會降低有效出光。","observationEn":"Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission; Contact shading reduces optical extraction.","failure":"若採用「只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring uniform emission from total flux\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電流擴展」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸遮光會降低有效出光」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Current spreading, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Contact shading reduces optical extraction\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-16-k1","title":"電流擴展／物理與模型","titleEn":"Current spreading / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸遮光會降低有效出光。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Contact shading reduces optical extraction."},{"id":"a084-v8-16-k2","title":"電流擴展／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Current spreading / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻」與「片電阻與接觸配置影響均勻發光」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring uniform emission from total flux\" is not equivalent to \"Sheet resistance and contact layout affect uniform emission\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電流擴展」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Current spreading?","options":["接觸遮光會降低有效出光","只看總光通量便證明整面發光均勻","量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強"],"optionsEn":["Contact shading reduces optical extraction","Inferring uniform emission from total flux","Equating strong well emission with packaged light output"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸遮光會降低有效出光；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact shading reduces optical extraction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-16"],"title":"光取出：建立模型","titleEn":"Light extraction: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency.","instruction":"畫逃逸錐、全反射及粗化表面路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw escape cone, total reflection and textured-surface paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同；外部效率還包括載子注入效率。","observationEn":"Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency; External efficiency also includes injection efficiency.","failure":"若採用「量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating strong well emission with packaged light output\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「光取出」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Light extraction diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-17-k1","title":"光取出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Light extraction / Physics and model","text":"機制：內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency."},{"id":"a084-v8-17-k2","title":"光取出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Light extraction / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating strong well emission with packaged light output."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「光取出」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Light extraction, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因","內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同","量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強"],"optionsEn":["Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone","Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency","Equating strong well emission with packaged light output"],"answer":1,"explanation":"內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-17"],"title":"光取出：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Light extraction: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating strong well emission with packaged light output.","instruction":"接續前一步「光取出」成果，先指出錯誤主張「量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：外部效率還包括載子注入效率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Light extraction artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating strong well emission with packaged light output\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: External efficiency also includes injection efficiency. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同；外部效率還包括載子注入效率。","observationEn":"Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency; External efficiency also includes injection efficiency.","failure":"若採用「量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating strong well emission with packaged light output\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「光取出」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「外部效率還包括載子注入效率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Light extraction, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"External efficiency also includes injection efficiency\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-18-k1","title":"光取出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Light extraction / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：外部效率還包括載子注入效率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: External efficiency also includes injection efficiency."},{"id":"a084-v8-18-k2","title":"光取出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Light extraction / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強」與「內部發光效率與外部取光效率不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating strong well emission with packaged light output\" is not equivalent to \"Internal efficiency differs from extraction efficiency\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「光取出」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Light extraction?","options":["量子井發光強就等同封裝出光強","看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因","外部效率還包括載子注入效率"],"optionsEn":["Equating strong well emission with packaged light output","Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone","External efficiency also includes injection efficiency"],"answer":2,"explanation":"外部效率還包括載子注入效率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"External efficiency also includes injection efficiency. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a084-stage04","order":4,"title":"效率下降 → 磊晶驗收","titleEn":"Efficiency droop to Epitaxy acceptance","description":"把「效率下降」「熱與色偏」「磊晶驗收」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Efficiency droop, Heat and color shift, Epitaxy acceptance.","steps":[{"id":"a084-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-18"],"title":"效率下降：建立模型","titleEn":"Efficiency droop: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism.","instruction":"對假設電流密度畫效率曲線並提出多種候選機制。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plot hypothetical efficiency versus current density with competing mechanisms. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制；自熱可與效率下降相互混淆。","observationEn":"One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism; Self-heating can confound efficiency droop.","failure":"若採用「看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「效率下降」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制。","checkEn":"Submit the Efficiency droop diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-19-k1","title":"效率下降／物理與模型","titleEn":"Efficiency droop / Physics and model","text":"機制：單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制。","textEn":"Mechanism: One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism."},{"id":"a084-v8-19-k2","title":"效率下降／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Efficiency droop / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「效率下降」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Efficiency droop, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制","看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因","把所有紅移都視為組成變化"],"optionsEn":["One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism","Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone","Attributing all redshift to composition changes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-19"],"title":"效率下降：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Efficiency droop: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「效率下降」成果，先指出錯誤主張「看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：自熱可與效率下降相互混淆。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Efficiency droop artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Self-heating can confound efficiency droop. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制；自熱可與效率下降相互混淆。","observationEn":"One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism; Self-heating can confound efficiency droop.","failure":"若採用「看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「效率下降」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「自熱可與效率下降相互混淆」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Efficiency droop, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Self-heating can confound efficiency droop\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-20-k1","title":"效率下降／物理與模型","titleEn":"Efficiency droop / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：自熱可與效率下降相互混淆。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Self-heating can confound efficiency droop."},{"id":"a084-v8-20-k2","title":"效率下降／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Efficiency droop / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因」與「單條 droop 曲線不足以唯一辨識機制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone\" is not equivalent to \"One droop curve cannot uniquely identify a mechanism\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「效率下降」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Efficiency droop?","options":["把所有紅移都視為組成變化","自熱可與效率下降相互混淆","看到效率下降就指定唯一復合原因"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all redshift to composition changes","Self-heating can confound efficiency droop","Assigning a unique recombination cause from droop alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"自熱可與效率下降相互混淆；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Self-heating can confound efficiency droop. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-20"],"title":"熱與色偏：建立模型","titleEn":"Heat and color shift: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra.","instruction":"比較短脈衝與連續驅動光譜，分離自熱與電流效應。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare pulsed/continuous spectra to separate heating and current effects. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜；脈衝占空比影響平均熱狀態。","observationEn":"Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra; Duty cycle affects average thermal state.","failure":"若採用「把所有紅移都視為組成變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all redshift to composition changes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱與色偏」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜。","checkEn":"Submit the Heat and color shift diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-21-k1","title":"熱與色偏／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heat and color shift / Physics and model","text":"機制：相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜。","textEn":"Mechanism: Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra."},{"id":"a084-v8-21-k2","title":"熱與色偏／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heat and color shift / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有紅移都視為組成變化」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing all redshift to composition changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱與色偏」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Heat and color shift, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把所有紅移都視為組成變化","單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性","相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all redshift to composition changes","Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak","Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra"],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-21"],"title":"熱與色偏：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Heat and color shift: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有紅移都視為組成變化」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing all redshift to composition changes.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱與色偏」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有紅移都視為組成變化」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：脈衝占空比影響平均熱狀態。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Heat and color shift artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing all redshift to composition changes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Duty cycle affects average thermal state. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜；脈衝占空比影響平均熱狀態。","observationEn":"Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra; Duty cycle affects average thermal state.","failure":"若採用「把所有紅移都視為組成變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all redshift to composition changes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱與色偏」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「脈衝占空比影響平均熱狀態」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Heat and color shift, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Duty cycle affects average thermal state\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-22-k1","title":"熱與色偏／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heat and color shift / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：脈衝占空比影響平均熱狀態。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Duty cycle affects average thermal state."},{"id":"a084-v8-22-k2","title":"熱與色偏／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heat and color shift / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有紅移都視為組成變化」與「相同電流在不同熱條件可有不同光譜」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing all redshift to composition changes\" is not equivalent to \"Equal current under different thermal conditions can shift spectra\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱與色偏」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Heat and color shift?","options":["脈衝占空比影響平均熱狀態","把所有紅移都視為組成變化","單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性"],"optionsEn":["Duty cycle affects average thermal state","Attributing all redshift to composition changes","Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak"],"answer":0,"explanation":"脈衝占空比影響平均熱狀態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Duty cycle affects average thermal state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-22"],"title":"磊晶驗收：建立模型","titleEn":"Epitaxy acceptance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence.","instruction":"結合 X 光、光致發光與電致發光，註明各法觀察深度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine X-ray, photoluminescence and electroluminescence with probe depth. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊；EL 和 PL 的激發空間不同。","observationEn":"Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence; EL and PL have different excitation profiles.","failure":"若採用「單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「磊晶驗收」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊。","checkEn":"Submit the Epitaxy acceptance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-23-k1","title":"磊晶驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Epitaxy acceptance / Physics and model","text":"機制：材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence."},{"id":"a084-v8-23-k2","title":"磊晶驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Epitaxy acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「磊晶驗收」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Epitaxy acceptance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["以注入電流直接等同光子流","材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊","單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性"],"optionsEn":["Equating injected current with photon flux","Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence","Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a084-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-led","v8-c-led-prize"],"prerequisiteIds":["a084-v8-23"],"title":"磊晶驗收：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Epitaxy acceptance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak.","instruction":"接續前一步「磊晶驗收」成果，先指出錯誤主張「單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：EL 和 PL 的激發空間不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Epitaxy acceptance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: EL and PL have different excitation profiles. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊；EL 和 PL 的激發空間不同。","observationEn":"Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence; EL and PL have different excitation profiles.","failure":"若採用「單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「磊晶驗收」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「EL 和 PL 的激發空間不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Epitaxy acceptance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"EL and PL have different excitation profiles\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a084-v8-24-k1","title":"磊晶驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Epitaxy acceptance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：EL 和 PL 的激發空間不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: EL and PL have different excitation profiles."},{"id":"a084-v8-24-k2","title":"磊晶驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Epitaxy acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性」與「材料發光與注入發光提供不同資訊」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak\" is not equivalent to \"Optical excitation and electrical injection provide different evidence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「磊晶驗收」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Epitaxy acceptance?","options":["單一 PL 峰就完整保證 LED 電性","以注入電流直接等同光子流","EL 和 PL 的激發空間不同"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing LED electrical behavior from one PL peak","Equating injected current with photon flux","EL and PL have different excitation profiles"],"answer":2,"explanation":"EL 和 PL 的激發空間不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"EL and PL have different excitation profiles. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"compound","subcategoryTitle":"化合物與新材料元件","subcategoryTitleEn":"Compound and emerging devices"},{"id":"a085","title":"砷化鎵射頻元件製作","titleEn":"Gallium-arsenide RF-device fabrication","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從HBT 與 pHEMT、閘長與寄生到技術選擇：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From HBT versus pHEMT and Gate length and parasitics to Technology selection: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["HBT 與 pHEMT","HBT 基極","隔離與漏電","線性與壓縮"],"labelsEn":["HBT versus pHEMT","HBT base","Isolation and leakage","Linearity and compression"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a085-stage01","order":1,"title":"HBT 與 pHEMT → 通道片電荷","titleEn":"HBT versus pHEMT to Channel sheet charge","description":"把「HBT 與 pHEMT」「異質磊晶」「通道片電荷」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for HBT versus pHEMT, Heteroepitaxy, Channel sheet charge.","steps":[{"id":"a085-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"HBT 與 pHEMT：建立模型","titleEn":"HBT versus pHEMT: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism.","instruction":"畫雙極載子注入與異質接面通道兩種截面。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw bipolar injection and heterojunction-channel sections. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制；HBT 與 HEMT 的輸入阻抗不同。","observationEn":"GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism; HBT and HEMT input impedances differ.","failure":"若採用「用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「HBT 與 pHEMT」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制。","checkEn":"Submit the HBT versus pHEMT diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-01-k1","title":"HBT 與 pHEMT／物理與模型","titleEn":"HBT versus pHEMT / Physics and model","text":"機制：同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制。","textEn":"Mechanism: GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism."},{"id":"a085-v8-01-k2","title":"HBT 與 pHEMT／驗證與限制","titleEn":"HBT versus pHEMT / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「HBT 與 pHEMT」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For HBT versus pHEMT, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制","用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極","只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格"],"optionsEn":["GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism","Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model","Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-01"],"title":"HBT 與 pHEMT：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"HBT versus pHEMT: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model.","instruction":"接續前一步「HBT 與 pHEMT」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：HBT 與 HEMT 的輸入阻抗不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding HBT versus pHEMT artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: HBT and HEMT input impedances differ. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制；HBT 與 HEMT 的輸入阻抗不同。","observationEn":"GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism; HBT and HEMT input impedances differ.","failure":"若採用「用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「HBT 與 pHEMT」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「HBT 與 HEMT 的輸入阻抗不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for HBT versus pHEMT, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"HBT and HEMT input impedances differ\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-02-k1","title":"HBT 與 pHEMT／物理與模型","titleEn":"HBT versus pHEMT / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：HBT 與 HEMT 的輸入阻抗不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: HBT and HEMT input impedances differ."},{"id":"a085-v8-02-k2","title":"HBT 與 pHEMT／驗證與限制","titleEn":"HBT versus pHEMT / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極」與「同為 GaAs RF 元件不代表相同控制機制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model\" is not equivalent to \"GaAs RF devices need not share a control mechanism\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「HBT 與 pHEMT」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of HBT versus pHEMT?","options":["只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格","HBT 與 HEMT 的輸入阻抗不同","用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極"],"optionsEn":["Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility","HBT and HEMT input impedances differ","Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model"],"answer":1,"explanation":"HBT 與 HEMT 的輸入阻抗不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"HBT and HEMT input impedances differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-02"],"title":"異質磊晶：建立模型","titleEn":"Heteroepitaxy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Heterostructures need band and lattice design together.","instruction":"畫晶格匹配與應變層，標出可能差排來源。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw matched/strained layers and possible dislocation origins. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格；假晶格匹配有臨界厚度限制。","observationEn":"Heterostructures need band and lattice design together; Pseudomorphic matching has thickness limits.","failure":"若採用「只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「異質磊晶」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格。","checkEn":"Submit the Heteroepitaxy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Heterostructures need band and lattice design together.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-03-k1","title":"異質磊晶／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heteroepitaxy / Physics and model","text":"機制：異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格。","textEn":"Mechanism: Heterostructures need band and lattice design together."},{"id":"a085-v8-03-k2","title":"異質磊晶／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heteroepitaxy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「異質磊晶」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Heteroepitaxy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格","把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3","異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格"],"optionsEn":["Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility","Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3","Heterostructures need band and lattice design together"],"answer":2,"explanation":"異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Heterostructures need band and lattice design together. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-03"],"title":"異質磊晶：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Heteroepitaxy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility.","instruction":"接續前一步「異質磊晶」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：假晶格匹配有臨界厚度限制。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Heteroepitaxy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pseudomorphic matching has thickness limits. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格；假晶格匹配有臨界厚度限制。","observationEn":"Heterostructures need band and lattice design together; Pseudomorphic matching has thickness limits.","failure":"若採用「只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「異質磊晶」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「假晶格匹配有臨界厚度限制」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Heteroepitaxy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pseudomorphic matching has thickness limits\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-04-k1","title":"異質磊晶／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heteroepitaxy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：假晶格匹配有臨界厚度限制。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pseudomorphic matching has thickness limits."},{"id":"a085-v8-04-k2","title":"異質磊晶／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heteroepitaxy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格」與「異質材料設計需兼顧能帶及晶格」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility\" is not equivalent to \"Heterostructures need band and lattice design together\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「異質磊晶」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Heteroepitaxy?","options":["假晶格匹配有臨界厚度限制","只選最高遷移率材料忽略晶格","把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3"],"optionsEn":["Pseudomorphic matching has thickness limits","Choosing mobility while ignoring lattice compatibility","Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"假晶格匹配有臨界厚度限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pseudomorphic matching has thickness limits. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-04"],"title":"通道片電荷：建立模型","titleEn":"Channel sheet charge: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「片密度與體密度單位不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Sheet and volume density have different units.","instruction":"分開片密度、遷移率與片電阻，做假設單位換算。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設單一載子通道的面密度 ns=10¹² cm⁻²、遷移率 μ=5,000 cm²/(V·s)，q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C。片電阻 Rs=1/(qnsμ)≈1,248.4 Ω/□。此式忽略平行通道及接觸電阻；不能直接當成整顆射頻元件導通電阻。","instructionEn":"Separate sheet density, mobility and resistance with unit checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a single-carrier channel with sheet density ns=10¹² cm⁻² and mobility μ=5,000 cm²/(V·s), using q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C. Sheet resistance Rs=1/(qnsμ)≈1,248.4 Ω/square. Parallel channels and contact resistance are excluded; this is not whole-device RF on-resistance.","observation":"片密度與體密度單位不同；Hall 量測也需要幾何校正。","observationEn":"Sheet and volume density have different units; Hall measurements need geometry corrections.","failure":"若採用「把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「通道片電荷」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：片密度與體密度單位不同。\n算例驗收：驗算約 1.25 kΩ/□，保留面密度單位，勿把 cm⁻² 當成 cm⁻³。","checkEn":"Submit the Channel sheet charge diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Sheet and volume density have different units.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify approximately 1.25 kΩ/square and keep sheet-density units distinct from volume density.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-05-k1","title":"通道片電荷／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel sheet charge / Physics and model","text":"機制：片密度與體密度單位不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Sheet and volume density have different units."},{"id":"a085-v8-05-k2","title":"通道片電荷／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel sheet charge / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3」。\n假設數值與推算：假設單一載子通道的面密度 ns=10¹² cm⁻²、遷移率 μ=5,000 cm²/(V·s)，q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C。片電阻 Rs=1/(qnsμ)≈1,248.4 Ω/□。此式忽略平行通道及接觸電阻；不能直接當成整顆射頻元件導通電阻。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a single-carrier channel with sheet density ns=10¹² cm⁻² and mobility μ=5,000 cm²/(V·s), using q=1.602×10⁻¹⁹ C. Sheet resistance Rs=1/(qnsμ)≈1,248.4 Ω/square. Parallel channels and contact resistance are excluded; this is not whole-device RF on-resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通道片電荷」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Channel sheet charge, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["基極越薄所有性能都單調改善","片密度與體密度單位不同","把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base","Sheet and volume density have different units","Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3"],"answer":1,"explanation":"片密度與體密度單位不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sheet and volume density have different units. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-05"],"title":"通道片電荷：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Channel sheet charge: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3.","instruction":"接續前一步「通道片電荷」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：Hall 量測也需要幾何校正。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Channel sheet charge artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Hall measurements need geometry corrections. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"片密度與體密度單位不同；Hall 量測也需要幾何校正。","observationEn":"Sheet and volume density have different units; Hall measurements need geometry corrections.","failure":"若採用「把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「通道片電荷」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「Hall 量測也需要幾何校正」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Channel sheet charge, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Hall measurements need geometry corrections\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-06-k1","title":"通道片電荷／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel sheet charge / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：Hall 量測也需要幾何校正。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Hall measurements need geometry corrections."},{"id":"a085-v8-06-k2","title":"通道片電荷／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel sheet charge / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3」與「片密度與體密度單位不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3\" is not equivalent to \"Sheet and volume density have different units\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「通道片電荷」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Channel sheet charge?","options":["把 cm^-2 直接當成 cm^-3","基極越薄所有性能都單調改善","Hall 量測也需要幾何校正"],"optionsEn":["Treating cm^-2 as cm^-3","Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base","Hall measurements need geometry corrections"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Hall 量測也需要幾何校正；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Hall measurements need geometry corrections. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a085-stage02","order":2,"title":"HBT 基極 → 接觸測試","titleEn":"HBT base to Contact testing","description":"把「HBT 基極」「閘長與寄生」「接觸測試」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for HBT base, Gate length and parasitics, Contact testing.","steps":[{"id":"a085-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-06"],"title":"HBT 基極：建立模型","titleEn":"HBT base: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking.","instruction":"畫射極、薄基極與集極，連結渡越時間和基極電阻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw emitter, thin base and collector and relate transit time/base resistance. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估；集極電容也限制高速性能。","observationEn":"A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking; Collector capacitance also limits speed.","failure":"若採用「基極越薄所有性能都單調改善」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「HBT 基極」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估。","checkEn":"Submit the HBT base diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-07-k1","title":"HBT 基極／物理與模型","titleEn":"HBT base / Physics and model","text":"機制：薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估。","textEn":"Mechanism: A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking."},{"id":"a085-v8-07-k2","title":"HBT 基極／驗證與限制","titleEn":"HBT base / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「基極越薄所有性能都單調改善」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「HBT 基極」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For HBT base, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估","基極越薄所有性能都單調改善","只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬"],"optionsEn":["A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking","Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base","Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length"],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-07"],"title":"HBT 基極：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"HBT base: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「基極越薄所有性能都單調改善」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base.","instruction":"接續前一步「HBT 基極」成果，先指出錯誤主張「基極越薄所有性能都單調改善」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：集極電容也限制高速性能。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding HBT base artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Collector capacitance also limits speed. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估；集極電容也限制高速性能。","observationEn":"A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking; Collector capacitance also limits speed.","failure":"若採用「基極越薄所有性能都單調改善」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「HBT 基極」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「集極電容也限制高速性能」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for HBT base, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Collector capacitance also limits speed\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-08-k1","title":"HBT 基極／物理與模型","titleEn":"HBT base / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：集極電容也限制高速性能。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Collector capacitance also limits speed."},{"id":"a085-v8-08-k2","title":"HBT 基極／驗證與限制","titleEn":"HBT base / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「基極越薄所有性能都單調改善」與「薄基極收益需連同電阻及耐壓評估」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base\" is not equivalent to \"A thin base must be assessed with resistance and blocking\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「HBT 基極」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of HBT base?","options":["只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬","集極電容也限制高速性能","基極越薄所有性能都單調改善"],"optionsEn":["Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length","Collector capacitance also limits speed","Assuming every metric improves with a thinner base"],"answer":1,"explanation":"集極電容也限制高速性能；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Collector capacitance also limits speed. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-08"],"title":"閘長與寄生：建立模型","titleEn":"Gate length and parasitics: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics.","instruction":"畫內在閘極及外接電阻電容，分開內外增益限制。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate intrinsic gate and extrinsic resistance/capacitance limits. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生；外在 gm 小於理想內在 gm。","observationEn":"Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics; Extrinsic transconductance differs from intrinsic values.","failure":"若採用「只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閘長與寄生」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生。","checkEn":"Submit the Gate length and parasitics diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-09-k1","title":"閘長與寄生／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate length and parasitics / Physics and model","text":"機制：短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生。","textEn":"Mechanism: Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics."},{"id":"a085-v8-09-k2","title":"閘長與寄生／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate length and parasitics / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘長與寄生」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Gate length and parasitics, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬","用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸","短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生"],"optionsEn":["Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length","Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result","Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics"],"answer":2,"explanation":"短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-09"],"title":"閘長與寄生：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Gate length and parasitics: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length.","instruction":"接續前一步「閘長與寄生」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：外在 gm 小於理想內在 gm。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Gate length and parasitics artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Extrinsic transconductance differs from intrinsic values. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生；外在 gm 小於理想內在 gm。","observationEn":"Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics; Extrinsic transconductance differs from intrinsic values.","failure":"若採用「只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閘長與寄生」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「外在 gm 小於理想內在 gm」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Gate length and parasitics, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Extrinsic transconductance differs from intrinsic values\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-10-k1","title":"閘長與寄生／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate length and parasitics / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：外在 gm 小於理想內在 gm。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Extrinsic transconductance differs from intrinsic values."},{"id":"a085-v8-10-k2","title":"閘長與寄生／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate length and parasitics / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬」與「短閘不自動消除封裝與接觸寄生」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length\" is not equivalent to \"Short gates do not eliminate package/contact parasitics\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閘長與寄生」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Gate length and parasitics?","options":["外在 gm 小於理想內在 gm","只用閘長倒數預測模組頻寬","用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸"],"optionsEn":["Extrinsic transconductance differs from intrinsic values","Predicting module bandwidth solely from inverse gate length","Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result"],"answer":0,"explanation":"外在 gm 小於理想內在 gm；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Extrinsic transconductance differs from intrinsic values. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-10"],"title":"接觸測試：建立模型","titleEn":"Contact testing: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「量測連接方式會影響所見電阻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Connection topology affects measured resistance.","instruction":"用假設 TLM 和 Kelvin 接點比較接觸與線路貢獻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare contact/line contributions with hypothetical TLM and Kelvin structures. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"量測連接方式會影響所見電阻；電流擁擠會影響接觸抽取。","observationEn":"Connection topology affects measured resistance; Current crowding affects contact extraction.","failure":"若採用「用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸測試」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：量測連接方式會影響所見電阻。","checkEn":"Submit the Contact testing diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Connection topology affects measured resistance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-11-k1","title":"接觸測試／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact testing / Physics and model","text":"機制：量測連接方式會影響所見電阻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Connection topology affects measured resistance."},{"id":"a085-v8-11-k2","title":"接觸測試／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact testing / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸測試」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Contact testing, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試","量測連接方式會影響所見電阻","用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸"],"optionsEn":["Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label","Connection topology affects measured resistance","Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result"],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測連接方式會影響所見電阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Connection topology affects measured resistance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-11"],"title":"接觸測試：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Contact testing: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸測試」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電流擁擠會影響接觸抽取。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Contact testing artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Current crowding affects contact extraction. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"量測連接方式會影響所見電阻；電流擁擠會影響接觸抽取。","observationEn":"Connection topology affects measured resistance; Current crowding affects contact extraction.","failure":"若採用「用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸測試」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電流擁擠會影響接觸抽取」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Contact testing, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Current crowding affects contact extraction\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-12-k1","title":"接觸測試／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact testing / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電流擁擠會影響接觸抽取。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Current crowding affects contact extraction."},{"id":"a085-v8-12-k2","title":"接觸測試／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact testing / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸」與「量測連接方式會影響所見電阻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result\" is not equivalent to \"Connection topology affects measured resistance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸測試」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Contact testing?","options":["用二線電阻代表去嵌入後接觸","只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試","電流擁擠會影響接觸抽取"],"optionsEn":["Calling two-wire resistance a de-embedded contact result","Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label","Current crowding affects contact extraction"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電流擁擠會影響接觸抽取；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Current crowding affects contact extraction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a085-stage03","order":3,"title":"隔離與漏電 → 去嵌入","titleEn":"Isolation and leakage to De-embedding","description":"把「隔離與漏電」「S 參數」「去嵌入」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Isolation and leakage, S-parameters, De-embedding.","steps":[{"id":"a085-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-12"],"title":"隔離與漏電：建立模型","titleEn":"Isolation and leakage: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage.","instruction":"畫元件間半絕緣基板及表面路徑，列出關斷量測。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw substrate/surface isolation paths and specify off-state tests. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電；隔離測試需涵蓋偏壓極性。","observationEn":"A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage; Isolation tests need bias-polarity coverage.","failure":"若採用「只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「隔離與漏電」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電。","checkEn":"Submit the Isolation and leakage diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-13-k1","title":"隔離與漏電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Isolation and leakage / Physics and model","text":"機制：半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電。","textEn":"Mechanism: A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage."},{"id":"a085-v8-13-k2","title":"隔離與漏電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Isolation and leakage / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隔離與漏電」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Isolation and leakage, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電","只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試","未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶"],"optionsEn":["A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage","Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label","Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data"],"answer":0,"explanation":"半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-13"],"title":"隔離與漏電：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Isolation and leakage: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label.","instruction":"接續前一步「隔離與漏電」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：隔離測試需涵蓋偏壓極性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Isolation and leakage artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Isolation tests need bias-polarity coverage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電；隔離測試需涵蓋偏壓極性。","observationEn":"A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage; Isolation tests need bias-polarity coverage.","failure":"若採用「只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「隔離與漏電」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「隔離測試需涵蓋偏壓極性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Isolation and leakage, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Isolation tests need bias-polarity coverage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-14-k1","title":"隔離與漏電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Isolation and leakage / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：隔離測試需涵蓋偏壓極性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Isolation tests need bias-polarity coverage."},{"id":"a085-v8-14-k2","title":"隔離與漏電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Isolation and leakage / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試」與「半絕緣基板不保證表面無漏電」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label\" is not equivalent to \"A semi-insulating substrate does not guarantee no surface leakage\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「隔離與漏電」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Isolation and leakage?","options":["未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶","隔離測試需涵蓋偏壓極性","只看基板名稱便取消隔離測試"],"optionsEn":["Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data","Isolation tests need bias-polarity coverage","Skipping isolation tests because of the substrate label"],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔離測試需涵蓋偏壓極性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Isolation tests need bias-polarity coverage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-14"],"title":"S 參數：建立模型","titleEn":"S-parameters: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance.","instruction":"標示兩埠參考面及校正件，區分晶片與探針線纜響應。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark two-port reference planes/calibration standards and separate fixture response. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗；校正後漂移仍可能產生誤差。","observationEn":"S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance; Drift after calibration still introduces error.","failure":"若採用「未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「S 參數」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗。","checkEn":"Submit the S-parameters diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-15-k1","title":"S 參數／物理與模型","titleEn":"S-parameters / Physics and model","text":"機制：S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗。","textEn":"Mechanism: S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance."},{"id":"a085-v8-15-k2","title":"S 參數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"S-parameters / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「S 參數」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For S-parameters, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶","任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生","S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗"],"optionsEn":["Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data","Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly","S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-15"],"title":"S 參數：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"S-parameters: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data.","instruction":"接續前一步「S 參數」成果，先指出錯誤主張「未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：校正後漂移仍可能產生誤差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding S-parameters artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Drift after calibration still introduces error. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗；校正後漂移仍可能產生誤差。","observationEn":"S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance; Drift after calibration still introduces error.","failure":"若採用「未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「S 參數」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「校正後漂移仍可能產生誤差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for S-parameters, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Drift after calibration still introduces error\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-16-k1","title":"S 參數／物理與模型","titleEn":"S-parameters / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：校正後漂移仍可能產生誤差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Drift after calibration still introduces error."},{"id":"a085-v8-16-k2","title":"S 參數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"S-parameters / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶」與「S 參數必須附頻率、偏壓和參考阻抗」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data\" is not equivalent to \"S-parameters require frequency, bias and reference impedance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「S 參數」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of S-parameters?","options":["校正後漂移仍可能產生誤差","未校正線纜便把總量測當裸晶","任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生"],"optionsEn":["Drift after calibration still introduces error","Treating uncalibrated cable response as bare-die data","Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly"],"answer":0,"explanation":"校正後漂移仍可能產生誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Drift after calibration still introduces error. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-16"],"title":"去嵌入：建立模型","titleEn":"De-embedding: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors.","instruction":"畫 open/short dummy 結構並列明它們移除的寄生。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw open/short dummies and list removed parasitics. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差；去嵌入後非物理解提示模型問題。","observationEn":"Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors; Nonphysical de-embedded results flag model issues.","failure":"若採用「任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「去嵌入」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差。","checkEn":"Submit the De-embedding diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-17-k1","title":"去嵌入／物理與模型","titleEn":"De-embedding / Physics and model","text":"機制：不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差。","textEn":"Mechanism: Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors."},{"id":"a085-v8-17-k2","title":"去嵌入／驗證與限制","titleEn":"De-embedding / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「去嵌入」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For De-embedding, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性","不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差","任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生"],"optionsEn":["Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain","Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors","Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-17"],"title":"去嵌入：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"De-embedding: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly.","instruction":"接續前一步「去嵌入」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：去嵌入後非物理解提示模型問題。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding De-embedding artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Nonphysical de-embedded results flag model issues. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差；去嵌入後非物理解提示模型問題。","observationEn":"Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors; Nonphysical de-embedded results flag model issues.","failure":"若採用「任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「去嵌入」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「去嵌入後非物理解提示模型問題」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for De-embedding, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Nonphysical de-embedded results flag model issues\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-18-k1","title":"去嵌入／物理與模型","titleEn":"De-embedding / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：去嵌入後非物理解提示模型問題。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Nonphysical de-embedded results flag model issues."},{"id":"a085-v8-18-k2","title":"去嵌入／驗證與限制","titleEn":"De-embedding / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生」與「不匹配的 dummy 可引入新誤差」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly\" is not equivalent to \"Mismatched dummy structures can introduce errors\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「去嵌入」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of De-embedding?","options":["任意空白焊墊都能精確去除全部寄生","高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性","去嵌入後非物理解提示模型問題"],"optionsEn":["Assuming any empty pad removes every parasitic exactly","Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain","Nonphysical de-embedded results flag model issues"],"answer":2,"explanation":"去嵌入後非物理解提示模型問題；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Nonphysical de-embedded results flag model issues. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a085-stage04","order":4,"title":"線性與壓縮 → 技術選擇","titleEn":"Linearity and compression to Technology selection","description":"把「線性與壓縮」「自熱」「技術選擇」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Linearity and compression, Self-heating, Technology selection.","steps":[{"id":"a085-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-18"],"title":"線性與壓縮：建立模型","titleEn":"Linearity and compression: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance.","instruction":"比較小訊號增益與輸出壓縮曲線，區分輸入功率範圍。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare small-signal gain and compression over input power. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能；PAE 還要計入輸入 RF 功率。","observationEn":"Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance; PAE includes input RF power.","failure":"若採用「高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「線性與壓縮」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能。","checkEn":"Submit the Linearity and compression diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-19-k1","title":"線性與壓縮／物理與模型","titleEn":"Linearity and compression / Physics and model","text":"機制：小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能。","textEn":"Mechanism: Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance."},{"id":"a085-v8-19-k2","title":"線性與壓縮／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Linearity and compression / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「線性與壓縮」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Linearity and compression, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能","高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性","全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率"],"optionsEn":["Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance","Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain","Attributing every pulse difference to mobility"],"answer":0,"explanation":"小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-19"],"title":"線性與壓縮：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Linearity and compression: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain.","instruction":"接續前一步「線性與壓縮」成果，先指出錯誤主張「高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：PAE 還要計入輸入 RF 功率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Linearity and compression artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: PAE includes input RF power. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能；PAE 還要計入輸入 RF 功率。","observationEn":"Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance; PAE includes input RF power.","failure":"若採用「高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「線性與壓縮」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「PAE 還要計入輸入 RF 功率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Linearity and compression, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"PAE includes input RF power\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-20-k1","title":"線性與壓縮／物理與模型","titleEn":"Linearity and compression / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：PAE 還要計入輸入 RF 功率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: PAE includes input RF power."},{"id":"a085-v8-20-k2","title":"線性與壓縮／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Linearity and compression / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性」與「小訊號指標不能完整預測大訊號性能」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain\" is not equivalent to \"Small-signal metrics do not fully predict large-signal performance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「線性與壓縮」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Linearity and compression?","options":["全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率","PAE 還要計入輸入 RF 功率","高小訊號增益就保證高功率線性"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every pulse difference to mobility","PAE includes input RF power","Inferring high-power linearity from high small-signal gain"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PAE 還要計入輸入 RF 功率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"PAE includes input RF power. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-20"],"title":"自熱：建立模型","titleEn":"Self-heating: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Thermal state affects RF bias and gain.","instruction":"比較相同峰值但不同脈寬的假設 I-V，檢查熱時間效應。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical I-V at equal peaks and different pulse widths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益；脈衝量測也需要偏壓穩定。","observationEn":"Thermal state affects RF bias and gain; Pulsed measurements require stable bias.","failure":"若採用「全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing every pulse difference to mobility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「自熱」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益。","checkEn":"Submit the Self-heating diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Thermal state affects RF bias and gain.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-21-k1","title":"自熱／物理與模型","titleEn":"Self-heating / Physics and model","text":"機制：RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益。","textEn":"Mechanism: Thermal state affects RF bias and gain."},{"id":"a085-v8-21-k2","title":"自熱／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Self-heating / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing every pulse difference to mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自熱」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Self-heating, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率","同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳","RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every pulse difference to mobility","Assuming one platform is best for every RF function","Thermal state affects RF bias and gain"],"answer":2,"explanation":"RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal state affects RF bias and gain. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-21"],"title":"自熱：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Self-heating: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing every pulse difference to mobility.","instruction":"接續前一步「自熱」成果，先指出錯誤主張「全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：脈衝量測也需要偏壓穩定。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Self-heating artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing every pulse difference to mobility\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pulsed measurements require stable bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益；脈衝量測也需要偏壓穩定。","observationEn":"Thermal state affects RF bias and gain; Pulsed measurements require stable bias.","failure":"若採用「全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing every pulse difference to mobility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「自熱」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「脈衝量測也需要偏壓穩定」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Self-heating, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pulsed measurements require stable bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-22-k1","title":"自熱／物理與模型","titleEn":"Self-heating / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：脈衝量測也需要偏壓穩定。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pulsed measurements require stable bias."},{"id":"a085-v8-22-k2","title":"自熱／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Self-heating / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率」與「RF 元件熱狀態會改變偏壓及增益」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing every pulse difference to mobility\" is not equivalent to \"Thermal state affects RF bias and gain\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「自熱」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Self-heating?","options":["脈衝量測也需要偏壓穩定","全部脈衝差異都歸為載子遷移率","同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳"],"optionsEn":["Pulsed measurements require stable bias","Attributing every pulse difference to mobility","Assuming one platform is best for every RF function"],"answer":0,"explanation":"脈衝量測也需要偏壓穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pulsed measurements require stable bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-22"],"title":"技術選擇：建立模型","titleEn":"Technology selection: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「最佳製程取決於系統角色」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: The preferred process depends on system role.","instruction":"對低雜訊接收與功率放大各建立 HBT/pHEMT 比較矩陣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare HBT/pHEMT for low-noise reception and power amplification. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"最佳製程取決於系統角色；匹配網路損耗會改變系統最佳選擇。","observationEn":"The preferred process depends on system role; Matching-network losses change system-level choices.","failure":"若採用「同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming one platform is best for every RF function\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「技術選擇」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：最佳製程取決於系統角色。","checkEn":"Submit the Technology selection diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: The preferred process depends on system role.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-23-k1","title":"技術選擇／物理與模型","titleEn":"Technology selection / Physics and model","text":"機制：最佳製程取決於系統角色。","textEn":"Mechanism: The preferred process depends on system role."},{"id":"a085-v8-23-k2","title":"技術選擇／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Technology selection / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming one platform is best for every RF function."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「技術選擇」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Technology selection, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極","最佳製程取決於系統角色","同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳"],"optionsEn":["Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model","The preferred process depends on system role","Assuming one platform is best for every RF function"],"answer":1,"explanation":"最佳製程取決於系統角色；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"The preferred process depends on system role. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a085-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gaas","v8-c-gaas-phemt","v8-c-gan-rf"],"prerequisiteIds":["a085-v8-23"],"title":"技術選擇：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Technology selection: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming one platform is best for every RF function.","instruction":"接續前一步「技術選擇」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：匹配網路損耗會改變系統最佳選擇。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Technology selection artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming one platform is best for every RF function\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Matching-network losses change system-level choices. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"最佳製程取決於系統角色；匹配網路損耗會改變系統最佳選擇。","observationEn":"The preferred process depends on system role; Matching-network losses change system-level choices.","failure":"若採用「同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming one platform is best for every RF function\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「技術選擇」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「匹配網路損耗會改變系統最佳選擇」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Technology selection, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Matching-network losses change system-level choices\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a085-v8-24-k1","title":"技術選擇／物理與模型","titleEn":"Technology selection / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：匹配網路損耗會改變系統最佳選擇。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Matching-network losses change system-level choices."},{"id":"a085-v8-24-k2","title":"技術選擇／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Technology selection / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳」與「最佳製程取決於系統角色」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming one platform is best for every RF function\" is not equivalent to \"The preferred process depends on system role\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「技術選擇」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Technology selection?","options":["同一材料平台在所有 RF 功能都最佳","用同一閘極模型描述 HBT 基極","匹配網路損耗會改變系統最佳選擇"],"optionsEn":["Assuming one platform is best for every RF function","Describing an HBT base with an unchanged gate model","Matching-network losses change system-level choices"],"answer":2,"explanation":"匹配網路損耗會改變系統最佳選擇；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Matching-network losses change system-level choices. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"compound","subcategoryTitle":"化合物與新材料元件","subcategoryTitleEn":"Compound and emerging devices"},{"id":"a086","title":"氧化鎵功率元件研究","titleEn":"Gallium-oxide power-device research","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical","v8-c-nict-place","v8-c-nict-coordinate","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從材料潛力與實現、橫向與垂直到研究成熟度：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Material potential versus realization and Lateral versus vertical to Research maturity: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["材料潛力與實現","摻雜與補償","閘極介電","異質散熱"],"labelsEn":["Material potential versus realization","Doping and compensation","Gate dielectric","Heterogeneous cooling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a086-stage01","order":1,"title":"材料潛力與實現 → 塊材與磊晶","titleEn":"Material potential versus realization to Bulk and epitaxy","description":"把「材料潛力與實現」「晶相與方向」「塊材與磊晶」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Material potential versus realization, Phase and orientation, Bulk and epitaxy.","steps":[{"id":"a086-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"材料潛力與實現：建立模型","titleEn":"Material potential versus realization: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「理想優值不等於實際元件效率」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency.","instruction":"將理想材料優值與實測元件指標分為兩張表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate ideal material figures of merit from measured device metrics. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"理想優值不等於實際元件效率；材料優值常假定理想漂移區。","observationEn":"An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency; Material figures often assume ideal drift regions.","failure":"若採用「把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「材料潛力與實現」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：理想優值不等於實際元件效率。","checkEn":"Submit the Material potential versus realization diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-01-k1","title":"材料潛力與實現／物理與模型","titleEn":"Material potential versus realization / Physics and model","text":"機制：理想優值不等於實際元件效率。","textEn":"Mechanism: An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency."},{"id":"a086-v8-01-k2","title":"材料潛力與實現／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Material potential versus realization / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料潛力與實現」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Material potential versus realization, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["理想優值不等於實際元件效率","把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名","以一個方向的數值代表所有方向"],"optionsEn":["An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency","Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone","Using one directional value for every orientation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"理想優值不等於實際元件效率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-01"],"title":"材料潛力與實現：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Material potential versus realization: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「材料潛力與實現」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：材料優值常假定理想漂移區。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Material potential versus realization artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Material figures often assume ideal drift regions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"理想優值不等於實際元件效率；材料優值常假定理想漂移區。","observationEn":"An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency; Material figures often assume ideal drift regions.","failure":"若採用「把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「材料潛力與實現」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「材料優值常假定理想漂移區」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Material potential versus realization, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Material figures often assume ideal drift regions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-02-k1","title":"材料潛力與實現／物理與模型","titleEn":"Material potential versus realization / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：材料優值常假定理想漂移區。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Material figures often assume ideal drift regions."},{"id":"a086-v8-02-k2","title":"材料潛力與實現／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Material potential versus realization / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名」與「理想優值不等於實際元件效率」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone\" is not equivalent to \"An ideal figure of merit is not actual efficiency\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「材料潛力與實現」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Material potential versus realization?","options":["以一個方向的數值代表所有方向","材料優值常假定理想漂移區","把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名"],"optionsEn":["Using one directional value for every orientation","Material figures often assume ideal drift regions","Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料優值常假定理想漂移區；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Material figures often assume ideal drift regions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-02"],"title":"晶相與方向：建立模型","titleEn":"Phase and orientation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同晶向的性質可能不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Properties can differ with crystallographic direction.","instruction":"畫 β-Ga2O3 晶向與測試方向，註明各向異性。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw beta-Ga2O3 orientation and measurement directions with anisotropy. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同晶向的性質可能不同；熱傳和電性可有不同各向異性。","observationEn":"Properties can differ with crystallographic direction; Thermal and electrical anisotropies can differ.","failure":"若採用「以一個方向的數值代表所有方向」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one directional value for every orientation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶相與方向」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同晶向的性質可能不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Phase and orientation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Properties can differ with crystallographic direction.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-03-k1","title":"晶相與方向／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and orientation / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同晶向的性質可能不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Properties can differ with crystallographic direction."},{"id":"a086-v8-03-k2","title":"晶相與方向／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and orientation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以一個方向的數值代表所有方向」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one directional value for every orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶相與方向」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Phase and orientation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["以一個方向的數值代表所有方向","大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成","不同晶向的性質可能不同"],"optionsEn":["Using one directional value for every orientation","Equating a large substrate with complete device integration","Properties can differ with crystallographic direction"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同晶向的性質可能不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Properties can differ with crystallographic direction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-03"],"title":"晶相與方向：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Phase and orientation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以一個方向的數值代表所有方向」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one directional value for every orientation.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶相與方向」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以一個方向的數值代表所有方向」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：熱傳和電性可有不同各向異性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Phase and orientation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one directional value for every orientation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thermal and electrical anisotropies can differ. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同晶向的性質可能不同；熱傳和電性可有不同各向異性。","observationEn":"Properties can differ with crystallographic direction; Thermal and electrical anisotropies can differ.","failure":"若採用「以一個方向的數值代表所有方向」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one directional value for every orientation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶相與方向」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「熱傳和電性可有不同各向異性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Phase and orientation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thermal and electrical anisotropies can differ\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-04-k1","title":"晶相與方向／物理與模型","titleEn":"Phase and orientation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：熱傳和電性可有不同各向異性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thermal and electrical anisotropies can differ."},{"id":"a086-v8-04-k2","title":"晶相與方向／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Phase and orientation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以一個方向的數值代表所有方向」與「不同晶向的性質可能不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one directional value for every orientation\" is not equivalent to \"Properties can differ with crystallographic direction\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶相與方向」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Phase and orientation?","options":["熱傳和電性可有不同各向異性","以一個方向的數值代表所有方向","大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成"],"optionsEn":["Thermal and electrical anisotropies can differ","Using one directional value for every orientation","Equating a large substrate with complete device integration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱傳和電性可有不同各向異性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal and electrical anisotropies can differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-04"],"title":"塊材與磊晶：建立模型","titleEn":"Bulk and epitaxy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality.","instruction":"區分熔融成長基板與後續主動磊晶層。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate melt-grown substrate from active epilayer. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求；基板雜質可影響磊晶及漏電。","observationEn":"Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality; Substrate impurities affect epitaxy and leakage.","failure":"若採用「大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating a large substrate with complete device integration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「塊材與磊晶」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求。","checkEn":"Submit the Bulk and epitaxy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-05-k1","title":"塊材與磊晶／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bulk and epitaxy / Physics and model","text":"機制：基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality."},{"id":"a086-v8-05-k2","title":"塊材與磊晶／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bulk and epitaxy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating a large substrate with complete device integration."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塊材與磊晶」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Bulk and epitaxy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞","基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求","大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成"],"optionsEn":["Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes","Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality","Equating a large substrate with complete device integration"],"answer":1,"explanation":"基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-05"],"title":"塊材與磊晶：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Bulk and epitaxy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating a large substrate with complete device integration.","instruction":"接續前一步「塊材與磊晶」成果，先指出錯誤主張「大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：基板雜質可影響磊晶及漏電。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Bulk and epitaxy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating a large substrate with complete device integration\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Substrate impurities affect epitaxy and leakage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求；基板雜質可影響磊晶及漏電。","observationEn":"Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality; Substrate impurities affect epitaxy and leakage.","failure":"若採用「大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating a large substrate with complete device integration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「塊材與磊晶」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「基板雜質可影響磊晶及漏電」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Bulk and epitaxy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Substrate impurities affect epitaxy and leakage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-06-k1","title":"塊材與磊晶／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bulk and epitaxy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：基板雜質可影響磊晶及漏電。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Substrate impurities affect epitaxy and leakage."},{"id":"a086-v8-06-k2","title":"塊材與磊晶／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bulk and epitaxy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成」與「基板可成長不代表元件層已達要求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating a large substrate with complete device integration\" is not equivalent to \"Growable substrates do not establish device-layer quality\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「塊材與磊晶」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Bulk and epitaxy?","options":["大基板存在就等於所有元件整合完成","植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞","基板雜質可影響磊晶及漏電"],"optionsEn":["Equating a large substrate with complete device integration","Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes","Substrate impurities affect epitaxy and leakage"],"answer":2,"explanation":"基板雜質可影響磊晶及漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Substrate impurities affect epitaxy and leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a086-stage02","order":2,"title":"摻雜與補償 → 接觸介面","titleEn":"Doping and compensation to Contact interface","description":"把「摻雜與補償」「橫向與垂直」「接觸介面」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Doping and compensation, Lateral versus vertical, Contact interface.","steps":[{"id":"a086-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-06"],"title":"摻雜與補償：建立模型","titleEn":"Doping and compensation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer.","instruction":"畫施體、深受體及自由載子，區分補償和電洞導電。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw donors, deep acceptors and carriers and distinguish compensation from hole conduction. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層；深受體可能只降低電子濃度。","observationEn":"A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer; Deep acceptors may only compensate electrons.","failure":"若採用「植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「摻雜與補償」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層。","checkEn":"Submit the Doping and compensation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-07-k1","title":"摻雜與補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Doping and compensation / Physics and model","text":"機制：補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層。","textEn":"Mechanism: A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer."},{"id":"a086-v8-07-k2","title":"摻雜與補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Doping and compensation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「摻雜與補償」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Doping and compensation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層","植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞","垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件"],"optionsEn":["A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer","Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes","Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-07"],"title":"摻雜與補償：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Doping and compensation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes.","instruction":"接續前一步「摻雜與補償」成果，先指出錯誤主張「植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：深受體可能只降低電子濃度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Doping and compensation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Deep acceptors may only compensate electrons. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層；深受體可能只降低電子濃度。","observationEn":"A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer; Deep acceptors may only compensate electrons.","failure":"若採用「植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「摻雜與補償」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「深受體可能只降低電子濃度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Doping and compensation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Deep acceptors may only compensate electrons\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-08-k1","title":"摻雜與補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Doping and compensation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：深受體可能只降低電子濃度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Deep acceptors may only compensate electrons."},{"id":"a086-v8-08-k2","title":"摻雜與補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Doping and compensation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞」與「補償區不自動等於成熟 p 型導電層」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes\" is not equivalent to \"A compensated region is not automatically a mature p-conducting layer\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「摻雜與補償」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Doping and compensation?","options":["垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件","深受體可能只降低電子濃度","植入受體就必然得到高遷移率電洞"],"optionsEn":["Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction","Deep acceptors may only compensate electrons","Assuming acceptor implantation guarantees mobile holes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"深受體可能只降低電子濃度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Deep acceptors may only compensate electrons. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-08"],"title":"橫向與垂直：建立模型","titleEn":"Lateral versus vertical: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Geometry changes both field and heat paths.","instruction":"畫兩種電流路徑和散熱出口，比較面積利用。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw current/heat paths for both geometries and compare area use. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑；垂直結構也需背面接觸。","observationEn":"Geometry changes both field and heat paths; Vertical structures need backside contacts.","failure":"若採用「垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「橫向與垂直」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑。","checkEn":"Submit the Lateral versus vertical diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Geometry changes both field and heat paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-09-k1","title":"橫向與垂直／物理與模型","titleEn":"Lateral versus vertical / Physics and model","text":"機制：幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑。","textEn":"Mechanism: Geometry changes both field and heat paths."},{"id":"a086-v8-09-k2","title":"橫向與垂直／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Lateral versus vertical / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橫向與垂直」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Lateral versus vertical, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件","所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體","幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑"],"optionsEn":["Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction","Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal","Geometry changes both field and heat paths"],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Geometry changes both field and heat paths. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-09"],"title":"橫向與垂直：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral versus vertical: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction.","instruction":"接續前一步「橫向與垂直」成果，先指出錯誤主張「垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：垂直結構也需背面接觸。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Lateral versus vertical artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Vertical structures need backside contacts. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑；垂直結構也需背面接觸。","observationEn":"Geometry changes both field and heat paths; Vertical structures need backside contacts.","failure":"若採用「垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「橫向與垂直」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「垂直結構也需背面接觸」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Lateral versus vertical, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Vertical structures need backside contacts\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-10-k1","title":"橫向與垂直／物理與模型","titleEn":"Lateral versus vertical / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：垂直結構也需背面接觸。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Vertical structures need backside contacts."},{"id":"a086-v8-10-k2","title":"橫向與垂直／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Lateral versus vertical / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件」與「幾何改變同時影響電場及熱路徑」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction\" is not equivalent to \"Geometry changes both field and heat paths\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「橫向與垂直」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Lateral versus vertical?","options":["垂直結構也需背面接觸","垂直結構只改電流方向不影響其他條件","所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體"],"optionsEn":["Vertical structures need backside contacts","Assuming vertical geometry changes only current direction","Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"垂直結構也需背面接觸；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Vertical structures need backside contacts. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-10"],"title":"接觸介面：建立模型","titleEn":"Contact interface: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Channel current can still be contact-limited.","instruction":"比較接觸限制和通道限制的假設 I-V 並設計 TLM 對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare contact/channel-limited I-V with a TLM control. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制；表面處理可能改變接觸障壁。","observationEn":"Channel current can still be contact-limited; Surface treatments change contact barriers.","failure":"若採用「所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸介面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制。","checkEn":"Submit the Contact interface diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Channel current can still be contact-limited.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-11-k1","title":"接觸介面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact interface / Physics and model","text":"機制：高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Channel current can still be contact-limited."},{"id":"a086-v8-11-k2","title":"接觸介面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact interface / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸介面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Contact interface, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣","高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制","所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體"],"optionsEn":["Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator","Channel current can still be contact-limited","Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Channel current can still be contact-limited. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-11"],"title":"接觸介面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Contact interface: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸介面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：表面處理可能改變接觸障壁。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Contact interface artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Surface treatments change contact barriers. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制；表面處理可能改變接觸障壁。","observationEn":"Channel current can still be contact-limited; Surface treatments change contact barriers.","failure":"若採用「所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸介面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「表面處理可能改變接觸障壁」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Contact interface, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Surface treatments change contact barriers\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-12-k1","title":"接觸介面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact interface / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：表面處理可能改變接觸障壁。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Surface treatments change contact barriers."},{"id":"a086-v8-12-k2","title":"接觸介面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact interface / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體」與「高通道電流可能仍受接觸限制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal\" is not equivalent to \"Channel current can still be contact-limited\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸介面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Contact interface?","options":["所有非線性都歸因於晶體本體","材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣","表面處理可能改變接觸障壁"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all nonlinearity to bulk crystal","Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator","Surface treatments change contact barriers"],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面處理可能改變接觸障壁；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface treatments change contact barriers. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a086-stage03","order":3,"title":"閘極介電 → 自熱侷限","titleEn":"Gate dielectric to Self-heating constraint","description":"把「閘極介電」「電場終端」「自熱侷限」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Gate dielectric, Field termination, Self-heating constraint.","steps":[{"id":"a086-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-12"],"title":"閘極介電：建立模型","titleEn":"Gate dielectric: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks.","instruction":"畫氧化物半導體與閘介電層的能帶邊界。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw band boundaries between semiconductor and gate dielectric. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電；陷阱可造成閾值遲滯。","observationEn":"Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks; Traps can cause threshold hysteresis.","failure":"若採用「材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閘極介電」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電。","checkEn":"Submit the Gate dielectric diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-13-k1","title":"閘極介電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate dielectric / Physics and model","text":"機制：寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電。","textEn":"Mechanism: Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks."},{"id":"a086-v8-13-k2","title":"閘極介電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate dielectric / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘極介電」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Gate dielectric, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電","材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣","直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓"],"optionsEn":["Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks","Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator","Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length"],"answer":0,"explanation":"寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-13"],"title":"閘極介電：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Gate dielectric: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator.","instruction":"接續前一步「閘極介電」成果，先指出錯誤主張「材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：陷阱可造成閾值遲滯。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Gate dielectric artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Traps can cause threshold hysteresis. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電；陷阱可造成閾值遲滯。","observationEn":"Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks; Traps can cause threshold hysteresis.","failure":"若採用「材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閘極介電」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「陷阱可造成閾值遲滯」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Gate dielectric, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Traps can cause threshold hysteresis\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-14-k1","title":"閘極介電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate dielectric / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：陷阱可造成閾值遲滯。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Traps can cause threshold hysteresis."},{"id":"a086-v8-14-k2","title":"閘極介電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate dielectric / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣」與「寬能隙半導體仍需驗證閘介面漏電」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator\" is not equivalent to \"Wide bandgap does not eliminate gate-interface leakage checks\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閘極介電」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Gate dielectric?","options":["直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓","陷阱可造成閾值遲滯","材料本身是氧化物便不需要閘絕緣"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length","Traps can cause threshold hysteresis","Assuming an oxide semiconductor needs no gate insulator"],"answer":1,"explanation":"陷阱可造成閾值遲滯；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Traps can cause threshold hysteresis. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-14"],"title":"電場終端：建立模型","titleEn":"Field termination: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first.","instruction":"比較裸邊緣和場形塑的等位線示意。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare equipotentials at bare and field-managed edges. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓；表面環境可改變邊緣漏電。","observationEn":"Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first; Surface environments change edge leakage.","failure":"若採用「直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電場終端」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓。","checkEn":"Submit the Field termination diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-15-k1","title":"電場終端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field termination / Physics and model","text":"機制：局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓。","textEn":"Mechanism: Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first."},{"id":"a086-v8-15-k2","title":"電場終端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field termination / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電場終端」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Field termination, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓","能隙大便代表熱導率一定高","局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length","Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity","Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first"],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-15"],"title":"電場終端：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Field termination: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length.","instruction":"接續前一步「電場終端」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：表面環境可改變邊緣漏電。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Field termination artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Surface environments change edge leakage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓；表面環境可改變邊緣漏電。","observationEn":"Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first; Surface environments change edge leakage.","failure":"若採用「直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電場終端」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「表面環境可改變邊緣漏電」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Field termination, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Surface environments change edge leakage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-16-k1","title":"電場終端／物理與模型","titleEn":"Field termination / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：表面環境可改變邊緣漏電。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Surface environments change edge leakage."},{"id":"a086-v8-16-k2","title":"電場終端／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Field termination / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓」與「局部場峰值可先限制實際耐壓」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length\" is not equivalent to \"Local field peaks can limit practical blocking first\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電場終端」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Field termination?","options":["表面環境可改變邊緣漏電","直接用材料臨界場乘全長保證耐壓","能隙大便代表熱導率一定高"],"optionsEn":["Surface environments change edge leakage","Guaranteeing blocking from critical field times total length","Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面環境可改變邊緣漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface environments change edge leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-16"],"title":"自熱侷限：建立模型","titleEn":"Self-heating constraint: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低電性損失不保證低接面溫度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature.","instruction":"建立假設熱阻網路並分開導通損耗和熱導能力。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設穩態集中熱模型中耗散 P=2 W、接面至環境熱阻 Rθ=20 K/W、環境 25°C，ΔT=PRθ=40 K，接面估計 65°C。若同一路徑熱阻 30 K/W，則為 85°C。這不是氧化鎵產品額定值；暫態熱容、非均勻熱點與溫度相依性未納入。","instructionEn":"Build a hypothetical thermal network separating electrical loss and conduction. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a steady lumped thermal model with P=2 W, junction-to-ambient Rθ=20 K/W and ambient 25°C. ΔT=PRθ=40 K gives 65°C junction temperature. At 30 K/W the estimate is 85°C. These are not gallium-oxide product ratings; thermal capacitance, nonuniform hotspots and temperature dependence are excluded.","observation":"低電性損失不保證低接面溫度；熱導率要連同晶向和溫度記錄。","observationEn":"Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature; Thermal conductivity needs orientation and temperature.","failure":"若採用「能隙大便代表熱導率一定高」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「自熱侷限」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低電性損失不保證低接面溫度。\n算例驗收：驗算 65°C 與 85°C，說明 K 的溫升可以加到 °C，但熱阻的路徑必須相同。","checkEn":"Submit the Self-heating constraint diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 65°C and 85°C; explain that a kelvin rise adds to Celsius temperature but the thermal-resistance path must match.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-17-k1","title":"自熱侷限／物理與模型","titleEn":"Self-heating constraint / Physics and model","text":"機制：低電性損失不保證低接面溫度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature."},{"id":"a086-v8-17-k2","title":"自熱侷限／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Self-heating constraint / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「能隙大便代表熱導率一定高」。\n假設數值與推算：假設穩態集中熱模型中耗散 P=2 W、接面至環境熱阻 Rθ=20 K/W、環境 25°C，ΔT=PRθ=40 K，接面估計 65°C。若同一路徑熱阻 30 K/W，則為 85°C。這不是氧化鎵產品額定值；暫態熱容、非均勻熱點與溫度相依性未納入。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a steady lumped thermal model with P=2 W, junction-to-ambient Rθ=20 K/W and ambient 25°C. ΔT=PRθ=40 K gives 65°C junction temperature. At 30 K/W the estimate is 85°C. These are not gallium-oxide product ratings; thermal capacitance, nonuniform hotspots and temperature dependence are excluded."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自熱侷限」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Self-heating constraint, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率","低電性損失不保證低接面溫度","能隙大便代表熱導率一定高"],"optionsEn":["Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond","Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature","Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"低電性損失不保證低接面溫度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-17"],"title":"自熱侷限：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Self-heating constraint: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「能隙大便代表熱導率一定高」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity.","instruction":"接續前一步「自熱侷限」成果，先指出錯誤主張「能隙大便代表熱導率一定高」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：熱導率要連同晶向和溫度記錄。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Self-heating constraint artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thermal conductivity needs orientation and temperature. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低電性損失不保證低接面溫度；熱導率要連同晶向和溫度記錄。","observationEn":"Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature; Thermal conductivity needs orientation and temperature.","failure":"若採用「能隙大便代表熱導率一定高」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「自熱侷限」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「熱導率要連同晶向和溫度記錄」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Self-heating constraint, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thermal conductivity needs orientation and temperature\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-18-k1","title":"自熱侷限／物理與模型","titleEn":"Self-heating constraint / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：熱導率要連同晶向和溫度記錄。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thermal conductivity needs orientation and temperature."},{"id":"a086-v8-18-k2","title":"自熱侷限／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Self-heating constraint / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「能隙大便代表熱導率一定高」與「低電性損失不保證低接面溫度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity\" is not equivalent to \"Low electrical loss does not guarantee low junction temperature\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「自熱侷限」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Self-heating constraint?","options":["能隙大便代表熱導率一定高","忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率","熱導率要連同晶向和溫度記錄"],"optionsEn":["Assuming wide bandgap implies high thermal conductivity","Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond","Thermal conductivity needs orientation and temperature"],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱導率要連同晶向和溫度記錄；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal conductivity needs orientation and temperature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a086-stage04","order":4,"title":"異質散熱 → 研究成熟度","titleEn":"Heterogeneous cooling to Research maturity","description":"把「異質散熱」「陷阱暫態」「研究成熟度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Heterogeneous cooling, Trap transients, Research maturity.","steps":[{"id":"a086-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-18"],"title":"異質散熱：建立模型","titleEn":"Heterogeneous cooling: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Carrier benefits may be interface-limited.","instruction":"畫與高熱導載板接合後的界面熱阻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw bonding to a thermally conductive carrier with interfacial resistance. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制；接合空洞會形成局部熱點。","observationEn":"Carrier benefits may be interface-limited; Bond voids create local hotspots.","failure":"若採用「忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「異質散熱」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制。","checkEn":"Submit the Heterogeneous cooling diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Carrier benefits may be interface-limited.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-19-k1","title":"異質散熱／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heterogeneous cooling / Physics and model","text":"機制：新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Carrier benefits may be interface-limited."},{"id":"a086-v8-19-k2","title":"異質散熱／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heterogeneous cooling / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「異質散熱」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Heterogeneous cooling, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制","忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率","一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Carrier benefits may be interface-limited","Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond","Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve"],"answer":0,"explanation":"新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Carrier benefits may be interface-limited. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-19"],"title":"異質散熱：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Heterogeneous cooling: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond.","instruction":"接續前一步「異質散熱」成果，先指出錯誤主張「忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接合空洞會形成局部熱點。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Heterogeneous cooling artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Bond voids create local hotspots. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制；接合空洞會形成局部熱點。","observationEn":"Carrier benefits may be interface-limited; Bond voids create local hotspots.","failure":"若採用「忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「異質散熱」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接合空洞會形成局部熱點」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Heterogeneous cooling, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Bond voids create local hotspots\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-20-k1","title":"異質散熱／物理與模型","titleEn":"Heterogeneous cooling / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接合空洞會形成局部熱點。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Bond voids create local hotspots."},{"id":"a086-v8-20-k2","title":"異質散熱／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Heterogeneous cooling / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率」與「新載板的收益可能受介面熱阻限制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond\" is not equivalent to \"Carrier benefits may be interface-limited\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「異質散熱」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Heterogeneous cooling?","options":["一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷","接合空洞會形成局部熱點","忽略接合界面就使用載板本體熱導率"],"optionsEn":["Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve","Bond voids create local hotspots","Using bulk carrier conductivity while ignoring the bond"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接合空洞會形成局部熱點；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bond voids create local hotspots. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-20"],"title":"陷阱暫態：建立模型","titleEn":"Trap transients: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls.","instruction":"比較應力後不同延遲的電流恢復，和純熱恢復作對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare delay-dependent current recovery against thermal recovery. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照；多個陷阱時間常數可重疊。","observationEn":"Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls; Several trap time constants can overlap.","failure":"若採用「一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「陷阱暫態」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照。","checkEn":"Submit the Trap transients diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-21-k1","title":"陷阱暫態／物理與模型","titleEn":"Trap transients / Physics and model","text":"機制：捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照。","textEn":"Mechanism: Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls."},{"id":"a086-v8-21-k2","title":"陷阱暫態／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Trap transients / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「陷阱暫態」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Trap transients, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷","宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠","捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照"],"optionsEn":["Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve","Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products","Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls"],"answer":2,"explanation":"捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-21"],"title":"陷阱暫態：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Trap transients: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve.","instruction":"接續前一步「陷阱暫態」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：多個陷阱時間常數可重疊。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Trap transients artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Several trap time constants can overlap. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照；多個陷阱時間常數可重疊。","observationEn":"Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls; Several trap time constants can overlap.","failure":"若採用「一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「陷阱暫態」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「多個陷阱時間常數可重疊」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Trap transients, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Several trap time constants can overlap\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-22-k1","title":"陷阱暫態／物理與模型","titleEn":"Trap transients / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：多個陷阱時間常數可重疊。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Several trap time constants can overlap."},{"id":"a086-v8-22-k2","title":"陷阱暫態／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Trap transients / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷」與「捕捉與熱效應需不同時間與溫度對照」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve\" is not equivalent to \"Trapping and heating require timing/temperature controls\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「陷阱暫態」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Trap transients?","options":["多個陷阱時間常數可重疊","一條恢復曲線足以唯一判斷缺陷","宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠"],"optionsEn":["Several trap time constants can overlap","Identifying a unique defect from one recovery curve","Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多個陷阱時間常數可重疊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Several trap time constants can overlap. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-22"],"title":"研究成熟度：建立模型","titleEn":"Research maturity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity.","instruction":"將展示、重複樣本、晶圓分布和產品認證分級。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate demonstrations, replicates, wafer distributions and qualification. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟；長期可靠度需加速模型和統計。","observationEn":"One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity; Long-term reliability requires models and statistics.","failure":"若採用「宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「研究成熟度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟。","checkEn":"Submit the Research maturity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-23-k1","title":"研究成熟度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Research maturity / Physics and model","text":"機制：單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟。","textEn":"Mechanism: One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity."},{"id":"a086-v8-23-k2","title":"研究成熟度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Research maturity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「研究成熟度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Research maturity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名","單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟","宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠"],"optionsEn":["Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone","One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity","Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products"],"answer":1,"explanation":"單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a086-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-ga2o3","v8-c-ga2o3-vertical"],"prerequisiteIds":["a086-v8-23"],"title":"研究成熟度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Research maturity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products.","instruction":"接續前一步「研究成熟度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：長期可靠度需加速模型和統計。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Research maturity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Long-term reliability requires models and statistics. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟；長期可靠度需加速模型和統計。","observationEn":"One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity; Long-term reliability requires models and statistics.","failure":"若採用「宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「研究成熟度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「長期可靠度需加速模型和統計」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Research maturity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Long-term reliability requires models and statistics\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a086-v8-24-k1","title":"研究成熟度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Research maturity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：長期可靠度需加速模型和統計。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Long-term reliability requires models and statistics."},{"id":"a086-v8-24-k2","title":"研究成熟度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Research maturity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠」與「單顆研究元件不足以證明量產成熟」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products\" is not equivalent to \"One research device does not establish manufacturing maturity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「研究成熟度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Research maturity?","options":["宣布新結構就等於市場產品已可靠","把理論材料排名當成產品能效排名","長期可靠度需加速模型和統計"],"optionsEn":["Equating a new structure announcement with reliable products","Ranking product efficiency by ideal materials alone","Long-term reliability requires models and statistics"],"answer":2,"explanation":"長期可靠度需加速模型和統計；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Long-term reliability requires models and statistics. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"compound","subcategoryTitle":"化合物與新材料元件","subcategoryTitleEn":"Compound and emerging devices"},{"id":"a087","title":"二維半導體轉移與接觸","titleEn":"Two-dimensional semiconductor transfer and contacts","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從單層與晶粒、轉移殘留到晶圓可製造性：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Monolayer and grains and Transfer residue to Wafer manufacturability: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["單層與晶粒","皺褶與裂縫","接觸抽取","n/p 配對"],"labelsEn":["Monolayer and grains","Wrinkles and cracks","Contact extraction","n/p pairing"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a087-stage01","order":1,"title":"單層與晶粒 → 暫時載板","titleEn":"Monolayer and grains to Temporary carrier","description":"把「單層與晶粒」「成長與轉移」「暫時載板」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Monolayer and grains, Growth and transfer, Temporary carrier.","steps":[{"id":"a087-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"單層與晶粒：建立模型","titleEn":"Monolayer and grains: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects.","instruction":"畫單層厚度、晶粒邊界與覆蓋率，分開三種品質指標。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate monolayer thickness, grain boundaries and coverage in a sketch. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷；晶粒取向也會改變接合邊界。","observationEn":"Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects; Grain orientation changes boundary character.","failure":"若採用「全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「單層與晶粒」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷。","checkEn":"Submit the Monolayer and grains diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-01-k1","title":"單層與晶粒／物理與模型","titleEn":"Monolayer and grains / Physics and model","text":"機制：連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects."},{"id":"a087-v8-01-k2","title":"單層與晶粒／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Monolayer and grains / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單層與晶粒」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Monolayer and grains, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷","全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同","可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片"],"optionsEn":["Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects","Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere","Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips"],"answer":0,"explanation":"連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-01"],"title":"單層與晶粒：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Monolayer and grains: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere.","instruction":"接續前一步「單層與晶粒」成果，先指出錯誤主張「全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：晶粒取向也會改變接合邊界。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Monolayer and grains artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Grain orientation changes boundary character. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷；晶粒取向也會改變接合邊界。","observationEn":"Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects; Grain orientation changes boundary character.","failure":"若採用「全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「單層與晶粒」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「晶粒取向也會改變接合邊界」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Monolayer and grains, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Grain orientation changes boundary character\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-02-k1","title":"單層與晶粒／物理與模型","titleEn":"Monolayer and grains / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：晶粒取向也會改變接合邊界。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Grain orientation changes boundary character."},{"id":"a087-v8-02-k2","title":"單層與晶粒／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Monolayer and grains / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同」與「連續覆蓋不保證單晶或無缺陷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere\" is not equivalent to \"Continuous coverage does not imply single crystal or no defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「單層與晶粒」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Monolayer and grains?","options":["可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片","晶粒取向也會改變接合邊界","全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同"],"optionsEn":["Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips","Grain orientation changes boundary character","Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶粒取向也會改變接合邊界；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Grain orientation changes boundary character. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-02"],"title":"成長與轉移：建立模型","titleEn":"Growth and transfer: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets.","instruction":"比較直接成長及外基板成長後轉移的熱流程。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare thermal flows for direct growth and growth followed by transfer. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算；轉移增加界面與對準需求。","observationEn":"Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets; Transfer adds interfaces and alignment needs.","failure":"若採用「可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「成長與轉移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算。","checkEn":"Submit the Growth and transfer diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-03-k1","title":"成長與轉移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Growth and transfer / Physics and model","text":"機制：生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算。","textEn":"Mechanism: Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets."},{"id":"a087-v8-03-k2","title":"成長與轉移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Growth and transfer / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「成長與轉移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Growth and transfer, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片","原子薄就必然沒有機械破損","生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算"],"optionsEn":["Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips","Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage","Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets"],"answer":2,"explanation":"生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-03"],"title":"成長與轉移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Growth and transfer: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips.","instruction":"接續前一步「成長與轉移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：轉移增加界面與對準需求。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Growth and transfer artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Transfer adds interfaces and alignment needs. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算；轉移增加界面與對準需求。","observationEn":"Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets; Transfer adds interfaces and alignment needs.","failure":"若採用「可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「成長與轉移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「轉移增加界面與對準需求」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Growth and transfer, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Transfer adds interfaces and alignment needs\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-04-k1","title":"成長與轉移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Growth and transfer / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：轉移增加界面與對準需求。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Transfer adds interfaces and alignment needs."},{"id":"a087-v8-04-k2","title":"成長與轉移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Growth and transfer / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片」與「生長最佳條件未必符合目標晶片熱預算」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips\" is not equivalent to \"Best growth conditions may violate target-chip thermal budgets\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「成長與轉移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Growth and transfer?","options":["轉移增加界面與對準需求","可在基板成長就能原樣搬到完成晶片","原子薄就必然沒有機械破損"],"optionsEn":["Transfer adds interfaces and alignment needs","Moving a growth process unchanged to completed chips","Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"轉移增加界面與對準需求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Transfer adds interfaces and alignment needs. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-04"],"title":"暫時載板：建立模型","titleEn":"Temporary carrier: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering.","instruction":"畫支撐、接合及釋離界面，追蹤單層受力。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw support, bonding and release interfaces and trace monolayer loading. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程；剝離前緣控制影響裂紋生成。","observationEn":"Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering; Release-front control affects cracking.","failure":"若採用「原子薄就必然沒有機械破損」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「暫時載板」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程。","checkEn":"Submit the Temporary carrier diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-05-k1","title":"暫時載板／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporary carrier / Physics and model","text":"機制：轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程。","textEn":"Mechanism: Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering."},{"id":"a087-v8-05-k2","title":"暫時載板／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporary carrier / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「原子薄就必然沒有機械破損」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「暫時載板」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Temporary carrier, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述","轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程","原子薄就必然沒有機械破損"],"optionsEn":["Using one resistance correction for every dark line","Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering","Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-05"],"title":"暫時載板：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Temporary carrier: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「原子薄就必然沒有機械破損」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage.","instruction":"接續前一步「暫時載板」成果，先指出錯誤主張「原子薄就必然沒有機械破損」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：剝離前緣控制影響裂紋生成。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Temporary carrier artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Release-front control affects cracking. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程；剝離前緣控制影響裂紋生成。","observationEn":"Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering; Release-front control affects cracking.","failure":"若採用「原子薄就必然沒有機械破損」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「暫時載板」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「剝離前緣控制影響裂紋生成」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Temporary carrier, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Release-front control affects cracking\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-06-k1","title":"暫時載板／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporary carrier / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：剝離前緣控制影響裂紋生成。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Release-front control affects cracking."},{"id":"a087-v8-06-k2","title":"暫時載板／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporary carrier / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「原子薄就必然沒有機械破損」與「轉移是界面與機械邊界的工程」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage\" is not equivalent to \"Transfer is interface and mechanical-boundary engineering\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「暫時載板」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Temporary carrier?","options":["原子薄就必然沒有機械破損","所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述","剝離前緣控制影響裂紋生成"],"optionsEn":["Assuming atomic thinness prevents mechanical damage","Using one resistance correction for every dark line","Release-front control affects cracking"],"answer":2,"explanation":"剝離前緣控制影響裂紋生成；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Release-front control affects cracking. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a087-stage02","order":2,"title":"皺褶與裂縫 → 接觸障壁","titleEn":"Wrinkles and cracks to Contact barrier","description":"把「皺褶與裂縫」「轉移殘留」「接觸障壁」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Wrinkles and cracks, Transfer residue, Contact barrier.","steps":[{"id":"a087-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-06"],"title":"皺褶與裂縫：建立模型","titleEn":"Wrinkles and cracks: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Different morphology defects have different electrical effects.","instruction":"將兩種缺陷覆到假設通道圖，分別預測應變及斷路。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Overlay wrinkles/cracks on channels and distinguish strain from breaks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果；皺褶可改變局部能帶與接觸。","observationEn":"Different morphology defects have different electrical effects; Wrinkles alter local bands and contacts.","failure":"若採用「所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one resistance correction for every dark line\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「皺褶與裂縫」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果。","checkEn":"Submit the Wrinkles and cracks diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Different morphology defects have different electrical effects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-07-k1","title":"皺褶與裂縫／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wrinkles and cracks / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果。","textEn":"Mechanism: Different morphology defects have different electrical effects."},{"id":"a087-v8-07-k2","title":"皺褶與裂縫／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wrinkles and cracks / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one resistance correction for every dark line."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「皺褶與裂縫」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Wrinkles and cracks, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果","所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述","只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面"],"optionsEn":["Different morphology defects have different electrical effects","Using one resistance correction for every dark line","Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Different morphology defects have different electrical effects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-07"],"title":"皺褶與裂縫：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Wrinkles and cracks: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one resistance correction for every dark line.","instruction":"接續前一步「皺褶與裂縫」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：皺褶可改變局部能帶與接觸。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Wrinkles and cracks artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one resistance correction for every dark line\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Wrinkles alter local bands and contacts. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果；皺褶可改變局部能帶與接觸。","observationEn":"Different morphology defects have different electrical effects; Wrinkles alter local bands and contacts.","failure":"若採用「所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one resistance correction for every dark line\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「皺褶與裂縫」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「皺褶可改變局部能帶與接觸」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Wrinkles and cracks, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Wrinkles alter local bands and contacts\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-08-k1","title":"皺褶與裂縫／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wrinkles and cracks / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：皺褶可改變局部能帶與接觸。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Wrinkles alter local bands and contacts."},{"id":"a087-v8-08-k2","title":"皺褶與裂縫／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wrinkles and cracks / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述」與「不同形貌缺陷產生不同電性後果」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one resistance correction for every dark line\" is not equivalent to \"Different morphology defects have different electrical effects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「皺褶與裂縫」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Wrinkles and cracks?","options":["只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面","皺褶可改變局部能帶與接觸","所有暗線都用同一電阻修正描述"],"optionsEn":["Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone","Wrinkles alter local bands and contacts","Using one resistance correction for every dark line"],"answer":1,"explanation":"皺褶可改變局部能帶與接觸；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Wrinkles alter local bands and contacts. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-08"],"title":"轉移殘留：建立模型","titleEn":"Transfer residue: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue.","instruction":"比較表面形貌、化學訊號及電性漂移，設置空白載板。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare morphology, chemistry and electrical drift with carrier blanks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留；殘留也可能產生表面摻雜。","observationEn":"Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue; Residue can create surface doping.","failure":"若採用「只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「轉移殘留」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留。","checkEn":"Submit the Transfer residue diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-09-k1","title":"轉移殘留／物理與模型","titleEn":"Transfer residue / Physics and model","text":"機制：光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue."},{"id":"a087-v8-09-k2","title":"轉移殘留／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Transfer residue / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「轉移殘留」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Transfer residue, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面","只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻","光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留"],"optionsEn":["Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone","Predicting all contact resistance from work function","Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue"],"answer":2,"explanation":"光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-09"],"title":"轉移殘留：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Transfer residue: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「轉移殘留」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：殘留也可能產生表面摻雜。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Transfer residue artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Residue can create surface doping. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留；殘留也可能產生表面摻雜。","observationEn":"Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue; Residue can create surface doping.","failure":"若採用「只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「轉移殘留」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「殘留也可能產生表面摻雜」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Transfer residue, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Residue can create surface doping\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-10-k1","title":"轉移殘留／物理與模型","titleEn":"Transfer residue / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：殘留也可能產生表面摻雜。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Residue can create surface doping."},{"id":"a087-v8-10-k2","title":"轉移殘留／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Transfer residue / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面」與「光學看似潔淨不保證無有機殘留」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone\" is not equivalent to \"Optical cleanliness does not prove absence of organic residue\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「轉移殘留」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Transfer residue?","options":["殘留也可能產生表面摻雜","只看顯微照片就核准原子級界面","只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻"],"optionsEn":["Residue can create surface doping","Accepting atomic interfaces from optical images alone","Predicting all contact resistance from work function"],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘留也可能產生表面摻雜；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Residue can create surface doping. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-10"],"title":"接觸障壁：建立模型","titleEn":"Contact barrier: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together.","instruction":"畫金屬與 2D 材料能帶，區分障壁高度及有效注入長度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw metal/2D bands and distinguish barrier height from injection length. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定；費米能階釘扎限制功函數選擇效果。","observationEn":"Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together; Fermi-level pinning limits work-function tuning.","failure":"若採用「只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting all contact resistance from work function\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸障壁」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定。","checkEn":"Submit the Contact barrier diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-11-k1","title":"接觸障壁／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact barrier / Physics and model","text":"機制：接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together."},{"id":"a087-v8-11-k2","title":"接觸障壁／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact barrier / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Predicting all contact resistance from work function."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸障壁」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Contact barrier, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸","接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定","只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻"],"optionsEn":["Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities","Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together","Predicting all contact resistance from work function"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-11"],"title":"接觸障壁：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Contact barrier: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Predicting all contact resistance from work function.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸障壁」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：費米能階釘扎限制功函數選擇效果。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Contact barrier artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Predicting all contact resistance from work function\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Fermi-level pinning limits work-function tuning. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定；費米能階釘扎限制功函數選擇效果。","observationEn":"Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together; Fermi-level pinning limits work-function tuning.","failure":"若採用「只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting all contact resistance from work function\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸障壁」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「費米能階釘扎限制功函數選擇效果」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Contact barrier, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Fermi-level pinning limits work-function tuning\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-12-k1","title":"接觸障壁／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact barrier / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：費米能階釘扎限制功函數選擇效果。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Fermi-level pinning limits work-function tuning."},{"id":"a087-v8-12-k2","title":"接觸障壁／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact barrier / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻」與「接觸性能由界面與幾何共同決定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Predicting all contact resistance from work function\" is not equivalent to \"Contacts depend on interfaces and geometry together\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸障壁」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Contact barrier?","options":["只以金屬功函數預測全部接觸電阻","混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸","費米能階釘扎限制功函數選擇效果"],"optionsEn":["Predicting all contact resistance from work function","Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities","Fermi-level pinning limits work-function tuning"],"answer":2,"explanation":"費米能階釘扎限制功函數選擇效果；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Fermi-level pinning limits work-function tuning. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a087-stage03","order":3,"title":"接觸抽取 → 摻雜方法","titleEn":"Contact extraction to Doping methods","description":"把「接觸抽取」「介電成核」「摻雜方法」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Contact extraction, Dielectric nucleation, Doping methods.","steps":[{"id":"a087-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-12"],"title":"接觸抽取：建立模型","titleEn":"Contact extraction: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias.","instruction":"用假設不同通道長度 TLM 比較接觸截距與片電阻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設二維材料元件的 TLM 資料符合線性 Rtotal(L)，截距 2 kΩ，且兩接觸相同，則每個接觸為 1 kΩ。若某長度的量測總阻為 5 kΩ，模型歸於通道的部分為 3 kΩ。此分解依賴接觸與通道一致性，不適用於任意非線性注入曲線。","instructionEn":"Use hypothetical channel-length TLM to separate intercept and sheet resistance. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a 2D-device TLM dataset follows linear Rtotal(L) with intercept 2 kΩ and identical contacts: each contact is 1 kΩ. If total resistance at one spacing is 5 kΩ, the model assigns 3 kΩ to the channel. This decomposition assumes contact/channel consistency and does not apply to arbitrary nonlinear injection curves.","observation":"長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓；尺寸縮放使接觸占比上升。","observationEn":"Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias; Scaling increases the contact contribution.","failure":"若採用「混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸抽取」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓。\n算例驗收：驗算每接觸 1 kΩ 與通道 3 kΩ；若負截距出現，先檢查模型而非宣稱負接觸電阻。","checkEn":"Submit the Contact extraction diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 1 kΩ per contact and 3 kΩ channel resistance; investigate a negative intercept instead of claiming negative contact resistance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-13-k1","title":"接觸抽取／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact extraction / Physics and model","text":"機制：長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓。","textEn":"Mechanism: Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias."},{"id":"a087-v8-13-k2","title":"接觸抽取／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact extraction / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸」。\n假設數值與推算：假設二維材料元件的 TLM 資料符合線性 Rtotal(L)，截距 2 kΩ，且兩接觸相同，則每個接觸為 1 kΩ。若某長度的量測總阻為 5 kΩ，模型歸於通道的部分為 3 kΩ。此分解依賴接觸與通道一致性，不適用於任意非線性注入曲線。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a 2D-device TLM dataset follows linear Rtotal(L) with intercept 2 kΩ and identical contacts: each contact is 1 kΩ. If total resistance at one spacing is 5 kΩ, the model assigns 3 kΩ to the channel. This decomposition assumes contact/channel consistency and does not apply to arbitrary nonlinear injection curves."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸抽取」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Contact extraction, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓","混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸","ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核"],"optionsEn":["Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias","Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities","Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-13"],"title":"接觸抽取：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Contact extraction: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸抽取」成果，先指出錯誤主張「混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：尺寸縮放使接觸占比上升。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Contact extraction artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Scaling increases the contact contribution. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓；尺寸縮放使接觸占比上升。","observationEn":"Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias; Scaling increases the contact contribution.","failure":"若採用「混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸抽取」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「尺寸縮放使接觸占比上升」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Contact extraction, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Scaling increases the contact contribution\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-14-k1","title":"接觸抽取／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contact extraction / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：尺寸縮放使接觸占比上升。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Scaling increases the contact contribution."},{"id":"a087-v8-14-k2","title":"接觸抽取／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contact extraction / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸」與「長度系列需要可比通道與閘偏壓」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities\" is not equivalent to \"Length-series extraction needs comparable channels and gate bias\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸抽取」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Contact extraction?","options":["ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核","尺寸縮放使接觸占比上升","混合不同載子密度樣本直接回歸"],"optionsEn":["Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface","Scaling increases the contact contribution","Regressing samples with mixed carrier densities"],"answer":1,"explanation":"尺寸縮放使接觸占比上升；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Scaling increases the contact contribution. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-14"],"title":"介電成核：建立模型","titleEn":"Dielectric nucleation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects.","instruction":"畫惰性基面與種子層成核，指出新增介面的代價。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Sketch nucleation on a passivated basal plane and seed layer with interface costs. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷；種子層可能增加散射或陷阱。","observationEn":"Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects; Seed layers can add scattering or traps.","failure":"若採用「ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「介電成核」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷。","checkEn":"Submit the Dielectric nucleation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-15-k1","title":"介電成核／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dielectric nucleation / Physics and model","text":"機制：促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects."},{"id":"a087-v8-15-k2","title":"介電成核／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric nucleation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「介電成核」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dielectric nucleation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核","直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估","促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface","Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment","Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects"],"answer":2,"explanation":"促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-15"],"title":"介電成核：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dielectric nucleation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface.","instruction":"接續前一步「介電成核」成果，先指出錯誤主張「ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：種子層可能增加散射或陷阱。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dielectric nucleation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Seed layers can add scattering or traps. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷；種子層可能增加散射或陷阱。","observationEn":"Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects; Seed layers can add scattering or traps.","failure":"若採用「ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「介電成核」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「種子層可能增加散射或陷阱」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dielectric nucleation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Seed layers can add scattering or traps\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-16-k1","title":"介電成核／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dielectric nucleation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：種子層可能增加散射或陷阱。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Seed layers can add scattering or traps."},{"id":"a087-v8-16-k2","title":"介電成核／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dielectric nucleation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核」與「促進沉積也可能增加 EOT 或缺陷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface\" is not equivalent to \"Promoting deposition can add EOT or defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「介電成核」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dielectric nucleation?","options":["種子層可能增加散射或陷阱","ALD 可不經驗證在所有惰性表面均勻成核","直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估"],"optionsEn":["Seed layers can add scattering or traps","Assuming ALD nucleates uniformly on every inert surface","Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment"],"answer":0,"explanation":"種子層可能增加散射或陷阱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Seed layers can add scattering or traps. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-16"],"title":"摻雜方法：建立模型","titleEn":"Doping methods: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「薄層對局部損傷特別敏感」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage.","instruction":"比較靜電、表面電荷轉移及取代摻雜的可逆性。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare reversibility of electrostatic, surface-transfer and substitutional doping. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"薄層對局部損傷特別敏感；表面摻雜可能受環境不穩定影響。","observationEn":"Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage; Surface doping can be environmentally unstable.","failure":"若採用「直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「摻雜方法」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：薄層對局部損傷特別敏感。","checkEn":"Submit the Doping methods diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-17-k1","title":"摻雜方法／物理與模型","titleEn":"Doping methods / Physics and model","text":"機制：薄層對局部損傷特別敏感。","textEn":"Mechanism: Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage."},{"id":"a087-v8-17-k2","title":"摻雜方法／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Doping methods / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「摻雜方法」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Doping methods, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟","薄層對局部損傷特別敏感","直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估"],"optionsEn":["Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success","Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage","Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄層對局部損傷特別敏感；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-17"],"title":"摻雜方法：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Doping methods: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment.","instruction":"接續前一步「摻雜方法」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：表面摻雜可能受環境不穩定影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Doping methods artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Surface doping can be environmentally unstable. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"薄層對局部損傷特別敏感；表面摻雜可能受環境不穩定影響。","observationEn":"Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage; Surface doping can be environmentally unstable.","failure":"若採用「直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「摻雜方法」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「表面摻雜可能受環境不穩定影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Doping methods, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Surface doping can be environmentally unstable\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-18-k1","title":"摻雜方法／物理與模型","titleEn":"Doping methods / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：表面摻雜可能受環境不穩定影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Surface doping can be environmentally unstable."},{"id":"a087-v8-18-k2","title":"摻雜方法／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Doping methods / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估」與「薄層對局部損傷特別敏感」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment\" is not equivalent to \"Atomically thin layers are sensitive to local damage\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「摻雜方法」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Doping methods?","options":["直接沿用塊材離子植入而無損傷評估","n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟","表面摻雜可能受環境不穩定影響"],"optionsEn":["Copying bulk implantation without damage assessment","Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success","Surface doping can be environmentally unstable"],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面摻雜可能受環境不穩定影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface doping can be environmentally unstable. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a087-stage04","order":4,"title":"n/p 配對 → 晶圓可製造性","titleEn":"n/p pairing to Wafer manufacturability","description":"把「n/p 配對」「穩定性」「晶圓可製造性」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for n/p pairing, Stability, Wafer manufacturability.","steps":[{"id":"a087-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-18"],"title":"n/p 配對：建立模型","titleEn":"n/p pairing: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS.","instruction":"為 MoS2 與 WSe2 畫互補元件需求，分開材料和接觸問題。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map complementary-device needs for MoS2/WSe2 and separate material/contact issues. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現；n/p 閾值配對也需考慮。","observationEn":"An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS; Complementary thresholds also need matching.","failure":"若採用「n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「n/p 配對」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現。","checkEn":"Submit the n/p pairing diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-19-k1","title":"n/p 配對／物理與模型","titleEn":"n/p pairing / Physics and model","text":"機制：一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現。","textEn":"Mechanism: An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS."},{"id":"a087-v8-19-k2","title":"n/p 配對／驗證與限制","titleEn":"n/p pairing / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「n/p 配對」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For n/p pairing, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現","n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟","任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較"],"optionsEn":["An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS","Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success","Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps"],"answer":0,"explanation":"一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-19"],"title":"n/p 配對：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"n/p pairing: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success.","instruction":"接續前一步「n/p 配對」成果，先指出錯誤主張「n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：n/p 閾值配對也需考慮。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding n/p pairing artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Complementary thresholds also need matching. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現；n/p 閾值配對也需考慮。","observationEn":"An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS; Complementary thresholds also need matching.","failure":"若採用「n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「n/p 配對」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「n/p 閾值配對也需考慮」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for n/p pairing, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Complementary thresholds also need matching\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-20-k1","title":"n/p 配對／物理與模型","titleEn":"n/p pairing / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：n/p 閾值配對也需考慮。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Complementary thresholds also need matching."},{"id":"a087-v8-20-k2","title":"n/p 配對／驗證與限制","titleEn":"n/p pairing / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟」與「一個優秀 nFET 不代表完整 CMOS 已實現」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success\" is not equivalent to \"An excellent nFET does not establish complete CMOS\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「n/p 配對」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of n/p pairing?","options":["任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較","n/p 閾值配對也需考慮","n 型成功即可宣稱 p 型同樣成熟"],"optionsEn":["Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps","Complementary thresholds also need matching","Inferring p-type maturity from n-type success"],"answer":1,"explanation":"n/p 閾值配對也需考慮；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Complementary thresholds also need matching. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-20"],"title":"穩定性：建立模型","titleEn":"Stability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption.","instruction":"比較不同環境及閘應力後遲滯，保留掃描方向和速度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare environment/gate-stress hysteresis with sweep direction and rate. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應；吸附效應可在真空與空氣不同。","observationEn":"Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption; Adsorption differs between vacuum and air.","failure":"若採用「任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「穩定性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應。","checkEn":"Submit the Stability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-21-k1","title":"穩定性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stability / Physics and model","text":"機制：遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption."},{"id":"a087-v8-21-k2","title":"穩定性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「穩定性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Stability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較","用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率","遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應"],"optionsEn":["Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps","Using morphology success as complete circuit yield","Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption"],"answer":2,"explanation":"遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-21"],"title":"穩定性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Stability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps.","instruction":"接續前一步「穩定性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：吸附效應可在真空與空氣不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Stability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Adsorption differs between vacuum and air. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應；吸附效應可在真空與空氣不同。","observationEn":"Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption; Adsorption differs between vacuum and air.","failure":"若採用「任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「穩定性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「吸附效應可在真空與空氣不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Stability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Adsorption differs between vacuum and air\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-22-k1","title":"穩定性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：吸附效應可在真空與空氣不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Adsorption differs between vacuum and air."},{"id":"a087-v8-22-k2","title":"穩定性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較」與「遲滯可能混合介面捕捉與吸附效應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps\" is not equivalent to \"Hysteresis can mix trapping and adsorption\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「穩定性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Stability?","options":["吸附效應可在真空與空氣不同","任意掃描所得遷移率都可直接比較","用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率"],"optionsEn":["Adsorption differs between vacuum and air","Comparing mobility from arbitrary sweeps","Using morphology success as complete circuit yield"],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸附效應可在真空與空氣不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Adsorption differs between vacuum and air. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-22"],"title":"晶圓可製造性：建立模型","titleEn":"Wafer manufacturability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: High coverage yield is not high functional yield.","instruction":"將形貌良率、元件電性良率與長期穩定分開記錄。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Record morphology yield, electrical yield and long-term stability separately. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率；形貌良率不涵蓋接觸及介電缺陷。","observationEn":"High coverage yield is not high functional yield; Morphology yield omits contact and dielectric failures.","failure":"若採用「用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using morphology success as complete circuit yield\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶圓可製造性」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率。","checkEn":"Submit the Wafer manufacturability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: High coverage yield is not high functional yield.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-23-k1","title":"晶圓可製造性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wafer manufacturability / Physics and model","text":"機制：高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率。","textEn":"Mechanism: High coverage yield is not high functional yield."},{"id":"a087-v8-23-k2","title":"晶圓可製造性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wafer manufacturability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using morphology success as complete circuit yield."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶圓可製造性」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Wafer manufacturability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同","高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率","用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率"],"optionsEn":["Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere","High coverage yield is not high functional yield","Using morphology success as complete circuit yield"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"High coverage yield is not high functional yield. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a087-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-2d","v8-c-2d-progress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a087-v8-23"],"title":"晶圓可製造性：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Wafer manufacturability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using morphology success as complete circuit yield.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶圓可製造性」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：形貌良率不涵蓋接觸及介電缺陷。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Wafer manufacturability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using morphology success as complete circuit yield\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Morphology yield omits contact and dielectric failures. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率；形貌良率不涵蓋接觸及介電缺陷。","observationEn":"High coverage yield is not high functional yield; Morphology yield omits contact and dielectric failures.","failure":"若採用「用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using morphology success as complete circuit yield\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶圓可製造性」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「形貌良率不涵蓋接觸及介電缺陷」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Wafer manufacturability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Morphology yield omits contact and dielectric failures\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a087-v8-24-k1","title":"晶圓可製造性／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wafer manufacturability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：形貌良率不涵蓋接觸及介電缺陷。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Morphology yield omits contact and dielectric failures."},{"id":"a087-v8-24-k2","title":"晶圓可製造性／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wafer manufacturability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率」與「高覆蓋率不等於高功能良率」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using morphology success as complete circuit yield\" is not equivalent to \"High coverage yield is not high functional yield\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶圓可製造性」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Wafer manufacturability?","options":["用形貌成功百分比代表全部電路良率","全片覆蓋便視為所有載子路徑相同","形貌良率不涵蓋接觸及介電缺陷"],"optionsEn":["Using morphology success as complete circuit yield","Treating full coverage as identical transport everywhere","Morphology yield omits contact and dielectric failures"],"answer":2,"explanation":"形貌良率不涵蓋接觸及介電缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Morphology yield omits contact and dielectric failures. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"compound","subcategoryTitle":"化合物與新材料元件","subcategoryTitleEn":"Compound and emerging devices"},{"id":"a088","title":"微機電慣性感測器製程","titleEn":"MEMS inertial-sensor processing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel","v8-c-bosch-place","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從質量彈簧、深矽輪廓到溫漂校正：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Mass and spring and Deep-silicon profile to Temperature calibration: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["質量彈簧","陀螺耦合","沾黏","交軸響應"],"labelsEn":["Mass and spring","Gyroscope coupling","Stiction","Cross-axis response"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a088-stage01","order":1,"title":"質量彈簧 → 共振與阻尼","titleEn":"Mass and spring to Resonance and damping","description":"把「質量彈簧」「差動梳齒」「共振與阻尼」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Mass and spring, Differential combs, Resonance and damping.","steps":[{"id":"a088-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"質量彈簧：建立模型","titleEn":"Mass and spring: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Static approximation needs operation below resonance.","instruction":"用假設 m、k 畫 F=ma 與 x=ma/k 靜態關係。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設準靜態加速度計質量 m=1 µg=10⁻⁹ kg、彈簧 k=1 N/m、加速度 a=9.81 m/s²，力 F=ma=9.81 nN，位移 x=F/k=9.81 nm。加速度加倍時位移加倍，但此例忽略阻尼、共振與非線性止擋，不能外推到衝擊量程。","instructionEn":"Use hypothetical mass/stiffness to draw F=ma and x=ma/k. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a quasistatic accelerometer mass m=1 µg=10⁻⁹ kg, spring constant k=1 N/m and acceleration a=9.81 m/s². F=ma=9.81 nN and x=F/k=9.81 nm. Doubling acceleration doubles displacement in this model. Damping, resonance and nonlinear stops are absent, so do not infer shock range.","observation":"靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件；動態方程還包含阻尼與慣性項。","observationEn":"Static approximation needs operation below resonance; Dynamics also include damping and inertia.","failure":"若採用「把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying static displacement at every frequency\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「質量彈簧」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件。\n算例驗收：驗算 9.81 nN 與 9.81 nm，確認 µg 到 kg 的轉換是 10⁻⁹。","checkEn":"Submit the Mass and spring diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Static approximation needs operation below resonance.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 9.81 nN and 9.81 nm and confirm the 10⁻⁹ conversion from micrograms to kilograms.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-01-k1","title":"質量彈簧／物理與模型","titleEn":"Mass and spring / Physics and model","text":"機制：靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Static approximation needs operation below resonance."},{"id":"a088-v8-01-k2","title":"質量彈簧／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Mass and spring / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率」。\n假設數值與推算：假設準靜態加速度計質量 m=1 µg=10⁻⁹ kg、彈簧 k=1 N/m、加速度 a=9.81 m/s²，力 F=ma=9.81 nN，位移 x=F/k=9.81 nm。加速度加倍時位移加倍，但此例忽略阻尼、共振與非線性止擋，不能外推到衝擊量程。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Applying static displacement at every frequency.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a quasistatic accelerometer mass m=1 µg=10⁻⁹ kg, spring constant k=1 N/m and acceleration a=9.81 m/s². F=ma=9.81 nN and x=F/k=9.81 nm. Doubling acceleration doubles displacement in this model. Damping, resonance and nonlinear stops are absent, so do not infer shock range."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「質量彈簧」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Mass and spring, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件","把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率","差動架構自動消除全部偏差"],"optionsEn":["Static approximation needs operation below resonance","Applying static displacement at every frequency","Assuming differential geometry removes every bias"],"answer":0,"explanation":"靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Static approximation needs operation below resonance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-01"],"title":"質量彈簧：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Mass and spring: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Applying static displacement at every frequency.","instruction":"接續前一步「質量彈簧」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：動態方程還包含阻尼與慣性項。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Mass and spring artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Applying static displacement at every frequency\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dynamics also include damping and inertia. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件；動態方程還包含阻尼與慣性項。","observationEn":"Static approximation needs operation below resonance; Dynamics also include damping and inertia.","failure":"若採用「把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying static displacement at every frequency\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「質量彈簧」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「動態方程還包含阻尼與慣性項」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Mass and spring, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dynamics also include damping and inertia\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-02-k1","title":"質量彈簧／物理與模型","titleEn":"Mass and spring / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：動態方程還包含阻尼與慣性項。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dynamics also include damping and inertia."},{"id":"a088-v8-02-k2","title":"質量彈簧／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Mass and spring / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率」與「靜態近似需要低於機械共振的條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Applying static displacement at every frequency\" is not equivalent to \"Static approximation needs operation below resonance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「質量彈簧」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Mass and spring?","options":["差動架構自動消除全部偏差","動態方程還包含阻尼與慣性項","把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率"],"optionsEn":["Assuming differential geometry removes every bias","Dynamics also include damping and inertia","Applying static displacement at every frequency"],"answer":1,"explanation":"動態方程還包含阻尼與慣性項；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dynamics also include damping and inertia. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-02"],"title":"差動梳齒：建立模型","titleEn":"Differential combs: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「差動訊號可分離部分共模變化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Differential signals reject some common-mode changes.","instruction":"畫正反位移下兩側電容變化與差動讀出。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw opposite capacitance changes and differential readout. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"差動訊號可分離部分共模變化；寄生電容會稀釋差動比例。","observationEn":"Differential signals reject some common-mode changes; Parasitics dilute differential capacitance ratios.","failure":"若採用「差動架構自動消除全部偏差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming differential geometry removes every bias\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「差動梳齒」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：差動訊號可分離部分共模變化。","checkEn":"Submit the Differential combs diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Differential signals reject some common-mode changes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-03-k1","title":"差動梳齒／物理與模型","titleEn":"Differential combs / Physics and model","text":"機制：差動訊號可分離部分共模變化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Differential signals reject some common-mode changes."},{"id":"a088-v8-03-k2","title":"差動梳齒／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Differential combs / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「差動架構自動消除全部偏差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming differential geometry removes every bias."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「差動梳齒」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Differential combs, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["差動架構自動消除全部偏差","Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好","差動訊號可分離部分共模變化"],"optionsEn":["Assuming differential geometry removes every bias","Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application","Differential signals reject some common-mode changes"],"answer":2,"explanation":"差動訊號可分離部分共模變化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Differential signals reject some common-mode changes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-03"],"title":"差動梳齒：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Differential combs: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「差動架構自動消除全部偏差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming differential geometry removes every bias.","instruction":"接續前一步「差動梳齒」成果，先指出錯誤主張「差動架構自動消除全部偏差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：寄生電容會稀釋差動比例。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Differential combs artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming differential geometry removes every bias\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Parasitics dilute differential capacitance ratios. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"差動訊號可分離部分共模變化；寄生電容會稀釋差動比例。","observationEn":"Differential signals reject some common-mode changes; Parasitics dilute differential capacitance ratios.","failure":"若採用「差動架構自動消除全部偏差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming differential geometry removes every bias\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「差動梳齒」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「寄生電容會稀釋差動比例」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Differential combs, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Parasitics dilute differential capacitance ratios\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-04-k1","title":"差動梳齒／物理與模型","titleEn":"Differential combs / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：寄生電容會稀釋差動比例。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Parasitics dilute differential capacitance ratios."},{"id":"a088-v8-04-k2","title":"差動梳齒／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Differential combs / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「差動架構自動消除全部偏差」與「差動訊號可分離部分共模變化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming differential geometry removes every bias\" is not equivalent to \"Differential signals reject some common-mode changes\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「差動梳齒」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Differential combs?","options":["寄生電容會稀釋差動比例","差動架構自動消除全部偏差","Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好"],"optionsEn":["Parasitics dilute differential capacitance ratios","Assuming differential geometry removes every bias","Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application"],"answer":0,"explanation":"寄生電容會稀釋差動比例；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Parasitics dilute differential capacitance ratios. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-04"],"title":"共振與阻尼：建立模型","titleEn":"Resonance and damping: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration.","instruction":"畫兩個阻尼值的頻率響應並標示量測頻寬。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plot two damping responses and mark usable bandwidth. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量；氣體阻尼可隨腔壓改變。","observationEn":"High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration; Gas damping varies with cavity pressure.","failure":"若採用「Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「共振與阻尼」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量。","checkEn":"Submit the Resonance and damping diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-05-k1","title":"共振與阻尼／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resonance and damping / Physics and model","text":"機制：高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量。","textEn":"Mechanism: High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration."},{"id":"a088-v8-05-k2","title":"共振與阻尼／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resonance and damping / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共振與阻尼」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Resonance and damping, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把靜止重力響應直接當角速度","高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量","Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好"],"optionsEn":["Treating static gravity response as angular rate","High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration","Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-05"],"title":"共振與阻尼：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Resonance and damping: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application.","instruction":"接續前一步「共振與阻尼」成果，先指出錯誤主張「Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：氣體阻尼可隨腔壓改變。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Resonance and damping artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Gas damping varies with cavity pressure. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量；氣體阻尼可隨腔壓改變。","observationEn":"High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration; Gas damping varies with cavity pressure.","failure":"若採用「Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「共振與阻尼」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「氣體阻尼可隨腔壓改變」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Resonance and damping, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Gas damping varies with cavity pressure\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-06-k1","title":"共振與阻尼／物理與模型","titleEn":"Resonance and damping / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：氣體阻尼可隨腔壓改變。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Gas damping varies with cavity pressure."},{"id":"a088-v8-06-k2","title":"共振與阻尼／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Resonance and damping / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好」與「高 Q 值不必然適合寬頻加速度測量」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application\" is not equivalent to \"High Q is not always suitable for broadband acceleration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「共振與阻尼」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Resonance and damping?","options":["Q 越高所有慣性感測用途都越好","把靜止重力響應直接當角速度","氣體阻尼可隨腔壓改變"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher Q benefits every inertial application","Treating static gravity response as angular rate","Gas damping varies with cavity pressure"],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣體阻尼可隨腔壓改變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Gas damping varies with cavity pressure. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a088-stage02","order":2,"title":"陀螺耦合 → 犧牲層釋放","titleEn":"Gyroscope coupling to Sacrificial release","description":"把「陀螺耦合」「深矽輪廓」「犧牲層釋放」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Gyroscope coupling, Deep-silicon profile, Sacrificial release.","steps":[{"id":"a088-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-06"],"title":"陀螺耦合：建立模型","titleEn":"Gyroscope coupling: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics.","instruction":"畫驅動軸、角速度與科氏感測軸的方向。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw drive, rotation and Coriolis-sensing directions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊；正交誤差可混入陀螺感測通道。","observationEn":"Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics; Quadrature error can enter gyro sensing.","failure":"若採用「把靜止重力響應直接當角速度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating static gravity response as angular rate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「陀螺耦合」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊。","checkEn":"Submit the Gyroscope coupling diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-07-k1","title":"陀螺耦合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gyroscope coupling / Physics and model","text":"機制：陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊。","textEn":"Mechanism: Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics."},{"id":"a088-v8-07-k2","title":"陀螺耦合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gyroscope coupling / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把靜止重力響應直接當角速度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating static gravity response as angular rate."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「陀螺耦合」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Gyroscope coupling, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊","把靜止重力響應直接當角速度","只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面"],"optionsEn":["Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics","Treating static gravity response as angular rate","Inferring the full spring section from top width"],"answer":0,"explanation":"陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-07"],"title":"陀螺耦合：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Gyroscope coupling: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把靜止重力響應直接當角速度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating static gravity response as angular rate.","instruction":"接續前一步「陀螺耦合」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把靜止重力響應直接當角速度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：正交誤差可混入陀螺感測通道。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Gyroscope coupling artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating static gravity response as angular rate\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Quadrature error can enter gyro sensing. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊；正交誤差可混入陀螺感測通道。","observationEn":"Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics; Quadrature error can enter gyro sensing.","failure":"若採用「把靜止重力響應直接當角速度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating static gravity response as angular rate\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「陀螺耦合」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「正交誤差可混入陀螺感測通道」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Gyroscope coupling, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Quadrature error can enter gyro sensing\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-08-k1","title":"陀螺耦合／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gyroscope coupling / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：正交誤差可混入陀螺感測通道。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Quadrature error can enter gyro sensing."},{"id":"a088-v8-08-k2","title":"陀螺耦合／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gyroscope coupling / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把靜止重力響應直接當角速度」與「陀螺和加速度計使用不同動態資訊」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating static gravity response as angular rate\" is not equivalent to \"Gyroscopes and accelerometers use different dynamics\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「陀螺耦合」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Gyroscope coupling?","options":["只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面","正交誤差可混入陀螺感測通道","把靜止重力響應直接當角速度"],"optionsEn":["Inferring the full spring section from top width","Quadrature error can enter gyro sensing","Treating static gravity response as angular rate"],"answer":1,"explanation":"正交誤差可混入陀螺感測通道；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Quadrature error can enter gyro sensing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-08"],"title":"深矽輪廓：建立模型","titleEn":"Deep-silicon profile: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness.","instruction":"畫彈簧側壁斜度與蝕刻 scallop，預測有效剛性變化。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw spring taper/scallops and predict effective stiffness changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性；側壁粗糙也會影響疲勞。","observationEn":"Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness; Sidewall roughness can affect fatigue.","failure":"若採用「只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring the full spring section from top width\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「深矽輪廓」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性。","checkEn":"Submit the Deep-silicon profile diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-09-k1","title":"深矽輪廓／物理與模型","titleEn":"Deep-silicon profile / Physics and model","text":"機制：微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness."},{"id":"a088-v8-09-k2","title":"深矽輪廓／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Deep-silicon profile / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring the full spring section from top width."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「深矽輪廓」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Deep-silicon profile, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面","釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠","微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性"],"optionsEn":["Inferring the full spring section from top width","Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion","Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness"],"answer":2,"explanation":"微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-09"],"title":"深矽輪廓：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Deep-silicon profile: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring the full spring section from top width.","instruction":"接續前一步「深矽輪廓」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：側壁粗糙也會影響疲勞。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Deep-silicon profile artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring the full spring section from top width\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sidewall roughness can affect fatigue. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性；側壁粗糙也會影響疲勞。","observationEn":"Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness; Sidewall roughness can affect fatigue.","failure":"若採用「只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring the full spring section from top width\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「深矽輪廓」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「側壁粗糙也會影響疲勞」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Deep-silicon profile, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sidewall roughness can affect fatigue\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-10-k1","title":"深矽輪廓／物理與模型","titleEn":"Deep-silicon profile / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：側壁粗糙也會影響疲勞。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sidewall roughness can affect fatigue."},{"id":"a088-v8-10-k2","title":"深矽輪廓／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Deep-silicon profile / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面」與「微小幾何偏差可能顯著改變彈簧剛性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring the full spring section from top width\" is not equivalent to \"Small geometry errors can strongly alter spring stiffness\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「深矽輪廓」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Deep-silicon profile?","options":["側壁粗糙也會影響疲勞","只量上表面線寬就完整知道彈簧截面","釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠"],"optionsEn":["Sidewall roughness can affect fatigue","Inferring the full spring section from top width","Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion"],"answer":0,"explanation":"側壁粗糙也會影響疲勞；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sidewall roughness can affect fatigue. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-10"],"title":"犧牲層釋放：建立模型","titleEn":"Sacrificial release: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors.","instruction":"畫釋放孔、移除路徑及保留錨點。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw release openings, removal paths and retained anchors. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接；錨點欠蝕會改變有效彈簧長度。","observationEn":"Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors; Anchor undercut changes effective spring length.","failure":"若採用「釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「犧牲層釋放」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接。","checkEn":"Submit the Sacrificial release diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-11-k1","title":"犧牲層釋放／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sacrificial release / Physics and model","text":"機制：釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接。","textEn":"Mechanism: Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors."},{"id":"a088-v8-11-k2","title":"犧牲層釋放／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sacrificial release / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「犧牲層釋放」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Sacrificial release, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住","釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接","釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠"],"optionsEn":["Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking","Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors","Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion"],"answer":1,"explanation":"釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-11"],"title":"犧牲層釋放：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Sacrificial release: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion.","instruction":"接續前一步「犧牲層釋放」成果，先指出錯誤主張「釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：錨點欠蝕會改變有效彈簧長度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Sacrificial release artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Anchor undercut changes effective spring length. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接；錨點欠蝕會改變有效彈簧長度。","observationEn":"Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors; Anchor undercut changes effective spring length.","failure":"若採用「釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「犧牲層釋放」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「錨點欠蝕會改變有效彈簧長度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Sacrificial release, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Anchor undercut changes effective spring length\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-12-k1","title":"犧牲層釋放／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sacrificial release / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：錨點欠蝕會改變有效彈簧長度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Anchor undercut changes effective spring length."},{"id":"a088-v8-12-k2","title":"犧牲層釋放／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sacrificial release / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠」與「釋放須去除犧牲層但保留機械連接」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion\" is not equivalent to \"Release removes sacrificial material while retaining anchors\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「犧牲層釋放」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Sacrificial release?","options":["釋放越多就一定活動越自由且更可靠","元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住","錨點欠蝕會改變有效彈簧長度"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more removal always improves reliable motion","Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking","Anchor undercut changes effective spring length"],"answer":2,"explanation":"錨點欠蝕會改變有效彈簧長度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Anchor undercut changes effective spring length. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a088-stage03","order":3,"title":"沾黏 → 殘留應力","titleEn":"Stiction to Residual stress","description":"把「沾黏」「封裝氣壓」「殘留應力」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Stiction, Package pressure, Residual stress.","steps":[{"id":"a088-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-12"],"title":"沾黏：建立模型","titleEn":"Stiction: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「表面力可能勝過微結構回復力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force.","instruction":"畫乾燥彎月面與彈簧回復力方向，區分接觸與永久黏住。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw meniscus/restoring forces and distinguish contact from lasting adhesion. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"表面力可能勝過微結構回復力；防沾黏表面也需相容性驗證。","observationEn":"Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force; Anti-stiction surfaces need compatibility checks.","failure":"若採用「元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「沾黏」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：表面力可能勝過微結構回復力。","checkEn":"Submit the Stiction diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-13-k1","title":"沾黏／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stiction / Physics and model","text":"機制：表面力可能勝過微結構回復力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force."},{"id":"a088-v8-13-k2","title":"沾黏／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stiction / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沾黏」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Stiction, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["表面力可能勝過微結構回復力","元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住","密封只防灰塵而不影響動態"],"optionsEn":["Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force","Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking","Treating sealing only as dust protection"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面力可能勝過微結構回復力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-13"],"title":"沾黏：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Stiction: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking.","instruction":"接續前一步「沾黏」成果，先指出錯誤主張「元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：防沾黏表面也需相容性驗證。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Stiction artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Anti-stiction surfaces need compatibility checks. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"表面力可能勝過微結構回復力；防沾黏表面也需相容性驗證。","observationEn":"Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force; Anti-stiction surfaces need compatibility checks.","failure":"若採用「元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「沾黏」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「防沾黏表面也需相容性驗證」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Stiction, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Anti-stiction surfaces need compatibility checks\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-14-k1","title":"沾黏／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stiction / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：防沾黏表面也需相容性驗證。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Anti-stiction surfaces need compatibility checks."},{"id":"a088-v8-14-k2","title":"沾黏／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stiction / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住」與「表面力可能勝過微結構回復力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking\" is not equivalent to \"Surface forces can exceed microstructure restoring force\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「沾黏」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Stiction?","options":["密封只防灰塵而不影響動態","防沾黏表面也需相容性驗證","元件重量很小就不可能被表面力拉住"],"optionsEn":["Treating sealing only as dust protection","Anti-stiction surfaces need compatibility checks","Assuming low weight prevents surface-force sticking"],"answer":1,"explanation":"防沾黏表面也需相容性驗證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Anti-stiction surfaces need compatibility checks. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-14"],"title":"封裝氣壓：建立模型","titleEn":"Package pressure: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition.","instruction":"比較假設腔壓對阻尼與響應時間的影響。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare cavity pressure effects on damping and response time. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件；漏氣會造成動態隨時間漂移。","observationEn":"Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition; Leaks cause time-dependent dynamic drift.","failure":"若採用「密封只防灰塵而不影響動態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating sealing only as dust protection\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「封裝氣壓」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件。","checkEn":"Submit the Package pressure diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-15-k1","title":"封裝氣壓／物理與模型","titleEn":"Package pressure / Physics and model","text":"機制：封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition."},{"id":"a088-v8-15-k2","title":"封裝氣壓／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Package pressure / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「密封只防灰塵而不影響動態」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating sealing only as dust protection."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「封裝氣壓」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Package pressure, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["密封只防灰塵而不影響動態","平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格","封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件"],"optionsEn":["Treating sealing only as dust protection","Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness","Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition"],"answer":2,"explanation":"封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-15"],"title":"封裝氣壓：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Package pressure: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「密封只防灰塵而不影響動態」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating sealing only as dust protection.","instruction":"接續前一步「封裝氣壓」成果，先指出錯誤主張「密封只防灰塵而不影響動態」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：漏氣會造成動態隨時間漂移。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Package pressure artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating sealing only as dust protection\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Leaks cause time-dependent dynamic drift. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件；漏氣會造成動態隨時間漂移。","observationEn":"Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition; Leaks cause time-dependent dynamic drift.","failure":"若採用「密封只防灰塵而不影響動態」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating sealing only as dust protection\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「封裝氣壓」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「漏氣會造成動態隨時間漂移」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Package pressure, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Leaks cause time-dependent dynamic drift\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-16-k1","title":"封裝氣壓／物理與模型","titleEn":"Package pressure / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：漏氣會造成動態隨時間漂移。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Leaks cause time-dependent dynamic drift."},{"id":"a088-v8-16-k2","title":"封裝氣壓／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Package pressure / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「密封只防灰塵而不影響動態」與「封裝氣氛是機械系統邊界條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating sealing only as dust protection\" is not equivalent to \"Package atmosphere is a mechanical boundary condition\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「封裝氣壓」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Package pressure?","options":["漏氣會造成動態隨時間漂移","密封只防灰塵而不影響動態","平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格"],"optionsEn":["Leaks cause time-dependent dynamic drift","Treating sealing only as dust protection","Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏氣會造成動態隨時間漂移；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Leaks cause time-dependent dynamic drift. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-16"],"title":"殘留應力：建立模型","titleEn":"Residual stress: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel.","instruction":"畫薄膜應力造成的翹曲與間隙改變。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw film-stress curvature and gap changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍；應力梯度而非平均值造成彎曲。","observationEn":"Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel; Stress gradients, not just means, cause curvature.","failure":"若採用「平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「殘留應力」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍。","checkEn":"Submit the Residual stress diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-17-k1","title":"殘留應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Residual stress / Physics and model","text":"機制：初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍。","textEn":"Mechanism: Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel."},{"id":"a088-v8-17-k2","title":"殘留應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Residual stress / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「殘留應力」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Residual stress, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只校正主軸就保證三軸正交","初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍","平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality","Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel","Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-17"],"title":"殘留應力：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Residual stress: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness.","instruction":"接續前一步「殘留應力」成果，先指出錯誤主張「平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：應力梯度而非平均值造成彎曲。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Residual stress artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Stress gradients, not just means, cause curvature. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍；應力梯度而非平均值造成彎曲。","observationEn":"Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel; Stress gradients, not just means, cause curvature.","failure":"若採用「平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「殘留應力」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「應力梯度而非平均值造成彎曲」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Residual stress, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Stress gradients, not just means, cause curvature\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-18-k1","title":"殘留應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Residual stress / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：應力梯度而非平均值造成彎曲。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Stress gradients, not just means, cause curvature."},{"id":"a088-v8-18-k2","title":"殘留應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Residual stress / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格」與「初始間隙改變會影響電容與運動範圍」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness\" is not equivalent to \"Initial gap changes affect capacitance and travel\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「殘留應力」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Residual stress?","options":["平均膜厚合格便證明機械零偏合格","只校正主軸就保證三軸正交","應力梯度而非平均值造成彎曲"],"optionsEn":["Inferring mechanical zero offset from average film thickness","Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality","Stress gradients, not just means, cause curvature"],"answer":2,"explanation":"應力梯度而非平均值造成彎曲；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Stress gradients, not just means, cause curvature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a088-stage04","order":4,"title":"交軸響應 → 溫漂校正","titleEn":"Cross-axis response to Temperature calibration","description":"把「交軸響應」「自我測試」「溫漂校正」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Cross-axis response, Self-test, Temperature calibration.","steps":[{"id":"a088-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-18"],"title":"交軸響應：建立模型","titleEn":"Cross-axis response: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor.","instruction":"設計三方向輸入矩陣並抽取靈敏度矩陣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Design three-axis inputs and extract a sensitivity matrix. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例；安裝角度也貢獻交軸響應。","observationEn":"Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor; Mounting angle also causes cross-axis response.","failure":"若採用「只校正主軸就保證三軸正交」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「交軸響應」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例。","checkEn":"Submit the Cross-axis response diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-19-k1","title":"交軸響應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cross-axis response / Physics and model","text":"機制：軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例。","textEn":"Mechanism: Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor."},{"id":"a088-v8-19-k2","title":"交軸響應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cross-axis response / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只校正主軸就保證三軸正交」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「交軸響應」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Cross-axis response, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例","只校正主軸就保證三軸正交","通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確"],"optionsEn":["Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor","Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality","Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects"],"answer":0,"explanation":"軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-19"],"title":"交軸響應：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Cross-axis response: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只校正主軸就保證三軸正交」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality.","instruction":"接續前一步「交軸響應」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只校正主軸就保證三軸正交」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：安裝角度也貢獻交軸響應。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Cross-axis response artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mounting angle also causes cross-axis response. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例；安裝角度也貢獻交軸響應。","observationEn":"Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor; Mounting angle also causes cross-axis response.","failure":"若採用「只校正主軸就保證三軸正交」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「交軸響應」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「安裝角度也貢獻交軸響應」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Cross-axis response, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mounting angle also causes cross-axis response\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-20-k1","title":"交軸響應／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cross-axis response / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：安裝角度也貢獻交軸響應。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mounting angle also causes cross-axis response."},{"id":"a088-v8-20-k2","title":"交軸響應／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cross-axis response / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只校正主軸就保證三軸正交」與「軸向耦合需矩陣校正而非單一比例」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality\" is not equivalent to \"Cross-axis coupling needs a matrix, not one scale factor\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「交軸響應」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Cross-axis response?","options":["通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確","安裝角度也貢獻交軸響應","只校正主軸就保證三軸正交"],"optionsEn":["Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects","Mounting angle also causes cross-axis response","Assuming main-axis calibration guarantees orthogonality"],"answer":1,"explanation":"安裝角度也貢獻交軸響應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mounting angle also causes cross-axis response. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-20"],"title":"自我測試：建立模型","titleEn":"Self-test: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path.","instruction":"畫靜電測試力和真實慣性力路徑，列出可及不可驗證項。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare electrostatic test and inertial-force paths and their coverage. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑；電子自測未必驗證外部加速度校正。","observationEn":"Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path; Electronic self-test may not verify acceleration calibration.","failure":"若採用「通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「自我測試」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑。","checkEn":"Submit the Self-test diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-21-k1","title":"自我測試／物理與模型","titleEn":"Self-test / Physics and model","text":"機制：自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑。","textEn":"Mechanism: Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path."},{"id":"a088-v8-21-k2","title":"自我測試／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Self-test / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自我測試」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Self-test, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確","一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差","自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑"],"optionsEn":["Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects","Using one offset correction for all thermal error","Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path"],"answer":2,"explanation":"自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-21"],"title":"自我測試：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Self-test: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects.","instruction":"接續前一步「自我測試」成果，先指出錯誤主張「通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電子自測未必驗證外部加速度校正。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Self-test artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electronic self-test may not verify acceleration calibration. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑；電子自測未必驗證外部加速度校正。","observationEn":"Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path; Electronic self-test may not verify acceleration calibration.","failure":"若採用「通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「自我測試」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電子自測未必驗證外部加速度校正」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Self-test, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electronic self-test may not verify acceleration calibration\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-22-k1","title":"自我測試／物理與模型","titleEn":"Self-test / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電子自測未必驗證外部加速度校正。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electronic self-test may not verify acceleration calibration."},{"id":"a088-v8-22-k2","title":"自我測試／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Self-test / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確」與「自我測試未必涵蓋完整外部機械路徑」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects\" is not equivalent to \"Self-test may not cover the full external mechanical path\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「自我測試」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Self-test?","options":["電子自測未必驗證外部加速度校正","通過自測就代表所有封裝與安裝都正確","一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差"],"optionsEn":["Electronic self-test may not verify acceleration calibration","Assuming self-test validates all mounting/package effects","Using one offset correction for all thermal error"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電子自測未必驗證外部加速度校正；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electronic self-test may not verify acceleration calibration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-22"],"title":"溫漂校正：建立模型","titleEn":"Temperature calibration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections.","instruction":"建立零偏和比例因子的溫度圖，保留加熱冷卻方向。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map offset/scale versus temperature with heating/cooling direction. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項；溫度遲滯需要往返循環檢查。","observationEn":"Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections; Thermal hysteresis needs heating/cooling cycles.","failure":"若採用「一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one offset correction for all thermal error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「溫漂校正」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項。","checkEn":"Submit the Temperature calibration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-23-k1","title":"溫漂校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temperature calibration / Physics and model","text":"機制：零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項。","textEn":"Mechanism: Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections."},{"id":"a088-v8-23-k2","title":"溫漂校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temperature calibration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using one offset correction for all thermal error."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫漂校正」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Temperature calibration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率","零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項","一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差"],"optionsEn":["Applying static displacement at every frequency","Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections","Using one offset correction for all thermal error"],"answer":1,"explanation":"零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a088-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-mems","v8-c-accel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a088-v8-23"],"title":"溫漂校正：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Temperature calibration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using one offset correction for all thermal error.","instruction":"接續前一步「溫漂校正」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：溫度遲滯需要往返循環檢查。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Temperature calibration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using one offset correction for all thermal error\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thermal hysteresis needs heating/cooling cycles. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項；溫度遲滯需要往返循環檢查。","observationEn":"Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections; Thermal hysteresis needs heating/cooling cycles.","failure":"若採用「一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using one offset correction for all thermal error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「溫漂校正」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「溫度遲滯需要往返循環檢查」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Temperature calibration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thermal hysteresis needs heating/cooling cycles\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a088-v8-24-k1","title":"溫漂校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temperature calibration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：溫度遲滯需要往返循環檢查。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thermal hysteresis needs heating/cooling cycles."},{"id":"a088-v8-24-k2","title":"溫漂校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temperature calibration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差」與「零偏溫漂與比例溫漂是不同校正項」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using one offset correction for all thermal error\" is not equivalent to \"Offset drift and scale drift are different corrections\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「溫漂校正」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Temperature calibration?","options":["一個零點補償足以修正所有溫度誤差","把靜態位移式套到所有振動頻率","溫度遲滯需要往返循環檢查"],"optionsEn":["Using one offset correction for all thermal error","Applying static displacement at every frequency","Thermal hysteresis needs heating/cooling cycles"],"answer":2,"explanation":"溫度遲滯需要往返循環檢查；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal hysteresis needs heating/cooling cycles. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"mems","subcategoryTitle":"微機電與顯示","subcategoryTitleEn":"MEMS and displays"},{"id":"a089","title":"微機電壓力感測器製程","titleEn":"MEMS pressure-sensor processing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems","v8-c-bosch-place","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從壓力定義、電容讀出到氣壓與高度：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Pressure definition and Capacitive readout to Pressure and altitude: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["壓力定義","壓阻讀出","參考腔","過壓與量程"],"labelsEn":["Pressure definition","Piezoresistive readout","Reference cavity","Overpressure and range"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a089-stage01","order":1,"title":"壓力定義 → 厚度靈敏度","titleEn":"Pressure definition to Thickness sensitivity","description":"把「壓力定義」「膜片彎曲」「厚度靈敏度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pressure definition, Diaphragm bending, Thickness sensitivity.","steps":[{"id":"a089-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"壓力定義：建立模型","titleEn":"Pressure definition: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「壓力讀值必須指定參考側」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Pressure readings require a reference side.","instruction":"畫絕對、表壓與差壓的兩側邊界。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw both sides for absolute, gauge and differential pressure. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"壓力讀值必須指定參考側；氣壓變動會改變表壓參考。","observationEn":"Pressure readings require a reference side; Ambient changes alter gauge references.","failure":"若採用「沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing all pressures without reference definitions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「壓力定義」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：壓力讀值必須指定參考側。","checkEn":"Submit the Pressure definition diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Pressure readings require a reference side.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-01-k1","title":"壓力定義／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pressure definition / Physics and model","text":"機制：壓力讀值必須指定參考側。","textEn":"Mechanism: Pressure readings require a reference side."},{"id":"a089-v8-01-k2","title":"壓力定義／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pressure definition / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing all pressures without reference definitions."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓力定義」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pressure definition, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["壓力讀值必須指定參考側","沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力","把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力"],"optionsEn":["Pressure readings require a reference side","Comparing all pressures without reference definitions","Equating center displacement with edge stress"],"answer":0,"explanation":"壓力讀值必須指定參考側；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pressure readings require a reference side. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-01"],"title":"壓力定義：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure definition: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing all pressures without reference definitions.","instruction":"接續前一步「壓力定義」成果，先指出錯誤主張「沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：氣壓變動會改變表壓參考。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pressure definition artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing all pressures without reference definitions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Ambient changes alter gauge references. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"壓力讀值必須指定參考側；氣壓變動會改變表壓參考。","observationEn":"Pressure readings require a reference side; Ambient changes alter gauge references.","failure":"若採用「沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing all pressures without reference definitions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「壓力定義」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「氣壓變動會改變表壓參考」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pressure definition, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Ambient changes alter gauge references\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-02-k1","title":"壓力定義／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pressure definition / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：氣壓變動會改變表壓參考。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Ambient changes alter gauge references."},{"id":"a089-v8-02-k2","title":"壓力定義／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pressure definition / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力」與「壓力讀值必須指定參考側」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing all pressures without reference definitions\" is not equivalent to \"Pressure readings require a reference side\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「壓力定義」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pressure definition?","options":["把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力","氣壓變動會改變表壓參考","沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力"],"optionsEn":["Equating center displacement with edge stress","Ambient changes alter gauge references","Comparing all pressures without reference definitions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氣壓變動會改變表壓參考；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Ambient changes alter gauge references. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-02"],"title":"膜片彎曲：建立模型","titleEn":"Diaphragm bending: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide.","instruction":"畫固定邊緣膜片的變形與應力分布。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw deflection/stress in a clamped diaphragm. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同；膜片大變形可引入張力非線性。","observationEn":"Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide; Large deflection introduces tension nonlinearity.","failure":"若採用「把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating center displacement with edge stress\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「膜片彎曲」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同。","checkEn":"Submit the Diaphragm bending diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-03-k1","title":"膜片彎曲／物理與模型","titleEn":"Diaphragm bending / Physics and model","text":"機制：最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide."},{"id":"a089-v8-03-k2","title":"膜片彎曲／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Diaphragm bending / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating center displacement with edge stress."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「膜片彎曲」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Diaphragm bending, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力","膜厚減半只令變形增加一半","最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同"],"optionsEn":["Equating center displacement with edge stress","Assuming a linear half-thickness response","Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide"],"answer":2,"explanation":"最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-03"],"title":"膜片彎曲：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Diaphragm bending: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating center displacement with edge stress.","instruction":"接續前一步「膜片彎曲」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：膜片大變形可引入張力非線性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Diaphragm bending artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating center displacement with edge stress\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Large deflection introduces tension nonlinearity. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同；膜片大變形可引入張力非線性。","observationEn":"Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide; Large deflection introduces tension nonlinearity.","failure":"若採用「把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating center displacement with edge stress\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「膜片彎曲」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「膜片大變形可引入張力非線性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Diaphragm bending, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Large deflection introduces tension nonlinearity\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-04-k1","title":"膜片彎曲／物理與模型","titleEn":"Diaphragm bending / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：膜片大變形可引入張力非線性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Large deflection introduces tension nonlinearity."},{"id":"a089-v8-04-k2","title":"膜片彎曲／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Diaphragm bending / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力」與「最大位移位置與最大應力位置未必相同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating center displacement with edge stress\" is not equivalent to \"Maximum displacement and stress need not coincide\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「膜片彎曲」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Diaphragm bending?","options":["膜片大變形可引入張力非線性","把中心位移直接等同邊緣應力","膜厚減半只令變形增加一半"],"optionsEn":["Large deflection introduces tension nonlinearity","Equating center displacement with edge stress","Assuming a linear half-thickness response"],"answer":0,"explanation":"膜片大變形可引入張力非線性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Large deflection introduces tension nonlinearity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-04"],"title":"厚度靈敏度：建立模型","titleEn":"Thickness sensitivity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect.","instruction":"比較兩個假設膜厚的小變形撓曲，標明近似限制。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare small-deflection models for two thicknesses and state limits. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響；殘留張力可改變厚度縮放。","observationEn":"Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect; Residual tension changes thickness scaling.","failure":"若採用「膜厚減半只令變形增加一半」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a linear half-thickness response\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「厚度靈敏度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響。","checkEn":"Submit the Thickness sensitivity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-05-k1","title":"厚度靈敏度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness sensitivity / Physics and model","text":"機制：膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響。","textEn":"Mechanism: Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect."},{"id":"a089-v8-05-k2","title":"厚度靈敏度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness sensitivity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「膜厚減半只令變形增加一半」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming a linear half-thickness response."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「厚度靈敏度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thickness sensitivity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號","膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響","膜厚減半只令變形增加一半"],"optionsEn":["Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal","Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect","Assuming a linear half-thickness response"],"answer":1,"explanation":"膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-05"],"title":"厚度靈敏度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thickness sensitivity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「膜厚減半只令變形增加一半」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming a linear half-thickness response.","instruction":"接續前一步「厚度靈敏度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「膜厚減半只令變形增加一半」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：殘留張力可改變厚度縮放。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thickness sensitivity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming a linear half-thickness response\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Residual tension changes thickness scaling. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響；殘留張力可改變厚度縮放。","observationEn":"Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect; Residual tension changes thickness scaling.","failure":"若採用「膜厚減半只令變形增加一半」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a linear half-thickness response\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「厚度靈敏度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「殘留張力可改變厚度縮放」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thickness sensitivity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Residual tension changes thickness scaling\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-06-k1","title":"厚度靈敏度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness sensitivity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：殘留張力可改變厚度縮放。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Residual tension changes thickness scaling."},{"id":"a089-v8-06-k2","title":"厚度靈敏度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness sensitivity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「膜厚減半只令變形增加一半」與「膜厚對剛性有強烈非線性影響」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming a linear half-thickness response\" is not equivalent to \"Thickness has a strong nonlinear stiffness effect\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「厚度靈敏度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thickness sensitivity?","options":["膜厚減半只令變形增加一半","任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號","殘留張力可改變厚度縮放"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a linear half-thickness response","Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal","Residual tension changes thickness scaling"],"answer":2,"explanation":"殘留張力可改變厚度縮放；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Residual tension changes thickness scaling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a089-stage02","order":2,"title":"壓阻讀出 → 背腔製作","titleEn":"Piezoresistive readout to Back-cavity formation","description":"把「壓阻讀出」「電容讀出」「背腔製作」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Piezoresistive readout, Capacitive readout, Back-cavity formation.","steps":[{"id":"a089-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-06"],"title":"壓阻讀出：建立模型","titleEn":"Piezoresistive readout: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity.","instruction":"畫四電阻電橋與受拉受壓位置，確認輸出符號。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw a four-resistor bridge with tensile/compressive sites and output sign. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度；壓阻係數隨晶向與溫度變化。","observationEn":"Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity; Piezoresistance depends on orientation and temperature.","failure":"若採用「任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「壓阻讀出」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度。","checkEn":"Submit the Piezoresistive readout diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-07-k1","title":"壓阻讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Piezoresistive readout / Physics and model","text":"機制：電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity."},{"id":"a089-v8-07-k2","title":"壓阻讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Piezoresistive readout / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「壓阻讀出」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Piezoresistive readout, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度","任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號","無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險"],"optionsEn":["Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity","Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal","Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-07"],"title":"壓阻讀出：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Piezoresistive readout: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal.","instruction":"接續前一步「壓阻讀出」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：壓阻係數隨晶向與溫度變化。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Piezoresistive readout artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Piezoresistance depends on orientation and temperature. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度；壓阻係數隨晶向與溫度變化。","observationEn":"Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity; Piezoresistance depends on orientation and temperature.","failure":"若採用「任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「壓阻讀出」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「壓阻係數隨晶向與溫度變化」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Piezoresistive readout, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Piezoresistance depends on orientation and temperature\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-08-k1","title":"壓阻讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Piezoresistive readout / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：壓阻係數隨晶向與溫度變化。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Piezoresistance depends on orientation and temperature."},{"id":"a089-v8-08-k2","title":"壓阻讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Piezoresistive readout / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號」與「電橋位置與晶向影響靈敏度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal\" is not equivalent to \"Bridge placement and crystal orientation affect sensitivity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「壓阻讀出」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Piezoresistive readout?","options":["無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險","壓阻係數隨晶向與溫度變化","任意放四個相同電阻都得到相同訊號"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty","Piezoresistance depends on orientation and temperature","Assuming any four resistor placements give equal signal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"壓阻係數隨晶向與溫度變化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Piezoresistance depends on orientation and temperature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-08"],"title":"電容讀出：建立模型","titleEn":"Capacitive readout: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel.","instruction":"畫膜片和固定電極，分開位移及邊緣寄生電容。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設理想空氣平板電容 A=1 mm²、間隙 g=10 µm，C=ε0A/g=0.8854 pF；膜片位移使間隙變 9 µm，C≈0.9838 pF。電容增加約 11.11%，並非正好 10%。例中忽略邊緣場、膜片非均勻變形與靜電拉入，不能由此直接回推壓力。","instructionEn":"Draw moving/fixed electrodes and separate displacement from parasitics. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume an ideal air parallel-plate capacitor with A=1 mm² and gap g=10 µm: C=ε0A/g=0.8854 pF. Reducing the gap to 9 µm gives approximately 0.9838 pF, an 11.11% increase rather than exactly 10%. Fringing, nonuniform deflection and electrostatic pull-in are absent; capacitance alone does not give pressure.","observation":"小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程；拉入不穩定限制電容偏壓。","observationEn":"Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel; Pull-in instability limits capacitive bias.","failure":"若採用「無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電容讀出」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程。\n算例驗收：驗算兩個電容與 11.11% 變化，註明仍缺少壓力到位移的機械模型。","checkEn":"Submit the Capacitive readout diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both capacitances and the 11.11% change and identify the missing pressure-to-deflection model.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-09-k1","title":"電容讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capacitive readout / Physics and model","text":"機制：小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程。","textEn":"Mechanism: Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel."},{"id":"a089-v8-09-k2","title":"電容讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capacitive readout / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險」。\n假設數值與推算：假設理想空氣平板電容 A=1 mm²、間隙 g=10 µm，C=ε0A/g=0.8854 pF；膜片位移使間隙變 9 µm，C≈0.9838 pF。電容增加約 11.11%，並非正好 10%。例中忽略邊緣場、膜片非均勻變形與靜電拉入，不能由此直接回推壓力。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume an ideal air parallel-plate capacitor with A=1 mm² and gap g=10 µm: C=ε0A/g=0.8854 pF. Reducing the gap to 9 µm gives approximately 0.9838 pF, an 11.11% increase rather than exactly 10%. Fringing, nonuniform deflection and electrostatic pull-in are absent; capacitance alone does not give pressure."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電容讀出」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Capacitive readout, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險","蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚","小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty","Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms","Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel"],"answer":2,"explanation":"小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-09"],"title":"電容讀出：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Capacitive readout: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty.","instruction":"接續前一步「電容讀出」成果，先指出錯誤主張「無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：拉入不穩定限制電容偏壓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Capacitive readout artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pull-in instability limits capacitive bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程；拉入不穩定限制電容偏壓。","observationEn":"Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel; Pull-in instability limits capacitive bias.","failure":"若採用「無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電容讀出」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「拉入不穩定限制電容偏壓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Capacitive readout, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pull-in instability limits capacitive bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-10-k1","title":"電容讀出／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capacitive readout / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：拉入不穩定限制電容偏壓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pull-in instability limits capacitive bias."},{"id":"a089-v8-10-k2","title":"電容讀出／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capacitive readout / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險」與「小間隙提高靈敏度但限制行程」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty\" is not equivalent to \"Small gaps improve sensitivity but limit travel\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電容讀出」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Capacitive readout?","options":["拉入不穩定限制電容偏壓","無限縮小間隙且完全不改過壓風險","蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚"],"optionsEn":["Pull-in instability limits capacitive bias","Shrinking gaps indefinitely with no overload penalty","Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms"],"answer":0,"explanation":"拉入不穩定限制電容偏壓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pull-in instability limits capacitive bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-10"],"title":"背腔製作：建立模型","titleEn":"Back-cavity formation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity.","instruction":"在正背對位圖追蹤腔體、膜片與停止層。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Trace cavity, diaphragm and stop layer in front/back views. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度；正背對準誤差改變有效膜片面積。","observationEn":"Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity; Front/back misalignment changes diaphragm area.","failure":"若採用「蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「背腔製作」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度。","checkEn":"Submit the Back-cavity formation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-11-k1","title":"背腔製作／物理與模型","titleEn":"Back-cavity formation / Physics and model","text":"機制：殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity."},{"id":"a089-v8-11-k2","title":"背腔製作／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Back-cavity formation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「背腔製作」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Back-cavity formation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證","殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度","蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚"],"optionsEn":["Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever","Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity","Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms"],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-11"],"title":"背腔製作：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Back-cavity formation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms.","instruction":"接續前一步「背腔製作」成果，先指出錯誤主張「蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：正背對準誤差改變有效膜片面積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Back-cavity formation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Front/back misalignment changes diaphragm area. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度；正背對準誤差改變有效膜片面積。","observationEn":"Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity; Front/back misalignment changes diaphragm area.","failure":"若採用「蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「背腔製作」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「正背對準誤差改變有效膜片面積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Back-cavity formation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Front/back misalignment changes diaphragm area\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-12-k1","title":"背腔製作／物理與模型","titleEn":"Back-cavity formation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：正背對準誤差改變有效膜片面積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Front/back misalignment changes diaphragm area."},{"id":"a089-v8-12-k2","title":"背腔製作／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Back-cavity formation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚」與「殘餘膜厚需要可量測的停止與均勻度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms\" is not equivalent to \"Residual thickness requires controlled stopping and uniformity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「背腔製作」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Back-cavity formation?","options":["蝕刻時間相同便保證所有膜片同厚","密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證","正背對準誤差改變有效膜片面積"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal etch time guarantees equal diaphragms","Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever","Front/back misalignment changes diaphragm area"],"answer":2,"explanation":"正背對準誤差改變有效膜片面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Front/back misalignment changes diaphragm area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a089-stage03","order":3,"title":"參考腔 → 保護介質","titleEn":"Reference cavity to Protective media","description":"把「參考腔」「封裝應力」「保護介質」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Reference cavity, Package stress, Protective media.","steps":[{"id":"a089-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-12"],"title":"參考腔：建立模型","titleEn":"Reference cavity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature.","instruction":"畫真空參考腔、漏氣與殘氣，預測零點變化。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw vacuum reference, leak and residual gas and predict offset changes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動；殘氣溫度改變會移动零點。","observationEn":"Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature; Residual-gas temperature shifts offset.","failure":"若採用「密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「參考腔」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動。","checkEn":"Submit the Reference cavity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-13-k1","title":"參考腔／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reference cavity / Physics and model","text":"機制：密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動。","textEn":"Mechanism: Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature."},{"id":"a089-v8-13-k2","title":"參考腔／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reference cavity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「參考腔」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Reference cavity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動","密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證","裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏"],"optionsEn":["Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature","Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever","Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset"],"answer":0,"explanation":"密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-13"],"title":"參考腔：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Reference cavity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever.","instruction":"接續前一步「參考腔」成果，先指出錯誤主張「密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：殘氣溫度改變會移动零點。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Reference cavity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Residual-gas temperature shifts offset. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動；殘氣溫度改變會移动零點。","observationEn":"Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature; Residual-gas temperature shifts offset.","failure":"若採用「密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「參考腔」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「殘氣溫度改變會移动零點」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Reference cavity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Residual-gas temperature shifts offset\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-14-k1","title":"參考腔／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reference cavity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：殘氣溫度改變會移动零點。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Residual-gas temperature shifts offset."},{"id":"a089-v8-14-k2","title":"參考腔／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reference cavity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證」與「密封參考壓力可能隨時間與溫度變動」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever\" is not equivalent to \"Sealed reference pressure can change with time/temperature\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「參考腔」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Reference cavity?","options":["裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏","殘氣溫度改變會移动零點","密封後參考壓力永遠固定不需驗證"],"optionsEn":["Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset","Residual-gas temperature shifts offset","Assuming sealed reference remains constant forever"],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘氣溫度改變會移动零點；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Residual-gas temperature shifts offset. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-14"],"title":"封裝應力：建立模型","titleEn":"Package stress: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Package stress can mimic pressure.","instruction":"畫黏著與基板熱膨脹拉扯膜片的路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Trace adhesive/substrate thermal stress reaching the diaphragm. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號；黏著固化收縮也會產生應力。","observationEn":"Package stress can mimic pressure; Adhesive cure shrinkage creates stress.","failure":"若採用「裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「封裝應力」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號。","checkEn":"Submit the Package stress diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Package stress can mimic pressure.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-15-k1","title":"封裝應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Package stress / Physics and model","text":"機制：外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號。","textEn":"Mechanism: Package stress can mimic pressure."},{"id":"a089-v8-15-k2","title":"封裝應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Package stress / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「封裝應力」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Package stress, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏","防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測","外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號"],"optionsEn":["Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset","Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect","Package stress can mimic pressure"],"answer":2,"explanation":"外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Package stress can mimic pressure. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-15"],"title":"封裝應力：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Package stress: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset.","instruction":"接續前一步「封裝應力」成果，先指出錯誤主張「裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：黏著固化收縮也會產生應力。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Package stress artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Adhesive cure shrinkage creates stress. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號；黏著固化收縮也會產生應力。","observationEn":"Package stress can mimic pressure; Adhesive cure shrinkage creates stress.","failure":"若採用「裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「封裝應力」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「黏著固化收縮也會產生應力」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Package stress, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Adhesive cure shrinkage creates stress\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-16-k1","title":"封裝應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Package stress / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：黏著固化收縮也會產生應力。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Adhesive cure shrinkage creates stress."},{"id":"a089-v8-16-k2","title":"封裝應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Package stress / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏」與「外部封裝應力可模仿壓力訊號」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset\" is not equivalent to \"Package stress can mimic pressure\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「封裝應力」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Package stress?","options":["黏著固化收縮也會產生應力","裸晶零偏合格便保證封裝零偏","防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測"],"optionsEn":["Adhesive cure shrinkage creates stress","Inferring packaged offset from bare-die offset","Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect"],"answer":0,"explanation":"黏著固化收縮也會產生應力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Adhesive cure shrinkage creates stress. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-16"],"title":"保護介質：建立模型","titleEn":"Protective media: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「保護介質也改變壓力響應動態」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics.","instruction":"比較凝膠、氣孔與壓力傳遞路徑，列出延遲和相容性。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare gel, vent and pressure paths with delay/compatibility. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"保護介質也改變壓力響應動態；凝膠吸濕可能造成長期漂移。","observationEn":"Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics; Gel moisture uptake can cause long-term drift.","failure":"若採用「防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「保護介質」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：保護介質也改變壓力響應動態。","checkEn":"Submit the Protective media diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-17-k1","title":"保護介質／物理與模型","titleEn":"Protective media / Physics and model","text":"機制：保護介質也改變壓力響應動態。","textEn":"Mechanism: Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics."},{"id":"a089-v8-17-k2","title":"保護介質／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Protective media / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「保護介質」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Protective media, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍","保護介質也改變壓力響應動態","防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測"],"optionsEn":["Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range","Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics","Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護介質也改變壓力響應動態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-17"],"title":"保護介質：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Protective media: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect.","instruction":"接續前一步「保護介質」成果，先指出錯誤主張「防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：凝膠吸濕可能造成長期漂移。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Protective media artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Gel moisture uptake can cause long-term drift. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"保護介質也改變壓力響應動態；凝膠吸濕可能造成長期漂移。","observationEn":"Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics; Gel moisture uptake can cause long-term drift.","failure":"若採用「防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「保護介質」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「凝膠吸濕可能造成長期漂移」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Protective media, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Gel moisture uptake can cause long-term drift\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-18-k1","title":"保護介質／物理與模型","titleEn":"Protective media / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：凝膠吸濕可能造成長期漂移。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Gel moisture uptake can cause long-term drift."},{"id":"a089-v8-18-k2","title":"保護介質／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Protective media / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測」與「保護介質也改變壓力響應動態」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect\" is not equivalent to \"Protection media alter pressure-response dynamics\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「保護介質」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Protective media?","options":["防水只增加保護而完全不影響量測","破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍","凝膠吸濕可能造成長期漂移"],"optionsEn":["Assuming waterproofing has no measurement effect","Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range","Gel moisture uptake can cause long-term drift"],"answer":2,"explanation":"凝膠吸濕可能造成長期漂移；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Gel moisture uptake can cause long-term drift. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a089-stage04","order":4,"title":"過壓與量程 → 氣壓與高度","titleEn":"Overpressure and range to Pressure and altitude","description":"把「過壓與量程」「溫度補償」「氣壓與高度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Overpressure and range, Temperature compensation, Pressure and altitude.","steps":[{"id":"a089-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-18"],"title":"過壓與量程：建立模型","titleEn":"Overpressure and range: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Survival does not imply accurate measurement.","instruction":"分開額定量程、可恢復過壓與破裂壓力的假設圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate rated, recoverable overload and burst ranges. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確；循環過壓可能留永久零偏。","observationEn":"Survival does not imply accurate measurement; Repeated overload can leave permanent offset.","failure":"若採用「破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「過壓與量程」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確。","checkEn":"Submit the Overpressure and range diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Survival does not imply accurate measurement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-19-k1","title":"過壓與量程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Overpressure and range / Physics and model","text":"機制：結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確。","textEn":"Mechanism: Survival does not imply accurate measurement."},{"id":"a089-v8-19-k2","title":"過壓與量程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Overpressure and range / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「過壓與量程」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Overpressure and range, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確","破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍","用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證"],"optionsEn":["Survival does not imply accurate measurement","Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range","Replacing range validation with one temperature line"],"answer":0,"explanation":"結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Survival does not imply accurate measurement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-19"],"title":"過壓與量程：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Overpressure and range: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range.","instruction":"接續前一步「過壓與量程」成果，先指出錯誤主張「破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：循環過壓可能留永久零偏。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Overpressure and range artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Repeated overload can leave permanent offset. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確；循環過壓可能留永久零偏。","observationEn":"Survival does not imply accurate measurement; Repeated overload can leave permanent offset.","failure":"若採用「破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「過壓與量程」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「循環過壓可能留永久零偏」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Overpressure and range, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Repeated overload can leave permanent offset\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-20-k1","title":"過壓與量程／物理與模型","titleEn":"Overpressure and range / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：循環過壓可能留永久零偏。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Repeated overload can leave permanent offset."},{"id":"a089-v8-20-k2","title":"過壓與量程／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Overpressure and range / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍」與「結構不破裂不等於讀值仍精確」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range\" is not equivalent to \"Survival does not imply accurate measurement\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「過壓與量程」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Overpressure and range?","options":["用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證","循環過壓可能留永久零偏","破裂壓力以内都當成線性量測範圍"],"optionsEn":["Replacing range validation with one temperature line","Repeated overload can leave permanent offset","Treating all sub-burst pressure as a linear range"],"answer":1,"explanation":"循環過壓可能留永久零偏；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Repeated overload can leave permanent offset. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-20"],"title":"溫度補償：建立模型","titleEn":"Temperature compensation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Single-temperature calibration misses interactions.","instruction":"用假設壓力溫度網格分離零點及靈敏度漂移。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate offset and sensitivity drift on a pressure-temperature grid. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用；校正網格密度影響插值誤差。","observationEn":"Single-temperature calibration misses interactions; Calibration-grid density affects interpolation error.","failure":"若採用「用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing range validation with one temperature line\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「溫度補償」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用。","checkEn":"Submit the Temperature compensation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Single-temperature calibration misses interactions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-21-k1","title":"溫度補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Physics and model","text":"機制：單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用。","textEn":"Mechanism: Single-temperature calibration misses interactions."},{"id":"a089-v8-21-k2","title":"溫度補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Replacing range validation with one temperature line."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度補償」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Temperature compensation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證","感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考","單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用"],"optionsEn":["Replacing range validation with one temperature line","Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs","Single-temperature calibration misses interactions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Single-temperature calibration misses interactions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-21"],"title":"溫度補償：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Temperature compensation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Replacing range validation with one temperature line.","instruction":"接續前一步「溫度補償」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：校正網格密度影響插值誤差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Temperature compensation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Replacing range validation with one temperature line\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Calibration-grid density affects interpolation error. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用；校正網格密度影響插值誤差。","observationEn":"Single-temperature calibration misses interactions; Calibration-grid density affects interpolation error.","failure":"若採用「用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing range validation with one temperature line\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「溫度補償」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「校正網格密度影響插值誤差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Temperature compensation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Calibration-grid density affects interpolation error\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-22-k1","title":"溫度補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：校正網格密度影響插值誤差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Calibration-grid density affects interpolation error."},{"id":"a089-v8-22-k2","title":"溫度補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temperature compensation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證」與「單一溫度校正不足以涵蓋交互作用」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Replacing range validation with one temperature line\" is not equivalent to \"Single-temperature calibration misses interactions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「溫度補償」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Temperature compensation?","options":["校正網格密度影響插值誤差","用一條溫度直線取代整個壓力範圍驗證","感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考"],"optionsEn":["Calibration-grid density affects interpolation error","Replacing range validation with one temperature line","Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs"],"answer":0,"explanation":"校正網格密度影響插值誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Calibration-grid density affects interpolation error. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-22"],"title":"氣壓與高度：建立模型","titleEn":"Pressure and altitude: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude.","instruction":"將同一壓力用兩種參考天氣條件換算高度並比較。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Convert equal pressure under two reference-weather assumptions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度；溫度及濕度也影響大氣高度換算。","observationEn":"Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude; Temperature and humidity affect altitude conversion.","failure":"若採用「感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「氣壓與高度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度。","checkEn":"Submit the Pressure and altitude diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-23-k1","title":"氣壓與高度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pressure and altitude / Physics and model","text":"機制：氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude."},{"id":"a089-v8-23-k2","title":"氣壓與高度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pressure and altitude / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氣壓與高度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pressure and altitude, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力","氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度","感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考"],"optionsEn":["Comparing all pressures without reference definitions","Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude","Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a089-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-pressure","v8-c-pressure-package","v8-c-mems"],"prerequisiteIds":["a089-v8-23"],"title":"氣壓與高度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pressure and altitude: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs.","instruction":"接續前一步「氣壓與高度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：溫度及濕度也影響大氣高度換算。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pressure and altitude artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Temperature and humidity affect altitude conversion. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度；溫度及濕度也影響大氣高度換算。","observationEn":"Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude; Temperature and humidity affect altitude conversion.","failure":"若採用「感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「氣壓與高度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「溫度及濕度也影響大氣高度換算」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pressure and altitude, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Temperature and humidity affect altitude conversion\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a089-v8-24-k1","title":"氣壓與高度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pressure and altitude / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：溫度及濕度也影響大氣高度換算。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Temperature and humidity affect altitude conversion."},{"id":"a089-v8-24-k2","title":"氣壓與高度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pressure and altitude / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考」與「氣壓高度不是無條件的幾何高度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs\" is not equivalent to \"Barometric altitude is not unconditional geometric altitude\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「氣壓與高度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pressure and altitude?","options":["感測器精準便代表不需天氣參考","沒有參考側也可直接比較所有壓力","溫度及濕度也影響大氣高度換算"],"optionsEn":["Assuming sensor precision removes weather-reference needs","Comparing all pressures without reference definitions","Temperature and humidity affect altitude conversion"],"answer":2,"explanation":"溫度及濕度也影響大氣高度換算；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Temperature and humidity affect altitude conversion. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"mems","subcategoryTitle":"微機電與顯示","subcategoryTitleEn":"MEMS and displays"},{"id":"a090","title":"薄膜電晶體顯示背板","titleEn":"Thin-film-transistor display backplanes","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films","v8-c-imec-place","v8-c-nanoic-open","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從像素開關、閘介面到面板驗收：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Pixel switching and Gate interface to Panel acceptance: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["像素開關","IGZO 化學","接觸與通道","偏壓照光應力"],"labelsEn":["Pixel switching","IGZO chemistry","Contacts and channel","Bias-illumination stress"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a090-stage01","order":1,"title":"像素開關 → 玻璃熱預算","titleEn":"Pixel switching to Glass thermal budget","description":"把「像素開關」「材料選擇」「玻璃熱預算」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pixel switching, Channel selection, Glass thermal budget.","steps":[{"id":"a090-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"像素開關：建立模型","titleEn":"Pixel switching: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「背板控制與發光材料是不同功能」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Backplane control and light emission are different functions.","instruction":"畫 TFT、儲存電容和顯示負載，追蹤一列更新。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw TFT, storage capacitor and display load and trace row updating. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"背板控制與發光材料是不同功能；像素保持需要低關斷漏電。","observationEn":"Backplane control and light emission are different functions; Pixel hold requires low off-state leakage.","failure":"若採用「把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「像素開關」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：背板控制與發光材料是不同功能。","checkEn":"Submit the Pixel switching diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Backplane control and light emission are different functions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-01-k1","title":"像素開關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel switching / Physics and model","text":"機制：背板控制與發光材料是不同功能。","textEn":"Mechanism: Backplane control and light emission are different functions."},{"id":"a090-v8-01-k2","title":"像素開關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel switching / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「像素開關」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pixel switching, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["背板控制與發光材料是不同功能","把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層","只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途"],"optionsEn":["Backplane control and light emission are different functions","Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer","Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility"],"answer":0,"explanation":"背板控制與發光材料是不同功能；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Backplane control and light emission are different functions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-01"],"title":"像素開關：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pixel switching: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer.","instruction":"接續前一步「像素開關」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：像素保持需要低關斷漏電。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pixel switching artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pixel hold requires low off-state leakage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"背板控制與發光材料是不同功能；像素保持需要低關斷漏電。","observationEn":"Backplane control and light emission are different functions; Pixel hold requires low off-state leakage.","failure":"若採用「把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「像素開關」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「像素保持需要低關斷漏電」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pixel switching, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pixel hold requires low off-state leakage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-02-k1","title":"像素開關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel switching / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：像素保持需要低關斷漏電。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pixel hold requires low off-state leakage."},{"id":"a090-v8-02-k2","title":"像素開關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel switching / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層」與「背板控制與發光材料是不同功能」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer\" is not equivalent to \"Backplane control and light emission are different functions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「像素開關」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pixel switching?","options":["只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途","像素保持需要低關斷漏電","把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層"],"optionsEn":["Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility","Pixel hold requires low off-state leakage","Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"像素保持需要低關斷漏電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pixel hold requires low off-state leakage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-02"],"title":"材料選擇：建立模型","titleEn":"Channel selection: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高遷移率只是背板需求之一」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Mobility is only one backplane requirement.","instruction":"比較 a-Si、LTPS、IGZO 的均勻度、遷移率與製程要求。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare uniformity, mobility and process needs for a-Si/LTPS/IGZO. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高遷移率只是背板需求之一；載子遷移率抽取需相同模型。","observationEn":"Mobility is only one backplane requirement; Mobility comparison needs consistent extraction models.","failure":"若採用「只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「材料選擇」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高遷移率只是背板需求之一。","checkEn":"Submit the Channel selection diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Mobility is only one backplane requirement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-03-k1","title":"材料選擇／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel selection / Physics and model","text":"機制：高遷移率只是背板需求之一。","textEn":"Mechanism: Mobility is only one backplane requirement."},{"id":"a090-v8-03-k2","title":"材料選擇／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel selection / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「材料選擇」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Channel selection, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途","套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃","高遷移率只是背板需求之一"],"optionsEn":["Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility","Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass","Mobility is only one backplane requirement"],"answer":2,"explanation":"高遷移率只是背板需求之一；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mobility is only one backplane requirement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-03"],"title":"材料選擇：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Channel selection: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility.","instruction":"接續前一步「材料選擇」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：載子遷移率抽取需相同模型。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Channel selection artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mobility comparison needs consistent extraction models. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高遷移率只是背板需求之一；載子遷移率抽取需相同模型。","observationEn":"Mobility is only one backplane requirement; Mobility comparison needs consistent extraction models.","failure":"若採用「只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「材料選擇」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「載子遷移率抽取需相同模型」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Channel selection, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mobility comparison needs consistent extraction models\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-04-k1","title":"材料選擇／物理與模型","titleEn":"Channel selection / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：載子遷移率抽取需相同模型。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mobility comparison needs consistent extraction models."},{"id":"a090-v8-04-k2","title":"材料選擇／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Channel selection / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途」與「高遷移率只是背板需求之一」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility\" is not equivalent to \"Mobility is only one backplane requirement\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「材料選擇」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Channel selection?","options":["載子遷移率抽取需相同模型","只按最高遷移率決定所有顯示用途","套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Mobility comparison needs consistent extraction models","Choosing all display uses by maximum mobility","Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"載子遷移率抽取需相同模型；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mobility comparison needs consistent extraction models. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-04"],"title":"玻璃熱預算：建立模型","titleEn":"Glass thermal budget: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「基板限制會改變可用製程」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Substrate constraints change feasible processing.","instruction":"把玻璃、薄膜與後續封裝的可接受熱條件列成表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"List compatible thermal conditions for glass, films and later integration. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"基板限制會改變可用製程；玻璃翹曲會影響圖形對準。","observationEn":"Substrate constraints change feasible processing; Glass bow affects pattern alignment.","failure":"若採用「套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「玻璃熱預算」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：基板限制會改變可用製程。","checkEn":"Submit the Glass thermal budget diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Substrate constraints change feasible processing.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-05-k1","title":"玻璃熱預算／物理與模型","titleEn":"Glass thermal budget / Physics and model","text":"機制：基板限制會改變可用製程。","textEn":"Mechanism: Substrate constraints change feasible processing."},{"id":"a090-v8-05-k2","title":"玻璃熱預算／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Glass thermal budget / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「玻璃熱預算」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Glass thermal budget, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好","基板限制會改變可用製程","套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs","Substrate constraints change feasible processing","Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass"],"answer":1,"explanation":"基板限制會改變可用製程；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Substrate constraints change feasible processing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-05"],"title":"玻璃熱預算：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Glass thermal budget: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass.","instruction":"接續前一步「玻璃熱預算」成果，先指出錯誤主張「套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：玻璃翹曲會影響圖形對準。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Glass thermal budget artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Glass bow affects pattern alignment. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"基板限制會改變可用製程；玻璃翹曲會影響圖形對準。","observationEn":"Substrate constraints change feasible processing; Glass bow affects pattern alignment.","failure":"若採用「套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「玻璃熱預算」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「玻璃翹曲會影響圖形對準」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Glass thermal budget, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Glass bow affects pattern alignment\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-06-k1","title":"玻璃熱預算／物理與模型","titleEn":"Glass thermal budget / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：玻璃翹曲會影響圖形對準。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Glass bow affects pattern alignment."},{"id":"a090-v8-06-k2","title":"玻璃熱預算／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Glass thermal budget / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃」與「基板限制會改變可用製程」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass\" is not equivalent to \"Substrate constraints change feasible processing\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「玻璃熱預算」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Glass thermal budget?","options":["套用矽晶圓高溫流程而不查玻璃","通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好","玻璃翹曲會影響圖形對準"],"optionsEn":["Applying silicon-wafer heating without checking glass","Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs","Glass bow affects pattern alignment"],"answer":2,"explanation":"玻璃翹曲會影響圖形對準；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Glass bow affects pattern alignment. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a090-stage02","order":2,"title":"IGZO 化學 → 氫與鈍化","titleEn":"IGZO chemistry to Hydrogen and passivation","description":"把「IGZO 化學」「閘介面」「氫與鈍化」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for IGZO chemistry, Gate interface, Hydrogen and passivation.","steps":[{"id":"a090-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-06"],"title":"IGZO 化學：建立模型","titleEn":"IGZO chemistry: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything.","instruction":"畫氧相關缺陷和載流子，分開導通與關斷需求。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw oxygen-related defects/carriers and separate on/off needs. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善；氧含量變動也會改變穩定性。","observationEn":"Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything; Oxygen variation also changes stability.","failure":"若採用「通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「IGZO 化學」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善。","checkEn":"Submit the IGZO chemistry diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-07-k1","title":"IGZO 化學／物理與模型","titleEn":"IGZO chemistry / Physics and model","text":"機制：載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善。","textEn":"Mechanism: Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything."},{"id":"a090-v8-07-k2","title":"IGZO 化學／驗證與限制","titleEn":"IGZO chemistry / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「IGZO 化學」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For IGZO chemistry, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善","通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好","只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質"],"optionsEn":["Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything","Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs","Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-07"],"title":"IGZO 化學：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"IGZO chemistry: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs.","instruction":"接續前一步「IGZO 化學」成果，先指出錯誤主張「通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：氧含量變動也會改變穩定性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding IGZO chemistry artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Oxygen variation also changes stability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善；氧含量變動也會改變穩定性。","observationEn":"Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything; Oxygen variation also changes stability.","failure":"若採用「通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「IGZO 化學」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「氧含量變動也會改變穩定性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for IGZO chemistry, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Oxygen variation also changes stability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-08-k1","title":"IGZO 化學／物理與模型","titleEn":"IGZO chemistry / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：氧含量變動也會改變穩定性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Oxygen variation also changes stability."},{"id":"a090-v8-08-k2","title":"IGZO 化學／驗證與限制","titleEn":"IGZO chemistry / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好」與「載子過多可能提高漏電而非全面改善」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs\" is not equivalent to \"Excess carriers can increase leakage rather than improve everything\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「IGZO 化學」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of IGZO chemistry?","options":["只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質","氧含量變動也會改變穩定性","通道越導電就代表 TFT 越好"],"optionsEn":["Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone","Oxygen variation also changes stability","Assuming more conductive channels always make better TFTs"],"answer":1,"explanation":"氧含量變動也會改變穩定性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Oxygen variation also changes stability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-08"],"title":"閘介面：建立模型","titleEn":"Gate interface: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Interface quality affects switching and stability.","instruction":"畫閘介電層陷阱及通道，預測次臨界斜率與遲滯。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw dielectric traps/channel and predict subthreshold/hysteresis effects. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定；介面電容需和有效閘電容區分。","observationEn":"Interface quality affects switching and stability; Distinguish interface response from effective gate capacitance.","failure":"若採用「只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閘介面」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定。","checkEn":"Submit the Gate interface diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Interface quality affects switching and stability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-09-k1","title":"閘介面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate interface / Physics and model","text":"機制：介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Interface quality affects switching and stability."},{"id":"a090-v8-09-k2","title":"閘介面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate interface / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閘介面」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Gate interface, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質","任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益","介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定"],"optionsEn":["Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone","Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial","Interface quality affects switching and stability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Interface quality affects switching and stability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-09"],"title":"閘介面：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Gate interface: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「閘介面」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：介面電容需和有效閘電容區分。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Gate interface artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Distinguish interface response from effective gate capacitance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定；介面電容需和有效閘電容區分。","observationEn":"Interface quality affects switching and stability; Distinguish interface response from effective gate capacitance.","failure":"若採用「只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閘介面」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「介面電容需和有效閘電容區分」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Gate interface, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Distinguish interface response from effective gate capacitance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-10-k1","title":"閘介面／物理與模型","titleEn":"Gate interface / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：介面電容需和有效閘電容區分。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Distinguish interface response from effective gate capacitance."},{"id":"a090-v8-10-k2","title":"閘介面／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Gate interface / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質」與「介面品質影響開關陡峭度與穩定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone\" is not equivalent to \"Interface quality affects switching and stability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閘介面」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Gate interface?","options":["介面電容需和有效閘電容區分","只測膜厚就證明閘介面品質","任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益"],"optionsEn":["Distinguish interface response from effective gate capacitance","Proving gate-interface quality from thickness alone","Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial"],"answer":0,"explanation":"介面電容需和有效閘電容區分；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Distinguish interface response from effective gate capacitance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-10"],"title":"氫與鈍化：建立模型","titleEn":"Hydrogen and passivation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function.","instruction":"比較有無阻隔層的氫擴散路徑與電性漂移。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hydrogen paths and drift with/without barriers. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估；沉積電漿也可能傷害通道。","observationEn":"Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function; Deposition plasma can damage channels.","failure":"若採用「任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「氫與鈍化」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估。","checkEn":"Submit the Hydrogen and passivation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-11-k1","title":"氫與鈍化／物理與模型","titleEn":"Hydrogen and passivation / Physics and model","text":"機制：保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估。","textEn":"Mechanism: Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function."},{"id":"a090-v8-11-k2","title":"氫與鈍化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Hydrogen and passivation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「氫與鈍化」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Hydrogen and passivation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["全部低電流都歸為遷移率差","保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估","任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益"],"optionsEn":["Attributing all low current to poor mobility","Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function","Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-11"],"title":"氫與鈍化：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrogen and passivation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial.","instruction":"接續前一步「氫與鈍化」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：沉積電漿也可能傷害通道。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Hydrogen and passivation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Deposition plasma can damage channels. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估；沉積電漿也可能傷害通道。","observationEn":"Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function; Deposition plasma can damage channels.","failure":"若採用「任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「氫與鈍化」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「沉積電漿也可能傷害通道」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Hydrogen and passivation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Deposition plasma can damage channels\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-12-k1","title":"氫與鈍化／物理與模型","titleEn":"Hydrogen and passivation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：沉積電漿也可能傷害通道。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Deposition plasma can damage channels."},{"id":"a090-v8-12-k2","title":"氫與鈍化／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Hydrogen and passivation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益」與「保護薄膜的化學影響需和阻隔功能一起評估」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial\" is not equivalent to \"Passivation chemistry must be assessed with barrier function\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「氫與鈍化」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Hydrogen and passivation?","options":["任何含氫鈍化都無條件有益","全部低電流都歸為遷移率差","沉積電漿也可能傷害通道"],"optionsEn":["Assuming hydrogen-containing passivation is always beneficial","Attributing all low current to poor mobility","Deposition plasma can damage channels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"沉積電漿也可能傷害通道；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Deposition plasma can damage channels. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a090-stage03","order":3,"title":"接觸與通道 → 保持與漏電","titleEn":"Contacts and channel to Hold and leakage","description":"把「接觸與通道」「大面積均勻」「保持與漏電」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Contacts and channel, Large-area uniformity, Hold and leakage.","steps":[{"id":"a090-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-12"],"title":"接觸與通道：建立模型","titleEn":"Contacts and channel: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited.","instruction":"以不同長度 TFT 假設 I-V 分離接觸限制。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Use hypothetical TFT length-series I-V to isolate contacts. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導；接觸影響會扭曲表觀遷移率。","observationEn":"Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited; Contact effects distort apparent mobility.","failure":"若採用「全部低電流都歸為遷移率差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all low current to poor mobility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸與通道」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導。","checkEn":"Submit the Contacts and channel diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-13-k1","title":"接觸與通道／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contacts and channel / Physics and model","text":"機制：低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導。","textEn":"Mechanism: Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited."},{"id":"a090-v8-13-k2","title":"接觸與通道／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and channel / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「全部低電流都歸為遷移率差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing all low current to poor mobility."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸與通道」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Contacts and channel, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導","全部低電流都歸為遷移率差","只測小試片便核准整張玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited","Attributing all low current to poor mobility","Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon"],"answer":0,"explanation":"低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-13"],"title":"接觸與通道：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Contacts and channel: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「全部低電流都歸為遷移率差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing all low current to poor mobility.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸與通道」成果，先指出錯誤主張「全部低電流都歸為遷移率差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸影響會扭曲表觀遷移率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Contacts and channel artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing all low current to poor mobility\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Contact effects distort apparent mobility. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導；接觸影響會扭曲表觀遷移率。","observationEn":"Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited; Contact effects distort apparent mobility.","failure":"若採用「全部低電流都歸為遷移率差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing all low current to poor mobility\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸與通道」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸影響會扭曲表觀遷移率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Contacts and channel, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Contact effects distort apparent mobility\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-14-k1","title":"接觸與通道／物理與模型","titleEn":"Contacts and channel / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸影響會扭曲表觀遷移率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Contact effects distort apparent mobility."},{"id":"a090-v8-14-k2","title":"接觸與通道／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Contacts and channel / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「全部低電流都歸為遷移率差」與「低通道電阻仍可能被接觸主導」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing all low current to poor mobility\" is not equivalent to \"Low channel resistance can remain contact-limited\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸與通道」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Contacts and channel?","options":["只測小試片便核准整張玻璃","接觸影響會扭曲表觀遷移率","全部低電流都歸為遷移率差"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon","Contact effects distort apparent mobility","Attributing all low current to poor mobility"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸影響會扭曲表觀遷移率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact effects distort apparent mobility. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-14"],"title":"大面積均勻：建立模型","titleEn":"Large-area uniformity: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity.","instruction":"畫面板中心到邊緣的膜厚及 Vth 地圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map thickness and threshold from panel center to edge. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻；大面積熱分布會改變膜性質。","observationEn":"Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity; Panel-scale temperature profiles change film properties.","failure":"若採用「只測小試片便核准整張玻璃」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「大面積均勻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻。","checkEn":"Submit the Large-area uniformity diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-15-k1","title":"大面積均勻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Large-area uniformity / Physics and model","text":"機制：晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity."},{"id":"a090-v8-15-k2","title":"大面積均勻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Large-area uniformity / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只測小試片便核准整張玻璃」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「大面積均勻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Large-area uniformity, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只測小試片便核准整張玻璃","刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電","晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon","Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh","Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity"],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-15"],"title":"大面積均勻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Large-area uniformity: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只測小試片便核准整張玻璃」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon.","instruction":"接續前一步「大面積均勻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只測小試片便核准整張玻璃」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：大面積熱分布會改變膜性質。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Large-area uniformity artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Panel-scale temperature profiles change film properties. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻；大面積熱分布會改變膜性質。","observationEn":"Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity; Panel-scale temperature profiles change film properties.","failure":"若採用「只測小試片便核准整張玻璃」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「大面積均勻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「大面積熱分布會改變膜性質」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Large-area uniformity, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Panel-scale temperature profiles change film properties\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-16-k1","title":"大面積均勻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Large-area uniformity / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：大面積熱分布會改變膜性質。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Panel-scale temperature profiles change film properties."},{"id":"a090-v8-16-k2","title":"大面積均勻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Large-area uniformity / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只測小試片便核准整張玻璃」與「晶圓級均勻度不自動等於玻璃大面積均勻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon\" is not equivalent to \"Wafer uniformity does not imply panel-scale uniformity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「大面積均勻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Large-area uniformity?","options":["大面積熱分布會改變膜性質","只測小試片便核准整張玻璃","刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電"],"optionsEn":["Panel-scale temperature profiles change film properties","Qualifying a whole panel from a small coupon","Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh"],"answer":0,"explanation":"大面積熱分布會改變膜性質；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Panel-scale temperature profiles change film properties. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-16"],"title":"保持與漏電：建立模型","titleEn":"Hold and leakage: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低刷新率會放大保持需求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Low refresh rates increase hold requirements.","instruction":"用假設電容和漏電估算一幀內的像素電壓下降。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設顯示像素保持電容 1 pF、固定漏電 1 pA、保持時間 16 ms，電壓衰減幅度 ΔV=IΔt/C=0.016 V=16 mV。漏電加倍則為 32 mV。這只是假設定值漏電的儲存節點模型，不是 IGZO 面板規格；光照、偏壓應力與寄生耦合另需驗證。","instructionEn":"Estimate pixel voltage loss over a frame from hypothetical capacitance/leakage. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a display-pixel storage capacitance of 1 pF, constant leakage of 1 pA and hold time of 16 ms. Voltage-loss magnitude ΔV=IΔt/C=0.016 V=16 mV; doubling leakage gives 32 mV. This constant-leakage model is not an IGZO-panel specification; illumination, bias stress and parasitic coupling need separate evaluation.","observation":"低刷新率會放大保持需求；儲存電容也占用像素面積。","observationEn":"Low refresh rates increase hold requirements; Storage capacitors consume pixel area.","failure":"若採用「刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「保持與漏電」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低刷新率會放大保持需求。\n算例驗收：驗算 16 mV 並保留 ms 到 s 的轉換；說明若漏電隨時間變化需以積分取代常數乘法。","checkEn":"Submit the Hold and leakage diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Low refresh rates increase hold requirements.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 16 mV and the millisecond-to-second conversion; explain that time-varying leakage requires integration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-17-k1","title":"保持與漏電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Hold and leakage / Physics and model","text":"機制：低刷新率會放大保持需求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Low refresh rates increase hold requirements."},{"id":"a090-v8-17-k2","title":"保持與漏電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Hold and leakage / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電」。\n假設數值與推算：假設顯示像素保持電容 1 pF、固定漏電 1 pA、保持時間 16 ms，電壓衰減幅度 ΔV=IΔt/C=0.016 V=16 mV。漏電加倍則為 32 mV。這只是假設定值漏電的儲存節點模型，不是 IGZO 面板規格；光照、偏壓應力與寄生耦合另需驗證。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a display-pixel storage capacitance of 1 pF, constant leakage of 1 pA and hold time of 16 ms. Voltage-loss magnitude ΔV=IΔt/C=0.016 V=16 mV; doubling leakage gives 32 mV. This constant-leakage model is not an IGZO-panel specification; illumination, bias stress and parasitic coupling need separate evaluation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「保持與漏電」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Hold and leakage, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過","低刷新率會放大保持需求","刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電"],"optionsEn":["Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success","Low refresh rates increase hold requirements","Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh"],"answer":1,"explanation":"低刷新率會放大保持需求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low refresh rates increase hold requirements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-17"],"title":"保持與漏電：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Hold and leakage: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh.","instruction":"接續前一步「保持與漏電」成果，先指出錯誤主張「刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：儲存電容也占用像素面積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Hold and leakage artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Storage capacitors consume pixel area. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低刷新率會放大保持需求；儲存電容也占用像素面積。","observationEn":"Low refresh rates increase hold requirements; Storage capacitors consume pixel area.","failure":"若採用「刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「保持與漏電」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「儲存電容也占用像素面積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Hold and leakage, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Storage capacitors consume pixel area\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-18-k1","title":"保持與漏電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Hold and leakage / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：儲存電容也占用像素面積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Storage capacitors consume pixel area."},{"id":"a090-v8-18-k2","title":"保持與漏電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Hold and leakage / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電」與「低刷新率會放大保持需求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh\" is not equivalent to \"Low refresh rates increase hold requirements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「保持與漏電」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Hold and leakage?","options":["刷新變慢便可忽略關斷漏電","單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過","儲存電容也占用像素面積"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring off leakage at slower refresh","Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success","Storage capacitors consume pixel area"],"answer":2,"explanation":"儲存電容也占用像素面積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Storage capacitors consume pixel area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a090-stage04","order":4,"title":"偏壓照光應力 → 面板驗收","titleEn":"Bias-illumination stress to Panel acceptance","description":"把「偏壓照光應力」「驅動補償」「面板驗收」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Bias-illumination stress, Drive compensation, Panel acceptance.","steps":[{"id":"a090-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-18"],"title":"偏壓照光應力：建立模型","titleEn":"Bias-illumination stress: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光與偏壓可能存在交互效應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Illumination and bias can interact.","instruction":"設計暗處偏壓、照光無偏壓與照光偏壓三個對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Design dark-bias, light-only and light-bias controls. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"光與偏壓可能存在交互效應；應力後等待時間影響觀察漂移。","observationEn":"Illumination and bias can interact; Post-stress delay affects observed drift.","failure":"若採用「單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「偏壓照光應力」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光與偏壓可能存在交互效應。","checkEn":"Submit the Bias-illumination stress diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Illumination and bias can interact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-19-k1","title":"偏壓照光應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bias-illumination stress / Physics and model","text":"機制：光與偏壓可能存在交互效應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Illumination and bias can interact."},{"id":"a090-v8-19-k2","title":"偏壓照光應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bias-illumination stress / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偏壓照光應力」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Bias-illumination stress, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["光與偏壓可能存在交互效應","單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過","軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效"],"optionsEn":["Illumination and bias can interact","Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success","Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"光與偏壓可能存在交互效應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Illumination and bias can interact. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-19"],"title":"偏壓照光應力：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Bias-illumination stress: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success.","instruction":"接續前一步「偏壓照光應力」成果，先指出錯誤主張「單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：應力後等待時間影響觀察漂移。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Bias-illumination stress artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Post-stress delay affects observed drift. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光與偏壓可能存在交互效應；應力後等待時間影響觀察漂移。","observationEn":"Illumination and bias can interact; Post-stress delay affects observed drift.","failure":"若採用「單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「偏壓照光應力」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「應力後等待時間影響觀察漂移」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Bias-illumination stress, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Post-stress delay affects observed drift\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-20-k1","title":"偏壓照光應力／物理與模型","titleEn":"Bias-illumination stress / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：應力後等待時間影響觀察漂移。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Post-stress delay affects observed drift."},{"id":"a090-v8-20-k2","title":"偏壓照光應力／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Bias-illumination stress / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過」與「光與偏壓可能存在交互效應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success\" is not equivalent to \"Illumination and bias can interact\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「偏壓照光應力」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Bias-illumination stress?","options":["軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效","應力後等待時間影響觀察漂移","單獨通過兩項測試即保證同時通過"],"optionsEn":["Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure","Post-stress delay affects observed drift","Assuming separate passes guarantee combined-stress success"],"answer":1,"explanation":"應力後等待時間影響觀察漂移；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Post-stress delay affects observed drift. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-20"],"title":"驅動補償：建立模型","titleEn":"Drive compensation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Compensation costs circuitry, time or area.","instruction":"畫感測 Vth 的像素電路與補償後殘差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw a threshold-sensing pixel circuit and residual error. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本；補償讀取本身需要穩定參考。","observationEn":"Compensation costs circuitry, time or area; Compensation sensing needs stable references.","failure":"若採用「軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「驅動補償」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本。","checkEn":"Submit the Drive compensation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Compensation costs circuitry, time or area.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-21-k1","title":"驅動補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Drive compensation / Physics and model","text":"機制：補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本。","textEn":"Mechanism: Compensation costs circuitry, time or area."},{"id":"a090-v8-21-k2","title":"驅動補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Drive compensation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「驅動補償」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Drive compensation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效","只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質","補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本"],"optionsEn":["Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure","Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph","Compensation costs circuitry, time or area"],"answer":2,"explanation":"補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Compensation costs circuitry, time or area. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-21"],"title":"驅動補償：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Drive compensation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure.","instruction":"接續前一步「驅動補償」成果，先指出錯誤主張「軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：補償讀取本身需要穩定參考。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Drive compensation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Compensation sensing needs stable references. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本；補償讀取本身需要穩定參考。","observationEn":"Compensation costs circuitry, time or area; Compensation sensing needs stable references.","failure":"若採用「軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「驅動補償」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「補償讀取本身需要穩定參考」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Drive compensation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Compensation sensing needs stable references\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-22-k1","title":"驅動補償／物理與模型","titleEn":"Drive compensation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：補償讀取本身需要穩定參考。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Compensation sensing needs stable references."},{"id":"a090-v8-22-k2","title":"驅動補償／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Drive compensation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效」與「補償需付出電路、時間或面積成本」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure\" is not equivalent to \"Compensation costs circuitry, time or area\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「驅動補償」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Drive compensation?","options":["補償讀取本身需要穩定參考","軟體補償可完全消除任何硬體失效","只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質"],"optionsEn":["Compensation sensing needs stable references","Assuming software compensation removes every hardware failure","Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph"],"answer":0,"explanation":"補償讀取本身需要穩定參考；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Compensation sensing needs stable references. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-22"],"title":"面板驗收：建立模型","titleEn":"Panel acceptance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Panel quality requires device and optical evidence.","instruction":"結合電性地圖、亮度不均、死點及長期漂移。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Combine electrical maps, luminance nonuniformity, dead pixels and aging. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證；亮度判斷應固定視角與光學條件。","observationEn":"Panel quality requires device and optical evidence; Luminance assessment needs fixed viewing conditions.","failure":"若採用「只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「面板驗收」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證。","checkEn":"Submit the Panel acceptance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Panel quality requires device and optical evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-23-k1","title":"面板驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Panel acceptance / Physics and model","text":"機制：面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證。","textEn":"Mechanism: Panel quality requires device and optical evidence."},{"id":"a090-v8-23-k2","title":"面板驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Panel acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「面板驗收」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Panel acceptance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層","面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證","只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質"],"optionsEn":["Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer","Panel quality requires device and optical evidence","Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph"],"answer":1,"explanation":"面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Panel quality requires device and optical evidence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a090-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-igzo","v8-c-tft-films"],"prerequisiteIds":["a090-v8-23"],"title":"面板驗收：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Panel acceptance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph.","instruction":"接續前一步「面板驗收」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：亮度判斷應固定視角與光學條件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Panel acceptance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Luminance assessment needs fixed viewing conditions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證；亮度判斷應固定視角與光學條件。","observationEn":"Panel quality requires device and optical evidence; Luminance assessment needs fixed viewing conditions.","failure":"若採用「只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「面板驗收」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「亮度判斷應固定視角與光學條件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Panel acceptance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Luminance assessment needs fixed viewing conditions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a090-v8-24-k1","title":"面板驗收／物理與模型","titleEn":"Panel acceptance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：亮度判斷應固定視角與光學條件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Luminance assessment needs fixed viewing conditions."},{"id":"a090-v8-24-k2","title":"面板驗收／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Panel acceptance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質」與「面板品質需要元件和光學共同驗證」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph\" is not equivalent to \"Panel quality requires device and optical evidence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「面板驗收」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Panel acceptance?","options":["只看最亮區域照片代表整板品質","把 TFT 通道直接當成發光層","亮度判斷應固定視角與光學條件"],"optionsEn":["Representing panel quality by its brightest photograph","Treating the TFT channel as the emitting layer","Luminance assessment needs fixed viewing conditions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"亮度判斷應固定視角與光學條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Luminance assessment needs fixed viewing conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"mems","subcategoryTitle":"微機電與顯示","subcategoryTitleEn":"MEMS and displays"},{"id":"a091","title":"晶圓臨界尺寸電子顯微量測","titleEn":"Wafer critical-dimension electron microscopy","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從灰階到邊緣、電子劑量到尺寸報告：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Grayscale to edge and Electron dose to Dimension report: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["灰階到邊緣","充電","上中下 CD","工具匹配"],"labelsEn":["Grayscale to edge","Charging","Top/middle/bottom CD","Tool matching"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a091-stage01","order":1,"title":"灰階到邊緣 → 低能電子","titleEn":"Grayscale to edge to Low-energy electrons","description":"把「灰階到邊緣」「像素校正」「低能電子」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Grayscale to edge, Pixel calibration, Low-energy electrons.","steps":[{"id":"a091-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"灰階到邊緣：建立模型","titleEn":"Grayscale to edge: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Image-edge position depends on signal and definition.","instruction":"畫跨越兩邊的線掃描灰階，標出候選邊緣演算法。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw a line-scan grayscale profile and mark candidate edge algorithms. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義；邊緣閾值改變會造成系統性 CD 偏差。","observationEn":"Image-edge position depends on signal and definition; Edge-threshold changes cause systematic CD bias.","failure":"若採用「最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「灰階到邊緣」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義。","checkEn":"Submit the Grayscale to edge diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Image-edge position depends on signal and definition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-01-k1","title":"灰階到邊緣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Grayscale to edge / Physics and model","text":"機制：影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義。","textEn":"Mechanism: Image-edge position depends on signal and definition."},{"id":"a091-v8-01-k2","title":"灰階到邊緣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Grayscale to edge / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「灰階到邊緣」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Grayscale to edge, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義","最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界","將放大倍率當成可追溯校正"],"optionsEn":["Image-edge position depends on signal and definition","Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge","Treating magnification as traceable calibration"],"answer":0,"explanation":"影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Image-edge position depends on signal and definition. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-01"],"title":"灰階到邊緣：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Grayscale to edge: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge.","instruction":"接續前一步「灰階到邊緣」成果，先指出錯誤主張「最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：邊緣閾值改變會造成系統性 CD 偏差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Grayscale to edge artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Edge-threshold changes cause systematic CD bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義；邊緣閾值改變會造成系統性 CD 偏差。","observationEn":"Image-edge position depends on signal and definition; Edge-threshold changes cause systematic CD bias.","failure":"若採用「最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「灰階到邊緣」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「邊緣閾值改變會造成系統性 CD 偏差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Grayscale to edge, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Edge-threshold changes cause systematic CD bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-02-k1","title":"灰階到邊緣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Grayscale to edge / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：邊緣閾值改變會造成系統性 CD 偏差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Edge-threshold changes cause systematic CD bias."},{"id":"a091-v8-02-k2","title":"灰階到邊緣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Grayscale to edge / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界」與「影像邊緣位置取決於訊號及定義」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge\" is not equivalent to \"Image-edge position depends on signal and definition\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「灰階到邊緣」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Grayscale to edge?","options":["將放大倍率當成可追溯校正","邊緣閾值改變會造成系統性 CD 偏差","最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界"],"optionsEn":["Treating magnification as traceable calibration","Edge-threshold changes cause systematic CD bias","Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊緣閾值改變會造成系統性 CD 偏差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edge-threshold changes cause systematic CD bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-02"],"title":"像素校正：建立模型","titleEn":"Pixel calibration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy.","instruction":"以假設標準節距換算 nm/pixel 並標示校正不確定度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設校正標準的 100 nm 節距在影像上占 40 pixel，比例為 2.5 nm/pixel；量得線寬 20 pixel，名目 CD=50 nm。若線寬抽取本身的不確定度為 1 pixel，單此項即 2.5 nm，尚未合併校正與邊緣模型誤差；不能把像素尺寸當成完整準確度。","instructionEn":"Calibrate nm/pixel with a hypothetical pitch standard and uncertainty. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a calibrated 100 nm pitch spans 40 pixels, giving 2.5 nm/pixel. A 20-pixel width has nominal CD=50 nm. If width extraction alone has 1-pixel uncertainty, that contribution is 2.5 nm before calibration and edge-model errors are combined. Pixel scale is not complete accuracy.","observation":"放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度；標準件本身也帶有不確定度。","observationEn":"Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy; Reference standards themselves have uncertainty.","failure":"若採用「將放大倍率當成可追溯校正」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating magnification as traceable calibration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「像素校正」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度。\n算例驗收：驗算 2.5 nm/pixel、50 nm 與 2.5 nm 誤差項，寫清 1 pixel 指線寬而不是每一側邊緣。","checkEn":"Submit the Pixel calibration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify scale, 50 nm width and the 2.5 nm contribution; state that one pixel refers to width, not independently to each edge.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-03-k1","title":"像素校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel calibration / Physics and model","text":"機制：放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy."},{"id":"a091-v8-03-k2","title":"像素校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel calibration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將放大倍率當成可追溯校正」。\n假設數值與推算：假設校正標準的 100 nm 節距在影像上占 40 pixel，比例為 2.5 nm/pixel；量得線寬 20 pixel，名目 CD=50 nm。若線寬抽取本身的不確定度為 1 pixel，單此項即 2.5 nm，尚未合併校正與邊緣模型誤差；不能把像素尺寸當成完整準確度。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating magnification as traceable calibration.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a calibrated 100 nm pitch spans 40 pixels, giving 2.5 nm/pixel. A 20-pixel width has nominal CD=50 nm. If width extraction alone has 1-pixel uncertainty, that contribution is 2.5 nm before calibration and edge-model errors are combined. Pixel scale is not complete accuracy."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「像素校正」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pixel calibration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將放大倍率當成可追溯校正","低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動","放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度"],"optionsEn":["Treating magnification as traceable calibration","Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples","Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy"],"answer":2,"explanation":"放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-03"],"title":"像素校正：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pixel calibration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將放大倍率當成可追溯校正」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating magnification as traceable calibration.","instruction":"接續前一步「像素校正」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將放大倍率當成可追溯校正」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：標準件本身也帶有不確定度。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pixel calibration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating magnification as traceable calibration\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reference standards themselves have uncertainty. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度；標準件本身也帶有不確定度。","observationEn":"Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy; Reference standards themselves have uncertainty.","failure":"若採用「將放大倍率當成可追溯校正」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating magnification as traceable calibration\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「像素校正」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「標準件本身也帶有不確定度」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pixel calibration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reference standards themselves have uncertainty\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-04-k1","title":"像素校正／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pixel calibration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：標準件本身也帶有不確定度。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reference standards themselves have uncertainty."},{"id":"a091-v8-04-k2","title":"像素校正／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pixel calibration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將放大倍率當成可追溯校正」與「放大影像不會自動提高尺度準確度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating magnification as traceable calibration\" is not equivalent to \"Magnification does not automatically improve scale accuracy\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「像素校正」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pixel calibration?","options":["標準件本身也帶有不確定度","將放大倍率當成可追溯校正","低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動"],"optionsEn":["Reference standards themselves have uncertainty","Treating magnification as traceable calibration","Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples"],"answer":0,"explanation":"標準件本身也帶有不確定度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reference standards themselves have uncertainty. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-04"],"title":"低能電子：建立模型","titleEn":"Low-energy electrons: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction.","instruction":"比較兩入射能量的表面敏感度、訊號與損傷取捨。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare surface sensitivity, signal and damage at two landing energies. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響；著陸能量不同於槍體設定的簡化名稱。","observationEn":"Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction; Landing energy must be distinguished from nominal gun labels.","failure":"若採用「低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「低能電子」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響。","checkEn":"Submit the Low-energy electrons diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-05-k1","title":"低能電子／物理與模型","titleEn":"Low-energy electrons / Physics and model","text":"機制：較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響。","textEn":"Mechanism: Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction."},{"id":"a091-v8-05-k2","title":"低能電子／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Low-energy electrons / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「低能電子」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Low-energy electrons, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化","較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響","低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動"],"optionsEn":["Treating all image drift as true CD change","Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction","Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples"],"answer":1,"explanation":"較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-05"],"title":"低能電子：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Low-energy electrons: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples.","instruction":"接續前一步「低能電子」成果，先指出錯誤主張「低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：著陸能量不同於槍體設定的簡化名稱。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Low-energy electrons artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Landing energy must be distinguished from nominal gun labels. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響；著陸能量不同於槍體設定的簡化名稱。","observationEn":"Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction; Landing energy must be distinguished from nominal gun labels.","failure":"若採用「低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「低能電子」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「著陸能量不同於槍體設定的簡化名稱」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Low-energy electrons, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Landing energy must be distinguished from nominal gun labels\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-06-k1","title":"低能電子／物理與模型","titleEn":"Low-energy electrons / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：著陸能量不同於槍體設定的簡化名稱。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Landing energy must be distinguished from nominal gun labels."},{"id":"a091-v8-06-k2","title":"低能電子／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Low-energy electrons / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動」與「較低能量可減少部分損傷但非完全無影響」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples\" is not equivalent to \"Lower energy reduces some damage, not all interaction\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「低能電子」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Low-energy electrons?","options":["低電壓影像一律沒有量測擾動","所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化","著陸能量不同於槍體設定的簡化名稱"],"optionsEn":["Assuming low-voltage images never perturb samples","Treating all image drift as true CD change","Landing energy must be distinguished from nominal gun labels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"著陸能量不同於槍體設定的簡化名稱；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Landing energy must be distinguished from nominal gun labels. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a091-stage02","order":2,"title":"充電 → 焦點與像散","titleEn":"Charging to Focus and astigmatism","description":"把「充電」「電子劑量」「焦點與像散」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Charging, Electron dose, Focus and astigmatism.","steps":[{"id":"a091-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-06"],"title":"充電：建立模型","titleEn":"Charging: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Insulator charging changes electron trajectories.","instruction":"畫連續掃描下位置偏移及亮度改變，加入導電參考。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw repeated-scan shifts/intensity changes with a conductive reference. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡；接地路徑影響充電累積。","observationEn":"Insulator charging changes electron trajectories; Grounding paths affect charge accumulation.","failure":"若採用「所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all image drift as true CD change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「充電」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡。","checkEn":"Submit the Charging diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Insulator charging changes electron trajectories.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-07-k1","title":"充電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Charging / Physics and model","text":"機制：絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡。","textEn":"Mechanism: Insulator charging changes electron trajectories."},{"id":"a091-v8-07-k2","title":"充電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Charging / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating all image drift as true CD change."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「充電」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Charging, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡","所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化","重複次數越多就無代價接近真值"],"optionsEn":["Insulator charging changes electron trajectories","Treating all image drift as true CD change","Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample"],"answer":0,"explanation":"絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Insulator charging changes electron trajectories. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-07"],"title":"充電：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Charging: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating all image drift as true CD change.","instruction":"接續前一步「充電」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接地路徑影響充電累積。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Charging artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating all image drift as true CD change\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Grounding paths affect charge accumulation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡；接地路徑影響充電累積。","observationEn":"Insulator charging changes electron trajectories; Grounding paths affect charge accumulation.","failure":"若採用「所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all image drift as true CD change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「充電」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接地路徑影響充電累積」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Charging, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Grounding paths affect charge accumulation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-08-k1","title":"充電／物理與模型","titleEn":"Charging / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接地路徑影響充電累積。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Grounding paths affect charge accumulation."},{"id":"a091-v8-08-k2","title":"充電／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Charging / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化」與「絕緣表面充電會改變電子軌跡」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating all image drift as true CD change\" is not equivalent to \"Insulator charging changes electron trajectories\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「充電」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Charging?","options":["重複次數越多就無代價接近真值","接地路徑影響充電累積","所有影像漂移都當成真實線寬變化"],"optionsEn":["Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample","Grounding paths affect charge accumulation","Treating all image drift as true CD change"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接地路徑影響充電累積；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Grounding paths affect charge accumulation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-08"],"title":"電子劑量：建立模型","titleEn":"Electron dose: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「重複量測本身可能改變光阻」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Repeated measurement can alter resist.","instruction":"比較先後掃描順序的假設光阻 CD，估算累積劑量。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare resist CD versus scan order and estimate accumulated dose. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"重複量測本身可能改變光阻；劑量由電流、停留與掃描次數共同決定。","observationEn":"Repeated measurement can alter resist; Dose combines current, dwell and repeated scans.","failure":"若採用「重複次數越多就無代價接近真值」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電子劑量」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：重複量測本身可能改變光阻。","checkEn":"Submit the Electron dose diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Repeated measurement can alter resist.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-09-k1","title":"電子劑量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electron dose / Physics and model","text":"機制：重複量測本身可能改變光阻。","textEn":"Mechanism: Repeated measurement can alter resist."},{"id":"a091-v8-09-k2","title":"電子劑量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electron dose / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「重複次數越多就無代價接近真值」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電子劑量」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Electron dose, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["重複次數越多就無代價接近真值","單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠","重複量測本身可能改變光阻"],"optionsEn":["Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample","Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation","Repeated measurement can alter resist"],"answer":2,"explanation":"重複量測本身可能改變光阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Repeated measurement can alter resist. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-09"],"title":"電子劑量：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Electron dose: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「重複次數越多就無代價接近真值」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample.","instruction":"接續前一步「電子劑量」成果，先指出錯誤主張「重複次數越多就無代價接近真值」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：劑量由電流、停留與掃描次數共同決定。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Electron dose artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dose combines current, dwell and repeated scans. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"重複量測本身可能改變光阻；劑量由電流、停留與掃描次數共同決定。","observationEn":"Repeated measurement can alter resist; Dose combines current, dwell and repeated scans.","failure":"若採用「重複次數越多就無代價接近真值」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電子劑量」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「劑量由電流、停留與掃描次數共同決定」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Electron dose, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dose combines current, dwell and repeated scans\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-10-k1","title":"電子劑量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electron dose / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：劑量由電流、停留與掃描次數共同決定。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dose combines current, dwell and repeated scans."},{"id":"a091-v8-10-k2","title":"電子劑量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electron dose / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「重複次數越多就無代價接近真值」與「重複量測本身可能改變光阻」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample\" is not equivalent to \"Repeated measurement can alter resist\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電子劑量」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Electron dose?","options":["劑量由電流、停留與掃描次數共同決定","重複次數越多就無代價接近真值","單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠"],"optionsEn":["Dose combines current, dwell and repeated scans","Assuming unlimited repeats converge without altering the sample","Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"劑量由電流、停留與掃描次數共同決定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dose combines current, dwell and repeated scans. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-10"],"title":"焦點與像散：建立模型","titleEn":"Focus and astigmatism: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Directional blur can mimic geometry differences.","instruction":"比較水平和垂直線的邊緣寬度，分辨像散與真實形貌。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare horizontal/vertical edge widths to separate astigmatism from geometry. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異；影像處理銳化可改變邊緣估計。","observationEn":"Directional blur can mimic geometry differences; Sharpening can change inferred edge positions.","failure":"若採用「單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「焦點與像散」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異。","checkEn":"Submit the Focus and astigmatism diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Directional blur can mimic geometry differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-11-k1","title":"焦點與像散／物理與模型","titleEn":"Focus and astigmatism / Physics and model","text":"機制：儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異。","textEn":"Mechanism: Directional blur can mimic geometry differences."},{"id":"a091-v8-11-k2","title":"焦點與像散／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Focus and astigmatism / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「焦點與像散」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Focus and astigmatism, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD","儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異","單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠"],"optionsEn":["Calling top-view CD the bottom CD","Directional blur can mimic geometry differences","Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Directional blur can mimic geometry differences. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-11"],"title":"焦點與像散：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Focus and astigmatism: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation.","instruction":"接續前一步「焦點與像散」成果，先指出錯誤主張「單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：影像處理銳化可改變邊緣估計。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Focus and astigmatism artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sharpening can change inferred edge positions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異；影像處理銳化可改變邊緣估計。","observationEn":"Directional blur can mimic geometry differences; Sharpening can change inferred edge positions.","failure":"若採用「單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「焦點與像散」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「影像處理銳化可改變邊緣估計」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Focus and astigmatism, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sharpening can change inferred edge positions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-12-k1","title":"焦點與像散／物理與模型","titleEn":"Focus and astigmatism / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：影像處理銳化可改變邊緣估計。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sharpening can change inferred edge positions."},{"id":"a091-v8-12-k2","title":"焦點與像散／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Focus and astigmatism / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠」與「儀器方向性模糊可能模仿圖形差異」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation\" is not equivalent to \"Directional blur can mimic geometry differences\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「焦點與像散」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Focus and astigmatism?","options":["單方向銳利即可證明所有方向量測可靠","將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD","影像處理銳化可改變邊緣估計"],"optionsEn":["Accepting all directions from one sharp orientation","Calling top-view CD the bottom CD","Sharpening can change inferred edge positions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"影像處理銳化可改變邊緣估計；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sharpening can change inferred edge positions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a091-stage03","order":3,"title":"上中下 CD → 抽樣位置","titleEn":"Top/middle/bottom CD to Sampling sites","description":"把「上中下 CD」「線邊粗糙」「抽樣位置」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Top/middle/bottom CD, Line-edge roughness, Sampling sites.","steps":[{"id":"a091-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-12"],"title":"上中下 CD：建立模型","titleEn":"Top/middle/bottom CD: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section.","instruction":"在梯形截面標出三種寬度並對應頂視可觀察量。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark three widths on a trapezoid and relate them to top-view observables. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面；側壁角會影響灰階輪廓。","observationEn":"Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section; Sidewall angle affects grayscale profiles.","failure":"若採用「將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling top-view CD the bottom CD\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「上中下 CD」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面。","checkEn":"Submit the Top/middle/bottom CD diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-13-k1","title":"上中下 CD／物理與模型","titleEn":"Top/middle/bottom CD / Physics and model","text":"機制：頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面。","textEn":"Mechanism: Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section."},{"id":"a091-v8-13-k2","title":"上中下 CD／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Top/middle/bottom CD / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling top-view CD the bottom CD."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「上中下 CD」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Top/middle/bottom CD, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面","將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD","將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR"],"optionsEn":["Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section","Calling top-view CD the bottom CD","Doubling one edge roughness as LWR"],"answer":0,"explanation":"頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-13"],"title":"上中下 CD：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Top/middle/bottom CD: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling top-view CD the bottom CD.","instruction":"接續前一步「上中下 CD」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：側壁角會影響灰階輪廓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Top/middle/bottom CD artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling top-view CD the bottom CD\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sidewall angle affects grayscale profiles. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面；側壁角會影響灰階輪廓。","observationEn":"Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section; Sidewall angle affects grayscale profiles.","failure":"若採用「將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling top-view CD the bottom CD\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「上中下 CD」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「側壁角會影響灰階輪廓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Top/middle/bottom CD, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sidewall angle affects grayscale profiles\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-14-k1","title":"上中下 CD／物理與模型","titleEn":"Top/middle/bottom CD / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：側壁角會影響灰階輪廓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sidewall angle affects grayscale profiles."},{"id":"a091-v8-14-k2","title":"上中下 CD／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Top/middle/bottom CD / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD」與「頂視輪廓未必唯一決定整個截面」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling top-view CD the bottom CD\" is not equivalent to \"Top-view profiles need not uniquely determine a section\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「上中下 CD」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Top/middle/bottom CD?","options":["將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR","側壁角會影響灰階輪廓","將頂視 CD 直接當成底部 CD"],"optionsEn":["Doubling one edge roughness as LWR","Sidewall angle affects grayscale profiles","Calling top-view CD the bottom CD"],"answer":1,"explanation":"側壁角會影響灰階輪廓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sidewall angle affects grayscale profiles. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-14"],"title":"線邊粗糙：建立模型","titleEn":"Line-edge roughness: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Edge correlation affects line-width roughness.","instruction":"對假設邊緣座標去趨勢，分開兩邊粗糙和線寬粗糙。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Detrend edge coordinates and separate each edge from width roughness. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙；取樣長度決定粗糙度頻率範圍。","observationEn":"Edge correlation affects line-width roughness; Sample length limits roughness-frequency coverage.","failure":"若採用「將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Doubling one edge roughness as LWR\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「線邊粗糙」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙。","checkEn":"Submit the Line-edge roughness diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Edge correlation affects line-width roughness.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-15-k1","title":"線邊粗糙／物理與模型","titleEn":"Line-edge roughness / Physics and model","text":"機制：左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙。","textEn":"Mechanism: Edge correlation affects line-width roughness."},{"id":"a091-v8-15-k2","title":"線邊粗糙／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Line-edge roughness / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Doubling one edge roughness as LWR."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「線邊粗糙」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Line-edge roughness, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR","只測容易找到的圖形代表整片","左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙"],"optionsEn":["Doubling one edge roughness as LWR","Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only","Edge correlation affects line-width roughness"],"answer":2,"explanation":"左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edge correlation affects line-width roughness. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-15"],"title":"線邊粗糙：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Line-edge roughness: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Doubling one edge roughness as LWR.","instruction":"接續前一步「線邊粗糙」成果，先指出錯誤主張「將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：取樣長度決定粗糙度頻率範圍。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Line-edge roughness artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Doubling one edge roughness as LWR\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sample length limits roughness-frequency coverage. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙；取樣長度決定粗糙度頻率範圍。","observationEn":"Edge correlation affects line-width roughness; Sample length limits roughness-frequency coverage.","failure":"若採用「將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Doubling one edge roughness as LWR\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「線邊粗糙」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「取樣長度決定粗糙度頻率範圍」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Line-edge roughness, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sample length limits roughness-frequency coverage\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-16-k1","title":"線邊粗糙／物理與模型","titleEn":"Line-edge roughness / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：取樣長度決定粗糙度頻率範圍。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sample length limits roughness-frequency coverage."},{"id":"a091-v8-16-k2","title":"線邊粗糙／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Line-edge roughness / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR」與「左右邊相關性影響線寬粗糙」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Doubling one edge roughness as LWR\" is not equivalent to \"Edge correlation affects line-width roughness\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「線邊粗糙」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Line-edge roughness?","options":["取樣長度決定粗糙度頻率範圍","將單邊粗糙度直接乘二當 LWR","只測容易找到的圖形代表整片"],"optionsEn":["Sample length limits roughness-frequency coverage","Doubling one edge roughness as LWR","Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only"],"answer":0,"explanation":"取樣長度決定粗糙度頻率範圍；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sample length limits roughness-frequency coverage. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-16"],"title":"抽樣位置：建立模型","titleEn":"Sampling sites: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「抽樣位置會影響所見分布」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Sampling locations affect observed distributions.","instruction":"在晶圓圖規劃中心、邊緣和圖形密度抽樣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plan center, edge and density-based wafer sampling. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"抽樣位置會影響所見分布；圖形方向也應列為抽樣因子。","observationEn":"Sampling locations affect observed distributions; Pattern orientation should be a sampling factor.","failure":"若採用「只測容易找到的圖形代表整片」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「抽樣位置」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：抽樣位置會影響所見分布。","checkEn":"Submit the Sampling sites diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Sampling locations affect observed distributions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-17-k1","title":"抽樣位置／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sampling sites / Physics and model","text":"機制：抽樣位置會影響所見分布。","textEn":"Mechanism: Sampling locations affect observed distributions."},{"id":"a091-v8-17-k2","title":"抽樣位置／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sampling sites / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只測容易找到的圖形代表整片」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「抽樣位置」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Sampling sites, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["散布小就直接宣稱準確","抽樣位置會影響所見分布","只測容易找到的圖形代表整片"],"optionsEn":["Equating small spread with accuracy","Sampling locations affect observed distributions","Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only"],"answer":1,"explanation":"抽樣位置會影響所見分布；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sampling locations affect observed distributions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-17"],"title":"抽樣位置：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Sampling sites: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只測容易找到的圖形代表整片」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only.","instruction":"接續前一步「抽樣位置」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只測容易找到的圖形代表整片」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：圖形方向也應列為抽樣因子。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Sampling sites artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pattern orientation should be a sampling factor. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"抽樣位置會影響所見分布；圖形方向也應列為抽樣因子。","observationEn":"Sampling locations affect observed distributions; Pattern orientation should be a sampling factor.","failure":"若採用「只測容易找到的圖形代表整片」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「抽樣位置」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「圖形方向也應列為抽樣因子」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Sampling sites, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pattern orientation should be a sampling factor\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-18-k1","title":"抽樣位置／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sampling sites / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：圖形方向也應列為抽樣因子。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pattern orientation should be a sampling factor."},{"id":"a091-v8-18-k2","title":"抽樣位置／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sampling sites / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只測容易找到的圖形代表整片」與「抽樣位置會影響所見分布」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only\" is not equivalent to \"Sampling locations affect observed distributions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「抽樣位置」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Sampling sites?","options":["只測容易找到的圖形代表整片","散布小就直接宣稱準確","圖形方向也應列為抽樣因子"],"optionsEn":["Representing a wafer by convenient patterns only","Equating small spread with accuracy","Pattern orientation should be a sampling factor"],"answer":2,"explanation":"圖形方向也應列為抽樣因子；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pattern orientation should be a sampling factor. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a091-stage04","order":4,"title":"工具匹配 → 尺寸報告","titleEn":"Tool matching to Dimension report","description":"把「工具匹配」「模型式量測」「尺寸報告」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Tool matching, Model-based measurement, Dimension report.","steps":[{"id":"a091-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-18"],"title":"工具匹配：建立模型","titleEn":"Tool matching: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement.","instruction":"對同一參考片做兩台儀器配對量測，分開偏差與散布。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Pair two tools on one reference wafer and separate bias/spread. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差；標準片污染可造成共同漂移。","observationEn":"Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement; Reference contamination can cause common drift.","failure":"若採用「散布小就直接宣稱準確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating small spread with accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「工具匹配」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差。","checkEn":"Submit the Tool matching diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-19-k1","title":"工具匹配／物理與模型","titleEn":"Tool matching / Physics and model","text":"機制：重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差。","textEn":"Mechanism: Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement."},{"id":"a091-v8-19-k2","title":"工具匹配／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Tool matching / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「散布小就直接宣稱準確」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating small spread with accuracy."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「工具匹配」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Tool matching, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差","散布小就直接宣稱準確","複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實"],"optionsEn":["Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement","Equating small spread with accuracy","Assuming complex model output is automatically truer"],"answer":0,"explanation":"重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-19"],"title":"工具匹配：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Tool matching: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「散布小就直接宣稱準確」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating small spread with accuracy.","instruction":"接續前一步「工具匹配」成果，先指出錯誤主張「散布小就直接宣稱準確」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：標準片污染可造成共同漂移。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Tool matching artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating small spread with accuracy\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reference contamination can cause common drift. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差；標準片污染可造成共同漂移。","observationEn":"Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement; Reference contamination can cause common drift.","failure":"若採用「散布小就直接宣稱準確」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating small spread with accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「工具匹配」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「標準片污染可造成共同漂移」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Tool matching, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reference contamination can cause common drift\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-20-k1","title":"工具匹配／物理與模型","titleEn":"Tool matching / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：標準片污染可造成共同漂移。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reference contamination can cause common drift."},{"id":"a091-v8-20-k2","title":"工具匹配／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Tool matching / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「散布小就直接宣稱準確」與「重複性良好不代表兩台無系統偏差」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating small spread with accuracy\" is not equivalent to \"Good repeatability does not imply tool agreement\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「工具匹配」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Tool matching?","options":["複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實","標準片污染可造成共同漂移","散布小就直接宣稱準確"],"optionsEn":["Assuming complex model output is automatically truer","Reference contamination can cause common drift","Equating small spread with accuracy"],"answer":1,"explanation":"標準片污染可造成共同漂移；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reference contamination can cause common drift. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-20"],"title":"模型式量測：建立模型","titleEn":"Model-based measurement: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Models add information and assumptions together.","instruction":"比較簡單閾值及電子訊號模型的邊緣推定。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare threshold and electron-signal-model edge inference. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設；模擬材料參數誤差可偏移推定輪廓。","observationEn":"Models add information and assumptions together; Simulation material errors bias inferred profiles.","failure":"若採用「複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming complex model output is automatically truer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「模型式量測」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設。","checkEn":"Submit the Model-based measurement diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Models add information and assumptions together.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-21-k1","title":"模型式量測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Model-based measurement / Physics and model","text":"機制：加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設。","textEn":"Mechanism: Models add information and assumptions together."},{"id":"a091-v8-21-k2","title":"模型式量測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Model-based measurement / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming complex model output is automatically truer."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型式量測」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Model-based measurement, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實","只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義","加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設"],"optionsEn":["Assuming complex model output is automatically truer","Reporting one nanometer number without its definition","Models add information and assumptions together"],"answer":2,"explanation":"加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Models add information and assumptions together. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-21"],"title":"模型式量測：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Model-based measurement: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming complex model output is automatically truer.","instruction":"接續前一步「模型式量測」成果，先指出錯誤主張「複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：模擬材料參數誤差可偏移推定輪廓。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Model-based measurement artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming complex model output is automatically truer\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Simulation material errors bias inferred profiles. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設；模擬材料參數誤差可偏移推定輪廓。","observationEn":"Models add information and assumptions together; Simulation material errors bias inferred profiles.","failure":"若採用「複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming complex model output is automatically truer\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「模型式量測」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「模擬材料參數誤差可偏移推定輪廓」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Model-based measurement, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Simulation material errors bias inferred profiles\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-22-k1","title":"模型式量測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Model-based measurement / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：模擬材料參數誤差可偏移推定輪廓。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Simulation material errors bias inferred profiles."},{"id":"a091-v8-22-k2","title":"模型式量測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Model-based measurement / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實」與「加入模型可用資訊也引入模型假設」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming complex model output is automatically truer\" is not equivalent to \"Models add information and assumptions together\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「模型式量測」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Model-based measurement?","options":["模擬材料參數誤差可偏移推定輪廓","複雜模型輸出就一定比原圖真實","只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義"],"optionsEn":["Simulation material errors bias inferred profiles","Assuming complex model output is automatically truer","Reporting one nanometer number without its definition"],"answer":0,"explanation":"模擬材料參數誤差可偏移推定輪廓；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Simulation material errors bias inferred profiles. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-22"],"title":"尺寸報告：建立模型","titleEn":"Dimension report: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Comparable CDs require measurement conditions.","instruction":"提交尺度、邊緣定義、劑量、樣本數和不確定度表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Report scale, edge definition, dose, sample count and uncertainty. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件；溯源鏈應連到長度標準。","observationEn":"Comparable CDs require measurement conditions; Traceability should connect to length standards.","failure":"若採用「只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting one nanometer number without its definition\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「尺寸報告」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件。","checkEn":"Submit the Dimension report diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Comparable CDs require measurement conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-23-k1","title":"尺寸報告／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dimension report / Physics and model","text":"機制：可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Comparable CDs require measurement conditions."},{"id":"a091-v8-23-k2","title":"尺寸報告／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dimension report / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Reporting one nanometer number without its definition."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「尺寸報告」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dimension report, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界","可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件","只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義"],"optionsEn":["Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge","Comparable CDs require measurement conditions","Reporting one nanometer number without its definition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Comparable CDs require measurement conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a091-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-cdsem","v8-c-cdsem-lab","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a091-v8-23"],"title":"尺寸報告：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dimension report: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Reporting one nanometer number without its definition.","instruction":"接續前一步「尺寸報告」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：溯源鏈應連到長度標準。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dimension report artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Reporting one nanometer number without its definition\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Traceability should connect to length standards. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件；溯源鏈應連到長度標準。","observationEn":"Comparable CDs require measurement conditions; Traceability should connect to length standards.","failure":"若採用「只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting one nanometer number without its definition\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「尺寸報告」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「溯源鏈應連到長度標準」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dimension report, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Traceability should connect to length standards\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a091-v8-24-k1","title":"尺寸報告／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dimension report / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：溯源鏈應連到長度標準。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Traceability should connect to length standards."},{"id":"a091-v8-24-k2","title":"尺寸報告／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dimension report / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義」與「可比較的 CD 需要完整量測條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Reporting one nanometer number without its definition\" is not equivalent to \"Comparable CDs require measurement conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「尺寸報告」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dimension report?","options":["只報一個奈米數而省略量測定義","最亮像素永遠就是實體邊界","溯源鏈應連到長度標準"],"optionsEn":["Reporting one nanometer number without its definition","Assuming the brightest pixel is always the physical edge","Traceability should connect to length standards"],"answer":2,"explanation":"溯源鏈應連到長度標準；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Traceability should connect to length standards. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"},{"id":"a092","title":"光學散射量測","titleEn":"Optical scatterometry","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從週期標靶、偏振和角度到製程回授：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Periodic targets and Polarization and angle to Process feedback: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["週期標靶","光學常數","靈敏度矩陣","交叉量測"],"labelsEn":["Periodic targets","Optical constants","Sensitivity matrix","Cross-metrology"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a092-stage01","order":1,"title":"週期標靶 → RCWA 假設","titleEn":"Periodic targets to RCWA assumptions","description":"把「週期標靶」「前向與反向」「RCWA 假設」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Periodic targets, Forward and inverse, RCWA assumptions.","steps":[{"id":"a092-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"週期標靶：建立模型","titleEn":"Periodic targets: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「散射反演需要明確幾何參數化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization.","instruction":"畫光柵節距、線寬、高度與側壁角的參數圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設對稱梯形線條高 100 nm、頂寬 40 nm、底寬 60 nm，每側水平差為 (60−40)/2=10 nm。相對水平面的側壁角 atan(100/10)≈84.29°；相對垂直面的傾斜約 5.71°。這是已知幾何的計算，不能證明光學反演已唯一決定此形貌。","instructionEn":"Parameterize grating pitch, width, height and sidewall angle. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a symmetric trapezoidal line 100 nm high, 40 nm wide at top and 60 nm at bottom. Each side shifts horizontally by 10 nm. Sidewall angle from horizontal is atan(100/10)≈84.29°, or 5.71° from vertical. This computes known geometry; it does not prove a unique optical inverse solution.","observation":"散射反演需要明確幾何參數化；節距可固定但須有獨立依據。","observationEn":"Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization; Fixing pitch needs independent evidence.","failure":"若採用「不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「週期標靶」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：散射反演需要明確幾何參數化。\n算例驗收：驗算兩種角度並在截面上標明參考方向，避免將 84.29° 與 5.71° 誤認互相矛盾。","checkEn":"Submit the Periodic targets diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both angles and mark reference directions so 84.29° and 5.71° are not mistaken for contradictory results.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-01-k1","title":"週期標靶／物理與模型","titleEn":"Periodic targets / Physics and model","text":"機制：散射反演需要明確幾何參數化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization."},{"id":"a092-v8-01-k2","title":"週期標靶／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Periodic targets / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬」。\n假設數值與推算：假設對稱梯形線條高 100 nm、頂寬 40 nm、底寬 60 nm，每側水平差為 (60−40)/2=10 nm。相對水平面的側壁角 atan(100/10)≈84.29°；相對垂直面的傾斜約 5.71°。這是已知幾何的計算，不能證明光學反演已唯一決定此形貌。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a symmetric trapezoidal line 100 nm high, 40 nm wide at top and 60 nm at bottom. Each side shifts horizontally by 10 nm. Sidewall angle from horizontal is atan(100/10)≈84.29°, or 5.71° from vertical. This computes known geometry; it does not prove a unique optical inverse solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「週期標靶」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Periodic targets, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["散射反演需要明確幾何參數化","不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬","一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一"],"optionsEn":["Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization","Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions","Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve"],"answer":0,"explanation":"散射反演需要明確幾何參數化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-01"],"title":"週期標靶：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Periodic targets: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions.","instruction":"接續前一步「週期標靶」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：節距可固定但須有獨立依據。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Periodic targets artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Fixing pitch needs independent evidence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"散射反演需要明確幾何參數化；節距可固定但須有獨立依據。","observationEn":"Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization; Fixing pitch needs independent evidence.","failure":"若採用「不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「週期標靶」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「節距可固定但須有獨立依據」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Periodic targets, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Fixing pitch needs independent evidence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-02-k1","title":"週期標靶／物理與模型","titleEn":"Periodic targets / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：節距可固定但須有獨立依據。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Fixing pitch needs independent evidence."},{"id":"a092-v8-02-k2","title":"週期標靶／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Periodic targets / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬」與「散射反演需要明確幾何參數化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions\" is not equivalent to \"Scatter inversion needs explicit geometry parameterization\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「週期標靶」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Periodic targets?","options":["一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一","節距可固定但須有獨立依據","不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬"],"optionsEn":["Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve","Fixing pitch needs independent evidence","Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"節距可固定但須有獨立依據；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Fixing pitch needs independent evidence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-02"],"title":"前向與反向：建立模型","titleEn":"Forward and inverse: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「易算前向不代表反問題唯一」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse.","instruction":"分開幾何生成光譜與光譜推回幾何兩個流程。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate geometry-to-spectrum and spectrum-to-geometry workflows. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"易算前向不代表反問題唯一；非線性反問題可能有局部極小。","observationEn":"A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse; Nonlinear inversions can have local minima.","failure":"若採用「一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「前向與反向」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：易算前向不代表反問題唯一。","checkEn":"Submit the Forward and inverse diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-03-k1","title":"前向與反向／物理與模型","titleEn":"Forward and inverse / Physics and model","text":"機制：易算前向不代表反問題唯一。","textEn":"Mechanism: A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse."},{"id":"a092-v8-03-k2","title":"前向與反向／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Forward and inverse / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「前向與反向」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Forward and inverse, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一","無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線","易算前向不代表反問題唯一"],"optionsEn":["Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve","Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks","A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse"],"answer":2,"explanation":"易算前向不代表反問題唯一；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-03"],"title":"前向與反向：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Forward and inverse: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve.","instruction":"接續前一步「前向與反向」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：非線性反問題可能有局部極小。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Forward and inverse artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Nonlinear inversions can have local minima. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"易算前向不代表反問題唯一；非線性反問題可能有局部極小。","observationEn":"A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse; Nonlinear inversions can have local minima.","failure":"若採用「一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「前向與反向」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「非線性反問題可能有局部極小」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Forward and inverse, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Nonlinear inversions can have local minima\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-04-k1","title":"前向與反向／物理與模型","titleEn":"Forward and inverse / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：非線性反問題可能有局部極小。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Nonlinear inversions can have local minima."},{"id":"a092-v8-04-k2","title":"前向與反向／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Forward and inverse / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一」與「易算前向不代表反問題唯一」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve\" is not equivalent to \"A tractable forward problem need not have a unique inverse\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「前向與反向」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Forward and inverse?","options":["非線性反問題可能有局部極小","一條模擬曲線就證明幾何唯一","無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線"],"optionsEn":["Nonlinear inversions can have local minima","Inferring unique geometry from one simulated curve","Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"非線性反問題可能有局部極小；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Nonlinear inversions can have local minima. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-04"],"title":"RCWA 假設：建立模型","titleEn":"RCWA assumptions: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment.","instruction":"畫無限週期模型和有限照明區，標出邊界差別。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw infinite-periodic and finite-illumination boundaries. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應；光斑邊緣會混入周邊結構。","observationEn":"Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment; Spot edges can mix surrounding structures.","failure":"若採用「無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「RCWA 假設」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應。","checkEn":"Submit the RCWA assumptions diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-05-k1","title":"RCWA 假設／物理與模型","titleEn":"RCWA assumptions / Physics and model","text":"機制：週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment."},{"id":"a092-v8-05-k2","title":"RCWA 假設／驗證與限制","titleEn":"RCWA assumptions / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「RCWA 假設」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For RCWA assumptions, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差","週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應","無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線"],"optionsEn":["Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error","Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment","Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-05"],"title":"RCWA 假設：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"RCWA assumptions: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks.","instruction":"接續前一步「RCWA 假設」成果，先指出錯誤主張「無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：光斑邊緣會混入周邊結構。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding RCWA assumptions artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Spot edges can mix surrounding structures. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應；光斑邊緣會混入周邊結構。","observationEn":"Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment; Spot edges can mix surrounding structures.","failure":"若採用「無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「RCWA 假設」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「光斑邊緣會混入周邊結構」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for RCWA assumptions, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Spot edges can mix surrounding structures\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-06-k1","title":"RCWA 假設／物理與模型","titleEn":"RCWA assumptions / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：光斑邊緣會混入周邊結構。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Spot edges can mix surrounding structures."},{"id":"a092-v8-06-k2","title":"RCWA 假設／驗證與限制","titleEn":"RCWA assumptions / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線」與「週期求解器需要評估有限標靶效應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks\" is not equivalent to \"Periodic solvers need finite-target assessment\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「RCWA 假設」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of RCWA assumptions?","options":["無限週期解可無條件套用孤立線","把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差","光斑邊緣會混入周邊結構"],"optionsEn":["Applying infinite-periodic solutions to isolated lines without checks","Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error","Spot edges can mix surrounding structures"],"answer":2,"explanation":"光斑邊緣會混入周邊結構；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Spot edges can mix surrounding structures. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a092-stage02","order":2,"title":"光學常數 → 參數相關","titleEn":"Optical constants to Parameter correlation","description":"把「光學常數」「偏振和角度」「參數相關」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Optical constants, Polarization and angle, Parameter correlation.","steps":[{"id":"a092-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-06"],"title":"光學常數：建立模型","titleEn":"Optical constants: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change.","instruction":"在同一幾何改變假設 n、k，觀察光譜變化。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Perturb hypothetical n and k at fixed geometry and compare spectra. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變；原生氧化層也會改變光譜。","observationEn":"Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change; Native oxide also changes spectra.","failure":"若採用「把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「光學常數」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變。","checkEn":"Submit the Optical constants diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-07-k1","title":"光學常數／物理與模型","titleEn":"Optical constants / Physics and model","text":"機制：材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change."},{"id":"a092-v8-07-k2","title":"光學常數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Optical constants / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「光學常數」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Optical constants, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變","把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差","增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊"],"optionsEn":["Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change","Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error","Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-07"],"title":"光學常數：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Optical constants: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error.","instruction":"接續前一步「光學常數」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：原生氧化層也會改變光譜。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Optical constants artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Native oxide also changes spectra. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變；原生氧化層也會改變光譜。","observationEn":"Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change; Native oxide also changes spectra.","failure":"若採用「把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「光學常數」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「原生氧化層也會改變光譜」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Optical constants, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Native oxide also changes spectra\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-08-k1","title":"光學常數／物理與模型","titleEn":"Optical constants / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：原生氧化層也會改變光譜。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Native oxide also changes spectra."},{"id":"a092-v8-08-k2","title":"光學常數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Optical constants / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差」與「材料常數誤差可能被誤擬合為幾何改變」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error\" is not equivalent to \"Optical-constant error can mimic geometry change\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「光學常數」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Optical constants?","options":["增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊","原生氧化層也會改變光譜","把所有光譜差異都解成尺寸偏差"],"optionsEn":["Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information","Native oxide also changes spectra","Interpreting every spectral difference as geometry error"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原生氧化層也會改變光譜；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Native oxide also changes spectra. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-08"],"title":"偏振和角度：建立模型","titleEn":"Polarization and angle: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「多條件量測可增加可識別資訊」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Multiple conditions can improve identifiability.","instruction":"比較兩偏振和兩角度資料對側壁及高度的敏感度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare two polarizations/angles for sidewall and height sensitivity. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"多條件量測可增加可識別資訊；入射角誤差會造成系統偏差。","observationEn":"Multiple conditions can improve identifiability; Angle error creates systematic bias.","failure":"若採用「增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「偏振和角度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：多條件量測可增加可識別資訊。","checkEn":"Submit the Polarization and angle diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Multiple conditions can improve identifiability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-09-k1","title":"偏振和角度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization and angle / Physics and model","text":"機制：多條件量測可增加可識別資訊。","textEn":"Mechanism: Multiple conditions can improve identifiability."},{"id":"a092-v8-09-k2","title":"偏振和角度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization and angle / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偏振和角度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Polarization and angle, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊","最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能","多條件量測可增加可識別資訊"],"optionsEn":["Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information","Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible","Multiple conditions can improve identifiability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"多條件量測可增加可識別資訊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multiple conditions can improve identifiability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-09"],"title":"偏振和角度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Polarization and angle: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information.","instruction":"接續前一步「偏振和角度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：入射角誤差會造成系統偏差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Polarization and angle artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Angle error creates systematic bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"多條件量測可增加可識別資訊；入射角誤差會造成系統偏差。","observationEn":"Multiple conditions can improve identifiability; Angle error creates systematic bias.","failure":"若採用「增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「偏振和角度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「入射角誤差會造成系統偏差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Polarization and angle, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Angle error creates systematic bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-10-k1","title":"偏振和角度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Polarization and angle / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：入射角誤差會造成系統偏差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Angle error creates systematic bias."},{"id":"a092-v8-10-k2","title":"偏振和角度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Polarization and angle / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊」與「多條件量測可增加可識別資訊」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information\" is not equivalent to \"Multiple conditions can improve identifiability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「偏振和角度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Polarization and angle?","options":["入射角誤差會造成系統偏差","增加同角度重複數就等於增加新物理資訊","最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能"],"optionsEn":["Angle error creates systematic bias","Equating repeated same-angle scans with new physical information","Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"入射角誤差會造成系統偏差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Angle error creates systematic bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-10"],"title":"參數相關：建立模型","titleEn":"Parameter correlation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「低殘差可同時對應多組參數」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets.","instruction":"用假設等誤差橢圓表示線寬和高度的互補變化。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw a hypothetical equal-error ellipse for width/height tradeoff. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"低殘差可同時對應多組參數；參數誤差橢圓比單獨誤差棒更完整。","observationEn":"Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets; Error ellipses reveal more than isolated bars.","failure":"若採用「最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「參數相關」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：低殘差可同時對應多組參數。","checkEn":"Submit the Parameter correlation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-11-k1","title":"參數相關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Parameter correlation / Physics and model","text":"機制：低殘差可同時對應多組參數。","textEn":"Mechanism: Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets."},{"id":"a092-v8-11-k2","title":"參數相關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Parameter correlation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「參數相關」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Parameter correlation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["對任何參數都保留任意多小數","低殘差可同時對應多組參數","最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能"],"optionsEn":["Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter","Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets","Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible"],"answer":1,"explanation":"低殘差可同時對應多組參數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-11"],"title":"參數相關：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Parameter correlation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible.","instruction":"接續前一步「參數相關」成果，先指出錯誤主張「最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：參數誤差橢圓比單獨誤差棒更完整。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Parameter correlation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Error ellipses reveal more than isolated bars. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"低殘差可同時對應多組參數；參數誤差橢圓比單獨誤差棒更完整。","observationEn":"Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets; Error ellipses reveal more than isolated bars.","failure":"若採用「最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「參數相關」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「參數誤差橢圓比單獨誤差棒更完整」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Parameter correlation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Error ellipses reveal more than isolated bars\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-12-k1","title":"參數相關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Parameter correlation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：參數誤差橢圓比單獨誤差棒更完整。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Error ellipses reveal more than isolated bars."},{"id":"a092-v8-12-k2","title":"參數相關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Parameter correlation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能」與「低殘差可同時對應多組參數」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible\" is not equivalent to \"Low residuals can correspond to multiple parameter sets\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「參數相關」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Parameter correlation?","options":["最佳擬合一組就證明其餘都不可能","對任何參數都保留任意多小數","參數誤差橢圓比單獨誤差棒更完整"],"optionsEn":["Treating one optimum as proof all alternatives are impossible","Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter","Error ellipses reveal more than isolated bars"],"answer":2,"explanation":"參數誤差橢圓比單獨誤差棒更完整；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Error ellipses reveal more than isolated bars. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a092-stage03","order":3,"title":"靈敏度矩陣 → 模型選擇","titleEn":"Sensitivity matrix to Model selection","description":"把「靈敏度矩陣」「粗糙度」「模型選擇」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Sensitivity matrix, Roughness, Model selection.","steps":[{"id":"a092-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-12"],"title":"靈敏度矩陣：建立模型","titleEn":"Sensitivity matrix: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate.","instruction":"分別小幅擾動每參數，建立各波長訊號變化矩陣。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Perturb each parameter and tabulate wavelength responses. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨；小奇異值提示弱可識別方向。","observationEn":"Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate; Small singular values indicate weak identifiability.","failure":"若採用「對任何參數都保留任意多小數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「靈敏度矩陣」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨。","checkEn":"Submit the Sensitivity matrix diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-13-k1","title":"靈敏度矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sensitivity matrix / Physics and model","text":"機制：類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨。","textEn":"Mechanism: Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate."},{"id":"a092-v8-13-k2","title":"靈敏度矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sensitivity matrix / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「對任何參數都保留任意多小數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「靈敏度矩陣」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Sensitivity matrix, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨","對任何參數都保留任意多小數","把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移"],"optionsEn":["Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate","Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter","Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift"],"answer":0,"explanation":"類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-13"],"title":"靈敏度矩陣：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Sensitivity matrix: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「對任何參數都保留任意多小數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter.","instruction":"接續前一步「靈敏度矩陣」成果，先指出錯誤主張「對任何參數都保留任意多小數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：小奇異值提示弱可識別方向。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Sensitivity matrix artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Small singular values indicate weak identifiability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨；小奇異值提示弱可識別方向。","observationEn":"Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate; Small singular values indicate weak identifiability.","failure":"若採用「對任何參數都保留任意多小數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「靈敏度矩陣」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「小奇異值提示弱可識別方向」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Sensitivity matrix, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Small singular values indicate weak identifiability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-14-k1","title":"靈敏度矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sensitivity matrix / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：小奇異值提示弱可識別方向。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Small singular values indicate weak identifiability."},{"id":"a092-v8-14-k2","title":"靈敏度矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sensitivity matrix / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「對任何參數都保留任意多小數」與「類似靈敏度向量造成參數難分辨」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter\" is not equivalent to \"Similar sensitivity vectors make parameters hard to separate\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「靈敏度矩陣」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Sensitivity matrix?","options":["把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移","小奇異值提示弱可識別方向","對任何參數都保留任意多小數"],"optionsEn":["Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift","Small singular values indicate weak identifiability","Reporting arbitrary precision for every parameter"],"answer":1,"explanation":"小奇異值提示弱可識別方向；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small singular values indicate weak identifiability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-14"],"title":"粗糙度：建立模型","titleEn":"Roughness: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Random roughness violates simple periodic models.","instruction":"比較理想週期與帶隨機邊緣的假設圖形。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare ideal periodic patterns with random edges. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型；粗糙相關長度影響散射。","observationEn":"Random roughness violates simple periodic models; Roughness correlation length affects scattering.","failure":"若採用「把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「粗糙度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型。","checkEn":"Submit the Roughness diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Random roughness violates simple periodic models.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-15-k1","title":"粗糙度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Roughness / Physics and model","text":"機制：隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型。","textEn":"Mechanism: Random roughness violates simple periodic models."},{"id":"a092-v8-15-k2","title":"粗糙度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Roughness / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「粗糙度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Roughness, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移","永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型","隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型"],"optionsEn":["Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift","Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model","Random roughness violates simple periodic models"],"answer":2,"explanation":"隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Random roughness violates simple periodic models. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-15"],"title":"粗糙度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Roughness: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift.","instruction":"接續前一步「粗糙度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：粗糙相關長度影響散射。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Roughness artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Roughness correlation length affects scattering. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型；粗糙相關長度影響散射。","observationEn":"Random roughness violates simple periodic models; Roughness correlation length affects scattering.","failure":"若採用「把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「粗糙度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「粗糙相關長度影響散射」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Roughness, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Roughness correlation length affects scattering\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-16-k1","title":"粗糙度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Roughness / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：粗糙相關長度影響散射。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Roughness correlation length affects scattering."},{"id":"a092-v8-16-k2","title":"粗糙度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Roughness / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移」與「隨機粗糙會破壞簡單週期模型」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift\" is not equivalent to \"Random roughness violates simple periodic models\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「粗糙度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Roughness?","options":["粗糙相關長度影響散射","把隨機粗糙完全當作平均 CD 位移","永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型"],"optionsEn":["Roughness correlation length affects scattering","Treating roughness solely as mean CD shift","Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model"],"answer":0,"explanation":"粗糙相關長度影響散射；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Roughness correlation length affects scattering. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-16"],"title":"模型選擇：建立模型","titleEn":"Model selection: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity.","instruction":"比較單梯形和雙層模型，使用保留波段判斷泛化。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare single-trapezoid/two-layer models using held-out spectra. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性；保留資料也需避免相鄰波長洩漏。","observationEn":"More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity; Holdouts must consider adjacent-wavelength dependence.","failure":"若採用「永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「模型選擇」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性。","checkEn":"Submit the Model selection diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-17-k1","title":"模型選擇／物理與模型","titleEn":"Model selection / Physics and model","text":"機制：更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性。","textEn":"Mechanism: More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity."},{"id":"a092-v8-17-k2","title":"模型選擇／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Model selection / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型選擇」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Model selection, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤","更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性","永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型"],"optionsEn":["Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ","More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity","Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model"],"answer":1,"explanation":"更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-17"],"title":"模型選擇：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Model selection: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model.","instruction":"接續前一步「模型選擇」成果，先指出錯誤主張「永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：保留資料也需避免相鄰波長洩漏。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Model selection artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Holdouts must consider adjacent-wavelength dependence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性；保留資料也需避免相鄰波長洩漏。","observationEn":"More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity; Holdouts must consider adjacent-wavelength dependence.","failure":"若採用「永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「模型選擇」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「保留資料也需避免相鄰波長洩漏」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Model selection, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Holdouts must consider adjacent-wavelength dependence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-18-k1","title":"模型選擇／物理與模型","titleEn":"Model selection / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：保留資料也需避免相鄰波長洩漏。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Holdouts must consider adjacent-wavelength dependence."},{"id":"a092-v8-18-k2","title":"模型選擇／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Model selection / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型」與「更多參數可降低訓練殘差而不提高真實性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model\" is not equivalent to \"More parameters can lower fitted error without increasing validity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「模型選擇」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Model selection?","options":["永遠選參數最多的最低殘差模型","不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤","保留資料也需避免相鄰波長洩漏"],"optionsEn":["Always selecting the most complex lowest-error model","Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ","Holdouts must consider adjacent-wavelength dependence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"保留資料也需避免相鄰波長洩漏；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Holdouts must consider adjacent-wavelength dependence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a092-stage04","order":4,"title":"交叉量測 → 製程回授","titleEn":"Cross-metrology to Process feedback","description":"把「交叉量測」「不確定度」「製程回授」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Cross-metrology, Uncertainty, Process feedback.","steps":[{"id":"a092-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-18"],"title":"交叉量測：建立模型","titleEn":"Cross-metrology: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同探針看見不同空間平均」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Different probes measure different spatial averages.","instruction":"將光學平均剖面與局部 SEM/TEM 對照，先對齊量測定義。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare averaged optical profiles with local microscopy after matching definitions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同探針看見不同空間平均；破壞性截面本身可能改變樣本。","observationEn":"Different probes measure different spatial averages; Destructive preparation can alter specimens.","failure":"若採用「不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「交叉量測」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同探針看見不同空間平均。","checkEn":"Submit the Cross-metrology diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Different probes measure different spatial averages.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-19-k1","title":"交叉量測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cross-metrology / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同探針看見不同空間平均。","textEn":"Mechanism: Different probes measure different spatial averages."},{"id":"a092-v8-19-k2","title":"交叉量測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cross-metrology / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「交叉量測」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Cross-metrology, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同探針看見不同空間平均","不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤","用重複標準差代替全部準確度"],"optionsEn":["Different probes measure different spatial averages","Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ","Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同探針看見不同空間平均；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Different probes measure different spatial averages. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-19"],"title":"交叉量測：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Cross-metrology: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ.","instruction":"接續前一步「交叉量測」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：破壞性截面本身可能改變樣本。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Cross-metrology artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Destructive preparation can alter specimens. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同探針看見不同空間平均；破壞性截面本身可能改變樣本。","observationEn":"Different probes measure different spatial averages; Destructive preparation can alter specimens.","failure":"若採用「不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「交叉量測」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「破壞性截面本身可能改變樣本」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Cross-metrology, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Destructive preparation can alter specimens\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-20-k1","title":"交叉量測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cross-metrology / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：破壞性截面本身可能改變樣本。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Destructive preparation can alter specimens."},{"id":"a092-v8-20-k2","title":"交叉量測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cross-metrology / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤」與「不同探針看見不同空間平均」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ\" is not equivalent to \"Different probes measure different spatial averages\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「交叉量測」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Cross-metrology?","options":["用重複標準差代替全部準確度","破壞性截面本身可能改變樣本","不同方法數字不等就直接判定某法錯誤"],"optionsEn":["Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy","Destructive preparation can alter specimens","Declaring one method wrong whenever values differ"],"answer":1,"explanation":"破壞性截面本身可能改變樣本；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Destructive preparation can alter specimens. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-20"],"title":"不確定度：建立模型","titleEn":"Uncertainty: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty.","instruction":"分開重複雜訊、角度校正和材料模型三項誤差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate repeat noise, angle calibration and material-model uncertainty. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分；材料模型錯誤常為系統性。","observationEn":"Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty; Material-model errors are often systematic.","failure":"若採用「用重複標準差代替全部準確度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「不確定度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分。","checkEn":"Submit the Uncertainty diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-21-k1","title":"不確定度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Uncertainty / Physics and model","text":"機制：重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分。","textEn":"Mechanism: Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty."},{"id":"a092-v8-21-k2","title":"不確定度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Uncertainty / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用重複標準差代替全部準確度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不確定度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Uncertainty, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用重複標準差代替全部準確度","把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量","重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分"],"optionsEn":["Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy","Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable","Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty"],"answer":2,"explanation":"重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-21"],"title":"不確定度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Uncertainty: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用重複標準差代替全部準確度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy.","instruction":"接續前一步「不確定度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用重複標準差代替全部準確度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：材料模型錯誤常為系統性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Uncertainty artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Material-model errors are often systematic. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分；材料模型錯誤常為系統性。","observationEn":"Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty; Material-model errors are often systematic.","failure":"若採用「用重複標準差代替全部準確度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「不確定度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「材料模型錯誤常為系統性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Uncertainty, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Material-model errors are often systematic\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-22-k1","title":"不確定度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Uncertainty / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：材料模型錯誤常為系統性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Material-model errors are often systematic."},{"id":"a092-v8-22-k2","title":"不確定度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Uncertainty / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用重複標準差代替全部準確度」與「重複性只涵蓋總不確定度的一部分」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy\" is not equivalent to \"Repeatability covers only part of total uncertainty\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「不確定度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Uncertainty?","options":["材料模型錯誤常為系統性","用重複標準差代替全部準確度","把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量"],"optionsEn":["Material-model errors are often systematic","Using repeat standard deviation as total accuracy","Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料模型錯誤常為系統性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Material-model errors are often systematic. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-22"],"title":"製程回授：建立模型","titleEn":"Process feedback: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「控制器不應追逐不可識別參數」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters.","instruction":"將可識別的尺寸與模糊參數分開，只回授有證據的變因。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate identifiable and ambiguous parameters and feed back supported variables. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"控制器不應追逐不可識別參數；回授延遲會改變控制穩定性。","observationEn":"Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters; Feedback latency affects control stability.","failure":"若採用「把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「製程回授」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：控制器不應追逐不可識別參數。","checkEn":"Submit the Process feedback diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-23-k1","title":"製程回授／物理與模型","titleEn":"Process feedback / Physics and model","text":"機制：控制器不應追逐不可識別參數。","textEn":"Mechanism: Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters."},{"id":"a092-v8-23-k2","title":"製程回授／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Process feedback / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「製程回授」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Process feedback, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬","控制器不應追逐不可識別參數","把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量"],"optionsEn":["Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions","Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters","Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable"],"answer":1,"explanation":"控制器不應追逐不可識別參數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a092-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-scatter","v8-c-scatter-u"],"prerequisiteIds":["a092-v8-23"],"title":"製程回授：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Process feedback: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable.","instruction":"接續前一步「製程回授」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：回授延遲會改變控制穩定性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Process feedback artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Feedback latency affects control stability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"控制器不應追逐不可識別參數；回授延遲會改變控制穩定性。","observationEn":"Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters; Feedback latency affects control stability.","failure":"若採用「把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「製程回授」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「回授延遲會改變控制穩定性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Process feedback, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Feedback latency affects control stability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a092-v8-24-k1","title":"製程回授／物理與模型","titleEn":"Process feedback / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：回授延遲會改變控制穩定性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Feedback latency affects control stability."},{"id":"a092-v8-24-k2","title":"製程回授／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Process feedback / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量」與「控制器不應追逐不可識別參數」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable\" is not equivalent to \"Controllers should not chase unidentifiable parameters\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「製程回授」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Process feedback?","options":["把所有擬合輸出直接當可靠控制量","不定義形狀便宣稱光譜能直接讀出線寬","回授延遲會改變控制穩定性"],"optionsEn":["Treating every fit output as a reliable control variable","Reading CD directly from spectra without geometry assumptions","Feedback latency affects control stability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"回授延遲會改變控制穩定性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Feedback latency affects control stability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"},{"id":"a093","title":"晶圓薄膜橢圓偏光量測","titleEn":"Wafer thin-film ellipsometry","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從p/s 偏振、厚度與 n到報告與限制：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From p/s polarization and Thickness-index coupling to Report and limits: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["p/s 偏振","堆疊模型","色散模型","去偏振"],"labelsEn":["p/s polarization","Stack model","Dispersion model","Depolarization"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a093-stage01","order":1,"title":"p/s 偏振 → 薄膜干涉","titleEn":"p/s polarization to Thin-film interference","description":"把「p/s 偏振」「Psi 與 Delta」「薄膜干涉」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for p/s polarization, Psi and Delta, Thin-film interference.","steps":[{"id":"a093-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"p/s 偏振：建立模型","titleEn":"p/s polarization: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「偏振定義需相對於入射平面」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane.","instruction":"定義入射平面並標出 p 與 s 場方向。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Define the incidence plane and mark p/s fields. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"偏振定義需相對於入射平面；偏振器零點誤差會混入相位。","observationEn":"Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane; Polarizer-zero errors contaminate phase.","failure":"若採用「把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「p/s 偏振」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：偏振定義需相對於入射平面。","checkEn":"Submit the p/s polarization diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-01-k1","title":"p/s 偏振／物理與模型","titleEn":"p/s polarization / Physics and model","text":"機制：偏振定義需相對於入射平面。","textEn":"Mechanism: Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane."},{"id":"a093-v8-01-k2","title":"p/s 偏振／驗證與限制","titleEn":"p/s polarization / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「p/s 偏振」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For p/s polarization, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["偏振定義需相對於入射平面","把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s","把 Psi 直接當反射率"],"optionsEn":["Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane","Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s","Calling Psi the reflectance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"偏振定義需相對於入射平面；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-01"],"title":"p/s 偏振：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"p/s polarization: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s.","instruction":"接續前一步「p/s 偏振」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：偏振器零點誤差會混入相位。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding p/s polarization artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Polarizer-zero errors contaminate phase. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"偏振定義需相對於入射平面；偏振器零點誤差會混入相位。","observationEn":"Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane; Polarizer-zero errors contaminate phase.","failure":"若採用「把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「p/s 偏振」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「偏振器零點誤差會混入相位」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for p/s polarization, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Polarizer-zero errors contaminate phase\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-02-k1","title":"p/s 偏振／物理與模型","titleEn":"p/s polarization / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：偏振器零點誤差會混入相位。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Polarizer-zero errors contaminate phase."},{"id":"a093-v8-02-k2","title":"p/s 偏振／驗證與限制","titleEn":"p/s polarization / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s」與「偏振定義需相對於入射平面」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s\" is not equivalent to \"Polarization definitions are relative to incidence plane\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「p/s 偏振」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of p/s polarization?","options":["把 Psi 直接當反射率","偏振器零點誤差會混入相位","把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s"],"optionsEn":["Calling Psi the reflectance","Polarizer-zero errors contaminate phase","Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s"],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏振器零點誤差會混入相位；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Polarizer-zero errors contaminate phase. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-02"],"title":"Psi 與 Delta：建立模型","titleEn":"Psi and Delta: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「橢偏量測是相對偏振響應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response.","instruction":"以 rho=rp/rs=tan(Psi)exp(iDelta) 分開振幅比與相位。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate amplitude ratio/phase using rho=rp/rs=tan(Psi)exp(iDelta). Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"橢偏量測是相對偏振響應；相位有週期性需處理展相。","observationEn":"Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response; Phase periodicity requires unwrapping care.","failure":"若採用「把 Psi 直接當反射率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling Psi the reflectance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「Psi 與 Delta」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：橢偏量測是相對偏振響應。","checkEn":"Submit the Psi and Delta diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-03-k1","title":"Psi 與 Delta／物理與模型","titleEn":"Psi and Delta / Physics and model","text":"機制：橢偏量測是相對偏振響應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response."},{"id":"a093-v8-03-k2","title":"Psi 與 Delta／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Psi and Delta / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把 Psi 直接當反射率」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling Psi the reflectance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「Psi 與 Delta」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Psi and Delta, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把 Psi 直接當反射率","只用幾何厚度而忽略 n","橢偏量測是相對偏振響應"],"optionsEn":["Calling Psi the reflectance","Ignoring refractive index in optical path","Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response"],"answer":2,"explanation":"橢偏量測是相對偏振響應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-03"],"title":"Psi 與 Delta：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Psi and Delta: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把 Psi 直接當反射率」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling Psi the reflectance.","instruction":"接續前一步「Psi 與 Delta」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把 Psi 直接當反射率」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：相位有週期性需處理展相。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Psi and Delta artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling Psi the reflectance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Phase periodicity requires unwrapping care. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"橢偏量測是相對偏振響應；相位有週期性需處理展相。","observationEn":"Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response; Phase periodicity requires unwrapping care.","failure":"若採用「把 Psi 直接當反射率」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling Psi the reflectance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「Psi 與 Delta」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「相位有週期性需處理展相」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Psi and Delta, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Phase periodicity requires unwrapping care\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-04-k1","title":"Psi 與 Delta／物理與模型","titleEn":"Psi and Delta / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：相位有週期性需處理展相。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Phase periodicity requires unwrapping care."},{"id":"a093-v8-04-k2","title":"Psi 與 Delta／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Psi and Delta / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把 Psi 直接當反射率」與「橢偏量測是相對偏振響應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling Psi the reflectance\" is not equivalent to \"Ellipsometry measures relative polarization response\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「Psi 與 Delta」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Psi and Delta?","options":["相位有週期性需處理展相","把 Psi 直接當反射率","只用幾何厚度而忽略 n"],"optionsEn":["Phase periodicity requires unwrapping care","Calling Psi the reflectance","Ignoring refractive index in optical path"],"answer":0,"explanation":"相位有週期性需處理展相；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Phase periodicity requires unwrapping care. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-04"],"title":"薄膜干涉：建立模型","titleEn":"Thin-film interference: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光程同時包含厚度及折射率」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Optical path includes thickness and refractive index.","instruction":"畫上表面反射與膜內往返路徑，標出相位差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設正入射且 n=1.5、厚度 t=100 nm，單程光學路徑 nt=150 nm、往返 300 nm。另一假設薄膜 n=2、t=75 nm 也有同樣 nt。這說明 n 與 t 可能耦合，但不表示兩者的完整橢圓偏光譜相同；Fresnel 振幅、色散與吸收仍有差異。","instructionEn":"Draw surface/interior paths and phase differences. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume normal incidence with n=1.5 and thickness t=100 nm: one-way optical path nt=150 nm and round trip 300 nm. A different hypothetical film with n=2 and t=75 nm has the same nt. This illustrates n–t coupling, not identical full ellipsometric spectra; Fresnel amplitudes, dispersion and absorption can differ.","observation":"光程同時包含厚度及折射率；界面粗糙會改變有效反射。","observationEn":"Optical path includes thickness and refractive index; Rough interfaces modify effective reflection.","failure":"若採用「只用幾何厚度而忽略 n」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring refractive index in optical path\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「薄膜干涉」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光程同時包含厚度及折射率。\n算例驗收：驗算兩組 nt，並列出至少一項可以幫助區分 n 與 t 的額外光學觀察。","checkEn":"Submit the Thin-film interference diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Optical path includes thickness and refractive index.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both nt products and name an additional optical observation that could help separate n and t.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-05-k1","title":"薄膜干涉／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thin-film interference / Physics and model","text":"機制：光程同時包含厚度及折射率。","textEn":"Mechanism: Optical path includes thickness and refractive index."},{"id":"a093-v8-05-k2","title":"薄膜干涉／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thin-film interference / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用幾何厚度而忽略 n」。\n假設數值與推算：假設正入射且 n=1.5、厚度 t=100 nm，單程光學路徑 nt=150 nm、往返 300 nm。另一假設薄膜 n=2、t=75 nm 也有同樣 nt。這說明 n 與 t 可能耦合，但不表示兩者的完整橢圓偏光譜相同；Fresnel 振幅、色散與吸收仍有差異。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Ignoring refractive index in optical path.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume normal incidence with n=1.5 and thickness t=100 nm: one-way optical path nt=150 nm and round trip 300 nm. A different hypothetical film with n=2 and t=75 nm has the same nt. This illustrates n–t coupling, not identical full ellipsometric spectra; Fresnel amplitudes, dispersion and absorption can differ."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「薄膜干涉」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thin-film interference, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["最低殘差就證明沒有漏層","光程同時包含厚度及折射率","只用幾何厚度而忽略 n"],"optionsEn":["Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted","Optical path includes thickness and refractive index","Ignoring refractive index in optical path"],"answer":1,"explanation":"光程同時包含厚度及折射率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Optical path includes thickness and refractive index. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-05"],"title":"薄膜干涉：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thin-film interference: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用幾何厚度而忽略 n」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Ignoring refractive index in optical path.","instruction":"接續前一步「薄膜干涉」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用幾何厚度而忽略 n」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：界面粗糙會改變有效反射。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thin-film interference artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Ignoring refractive index in optical path\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Rough interfaces modify effective reflection. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光程同時包含厚度及折射率；界面粗糙會改變有效反射。","observationEn":"Optical path includes thickness and refractive index; Rough interfaces modify effective reflection.","failure":"若採用「只用幾何厚度而忽略 n」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring refractive index in optical path\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「薄膜干涉」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「界面粗糙會改變有效反射」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thin-film interference, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Rough interfaces modify effective reflection\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-06-k1","title":"薄膜干涉／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thin-film interference / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：界面粗糙會改變有效反射。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Rough interfaces modify effective reflection."},{"id":"a093-v8-06-k2","title":"薄膜干涉／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thin-film interference / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用幾何厚度而忽略 n」與「光程同時包含厚度及折射率」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Ignoring refractive index in optical path\" is not equivalent to \"Optical path includes thickness and refractive index\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「薄膜干涉」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thin-film interference?","options":["只用幾何厚度而忽略 n","最低殘差就證明沒有漏層","界面粗糙會改變有效反射"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring refractive index in optical path","Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted","Rough interfaces modify effective reflection"],"answer":2,"explanation":"界面粗糙會改變有效反射；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Rough interfaces modify effective reflection. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a093-stage02","order":2,"title":"堆疊模型 → 吸收限制","titleEn":"Stack model to Absorption limits","description":"把「堆疊模型」「厚度與 n」「吸收限制」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Stack model, Thickness-index coupling, Absorption limits.","steps":[{"id":"a093-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-06"],"title":"堆疊模型：建立模型","titleEn":"Stack model: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters.","instruction":"建立空氣、粗糙層、薄膜及基板的層序。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Build air, roughness, film and substrate ordering. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數；有效介質近似有尺寸適用條件。","observationEn":"Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters; Effective-medium approximations have scale limits.","failure":"若採用「最低殘差就證明沒有漏層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「堆疊模型」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數。","checkEn":"Submit the Stack model diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-07-k1","title":"堆疊模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stack model / Physics and model","text":"機制：漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數。","textEn":"Mechanism: Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters."},{"id":"a093-v8-07-k2","title":"堆疊模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stack model / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「最低殘差就證明沒有漏層」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「堆疊模型」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Stack model, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數","最低殘差就證明沒有漏層","一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度"],"optionsEn":["Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters","Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted","Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength"],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-07"],"title":"堆疊模型：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Stack model: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「最低殘差就證明沒有漏層」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted.","instruction":"接續前一步「堆疊模型」成果，先指出錯誤主張「最低殘差就證明沒有漏層」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：有效介質近似有尺寸適用條件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Stack model artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Effective-medium approximations have scale limits. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數；有效介質近似有尺寸適用條件。","observationEn":"Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters; Effective-medium approximations have scale limits.","failure":"若採用「最低殘差就證明沒有漏層」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「堆疊模型」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「有效介質近似有尺寸適用條件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Stack model, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Effective-medium approximations have scale limits\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-08-k1","title":"堆疊模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Stack model / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：有效介質近似有尺寸適用條件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Effective-medium approximations have scale limits."},{"id":"a093-v8-08-k2","title":"堆疊模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Stack model / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「最低殘差就證明沒有漏層」與「漏掉介面層會改變抽取的其他參數」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted\" is not equivalent to \"Omitted interface layers bias other extracted parameters\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「堆疊模型」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Stack model?","options":["一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度","有效介質近似有尺寸適用條件","最低殘差就證明沒有漏層"],"optionsEn":["Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength","Effective-medium approximations have scale limits","Treating low residual as proof no layer is omitted"],"answer":1,"explanation":"有效介質近似有尺寸適用條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Effective-medium approximations have scale limits. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-08"],"title":"厚度與 n：建立模型","titleEn":"Thickness-index coupling: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相同光程可能產生參數退化」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy.","instruction":"畫兩組 n、t 近似相同光程，規劃第二角度量測。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw two n/t pairs with similar path length and plan another angle. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"相同光程可能產生參數退化；吸收係數 k 也可能和厚度相關。","observationEn":"Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy; Absorption k can also correlate with thickness.","failure":"若採用「一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「厚度與 n」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相同光程可能產生參數退化。","checkEn":"Submit the Thickness-index coupling diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-09-k1","title":"厚度與 n／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness-index coupling / Physics and model","text":"機制：相同光程可能產生參數退化。","textEn":"Mechanism: Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy."},{"id":"a093-v8-09-k2","title":"厚度與 n／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness-index coupling / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「厚度與 n」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thickness-index coupling, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度","增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面","相同光程可能產生參數退化"],"optionsEn":["Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength","Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal","Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy"],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同光程可能產生參數退化；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-09"],"title":"厚度與 n：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thickness-index coupling: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength.","instruction":"接續前一步「厚度與 n」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：吸收係數 k 也可能和厚度相關。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thickness-index coupling artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Absorption k can also correlate with thickness. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相同光程可能產生參數退化；吸收係數 k 也可能和厚度相關。","observationEn":"Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy; Absorption k can also correlate with thickness.","failure":"若採用「一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「厚度與 n」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「吸收係數 k 也可能和厚度相關」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thickness-index coupling, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Absorption k can also correlate with thickness\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-10-k1","title":"厚度與 n／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thickness-index coupling / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：吸收係數 k 也可能和厚度相關。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Absorption k can also correlate with thickness."},{"id":"a093-v8-10-k2","title":"厚度與 n／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thickness-index coupling / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度」與「相同光程可能產生參數退化」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength\" is not equivalent to \"Similar path lengths can produce parameter degeneracy\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「厚度與 n」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thickness-index coupling?","options":["吸收係數 k 也可能和厚度相關","一個波長便任意解出 n、k 和厚度","增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面"],"optionsEn":["Absorption k can also correlate with thickness","Solving arbitrary n, k and thickness from one wavelength","Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸收係數 k 也可能和厚度相關；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Absorption k can also correlate with thickness. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-10"],"title":"吸收限制：建立模型","titleEn":"Absorption limits: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption.","instruction":"比較透明與強吸收薄膜的返回光路。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare return paths in transparent/absorbing films. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見；選擇較透明波段可增加穿透。","observationEn":"Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption; Transparent spectral regions improve penetration.","failure":"若採用「增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「吸收限制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見。","checkEn":"Submit the Absorption limits diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-11-k1","title":"吸收限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Absorption limits / Physics and model","text":"機制：太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見。","textEn":"Mechanism: Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption."},{"id":"a093-v8-11-k2","title":"吸收限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Absorption limits / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吸收限制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Absorption limits, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同一透明模型適用所有波長","太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見","增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面"],"optionsEn":["Applying one transparency model at every wavelength","Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption","Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-11"],"title":"吸收限制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Absorption limits: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal.","instruction":"接續前一步「吸收限制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：選擇較透明波段可增加穿透。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Absorption limits artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Transparent spectral regions improve penetration. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見；選擇較透明波段可增加穿透。","observationEn":"Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption; Transparent spectral regions improve penetration.","failure":"若採用「增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「吸收限制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「選擇較透明波段可增加穿透」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Absorption limits, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Transparent spectral regions improve penetration\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-12-k1","title":"吸收限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Absorption limits / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：選擇較透明波段可增加穿透。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Transparent spectral regions improve penetration."},{"id":"a093-v8-12-k2","title":"吸收限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Absorption limits / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面」與「太深處的介面在強吸收下可能不可見」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal\" is not equivalent to \"Deep interfaces may be invisible under strong absorption\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「吸收限制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Absorption limits?","options":["增厚金屬仍可無限精確測其底界面","同一透明模型適用所有波長","選擇較透明波段可增加穿透"],"optionsEn":["Assuming unlimited bottom-interface access through thick metal","Applying one transparency model at every wavelength","Transparent spectral regions improve penetration"],"answer":2,"explanation":"選擇較透明波段可增加穿透；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Transparent spectral regions improve penetration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a093-stage03","order":3,"title":"色散模型 → 背面反射","titleEn":"Dispersion model to Backside reflection","description":"把「色散模型」「多角度資料」「背面反射」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Dispersion model, Multi-angle data, Backside reflection.","steps":[{"id":"a093-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-12"],"title":"色散模型：建立模型","titleEn":"Dispersion model: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption.","instruction":"對透明區使用假設 Cauchy 曲線，標記不適用的吸收區。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Use a hypothetical Cauchy curve in transparency and mark absorbing regions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶；色散模型需檢查物理一致性。","observationEn":"Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption; Dispersion models require physical-consistency checks.","failure":"若採用「同一透明模型適用所有波長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying one transparency model at every wavelength\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「色散模型」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶。","checkEn":"Submit the Dispersion model diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-13-k1","title":"色散模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dispersion model / Physics and model","text":"機制：透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶。","textEn":"Mechanism: Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption."},{"id":"a093-v8-13-k2","title":"色散模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dispersion model / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同一透明模型適用所有波長」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Applying one transparency model at every wavelength."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「色散模型」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Dispersion model, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶","同一透明模型適用所有波長","各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合"],"optionsEn":["Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption","Applying one transparency model at every wavelength","Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well"],"answer":0,"explanation":"透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-13"],"title":"色散模型：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Dispersion model: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同一透明模型適用所有波長」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Applying one transparency model at every wavelength.","instruction":"接續前一步「色散模型」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同一透明模型適用所有波長」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：色散模型需檢查物理一致性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Dispersion model artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Applying one transparency model at every wavelength\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dispersion models require physical-consistency checks. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶；色散模型需檢查物理一致性。","observationEn":"Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption; Dispersion models require physical-consistency checks.","failure":"若採用「同一透明模型適用所有波長」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying one transparency model at every wavelength\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「色散模型」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「色散模型需檢查物理一致性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Dispersion model, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dispersion models require physical-consistency checks\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-14-k1","title":"色散模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Dispersion model / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：色散模型需檢查物理一致性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dispersion models require physical-consistency checks."},{"id":"a093-v8-14-k2","title":"色散模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Dispersion model / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同一透明模型適用所有波長」與「透明模型不能無條件延伸到吸收能帶」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Applying one transparency model at every wavelength\" is not equivalent to \"Transparent models cannot be extended blindly into absorption\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「色散模型」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Dispersion model?","options":["各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合","色散模型需檢查物理一致性","同一透明模型適用所有波長"],"optionsEn":["Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well","Dispersion models require physical-consistency checks","Applying one transparency model at every wavelength"],"answer":1,"explanation":"色散模型需檢查物理一致性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dispersion models require physical-consistency checks. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-14"],"title":"多角度資料：建立模型","titleEn":"Multi-angle data: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies.","instruction":"比較同片兩角度共同擬合和分別擬合的參數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare joint and separate fits at two angles. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致；角度校正偏差可共同影響多角擬合。","observationEn":"Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies; Angle calibration can bias joint fits.","failure":"若採用「各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「多角度資料」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致。","checkEn":"Submit the Multi-angle data diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-15-k1","title":"多角度資料／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multi-angle data / Physics and model","text":"機制：共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致。","textEn":"Mechanism: Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies."},{"id":"a093-v8-15-k2","title":"多角度資料／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multi-angle data / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多角度資料」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Multi-angle data, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合","所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜","共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致"],"optionsEn":["Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well","Attributing every extra reflection to the target film","Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies"],"answer":2,"explanation":"共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-15"],"title":"多角度資料：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Multi-angle data: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well.","instruction":"接續前一步「多角度資料」成果，先指出錯誤主張「各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：角度校正偏差可共同影響多角擬合。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Multi-angle data artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Angle calibration can bias joint fits. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致；角度校正偏差可共同影響多角擬合。","observationEn":"Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies; Angle calibration can bias joint fits.","failure":"若採用「各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「多角度資料」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「角度校正偏差可共同影響多角擬合」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Multi-angle data, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Angle calibration can bias joint fits\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-16-k1","title":"多角度資料／物理與模型","titleEn":"Multi-angle data / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：角度校正偏差可共同影響多角擬合。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Angle calibration can bias joint fits."},{"id":"a093-v8-16-k2","title":"多角度資料／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Multi-angle data / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合」與「共用物理參數可揭露角度間不一致」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well\" is not equivalent to \"Shared parameters reveal cross-angle inconsistencies\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「多角度資料」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Multi-angle data?","options":["角度校正偏差可共同影響多角擬合","各角度隨意改厚度以取得好擬合","所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜"],"optionsEn":["Angle calibration can bias joint fits","Changing thickness per angle solely to fit well","Attributing every extra reflection to the target film"],"answer":0,"explanation":"角度校正偏差可共同影響多角擬合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Angle calibration can bias joint fits. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-16"],"title":"背面反射：建立模型","titleEn":"Backside reflection: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「基板背反射可污染前表面模型」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling.","instruction":"畫透明基板背面光路，比較遮背與未遮背訊號。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Trace backside reflection and compare suppressed/unsuppressed data. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"基板背反射可污染前表面模型；基板楔角可能分離背面反射。","observationEn":"Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling; Substrate wedge can separate backside reflections.","failure":"若採用「所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing every extra reflection to the target film\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「背面反射」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：基板背反射可污染前表面模型。","checkEn":"Submit the Backside reflection diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-17-k1","title":"背面反射／物理與模型","titleEn":"Backside reflection / Physics and model","text":"機制：基板背反射可污染前表面模型。","textEn":"Mechanism: Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling."},{"id":"a093-v8-17-k2","title":"背面反射／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Backside reflection / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing every extra reflection to the target film."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「背面反射」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Backside reflection, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊","基板背反射可污染前表面模型","所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜"],"optionsEn":["Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise","Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling","Attributing every extra reflection to the target film"],"answer":1,"explanation":"基板背反射可污染前表面模型；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-17"],"title":"背面反射：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Backside reflection: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing every extra reflection to the target film.","instruction":"接續前一步「背面反射」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：基板楔角可能分離背面反射。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Backside reflection artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing every extra reflection to the target film\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Substrate wedge can separate backside reflections. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"基板背反射可污染前表面模型；基板楔角可能分離背面反射。","observationEn":"Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling; Substrate wedge can separate backside reflections.","failure":"若採用「所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing every extra reflection to the target film\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「背面反射」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「基板楔角可能分離背面反射」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Backside reflection, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Substrate wedge can separate backside reflections\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-18-k1","title":"背面反射／物理與模型","titleEn":"Backside reflection / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：基板楔角可能分離背面反射。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Substrate wedge can separate backside reflections."},{"id":"a093-v8-18-k2","title":"背面反射／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Backside reflection / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜」與「基板背反射可污染前表面模型」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing every extra reflection to the target film\" is not equivalent to \"Backside reflection can contaminate front-surface modeling\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「背面反射」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Backside reflection?","options":["所有多重反射都一定來自目標薄膜","把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊","基板楔角可能分離背面反射"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every extra reflection to the target film","Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise","Substrate wedge can separate backside reflections"],"answer":2,"explanation":"基板楔角可能分離背面反射；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Substrate wedge can separate backside reflections. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a093-stage04","order":4,"title":"去偏振 → 報告與限制","titleEn":"Depolarization to Report and limits","description":"把「去偏振」「標準與漂移」「報告與限制」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Depolarization, Standards and drift, Report and limits.","steps":[{"id":"a093-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-18"],"title":"去偏振：建立模型","titleEn":"Depolarization: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「光斑內不均可能造成去偏振」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization.","instruction":"比較均勻光斑與跨越兩種厚度的光斑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare a uniform spot with one spanning two thicknesses. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"光斑內不均可能造成去偏振；Mueller 矩陣可提供額外偏振資訊。","observationEn":"Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization; Mueller matrices provide additional polarization information.","failure":"若採用「把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「去偏振」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：光斑內不均可能造成去偏振。","checkEn":"Submit the Depolarization diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-19-k1","title":"去偏振／物理與模型","titleEn":"Depolarization / Physics and model","text":"機制：光斑內不均可能造成去偏振。","textEn":"Mechanism: Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization."},{"id":"a093-v8-19-k2","title":"去偏振／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Depolarization / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「去偏振」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Depolarization, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["光斑內不均可能造成去偏振","把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊","參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤"],"optionsEn":["Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization","Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise","Assuming every reference change is instrument error"],"answer":0,"explanation":"光斑內不均可能造成去偏振；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-19"],"title":"去偏振：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Depolarization: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise.","instruction":"接續前一步「去偏振」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：Mueller 矩陣可提供額外偏振資訊。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Depolarization artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mueller matrices provide additional polarization information. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"光斑內不均可能造成去偏振；Mueller 矩陣可提供額外偏振資訊。","observationEn":"Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization; Mueller matrices provide additional polarization information.","failure":"若採用「把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「去偏振」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「Mueller 矩陣可提供額外偏振資訊」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Depolarization, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mueller matrices provide additional polarization information\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-20-k1","title":"去偏振／物理與模型","titleEn":"Depolarization / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：Mueller 矩陣可提供額外偏振資訊。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mueller matrices provide additional polarization information."},{"id":"a093-v8-20-k2","title":"去偏振／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Depolarization / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊」與「光斑內不均可能造成去偏振」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise\" is not equivalent to \"Within-spot nonuniformity can cause depolarization\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「去偏振」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Depolarization?","options":["參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤","Mueller 矩陣可提供額外偏振資訊","把去偏振完全當成儀器隨機雜訊"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every reference change is instrument error","Mueller matrices provide additional polarization information","Treating all depolarization as random instrument noise"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Mueller 矩陣可提供額外偏振資訊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mueller matrices provide additional polarization information. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-20"],"title":"標準與漂移：建立模型","titleEn":"Standards and drift: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable.","instruction":"用假設穩定參考片追蹤每日 Psi/Delta 殘差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Track daily Psi/Delta residuals on a stable reference. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性；參考片表面污染可假裝成儀器漂移。","observationEn":"Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable; Reference contamination can mimic drift.","failure":"若採用「參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every reference change is instrument error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「標準與漂移」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性。","checkEn":"Submit the Standards and drift diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-21-k1","title":"標準與漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Standards and drift / Physics and model","text":"機制：校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable."},{"id":"a093-v8-21-k2","title":"標準與漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Standards and drift / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming every reference change is instrument error."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「標準與漂移」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Standards and drift, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤","省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值","校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every reference change is instrument error","Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading","Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable"],"answer":2,"explanation":"校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-21"],"title":"標準與漂移：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Standards and drift: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming every reference change is instrument error.","instruction":"接續前一步「標準與漂移」成果，先指出錯誤主張「參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：參考片表面污染可假裝成儀器漂移。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Standards and drift artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming every reference change is instrument error\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reference contamination can mimic drift. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性；參考片表面污染可假裝成儀器漂移。","observationEn":"Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable; Reference contamination can mimic drift.","failure":"若採用「參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every reference change is instrument error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「標準與漂移」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「參考片表面污染可假裝成儀器漂移」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Standards and drift, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reference contamination can mimic drift\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-22-k1","title":"標準與漂移／物理與模型","titleEn":"Standards and drift / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：參考片表面污染可假裝成儀器漂移。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reference contamination can mimic drift."},{"id":"a093-v8-22-k2","title":"標準與漂移／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Standards and drift / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤」與「校驗片能監控漂移但仍需其自身穩定性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming every reference change is instrument error\" is not equivalent to \"Check standards monitor drift but must themselves be stable\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「標準與漂移」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Standards and drift?","options":["參考片表面污染可假裝成儀器漂移","參考片數值變動一定只是儀器錯誤","省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值"],"optionsEn":["Reference contamination can mimic drift","Assuming every reference change is instrument error","Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading"],"answer":0,"explanation":"參考片表面污染可假裝成儀器漂移；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reference contamination can mimic drift. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-22"],"title":"報告與限制：建立模型","titleEn":"Report and limits: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「厚度結果是條件化的模型推論」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Thickness is a model-conditioned inference.","instruction":"同時提交模型層序、波段、角度、相關係數和厚度區間。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Report layer model, spectrum, angles, correlations and thickness interval. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"厚度結果是條件化的模型推論；參數信賴區間應包含模型限制。","observationEn":"Thickness is a model-conditioned inference; Confidence reporting should include model limitations.","failure":"若採用「省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「報告與限制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：厚度結果是條件化的模型推論。","checkEn":"Submit the Report and limits diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Thickness is a model-conditioned inference.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-23-k1","title":"報告與限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Report and limits / Physics and model","text":"機制：厚度結果是條件化的模型推論。","textEn":"Mechanism: Thickness is a model-conditioned inference."},{"id":"a093-v8-23-k2","title":"報告與限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Report and limits / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「報告與限制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Report and limits, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s","厚度結果是條件化的模型推論","省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值"],"optionsEn":["Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s","Thickness is a model-conditioned inference","Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading"],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚度結果是條件化的模型推論；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thickness is a model-conditioned inference. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a093-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-elli","v8-c-elli-nk","v8-c-elli-thick"],"prerequisiteIds":["a093-v8-23"],"title":"報告與限制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Report and limits: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading.","instruction":"接續前一步「報告與限制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：參數信賴區間應包含模型限制。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Report and limits artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Confidence reporting should include model limitations. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"厚度結果是條件化的模型推論；參數信賴區間應包含模型限制。","observationEn":"Thickness is a model-conditioned inference; Confidence reporting should include model limitations.","failure":"若採用「省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「報告與限制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「參數信賴區間應包含模型限制」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Report and limits, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Confidence reporting should include model limitations\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a093-v8-24-k1","title":"報告與限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Report and limits / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：參數信賴區間應包含模型限制。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Confidence reporting should include model limitations."},{"id":"a093-v8-24-k2","title":"報告與限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Report and limits / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值」與「厚度結果是條件化的模型推論」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading\" is not equivalent to \"Thickness is a model-conditioned inference\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「報告與限制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Report and limits?","options":["省略模型仍可把厚度當直接量尺讀值","把水平與垂直永遠當 p 和 s","參數信賴區間應包含模型限制"],"optionsEn":["Presenting model-free thickness as a direct ruler reading","Treating horizontal/vertical as universally p/s","Confidence reporting should include model limitations"],"answer":2,"explanation":"參數信賴區間應包含模型限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Confidence reporting should include model limitations. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"},{"id":"a094","title":"晶圓缺陷分類與良率分析","titleEn":"Wafer defect classification and yield analysis","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從缺陷單位、混淆矩陣到改善驗證：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Defect units and Confusion matrix to Improvement verification: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["缺陷單位","人工真值","空間模式","良率模型"],"labelsEn":["Defect units","Reference labels","Spatial patterns","Yield model"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a094-stage01","order":1,"title":"缺陷單位 → 檢出門檻","titleEn":"Defect units to Detection threshold","description":"把「缺陷單位」「座標配準」「檢出門檻」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Defect units, Coordinate registration, Detection threshold.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"缺陷單位：建立模型","titleEn":"Defect units: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects.","instruction":"分開影像缺陷、實體缺陷與失效晶粒三種計數。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate image detections, physical defects and failed dies. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷；同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。","observationEn":"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects; One defect may appear on several layers.","failure":"若採用「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「缺陷單位」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷。","checkEn":"Submit the Defect units diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-01-k1","title":"缺陷單位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect units / Physics and model","text":"機制：多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷。","textEn":"Mechanism: Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects."},{"id":"a094-v8-01-k2","title":"缺陷單位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect units / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating detection count with failed-die count."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷單位」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Defect units, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷","把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數","直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像"],"optionsEn":["Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects","Equating detection count with failed-die count","Overlaying maps without checking mirroring"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-01"],"title":"缺陷單位：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Defect units: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating detection count with failed-die count.","instruction":"接續前一步「缺陷單位」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Defect units artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: One defect may appear on several layers. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷；同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。","observationEn":"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects; One defect may appear on several layers.","failure":"若採用「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「缺陷單位」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Defect units, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"One defect may appear on several layers\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-02-k1","title":"缺陷單位／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect units / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: One defect may appear on several layers."},{"id":"a094-v8-02-k2","title":"缺陷單位／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect units / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數」與「多次檢出不一定代表多個實體缺陷」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating detection count with failed-die count\" is not equivalent to \"Multiple detections need not mean multiple physical defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「缺陷單位」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Defect units?","options":["直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像","同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察","把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數"],"optionsEn":["Overlaying maps without checking mirroring","One defect may appear on several layers","Equating detection count with failed-die count"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一缺陷可能在多層被重複觀察；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"One defect may appear on several layers. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-02"],"title":"座標配準：建立模型","titleEn":"Coordinate registration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence.","instruction":"用晶圓缺口和三個不對稱標记對齊兩站地圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Register two maps with a notch and asymmetric marks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應；鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。","observationEn":"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence; Mirror errors break causal tracing.","failure":"若採用「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「座標配準」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應。","checkEn":"Submit the Coordinate registration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-03-k1","title":"座標配準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Physics and model","text":"機制：翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence."},{"id":"a094-v8-03-k2","title":"座標配準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Overlaying maps without checking mirroring."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「座標配準」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Coordinate registration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像","檢出越多就必然代表製程更差","翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應"],"optionsEn":["Overlaying maps without checking mirroring","Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing","Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-03"],"title":"座標配準：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Coordinate registration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Overlaying maps without checking mirroring.","instruction":"接續前一步「座標配準」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Coordinate registration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mirror errors break causal tracing. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應；鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。","observationEn":"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence; Mirror errors break causal tracing.","failure":"若採用「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「座標配準」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Coordinate registration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mirror errors break causal tracing\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-04-k1","title":"座標配準／物理與模型","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mirror errors break causal tracing."},{"id":"a094-v8-04-k2","title":"座標配準／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Coordinate registration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像」與「翻面及旋轉會改變座標對應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Overlaying maps without checking mirroring\" is not equivalent to \"Flips and rotations change coordinate correspondence\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「座標配準」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Coordinate registration?","options":["鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤","直接疊圖而不檢查鏡像","檢出越多就必然代表製程更差"],"optionsEn":["Mirror errors break causal tracing","Overlaying maps without checking mirroring","Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"鏡像配準錯誤會破壞因果追蹤；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mirror errors break causal tracing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-04"],"title":"檢出門檻：建立模型","titleEn":"Detection threshold: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms.","instruction":"以假設真缺陷和背景分布繪製門檻取捨。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Plot a hypothetical detection/background threshold tradeoff. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警；ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。","observationEn":"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms; ROC comparisons need the same reference labels.","failure":"若採用「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「檢出門檻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警。","checkEn":"Submit the Detection threshold diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-05-k1","title":"檢出門檻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Physics and model","text":"機制：降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警。","textEn":"Mechanism: Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms."},{"id":"a094-v8-05-k2","title":"檢出門檻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「檢出門檻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Detection threshold, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類","降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警","檢出越多就必然代表製程更差"],"optionsEn":["Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes","Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms","Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing"],"answer":1,"explanation":"降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-05"],"title":"檢出門檻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Detection threshold: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing.","instruction":"接續前一步「檢出門檻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Detection threshold artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: ROC comparisons need the same reference labels. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警；ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。","observationEn":"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms; ROC comparisons need the same reference labels.","failure":"若採用「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「檢出門檻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「ROC 比較需相同參考標籤」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Detection threshold, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"ROC comparisons need the same reference labels\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-06-k1","title":"檢出門檻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：ROC 比較需相同參考標籤。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: ROC comparisons need the same reference labels."},{"id":"a094-v8-06-k2","title":"檢出門檻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Detection threshold / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「檢出越多就必然代表製程更差」與「降低門檻可增加召回也增加誤警」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing\" is not equivalent to \"Lower thresholds can increase recall and false alarms\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「檢出門檻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Detection threshold?","options":["檢出越多就必然代表製程更差","強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類","ROC 比較需相同參考標籤"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more detections necessarily mean worse processing","Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes","ROC comparisons need the same reference labels"],"answer":2,"explanation":"ROC 比較需相同參考標籤；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"ROC comparisons need the same reference labels. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a094-stage02","order":2,"title":"人工真值 → 尺寸與危害","titleEn":"Reference labels to Size and criticality","description":"把「人工真值」「混淆矩陣」「尺寸與危害」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Reference labels, Confusion matrix, Size and criticality.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-06"],"title":"人工真值：建立模型","titleEn":"Reference labels: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「參考標籤本身也有不確定性」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Reference labels themselves have uncertainty.","instruction":"建立雙人複核及爭議標籤，保留未知類別。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Create dual review/disagreement labels and retain unknowns. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"參考標籤本身也有不確定性；審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。","observationEn":"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty; Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality.","failure":"若採用「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「人工真值」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：參考標籤本身也有不確定性。","checkEn":"Submit the Reference labels diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Reference labels themselves have uncertainty.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-07-k1","title":"人工真值／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reference labels / Physics and model","text":"機制：參考標籤本身也有不確定性。","textEn":"Mechanism: Reference labels themselves have uncertainty."},{"id":"a094-v8-07-k2","title":"人工真值／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reference labels / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「人工真值」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Reference labels, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["參考標籤本身也有不確定性","強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類","只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到"],"optionsEn":["Reference labels themselves have uncertainty","Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes","Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture"],"answer":0,"explanation":"參考標籤本身也有不確定性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-07"],"title":"人工真值：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Reference labels: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes.","instruction":"接續前一步「人工真值」成果，先指出錯誤主張「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Reference labels artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"參考標籤本身也有不確定性；審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。","observationEn":"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty; Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality.","failure":"若採用「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「人工真值」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「審查者一致率可量化標籤品質」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Reference labels, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-08-k1","title":"人工真值／物理與模型","titleEn":"Reference labels / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：審查者一致率可量化標籤品質。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality."},{"id":"a094-v8-08-k2","title":"人工真值／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Reference labels / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類」與「參考標籤本身也有不確定性」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes\" is not equivalent to \"Reference labels themselves have uncertainty\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「人工真值」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Reference labels?","options":["只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到","審查者一致率可量化標籤品質","強迫所有模糊影像歸入已知類"],"optionsEn":["Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture","Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality","Forcing every ambiguous image into known classes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"審查者一致率可量化標籤品質；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Reviewer agreement quantifies label quality. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-08"],"title":"混淆矩陣：建立模型","titleEn":"Confusion matrix: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data.","instruction":"用假設刮傷、粒子與正常樣本算每類精確率召回率。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compute per-class precision/recall for scratches, particles and normal samples. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效；精確率受類別盛行率影響。","observationEn":"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data; Precision depends on class prevalence.","failure":"若採用「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「混淆矩陣」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效。","checkEn":"Submit the Confusion matrix diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-09-k1","title":"混淆矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Physics and model","text":"機制：不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效。","textEn":"Mechanism: Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data."},{"id":"a094-v8-09-k2","title":"混淆矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混淆矩陣」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Confusion matrix, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到","最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命","不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效"],"optionsEn":["Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture","Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal","Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-09"],"title":"混淆矩陣：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Confusion matrix: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture.","instruction":"接續前一步「混淆矩陣」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：精確率受類別盛行率影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Confusion matrix artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Precision depends on class prevalence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效；精確率受類別盛行率影響。","observationEn":"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data; Precision depends on class prevalence.","failure":"若採用「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「混淆矩陣」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「精確率受類別盛行率影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Confusion matrix, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Precision depends on class prevalence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-10-k1","title":"混淆矩陣／物理與模型","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：精確率受類別盛行率影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Precision depends on class prevalence."},{"id":"a094-v8-10-k2","title":"混淆矩陣／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Confusion matrix / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到」與「不平衡資料的總準確率可掩蓋少數失效」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture\" is not equivalent to \"Overall accuracy can hide rare failures in imbalanced data\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「混淆矩陣」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Confusion matrix?","options":["精確率受類別盛行率影響","只報全體準確率即證明關鍵缺陷可抓到","最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命"],"optionsEn":["Precision depends on class prevalence","Using overall accuracy to prove critical-defect capture","Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"精確率受類別盛行率影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Precision depends on class prevalence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-10"],"title":"尺寸與危害：建立模型","titleEn":"Size and criticality: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Criticality depends on defect position and layout.","instruction":"將缺陷投到線距及接觸孔版圖，判讀短路與開路風險。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Overlay defects on spacing/contact layouts and assess bridge/open risk. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形；接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。","observationEn":"Criticality depends on defect position and layout; Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal.","failure":"若採用「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「尺寸與危害」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形。","checkEn":"Submit the Size and criticality diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Criticality depends on defect position and layout.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-11-k1","title":"尺寸與危害／物理與模型","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Physics and model","text":"機制：缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形。","textEn":"Mechanism: Criticality depends on defect position and layout."},{"id":"a094-v8-11-k2","title":"尺寸與危害／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「尺寸與危害」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Size and criticality, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備","缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形","最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命"],"optionsEn":["Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring","Criticality depends on defect position and layout","Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Criticality depends on defect position and layout. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-11"],"title":"尺寸與危害：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Size and criticality: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal.","instruction":"接續前一步「尺寸與危害」成果，先指出錯誤主張「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Size and criticality artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形；接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。","observationEn":"Criticality depends on defect position and layout; Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal.","failure":"若採用「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「尺寸與危害」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Size and criticality, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-12-k1","title":"尺寸與危害／物理與模型","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal."},{"id":"a094-v8-12-k2","title":"尺寸與危害／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Size and criticality / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命」與「缺陷危害取決於位置與圖形」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal\" is not equivalent to \"Criticality depends on defect position and layout\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「尺寸與危害」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Size and criticality?","options":["最大顆粒必然比所有小顆粒更致命","看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備","接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命"],"optionsEn":["Assuming the largest particle is always most fatal","Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring","Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸孔附近小缺陷也可能致命；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Small contact-adjacent defects can be fatal. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a094-stage03","order":3,"title":"空間模式 → 缺陷增量","titleEn":"Spatial patterns to Defect adders","description":"把「空間模式」「時間追溯」「缺陷增量」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Spatial patterns, Temporal genealogy, Defect adders.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-12"],"title":"空間模式：建立模型","titleEn":"Spatial patterns: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness.","instruction":"比較邊環、刮痕與隨機點的假設地圖。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical edge-ring, scratch and random maps. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果；晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。","observationEn":"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness; Edge exclusion changes visible patterns.","failure":"若採用「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「空間模式」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果。","checkEn":"Submit the Spatial patterns diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-13-k1","title":"空間模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Physics and model","text":"機制：空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果。","textEn":"Mechanism: Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness."},{"id":"a094-v8-13-k2","title":"空間模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「空間模式」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Spatial patterns, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果","看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備","只看最後一台設備便確定來源"],"optionsEn":["Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness","Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring","Blaming only the final tool"],"answer":0,"explanation":"空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-13"],"title":"空間模式：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Spatial patterns: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring.","instruction":"接續前一步「空間模式」成果，先指出錯誤主張「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Spatial patterns artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Edge exclusion changes visible patterns. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果；晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。","observationEn":"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness; Edge exclusion changes visible patterns.","failure":"若採用「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「空間模式」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Spatial patterns, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Edge exclusion changes visible patterns\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-14-k1","title":"空間模式／物理與模型","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Edge exclusion changes visible patterns."},{"id":"a094-v8-14-k2","title":"空間模式／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Spatial patterns / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備」與「空間模式可產生候選原因但非唯一因果」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring\" is not equivalent to \"Spatial patterns suggest causes without proving uniqueness\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「空間模式」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Spatial patterns?","options":["只看最後一台設備便確定來源","晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式","看到邊環就唯一指定某台設備"],"optionsEn":["Blaming only the final tool","Edge exclusion changes visible patterns","Assigning one tool uniquely from an edge ring"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶圓邊緣排除會改變可見模式；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edge exclusion changes visible patterns. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-14"],"title":"時間追溯：建立模型","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone.","instruction":"將缺陷發生片號連到設備、腔室與保養時刻。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Link defect wafer IDs to tools, chambers and maintenance times. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力；混批會破壞腔室追溯。","observationEn":"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone; Mixed lots can break chamber traceability.","failure":"若採用「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Blaming only the final tool\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「時間追溯」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力。","checkEn":"Submit the Temporal genealogy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-15-k1","title":"時間追溯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Physics and model","text":"機制：共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力。","textEn":"Mechanism: Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone."},{"id":"a094-v8-15-k2","title":"時間追溯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Blaming only the final tool."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間追溯」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Temporal genealogy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看最後一台設備便確定來源","直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數","共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力"],"optionsEn":["Blaming only the final tool","Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders","Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone"],"answer":2,"explanation":"共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-15"],"title":"時間追溯：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Blaming only the final tool.","instruction":"接續前一步「時間追溯」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：混批會破壞腔室追溯。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Temporal genealogy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Blaming only the final tool\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mixed lots can break chamber traceability. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力；混批會破壞腔室追溯。","observationEn":"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone; Mixed lots can break chamber traceability.","failure":"若採用「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Blaming only the final tool\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「時間追溯」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「混批會破壞腔室追溯」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Temporal genealogy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mixed lots can break chamber traceability\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-16-k1","title":"時間追溯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：混批會破壞腔室追溯。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mixed lots can break chamber traceability."},{"id":"a094-v8-16-k2","title":"時間追溯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporal genealogy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看最後一台設備便確定來源」與「共同暴露史比單一同時性更有辨識力」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Blaming only the final tool\" is not equivalent to \"Shared exposure history is more informative than coincidence alone\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「時間追溯」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Temporal genealogy?","options":["混批會破壞腔室追溯","只看最後一台設備便確定來源","直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數"],"optionsEn":["Mixed lots can break chamber traceability","Blaming only the final tool","Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders"],"answer":0,"explanation":"混批會破壞腔室追溯；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mixed lots can break chamber traceability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-16"],"title":"缺陷增量：建立模型","titleEn":"Defect adders: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions.","instruction":"配對前後圖並保留消失、移動與新增三種情況。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Pair pre/post maps and separate disappearing, moved and new detections. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比；靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。","observationEn":"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions; Sensitivity differences create false adders.","failure":"若採用「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「缺陷增量」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比。","checkEn":"Submit the Defect adders diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-17-k1","title":"缺陷增量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect adders / Physics and model","text":"機制：新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比。","textEn":"Mechanism: Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions."},{"id":"a094-v8-17-k2","title":"缺陷增量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect adders / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「缺陷增量」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Defect adders, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測","新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比","直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數"],"optionsEn":["Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone","Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions","Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders"],"answer":1,"explanation":"新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-17"],"title":"缺陷增量：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Defect adders: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders.","instruction":"接續前一步「缺陷增量」成果，先指出錯誤主張「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Defect adders artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sensitivity differences create false adders. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比；靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。","observationEn":"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions; Sensitivity differences create false adders.","failure":"若採用「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「缺陷增量」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「靈敏度不同可產生假的增量」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Defect adders, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sensitivity differences create false adders\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-18-k1","title":"缺陷增量／物理與模型","titleEn":"Defect adders / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：靈敏度不同可產生假的增量。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sensitivity differences create false adders."},{"id":"a094-v8-18-k2","title":"缺陷增量／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Defect adders / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數」與「新增數需要配準及檢出條件可比」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders\" is not equivalent to \"Adders require registration and comparable detection conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「缺陷增量」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Defect adders?","options":["直接用兩站總數相減當新增實體數","任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測","靈敏度不同可產生假的增量"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting unaligned totals as physical adders","Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone","Sensitivity differences create false adders"],"answer":2,"explanation":"靈敏度不同可產生假的增量；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sensitivity differences create false adders. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a094-stage04","order":4,"title":"良率模型 → 改善驗證","titleEn":"Yield model to Improvement verification","description":"把「良率模型」「電性關聯」「改善驗證」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Yield model, Electrical correlation, Improvement verification.","steps":[{"id":"a094-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-18"],"title":"良率模型：建立模型","titleEn":"Yield model: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects.","instruction":"用假設隨機獨立缺陷比較 Y=exp(-AD0) 與聚集情況。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設致命缺陷為空間獨立均勻 Poisson 過程，晶粒面積 A=1 cm²、缺陷密度 D0=0.1 cm⁻²，零缺陷良率 Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%。面積加倍時 Y≈81.87%。聚集缺陷、冗餘修復與參數失效不在模型內，不能當實廠良率預測。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical Poisson yield with clustered defects. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume spatially independent uniform Poisson killer defects with die area A=1 cm² and density D0=0.1 cm⁻². Zero-defect yield Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%; doubling area gives 81.87%. Clustering, repair redundancy and parametric failures are excluded; this is not a fab-yield prediction.","observation":"Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設；聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。","observationEn":"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects; Cluster models can suit some defect populations.","failure":"若採用「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「良率模型」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設。\n算例驗收：驗算兩個良率，確認 AD0 無單位，並說明良率並非隨面積線性下降。","checkEn":"Submit the Yield model diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify both yields, confirm dimensionless AD0 and explain why yield does not decrease linearly with area.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-19-k1","title":"良率模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Yield model / Physics and model","text":"機制：Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設。","textEn":"Mechanism: Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects."},{"id":"a094-v8-19-k2","title":"良率模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Yield model / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」。\n假設數值與推算：假設致命缺陷為空間獨立均勻 Poisson 過程，晶粒面積 A=1 cm²、缺陷密度 D0=0.1 cm⁻²，零缺陷良率 Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%。面積加倍時 Y≈81.87%。聚集缺陷、冗餘修復與參數失效不在模型內，不能當實廠良率預測。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume spatially independent uniform Poisson killer defects with die area A=1 cm² and density D0=0.1 cm⁻². Zero-defect yield Y=exp(−AD0)=exp(−0.1)≈90.48%; doubling area gives 81.87%. Clustering, repair redundancy and parametric failures are excluded; this is not a fab-yield prediction."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「良率模型」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Yield model, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設","任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測","影像分類即可取代電性驗證"],"optionsEn":["Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects","Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone","Replacing electrical validation with image classification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-19"],"title":"良率模型：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Yield model: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「良率模型」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Yield model artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cluster models can suit some defect populations. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設；聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。","observationEn":"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects; Cluster models can suit some defect populations.","failure":"若採用「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「良率模型」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Yield model, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cluster models can suit some defect populations\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-20-k1","title":"良率模型／物理與模型","titleEn":"Yield model / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cluster models can suit some defect populations."},{"id":"a094-v8-20-k2","title":"良率模型／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Yield model / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測」與「Poisson 良率近似依賴獨立均勻假設」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone\" is not equivalent to \"Poisson yield depends on independent uniform defects\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「良率模型」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Yield model?","options":["影像分類即可取代電性驗證","聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群","任意聚集分布都用同一密度精確預測"],"optionsEn":["Replacing electrical validation with image classification","Cluster models can suit some defect populations","Predicting arbitrary clustering from mean density alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聚集模型可能較符合某些缺陷族群；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cluster models can suit some defect populations. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-20"],"title":"電性關聯：建立模型","titleEn":"Electrical correlation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Not every visible defect has electrical impact.","instruction":"交叉列出視覺缺陷與電性失效，保留無對應案例。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Cross-tab visual defects/electrical failures and retain unmatched cases. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響；電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。","observationEn":"Not every visible defect has electrical impact; Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects.","failure":"若採用「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電性關聯」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響。","checkEn":"Submit the Electrical correlation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Not every visible defect has electrical impact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-21-k1","title":"電性關聯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Physics and model","text":"機制：不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響。","textEn":"Mechanism: Not every visible defect has electrical impact."},{"id":"a094-v8-21-k2","title":"電性關聯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Replacing electrical validation with image classification."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電性關聯」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Electrical correlation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["影像分類即可取代電性驗證","降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低","不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響"],"optionsEn":["Replacing electrical validation with image classification","Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction","Not every visible defect has electrical impact"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Not every visible defect has electrical impact. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-21"],"title":"電性關聯：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Electrical correlation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Replacing electrical validation with image classification.","instruction":"接續前一步「電性關聯」成果，先指出錯誤主張「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Electrical correlation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響；電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。","observationEn":"Not every visible defect has electrical impact; Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects.","failure":"若採用「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電性關聯」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「電性測試也有漏檢與誤警」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Electrical correlation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-22-k1","title":"電性關聯／物理與模型","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：電性測試也有漏檢與誤警。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects."},{"id":"a094-v8-22-k2","title":"電性關聯／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Electrical correlation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「影像分類即可取代電性驗證」與「不是每個可見缺陷都具電性影響」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Replacing electrical validation with image classification\" is not equivalent to \"Not every visible defect has electrical impact\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電性關聯」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Electrical correlation?","options":["電性測試也有漏檢與誤警","影像分類即可取代電性驗證","降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低"],"optionsEn":["Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects","Replacing electrical validation with image classification","Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性測試也有漏檢與誤警；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Electrical tests also miss and falsely flag defects. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-22"],"title":"改善驗證：建立模型","titleEn":"Improvement verification: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement.","instruction":"用時間分割對照檢查修正前後缺陷和良率，固定檢出設定。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Use time-separated controls with fixed detection settings. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善；改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。","observationEn":"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement; Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes.","failure":"若採用「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「改善驗證」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善。","checkEn":"Submit the Improvement verification diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-23-k1","title":"改善驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Physics and model","text":"機制：檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善。","textEn":"Mechanism: Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement."},{"id":"a094-v8-23-k2","title":"改善驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「改善驗證」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Improvement verification, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數","檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善","降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低"],"optionsEn":["Equating detection count with failed-die count","Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement","Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction"],"answer":1,"explanation":"檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a094-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-yield","v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a094-v8-23"],"title":"改善驗證：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Improvement verification: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction.","instruction":"接續前一步「改善驗證」成果，先指出錯誤主張「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Improvement verification artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善；改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。","observationEn":"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement; Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes.","failure":"若採用「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「改善驗證」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Improvement verification, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a094-v8-24-k1","title":"改善驗證／物理與模型","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes."},{"id":"a094-v8-24-k2","title":"改善驗證／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Improvement verification / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低」與「檢查靈敏度改變可偽裝成製程改善」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction\" is not equivalent to \"Inspection-sensitivity changes can mimic process improvement\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「改善驗證」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Improvement verification?","options":["降低檢出靈敏度就當缺陷降低","把檢出事件數直接當失效晶粒數","改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合"],"optionsEn":["Calling reduced sensitivity a defect reduction","Equating detection count with failed-die count","Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes"],"answer":2,"explanation":"改善評估應固定產品與圖形組合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Improvement reviews need comparable products/pattern mixes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"},{"id":"a095","title":"製程統計管制系統","titleEn":"Statistical process-control systems","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從規格與控制、Xbar 與 R到變更管理：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Specifications and control and Xbar and range to Change management: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["規格與控制","基線期間","屬性資料","能力指標"],"labelsEn":["Specifications and control","Baseline period","Attribute data","Capability indices"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a095-stage01","order":1,"title":"規格與控制 → 量測系統","titleEn":"Specifications and control to Measurement system","description":"把「規格與控制」「合理分組」「量測系統」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Specifications and control, Rational subgroups, Measurement system.","steps":[{"id":"a095-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"規格與控制：建立模型","titleEn":"Specifications and control: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements.","instruction":"畫客戶規格線及由歷史資料估計的控制線。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw customer specifications and history-estimated control limits. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求；穩定製程仍可能不符客戶規格。","observationEn":"Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements; Stable processes can still miss specifications.","failure":"若採用「把上下規格限直接當控制限」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using specification limits as control limits\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「規格與控制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求。","checkEn":"Submit the Specifications and control diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-01-k1","title":"規格與控制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Specifications and control / Physics and model","text":"機制：控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements."},{"id":"a095-v8-01-k2","title":"規格與控制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Specifications and control / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把上下規格限直接當控制限」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using specification limits as control limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「規格與控制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Specifications and control, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求","把上下規格限直接當控制限","隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定"],"optionsEn":["Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements","Using specification limits as control limits","Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages"],"answer":0,"explanation":"控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-01"],"title":"規格與控制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Specifications and control: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把上下規格限直接當控制限」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using specification limits as control limits.","instruction":"接續前一步「規格與控制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把上下規格限直接當控制限」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：穩定製程仍可能不符客戶規格。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Specifications and control artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using specification limits as control limits\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Stable processes can still miss specifications. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求；穩定製程仍可能不符客戶規格。","observationEn":"Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements; Stable processes can still miss specifications.","failure":"若採用「把上下規格限直接當控制限」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using specification limits as control limits\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「規格與控制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「穩定製程仍可能不符客戶規格」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Specifications and control, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Stable processes can still miss specifications\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-02-k1","title":"規格與控制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Specifications and control / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：穩定製程仍可能不符客戶規格。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Stable processes can still miss specifications."},{"id":"a095-v8-02-k2","title":"規格與控制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Specifications and control / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把上下規格限直接當控制限」與「控制線描述製程行為，規格線描述需求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using specification limits as control limits\" is not equivalent to \"Control limits describe behavior; specifications describe requirements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「規格與控制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Specifications and control?","options":["隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定","穩定製程仍可能不符客戶規格","把上下規格限直接當控制限"],"optionsEn":["Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages","Stable processes can still miss specifications","Using specification limits as control limits"],"answer":1,"explanation":"穩定製程仍可能不符客戶規格；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Stable processes can still miss specifications. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-02"],"title":"合理分組：建立模型","titleEn":"Rational subgroups: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect.","instruction":"對批次、腔室和時間排列假設量測，選擇組內與組間變異。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Arrange data by lot/chamber/time and define within/between variation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動；組內變異不等於長期全部變異。","observationEn":"Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect; Within-group variation is not all long-term variation.","failure":"若採用「隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「合理分組」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動。","checkEn":"Submit the Rational subgroups diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-03-k1","title":"合理分組／物理與模型","titleEn":"Rational subgroups / Physics and model","text":"機制：分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動。","textEn":"Mechanism: Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect."},{"id":"a095-v8-03-k2","title":"合理分組／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Rational subgroups / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「合理分組」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Rational subgroups, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定","量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異","分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動"],"optionsEn":["Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages","Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals","Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect"],"answer":2,"explanation":"分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-03"],"title":"合理分組：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Rational subgroups: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages.","instruction":"接續前一步「合理分組」成果，先指出錯誤主張「隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：組內變異不等於長期全部變異。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Rational subgroups artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Within-group variation is not all long-term variation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動；組內變異不等於長期全部變異。","observationEn":"Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect; Within-group variation is not all long-term variation.","failure":"若採用「隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「合理分組」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「組內變異不等於長期全部變異」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Rational subgroups, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Within-group variation is not all long-term variation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-04-k1","title":"合理分組／物理與模型","titleEn":"Rational subgroups / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：組內變異不等於長期全部變異。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Within-group variation is not all long-term variation."},{"id":"a095-v8-04-k2","title":"合理分組／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Rational subgroups / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定」與「分組方式決定控制圖可看見的變動」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages\" is not equivalent to \"Subgrouping determines which changes a chart can detect\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「合理分組」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Rational subgroups?","options":["組內變異不等於長期全部變異","隨機混合不同腔室讓平均更穩定","量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異"],"optionsEn":["Within-group variation is not all long-term variation","Mixing chambers randomly to stabilize averages","Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals"],"answer":0,"explanation":"組內變異不等於長期全部變異；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Within-group variation is not all long-term variation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-04"],"title":"量測系統：建立模型","titleEn":"Measurement system: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Measurement noise affects estimated process variation.","instruction":"比較重複量測與片間差異，估計儀器噪聲占比。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare repeat measurements with wafer variation. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計；儀器偏差不會因大量重測自動消失。","observationEn":"Measurement noise affects estimated process variation; Repeated measurements do not remove instrument bias.","failure":"若採用「量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「量測系統」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計。","checkEn":"Submit the Measurement system diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Measurement noise affects estimated process variation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-05-k1","title":"量測系統／物理與模型","titleEn":"Measurement system / Physics and model","text":"機制：量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計。","textEn":"Mechanism: Measurement noise affects estimated process variation."},{"id":"a095-v8-05-k2","title":"量測系統／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Measurement system / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測系統」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Measurement system, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數","量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計","量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異"],"optionsEn":["Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size","Measurement noise affects estimated process variation","Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals"],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Measurement noise affects estimated process variation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-05"],"title":"量測系統：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Measurement system: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals.","instruction":"接續前一步「量測系統」成果，先指出錯誤主張「量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：儀器偏差不會因大量重測自動消失。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Measurement system artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Repeated measurements do not remove instrument bias. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計；儀器偏差不會因大量重測自動消失。","observationEn":"Measurement noise affects estimated process variation; Repeated measurements do not remove instrument bias.","failure":"若採用「量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「量測系統」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「儀器偏差不會因大量重測自動消失」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Measurement system, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Repeated measurements do not remove instrument bias\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-06-k1","title":"量測系統／物理與模型","titleEn":"Measurement system / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：儀器偏差不會因大量重測自動消失。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Repeated measurements do not remove instrument bias."},{"id":"a095-v8-06-k2","title":"量測系統／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Measurement system / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異」與「量測噪聲會影響製程變異估計」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals\" is not equivalent to \"Measurement noise affects estimated process variation\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「量測系統」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Measurement system?","options":["量測數字有小數點就忽略量具變異","把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數","儀器偏差不會因大量重測自動消失"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring gauge variation because readings have decimals","Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size","Repeated measurements do not remove instrument bias"],"answer":2,"explanation":"儀器偏差不會因大量重測自動消失；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Repeated measurements do not remove instrument bias. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a095-stage02","order":2,"title":"基線期間 → 個別值與移動極差","titleEn":"Baseline period to Individuals and moving range","description":"把「基線期間」「Xbar 與 R」「個別值與移動極差」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Baseline period, Xbar and range, Individuals and moving range.","steps":[{"id":"a095-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-06"],"title":"基線期間：建立模型","titleEn":"Baseline period: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「基線需要代表同一運作條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions.","instruction":"標出已知維護、改版和异常，建立可追溯基線。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark maintenance, changes and anomalies in a traceable baseline. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"基線需要代表同一運作條件；已知特殊原因應留可追溯紀錄。","observationEn":"A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions; Known special causes need traceable records.","failure":"若採用「把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「基線期間」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：基線需要代表同一運作條件。","checkEn":"Submit the Baseline period diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-07-k1","title":"基線期間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Baseline period / Physics and model","text":"機制：基線需要代表同一運作條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions."},{"id":"a095-v8-07-k2","title":"基線期間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Baseline period / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基線期間」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Baseline period, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["基線需要代表同一運作條件","把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數","只看平均圖就核准製程穩定"],"optionsEn":["A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions","Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size","Approving stability from the mean chart alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"基線需要代表同一運作條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-07"],"title":"基線期間：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Baseline period: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size.","instruction":"接續前一步「基線期間」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：已知特殊原因應留可追溯紀錄。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Baseline period artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Known special causes need traceable records. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"基線需要代表同一運作條件；已知特殊原因應留可追溯紀錄。","observationEn":"A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions; Known special causes need traceable records.","failure":"若採用「把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「基線期間」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「已知特殊原因應留可追溯紀錄」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Baseline period, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Known special causes need traceable records\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-08-k1","title":"基線期間／物理與模型","titleEn":"Baseline period / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：已知特殊原因應留可追溯紀錄。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Known special causes need traceable records."},{"id":"a095-v8-08-k2","title":"基線期間／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Baseline period / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數」與「基線需要代表同一運作條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size\" is not equivalent to \"A baseline must represent comparable operating conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「基線期間」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Baseline period?","options":["只看平均圖就核准製程穩定","已知特殊原因應留可追溯紀錄","把所有歷史混在一起增加樣本數"],"optionsEn":["Approving stability from the mean chart alone","Known special causes need traceable records","Pooling incompatible history solely to increase sample size"],"answer":1,"explanation":"已知特殊原因應留可追溯紀錄；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Known special causes need traceable records. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-08"],"title":"Xbar 與 R：建立模型","titleEn":"Xbar and range: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「平均穩定不代表散布穩定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Stable means do not imply stable dispersion.","instruction":"對假設小組計算平均與極差，分開位置及散布警報。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Calculate subgroup means/ranges and separate location/spread alarms. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"平均穩定不代表散布穩定；組大小變動會影響控制限。","observationEn":"Stable means do not imply stable dispersion; Changing subgroup size changes limits.","failure":"若採用「只看平均圖就核准製程穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Approving stability from the mean chart alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「Xbar 與 R」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：平均穩定不代表散布穩定。","checkEn":"Submit the Xbar and range diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Stable means do not imply stable dispersion.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-09-k1","title":"Xbar 與 R／物理與模型","titleEn":"Xbar and range / Physics and model","text":"機制：平均穩定不代表散布穩定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Stable means do not imply stable dispersion."},{"id":"a095-v8-09-k2","title":"Xbar 與 R／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Xbar and range / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只看平均圖就核准製程穩定」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Approving stability from the mean chart alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「Xbar 與 R」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Xbar and range, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只看平均圖就核准製程穩定","排序大小後再算移動極差","平均穩定不代表散布穩定"],"optionsEn":["Approving stability from the mean chart alone","Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges","Stable means do not imply stable dispersion"],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均穩定不代表散布穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Stable means do not imply stable dispersion. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-09"],"title":"Xbar 與 R：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Xbar and range: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只看平均圖就核准製程穩定」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Approving stability from the mean chart alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「Xbar 與 R」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只看平均圖就核准製程穩定」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：組大小變動會影響控制限。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Xbar and range artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Approving stability from the mean chart alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Changing subgroup size changes limits. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"平均穩定不代表散布穩定；組大小變動會影響控制限。","observationEn":"Stable means do not imply stable dispersion; Changing subgroup size changes limits.","failure":"若採用「只看平均圖就核准製程穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Approving stability from the mean chart alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「Xbar 與 R」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「組大小變動會影響控制限」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Xbar and range, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Changing subgroup size changes limits\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-10-k1","title":"Xbar 與 R／物理與模型","titleEn":"Xbar and range / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：組大小變動會影響控制限。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Changing subgroup size changes limits."},{"id":"a095-v8-10-k2","title":"Xbar 與 R／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Xbar and range / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只看平均圖就核准製程穩定」與「平均穩定不代表散布穩定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Approving stability from the mean chart alone\" is not equivalent to \"Stable means do not imply stable dispersion\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「Xbar 與 R」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Xbar and range?","options":["組大小變動會影響控制限","只看平均圖就核准製程穩定","排序大小後再算移動極差"],"optionsEn":["Changing subgroup size changes limits","Approving stability from the mean chart alone","Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges"],"answer":0,"explanation":"組大小變動會影響控制限；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Changing subgroup size changes limits. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-10"],"title":"個別值與移動極差：建立模型","titleEn":"Individuals and moving range: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「時間順序是移動極差的必要條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Time order is essential to moving ranges.","instruction":"排列一次一筆的時間序列並計算相鄰差異。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Order individual observations and compute successive differences. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"時間順序是移動極差的必要條件；移動極差也受自相關影響。","observationEn":"Time order is essential to moving ranges; Autocorrelation affects moving ranges.","failure":"若採用「排序大小後再算移動極差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「個別值與移動極差」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：時間順序是移動極差的必要條件。","checkEn":"Submit the Individuals and moving range diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Time order is essential to moving ranges.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-11-k1","title":"個別值與移動極差／物理與模型","titleEn":"Individuals and moving range / Physics and model","text":"機制：時間順序是移動極差的必要條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Time order is essential to moving ranges."},{"id":"a095-v8-11-k2","title":"個別值與移動極差／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Individuals and moving range / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「排序大小後再算移動極差」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「個別值與移動極差」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Individuals and moving range, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["一片多缺陷就算多片不合格","時間順序是移動極差的必要條件","排序大小後再算移動極差"],"optionsEn":["Counting several defects as several defective wafers","Time order is essential to moving ranges","Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges"],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間順序是移動極差的必要條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Time order is essential to moving ranges. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-11"],"title":"個別值與移動極差：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Individuals and moving range: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「排序大小後再算移動極差」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges.","instruction":"接續前一步「個別值與移動極差」成果，先指出錯誤主張「排序大小後再算移動極差」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：移動極差也受自相關影響。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Individuals and moving range artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Autocorrelation affects moving ranges. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"時間順序是移動極差的必要條件；移動極差也受自相關影響。","observationEn":"Time order is essential to moving ranges; Autocorrelation affects moving ranges.","failure":"若採用「排序大小後再算移動極差」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「個別值與移動極差」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「移動極差也受自相關影響」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Individuals and moving range, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Autocorrelation affects moving ranges\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-12-k1","title":"個別值與移動極差／物理與模型","titleEn":"Individuals and moving range / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：移動極差也受自相關影響。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Autocorrelation affects moving ranges."},{"id":"a095-v8-12-k2","title":"個別值與移動極差／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Individuals and moving range / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「排序大小後再算移動極差」與「時間順序是移動極差的必要條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges\" is not equivalent to \"Time order is essential to moving ranges\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「個別值與移動極差」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Individuals and moving range?","options":["排序大小後再算移動極差","一片多缺陷就算多片不合格","移動極差也受自相關影響"],"optionsEn":["Sorting by value before calculating moving ranges","Counting several defects as several defective wafers","Autocorrelation affects moving ranges"],"answer":2,"explanation":"移動極差也受自相關影響；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Autocorrelation affects moving ranges. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a095-stage03","order":3,"title":"屬性資料 → 自相關","titleEn":"Attribute data to Autocorrelation","description":"把「屬性資料」「EWMA」「自相關」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Attribute data, Exponentially weighted averages, Autocorrelation.","steps":[{"id":"a095-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-12"],"title":"屬性資料：建立模型","titleEn":"Attribute data: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ.","instruction":"比較每片缺陷數與不合格片比例，選擇合適分母。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate defects per wafer from fraction defective with denominators. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布；樣本數改變會影響比例圖控制限。","observationEn":"Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ; Sample size changes proportion-chart limits.","failure":"若採用「一片多缺陷就算多片不合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Counting several defects as several defective wafers\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「屬性資料」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布。","checkEn":"Submit the Attribute data diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-13-k1","title":"屬性資料／物理與模型","titleEn":"Attribute data / Physics and model","text":"機制：缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布。","textEn":"Mechanism: Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ."},{"id":"a095-v8-13-k2","title":"屬性資料／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Attribute data / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一片多缺陷就算多片不合格」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Counting several defects as several defective wafers."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「屬性資料」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Attribute data, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布","一片多缺陷就算多片不合格","λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變"],"optionsEn":["Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ","Counting several defects as several defective wafers","Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change"],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-13"],"title":"屬性資料：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Attribute data: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一片多缺陷就算多片不合格」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Counting several defects as several defective wafers.","instruction":"接續前一步「屬性資料」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一片多缺陷就算多片不合格」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：樣本數改變會影響比例圖控制限。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Attribute data artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Counting several defects as several defective wafers\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sample size changes proportion-chart limits. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布；樣本數改變會影響比例圖控制限。","observationEn":"Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ; Sample size changes proportion-chart limits.","failure":"若採用「一片多缺陷就算多片不合格」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Counting several defects as several defective wafers\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「屬性資料」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「樣本數改變會影響比例圖控制限」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Attribute data, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sample size changes proportion-chart limits\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-14-k1","title":"屬性資料／物理與模型","titleEn":"Attribute data / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：樣本數改變會影響比例圖控制限。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sample size changes proportion-chart limits."},{"id":"a095-v8-14-k2","title":"屬性資料／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Attribute data / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一片多缺陷就算多片不合格」與「缺陷數與不合格單位数不是同一分布」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Counting several defects as several defective wafers\" is not equivalent to \"Defect counts and defective-unit counts differ\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「屬性資料」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Attribute data?","options":["λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變","樣本數改變會影響比例圖控制限","一片多缺陷就算多片不合格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change","Sample size changes proportion-chart limits","Counting several defects as several defective wafers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"樣本數改變會影響比例圖控制限；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sample size changes proportion-chart limits. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-14"],"title":"EWMA：建立模型","titleEn":"Exponentially weighted averages: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Smoothing weights control memory and response.","instruction":"用自訂 λ 計算小偏移的 EWMA，畫反應速度。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Calculate EWMA for a small hypothetical shift with chosen lambda. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應；EWMA 初始值影響早期警報。","observationEn":"Smoothing weights control memory and response; EWMA initialization affects early alarms.","failure":"若採用「λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「EWMA」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應。","checkEn":"Submit the Exponentially weighted averages diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Smoothing weights control memory and response.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-15-k1","title":"EWMA／物理與模型","titleEn":"Exponentially weighted averages / Physics and model","text":"機制：平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應。","textEn":"Mechanism: Smoothing weights control memory and response."},{"id":"a095-v8-15-k2","title":"EWMA／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Exponentially weighted averages / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「EWMA」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Exponentially weighted averages, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變","相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為","平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應"],"optionsEn":["Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change","Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior","Smoothing weights control memory and response"],"answer":2,"explanation":"平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Smoothing weights control memory and response. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-15"],"title":"EWMA：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Exponentially weighted averages: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change.","instruction":"接續前一步「EWMA」成果，先指出錯誤主張「λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：EWMA 初始值影響早期警報。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Exponentially weighted averages artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: EWMA initialization affects early alarms. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應；EWMA 初始值影響早期警報。","observationEn":"Smoothing weights control memory and response; EWMA initialization affects early alarms.","failure":"若採用「λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「EWMA」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「EWMA 初始值影響早期警報」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Exponentially weighted averages, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"EWMA initialization affects early alarms\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-16-k1","title":"EWMA／物理與模型","titleEn":"Exponentially weighted averages / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：EWMA 初始值影響早期警報。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: EWMA initialization affects early alarms."},{"id":"a095-v8-16-k2","title":"EWMA／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Exponentially weighted averages / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變」與「平滑權重控制記憶長度與反應」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change\" is not equivalent to \"Smoothing weights control memory and response\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「EWMA」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Exponentially weighted averages?","options":["EWMA 初始值影響早期警報","λ 越小就能瞬間看出所有改變","相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為"],"optionsEn":["EWMA initialization affects early alarms","Assuming smaller lambda instantly detects every change","Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior"],"answer":0,"explanation":"EWMA 初始值影響早期警報；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"EWMA initialization affects early alarms. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-16"],"title":"自相關：建立模型","titleEn":"Autocorrelation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates.","instruction":"比較交替、緩慢漂移與獨立序列的相鄰相關。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare alternating, drifting and independent sequences. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率；去除相關性需要可驗證的模型。","observationEn":"Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates; Removing correlation needs a validated model.","failure":"若採用「相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「自相關」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率。","checkEn":"Submit the Autocorrelation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-17-k1","title":"自相關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Autocorrelation / Physics and model","text":"機制：相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率。","textEn":"Mechanism: Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates."},{"id":"a095-v8-17-k2","title":"自相關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Autocorrelation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自相關」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Autocorrelation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證","相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率","相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為"],"optionsEn":["Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence","Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates","Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior"],"answer":1,"explanation":"相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-17"],"title":"自相關：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Autocorrelation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior.","instruction":"接續前一步「自相關」成果，先指出錯誤主張「相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：去除相關性需要可驗證的模型。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Autocorrelation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Removing correlation needs a validated model. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率；去除相關性需要可驗證的模型。","observationEn":"Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates; Removing correlation needs a validated model.","failure":"若採用「相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「自相關」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「去除相關性需要可驗證的模型」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Autocorrelation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Removing correlation needs a validated model\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-18-k1","title":"自相關／物理與模型","titleEn":"Autocorrelation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：去除相關性需要可驗證的模型。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Removing correlation needs a validated model."},{"id":"a095-v8-18-k2","title":"自相關／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Autocorrelation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為」與「相關資料可能改變控制圖誤警率」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior\" is not equivalent to \"Correlated data can alter chart false-alarm rates\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「自相關」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Autocorrelation?","options":["相同直方圖就代表相同時間行為","任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證","去除相關性需要可驗證的模型"],"optionsEn":["Equating identical histograms with identical temporal behavior","Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence","Removing correlation needs a validated model"],"answer":2,"explanation":"去除相關性需要可驗證的模型；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Removing correlation needs a validated model. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a095-stage04","order":4,"title":"能力指標 → 變更管理","titleEn":"Capability indices to Change management","description":"把「能力指標」「失控處置」「變更管理」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Capability indices, Out-of-control action, Change management.","steps":[{"id":"a095-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-18"],"title":"能力指標：建立模型","titleEn":"Capability indices: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability.","instruction":"用假設平均與標準差算 Cp、Cpk，先驗證穩定與分布。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設穩定且近似常態的製程，規格 LSL=95、USL=105，平均 μ=101、組內標準差 σ=1（使用同一單位）。Cp=(105−95)/(6σ)=1.667；Cpk=min((105−101)/(3σ),(101−95)/(3σ))=1.333。此組假設尚未由資料驗證，控制界限也不等於 95/105 規格界限。","instructionEn":"Compute hypothetical Cp/Cpk after checking stability and distribution. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a stable approximately normal process with LSL=95, USL=105, mean μ=101 and within-process σ=1 in common units. Cp=10/(6σ)=1.667; Cpk=min(4/(3σ),6/(3σ))=1.333. These assumptions still need data support; control limits are not the 95/105 specification limits.","observation":"能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件；非正態資料需要合適分布處理。","observationEn":"Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability; Nonnormal data need suitable distribution handling.","failure":"若採用「任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「能力指標」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件。\n算例驗收：驗算 Cp 與 Cpk，指出偏離規格中心使 Cpk 低於 Cp，並保留穩定性驗證步驟。","checkEn":"Submit the Capability indices diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify Cp and Cpk, explain the reduction from off-centering and retain a process-stability check.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-19-k1","title":"能力指標／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capability indices / Physics and model","text":"機制：能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件。","textEn":"Mechanism: Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability."},{"id":"a095-v8-19-k2","title":"能力指標／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capability indices / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證」。\n假設數值與推算：假設穩定且近似常態的製程，規格 LSL=95、USL=105，平均 μ=101、組內標準差 σ=1（使用同一單位）。Cp=(105−95)/(6σ)=1.667；Cpk=min((105−101)/(3σ),(101−95)/(3σ))=1.333。此組假設尚未由資料驗證，控制界限也不等於 95/105 規格界限。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a stable approximately normal process with LSL=95, USL=105, mean μ=101 and within-process σ=1 in common units. Cp=10/(6σ)=1.667; Cpk=min(4/(3σ),6/(3σ))=1.333. These assumptions still need data support; control limits are not the 95/105 specification limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「能力指標」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Capability indices, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件","任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證","所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用"],"optionsEn":["Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability","Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence","Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-19"],"title":"能力指標：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Capability indices: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence.","instruction":"接續前一步「能力指標」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：非正態資料需要合適分布處理。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Capability indices artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Nonnormal data need suitable distribution handling. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件；非正態資料需要合適分布處理。","observationEn":"Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability; Nonnormal data need suitable distribution handling.","failure":"若採用「任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「能力指標」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「非正態資料需要合適分布處理」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Capability indices, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Nonnormal data need suitable distribution handling\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-20-k1","title":"能力指標／物理與模型","titleEn":"Capability indices / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：非正態資料需要合適分布處理。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Nonnormal data need suitable distribution handling."},{"id":"a095-v8-20-k2","title":"能力指標／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Capability indices / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證」與「能力指標需要適用假設與穩定條件」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence\" is not equivalent to \"Capability requires suitable assumptions and stability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「能力指標」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Capability indices?","options":["所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用","非正態資料需要合適分布處理","任意失控序列也可直接宣稱 Cpk 保證"],"optionsEn":["Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable","Nonnormal data need suitable distribution handling","Claiming capability guarantees for an unstable sequence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"非正態資料需要合適分布處理；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Nonnormal data need suitable distribution handling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-20"],"title":"失控處置：建立模型","titleEn":"Out-of-control action: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof.","instruction":"設計暫停、隔離、複測與原因調查的決策流程。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Design hold, containment, remeasurement and investigation decisions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢；複測不能抹去原始警報。","observationEn":"An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof; Retesting must not erase original alarms.","failure":"若採用「所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「失控處置」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢。","checkEn":"Submit the Out-of-control action diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-21-k1","title":"失控處置／物理與模型","titleEn":"Out-of-control action / Physics and model","text":"機制：警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢。","textEn":"Mechanism: An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof."},{"id":"a095-v8-21-k2","title":"失控處置／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Out-of-control action / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「失控處置」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Out-of-control action, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用","每次警報就放寬控制限","警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢"],"optionsEn":["Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable","Widening limits after every alarm","An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof"],"answer":2,"explanation":"警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-21"],"title":"失控處置：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Out-of-control action: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable.","instruction":"接續前一步「失控處置」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：複測不能抹去原始警報。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Out-of-control action artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Retesting must not erase original alarms. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢；複測不能抹去原始警報。","observationEn":"An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof; Retesting must not erase original alarms.","failure":"若採用「所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「失控處置」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「複測不能抹去原始警報」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Out-of-control action, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Retesting must not erase original alarms\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-22-k1","title":"失控處置／物理與模型","titleEn":"Out-of-control action / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：複測不能抹去原始警報。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Retesting must not erase original alarms."},{"id":"a095-v8-22-k2","title":"失控處置／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Out-of-control action / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用」與「警報是調查信號，不是自動證明產品報廢」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable\" is not equivalent to \"An alarm triggers investigation, not automatic scrap proof\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「失控處置」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Out-of-control action?","options":["複測不能抹去原始警報","所有超控制限產品立即判定無法使用","每次警報就放寬控制限"],"optionsEn":["Retesting must not erase original alarms","Declaring every control-limit exceedance unusable","Widening limits after every alarm"],"answer":0,"explanation":"複測不能抹去原始警報；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Retesting must not erase original alarms. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-22"],"title":"變更管理：建立模型","titleEn":"Change management: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「重設控制線不能取代原因改善」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Resetting limits does not replace cause correction.","instruction":"保存控制限版本、重新基線理由及舊新並行比較。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Preserve limit versions, rebaseline reasons and parallel comparison. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"重設控制線不能取代原因改善；新舊版本比較需防止挑選有利期間。","observationEn":"Resetting limits does not replace cause correction; Version comparisons must avoid cherry-picked periods.","failure":"若採用「每次警報就放寬控制限」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Widening limits after every alarm\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「變更管理」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：重設控制線不能取代原因改善。","checkEn":"Submit the Change management diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Resetting limits does not replace cause correction.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-23-k1","title":"變更管理／物理與模型","titleEn":"Change management / Physics and model","text":"機制：重設控制線不能取代原因改善。","textEn":"Mechanism: Resetting limits does not replace cause correction."},{"id":"a095-v8-23-k2","title":"變更管理／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Change management / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「每次警報就放寬控制限」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Widening limits after every alarm."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「變更管理」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Change management, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把上下規格限直接當控制限","重設控制線不能取代原因改善","每次警報就放寬控制限"],"optionsEn":["Using specification limits as control limits","Resetting limits does not replace cause correction","Widening limits after every alarm"],"answer":1,"explanation":"重設控制線不能取代原因改善；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Resetting limits does not replace cause correction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a095-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-spc","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a095-v8-23"],"title":"變更管理：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Change management: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「每次警報就放寬控制限」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Widening limits after every alarm.","instruction":"接續前一步「變更管理」成果，先指出錯誤主張「每次警報就放寬控制限」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：新舊版本比較需防止挑選有利期間。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Change management artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Widening limits after every alarm\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Version comparisons must avoid cherry-picked periods. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"重設控制線不能取代原因改善；新舊版本比較需防止挑選有利期間。","observationEn":"Resetting limits does not replace cause correction; Version comparisons must avoid cherry-picked periods.","failure":"若採用「每次警報就放寬控制限」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Widening limits after every alarm\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「變更管理」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「新舊版本比較需防止挑選有利期間」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Change management, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Version comparisons must avoid cherry-picked periods\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a095-v8-24-k1","title":"變更管理／物理與模型","titleEn":"Change management / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：新舊版本比較需防止挑選有利期間。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Version comparisons must avoid cherry-picked periods."},{"id":"a095-v8-24-k2","title":"變更管理／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Change management / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「每次警報就放寬控制限」與「重設控制線不能取代原因改善」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Widening limits after every alarm\" is not equivalent to \"Resetting limits does not replace cause correction\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「變更管理」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Change management?","options":["每次警報就放寬控制限","把上下規格限直接當控制限","新舊版本比較需防止挑選有利期間"],"optionsEn":["Widening limits after every alarm","Using specification limits as control limits","Version comparisons must avoid cherry-picked periods"],"answer":2,"explanation":"新舊版本比較需防止挑選有利期間；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Version comparisons must avoid cherry-picked periods. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"},{"id":"a096","title":"先進製程控制與虛擬量測","titleEn":"Advanced process control and virtual metrology","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從閉迴路邊界、時間切割到版本回復：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Closed-loop boundary and Temporal splitting to Version rollback: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["閉迴路邊界","特徵萃取","域外偵測","控制限幅"],"labelsEn":["Closed-loop boundary","Feature extraction","Out-of-domain detection","Control bounds"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a096-stage01","order":1,"title":"閉迴路邊界 → 資料時間戳","titleEn":"Closed-loop boundary to Data timestamps","description":"把「閉迴路邊界」「Run-to-run 控制」「資料時間戳」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Closed-loop boundary, Run-to-run control, Data timestamps.","steps":[{"id":"a096-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"閉迴路邊界：建立模型","titleEn":"Closed-loop boundary: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor.","instruction":"畫設定、製程、實測、估測及控制器的訊號方向。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw setpoint, process, measurement, prediction and controller signal paths. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器；回授與前饋使用不同資訊時點。","observationEn":"Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor; Feedback and feedforward use different timing.","failure":"若採用「預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling a prediction a physical measurement\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「閉迴路邊界」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器。","checkEn":"Submit the Closed-loop boundary diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-01-k1","title":"閉迴路邊界／物理與模型","titleEn":"Closed-loop boundary / Physics and model","text":"機制：虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器。","textEn":"Mechanism: Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor."},{"id":"a096-v8-01-k2","title":"閉迴路邊界／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Closed-loop boundary / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling a prediction a physical measurement."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「閉迴路邊界」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Closed-loop boundary, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器","預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到","不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正"],"optionsEn":["Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor","Calling a prediction a physical measurement","Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign"],"answer":0,"explanation":"虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-01"],"title":"閉迴路邊界：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Closed-loop boundary: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling a prediction a physical measurement.","instruction":"接續前一步「閉迴路邊界」成果，先指出錯誤主張「預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：回授與前饋使用不同資訊時點。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Closed-loop boundary artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling a prediction a physical measurement\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Feedback and feedforward use different timing. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器；回授與前饋使用不同資訊時點。","observationEn":"Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor; Feedback and feedforward use different timing.","failure":"若採用「預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling a prediction a physical measurement\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「閉迴路邊界」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「回授與前饋使用不同資訊時點」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Closed-loop boundary, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Feedback and feedforward use different timing\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-02-k1","title":"閉迴路邊界／物理與模型","titleEn":"Closed-loop boundary / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：回授與前饋使用不同資訊時點。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Feedback and feedforward use different timing."},{"id":"a096-v8-02-k2","title":"閉迴路邊界／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Closed-loop boundary / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到」與「虛擬量測是推估，不是新增實體感測器」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling a prediction a physical measurement\" is not equivalent to \"Virtual metrology is inference, not another physical sensor\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「閉迴路邊界」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Closed-loop boundary?","options":["不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正","回授與前饋使用不同資訊時點","預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到"],"optionsEn":["Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign","Feedback and feedforward use different timing","Calling a prediction a physical measurement"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回授與前饋使用不同資訊時點；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Feedback and feedforward use different timing. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-02"],"title":"Run-to-run 控制：建立模型","titleEn":"Run-to-run control: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign.","instruction":"用假設線性增益將上一片誤差換成下一片小幅修正。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設無延遲、無雜訊的教學模型 y=2u+1，現在 u=4 得 y=9，目標 y*=11。以模型反算 Δu=(11−9)/2=1，故下次 u=5、預測 y=11。若真實斜率不是 2 或量測有延遲，這次修正可能過度；這是紙上控制練習，不能作機台指令。","instructionEn":"Convert prior-wafer error to a bounded next-run correction. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a delay-free noise-free teaching model y=2u+1. Current u=4 gives y=9; target y*=11. Model inversion gives Δu=(11−9)/2=1, so next u=5 predicts y=11. A different real slope or delayed measurement can cause overcorrection. This is a paper control exercise, not a machine command.","observation":"控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向；增益估計錯誤可放大振盪。","observationEn":"Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign; Gain-estimation errors can amplify oscillation.","failure":"若採用「不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「Run-to-run 控制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向。\n算例驗收：驗算 u=5，並以斜率改為 3 的另一假設檢查模型失配為何改變控制增益。","checkEn":"Submit the Run-to-run control diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify u=5 and use an alternative slope of 3 to explain why model mismatch changes the required control gain.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-03-k1","title":"Run-to-run 控制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Run-to-run control / Physics and model","text":"機制：控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向。","textEn":"Mechanism: Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign."},{"id":"a096-v8-03-k2","title":"Run-to-run 控制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Run-to-run control / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正」。\n假設數值與推算：假設無延遲、無雜訊的教學模型 y=2u+1，現在 u=4 得 y=9，目標 y*=11。以模型反算 Δu=(11−9)/2=1，故下次 u=5、預測 y=11。若真實斜率不是 2 或量測有延遲，這次修正可能過度；這是紙上控制練習，不能作機台指令。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a delay-free noise-free teaching model y=2u+1. Current u=4 gives y=9; target y*=11. Model inversion gives Δu=(11−9)/2=1, so next u=5 predicts y=11. A different real slope or delayed measurement can cause overcorrection. This is a paper control exercise, not a machine command."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「Run-to-run 控制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Run-to-run control, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正","把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵","控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向"],"optionsEn":["Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign","Using future measurements as real-time features","Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign"],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-03"],"title":"Run-to-run 控制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Run-to-run control: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign.","instruction":"接續前一步「Run-to-run 控制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：增益估計錯誤可放大振盪。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Run-to-run control artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Gain-estimation errors can amplify oscillation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向；增益估計錯誤可放大振盪。","observationEn":"Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign; Gain-estimation errors can amplify oscillation.","failure":"若採用「不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「Run-to-run 控制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「增益估計錯誤可放大振盪」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Run-to-run control, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Gain-estimation errors can amplify oscillation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-04-k1","title":"Run-to-run 控制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Run-to-run control / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：增益估計錯誤可放大振盪。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Gain-estimation errors can amplify oscillation."},{"id":"a096-v8-04-k2","title":"Run-to-run 控制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Run-to-run control / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正」與「控制更新有延遲且需要製程增益方向」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign\" is not equivalent to \"Updates have delay and need the correct gain sign\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「Run-to-run 控制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Run-to-run control?","options":["增益估計錯誤可放大振盪","不知增益正負就直接反覆加大修正","把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵"],"optionsEn":["Gain-estimation errors can amplify oscillation","Escalating corrections without knowing gain sign","Using future measurements as real-time features"],"answer":0,"explanation":"增益估計錯誤可放大振盪；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Gain-estimation errors can amplify oscillation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-04"],"title":"資料時間戳：建立模型","titleEn":"Data timestamps: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Training features must be available at prediction time.","instruction":"對齊設備訊號、晶圓 ID 與量測回傳時間。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Align tool signals, wafer IDs and metrology return time. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得；時鐘偏差可能造成錯誤對齊。","observationEn":"Training features must be available at prediction time; Clock offsets cause incorrect alignment.","failure":"若採用「把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using future measurements as real-time features\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「資料時間戳」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得。","checkEn":"Submit the Data timestamps diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Training features must be available at prediction time.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-05-k1","title":"資料時間戳／物理與模型","titleEn":"Data timestamps / Physics and model","text":"機制：訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得。","textEn":"Mechanism: Training features must be available at prediction time."},{"id":"a096-v8-05-k2","title":"資料時間戳／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Data timestamps / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using future measurements as real-time features."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資料時間戳」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Data timestamps, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位","訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得","把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵"],"optionsEn":["Concatenating every value without unit checks","Training features must be available at prediction time","Using future measurements as real-time features"],"answer":1,"explanation":"訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Training features must be available at prediction time. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-05"],"title":"資料時間戳：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Data timestamps: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using future measurements as real-time features.","instruction":"接續前一步「資料時間戳」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：時鐘偏差可能造成錯誤對齊。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Data timestamps artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using future measurements as real-time features\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Clock offsets cause incorrect alignment. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得；時鐘偏差可能造成錯誤對齊。","observationEn":"Training features must be available at prediction time; Clock offsets cause incorrect alignment.","failure":"若採用「把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using future measurements as real-time features\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「資料時間戳」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「時鐘偏差可能造成錯誤對齊」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Data timestamps, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Clock offsets cause incorrect alignment\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-06-k1","title":"資料時間戳／物理與模型","titleEn":"Data timestamps / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：時鐘偏差可能造成錯誤對齊。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Clock offsets cause incorrect alignment."},{"id":"a096-v8-06-k2","title":"資料時間戳／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Data timestamps / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵」與「訓練特徵必須在預測時已可取得」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using future measurements as real-time features\" is not equivalent to \"Training features must be available at prediction time\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「資料時間戳」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Data timestamps?","options":["把未來量測結果放入即時預測特徵","任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位","時鐘偏差可能造成錯誤對齊"],"optionsEn":["Using future measurements as real-time features","Concatenating every value without unit checks","Clock offsets cause incorrect alignment"],"answer":2,"explanation":"時鐘偏差可能造成錯誤對齊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Clock offsets cause incorrect alignment. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a096-stage02","order":2,"title":"特徵萃取 → 不確定度","titleEn":"Feature extraction to Uncertainty estimates","description":"把「特徵萃取」「時間切割」「不確定度」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Feature extraction, Temporal splitting, Uncertainty estimates.","steps":[{"id":"a096-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-06"],"title":"特徵萃取：建立模型","titleEn":"Feature extraction: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「統計特徵要有對應的製程語意」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Statistical features need process meaning.","instruction":"由假設腔室曲線抽取穩態、斜率與積分，保留物理單位。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Extract steady value, slope and integral from chamber traces with units. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"統計特徵要有對應的製程語意；過度平滑會刪掉短暫異常。","observationEn":"Statistical features need process meaning; Oversmoothing removes transient anomalies.","failure":"若採用「任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Concatenating every value without unit checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「特徵萃取」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：統計特徵要有對應的製程語意。","checkEn":"Submit the Feature extraction diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Statistical features need process meaning.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-07-k1","title":"特徵萃取／物理與模型","titleEn":"Feature extraction / Physics and model","text":"機制：統計特徵要有對應的製程語意。","textEn":"Mechanism: Statistical features need process meaning."},{"id":"a096-v8-07-k2","title":"特徵萃取／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Feature extraction / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Concatenating every value without unit checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「特徵萃取」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Feature extraction, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["統計特徵要有對應的製程語意","任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位","同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化"],"optionsEn":["Statistical features need process meaning","Concatenating every value without unit checks","Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides"],"answer":0,"explanation":"統計特徵要有對應的製程語意；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Statistical features need process meaning. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-07"],"title":"特徵萃取：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Feature extraction: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Concatenating every value without unit checks.","instruction":"接續前一步「特徵萃取」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：過度平滑會刪掉短暫異常。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Feature extraction artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Concatenating every value without unit checks\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Oversmoothing removes transient anomalies. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"統計特徵要有對應的製程語意；過度平滑會刪掉短暫異常。","observationEn":"Statistical features need process meaning; Oversmoothing removes transient anomalies.","failure":"若採用「任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Concatenating every value without unit checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「特徵萃取」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「過度平滑會刪掉短暫異常」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Feature extraction, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Oversmoothing removes transient anomalies\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-08-k1","title":"特徵萃取／物理與模型","titleEn":"Feature extraction / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：過度平滑會刪掉短暫異常。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Oversmoothing removes transient anomalies."},{"id":"a096-v8-08-k2","title":"特徵萃取／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Feature extraction / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位」與「統計特徵要有對應的製程語意」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Concatenating every value without unit checks\" is not equivalent to \"Statistical features need process meaning\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「特徵萃取」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Feature extraction?","options":["同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化","過度平滑會刪掉短暫異常","任意拼接所有數值不檢查單位"],"optionsEn":["Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides","Oversmoothing removes transient anomalies","Concatenating every value without unit checks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"過度平滑會刪掉短暫異常；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Oversmoothing removes transient anomalies. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-08"],"title":"時間切割：建立模型","titleEn":"Temporal splitting: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information.","instruction":"用前期訓練、後期測試並把同批片放在同一側。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Train on earlier data and test later with lot grouping. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊；維護前後可視為不同資料域。","observationEn":"Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information; Pre/post-maintenance can form different domains.","failure":"若採用「同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「時間切割」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊。","checkEn":"Submit the Temporal splitting diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-09-k1","title":"時間切割／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporal splitting / Physics and model","text":"機制：隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊。","textEn":"Mechanism: Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information."},{"id":"a096-v8-09-k2","title":"時間切割／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporal splitting / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「時間切割」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Temporal splitting, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化","模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋","隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊"],"optionsEn":["Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides","Accepting model confidence without coverage checks","Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information"],"answer":2,"explanation":"隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-09"],"title":"時間切割：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Temporal splitting: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides.","instruction":"接續前一步「時間切割」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：維護前後可視為不同資料域。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Temporal splitting artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pre/post-maintenance can form different domains. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊；維護前後可視為不同資料域。","observationEn":"Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information; Pre/post-maintenance can form different domains.","failure":"若採用「同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「時間切割」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「維護前後可視為不同資料域」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Temporal splitting, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pre/post-maintenance can form different domains\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-10-k1","title":"時間切割／物理與模型","titleEn":"Temporal splitting / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：維護前後可視為不同資料域。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pre/post-maintenance can form different domains."},{"id":"a096-v8-10-k2","title":"時間切割／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Temporal splitting / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化」與「隨機切片可能洩漏相同批次與漂移資訊」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides\" is not equivalent to \"Random wafer splitting can leak lot/drift information\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「時間切割」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Temporal splitting?","options":["維護前後可視為不同資料域","同批高度相似片跨訓練測試宣稱泛化","模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["Pre/post-maintenance can form different domains","Claiming generalization with near-identical lot samples on both sides","Accepting model confidence without coverage checks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"維護前後可視為不同資料域；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pre/post-maintenance can form different domains. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-10"],"title":"不確定度：建立模型","titleEn":"Uncertainty estimates: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「預測區間需要校準而非只給數字」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Prediction intervals need calibration.","instruction":"為每個預測附區間，檢查假設真值落入比例。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Attach intervals and check hypothetical truth coverage. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"預測區間需要校準而非只給數字；異方差代表不同條件有不同誤差。","observationEn":"Prediction intervals need calibration; Heteroscedasticity means condition-dependent error.","failure":"若採用「模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting model confidence without coverage checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「不確定度」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：預測區間需要校準而非只給數字。","checkEn":"Submit the Uncertainty estimates diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Prediction intervals need calibration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-11-k1","title":"不確定度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Uncertainty estimates / Physics and model","text":"機制：預測區間需要校準而非只給數字。","textEn":"Mechanism: Prediction intervals need calibration."},{"id":"a096-v8-11-k2","title":"不確定度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Uncertainty estimates / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Accepting model confidence without coverage checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不確定度」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Uncertainty estimates, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品","預測區間需要校準而非只給數字","模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["Applying low-training-error models to every new product","Prediction intervals need calibration","Accepting model confidence without coverage checks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"預測區間需要校準而非只給數字；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Prediction intervals need calibration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-11"],"title":"不確定度：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Uncertainty estimates: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Accepting model confidence without coverage checks.","instruction":"接續前一步「不確定度」成果，先指出錯誤主張「模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：異方差代表不同條件有不同誤差。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Uncertainty estimates artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Accepting model confidence without coverage checks\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Heteroscedasticity means condition-dependent error. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"預測區間需要校準而非只給數字；異方差代表不同條件有不同誤差。","observationEn":"Prediction intervals need calibration; Heteroscedasticity means condition-dependent error.","failure":"若採用「模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Accepting model confidence without coverage checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「不確定度」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「異方差代表不同條件有不同誤差」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Uncertainty estimates, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Heteroscedasticity means condition-dependent error\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-12-k1","title":"不確定度／物理與模型","titleEn":"Uncertainty estimates / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：異方差代表不同條件有不同誤差。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Heteroscedasticity means condition-dependent error."},{"id":"a096-v8-12-k2","title":"不確定度／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Uncertainty estimates / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋」與「預測區間需要校準而非只給數字」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Accepting model confidence without coverage checks\" is not equivalent to \"Prediction intervals need calibration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「不確定度」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Uncertainty estimates?","options":["模型說有信心就不需查真值覆蓋","訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品","異方差代表不同條件有不同誤差"],"optionsEn":["Accepting model confidence without coverage checks","Applying low-training-error models to every new product","Heteroscedasticity means condition-dependent error"],"answer":2,"explanation":"異方差代表不同條件有不同誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Heteroscedasticity means condition-dependent error. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a096-stage03","order":3,"title":"域外偵測 → 漂移監控","titleEn":"Out-of-domain detection to Drift monitoring","description":"把「域外偵測」「抽樣策略」「漂移監控」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Out-of-domain detection, Sampling strategy, Drift monitoring.","steps":[{"id":"a096-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-12"],"title":"域外偵測：建立模型","titleEn":"Out-of-domain detection: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals.","instruction":"將新配方、維護後及感測器異常和訓練範圍比較。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare new recipes, post-maintenance and sensor faults with training coverage. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效；新材料可能需要完全不同映射。","observationEn":"Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals; New materials may require different mappings.","failure":"若採用「訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying low-training-error models to every new product\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「域外偵測」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效。","checkEn":"Submit the Out-of-domain detection diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-13-k1","title":"域外偵測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Out-of-domain detection / Physics and model","text":"機制：域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效。","textEn":"Mechanism: Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals."},{"id":"a096-v8-13-k2","title":"域外偵測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Out-of-domain detection / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Applying low-training-error models to every new product."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「域外偵測」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Out-of-domain detection, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效","訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品","永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本"],"optionsEn":["Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals","Applying low-training-error models to every new product","Measuring only the most confident predictions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-13"],"title":"域外偵測：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Out-of-domain detection: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Applying low-training-error models to every new product.","instruction":"接續前一步「域外偵測」成果，先指出錯誤主張「訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：新材料可能需要完全不同映射。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Out-of-domain detection artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Applying low-training-error models to every new product\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: New materials may require different mappings. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效；新材料可能需要完全不同映射。","observationEn":"Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals; New materials may require different mappings.","failure":"若採用「訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Applying low-training-error models to every new product\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「域外偵測」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「新材料可能需要完全不同映射」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Out-of-domain detection, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"New materials may require different mappings\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-14-k1","title":"域外偵測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Out-of-domain detection / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：新材料可能需要完全不同映射。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: New materials may require different mappings."},{"id":"a096-v8-14-k2","title":"域外偵測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Out-of-domain detection / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品」與「域外資料可能使小殘差歷史失效」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Applying low-training-error models to every new product\" is not equivalent to \"Out-of-domain data can invalidate good historical residuals\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「域外偵測」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Out-of-domain detection?","options":["永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本","新材料可能需要完全不同映射","訓練誤差小就可套用所有新產品"],"optionsEn":["Measuring only the most confident predictions","New materials may require different mappings","Applying low-training-error models to every new product"],"answer":1,"explanation":"新材料可能需要完全不同映射；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"New materials may require different mappings. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-14"],"title":"抽樣策略：建立模型","titleEn":"Sampling strategy: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions.","instruction":"按不確定度和風險分配假設實測預算，保留隨機查核。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Allocate physical measurements by uncertainty/risk with random audits. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域；標籤延遲會限制主動抽樣更新。","observationEn":"Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions; Label delays constrain active sampling.","failure":"若採用「永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Measuring only the most confident predictions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「抽樣策略」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域。","checkEn":"Submit the Sampling strategy diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-15-k1","title":"抽樣策略／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sampling strategy / Physics and model","text":"機制：主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域。","textEn":"Mechanism: Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions."},{"id":"a096-v8-15-k2","title":"抽樣策略／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sampling strategy / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Measuring only the most confident predictions."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「抽樣策略」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Sampling strategy, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本","只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定","主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域"],"optionsEn":["Measuring only the most confident predictions","Proving model stability from mean inputs alone","Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-15"],"title":"抽樣策略：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Sampling strategy: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Measuring only the most confident predictions.","instruction":"接續前一步「抽樣策略」成果，先指出錯誤主張「永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：標籤延遲會限制主動抽樣更新。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Sampling strategy artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Measuring only the most confident predictions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Label delays constrain active sampling. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域；標籤延遲會限制主動抽樣更新。","observationEn":"Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions; Label delays constrain active sampling.","failure":"若採用「永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Measuring only the most confident predictions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「抽樣策略」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「標籤延遲會限制主動抽樣更新」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Sampling strategy, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Label delays constrain active sampling\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-16-k1","title":"抽樣策略／物理與模型","titleEn":"Sampling strategy / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：標籤延遲會限制主動抽樣更新。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Label delays constrain active sampling."},{"id":"a096-v8-16-k2","title":"抽樣策略／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Sampling strategy / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本」與「主動抽樣仍需避免永久忽略特定區域」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Measuring only the most confident predictions\" is not equivalent to \"Active sampling must avoid permanently neglecting regions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「抽樣策略」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Sampling strategy?","options":["標籤延遲會限制主動抽樣更新","永遠只測模型最有把握的樣本","只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定"],"optionsEn":["Label delays constrain active sampling","Measuring only the most confident predictions","Proving model stability from mean inputs alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"標籤延遲會限制主動抽樣更新；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Label delays constrain active sampling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-16"],"title":"漂移監控：建立模型","titleEn":"Drift monitoring: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed.","instruction":"分開輸入分布變動與預測殘差漂移。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate input-distribution shift from residual drift. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效；感測器重新校正會改變特徵基準。","observationEn":"Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed; Sensor recalibration changes feature baselines.","failure":"若採用「只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Proving model stability from mean inputs alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「漂移監控」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效。","checkEn":"Submit the Drift monitoring diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-17-k1","title":"漂移監控／物理與模型","titleEn":"Drift monitoring / Physics and model","text":"機制：輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效。","textEn":"Mechanism: Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed."},{"id":"a096-v8-17-k2","title":"漂移監控／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Drift monitoring / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Proving model stability from mean inputs alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漂移監控」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Drift monitoring, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備","輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效","只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定"],"optionsEn":["Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment","Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed","Proving model stability from mean inputs alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-17"],"title":"漂移監控：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Drift monitoring: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Proving model stability from mean inputs alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「漂移監控」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：感測器重新校正會改變特徵基準。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Drift monitoring artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Proving model stability from mean inputs alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Sensor recalibration changes feature baselines. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效；感測器重新校正會改變特徵基準。","observationEn":"Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed; Sensor recalibration changes feature baselines.","failure":"若採用「只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Proving model stability from mean inputs alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「漂移監控」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「感測器重新校正會改變特徵基準」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Drift monitoring, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Sensor recalibration changes feature baselines\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-18-k1","title":"漂移監控／物理與模型","titleEn":"Drift monitoring / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：感測器重新校正會改變特徵基準。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Sensor recalibration changes feature baselines."},{"id":"a096-v8-18-k2","title":"漂移監控／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Drift monitoring / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定」與「輸入改變不一定等於輸出關係失效」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Proving model stability from mean inputs alone\" is not equivalent to \"Input shift does not necessarily mean the mapping failed\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「漂移監控」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Drift monitoring?","options":["只檢查平均輸入就證明模型穩定","模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備","感測器重新校正會改變特徵基準"],"optionsEn":["Proving model stability from mean inputs alone","Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment","Sensor recalibration changes feature baselines"],"answer":2,"explanation":"感測器重新校正會改變特徵基準；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sensor recalibration changes feature baselines. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a096-stage04","order":4,"title":"控制限幅 → 版本回復","titleEn":"Control bounds to Version rollback","description":"把「控制限幅」「影子運行」「版本回復」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Control bounds, Shadow operation, Version rollback.","steps":[{"id":"a096-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-18"],"title":"控制限幅：建立模型","titleEn":"Control bounds: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes.","instruction":"為假設修正設定變化幅度限制及人工回復條件。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Set hypothetical correction bounds and manual-recovery conditions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程；回退規則應保留人員與原因紀錄。","observationEn":"Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes; Rollback needs operator/reason records.","failure":"若採用「模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「控制限幅」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程。","checkEn":"Submit the Control bounds diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-19-k1","title":"控制限幅／物理與模型","titleEn":"Control bounds / Physics and model","text":"機制：高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程。","textEn":"Mechanism: Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes."},{"id":"a096-v8-19-k2","title":"控制限幅／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Control bounds / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制限幅」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Control bounds, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程","模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備","離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗"],"optionsEn":["Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes","Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment","Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-19"],"title":"控制限幅：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Control bounds: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment.","instruction":"接續前一步「控制限幅」成果，先指出錯誤主張「模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：回退規則應保留人員與原因紀錄。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Control bounds artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Rollback needs operator/reason records. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程；回退規則應保留人員與原因紀錄。","observationEn":"Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes; Rollback needs operator/reason records.","failure":"若採用「模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「控制限幅」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「回退規則應保留人員與原因紀錄」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Control bounds, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Rollback needs operator/reason records\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-20-k1","title":"控制限幅／物理與模型","titleEn":"Control bounds / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：回退規則應保留人員與原因紀錄。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Rollback needs operator/reason records."},{"id":"a096-v8-20-k2","title":"控制限幅／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Control bounds / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備」與「高不確定度預測不應無限制驅動製程」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment\" is not equivalent to \"Uncertain predictions should not drive unbounded changes\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「控制限幅」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Control bounds?","options":["離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗","回退規則應保留人員與原因紀錄","模型輸出再極端也直接寫入設備"],"optionsEn":["Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy","Rollback needs operator/reason records","Sending arbitrarily extreme predictions directly to equipment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回退規則應保留人員與原因紀錄；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Rollback needs operator/reason records. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-20"],"title":"影子運行：建立模型","titleEn":"Shadow operation: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability.","instruction":"同步計算建議但不下指令，與既有控制比較。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compute recommendations without actuation and compare existing control. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定；影子模式沒有控制器造成的資料改變。","observationEn":"Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability; Shadow mode omits controller-induced data changes.","failure":"若採用「離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「影子運行」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定。","checkEn":"Submit the Shadow operation diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-21-k1","title":"影子運行／物理與模型","titleEn":"Shadow operation / Physics and model","text":"機制：影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability."},{"id":"a096-v8-21-k2","title":"影子運行／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Shadow operation / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「影子運行」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Shadow operation, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗","只備份權重便可完整重現控制","影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定"],"optionsEn":["Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy","Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control","Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability"],"answer":2,"explanation":"影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-21"],"title":"影子運行：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Shadow operation: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy.","instruction":"接續前一步「影子運行」成果，先指出錯誤主張「離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：影子模式沒有控制器造成的資料改變。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Shadow operation artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Shadow mode omits controller-induced data changes. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定；影子模式沒有控制器造成的資料改變。","observationEn":"Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability; Shadow mode omits controller-induced data changes.","failure":"若採用「離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「影子運行」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「影子模式沒有控制器造成的資料改變」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Shadow operation, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Shadow mode omits controller-induced data changes\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-22-k1","title":"影子運行／物理與模型","titleEn":"Shadow operation / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：影子模式沒有控制器造成的資料改變。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Shadow mode omits controller-induced data changes."},{"id":"a096-v8-22-k2","title":"影子運行／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Shadow operation / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗」與「影子結果可評估預測但不能完整證明閉環穩定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy\" is not equivalent to \"Shadow results assess predictions, not full closed-loop stability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「影子運行」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Shadow operation?","options":["影子模式沒有控制器造成的資料改變","離線準確就跳過所有閉迴路試驗","只備份權重便可完整重現控制"],"optionsEn":["Shadow mode omits controller-induced data changes","Skipping closed-loop trials after offline accuracy","Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control"],"answer":0,"explanation":"影子模式沒有控制器造成的資料改變；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shadow mode omits controller-induced data changes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-22"],"title":"版本回復：建立模型","titleEn":"Version rollback: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results.","instruction":"保存特徵、模型、標準化與控制規則的共同版本。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Version features, model, scaling and control policy together. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果；標準化參數必須只用訓練資料估計。","observationEn":"Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results; Scaling parameters must use training data only.","failure":"若採用「只備份權重便可完整重現控制」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「版本回復」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果。","checkEn":"Submit the Version rollback diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-23-k1","title":"版本回復／物理與模型","titleEn":"Version rollback / Physics and model","text":"機制：模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果。","textEn":"Mechanism: Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results."},{"id":"a096-v8-23-k2","title":"版本回復／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Version rollback / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只備份權重便可完整重現控制」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「版本回復」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Version rollback, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到","模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果","只備份權重便可完整重現控制"],"optionsEn":["Calling a prediction a physical measurement","Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results","Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control"],"answer":1,"explanation":"模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a096-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-vm","v8-c-vm-white","v8-c-spc"],"prerequisiteIds":["a096-v8-23"],"title":"版本回復：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Version rollback: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只備份權重便可完整重現控制」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control.","instruction":"接續前一步「版本回復」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只備份權重便可完整重現控制」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：標準化參數必須只用訓練資料估計。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Version rollback artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Scaling parameters must use training data only. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果；標準化參數必須只用訓練資料估計。","observationEn":"Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results; Scaling parameters must use training data only.","failure":"若採用「只備份權重便可完整重現控制」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「版本回復」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「標準化參數必須只用訓練資料估計」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Version rollback, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Scaling parameters must use training data only\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a096-v8-24-k1","title":"版本回復／物理與模型","titleEn":"Version rollback / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：標準化參數必須只用訓練資料估計。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Scaling parameters must use training data only."},{"id":"a096-v8-24-k2","title":"版本回復／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Version rollback / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只備份權重便可完整重現控制」與「模型檔相同但前處理不同仍可能改變結果」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control\" is not equivalent to \"Identical weights with changed preprocessing can change results\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「版本回復」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Version rollback?","options":["只備份權重便可完整重現控制","預測值存在就可宣稱已實際量到","標準化參數必須只用訓練資料估計"],"optionsEn":["Assuming weight backup alone reproduces control","Calling a prediction a physical measurement","Scaling parameters must use training data only"],"answer":2,"explanation":"標準化參數必須只用訓練資料估計；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Scaling parameters must use training data only. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"},{"id":"a097","title":"晶圓級參數測試","titleEn":"Wafer-level parametric testing","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement","v8-c-nist-place","v8-c-nist-history","v8-c-nist-metrology","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從SMU 四象限、量測等待到判限與重測：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From SMU quadrants and Settling time to Limits and retest: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["SMU 四象限","防漏與守衛","MOS 參數","晶圓測點"],"labelsEn":["SMU quadrants","Leakage and guarding","MOS parameters","Wafer sites"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a097-stage01","order":1,"title":"SMU 四象限 → 四線 Kelvin","titleEn":"SMU quadrants to Four-wire Kelvin","description":"把「SMU 四象限」「接觸落針」「四線 Kelvin」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for SMU quadrants, Probe contact, Four-wire Kelvin.","steps":[{"id":"a097-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"SMU 四象限：建立模型","titleEn":"SMU quadrants: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「設定源量不等於被測端實際值」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value.","instruction":"畫源電壓量電流與源電流量電壓的模式。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw voltage-source/current-measure and current-source/voltage-measure modes. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"設定源量不等於被測端實際值；SMU 的量程切換可能產生暫態。","observationEn":"A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value; SMU range switching can create transients.","failure":"若採用「只記設定值就當成實測電壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Recording setpoints as measured voltage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「SMU 四象限」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：設定源量不等於被測端實際值。","checkEn":"Submit the SMU quadrants diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-01-k1","title":"SMU 四象限／物理與模型","titleEn":"SMU quadrants / Physics and model","text":"機制：設定源量不等於被測端實際值。","textEn":"Mechanism: A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value."},{"id":"a097-v8-01-k2","title":"SMU 四象限／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SMU quadrants / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只記設定值就當成實測電壓」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Recording setpoints as measured voltage."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「SMU 四象限」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For SMU quadrants, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["設定源量不等於被測端實際值","只記設定值就當成實測電壓","第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒"],"optionsEn":["A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value","Recording setpoints as measured voltage","Rejecting a die after one open contact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"設定源量不等於被測端實際值；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-01"],"title":"SMU 四象限：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"SMU quadrants: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只記設定值就當成實測電壓」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Recording setpoints as measured voltage.","instruction":"接續前一步「SMU 四象限」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只記設定值就當成實測電壓」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：SMU 的量程切換可能產生暫態。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding SMU quadrants artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Recording setpoints as measured voltage\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: SMU range switching can create transients. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"設定源量不等於被測端實際值；SMU 的量程切換可能產生暫態。","observationEn":"A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value; SMU range switching can create transients.","failure":"若採用「只記設定值就當成實測電壓」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Recording setpoints as measured voltage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「SMU 四象限」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「SMU 的量程切換可能產生暫態」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for SMU quadrants, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"SMU range switching can create transients\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-02-k1","title":"SMU 四象限／物理與模型","titleEn":"SMU quadrants / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：SMU 的量程切換可能產生暫態。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: SMU range switching can create transients."},{"id":"a097-v8-02-k2","title":"SMU 四象限／驗證與限制","titleEn":"SMU quadrants / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只記設定值就當成實測電壓」與「設定源量不等於被測端實際值」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Recording setpoints as measured voltage\" is not equivalent to \"A source setting need not equal the actual DUT value\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「SMU 四象限」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of SMU quadrants?","options":["第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒","SMU 的量程切換可能產生暫態","只記設定值就當成實測電壓"],"optionsEn":["Rejecting a die after one open contact","SMU range switching can create transients","Recording setpoints as measured voltage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"SMU 的量程切換可能產生暫態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"SMU range switching can create transients. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-02"],"title":"接觸落針：建立模型","titleEn":"Probe contact: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「接觸不良可模仿元件失效」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Bad contact can mimic device failure.","instruction":"畫探針、焊墊與接觸污染，規劃接觸前後參考。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw probe/pad contamination and pre/post contact checks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"接觸不良可模仿元件失效；接觸重測應保留首次紀錄。","observationEn":"Bad contact can mimic device failure; Contact retesting should preserve first results.","failure":"若採用「第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Rejecting a die after one open contact\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「接觸落針」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：接觸不良可模仿元件失效。","checkEn":"Submit the Probe contact diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Bad contact can mimic device failure.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-03-k1","title":"接觸落針／物理與模型","titleEn":"Probe contact / Physics and model","text":"機制：接觸不良可模仿元件失效。","textEn":"Mechanism: Bad contact can mimic device failure."},{"id":"a097-v8-03-k2","title":"接觸落針／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Probe contact / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Rejecting a die after one open contact."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸落針」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Probe contact, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒","四線就不需要檢查任何接觸","接觸不良可模仿元件失效"],"optionsEn":["Rejecting a die after one open contact","Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks","Bad contact can mimic device failure"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸不良可模仿元件失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Bad contact can mimic device failure. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-03"],"title":"接觸落針：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Probe contact: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Rejecting a die after one open contact.","instruction":"接續前一步「接觸落針」成果，先指出錯誤主張「第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：接觸重測應保留首次紀錄。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Probe contact artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Rejecting a die after one open contact\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Contact retesting should preserve first results. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"接觸不良可模仿元件失效；接觸重測應保留首次紀錄。","observationEn":"Bad contact can mimic device failure; Contact retesting should preserve first results.","failure":"若採用「第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Rejecting a die after one open contact\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「接觸落針」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「接觸重測應保留首次紀錄」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Probe contact, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Contact retesting should preserve first results\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-04-k1","title":"接觸落針／物理與模型","titleEn":"Probe contact / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：接觸重測應保留首次紀錄。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Contact retesting should preserve first results."},{"id":"a097-v8-04-k2","title":"接觸落針／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Probe contact / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒」與「接觸不良可模仿元件失效」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Rejecting a die after one open contact\" is not equivalent to \"Bad contact can mimic device failure\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「接觸落針」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Probe contact?","options":["接觸重測應保留首次紀錄","第一次開路就直接報廢晶粒","四線就不需要檢查任何接觸"],"optionsEn":["Contact retesting should preserve first results","Rejecting a die after one open contact","Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸重測應保留首次紀錄；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact retesting should preserve first results. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-04"],"title":"四線 Kelvin：建立模型","titleEn":"Four-wire Kelvin: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error.","instruction":"分開 force 和 sense 線，指出感測輸入電流近似。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設 DUT=100 Ω、兩條 force 引線各 2 Ω，輸入 1 mA。二線總壓降為 104 mV，反算 104 Ω；理想四線 Kelvin 的 sense 電流可忽略，僅量 DUT 100 mV，得 100 Ω。接點位於哪裡仍決定是否包含接觸電阻，四線並不自動消除所有誤差。","instructionEn":"Separate force/sense and state the low-sense-current assumption. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a 100 Ω DUT, two 2 Ω force leads and 1 mA. A two-wire measurement reads 104 mV and infers 104 Ω; ideal four-wire Kelvin sensing with negligible sense current reads 100 mV across the DUT, giving 100 Ω. Sense-contact placement determines whether contact resistance is included; four-wire does not remove every error.","observation":"Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差；Sense 接觸開路仍會破壞量測。","observationEn":"Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error; An open sense contact still breaks measurement.","failure":"若採用「四線就不需要檢查任何接觸」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「四線 Kelvin」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差。\n算例驗收：驗算 104 與 100 Ω，畫出 force/sense 接點與電壓量測邊界。","checkEn":"Submit the Four-wire Kelvin diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 104 and 100 Ω and draw force/sense contacts and the voltage-measurement boundary.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-05-k1","title":"四線 Kelvin／物理與模型","titleEn":"Four-wire Kelvin / Physics and model","text":"機制：Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差。","textEn":"Mechanism: Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error."},{"id":"a097-v8-05-k2","title":"四線 Kelvin／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Four-wire Kelvin / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「四線就不需要檢查任何接觸」。\n假設數值與推算：假設 DUT=100 Ω、兩條 force 引線各 2 Ω，輸入 1 mA。二線總壓降為 104 mV，反算 104 Ω；理想四線 Kelvin 的 sense 電流可忽略，僅量 DUT 100 mV，得 100 Ω。接點位於哪裡仍決定是否包含接觸電阻，四線並不自動消除所有誤差。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a 100 Ω DUT, two 2 Ω force leads and 1 mA. A two-wire measurement reads 104 mV and infers 104 Ω; ideal four-wire Kelvin sensing with negligible sense current reads 100 mV across the DUT, giving 100 Ω. Sense-contact placement determines whether contact resistance is included; four-wire does not remove every error."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「四線 Kelvin」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Four-wire Kelvin, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳","Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差","四線就不需要檢查任何接觸"],"optionsEn":["Grounding every guard regardless of measurement","Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error","Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-05"],"title":"四線 Kelvin：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Four-wire Kelvin: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「四線就不需要檢查任何接觸」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks.","instruction":"接續前一步「四線 Kelvin」成果，先指出錯誤主張「四線就不需要檢查任何接觸」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：Sense 接觸開路仍會破壞量測。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Four-wire Kelvin artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: An open sense contact still breaks measurement. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差；Sense 接觸開路仍會破壞量測。","observationEn":"Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error; An open sense contact still breaks measurement.","failure":"若採用「四線就不需要檢查任何接觸」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「四線 Kelvin」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「Sense 接觸開路仍會破壞量測」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Four-wire Kelvin, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"An open sense contact still breaks measurement\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-06-k1","title":"四線 Kelvin／物理與模型","titleEn":"Four-wire Kelvin / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：Sense 接觸開路仍會破壞量測。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: An open sense contact still breaks measurement."},{"id":"a097-v8-06-k2","title":"四線 Kelvin／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Four-wire Kelvin / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「四線就不需要檢查任何接觸」與「Kelvin 可降低引線壓降但不能取消所有誤差」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks\" is not equivalent to \"Kelvin reduces lead drop but not every error\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「四線 Kelvin」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Four-wire Kelvin?","options":["四線就不需要檢查任何接觸","把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳","Sense 接觸開路仍會破壞量測"],"optionsEn":["Assuming four-wire measurement requires no contact checks","Grounding every guard regardless of measurement","An open sense contact still breaks measurement"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Sense 接觸開路仍會破壞量測；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"An open sense contact still breaks measurement. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a097-stage02","order":2,"title":"防漏與守衛 → 電流限制","titleEn":"Leakage and guarding to Compliance","description":"把「防漏與守衛」「量測等待」「電流限制」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Leakage and guarding, Settling time, Compliance.","steps":[{"id":"a097-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-06"],"title":"防漏與守衛：建立模型","titleEn":"Leakage and guarding: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground.","instruction":"畫高阻量測表面漏電及守衛路徑。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw leakage and guard paths in a high-resistance measurement. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地；護衛放大器也有穩定度限制。","observationEn":"Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground; Guard amplifiers also have stability limits.","failure":"若採用「把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Grounding every guard regardless of measurement\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「防漏與守衛」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地。","checkEn":"Submit the Leakage and guarding diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-07-k1","title":"防漏與守衛／物理與模型","titleEn":"Leakage and guarding / Physics and model","text":"機制：守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地。","textEn":"Mechanism: Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground."},{"id":"a097-v8-07-k2","title":"防漏與守衛／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Leakage and guarding / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Grounding every guard regardless of measurement."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「防漏與守衛」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Leakage and guarding, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地","把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳","更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度"],"optionsEn":["Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground","Grounding every guard regardless of measurement","Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-07"],"title":"防漏與守衛：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Leakage and guarding: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Grounding every guard regardless of measurement.","instruction":"接續前一步「防漏與守衛」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：護衛放大器也有穩定度限制。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Leakage and guarding artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Grounding every guard regardless of measurement\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Guard amplifiers also have stability limits. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地；護衛放大器也有穩定度限制。","observationEn":"Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground; Guard amplifiers also have stability limits.","failure":"若採用「把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Grounding every guard regardless of measurement\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「防漏與守衛」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「護衛放大器也有穩定度限制」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Leakage and guarding, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Guard amplifiers also have stability limits\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-08-k1","title":"防漏與守衛／物理與模型","titleEn":"Leakage and guarding / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：護衛放大器也有穩定度限制。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Guard amplifiers also have stability limits."},{"id":"a097-v8-08-k2","title":"防漏與守衛／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Leakage and guarding / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳」與「守衛需跟隨合適電位，不只是接地」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Grounding every guard regardless of measurement\" is not equivalent to \"Guarding uses an appropriate potential, not simply ground\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「防漏與守衛」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Leakage and guarding?","options":["更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度","護衛放大器也有穩定度限制","把所有守衛都接地便一定最佳"],"optionsEn":["Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy","Guard amplifiers also have stability limits","Grounding every guard regardless of measurement"],"answer":1,"explanation":"護衛放大器也有穩定度限制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Guard amplifiers also have stability limits. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-08"],"title":"量測等待：建立模型","titleEn":"Settling time: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state.","instruction":"對假設 RC 響應比較不同等待時間的誤差。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare measurement error at different delays on a hypothetical RC response. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態；積分時間可抑制電源頻率干擾。","observationEn":"Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state; Integration time can suppress mains interference.","failure":"若採用「更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「量測等待」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態。","checkEn":"Submit the Settling time diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-09-k1","title":"量測等待／物理與模型","titleEn":"Settling time / Physics and model","text":"機制：過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態。","textEn":"Mechanism: Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state."},{"id":"a097-v8-09-k2","title":"量測等待／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Settling time / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測等待」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Settling time, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度","被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測","過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態"],"optionsEn":["Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy","Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements","Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state"],"answer":2,"explanation":"過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-09"],"title":"量測等待：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Settling time: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy.","instruction":"接續前一步「量測等待」成果，先指出錯誤主張「更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：積分時間可抑制電源頻率干擾。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Settling time artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Integration time can suppress mains interference. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態；積分時間可抑制電源頻率干擾。","observationEn":"Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state; Integration time can suppress mains interference.","failure":"若採用「更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「量測等待」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「積分時間可抑制電源頻率干擾」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Settling time, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Integration time can suppress mains interference\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-10-k1","title":"量測等待／物理與模型","titleEn":"Settling time / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：積分時間可抑制電源頻率干擾。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Integration time can suppress mains interference."},{"id":"a097-v8-10-k2","title":"量測等待／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Settling time / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度」與「過快採樣可能量到暫態而非穩態」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy\" is not equivalent to \"Sampling too soon can measure transients rather than steady state\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「量測等待」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Settling time?","options":["積分時間可抑制電源頻率干擾","更快讀取不會影響 DC 準確度","被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測"],"optionsEn":["Integration time can suppress mains interference","Assuming faster reads cannot affect DC accuracy","Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements"],"answer":0,"explanation":"積分時間可抑制電源頻率干擾；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Integration time can suppress mains interference. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-10"],"title":"電流限制：建立模型","titleEn":"Compliance: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance.","instruction":"在假設 I-V 標出進入 compliance 的區段並區分設定和實際。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Mark compliance regions and separate commanded/actual quantities. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定；儀器輸出電容可造成瞬態超調。","observationEn":"Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance; Output capacitance can create transient overshoot.","failure":"若採用「被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「電流限制」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定。","checkEn":"Submit the Compliance diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-11-k1","title":"電流限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Compliance / Physics and model","text":"機制：限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance."},{"id":"a097-v8-11-k2","title":"電流限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Compliance / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電流限制」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Compliance, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯","限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定","被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測"],"optionsEn":["Calling every method difference an error","Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance","Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-11"],"title":"電流限制：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Compliance: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements.","instruction":"接續前一步「電流限制」成果，先指出錯誤主張「被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：儀器輸出電容可造成瞬態超調。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Compliance artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Output capacitance can create transient overshoot. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定；儀器輸出電容可造成瞬態超調。","observationEn":"Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance; Output capacitance can create transient overshoot.","failure":"若採用「被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「電流限制」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「儀器輸出電容可造成瞬態超調」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Compliance, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Output capacitance can create transient overshoot\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-12-k1","title":"電流限制／物理與模型","titleEn":"Compliance / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：儀器輸出電容可造成瞬態超調。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Output capacitance can create transient overshoot."},{"id":"a097-v8-12-k2","title":"電流限制／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Compliance / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測」與「限流期間施加條件可能偏離設定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements\" is not equivalent to \"Applied conditions can depart from setpoints during compliance\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「電流限制」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Compliance?","options":["被限流點仍當作固定設定電壓量測","不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯","儀器輸出電容可造成瞬態超調"],"optionsEn":["Treating limited points as exact voltage-setpoint measurements","Calling every method difference an error","Output capacitance can create transient overshoot"],"answer":2,"explanation":"儀器輸出電容可造成瞬態超調；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Output capacitance can create transient overshoot. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a097-stage03","order":3,"title":"MOS 參數 → TLM 結構","titleEn":"MOS parameters to TLM structures","description":"把「MOS 參數」「C-V 測試」「TLM 結構」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for MOS parameters, C-V tests, TLM structures.","steps":[{"id":"a097-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-12"],"title":"MOS 參數：建立模型","titleEn":"MOS parameters: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Different threshold definitions produce different values.","instruction":"用同一假設曲線比較固定電流及外推 Vth 定義。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare constant-current and extrapolated thresholds on one curve. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值；遷移率抽取也依有效幾何。","observationEn":"Different threshold definitions produce different values; Mobility extraction needs effective geometry.","failure":"若採用「不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling every method difference an error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「MOS 參數」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值。","checkEn":"Submit the MOS parameters diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Different threshold definitions produce different values.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-13-k1","title":"MOS 參數／物理與模型","titleEn":"MOS parameters / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值。","textEn":"Mechanism: Different threshold definitions produce different values."},{"id":"a097-v8-13-k2","title":"MOS 參數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"MOS parameters / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Calling every method difference an error."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「MOS 參數」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For MOS parameters, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值","不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯","不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較"],"optionsEn":["Different threshold definitions produce different values","Calling every method difference an error","Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Different threshold definitions produce different values. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-13"],"title":"MOS 參數：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"MOS parameters: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Calling every method difference an error.","instruction":"接續前一步「MOS 參數」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：遷移率抽取也依有效幾何。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding MOS parameters artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Calling every method difference an error\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Mobility extraction needs effective geometry. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值；遷移率抽取也依有效幾何。","observationEn":"Different threshold definitions produce different values; Mobility extraction needs effective geometry.","failure":"若採用「不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Calling every method difference an error\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「MOS 參數」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「遷移率抽取也依有效幾何」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for MOS parameters, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Mobility extraction needs effective geometry\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-14-k1","title":"MOS 參數／物理與模型","titleEn":"MOS parameters / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：遷移率抽取也依有效幾何。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Mobility extraction needs effective geometry."},{"id":"a097-v8-14-k2","title":"MOS 參數／驗證與限制","titleEn":"MOS parameters / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯」與「不同 Vth 定義可產生不同數值」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Calling every method difference an error\" is not equivalent to \"Different threshold definitions produce different values\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「MOS 參數」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of MOS parameters?","options":["不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較","遷移率抽取也依有效幾何","不同抽取法數字不等就一定量測錯"],"optionsEn":["Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification","Mobility extraction needs effective geometry","Calling every method difference an error"],"answer":1,"explanation":"遷移率抽取也依有效幾何；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Mobility extraction needs effective geometry. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-14"],"title":"C-V 測試：建立模型","titleEn":"C-V tests: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction.","instruction":"畫小訊號疊加 DC 偏壓並分開頻率與振幅。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw small-signal AC on DC bias with frequency/amplitude. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償；Open/short 補償需同一夾具配置。","observationEn":"C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction; Open/short correction needs the same fixture.","failure":"若採用「不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「C-V 測試」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償。","checkEn":"Submit the C-V tests diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-15-k1","title":"C-V 測試／物理與模型","titleEn":"C-V tests / Physics and model","text":"機制：C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償。","textEn":"Mechanism: C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction."},{"id":"a097-v8-15-k2","title":"C-V 測試／驗證與限制","titleEn":"C-V tests / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「C-V 測試」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For C-V tests, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較","負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻","C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償"],"optionsEn":["Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification","Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance","C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction"],"answer":2,"explanation":"C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-15"],"title":"C-V 測試：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"C-V tests: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification.","instruction":"接續前一步「C-V 測試」成果，先指出錯誤主張「不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：Open/short 補償需同一夾具配置。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding C-V tests artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Open/short correction needs the same fixture. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償；Open/short 補償需同一夾具配置。","observationEn":"C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction; Open/short correction needs the same fixture.","failure":"若採用「不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「C-V 測試」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「Open/short 補償需同一夾具配置」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for C-V tests, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Open/short correction needs the same fixture\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-16-k1","title":"C-V 測試／物理與模型","titleEn":"C-V tests / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：Open/short 補償需同一夾具配置。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Open/short correction needs the same fixture."},{"id":"a097-v8-16-k2","title":"C-V 測試／驗證與限制","titleEn":"C-V tests / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較」與「C-V 結果依頻率與寄生補償」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification\" is not equivalent to \"C-V depends on frequency and parasitic correction\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「C-V 測試」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of C-V tests?","options":["Open/short 補償需同一夾具配置","不同頻率的電容可以無條件直接比較","負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻"],"optionsEn":["Open/short correction needs the same fixture","Comparing capacitance at different frequencies without qualification","Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Open/short 補償需同一夾具配置；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Open/short correction needs the same fixture. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-16"],"title":"TLM 結構：建立模型","titleEn":"TLM structures: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency.","instruction":"以假設距離系列回歸總電阻，檢查截距和非線性。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Fit total resistance versus spacing and check intercept/nonlinearity. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何；有效線寬誤差會改變片電阻。","observationEn":"Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency; Width errors bias sheet resistance.","failure":"若採用「負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「TLM 結構」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何。","checkEn":"Submit the TLM structures diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-17-k1","title":"TLM 結構／物理與模型","titleEn":"TLM structures / Physics and model","text":"機制：接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何。","textEn":"Mechanism: Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency."},{"id":"a097-v8-17-k2","title":"TLM 結構／驗證與限制","titleEn":"TLM structures / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「TLM 結構」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For TLM structures, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID","接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何","負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻"],"optionsEn":["Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs","Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency","Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-17"],"title":"TLM 結構：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"TLM structures: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance.","instruction":"接續前一步「TLM 結構」成果，先指出錯誤主張「負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：有效線寬誤差會改變片電阻。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding TLM structures artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Width errors bias sheet resistance. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何；有效線寬誤差會改變片電阻。","observationEn":"Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency; Width errors bias sheet resistance.","failure":"若採用「負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「TLM 結構」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「有效線寬誤差會改變片電阻」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for TLM structures, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Width errors bias sheet resistance\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-18-k1","title":"TLM 結構／物理與模型","titleEn":"TLM structures / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：有效線寬誤差會改變片電阻。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Width errors bias sheet resistance."},{"id":"a097-v8-18-k2","title":"TLM 結構／驗證與限制","titleEn":"TLM structures / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻」與「接觸抽取依賴模型與一致幾何」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance\" is not equivalent to \"Contact extraction depends on model and geometry consistency\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「TLM 結構」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of TLM structures?","options":["負截距直接當作真實負接觸電阻","測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID","有效線寬誤差會改變片電阻"],"optionsEn":["Interpreting a negative intercept as physical negative contact resistance","Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs","Width errors bias sheet resistance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"有效線寬誤差會改變片電阻；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Width errors bias sheet resistance. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a097-stage04","order":4,"title":"晶圓測點 → 判限與重測","titleEn":"Wafer sites to Limits and retest","description":"把「晶圓測點」「測試順序」「判限與重測」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Wafer sites, Test ordering, Limits and retest.","steps":[{"id":"a097-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-18"],"title":"晶圓測點：建立模型","titleEn":"Wafer sites: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「地圖分布需要正確測點身份」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Spatial distributions require correct site identity.","instruction":"以坐標、晶粒、結構 ID 建立可追溯測試表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Build a traceable table of coordinates, die and structure IDs. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"地圖分布需要正確測點身份；邊緣排除區需明確標示。","observationEn":"Spatial distributions require correct site identity; Edge exclusions need explicit marking.","failure":"若採用「測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「晶圓測點」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：地圖分布需要正確測點身份。","checkEn":"Submit the Wafer sites diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Spatial distributions require correct site identity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-19-k1","title":"晶圓測點／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wafer sites / Physics and model","text":"機制：地圖分布需要正確測點身份。","textEn":"Mechanism: Spatial distributions require correct site identity."},{"id":"a097-v8-19-k2","title":"晶圓測點／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wafer sites / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「晶圓測點」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Wafer sites, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["地圖分布需要正確測點身份","測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID","任何測試順序都必然互不影響"],"optionsEn":["Spatial distributions require correct site identity","Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs","Assuming every test order is noninteracting"],"answer":0,"explanation":"地圖分布需要正確測點身份；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Spatial distributions require correct site identity. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-19"],"title":"晶圓測點：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Wafer sites: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs.","instruction":"接續前一步「晶圓測點」成果，先指出錯誤主張「測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：邊緣排除區需明確標示。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Wafer sites artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Edge exclusions need explicit marking. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"地圖分布需要正確測點身份；邊緣排除區需明確標示。","observationEn":"Spatial distributions require correct site identity; Edge exclusions need explicit marking.","failure":"若採用「測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「晶圓測點」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「邊緣排除區需明確標示」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Wafer sites, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Edge exclusions need explicit marking\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-20-k1","title":"晶圓測點／物理與模型","titleEn":"Wafer sites / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：邊緣排除區需明確標示。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Edge exclusions need explicit marking."},{"id":"a097-v8-20-k2","title":"晶圓測點／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Wafer sites / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID」與「地圖分布需要正確測點身份」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs\" is not equivalent to \"Spatial distributions require correct site identity\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「晶圓測點」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Wafer sites?","options":["任何測試順序都必然互不影響","邊緣排除區需明確標示","測點順序可以取代永久結構 ID"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every test order is noninteracting","Edge exclusions need explicit marking","Using run order instead of persistent structure IDs"],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊緣排除區需明確標示；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Edge exclusions need explicit marking. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-20"],"title":"測試順序：建立模型","titleEn":"Test ordering: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「測試本身可能改變後續結果」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Testing can alter subsequent results.","instruction":"比較先高應力再低漏電與相反順序的假設結果。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Compare hypothetical high-stress-first and leakage-first sequences. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"測試本身可能改變後續結果；熱穩定時間與電性等待時間不同。","observationEn":"Testing can alter subsequent results; Thermal settling differs from electrical settling.","failure":"若採用「任何測試順序都必然互不影響」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every test order is noninteracting\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「測試順序」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：測試本身可能改變後續結果。","checkEn":"Submit the Test ordering diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Testing can alter subsequent results.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-21-k1","title":"測試順序／物理與模型","titleEn":"Test ordering / Physics and model","text":"機制：測試本身可能改變後續結果。","textEn":"Mechanism: Testing can alter subsequent results."},{"id":"a097-v8-21-k2","title":"測試順序／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Test ordering / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「任何測試順序都必然互不影響」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming every test order is noninteracting."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測試順序」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Test ordering, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["任何測試順序都必然互不影響","一直重測到通過就記最後一筆","測試本身可能改變後續結果"],"optionsEn":["Assuming every test order is noninteracting","Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result","Testing can alter subsequent results"],"answer":2,"explanation":"測試本身可能改變後續結果；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Testing can alter subsequent results. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-21"],"title":"測試順序：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Test ordering: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「任何測試順序都必然互不影響」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming every test order is noninteracting.","instruction":"接續前一步「測試順序」成果，先指出錯誤主張「任何測試順序都必然互不影響」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：熱穩定時間與電性等待時間不同。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Test ordering artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming every test order is noninteracting\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Thermal settling differs from electrical settling. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"測試本身可能改變後續結果；熱穩定時間與電性等待時間不同。","observationEn":"Testing can alter subsequent results; Thermal settling differs from electrical settling.","failure":"若採用「任何測試順序都必然互不影響」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming every test order is noninteracting\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「測試順序」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「熱穩定時間與電性等待時間不同」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Test ordering, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Thermal settling differs from electrical settling\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-22-k1","title":"測試順序／物理與模型","titleEn":"Test ordering / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：熱穩定時間與電性等待時間不同。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Thermal settling differs from electrical settling."},{"id":"a097-v8-22-k2","title":"測試順序／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Test ordering / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「任何測試順序都必然互不影響」與「測試本身可能改變後續結果」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming every test order is noninteracting\" is not equivalent to \"Testing can alter subsequent results\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「測試順序」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Test ordering?","options":["熱穩定時間與電性等待時間不同","任何測試順序都必然互不影響","一直重測到通過就記最後一筆"],"optionsEn":["Thermal settling differs from electrical settling","Assuming every test order is noninteracting","Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱穩定時間與電性等待時間不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Thermal settling differs from electrical settling. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-22"],"title":"判限與重測：建立模型","titleEn":"Limits and retest: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results.","instruction":"區分規格限、量測不確定度與接觸重測規則。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate specification limits, uncertainty and contact-retest rules. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據；判限守門需考慮假接受和假拒絕。","observationEn":"Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results; Guardbanding balances false acceptance/rejection.","failure":"若採用「一直重測到通過就記最後一筆」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「判限與重測」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據。","checkEn":"Submit the Limits and retest diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-23-k1","title":"判限與重測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Limits and retest / Physics and model","text":"機制：重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據。","textEn":"Mechanism: Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results."},{"id":"a097-v8-23-k2","title":"判限與重測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Limits and retest / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「一直重測到通過就記最後一筆」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「判限與重測」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Limits and retest, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只記設定值就當成實測電壓","重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據","一直重測到通過就記最後一筆"],"optionsEn":["Recording setpoints as measured voltage","Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results","Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result"],"answer":1,"explanation":"重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a097-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-param","v8-c-param-guide","v8-c-measurement"],"prerequisiteIds":["a097-v8-23"],"title":"判限與重測：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Limits and retest: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「一直重測到通過就記最後一筆」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result.","instruction":"接續前一步「判限與重測」成果，先指出錯誤主張「一直重測到通過就記最後一筆」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：判限守門需考慮假接受和假拒絕。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Limits and retest artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Guardbanding balances false acceptance/rejection. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據；判限守門需考慮假接受和假拒絕。","observationEn":"Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results; Guardbanding balances false acceptance/rejection.","failure":"若採用「一直重測到通過就記最後一筆」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「判限與重測」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「判限守門需考慮假接受和假拒絕」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Limits and retest, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Guardbanding balances false acceptance/rejection\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a097-v8-24-k1","title":"判限與重測／物理與模型","titleEn":"Limits and retest / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：判限守門需考慮假接受和假拒絕。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Guardbanding balances false acceptance/rejection."},{"id":"a097-v8-24-k2","title":"判限與重測／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Limits and retest / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「一直重測到通過就記最後一筆」與「重測需事先規則避免挑選有利數據」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result\" is not equivalent to \"Retest rules prevent selection of favorable results\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「判限與重測」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Limits and retest?","options":["一直重測到通過就記最後一筆","只記設定值就當成實測電壓","判限守門需考慮假接受和假拒絕"],"optionsEn":["Retesting until a pass and retaining only that result","Recording setpoints as measured voltage","Guardbanding balances false acceptance/rejection"],"answer":2,"explanation":"判限守門需考慮假接受和假拒絕；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Guardbanding balances false acceptance/rejection. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"metrology","subcategoryTitle":"量測、良率與控制","subcategoryTitleEn":"Metrology, yield and control"},{"id":"a098","title":"台積電 GIGAFAB 廠務整合案例","titleEn":"TSMC GIGAFAB facility-integration case study","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy","v8-c-tsmc-place","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從工廠與供應鏈、振動與基礎到公開案例審查：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Fab and supply chain and Vibration and foundations to Public-case review: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["工廠與供應鏈","潔淨氣流","冗餘與切換","設備節能"],"labelsEn":["Fab and supply chain","Cleanroom airflow","Redundancy and switching","Equipment energy saving"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a098-stage01","order":1,"title":"工廠與供應鏈 → 超純水回路","titleEn":"Fab and supply chain to Ultrapure-water loop","description":"把「工廠與供應鏈」「公用系統接口」「超純水回路」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Fab and supply chain, Utility interfaces, Ultrapure-water loop.","steps":[{"id":"a098-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"工廠與供應鏈：建立模型","titleEn":"Fab and supply chain: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe.","instruction":"畫設計、晶圓製造、封裝與測試邊界，不填入未公開管線。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw design, fab, packaging and test boundaries without inventing utility layouts. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方；廠區公開位置不等於內部設備座標。","observationEn":"GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe; Public fab locations do not expose tool positions.","failure":"若採用「用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring identical internal flows from a company name\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「工廠與供應鏈」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方。","checkEn":"Submit the Fab and supply chain diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-01-k1","title":"工廠與供應鏈／物理與模型","titleEn":"Fab and supply chain / Physics and model","text":"機制：GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方。","textEn":"Mechanism: GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe."},{"id":"a098-v8-01-k2","title":"工廠與供應鏈／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Fab and supply chain / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Inferring identical internal flows from a company name."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「工廠與供應鏈」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Fab and supply chain, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方","用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同","只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作"],"optionsEn":["GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe","Inferring identical internal flows from a company name","Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-01"],"title":"工廠與供應鏈：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Fab and supply chain: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Inferring identical internal flows from a company name.","instruction":"接續前一步「工廠與供應鏈」成果，先指出錯誤主張「用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：廠區公開位置不等於內部設備座標。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Fab and supply chain artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Inferring identical internal flows from a company name\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Public fab locations do not expose tool positions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方；廠區公開位置不等於內部設備座標。","observationEn":"GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe; Public fab locations do not expose tool positions.","failure":"若採用「用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Inferring identical internal flows from a company name\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「工廠與供應鏈」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「廠區公開位置不等於內部設備座標」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Fab and supply chain, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Public fab locations do not expose tool positions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-02-k1","title":"工廠與供應鏈／物理與模型","titleEn":"Fab and supply chain / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：廠區公開位置不等於內部設備座標。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Public fab locations do not expose tool positions."},{"id":"a098-v8-02-k2","title":"工廠與供應鏈／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Fab and supply chain / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同」與「GIGAFAB 是製造組織與規模概念，不是一份公開設備配方」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Inferring identical internal flows from a company name\" is not equivalent to \"GIGAFAB describes manufacturing organization and scale, not a public equipment recipe\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「工廠與供應鏈」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Fab and supply chain?","options":["只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作","廠區公開位置不等於內部設備座標","用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone","Public fab locations do not expose tool positions","Inferring identical internal flows from a company name"],"answer":1,"explanation":"廠區公開位置不等於內部設備座標；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Public fab locations do not expose tool positions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-02"],"title":"公用系統接口：建立模型","titleEn":"Utility interfaces: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements.","instruction":"用功能方塊連接電力、水、氣、真空與設備需求。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Connect power, water, gas and vacuum to tool needs using functional blocks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求；供應品質變動可造成共同失效。","observationEn":"Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements; Utility-quality shifts can create common failures.","failure":"若採用「只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「公用系統接口」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求。","checkEn":"Submit the Utility interfaces diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-03-k1","title":"公用系統接口／物理與模型","titleEn":"Utility interfaces / Physics and model","text":"機制：每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements."},{"id":"a098-v8-03-k2","title":"公用系統接口／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Utility interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「公用系統接口」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Utility interfaces, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作","只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水","每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求"],"optionsEn":["Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone","Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water","Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-03"],"title":"公用系統接口：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Utility interfaces: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone.","instruction":"接續前一步「公用系統接口」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：供應品質變動可造成共同失效。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Utility interfaces artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Utility-quality shifts can create common failures. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求；供應品質變動可造成共同失效。","observationEn":"Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements; Utility-quality shifts can create common failures.","failure":"若採用「只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「公用系統接口」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「供應品質變動可造成共同失效」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Utility interfaces, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Utility-quality shifts can create common failures\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-04-k1","title":"公用系統接口／物理與模型","titleEn":"Utility interfaces / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：供應品質變動可造成共同失效。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Utility-quality shifts can create common failures."},{"id":"a098-v8-04-k2","title":"公用系統接口／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Utility interfaces / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作」與「每種公用系統有不同品質與連續性需求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone\" is not equivalent to \"Utilities have different purity and continuity requirements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「公用系統接口」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Utility interfaces?","options":["供應品質變動可造成共同失效","只比較總供應量就保證設備可運作","只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水"],"optionsEn":["Utility-quality shifts can create common failures","Guaranteeing tool operation from supply quantity alone","Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"供應品質變動可造成共同失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Utility-quality shifts can create common failures. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-04"],"title":"超純水回路：建立模型","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water loop: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions.","instruction":"畫回流、監測和取用點，分開製程水與一般冷卻水。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw return, monitoring and use points and distinguish process/cooling water. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致；回流監測也需考慮管路停滯。","observationEn":"Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions; Return monitoring must consider stagnation.","failure":"若採用「只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「超純水回路」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致。","checkEn":"Submit the Ultrapure-water loop diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-05-k1","title":"超純水回路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water loop / Physics and model","text":"機制：入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致。","textEn":"Mechanism: Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions."},{"id":"a098-v8-05-k2","title":"超純水回路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water loop / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超純水回路」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Ultrapure-water loop, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控","入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致","只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水"],"optionsEn":["Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled","Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions","Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water"],"answer":1,"explanation":"入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-05"],"title":"超純水回路：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water loop: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water.","instruction":"接續前一步「超純水回路」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：回流監測也需考慮管路停滯。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Ultrapure-water loop artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Return monitoring must consider stagnation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致；回流監測也需考慮管路停滯。","observationEn":"Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions; Return monitoring must consider stagnation.","failure":"若採用「只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「超純水回路」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「回流監測也需考慮管路停滯」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Ultrapure-water loop, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Return monitoring must consider stagnation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-06-k1","title":"超純水回路／物理與模型","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water loop / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：回流監測也需考慮管路停滯。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Return monitoring must consider stagnation."},{"id":"a098-v8-06-k2","title":"超純水回路／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Ultrapure-water loop / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水」與「入口合格不代表所有取用點條件一致」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water\" is not equivalent to \"Inlet quality does not guarantee all point-of-use conditions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「超純水回路」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Ultrapure-water loop?","options":["只用市政水質標準代表晶圓接觸水","空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控","回流監測也需考慮管路停滯"],"optionsEn":["Using municipal-water criteria for wafer-contact water","Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled","Return monitoring must consider stagnation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"回流監測也需考慮管路停滯；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Return monitoring must consider stagnation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a098-stage02","order":2,"title":"潔淨氣流 → 熱負載","titleEn":"Cleanroom airflow to Thermal loads","description":"把「潔淨氣流」「振動與基礎」「熱負載」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Cleanroom airflow, Vibration and foundations, Thermal loads.","steps":[{"id":"a098-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-06"],"title":"潔淨氣流：建立模型","titleEn":"Cleanroom airflow: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control.","instruction":"畫潔淨區與設備區的概念氣流，分開粒子與分子污染。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw conceptual clean/tool-area airflow and distinguish particles from molecules. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制；分子污染可能來自材料逸氣。","observationEn":"Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control; Outgassing can cause molecular contamination.","failure":"若採用「空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「潔淨氣流」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制。","checkEn":"Submit the Cleanroom airflow diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-07-k1","title":"潔淨氣流／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cleanroom airflow / Physics and model","text":"機制：粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制。","textEn":"Mechanism: Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control."},{"id":"a098-v8-07-k2","title":"潔淨氣流／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cleanroom airflow / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潔淨氣流」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Cleanroom airflow, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制","空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控","只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台"],"optionsEn":["Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control","Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled","Approving all tools from one average amplitude"],"answer":0,"explanation":"粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-07"],"title":"潔淨氣流：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Cleanroom airflow: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled.","instruction":"接續前一步「潔淨氣流」成果，先指出錯誤主張「空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：分子污染可能來自材料逸氣。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Cleanroom airflow artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Outgassing can cause molecular contamination. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制；分子污染可能來自材料逸氣。","observationEn":"Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control; Outgassing can cause molecular contamination.","failure":"若採用「空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「潔淨氣流」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「分子污染可能來自材料逸氣」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Cleanroom airflow, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Outgassing can cause molecular contamination\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-08-k1","title":"潔淨氣流／物理與模型","titleEn":"Cleanroom airflow / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：分子污染可能來自材料逸氣。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Outgassing can cause molecular contamination."},{"id":"a098-v8-08-k2","title":"潔淨氣流／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Cleanroom airflow / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控」與「粒子潔淨度不能取代分子污染控制」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled\" is not equivalent to \"Particle cleanliness does not replace molecular-contamination control\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「潔淨氣流」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Cleanroom airflow?","options":["只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台","分子污染可能來自材料逸氣","空氣看不見塵便證明所有污染受控"],"optionsEn":["Approving all tools from one average amplitude","Outgassing can cause molecular contamination","Treating invisible dust as proof all contamination is controlled"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分子污染可能來自材料逸氣；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Outgassing can cause molecular contamination. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-08"],"title":"振動與基礎：建立模型","titleEn":"Vibration and foundations: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities.","instruction":"列出設備、地板及鄰近機電的耦合路徑，指定頻率量測。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"List tool/floor/mechanical coupling paths with frequency measurements. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度；共振可能放大特定頻率擾動。","observationEn":"Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities; Resonance amplifies specific frequencies.","failure":"若採用「只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Approving all tools from one average amplitude\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「振動與基礎」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度。","checkEn":"Submit the Vibration and foundations diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-09-k1","title":"振動與基礎／物理與模型","titleEn":"Vibration and foundations / Physics and model","text":"機制：不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities."},{"id":"a098-v8-09-k2","title":"振動與基礎／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Vibration and foundations / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Approving all tools from one average amplitude."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「振動與基礎」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Vibration and foundations, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台","冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂","不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度"],"optionsEn":["Approving all tools from one average amplitude","Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift","Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-09"],"title":"振動與基礎：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Vibration and foundations: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Approving all tools from one average amplitude.","instruction":"接續前一步「振動與基礎」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：共振可能放大特定頻率擾動。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Vibration and foundations artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Approving all tools from one average amplitude\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Resonance amplifies specific frequencies. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度；共振可能放大特定頻率擾動。","observationEn":"Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities; Resonance amplifies specific frequencies.","failure":"若採用「只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Approving all tools from one average amplitude\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「振動與基礎」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「共振可能放大特定頻率擾動」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Vibration and foundations, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Resonance amplifies specific frequencies\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-10-k1","title":"振動與基礎／物理與模型","titleEn":"Vibration and foundations / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：共振可能放大特定頻率擾動。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Resonance amplifies specific frequencies."},{"id":"a098-v8-10-k2","title":"振動與基礎／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Vibration and foundations / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台」與「不同頻帶對不同設備有不同敏感度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Approving all tools from one average amplitude\" is not equivalent to \"Tools have frequency-dependent vibration sensitivities\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「振動與基礎」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Vibration and foundations?","options":["共振可能放大特定頻率擾動","只用單一平均振幅核准所有機台","冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂"],"optionsEn":["Resonance amplifies specific frequencies","Approving all tools from one average amplitude","Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift"],"answer":0,"explanation":"共振可能放大特定頻率擾動；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Resonance amplifies specific frequencies. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-10"],"title":"熱負載：建立模型","titleEn":"Thermal loads: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required.","instruction":"建立設備、冷卻水與環境的假設能量平衡。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Create a hypothetical tool/cooling/environment energy balance. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求；換熱器接近溫差限制效率。","observationEn":"Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required; Approach temperatures constrain heat exchange.","failure":"若採用「冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「熱負載」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求。","checkEn":"Submit the Thermal loads diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-11-k1","title":"熱負載／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal loads / Physics and model","text":"機制：排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求。","textEn":"Mechanism: Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required."},{"id":"a098-v8-11-k2","title":"熱負載／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal loads / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱負載」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Thermal loads, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["有兩台設備就必然完全容錯","排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求","冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂"],"optionsEn":["Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance","Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required","Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift"],"answer":1,"explanation":"排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-11"],"title":"熱負載：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal loads: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift.","instruction":"接續前一步「熱負載」成果，先指出錯誤主張「冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：換熱器接近溫差限制效率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Thermal loads artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Approach temperatures constrain heat exchange. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求；換熱器接近溫差限制效率。","observationEn":"Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required; Approach temperatures constrain heat exchange.","failure":"若採用「冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「熱負載」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「換熱器接近溫差限制效率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Thermal loads, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Approach temperatures constrain heat exchange\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-12-k1","title":"熱負載／物理與模型","titleEn":"Thermal loads / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：換熱器接近溫差限制效率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Approach temperatures constrain heat exchange."},{"id":"a098-v8-12-k2","title":"熱負載／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Thermal loads / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂」與「排熱能力與局部溫度穩定都是需求」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift\" is not equivalent to \"Heat rejection and local temperature stability are both required\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「熱負載」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Thermal loads?","options":["冷凍噸足夠就必然沒有局部溫漂","有兩台設備就必然完全容錯","換熱器接近溫差限制效率"],"optionsEn":["Assuming sufficient cooling capacity eliminates local drift","Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance","Approach temperatures constrain heat exchange"],"answer":2,"explanation":"換熱器接近溫差限制效率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Approach temperatures constrain heat exchange. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a098-stage03","order":3,"title":"冗餘與切換 → 集中管理","titleEn":"Redundancy and switching to Centralized management","description":"把「冗餘與切換」「自動搬運」「集中管理」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Redundancy and switching, Automated transport, Centralized management.","steps":[{"id":"a098-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-12"],"title":"冗餘與切換：建立模型","titleEn":"Redundancy and switching: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「重複設備可能仍共享失效來源」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Duplicated equipment may share failure causes.","instruction":"畫雙路供應與共用節點，找出單點失效。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw dual feeds and shared nodes and identify single points of failure. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"重複設備可能仍共享失效來源；共用控制器也可能是單點失效。","observationEn":"Duplicated equipment may share failure causes; Shared controllers can be single failure points.","failure":"若採用「有兩台設備就必然完全容錯」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「冗餘與切換」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：重複設備可能仍共享失效來源。","checkEn":"Submit the Redundancy and switching diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Duplicated equipment may share failure causes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-13-k1","title":"冗餘與切換／物理與模型","titleEn":"Redundancy and switching / Physics and model","text":"機制：重複設備可能仍共享失效來源。","textEn":"Mechanism: Duplicated equipment may share failure causes."},{"id":"a098-v8-13-k2","title":"冗餘與切換／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Redundancy and switching / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「有兩台設備就必然完全容錯」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「冗餘與切換」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Redundancy and switching, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["重複設備可能仍共享失效來源","有兩台設備就必然完全容錯","只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期"],"optionsEn":["Duplicated equipment may share failure causes","Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance","Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle"],"answer":0,"explanation":"重複設備可能仍共享失效來源；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Duplicated equipment may share failure causes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-13"],"title":"冗餘與切換：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Redundancy and switching: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「有兩台設備就必然完全容錯」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance.","instruction":"接續前一步「冗餘與切換」成果，先指出錯誤主張「有兩台設備就必然完全容錯」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：共用控制器也可能是單點失效。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Redundancy and switching artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Shared controllers can be single failure points. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"重複設備可能仍共享失效來源；共用控制器也可能是單點失效。","observationEn":"Duplicated equipment may share failure causes; Shared controllers can be single failure points.","failure":"若採用「有兩台設備就必然完全容錯」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「冗餘與切換」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「共用控制器也可能是單點失效」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Redundancy and switching, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Shared controllers can be single failure points\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-14-k1","title":"冗餘與切換／物理與模型","titleEn":"Redundancy and switching / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：共用控制器也可能是單點失效。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Shared controllers can be single failure points."},{"id":"a098-v8-14-k2","title":"冗餘與切換／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Redundancy and switching / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「有兩台設備就必然完全容錯」與「重複設備可能仍共享失效來源」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance\" is not equivalent to \"Duplicated equipment may share failure causes\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「冗餘與切換」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Redundancy and switching?","options":["只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期","共用控制器也可能是單點失效","有兩台設備就必然完全容錯"],"optionsEn":["Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle","Shared controllers can be single failure points","Assuming two devices guarantee complete fault tolerance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"共用控制器也可能是單點失效；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shared controllers can be single failure points. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-14"],"title":"自動搬運：建立模型","titleEn":"Automated transport: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks.","instruction":"用假設載具佇列追蹤機台等待、在製品與交接。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Track hypothetical carrier queues, tool waits and WIP handoffs. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析；派工規則會改變機台閒置時間。","observationEn":"Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks; Dispatch policy changes tool idle time.","failure":"若採用「只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「自動搬運」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析。","checkEn":"Submit the Automated transport diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-15-k1","title":"自動搬運／物理與模型","titleEn":"Automated transport / Physics and model","text":"機制：搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析。","textEn":"Mechanism: Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks."},{"id":"a098-v8-15-k2","title":"自動搬運／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Automated transport / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「自動搬運」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Automated transport, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期","集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異","搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析"],"optionsEn":["Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle","Assuming central management removes tool differences","Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks"],"answer":2,"explanation":"搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-15"],"title":"自動搬運：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Automated transport: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle.","instruction":"接續前一步「自動搬運」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：派工規則會改變機台閒置時間。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Automated transport artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Dispatch policy changes tool idle time. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析；派工規則會改變機台閒置時間。","observationEn":"Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks; Dispatch policy changes tool idle time.","failure":"若採用「只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「自動搬運」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「派工規則會改變機台閒置時間」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Automated transport, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Dispatch policy changes tool idle time\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-16-k1","title":"自動搬運／物理與模型","titleEn":"Automated transport / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：派工規則會改變機台閒置時間。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Dispatch policy changes tool idle time."},{"id":"a098-v8-16-k2","title":"自動搬運／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Automated transport / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期」與「搬運效率需要和設備瓶頸一起分析」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle\" is not equivalent to \"Transport efficiency must be analyzed with tool bottlenecks\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「自動搬運」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Automated transport?","options":["派工規則會改變機台閒置時間","只加快運輸就必然縮短所有周期","集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異"],"optionsEn":["Dispatch policy changes tool idle time","Assuming faster transport shortens every cycle","Assuming central management removes tool differences"],"answer":0,"explanation":"派工規則會改變機台閒置時間；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Dispatch policy changes tool idle time. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-16"],"title":"集中管理：建立模型","titleEn":"Centralized management: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability.","instruction":"畫跨廠製程版本、派工與品質資料的交換界面。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw cross-fab recipe-version, dispatch and quality-data interfaces. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯；版本一致不代表機台硬體狀態一致。","observationEn":"Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability; Version agreement does not guarantee hardware equivalence.","failure":"若採用「集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming central management removes tool differences\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「集中管理」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯。","checkEn":"Submit the Centralized management diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-17-k1","title":"集中管理／物理與模型","titleEn":"Centralized management / Physics and model","text":"機制：中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯。","textEn":"Mechanism: Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability."},{"id":"a098-v8-17-k2","title":"集中管理／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Centralized management / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming central management removes tool differences."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集中管理」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Centralized management, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["關機時間越長就一定總成本最低","中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯","集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異"],"optionsEn":["Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost","Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability","Assuming central management removes tool differences"],"answer":1,"explanation":"中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-17"],"title":"集中管理：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Centralized management: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming central management removes tool differences.","instruction":"接續前一步「集中管理」成果，先指出錯誤主張「集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：版本一致不代表機台硬體狀態一致。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Centralized management artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming central management removes tool differences\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Version agreement does not guarantee hardware equivalence. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯；版本一致不代表機台硬體狀態一致。","observationEn":"Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability; Version agreement does not guarantee hardware equivalence.","failure":"若採用「集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming central management removes tool differences\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「集中管理」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「版本一致不代表機台硬體狀態一致」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Centralized management, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Version agreement does not guarantee hardware equivalence\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-18-k1","title":"集中管理／物理與模型","titleEn":"Centralized management / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：版本一致不代表機台硬體狀態一致。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Version agreement does not guarantee hardware equivalence."},{"id":"a098-v8-18-k2","title":"集中管理／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Centralized management / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異」與「中央協作需保留各設備與批次追溯」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming central management removes tool differences\" is not equivalent to \"Central coordination must preserve tool/lot traceability\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「集中管理」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Centralized management?","options":["集中管理便可抹除所有設備差異","關機時間越長就一定總成本最低","版本一致不代表機台硬體狀態一致"],"optionsEn":["Assuming central management removes tool differences","Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost","Version agreement does not guarantee hardware equivalence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"版本一致不代表機台硬體狀態一致；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Version agreement does not guarantee hardware equivalence. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a098-stage04","order":4,"title":"設備節能 → 公開案例審查","titleEn":"Equipment energy saving to Public-case review","description":"把「設備節能」「水循環盤查」「公開案例審查」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Equipment energy saving, Water accounting, Public-case review.","steps":[{"id":"a098-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-18"],"title":"設備節能：建立模型","titleEn":"Equipment energy saving: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks.","instruction":"依假設排程比較工作、待機與喚醒能量，加入重新穩定時間。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設同一設備在 8 小時比較窗口中，維持工作狀態為 10 kW、可用待機狀態為 2 kW。能耗分別 80 與 16 kWh，差 64 kWh；若喚醒與重新穩定另耗 10 kWh，淨差才是 54 kWh。這是自訂能源帳，不是台積電實測資料，也未計產能與良率代價。","instructionEn":"Compare active/idle/wakeup energy with restabilization time. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume an 8-hour comparison for one tool: active power 10 kW versus an available standby state at 2 kW. Energy is 80 versus 16 kWh, a 64 kWh difference; if wakeup and restabilization add 10 kWh, net savings are 54 kWh. These invented teaching inputs are not TSMC measurements and exclude throughput and yield costs.","observation":"節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定；喚醒後需驗證可用而非只顯示通電。","observationEn":"Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks; Wakeup needs readiness, not merely power-on status.","failure":"若採用「關機時間越長就一定總成本最低」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「設備節能」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定。\n算例驗收：驗算 64 與 54 kWh，區分 kW 功率和 kWh 能量，並列出喚醒驗收需求。","checkEn":"Submit the Equipment energy saving diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks.\nWorked-example acceptance: Verify 64 and 54 kWh, distinguish kW from kWh and list a wakeup-qualification requirement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-19-k1","title":"設備節能／物理與模型","titleEn":"Equipment energy saving / Physics and model","text":"機制：節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定。","textEn":"Mechanism: Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks."},{"id":"a098-v8-19-k2","title":"設備節能／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Equipment energy saving / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「關機時間越長就一定總成本最低」。\n假設數值與推算：假設同一設備在 8 小時比較窗口中，維持工作狀態為 10 kW、可用待機狀態為 2 kW。能耗分別 80 與 16 kWh，差 64 kWh；若喚醒與重新穩定另耗 10 kWh，淨差才是 54 kWh。這是自訂能源帳，不是台積電實測資料，也未計產能與良率代價。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume an 8-hour comparison for one tool: active power 10 kW versus an available standby state at 2 kW. Energy is 80 versus 16 kWh, a 64 kWh difference; if wakeup and restabilization add 10 kWh, net savings are 54 kWh. These invented teaching inputs are not TSMC measurements and exclude throughput and yield costs."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「設備節能」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Equipment energy saving, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定","關機時間越長就一定總成本最低","把循環流量重複算成新增節水量"],"optionsEn":["Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks","Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost","Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings"],"answer":0,"explanation":"節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-19"],"title":"設備節能：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Equipment energy saving: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「關機時間越長就一定總成本最低」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost.","instruction":"接續前一步「設備節能」成果，先指出錯誤主張「關機時間越長就一定總成本最低」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：喚醒後需驗證可用而非只顯示通電。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Equipment energy saving artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Wakeup needs readiness, not merely power-on status. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定；喚醒後需驗證可用而非只顯示通電。","observationEn":"Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks; Wakeup needs readiness, not merely power-on status.","failure":"若採用「關機時間越長就一定總成本最低」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「設備節能」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「喚醒後需驗證可用而非只顯示通電」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Equipment energy saving, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Wakeup needs readiness, not merely power-on status\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-20-k1","title":"設備節能／物理與模型","titleEn":"Equipment energy saving / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：喚醒後需驗證可用而非只顯示通電。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Wakeup needs readiness, not merely power-on status."},{"id":"a098-v8-20-k2","title":"設備節能／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Equipment energy saving / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「關機時間越長就一定總成本最低」與「節能策略須同時驗證產能和製程穩定」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost\" is not equivalent to \"Energy strategies need throughput and process-stability checks\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「設備節能」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Equipment energy saving?","options":["把循環流量重複算成新增節水量","喚醒後需驗證可用而非只顯示通電","關機時間越長就一定總成本最低"],"optionsEn":["Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings","Wakeup needs readiness, not merely power-on status","Assuming longer shutdown always minimizes total cost"],"answer":1,"explanation":"喚醒後需驗證可用而非只顯示通電；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Wakeup needs readiness, not merely power-on status. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-20"],"title":"水循環盤查：建立模型","titleEn":"Water accounting: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries.","instruction":"分開取水、回收、再使用與排放，檢查假設質量平衡。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate withdrawal, recovery, reuse and discharge in a mass balance. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界；水質不同不能直接互換用途。","observationEn":"Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries; Different water qualities are not interchangeable.","failure":"若採用「把循環流量重複算成新增節水量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「水循環盤查」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界。","checkEn":"Submit the Water accounting diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-21-k1","title":"水循環盤查／物理與模型","titleEn":"Water accounting / Physics and model","text":"機制：回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界。","textEn":"Mechanism: Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries."},{"id":"a098-v8-21-k2","title":"水循環盤查／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Water accounting / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把循環流量重複算成新增節水量」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水循環盤查」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Water accounting, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["把循環流量重複算成新增節水量","以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定","回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界"],"optionsEn":["Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings","Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage","Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries"],"answer":2,"explanation":"回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-21"],"title":"水循環盤查：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Water accounting: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把循環流量重複算成新增節水量」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings.","instruction":"接續前一步「水循環盤查」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把循環流量重複算成新增節水量」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：水質不同不能直接互換用途。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Water accounting artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Different water qualities are not interchangeable. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界；水質不同不能直接互換用途。","observationEn":"Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries; Different water qualities are not interchangeable.","failure":"若採用「把循環流量重複算成新增節水量」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「水循環盤查」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「水質不同不能直接互換用途」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Water accounting, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Different water qualities are not interchangeable\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-22-k1","title":"水循環盤查／物理與模型","titleEn":"Water accounting / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：水質不同不能直接互換用途。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Different water qualities are not interchangeable."},{"id":"a098-v8-22-k2","title":"水循環盤查／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Water accounting / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把循環流量重複算成新增節水量」與「回收率須清楚定義分母和邊界」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings\" is not equivalent to \"Recovery rates require defined denominators and boundaries\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「水循環盤查」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Water accounting?","options":["水質不同不能直接互換用途","把循環流量重複算成新增節水量","以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定"],"optionsEn":["Different water qualities are not interchangeable","Counting circulating flow repeatedly as new savings","Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"水質不同不能直接互換用途；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Different water qualities are not interchangeable. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-22"],"title":"公開案例審查：建立模型","titleEn":"Public-case review: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes.","instruction":"將官方事實、教學假設和未公開部分三欄列明。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate official facts, teaching assumptions and undisclosed details. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方；廣告目標與已量測成果應分開。","observationEn":"Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes; Separate announced targets from measured achievements.","failure":"若採用「以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「公開案例審查」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方。","checkEn":"Submit the Public-case review diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-23-k1","title":"公開案例審查／物理與模型","titleEn":"Public-case review / Physics and model","text":"機制：公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方。","textEn":"Mechanism: Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes."},{"id":"a098-v8-23-k2","title":"公開案例審查／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Public-case review / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「公開案例審查」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Public-case review, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同","公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方","以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定"],"optionsEn":["Inferring identical internal flows from a company name","Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes","Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a098-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-gigafab","v8-c-fab-energy"],"prerequisiteIds":["a098-v8-23"],"title":"公開案例審查：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Public-case review: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage.","instruction":"接續前一步「公開案例審查」成果，先指出錯誤主張「以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：廣告目標與已量測成果應分開。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Public-case review artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Separate announced targets from measured achievements. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方；廣告目標與已量測成果應分開。","observationEn":"Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes; Separate announced targets from measured achievements.","failure":"若採用「以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「公開案例審查」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「廣告目標與已量測成果應分開」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Public-case review, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Separate announced targets from measured achievements\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a098-v8-24-k1","title":"公開案例審查／物理與模型","titleEn":"Public-case review / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：廣告目標與已量測成果應分開。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Separate announced targets from measured achievements."},{"id":"a098-v8-24-k2","title":"公開案例審查／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Public-case review / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定」與「公開績效不能反推出專有控制配方」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage\" is not equivalent to \"Public performance does not reveal proprietary control recipes\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「公開案例審查」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Public-case review?","options":["以公開節能百分比還原內部所有設定","用企業名稱推斷所有內部製程完全相同","廣告目標與已量測成果應分開"],"optionsEn":["Reconstructing all settings from a public savings percentage","Inferring identical internal flows from a company name","Separate announced targets from measured achievements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"廣告目標與已量測成果應分開；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Separate announced targets from measured achievements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"a099","title":"imec NanoIC 試驗線架構","titleEn":"imec NanoIC pilot-line architecture","category":"semiconductor","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":8,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":550,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool","v8-c-imec-place","v3-media-80679a241086"],"simulationOnly":true,"summary":"從試驗線目的、系統探索到里程碑核對：以 12 項工程決策、24 個模型與診斷工作包建立證據。","summaryEn":"From Pilot-line purpose and System exploration to Milestone verification: build evidence through twelve engineering decisions and twenty-four modeling/diagnostic work packages.","scope":"公開原理的教學拆解：12 個技術主題各有模型／分析及故障／驗證兩步，共四階段 24 步。不是 24 道實際製造配方，也不是任何廠商量產流程。數值由學員自訂並標示為假設；涉及材料加工、高壓、雷射或化學品的活動僅做圖上與資料分析，不由網頁授權實機操作。","scopeEn":"A public-principles educational decomposition: twelve technical topics each have a model/analysis step and a diagnosis/verification step, organized as four stages and twenty-four work packages. These are not twenty-four fabrication recipes or a manufacturer flow. Learner-selected numbers are hypothetical; materials processing, high voltage, lasers and chemicals are studied through diagrams/data, not authorized physical operation.","diagram":{"type":"wafer","labels":["試驗線目的","探索 PDK","測試載具","資料與存取"],"labelsEn":["Pilot-line purpose","Pathfinding PDK","Test vehicles","Data and access"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a099-stage01","order":1,"title":"試驗線目的 → 技術模組","titleEn":"Pilot-line purpose to Technology modules","description":"把「試驗線目的」「跨國節點」「技術模組」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pilot-line purpose, Distributed nodes, Technology modules.","steps":[{"id":"a099-v8-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"試驗線目的：建立模型","titleEn":"Pilot-line purpose: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives.","instruction":"畫研究假說、試片、學習迴圈與量產移轉四個功能。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw hypothesis, test vehicle, learning cycle and production-transfer functions. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同；技術成功也需評估可移轉性。","observationEn":"Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives; Technical success also needs transferability assessment.","failure":"若採用「有最先進設備便等於產品已量產」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「試驗線目的」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同。","checkEn":"Submit the Pilot-line purpose diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-01-k1","title":"試驗線目的／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pilot-line purpose / Physics and model","text":"機制：試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同。","textEn":"Mechanism: Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives."},{"id":"a099-v8-01-k2","title":"試驗線目的／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pilot-line purpose / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「有最先進設備便等於產品已量產」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「試驗線目的」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pilot-line purpose, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同","有最先進設備便等於產品已量產","所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室"],"optionsEn":["Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives","Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products","Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom"],"answer":0,"explanation":"試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-01"],"title":"試驗線目的：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pilot-line purpose: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「有最先進設備便等於產品已量產」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products.","instruction":"接續前一步「試驗線目的」成果，先指出錯誤主張「有最先進設備便等於產品已量產」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：技術成功也需評估可移轉性。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pilot-line purpose artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Technical success also needs transferability assessment. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同；技術成功也需評估可移轉性。","observationEn":"Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives; Technical success also needs transferability assessment.","failure":"若採用「有最先進設備便等於產品已量產」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「試驗線目的」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「技術成功也需評估可移轉性」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pilot-line purpose, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Technical success also needs transferability assessment\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-02-k1","title":"試驗線目的／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pilot-line purpose / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：技術成功也需評估可移轉性。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Technical success also needs transferability assessment."},{"id":"a099-v8-02-k2","title":"試驗線目的／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pilot-line purpose / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「有最先進設備便等於產品已量產」與「試驗線用於技術驗證，與量產工廠目標不同」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products\" is not equivalent to \"Pilot lines validate technology and differ from volume-fab objectives\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「試驗線目的」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pilot-line purpose?","options":["所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室","技術成功也需評估可移轉性","有最先進設備便等於產品已量產"],"optionsEn":["Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom","Technical success also needs transferability assessment","Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products"],"answer":1,"explanation":"技術成功也需評估可移轉性；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Technical success also needs transferability assessment. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-02"],"title":"跨國節點：建立模型","titleEn":"Distributed nodes: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility.","instruction":"依官方資料畫 imec 與合作研究機構，不臆測每台設備所在地。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Map imec and official research partners without guessing tool locations. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任；共通文件格式仍需語意一致。","observationEn":"Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility; Common file formats still need semantic consistency.","failure":"若採用「所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「跨國節點」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任。","checkEn":"Submit the Distributed nodes diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-03-k1","title":"跨國節點／物理與模型","titleEn":"Distributed nodes / Physics and model","text":"機制：分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任。","textEn":"Mechanism: Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility."},{"id":"a099-v8-03-k2","title":"跨國節點／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Distributed nodes / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨國節點」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Distributed nodes, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室","小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力","分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任"],"optionsEn":["Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom","Treating a node label as a complete system capability description","Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility"],"answer":2,"explanation":"分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-03"],"title":"跨國節點：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Distributed nodes: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom.","instruction":"接續前一步「跨國節點」成果，先指出錯誤主張「所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：共通文件格式仍需語意一致。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Distributed nodes artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Common file formats still need semantic consistency. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任；共通文件格式仍需語意一致。","observationEn":"Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility; Common file formats still need semantic consistency.","failure":"若採用「所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「跨國節點」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「共通文件格式仍需語意一致」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Distributed nodes, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Common file formats still need semantic consistency\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-04-k1","title":"跨國節點／物理與模型","titleEn":"Distributed nodes / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：共通文件格式仍需語意一致。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Common file formats still need semantic consistency."},{"id":"a099-v8-04-k2","title":"跨國節點／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Distributed nodes / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室」與「分散合作需要清楚接口及資料責任」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom\" is not equivalent to \"Distributed collaboration needs clear interfaces and data responsibility\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「跨國節點」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Distributed nodes?","options":["共通文件格式仍需語意一致","所有合作工作都假設在同一無塵室","小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力"],"optionsEn":["Common file formats still need semantic consistency","Assuming all partner work happens in one cleanroom","Treating a node label as a complete system capability description"],"answer":0,"explanation":"共通文件格式仍需語意一致；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Common file formats still need semantic consistency. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-04"],"title":"技術模組：建立模型","titleEn":"Technology modules: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「超越節點縮放還包括異質整合」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration.","instruction":"分開邏輯、記憶體、光電互連及封裝的輸入輸出。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate logic, memory, optical/electrical links and packaging interfaces. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"超越節點縮放還包括異質整合；系統瓶頸不一定是最小電晶體。","observationEn":"Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration; System bottlenecks are not necessarily smallest transistors.","failure":"若採用「小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a node label as a complete system capability description\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「技術模組」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：超越節點縮放還包括異質整合。","checkEn":"Submit the Technology modules diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-05-k1","title":"技術模組／物理與模型","titleEn":"Technology modules / Physics and model","text":"機制：超越節點縮放還包括異質整合。","textEn":"Mechanism: Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration."},{"id":"a099-v8-05-k2","title":"技術模組／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Technology modules / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating a node label as a complete system capability description."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「技術模組」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Technology modules, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產","超越節點縮放還包括異質整合","小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication","Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration","Treating a node label as a complete system capability description"],"answer":1,"explanation":"超越節點縮放還包括異質整合；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-05"],"title":"技術模組：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Technology modules: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating a node label as a complete system capability description.","instruction":"接續前一步「技術模組」成果，先指出錯誤主張「小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：系統瓶頸不一定是最小電晶體。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Technology modules artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating a node label as a complete system capability description\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: System bottlenecks are not necessarily smallest transistors. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"超越節點縮放還包括異質整合；系統瓶頸不一定是最小電晶體。","observationEn":"Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration; System bottlenecks are not necessarily smallest transistors.","failure":"若採用「小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a node label as a complete system capability description\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「技術模組」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「系統瓶頸不一定是最小電晶體」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Technology modules, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"System bottlenecks are not necessarily smallest transistors\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-06-k1","title":"技術模組／物理與模型","titleEn":"Technology modules / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：系統瓶頸不一定是最小電晶體。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: System bottlenecks are not necessarily smallest transistors."},{"id":"a099-v8-06-k2","title":"技術模組／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Technology modules / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力」與「超越節點縮放還包括異質整合」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating a node label as a complete system capability description\" is not equivalent to \"Beyond-node development also involves heterogeneous integration\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「技術模組」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Technology modules?","options":["小節點名稱已完整描述全部系統能力","探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產","系統瓶頸不一定是最小電晶體"],"optionsEn":["Treating a node label as a complete system capability description","Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication","System bottlenecks are not necessarily smallest transistors"],"answer":2,"explanation":"系統瓶頸不一定是最小電晶體；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"System bottlenecks are not necessarily smallest transistors. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a099-stage02","order":2,"title":"探索 PDK → High-NA 接入","titleEn":"Pathfinding PDK to High-NA integration","description":"把「探索 PDK」「系統探索」「High-NA 接入」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Pathfinding PDK, System exploration, High-NA integration.","steps":[{"id":"a099-v8-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-06"],"title":"探索 PDK：建立模型","titleEn":"Pathfinding PDK: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「探索模型不等於量產保證模型」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models.","instruction":"列出設計探索模型、設計規則與已知不確定性。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"List pathfinding models, rules and known uncertainties. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"探索模型不等於量產保證模型；PDK 版本改動可改變設計結論。","observationEn":"Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models; PDK versions can change design conclusions.","failure":"若採用「探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「探索 PDK」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：探索模型不等於量產保證模型。","checkEn":"Submit the Pathfinding PDK diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-07-k1","title":"探索 PDK／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pathfinding PDK / Physics and model","text":"機制：探索模型不等於量產保證模型。","textEn":"Mechanism: Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models."},{"id":"a099-v8-07-k2","title":"探索 PDK／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pathfinding PDK / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「探索 PDK」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Pathfinding PDK, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["探索模型不等於量產保證模型","探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產","新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能"],"optionsEn":["Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models","Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication","Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"探索模型不等於量產保證模型；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-07"],"title":"探索 PDK：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Pathfinding PDK: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication.","instruction":"接續前一步「探索 PDK」成果，先指出錯誤主張「探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：PDK 版本改動可改變設計結論。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Pathfinding PDK artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: PDK versions can change design conclusions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"探索模型不等於量產保證模型；PDK 版本改動可改變設計結論。","observationEn":"Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models; PDK versions can change design conclusions.","failure":"若採用「探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「探索 PDK」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「PDK 版本改動可改變設計結論」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Pathfinding PDK, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"PDK versions can change design conclusions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-08-k1","title":"探索 PDK／物理與模型","titleEn":"Pathfinding PDK / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：PDK 版本改動可改變設計結論。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: PDK versions can change design conclusions."},{"id":"a099-v8-08-k2","title":"探索 PDK／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Pathfinding PDK / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產」與「探索模型不等於量產保證模型」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication\" is not equivalent to \"Pathfinding models are not production-guaranteed models\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「探索 PDK」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Pathfinding PDK?","options":["新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能","PDK 版本改動可改變設計結論","探索 PDK 通過便保證可立即流片量產"],"optionsEn":["Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions","PDK versions can change design conclusions","Assuming a pathfinding pass guarantees immediate volume fabrication"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PDK 版本改動可改變設計結論；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"PDK versions can change design conclusions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-08"],"title":"系統探索：建立模型","titleEn":"System exploration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits.","instruction":"畫既有晶圓與新增模組的相容接口。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw compatibility interfaces between existing wafers and new modules. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界；新模組的良率會乘入整體良率。","observationEn":"System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits; New-module yield compounds system yield.","failure":"若採用「新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「系統探索」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界。","checkEn":"Submit the System exploration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-09-k1","title":"系統探索／物理與模型","titleEn":"System exploration / Physics and model","text":"機制：系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界。","textEn":"Mechanism: System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits."},{"id":"a099-v8-09-k2","title":"系統探索／驗證與限制","titleEn":"System exploration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「系統探索」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For System exploration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能","設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造","系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界"],"optionsEn":["Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions","Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture","System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits"],"answer":2,"explanation":"系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-09"],"title":"系統探索：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"System exploration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions.","instruction":"接續前一步「系統探索」成果，先指出錯誤主張「新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：新模組的良率會乘入整體良率。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding System exploration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: New-module yield compounds system yield. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界；新模組的良率會乘入整體良率。","observationEn":"System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits; New-module yield compounds system yield.","failure":"若採用「新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「系統探索」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「新模組的良率會乘入整體良率」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for System exploration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"New-module yield compounds system yield\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-10-k1","title":"系統探索／物理與模型","titleEn":"System exploration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：新模組的良率會乘入整體良率。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: New-module yield compounds system yield."},{"id":"a099-v8-10-k2","title":"系統探索／驗證與限制","titleEn":"System exploration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能」與「系統探索需考慮既有層的熱及電性邊界」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions\" is not equivalent to \"System exploration must respect existing-layer thermal/electrical limits\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「系統探索」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of System exploration?","options":["新模組的良率會乘入整體良率","新模組可任意改變已完成晶圓而不影響其餘功能","設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造"],"optionsEn":["New-module yield compounds system yield","Changing finished wafers without affecting existing functions","Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture"],"answer":0,"explanation":"新模組的良率會乘入整體良率；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"New-module yield compounds system yield. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-10"],"title":"High-NA 接入：建立模型","titleEn":"High-NA integration: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: New scanners need validation with other process modules.","instruction":"畫曝光、光阻、蝕刻與量測的閉環學習鏈。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Draw the lithography/resist/etch/metrology learning loop. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證；圖形轉移損傷也需獨立驗證。","observationEn":"New scanners need validation with other process modules; Pattern-transfer damage needs independent validation.","failure":"若採用「設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「High-NA 接入」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證。","checkEn":"Submit the High-NA integration diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: New scanners need validation with other process modules.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-11-k1","title":"High-NA 接入／物理與模型","titleEn":"High-NA integration / Physics and model","text":"機制：新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證。","textEn":"Mechanism: New scanners need validation with other process modules."},{"id":"a099-v8-11-k2","title":"High-NA 接入／驗證與限制","titleEn":"High-NA integration / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「High-NA 接入」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For High-NA integration, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["只做完整大晶片才算有效研究","新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證","設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造"],"optionsEn":["Treating only full large chips as useful research","New scanners need validation with other process modules","Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture"],"answer":1,"explanation":"新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"New scanners need validation with other process modules. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-11"],"title":"High-NA 接入：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"High-NA integration: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture.","instruction":"接續前一步「High-NA 接入」成果，先指出錯誤主張「設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：圖形轉移損傷也需獨立驗證。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding High-NA integration artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Pattern-transfer damage needs independent validation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證；圖形轉移損傷也需獨立驗證。","observationEn":"New scanners need validation with other process modules; Pattern-transfer damage needs independent validation.","failure":"若採用「設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「High-NA 接入」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「圖形轉移損傷也需獨立驗證」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for High-NA integration, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Pattern-transfer damage needs independent validation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-12-k1","title":"High-NA 接入／物理與模型","titleEn":"High-NA integration / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：圖形轉移損傷也需獨立驗證。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Pattern-transfer damage needs independent validation."},{"id":"a099-v8-12-k2","title":"High-NA 接入／驗證與限制","titleEn":"High-NA integration / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造」與「新曝光機必須與其他製程模組共同驗證」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture\" is not equivalent to \"New scanners need validation with other process modules\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「High-NA 接入」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of High-NA integration?","options":["設備到貨就等於所有圖形已可穩定製造","只做完整大晶片才算有效研究","圖形轉移損傷也需獨立驗證"],"optionsEn":["Equating tool arrival with stable pattern manufacture","Treating only full large chips as useful research","Pattern-transfer damage needs independent validation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"圖形轉移損傷也需獨立驗證；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Pattern-transfer damage needs independent validation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a099-stage03","order":3,"title":"測試載具 → 量測互通","titleEn":"Test vehicles to Metrology interoperability","description":"把「測試載具」「分批實驗」「量測互通」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Test vehicles, Split experiments, Metrology interoperability.","steps":[{"id":"a099-v8-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-12"],"title":"測試載具：建立模型","titleEn":"Test vehicles: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements.","instruction":"為接觸、互連與記憶各設計一個隔離風險的假設試片。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Design hypothetical contact, link and memory vehicles isolating risks. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題；對照試片應保留相同量測條件。","observationEn":"Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements; Controls need matching measurement conditions.","failure":"若採用「只做完整大晶片才算有效研究」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating only full large chips as useful research\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「測試載具」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題。","checkEn":"Submit the Test vehicles diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-13-k1","title":"測試載具／物理與模型","titleEn":"Test vehicles / Physics and model","text":"機制：試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題。","textEn":"Mechanism: Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements."},{"id":"a099-v8-13-k2","title":"測試載具／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Test vehicles / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「只做完整大晶片才算有效研究」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating only full large chips as useful research."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測試載具」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Test vehicles, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題","只做完整大晶片才算有效研究","同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因"],"optionsEn":["Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements","Treating only full large chips as useful research","Attributing causes after changing every module"],"answer":0,"explanation":"試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-13"],"title":"測試載具：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Test vehicles: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「只做完整大晶片才算有效研究」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating only full large chips as useful research.","instruction":"接續前一步「測試載具」成果，先指出錯誤主張「只做完整大晶片才算有效研究」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：對照試片應保留相同量測條件。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Test vehicles artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating only full large chips as useful research\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Controls need matching measurement conditions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題；對照試片應保留相同量測條件。","observationEn":"Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements; Controls need matching measurement conditions.","failure":"若採用「只做完整大晶片才算有效研究」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating only full large chips as useful research\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「測試載具」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「對照試片應保留相同量測條件」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Test vehicles, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Controls need matching measurement conditions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-14-k1","title":"測試載具／物理與模型","titleEn":"Test vehicles / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：對照試片應保留相同量測條件。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Controls need matching measurement conditions."},{"id":"a099-v8-14-k2","title":"測試載具／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Test vehicles / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「只做完整大晶片才算有效研究」與「試片應將技術風險轉為可量測問題」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating only full large chips as useful research\" is not equivalent to \"Test vehicles turn technology risks into measurements\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「測試載具」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Test vehicles?","options":["同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因","對照試片應保留相同量測條件","只做完整大晶片才算有效研究"],"optionsEn":["Attributing causes after changing every module","Controls need matching measurement conditions","Treating only full large chips as useful research"],"answer":1,"explanation":"對照試片應保留相同量測條件；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Controls need matching measurement conditions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-14"],"title":"分批實驗：建立模型","titleEn":"Split experiments: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Experimental matrices help separate interactions.","instruction":"建立只改兩項變因的假設分批矩陣，保留對照。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。\n\n具體算例（全部數值為教學假設）：假設試驗線比較兩個因子 A、B，各低／高兩水準，全因子需要 2²=4 組條件。每組做 3 個獨立製程重複，共 12 次；對同一試片讀三次不是三個獨立製程重複。若四組平均響應依 A低B低、A高B低、A低B高、A高B高為 10、14、12、20，A 效應在 B低為 4、B高為 8，交互作用的差中之差為 4。","instructionEn":"Build a two-factor hypothetical split with controls. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.\n\nWorked example (all values are hypothetical teaching inputs): Assume a pilot-line experiment with two factors A and B at low/high levels. A full factorial needs 2²=4 conditions; three independent process replicates per condition require 12 runs. Three readings of one specimen are not three independent process replicates. If condition means in low-low, high-low, low-high and high-high order are 10, 14, 12 and 20, A effects are 4 at low B and 8 at high B, giving a difference-in-differences interaction contrast of 4.","observation":"實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用；分批設計須記錄交互作用假設。","observationEn":"Experimental matrices help separate interactions; Split designs need stated interaction assumptions.","failure":"若採用「同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing causes after changing every module\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「分批實驗」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用。\n算例驗收：列出四組矩陣、12 次獨立重複及交互作用對比 4；註明此為未標準化差中之差，不等同所有軟體的效應係數定義。","checkEn":"Submit the Split experiments diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Experimental matrices help separate interactions.\nWorked-example acceptance: List four conditions, 12 independent runs and interaction contrast 4; note that this unscaled difference-in-differences is not every software package's effect-coefficient definition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-15-k1","title":"分批實驗／物理與模型","titleEn":"Split experiments / Physics and model","text":"機制：實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用。","textEn":"Mechanism: Experimental matrices help separate interactions."},{"id":"a099-v8-15-k2","title":"分批實驗／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Split experiments / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因」。\n假設數值與推算：假設試驗線比較兩個因子 A、B，各低／高兩水準，全因子需要 2²=4 組條件。每組做 3 個獨立製程重複，共 12 次；對同一試片讀三次不是三個獨立製程重複。若四組平均響應依 A低B低、A高B低、A低B高、A高B高為 10、14、12、20，A 效應在 B低為 4、B高為 8，交互作用的差中之差為 4。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Attributing causes after changing every module.\nHypothetical inputs and calculation: Assume a pilot-line experiment with two factors A and B at low/high levels. A full factorial needs 2²=4 conditions; three independent process replicates per condition require 12 runs. Three readings of one specimen are not three independent process replicates. If condition means in low-low, high-low, low-high and high-high order are 10, 14, 12 and 20, A effects are 4 at low B and 8 at high B, giving a difference-in-differences interaction contrast of 4."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「分批實驗」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Split experiments, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因","同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據","實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用"],"optionsEn":["Attributing causes after changing every module","Pooling every CD value solely from its label","Experimental matrices help separate interactions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Experimental matrices help separate interactions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-15"],"title":"分批實驗：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Split experiments: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Attributing causes after changing every module.","instruction":"接續前一步「分批實驗」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：分批設計須記錄交互作用假設。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Split experiments artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Attributing causes after changing every module\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Split designs need stated interaction assumptions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用；分批設計須記錄交互作用假設。","observationEn":"Experimental matrices help separate interactions; Split designs need stated interaction assumptions.","failure":"若採用「同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Attributing causes after changing every module\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「分批實驗」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「分批設計須記錄交互作用假設」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Split experiments, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Split designs need stated interaction assumptions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-16-k1","title":"分批實驗／物理與模型","titleEn":"Split experiments / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：分批設計須記錄交互作用假設。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Split designs need stated interaction assumptions."},{"id":"a099-v8-16-k2","title":"分批實驗／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Split experiments / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因」與「實驗矩陣有助區分交互作用」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Attributing causes after changing every module\" is not equivalent to \"Experimental matrices help separate interactions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「分批實驗」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Split experiments?","options":["分批設計須記錄交互作用假設","同時更改全部模組後仍能單獨歸因","同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據"],"optionsEn":["Split designs need stated interaction assumptions","Attributing causes after changing every module","Pooling every CD value solely from its label"],"answer":0,"explanation":"分批設計須記錄交互作用假設；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Split designs need stated interaction assumptions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-16"],"title":"量測互通：建立模型","titleEn":"Metrology interoperability: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「相同欄名不保證相同量測定義」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands.","instruction":"將跨機構尺寸定義、校正和不確定度放入交換表。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Align cross-institution definitions, calibration and uncertainties. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"相同欄名不保證相同量測定義；跨站時間戳也需共同定義。","observationEn":"Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands; Cross-site timestamps require common definitions.","failure":"若採用「同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Pooling every CD value solely from its label\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「量測互通」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：相同欄名不保證相同量測定義。","checkEn":"Submit the Metrology interoperability diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-17-k1","title":"量測互通／物理與模型","titleEn":"Metrology interoperability / Physics and model","text":"機制：相同欄名不保證相同量測定義。","textEn":"Mechanism: Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands."},{"id":"a099-v8-17-k2","title":"量測互通／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Metrology interoperability / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Pooling every CD value solely from its label."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測互通」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Metrology interoperability, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔","相同欄名不保證相同量測定義","同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據"],"optionsEn":["Assuming participation permits publication of all files","Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands","Pooling every CD value solely from its label"],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同欄名不保證相同量測定義；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-17"],"title":"量測互通：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Metrology interoperability: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Pooling every CD value solely from its label.","instruction":"接續前一步「量測互通」成果，先指出錯誤主張「同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：跨站時間戳也需共同定義。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Metrology interoperability artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Pooling every CD value solely from its label\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Cross-site timestamps require common definitions. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"相同欄名不保證相同量測定義；跨站時間戳也需共同定義。","observationEn":"Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands; Cross-site timestamps require common definitions.","failure":"若採用「同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Pooling every CD value solely from its label\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「量測互通」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「跨站時間戳也需共同定義」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Metrology interoperability, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Cross-site timestamps require common definitions\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-18-k1","title":"量測互通／物理與模型","titleEn":"Metrology interoperability / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：跨站時間戳也需共同定義。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Cross-site timestamps require common definitions."},{"id":"a099-v8-18-k2","title":"量測互通／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Metrology interoperability / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據」與「相同欄名不保證相同量測定義」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Pooling every CD value solely from its label\" is not equivalent to \"Identical column names do not ensure identical measurands\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「量測互通」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Metrology interoperability?","options":["同寫 CD 就可直接合併所有數據","參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔","跨站時間戳也需共同定義"],"optionsEn":["Pooling every CD value solely from its label","Assuming participation permits publication of all files","Cross-site timestamps require common definitions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"跨站時間戳也需共同定義；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Cross-site timestamps require common definitions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]},{"id":"a099-stage04","order":4,"title":"資料與存取 → 里程碑核對","titleEn":"Data and access to Milestone verification","description":"把「資料與存取」「成熟度門檻」「里程碑核對」各拆成模型與診斷兩項工作，保留可檢查成果。","descriptionEn":"Develop model and diagnostic deliverables for Data and access, Maturity gates, Milestone verification.","steps":[{"id":"a099-v8-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-18"],"title":"資料與存取：建立模型","titleEn":"Data and access: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions.","instruction":"用假設合作案分開公開結果、受限資料與可分享模型。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate public results, restricted data and shareable models in a hypothetical project. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權；分享模型也須說明使用邊界。","observationEn":"Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions; Shared models need use-boundary documentation.","failure":"若採用「參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming participation permits publication of all files\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「資料與存取」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權。","checkEn":"Submit the Data and access diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-19-k1","title":"資料與存取／物理與模型","titleEn":"Data and access / Physics and model","text":"機制：技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權。","textEn":"Mechanism: Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions."},{"id":"a099-v8-19-k2","title":"資料與存取／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Data and access / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Assuming participation permits publication of all files."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資料與存取」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Data and access, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權","參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔","單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟"],"optionsEn":["Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions","Assuming participation permits publication of all files","Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-19"],"title":"資料與存取：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Data and access: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Assuming participation permits publication of all files.","instruction":"接續前一步「資料與存取」成果，先指出錯誤主張「參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：分享模型也須說明使用邊界。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Data and access artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Assuming participation permits publication of all files\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Shared models need use-boundary documentation. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權；分享模型也須說明使用邊界。","observationEn":"Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions; Shared models need use-boundary documentation.","failure":"若採用「參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Assuming participation permits publication of all files\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「資料與存取」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「分享模型也須說明使用邊界」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Data and access, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Shared models need use-boundary documentation\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-20-k1","title":"資料與存取／物理與模型","titleEn":"Data and access / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：分享模型也須說明使用邊界。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Shared models need use-boundary documentation."},{"id":"a099-v8-20-k2","title":"資料與存取／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Data and access / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔」與「技術存取和公開再散布是不同授權」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Assuming participation permits publication of all files\" is not equivalent to \"Technology access and public redistribution are different permissions\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「資料與存取」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Data and access?","options":["單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟","分享模型也須說明使用邊界","參與試驗線便代表可以公開所有圖檔"],"optionsEn":["Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity","Shared models need use-boundary documentation","Assuming participation permits publication of all files"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分享模型也須說明使用邊界；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Shared models need use-boundary documentation. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-20"],"title":"成熟度門檻：建立模型","titleEn":"Maturity gates: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric.","instruction":"定義可重複性、晶圓分布、可靠度與移轉文件的驗收。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Define repeatability, wafer distributions, reliability and transfer evidence. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標；樣本數與失敗樣本不能從門檻中消失。","observationEn":"Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric; Gates must retain sample counts and failures.","failure":"若採用「單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「成熟度門檻」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標。","checkEn":"Submit the Maturity gates diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-21-k1","title":"成熟度門檻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Maturity gates / Physics and model","text":"機制：成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標。","textEn":"Mechanism: Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric."},{"id":"a099-v8-21-k2","title":"成熟度門檻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Maturity gates / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「成熟度門檻」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Maturity gates, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟","把預定時程當成已完成量測結果","成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標"],"optionsEn":["Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity","Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence","Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric"],"answer":2,"explanation":"成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-21"],"title":"成熟度門檻：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Maturity gates: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity.","instruction":"接續前一步「成熟度門檻」成果，先指出錯誤主張「單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：樣本數與失敗樣本不能從門檻中消失。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Maturity gates artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Gates must retain sample counts and failures. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標；樣本數與失敗樣本不能從門檻中消失。","observationEn":"Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric; Gates must retain sample counts and failures.","failure":"若採用「單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「成熟度門檻」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「樣本數與失敗樣本不能從門檻中消失」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Maturity gates, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Gates must retain sample counts and failures\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-22-k1","title":"成熟度門檻／物理與模型","titleEn":"Maturity gates / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：樣本數與失敗樣本不能從門檻中消失。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Gates must retain sample counts and failures."},{"id":"a099-v8-22-k2","title":"成熟度門檻／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Maturity gates / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟」與「成熟度是證據集合，不只是單一最佳指標」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity\" is not equivalent to \"Maturity is a body of evidence, not a record metric\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「成熟度門檻」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Maturity gates?","options":["樣本數與失敗樣本不能從門檻中消失","單顆最佳展示就視為可量產成熟","把預定時程當成已完成量測結果"],"optionsEn":["Gates must retain sample counts and failures","Treating one record device as manufacturing maturity","Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"樣本數與失敗樣本不能從門檻中消失；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Gates must retain sample counts and failures. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-22"],"title":"里程碑核對：建立模型","titleEn":"Milestone verification: construct and analyze","objective":"用可檢查的成果說明「各里程碑代表不同完成程度」。","objectiveEn":"Demonstrate the following with inspectable work: Milestones represent different completion states.","instruction":"分開無塵室啟用、設備到貨、安裝校正與試片產出。先標出輸入、輸出與適用假設；依圖形、計算或比較表完成推理；把估算、來源事實與待量測項分開。所有自行設定數值均標為教學假設。","instructionEn":"Separate cleanroom opening, arrival, qualification and test output. Mark inputs, outputs and assumptions; complete the diagram, calculation or comparison; separate estimates, source facts and measurements still needed. Label all chosen values as hypothetical.","observation":"各里程碑代表不同完成程度；設備校正和產品資格是不同驗收。","observationEn":"Milestones represent different completion states; Tool qualification and product qualification differ.","failure":"若採用「把預定時程當成已完成量測結果」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"提交「里程碑核對」的圖表或計算、單位與至少一項假設；成果須能追溯到本步指定的輸入和輸出，並說明：各里程碑代表不同完成程度。","checkEn":"Submit the Milestone verification diagram/table or calculation with units and at least one assumption, tracing inputs to outputs and explaining: Milestones represent different completion states.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-23-k1","title":"里程碑核對／物理與模型","titleEn":"Milestone verification / Physics and model","text":"機制：各里程碑代表不同完成程度。","textEn":"Mechanism: Milestones represent different completion states."},{"id":"a099-v8-23-k2","title":"里程碑核對／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Milestone verification / Verification and limits","text":"模型邊界：不可由目前成果直接推出「把預定時程當成已完成量測結果」。","textEn":"Model boundary: the current result does not establish the following claim: Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「里程碑核對」，哪項推論有物理依據？","questionEn":"For Milestone verification, which inference has a physical basis?","options":["有最先進設備便等於產品已量產","各里程碑代表不同完成程度","把預定時程當成已完成量測結果"],"optionsEn":["Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products","Milestones represent different completion states","Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"各里程碑代表不同完成程度；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Milestones represent different completion states. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}},{"id":"a099-v8-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8-c-nanoic","v8-c-nanoic-open","v8-c-nanoic-tool"],"prerequisiteIds":["a099-v8-23"],"title":"里程碑核對：故障判讀與驗證","titleEn":"Milestone verification: diagnose and verify","objective":"以新增對照檢查「把預定時程當成已完成量測結果」這項錯誤主張。","objectiveEn":"Test the faulty claim: Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence.","instruction":"接續前一步「里程碑核對」成果，先指出錯誤主張「把預定時程當成已完成量測結果」漏掉哪個條件。新增診斷原理：設備校正和產品資格是不同驗收。據此設計一組正常與異常對照；指定可區分兩者的觀察量、取樣位置或時間；寫下證據不足時應保留的未決結論。不得虛構實測數字。","instructionEn":"Continue the preceding Milestone verification artifact. Identify the missing condition in the faulty claim \"Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence\". Introduce this diagnostic principle: Tool qualification and product qualification differ. Design normal/fault controls; specify a distinguishing observable, sampling location or time; state what remains undecided without evidence. Do not fabricate measurements.","observation":"各里程碑代表不同完成程度；設備校正和產品資格是不同驗收。","observationEn":"Milestones represent different completion states; Tool qualification and product qualification differ.","failure":"若採用「把預定時程當成已完成量測結果」，先回到前一步模型，檢查假設、量測條件及本步的診斷因素。","failureEn":"If using the claim \"Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence\", return to the model and check assumptions, measurement conditions and the diagnostic factor.","check":"交出「里程碑核對」的正常／異常比較、可觀察量與一項仍未確定事項；必須解釋「設備校正和產品資格是不同驗收」如何改變前一步的判讀。","checkEn":"Submit a normal/fault comparison for Milestone verification, its observable and one remaining uncertainty. Explain how \"Tool qualification and product qualification differ\" changes interpretation of the preceding artifact.","knowledge":[{"id":"a099-v8-24-k1","title":"里程碑核對／物理與模型","titleEn":"Milestone verification / Physics and model","text":"診斷機制：設備校正和產品資格是不同驗收。","textEn":"Diagnostic mechanism: Tool qualification and product qualification differ."},{"id":"a099-v8-24-k2","title":"里程碑核對／驗證與限制","titleEn":"Milestone verification / Verification and limits","text":"可證偽性：「把預定時程當成已完成量測結果」與「各里程碑代表不同完成程度」不可混為同一推論；對照需能觀察兩者的差別。","textEn":"Falsifiability: \"Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence\" is not equivalent to \"Milestones represent different completion states\"; the control must expose their difference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「里程碑核對」時，哪個新增因素應納入？","questionEn":"Which additional factor belongs in a check of Milestone verification?","options":["把預定時程當成已完成量測結果","有最先進設備便等於產品已量產","設備校正和產品資格是不同驗收"],"optionsEn":["Treating a schedule as completed measurement evidence","Equating advanced equipment with production-ready products","Tool qualification and product qualification differ"],"answer":2,"explanation":"設備校正和產品資格是不同驗收；錯誤主張的問題是未保留必要條件或機制。","explanationEn":"Tool qualification and product qualification differ. The competing claim omits a necessary condition or mechanism."}}]}],"subcategory":"fab","subcategoryTitle":"廠務與搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Fab infrastructure"},{"id":"packaging","title":"先進封裝共同設計","titleEn":"Advanced Packaging Co-Design","category":"packaging","summary":"以 20 模組、520 項可保存進度的教學操作，串聯來料、薄化、切割、接合、扇出、RDL、TSV、HBM、散熱與 CPO 驗證；其中 40 項另有定量算例、模型邊界與診斷策略。","summaryEn":"Twenty modules and 520 progress-preserving educational operations connect incoming inspection, thinning, dicing, bonding, fan-out, RDL, TSVs, HBM, cooling and CPO verification; 40 selected operations add quantitative examples, model boundaries and diagnostics.","scope":"公開原理與原創教學模型的分支流程；520 步涵蓋互斥或可選工法，不是每件產品都須依序執行的單一量產配方。新算例皆明示假設；原有步驟 ID 與進度對應保留。","scopeEn":"A branching curriculum based on public principles and authored models. The 520 operations include alternative and optional routes, not one production recipe every product follows. New examples are hypothetical, and original step IDs remain stable.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes","pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-disco-review","pk-besi-dieattach","pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-atotech-rdl","pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-disco-thin","pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap","pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress","v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v3-media-698d26511517","v9-media-76504c18d14b","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"diagram":{"type":"package","labels":["晶粒","互連","中介層","基板","散熱"],"labelsEn":["Dies","Interconnect","Interposer","Substrate","Cooling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"pk-m01","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"封裝架構、DFM與材料選擇","titleEn":"Package architecture, DFM and material selection","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查封裝架構、DFM與材料選擇的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for package architecture, dfm and material selection. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"共用架構規劃；選定分支後才建立製程旅行單。","routeEn":"Shared architecture planning; select a branch before building a traveler.","sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-001","order":1,"sequence":1,"title":"辨識封裝功能邊界","titleEn":"Identify package functions","objective":"把晶粒、封裝及電路板畫成三個介面區，並能說明「封裝同時承擔電連接、散熱與保護」。","objectiveEn":"Draw die, package and PCB as separate interfaces and explain: Packaging provides connection, heat removal and protection.","instruction":"把晶粒、封裝及電路板畫成三個介面區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每條跨區連線都有訊號或熱的角色。","instructionEn":"Draw die, package and PCB as separate interfaces. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Every crossing has an electrical or thermal role.","observation":"每條跨區連線都有訊號或熱的角色；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Every crossing has an electrical or thermal role; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把板級功能算入晶粒會漏掉封裝介面。","failureEn":"Assigning board functions to the die hides package interfaces.","check":"每條跨區連線都有訊號或熱的角色。","checkEn":"Every crossing has an electrical or thermal role.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-001-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"封裝同時承擔電連接、散熱與保護。","textEn":"Packaging provides connection, heat removal and protection."},{"id":"pk-001-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把板級功能算入晶粒會漏掉封裝介面；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Assigning board functions to the die hides package interfaces. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識封裝功能邊界」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify package functions\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["熱網路的串並聯關係與剖面相符","選址理由包含迴路而不只電容值","每條跨區連線都有訊號或熱的角色"],"optionsEn":["Thermal-network topology matches the cross-section","Placement reasoning includes loop geometry and capacitance","Every crossing has an electrical or thermal role"],"answer":2,"explanation":"封裝同時承擔電連接、散熱與保護。本步要確認：每條跨區連線都有訊號或熱的角色；常見誤判是：把板級功能算入晶粒會漏掉封裝介面。","explanationEn":"Packaging provides connection, heat removal and protection. Verify: Every crossing has an electrical or thermal role. A common misinterpretation is: Assigning board functions to the die hides package interfaces."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":[],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-002","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"建立 I/O 需求表","titleEn":"Create an I/O requirement table","objective":"分列訊號、電源與接地接點，並能說明「接點數不等於可用訊號數」。","objectiveEn":"Separate signal, power and ground connections and explain: Total connections do not equal available signal pins.","instruction":"分列訊號、電源與接地接點。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：接點總和與封裝配置一致。","instructionEn":"Separate signal, power and ground connections. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Connection totals agree with the package layout.","observation":"接點總和與封裝配置一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Connection totals agree with the package layout; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"漏算回流接地會高估可用訊號。","failureEn":"Missing return grounds overstates signal capacity.","check":"接點總和與封裝配置一致。","checkEn":"Connection totals agree with the package layout.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-002-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"接點數不等於可用訊號數。","textEn":"Total connections do not equal available signal pins."},{"id":"pk-002-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"漏算回流接地會高估可用訊號；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Missing return grounds overstates signal capacity. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立 I/O 需求表」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Create an I/O requirement table\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["接點總和與封裝配置一致","每個主要界面已標示失配方向","量測定義足以讓另一人重建座標"],"optionsEn":["Connection totals agree with the package layout","Each major interface has an indicated mismatch direction","The definition allows another person to reconstruct coordinates"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接點數不等於可用訊號數。本步要確認：接點總和與封裝配置一致；常見誤判是：漏算回流接地會高估可用訊號。","explanationEn":"Total connections do not equal available signal pins. Verify: Connection totals agree with the package layout. A common misinterpretation is: Missing return grounds overstates signal capacity."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-001"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-003","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"定義封裝高度預算","titleEn":"Define the package-height budget","objective":"將晶粒、接合層及封膠厚度分項相加，並能說明「堆疊厚度與局部公差共同影響高度」。","objectiveEn":"Sum die, bond layer and molding thicknesses separately and explain: Stack thickness and local tolerances determine height.","instruction":"將晶粒、接合層及封膠厚度分項相加。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最不利組合未超過教學圖面包絡。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Sum die, bond layer and molding thicknesses separately. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The worst-case stack fits the exercise envelope. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"最不利組合未超過教學圖面包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The worst-case stack fits the exercise envelope; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只加名目值可能掩蓋公差超限。","failureEn":"Adding nominal values hides tolerance violations.","check":"最不利組合未超過教學圖面包絡。","checkEn":"The worst-case stack fits the exercise envelope.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-003-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"堆疊厚度與局部公差共同影響高度。","textEn":"Stack thickness and local tolerances determine height."},{"id":"pk-003-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只加名目值可能掩蓋公差超限；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Adding nominal values hides tolerance violations. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-003-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"教學高度堆疊：晶粒 100±5 µm、黏著層 20±3 µm、上蓋間隙 50±4 µm，名目 170 µm，線性最壞範圍 158–182 µm。若公差是獨立零均值標準差，RSS 為 7.07 µm；不能把圖面最大公差直接當標準差。","textEn":"Teaching stack: die 100±5 µm, adhesive 20±3 µm and lid gap 50±4 µm give nominal 170 µm and worst-case 158–182 µm. RSS is 7.07 µm only if terms are independent zero-mean standard deviations; drawing limits are not automatically standard deviations."},{"id":"pk-003-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"先定基準面，再檢查翹曲、傾斜與局部最高點；單一中心厚度不能證明整個包絡不碰蓋。","textEn":"Define reference planes, then inspect bow, tilt and local peaks; one center thickness does not prove clearance over the full envelope."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「定義封裝高度預算」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Define the package-height budget\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["返工路線包含重新檢驗點","最不利組合未超過教學圖面包絡","材料表未將模數當作破壞門檻"],"optionsEn":["Rework routes include reinspection points","The worst-case stack fits the exercise envelope","The material table does not use modulus as a failure limit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"堆疊厚度與局部公差共同影響高度。本步要確認：最不利組合未超過教學圖面包絡；常見誤判是：只加名目值可能掩蓋公差超限。","explanationEn":"Stack thickness and local tolerances determine height. Verify: The worst-case stack fits the exercise envelope. A common misinterpretation is: Adding nominal values hides tolerance violations."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-002"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-004","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"選擇打線或覆晶分支","titleEn":"Select wirebond or flipchip branch","objective":"對照焊墊排列選擇連接方式，並能說明「周邊打線與面陣列凸塊具有不同幾何限制」。","objectiveEn":"Choose interconnection from pad arrangement and explain: Peripheral wires and area-array bumps have different geometry constraints.","instruction":"對照焊墊排列選擇連接方式。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：選定分支的焊墊能接到所有指定網路。","instructionEn":"Choose interconnection from pad arrangement. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The selected branch connects all required nets.","observation":"選定分支的焊墊能接到所有指定網路；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The selected branch connects all required nets; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未轉換焊墊圖便換分支會造成錯接。","failureEn":"Changing branch without remapping pads creates misconnection.","check":"選定分支的焊墊能接到所有指定網路。","checkEn":"The selected branch connects all required nets.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-004-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"周邊打線與面陣列凸塊具有不同幾何限制。","textEn":"Peripheral wires and area-array bumps have different geometry constraints."},{"id":"pk-004-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未轉換焊墊圖便換分支會造成錯接；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Changing branch without remapping pads creates misconnection. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇打線或覆晶分支」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select wirebond or flipchip branch\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["模型在跨區時更新相應材料性質","每個測試端對應明確的故障假設","選定分支的焊墊能接到所有指定網路"],"optionsEn":["The model updates properties across the transition","Each test terminal addresses a defined failure hypothesis","The selected branch connects all required nets"],"answer":2,"explanation":"周邊打線與面陣列凸塊具有不同幾何限制。本步要確認：選定分支的焊墊能接到所有指定網路；常見誤判是：未轉換焊墊圖便換分支會造成錯接。","explanationEn":"Peripheral wires and area-array bumps have different geometry constraints. Verify: The selected branch connects all required nets. A common misinterpretation is: Changing branch without remapping pads creates misconnection."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-003"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-005","order":5,"sequence":5,"title":"判定扇入或扇出需求","titleEn":"Determine fan-in or fan-out needs","objective":"比較接點配置面積與裸晶面積，並能說明「扇出以重組材料擴大可布線區」。","objectiveEn":"Compare connection footprint with bare-die area and explain: Fan-out expands routing area using reconstituted material.","instruction":"比較接點配置面積與裸晶面積。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：需要超出晶粒邊界的接點已標示。","instructionEn":"Compare connection footprint with bare-die area. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Connections extending beyond the die are identified.","observation":"需要超出晶粒邊界的接點已標示；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Connections extending beyond the die are identified; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"誤把擴大晶粒當作扇出會扭曲成本。","failureEn":"Treating fan-out as a larger die distorts cost.","check":"需要超出晶粒邊界的接點已標示。","checkEn":"Connections extending beyond the die are identified.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-005-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"扇出以重組材料擴大可布線區。","textEn":"Fan-out expands routing area using reconstituted material."},{"id":"pk-005-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"誤把擴大晶粒當作扇出會扭曲成本；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Treating fan-out as a larger die distorts cost. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判定扇入或扇出需求」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Determine fan-in or fan-out needs\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["需要超出晶粒邊界的接點已標示","敏感材料有儲存及暴露紀錄需求","工具與刀路不跨越禁止區"],"optionsEn":["Connections extending beyond the die are identified","Sensitive materials have storage and exposure records","Tools and cutting paths avoid prohibited regions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"扇出以重組材料擴大可布線區。本步要確認：需要超出晶粒邊界的接點已標示；常見誤判是：誤把擴大晶粒當作扇出會扭曲成本。","explanationEn":"Fan-out expands routing area using reconstituted material. Verify: Connections extending beyond the die are identified. A common misinterpretation is: Treating fan-out as a larger die distorts cost."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-004"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-006","order":6,"sequence":6,"title":"選擇導線架或有機基板","titleEn":"Choose leadframe or organic substrate","objective":"比較載流路徑與可布線層，並能說明「載體結構限制散熱和布線自由度」。","objectiveEn":"Compare current paths and routing layers and explain: Carrier structure constrains heat paths and routing.","instruction":"比較載流路徑與可布線層。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：載體支持所需接點及散熱接觸。","instructionEn":"Compare current paths and routing layers. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The carrier supports required connections and thermal contact.","observation":"載體支持所需接點及散熱接觸；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The carrier supports required connections and thermal contact; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略載體限制會產生不可布線網路。","failureEn":"Ignoring carrier limits creates unroutable nets.","check":"載體支持所需接點及散熱接觸。","checkEn":"The carrier supports required connections and thermal contact.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-006-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"載體結構限制散熱和布線自由度。","textEn":"Carrier structure constrains heat paths and routing."},{"id":"pk-006-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略載體限制會產生不可布線網路；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring carrier limits creates unroutable nets. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇導線架或有機基板」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Choose leadframe or organic substrate\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["能由任一封裝找回全部關鍵材料批號","載體支持所需接點及散熱接觸","電性要求與所選材料功能一致"],"optionsEn":["Each package resolves to all critical material lots","The carrier supports required connections and thermal contact","Electrical requirements match material function"],"answer":1,"explanation":"載體結構限制散熱和布線自由度。本步要確認：載體支持所需接點及散熱接觸；常見誤判是：忽略載體限制會產生不可布線網路。","explanationEn":"Carrier structure constrains heat paths and routing. Verify: The carrier supports required connections and thermal contact. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring carrier limits creates unroutable nets."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-005"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-007","order":7,"sequence":7,"title":"檢查裸晶焊墊金屬相容性","titleEn":"Check die-pad metallurgical compatibility","objective":"建立焊墊與接合材料的配對表，並能說明「不同金屬配對有不同反應與腐蝕行為」。","objectiveEn":"Pair pad finishes with interconnect materials and explain: Metal pairs differ in reaction and corrosion behavior.","instruction":"建立焊墊與接合材料的配對表。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每種配對都有公開依據或待驗證標記。","instructionEn":"Pair pad finishes with interconnect materials. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Every pair has evidence or a pending-validation flag.","observation":"每種配對都有公開依據或待驗證標記；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Every pair has evidence or a pending-validation flag; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"僅按導電率選材會漏掉界面反應。","failureEn":"Conductivity alone misses interface reactions.","check":"每種配對都有公開依據或待驗證標記。","checkEn":"Every pair has evidence or a pending-validation flag.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-007-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同金屬配對有不同反應與腐蝕行為。","textEn":"Metal pairs differ in reaction and corrosion behavior."},{"id":"pk-007-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"僅按導電率選材會漏掉界面反應；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Conductivity alone misses interface reactions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查裸晶焊墊金屬相容性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check die-pad metallurgical compatibility\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["相鄰元件不進入線弧包絡","每個高關注風險有檢查或試驗對策","每種配對都有公開依據或待驗證標記"],"optionsEn":["Adjacent parts stay outside wire-loop envelopes","Each major risk has an inspection or test response","Every pair has evidence or a pending-validation flag"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同金屬配對有不同反應與腐蝕行為。本步要確認：每種配對都有公開依據或待驗證標記；常見誤判是：僅按導電率選材會漏掉界面反應。","explanationEn":"Metal pairs differ in reaction and corrosion behavior. Verify: Every pair has evidence or a pending-validation flag. A common misinterpretation is: Conductivity alone misses interface reactions."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-006"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-008","order":8,"sequence":8,"title":"配置晶粒間距","titleEn":"Allocate inter-die spacing","objective":"在平面圖疊加取放與布線包絡，並能說明「名目間距需容納製程與工具偏差」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay placement and routing envelopes and explain: Nominal gaps must accommodate process and tool errors.","instruction":"在平面圖疊加取放與布線包絡。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最小間隙符合本例明示的包絡要求。","instructionEn":"Overlay placement and routing envelopes. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Minimum gaps meet the stated exercise envelope.","observation":"最小間隙符合本例明示的包絡要求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Minimum gaps meet the stated exercise envelope; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未計工具寬度會造成取放碰撞。","failureEn":"Ignoring tool width causes placement collisions.","check":"最小間隙符合本例明示的包絡要求。","checkEn":"Minimum gaps meet the stated exercise envelope.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-008-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"名目間距需容納製程與工具偏差。","textEn":"Nominal gaps must accommodate process and tool errors."},{"id":"pk-008-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未計工具寬度會造成取放碰撞；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring tool width causes placement collisions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「配置晶粒間距」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Allocate inter-die spacing\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最小間隙符合本例明示的包絡要求","內圈網路具有不中斷的逃線通道","三條路線的專屬與共用工站已標清"],"optionsEn":["Minimum gaps meet the stated exercise envelope","Inner nets have continuous escape routes","Shared and branch-specific stations are clearly marked"],"answer":0,"explanation":"名目間距需容納製程與工具偏差。本步要確認：最小間隙符合本例明示的包絡要求；常見誤判是：未計工具寬度會造成取放碰撞。","explanationEn":"Nominal gaps must accommodate process and tool errors. Verify: Minimum gaps meet the stated exercise envelope. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring tool width causes placement collisions."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-007"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-009","order":9,"sequence":9,"title":"繪製熱流路徑","titleEn":"Draw heat-flow paths","objective":"從接面追蹤至基板及上方散熱端，並能說明「平行熱路不可直接串聯相加」。","objectiveEn":"Trace junction heat toward substrate and top cooling and explain: Parallel heat paths cannot be summed as series paths.","instruction":"從接面追蹤至基板及上方散熱端。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：熱網路的串並聯關係與剖面相符。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Trace junction heat toward substrate and top cooling. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Thermal-network topology matches the cross-section. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"熱網路的串並聯關係與剖面相符；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Thermal-network topology matches the cross-section; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"錯置串並聯會誤判溫升。","failureEn":"Incorrect topology mispredicts temperature rise.","check":"熱網路的串並聯關係與剖面相符。","checkEn":"Thermal-network topology matches the cross-section.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-009-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"平行熱路不可直接串聯相加。","textEn":"Parallel heat paths cannot be summed as series paths."},{"id":"pk-009-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"錯置串並聯會誤判溫升；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Incorrect topology mispredicts temperature rise. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-009-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設兩條熱路並聯，上方 0.5 K/W、下方 2 K/W，等效為 0.4 K/W；50 W 對共同等溫邊界的溫升為 20 K。若兩端冷卻溫度不同，不能直接使用這個並聯公式。","textEn":"For hypothetical parallel paths of 0.5 and 2 K/W, equivalent resistance is 0.4 K/W; 50 W gives 20 K rise above a common isothermal boundary. Different sink temperatures invalidate this direct parallel reduction."},{"id":"pk-009-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"把晶粒功率、散熱器溫度、接觸熱阻與邊界對流分開記錄。熱阻測試的邊界條件是數值的一部分，不能把資料表 θJA 當任何系統通用常數。","textEn":"Record die power, sink temperature, contact resistance and convection separately. Test boundary conditions are part of thermal resistance; datasheet θJA is not a universal system constant."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「繪製熱流路徑」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Draw heat-flow paths\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每條跨區連線都有訊號或熱的角色","熱網路的串並聯關係與剖面相符","違規位置能回指到具體規則"],"optionsEn":["Every crossing has an electrical or thermal role","Thermal-network topology matches the cross-section","Violations reference specific rules"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平行熱路不可直接串聯相加。本步要確認：熱網路的串並聯關係與剖面相符；常見誤判是：錯置串並聯會誤判溫升。","explanationEn":"Parallel heat paths cannot be summed as series paths. Verify: Thermal-network topology matches the cross-section. A common misinterpretation is: Incorrect topology mispredicts temperature rise."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials","v9deep-thermal-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-008"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-010","order":10,"sequence":10,"title":"建立 CTE 配對圖","titleEn":"Map thermal-expansion pairs","objective":"比較矽、基板與模封料膨脹趨勢，並能說明「熱膨脹失配形成相對位移」。","objectiveEn":"Compare expansion trends of silicon, substrate and mold and explain: Expansion mismatch creates relative displacement.","instruction":"比較矽、基板與模封料膨脹趨勢。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每個主要界面已標示失配方向。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Compare expansion trends of silicon, substrate and mold. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each major interface has an indicated mismatch direction. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"每個主要界面已標示失配方向；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each major interface has an indicated mismatch direction; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看單一材料膨脹會漏掉界面負荷。","failureEn":"Single-material expansion misses interface loading.","check":"每個主要界面已標示失配方向。","checkEn":"Each major interface has an indicated mismatch direction.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-010-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"熱膨脹失配形成相對位移。","textEn":"Expansion mismatch creates relative displacement."},{"id":"pk-010-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看單一材料膨脹會漏掉界面負荷；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Single-material expansion misses interface loading. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-010-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設材料膨脹差 10 ppm/K、距中性點 10 mm、溫差 100 K，自由失配位移約 10 µm。此為量級估算，尚未計入支承、黏彈性、塑性與中性點移動。","textEn":"For hypothetical expansion mismatch 10 ppm/K, distance from neutral point 10 mm and ΔT=100 K, free mismatch is about 10 µm. This excludes constraint, viscoelasticity, plasticity and neutral-point movement."},{"id":"pk-010-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"Cu、W、AlN、矽與有機材料應分列溫度相關 CTE、彈性和導熱資料；單看室溫 CTE 接近，不足以證明熱循環應力最小。","textEn":"Compare temperature-dependent CTE, elasticity and conductivity for Cu, W, AlN, silicon and organics; matching room-temperature CTE alone does not prove minimum cyclic stress."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立 CTE 配對圖」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Map thermal-expansion pairs\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["訊號與回流路徑沒有未說明的中斷","接點總和與封裝配置一致","每個主要界面已標示失配方向"],"optionsEn":["Signal and return paths have no unexplained discontinuities","Connection totals agree with the package layout","Each major interface has an indicated mismatch direction"],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱膨脹失配形成相對位移。本步要確認：每個主要界面已標示失配方向；常見誤判是：只看單一材料膨脹會漏掉界面負荷。","explanationEn":"Expansion mismatch creates relative displacement. Verify: Each major interface has an indicated mismatch direction. A common misinterpretation is: Single-material expansion misses interface loading."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-009"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-011","order":11,"sequence":11,"title":"區分彈性模數與強度","titleEn":"Distinguish modulus from strength","objective":"將剛性及破壞指標放入不同欄位，並能說明「低模數不保證較高界面強度」。","objectiveEn":"Place stiffness and failure metrics in separate columns and explain: Low modulus does not guarantee stronger adhesion.","instruction":"將剛性及破壞指標放入不同欄位。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：材料表未將模數當作破壞門檻。","instructionEn":"Place stiffness and failure metrics in separate columns. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The material table does not use modulus as a failure limit.","observation":"材料表未將模數當作破壞門檻；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The material table does not use modulus as a failure limit; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"混用指標會錯選緩衝材料。","failureEn":"Confusing metrics misselects compliant materials.","check":"材料表未將模數當作破壞門檻。","checkEn":"The material table does not use modulus as a failure limit.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-011-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"低模數不保證較高界面強度。","textEn":"Low modulus does not guarantee stronger adhesion."},{"id":"pk-011-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"混用指標會錯選緩衝材料；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Confusing metrics misselects compliant materials. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「區分彈性模數與強度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Distinguish modulus from strength\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["材料表未將模數當作破壞門檻","選址理由包含迴路而不只電容值","最不利組合未超過教學圖面包絡"],"optionsEn":["The material table does not use modulus as a failure limit","Placement reasoning includes loop geometry and capacitance","The worst-case stack fits the exercise envelope"],"answer":0,"explanation":"低模數不保證較高界面強度。本步要確認：材料表未將模數當作破壞門檻；常見誤判是：混用指標會錯選緩衝材料。","explanationEn":"Low modulus does not guarantee stronger adhesion. Verify: The material table does not use modulus as a failure limit. A common misinterpretation is: Confusing metrics misselects compliant materials."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-010"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-012","order":12,"sequence":12,"title":"核對玻璃轉移行為","titleEn":"Review glass-transition behavior","objective":"對照溫度相依模數與膨脹曲線，並能說明「聚合物跨轉移區時性質會改變」。","objectiveEn":"Compare temperature-dependent modulus and expansion curves and explain: Polymer properties change across transition regions.","instruction":"對照溫度相依模數與膨脹曲線。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：模型在跨區時更新相應材料性質。","instructionEn":"Compare temperature-dependent modulus and expansion curves. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The model updates properties across the transition.","observation":"模型在跨區時更新相應材料性質；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The model updates properties across the transition; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"固定室溫參數會低估熱態變形。","failureEn":"Room-temperature constants can underpredict hot deformation.","check":"模型在跨區時更新相應材料性質。","checkEn":"The model updates properties across the transition.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-012-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"聚合物跨轉移區時性質會改變。","textEn":"Polymer properties change across transition regions."},{"id":"pk-012-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"固定室溫參數會低估熱態變形；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Room-temperature constants can underpredict hot deformation. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對玻璃轉移行為」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review glass-transition behavior\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["選定分支的焊墊能接到所有指定網路","模型在跨區時更新相應材料性質","量測定義足以讓另一人重建座標"],"optionsEn":["The selected branch connects all required nets","The model updates properties across the transition","The definition allows another person to reconstruct coordinates"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聚合物跨轉移區時性質會改變。本步要確認：模型在跨區時更新相應材料性質；常見誤判是：固定室溫參數會低估熱態變形。","explanationEn":"Polymer properties change across transition regions. Verify: The model updates properties across the transition. A common misinterpretation is: Room-temperature constants can underpredict hot deformation."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-011"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-013","order":13,"sequence":13,"title":"篩選吸濕敏感材料","titleEn":"Screen moisture-sensitive materials","objective":"比較材料吸濕與界面位置，並能說明「吸濕可影響黏著及熱製程反應」。","objectiveEn":"Compare moisture uptake with interface locations and explain: Moisture affects adhesion and thermal-process behavior.","instruction":"比較材料吸濕與界面位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：敏感材料有儲存及暴露紀錄需求。","instructionEn":"Compare moisture uptake with interface locations. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Sensitive materials have storage and exposure records.","observation":"敏感材料有儲存及暴露紀錄需求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Sensitive materials have storage and exposure records; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"外觀乾燥不代表內部無水分。","failureEn":"A dry appearance does not prove low internal moisture.","check":"敏感材料有儲存及暴露紀錄需求。","checkEn":"Sensitive materials have storage and exposure records.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-013-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"吸濕可影響黏著及熱製程反應。","textEn":"Moisture affects adhesion and thermal-process behavior."},{"id":"pk-013-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"外觀乾燥不代表內部無水分；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A dry appearance does not prove low internal moisture. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「篩選吸濕敏感材料」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Screen moisture-sensitive materials\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["返工路線包含重新檢驗點","需要超出晶粒邊界的接點已標示","敏感材料有儲存及暴露紀錄需求"],"optionsEn":["Rework routes include reinspection points","Connections extending beyond the die are identified","Sensitive materials have storage and exposure records"],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸濕可影響黏著及熱製程反應。本步要確認：敏感材料有儲存及暴露紀錄需求；常見誤判是：外觀乾燥不代表內部無水分。","explanationEn":"Moisture affects adhesion and thermal-process behavior. Verify: Sensitive materials have storage and exposure records. A common misinterpretation is: A dry appearance does not prove low internal moisture."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-012"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-014","order":14,"sequence":14,"title":"評估導電膠或絕緣膠","titleEn":"Assess conductive versus insulating adhesive","objective":"按背面電性需求選擇接合層，並能說明「黏著層可能同時是電流與熱流通道」。","objectiveEn":"Select the bond layer from backside electrical needs and explain: The adhesive may carry both current and heat.","instruction":"按背面電性需求選擇接合層。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：電性要求與所選材料功能一致。","instructionEn":"Select the bond layer from backside electrical needs. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Electrical requirements match material function.","observation":"電性要求與所選材料功能一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Electrical requirements match material function; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"誤用導電膠可能短接不同電位。","failureEn":"Conductive adhesive may short unlike potentials.","check":"電性要求與所選材料功能一致。","checkEn":"Electrical requirements match material function.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-014-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"黏著層可能同時是電流與熱流通道。","textEn":"The adhesive may carry both current and heat."},{"id":"pk-014-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"誤用導電膠可能短接不同電位；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Conductive adhesive may short unlike potentials. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估導電膠或絕緣膠」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess conductive versus insulating adhesive\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["電性要求與所選材料功能一致","每個測試端對應明確的故障假設","載體支持所需接點及散熱接觸"],"optionsEn":["Electrical requirements match material function","Each test terminal addresses a defined failure hypothesis","The carrier supports required connections and thermal contact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"黏著層可能同時是電流與熱流通道。本步要確認：電性要求與所選材料功能一致；常見誤判是：誤用導電膠可能短接不同電位。","explanationEn":"The adhesive may carry both current and heat. Verify: Electrical requirements match material function. A common misinterpretation is: Conductive adhesive may short unlike potentials."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-013"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-015","order":15,"sequence":15,"title":"分配打線禁布區","titleEn":"Allocate wirebond keep-outs","objective":"在晶粒外圍畫出線弧投影區，並能說明「線弧佔用三維空間而非平面線段」。","objectiveEn":"Draw projected wire-loop keep-outs around the die and explain: Wire loops occupy volume rather than planar lines.","instruction":"在晶粒外圍畫出線弧投影區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：相鄰元件不進入線弧包絡。","instructionEn":"Draw projected wire-loop keep-outs around the die. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Adjacent parts stay outside wire-loop envelopes.","observation":"相鄰元件不進入線弧包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Adjacent parts stay outside wire-loop envelopes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只查平面不查高度會碰線。","failureEn":"Planar checks alone miss vertical wire collisions.","check":"相鄰元件不進入線弧包絡。","checkEn":"Adjacent parts stay outside wire-loop envelopes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-015-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"線弧佔用三維空間而非平面線段。","textEn":"Wire loops occupy volume rather than planar lines."},{"id":"pk-015-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只查平面不查高度會碰線；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Planar checks alone miss vertical wire collisions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分配打線禁布區」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Allocate wirebond keep-outs\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每種配對都有公開依據或待驗證標記","相鄰元件不進入線弧包絡","工具與刀路不跨越禁止區"],"optionsEn":["Every pair has evidence or a pending-validation flag","Adjacent parts stay outside wire-loop envelopes","Tools and cutting paths avoid prohibited regions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"線弧佔用三維空間而非平面線段。本步要確認：相鄰元件不進入線弧包絡；常見誤判是：只查平面不查高度會碰線。","explanationEn":"Wire loops occupy volume rather than planar lines. Verify: Adjacent parts stay outside wire-loop envelopes. A common misinterpretation is: Planar checks alone miss vertical wire collisions."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-014"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-016","order":16,"sequence":16,"title":"分配凸塊逃線通道","titleEn":"Allocate bump escape channels","objective":"在面陣列中追蹤內圈接點的出口，並能說明「陣列密度增加會限制可用逃線」。","objectiveEn":"Trace escape routes from inner array connections and explain: Dense arrays constrain routing escape.","instruction":"在面陣列中追蹤內圈接點的出口。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：內圈網路具有不中斷的逃線通道。","instructionEn":"Trace escape routes from inner array connections. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Inner nets have continuous escape routes.","observation":"內圈網路具有不中斷的逃線通道；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Inner nets have continuous escape routes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只連外圈會留下內部不可達接點。","failureEn":"Routing only the perimeter leaves inner contacts inaccessible.","check":"內圈網路具有不中斷的逃線通道。","checkEn":"Inner nets have continuous escape routes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-016-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"陣列密度增加會限制可用逃線。","textEn":"Dense arrays constrain routing escape."},{"id":"pk-016-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只連外圈會留下內部不可達接點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Routing only the perimeter leaves inner contacts inaccessible. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分配凸塊逃線通道」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Allocate bump escape channels\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["能由任一封裝找回全部關鍵材料批號","最小間隙符合本例明示的包絡要求","內圈網路具有不中斷的逃線通道"],"optionsEn":["Each package resolves to all critical material lots","Minimum gaps meet the stated exercise envelope","Inner nets have continuous escape routes"],"answer":2,"explanation":"陣列密度增加會限制可用逃線。本步要確認：內圈網路具有不中斷的逃線通道；常見誤判是：只連外圈會留下內部不可達接點。","explanationEn":"Dense arrays constrain routing escape. Verify: Inner nets have continuous escape routes. A common misinterpretation is: Routing only the perimeter leaves inner contacts inaccessible."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-015"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-017","order":17,"sequence":17,"title":"檢查 RDL 線距規則","titleEn":"Check RDL spacing rules","objective":"將示意線寬線距與規則表逐項比對，並能說明「製造規則取決於選定製程能力」。","objectiveEn":"Compare illustrative width and spacing with the rule table and explain: Design rules depend on the selected process capability.","instruction":"將示意線寬線距與規則表逐項比對。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：違規位置能回指到具體規則。","instructionEn":"Compare illustrative width and spacing with the rule table. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Violations reference specific rules.","observation":"違規位置能回指到具體規則；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Violations reference specific rules; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把示意規則當廠商量產值會誤導設計。","failureEn":"Treating teaching rules as vendor limits misleads design.","check":"違規位置能回指到具體規則。","checkEn":"Violations reference specific rules.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-017-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"製造規則取決於選定製程能力。","textEn":"Design rules depend on the selected process capability."},{"id":"pk-017-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把示意規則當廠商量產值會誤導設計；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Treating teaching rules as vendor limits misleads design. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查 RDL 線距規則」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check RDL spacing rules\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["違規位置能回指到具體規則","每個高關注風險有檢查或試驗對策","熱網路的串並聯關係與剖面相符"],"optionsEn":["Violations reference specific rules","Each major risk has an inspection or test response","Thermal-network topology matches the cross-section"],"answer":0,"explanation":"製造規則取決於選定製程能力。本步要確認：違規位置能回指到具體規則；常見誤判是：把示意規則當廠商量產值會誤導設計。","explanationEn":"Design rules depend on the selected process capability. Verify: Violations reference specific rules. A common misinterpretation is: Treating teaching rules as vendor limits misleads design."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-016"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-018","order":18,"sequence":18,"title":"建立接地回流剖面","titleEn":"Create a ground-return section","objective":"沿訊號旁標示回流導體，並能說明「回流幾何影響迴路電感」。","objectiveEn":"Mark return conductors beside signal paths and explain: Return geometry affects loop inductance.","instruction":"沿訊號旁標示回流導體。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：訊號與回流路徑沒有未說明的中斷。","instructionEn":"Mark return conductors beside signal paths. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Signal and return paths have no unexplained discontinuities.","observation":"訊號與回流路徑沒有未說明的中斷；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Signal and return paths have no unexplained discontinuities; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只畫訊號線會漏掉電流迴路。","failureEn":"Signal-only drawings omit the current loop.","check":"訊號與回流路徑沒有未說明的中斷。","checkEn":"Signal and return paths have no unexplained discontinuities.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-018-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"回流幾何影響迴路電感。","textEn":"Return geometry affects loop inductance."},{"id":"pk-018-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只畫訊號線會漏掉電流迴路；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Signal-only drawings omit the current loop. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立接地回流剖面」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Create a ground-return section\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每個主要界面已標示失配方向","訊號與回流路徑沒有未說明的中斷","三條路線的專屬與共用工站已標清"],"optionsEn":["Each major interface has an indicated mismatch direction","Signal and return paths have no unexplained discontinuities","Shared and branch-specific stations are clearly marked"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回流幾何影響迴路電感。本步要確認：訊號與回流路徑沒有未說明的中斷；常見誤判是：只畫訊號線會漏掉電流迴路。","explanationEn":"Return geometry affects loop inductance. Verify: Signal and return paths have no unexplained discontinuities. A common misinterpretation is: Signal-only drawings omit the current loop."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-017"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-019","order":19,"sequence":19,"title":"分配去耦元件位置","titleEn":"Allocate decoupling locations","objective":"比較電源接點到去耦元件的連接長度，並能說明「連接寄生會削弱去耦作用」。","objectiveEn":"Compare power-pin-to-decoupler connection lengths and explain: Connection parasitics weaken decoupling.","instruction":"比較電源接點到去耦元件的連接長度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：選址理由包含迴路而不只電容值。","instructionEn":"Compare power-pin-to-decoupler connection lengths. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Placement reasoning includes loop geometry and capacitance.","observation":"選址理由包含迴路而不只電容值；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Placement reasoning includes loop geometry and capacitance; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"遠距大電容不一定替代近端去耦。","failureEn":"A remote large capacitor may not replace local decoupling.","check":"選址理由包含迴路而不只電容值。","checkEn":"Placement reasoning includes loop geometry and capacitance.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-019-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"連接寄生會削弱去耦作用。","textEn":"Connection parasitics weaken decoupling."},{"id":"pk-019-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"遠距大電容不一定替代近端去耦；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A remote large capacitor may not replace local decoupling. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分配去耦元件位置」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Allocate decoupling locations\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每條跨區連線都有訊號或熱的角色","材料表未將模數當作破壞門檻","選址理由包含迴路而不只電容值"],"optionsEn":["Every crossing has an electrical or thermal role","The material table does not use modulus as a failure limit","Placement reasoning includes loop geometry and capacitance"],"answer":2,"explanation":"連接寄生會削弱去耦作用。本步要確認：選址理由包含迴路而不只電容值；常見誤判是：遠距大電容不一定替代近端去耦。","explanationEn":"Connection parasitics weaken decoupling. Verify: Placement reasoning includes loop geometry and capacitance. A common misinterpretation is: A remote large capacitor may not replace local decoupling."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-018"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-020","order":20,"sequence":20,"title":"建立封裝翹曲量測基準","titleEn":"Define package-warpage references","objective":"指定參考平面、量測面與溫度，並能說明「不同基準下的翹曲值不可直接比較」。","objectiveEn":"Specify reference plane, measurement side and temperature and explain: Warpage values with different references are not directly comparable.","instruction":"指定參考平面、量測面與溫度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：量測定義足以讓另一人重建座標。","instructionEn":"Specify reference plane, measurement side and temperature. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The definition allows another person to reconstruct coordinates.","observation":"量測定義足以讓另一人重建座標；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The definition allows another person to reconstruct coordinates; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"基準反轉會使凸凹方向看似相反。","failureEn":"Reversing the reference changes apparent curvature sign.","check":"量測定義足以讓另一人重建座標。","checkEn":"The definition allows another person to reconstruct coordinates.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-020-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同基準下的翹曲值不可直接比較。","textEn":"Warpage values with different references are not directly comparable."},{"id":"pk-020-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"基準反轉會使凸凹方向看似相反；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Reversing the reference changes apparent curvature sign. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立封裝翹曲量測基準」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Define package-warpage references\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["量測定義足以讓另一人重建座標","接點總和與封裝配置一致","模型在跨區時更新相應材料性質"],"optionsEn":["The definition allows another person to reconstruct coordinates","Connection totals agree with the package layout","The model updates properties across the transition"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同基準下的翹曲值不可直接比較。本步要確認：量測定義足以讓另一人重建座標；常見誤判是：基準反轉會使凸凹方向看似相反。","explanationEn":"Warpage values with different references are not directly comparable. Verify: The definition allows another person to reconstruct coordinates. A common misinterpretation is: Reversing the reference changes apparent curvature sign."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-019"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-021","order":21,"sequence":21,"title":"辨識可返工界面","titleEn":"Identify reworkable interfaces","objective":"為各接合界面標出可分離或不可分離，並能說明「返工會消耗材料及熱歷程餘量」。","objectiveEn":"Mark interfaces as separable or nonseparable and explain: Rework consumes material and thermal-history margins.","instruction":"為各接合界面標出可分離或不可分離。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：返工路線包含重新檢驗點。","instructionEn":"Mark interfaces as separable or nonseparable. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Rework routes include reinspection points.","observation":"返工路線包含重新檢驗點；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Rework routes include reinspection points; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把重加熱視為無代價會累積損傷。","failureEn":"Treating reheating as free accumulates damage.","check":"返工路線包含重新檢驗點。","checkEn":"Rework routes include reinspection points.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-021-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"返工會消耗材料及熱歷程餘量。","textEn":"Rework consumes material and thermal-history margins."},{"id":"pk-021-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把重加熱視為無代價會累積損傷；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Treating reheating as free accumulates damage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識可返工界面」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify reworkable interfaces\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["敏感材料有儲存及暴露紀錄需求","返工路線包含重新檢驗點","最不利組合未超過教學圖面包絡"],"optionsEn":["Sensitive materials have storage and exposure records","Rework routes include reinspection points","The worst-case stack fits the exercise envelope"],"answer":1,"explanation":"返工會消耗材料及熱歷程餘量。本步要確認：返工路線包含重新檢驗點；常見誤判是：把重加熱視為無代價會累積損傷。","explanationEn":"Rework consumes material and thermal-history margins. Verify: Rework routes include reinspection points. A common misinterpretation is: Treating reheating as free accumulates damage."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-020"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-022","order":22,"sequence":22,"title":"設計測試鏈","titleEn":"Design electrical test chains","objective":"在封裝示意中接入菊鏈與測試端，並能說明「菊鏈能揭示連通性但不涵蓋所有功能」。","objectiveEn":"Add daisy chains and accessible test terminals and explain: Daisy chains reveal continuity but not every function.","instruction":"在封裝示意中接入菊鏈與測試端。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每個測試端對應明確的故障假設。","instructionEn":"Add daisy chains and accessible test terminals. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each test terminal addresses a defined failure hypothesis.","observation":"每個測試端對應明確的故障假設；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each test terminal addresses a defined failure hypothesis; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單一通過不能證明全部訊號品質。","failureEn":"One passing chain cannot prove all signal quality.","check":"每個測試端對應明確的故障假設。","checkEn":"Each test terminal addresses a defined failure hypothesis.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-022-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"菊鏈能揭示連通性但不涵蓋所有功能。","textEn":"Daisy chains reveal continuity but not every function."},{"id":"pk-022-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單一通過不能證明全部訊號品質；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One passing chain cannot prove all signal quality. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「設計測試鏈」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Design electrical test chains\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["選定分支的焊墊能接到所有指定網路","電性要求與所選材料功能一致","每個測試端對應明確的故障假設"],"optionsEn":["The selected branch connects all required nets","Electrical requirements match material function","Each test terminal addresses a defined failure hypothesis"],"answer":2,"explanation":"菊鏈能揭示連通性但不涵蓋所有功能。本步要確認：每個測試端對應明確的故障假設；常見誤判是：單一通過不能證明全部訊號品質。","explanationEn":"Daisy chains reveal continuity but not every function. Verify: Each test terminal addresses a defined failure hypothesis. A common misinterpretation is: One passing chain cannot prove all signal quality."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-021"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-023","order":23,"sequence":23,"title":"規劃切割與吸取區","titleEn":"Plan singulation and pickup zones","objective":"保留切割道、吸取面與邊緣保護，並能說明「後段機械接觸需要可達空間」。","objectiveEn":"Reserve streets, pickup surfaces and edge protection and explain: Downstream handling needs accessible contact areas.","instruction":"保留切割道、吸取面與邊緣保護。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：工具與刀路不跨越禁止區。","instructionEn":"Reserve streets, pickup surfaces and edge protection. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Tools and cutting paths avoid prohibited regions.","observation":"工具與刀路不跨越禁止區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Tools and cutting paths avoid prohibited regions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略吸取面會使成品難以搬運。","failureEn":"Ignoring pickup surfaces makes handling impractical.","check":"工具與刀路不跨越禁止區。","checkEn":"Tools and cutting paths avoid prohibited regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-023-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"後段機械接觸需要可達空間。","textEn":"Downstream handling needs accessible contact areas."},{"id":"pk-023-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略吸取面會使成品難以搬運；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring pickup surfaces makes handling impractical. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「規劃切割與吸取區」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Plan singulation and pickup zones\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["工具與刀路不跨越禁止區","需要超出晶粒邊界的接點已標示","相鄰元件不進入線弧包絡"],"optionsEn":["Tools and cutting paths avoid prohibited regions","Connections extending beyond the die are identified","Adjacent parts stay outside wire-loop envelopes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"後段機械接觸需要可達空間。本步要確認：工具與刀路不跨越禁止區；常見誤判是：忽略吸取面會使成品難以搬運。","explanationEn":"Downstream handling needs accessible contact areas. Verify: Tools and cutting paths avoid prohibited regions. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring pickup surfaces makes handling impractical."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-022"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-024","order":24,"sequence":24,"title":"建立材料批次追溯","titleEn":"Establish material-lot traceability","objective":"將膠材、基板及晶粒批號連到封裝編號，並能說明「追溯依賴材料與工序事件的連結」。","objectiveEn":"Link adhesive, substrate and die lots to package IDs and explain: Traceability depends on material-to-process event links.","instruction":"將膠材、基板及晶粒批號連到封裝編號。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：能由任一封裝找回全部關鍵材料批號。","instructionEn":"Link adhesive, substrate and die lots to package IDs. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each package resolves to all critical material lots.","observation":"能由任一封裝找回全部關鍵材料批號；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each package resolves to all critical material lots; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只記供應商不記批號難以隔離異常。","failureEn":"Supplier names without lots cannot isolate excursions.","check":"能由任一封裝找回全部關鍵材料批號。","checkEn":"Each package resolves to all critical material lots.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-024-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"追溯依賴材料與工序事件的連結。","textEn":"Traceability depends on material-to-process event links."},{"id":"pk-024-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只記供應商不記批號難以隔離異常；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Supplier names without lots cannot isolate excursions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立材料批次追溯」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Establish material-lot traceability\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["內圈網路具有不中斷的逃線通道","能由任一封裝找回全部關鍵材料批號","載體支持所需接點及散熱接觸"],"optionsEn":["Inner nets have continuous escape routes","Each package resolves to all critical material lots","The carrier supports required connections and thermal contact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"追溯依賴材料與工序事件的連結。本步要確認：能由任一封裝找回全部關鍵材料批號；常見誤判是：只記供應商不記批號難以隔離異常。","explanationEn":"Traceability depends on material-to-process event links. Verify: Each package resolves to all critical material lots. A common misinterpretation is: Supplier names without lots cannot isolate excursions."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-023"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-025","order":25,"sequence":25,"title":"完成架構失效模式分析","titleEn":"Review architectural failure modes","objective":"為熱路、接點與密封各列失效及觀測，並能說明「失效模式應連到可驗證的影響」。","objectiveEn":"List failures and observations for heat paths, joints and seals and explain: Failure modes should connect to verifiable effects.","instruction":"為熱路、接點與密封各列失效及觀測。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每個高關注風險有檢查或試驗對策。","instructionEn":"List failures and observations for heat paths, joints and seals. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each major risk has an inspection or test response.","observation":"每個高關注風險有檢查或試驗對策；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each major risk has an inspection or test response; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只列嚴重度而無檢測方法不能形成控制。","failureEn":"Severity scores alone do not create control.","check":"每個高關注風險有檢查或試驗對策。","checkEn":"Each major risk has an inspection or test response.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-025-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"失效模式應連到可驗證的影響。","textEn":"Failure modes should connect to verifiable effects."},{"id":"pk-025-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只列嚴重度而無檢測方法不能形成控制；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Severity scores alone do not create control. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「完成架構失效模式分析」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review architectural failure modes\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每種配對都有公開依據或待驗證標記","違規位置能回指到具體規則","每個高關注風險有檢查或試驗對策"],"optionsEn":["Every pair has evidence or a pending-validation flag","Violations reference specific rules","Each major risk has an inspection or test response"],"answer":2,"explanation":"失效模式應連到可驗證的影響。本步要確認：每個高關注風險有檢查或試驗對策；常見誤判是：只列嚴重度而無檢測方法不能形成控制。","explanationEn":"Failure modes should connect to verifiable effects. Verify: Each major risk has an inspection or test response. A common misinterpretation is: Severity scores alone do not create control."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-024"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-026","order":26,"sequence":26,"title":"簽核分支製程圖","titleEn":"Release the branched process map","objective":"將打線、覆晶與扇出分開連線，並能說明「課程順序不等於單一量產工序順序」。","objectiveEn":"Draw separate wirebond, flipchip and fan-out routes and explain: Curriculum order is not a universal production sequence.","instruction":"將打線、覆晶與扇出分開連線。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：三條路線的專屬與共用工站已標清。","instructionEn":"Draw separate wirebond, flipchip and fan-out routes. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Shared and branch-specific stations are clearly marked.","observation":"三條路線的專屬與共用工站已標清；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Shared and branch-specific stations are clearly marked; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把三分支串成一條會重複或逆序加工。","failureEn":"Chaining all branches causes duplicate or reversed processing.","check":"三條路線的專屬與共用工站已標清。","checkEn":"Shared and branch-specific stations are clearly marked.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-026-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"課程順序不等於單一量產工序順序。","textEn":"Curriculum order is not a universal production sequence."},{"id":"pk-026-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把三分支串成一條會重複或逆序加工；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Chaining all branches causes duplicate or reversed processing. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「簽核分支製程圖」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release the branched process map\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["三條路線的專屬與共用工站已標清","最小間隙符合本例明示的包絡要求","訊號與回流路徑沒有未說明的中斷"],"optionsEn":["Shared and branch-specific stations are clearly marked","Minimum gaps meet the stated exercise envelope","Signal and return paths have no unexplained discontinuities"],"answer":0,"explanation":"課程順序不等於單一量產工序順序。本步要確認：三條路線的專屬與共用工站已標清；常見誤判是：把三分支串成一條會重複或逆序加工。","explanationEn":"Curriculum order is not a universal production sequence. Verify: Shared and branch-specific stations are clearly marked. A common misinterpretation is: Chaining all branches causes duplicate or reversed processing."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-market","pk-amkor-fanout","pk-henkel-materials"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-025"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m02","order":2,"sequence":2,"title":"進料晶圓、晶粒檢查與晶圓地圖","titleEn":"Incoming wafer/die inspection and wafer maps","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查進料晶圓、晶粒檢查與晶圓地圖的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for incoming wafer/die inspection and wafer maps. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"共用進料；提供晶圓級與晶粒級分支的追溯起點。","routeEn":"Shared incoming control; traceability starts for wafer and die routes.","sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-027","order":1,"sequence":27,"title":"核對到貨晶圓身分","titleEn":"Verify incoming wafer identity","objective":"比對盒標、晶圓編號與電子旅行單，並能說明「身分錯置會污染全部後續追溯」。","objectiveEn":"Match carrier label, wafer ID and electronic traveler and explain: Identity mismatch corrupts downstream traceability.","instruction":"比對盒標、晶圓編號與電子旅行單。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：三種識別資訊無未解決差異。","instructionEn":"Match carrier label, wafer ID and electronic traveler. Check evidence you create or obtain against: All three identifiers agree without unresolved differences.","observation":"三種識別資訊無未解決差異；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"All three identifiers agree without unresolved differences; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"外盒相同不表示內部晶圓相同。","failureEn":"Matching boxes do not prove wafer identity.","check":"三種識別資訊無未解決差異。","checkEn":"All three identifiers agree without unresolved differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-027-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"身分錯置會污染全部後續追溯。","textEn":"Identity mismatch corrupts downstream traceability."},{"id":"pk-027-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"外盒相同不表示內部晶圓相同；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Matching boxes do not prove wafer identity. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對到貨晶圓身分」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify incoming wafer identity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["分類加總等於可辨識晶粒總數","背面製程要求與實際層別相符","三種識別資訊無未解決差異"],"optionsEn":["Category totals equal the identifiable die count","Backside process requirements match observed layers","All three identifiers agree without unresolved differences"],"answer":2,"explanation":"身分錯置會污染全部後續追溯。本步要確認：三種識別資訊無未解決差異；常見誤判是：外盒相同不表示內部晶圓相同。","explanationEn":"Identity mismatch corrupts downstream traceability. Verify: All three identifiers agree without unresolved differences. A common misinterpretation is: Matching boxes do not prove wafer identity."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-026"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-028","order":2,"sequence":28,"title":"檢查運輸包裝完整性","titleEn":"Inspect transport-package integrity","objective":"記錄封條、破袋與撞擊指示狀態，並能說明「運輸證據可解釋進料缺陷來源」。","objectiveEn":"Record seals, breached bags and impact indicators and explain: Transport evidence helps explain incoming damage.","instruction":"記錄封條、破袋與撞擊指示狀態。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常包裝批次被標示待判定。","instructionEn":"Record seals, breached bags and impact indicators. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Compromised shipments are flagged for disposition.","observation":"異常包裝批次被標示待判定；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Compromised shipments are flagged for disposition; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"拆箱後未記錄會失去受損時間線。","failureEn":"Unrecorded unpacking loses the damage timeline.","check":"異常包裝批次被標示待判定。","checkEn":"Compromised shipments are flagged for disposition.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-028-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"運輸證據可解釋進料缺陷來源。","textEn":"Transport evidence helps explain incoming damage."},{"id":"pk-028-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"拆箱後未記錄會失去受損時間線；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Unrecorded unpacking loses the damage timeline. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查運輸包裝完整性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect transport-package integrity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常包裝批次被標示待判定","衝突晶粒被隔離而非自動挑選","工具能力能回答指定檢查問題"],"optionsEn":["Compromised shipments are flagged for disposition","Conflicting dies are quarantined rather than selected","Tool capability addresses the specified inspection question"],"answer":0,"explanation":"運輸證據可解釋進料缺陷來源。本步要確認：異常包裝批次被標示待判定；常見誤判是：拆箱後未記錄會失去受損時間線。","explanationEn":"Transport evidence helps explain incoming damage. Verify: Compromised shipments are flagged for disposition. A common misinterpretation is: Unrecorded unpacking loses the damage timeline."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-027"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-029","order":3,"sequence":29,"title":"核對濕度暴露紀錄","titleEn":"Review humidity-exposure history","objective":"比較乾燥包裝與開封時間紀錄，並能說明「濕度卡只反映限定的指示條件」。","objectiveEn":"Compare dry-pack condition and opening-time records and explain: Humidity indicators reflect limited indicator conditions.","instruction":"比較乾燥包裝與開封時間紀錄。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：未知暴露歷程沒有被視為零暴露。","instructionEn":"Compare dry-pack condition and opening-time records. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Unknown exposure is not treated as zero exposure.","observation":"未知暴露歷程沒有被視為零暴露；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Unknown exposure is not treated as zero exposure; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略開封歷程會錯估材料狀態。","failureEn":"Ignoring opening history misjudges material condition.","check":"未知暴露歷程沒有被視為零暴露。","checkEn":"Unknown exposure is not treated as zero exposure.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-029-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"濕度卡只反映限定的指示條件。","textEn":"Humidity indicators reflect limited indicator conditions."},{"id":"pk-029-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略開封歷程會錯估材料狀態；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring opening history misjudges material condition. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對濕度暴露紀錄」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review humidity-exposure history\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["重複分布與接受準則一併呈現","未知暴露歷程沒有被視為零暴露","缺陷位置與量測尺度已記錄"],"optionsEn":["Repeat distributions are shown against acceptance criteria","Unknown exposure is not treated as zero exposure","Defect locations and measurement scales are recorded"],"answer":1,"explanation":"濕度卡只反映限定的指示條件。本步要確認：未知暴露歷程沒有被視為零暴露；常見誤判是：忽略開封歷程會錯估材料狀態。","explanationEn":"Humidity indicators reflect limited indicator conditions. Verify: Unknown exposure is not treated as zero exposure. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring opening history misjudges material condition."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-028"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-030","order":4,"sequence":30,"title":"建立晶圓正背面定義","titleEn":"Define wafer front and back","objective":"在影像中標示主動面、背面與缺口，並能說明「翻面會改變座標觀察方向」。","objectiveEn":"Mark active face, back face and notch and explain: Flipping changes the viewed coordinate orientation.","instruction":"在影像中標示主動面、背面與缺口。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：影像方向能與旅行單相互轉換。","instructionEn":"Mark active face, back face and notch. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Image orientation maps consistently to the traveler.","observation":"影像方向能與旅行單相互轉換；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Image orientation maps consistently to the traveler; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"鏡射未處理會挑錯晶粒。","failureEn":"Unresolved mirroring selects incorrect dies.","check":"影像方向能與旅行單相互轉換。","checkEn":"Image orientation maps consistently to the traveler.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-030-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"翻面會改變座標觀察方向。","textEn":"Flipping changes the viewed coordinate orientation."},{"id":"pk-030-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"鏡射未處理會挑錯晶粒；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Unresolved mirroring selects incorrect dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立晶圓正背面定義」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Define wafer front and back\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["量測點位與極值可追溯","抽樣策略有批次與缺陷假設","影像方向能與旅行單相互轉換"],"optionsEn":["Measurement locations and extrema are traceable","The sampling plan states lot and defect assumptions","Image orientation maps consistently to the traveler"],"answer":2,"explanation":"翻面會改變座標觀察方向。本步要確認：影像方向能與旅行單相互轉換；常見誤判是：鏡射未處理會挑錯晶粒。","explanationEn":"Flipping changes the viewed coordinate orientation. Verify: Image orientation maps consistently to the traveler. A common misinterpretation is: Unresolved mirroring selects incorrect dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-029"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-031","order":5,"sequence":31,"title":"驗證晶圓地圖版本","titleEn":"Verify wafer-map revision","objective":"核對探針測試地圖與產品版本，並能說明「舊地圖可能含不同晶粒排列或分檔」。","objectiveEn":"Match probe-map revision to product revision and explain: Old maps may contain different grids or binning.","instruction":"核對探針測試地圖與產品版本。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：版本與測試時間符合指定進料條件。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Match probe-map revision to product revision. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Revision and test time meet the incoming requirements. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"版本與測試時間符合指定進料條件；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Revision and test time meet the incoming requirements; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"檔名相似不能替代版本核對。","failureEn":"Similar filenames do not replace revision checking.","check":"版本與測試時間符合指定進料條件。","checkEn":"Revision and test time meet the incoming requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-031-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"舊地圖可能含不同晶粒排列或分檔。","textEn":"Old maps may contain different grids or binning."},{"id":"pk-031-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"檔名相似不能替代版本核對；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Similar filenames do not replace revision checking. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-031-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"教學地圖有 100 個實體晶粒，電子檔標示 92 良品、5 不良、3 未測。可挑選數是 92，而不是以非不良數 95 代替；未測需維持獨立狀態。","textEn":"A teaching map has 100 physical dies: 92 good, 5 bad and 3 untested. Pickable count is 92, not 95 inferred from not-bad status; untested remains separate."},{"id":"pk-031-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"驗證晶圓 ID、座標原點、旋轉、鏡射、bin 定義及版本雜湊。相同檔名不代表相同地圖，且更新後不得讓舊快取挑選未授權晶粒。","textEn":"Verify wafer ID, origin, rotation, reflection, bin meanings and version hash. Identical filenames need not mean identical maps, and stale caches must not select unauthorized dies."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證晶圓地圖版本」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify wafer-map revision\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["版本與測試時間符合指定進料條件","支承、溫度與量測面完整記錄","相關與無相關位置都保留證據"],"optionsEn":["Revision and test time meet the incoming requirements","Support, temperature and measured side are recorded","Both matching and nonmatching locations retain evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊地圖可能含不同晶粒排列或分檔。本步要確認：版本與測試時間符合指定進料條件；常見誤判是：檔名相似不能替代版本核對。","explanationEn":"Old maps may contain different grids or binning. Verify: Revision and test time meet the incoming requirements. A common misinterpretation is: Similar filenames do not replace revision checking."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-030"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-032","order":6,"sequence":32,"title":"校正地圖原點","titleEn":"Calibrate the map origin","objective":"以缺口和參考晶粒對齊座標原點，並能說明「原點偏一格會影響整片挑選」。","objectiveEn":"Align the origin using notch and reference die and explain: A one-cell origin error affects wafer-wide selection.","instruction":"以缺口和參考晶粒對齊座標原點。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：至少兩個獨立參考點同時吻合。","instructionEn":"Align the origin using notch and reference die. Check evidence you create or obtain against: At least two independent references agree.","observation":"至少兩個獨立參考點同時吻合；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"At least two independent references agree; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單點吻合可能掩蓋旋轉或偏移。","failureEn":"A single matching point can hide rotation or translation.","check":"至少兩個獨立參考點同時吻合。","checkEn":"At least two independent references agree.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-032-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"原點偏一格會影響整片挑選。","textEn":"A one-cell origin error affects wafer-wide selection."},{"id":"pk-032-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單點吻合可能掩蓋旋轉或偏移；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A single matching point can hide rotation or translation. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「校正地圖原點」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calibrate the map origin\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["放行或退回都有理由與負責紀錄","至少兩個獨立參考點同時吻合","每道刮痕都有受影響結構判讀"],"optionsEn":["Release or return includes reasoning and ownership","At least two independent references agree","Each scratch has an affected-feature assessment"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原點偏一格會影響整片挑選。本步要確認：至少兩個獨立參考點同時吻合；常見誤判是：單點吻合可能掩蓋旋轉或偏移。","explanationEn":"A one-cell origin error affects wafer-wide selection. Verify: At least two independent references agree. A common misinterpretation is: A single matching point can hide rotation or translation."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-031"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-033","order":7,"sequence":33,"title":"確認地圖旋轉與鏡射","titleEn":"Confirm map rotation and reflection","objective":"比較角落特徵在各轉換下的位置，並能說明「旋轉與鏡射是不同座標操作」。","objectiveEn":"Compare corner features under coordinate transforms and explain: Rotation and reflection are different transforms.","instruction":"比較角落特徵在各轉換下的位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：唯一轉換能解釋所有已知標記。","instructionEn":"Compare corner features under coordinate transforms. Check evidence you create or obtain against: One transform explains every known marker.","observation":"唯一轉換能解釋所有已知標記；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"One transform explains every known marker; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"以旋轉修正鏡射會保留錯誤。","failureEn":"Correcting reflection with rotation leaves errors.","check":"唯一轉換能解釋所有已知標記。","checkEn":"One transform explains every known marker.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-033-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"旋轉與鏡射是不同座標操作。","textEn":"Rotation and reflection are different transforms."},{"id":"pk-033-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"以旋轉修正鏡射會保留錯誤；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Correcting reflection with rotation leaves errors. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「確認地圖旋轉與鏡射」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Confirm map rotation and reflection\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["可疑位置連到後續表面分析需求","每個可挑選座標能回溯測試狀態","唯一轉換能解釋所有已知標記"],"optionsEn":["Suspect locations link to follow-up surface analysis","Each selectable coordinate resolves to test status","One transform explains every known marker"],"answer":2,"explanation":"旋轉與鏡射是不同座標操作。本步要確認：唯一轉換能解釋所有已知標記；常見誤判是：以旋轉修正鏡射會保留錯誤。","explanationEn":"Rotation and reflection are different transforms. Verify: One transform explains every known marker. A common misinterpretation is: Correcting reflection with rotation leaves errors."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-032"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-034","order":8,"sequence":34,"title":"解讀良率分檔代碼","titleEn":"Interpret yield-bin codes","objective":"將每個代碼對應可挑選或隔離狀態，並能說明「測試分檔語意由測試方案定義」。","objectiveEn":"Map each bin code to pickable or quarantined status and explain: Bin semantics are defined by the test program.","instruction":"將每個代碼對應可挑選或隔離狀態。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：所有出現的代碼都有明確處置。","instructionEn":"Map each bin code to pickable or quarantined status. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Every observed code has a defined disposition.","observation":"所有出現的代碼都有明確處置；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Every observed code has a defined disposition; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把非零代碼一律當良品會誤放行。","failureEn":"Treating all nonzero codes as good misreleases dies.","check":"所有出現的代碼都有明確處置。","checkEn":"Every observed code has a defined disposition.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-034-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"測試分檔語意由測試方案定義。","textEn":"Bin semantics are defined by the test program."},{"id":"pk-034-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把非零代碼一律當良品會誤放行；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Treating all nonzero codes as good misreleases dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「解讀良率分檔代碼」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret yield-bin codes\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["所有出現的代碼都有明確處置","開口與焊墊位置及完整性均已核對","下游可直接取得地圖版本及限制"],"optionsEn":["Every observed code has a defined disposition","Opening alignment and integrity are verified","Downstream stations receive map revision and restrictions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"測試分檔語意由測試方案定義。本步要確認：所有出現的代碼都有明確處置；常見誤判是：把非零代碼一律當良品會誤放行。","explanationEn":"Bin semantics are defined by the test program. Verify: Every observed code has a defined disposition. A common misinterpretation is: Treating all nonzero codes as good misreleases dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-033"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-035","order":9,"sequence":35,"title":"核算晶粒數量","titleEn":"Reconcile die counts","objective":"加總良品、不良與邊緣排除晶粒，並能說明「總量守恆可揭露地圖遺漏」。","objectiveEn":"Sum good, failed and edge-excluded dies and explain: Count reconciliation reveals missing map entries.","instruction":"加總良品、不良與邊緣排除晶粒。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：分類加總等於可辨識晶粒總數。","instructionEn":"Sum good, failed and edge-excluded dies. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Category totals equal the identifiable die count.","observation":"分類加總等於可辨識晶粒總數；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Category totals equal the identifiable die count; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"遺漏邊緣半晶粒會造成數量差。","failureEn":"Missing partial edge dies creates discrepancies.","check":"分類加總等於可辨識晶粒總數。","checkEn":"Category totals equal the identifiable die count.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-035-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"總量守恆可揭露地圖遺漏。","textEn":"Count reconciliation reveals missing map entries."},{"id":"pk-035-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"遺漏邊緣半晶粒會造成數量差；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Missing partial edge dies creates discrepancies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核算晶粒數量」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Reconcile die counts\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["三種識別資訊無未解決差異","分類加總等於可辨識晶粒總數","疑似顆粒保留原始影像與尺度"],"optionsEn":["All three identifiers agree without unresolved differences","Category totals equal the identifiable die count","Suspected particles retain original images and scale"],"answer":1,"explanation":"總量守恆可揭露地圖遺漏。本步要確認：分類加總等於可辨識晶粒總數；常見誤判是：遺漏邊緣半晶粒會造成數量差。","explanationEn":"Count reconciliation reveals missing map entries. Verify: Category totals equal the identifiable die count. A common misinterpretation is: Missing partial edge dies creates discrepancies."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-034"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-036","order":10,"sequence":36,"title":"比對實體與電子墨點","titleEn":"Compare physical and electronic marks","objective":"對照表面墨點與地圖剔除位置，並能說明「不同剔除方式需建立優先判定規則」。","objectiveEn":"Compare physical marks with map exclusions and explain: Different exclusion systems need precedence rules.","instruction":"對照表面墨點與地圖剔除位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：衝突晶粒被隔離而非自動挑選。","instructionEn":"Compare physical marks with map exclusions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Conflicting dies are quarantined rather than selected.","observation":"衝突晶粒被隔離而非自動挑選；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Conflicting dies are quarantined rather than selected; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把所有墨跡當測試標記會誤分類。","failureEn":"Treating every stain as a test mark misclassifies dies.","check":"衝突晶粒被隔離而非自動挑選。","checkEn":"Conflicting dies are quarantined rather than selected.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-036-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同剔除方式需建立優先判定規則。","textEn":"Different exclusion systems need precedence rules."},{"id":"pk-036-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把所有墨跡當測試標記會誤分類；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Treating every stain as a test mark misclassifies dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「比對實體與電子墨點」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Compare physical and electronic marks\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["刀路所遇材料已納入流程選擇","異常包裝批次被標示待判定","衝突晶粒被隔離而非自動挑選"],"optionsEn":["Materials encountered by the cut are included in route selection","Compromised shipments are flagged for disposition","Conflicting dies are quarantined rather than selected"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同剔除方式需建立優先判定規則。本步要確認：衝突晶粒被隔離而非自動挑選；常見誤判是：把所有墨跡當測試標記會誤分類。","explanationEn":"Different exclusion systems need precedence rules. Verify: Conflicting dies are quarantined rather than selected. A common misinterpretation is: Treating every stain as a test mark misclassifies dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-035"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-037","order":11,"sequence":37,"title":"檢查晶圓邊緣崩裂","titleEn":"Inspect wafer-edge chipping","objective":"在全周影像中圈出缺口及裂紋，並能說明「邊緣缺陷可在搬運及薄化時擴展」。","objectiveEn":"Annotate chips and cracks around the perimeter and explain: Edge damage can propagate during handling and thinning.","instruction":"在全周影像中圈出缺口及裂紋。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：缺陷位置與量測尺度已記錄。","instructionEn":"Annotate chips and cracks around the perimeter. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Defect locations and measurement scales are recorded.","observation":"缺陷位置與量測尺度已記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Defect locations and measurement scales are recorded; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看正面中心會漏掉邊緣風險。","failureEn":"Center-only inspection misses edge risk.","check":"缺陷位置與量測尺度已記錄。","checkEn":"Defect locations and measurement scales are recorded.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-037-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"邊緣缺陷可在搬運及薄化時擴展。","textEn":"Edge damage can propagate during handling and thinning."},{"id":"pk-037-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看正面中心會漏掉邊緣風險；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Center-only inspection misses edge risk. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查晶圓邊緣崩裂」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect wafer-edge chipping\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["缺陷位置與量測尺度已記錄","背面製程要求與實際層別相符","未知暴露歷程沒有被視為零暴露"],"optionsEn":["Defect locations and measurement scales are recorded","Backside process requirements match observed layers","Unknown exposure is not treated as zero exposure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣缺陷可在搬運及薄化時擴展。本步要確認：缺陷位置與量測尺度已記錄；常見誤判是：只看正面中心會漏掉邊緣風險。","explanationEn":"Edge damage can propagate during handling and thinning. Verify: Defect locations and measurement scales are recorded. A common misinterpretation is: Center-only inspection misses edge risk."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-036"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-038","order":12,"sequence":38,"title":"量測進料厚度分布","titleEn":"Measure incoming thickness distribution","objective":"在固定座標取厚度點並生成地圖，並能說明「單點厚度不能代表整片均勻性」。","objectiveEn":"Sample thickness on fixed coordinates and form a map and explain: One thickness point cannot represent wafer uniformity.","instruction":"在固定座標取厚度點並生成地圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：量測點位與極值可追溯。","instructionEn":"Sample thickness on fixed coordinates and form a map. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Measurement locations and extrema are traceable.","observation":"量測點位與極值可追溯；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Measurement locations and extrema are traceable; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"不一致量測點會製造假批次差。","failureEn":"Inconsistent sampling creates false lot differences.","check":"量測點位與極值可追溯。","checkEn":"Measurement locations and extrema are traceable.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-038-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"單點厚度不能代表整片均勻性。","textEn":"One thickness point cannot represent wafer uniformity."},{"id":"pk-038-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"不一致量測點會製造假批次差；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Inconsistent sampling creates false lot differences. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測進料厚度分布」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure incoming thickness distribution\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["影像方向能與旅行單相互轉換","量測點位與極值可追溯","工具能力能回答指定檢查問題"],"optionsEn":["Image orientation maps consistently to the traveler","Measurement locations and extrema are traceable","Tool capability addresses the specified inspection question"],"answer":1,"explanation":"單點厚度不能代表整片均勻性。本步要確認：量測點位與極值可追溯；常見誤判是：不一致量測點會製造假批次差。","explanationEn":"One thickness point cannot represent wafer uniformity. Verify: Measurement locations and extrema are traceable. A common misinterpretation is: Inconsistent sampling creates false lot differences."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-037"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-039","order":13,"sequence":39,"title":"量測進料翹曲","titleEn":"Measure incoming wafer warpage","objective":"依指定支承比較自由表面高度，並能說明「支承方式會改變觀測形貌」。","objectiveEn":"Measure surface height under defined support conditions and explain: Support conditions change measured shape.","instruction":"依指定支承比較自由表面高度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：支承、溫度與量測面完整記錄。","instructionEn":"Measure surface height under defined support conditions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Support, temperature and measured side are recorded.","observation":"支承、溫度與量測面完整記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Support, temperature and measured side are recorded; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"吸附狀態與自由狀態不能直接比較。","failureEn":"Chucked and free-state shapes are not directly comparable.","check":"支承、溫度與量測面完整記錄。","checkEn":"Support, temperature and measured side are recorded.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-039-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"支承方式會改變觀測形貌。","textEn":"Support conditions change measured shape."},{"id":"pk-039-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"吸附狀態與自由狀態不能直接比較；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Chucked and free-state shapes are not directly comparable. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測進料翹曲」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure incoming wafer warpage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["重複分布與接受準則一併呈現","版本與測試時間符合指定進料條件","支承、溫度與量測面完整記錄"],"optionsEn":["Repeat distributions are shown against acceptance criteria","Revision and test time meet the incoming requirements","Support, temperature and measured side are recorded"],"answer":2,"explanation":"支承方式會改變觀測形貌。本步要確認：支承、溫度與量測面完整記錄；常見誤判是：吸附狀態與自由狀態不能直接比較。","explanationEn":"Support conditions change measured shape. Verify: Support, temperature and measured side are recorded. A common misinterpretation is: Chucked and free-state shapes are not directly comparable."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-038"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-040","order":14,"sequence":40,"title":"檢查主動面刮傷","titleEn":"Inspect active-face scratches","objective":"將刮痕與焊墊及鈍化開口疊圖，並能說明「缺陷嚴重度取決於位置與功能」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay scratches with pads and passivation openings and explain: Defect severity depends on location and function.","instruction":"將刮痕與焊墊及鈍化開口疊圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每道刮痕都有受影響結構判讀。","instructionEn":"Overlay scratches with pads and passivation openings. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each scratch has an affected-feature assessment.","observation":"每道刮痕都有受影響結構判讀；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each scratch has an affected-feature assessment; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單看長度可能漏掉穿越關鍵焊墊。","failureEn":"Length alone misses critical-pad intersections.","check":"每道刮痕都有受影響結構判讀。","checkEn":"Each scratch has an affected-feature assessment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-040-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"缺陷嚴重度取決於位置與功能。","textEn":"Defect severity depends on location and function."},{"id":"pk-040-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單看長度可能漏掉穿越關鍵焊墊；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Length alone misses critical-pad intersections. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查主動面刮傷」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect active-face scratches\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每道刮痕都有受影響結構判讀","抽樣策略有批次與缺陷假設","至少兩個獨立參考點同時吻合"],"optionsEn":["Each scratch has an affected-feature assessment","The sampling plan states lot and defect assumptions","At least two independent references agree"],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷嚴重度取決於位置與功能。本步要確認：每道刮痕都有受影響結構判讀；常見誤判是：單看長度可能漏掉穿越關鍵焊墊。","explanationEn":"Defect severity depends on location and function. Verify: Each scratch has an affected-feature assessment. A common misinterpretation is: Length alone misses critical-pad intersections."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-039"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-041","order":15,"sequence":41,"title":"檢查焊墊氧化與變色","titleEn":"Inspect pad oxidation and discoloration","objective":"比較正常與異常焊墊反射影像，並能說明「顏色差異是線索而非化學定論」。","objectiveEn":"Compare reference and abnormal pad images and explain: Color difference is a clue, not chemical proof.","instruction":"比較正常與異常焊墊反射影像。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：可疑位置連到後續表面分析需求。","instructionEn":"Compare reference and abnormal pad images. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Suspect locations link to follow-up surface analysis.","observation":"可疑位置連到後續表面分析需求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Suspect locations link to follow-up surface analysis; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"外觀判斷無法單獨識別氧化成分。","failureEn":"Appearance alone cannot identify oxide chemistry.","check":"可疑位置連到後續表面分析需求。","checkEn":"Suspect locations link to follow-up surface analysis.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-041-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"顏色差異是線索而非化學定論。","textEn":"Color difference is a clue, not chemical proof."},{"id":"pk-041-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"外觀判斷無法單獨識別氧化成分；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Appearance alone cannot identify oxide chemistry. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查焊墊氧化與變色」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect pad oxidation and discoloration\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["唯一轉換能解釋所有已知標記","可疑位置連到後續表面分析需求","相關與無相關位置都保留證據"],"optionsEn":["One transform explains every known marker","Suspect locations link to follow-up surface analysis","Both matching and nonmatching locations retain evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"顏色差異是線索而非化學定論。本步要確認：可疑位置連到後續表面分析需求；常見誤判是：外觀判斷無法單獨識別氧化成分。","explanationEn":"Color difference is a clue, not chemical proof. Verify: Suspect locations link to follow-up surface analysis. A common misinterpretation is: Appearance alone cannot identify oxide chemistry."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-040"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-042","order":16,"sequence":42,"title":"檢查鈍化層開口","titleEn":"Inspect passivation openings","objective":"量測焊墊可接觸區及周邊裂口，並能說明「鈍化開口限制接合可用面積」。","objectiveEn":"Measure accessible pad area and surrounding cracks and explain: Passivation openings limit bondable area.","instruction":"量測焊墊可接觸區及周邊裂口。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：開口與焊墊位置及完整性均已核對。","instructionEn":"Measure accessible pad area and surrounding cracks. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Opening alignment and integrity are verified.","observation":"開口與焊墊位置及完整性均已核對；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Opening alignment and integrity are verified; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只量金屬墊會高估可接合區。","failureEn":"Measuring only metal overstates bondable area.","check":"開口與焊墊位置及完整性均已核對。","checkEn":"Opening alignment and integrity are verified.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-042-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"鈍化開口限制接合可用面積。","textEn":"Passivation openings limit bondable area."},{"id":"pk-042-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只量金屬墊會高估可接合區；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Measuring only metal overstates bondable area. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查鈍化層開口」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect passivation openings\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["放行或退回都有理由與負責紀錄","所有出現的代碼都有明確處置","開口與焊墊位置及完整性均已核對"],"optionsEn":["Release or return includes reasoning and ownership","Every observed code has a defined disposition","Opening alignment and integrity are verified"],"answer":2,"explanation":"鈍化開口限制接合可用面積。本步要確認：開口與焊墊位置及完整性均已核對；常見誤判是：只量金屬墊會高估可接合區。","explanationEn":"Passivation openings limit bondable area. Verify: Opening alignment and integrity are verified. A common misinterpretation is: Measuring only metal overstates bondable area."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-041"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-043","order":17,"sequence":43,"title":"辨識表面顆粒","titleEn":"Classify surface particles","objective":"按位置和形態區分顆粒及圖案結構，並能說明「缺陷分類需避免把正常結構當顆粒」。","objectiveEn":"Classify particles versus patterned features by shape and location and explain: Classification must distinguish defects from intended structures.","instruction":"按位置和形態區分顆粒及圖案結構。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：疑似顆粒保留原始影像與尺度。","instructionEn":"Classify particles versus patterned features by shape and location. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Suspected particles retain original images and scale.","observation":"疑似顆粒保留原始影像與尺度；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Suspected particles retain original images and scale; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過度降噪可能抹除真實小缺陷。","failureEn":"Excessive denoising can erase real small defects.","check":"疑似顆粒保留原始影像與尺度。","checkEn":"Suspected particles retain original images and scale.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-043-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"缺陷分類需避免把正常結構當顆粒。","textEn":"Classification must distinguish defects from intended structures."},{"id":"pk-043-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過度降噪可能抹除真實小缺陷；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excessive denoising can erase real small defects. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識表面顆粒」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Classify surface particles\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["疑似顆粒保留原始影像與尺度","每個可挑選座標能回溯測試狀態","分類加總等於可辨識晶粒總數"],"optionsEn":["Suspected particles retain original images and scale","Each selectable coordinate resolves to test status","Category totals equal the identifiable die count"],"answer":0,"explanation":"缺陷分類需避免把正常結構當顆粒。本步要確認：疑似顆粒保留原始影像與尺度；常見誤判是：過度降噪可能抹除真實小缺陷。","explanationEn":"Classification must distinguish defects from intended structures. Verify: Suspected particles retain original images and scale. A common misinterpretation is: Excessive denoising can erase real small defects."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-042"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-044","order":18,"sequence":44,"title":"核對切割道金屬","titleEn":"Review street metallization","objective":"標示測試結構與切割道交會位置，並能說明「街道金屬改變分離方式的適用性」。","objectiveEn":"Mark test structures crossing the streets and explain: Street metal affects singulation-method suitability.","instruction":"標示測試結構與切割道交會位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：刀路所遇材料已納入流程選擇。","instructionEn":"Mark test structures crossing the streets. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Materials encountered by the cut are included in route selection.","observation":"刀路所遇材料已納入流程選擇；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Materials encountered by the cut are included in route selection; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"假設整條街道只有矽會漏掉分層風險。","failureEn":"Assuming silicon-only streets misses delamination risk.","check":"刀路所遇材料已納入流程選擇。","checkEn":"Materials encountered by the cut are included in route selection.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-044-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"街道金屬改變分離方式的適用性。","textEn":"Street metal affects singulation-method suitability."},{"id":"pk-044-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"假設整條街道只有矽會漏掉分層風險；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Assuming silicon-only streets misses delamination risk. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對切割道金屬」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review street metallization\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["衝突晶粒被隔離而非自動挑選","刀路所遇材料已納入流程選擇","下游可直接取得地圖版本及限制"],"optionsEn":["Conflicting dies are quarantined rather than selected","Materials encountered by the cut are included in route selection","Downstream stations receive map revision and restrictions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"街道金屬改變分離方式的適用性。本步要確認：刀路所遇材料已納入流程選擇；常見誤判是：假設整條街道只有矽會漏掉分層風險。","explanationEn":"Street metal affects singulation-method suitability. Verify: Materials encountered by the cut are included in route selection. A common misinterpretation is: Assuming silicon-only streets misses delamination risk."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-043"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-045","order":19,"sequence":45,"title":"檢查背面鍍層","titleEn":"Inspect backside metallization","objective":"核對背面覆膜種類、缺陷與覆蓋，並能說明「背面層會影響研磨、接合與電性」。","objectiveEn":"Check backside film type, defects and coverage and explain: Backside layers affect grinding, attachment and electrical behavior.","instruction":"核對背面覆膜種類、缺陷與覆蓋。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：背面製程要求與實際層別相符。","instructionEn":"Check backside film type, defects and coverage. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Backside process requirements match observed layers.","observation":"背面製程要求與實際層別相符；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Backside process requirements match observed layers; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略背金可能導致錯誤薄化方案。","failureEn":"Ignoring backside metal can invalidate thinning plans.","check":"背面製程要求與實際層別相符。","checkEn":"Backside process requirements match observed layers.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-045-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"背面層會影響研磨、接合與電性。","textEn":"Backside layers affect grinding, attachment and electrical behavior."},{"id":"pk-045-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略背金可能導致錯誤薄化方案；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring backside metal can invalidate thinning plans. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查背面鍍層」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect backside metallization\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["三種識別資訊無未解決差異","缺陷位置與量測尺度已記錄","背面製程要求與實際層別相符"],"optionsEn":["All three identifiers agree without unresolved differences","Defect locations and measurement scales are recorded","Backside process requirements match observed layers"],"answer":2,"explanation":"背面層會影響研磨、接合與電性。本步要確認：背面製程要求與實際層別相符；常見誤判是：忽略背金可能導致錯誤薄化方案。","explanationEn":"Backside layers affect grinding, attachment and electrical behavior. Verify: Backside process requirements match observed layers. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring backside metal can invalidate thinning plans."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-044"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-046","order":20,"sequence":46,"title":"選定進料量測方法","titleEn":"Select incoming metrology","objective":"依缺陷尺度選擇光學、厚度或聲學量測，並能說明「量測工具有各自解析與敏感範圍」。","objectiveEn":"Select optical, thickness or acoustic methods by defect scale and explain: Metrology tools have distinct resolution and sensitivity.","instruction":"依缺陷尺度選擇光學、厚度或聲學量測。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：工具能力能回答指定檢查問題。","instructionEn":"Select optical, thickness or acoustic methods by defect scale. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Tool capability addresses the specified inspection question.","observation":"工具能力能回答指定檢查問題；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Tool capability addresses the specified inspection question; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"工具看不到缺陷不代表缺陷不存在。","failureEn":"A tool's blind spot does not prove absence.","check":"工具能力能回答指定檢查問題。","checkEn":"Tool capability addresses the specified inspection question.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-046-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"量測工具有各自解析與敏感範圍。","textEn":"Metrology tools have distinct resolution and sensitivity."},{"id":"pk-046-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"工具看不到缺陷不代表缺陷不存在；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A tool's blind spot does not prove absence. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選定進料量測方法」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select incoming metrology\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["工具能力能回答指定檢查問題","異常包裝批次被標示待判定","量測點位與極值可追溯"],"optionsEn":["Tool capability addresses the specified inspection question","Compromised shipments are flagged for disposition","Measurement locations and extrema are traceable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測工具有各自解析與敏感範圍。本步要確認：工具能力能回答指定檢查問題；常見誤判是：工具看不到缺陷不代表缺陷不存在。","explanationEn":"Metrology tools have distinct resolution and sensitivity. Verify: Tool capability addresses the specified inspection question. A common misinterpretation is: A tool's blind spot does not prove absence."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-045"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-047","order":21,"sequence":47,"title":"檢查量測系統重複性","titleEn":"Check metrology repeatability","objective":"對同一標準樣本重複量測，並能說明「設備波動會混入產品變異」。","objectiveEn":"Repeat measurements on one reference sample and explain: Instrument variation mixes with product variation.","instruction":"對同一標準樣本重複量測。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：重複分布與接受準則一併呈現。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Repeat measurements on one reference sample. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Repeat distributions are shown against acceptance criteria. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"重複分布與接受準則一併呈現；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Repeat distributions are shown against acceptance criteria; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把設備漂移算成晶圓異常會誤隔離。","failureEn":"Instrument drift mistaken for wafer variation causes false quarantine.","check":"重複分布與接受準則一併呈現。","checkEn":"Repeat distributions are shown against acceptance criteria.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-047-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"設備波動會混入產品變異。","textEn":"Instrument variation mixes with product variation."},{"id":"pk-047-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把設備漂移算成晶圓異常會誤隔離；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Instrument drift mistaken for wafer variation causes false quarantine. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-047-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設同位置五次厚度量測為 99、100、101、100、100 µm，平均 100 µm、樣本標準差約 0.707 µm。這只描述重複性，未包含不同人、日期、治具與校正偏差。","textEn":"Five hypothetical thickness readings 99, 100, 101, 100 and 100 µm give mean 100 µm and sample standard deviation about 0.707 µm. This is repeatability only, excluding operators, days, fixtures and calibration bias."},{"id":"pk-047-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"先確認量測不確定度相對製程窗口是否足夠小，再解讀改善。若觀測改變小於儀器可分辨的差異，不能以單次讀值宣稱製程提升。","textEn":"Check measurement uncertainty against the process window before interpreting improvement. A change below resolvable measurement difference cannot establish process improvement from one reading."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查量測系統重複性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check metrology repeatability\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["支承、溫度與量測面完整記錄","重複分布與接受準則一併呈現","未知暴露歷程沒有被視為零暴露"],"optionsEn":["Support, temperature and measured side are recorded","Repeat distributions are shown against acceptance criteria","Unknown exposure is not treated as zero exposure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"設備波動會混入產品變異。本步要確認：重複分布與接受準則一併呈現；常見誤判是：把設備漂移算成晶圓異常會誤隔離。","explanationEn":"Instrument variation mixes with product variation. Verify: Repeat distributions are shown against acceptance criteria. A common misinterpretation is: Instrument drift mistaken for wafer variation causes false quarantine."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-046"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-048","order":22,"sequence":48,"title":"設定抽樣與全檢邊界","titleEn":"Define sampling versus full inspection","objective":"按關鍵特徵分配抽樣或全檢，並能說明「抽樣結論需保留漏檢風險」。","objectiveEn":"Assign sampling or full inspection to critical features and explain: Sampling conclusions retain escape risk.","instruction":"按關鍵特徵分配抽樣或全檢。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：抽樣策略有批次與缺陷假設。","instructionEn":"Assign sampling or full inspection to critical features. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The sampling plan states lot and defect assumptions.","observation":"抽樣策略有批次與缺陷假設；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The sampling plan states lot and defect assumptions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"少量無缺陷不能證明整批全良。","failureEn":"A few clean samples do not prove a perfect lot.","check":"抽樣策略有批次與缺陷假設。","checkEn":"The sampling plan states lot and defect assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-048-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"抽樣結論需保留漏檢風險。","textEn":"Sampling conclusions retain escape risk."},{"id":"pk-048-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"少量無缺陷不能證明整批全良；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A few clean samples do not prove a perfect lot. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「設定抽樣與全檢邊界」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Define sampling versus full inspection\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["影像方向能與旅行單相互轉換","每道刮痕都有受影響結構判讀","抽樣策略有批次與缺陷假設"],"optionsEn":["Image orientation maps consistently to the traveler","Each scratch has an affected-feature assessment","The sampling plan states lot and defect assumptions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"抽樣結論需保留漏檢風險。本步要確認：抽樣策略有批次與缺陷假設；常見誤判是：少量無缺陷不能證明整批全良。","explanationEn":"Sampling conclusions retain escape risk. Verify: The sampling plan states lot and defect assumptions. A common misinterpretation is: A few clean samples do not prove a perfect lot."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-047"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-049","order":23,"sequence":49,"title":"交叉比對電性與外觀","titleEn":"Cross-check electrical and visual results","objective":"疊加測試失效位置及外觀缺陷位置，並能說明「空間相關能形成假設但不是因果證明」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay test failures and visual defects and explain: Spatial correlation suggests hypotheses, not causation.","instruction":"疊加測試失效位置及外觀缺陷位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：相關與無相關位置都保留證據。","instructionEn":"Overlay test failures and visual defects. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Both matching and nonmatching locations retain evidence.","observation":"相關與無相關位置都保留證據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Both matching and nonmatching locations retain evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只挑吻合案例會放大錯誤因果。","failureEn":"Selecting only matches exaggerates false causality.","check":"相關與無相關位置都保留證據。","checkEn":"Both matching and nonmatching locations retain evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-049-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"空間相關能形成假設但不是因果證明。","textEn":"Spatial correlation suggests hypotheses, not causation."},{"id":"pk-049-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只挑吻合案例會放大錯誤因果；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Selecting only matches exaggerates false causality. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「交叉比對電性與外觀」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Cross-check electrical and visual results\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["相關與無相關位置都保留證據","版本與測試時間符合指定進料條件","可疑位置連到後續表面分析需求"],"optionsEn":["Both matching and nonmatching locations retain evidence","Revision and test time meet the incoming requirements","Suspect locations link to follow-up surface analysis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"空間相關能形成假設但不是因果證明。本步要確認：相關與無相關位置都保留證據；常見誤判是：只挑吻合案例會放大錯誤因果。","explanationEn":"Spatial correlation suggests hypotheses, not causation. Verify: Both matching and nonmatching locations retain evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Selecting only matches exaggerates false causality."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-048"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-050","order":24,"sequence":50,"title":"處置身分或品質衝突","titleEn":"Disposition identity or quality conflicts","objective":"把衝突項目列入待判定隔離清單，並能說明「未解決衝突不能靠任意平均消除」。","objectiveEn":"Place conflicting items on a quarantine list and explain: Unresolved conflicts cannot be averaged away.","instruction":"把衝突項目列入待判定隔離清單。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：放行或退回都有理由與負責紀錄。","instructionEn":"Place conflicting items on a quarantine list. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Release or return includes reasoning and ownership.","observation":"放行或退回都有理由與負責紀錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Release or return includes reasoning and ownership; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"直接覆寫原始結果會破壞證據。","failureEn":"Overwriting original results destroys evidence.","check":"放行或退回都有理由與負責紀錄。","checkEn":"Release or return includes reasoning and ownership.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-050-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"未解決衝突不能靠任意平均消除。","textEn":"Unresolved conflicts cannot be averaged away."},{"id":"pk-050-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"直接覆寫原始結果會破壞證據；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Overwriting original results destroys evidence. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「處置身分或品質衝突」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Disposition identity or quality conflicts\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["開口與焊墊位置及完整性均已核對","放行或退回都有理由與負責紀錄","至少兩個獨立參考點同時吻合"],"optionsEn":["Opening alignment and integrity are verified","Release or return includes reasoning and ownership","At least two independent references agree"],"answer":1,"explanation":"未解決衝突不能靠任意平均消除。本步要確認：放行或退回都有理由與負責紀錄；常見誤判是：直接覆寫原始結果會破壞證據。","explanationEn":"Unresolved conflicts cannot be averaged away. Verify: Release or return includes reasoning and ownership. A common misinterpretation is: Overwriting original results destroys evidence."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-049"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-051","order":25,"sequence":51,"title":"凍結可挑選晶粒地圖","titleEn":"Freeze the pickable-die map","objective":"輸出只含核准晶粒的挑選清單，並能說明「挑選清單需與原始地圖保持可追溯」。","objectiveEn":"Export a selection list containing approved dies only and explain: Selection lists must remain traceable to original maps.","instruction":"輸出只含核准晶粒的挑選清單。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每個可挑選座標能回溯測試狀態。","instructionEn":"Export a selection list containing approved dies only. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each selectable coordinate resolves to test status.","observation":"每個可挑選座標能回溯測試狀態；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each selectable coordinate resolves to test status; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"手動改圖未留版本會失去一致性。","failureEn":"Unversioned map edits lose consistency.","check":"每個可挑選座標能回溯測試狀態。","checkEn":"Each selectable coordinate resolves to test status.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-051-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"挑選清單需與原始地圖保持可追溯。","textEn":"Selection lists must remain traceable to original maps."},{"id":"pk-051-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"手動改圖未留版本會失去一致性；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Unversioned map edits lose consistency. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「凍結可挑選晶粒地圖」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Freeze the pickable-die map\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["唯一轉換能解釋所有已知標記","疑似顆粒保留原始影像與尺度","每個可挑選座標能回溯測試狀態"],"optionsEn":["One transform explains every known marker","Suspected particles retain original images and scale","Each selectable coordinate resolves to test status"],"answer":2,"explanation":"挑選清單需與原始地圖保持可追溯。本步要確認：每個可挑選座標能回溯測試狀態；常見誤判是：手動改圖未留版本會失去一致性。","explanationEn":"Selection lists must remain traceable to original maps. Verify: Each selectable coordinate resolves to test status. A common misinterpretation is: Unversioned map edits lose consistency."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-050"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-052","order":26,"sequence":52,"title":"建立進料放行封包","titleEn":"Assemble the incoming-release package","objective":"整合身分、量測與處置到同一批次紀錄，並能說明「放行依據包含量測條件與未決事項」。","objectiveEn":"Combine identity, measurements and disposition by lot and explain: Release evidence includes conditions and unresolved items.","instruction":"整合身分、量測與處置到同一批次紀錄。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：下游可直接取得地圖版本及限制。","instructionEn":"Combine identity, measurements and disposition by lot. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Downstream stations receive map revision and restrictions.","observation":"下游可直接取得地圖版本及限制；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Downstream stations receive map revision and restrictions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只傳送良率百分比不足以指導加工。","failureEn":"Yield percentage alone cannot guide processing.","check":"下游可直接取得地圖版本及限制。","checkEn":"Downstream stations receive map revision and restrictions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-052-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"放行依據包含量測條件與未決事項。","textEn":"Release evidence includes conditions and unresolved items."},{"id":"pk-052-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只傳送良率百分比不足以指導加工；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Yield percentage alone cannot guide processing. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立進料放行封包」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assemble the incoming-release package\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["下游可直接取得地圖版本及限制","所有出現的代碼都有明確處置","刀路所遇材料已納入流程選擇"],"optionsEn":["Downstream stations receive map revision and restrictions","Every observed code has a defined disposition","Materials encountered by the cut are included in route selection"],"answer":0,"explanation":"放行依據包含量測條件與未決事項。本步要確認：下游可直接取得地圖版本及限制；常見誤判是：只傳送良率百分比不足以指導加工。","explanationEn":"Release evidence includes conditions and unresolved items. Verify: Downstream stations receive map revision and restrictions. A common misinterpretation is: Yield percentage alone cannot guide processing."},"sourceIds":["pk-kla-inspection","pk-asmpt-processes"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-051"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m03","order":3,"sequence":3,"title":"晶圓薄化、研磨與應力消除","titleEn":"Wafer thinning, grinding and stress relief","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查晶圓薄化、研磨與應力消除的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for wafer thinning, grinding and stress relief. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"比較支承與薄化方法；覆晶路線需先評估m07凸塊對支承的影響。","routeEn":"Compare support and thinning methods; flipchip routes first assess m07 bump support.","sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-053","order":1,"sequence":53,"title":"分配薄化終厚","titleEn":"Allocate final wafer thickness","objective":"從堆疊預算扣除其他層厚度，並能說明「薄化裕量需包含後續移除量」。","objectiveEn":"Subtract other layers from the stack budget and explain: Thinning allowance includes later removal.","instruction":"從堆疊預算扣除其他層厚度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：終厚與後續損耗均已列出。","instructionEn":"Subtract other layers from the stack budget. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Final thickness and later losses are listed.","observation":"終厚與後續損耗均已列出；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Final thickness and later losses are listed; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略拋光移除會磨得過薄。","failureEn":"Ignoring polishing removal overthins wafers.","check":"終厚與後續損耗均已列出。","checkEn":"Final thickness and later losses are listed.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-053-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"薄化裕量需包含後續移除量。","textEn":"Thinning allowance includes later removal."},{"id":"pk-053-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略拋光移除會磨得過薄；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring polishing removal overthins wafers. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分配薄化終厚」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Allocate final wafer thickness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["有效吸附區符合選定支承方案","厚度極差採相同有效區域","終厚與後續損耗均已列出"],"optionsEn":["Active vacuum zones match the support plan","Thickness range uses one defined area","Final thickness and later losses are listed"],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄化裕量需包含後續移除量。本步要確認：終厚與後續損耗均已列出；常見誤判是：忽略拋光移除會磨得過薄。","explanationEn":"Thinning allowance includes later removal. Verify: Final thickness and later losses are listed. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring polishing removal overthins wafers."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-052"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-054","order":2,"sequence":54,"title":"選擇正面保護膜","titleEn":"Select front-side protection tape","objective":"比較保護膜與表面地形相容性，並能說明「膜層需支承又不損傷凸起」。","objectiveEn":"Compare tape compatibility with surface topography and explain: Tape must support without damaging protrusions.","instruction":"比較保護膜與表面地形相容性。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：凸起區沒有未支承空隙。","instructionEn":"Compare tape compatibility with surface topography. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Protruding regions have no unsupported gaps.","observation":"凸起區沒有未支承空隙；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Protruding regions have no unsupported gaps; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"薄膜跨橋會集中研磨應力。","failureEn":"Tape bridging concentrates grinding stress.","check":"凸起區沒有未支承空隙。","checkEn":"Protruding regions have no unsupported gaps.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-054-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"膜層需支承又不損傷凸起。","textEn":"Tape must support without damaging protrusions."},{"id":"pk-054-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"薄膜跨橋會集中研磨應力；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Tape bridging concentrates grinding stress. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇正面保護膜」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select front-side protection tape\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["凸起區沒有未支承空隙","選輪理由包含材料與損傷限制","斜率方向與支承調整假設一致"],"optionsEn":["Protruding regions have no unsupported gaps","Selection includes material and damage limits","Slope direction matches the support hypothesis"],"answer":0,"explanation":"膜層需支承又不損傷凸起。本步要確認：凸起區沒有未支承空隙；常見誤判是：薄膜跨橋會集中研磨應力。","explanationEn":"Tape must support without damaging protrusions. Verify: Protruding regions have no unsupported gaps. A common misinterpretation is: Tape bridging concentrates grinding stress."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-053"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-055","order":3,"sequence":55,"title":"檢查貼膜前清潔","titleEn":"Inspect pre-lamination cleanliness","objective":"標記顆粒可能夾入的位置，並能說明「夾粒會形成局部支承凸點」。","objectiveEn":"Mark potential trapped-particle locations and explain: Trapped particles create local support peaks.","instruction":"標記顆粒可能夾入的位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：接觸面疑似顆粒已隔離。","instructionEn":"Mark potential trapped-particle locations. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Suspected contact-face particles are isolated.","observation":"接觸面疑似顆粒已隔離；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Suspected contact-face particles are isolated; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"局部硬點可能造成晶圓裂紋。","failureEn":"Local hard spots can crack wafers.","check":"接觸面疑似顆粒已隔離。","checkEn":"Suspected contact-face particles are isolated.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-055-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"夾粒會形成局部支承凸點。","textEn":"Trapped particles create local support peaks."},{"id":"pk-055-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"局部硬點可能造成晶圓裂紋；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Local hard spots can crack wafers. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查貼膜前清潔」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect pre-lamination cleanliness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["選定路線不傷害暴露材料","接觸面疑似顆粒已隔離","負載異常與輪面狀態被交叉核對"],"optionsEn":["The selected route preserves exposed materials","Suspected contact-face particles are isolated","Load anomalies are checked against wheel condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"夾粒會形成局部支承凸點。本步要確認：接觸面疑似顆粒已隔離；常見誤判是：局部硬點可能造成晶圓裂紋。","explanationEn":"Trapped particles create local support peaks. Verify: Suspected contact-face particles are isolated. A common misinterpretation is: Local hard spots can crack wafers."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-054"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-056","order":4,"sequence":56,"title":"模擬貼膜排氣","titleEn":"Simulate lamination air removal","objective":"比較貼合方向與氣泡殘留，並能說明「氣泡形成不均勻支承」。","objectiveEn":"Compare lamination direction and trapped bubbles and explain: Bubbles create uneven support.","instruction":"比較貼合方向與氣泡殘留。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：氣泡分布不侵入受力敏感區。","instructionEn":"Compare lamination direction and trapped bubbles. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Bubbles avoid load-sensitive regions.","observation":"氣泡分布不侵入受力敏感區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Bubbles avoid load-sensitive regions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未排氣區在薄化後可能破裂。","failureEn":"Unvented regions may fracture after thinning.","check":"氣泡分布不侵入受力敏感區。","checkEn":"Bubbles avoid load-sensitive regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-056-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"氣泡形成不均勻支承。","textEn":"Bubbles create uneven support."},{"id":"pk-056-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未排氣區在薄化後可能破裂；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Unvented regions may fracture after thinning. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「模擬貼膜排氣」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Simulate lamination air removal\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["粗磨停點保留足夠後段餘量","結論同時引用形貌和強度資料","氣泡分布不侵入受力敏感區"],"optionsEn":["Coarse endpoint preserves finishing allowance","Conclusions cite shape and strength evidence","Bubbles avoid load-sensitive regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"氣泡形成不均勻支承。本步要確認：氣泡分布不侵入受力敏感區；常見誤判是：未排氣區在薄化後可能破裂。","explanationEn":"Bubbles create uneven support. Verify: Bubbles avoid load-sensitive regions. A common misinterpretation is: Unvented regions may fracture after thinning."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-055"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-057","order":5,"sequence":57,"title":"修整保護膜邊界","titleEn":"Review protection-tape trimming","objective":"核對膜邊與晶圓外緣，並能說明「外露黏膠可能污染吸盤」。","objectiveEn":"Compare tape boundaries with wafer edges and explain: Exposed adhesive can contaminate the chuck.","instruction":"核對膜邊與晶圓外緣。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：膜邊不超出指定裝夾包絡。","instructionEn":"Compare tape boundaries with wafer edges. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Tape edges fit the fixture envelope.","observation":"膜邊不超出指定裝夾包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Tape edges fit the fixture envelope; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"不規則膜邊會擾動真空支承。","failureEn":"Irregular tape edges disturb vacuum support.","check":"膜邊不超出指定裝夾包絡。","checkEn":"Tape edges fit the fixture envelope.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-057-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"外露黏膠可能污染吸盤。","textEn":"Exposed adhesive can contaminate the chuck."},{"id":"pk-057-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"不規則膜邊會擾動真空支承；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Irregular tape edges disturb vacuum support. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「修整保護膜邊界」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review protection-tape trimming\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["膜邊不超出指定裝夾包絡","突變位置連到輪況或支承檢查","邊緣改變未侵入功能區"],"optionsEn":["Tape edges fit the fixture envelope","Jumps trigger wheel or support checks","Edge changes avoid functional regions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"外露黏膠可能污染吸盤。本步要確認：膜邊不超出指定裝夾包絡；常見誤判是：不規則膜邊會擾動真空支承。","explanationEn":"Exposed adhesive can contaminate the chuck. Verify: Tape edges fit the fixture envelope. A common misinterpretation is: Irregular tape edges disturb vacuum support."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-056"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-058","order":6,"sequence":58,"title":"選擇載體支承方案","titleEn":"Select carrier support","objective":"比較膠膜與暫時載板路線，並能說明「極薄晶圓需要合適搬運支承」。","objectiveEn":"Compare tape and temporary-carrier routes and explain: Thin wafers need suitable handling support.","instruction":"比較膠膜與暫時載板路線。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：轉移時沒有無支承狀態。","instructionEn":"Compare tape and temporary-carrier routes. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Transfers avoid unsupported states.","observation":"轉移時沒有無支承狀態；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Transfers avoid unsupported states; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只驗證研磨未驗證轉移會破片。","failureEn":"Checking grinding alone misses transfer breakage.","check":"轉移時沒有無支承狀態。","checkEn":"Transfers avoid unsupported states.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-058-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"極薄晶圓需要合適搬運支承。","textEn":"Thin wafers need suitable handling support."},{"id":"pk-058-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只驗證研磨未驗證轉移會破片；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Checking grinding alone misses transfer breakage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇載體支承方案」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select carrier support\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["兩種指標均有各自驗收依據","轉移時沒有無支承狀態","作用區沒有明顯沖洗死角"],"optionsEn":["Both metrics have separate acceptance evidence","Transfers avoid unsupported states","The contact zone lacks obvious dead zones"],"answer":1,"explanation":"極薄晶圓需要合適搬運支承。本步要確認：轉移時沒有無支承狀態；常見誤判是：只驗證研磨未驗證轉移會破片。","explanationEn":"Thin wafers need suitable handling support. Verify: Transfers avoid unsupported states. A common misinterpretation is: Checking grinding alone misses transfer breakage."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-057"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-059","order":7,"sequence":59,"title":"判定邊緣修整需求","titleEn":"Determine edge-trimming need","objective":"比較薄化前後外緣剖面，並能說明「薄化可使倒角形成脆弱薄邊」。","objectiveEn":"Compare edge sections before and after thinning and explain: Thinning can leave fragile bevel edges.","instruction":"比較薄化前後外緣剖面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：薄邊風險及替代方案已標記。","instructionEn":"Compare edge sections before and after thinning. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Fragile-edge risk and alternatives are marked.","observation":"薄邊風險及替代方案已標記；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Fragile-edge risk and alternatives are marked; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略倒角會產生外緣崩落。","failureEn":"Ignoring the bevel invites edge chipping.","check":"薄邊風險及替代方案已標記。","checkEn":"Fragile-edge risk and alternatives are marked.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-059-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"薄化可使倒角形成脆弱薄邊。","textEn":"Thinning can leave fragile bevel edges."},{"id":"pk-059-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略倒角會產生外緣崩落；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring the bevel invites edge chipping. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判定邊緣修整需求」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Determine edge-trimming need\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["偏差與補償皆有可追溯紀錄","轉貼前後身分與支承連續","薄邊風險及替代方案已標記"],"optionsEn":["Offset and compensation are traceable","Identity and support persist through remounting","Fragile-edge risk and alternatives are marked"],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄化可使倒角形成脆弱薄邊。本步要確認：薄邊風險及替代方案已標記；常見誤判是：忽略倒角會產生外緣崩落。","explanationEn":"Thinning can leave fragile bevel edges. Verify: Fragile-edge risk and alternatives are marked. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring the bevel invites edge chipping."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-058"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-060","order":8,"sequence":60,"title":"核對吸盤表面","titleEn":"Inspect the grinding chuck","objective":"從表面圖找污染及不平整，並能說明「支承誤差可轉移到厚度分布」。","objectiveEn":"Find contamination and unevenness in chuck maps and explain: Support error transfers into thickness variation.","instruction":"從表面圖找污染及不平整。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：吸盤異常與晶圓位置可對照。","instructionEn":"Find contamination and unevenness in chuck maps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Chuck anomalies map to wafer locations.","observation":"吸盤異常與晶圓位置可對照；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Chuck anomalies map to wafer locations; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"吸盤污點可能被誤認為材料不均。","failureEn":"Chuck dirt can mimic material nonuniformity.","check":"吸盤異常與晶圓位置可對照。","checkEn":"Chuck anomalies map to wafer locations.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-060-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"支承誤差可轉移到厚度分布。","textEn":"Support error transfers into thickness variation."},{"id":"pk-060-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"吸盤污點可能被誤認為材料不均；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Chuck dirt can mimic material nonuniformity. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對吸盤表面」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect the grinding chuck\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["吸盤異常與晶圓位置可對照","精磨預算涵蓋需移除的受損層","所有未決裂損均已隔離"],"optionsEn":["Chuck anomalies map to wafer locations","Finishing allowance covers the damaged layer","All unresolved cracks are quarantined"],"answer":0,"explanation":"支承誤差可轉移到厚度分布。本步要確認：吸盤異常與晶圓位置可對照；常見誤判是：吸盤污點可能被誤認為材料不均。","explanationEn":"Support error transfers into thickness variation. Verify: Chuck anomalies map to wafer locations. A common misinterpretation is: Chuck dirt can mimic material nonuniformity."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-059"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-061","order":9,"sequence":61,"title":"確認真空支承狀態","titleEn":"Confirm vacuum support","objective":"解讀吸附區與洩漏訊號，並能說明「固定不足會允許局部滑動」。","objectiveEn":"Interpret chuck zones and leak signals and explain: Weak retention allows local slip.","instruction":"解讀吸附區與洩漏訊號。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：有效吸附區符合選定支承方案。","instructionEn":"Interpret chuck zones and leak signals. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Active vacuum zones match the support plan.","observation":"有效吸附區符合選定支承方案；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Active vacuum zones match the support plan; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"局部漏氣可形成偏磨。","failureEn":"Local leakage causes uneven grinding.","check":"有效吸附區符合選定支承方案。","checkEn":"Active vacuum zones match the support plan.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-061-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"固定不足會允許局部滑動。","textEn":"Weak retention allows local slip."},{"id":"pk-061-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"局部漏氣可形成偏磨；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Local leakage causes uneven grinding. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「確認真空支承狀態」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Confirm vacuum support\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["終厚與後續損耗均已列出","有效吸附區符合選定支承方案","異常紋理位置可回指工站座標"],"optionsEn":["Final thickness and later losses are listed","Active vacuum zones match the support plan","Abnormal patterns resolve to station coordinates"],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定不足會允許局部滑動。本步要確認：有效吸附區符合選定支承方案；常見誤判是：局部漏氣可形成偏磨。","explanationEn":"Weak retention allows local slip. Verify: Active vacuum zones match the support plan. A common misinterpretation is: Local leakage causes uneven grinding."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-060"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-062","order":10,"sequence":62,"title":"匹配粗磨砂輪","titleEn":"Match the coarse wheel","objective":"比較砂粒及結合劑適用說明，並能說明「去除效率與損傷之間存在取捨」。","objectiveEn":"Compare abrasive and bond applicability and explain: Removal efficiency trades against damage.","instruction":"比較砂粒及結合劑適用說明。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：選輪理由包含材料與損傷限制。","instructionEn":"Compare abrasive and bond applicability. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Selection includes material and damage limits.","observation":"選輪理由包含材料與損傷限制；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Selection includes material and damage limits; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只追求去除率會放大裂損。","failureEn":"Removal-rate-only selection increases damage.","check":"選輪理由包含材料與損傷限制。","checkEn":"Selection includes material and damage limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-062-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"去除效率與損傷之間存在取捨。","textEn":"Removal efficiency trades against damage."},{"id":"pk-062-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只追求去除率會放大裂損；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Removal-rate-only selection increases damage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「匹配粗磨砂輪」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Match the coarse wheel\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["報告標明尺度與評估長度","凸起區沒有未支承空隙","選輪理由包含材料與損傷限制"],"optionsEn":["Reports state scale and evaluation length","Protruding regions have no unsupported gaps","Selection includes material and damage limits"],"answer":2,"explanation":"去除效率與損傷之間存在取捨。本步要確認：選輪理由包含材料與損傷限制；常見誤判是：只追求去除率會放大裂損。","explanationEn":"Removal efficiency trades against damage. Verify: Selection includes material and damage limits. A common misinterpretation is: Removal-rate-only selection increases damage."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-061"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-063","order":11,"sequence":63,"title":"判讀砂輪修整狀態","titleEn":"Assess wheel dressing condition","objective":"比較修整前後負載與表面跡象，並能說明「堵塞砂輪改變切削作用」。","objectiveEn":"Compare load and surface signs around dressing and explain: Loaded wheels change cutting behavior.","instruction":"比較修整前後負載與表面跡象。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：負載異常與輪面狀態被交叉核對。","instructionEn":"Compare load and surface signs around dressing. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Load anomalies are checked against wheel condition.","observation":"負載異常與輪面狀態被交叉核對；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Load anomalies are checked against wheel condition; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"盲目增壓不能修復堵塞砂輪。","failureEn":"More force does not repair a loaded wheel.","check":"負載異常與輪面狀態被交叉核對。","checkEn":"Load anomalies are checked against wheel condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-063-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"堵塞砂輪改變切削作用。","textEn":"Loaded wheels change cutting behavior."},{"id":"pk-063-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"盲目增壓不能修復堵塞砂輪；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"More force does not repair a loaded wheel. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀砂輪修整狀態」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess wheel dressing condition\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["負載異常與輪面狀態被交叉核對","厚度極差採相同有效區域","接觸面疑似顆粒已隔離"],"optionsEn":["Load anomalies are checked against wheel condition","Thickness range uses one defined area","Suspected contact-face particles are isolated"],"answer":0,"explanation":"堵塞砂輪改變切削作用。本步要確認：負載異常與輪面狀態被交叉核對；常見誤判是：盲目增壓不能修復堵塞砂輪。","explanationEn":"Loaded wheels change cutting behavior. Verify: Load anomalies are checked against wheel condition. A common misinterpretation is: More force does not repair a loaded wheel."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-062"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-064","order":12,"sequence":64,"title":"建立粗磨移除預算","titleEn":"Budget coarse-grinding removal","objective":"保留精磨與應力消除餘量，並能說明「各段移除量共同決定終厚」。","objectiveEn":"Reserve fine-grind and stress-relief allowances and explain: Stage removals determine final thickness.","instruction":"保留精磨與應力消除餘量。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：粗磨停點保留足夠後段餘量。","instructionEn":"Reserve fine-grind and stress-relief allowances. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Coarse endpoint preserves finishing allowance.","observation":"粗磨停點保留足夠後段餘量；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Coarse endpoint preserves finishing allowance; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"粗磨過深會失去損傷去除空間。","failureEn":"Excess coarse removal leaves no finishing margin.","check":"粗磨停點保留足夠後段餘量。","checkEn":"Coarse endpoint preserves finishing allowance.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-064-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"各段移除量共同決定終厚。","textEn":"Stage removals determine final thickness."},{"id":"pk-064-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"粗磨過深會失去損傷去除空間；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excess coarse removal leaves no finishing margin. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立粗磨移除預算」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Budget coarse-grinding removal\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["氣泡分布不侵入受力敏感區","粗磨停點保留足夠後段餘量","斜率方向與支承調整假設一致"],"optionsEn":["Bubbles avoid load-sensitive regions","Coarse endpoint preserves finishing allowance","Slope direction matches the support hypothesis"],"answer":1,"explanation":"各段移除量共同決定終厚。本步要確認：粗磨停點保留足夠後段餘量；常見誤判是：粗磨過深會失去損傷去除空間。","explanationEn":"Stage removals determine final thickness. Verify: Coarse endpoint preserves finishing allowance. A common misinterpretation is: Excess coarse removal leaves no finishing margin."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-063"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-065","order":13,"sequence":65,"title":"監看粗磨負載趨勢","titleEn":"Monitor coarse-grind load","objective":"標示負載曲線的突變區，並能說明「負載突變可指向接觸異常」。","objectiveEn":"Mark abrupt changes in load traces and explain: Load jumps can indicate abnormal contact.","instruction":"標示負載曲線的突變區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：突變位置連到輪況或支承檢查。","instructionEn":"Mark abrupt changes in load traces. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Jumps trigger wheel or support checks.","observation":"突變位置連到輪況或支承檢查；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Jumps trigger wheel or support checks; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平均負載會掩蓋短暫衝擊。","failureEn":"Average load hides short impacts.","check":"突變位置連到輪況或支承檢查。","checkEn":"Jumps trigger wheel or support checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-065-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"負載突變可指向接觸異常。","textEn":"Load jumps can indicate abnormal contact."},{"id":"pk-065-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平均負載會掩蓋短暫衝擊；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Average load hides short impacts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「監看粗磨負載趨勢」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Monitor coarse-grind load\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["選定路線不傷害暴露材料","膜邊不超出指定裝夾包絡","突變位置連到輪況或支承檢查"],"optionsEn":["The selected route preserves exposed materials","Tape edges fit the fixture envelope","Jumps trigger wheel or support checks"],"answer":2,"explanation":"負載突變可指向接觸異常。本步要確認：突變位置連到輪況或支承檢查；常見誤判是：平均負載會掩蓋短暫衝擊。","explanationEn":"Load jumps can indicate abnormal contact. Verify: Jumps trigger wheel or support checks. A common misinterpretation is: Average load hides short impacts."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-064"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-066","order":14,"sequence":66,"title":"評估研磨冷卻覆蓋","titleEn":"Assess grinding-coolant coverage","objective":"比較接觸區與沖洗覆蓋，並能說明「冷卻也負責帶走磨屑」。","objectiveEn":"Compare contact and coolant coverage and explain: Coolant also removes grinding debris.","instruction":"比較接觸區與沖洗覆蓋。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：作用區沒有明顯沖洗死角。","instructionEn":"Compare contact and coolant coverage. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The contact zone lacks obvious dead zones.","observation":"作用區沒有明顯沖洗死角；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The contact zone lacks obvious dead zones; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"磨屑堆積可造成刮傷與熱點。","failureEn":"Debris accumulation causes scratches and hot spots.","check":"作用區沒有明顯沖洗死角。","checkEn":"The contact zone lacks obvious dead zones.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-066-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"冷卻也負責帶走磨屑。","textEn":"Coolant also removes grinding debris."},{"id":"pk-066-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"磨屑堆積可造成刮傷與熱點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Debris accumulation causes scratches and hot spots. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估研磨冷卻覆蓋」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess grinding-coolant coverage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["作用區沒有明顯沖洗死角","結論同時引用形貌和強度資料","轉移時沒有無支承狀態"],"optionsEn":["The contact zone lacks obvious dead zones","Conclusions cite shape and strength evidence","Transfers avoid unsupported states"],"answer":0,"explanation":"冷卻也負責帶走磨屑。本步要確認：作用區沒有明顯沖洗死角；常見誤判是：磨屑堆積可造成刮傷與熱點。","explanationEn":"Coolant also removes grinding debris. Verify: The contact zone lacks obvious dead zones. A common misinterpretation is: Debris accumulation causes scratches and hot spots."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-065"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-067","order":15,"sequence":67,"title":"校準在線厚度量測","titleEn":"Calibrate in-process thickness sensing","objective":"以參考片比較量測偏差，並能說明「感測偏移會系統性改變停點」。","objectiveEn":"Compare readings against a reference wafer and explain: Sensor offset shifts the endpoint systematically.","instruction":"以參考片比較量測偏差。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：偏差與補償皆有可追溯紀錄。","instructionEn":"Compare readings against a reference wafer. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Offset and compensation are traceable.","observation":"偏差與補償皆有可追溯紀錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Offset and compensation are traceable; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"誤把感測漂移當去除率變化。","failureEn":"Sensor drift can mimic removal-rate changes.","check":"偏差與補償皆有可追溯紀錄。","checkEn":"Offset and compensation are traceable.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-067-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"感測偏移會系統性改變停點。","textEn":"Sensor offset shifts the endpoint systematically."},{"id":"pk-067-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"誤把感測漂移當去除率變化；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Sensor drift can mimic removal-rate changes. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「校準在線厚度量測」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calibrate in-process thickness sensing\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["薄邊風險及替代方案已標記","偏差與補償皆有可追溯紀錄","邊緣改變未侵入功能區"],"optionsEn":["Fragile-edge risk and alternatives are marked","Offset and compensation are traceable","Edge changes avoid functional regions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測偏移會系統性改變停點。本步要確認：偏差與補償皆有可追溯紀錄；常見誤判是：誤把感測漂移當去除率變化。","explanationEn":"Sensor offset shifts the endpoint systematically. Verify: Offset and compensation are traceable. A common misinterpretation is: Sensor drift can mimic removal-rate changes."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-066"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-068","order":16,"sequence":68,"title":"切換精磨接觸","titleEn":"Transition to fine grinding","objective":"比較粗磨殘痕與精磨目標，並能說明「精磨需減少粗磨造成的損傷」。","objectiveEn":"Compare coarse marks with finishing objectives and explain: Fine grinding reduces coarse-grind damage.","instruction":"比較粗磨殘痕與精磨目標。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：精磨預算涵蓋需移除的受損層。","instructionEn":"Compare coarse marks with finishing objectives. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Finishing allowance covers the damaged layer.","observation":"精磨預算涵蓋需移除的受損層；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Finishing allowance covers the damaged layer; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只求鏡亮可能留下次表面裂紋。","failureEn":"Visual gloss may hide subsurface cracks.","check":"精磨預算涵蓋需移除的受損層。","checkEn":"Finishing allowance covers the damaged layer.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-068-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"精磨需減少粗磨造成的損傷。","textEn":"Fine grinding reduces coarse-grind damage."},{"id":"pk-068-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只求鏡亮可能留下次表面裂紋；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Visual gloss may hide subsurface cracks. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「切換精磨接觸」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Transition to fine grinding\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["兩種指標均有各自驗收依據","吸盤異常與晶圓位置可對照","精磨預算涵蓋需移除的受損層"],"optionsEn":["Both metrics have separate acceptance evidence","Chuck anomalies map to wafer locations","Finishing allowance covers the damaged layer"],"answer":2,"explanation":"精磨需減少粗磨造成的損傷。本步要確認：精磨預算涵蓋需移除的受損層；常見誤判是：只求鏡亮可能留下次表面裂紋。","explanationEn":"Fine grinding reduces coarse-grind damage. Verify: Finishing allowance covers the damaged layer. A common misinterpretation is: Visual gloss may hide subsurface cracks."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-067"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-069","order":17,"sequence":69,"title":"判讀研磨紋方向","titleEn":"Interpret grinding-mark patterns","objective":"追蹤弧紋與設備運動方向，並能說明「表面紋理可指示接觸均勻性」。","objectiveEn":"Relate curved marks to machine motion and explain: Surface patterns indicate contact uniformity.","instruction":"追蹤弧紋與設備運動方向。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常紋理位置可回指工站座標。","instructionEn":"Relate curved marks to machine motion. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Abnormal patterns resolve to station coordinates.","observation":"異常紋理位置可回指工站座標；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Abnormal patterns resolve to station coordinates; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把週期紋當隨機顆粒會誤診。","failureEn":"Periodic marks mistaken for particles mislead diagnosis.","check":"異常紋理位置可回指工站座標。","checkEn":"Abnormal patterns resolve to station coordinates.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-069-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"表面紋理可指示接觸均勻性。","textEn":"Surface patterns indicate contact uniformity."},{"id":"pk-069-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把週期紋當隨機顆粒會誤診；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Periodic marks mistaken for particles mislead diagnosis. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀研磨紋方向」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret grinding-mark patterns\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常紋理位置可回指工站座標","轉貼前後身分與支承連續","有效吸附區符合選定支承方案"],"optionsEn":["Abnormal patterns resolve to station coordinates","Identity and support persist through remounting","Active vacuum zones match the support plan"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面紋理可指示接觸均勻性。本步要確認：異常紋理位置可回指工站座標；常見誤判是：把週期紋當隨機顆粒會誤診。","explanationEn":"Surface patterns indicate contact uniformity. Verify: Abnormal patterns resolve to station coordinates. A common misinterpretation is: Periodic marks mistaken for particles mislead diagnosis."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-068"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-070","order":18,"sequence":70,"title":"量測背面粗糙度","titleEn":"Measure backside roughness","objective":"區分粗糙度與整片形狀，並能說明「短尺度紋理與翹曲是不同量」。","objectiveEn":"Separate roughness from wafer-scale shape and explain: Texture and warpage are different quantities.","instruction":"區分粗糙度與整片形狀。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：報告標明尺度與評估長度。","instructionEn":"Separate roughness from wafer-scale shape. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Reports state scale and evaluation length.","observation":"報告標明尺度與評估長度；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Reports state scale and evaluation length; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單一粗糙度數值不能描述翹曲。","failureEn":"One roughness value cannot describe warpage.","check":"報告標明尺度與評估長度。","checkEn":"Reports state scale and evaluation length.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-070-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"短尺度紋理與翹曲是不同量。","textEn":"Texture and warpage are different quantities."},{"id":"pk-070-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單一粗糙度數值不能描述翹曲；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One roughness value cannot describe warpage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測背面粗糙度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure backside roughness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["選輪理由包含材料與損傷限制","報告標明尺度與評估長度","所有未決裂損均已隔離"],"optionsEn":["Selection includes material and damage limits","Reports state scale and evaluation length","All unresolved cracks are quarantined"],"answer":1,"explanation":"短尺度紋理與翹曲是不同量。本步要確認：報告標明尺度與評估長度；常見誤判是：單一粗糙度數值不能描述翹曲。","explanationEn":"Texture and warpage are different quantities. Verify: Reports state scale and evaluation length. A common misinterpretation is: One roughness value cannot describe warpage."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-069"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-071","order":19,"sequence":71,"title":"計算總厚度變異","titleEn":"Calculate total thickness variation","objective":"從厚度地圖取最大與最小值，並能說明「TTV 衡量厚度而非表面位移」。","objectiveEn":"Extract maximum and minimum thickness and explain: TTV measures thickness, not surface displacement.","instruction":"從厚度地圖取最大與最小值。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：厚度極差採相同有效區域。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Extract maximum and minimum thickness. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Thickness range uses one defined area. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"厚度極差採相同有效區域；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Thickness range uses one defined area; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"混入膜厚會錯估矽厚變異。","failureEn":"Including tape thickness misstates silicon variation.","check":"厚度極差採相同有效區域。","checkEn":"Thickness range uses one defined area.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-071-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"TTV 衡量厚度而非表面位移。","textEn":"TTV measures thickness, not surface displacement."},{"id":"pk-071-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"混入膜厚會錯估矽厚變異；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Including tape thickness misstates silicon variation. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-071-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設五點厚度 48、50、51、49、52 µm，TTV=max−min=4 µm、平均 50 µm。TTV 不是粗糙度，也不等於全片 bow；量測點稀疏可能漏掉局部極值。","textEn":"For hypothetical thicknesses 48, 50, 51, 49 and 52 µm, TTV=max−min=4 µm and mean=50 µm. TTV differs from roughness and bow, and sparse sampling can miss local extrema."},{"id":"pk-071-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"保留正背面基準、邊緣排除區和量測網格。用同一網格比較研磨前後，避免以抽樣位置改變假裝均勻度改善。","textEn":"Retain front/back references, edge exclusion and measurement grid. Compare before and after on the same grid so sampling changes do not masquerade as uniformity improvement."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「計算總厚度變異」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calculate total thickness variation\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["終厚與後續損耗均已列出","負載異常與輪面狀態被交叉核對","厚度極差採相同有效區域"],"optionsEn":["Final thickness and later losses are listed","Load anomalies are checked against wheel condition","Thickness range uses one defined area"],"answer":2,"explanation":"TTV 衡量厚度而非表面位移。本步要確認：厚度極差採相同有效區域；常見誤判是：混入膜厚會錯估矽厚變異。","explanationEn":"TTV measures thickness, not surface displacement. Verify: Thickness range uses one defined area. A common misinterpretation is: Including tape thickness misstates silicon variation."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-070"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-072","order":20,"sequence":72,"title":"辨識厚度楔形","titleEn":"Identify wafer wedge","objective":"對厚度圖擬合方向性斜率，並能說明「系統性楔形不同於局部缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Fit directional slopes to thickness maps and explain: Systematic wedge differs from local defects.","instruction":"對厚度圖擬合方向性斜率。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：斜率方向與支承調整假設一致。","instructionEn":"Fit directional slopes to thickness maps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Slope direction matches the support hypothesis.","observation":"斜率方向與支承調整假設一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Slope direction matches the support hypothesis; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看TTV無法區分楔形與坑點。","failureEn":"TTV alone cannot separate wedge from pits.","check":"斜率方向與支承調整假設一致。","checkEn":"Slope direction matches the support hypothesis.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-072-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"系統性楔形不同於局部缺陷。","textEn":"Systematic wedge differs from local defects."},{"id":"pk-072-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看TTV無法區分楔形與坑點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"TTV alone cannot separate wedge from pits. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識厚度楔形」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify wafer wedge\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["斜率方向與支承調整假設一致","凸起區沒有未支承空隙","粗磨停點保留足夠後段餘量"],"optionsEn":["Slope direction matches the support hypothesis","Protruding regions have no unsupported gaps","Coarse endpoint preserves finishing allowance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"系統性楔形不同於局部缺陷。本步要確認：斜率方向與支承調整假設一致；常見誤判是：只看TTV無法區分楔形與坑點。","explanationEn":"Systematic wedge differs from local defects. Verify: Slope direction matches the support hypothesis. A common misinterpretation is: TTV alone cannot separate wedge from pits."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-071"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-073","order":21,"sequence":73,"title":"選擇應力消除路線","titleEn":"Select stress-relief route","objective":"比較乾式拋光與乾蝕刻目的，並能說明「不同路線具有不同材料相容性」。","objectiveEn":"Compare dry-polishing and dry-etch objectives and explain: Routes differ in material compatibility.","instruction":"比較乾式拋光與乾蝕刻目的。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：選定路線不傷害暴露材料。","instructionEn":"Compare dry-polishing and dry-etch objectives. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The selected route preserves exposed materials.","observation":"選定路線不傷害暴露材料；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The selected route preserves exposed materials; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把所有材料套同一路線會失效。","failureEn":"One route does not suit every material.","check":"選定路線不傷害暴露材料。","checkEn":"The selected route preserves exposed materials.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-073-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同路線具有不同材料相容性。","textEn":"Routes differ in material compatibility."},{"id":"pk-073-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把所有材料套同一路線會失效；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One route does not suit every material. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇應力消除路線」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select stress-relief route\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["突變位置連到輪況或支承檢查","選定路線不傷害暴露材料","接觸面疑似顆粒已隔離"],"optionsEn":["Jumps trigger wheel or support checks","The selected route preserves exposed materials","Suspected contact-face particles are isolated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同路線具有不同材料相容性。本步要確認：選定路線不傷害暴露材料；常見誤判是：把所有材料套同一路線會失效。","explanationEn":"Routes differ in material compatibility. Verify: The selected route preserves exposed materials. A common misinterpretation is: One route does not suit every material."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-072"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-074","order":22,"sequence":74,"title":"評估乾式拋光損傷去除","titleEn":"Assess dry-polish damage removal","objective":"比較處理前後表面與強度資料，並能說明「表面改善需與機械證據聯讀」。","objectiveEn":"Compare surface and strength before and after polishing and explain: Surface improvement needs mechanical evidence.","instruction":"比較處理前後表面與強度資料。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：結論同時引用形貌和強度資料。","instructionEn":"Compare surface and strength before and after polishing. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Conclusions cite shape and strength evidence.","observation":"結論同時引用形貌和強度資料；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Conclusions cite shape and strength evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"僅憑亮度不能證明強度改善。","failureEn":"Brightness alone cannot prove stronger dies.","check":"結論同時引用形貌和強度資料。","checkEn":"Conclusions cite shape and strength evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-074-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"表面改善需與機械證據聯讀。","textEn":"Surface improvement needs mechanical evidence."},{"id":"pk-074-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"僅憑亮度不能證明強度改善；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Brightness alone cannot prove stronger dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估乾式拋光損傷去除」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess dry-polish damage removal\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["氣泡分布不侵入受力敏感區","作用區沒有明顯沖洗死角","結論同時引用形貌和強度資料"],"optionsEn":["Bubbles avoid load-sensitive regions","The contact zone lacks obvious dead zones","Conclusions cite shape and strength evidence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面改善需與機械證據聯讀。本步要確認：結論同時引用形貌和強度資料；常見誤判是：僅憑亮度不能證明強度改善。","explanationEn":"Surface improvement needs mechanical evidence. Verify: Conclusions cite shape and strength evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Brightness alone cannot prove stronger dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-073"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-075","order":23,"sequence":75,"title":"評估乾蝕刻邊緣效果","titleEn":"Assess dry-etch edge effects","objective":"比較邊緣損傷與蝕刻後輪廓，並能說明「材料移除可能改變邊緣幾何」。","objectiveEn":"Compare edge damage and etched contours and explain: Removal can change edge geometry.","instruction":"比較邊緣損傷與蝕刻後輪廓。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：邊緣改變未侵入功能區。","instructionEn":"Compare edge damage and etched contours. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Edge changes avoid functional regions.","observation":"邊緣改變未侵入功能區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Edge changes avoid functional regions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過度移除會縮減結構裕量。","failureEn":"Excess removal reduces structural margin.","check":"邊緣改變未侵入功能區。","checkEn":"Edge changes avoid functional regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-075-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"材料移除可能改變邊緣幾何。","textEn":"Removal can change edge geometry."},{"id":"pk-075-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過度移除會縮減結構裕量；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excess removal reduces structural margin. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估乾蝕刻邊緣效果」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess dry-etch edge effects\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["邊緣改變未侵入功能區","膜邊不超出指定裝夾包絡","偏差與補償皆有可追溯紀錄"],"optionsEn":["Edge changes avoid functional regions","Tape edges fit the fixture envelope","Offset and compensation are traceable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料移除可能改變邊緣幾何。本步要確認：邊緣改變未侵入功能區；常見誤判是：過度移除會縮減結構裕量。","explanationEn":"Removal can change edge geometry. Verify: Edge changes avoid functional regions. A common misinterpretation is: Excess removal reduces structural margin."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-074"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-076","order":24,"sequence":76,"title":"核對薄化後彎曲與強度","titleEn":"Review post-thinning bow and strength","objective":"將曲率與破壞試驗分開解讀，並能說明「低翹曲不等於高破裂強度」。","objectiveEn":"Interpret curvature and fracture tests separately and explain: Low bow does not equal high fracture strength.","instruction":"將曲率與破壞試驗分開解讀。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：兩種指標均有各自驗收依據。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Interpret curvature and fracture tests separately. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Both metrics have separate acceptance evidence. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"兩種指標均有各自驗收依據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Both metrics have separate acceptance evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"以平坦度替代強度會漏掉裂紋。","failureEn":"Flatness cannot replace crack-strength assessment.","check":"兩種指標均有各自驗收依據。","checkEn":"Both metrics have separate acceptance evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-076-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"低翹曲不等於高破裂強度。","textEn":"Low bow does not equal high fracture strength."},{"id":"pk-076-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"以平坦度替代強度會漏掉裂紋；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Flatness cannot replace crack-strength assessment. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-076-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"薄板彎曲剛性在同材料線彈性模型中約隨厚度 t³。厚度從 100 降至 50 µm，剛性約成原來 1/8；這不表示破壞強度必定成 1/8，缺陷與載荷模式也重要。","textEn":"In a same-material linear-elastic plate model, bending stiffness scales approximately with t³. Thinning 100 to 50 µm reduces stiffness to about 1/8, but not necessarily strength to 1/8; flaws and loading matter."},{"id":"pk-076-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"比較搬運時的支承跨距、吸附點與邊緣缺口。只以薄化厚度達標放行，會漏掉實際轉移時的彎曲與崩裂風險。","textEn":"Compare support spans, suction points and edge notches during handling. Thickness-only acceptance misses bending and chipping during actual transfer."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對薄化後彎曲與強度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review post-thinning bow and strength\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["精磨預算涵蓋需移除的受損層","兩種指標均有各自驗收依據","轉移時沒有無支承狀態"],"optionsEn":["Finishing allowance covers the damaged layer","Both metrics have separate acceptance evidence","Transfers avoid unsupported states"],"answer":1,"explanation":"低翹曲不等於高破裂強度。本步要確認：兩種指標均有各自驗收依據；常見誤判是：以平坦度替代強度會漏掉裂紋。","explanationEn":"Low bow does not equal high fracture strength. Verify: Both metrics have separate acceptance evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Flatness cannot replace crack-strength assessment."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-075"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-077","order":25,"sequence":77,"title":"規劃清洗乾燥與轉貼","titleEn":"Plan cleaning, drying and remounting","objective":"追蹤磨屑去除及全程支承，並能說明「薄片搬運風險延續至下站」。","objectiveEn":"Track debris removal and continuous support and explain: Thin-wafer risk continues during transfer.","instruction":"追蹤磨屑去除及全程支承。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：轉貼前後身分與支承連續。","instructionEn":"Track debris removal and continuous support. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Identity and support persist through remounting.","observation":"轉貼前後身分與支承連續；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Identity and support persist through remounting; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"乾燥水痕可能污染後續接合。","failureEn":"Drying residues can contaminate later bonding.","check":"轉貼前後身分與支承連續。","checkEn":"Identity and support persist through remounting.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-077-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"薄片搬運風險延續至下站。","textEn":"Thin-wafer risk continues during transfer."},{"id":"pk-077-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"乾燥水痕可能污染後續接合；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Drying residues can contaminate later bonding. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「規劃清洗乾燥與轉貼」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Plan cleaning, drying and remounting\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["薄邊風險及替代方案已標記","異常紋理位置可回指工站座標","轉貼前後身分與支承連續"],"optionsEn":["Fragile-edge risk and alternatives are marked","Abnormal patterns resolve to station coordinates","Identity and support persist through remounting"],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄片搬運風險延續至下站。本步要確認：轉貼前後身分與支承連續；常見誤判是：乾燥水痕可能污染後續接合。","explanationEn":"Thin-wafer risk continues during transfer. Verify: Identity and support persist through remounting. A common misinterpretation is: Drying residues can contaminate later bonding."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-076"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-078","order":26,"sequence":78,"title":"放行薄化晶圓","titleEn":"Release thinned wafers","objective":"整合終厚、TTV、邊緣與支承紀錄，並能說明「放行需同時滿足幾何與完整性」。","objectiveEn":"Combine thickness, TTV, edge and support records and explain: Release needs geometry and integrity.","instruction":"整合終厚、TTV、邊緣與支承紀錄。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：所有未決裂損均已隔離。","instructionEn":"Combine thickness, TTV, edge and support records. Check evidence you create or obtain against: All unresolved cracks are quarantined.","observation":"所有未決裂損均已隔離；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"All unresolved cracks are quarantined; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看終厚合格會漏掉受損晶圓。","failureEn":"Thickness alone can release damaged wafers.","check":"所有未決裂損均已隔離。","checkEn":"All unresolved cracks are quarantined.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-078-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"放行需同時滿足幾何與完整性。","textEn":"Release needs geometry and integrity."},{"id":"pk-078-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看終厚合格會漏掉受損晶圓；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Thickness alone can release damaged wafers. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「放行薄化晶圓」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release thinned wafers\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["所有未決裂損均已隔離","吸盤異常與晶圓位置可對照","報告標明尺度與評估長度"],"optionsEn":["All unresolved cracks are quarantined","Chuck anomalies map to wafer locations","Reports state scale and evaluation length"],"answer":0,"explanation":"放行需同時滿足幾何與完整性。本步要確認：所有未決裂損均已隔離；常見誤判是：只看終厚合格會漏掉受損晶圓。","explanationEn":"Release needs geometry and integrity. Verify: All unresolved cracks are quarantined. A common misinterpretation is: Thickness alone can release damaged wafers."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-thinning","pk-disco-polishing","pk-disco-grinding","pk-disco-dbg","pk-evg-tbdb"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-077"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafer-tweezers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓夾持工具的接觸端；這不是自動晶圓搬運設備，也未展示本步清洗或熱處理。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the contact end of wafer tweezers; this is not an automated wafer handler and does not show this step’s cleaning or thermal treatment.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"晶圓切割、分離與切後清潔","titleEn":"Wafer dicing, singulation and cleaning","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查晶圓切割、分離與切後清潔的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for wafer dicing, singulation and cleaning. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"以先磨後切的刀輪路線為主；雷射與電漿是替代方法，不是連續必經站。","routeEn":"Primarily grind-before-blade-dice; laser and plasma are alternatives, not mandatory serial stations.","sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-079","order":1,"sequence":79,"title":"選擇晶粒分離分支","titleEn":"Select the singulation branch","objective":"按材料與街道比較刀輪、雷射及電漿，並能說明「不同分離方式不可直接共用配方」。","objectiveEn":"Compare blade, laser and plasma by materials and streets and explain: Singulation methods cannot share one recipe.","instruction":"按材料與街道比較刀輪、雷射及電漿。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：選擇有材料與損傷理由。","instructionEn":"Compare blade, laser and plasma by materials and streets. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Selection states material and damage reasons.","observation":"選擇有材料與損傷理由；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Selection states material and damage reasons; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只按晶圓厚度選法會漏掉膜層。","failureEn":"Thickness-only selection ignores film stacks.","check":"選擇有材料與損傷理由。","checkEn":"Selection states material and damage reasons.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-079-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同分離方式不可直接共用配方。","textEn":"Singulation methods cannot share one recipe."},{"id":"pk-079-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只按晶圓厚度選法會漏掉膜層；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Thickness-only selection ignores film stacks. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇晶粒分離分支」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select the singulation branch\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["兩組街道均有獨立核對","熱影響與殘留物分開記錄","選擇有材料與損傷理由"],"optionsEn":["Both street families are independently checked","Thermal effects and residues are recorded separately","Selection states material and damage reasons"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同分離方式不可直接共用配方。本步要確認：選擇有材料與損傷理由；常見誤判是：只按晶圓厚度選法會漏掉膜層。","explanationEn":"Singulation methods cannot share one recipe. Verify: Selection states material and damage reasons. A common misinterpretation is: Thickness-only selection ignores film stacks."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-078"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-080","order":2,"sequence":80,"title":"配對切割膠膜","titleEn":"Match dicing tape","objective":"比較黏著保持與後續拾取需求，並能說明「切割固定與拾取釋放需要平衡」。","objectiveEn":"Compare retention and later pickup needs and explain: Cut retention trades against pickup release.","instruction":"比較黏著保持與後續拾取需求。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：兩個階段的需求皆被滿足。","instructionEn":"Compare retention and later pickup needs. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Both stages' needs are addressed.","observation":"兩個階段的需求皆被滿足；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Both stages' needs are addressed; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過黏可能在拾取時拉裂薄晶粒。","failureEn":"Excess adhesion can crack thin dies during pickup.","check":"兩個階段的需求皆被滿足。","checkEn":"Both stages' needs are addressed.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-080-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"切割固定與拾取釋放需要平衡。","textEn":"Cut retention trades against pickup release."},{"id":"pk-080-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過黏可能在拾取時拉裂薄晶粒；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excess adhesion can crack thin dies during pickup. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「配對切割膠膜」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Match dicing tape\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["兩個階段的需求皆被滿足","剖面標示切穿與保護界線","開口只覆蓋核准分離區"],"optionsEn":["Both stages' needs are addressed","Sections show cut-through and protection boundaries","Openings cover approved separation regions only"],"answer":0,"explanation":"切割固定與拾取釋放需要平衡。本步要確認：兩個階段的需求皆被滿足；常見誤判是：過黏可能在拾取時拉裂薄晶粒。","explanationEn":"Cut retention trades against pickup release. Verify: Both stages' needs are addressed. A common misinterpretation is: Excess adhesion can crack thin dies during pickup."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-079"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-081","order":3,"sequence":81,"title":"檢查切割膜貼合","titleEn":"Inspect dicing-tape lamination","objective":"標記氣泡、皺折與框架偏斜，並能說明「支承不均使刀路深度失準」。","objectiveEn":"Mark bubbles, wrinkles and frame skew and explain: Uneven support distorts effective cut depth.","instruction":"標記氣泡、皺折與框架偏斜。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：刀路下方支承無未解決異常。","instructionEn":"Mark bubbles, wrinkles and frame skew. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Support under cut paths has no unresolved defects.","observation":"刀路下方支承無未解決異常；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Support under cut paths has no unresolved defects; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"膜皺折可能造成未切透。","failureEn":"Wrinkles can leave incomplete cuts.","check":"刀路下方支承無未解決異常。","checkEn":"Support under cut paths has no unresolved defects.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-081-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"支承不均使刀路深度失準。","textEn":"Uneven support distorts effective cut depth."},{"id":"pk-081-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"膜皺折可能造成未切透；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Wrinkles can leave incomplete cuts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查切割膜貼合」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect dicing-tape lamination\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["殘屑下降且未移入焊墊區","刀路下方支承無未解決異常","入刀與出刀處均無死角"],"optionsEn":["Debris decreases without entering pad areas","Support under cut paths has no unresolved defects","Entry and exit have no uncovered zones"],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承不均使刀路深度失準。本步要確認：刀路下方支承無未解決異常；常見誤判是：膜皺折可能造成未切透。","explanationEn":"Uneven support distorts effective cut depth. Verify: Support under cut paths has no unresolved defects. A common misinterpretation is: Wrinkles can leave incomplete cuts."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-080"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-082","order":4,"sequence":82,"title":"核對晶圓框架定位","titleEn":"Verify wafer-frame orientation","objective":"把框架鍵位連到地圖方向，並能說明「框架方向是挑晶座標的一環」。","objectiveEn":"Link frame keys to wafer-map orientation and explain: Frame orientation participates in pickup coordinates.","instruction":"把框架鍵位連到地圖方向。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：框架與地圖能一一映射。","instructionEn":"Link frame keys to wafer-map orientation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Frame and map coordinates map consistently.","observation":"框架與地圖能一一映射；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Frame and map coordinates map consistently; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"框架翻轉未記錄會錯挑晶粒。","failureEn":"Unrecorded frame reversal causes wrong-die pickup.","check":"框架與地圖能一一映射。","checkEn":"Frame and map coordinates map consistently.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-082-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"框架方向是挑晶座標的一環。","textEn":"Frame orientation participates in pickup coordinates."},{"id":"pk-082-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"框架翻轉未記錄會錯挑晶粒；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Unrecorded frame reversal causes wrong-die pickup. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對晶圓框架定位」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify wafer-frame orientation\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["電性控制與材料相容性分開檢核","疑似殘留有後續確認方法","框架與地圖能一一映射"],"optionsEn":["Electrical control and material compatibility are checked separately","Suspected residues have follow-up checks","Frame and map coordinates map consistently"],"answer":2,"explanation":"框架方向是挑晶座標的一環。本步要確認：框架與地圖能一一映射；常見誤判是：框架翻轉未記錄會錯挑晶粒。","explanationEn":"Frame orientation participates in pickup coordinates. Verify: Frame and map coordinates map consistently. A common misinterpretation is: Unrecorded frame reversal causes wrong-die pickup."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-081"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-083","order":5,"sequence":83,"title":"計算刀口安全包絡","titleEn":"Calculate the blade-clearance envelope","objective":"疊加刀寬、偏移與崩裂預留區，並能說明「切割道需容納多個誤差來源」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay kerf, offset and chipping allowance and explain: Streets accommodate multiple errors.","instruction":"疊加刀寬、偏移與崩裂預留區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：包絡不跨入有效晶粒區。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Overlay kerf, offset and chipping allowance. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The envelope avoids active die regions. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"包絡不跨入有效晶粒區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The envelope avoids active die regions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只比較刀寬與街寬會低估風險。","failureEn":"Blade-width-only checks underestimate risk.","check":"包絡不跨入有效晶粒區。","checkEn":"The envelope avoids active die regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-083-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"切割道需容納多個誤差來源。","textEn":"Streets accommodate multiple errors."},{"id":"pk-083-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只比較刀寬與街寬會低估風險；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Blade-width-only checks underestimate risk. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-083-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"教學街道寬 80 µm、刀口 30 µm，理想中心切割每側剩 25 µm；若定位偏差 8 µm、崩裂包絡 10 µm，同側可用餘裕只剩 7 µm。","textEn":"For hypothetical street width 80 µm and kerf 30 µm, a centered cut leaves 25 µm each side. An 8 µm position error and 10 µm chipping envelope leave only 7 µm on one side."},{"id":"pk-083-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"分開刀口、定位、崩裂與封裝保護區；不同材料堆疊須檢查金屬拖曳和界面剝離，不能僅用裸矽刀口尺寸判斷。","textEn":"Separate kerf, positioning, chipping and protected regions; heterogeneous stacks require checks for metal smearing and delamination rather than bare-silicon kerf alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「計算刀口安全包絡」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calculate the blade-clearance envelope\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["包絡不跨入有效晶粒區","實測切口落在核准包絡內","所選釋黏方法與材料相符"],"optionsEn":["The envelope avoids active die regions","Measured kerf stays within the approved envelope","Release method matches the tape"],"answer":0,"explanation":"切割道需容納多個誤差來源。本步要確認：包絡不跨入有效晶粒區；常見誤判是：只比較刀寬與街寬會低估風險。","explanationEn":"Streets accommodate multiple errors. Verify: The envelope avoids active die regions. A common misinterpretation is: Blade-width-only checks underestimate risk."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-082"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-084","order":6,"sequence":84,"title":"檢查刀片材料匹配","titleEn":"Check blade-material compatibility","objective":"對照刀片用途與街道材料，並能說明「刀片適用性受材料堆疊影響」。","objectiveEn":"Match blade applicability to street materials and explain: Blade suitability depends on the material stack.","instruction":"對照刀片用途與街道材料。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：矽與金屬跨層皆有考慮。","instructionEn":"Match blade applicability to street materials. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Both silicon and crossing metal are considered.","observation":"矽與金屬跨層皆有考慮；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Both silicon and crossing metal are considered; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"金屬堵刀會改變切削品質。","failureEn":"Metal loading changes cutting quality.","check":"矽與金屬跨層皆有考慮。","checkEn":"Both silicon and crossing metal are considered.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-084-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"刀片適用性受材料堆疊影響。","textEn":"Blade suitability depends on the material stack."},{"id":"pk-084-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"金屬堵刀會改變切削品質；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Metal loading changes cutting quality. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查刀片材料匹配」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check blade-material compatibility\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["間隙增加且晶粒姿態可追溯","矽與金屬跨層皆有考慮","各位置寬度與尺度有紀錄"],"optionsEn":["Gaps increase while die poses remain traceable","Both silicon and crossing metal are considered","Widths and scales are recorded by position"],"answer":1,"explanation":"刀片適用性受材料堆疊影響。本步要確認：矽與金屬跨層皆有考慮；常見誤判是：金屬堵刀會改變切削品質。","explanationEn":"Blade suitability depends on the material stack. Verify: Both silicon and crossing metal are considered. A common misinterpretation is: Metal loading changes cutting quality."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-083"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-085","order":7,"sequence":85,"title":"判讀刀片磨耗","titleEn":"Assess blade wear","objective":"比較輪徑、切口與負載趨勢，並能說明「磨耗可改變有效切深及刀口」。","objectiveEn":"Compare diameter, kerf and load trends and explain: Wear changes effective depth and kerf.","instruction":"比較輪徑、切口與負載趨勢。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：磨耗訊號與切深補償一致。","instructionEn":"Compare diameter, kerf and load trends. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Wear indicators match depth compensation.","observation":"磨耗訊號與切深補償一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Wear indicators match depth compensation; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略輪徑變化會殘留底部連接。","failureEn":"Ignoring diameter loss leaves bottom bridges.","check":"磨耗訊號與切深補償一致。","checkEn":"Wear indicators match depth compensation.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-085-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"磨耗可改變有效切深及刀口。","textEn":"Wear changes effective depth and kerf."},{"id":"pk-085-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略輪徑變化會殘留底部連接；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring diameter loss leaves bottom bridges. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀刀片磨耗」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess blade wear\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["侵入量按正確邊界判讀","參考點殘差符合教學圖面要求","磨耗訊號與切深補償一致"],"optionsEn":["Intrusion is measured from the correct boundary","Reference residuals meet exercise requirements","Wear indicators match depth compensation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"磨耗可改變有效切深及刀口。本步要確認：磨耗訊號與切深補償一致；常見誤判是：忽略輪徑變化會殘留底部連接。","explanationEn":"Wear changes effective depth and kerf. Verify: Wear indicators match depth compensation. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring diameter loss leaves bottom bridges."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-084"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-086","order":8,"sequence":86,"title":"檢查主軸與刀片跳動","titleEn":"Inspect spindle and blade runout","objective":"區分週期寬切與隨機崩裂，並能說明「機械跳動造成規律性偏差」。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish periodic widening from random chipping and explain: Runout creates systematic variation.","instruction":"區分週期寬切與隨機崩裂。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常週期與旋轉相關性有記錄。","instructionEn":"Distinguish periodic widening from random chipping. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Periodic anomalies are compared with rotation.","observation":"異常週期與旋轉相關性有記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Periodic anomalies are compared with rotation; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把跳動當材料脆性會錯誤換材。","failureEn":"Runout mistaken for brittleness misguides material changes.","check":"異常週期與旋轉相關性有記錄。","checkEn":"Periodic anomalies are compared with rotation.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-086-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"機械跳動造成規律性偏差。","textEn":"Runout creates systematic variation."},{"id":"pk-086-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把跳動當材料脆性會錯誤換材；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Runout mistaken for brittleness misguides material changes. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查主軸與刀片跳動」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect spindle and blade runout\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常週期與旋轉相關性有記錄","背面檢查沒有被正面AOI取代","每顆晶粒都有可選或隔離狀態"],"optionsEn":["Periodic anomalies are compared with rotation","Backside inspection is not replaced by front AOI","Every die has pickable or quarantine status"],"answer":0,"explanation":"機械跳動造成規律性偏差。本步要確認：異常週期與旋轉相關性有記錄；常見誤判是：把跳動當材料脆性會錯誤換材。","explanationEn":"Runout creates systematic variation. Verify: Periodic anomalies are compared with rotation. A common misinterpretation is: Runout mistaken for brittleness misguides material changes."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-085"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-087","order":9,"sequence":87,"title":"建立雙軸街道座標","titleEn":"Define two-axis street coordinates","objective":"分別對齊兩組垂直街道，並能說明「一軸對準不保證另一軸正確」。","objectiveEn":"Align both orthogonal street families and explain: One aligned axis does not validate the other.","instruction":"分別對齊兩組垂直街道。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：兩組街道均有獨立核對。","instructionEn":"Align both orthogonal street families. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Both street families are independently checked.","observation":"兩組街道均有獨立核對；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Both street families are independently checked; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只校正第一方向會留下旋轉誤差。","failureEn":"One-direction calibration leaves rotational error.","check":"兩組街道均有獨立核對。","checkEn":"Both street families are independently checked.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-087-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"一軸對準不保證另一軸正確。","textEn":"One aligned axis does not validate the other."},{"id":"pk-087-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只校正第一方向會留下旋轉誤差；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One-direction calibration leaves rotational error. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立雙軸街道座標」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Define two-axis street coordinates\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["選擇有材料與損傷理由","兩組街道均有獨立核對","角點完整性按獨立區域評估"],"optionsEn":["Selection states material and damage reasons","Both street families are independently checked","Corner integrity is assessed separately"],"answer":1,"explanation":"一軸對準不保證另一軸正確。本步要確認：兩組街道均有獨立核對；常見誤判是：只校正第一方向會留下旋轉誤差。","explanationEn":"One aligned axis does not validate the other. Verify: Both street families are independently checked. A common misinterpretation is: One-direction calibration leaves rotational error."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-086"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-088","order":10,"sequence":88,"title":"校準刀片高度基準","titleEn":"Calibrate blade-height reference","objective":"比較刀底、晶圓底與膠膜面，並能說明「切透晶圓不等於切透膠膜」。","objectiveEn":"Compare blade bottom, wafer bottom and tape plane and explain: Cutting through wafer differs from cutting through tape.","instruction":"比較刀底、晶圓底與膠膜面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：剖面標示切穿與保護界線。","instructionEn":"Compare blade bottom, wafer bottom and tape plane. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Sections show cut-through and protection boundaries.","observation":"剖面標示切穿與保護界線；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Sections show cut-through and protection boundaries; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"基準錯置會割破支承膜。","failureEn":"Wrong referencing cuts the support tape.","check":"剖面標示切穿與保護界線。","checkEn":"Sections show cut-through and protection boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-088-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"切透晶圓不等於切透膠膜。","textEn":"Cutting through wafer differs from cutting through tape."},{"id":"pk-088-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"基準錯置會割破支承膜；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Wrong referencing cuts the support tape. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「校準刀片高度基準」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calibrate blade-height reference\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["缺陷分類保留層別與界面","兩個階段的需求皆被滿足","剖面標示切穿與保護界線"],"optionsEn":["Classification records layer and interface","Both stages' needs are addressed","Sections show cut-through and protection boundaries"],"answer":2,"explanation":"切透晶圓不等於切透膠膜。本步要確認：剖面標示切穿與保護界線；常見誤判是：基準錯置會割破支承膜。","explanationEn":"Cutting through wafer differs from cutting through tape. Verify: Sections show cut-through and protection boundaries. A common misinterpretation is: Wrong referencing cuts the support tape."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-087"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-089","order":11,"sequence":89,"title":"評估冷卻水覆蓋","titleEn":"Assess dicing-water coverage","objective":"標記刀口入口出口的沖洗區，並能說明「冷卻與排屑共同影響切口」。","objectiveEn":"Mark coolant coverage around blade entry and exit and explain: Cooling and debris flushing affect kerf quality.","instruction":"標記刀口入口出口的沖洗區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：入刀與出刀處均無死角。","instructionEn":"Mark coolant coverage around blade entry and exit. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Entry and exit have no uncovered zones.","observation":"入刀與出刀處均無死角；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Entry and exit have no uncovered zones; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"出口積屑可加劇背崩。","failureEn":"Exit debris can worsen backside chipping.","check":"入刀與出刀處均無死角。","checkEn":"Entry and exit have no uncovered zones.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-089-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"冷卻與排屑共同影響切口。","textEn":"Cooling and debris flushing affect kerf quality."},{"id":"pk-089-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"出口積屑可加劇背崩；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Exit debris can worsen backside chipping. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估冷卻水覆蓋」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess dicing-water coverage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["入刀與出刀處均無死角","熱影響與殘留物分開記錄","刀路下方支承無未解決異常"],"optionsEn":["Entry and exit have no uncovered zones","Thermal effects and residues are recorded separately","Support under cut paths has no unresolved defects"],"answer":0,"explanation":"冷卻與排屑共同影響切口。本步要確認：入刀與出刀處均無死角；常見誤判是：出口積屑可加劇背崩。","explanationEn":"Cooling and debris flushing affect kerf quality. Verify: Entry and exit have no uncovered zones. A common misinterpretation is: Exit debris can worsen backside chipping."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-088"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-090","order":12,"sequence":90,"title":"檢查切割水電性管理","titleEn":"Review dicing-water electrical control","objective":"辨識水路及靜電敏感介面，並能說明「水質及帶電行為都需管理」。","objectiveEn":"Identify water paths and ESD-sensitive interfaces and explain: Water chemistry and charging need control.","instruction":"辨識水路及靜電敏感介面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：電性控制與材料相容性分開檢核。","instructionEn":"Identify water paths and ESD-sensitive interfaces. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Electrical control and material compatibility are checked separately.","observation":"電性控制與材料相容性分開檢核；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Electrical control and material compatibility are checked separately; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只追求高純度可能忽略帶電風險。","failureEn":"Purity alone can overlook charging risk.","check":"電性控制與材料相容性分開檢核。","checkEn":"Electrical control and material compatibility are checked separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-090-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"水質及帶電行為都需管理。","textEn":"Water chemistry and charging need control."},{"id":"pk-090-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只追求高純度可能忽略帶電風險；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Purity alone can overlook charging risk. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查切割水電性管理」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review dicing-water electrical control\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["框架與地圖能一一映射","電性控制與材料相容性分開檢核","開口只覆蓋核准分離區"],"optionsEn":["Frame and map coordinates map consistently","Electrical control and material compatibility are checked separately","Openings cover approved separation regions only"],"answer":1,"explanation":"水質及帶電行為都需管理。本步要確認：電性控制與材料相容性分開檢核；常見誤判是：只追求高純度可能忽略帶電風險。","explanationEn":"Water chemistry and charging need control. Verify: Electrical control and material compatibility are checked separately. A common misinterpretation is: Purity alone can overlook charging risk."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-089"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-091","order":13,"sequence":91,"title":"驗收首刀位置","titleEn":"Accept the first-cut position","objective":"將首刀影像疊加街道中線，並能說明「首刀可揭露座標或偏移錯誤」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay the first kerf on the street centerline and explain: The first cut reveals coordinate and offset errors.","instruction":"將首刀影像疊加街道中線。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：實測切口落在核准包絡內。","instructionEn":"Overlay the first kerf on the street centerline. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Measured kerf stays within the approved envelope.","observation":"實測切口落在核准包絡內；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Measured kerf stays within the approved envelope; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未驗首刀就連切會放大報廢。","failureEn":"Skipping first-cut checks multiplies scrap.","check":"實測切口落在核准包絡內。","checkEn":"Measured kerf stays within the approved envelope.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-091-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"首刀可揭露座標或偏移錯誤。","textEn":"The first cut reveals coordinate and offset errors."},{"id":"pk-091-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未驗首刀就連切會放大報廢；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Skipping first-cut checks multiplies scrap. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗收首刀位置」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Accept the first-cut position\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["殘屑下降且未移入焊墊區","包絡不跨入有效晶粒區","實測切口落在核准包絡內"],"optionsEn":["Debris decreases without entering pad areas","The envelope avoids active die regions","Measured kerf stays within the approved envelope"],"answer":2,"explanation":"首刀可揭露座標或偏移錯誤。本步要確認：實測切口落在核准包絡內；常見誤判是：未驗首刀就連切會放大報廢。","explanationEn":"The first cut reveals coordinate and offset errors. Verify: Measured kerf stays within the approved envelope. A common misinterpretation is: Skipping first-cut checks multiplies scrap."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-090"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-092","order":14,"sequence":92,"title":"量測首刀切口形狀","titleEn":"Measure first-cut kerf shape","objective":"比較入口、中段與出口寬度，並能說明「切口寬度可沿路徑變化」。","objectiveEn":"Compare entry, middle and exit widths and explain: Kerf width can vary along the path.","instruction":"比較入口、中段與出口寬度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：各位置寬度與尺度有紀錄。","instructionEn":"Compare entry, middle and exit widths. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Widths and scales are recorded by position.","observation":"各位置寬度與尺度有紀錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Widths and scales are recorded by position; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單點量測可能漏掉喇叭口。","failureEn":"One point can miss flared openings.","check":"各位置寬度與尺度有紀錄。","checkEn":"Widths and scales are recorded by position.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-092-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"切口寬度可沿路徑變化。","textEn":"Kerf width can vary along the path."},{"id":"pk-092-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單點量測可能漏掉喇叭口；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One point can miss flared openings. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測首刀切口形狀」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure first-cut kerf shape\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["各位置寬度與尺度有紀錄","疑似殘留有後續確認方法","矽與金屬跨層皆有考慮"],"optionsEn":["Widths and scales are recorded by position","Suspected residues have follow-up checks","Both silicon and crossing metal are considered"],"answer":0,"explanation":"切口寬度可沿路徑變化。本步要確認：各位置寬度與尺度有紀錄；常見誤判是：單點量測可能漏掉喇叭口。","explanationEn":"Kerf width can vary along the path. Verify: Widths and scales are recorded by position. A common misinterpretation is: One point can miss flared openings."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-091"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-093","order":15,"sequence":93,"title":"辨識正面崩裂","titleEn":"Identify front-side chipping","objective":"沿兩側量測缺口侵入深度，並能說明「崩裂距有效區的距離比外觀更關鍵」。","objectiveEn":"Measure chip intrusion on both kerf edges and explain: Distance to active areas matters beyond appearance.","instruction":"沿兩側量測缺口侵入深度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：侵入量按正確邊界判讀。","instructionEn":"Measure chip intrusion on both kerf edges. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Intrusion is measured from the correct boundary.","observation":"侵入量按正確邊界判讀；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Intrusion is measured from the correct boundary; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把崩屑寬度當裂紋長度會混淆。","failureEn":"Chip width is not crack length.","check":"侵入量按正確邊界判讀。","checkEn":"Intrusion is measured from the correct boundary.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-093-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"崩裂距有效區的距離比外觀更關鍵。","textEn":"Distance to active areas matters beyond appearance."},{"id":"pk-093-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把崩屑寬度當裂紋長度會混淆；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Chip width is not crack length. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識正面崩裂」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify front-side chipping\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["磨耗訊號與切深補償一致","侵入量按正確邊界判讀","所選釋黏方法與材料相符"],"optionsEn":["Wear indicators match depth compensation","Intrusion is measured from the correct boundary","Release method matches the tape"],"answer":1,"explanation":"崩裂距有效區的距離比外觀更關鍵。本步要確認：侵入量按正確邊界判讀；常見誤判是：把崩屑寬度當裂紋長度會混淆。","explanationEn":"Distance to active areas matters beyond appearance. Verify: Intrusion is measured from the correct boundary. A common misinterpretation is: Chip width is not crack length."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-092"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-094","order":16,"sequence":94,"title":"辨識背面崩裂","titleEn":"Identify backside chipping","objective":"比較背面影像與支承狀態，並能說明「背崩可受出刀與支承影響」。","objectiveEn":"Compare backside images and support condition and explain: Backside chipping depends on exit and support.","instruction":"比較背面影像與支承狀態。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：背面檢查沒有被正面AOI取代。","instructionEn":"Compare backside images and support condition. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Backside inspection is not replaced by front AOI.","observation":"背面檢查沒有被正面AOI取代；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Backside inspection is not replaced by front AOI; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"正面完好不能排除背面損傷。","failureEn":"A clean front cannot exclude backside damage.","check":"背面檢查沒有被正面AOI取代。","checkEn":"Backside inspection is not replaced by front AOI.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-094-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"背崩可受出刀與支承影響。","textEn":"Backside chipping depends on exit and support."},{"id":"pk-094-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"正面完好不能排除背面損傷；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A clean front cannot exclude backside damage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識背面崩裂」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify backside chipping\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["間隙增加且晶粒姿態可追溯","異常週期與旋轉相關性有記錄","背面檢查沒有被正面AOI取代"],"optionsEn":["Gaps increase while die poses remain traceable","Periodic anomalies are compared with rotation","Backside inspection is not replaced by front AOI"],"answer":2,"explanation":"背崩可受出刀與支承影響。本步要確認：背面檢查沒有被正面AOI取代；常見誤判是：正面完好不能排除背面損傷。","explanationEn":"Backside chipping depends on exit and support. Verify: Backside inspection is not replaced by front AOI. A common misinterpretation is: A clean front cannot exclude backside damage."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-093"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-095","order":17,"sequence":95,"title":"檢查交叉切口角點","titleEn":"Inspect crossing-cut corners","objective":"放大兩方向交會處的缺角，並能說明「角點在第二方向切割後更脆弱」。","objectiveEn":"Magnify corners at intersecting cuts and explain: Corners become vulnerable after cross-cutting.","instruction":"放大兩方向交會處的缺角。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：角點完整性按獨立區域評估。","instructionEn":"Magnify corners at intersecting cuts. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Corner integrity is assessed separately.","observation":"角點完整性按獨立區域評估；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Corner integrity is assessed separately; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看直線段會漏掉角部掉片。","failureEn":"Straight-segment checks miss corner breakage.","check":"角點完整性按獨立區域評估。","checkEn":"Corner integrity is assessed separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-095-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"角點在第二方向切割後更脆弱。","textEn":"Corners become vulnerable after cross-cutting."},{"id":"pk-095-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看直線段會漏掉角部掉片；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Straight-segment checks miss corner breakage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查交叉切口角點」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect crossing-cut corners\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["角點完整性按獨立區域評估","參考點殘差符合教學圖面要求","兩組街道均有獨立核對"],"optionsEn":["Corner integrity is assessed separately","Reference residuals meet exercise requirements","Both street families are independently checked"],"answer":0,"explanation":"角點在第二方向切割後更脆弱。本步要確認：角點完整性按獨立區域評估；常見誤判是：只看直線段會漏掉角部掉片。","explanationEn":"Corners become vulnerable after cross-cutting. Verify: Corner integrity is assessed separately. A common misinterpretation is: Straight-segment checks miss corner breakage."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-094"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-096","order":18,"sequence":96,"title":"辨識膜層剝離","titleEn":"Identify film delamination","objective":"將剝離區與街道金屬相對照，並能說明「分層與矽本體崩裂機制不同」。","objectiveEn":"Compare lifted films with street metal and explain: Film separation differs from bulk-silicon chipping.","instruction":"將剝離區與街道金屬相對照。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：缺陷分類保留層別與界面。","instructionEn":"Compare lifted films with street metal. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Classification records layer and interface.","observation":"缺陷分類保留層別與界面；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Classification records layer and interface; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"將兩者混標會妨礙根因分析。","failureEn":"Combining labels hinders root-cause analysis.","check":"缺陷分類保留層別與界面。","checkEn":"Classification records layer and interface.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-096-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"分層與矽本體崩裂機制不同。","textEn":"Film separation differs from bulk-silicon chipping."},{"id":"pk-096-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"將兩者混標會妨礙根因分析；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Combining labels hinders root-cause analysis. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識膜層剝離」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify film delamination\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["剖面標示切穿與保護界線","缺陷分類保留層別與界面","每顆晶粒都有可選或隔離狀態"],"optionsEn":["Sections show cut-through and protection boundaries","Classification records layer and interface","Every die has pickable or quarantine status"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分層與矽本體崩裂機制不同。本步要確認：缺陷分類保留層別與界面；常見誤判是：將兩者混標會妨礙根因分析。","explanationEn":"Film separation differs from bulk-silicon chipping. Verify: Classification records layer and interface. A common misinterpretation is: Combining labels hinders root-cause analysis."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-095"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-097","order":19,"sequence":97,"title":"評估雷射分離熱影響","titleEn":"Assess laser-singulation thermal effects","objective":"比较切邊變色與微裂線索，並能說明「非接觸不代表沒有熱損傷」。","objectiveEn":"Compare edge discoloration and microcrack clues and explain: Noncontact processing does not imply no thermal damage.","instruction":"比较切邊變色與微裂線索。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：熱影響與殘留物分開記錄。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Compare edge discoloration and microcrack clues. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Thermal effects and residues are recorded separately. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"熱影響與殘留物分開記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Thermal effects and residues are recorded separately; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只見無刀痕便判無損傷不成立。","failureEn":"No blade marks do not prove no damage.","check":"熱影響與殘留物分開記錄。","checkEn":"Thermal effects and residues are recorded separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-097-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"非接觸不代表沒有熱損傷。","textEn":"Noncontact processing does not imply no thermal damage."},{"id":"pk-097-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只見無刀痕便判無損傷不成立；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"No blade marks do not prove no damage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-097-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"雷射分離的熱影響不能只由平均功率判斷；脈衝寬度、重複率、掃描重疊與吸收層都會影響局部作用。教學比較應固定其中參數，再改變單一因素。","textEn":"Laser-separation heating cannot be inferred from average power alone; pulse duration, repetition rate, scan overlap and absorbing layers affect local response. Hold other variables fixed in an authored comparison."},{"id":"pk-097-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"保留切割邊緣光學影像、截面和電性差異。外觀乾淨不能排除埋藏裂紋；可見變色也不自動等於電性報廢，需依證據分判。","textEn":"Retain edge optical images, sections and electrical changes. Clean appearance does not exclude buried cracks, while discoloration alone does not establish electrical failure."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估雷射分離熱影響」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess laser-singulation thermal effects\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["選擇有材料與損傷理由","入刀與出刀處均無死角","熱影響與殘留物分開記錄"],"optionsEn":["Selection states material and damage reasons","Entry and exit have no uncovered zones","Thermal effects and residues are recorded separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"非接觸不代表沒有熱損傷。本步要確認：熱影響與殘留物分開記錄；常見誤判是：只見無刀痕便判無損傷不成立。","explanationEn":"Noncontact processing does not imply no thermal damage. Verify: Thermal effects and residues are recorded separately. A common misinterpretation is: No blade marks do not prove no damage."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-096"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-098","order":20,"sequence":98,"title":"評估電漿分離遮罩","titleEn":"Assess plasma-singulation masking","objective":"檢查遮罩開口和保護區，並能說明「遮罩圖案決定移除位置」。","objectiveEn":"Inspect mask openings and protected regions and explain: Mask patterns determine removal locations.","instruction":"檢查遮罩開口和保護區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：開口只覆蓋核准分離區。","instructionEn":"Inspect mask openings and protected regions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Openings cover approved separation regions only.","observation":"開口只覆蓋核准分離區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Openings cover approved separation regions only; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"遮罩缺口可能侵蝕功能區。","failureEn":"Mask defects can erode functional regions.","check":"開口只覆蓋核准分離區。","checkEn":"Openings cover approved separation regions only.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-098-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"遮罩圖案決定移除位置。","textEn":"Mask patterns determine removal locations."},{"id":"pk-098-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"遮罩缺口可能侵蝕功能區；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mask defects can erode functional regions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估電漿分離遮罩」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess plasma-singulation masking\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["開口只覆蓋核准分離區","兩個階段的需求皆被滿足","電性控制與材料相容性分開檢核"],"optionsEn":["Openings cover approved separation regions only","Both stages' needs are addressed","Electrical control and material compatibility are checked separately"],"answer":0,"explanation":"遮罩圖案決定移除位置。本步要確認：開口只覆蓋核准分離區；常見誤判是：遮罩缺口可能侵蝕功能區。","explanationEn":"Mask patterns determine removal locations. Verify: Openings cover approved separation regions only. A common misinterpretation is: Mask defects can erode functional regions."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-097"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-099","order":21,"sequence":99,"title":"清除切割殘屑","titleEn":"Remove singulation debris conceptually","objective":"比較清洗前後顆粒位置圖，並能說明「去屑效果需避免二次搬移污染」。","objectiveEn":"Compare particle maps before and after cleaning and explain: Debris removal must avoid redeposition.","instruction":"比較清洗前後顆粒位置圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：殘屑下降且未移入焊墊區。","instructionEn":"Compare particle maps before and after cleaning. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Debris decreases without entering pad areas.","observation":"殘屑下降且未移入焊墊區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Debris decreases without entering pad areas; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只計顆粒數可能漏掉關鍵區再沉積。","failureEn":"Counts alone miss critical-area redeposition.","check":"殘屑下降且未移入焊墊區。","checkEn":"Debris decreases without entering pad areas.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-099-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"去屑效果需避免二次搬移污染。","textEn":"Debris removal must avoid redeposition."},{"id":"pk-099-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只計顆粒數可能漏掉關鍵區再沉積；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Counts alone miss critical-area redeposition. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「清除切割殘屑」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Remove singulation debris conceptually\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["實測切口落在核准包絡內","殘屑下降且未移入焊墊區","刀路下方支承無未解決異常"],"optionsEn":["Measured kerf stays within the approved envelope","Debris decreases without entering pad areas","Support under cut paths has no unresolved defects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"去屑效果需避免二次搬移污染。本步要確認：殘屑下降且未移入焊墊區；常見誤判是：只計顆粒數可能漏掉關鍵區再沉積。","explanationEn":"Debris removal must avoid redeposition. Verify: Debris decreases without entering pad areas. A common misinterpretation is: Counts alone miss critical-area redeposition."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-098"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-100","order":22,"sequence":100,"title":"評估切後乾燥","titleEn":"Assess post-cut drying","objective":"區分水痕、顆粒與膜層色差，並能說明「水痕可影響後續表面接合」。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish watermarks, particles and film color and explain: Watermarks can affect later bonding.","instruction":"區分水痕、顆粒與膜層色差。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：疑似殘留有後續確認方法。","instructionEn":"Distinguish watermarks, particles and film color. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Suspected residues have follow-up checks.","observation":"疑似殘留有後續確認方法；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Suspected residues have follow-up checks; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"強行擦拭可能刮傷裸露晶粒。","failureEn":"Aggressive wiping can scratch exposed dies.","check":"疑似殘留有後續確認方法。","checkEn":"Suspected residues have follow-up checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-100-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"水痕可影響後續表面接合。","textEn":"Watermarks can affect later bonding."},{"id":"pk-100-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"強行擦拭可能刮傷裸露晶粒；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Aggressive wiping can scratch exposed dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估切後乾燥」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess post-cut drying\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["框架與地圖能一一映射","各位置寬度與尺度有紀錄","疑似殘留有後續確認方法"],"optionsEn":["Frame and map coordinates map consistently","Widths and scales are recorded by position","Suspected residues have follow-up checks"],"answer":2,"explanation":"水痕可影響後續表面接合。本步要確認：疑似殘留有後續確認方法；常見誤判是：強行擦拭可能刮傷裸露晶粒。","explanationEn":"Watermarks can affect later bonding. Verify: Suspected residues have follow-up checks. A common misinterpretation is: Aggressive wiping can scratch exposed dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-099"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-101","order":23,"sequence":101,"title":"判讀膠膜釋黏","titleEn":"Assess tape-adhesion release","objective":"比較釋黏前後剝離需求，並能說明「釋黏方案取決於膠膜種類」。","objectiveEn":"Compare release requirements before and after treatment and explain: Release methods depend on tape chemistry.","instruction":"比較釋黏前後剝離需求。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：所選釋黏方法與材料相符。","instructionEn":"Compare release requirements before and after treatment. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Release method matches the tape.","observation":"所選釋黏方法與材料相符；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Release method matches the tape; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"對錯誤膜種施加處理不會有效釋放。","failureEn":"Wrong treatment does not release incompatible tape.","check":"所選釋黏方法與材料相符。","checkEn":"Release method matches the tape.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-101-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"釋黏方案取決於膠膜種類。","textEn":"Release methods depend on tape chemistry."},{"id":"pk-101-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"對錯誤膜種施加處理不會有效釋放；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Wrong treatment does not release incompatible tape. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀膠膜釋黏」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess tape-adhesion release\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["所選釋黏方法與材料相符","包絡不跨入有效晶粒區","侵入量按正確邊界判讀"],"optionsEn":["Release method matches the tape","The envelope avoids active die regions","Intrusion is measured from the correct boundary"],"answer":0,"explanation":"釋黏方案取決於膠膜種類。本步要確認：所選釋黏方法與材料相符；常見誤判是：對錯誤膜種施加處理不會有效釋放。","explanationEn":"Release methods depend on tape chemistry. Verify: Release method matches the tape. A common misinterpretation is: Wrong treatment does not release incompatible tape."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-100"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-102","order":24,"sequence":102,"title":"檢查擴膜間距","titleEn":"Inspect tape-expansion spacing","objective":"量測擴膜後相鄰晶粒間隙，並能說明「擴膜改變晶粒間距與座標」。","objectiveEn":"Measure neighboring gaps after expansion and explain: Expansion changes spacing and coordinates.","instruction":"量測擴膜後相鄰晶粒間隙。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：間隙增加且晶粒姿態可追溯。","instructionEn":"Measure neighboring gaps after expansion. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Gaps increase while die poses remain traceable.","observation":"間隙增加且晶粒姿態可追溯；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Gaps increase while die poses remain traceable; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"不均擴膜會扭曲挑晶位置。","failureEn":"Uneven expansion distorts pickup coordinates.","check":"間隙增加且晶粒姿態可追溯。","checkEn":"Gaps increase while die poses remain traceable.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-102-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"擴膜改變晶粒間距與座標。","textEn":"Expansion changes spacing and coordinates."},{"id":"pk-102-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"不均擴膜會扭曲挑晶位置；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Uneven expansion distorts pickup coordinates. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查擴膜間距」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect tape-expansion spacing\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["背面檢查沒有被正面AOI取代","間隙增加且晶粒姿態可追溯","矽與金屬跨層皆有考慮"],"optionsEn":["Backside inspection is not replaced by front AOI","Gaps increase while die poses remain traceable","Both silicon and crossing metal are considered"],"answer":1,"explanation":"擴膜改變晶粒間距與座標。本步要確認：間隙增加且晶粒姿態可追溯；常見誤判是：不均擴膜會扭曲挑晶位置。","explanationEn":"Expansion changes spacing and coordinates. Verify: Gaps increase while die poses remain traceable. A common misinterpretation is: Uneven expansion distorts pickup coordinates."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-101"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-103","order":25,"sequence":103,"title":"驗證分離後地圖轉換","titleEn":"Verify post-singulation map transforms","objective":"以多顆參考晶粒更新拾取座標，並能說明「材料形變需被座標模型吸收」。","objectiveEn":"Update pickup coordinates using multiple reference dies and explain: Coordinate models must account for deformation.","instruction":"以多顆參考晶粒更新拾取座標。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：參考點殘差符合教學圖面要求。","instructionEn":"Update pickup coordinates using multiple reference dies. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Reference residuals meet exercise requirements.","observation":"參考點殘差符合教學圖面要求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Reference residuals meet exercise requirements; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"沿用切前座標可偏離實體位置。","failureEn":"Pre-cut coordinates can miss actual positions.","check":"參考點殘差符合教學圖面要求。","checkEn":"Reference residuals meet exercise requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-103-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"材料形變需被座標模型吸收。","textEn":"Coordinate models must account for deformation."},{"id":"pk-103-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"沿用切前座標可偏離實體位置；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Pre-cut coordinates can miss actual positions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證分離後地圖轉換」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify post-singulation map transforms\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["磨耗訊號與切深補償一致","角點完整性按獨立區域評估","參考點殘差符合教學圖面要求"],"optionsEn":["Wear indicators match depth compensation","Corner integrity is assessed separately","Reference residuals meet exercise requirements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料形變需被座標模型吸收。本步要確認：參考點殘差符合教學圖面要求；常見誤判是：沿用切前座標可偏離實體位置。","explanationEn":"Coordinate models must account for deformation. Verify: Reference residuals meet exercise requirements. A common misinterpretation is: Pre-cut coordinates can miss actual positions."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-102"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-104","order":26,"sequence":104,"title":"放行分離晶粒框","titleEn":"Release the singulated frame","objective":"整合缺陷圖、地圖版本與拾取限制，並能說明「下游需要單顆晶粒的可用狀態」。","objectiveEn":"Combine defect map, revision and pickup restrictions and explain: Downstream requires per-die availability.","instruction":"整合缺陷圖、地圖版本與拾取限制。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每顆晶粒都有可選或隔離狀態。","instructionEn":"Combine defect map, revision and pickup restrictions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Every die has pickable or quarantine status.","observation":"每顆晶粒都有可選或隔離狀態；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Every die has pickable or quarantine status; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"整框良率不能替代單顆判定。","failureEn":"Frame yield cannot replace per-die disposition.","check":"每顆晶粒都有可選或隔離狀態。","checkEn":"Every die has pickable or quarantine status.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-104-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"下游需要單顆晶粒的可用狀態。","textEn":"Downstream requires per-die availability."},{"id":"pk-104-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"整框良率不能替代單顆判定；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Frame yield cannot replace per-die disposition. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「放行分離晶粒框」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release the singulated frame\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每顆晶粒都有可選或隔離狀態","異常週期與旋轉相關性有記錄","缺陷分類保留層別與界面"],"optionsEn":["Every die has pickable or quarantine status","Periodic anomalies are compared with rotation","Classification records layer and interface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"下游需要單顆晶粒的可用狀態。本步要確認：每顆晶粒都有可選或隔離狀態；常見誤判是：整框良率不能替代單顆判定。","explanationEn":"Downstream requires per-die availability. Verify: Every die has pickable or quarantine status. A common misinterpretation is: Frame yield cannot replace per-die disposition."},"sourceIds":["pk-disco-review","pk-disco-dbg","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-103"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m05","order":5,"sequence":5,"title":"晶粒拾取、黏晶與接合熱介面","titleEn":"Die pickup, attachment and thermal bond interfaces","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查晶粒拾取、黏晶與接合熱介面的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for die pickup, attachment and thermal bond interfaces. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"主要為打線前黏晶；貼晶膜是材料替代分支，扇出載體放置另見m08。","routeEn":"Mainly pre-wirebond attachment; film is an alternative material, while fan-out placement is m08.","sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-105","order":1,"sequence":105,"title":"載入可挑選晶粒清單","titleEn":"Load the pickable-die list","objective":"依核准地圖繪製取放位置示意，並能說明「取放不可自行改寫測試分檔」。","objectiveEn":"Draw placement locations from the approved map and explain: Placement must not rewrite test bins.","instruction":"依核准地圖繪製取放位置示意。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：實際挑選只來自核准座標。","instructionEn":"Draw placement locations from the approved map. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Selected dies come only from approved coordinates.","observation":"實際挑選只來自核准座標；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Selected dies come only from approved coordinates; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"離線地圖版本過期會錯挑晶粒。","failureEn":"Outdated maps select incorrect dies.","check":"實際挑選只來自核准座標。","checkEn":"Selected dies come only from approved coordinates.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-105-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"取放不可自行改寫測試分檔。","textEn":"Placement must not rewrite test bins."},{"id":"pk-105-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"離線地圖版本過期會錯挑晶粒；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Outdated maps select incorrect dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「載入可挑選晶粒清單」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Load the pickable-die list\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["承載面異常已有處置記錄","BLT計算明確列出參考高度","實際挑選只來自核准座標"],"optionsEn":["Attach-surface anomalies have dispositions","BLT calculation states reference heights","Selected dies come only from approved coordinates"],"answer":2,"explanation":"取放不可自行改寫測試分檔。本步要確認：實際挑選只來自核准座標；常見誤判是：離線地圖版本過期會錯挑晶粒。","explanationEn":"Placement must not rewrite test bins. Verify: Selected dies come only from approved coordinates. A common misinterpretation is: Outdated maps select incorrect dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-104"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-106","order":2,"sequence":106,"title":"選擇吸嘴接觸面","titleEn":"Select collet contact area","objective":"對照吸嘴輪廓與晶粒表面禁區，並能說明「吸力分布與接觸位置影響彎曲」。","objectiveEn":"Compare collet footprints with prohibited surface zones and explain: Suction distribution and contact location affect bending.","instruction":"對照吸嘴輪廓與晶粒表面禁區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：接觸區避開敏感結構與懸空邊緣。","instructionEn":"Compare collet footprints with prohibited surface zones. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Contact avoids sensitive structures and unsupported edges.","observation":"接觸區避開敏感結構與懸空邊緣；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Contact avoids sensitive structures and unsupported edges; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"小吸嘴可能使薄晶粒局部彎折。","failureEn":"A small collet can locally bend thin dies.","check":"接觸區避開敏感結構與懸空邊緣。","checkEn":"Contact avoids sensitive structures and unsupported edges.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-106-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"吸力分布與接觸位置影響彎曲。","textEn":"Suction distribution and contact location affect bending."},{"id":"pk-106-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"小吸嘴可能使薄晶粒局部彎折；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A small collet can locally bend thin dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇吸嘴接觸面」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select collet contact area\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["接觸區避開敏感結構與懸空邊緣","可用狀態有資料表依據","平面斜率與局部高度均記錄"],"optionsEn":["Contact avoids sensitive structures and unsupported edges","Usability is supported by the material datasheet","Plane slope and local heights are recorded"],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸力分布與接觸位置影響彎曲。本步要確認：接觸區避開敏感結構與懸空邊緣；常見誤判是：小吸嘴可能使薄晶粒局部彎折。","explanationEn":"Suction distribution and contact location affect bending. Verify: Contact avoids sensitive structures and unsupported edges. A common misinterpretation is: A small collet can locally bend thin dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-105"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-107","order":3,"sequence":107,"title":"配置頂針支承","titleEn":"Configure ejector support","objective":"比較頂針位置與薄晶粒剖面，並能說明「頂升力需配合剝離而非穿刺」。","objectiveEn":"Compare ejector positions with thin-die sections and explain: Ejection should aid peeling rather than puncture.","instruction":"比較頂針位置與薄晶粒剖面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：支承點不形成未評估應力集中。","instructionEn":"Compare ejector positions with thin-die sections. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Support points avoid unassessed stress concentrations.","observation":"支承點不形成未評估應力集中；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Support points avoid unassessed stress concentrations; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"集中頂力可能造成背面裂紋。","failureEn":"Concentrated ejection can crack the backside.","check":"支承點不形成未評估應力集中。","checkEn":"Support points avoid unassessed stress concentrations.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-107-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"頂升力需配合剝離而非穿刺。","textEn":"Ejection should aid peeling rather than puncture."},{"id":"pk-107-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"集中頂力可能造成背面裂紋；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Concentrated ejection can crack the backside. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「配置頂針支承」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Configure ejector support\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["引用材料資料而非自行猜測時間溫度","支承點不形成未評估應力集中","未超出核准工作條件"],"optionsEn":["The plan uses material data rather than invented settings","Support points avoid unassessed stress concentrations","Qualified working conditions are not exceeded"],"answer":1,"explanation":"頂升力需配合剝離而非穿刺。本步要確認：支承點不形成未評估應力集中；常見誤判是：集中頂力可能造成背面裂紋。","explanationEn":"Ejection should aid peeling rather than puncture. Verify: Support points avoid unassessed stress concentrations. A common misinterpretation is: Concentrated ejection can crack the backside."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-106"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-108","order":4,"sequence":108,"title":"判讀膠膜剝離順序","titleEn":"Assess tape-peeling sequence","objective":"追蹤邊緣釋離與晶粒上升關係，並能說明「先剝離可減少整面拉伸負荷」。","objectiveEn":"Track edge release relative to die lift and explain: Peeling can reduce full-area tensile loading.","instruction":"追蹤邊緣釋離與晶粒上升關係。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：晶粒抬升時未被局部膜區拖住。","instructionEn":"Track edge release relative to die lift. Check evidence you create or obtain against: No tape region restrains the lifted die.","observation":"晶粒抬升時未被局部膜區拖住；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"No tape region restrains the lifted die; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"直接上拉可能使晶粒折裂。","failureEn":"Direct pulling can fracture the die.","check":"晶粒抬升時未被局部膜區拖住。","checkEn":"No tape region restrains the lifted die.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-108-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"先剝離可減少整面拉伸負荷。","textEn":"Peeling can reduce full-area tensile loading."},{"id":"pk-108-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"直接上拉可能使晶粒折裂；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Direct pulling can fracture the die. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀膠膜剝離順序」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess tape-peeling sequence\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["材料能形成需求中的覆蓋形態","位移變化未超過教學設計包絡","晶粒抬升時未被局部膜區拖住"],"optionsEn":["The material forms the required coverage pattern","Displacement remains within the teaching envelope","No tape region restrains the lifted die"],"answer":2,"explanation":"先剝離可減少整面拉伸負荷。本步要確認：晶粒抬升時未被局部膜區拖住；常見誤判是：直接上拉可能使晶粒折裂。","explanationEn":"Peeling can reduce full-area tensile loading. Verify: No tape region restrains the lifted die. A common misinterpretation is: Direct pulling can fracture the die."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-107"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-109","order":5,"sequence":109,"title":"驗證吸取真空回授","titleEn":"Verify pickup vacuum feedback","objective":"比較空吸、正常吸取與漏氣訊號，並能說明「真空訊號可辨識部分取放異常」。","objectiveEn":"Compare empty, successful and leaking pickup signals and explain: Vacuum feedback detects some pickup faults.","instruction":"比較空吸、正常吸取與漏氣訊號。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：空吸與漏氣不被判作成功。","instructionEn":"Compare empty, successful and leaking pickup signals. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Empty pickup and leaks are not counted as success.","observation":"空吸與漏氣不被判作成功；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Empty pickup and leaks are not counted as success; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只記動作完成會放過失晶。","failureEn":"Motion completion alone misses missing dies.","check":"空吸與漏氣不被判作成功。","checkEn":"Empty pickup and leaks are not counted as success.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-109-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"真空訊號可辨識部分取放異常。","textEn":"Vacuum feedback detects some pickup faults."},{"id":"pk-109-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只記動作完成會放過失晶；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Motion completion alone misses missing dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證吸取真空回授」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify pickup vacuum feedback\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["空吸與漏氣不被判作成功","離散程度與偏移分開報告","空洞結論注明方法與遮蔽限制"],"optionsEn":["Empty pickup and leaks are not counted as success","Scatter and bias are reported separately","Void conclusions state method and visibility limits"],"answer":0,"explanation":"真空訊號可辨識部分取放異常。本步要確認：空吸與漏氣不被判作成功；常見誤判是：只記動作完成會放過失晶。","explanationEn":"Vacuum feedback detects some pickup faults. Verify: Empty pickup and leaks are not counted as success. A common misinterpretation is: Motion completion alone misses missing dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-108"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-110","order":6,"sequence":110,"title":"檢查取後晶粒完整性","titleEn":"Inspect die integrity after pickup","objective":"比對取前取後邊緣影像，並能說明「拾取可能新增邊角損傷」。","objectiveEn":"Compare die edges before and after pickup and explain: Pickup can introduce edge damage.","instruction":"比對取前取後邊緣影像。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：新增缺陷與原有缺陷分開記錄。","instructionEn":"Compare die edges before and after pickup. Check evidence you create or obtain against: New and preexisting defects are separated.","observation":"新增缺陷與原有缺陷分開記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"New and preexisting defects are separated; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未保留取前影像難以定位責任工站。","failureEn":"Missing before-images obscures the damaging station.","check":"新增缺陷與原有缺陷分開記錄。","checkEn":"New and preexisting defects are separated.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-110-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"拾取可能新增邊角損傷。","textEn":"Pickup can introduce edge damage."},{"id":"pk-110-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未保留取前影像難以定位責任工站；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Missing before-images obscures the damaging station. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查取後晶粒完整性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect die integrity after pickup\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["數值與破壞模式成對呈現","新增缺陷與原有缺陷分開記錄","預測流路保留氣體排出方向"],"optionsEn":["Values are paired with failure modes","New and preexisting defects are separated","Predicted flow preserves air-escape paths"],"answer":1,"explanation":"拾取可能新增邊角損傷。本步要確認：新增缺陷與原有缺陷分開記錄；常見誤判是：未保留取前影像難以定位責任工站。","explanationEn":"Pickup can introduce edge damage. Verify: New and preexisting defects are separated. A common misinterpretation is: Missing before-images obscures the damaging station."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-109"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-111","order":7,"sequence":111,"title":"校準上下視覺座標","titleEn":"Calibrate upper and lower vision coordinates","objective":"用參考件對齊晶粒與基板座標，並能說明「不同相機需要共同座標轉換」。","objectiveEn":"Align die and substrate coordinates with a reference and explain: Different cameras need a common transform.","instruction":"用參考件對齊晶粒與基板座標。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：多點殘差都落在本例容許範圍。","instructionEn":"Align die and substrate coordinates with a reference. Check evidence you create or obtain against: All reference residuals meet exercise limits.","observation":"多點殘差都落在本例容許範圍；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"All reference residuals meet exercise limits; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只校正平移會留下角度偏差。","failureEn":"Translation-only calibration leaves angular error.","check":"多點殘差都落在本例容許範圍。","checkEn":"All reference residuals meet exercise limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-111-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同相機需要共同座標轉換。","textEn":"Different cameras need a common transform."},{"id":"pk-111-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只校正平移會留下角度偏差；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Translation-only calibration leaves angular error. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「校準上下視覺座標」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calibrate upper and lower vision coordinates\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["溢膠不進入禁止接觸區","熱點附近的缺口被單獨評估","多點殘差都落在本例容許範圍"],"optionsEn":["Bleed stays outside prohibited regions","Gaps near hot spots are evaluated separately","All reference residuals meet exercise limits"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同相機需要共同座標轉換。本步要確認：多點殘差都落在本例容許範圍；常見誤判是：只校正平移會留下角度偏差。","explanationEn":"Different cameras need a common transform. Verify: All reference residuals meet exercise limits. A common misinterpretation is: Translation-only calibration leaves angular error."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-110"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-112","order":8,"sequence":112,"title":"辨識晶粒正反與方向","titleEn":"Identify die face and orientation","objective":"以非對稱標記核對朝向，並能說明「正反與旋轉是獨立判定」。","objectiveEn":"Verify orientation using asymmetric marks and explain: Face and rotation are separate decisions.","instruction":"以非對稱標記核對朝向。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：所有定位標記與目標方向一致。","instructionEn":"Verify orientation using asymmetric marks. Check evidence you create or obtain against: All orientation marks match the target.","observation":"所有定位標記與目標方向一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"All orientation marks match the target; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"對稱外形可能掩蓋翻面錯誤。","failureEn":"Symmetric outlines can hide face reversal.","check":"所有定位標記與目標方向一致。","checkEn":"All orientation marks match the target.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-112-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"正反與旋轉是獨立判定。","textEn":"Face and rotation are separate decisions."},{"id":"pk-112-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"對稱外形可能掩蓋翻面錯誤；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Symmetric outlines can hide face reversal. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識晶粒正反與方向」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify die face and orientation\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["所有定位標記與目標方向一致","膜材分支有獨立貼合與檢查需求","異常件不混入下一分支的合格清單"],"optionsEn":["All orientation marks match the target","The film route has distinct bonding and inspection needs","Abnormal parts stay out of downstream accepted lists"],"answer":0,"explanation":"正反與旋轉是獨立判定。本步要確認：所有定位標記與目標方向一致；常見誤判是：對稱外形可能掩蓋翻面錯誤。","explanationEn":"Face and rotation are separate decisions. Verify: All orientation marks match the target. A common misinterpretation is: Symmetric outlines can hide face reversal."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-111"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-113","order":9,"sequence":113,"title":"檢查貼晶承載面","titleEn":"Inspect the attach surface","objective":"標記基板污染、翹曲及焊墊台階，並能說明「接合層需跨越真實表面形貌」。","objectiveEn":"Mark contamination, warpage and pad steps and explain: The bond layer follows actual surface topography.","instruction":"標記基板污染、翹曲及焊墊台階。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：承載面異常已有處置記錄。","instructionEn":"Mark contamination, warpage and pad steps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Attach-surface anomalies have dispositions.","observation":"承載面異常已有處置記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Attach-surface anomalies have dispositions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"名目平面可能掩蓋局部高點。","failureEn":"A nominal plane can hide local high spots.","check":"承載面異常已有處置記錄。","checkEn":"Attach-surface anomalies have dispositions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-113-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"接合層需跨越真實表面形貌。","textEn":"The bond layer follows actual surface topography."},{"id":"pk-113-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"名目平面可能掩蓋局部高點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A nominal plane can hide local high spots. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查貼晶承載面」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect the attach surface\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["實際挑選只來自核准座標","承載面異常已有處置記錄","中心與角點誤差均符合示意規則"],"optionsEn":["Selected dies come only from approved coordinates","Attach-surface anomalies have dispositions","Center and corner errors meet exercise rules"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接合層需跨越真實表面形貌。本步要確認：承載面異常已有處置記錄；常見誤判是：名目平面可能掩蓋局部高點。","explanationEn":"The bond layer follows actual surface topography. Verify: Attach-surface anomalies have dispositions. A common misinterpretation is: A nominal plane can hide local high spots."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-112"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-114","order":10,"sequence":114,"title":"核對膠材使用歷程","titleEn":"Review adhesive use history","objective":"比對批號、保存與回溫紀錄，並能說明「材料狀態受時間與保存歷程影響」。","objectiveEn":"Check lot, storage and conditioning records and explain: Material state depends on time and storage history.","instruction":"比對批號、保存與回溫紀錄。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：可用狀態有資料表依據。","instructionEn":"Check lot, storage and conditioning records. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Usability is supported by the material datasheet.","observation":"可用狀態有資料表依據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Usability is supported by the material datasheet; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未記回溫歷程會混淆黏度異常。","failureEn":"Missing conditioning history obscures viscosity changes.","check":"可用狀態有資料表依據。","checkEn":"Usability is supported by the material datasheet.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-114-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"材料狀態受時間與保存歷程影響。","textEn":"Material state depends on time and storage history."},{"id":"pk-114-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未記回溫歷程會混淆黏度異常；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Missing conditioning history obscures viscosity changes. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對膠材使用歷程」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review adhesive use history\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常尖峰已連到檢查假設","接觸區避開敏感結構與懸空邊緣","可用狀態有資料表依據"],"optionsEn":["Abnormal spikes have inspection hypotheses","Contact avoids sensitive structures and unsupported edges","Usability is supported by the material datasheet"],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料狀態受時間與保存歷程影響。本步要確認：可用狀態有資料表依據；常見誤判是：未記回溫歷程會混淆黏度異常。","explanationEn":"Material state depends on time and storage history. Verify: Usability is supported by the material datasheet. A common misinterpretation is: Missing conditioning history obscures viscosity changes."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-113"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-115","order":11,"sequence":115,"title":"檢查工作時間窗","titleEn":"Check adhesive working-time window","objective":"將使用時間與材料核准條件比對，並能說明「工作時間與未開封壽命不同」。","objectiveEn":"Compare elapsed use with qualified material conditions and explain: Working time differs from unopened shelf life.","instruction":"將使用時間與材料核准條件比對。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：未超出核准工作條件。","instructionEn":"Compare elapsed use with qualified material conditions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Qualified working conditions are not exceeded.","observation":"未超出核准工作條件；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Qualified working conditions are not exceeded; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"用保存期限替代工作時間會誤放行。","failureEn":"Shelf life cannot replace working time.","check":"未超出核准工作條件。","checkEn":"Qualified working conditions are not exceeded.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-115-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"工作時間與未開封壽命不同。","textEn":"Working time differs from unopened shelf life."},{"id":"pk-115-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"用保存期限替代工作時間會誤放行；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Shelf life cannot replace working time. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查工作時間窗」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check adhesive working-time window\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["未超出核准工作條件","BLT計算明確列出參考高度","支承點不形成未評估應力集中"],"optionsEn":["Qualified working conditions are not exceeded","BLT calculation states reference heights","Support points avoid unassessed stress concentrations"],"answer":0,"explanation":"工作時間與未開封壽命不同。本步要確認：未超出核准工作條件；常見誤判是：用保存期限替代工作時間會誤放行。","explanationEn":"Working time differs from unopened shelf life. Verify: Qualified working conditions are not exceeded. A common misinterpretation is: Shelf life cannot replace working time."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-114"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-116","order":12,"sequence":116,"title":"比較膠材流變行為","titleEn":"Compare adhesive rheology","objective":"對照流動及停止剪切後形態，並能說明「流變性影響點膠和塌落」。","objectiveEn":"Compare flow and shape after shear stops and explain: Rheology affects dispensing and slump.","instruction":"對照流動及停止剪切後形態。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：材料能形成需求中的覆蓋形態。","instructionEn":"Compare flow and shape after shear stops. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The material forms the required coverage pattern.","observation":"材料能形成需求中的覆蓋形態；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The material forms the required coverage pattern; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"同黏度標稱未必有相同流變。","failureEn":"Equal nominal viscosity need not mean equal rheology.","check":"材料能形成需求中的覆蓋形態。","checkEn":"The material forms the required coverage pattern.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-116-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"流變性影響點膠和塌落。","textEn":"Rheology affects dispensing and slump."},{"id":"pk-116-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"同黏度標稱未必有相同流變；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Equal nominal viscosity need not mean equal rheology. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「比較膠材流變行為」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Compare adhesive rheology\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["晶粒抬升時未被局部膜區拖住","材料能形成需求中的覆蓋形態","平面斜率與局部高度均記錄"],"optionsEn":["No tape region restrains the lifted die","The material forms the required coverage pattern","Plane slope and local heights are recorded"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流變性影響點膠和塌落。本步要確認：材料能形成需求中的覆蓋形態；常見誤判是：同黏度標稱未必有相同流變。","explanationEn":"Rheology affects dispensing and slump. Verify: The material forms the required coverage pattern. A common misinterpretation is: Equal nominal viscosity need not mean equal rheology."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-115"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-117","order":13,"sequence":117,"title":"校準單次出膠量","titleEn":"Calibrate dispensed volume","objective":"比較多次出膠質量或體積，並能說明「出膠穩定性控制接合層材料量」。","objectiveEn":"Compare repeated dispense mass or volume and explain: Dispense stability controls bond-layer quantity.","instruction":"比較多次出膠質量或體積。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：離散程度與偏移分開報告。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Compare repeated dispense mass or volume. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Scatter and bias are reported separately. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"離散程度與偏移分開報告；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Scatter and bias are reported separately; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看平均可能漏掉間歇堵針。","failureEn":"Averages can hide intermittent nozzle blockage.","check":"離散程度與偏移分開報告。","checkEn":"Scatter and bias are reported separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-117-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"出膠穩定性控制接合層材料量。","textEn":"Dispense stability controls bond-layer quantity."},{"id":"pk-117-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看平均可能漏掉間歇堵針；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Averages can hide intermittent nozzle blockage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-117-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設點膠稱重 20 次合計 10 mg，平均 0.5 mg/次；密度若為教學值 1 mg/mm³，體積 0.5 mm³。密度與溫度、填料批次及氣泡相關，需另核對。","textEn":"Twenty hypothetical dispenses totaling 10 mg average 0.5 mg each; at an assumed density 1 mg/mm³, volume is 0.5 mm³. Density depends on temperature, filler lot and bubbles and needs confirmation."},{"id":"pk-117-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"平均出膠量不表示每點重複性合格。記錄單點散布、首點/末點和停機再啟動偏差，再與溢膠和缺膠窗口對照。","textEn":"Mean dispense volume does not establish repeatability. Record point scatter, first/last deposits and restart offsets and compare with overflow and starvation limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「校準單次出膠量」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calibrate dispensed volume\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["引用材料資料而非自行猜測時間溫度","空吸與漏氣不被判作成功","離散程度與偏移分開報告"],"optionsEn":["The plan uses material data rather than invented settings","Empty pickup and leaks are not counted as success","Scatter and bias are reported separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"出膠穩定性控制接合層材料量。本步要確認：離散程度與偏移分開報告；常見誤判是：只看平均可能漏掉間歇堵針。","explanationEn":"Dispense stability controls bond-layer quantity. Verify: Scatter and bias are reported separately. A common misinterpretation is: Averages can hide intermittent nozzle blockage."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-116"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-118","order":14,"sequence":118,"title":"設計出膠圖樣","titleEn":"Design the dispense pattern","objective":"比較中心點與分布圖樣的展開，並能說明「流動前緣相遇可能困住氣體」。","objectiveEn":"Compare spreading from central and distributed patterns and explain: Meeting flow fronts may trap gas.","instruction":"比較中心點與分布圖樣的展開。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：預測流路保留氣體排出方向。","instructionEn":"Compare spreading from central and distributed patterns. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Predicted flow preserves air-escape paths.","observation":"預測流路保留氣體排出方向；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Predicted flow preserves air-escape paths; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過早封閉周邊可能形成中央空洞。","failureEn":"Early perimeter closure may trap central voids.","check":"預測流路保留氣體排出方向。","checkEn":"Predicted flow preserves air-escape paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-118-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"流動前緣相遇可能困住氣體。","textEn":"Meeting flow fronts may trap gas."},{"id":"pk-118-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過早封閉周邊可能形成中央空洞；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Early perimeter closure may trap central voids. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「設計出膠圖樣」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Design the dispense pattern\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["預測流路保留氣體排出方向","位移變化未超過教學設計包絡","新增缺陷與原有缺陷分開記錄"],"optionsEn":["Predicted flow preserves air-escape paths","Displacement remains within the teaching envelope","New and preexisting defects are separated"],"answer":0,"explanation":"流動前緣相遇可能困住氣體。本步要確認：預測流路保留氣體排出方向；常見誤判是：過早封閉周邊可能形成中央空洞。","explanationEn":"Meeting flow fronts may trap gas. Verify: Predicted flow preserves air-escape paths. A common misinterpretation is: Early perimeter closure may trap central voids."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-117"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-119","order":15,"sequence":119,"title":"檢查膠量與溢膠風險","titleEn":"Check volume and bleed risk","objective":"疊加膠液展開區與焊墊禁區，並能說明「多餘材料可污染後續接合區」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay adhesive spread with pad keep-outs and explain: Excess material can contaminate later bond sites.","instruction":"疊加膠液展開區與焊墊禁區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：溢膠不進入禁止接觸區。","instructionEn":"Overlay adhesive spread with pad keep-outs. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Bleed stays outside prohibited regions.","observation":"溢膠不進入禁止接觸區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Bleed stays outside prohibited regions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"膠層飽滿不代表沒有溢膠風險。","failureEn":"Full coverage does not exclude bleed risk.","check":"溢膠不進入禁止接觸區。","checkEn":"Bleed stays outside prohibited regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-119-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"多餘材料可污染後續接合區。","textEn":"Excess material can contaminate later bond sites."},{"id":"pk-119-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"膠層飽滿不代表沒有溢膠風險；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Full coverage does not exclude bleed risk. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查膠量與溢膠風險」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check volume and bleed risk\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["多點殘差都落在本例容許範圍","溢膠不進入禁止接觸區","空洞結論注明方法與遮蔽限制"],"optionsEn":["All reference residuals meet exercise limits","Bleed stays outside prohibited regions","Void conclusions state method and visibility limits"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多餘材料可污染後續接合區。本步要確認：溢膠不進入禁止接觸區；常見誤判是：膠層飽滿不代表沒有溢膠風險。","explanationEn":"Excess material can contaminate later bond sites. Verify: Bleed stays outside prohibited regions. A common misinterpretation is: Full coverage does not exclude bleed risk."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-118"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-120","order":16,"sequence":120,"title":"辨識貼晶膜替代分支","titleEn":"Identify die-attach-film alternative","objective":"比較膜材與膏材的界面形成，並能說明「膜材均厚不保證無界面空洞」。","objectiveEn":"Compare film and paste interface formation and explain: Uniform film thickness does not guarantee void-free interfaces.","instruction":"比較膜材與膏材的界面形成。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：膜材分支有獨立貼合與檢查需求。","instructionEn":"Compare film and paste interface formation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The film route has distinct bonding and inspection needs.","observation":"膜材分支有獨立貼合與檢查需求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The film route has distinct bonding and inspection needs; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把膏材點膠步驟套用膜材會錯序。","failureEn":"Applying paste dispensing to film creates wrong steps.","check":"膜材分支有獨立貼合與檢查需求。","checkEn":"The film route has distinct bonding and inspection needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-120-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"膜材均厚不保證無界面空洞。","textEn":"Uniform film thickness does not guarantee void-free interfaces."},{"id":"pk-120-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把膏材點膠步驟套用膜材會錯序；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Applying paste dispensing to film creates wrong steps. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識貼晶膜替代分支」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify die-attach-film alternative\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["數值與破壞模式成對呈現","所有定位標記與目標方向一致","膜材分支有獨立貼合與檢查需求"],"optionsEn":["Values are paired with failure modes","All orientation marks match the target","The film route has distinct bonding and inspection needs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"膜材均厚不保證無界面空洞。本步要確認：膜材分支有獨立貼合與檢查需求；常見誤判是：把膏材點膠步驟套用膜材會錯序。","explanationEn":"Uniform film thickness does not guarantee void-free interfaces. Verify: The film route has distinct bonding and inspection needs. A common misinterpretation is: Applying paste dispensing to film creates wrong steps."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-119"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-121","order":17,"sequence":121,"title":"核對放置XY與角度","titleEn":"Verify placement XY and angle","objective":"從角點量測晶粒相對基板姿態，並能說明「平移及轉角造成不同接點誤差」。","objectiveEn":"Measure die pose relative to substrate corners and explain: Translation and rotation create different contact errors.","instruction":"從角點量測晶粒相對基板姿態。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：中心與角點誤差均符合示意規則。","instructionEn":"Measure die pose relative to substrate corners. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Center and corner errors meet exercise rules.","observation":"中心與角點誤差均符合示意規則；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Center and corner errors meet exercise rules; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"中心準確仍可能四角偏離。","failureEn":"An accurate center can coexist with rotated corners.","check":"中心與角點誤差均符合示意規則。","checkEn":"Center and corner errors meet exercise rules.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-121-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"平移及轉角造成不同接點誤差。","textEn":"Translation and rotation create different contact errors."},{"id":"pk-121-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"中心準確仍可能四角偏離；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"An accurate center can coexist with rotated corners. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對放置XY與角度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify placement XY and angle\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["中心與角點誤差均符合示意規則","熱點附近的缺口被單獨評估","承載面異常已有處置記錄"],"optionsEn":["Center and corner errors meet exercise rules","Gaps near hot spots are evaluated separately","Attach-surface anomalies have dispositions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"平移及轉角造成不同接點誤差。本步要確認：中心與角點誤差均符合示意規則；常見誤判是：中心準確仍可能四角偏離。","explanationEn":"Translation and rotation create different contact errors. Verify: Center and corner errors meet exercise rules. A common misinterpretation is: An accurate center can coexist with rotated corners."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-120"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-122","order":18,"sequence":122,"title":"解讀放置力位移曲線","titleEn":"Interpret placement force-displacement","objective":"標示初始接觸與持續壓入區，並能說明「曲線可辨識表面接觸與材料流動」。","objectiveEn":"Mark initial contact and subsequent compression and explain: The trace distinguishes contact from material flow.","instruction":"標示初始接觸與持續壓入區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常尖峰已連到檢查假設。","instructionEn":"Mark initial contact and subsequent compression. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Abnormal spikes have inspection hypotheses.","observation":"異常尖峰已連到檢查假設；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Abnormal spikes have inspection hypotheses; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把所有力增加當膠材流動會漏掉撞擊。","failureEn":"Not every force increase represents adhesive flow.","check":"異常尖峰已連到檢查假設。","checkEn":"Abnormal spikes have inspection hypotheses.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-122-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"曲線可辨識表面接觸與材料流動。","textEn":"The trace distinguishes contact from material flow."},{"id":"pk-122-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把所有力增加當膠材流動會漏掉撞擊；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Not every force increase represents adhesive flow. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「解讀放置力位移曲線」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret placement force-displacement\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["可用狀態有資料表依據","異常尖峰已連到檢查假設","異常件不混入下一分支的合格清單"],"optionsEn":["Usability is supported by the material datasheet","Abnormal spikes have inspection hypotheses","Abnormal parts stay out of downstream accepted lists"],"answer":1,"explanation":"曲線可辨識表面接觸與材料流動。本步要確認：異常尖峰已連到檢查假設；常見誤判是：把所有力增加當膠材流動會漏掉撞擊。","explanationEn":"The trace distinguishes contact from material flow. Verify: Abnormal spikes have inspection hypotheses. A common misinterpretation is: Not every force increase represents adhesive flow."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-121"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-123","order":19,"sequence":123,"title":"量測接合層厚度","titleEn":"Measure bond-line thickness","objective":"由基板與晶粒高度差求接合層，並能說明「量測需扣除晶粒與基板幾何」。","objectiveEn":"Derive bond-line thickness from reference heights and explain: Measurement must account for die and substrate geometry.","instruction":"由基板與晶粒高度差求接合層。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：BLT計算明確列出參考高度。","instructionEn":"Derive bond-line thickness from reference heights. Check evidence you create or obtain against: BLT calculation states reference heights.","observation":"BLT計算明確列出參考高度；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"BLT calculation states reference heights; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"直接使用頂面高度會混入基板厚度。","failureEn":"Top height alone includes substrate thickness.","check":"BLT計算明確列出參考高度。","checkEn":"BLT calculation states reference heights.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-123-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"量測需扣除晶粒與基板幾何。","textEn":"Measurement must account for die and substrate geometry."},{"id":"pk-123-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"直接使用頂面高度會混入基板厚度；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Top height alone includes substrate thickness. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測接合層厚度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure bond-line thickness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["實際挑選只來自核准座標","未超出核准工作條件","BLT計算明確列出參考高度"],"optionsEn":["Selected dies come only from approved coordinates","Qualified working conditions are not exceeded","BLT calculation states reference heights"],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測需扣除晶粒與基板幾何。本步要確認：BLT計算明確列出參考高度；常見誤判是：直接使用頂面高度會混入基板厚度。","explanationEn":"Measurement must account for die and substrate geometry. Verify: BLT calculation states reference heights. A common misinterpretation is: Top height alone includes substrate thickness."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-122"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-124","order":20,"sequence":124,"title":"量測晶粒傾斜","titleEn":"Measure die tilt","objective":"擬合晶粒角點的高度平面，並能說明「平均BLT相同仍可能存在傾斜」。","objectiveEn":"Fit a plane to die-corner heights and explain: Equal mean BLT can coexist with tilt.","instruction":"擬合晶粒角點的高度平面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：平面斜率與局部高度均記錄。","instructionEn":"Fit a plane to die-corner heights. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Plane slope and local heights are recorded.","observation":"平面斜率與局部高度均記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Plane slope and local heights are recorded; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只量中心會漏掉傾斜貼晶。","failureEn":"Center-only measurement misses tilt.","check":"平面斜率與局部高度均記錄。","checkEn":"Plane slope and local heights are recorded.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-124-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"平均BLT相同仍可能存在傾斜。","textEn":"Equal mean BLT can coexist with tilt."},{"id":"pk-124-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只量中心會漏掉傾斜貼晶；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Center-only measurement misses tilt. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測晶粒傾斜」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure die tilt\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["平面斜率與局部高度均記錄","接觸區避開敏感結構與懸空邊緣","材料能形成需求中的覆蓋形態"],"optionsEn":["Plane slope and local heights are recorded","Contact avoids sensitive structures and unsupported edges","The material forms the required coverage pattern"],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均BLT相同仍可能存在傾斜。本步要確認：平面斜率與局部高度均記錄；常見誤判是：只量中心會漏掉傾斜貼晶。","explanationEn":"Equal mean BLT can coexist with tilt. Verify: Plane slope and local heights are recorded. A common misinterpretation is: Center-only measurement misses tilt."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-123"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-125","order":21,"sequence":125,"title":"規劃固化歷程驗證","titleEn":"Plan cure-history verification","objective":"把材料核准曲線與實際件溫比較，並能說明「設備設定值不同於零件溫度」。","objectiveEn":"Compare qualified cure profile with part temperature and explain: Tool setpoint differs from part temperature.","instruction":"把材料核准曲線與實際件溫比較。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：引用材料資料而非自行猜測時間溫度。","instructionEn":"Compare qualified cure profile with part temperature. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The plan uses material data rather than invented settings.","observation":"引用材料資料而非自行猜測時間溫度；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The plan uses material data rather than invented settings; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未量件溫會錯判固化不足。","failureEn":"Unmeasured part temperature can hide undercure.","check":"引用材料資料而非自行猜測時間溫度。","checkEn":"The plan uses material data rather than invented settings.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-125-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"設備設定值不同於零件溫度。","textEn":"Tool setpoint differs from part temperature."},{"id":"pk-125-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未量件溫會錯判固化不足；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Unmeasured part temperature can hide undercure. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「規劃固化歷程驗證」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Plan cure-history verification\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["離散程度與偏移分開報告","引用材料資料而非自行猜測時間溫度","支承點不形成未評估應力集中"],"optionsEn":["Scatter and bias are reported separately","The plan uses material data rather than invented settings","Support points avoid unassessed stress concentrations"],"answer":1,"explanation":"設備設定值不同於零件溫度。本步要確認：引用材料資料而非自行猜測時間溫度；常見誤判是：未量件溫會錯判固化不足。","explanationEn":"Tool setpoint differs from part temperature. Verify: The plan uses material data rather than invented settings. A common misinterpretation is: Unmeasured part temperature can hide undercure."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-124"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-126","order":22,"sequence":126,"title":"檢查固化收縮位移","titleEn":"Inspect cure-shrinkage displacement","objective":"比較固化前後位置與高度，並能說明「固化可能改變界面應力與姿態」。","objectiveEn":"Compare position and height before and after cure and explain: Curing can change interface stress and pose.","instruction":"比較固化前後位置與高度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：位移變化未超過教學設計包絡。","instructionEn":"Compare position and height before and after cure. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Displacement remains within the teaching envelope.","observation":"位移變化未超過教學設計包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Displacement remains within the teaching envelope; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只驗貼下瞬間會漏掉固化漂移。","failureEn":"Placement-only checks miss cure drift.","check":"位移變化未超過教學設計包絡。","checkEn":"Displacement remains within the teaching envelope.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-126-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"固化可能改變界面應力與姿態。","textEn":"Curing can change interface stress and pose."},{"id":"pk-126-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只驗貼下瞬間會漏掉固化漂移；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Placement-only checks miss cure drift. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查固化收縮位移」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect cure-shrinkage displacement\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["晶粒抬升時未被局部膜區拖住","預測流路保留氣體排出方向","位移變化未超過教學設計包絡"],"optionsEn":["No tape region restrains the lifted die","Predicted flow preserves air-escape paths","Displacement remains within the teaching envelope"],"answer":2,"explanation":"固化可能改變界面應力與姿態。本步要確認：位移變化未超過教學設計包絡；常見誤判是：只驗貼下瞬間會漏掉固化漂移。","explanationEn":"Curing can change interface stress and pose. Verify: Displacement remains within the teaching envelope. A common misinterpretation is: Placement-only checks miss cure drift."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-125"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-127","order":23,"sequence":127,"title":"辨識接合層空洞","titleEn":"Identify bond-layer voids","objective":"對照聲學或X光資料與材料透視性，並能說明「不同方法對空洞敏感度不同」。","objectiveEn":"Match acoustic or X-ray data to material visibility and explain: Methods differ in void sensitivity.","instruction":"對照聲學或X光資料與材料透視性。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：空洞結論注明方法與遮蔽限制。","instructionEn":"Match acoustic or X-ray data to material visibility. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Void conclusions state method and visibility limits.","observation":"空洞結論注明方法與遮蔽限制；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Void conclusions state method and visibility limits; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"看不到空洞不等於所有區域無空洞。","failureEn":"Invisible voids do not prove void-free coverage.","check":"空洞結論注明方法與遮蔽限制。","checkEn":"Void conclusions state method and visibility limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-127-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同方法對空洞敏感度不同。","textEn":"Methods differ in void sensitivity."},{"id":"pk-127-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"看不到空洞不等於所有區域無空洞；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Invisible voids do not prove void-free coverage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識接合層空洞」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify bond-layer voids\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["空洞結論注明方法與遮蔽限制","空吸與漏氣不被判作成功","溢膠不進入禁止接觸區"],"optionsEn":["Void conclusions state method and visibility limits","Empty pickup and leaks are not counted as success","Bleed stays outside prohibited regions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同方法對空洞敏感度不同。本步要確認：空洞結論注明方法與遮蔽限制；常見誤判是：看不到空洞不等於所有區域無空洞。","explanationEn":"Methods differ in void sensitivity. Verify: Void conclusions state method and visibility limits. A common misinterpretation is: Invisible voids do not prove void-free coverage."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-126"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-128","order":24,"sequence":128,"title":"判讀晶粒剪切失效","titleEn":"Interpret die-shear failures","objective":"同時記錄峰值與破壞面位置，並能說明「破壞位置有助區分材料與界面弱點」。","objectiveEn":"Record peak force and fracture location and explain: Fracture location distinguishes bulk and interface weakness.","instruction":"同時記錄峰值與破壞面位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：數值與破壞模式成對呈現。","instructionEn":"Record peak force and fracture location. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Values are paired with failure modes.","observation":"數值與破壞模式成對呈現；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Values are paired with failure modes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單比峰值可能忽略不同破壞機制。","failureEn":"Peak-only comparison ignores different mechanisms.","check":"數值與破壞模式成對呈現。","checkEn":"Values are paired with failure modes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-128-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"破壞位置有助區分材料與界面弱點。","textEn":"Fracture location distinguishes bulk and interface weakness."},{"id":"pk-128-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單比峰值可能忽略不同破壞機制；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Peak-only comparison ignores different mechanisms. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀晶粒剪切失效」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret die-shear failures\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["膜材分支有獨立貼合與檢查需求","數值與破壞模式成對呈現","新增缺陷與原有缺陷分開記錄"],"optionsEn":["The film route has distinct bonding and inspection needs","Values are paired with failure modes","New and preexisting defects are separated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"破壞位置有助區分材料與界面弱點。本步要確認：數值與破壞模式成對呈現；常見誤判是：單比峰值可能忽略不同破壞機制。","explanationEn":"Fracture location distinguishes bulk and interface weakness. Verify: Values are paired with failure modes. A common misinterpretation is: Peak-only comparison ignores different mechanisms."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-127"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-129","order":25,"sequence":129,"title":"比較熱介面接觸品質","titleEn":"Compare thermal-interface contact","objective":"將空洞位置疊加預期熱流密度，並能說明「熱阻影響取決於空洞位置和接觸」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay void locations with expected heat flux and explain: Thermal impact depends on void location and contact.","instruction":"將空洞位置疊加預期熱流密度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：熱點附近的缺口被單獨評估。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Overlay void locations with expected heat flux. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Gaps near hot spots are evaluated separately. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"熱點附近的缺口被單獨評估；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Gaps near hot spots are evaluated separately; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"相同空洞比例不保證相同熱阻。","failureEn":"Equal void fraction does not imply equal resistance.","check":"熱點附近的缺口被單獨評估。","checkEn":"Gaps near hot spots are evaluated separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-129-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"熱阻影響取決於空洞位置和接觸。","textEn":"Thermal impact depends on void location and contact."},{"id":"pk-129-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"相同空洞比例不保證相同熱阻；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Equal void fraction does not imply equal resistance. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-129-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設黏晶層厚 20 µm、k=2 W/(m·K)、面積 25 mm²，理想一維熱阻 0.4 K/W；10 W 導熱造成 4 K 溫差，尚未計界面與擴散熱阻。","textEn":"For a hypothetical 20 µm die-attach layer, k=2 W/(m·K) and area 25 mm², ideal 1D resistance is 0.4 K/W; 10 W gives 4 K rise before contact and spreading resistance."},{"id":"pk-129-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"空洞位置比面積比例本身更有意義：熱點正下方空洞可比邊角同面積空洞影響更大。應將影像與功率密度地圖配準。","textEn":"Void location matters beyond area fraction: a void under a hotspot may be worse than the same area at a corner. Register inspection images with power-density maps."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「比較熱介面接觸品質」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Compare thermal-interface contact\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["多點殘差都落在本例容許範圍","中心與角點誤差均符合示意規則","熱點附近的缺口被單獨評估"],"optionsEn":["All reference residuals meet exercise limits","Center and corner errors meet exercise rules","Gaps near hot spots are evaluated separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱阻影響取決於空洞位置和接觸。本步要確認：熱點附近的缺口被單獨評估；常見誤判是：相同空洞比例不保證相同熱阻。","explanationEn":"Thermal impact depends on void location and contact. Verify: Gaps near hot spots are evaluated separately. A common misinterpretation is: Equal void fraction does not imply equal resistance."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection","v9deep-thermal-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-128"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-130","order":26,"sequence":130,"title":"交付貼晶界面紀錄","titleEn":"Release die-attach interface records","objective":"整合座標、BLT、傾斜及固化證據，並能說明「下游打線或其他組裝需要穩定界面」。","objectiveEn":"Combine pose, BLT, tilt and cure evidence and explain: Downstream assembly needs a stable interface.","instruction":"整合座標、BLT、傾斜及固化證據。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常件不混入下一分支的合格清單。","instructionEn":"Combine pose, BLT, tilt and cure evidence. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Abnormal parts stay out of downstream accepted lists.","observation":"異常件不混入下一分支的合格清單；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Abnormal parts stay out of downstream accepted lists; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只記已貼晶會漏掉界面品質。","failureEn":"Recording attachment alone misses interface quality.","check":"異常件不混入下一分支的合格清單。","checkEn":"Abnormal parts stay out of downstream accepted lists.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-130-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"下游打線或其他組裝需要穩定界面。","textEn":"Downstream assembly needs a stable interface."},{"id":"pk-130-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只記已貼晶會漏掉界面品質；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Recording attachment alone misses interface quality. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「交付貼晶界面紀錄」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release die-attach interface records\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常件不混入下一分支的合格清單","所有定位標記與目標方向一致","異常尖峰已連到檢查假設"],"optionsEn":["Abnormal parts stay out of downstream accepted lists","All orientation marks match the target","Abnormal spikes have inspection hypotheses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"下游打線或其他組裝需要穩定界面。本步要確認：異常件不混入下一分支的合格清單；常見誤判是：只記已貼晶會漏掉界面品質。","explanationEn":"Downstream assembly needs a stable interface. Verify: Abnormal parts stay out of downstream accepted lists. A common misinterpretation is: Recording attachment alone misses interface quality."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-dieattach","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-129"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m06","order":6,"sequence":6,"title":"打線接合與接點檢核","titleEn":"Wirebonding and joint verification","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查打線接合與接點檢核的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for wirebonding and joint verification. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"打線專屬分支，不能當作覆晶或扇出的必要站。","routeEn":"Wirebond-only branch, not a required flipchip or fan-out station.","sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-131","order":1,"sequence":131,"title":"確認打線專屬路線","titleEn":"Confirm the wirebond-only route","objective":"將周邊焊墊連到導線架或基板，並能說明「打線不是覆晶凸塊後的必經站」。","objectiveEn":"Connect peripheral pads to leadframe or substrate and explain: Wirebonding is not mandatory after flipchip bumping.","instruction":"將周邊焊墊連到導線架或基板。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：流程圖未把兩分支強制串接。","instructionEn":"Connect peripheral pads to leadframe or substrate. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The map does not force both branches in series.","observation":"流程圖未把兩分支強制串接；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The map does not force both branches in series; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"混接分支會增加不存在的接點。","failureEn":"Mixed branches introduce nonexistent interconnects.","check":"流程圖未把兩分支強制串接。","checkEn":"The map does not force both branches in series.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-131-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"打線不是覆晶凸塊後的必經站。","textEn":"Wirebonding is not mandatory after flipchip bumping."},{"id":"pk-131-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"混接分支會增加不存在的接點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mixed branches introduce nonexistent interconnects. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「確認打線專屬路線」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Confirm the wirebond-only route\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["偏心與球徑分開記錄","急彎位置與後續強度證據聯讀","流程圖未把兩分支強制串接"],"optionsEn":["Eccentricity and diameter are recorded separately","Sharp bends are checked against strength evidence","The map does not force both branches in series"],"answer":2,"explanation":"打線不是覆晶凸塊後的必經站。本步要確認：流程圖未把兩分支強制串接；常見誤判是：混接分支會增加不存在的接點。","explanationEn":"Wirebonding is not mandatory after flipchip bumping. Verify: The map does not force both branches in series. A common misinterpretation is: Mixed branches introduce nonexistent interconnects."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-130"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-132","order":2,"sequence":132,"title":"檢查焊墊潔淨狀態","titleEn":"Inspect bond-pad cleanliness","objective":"比較焊墊殘留與可接合面，並能說明「殘留可阻止有效金屬接觸」。","objectiveEn":"Compare pad residue and bondable area and explain: Residue can prevent effective metal contact.","instruction":"比較焊墊殘留與可接合面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：疑似污染先隔離再判定。","instructionEn":"Compare pad residue and bondable area. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Suspected contamination is isolated before disposition.","observation":"疑似污染先隔離再判定；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Suspected contamination is isolated before disposition; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"加大能量未必能彌補污染。","failureEn":"More energy may not compensate for contamination.","check":"疑似污染先隔離再判定。","checkEn":"Suspected contamination is isolated before disposition.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-132-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"殘留可阻止有效金屬接觸。","textEn":"Residue can prevent effective metal contact."},{"id":"pk-132-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"加大能量未必能彌補污染；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"More energy may not compensate for contamination. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查焊墊潔淨狀態」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect bond-pad cleanliness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["疑似污染先隔離再判定","環境需求有材料來源支持","接點輪廓位於允許金屬區"],"optionsEn":["Suspected contamination is isolated before disposition","Environmental needs have material support","The footprint stays on permitted metal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘留可阻止有效金屬接觸。本步要確認：疑似污染先隔離再判定；常見誤判是：加大能量未必能彌補污染。","explanationEn":"Residue can prevent effective metal contact. Verify: Suspected contamination is isolated before disposition. A common misinterpretation is: More energy may not compensate for contamination."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-131"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-133","order":3,"sequence":133,"title":"配對線材與焊墊","titleEn":"Match wire and pad metallurgy","objective":"列出線材、焊墊與環境需求，並能說明「金屬配對影響接合與長期反應」。","objectiveEn":"List wire, pad and environmental requirements and explain: Metal pairing affects bonding and aging.","instruction":"列出線材、焊墊與環境需求。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每種配對都有驗證路徑。","instructionEn":"List wire, pad and environmental requirements. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each pair has a validation path.","observation":"每種配對都有驗證路徑；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each pair has a validation path; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"金線經驗不能直接套用銅線。","failureEn":"Gold-wire experience does not directly transfer to copper.","check":"每種配對都有驗證路徑。","checkEn":"Each pair has a validation path.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-133-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"金屬配對影響接合與長期反應。","textEn":"Metal pairing affects bonding and aging."},{"id":"pk-133-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"金線經驗不能直接套用銅線；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Gold-wire experience does not directly transfer to copper. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「配對線材與焊墊」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Match wire and pad metallurgy\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["沒有抬起或意外殘線短接","每種配對都有驗證路徑","考慮位置偏差後仍在開口內"],"optionsEn":["No lifted bond or unintended tail short appears","Each pair has a validation path","The footprint stays inside after position error"],"answer":1,"explanation":"金屬配對影響接合與長期反應。本步要確認：每種配對都有驗證路徑；常見誤判是：金線經驗不能直接套用銅線。","explanationEn":"Metal pairing affects bonding and aging. Verify: Each pair has a validation path. A common misinterpretation is: Gold-wire experience does not directly transfer to copper."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-132"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-134","order":4,"sequence":134,"title":"評估線徑與間距","titleEn":"Assess wire diameter and pitch","objective":"把線徑與焊墊可用面積相比，並能說明「線徑同時影響電性與幾何」。","objectiveEn":"Compare wire diameter with usable pad area and explain: Wire diameter affects electrical and geometric behavior.","instruction":"把線徑與焊墊可用面積相比。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：線徑選擇不侵入相鄰接點包絡。","instructionEn":"Compare wire diameter with usable pad area. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Diameter selection respects neighboring envelopes.","observation":"線徑選擇不侵入相鄰接點包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Diameter selection respects neighboring envelopes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只按載流量選線可能無法接合。","failureEn":"Current-only selection may not fit the pad.","check":"線徑選擇不侵入相鄰接點包絡。","checkEn":"Diameter selection respects neighboring envelopes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-134-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"線徑同時影響電性與幾何。","textEn":"Wire diameter affects electrical and geometric behavior."},{"id":"pk-134-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只按載流量選線可能無法接合；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Current-only selection may not fit the pad. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估線徑與間距」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess wire diameter and pitch\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常峰值不被平均化隱藏","尾長變化與時序事件能對照","線徑選擇不侵入相鄰接點包絡"],"optionsEn":["Abnormal peaks are not hidden by averaging","Tail variation maps to timing events","Diameter selection respects neighboring envelopes"],"answer":2,"explanation":"線徑同時影響電性與幾何。本步要確認：線徑選擇不侵入相鄰接點包絡；常見誤判是：只按載流量選線可能無法接合。","explanationEn":"Wire diameter affects electrical and geometric behavior. Verify: Diameter selection respects neighboring envelopes. A common misinterpretation is: Current-only selection may not fit the pad."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-133"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-135","order":5,"sequence":135,"title":"檢查毛細管端部幾何","titleEn":"Inspect capillary-tip geometry","objective":"對照孔徑與端面形狀的角色，並能說明「工具形狀影響球壓痕與第二接點」。","objectiveEn":"Compare bore and tip-face functions and explain: Tool shape affects ball impression and second bond.","instruction":"對照孔徑與端面形狀的角色。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：工具輪廓符合示意接點需求。","instructionEn":"Compare bore and tip-face functions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Tool geometry fits the exercise joint.","observation":"工具輪廓符合示意接點需求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Tool geometry fits the exercise joint; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"磨損端面可能改變接點形狀。","failureEn":"Worn tips can change bond shape.","check":"工具輪廓符合示意接點需求。","checkEn":"Tool geometry fits the exercise joint.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-135-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"工具形狀影響球壓痕與第二接點。","textEn":"Tool shape affects ball impression and second bond."},{"id":"pk-135-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"磨損端面可能改變接點形狀；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Worn tips can change bond shape. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查毛細管端部幾何」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect capillary-tip geometry\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["工具輪廓符合示意接點需求","耦合異常有支承與工具檢查","開路與短路都有明確判定"],"optionsEn":["Tool geometry fits the exercise joint","Coupling anomalies trigger support and tool checks","Opens and shorts have explicit dispositions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"工具形狀影響球壓痕與第二接點。本步要確認：工具輪廓符合示意接點需求；常見誤判是：磨損端面可能改變接點形狀。","explanationEn":"Tool shape affects ball impression and second bond. Verify: Tool geometry fits the exercise joint. A common misinterpretation is: Worn tips can change bond shape."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-134"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-136","order":6,"sequence":136,"title":"核對線材進給阻力","titleEn":"Review wire-feed resistance","objective":"比較送料順暢與卡滯訊號，並能說明「送料阻力會影響線弧與尾長」。","objectiveEn":"Compare smooth-feed and snag signals and explain: Feed resistance affects loops and tail length.","instruction":"比較送料順暢與卡滯訊號。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：送料異常能被偵測並隔離。","instructionEn":"Compare smooth-feed and snag signals. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Feed faults are detectable and isolated.","observation":"送料異常能被偵測並隔離；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Feed faults are detectable and isolated; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"卡線會被誤認為線弧程式錯誤。","failureEn":"Snags can mimic loop-program errors.","check":"送料異常能被偵測並隔離。","checkEn":"Feed faults are detectable and isolated.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-136-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"送料阻力會影響線弧與尾長。","textEn":"Feed resistance affects loops and tail length."},{"id":"pk-136-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"卡線會被誤認為線弧程式錯誤；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Snags can mimic loop-program errors. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對線材進給阻力」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review wire-feed resistance\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["拉力數據附測試幾何與模式","送料異常能被偵測並隔離","形狀與焊墊邊界一同核對"],"optionsEn":["Pull data include geometry and failure mode","Feed faults are detectable and isolated","Shape is checked against pad boundaries"],"answer":1,"explanation":"送料阻力會影響線弧與尾長。本步要確認：送料異常能被偵測並隔離；常見誤判是：卡線會被誤認為線弧程式錯誤。","explanationEn":"Feed resistance affects loops and tail length. Verify: Feed faults are detectable and isolated. A common misinterpretation is: Snags can mimic loop-program errors."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-135"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-137","order":7,"sequence":137,"title":"確認基板夾持支承","titleEn":"Confirm substrate clamping support","objective":"檢查接合位置下的支承連續性，並能說明「支承柔度改變能量傳遞」。","objectiveEn":"Check support beneath bonding locations and explain: Support compliance changes energy transmission.","instruction":"檢查接合位置下的支承連續性。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：關鍵接點下沒有未評估懸空。","instructionEn":"Check support beneath bonding locations. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Critical sites have no unassessed unsupported spans.","observation":"關鍵接點下沒有未評估懸空；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Critical sites have no unassessed unsupported spans; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"局部彈跳可造成不穩定接點。","failureEn":"Local bounce causes inconsistent bonds.","check":"關鍵接點下沒有未評估懸空。","checkEn":"Critical sites have no unassessed unsupported spans.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-137-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"支承柔度改變能量傳遞。","textEn":"Support compliance changes energy transmission."},{"id":"pk-137-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"局部彈跳可造成不穩定接點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Local bounce causes inconsistent bonds. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「確認基板夾持支承」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Confirm substrate clamping support\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["潛在底層破壞有專屬檢查","剪切結果包含工具條件與破壞面","關鍵接點下沒有未評估懸空"],"optionsEn":["Potential underlying damage receives dedicated inspection","Shear results include tooling and fracture surface","Critical sites have no unassessed unsupported spans"],"answer":2,"explanation":"支承柔度改變能量傳遞。本步要確認：關鍵接點下沒有未評估懸空；常見誤判是：局部彈跳可造成不穩定接點。","explanationEn":"Support compliance changes energy transmission. Verify: Critical sites have no unassessed unsupported spans. A common misinterpretation is: Local bounce causes inconsistent bonds."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-136"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-138","order":8,"sequence":138,"title":"理解自由空氣球形成","titleEn":"Understand free-air-ball formation","objective":"對照尾線與球化示意的體積關係，並能說明「球化需形成可重複的初始端形」。","objectiveEn":"Compare tail wire and ball volume schematically and explain: Ball formation needs a repeatable starting geometry.","instruction":"對照尾線與球化示意的體積關係。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：圖中保留材料體積一致性。","instructionEn":"Compare tail wire and ball volume schematically. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The model preserves material-volume consistency.","observation":"圖中保留材料體積一致性；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The model preserves material-volume consistency; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"尾長波動可能導致球徑波動。","failureEn":"Tail-length variation can vary ball diameter.","check":"圖中保留材料體積一致性。","checkEn":"The model preserves material-volume consistency.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-138-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"球化需形成可重複的初始端形。","textEn":"Ball formation needs a repeatable starting geometry."},{"id":"pk-138-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"尾長波動可能導致球徑波動；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Tail-length variation can vary ball diameter. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「理解自由空氣球形成」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Understand free-air-ball formation\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["圖中保留材料體積一致性","全弧線未穿入限制包絡","抽樣範圍與隔離件清單完整"],"optionsEn":["The model preserves material-volume consistency","The entire loop avoids forbidden envelopes","Sample coverage and quarantine lists are complete"],"answer":0,"explanation":"球化需形成可重複的初始端形。本步要確認：圖中保留材料體積一致性；常見誤判是：尾長波動可能導致球徑波動。","explanationEn":"Ball formation needs a repeatable starting geometry. Verify: The model preserves material-volume consistency. A common misinterpretation is: Tail-length variation can vary ball diameter."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-137"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-139","order":9,"sequence":139,"title":"檢查初始球偏心","titleEn":"Inspect initial-ball eccentricity","objective":"量測球心相對線軸位置，並能說明「偏心球會改變壓合對稱性」。","objectiveEn":"Measure ball center relative to wire axis and explain: Off-center balls change bonding symmetry.","instruction":"量測球心相對線軸位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：偏心與球徑分開記錄。","instructionEn":"Measure ball center relative to wire axis. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Eccentricity and diameter are recorded separately.","observation":"偏心與球徑分開記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Eccentricity and diameter are recorded separately; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平均球徑正常仍可能偏心。","failureEn":"Normal average diameter can hide eccentricity.","check":"偏心與球徑分開記錄。","checkEn":"Eccentricity and diameter are recorded separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-139-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"偏心球會改變壓合對稱性。","textEn":"Off-center balls change bonding symmetry."},{"id":"pk-139-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平均球徑正常仍可能偏心；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Normal average diameter can hide eccentricity. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查初始球偏心」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect initial-ball eccentricity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["流程圖未把兩分支強制串接","偏心與球徑分開記錄","最低點仍有指定隔離裕量"],"optionsEn":["The map does not force both branches in series","Eccentricity and diameter are recorded separately","The lowest point retains required clearance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏心球會改變壓合對稱性。本步要確認：偏心與球徑分開記錄；常見誤判是：平均球徑正常仍可能偏心。","explanationEn":"Off-center balls change bonding symmetry. Verify: Eccentricity and diameter are recorded separately. A common misinterpretation is: Normal average diameter can hide eccentricity."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-138"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-140","order":10,"sequence":140,"title":"辨識線材氧化保護需求","titleEn":"Identify wire oxidation protection","objective":"核對線材與指定保護環境，並能說明「保護要求依線材與製程而變」。","objectiveEn":"Match wire material to its protection needs and explain: Protection needs vary by wire and process.","instruction":"核對線材與指定保護環境。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：環境需求有材料來源支持。","instructionEn":"Match wire material to its protection needs. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Environmental needs have material support.","observation":"環境需求有材料來源支持；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Environmental needs have material support; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把惰性環境當通用配方不恰當。","failureEn":"Inert atmosphere is not a universal recipe.","check":"環境需求有材料來源支持。","checkEn":"Environmental needs have material support.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-140-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"保護要求依線材與製程而變。","textEn":"Protection needs vary by wire and process."},{"id":"pk-140-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把惰性環境當通用配方不恰當；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Inert atmosphere is not a universal recipe. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識線材氧化保護需求」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify wire oxidation protection\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["交叉點的高度差被量測","疑似污染先隔離再判定","環境需求有材料來源支持"],"optionsEn":["Height separation is measured at crossings","Suspected contamination is isolated before disposition","Environmental needs have material support"],"answer":2,"explanation":"保護要求依線材與製程而變。本步要確認：環境需求有材料來源支持；常見誤判是：把惰性環境當通用配方不恰當。","explanationEn":"Protection needs vary by wire and process. Verify: Environmental needs have material support. A common misinterpretation is: Inert atmosphere is not a universal recipe."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-139"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-141","order":11,"sequence":141,"title":"校準第一接點位置","titleEn":"Calibrate the first-bond location","objective":"疊加球接點包絡與焊墊開口，並能說明「球接點必須留在可接合區」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay ball footprint and pad opening and explain: The ball footprint must stay bondable.","instruction":"疊加球接點包絡與焊墊開口。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：考慮位置偏差後仍在開口內。","instructionEn":"Overlay ball footprint and pad opening. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The footprint stays inside after position error.","observation":"考慮位置偏差後仍在開口內；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The footprint stays inside after position error; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只對焊墊中心不查球徑會越界。","failureEn":"Centering alone can allow an oversized ball.","check":"考慮位置偏差後仍在開口內。","checkEn":"The footprint stays inside after position error.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-141-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"球接點必須留在可接合區。","textEn":"The ball footprint must stay bondable."},{"id":"pk-141-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只對焊墊中心不查球徑會越界；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Centering alone can allow an oversized ball. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「校準第一接點位置」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calibrate the first-bond location\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["考慮位置偏差後仍在開口內","急彎位置與後續強度證據聯讀","每種配對都有驗證路徑"],"optionsEn":["The footprint stays inside after position error","Sharp bends are checked against strength evidence","Each pair has a validation path"],"answer":0,"explanation":"球接點必須留在可接合區。本步要確認：考慮位置偏差後仍在開口內；常見誤判是：只對焊墊中心不查球徑會越界。","explanationEn":"The ball footprint must stay bondable. Verify: The footprint stays inside after position error. A common misinterpretation is: Centering alone can allow an oversized ball."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-140"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-142","order":12,"sequence":142,"title":"判讀第一接點力訊號","titleEn":"Interpret first-bond force traces","objective":"區分接觸、加載與卸載區段，並能說明「受力歷程影響接觸與下層損傷」。","objectiveEn":"Separate contact, loading and unloading and explain: Force history affects contact and underlying damage.","instruction":"區分接觸、加載與卸載區段。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常峰值不被平均化隱藏。","instructionEn":"Separate contact, loading and unloading. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Abnormal peaks are not hidden by averaging.","observation":"異常峰值不被平均化隱藏；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Abnormal peaks are not hidden by averaging; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過大負荷可能造成焊墊下裂損。","failureEn":"Excess load can damage structures below pads.","check":"異常峰值不被平均化隱藏。","checkEn":"Abnormal peaks are not hidden by averaging.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-142-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"受力歷程影響接觸與下層損傷。","textEn":"Force history affects contact and underlying damage."},{"id":"pk-142-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過大負荷可能造成焊墊下裂損；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excess load can damage structures below pads. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀第一接點力訊號」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret first-bond force traces\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["線徑選擇不侵入相鄰接點包絡","異常峰值不被平均化隱藏","接點輪廓位於允許金屬區"],"optionsEn":["Diameter selection respects neighboring envelopes","Abnormal peaks are not hidden by averaging","The footprint stays on permitted metal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"受力歷程影響接觸與下層損傷。本步要確認：異常峰值不被平均化隱藏；常見誤判是：過大負荷可能造成焊墊下裂損。","explanationEn":"Force history affects contact and underlying damage. Verify: Abnormal peaks are not hidden by averaging. A common misinterpretation is: Excess load can damage structures below pads."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-141"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-143","order":13,"sequence":143,"title":"判讀超音波耦合","titleEn":"Interpret ultrasonic coupling","objective":"比較振動輸入與接合回應，並能說明「輸入設定不等於界面實際能量」。","objectiveEn":"Compare vibration input with bonding response and explain: Input settings do not equal interface energy.","instruction":"比較振動輸入與接合回應。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：耦合異常有支承與工具檢查。","instructionEn":"Compare vibration input with bonding response. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Coupling anomalies trigger support and tool checks.","observation":"耦合異常有支承與工具檢查；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Coupling anomalies trigger support and tool checks; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只調設定值可能掩蓋鬆動支承。","failureEn":"Settings alone can hide loose support.","check":"耦合異常有支承與工具檢查。","checkEn":"Coupling anomalies trigger support and tool checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-143-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"輸入設定不等於界面實際能量。","textEn":"Input settings do not equal interface energy."},{"id":"pk-143-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只調設定值可能掩蓋鬆動支承；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Settings alone can hide loose support. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀超音波耦合」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret ultrasonic coupling\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["沒有抬起或意外殘線短接","工具輪廓符合示意接點需求","耦合異常有支承與工具檢查"],"optionsEn":["No lifted bond or unintended tail short appears","Tool geometry fits the exercise joint","Coupling anomalies trigger support and tool checks"],"answer":2,"explanation":"輸入設定不等於界面實際能量。本步要確認：耦合異常有支承與工具檢查；常見誤判是：只調設定值可能掩蓋鬆動支承。","explanationEn":"Input settings do not equal interface energy. Verify: Coupling anomalies trigger support and tool checks. A common misinterpretation is: Settings alone can hide loose support."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-142"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-144","order":14,"sequence":144,"title":"量測壓後球形","titleEn":"Measure bonded-ball geometry","objective":"量測球高與外徑及對稱性，並能說明「壓後幾何反映塑性變形程度」。","objectiveEn":"Measure ball height, diameter and symmetry and explain: Bonded geometry reflects plastic deformation.","instruction":"量測球高與外徑及對稱性。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：形狀與焊墊邊界一同核對。","instructionEn":"Measure ball height, diameter and symmetry. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Shape is checked against pad boundaries.","observation":"形狀與焊墊邊界一同核對；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Shape is checked against pad boundaries; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"扁平大球不自動代表強接合。","failureEn":"A broad flat ball is not automatically strong.","check":"形狀與焊墊邊界一同核對。","checkEn":"Shape is checked against pad boundaries.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-144-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"壓後幾何反映塑性變形程度。","textEn":"Bonded geometry reflects plastic deformation."},{"id":"pk-144-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"扁平大球不自動代表強接合；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A broad flat ball is not automatically strong. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測壓後球形」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure bonded-ball geometry\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["形狀與焊墊邊界一同核對","尾長變化與時序事件能對照","送料異常能被偵測並隔離"],"optionsEn":["Shape is checked against pad boundaries","Tail variation maps to timing events","Feed faults are detectable and isolated"],"answer":0,"explanation":"壓後幾何反映塑性變形程度。本步要確認：形狀與焊墊邊界一同核對；常見誤判是：扁平大球不自動代表強接合。","explanationEn":"Bonded geometry reflects plastic deformation. Verify: Shape is checked against pad boundaries. A common misinterpretation is: A broad flat ball is not automatically strong."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-143"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-145","order":15,"sequence":145,"title":"檢查焊墊下損傷","titleEn":"Inspect damage beneath pads","objective":"比較表面合格與截面異常案例，並能說明「表面外觀無法排除底層裂紋」。","objectiveEn":"Compare acceptable surfaces with abnormal sections and explain: Surface appearance cannot exclude underlying cracks.","instruction":"比較表面合格與截面異常案例。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：潛在底層破壞有專屬檢查。","instructionEn":"Compare acceptable surfaces with abnormal sections. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Potential underlying damage receives dedicated inspection.","observation":"潛在底層破壞有專屬檢查；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Potential underlying damage receives dedicated inspection; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只做外觀檢查會漏掉cratering。","failureEn":"Visual inspection alone misses cratering.","check":"潛在底層破壞有專屬檢查。","checkEn":"Potential underlying damage receives dedicated inspection.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-145-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"表面外觀無法排除底層裂紋。","textEn":"Surface appearance cannot exclude underlying cracks."},{"id":"pk-145-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只做外觀檢查會漏掉cratering；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Visual inspection alone misses cratering. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查焊墊下損傷」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect damage beneath pads\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["關鍵接點下沒有未評估懸空","潛在底層破壞有專屬檢查","開路與短路都有明確判定"],"optionsEn":["Critical sites have no unassessed unsupported spans","Potential underlying damage receives dedicated inspection","Opens and shorts have explicit dispositions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面外觀無法排除底層裂紋。本步要確認：潛在底層破壞有專屬檢查；常見誤判是：只做外觀檢查會漏掉cratering。","explanationEn":"Surface appearance cannot exclude underlying cracks. Verify: Potential underlying damage receives dedicated inspection. A common misinterpretation is: Visual inspection alone misses cratering."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-144"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-146","order":16,"sequence":146,"title":"建立線弧高度包絡","titleEn":"Define wire-loop height envelope","objective":"畫出線弧及模封空間限制，並能說明「線弧必須滿足三維間隙」。","objectiveEn":"Draw loops within mold-clearance limits and explain: Loops must satisfy three-dimensional clearance.","instruction":"畫出線弧及模封空間限制。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：全弧線未穿入限制包絡。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Draw loops within mold-clearance limits. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The entire loop avoids forbidden envelopes. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"全弧線未穿入限制包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The entire loop avoids forbidden envelopes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看最高點會漏掉局部碰線。","failureEn":"Peak-height checks miss local collisions.","check":"全弧線未穿入限制包絡。","checkEn":"The entire loop avoids forbidden envelopes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-146-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"線弧必須滿足三維間隙。","textEn":"Loops must satisfy three-dimensional clearance."},{"id":"pk-146-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看最高點會漏掉局部碰線；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Peak-height checks miss local collisions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-146-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"教學線弧名目高 150 µm、變動 ±20 µm，上方間隙 180 µm，最壞剩 10 µm；還需考慮模流造成的橫向偏移，而不只垂直高度。","textEn":"A hypothetical 150±20 µm loop under 180 µm clearance leaves 10 µm worst-case vertical margin; molding-induced lateral sweep must also be considered."},{"id":"pk-146-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"用三維線弧包絡檢查相鄰線和晶粒邊緣。只看正視圖可能把前後交叉誤判成安全，也可能把不同高度誤判短路。","textEn":"Check adjacent wires and die edges using 3D loop envelopes. A front view can hide depth crossings or misclassify different-height wires as shorts."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立線弧高度包絡」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Define wire-loop height envelope\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["拉力數據附測試幾何與模式","圖中保留材料體積一致性","全弧線未穿入限制包絡"],"optionsEn":["Pull data include geometry and failure mode","The model preserves material-volume consistency","The entire loop avoids forbidden envelopes"],"answer":2,"explanation":"線弧必須滿足三維間隙。本步要確認：全弧線未穿入限制包絡；常見誤判是：只看最高點會漏掉局部碰線。","explanationEn":"Loops must satisfy three-dimensional clearance. Verify: The entire loop avoids forbidden envelopes. A common misinterpretation is: Peak-height checks miss local collisions."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-145"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-147","order":17,"sequence":147,"title":"檢查線弧下垂","titleEn":"Inspect wire-loop sag","objective":"比較中段高度與下方結構，並能說明「跨距及機械狀態影響下垂」。","objectiveEn":"Compare midspan height with underlying features and explain: Span and mechanical condition affect sag.","instruction":"比較中段高度與下方結構。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最低點仍有指定隔離裕量。","instructionEn":"Compare midspan height with underlying features. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The lowest point retains required clearance.","observation":"最低點仍有指定隔離裕量；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The lowest point retains required clearance; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"端點高度正確不能保證中段安全。","failureEn":"Correct endpoints do not guarantee midspan safety.","check":"最低點仍有指定隔離裕量。","checkEn":"The lowest point retains required clearance.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-147-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"跨距及機械狀態影響下垂。","textEn":"Span and mechanical condition affect sag."},{"id":"pk-147-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"端點高度正確不能保證中段安全；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Correct endpoints do not guarantee midspan safety. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查線弧下垂」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect wire-loop sag\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最低點仍有指定隔離裕量","剪切結果包含工具條件與破壞面","偏心與球徑分開記錄"],"optionsEn":["The lowest point retains required clearance","Shear results include tooling and fracture surface","Eccentricity and diameter are recorded separately"],"answer":0,"explanation":"跨距及機械狀態影響下垂。本步要確認：最低點仍有指定隔離裕量；常見誤判是：端點高度正確不能保證中段安全。","explanationEn":"Span and mechanical condition affect sag. Verify: The lowest point retains required clearance. A common misinterpretation is: Correct endpoints do not guarantee midspan safety."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-146"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-148","order":18,"sequence":148,"title":"檢查相鄰線交叉","titleEn":"Inspect neighboring-wire crossings","objective":"以側視和俯視核對交叉區，並能說明「俯視相交不必然代表實際接觸」。","objectiveEn":"Inspect crossings in top and side views and explain: Top-view crossing does not necessarily mean contact.","instruction":"以側視和俯視核對交叉區。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：交叉點的高度差被量測。","instructionEn":"Inspect crossings in top and side views. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Height separation is measured at crossings.","observation":"交叉點的高度差被量測；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Height separation is measured at crossings; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"二維投影容易誤判短路。","failureEn":"Two-dimensional projection can misclassify shorts.","check":"交叉點的高度差被量測。","checkEn":"Height separation is measured at crossings.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-148-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"俯視相交不必然代表實際接觸。","textEn":"Top-view crossing does not necessarily mean contact."},{"id":"pk-148-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"二維投影容易誤判短路；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Two-dimensional projection can misclassify shorts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查相鄰線交叉」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect neighboring-wire crossings\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["環境需求有材料來源支持","交叉點的高度差被量測","抽樣範圍與隔離件清單完整"],"optionsEn":["Environmental needs have material support","Height separation is measured at crossings","Sample coverage and quarantine lists are complete"],"answer":1,"explanation":"俯視相交不必然代表實際接觸。本步要確認：交叉點的高度差被量測；常見誤判是：二維投影容易誤判短路。","explanationEn":"Top-view crossing does not necessarily mean contact. Verify: Height separation is measured at crossings. A common misinterpretation is: Two-dimensional projection can misclassify shorts."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-147"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-149","order":19,"sequence":149,"title":"評估頸部與跟部彎曲","titleEn":"Assess neck and heel bending","objective":"標示接點附近曲率突變，並能說明「局部彎曲可集中循環應變」。","objectiveEn":"Mark curvature changes near bond ends and explain: Local bends concentrate cyclic strain.","instruction":"標示接點附近曲率突變。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：急彎位置與後續強度證據聯讀。","instructionEn":"Mark curvature changes near bond ends. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Sharp bends are checked against strength evidence.","observation":"急彎位置與後續強度證據聯讀；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Sharp bends are checked against strength evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只量線弧總高會漏掉局部急彎。","failureEn":"Total loop height misses local kinks.","check":"急彎位置與後續強度證據聯讀。","checkEn":"Sharp bends are checked against strength evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-149-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"局部彎曲可集中循環應變。","textEn":"Local bends concentrate cyclic strain."},{"id":"pk-149-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只量線弧總高會漏掉局部急彎；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Total loop height misses local kinks. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估頸部與跟部彎曲」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess neck and heel bending\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["流程圖未把兩分支強制串接","考慮位置偏差後仍在開口內","急彎位置與後續強度證據聯讀"],"optionsEn":["The map does not force both branches in series","The footprint stays inside after position error","Sharp bends are checked against strength evidence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部彎曲可集中循環應變。本步要確認：急彎位置與後續強度證據聯讀；常見誤判是：只量線弧總高會漏掉局部急彎。","explanationEn":"Local bends concentrate cyclic strain. Verify: Sharp bends are checked against strength evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Total loop height misses local kinks."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-148"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-150","order":20,"sequence":150,"title":"校準第二接點位置","titleEn":"Calibrate second-bond placement","objective":"把線尾接點對齊載體焊墊，並能說明「第二接點有不同工具接觸形狀」。","objectiveEn":"Align the second bond to the carrier pad and explain: The second bond has different tool-contact geometry.","instruction":"把線尾接點對齊載體焊墊。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：接點輪廓位於允許金屬區。","instructionEn":"Align the second bond to the carrier pad. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The footprint stays on permitted metal.","observation":"接點輪廓位於允許金屬區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The footprint stays on permitted metal; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"第一球合格不保證第二接點合格。","failureEn":"A good first ball does not validate the second bond.","check":"接點輪廓位於允許金屬區。","checkEn":"The footprint stays on permitted metal.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-150-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"第二接點有不同工具接觸形狀。","textEn":"The second bond has different tool-contact geometry."},{"id":"pk-150-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"第一球合格不保證第二接點合格；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A good first ball does not validate the second bond. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「校準第二接點位置」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calibrate second-bond placement\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["接點輪廓位於允許金屬區","疑似污染先隔離再判定","異常峰值不被平均化隱藏"],"optionsEn":["The footprint stays on permitted metal","Suspected contamination is isolated before disposition","Abnormal peaks are not hidden by averaging"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第二接點有不同工具接觸形狀。本步要確認：接點輪廓位於允許金屬區；常見誤判是：第一球合格不保證第二接點合格。","explanationEn":"The second bond has different tool-contact geometry. Verify: The footprint stays on permitted metal. A common misinterpretation is: A good first ball does not validate the second bond."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-149"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-151","order":21,"sequence":151,"title":"檢查第二接點形貌","titleEn":"Inspect second-bond morphology","objective":"比較線尾接合長度與殘線，並能說明「尾部接合需兼顧連接與斷線」。","objectiveEn":"Compare bonded length and remaining tail and explain: The second bond balances attachment and termination.","instruction":"比較線尾接合長度與殘線。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：沒有抬起或意外殘線短接。","instructionEn":"Compare bonded length and remaining tail. Check evidence you create or obtain against: No lifted bond or unintended tail short appears.","observation":"沒有抬起或意外殘線短接；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"No lifted bond or unintended tail short appears; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過長殘線可跨接相鄰金屬。","failureEn":"A long tail can bridge neighboring metal.","check":"沒有抬起或意外殘線短接。","checkEn":"No lifted bond or unintended tail short appears.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-151-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"尾部接合需兼顧連接與斷線。","textEn":"The second bond balances attachment and termination."},{"id":"pk-151-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過長殘線可跨接相鄰金屬；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A long tail can bridge neighboring metal. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查第二接點形貌」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect second-bond morphology\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["耦合異常有支承與工具檢查","沒有抬起或意外殘線短接","每種配對都有驗證路徑"],"optionsEn":["Coupling anomalies trigger support and tool checks","No lifted bond or unintended tail short appears","Each pair has a validation path"],"answer":1,"explanation":"尾部接合需兼顧連接與斷線。本步要確認：沒有抬起或意外殘線短接；常見誤判是：過長殘線可跨接相鄰金屬。","explanationEn":"The second bond balances attachment and termination. Verify: No lifted bond or unintended tail short appears. A common misinterpretation is: A long tail can bridge neighboring metal."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-150"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-152","order":22,"sequence":152,"title":"核對夾線與斷尾時序","titleEn":"Review clamp and tail-break timing","objective":"追蹤夾具閉合與工具抬升，並能說明「斷尾時序影響下一次初始球」。","objectiveEn":"Track clamp closure and tool lift and explain: Tail termination affects the next initial ball.","instruction":"追蹤夾具閉合與工具抬升。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：尾長變化與時序事件能對照。","instructionEn":"Track clamp closure and tool lift. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Tail variation maps to timing events.","observation":"尾長變化與時序事件能對照；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Tail variation maps to timing events; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"斷尾異常會跨循環傳遞。","failureEn":"Tail faults propagate into the next cycle.","check":"尾長變化與時序事件能對照。","checkEn":"Tail variation maps to timing events.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-152-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"斷尾時序影響下一次初始球。","textEn":"Tail termination affects the next initial ball."},{"id":"pk-152-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"斷尾異常會跨循環傳遞；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Tail faults propagate into the next cycle. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對夾線與斷尾時序」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review clamp and tail-break timing\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["線徑選擇不侵入相鄰接點包絡","形狀與焊墊邊界一同核對","尾長變化與時序事件能對照"],"optionsEn":["Diameter selection respects neighboring envelopes","Shape is checked against pad boundaries","Tail variation maps to timing events"],"answer":2,"explanation":"斷尾時序影響下一次初始球。本步要確認：尾長變化與時序事件能對照；常見誤判是：斷尾異常會跨循環傳遞。","explanationEn":"Tail termination affects the next initial ball. Verify: Tail variation maps to timing events. A common misinterpretation is: Tail faults propagate into the next cycle."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-151"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-153","order":23,"sequence":153,"title":"電性檢查線路完整","titleEn":"Check wire electrical continuity","objective":"將量測結果對回接線網表，並能說明「連通與相鄰隔離需分別檢查」。","objectiveEn":"Map measurements to the bonding netlist and explain: Continuity and neighboring isolation require separate checks.","instruction":"將量測結果對回接線網表。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：開路與短路都有明確判定。","instructionEn":"Map measurements to the bonding netlist. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Opens and shorts have explicit dispositions.","observation":"開路與短路都有明確判定；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Opens and shorts have explicit dispositions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只測連通會漏掉相鄰短路。","failureEn":"Continuity-only tests miss adjacent shorts.","check":"開路與短路都有明確判定。","checkEn":"Opens and shorts have explicit dispositions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-153-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"連通與相鄰隔離需分別檢查。","textEn":"Continuity and neighboring isolation require separate checks."},{"id":"pk-153-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只測連通會漏掉相鄰短路；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Continuity-only tests miss adjacent shorts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「電性檢查線路完整」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check wire electrical continuity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["開路與短路都有明確判定","工具輪廓符合示意接點需求","潛在底層破壞有專屬檢查"],"optionsEn":["Opens and shorts have explicit dispositions","Tool geometry fits the exercise joint","Potential underlying damage receives dedicated inspection"],"answer":0,"explanation":"連通與相鄰隔離需分別檢查。本步要確認：開路與短路都有明確判定；常見誤判是：只測連通會漏掉相鄰短路。","explanationEn":"Continuity and neighboring isolation require separate checks. Verify: Opens and shorts have explicit dispositions. A common misinterpretation is: Continuity-only tests miss adjacent shorts."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-152"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-154","order":24,"sequence":154,"title":"判讀拉力破壞位置","titleEn":"Interpret wire-pull failure location","objective":"記錄斷線、頸斷與接點抬起，並能說明「破壞模式決定測值的物理意義」。","objectiveEn":"Record wire break, neck break and bond lift and explain: Failure mode determines force meaning.","instruction":"記錄斷線、頸斷與接點抬起。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：拉力數據附測試幾何與模式。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Record wire break, neck break and bond lift. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Pull data include geometry and failure mode. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"拉力數據附測試幾何與模式；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Pull data include geometry and failure mode; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"不同拉點不能直接比較力值。","failureEn":"Different hook positions cannot be compared blindly.","check":"拉力數據附測試幾何與模式。","checkEn":"Pull data include geometry and failure mode.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-154-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"破壞模式決定測值的物理意義。","textEn":"Failure mode determines force meaning."},{"id":"pk-154-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"不同拉點不能直接比較力值；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Different hook positions cannot be compared blindly. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-154-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"兩條線都在 8 gf 拉斷，但一條為線材中段、另一條為焊墊剝離，代表不同機制；相同荷重不能視為接合品質等效。gf 為力單位，不可直接當質量公克。","textEn":"Two hypothetical wires break at 8 gf, one mid-wire and one by pad lift, indicating different mechanisms; equal load does not imply equivalent bonding. gf is force, not mass in grams."},{"id":"pk-154-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"記錄勾點位置、拉伸方向、線弧幾何與破壞分類。若試驗幾何改變，應先校正比較條件，不能直接把數值差歸因製程。","textEn":"Record hook location, pull direction, loop geometry and fracture class. Normalize changed geometry before attributing load differences to process variation."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀拉力破壞位置」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret wire-pull failure location\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["全弧線未穿入限制包絡","拉力數據附測試幾何與模式","送料異常能被偵測並隔離"],"optionsEn":["The entire loop avoids forbidden envelopes","Pull data include geometry and failure mode","Feed faults are detectable and isolated"],"answer":1,"explanation":"破壞模式決定測值的物理意義。本步要確認：拉力數據附測試幾何與模式；常見誤判是：不同拉點不能直接比較力值。","explanationEn":"Failure mode determines force meaning. Verify: Pull data include geometry and failure mode. A common misinterpretation is: Different hook positions cannot be compared blindly."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-153"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-155","order":25,"sequence":155,"title":"判讀球剪切證據","titleEn":"Interpret ball-shear evidence","objective":"對照推刀位置與接合殘留面，並能說明「推刀幾何會改變受力模式」。","objectiveEn":"Compare shear-tool placement and residual bond face and explain: Tool geometry changes loading mode.","instruction":"對照推刀位置與接合殘留面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：剪切結果包含工具條件與破壞面。","instructionEn":"Compare shear-tool placement and residual bond face. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Shear results include tooling and fracture surface.","observation":"剪切結果包含工具條件與破壞面；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Shear results include tooling and fracture surface; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"刮入焊墊的數值不代表正常剪切強度。","failureEn":"Pad-scraping force is not valid bond shear strength.","check":"剪切結果包含工具條件與破壞面。","checkEn":"Shear results include tooling and fracture surface.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-155-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"推刀幾何會改變受力模式。","textEn":"Tool geometry changes loading mode."},{"id":"pk-155-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"刮入焊墊的數值不代表正常剪切強度；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Pad-scraping force is not valid bond shear strength. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀球剪切證據」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret ball-shear evidence\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["關鍵接點下沒有未評估懸空","最低點仍有指定隔離裕量","剪切結果包含工具條件與破壞面"],"optionsEn":["Critical sites have no unassessed unsupported spans","The lowest point retains required clearance","Shear results include tooling and fracture surface"],"answer":2,"explanation":"推刀幾何會改變受力模式。本步要確認：剪切結果包含工具條件與破壞面；常見誤判是：刮入焊墊的數值不代表正常剪切強度。","explanationEn":"Tool geometry changes loading mode. Verify: Shear results include tooling and fracture surface. A common misinterpretation is: Pad-scraping force is not valid bond shear strength."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-154"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-156","order":26,"sequence":156,"title":"放行打線組件","titleEn":"Release the wirebond assembly","objective":"整合外觀、電性與破壞性抽樣證據，並能說明「單一方法不足以涵蓋所有線路缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Combine visual, electrical and sampled destructive evidence and explain: One method cannot cover every wire defect.","instruction":"整合外觀、電性與破壞性抽樣證據。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：抽樣範圍與隔離件清單完整。","instructionEn":"Combine visual, electrical and sampled destructive evidence. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Sample coverage and quarantine lists are complete.","observation":"抽樣範圍與隔離件清單完整；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Sample coverage and quarantine lists are complete; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"以一根線合格代表整件有逃逸風險。","failureEn":"One passing wire does not validate the assembly.","check":"抽樣範圍與隔離件清單完整。","checkEn":"Sample coverage and quarantine lists are complete.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-156-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"單一方法不足以涵蓋所有線路缺陷。","textEn":"One method cannot cover every wire defect."},{"id":"pk-156-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"以一根線合格代表整件有逃逸風險；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One passing wire does not validate the assembly. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「放行打線組件」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release the wirebond assembly\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["抽樣範圍與隔離件清單完整","圖中保留材料體積一致性","交叉點的高度差被量測"],"optionsEn":["Sample coverage and quarantine lists are complete","The model preserves material-volume consistency","Height separation is measured at crossings"],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一方法不足以涵蓋所有線路缺陷。本步要確認：抽樣範圍與隔離件清單完整；常見誤判是：以一根線合格代表整件有逃逸風險。","explanationEn":"One method cannot cover every wire defect. Verify: Sample coverage and quarantine lists are complete. A common misinterpretation is: One passing wire does not validate the assembly."},"sourceIds":["pk-kns-wirebond","pk-kns-capillary","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-155"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"wirebond","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察開蓋晶粒、接合線與周邊接點；它示範打線結構，不代表倒裝、混合鍵合或特定先進節點。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a decapped die, bond wires and surrounding contacts; it illustrates wire bonding, not flip-chip, hybrid bonding or a particular advanced node.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m07","order":7,"sequence":7,"title":"覆晶用UBM、凸塊電鍍與回流","titleEn":"Flipchip UBM, bump electroplating and reflow","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查覆晶用UBM、凸塊電鍍與回流的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for flipchip ubm, bump electroplating and reflow. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"晶圓級凸塊分支從進料接續；實際應在指定薄化與分離之前，不接在打線後。","routeEn":"Wafer bumping follows incoming control and precedes selected thinning/singulation, not wirebonding.","sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-157","order":1,"sequence":157,"title":"確認晶圓凸塊前置路線","titleEn":"Confirm wafer-bumping precedence","objective":"把UBM凸塊放在選定薄化分離之前，並能說明「本模組不是打線完成後的追加站」。","objectiveEn":"Place UBM bumping before selected thinning and singulation and explain: This module is not an addition after wirebonding.","instruction":"把UBM凸塊放在選定薄化分離之前。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：流程箭頭維持晶圓級加工狀態。","instructionEn":"Place UBM bumping before selected thinning and singulation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Process arrows preserve wafer-level processing.","observation":"流程箭頭維持晶圓級加工狀態；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Process arrows preserve wafer-level processing; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"已分離晶粒不能直接套整片電鍍流程。","failureEn":"Singulated dies cannot directly use wafer plating flow.","check":"流程箭頭維持晶圓級加工狀態。","checkEn":"Process arrows preserve wafer-level processing.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-157-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"本模組不是打線完成後的追加站。","textEn":"This module is not an addition after wirebonding."},{"id":"pk-157-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"已分離晶粒不能直接套整片電鍍流程；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Singulated dies cannot directly use wafer plating flow. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「確認晶圓凸塊前置路線」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Confirm wafer-bumping precedence\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["中心與周邊標記同時符合規則","報告呈現空間圖與批次差","流程箭頭維持晶圓級加工狀態"],"optionsEn":["Center and edge marks meet rules together","Reports show spatial maps and lot differences","Process arrows preserve wafer-level processing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本模組不是打線完成後的追加站。本步要確認：流程箭頭維持晶圓級加工狀態；常見誤判是：已分離晶粒不能直接套整片電鍍流程。","explanationEn":"This module is not an addition after wirebonding. Verify: Process arrows preserve wafer-level processing. A common misinterpretation is: Singulated dies cannot directly use wafer plating flow."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-052"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-158","order":2,"sequence":158,"title":"核對焊墊開口與陣列","titleEn":"Verify pad openings and array","objective":"比較鈍化開口與凸塊設計位置，並能說明「可接觸金屬決定互連起始面積」。","objectiveEn":"Compare passivation openings and bump locations and explain: Accessible metal defines initial interconnect area.","instruction":"比較鈍化開口與凸塊設計位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每個凸塊對到正確開口。","instructionEn":"Compare passivation openings and bump locations. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Every bump maps to its intended opening.","observation":"每個凸塊對到正確開口；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Every bump maps to its intended opening; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"座標鏡射會使整個陣列錯配。","failureEn":"Mirrored coordinates mismatch the entire array.","check":"每個凸塊對到正確開口。","checkEn":"Every bump maps to its intended opening.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-158-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"可接觸金屬決定互連起始面積。","textEn":"Accessible metal defines initial interconnect area."},{"id":"pk-158-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"座標鏡射會使整個陣列錯配；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mirrored coordinates mismatch the entire array. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對焊墊開口與陣列」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify pad openings and array\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每個凸塊對到正確開口","比較包含開口頂部與底部","狹窄區也有可驗證清潔證據"],"optionsEn":["Every bump maps to its intended opening","Comparison includes opening top and bottom","Narrow regions have verified cleaning evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"可接觸金屬決定互連起始面積。本步要確認：每個凸塊對到正確開口；常見誤判是：座標鏡射會使整個陣列錯配。","explanationEn":"Accessible metal defines initial interconnect area. Verify: Every bump maps to its intended opening. A common misinterpretation is: Mirrored coordinates mismatch the entire array."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-157"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-159","order":3,"sequence":159,"title":"評估焊墊前處理","titleEn":"Assess pad pretreatment","objective":"辨識氧化與有機殘留的不同對策，並能說明「清潔方法需與焊墊材料相容」。","objectiveEn":"Separate oxide and organic-residue responses and explain: Cleaning must suit the pad material.","instruction":"辨識氧化與有機殘留的不同對策。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：對策未侵蝕需要保留的金屬。","instructionEn":"Separate oxide and organic-residue responses. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Treatment preserves required metal.","observation":"對策未侵蝕需要保留的金屬；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Treatment preserves required metal; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"通用強清洗可能損傷薄焊墊。","failureEn":"Aggressive generic cleaning can damage thin pads.","check":"對策未侵蝕需要保留的金屬。","checkEn":"Treatment preserves required metal.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-159-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"清潔方法需與焊墊材料相容。","textEn":"Cleaning must suit the pad material."},{"id":"pk-159-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"通用強清洗可能損傷薄焊墊；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Aggressive generic cleaning can damage thin pads. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估焊墊前處理」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess pad pretreatment\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["導通橋消失且底部結構保留","對策未侵蝕需要保留的金屬","底部金屬外露且側壁符合設計"],"optionsEn":["Bridges disappear while bases remain intact","Treatment preserves required metal","Bottom metal is exposed and walls match design"],"answer":1,"explanation":"清潔方法需與焊墊材料相容。本步要確認：對策未侵蝕需要保留的金屬；常見誤判是：通用強清洗可能損傷薄焊墊。","explanationEn":"Cleaning must suit the pad material. Verify: Treatment preserves required metal. A common misinterpretation is: Aggressive generic cleaning can damage thin pads."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-158"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-160","order":4,"sequence":160,"title":"拆解UBM層功能","titleEn":"Separate UBM layer functions","objective":"分配黏著、阻障與潤濕角色，並能說明「不同層承擔不同界面功能」。","objectiveEn":"Assign adhesion, barrier and wetting roles and explain: Different layers serve distinct interface functions.","instruction":"分配黏著、阻障與潤濕角色。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每層角色與相鄰材料一致。","instructionEn":"Assign adhesion, barrier and wetting roles. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each role matches adjacent materials.","observation":"每層角色與相鄰材料一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each role matches adjacent materials; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單用導電層不能保證界面可靠。","failureEn":"Conductivity alone does not guarantee interface reliability.","check":"每層角色與相鄰材料一致。","checkEn":"Each role matches adjacent materials.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-160-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同層承擔不同界面功能。","textEn":"Different layers serve distinct interface functions."},{"id":"pk-160-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單用導電層不能保證界面可靠；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Conductivity alone does not guarantee interface reliability. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「拆解UBM層功能」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Separate UBM layer functions\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["底部清潔與尺寸保留同時確認","只對應隔離的網路要求絕緣","每層角色與相鄰材料一致"],"optionsEn":["Clean bottoms and retained dimensions are both checked","Isolation is required only where intended","Each role matches adjacent materials"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同層承擔不同界面功能。本步要確認：每層角色與相鄰材料一致；常見誤判是：單用導電層不能保證界面可靠。","explanationEn":"Different layers serve distinct interface functions. Verify: Each role matches adjacent materials. A common misinterpretation is: Conductivity alone does not guarantee interface reliability."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-159"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-161","order":5,"sequence":161,"title":"檢查種子層覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect seed-layer coverage","objective":"查看台階與開口側壁的連續性，並能說明「不連續種子層會阻斷電鍍供電」。","objectiveEn":"Inspect continuity across steps and opening sidewalls and explain: Discontinuous seed interrupts plating current.","instruction":"查看台階與開口側壁的連續性。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：所有待鍍區均有導電路徑。","instructionEn":"Inspect continuity across steps and opening sidewalls. Check evidence you create or obtain against: All plated regions have conductive paths.","observation":"所有待鍍區均有導電路徑；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"All plated regions have conductive paths; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平面覆蓋合格可能漏掉側壁斷點。","failureEn":"Planar coverage can hide sidewall breaks.","check":"所有待鍍區均有導電路徑。","checkEn":"All plated regions have conductive paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-161-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不連續種子層會阻斷電鍍供電。","textEn":"Discontinuous seed interrupts plating current."},{"id":"pk-161-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平面覆蓋合格可能漏掉側壁斷點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Planar coverage can hide sidewall breaks. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查種子層覆蓋」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect seed-layer coverage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["所有待鍍區均有導電路徑","接電區沒有污染或斷續證據","異常形態與表面證據聯讀"],"optionsEn":["All plated regions have conductive paths","Contacts show no contamination or discontinuity","Abnormal shapes are paired with surface evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不連續種子層會阻斷電鍍供電。本步要確認：所有待鍍區均有導電路徑；常見誤判是：平面覆蓋合格可能漏掉側壁斷點。","explanationEn":"Discontinuous seed interrupts plating current. Verify: All plated regions have conductive paths. A common misinterpretation is: Planar coverage can hide sidewall breaks."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-160"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-162","order":6,"sequence":162,"title":"量測種子層片電阻","titleEn":"Measure seed sheet resistance","objective":"以固定點位繪製片電阻分布，並能說明「片電阻反映厚度與材料狀態」。","objectiveEn":"Map sheet resistance at fixed positions and explain: Sheet resistance reflects thickness and material state.","instruction":"以固定點位繪製片電阻分布。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常區與覆膜資料交叉核對。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Map sheet resistance at fixed positions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Anomalies are compared with deposition evidence. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"異常區與覆膜資料交叉核對；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Anomalies are compared with deposition evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"片電阻變化不必全由厚度造成。","failureEn":"Resistance variation need not arise only from thickness.","check":"異常區與覆膜資料交叉核對。","checkEn":"Anomalies are compared with deposition evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-162-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"片電阻反映厚度與材料狀態。","textEn":"Sheet resistance reflects thickness and material state."},{"id":"pk-162-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"片電阻變化不必全由厚度造成；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Resistance variation need not arise only from thickness. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-162-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"片電阻 Rs=ρ/t；假設 ρ=2×10⁻⁸ Ω·m、t=100 nm，Rs=0.2 Ω/□。20 squares 的理想條帶電阻 4 Ω，不含接觸與尺寸效應。","textEn":"For Rs=ρ/t, hypothetical ρ=2×10⁻⁸ Ω·m and t=100 nm give 0.2 Ω/□. An ideal 20-square strip has 4 Ω excluding contacts and size effects."},{"id":"pk-162-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"低片電阻不保證深孔側壁和孔底連續。應把平面量測與截面覆蓋證據分開，薄膜電阻率也可能不同於塊材。","textEn":"Low sheet resistance does not prove continuity at deep via walls and bottoms. Separate planar measurements from sectional coverage; film resistivity may differ from bulk values."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測種子層片電阻」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure seed sheet resistance\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["時間溫度證據來自件溫記錄","異常區與覆膜資料交叉核對","面積定義與使用的電流量一致"],"optionsEn":["Time-temperature evidence comes from part records","Anomalies are compared with deposition evidence","Area definition matches the current used"],"answer":1,"explanation":"片電阻反映厚度與材料狀態。本步要確認：異常區與覆膜資料交叉核對；常見誤判是：片電阻變化不必全由厚度造成。","explanationEn":"Sheet resistance reflects thickness and material state. Verify: Anomalies are compared with deposition evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Resistance variation need not arise only from thickness."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-161"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-163","order":7,"sequence":163,"title":"檢查厚光阻塗佈","titleEn":"Inspect thick-resist coating","objective":"比較凸塊模穴需求與膜厚地圖，並能說明「光阻厚度限制可形成的鍍層高度」。","objectiveEn":"Compare mold-height needs and resist-thickness maps and explain: Resist thickness limits plated structure height.","instruction":"比較凸塊模穴需求與膜厚地圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最薄區仍滿足教學模穴需求。","instructionEn":"Compare mold-height needs and resist-thickness maps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The thinnest area meets exercise mold requirements.","observation":"最薄區仍滿足教學模穴需求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The thinnest area meets exercise mold requirements; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看平均膜厚會漏掉局部不足。","failureEn":"Average thickness hides local shortages.","check":"最薄區仍滿足教學模穴需求。","checkEn":"The thinnest area meets exercise mold requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-163-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"光阻厚度限制可形成的鍍層高度。","textEn":"Resist thickness limits plated structure height."},{"id":"pk-163-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看平均膜厚會漏掉局部不足；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Average thickness hides local shortages. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查厚光阻塗佈」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect thick-resist coating\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["結果按供應商核准範圍判讀","共平面與空洞各有判定記錄","最薄區仍滿足教學模穴需求"],"optionsEn":["Results use supplier-qualified ranges","Coplanarity and voids have separate dispositions","The thinnest area meets exercise mold requirements"],"answer":2,"explanation":"光阻厚度限制可形成的鍍層高度。本步要確認：最薄區仍滿足教學模穴需求；常見誤判是：只看平均膜厚會漏掉局部不足。","explanationEn":"Resist thickness limits plated structure height. Verify: The thinnest area meets exercise mold requirements. A common misinterpretation is: Average thickness hides local shortages."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-162"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-164","order":8,"sequence":164,"title":"評估光阻軟烤均勻性","titleEn":"Assess resist soft-bake uniformity","objective":"對照基板溫度與殘留溶劑線索，並能說明「烘烤狀態影響後續曝光與顯影」。","objectiveEn":"Compare substrate temperature and solvent-residue clues and explain: Bake state affects exposure and development.","instruction":"對照基板溫度與殘留溶劑線索。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：熱均勻性與膜層反應相符。","instructionEn":"Compare substrate temperature and solvent-residue clues. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Thermal uniformity agrees with film response.","observation":"熱均勻性與膜層反應相符；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Thermal uniformity agrees with film response; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"表面乾燥不保證內部狀態一致。","failureEn":"A dry surface does not prove uniform internal condition.","check":"熱均勻性與膜層反應相符。","checkEn":"Thermal uniformity agrees with film response.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-164-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"烘烤狀態影響後續曝光與顯影。","textEn":"Bake state affects exposure and development."},{"id":"pk-164-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"表面乾燥不保證內部狀態一致；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A dry surface does not prove uniform internal condition. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估光阻軟烤均勻性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess resist soft-bake uniformity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["熱均勻性與膜層反應相符","模型能區分中心與邊緣趨勢","下站取得凸塊高度及禁壓區"],"optionsEn":["Thermal uniformity agrees with film response","The model separates center and edge trends","Downstream receives bump height and no-pressure zones"],"answer":0,"explanation":"烘烤狀態影響後續曝光與顯影。本步要確認：熱均勻性與膜層反應相符；常見誤判是：表面乾燥不保證內部狀態一致。","explanationEn":"Bake state affects exposure and development. Verify: Thermal uniformity agrees with film response. A common misinterpretation is: A dry surface does not prove uniform internal condition."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-163"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-165","order":9,"sequence":165,"title":"對準凸塊光罩","titleEn":"Align the bump mask","objective":"以多處標記核對全片套刻，並能說明「局部對準不能證明全片無變形」。","objectiveEn":"Check wafer-wide overlay with multiple marks and explain: Local alignment cannot exclude global distortion.","instruction":"以多處標記核對全片套刻。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：中心與周邊標記同時符合規則。","instructionEn":"Check wafer-wide overlay with multiple marks. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Center and edge marks meet rules together.","observation":"中心與周邊標記同時符合規則；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Center and edge marks meet rules together; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只用單點對準會漏掉尺度誤差。","failureEn":"Single-point alignment misses scale errors.","check":"中心與周邊標記同時符合規則。","checkEn":"Center and edge marks meet rules together.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-165-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"局部對準不能證明全片無變形。","textEn":"Local alignment cannot exclude global distortion."},{"id":"pk-165-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只用單點對準會漏掉尺度誤差；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Single-point alignment misses scale errors. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「對準凸塊光罩」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Align the bump mask\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["流程箭頭維持晶圓級加工狀態","中心與周邊標記同時符合規則","覆蓋證據包含邊緣區域"],"optionsEn":["Process arrows preserve wafer-level processing","Center and edge marks meet rules together","Coverage evidence includes edge regions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部對準不能證明全片無變形。本步要確認：中心與周邊標記同時符合規則；常見誤判是：只用單點對準會漏掉尺度誤差。","explanationEn":"Local alignment cannot exclude global distortion. Verify: Center and edge marks meet rules together. A common misinterpretation is: Single-point alignment misses scale errors."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-164"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-166","order":10,"sequence":166,"title":"建立曝光視窗試片","titleEn":"Create an exposure-window coupon","objective":"比較不同示意曝光條件的模穴，並能說明「厚阻曝光需考慮深度方向圖形」。","objectiveEn":"Compare openings under illustrative exposure conditions and explain: Thick-resist exposure involves depth profiles.","instruction":"比較不同示意曝光條件的模穴。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：比較包含開口頂部與底部。","instructionEn":"Compare openings under illustrative exposure conditions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Comparison includes opening top and bottom.","observation":"比較包含開口頂部與底部；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Comparison includes opening top and bottom; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"頂部開口正確不保證底部清通。","failureEn":"A correct top opening may hide bottom residue.","check":"比較包含開口頂部與底部。","checkEn":"Comparison includes opening top and bottom.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-166-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"厚阻曝光需考慮深度方向圖形。","textEn":"Thick-resist exposure involves depth profiles."},{"id":"pk-166-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"頂部開口正確不保證底部清通；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A correct top opening may hide bottom residue. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立曝光視窗試片」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Create an exposure-window coupon\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["體積與位置均符合示意設計","每個凸塊對到正確開口","比較包含開口頂部與底部"],"optionsEn":["Volume and placement match the exercise design","Every bump maps to its intended opening","Comparison includes opening top and bottom"],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚阻曝光需考慮深度方向圖形。本步要確認：比較包含開口頂部與底部；常見誤判是：頂部開口正確不保證底部清通。","explanationEn":"Thick-resist exposure involves depth profiles. Verify: Comparison includes opening top and bottom. A common misinterpretation is: A correct top opening may hide bottom residue."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-165"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-167","order":11,"sequence":167,"title":"檢查顯影後模穴","titleEn":"Inspect developed plating molds","objective":"觀察開口底部、側壁與殘渣，並能說明「模穴幾何會被電鍍複製」。","objectiveEn":"Inspect mold bottoms, sidewalls and residue and explain: Plating reproduces mold geometry.","instruction":"觀察開口底部、側壁與殘渣。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：底部金屬外露且側壁符合設計。","instructionEn":"Inspect mold bottoms, sidewalls and residue. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Bottom metal is exposed and walls match design.","observation":"底部金屬外露且側壁符合設計；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Bottom metal is exposed and walls match design; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"殘渣可形成未鍍或不均成核。","failureEn":"Residue causes missing plate or uneven nucleation.","check":"底部金屬外露且側壁符合設計。","checkEn":"Bottom metal is exposed and walls match design.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-167-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"模穴幾何會被電鍍複製。","textEn":"Plating reproduces mold geometry."},{"id":"pk-167-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"殘渣可形成未鍍或不均成核；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Residue causes missing plate or uneven nucleation. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查顯影後模穴」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect developed plating molds\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["底部金屬外露且側壁符合設計","報告呈現空間圖與批次差","對策未侵蝕需要保留的金屬"],"optionsEn":["Bottom metal is exposed and walls match design","Reports show spatial maps and lot differences","Treatment preserves required metal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"模穴幾何會被電鍍複製。本步要確認：底部金屬外露且側壁符合設計；常見誤判是：殘渣可形成未鍍或不均成核。","explanationEn":"Plating reproduces mold geometry. Verify: Bottom metal is exposed and walls match design. A common misinterpretation is: Residue causes missing plate or uneven nucleation."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-166"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-168","order":12,"sequence":168,"title":"評估去殘膠邊界","titleEn":"Assess descum boundaries","objective":"區分去殘膠與過度蝕耗，並能說明「去殘膠可能改變開口尺寸」。","objectiveEn":"Separate residue removal from excessive erosion and explain: Descum can change opening dimensions.","instruction":"區分去殘膠與過度蝕耗。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：底部清潔與尺寸保留同時確認。","instructionEn":"Separate residue removal from excessive erosion. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Clean bottoms and retained dimensions are both checked.","observation":"底部清潔與尺寸保留同時確認；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Clean bottoms and retained dimensions are both checked; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過度處理會擴大模穴或傷金屬。","failureEn":"Excess treatment widens molds or damages metal.","check":"底部清潔與尺寸保留同時確認。","checkEn":"Clean bottoms and retained dimensions are both checked.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-168-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"去殘膠可能改變開口尺寸。","textEn":"Descum can change opening dimensions."},{"id":"pk-168-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過度處理會擴大模穴或傷金屬；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excess treatment widens molds or damages metal. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估去殘膠邊界」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess descum boundaries\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每層角色與相鄰材料一致","底部清潔與尺寸保留同時確認","狹窄區也有可驗證清潔證據"],"optionsEn":["Each role matches adjacent materials","Clean bottoms and retained dimensions are both checked","Narrow regions have verified cleaning evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"去殘膠可能改變開口尺寸。本步要確認：底部清潔與尺寸保留同時確認；常見誤判是：過度處理會擴大模穴或傷金屬。","explanationEn":"Descum can change opening dimensions. Verify: Clean bottoms and retained dimensions are both checked. A common misinterpretation is: Excess treatment widens molds or damages metal."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-167"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-169","order":13,"sequence":169,"title":"核對電鍍接電區","titleEn":"Verify plating-contact areas","objective":"追蹤邊緣接點到種子層的導通，並能說明「接觸電阻影响區域電流分配」。","objectiveEn":"Trace edge contacts into the seed layer and explain: Contact resistance affects regional current distribution.","instruction":"追蹤邊緣接點到種子層的導通。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：接電區沒有污染或斷續證據。","instructionEn":"Trace edge contacts into the seed layer. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Contacts show no contamination or discontinuity.","observation":"接電區沒有污染或斷續證據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Contacts show no contamination or discontinuity; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"接點問題可能被誤認為槽液失效。","failureEn":"Contact faults can mimic bath failure.","check":"接電區沒有污染或斷續證據。","checkEn":"Contacts show no contamination or discontinuity.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-169-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"接觸電阻影响區域電流分配。","textEn":"Contact resistance affects regional current distribution."},{"id":"pk-169-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"接點問題可能被誤認為槽液失效；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Contact faults can mimic bath failure. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對電鍍接電區」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify plating-contact areas\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["導通橋消失且底部結構保留","所有待鍍區均有導電路徑","接電區沒有污染或斷續證據"],"optionsEn":["Bridges disappear while bases remain intact","All plated regions have conductive paths","Contacts show no contamination or discontinuity"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸電阻影响區域電流分配。本步要確認：接電區沒有污染或斷續證據；常見誤判是：接點問題可能被誤認為槽液失效。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance affects regional current distribution. Verify: Contacts show no contamination or discontinuity. A common misinterpretation is: Contact faults can mimic bath failure."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-168"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-170","order":14,"sequence":170,"title":"計算有效電鍍面積","titleEn":"Calculate active plating area","objective":"加總開口面積而非整片面積，並能說明「電流密度取決於實際作用面積」。","objectiveEn":"Sum opening areas rather than wafer area and explain: Current density depends on active area.","instruction":"加總開口面積而非整片面積。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：面積定義與使用的電流量一致。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Sum opening areas rather than wafer area. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Area definition matches the current used. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"面積定義與使用的電流量一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Area definition matches the current used; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"用整片面積會錯估開口電流密度。","failureEn":"Wafer area misstates current density in openings.","check":"面積定義與使用的電流量一致。","checkEn":"Area definition matches the current used.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-170-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"電流密度取決於實際作用面積。","textEn":"Current density depends on active area."},{"id":"pk-170-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"用整片面積會錯估開口電流密度；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Wafer area misstates current density in openings. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-170-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設每個開口 100 µm²、共 10^6 個，有效面積 100 mm²。若只用整片面積計算電流密度，會稀釋局部數值；dummy 和實際連通區也要計入。","textEn":"One million hypothetical 100 µm² openings total 100 mm². Using the entire wafer area dilutes local current-density estimates; dummy and electrically connected areas also matter."},{"id":"pk-170-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"在 J=I/A 前明確定義 A 是開口面積、實際可鍍面積或投影面積。全片平均 J 不能替代邊緣和密集區的局部傳質分析。","textEn":"Before J=I/A, define whether A is opening, plateable or projected area. Wafer-average J does not replace local mass-transport analysis at edges and dense patterns."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「計算有效電鍍面積」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Calculate active plating area\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["面積定義與使用的電流量一致","只對應隔離的網路要求絕緣","異常區與覆膜資料交叉核對"],"optionsEn":["Area definition matches the current used","Isolation is required only where intended","Anomalies are compared with deposition evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電流密度取決於實際作用面積。本步要確認：面積定義與使用的電流量一致；常見誤判是：用整片面積會錯估開口電流密度。","explanationEn":"Current density depends on active area. Verify: Area definition matches the current used. A common misinterpretation is: Wafer area misstates current density in openings."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-169"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-171","order":15,"sequence":171,"title":"判讀鍍液分析紀錄","titleEn":"Interpret plating-bath analysis","objective":"區分金屬離子與添加劑監測，並能說明「多項成分共同決定沉積行為」。","objectiveEn":"Separate metal-ion and additive monitoring and explain: Multiple constituents govern deposition.","instruction":"區分金屬離子與添加劑監測。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：結果按供應商核准範圍判讀。","instructionEn":"Separate metal-ion and additive monitoring. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Results use supplier-qualified ranges.","observation":"結果按供應商核准範圍判讀；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Results use supplier-qualified ranges; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只測主鹽不能證明添加劑正常。","failureEn":"Main-salt testing cannot validate additives.","check":"結果按供應商核准範圍判讀。","checkEn":"Results use supplier-qualified ranges.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-171-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"多項成分共同決定沉積行為。","textEn":"Multiple constituents govern deposition."},{"id":"pk-171-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只測主鹽不能證明添加劑正常；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Main-salt testing cannot validate additives. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀鍍液分析紀錄」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret plating-bath analysis\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最薄區仍滿足教學模穴需求","結果按供應商核准範圍判讀","異常形態與表面證據聯讀"],"optionsEn":["The thinnest area meets exercise mold requirements","Results use supplier-qualified ranges","Abnormal shapes are paired with surface evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多項成分共同決定沉積行為。本步要確認：結果按供應商核准範圍判讀；常見誤判是：只測主鹽不能證明添加劑正常。","explanationEn":"Multiple constituents govern deposition. Verify: Results use supplier-qualified ranges. A common misinterpretation is: Main-salt testing cannot validate additives."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-170"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-172","order":16,"sequence":172,"title":"模擬銅柱成長","titleEn":"Simulate copper-pillar growth","objective":"比較時間與各區高度增量，並能說明「電流分布和質傳影響柱高」。","objectiveEn":"Compare time and regional height increments and explain: Current distribution and transport affect height.","instruction":"比較時間與各區高度增量。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：模型能區分中心與邊緣趨勢。","instructionEn":"Compare time and regional height increments. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The model separates center and edge trends.","observation":"模型能區分中心與邊緣趨勢；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The model separates center and edge trends; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"線性時間比例不一定涵蓋局部變化。","failureEn":"Linear time scaling may miss local changes.","check":"模型能區分中心與邊緣趨勢。","checkEn":"The model separates center and edge trends.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-172-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"電流分布和質傳影響柱高。","textEn":"Current distribution and transport affect height."},{"id":"pk-172-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"線性時間比例不一定涵蓋局部變化；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Linear time scaling may miss local changes. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「模擬銅柱成長」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Simulate copper-pillar growth\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["時間溫度證據來自件溫記錄","熱均勻性與膜層反應相符","模型能區分中心與邊緣趨勢"],"optionsEn":["Time-temperature evidence comes from part records","Thermal uniformity agrees with film response","The model separates center and edge trends"],"answer":2,"explanation":"電流分布和質傳影響柱高。本步要確認：模型能區分中心與邊緣趨勢；常見誤判是：線性時間比例不一定涵蓋局部變化。","explanationEn":"Current distribution and transport affect height. Verify: The model separates center and edge trends. A common misinterpretation is: Linear time scaling may miss local changes."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-171"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-173","order":17,"sequence":173,"title":"檢查阻障層連續性","titleEn":"Inspect barrier-layer continuity","objective":"標示柱頂阻障層覆蓋與缺口，並能說明「阻障層抑制特定元素互擴散」。","objectiveEn":"Mark top-barrier coverage and gaps and explain: Barrier layers limit specific interdiffusion.","instruction":"標示柱頂阻障層覆蓋與缺口。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：覆蓋證據包含邊緣區域。","instructionEn":"Mark top-barrier coverage and gaps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Coverage evidence includes edge regions.","observation":"覆蓋證據包含邊緣區域；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Coverage evidence includes edge regions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"頂部平均厚度無法排除局部缺口。","failureEn":"Mean top thickness cannot exclude local gaps.","check":"覆蓋證據包含邊緣區域。","checkEn":"Coverage evidence includes edge regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-173-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"阻障層抑制特定元素互擴散。","textEn":"Barrier layers limit specific interdiffusion."},{"id":"pk-173-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"頂部平均厚度無法排除局部缺口；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mean top thickness cannot exclude local gaps. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查阻障層連續性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect barrier-layer continuity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["覆蓋證據包含邊緣區域","共平面與空洞各有判定記錄","中心與周邊標記同時符合規則"],"optionsEn":["Coverage evidence includes edge regions","Coplanarity and voids have separate dispositions","Center and edge marks meet rules together"],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻障層抑制特定元素互擴散。本步要確認：覆蓋證據包含邊緣區域；常見誤判是：頂部平均厚度無法排除局部缺口。","explanationEn":"Barrier layers limit specific interdiffusion. Verify: Coverage evidence includes edge regions. A common misinterpretation is: Mean top thickness cannot exclude local gaps."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-172"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-174","order":18,"sequence":174,"title":"檢查焊料帽沉積","titleEn":"Inspect solder-cap deposition","objective":"比較柱頂焊料體積與偏心，並能說明「焊料量影響回流後接點形狀」。","objectiveEn":"Compare cap volume and eccentricity and explain: Solder volume affects reflowed geometry.","instruction":"比較柱頂焊料體積與偏心。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：體積與位置均符合示意設計。","instructionEn":"Compare cap volume and eccentricity. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Volume and placement match the exercise design.","observation":"體積與位置均符合示意設計；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Volume and placement match the exercise design; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"等高柱體也可能有不等焊料量。","failureEn":"Equal pillars can carry unequal solder volume.","check":"體積與位置均符合示意設計。","checkEn":"Volume and placement match the exercise design.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-174-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"焊料量影響回流後接點形狀。","textEn":"Solder volume affects reflowed geometry."},{"id":"pk-174-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"等高柱體也可能有不等焊料量；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Equal pillars can carry unequal solder volume. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查焊料帽沉積」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect solder-cap deposition\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["比較包含開口頂部與底部","體積與位置均符合示意設計","下站取得凸塊高度及禁壓區"],"optionsEn":["Comparison includes opening top and bottom","Volume and placement match the exercise design","Downstream receives bump height and no-pressure zones"],"answer":1,"explanation":"焊料量影響回流後接點形狀。本步要確認：體積與位置均符合示意設計；常見誤判是：等高柱體也可能有不等焊料量。","explanationEn":"Solder volume affects reflowed geometry. Verify: Volume and placement match the exercise design. A common misinterpretation is: Equal pillars can carry unequal solder volume."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-173"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-175","order":19,"sequence":175,"title":"量測全片凸塊均勻性","titleEn":"Measure wafer-wide bump uniformity","objective":"分離片內與片間高度差，並能說明「兩種變異需要不同診斷」。","objectiveEn":"Separate within-wafer and between-wafer variation and explain: The variations need different diagnosis.","instruction":"分離片內與片間高度差。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：報告呈現空間圖與批次差。","instructionEn":"Separate within-wafer and between-wafer variation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Reports show spatial maps and lot differences.","observation":"報告呈現空間圖與批次差；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Reports show spatial maps and lot differences; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把兩種變異混算會錯判設備問題。","failureEn":"Combining variations misidentifies equipment issues.","check":"報告呈現空間圖與批次差。","checkEn":"Reports show spatial maps and lot differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-175-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"兩種變異需要不同診斷。","textEn":"The variations need different diagnosis."},{"id":"pk-175-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把兩種變異混算會錯判設備問題；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Combining variations misidentifies equipment issues. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測全片凸塊均勻性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure wafer-wide bump uniformity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["流程箭頭維持晶圓級加工狀態","底部金屬外露且側壁符合設計","報告呈現空間圖與批次差"],"optionsEn":["Process arrows preserve wafer-level processing","Bottom metal is exposed and walls match design","Reports show spatial maps and lot differences"],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩種變異需要不同診斷。本步要確認：報告呈現空間圖與批次差；常見誤判是：把兩種變異混算會錯判設備問題。","explanationEn":"The variations need different diagnosis. Verify: Reports show spatial maps and lot differences. A common misinterpretation is: Combining variations misidentifies equipment issues."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-174"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-176","order":20,"sequence":176,"title":"驗證光阻剝除","titleEn":"Verify plating-resist stripping","objective":"檢查柱間與柱底殘留，並能說明「殘阻可能妨礙種子層去除」。","objectiveEn":"Inspect residue between and beneath pillars and explain: Resist residue can obstruct seed removal.","instruction":"檢查柱間與柱底殘留。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：狹窄區也有可驗證清潔證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect residue between and beneath pillars. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Narrow regions have verified cleaning evidence.","observation":"狹窄區也有可驗證清潔證據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Narrow regions have verified cleaning evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平面乾淨可能掩蓋柱底殘膠。","failureEn":"Clean planes can hide pillar-foot residue.","check":"狹窄區也有可驗證清潔證據。","checkEn":"Narrow regions have verified cleaning evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-176-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"殘阻可能妨礙種子層去除。","textEn":"Resist residue can obstruct seed removal."},{"id":"pk-176-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平面乾淨可能掩蓋柱底殘膠；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Clean planes can hide pillar-foot residue. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證光阻剝除」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify plating-resist stripping\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["狹窄區也有可驗證清潔證據","每個凸塊對到正確開口","底部清潔與尺寸保留同時確認"],"optionsEn":["Narrow regions have verified cleaning evidence","Every bump maps to its intended opening","Clean bottoms and retained dimensions are both checked"],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘阻可能妨礙種子層去除。本步要確認：狹窄區也有可驗證清潔證據；常見誤判是：平面乾淨可能掩蓋柱底殘膠。","explanationEn":"Resist residue can obstruct seed removal. Verify: Narrow regions have verified cleaning evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Clean planes can hide pillar-foot residue."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-175"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-177","order":21,"sequence":177,"title":"核對種子層蝕除","titleEn":"Review seed-layer removal","objective":"追蹤柱間清除與柱底側蝕，並能說明「隔離需要清除種子而保留接點」。","objectiveEn":"Compare inter-pillar removal and base undercut and explain: Isolation removes seed while preserving joints.","instruction":"追蹤柱間清除與柱底側蝕。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：導通橋消失且底部結構保留。","instructionEn":"Compare inter-pillar removal and base undercut. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Bridges disappear while bases remain intact.","observation":"導通橋消失且底部結構保留；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Bridges disappear while bases remain intact; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過度蝕除可能掏空柱底。","failureEn":"Excess etch can undercut pillar bases.","check":"導通橋消失且底部結構保留。","checkEn":"Bridges disappear while bases remain intact.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-177-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"隔離需要清除種子而保留接點。","textEn":"Isolation removes seed while preserving joints."},{"id":"pk-177-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過度蝕除可能掏空柱底；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excess etch can undercut pillar bases. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對種子層蝕除」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review seed-layer removal\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["接電區沒有污染或斷續證據","導通橋消失且底部結構保留","對策未侵蝕需要保留的金屬"],"optionsEn":["Contacts show no contamination or discontinuity","Bridges disappear while bases remain intact","Treatment preserves required metal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔離需要清除種子而保留接點。本步要確認：導通橋消失且底部結構保留；常見誤判是：過度蝕除可能掏空柱底。","explanationEn":"Isolation removes seed while preserving joints. Verify: Bridges disappear while bases remain intact. A common misinterpretation is: Excess etch can undercut pillar bases."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-176"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-178","order":22,"sequence":178,"title":"驗證相鄰凸塊隔離","titleEn":"Verify neighboring-bump isolation","objective":"將絕緣量測對回設計網路，並能說明「同網路與不同網路判定不同」。","objectiveEn":"Map isolation measurements to intended nets and explain: Same-net and different-net tests differ.","instruction":"將絕緣量測對回設計網路。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：只對應隔離的網路要求絕緣。","instructionEn":"Map isolation measurements to intended nets. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Isolation is required only where intended.","observation":"只對應隔離的網路要求絕緣；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Isolation is required only where intended; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"不看網表可能把正常連接判短路。","failureEn":"Ignoring nets can label intended connections as shorts.","check":"只對應隔離的網路要求絕緣。","checkEn":"Isolation is required only where intended.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-178-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"同網路與不同網路判定不同。","textEn":"Same-net and different-net tests differ."},{"id":"pk-178-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"不看網表可能把正常連接判短路；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring nets can label intended connections as shorts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證相鄰凸塊隔離」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify neighboring-bump isolation\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每層角色與相鄰材料一致","面積定義與使用的電流量一致","只對應隔離的網路要求絕緣"],"optionsEn":["Each role matches adjacent materials","Area definition matches the current used","Isolation is required only where intended"],"answer":2,"explanation":"同網路與不同網路判定不同。本步要確認：只對應隔離的網路要求絕緣；常見誤判是：不看網表可能把正常連接判短路。","explanationEn":"Same-net and different-net tests differ. Verify: Isolation is required only where intended. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring nets can label intended connections as shorts."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-177"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-179","order":23,"sequence":179,"title":"觀察回流潤濕形態","titleEn":"Observe reflow wetting morphology","objective":"比較焊料收縮、展開與未潤濕，並能說明「表面能與材料相容性影響潤濕」。","objectiveEn":"Compare solder collapse, spreading and nonwetting and explain: Surface energy and compatibility affect wetting.","instruction":"比較焊料收縮、展開與未潤濕。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常形態與表面證據聯讀。","instructionEn":"Compare solder collapse, spreading and nonwetting. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Abnormal shapes are paired with surface evidence.","observation":"異常形態與表面證據聯讀；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Abnormal shapes are paired with surface evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"球形外觀不能單獨證明界面良好。","failureEn":"A rounded shape cannot prove interface quality.","check":"異常形態與表面證據聯讀。","checkEn":"Abnormal shapes are paired with surface evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-179-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"表面能與材料相容性影響潤濕。","textEn":"Surface energy and compatibility affect wetting."},{"id":"pk-179-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"球形外觀不能單獨證明界面良好；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A rounded shape cannot prove interface quality. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「觀察回流潤濕形態」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Observe reflow wetting morphology\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常形態與表面證據聯讀","所有待鍍區均有導電路徑","結果按供應商核准範圍判讀"],"optionsEn":["Abnormal shapes are paired with surface evidence","All plated regions have conductive paths","Results use supplier-qualified ranges"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面能與材料相容性影響潤濕。本步要確認：異常形態與表面證據聯讀；常見誤判是：球形外觀不能單獨證明界面良好。","explanationEn":"Surface energy and compatibility affect wetting. Verify: Abnormal shapes are paired with surface evidence. A common misinterpretation is: A rounded shape cannot prove interface quality."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-178"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-180","order":24,"sequence":180,"title":"核對回流件溫歷程","titleEn":"Verify reflow part-temperature history","objective":"比較實測件溫與核准材料窗口，並能說明「爐溫設定與接點熱歷程不同」。","objectiveEn":"Compare measured part temperature with the qualified window and explain: Oven settings differ from joint thermal history.","instruction":"比較實測件溫與核准材料窗口。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：時間溫度證據來自件溫記錄。","instructionEn":"Compare measured part temperature with the qualified window. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Time-temperature evidence comes from part records.","observation":"時間溫度證據來自件溫記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Time-temperature evidence comes from part records; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略熱容量差會低估局部冷點。","failureEn":"Ignoring thermal mass misses local cold spots.","check":"時間溫度證據來自件溫記錄。","checkEn":"Time-temperature evidence comes from part records.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-180-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"爐溫設定與接點熱歷程不同。","textEn":"Oven settings differ from joint thermal history."},{"id":"pk-180-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略熱容量差會低估局部冷點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring thermal mass misses local cold spots. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對回流件溫歷程」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify reflow part-temperature history\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["模型能區分中心與邊緣趨勢","時間溫度證據來自件溫記錄","異常區與覆膜資料交叉核對"],"optionsEn":["The model separates center and edge trends","Time-temperature evidence comes from part records","Anomalies are compared with deposition evidence"],"answer":1,"explanation":"爐溫設定與接點熱歷程不同。本步要確認：時間溫度證據來自件溫記錄；常見誤判是：忽略熱容量差會低估局部冷點。","explanationEn":"Oven settings differ from joint thermal history. Verify: Time-temperature evidence comes from part records. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring thermal mass misses local cold spots."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-179"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-181","order":25,"sequence":181,"title":"檢查共平面與內部空洞","titleEn":"Inspect coplanarity and internal voids","objective":"分開量測最高低接點與截面缺陷，並能說明「外形與內部結構是獨立證據」。","objectiveEn":"Separately assess contact heights and section defects and explain: External shape and internal structure are independent evidence.","instruction":"分開量測最高低接點與截面缺陷。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：共平面與空洞各有判定記錄。","instructionEn":"Separately assess contact heights and section defects. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Coplanarity and voids have separate dispositions.","observation":"共平面與空洞各有判定記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Coplanarity and voids have separate dispositions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"外觀等高不代表內部無空洞。","failureEn":"Equal heights do not imply void-free interiors.","check":"共平面與空洞各有判定記錄。","checkEn":"Coplanarity and voids have separate dispositions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-181-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"外形與內部結構是獨立證據。","textEn":"External shape and internal structure are independent evidence."},{"id":"pk-181-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"外觀等高不代表內部無空洞；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Equal heights do not imply void-free interiors. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查共平面與內部空洞」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect coplanarity and internal voids\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最薄區仍滿足教學模穴需求","覆蓋證據包含邊緣區域","共平面與空洞各有判定記錄"],"optionsEn":["The thinnest area meets exercise mold requirements","Coverage evidence includes edge regions","Coplanarity and voids have separate dispositions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"外形與內部結構是獨立證據。本步要確認：共平面與空洞各有判定記錄；常見誤判是：外觀等高不代表內部無空洞。","explanationEn":"External shape and internal structure are independent evidence. Verify: Coplanarity and voids have separate dispositions. A common misinterpretation is: Equal heights do not imply void-free interiors."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-180"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-182","order":26,"sequence":182,"title":"放行凸塊晶圓至後段","titleEn":"Release bumped wafers downstream","objective":"交付凸塊圖、材料及薄化支承限制，並能說明「凸起會改變後續貼膜與搬運條件」。","objectiveEn":"Deliver bump maps, materials and support restrictions and explain: Bumps change later taping and handling.","instruction":"交付凸塊圖、材料及薄化支承限制。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：下站取得凸塊高度及禁壓區。","instructionEn":"Deliver bump maps, materials and support restrictions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Downstream receives bump height and no-pressure zones.","observation":"下站取得凸塊高度及禁壓區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Downstream receives bump height and no-pressure zones; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略凸塊支承會在薄化時壓傷。","failureEn":"Ignoring bump support damages bumps during thinning.","check":"下站取得凸塊高度及禁壓區。","checkEn":"Downstream receives bump height and no-pressure zones.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-182-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"凸起會改變後續貼膜與搬運條件。","textEn":"Bumps change later taping and handling."},{"id":"pk-182-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略凸塊支承會在薄化時壓傷；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring bump support damages bumps during thinning. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「放行凸塊晶圓至後段」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release bumped wafers downstream\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["下站取得凸塊高度及禁壓區","熱均勻性與膜層反應相符","體積與位置均符合示意設計"],"optionsEn":["Downstream receives bump height and no-pressure zones","Thermal uniformity agrees with film response","Volume and placement match the exercise design"],"answer":0,"explanation":"凸起會改變後續貼膜與搬運條件。本步要確認：下站取得凸塊高度及禁壓區；常見誤判是：忽略凸塊支承會在薄化時壓傷。","explanationEn":"Bumps change later taping and handling. Verify: Downstream receives bump height and no-pressure zones. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring bump support damages bumps during thinning."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-bumping","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-atotech-pillars","pk-suss-coating"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-181"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m08","order":8,"sequence":8,"title":"扇出載體、晶粒重組與解黏","titleEn":"Fan-out carriers, die reconstitution and debonding","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查扇出載體、晶粒重組與解黏的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for fan-out carriers, die reconstitution and debonding. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"本例為晶粒先置、正面朝下：前19步後進m09；完成m09後回第20步解黏，再進m10。","routeEn":"Die-first face-down example: after step 19 visit m09; after m09 resume step 20, debond and enter m10.","sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-183","order":1,"sequence":183,"title":"選定晶粒先置扇出路線","titleEn":"Select a die-first fan-out route","objective":"對比晶粒先置與RDL先置流程，並能說明「兩種扇出路線順序不同」。","objectiveEn":"Compare die-first and RDL-first routes and explain: Fan-out routes have different process orders.","instruction":"對比晶粒先置與RDL先置流程。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：本例明確選晶粒先置正面朝下載體。","instructionEn":"Compare die-first and RDL-first routes. Check evidence you create or obtain against: This example selects face-down die-first placement.","observation":"本例明確選晶粒先置正面朝下載體；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"This example selects face-down die-first placement; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把不同路線混合會造成介面不可達。","failureEn":"Mixing routes creates inaccessible interfaces.","check":"本例明確選晶粒先置正面朝下載體。","checkEn":"This example selects face-down die-first placement.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-183-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"兩種扇出路線順序不同。","textEn":"Fan-out routes have different process orders."},{"id":"pk-183-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把不同路線混合會造成介面不可達；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mixing routes creates inaccessible interfaces. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選定晶粒先置扇出路線」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select a die-first fan-out route\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每個重組位置具有唯一來源ID","資料封包可供模封m09使用","本例明確選晶粒先置正面朝下載體"],"optionsEn":["Each reconstituted location has one source ID","The evidence package is ready for molding module m09","This example selects face-down die-first placement"],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩種扇出路線順序不同。本步要確認：本例明確選晶粒先置正面朝下載體；常見誤判是：把不同路線混合會造成介面不可達。","explanationEn":"Fan-out routes have different process orders. Verify: This example selects face-down die-first placement. A common misinterpretation is: Mixing routes creates inaccessible interfaces."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-104"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-184","order":2,"sequence":184,"title":"挑選重組良品晶粒","titleEn":"Select known-good dies for reconstitution","objective":"核對單顆測試狀態與來源晶圓，並能說明「重組後仍需保留原始晶粒履歷」。","objectiveEn":"Check die test status and source wafer and explain: Reconstitution must preserve original die history.","instruction":"核對單顆測試狀態與來源晶圓。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每顆配置位置可回溯原晶圓座標。","instructionEn":"Check die test status and source wafer. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each placement resolves to original wafer coordinates.","observation":"每顆配置位置可回溯原晶圓座標；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each placement resolves to original wafer coordinates; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"失去來源對應會妨礙異常隔離。","failureEn":"Lost provenance prevents excursion isolation.","check":"每顆配置位置可回溯原晶圓座標。","checkEn":"Each placement resolves to original wafer coordinates.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-184-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"重組後仍需保留原始晶粒履歷。","textEn":"Reconstitution must preserve original die history."},{"id":"pk-184-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"失去來源對應會妨礙異常隔離；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Lost provenance prevents excursion isolation. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「挑選重組良品晶粒」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select known-good dies for reconstitution\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每顆配置位置可回溯原晶圓座標","解黏後焊墊朝向RDL工站","輸入含模封放行pk-234證據"],"optionsEn":["Each placement resolves to original wafer coordinates","Pads face the RDL station after debonding","Input includes molding-release evidence pk-234"],"answer":0,"explanation":"重組後仍需保留原始晶粒履歷。本步要確認：每顆配置位置可回溯原晶圓座標；常見誤判是：失去來源對應會妨礙異常隔離。","explanationEn":"Reconstitution must preserve original die history. Verify: Each placement resolves to original wafer coordinates. A common misinterpretation is: Lost provenance prevents excursion isolation."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-183"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-185","order":3,"sequence":185,"title":"比較載體材料熱膨脹","titleEn":"Compare carrier thermal expansion","objective":"對照載體與模封體熱變形方向，並能說明「載體會限制模封體自由收縮」。","objectiveEn":"Compare carrier and mold thermal deformation and explain: Carriers constrain free mold contraction.","instruction":"對照載體與模封體熱變形方向。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：模型保留相對膨脹與支承條件。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Compare carrier and mold thermal deformation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The model retains relative expansion and support. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"模型保留相對膨脹與支承條件；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The model retains relative expansion and support; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只算模封料CTE會漏掉載體約束。","failureEn":"Mold CTE alone misses carrier constraint.","check":"模型保留相對膨脹與支承條件。","checkEn":"The model retains relative expansion and support.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-185-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"載體會限制模封體自由收縮。","textEn":"Carriers constrain free mold contraction."},{"id":"pk-185-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只算模封料CTE會漏掉載體約束；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mold CTE alone misses carrier constraint. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-185-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設載體與模封重組層 CTE 相差 8 ppm/K、長度 200 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由長度差為 160 µm；真正受拘束結構可能以翹曲與應力釋放此失配。","textEn":"For hypothetical carrier/reconstituted-layer CTE mismatch 8 ppm/K, length 200 mm and ΔT=100 K, free mismatch is 160 µm; constrained structures can release it through bow and stress."},{"id":"pk-185-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"比較玻璃與矽載體時，同時列平坦度、厚度、透光解黏相容性及回收條件，避免把低 CTE 當唯一選擇準則。","textEn":"Compare glass and silicon carriers by flatness, thickness, optical debond compatibility and reuse conditions rather than CTE alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「比較載體材料熱膨脹」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Compare carrier thermal expansion\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["分離前後皆有明確承載面","模型保留相對膨脹與支承條件","吸取區與指定非敏感面一致"],"optionsEn":["Both sides of separation have defined supports","The model retains relative expansion and support","Pickup matches designated nonsensitive areas"],"answer":1,"explanation":"載體會限制模封體自由收縮。本步要確認：模型保留相對膨脹與支承條件；常見誤判是：只算模封料CTE會漏掉載體約束。","explanationEn":"Carriers constrain free mold contraction. Verify: The model retains relative expansion and support. A common misinterpretation is: Mold CTE alone misses carrier constraint."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-184"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-186","order":4,"sequence":186,"title":"量測載體平坦度","titleEn":"Measure carrier flatness","objective":"以一致基準繪製載體高度圖，並能說明「載體形貌會影響放置高度」。","objectiveEn":"Map carrier height using one reference and explain: Carrier shape affects placement height.","instruction":"以一致基準繪製載體高度圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：放置區局部形貌可追溯。","instructionEn":"Map carrier height using one reference. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Local placement-area shape is traceable.","observation":"放置區局部形貌可追溯；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Local placement-area shape is traceable; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平均平坦度可能漏掉局部凸點。","failureEn":"Average flatness can miss local peaks.","check":"放置區局部形貌可追溯。","checkEn":"Local placement-area shape is traceable.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-186-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"載體形貌會影響放置高度。","textEn":"Carrier shape affects placement height."},{"id":"pk-186-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平均平坦度可能漏掉局部凸點；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Average flatness can miss local peaks. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測載體平坦度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure carrier flatness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["位置分布不超出教學補償包絡","方法與載體透光性和材料相符","放置區局部形貌可追溯"],"optionsEn":["Positions stay within the teaching compensation envelope","Method matches carrier transmission and material","Local placement-area shape is traceable"],"answer":2,"explanation":"載體形貌會影響放置高度。本步要確認：放置區局部形貌可追溯；常見誤判是：平均平坦度可能漏掉局部凸點。","explanationEn":"Carrier shape affects placement height. Verify: Local placement-area shape is traceable. A common misinterpretation is: Average flatness can miss local peaks."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-185"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-187","order":5,"sequence":187,"title":"檢查離型層相容性","titleEn":"Check release-layer compatibility","objective":"核對離型材料與後續熱製程，並能說明「離型層需先耐製程再可分離」。","objectiveEn":"Check release material against later thermal processing and explain: Release layers must survive processing before separation.","instruction":"核對離型材料與後續熱製程。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：耐受與釋離條件分開定義。","instructionEn":"Check release material against later thermal processing. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Survival and release conditions are separately defined.","observation":"耐受與釋離條件分開定義；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Survival and release conditions are separately defined; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"容易剝離不代表能承受模封。","failureEn":"Easy release does not guarantee molding endurance.","check":"耐受與釋離條件分開定義。","checkEn":"Survival and release conditions are separately defined.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-187-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"離型層需先耐製程再可分離。","textEn":"Release layers must survive processing before separation."},{"id":"pk-187-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"容易剝離不代表能承受模封；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Easy release does not guarantee molding endurance. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查離型層相容性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check release-layer compatibility\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["耐受與釋離條件分開定義","高度分布與後續平坦化需求相符","異常阻力區有對應表面檢查"],"optionsEn":["Survival and release conditions are separately defined","Height distribution suits later planarization","High-resistance regions have surface checks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"離型層需先耐製程再可分離。本步要確認：耐受與釋離條件分開定義；常見誤判是：容易剝離不代表能承受模封。","explanationEn":"Release layers must survive processing before separation. Verify: Survival and release conditions are separately defined. A common misinterpretation is: Easy release does not guarantee molding endurance."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-186"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-188","order":6,"sequence":188,"title":"驗證暫黏層厚度","titleEn":"Verify temporary-adhesive thickness","objective":"比較載體各區黏層與晶粒高度，並能說明「黏層不均會改變晶粒共平面」。","objectiveEn":"Compare adhesive thickness and die seating height and explain: Uneven adhesive changes die coplanarity.","instruction":"比較載體各區黏層與晶粒高度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：局部厚度未侵蝕高度預算。","instructionEn":"Compare adhesive thickness and die seating height. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Local thickness preserves the height budget.","observation":"局部厚度未侵蝕高度預算；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Local thickness preserves the height budget; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只量空白區可能漏掉晶粒下差異。","failureEn":"Blank-area sampling may miss under-die variation.","check":"局部厚度未侵蝕高度預算。","checkEn":"Local thickness preserves the height budget.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-188-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"黏層不均會改變晶粒共平面。","textEn":"Uneven adhesive changes die coplanarity."},{"id":"pk-188-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只量空白區可能漏掉晶粒下差異；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Blank-area sampling may miss under-die variation. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證暫黏層厚度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify temporary-adhesive thickness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["去殘留方案保留所有暴露材料","局部厚度未侵蝕高度預算","局部離群點與整體趨勢分開"],"optionsEn":["Residue removal preserves all exposed materials","Local thickness preserves the height budget","Local outliers are separated from global trends"],"answer":1,"explanation":"黏層不均會改變晶粒共平面。本步要確認：局部厚度未侵蝕高度預算；常見誤判是：只量空白區可能漏掉晶粒下差異。","explanationEn":"Uneven adhesive changes die coplanarity. Verify: Local thickness preserves the height budget. A common misinterpretation is: Blank-area sampling may miss under-die variation."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-187"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-189","order":7,"sequence":189,"title":"配置永久對準標記","titleEn":"Place persistent alignment marks","objective":"規劃模封與解黏後仍可辨認的標記，並能說明「可見性需跨越後續製程」。","objectiveEn":"Plan marks visible after molding and debonding and explain: Mark visibility must survive later processing.","instruction":"規劃模封與解黏後仍可辨認的標記。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：至少一組標記在每個關鍵階段可讀。","instructionEn":"Plan marks visible after molding and debonding. Check evidence you create or obtain against: At least one mark set survives each key stage.","observation":"至少一組標記在每個關鍵階段可讀；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"At least one mark set survives each key stage; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把標記放在被覆區會失去對位。","failureEn":"Covered marks remove alignment references.","check":"至少一組標記在每個關鍵階段可讀。","checkEn":"At least one mark set survives each key stage.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-189-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"可見性需跨越後續製程。","textEn":"Mark visibility must survive later processing."},{"id":"pk-189-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把標記放在被覆區會失去對位；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Covered marks remove alignment references. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「配置永久對準標記」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Place persistent alignment marks\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["移載後姿態改變可被量出","每個必要焊墊都有可用接觸面","至少一組標記在每個關鍵階段可讀"],"optionsEn":["Pose changes after transfer are measurable","Every required pad has accessible contact area","At least one mark set survives each key stage"],"answer":2,"explanation":"可見性需跨越後續製程。本步要確認：至少一組標記在每個關鍵階段可讀；常見誤判是：把標記放在被覆區會失去對位。","explanationEn":"Mark visibility must survive later processing. Verify: At least one mark set survives each key stage. A common misinterpretation is: Covered marks remove alignment references."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-188"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-190","order":8,"sequence":190,"title":"分配重組晶粒間距","titleEn":"Allocate reconstituted die spacing","objective":"在晶粒間保留RDL及切割空間，並能說明「間距同時服務布線與分離」。","objectiveEn":"Reserve RDL and singulation space between dies and explain: Spacing supports routing and singulation.","instruction":"在晶粒間保留RDL及切割空間。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：間隙可容納兩項功能包絡。","instructionEn":"Reserve RDL and singulation space between dies. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Gaps accommodate both functional envelopes.","observation":"間隙可容納兩項功能包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Gaps accommodate both functional envelopes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只為切割留距可能使RDL無路可走。","failureEn":"Singulation-only gaps may block RDL routing.","check":"間隙可容納兩項功能包絡。","checkEn":"Gaps accommodate both functional envelopes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-190-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"間距同時服務布線與分離。","textEn":"Spacing supports routing and singulation."},{"id":"pk-190-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只為切割留距可能使RDL無路可走；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Singulation-only gaps may block RDL routing. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分配重組晶粒間距」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Allocate reconstituted die spacing\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["間隙可容納兩項功能包絡","狹窄區具有可評估排氣路徑","座標轉換、版本與量測誤差完整"],"optionsEn":["Gaps accommodate both functional envelopes","Narrow regions have assessable vent paths","Transforms, revisions and measurement errors are complete"],"answer":0,"explanation":"間距同時服務布線與分離。本步要確認：間隙可容納兩項功能包絡；常見誤判是：只為切割留距可能使RDL無路可走。","explanationEn":"Spacing supports routing and singulation. Verify: Gaps accommodate both functional envelopes. A common misinterpretation is: Singulation-only gaps may block RDL routing."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-189"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-191","order":9,"sequence":191,"title":"轉換來源與重組座標","titleEn":"Transform source and reconstituted coordinates","objective":"建立原晶圓到載體位置表，並能說明「多片來源不能共用模糊座標」。","objectiveEn":"Map source-wafer coordinates to carrier positions and explain: Multiple source wafers require unambiguous coordinates.","instruction":"建立原晶圓到載體位置表。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每個重組位置具有唯一來源ID。","instructionEn":"Map source-wafer coordinates to carrier positions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each reconstituted location has one source ID.","observation":"每個重組位置具有唯一來源ID；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each reconstituted location has one source ID; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"重複座標無晶圓ID會造成身份衝突。","failureEn":"Coordinates without wafer IDs cause collisions.","check":"每個重組位置具有唯一來源ID。","checkEn":"Each reconstituted location has one source ID.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-191-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"多片來源不能共用模糊座標。","textEn":"Multiple source wafers require unambiguous coordinates."},{"id":"pk-191-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"重複座標無晶圓ID會造成身份衝突；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Coordinates without wafer IDs cause collisions. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「轉換來源與重組座標」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Transform source and reconstituted coordinates\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["本例明確選晶粒先置正面朝下載體","每個重組位置具有唯一來源ID","晶粒未落入模具或夾具接觸區"],"optionsEn":["This example selects face-down die-first placement","Each reconstituted location has one source ID","Dies avoid mold and clamp contact zones"],"answer":1,"explanation":"多片來源不能共用模糊座標。本步要確認：每個重組位置具有唯一來源ID；常見誤判是：重複座標無晶圓ID會造成身份衝突。","explanationEn":"Multiple source wafers require unambiguous coordinates. Verify: Each reconstituted location has one source ID. A common misinterpretation is: Coordinates without wafer IDs cause collisions."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-190"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-192","order":10,"sequence":192,"title":"檢查正面朝下朝向","titleEn":"Check face-down orientation","objective":"標示主動面與後續露墊方向，並能說明「朝向決定解黏後可接觸表面」。","objectiveEn":"Mark the active face and future pad exposure and explain: Orientation determines the accessible debonded face.","instruction":"標示主動面與後續露墊方向。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：解黏後焊墊朝向RDL工站。","instructionEn":"Mark the active face and future pad exposure. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Pads face the RDL station after debonding.","observation":"解黏後焊墊朝向RDL工站；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Pads face the RDL station after debonding; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"放反晶粒會把焊墊封在內部。","failureEn":"Reversed dies bury the pads.","check":"解黏後焊墊朝向RDL工站。","checkEn":"Pads face the RDL station after debonding.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-192-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"朝向決定解黏後可接觸表面。","textEn":"Orientation determines the accessible debonded face."},{"id":"pk-192-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"放反晶粒會把焊墊封在內部；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Reversed dies bury the pads. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查正面朝下朝向」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check face-down orientation\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["每種晶粒均有覆蓋及露出策略","每顆配置位置可回溯原晶圓座標","解黏後焊墊朝向RDL工站"],"optionsEn":["Each die type has coverage and exposure planning","Each placement resolves to original wafer coordinates","Pads face the RDL station after debonding"],"answer":2,"explanation":"朝向決定解黏後可接觸表面。本步要確認：解黏後焊墊朝向RDL工站；常見誤判是：放反晶粒會把焊墊封在內部。","explanationEn":"Orientation determines the accessible debonded face. Verify: Pads face the RDL station after debonding. A common misinterpretation is: Reversed dies bury the pads."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-191"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-193","order":11,"sequence":193,"title":"匹配重組取放工具","titleEn":"Match reconstitution handling tools","objective":"比較工具接觸面與晶粒尺寸，並能說明「工具需避免敏感面壓傷」。","objectiveEn":"Compare tool contact and die dimensions and explain: Tools must avoid damaging sensitive surfaces.","instruction":"比較工具接觸面與晶粒尺寸。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：吸取區與指定非敏感面一致。","instructionEn":"Compare tool contact and die dimensions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Pickup matches designated nonsensitive areas.","observation":"吸取區與指定非敏感面一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Pickup matches designated nonsensitive areas; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"通用吸嘴可能壓到未保護結構。","failureEn":"Generic collets can hit unprotected structures.","check":"吸取區與指定非敏感面一致。","checkEn":"Pickup matches designated nonsensitive areas.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-193-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"工具需避免敏感面壓傷。","textEn":"Tools must avoid damaging sensitive surfaces."},{"id":"pk-193-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"通用吸嘴可能壓到未保護結構；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Generic collets can hit unprotected structures. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「匹配重組取放工具」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Match reconstitution handling tools\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["吸取區與指定非敏感面一致","資料封包可供模封m09使用","模型保留相對膨脹與支承條件"],"optionsEn":["Pickup matches designated nonsensitive areas","The evidence package is ready for molding module m09","The model retains relative expansion and support"],"answer":0,"explanation":"工具需避免敏感面壓傷。本步要確認：吸取區與指定非敏感面一致；常見誤判是：通用吸嘴可能壓到未保護結構。","explanationEn":"Tools must avoid damaging sensitive surfaces. Verify: Pickup matches designated nonsensitive areas. A common misinterpretation is: Generic collets can hit unprotected structures."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-192"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-194","order":12,"sequence":194,"title":"驗收載體放置精度","titleEn":"Accept carrier placement accuracy","objective":"量測每顆晶粒XY及轉角，並能說明「誤差將傳遞到後續RDL對準」。","objectiveEn":"Measure each die's XY and rotation and explain: Errors propagate to later RDL alignment.","instruction":"量測每顆晶粒XY及轉角。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：位置分布不超出教學補償包絡。","instructionEn":"Measure each die's XY and rotation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Positions stay within the teaching compensation envelope.","observation":"位置分布不超出教學補償包絡；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Positions stay within the teaching compensation envelope; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平均位置正確可能掩蓋局部偏轉。","failureEn":"A correct average can hide local rotations.","check":"位置分布不超出教學補償包絡。","checkEn":"Positions stay within the teaching compensation envelope.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-194-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"誤差將傳遞到後續RDL對準。","textEn":"Errors propagate to later RDL alignment."},{"id":"pk-194-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平均位置正確可能掩蓋局部偏轉；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A correct average can hide local rotations. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗收載體放置精度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Accept carrier placement accuracy\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["放置區局部形貌可追溯","位置分布不超出教學補償包絡","輸入含模封放行pk-234證據"],"optionsEn":["Local placement-area shape is traceable","Positions stay within the teaching compensation envelope","Input includes molding-release evidence pk-234"],"answer":1,"explanation":"誤差將傳遞到後續RDL對準。本步要確認：位置分布不超出教學補償包絡；常見誤判是：平均位置正確可能掩蓋局部偏轉。","explanationEn":"Errors propagate to later RDL alignment. Verify: Positions stay within the teaching compensation envelope. A common misinterpretation is: A correct average can hide local rotations."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-193"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-195","order":13,"sequence":195,"title":"量測晶粒嵌入深度","titleEn":"Measure die seating depth","objective":"比較晶粒表面與黏層基準高度，並能說明「嵌入量影響解黏後面內平坦性」。","objectiveEn":"Compare die surfaces with adhesive reference height and explain: Seating depth affects later surface planarity.","instruction":"比較晶粒表面與黏層基準高度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：高度分布與後續平坦化需求相符。","instructionEn":"Compare die surfaces with adhesive reference height. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Height distribution suits later planarization.","observation":"高度分布與後續平坦化需求相符；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Height distribution suits later planarization; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"局部深陷會形成焊墊凹陷。","failureEn":"Deep seating can recess the pads.","check":"高度分布與後續平坦化需求相符。","checkEn":"Height distribution suits later planarization.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-195-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"嵌入量影響解黏後面內平坦性。","textEn":"Seating depth affects later surface planarity."},{"id":"pk-195-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"局部深陷會形成焊墊凹陷；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Deep seating can recess the pads. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測晶粒嵌入深度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure die seating depth\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["分離前後皆有明確承載面","耐受與釋離條件分開定義","高度分布與後續平坦化需求相符"],"optionsEn":["Both sides of separation have defined supports","Survival and release conditions are separately defined","Height distribution suits later planarization"],"answer":2,"explanation":"嵌入量影響解黏後面內平坦性。本步要確認：高度分布與後續平坦化需求相符；常見誤判是：局部深陷會形成焊墊凹陷。","explanationEn":"Seating depth affects later surface planarity. Verify: Height distribution suits later planarization. A common misinterpretation is: Deep seating can recess the pads."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-194"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-196","order":14,"sequence":196,"title":"檢查重組節距分布","titleEn":"Inspect reconstituted pitch distribution","objective":"比較相鄰晶粒中心間距，並能說明「局部節距變化不同於整片縮放」。","objectiveEn":"Compare neighboring die-center distances and explain: Local pitch changes differ from global scaling.","instruction":"比較相鄰晶粒中心間距。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：局部離群點與整體趨勢分開。","instructionEn":"Compare neighboring die-center distances. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Local outliers are separated from global trends.","observation":"局部離群點與整體趨勢分開；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Local outliers are separated from global trends; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"全片平均節距不能修正局部位移。","failureEn":"Mean pitch cannot correct local shifts.","check":"局部離群點與整體趨勢分開。","checkEn":"Local outliers are separated from global trends.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-196-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"局部節距變化不同於整片縮放。","textEn":"Local pitch changes differ from global scaling."},{"id":"pk-196-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"全片平均節距不能修正局部位移；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mean pitch cannot correct local shifts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查重組節距分布」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect reconstituted pitch distribution\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["局部離群點與整體趨勢分開","方法與載體透光性和材料相符","局部厚度未侵蝕高度預算"],"optionsEn":["Local outliers are separated from global trends","Method matches carrier transmission and material","Local thickness preserves the height budget"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部節距變化不同於整片縮放。本步要確認：局部離群點與整體趨勢分開；常見誤判是：全片平均節距不能修正局部位移。","explanationEn":"Local pitch changes differ from global scaling. Verify: Local outliers are separated from global trends. A common misinterpretation is: Mean pitch cannot correct local shifts."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-195"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-197","order":15,"sequence":197,"title":"驗證暫黏保持力","titleEn":"Verify temporary placement retention","objective":"比較搬運前後晶粒座標，並能說明「暫黏需抵抗後續移載擾動」。","objectiveEn":"Compare die positions around handling and explain: Temporary adhesion must resist transfer disturbances.","instruction":"比較搬運前後晶粒座標。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：移載後姿態改變可被量出。","instructionEn":"Compare die positions around handling. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Pose changes after transfer are measurable.","observation":"移載後姿態改變可被量出；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Pose changes after transfer are measurable; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"外觀看似固定仍可能微量滑移。","failureEn":"Apparently fixed dies can still drift.","check":"移載後姿態改變可被量出。","checkEn":"Pose changes after transfer are measurable.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-197-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"暫黏需抵抗後續移載擾動。","textEn":"Temporary adhesion must resist transfer disturbances."},{"id":"pk-197-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"外觀看似固定仍可能微量滑移；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Apparently fixed dies can still drift. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證暫黏保持力」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify temporary placement retention\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["至少一組標記在每個關鍵階段可讀","移載後姿態改變可被量出","異常阻力區有對應表面檢查"],"optionsEn":["At least one mark set survives each key stage","Pose changes after transfer are measurable","High-resistance regions have surface checks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫黏需抵抗後續移載擾動。本步要確認：移載後姿態改變可被量出；常見誤判是：外觀看似固定仍可能微量滑移。","explanationEn":"Temporary adhesion must resist transfer disturbances. Verify: Pose changes after transfer are measurable. A common misinterpretation is: Apparently fixed dies can still drift."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-196"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-198","order":16,"sequence":198,"title":"評估晶粒密度與流道","titleEn":"Assess die density and mold flow paths","objective":"標記密集區與狹窄填充通道，並能說明「布置改變模封料流動阻力」。","objectiveEn":"Mark dense regions and narrow fill channels and explain: Layout changes molding-flow resistance.","instruction":"標記密集區與狹窄填充通道。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：狹窄區具有可評估排氣路徑。","instructionEn":"Mark dense regions and narrow fill channels. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Narrow regions have assessable vent paths.","observation":"狹窄區具有可評估排氣路徑；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Narrow regions have assessable vent paths; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"均勻面積密度不保證局部流道通暢。","failureEn":"Uniform density does not guarantee open local channels.","check":"狹窄區具有可評估排氣路徑。","checkEn":"Narrow regions have assessable vent paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-198-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"布置改變模封料流動阻力。","textEn":"Layout changes molding-flow resistance."},{"id":"pk-198-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"均勻面積密度不保證局部流道通暢；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Uniform density does not guarantee open local channels. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估晶粒密度與流道」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess die density and mold flow paths\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["去殘留方案保留所有暴露材料","間隙可容納兩項功能包絡","狹窄區具有可評估排氣路徑"],"optionsEn":["Residue removal preserves all exposed materials","Gaps accommodate both functional envelopes","Narrow regions have assessable vent paths"],"answer":2,"explanation":"布置改變模封料流動阻力。本步要確認：狹窄區具有可評估排氣路徑；常見誤判是：均勻面積密度不保證局部流道通暢。","explanationEn":"Layout changes molding-flow resistance. Verify: Narrow regions have assessable vent paths. A common misinterpretation is: Uniform density does not guarantee open local channels."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-197"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-199","order":17,"sequence":199,"title":"定義載體邊緣排除區","titleEn":"Define carrier edge exclusion","objective":"將夾持、密封與有效晶粒區分開，並能說明「邊緣設備接觸限制有效面積」。","objectiveEn":"Separate clamping, sealing and active placement zones and explain: Edge tooling reduces usable placement area.","instruction":"將夾持、密封與有效晶粒區分開。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：晶粒未落入模具或夾具接觸區。","instructionEn":"Separate clamping, sealing and active placement zones. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Dies avoid mold and clamp contact zones.","observation":"晶粒未落入模具或夾具接觸區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Dies avoid mold and clamp contact zones; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"追求滿載可能使邊緣晶粒受壓。","failureEn":"Maximal loading can crush edge dies.","check":"晶粒未落入模具或夾具接觸區。","checkEn":"Dies avoid mold and clamp contact zones.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-199-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"邊緣設備接觸限制有效面積。","textEn":"Edge tooling reduces usable placement area."},{"id":"pk-199-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"追求滿載可能使邊緣晶粒受壓；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Maximal loading can crush edge dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「定義載體邊緣排除區」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Define carrier edge exclusion\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["晶粒未落入模具或夾具接觸區","每個必要焊墊都有可用接觸面","每個重組位置具有唯一來源ID"],"optionsEn":["Dies avoid mold and clamp contact zones","Every required pad has accessible contact area","Each reconstituted location has one source ID"],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣設備接觸限制有效面積。本步要確認：晶粒未落入模具或夾具接觸區；常見誤判是：追求滿載可能使邊緣晶粒受壓。","explanationEn":"Edge tooling reduces usable placement area. Verify: Dies avoid mold and clamp contact zones. A common misinterpretation is: Maximal loading can crush edge dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-198"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-200","order":18,"sequence":200,"title":"比較異質晶粒厚度","titleEn":"Compare heterogeneous die thicknesses","objective":"把不同晶粒高度放入共同剖面，並能說明「厚度差改變模封覆蓋與研磨需求」。","objectiveEn":"Place different die heights in one section and explain: Thickness differences alter mold coverage and grinding.","instruction":"把不同晶粒高度放入共同剖面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每種晶粒均有覆蓋及露出策略。","instructionEn":"Place different die heights in one section. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each die type has coverage and exposure planning.","observation":"每種晶粒均有覆蓋及露出策略；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each die type has coverage and exposure planning; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只按最高晶粒規劃會漏掉低晶粒界面。","failureEn":"Planning only the tallest die misses lower interfaces.","check":"每種晶粒均有覆蓋及露出策略。","checkEn":"Each die type has coverage and exposure planning.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-200-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"厚度差改變模封覆蓋與研磨需求。","textEn":"Thickness differences alter mold coverage and grinding."},{"id":"pk-200-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只按最高晶粒規劃會漏掉低晶粒界面；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Planning only the tallest die misses lower interfaces. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「比較異質晶粒厚度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Compare heterogeneous die thicknesses\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["解黏後焊墊朝向RDL工站","每種晶粒均有覆蓋及露出策略","座標轉換、版本與量測誤差完整"],"optionsEn":["Pads face the RDL station after debonding","Each die type has coverage and exposure planning","Transforms, revisions and measurement errors are complete"],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚度差改變模封覆蓋與研磨需求。本步要確認：每種晶粒均有覆蓋及露出策略；常見誤判是：只按最高晶粒規劃會漏掉低晶粒界面。","explanationEn":"Thickness differences alter mold coverage and grinding. Verify: Each die type has coverage and exposure planning. A common misinterpretation is: Planning only the tallest die misses lower interfaces."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-199"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-201","order":19,"sequence":201,"title":"交付模封前重組地圖","titleEn":"Release the pre-mold reconstitution map","objective":"凍結身分、姿態及暫黏異常清單，並能說明「模封前基準可量化後續位移」。","objectiveEn":"Freeze identities, poses and temporary-bond anomalies and explain: Pre-mold references quantify later die shift.","instruction":"凍結身分、姿態及暫黏異常清單。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：資料封包可供模封m09使用。","instructionEn":"Freeze identities, poses and temporary-bond anomalies. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The evidence package is ready for molding module m09.","observation":"資料封包可供模封m09使用；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The evidence package is ready for molding module m09; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"缺少前基準不能量出模封位移。","failureEn":"Without a baseline, mold-induced shift is unknown.","check":"資料封包可供模封m09使用。","checkEn":"The evidence package is ready for molding module m09.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-201-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"模封前基準可量化後續位移。","textEn":"Pre-mold references quantify later die shift."},{"id":"pk-201-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"缺少前基準不能量出模封位移；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Without a baseline, mold-induced shift is unknown. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「交付模封前重組地圖」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release the pre-mold reconstitution map\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["本例明確選晶粒先置正面朝下載體","吸取區與指定非敏感面一致","資料封包可供模封m09使用"],"optionsEn":["This example selects face-down die-first placement","Pickup matches designated nonsensitive areas","The evidence package is ready for molding module m09"],"answer":2,"explanation":"模封前基準可量化後續位移。本步要確認：資料封包可供模封m09使用；常見誤判是：缺少前基準不能量出模封位移。","explanationEn":"Pre-mold references quantify later die shift. Verify: The evidence package is ready for molding module m09. A common misinterpretation is: Without a baseline, mold-induced shift is unknown."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-200"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"before-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-202","order":20,"sequence":202,"title":"回收模封後位移地圖","titleEn":"Receive the post-mold shift map","objective":"完成m09後比較晶粒位移與旋轉，並能說明「本工序在實際模封完成後執行」。","objectiveEn":"After m09, compare die translation and rotation and explain: This operation follows physical molding.","instruction":"完成m09後比較晶粒位移與旋轉。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：輸入含模封放行pk-234證據。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"After m09, compare die translation and rotation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Input includes molding-release evidence pk-234. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"輸入含模封放行pk-234證據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Input includes molding-release evidence pk-234; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"在模封前執行會缺少必要形變資訊。","failureEn":"Pre-mold execution lacks deformation evidence.","check":"輸入含模封放行pk-234證據。","checkEn":"Input includes molding-release evidence pk-234.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-202-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"本工序在實際模封完成後執行。","textEn":"This operation follows physical molding."},{"id":"pk-202-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"在模封前執行會缺少必要形變資訊；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Pre-mold execution lacks deformation evidence. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-202-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設模封後某晶粒中心位移 dx=12 µm、dy=5 µm，位移長度 13 µm；若另有旋轉，晶粒角落位移可能更大，不能只補償中心。","textEn":"A hypothetical die shift dx=12 µm and dy=5 µm has magnitude 13 µm. Rotation may make corner displacement larger, so center correction alone is insufficient."},{"id":"pk-202-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"位移圖應保留每顆身份、中心、角度、局部尺度及擬合殘差。RDL 補償能力與曝光設備可修正模型相符才有意義。","textEn":"Displacement maps should retain die identity, center, angle, local scale and residuals. RDL correction is meaningful only within the exposure system's supported model."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「回收模封後位移地圖」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Receive the post-mold shift map\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["輸入含模封放行pk-234證據","每顆配置位置可回溯原晶圓座標","位置分布不超出教學補償包絡"],"optionsEn":["Input includes molding-release evidence pk-234","Each placement resolves to original wafer coordinates","Positions stay within the teaching compensation envelope"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本工序在實際模封完成後執行。本步要確認：輸入含模封放行pk-234證據；常見誤判是：在模封前執行會缺少必要形變資訊。","explanationEn":"This operation follows physical molding. Verify: Input includes molding-release evidence pk-234. A common misinterpretation is: Pre-mold execution lacks deformation evidence."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-234"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"after-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-203","order":21,"sequence":203,"title":"配置解黏承載轉移","titleEn":"Configure debond support transfer","objective":"在示意中保持模封體連續支承，並能說明「解黏會改變受力及支承界面」。","objectiveEn":"Maintain continuous molded-body support schematically and explain: Debonding changes load and support interfaces.","instruction":"在示意中保持模封體連續支承。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：分離前後皆有明確承載面。","instructionEn":"Maintain continuous molded-body support schematically. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Both sides of separation have defined supports.","observation":"分離前後皆有明確承載面；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Both sides of separation have defined supports; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"無支承剝離可能造成整片彎裂。","failureEn":"Unsupported peeling can crack the reconstructed wafer.","check":"分離前後皆有明確承載面。","checkEn":"Both sides of separation have defined supports.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-203-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"解黏會改變受力及支承界面。","textEn":"Debonding changes load and support interfaces."},{"id":"pk-203-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"無支承剝離可能造成整片彎裂；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Unsupported peeling can crack the reconstructed wafer. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「配置解黏承載轉移」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Configure debond support transfer\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["高度分布與後續平坦化需求相符","分離前後皆有明確承載面","模型保留相對膨脹與支承條件"],"optionsEn":["Height distribution suits later planarization","Both sides of separation have defined supports","The model retains relative expansion and support"],"answer":1,"explanation":"解黏會改變受力及支承界面。本步要確認：分離前後皆有明確承載面；常見誤判是：無支承剝離可能造成整片彎裂。","explanationEn":"Debonding changes load and support interfaces. Verify: Both sides of separation have defined supports. A common misinterpretation is: Unsupported peeling can crack the reconstructed wafer."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-202"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"after-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-204","order":22,"sequence":204,"title":"選擇相容解黏機制","titleEn":"Select compatible debond mechanism","objective":"對照熱、光或機械釋離材料資料，並能說明「不同離型材料需要不同釋離機制」。","objectiveEn":"Compare qualified thermal, optical or mechanical release data and explain: Release materials require distinct mechanisms.","instruction":"對照熱、光或機械釋離材料資料。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：方法與載體透光性和材料相符。","instructionEn":"Compare qualified thermal, optical or mechanical release data. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Method matches carrier transmission and material.","observation":"方法與載體透光性和材料相符；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Method matches carrier transmission and material; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"將光解黏套到不透光載體會失效。","failureEn":"Optical release may fail through opaque carriers.","check":"方法與載體透光性和材料相符。","checkEn":"Method matches carrier transmission and material.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-204-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同離型材料需要不同釋離機制。","textEn":"Release materials require distinct mechanisms."},{"id":"pk-204-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"將光解黏套到不透光載體會失效；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Optical release may fail through opaque carriers. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「選擇相容解黏機制」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Select compatible debond mechanism\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["放置區局部形貌可追溯","局部離群點與整體趨勢分開","方法與載體透光性和材料相符"],"optionsEn":["Local placement-area shape is traceable","Local outliers are separated from global trends","Method matches carrier transmission and material"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同離型材料需要不同釋離機制。本步要確認：方法與載體透光性和材料相符；常見誤判是：將光解黏套到不透光載體會失效。","explanationEn":"Release materials require distinct mechanisms. Verify: Method matches carrier transmission and material. A common misinterpretation is: Optical release may fail through opaque carriers."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-203"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"after-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-205","order":23,"sequence":205,"title":"判讀分離力與殘黏","titleEn":"Interpret separation force and residue","objective":"比較分離位置與殘黏圖，並能說明「殘黏分布揭示分離界面差異」。","objectiveEn":"Compare separation location and residue maps and explain: Residue distribution reveals interface differences.","instruction":"比較分離位置與殘黏圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常阻力區有對應表面檢查。","instructionEn":"Compare separation location and residue maps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: High-resistance regions have surface checks.","observation":"異常阻力區有對應表面檢查；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"High-resistance regions have surface checks; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"強拉可把可清殘膠變成結構損傷。","failureEn":"Forceful pulling turns residue into structural damage.","check":"異常阻力區有對應表面檢查。","checkEn":"High-resistance regions have surface checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-205-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"殘黏分布揭示分離界面差異。","textEn":"Residue distribution reveals interface differences."},{"id":"pk-205-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"強拉可把可清殘膠變成結構損傷；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Forceful pulling turns residue into structural damage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀分離力與殘黏」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret separation force and residue\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常阻力區有對應表面檢查","耐受與釋離條件分開定義","移載後姿態改變可被量出"],"optionsEn":["High-resistance regions have surface checks","Survival and release conditions are separately defined","Pose changes after transfer are measurable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘黏分布揭示分離界面差異。本步要確認：異常阻力區有對應表面檢查；常見誤判是：強拉可把可清殘膠變成結構損傷。","explanationEn":"Residue distribution reveals interface differences. Verify: High-resistance regions have surface checks. A common misinterpretation is: Forceful pulling turns residue into structural damage."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-204"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"after-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-206","order":24,"sequence":206,"title":"檢查解黏後殘留","titleEn":"Inspect post-debond residue","objective":"標示焊墊、鈍化面及模封料上的殘留，並能說明「不同表面可採的清潔相容性不同」。","objectiveEn":"Map residue on pads, passivation and mold and explain: Cleaning compatibility varies by surface.","instruction":"標示焊墊、鈍化面及模封料上的殘留。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：去殘留方案保留所有暴露材料。","instructionEn":"Map residue on pads, passivation and mold. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Residue removal preserves all exposed materials.","observation":"去殘留方案保留所有暴露材料；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Residue removal preserves all exposed materials; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"同一清洗可能傷害另一暴露材質。","failureEn":"One cleaning method can attack another material.","check":"去殘留方案保留所有暴露材料。","checkEn":"Residue removal preserves all exposed materials.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-206-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同表面可採的清潔相容性不同。","textEn":"Cleaning compatibility varies by surface."},{"id":"pk-206-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"同一清洗可能傷害另一暴露材質；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One cleaning method can attack another material. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查解黏後殘留」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect post-debond residue\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["狹窄區具有可評估排氣路徑","去殘留方案保留所有暴露材料","局部厚度未侵蝕高度預算"],"optionsEn":["Narrow regions have assessable vent paths","Residue removal preserves all exposed materials","Local thickness preserves the height budget"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同表面可採的清潔相容性不同。本步要確認：去殘留方案保留所有暴露材料；常見誤判是：同一清洗可能傷害另一暴露材質。","explanationEn":"Cleaning compatibility varies by surface. Verify: Residue removal preserves all exposed materials. A common misinterpretation is: One cleaning method can attack another material."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-205"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"after-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-207","order":25,"sequence":207,"title":"核對露出焊墊可接觸性","titleEn":"Check exposed-pad accessibility","objective":"比對露墊影像與原始焊墊地圖，並能說明「露出不完全會阻斷RDL接觸」。","objectiveEn":"Compare exposed pads with the original pad map and explain: Incomplete exposure blocks RDL contact.","instruction":"比對露墊影像與原始焊墊地圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：每個必要焊墊都有可用接觸面。","instructionEn":"Compare exposed pads with the original pad map. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Every required pad has accessible contact area.","observation":"每個必要焊墊都有可用接觸面；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Every required pad has accessible contact area; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"薄殘膜可能在外觀上難以辨識。","failureEn":"Thin residual films can be visually subtle.","check":"每個必要焊墊都有可用接觸面。","checkEn":"Every required pad has accessible contact area.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-207-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"露出不完全會阻斷RDL接觸。","textEn":"Incomplete exposure blocks RDL contact."},{"id":"pk-207-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"薄殘膜可能在外觀上難以辨識；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Thin residual films can be visually subtle. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對露出焊墊可接觸性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Check exposed-pad accessibility\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["至少一組標記在每個關鍵階段可讀","晶粒未落入模具或夾具接觸區","每個必要焊墊都有可用接觸面"],"optionsEn":["At least one mark set survives each key stage","Dies avoid mold and clamp contact zones","Every required pad has accessible contact area"],"answer":2,"explanation":"露出不完全會阻斷RDL接觸。本步要確認：每個必要焊墊都有可用接觸面；常見誤判是：薄殘膜可能在外觀上難以辨識。","explanationEn":"Incomplete exposure blocks RDL contact. Verify: Every required pad has accessible contact area. A common misinterpretation is: Thin residual films can be visually subtle."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-206"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"after-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-208","order":26,"sequence":208,"title":"交付重組RDL對準資料","titleEn":"Release reconstituted RDL alignment data","objective":"輸出晶粒真實座標與露墊狀態，並能說明「RDL應對準實際位置而非原放置理想值」。","objectiveEn":"Export actual die coordinates and pad accessibility and explain: RDL aligns to actual rather than ideal die positions.","instruction":"輸出晶粒真實座標與露墊狀態。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：座標轉換、版本與量測誤差完整。","instructionEn":"Export actual die coordinates and pad accessibility. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Transforms, revisions and measurement errors are complete.","observation":"座標轉換、版本與量測誤差完整；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Transforms, revisions and measurement errors are complete; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"沿用模封前座標可能造成接觸偏離。","failureEn":"Pre-mold coordinates can misalign contacts.","check":"座標轉換、版本與量測誤差完整。","checkEn":"Transforms, revisions and measurement errors are complete.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-208-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"RDL應對準實際位置而非原放置理想值。","textEn":"RDL aligns to actual rather than ideal die positions."},{"id":"pk-208-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"沿用模封前座標可能造成接觸偏離；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Pre-mold coordinates can misalign contacts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「交付重組RDL對準資料」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release reconstituted RDL alignment data\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["座標轉換、版本與量測誤差完整","間隙可容納兩項功能包絡","每種晶粒均有覆蓋及露出策略"],"optionsEn":["Transforms, revisions and measurement errors are complete","Gaps accommodate both functional envelopes","Each die type has coverage and exposure planning"],"answer":0,"explanation":"RDL應對準實際位置而非原放置理想值。本步要確認：座標轉換、版本與量測誤差完整；常見誤判是：沿用模封前座標可能造成接觸偏離。","explanationEn":"RDL aligns to actual rather than ideal die positions. Verify: Transforms, revisions and measurement errors are complete. A common misinterpretation is: Pre-mold coordinates can misalign contacts."},"sourceIds":["pk-amkor-fanout","pk-evg-tbdb","pk-evg-tbdb-flow","pk-besi-dieattach"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-207"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","manufacturingPosition":"after-molding","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m09","order":9,"sequence":9,"title":"模封、翹曲與模封研磨","titleEn":"Molding, warpage and mold grinding","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查模封、翹曲與模封研磨的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for molding, warpage and mold grinding. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"主要接扇出pk-201，結束pk-234後回pk-202；打線偏移僅為有線產品的替代案例。","routeEn":"Main route joins pk-201 and returns from pk-234 to pk-202; wire sweep is an alternative wirebond case.","sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-209","order":1,"sequence":209,"title":"確認模封分支與輸入","titleEn":"Confirm molding route and input","objective":"區分打線封膠與本例扇出重組模封，並能說明「不同輸入有不同脆弱結構」。","objectiveEn":"Separate wirebond encapsulation from fan-out reconstitution and explain: Different inputs expose different fragile structures.","instruction":"區分打線封膠與本例扇出重組模封。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：本例主路線接收pk-201重組資料。","instructionEn":"Separate wirebond encapsulation from fan-out reconstitution. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The main route receives pk-201 reconstitution data.","observation":"本例主路線接收pk-201重組資料；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The main route receives pk-201 reconstitution data; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"混用輸入會漏掉線弧或裸晶保護。","failureEn":"Mixed inputs overlook wire or die protection.","check":"本例主路線接收pk-201重組資料。","checkEn":"The main route receives pk-201 reconstitution data.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-209-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同輸入有不同脆弱結構。","textEn":"Different inputs expose different fragile structures."},{"id":"pk-209-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"混用輸入會漏掉線弧或裸晶保護；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mixed inputs overlook wire or die protection. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「確認模封分支與輸入」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Confirm molding route and input\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最後填充區保有排氣路徑","受力點避開未支持脆弱區","本例主路線接收pk-201重組資料"],"optionsEn":["Last-fill regions retain vent paths","Load points avoid unsupported fragile regions","The main route receives pk-201 reconstitution data"],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同輸入有不同脆弱結構。本步要確認：本例主路線接收pk-201重組資料；常見誤判是：混用輸入會漏掉線弧或裸晶保護。","explanationEn":"Different inputs expose different fragile structures. Verify: The main route receives pk-201 reconstitution data. A common misinterpretation is: Mixed inputs overlook wire or die protection."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-201"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","alternativePrerequisiteIds":["pk-156"],"alternativeRouteNote":"僅打線封膠案例；不得與扇出先決條件當作同時必須。","alternativeRouteNoteEn":"Wirebond encapsulation case only; not an additional mandatory fan-out prerequisite.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-210","order":2,"sequence":210,"title":"核對模封料批次","titleEn":"Verify molding-compound lot","objective":"比對批號、保存與核准材料等級，並能說明「模封料不是可任意互換的填料」。","objectiveEn":"Match lot, storage and qualified material grade and explain: Molding compounds are not interchangeable fillers.","instruction":"比對批號、保存與核准材料等級。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：實際材料與指定材料一致。","instructionEn":"Match lot, storage and qualified material grade. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Actual and specified material agree.","observation":"實際材料與指定材料一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Actual and specified material agree; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"相似名稱可能掩蓋不同固化體系。","failureEn":"Similar names may hide different cure systems.","check":"實際材料與指定材料一致。","checkEn":"Actual and specified material agree.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-210-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"模封料不是可任意互換的填料。","textEn":"Molding compounds are not interchangeable fillers."},{"id":"pk-210-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"相似名稱可能掩蓋不同固化體系；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Similar names may hide different cure systems. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對模封料批次」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify molding-compound lot\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["實際材料與指定材料一致","異常曲線能區分慢抽與洩漏假設","缺陷位置能回指模具界面"],"optionsEn":["Actual and specified material agree","Abnormal traces distinguish slow pumping from leaks","Defects map back to mold interfaces"],"answer":0,"explanation":"模封料不是可任意互換的填料。本步要確認：實際材料與指定材料一致；常見誤判是：相似名稱可能掩蓋不同固化體系。","explanationEn":"Molding compounds are not interchangeable fillers. Verify: Actual and specified material agree. A common misinterpretation is: Similar names may hide different cure systems."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-209"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-211","order":3,"sequence":211,"title":"評估材料預處理","titleEn":"Assess material preconditioning","objective":"依供應商資料解讀回溫與防潮需求，並能說明「水分與溫度會影響流動及氣泡」。","objectiveEn":"Interpret conditioning and moisture control from supplier data and explain: Moisture and temperature affect flow and bubbles.","instruction":"依供應商資料解讀回溫與防潮需求。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：狀態判定含完整暴露紀錄。","instructionEn":"Interpret conditioning and moisture control from supplier data. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Material-state decisions include exposure history.","observation":"狀態判定含完整暴露紀錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Material-state decisions include exposure history; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"任意烘烤可能改變材料可加工性。","failureEn":"Arbitrary baking can alter processability.","check":"狀態判定含完整暴露紀錄。","checkEn":"Material-state decisions include exposure history.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-211-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"水分與溫度會影響流動及氣泡。","textEn":"Moisture and temperature affect flow and bubbles."},{"id":"pk-211-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"任意烘烤可能改變材料可加工性；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Arbitrary baking can alter processability. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估材料預處理」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess material preconditioning\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["差值使用一致支承與座標","狀態判定含完整暴露紀錄","各階段對應正確物理事件"],"optionsEn":["Differences use consistent support and coordinates","Material-state decisions include exposure history","Each phase matches its physical event"],"answer":1,"explanation":"水分與溫度會影響流動及氣泡。本步要確認：狀態判定含完整暴露紀錄；常見誤判是：任意烘烤可能改變材料可加工性。","explanationEn":"Moisture and temperature affect flow and bubbles. Verify: Material-state decisions include exposure history. A common misinterpretation is: Arbitrary baking can alter processability."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-210"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-212","order":4,"sequence":212,"title":"比較填料尺度與間隙","titleEn":"Compare filler scale and gaps","objective":"將填料尺度分布對照最窄流道，並能說明「細間隙可能篩阻大顆粒填料」。","objectiveEn":"Compare filler-size distribution with narrow gaps and explain: Narrow gaps can exclude larger fillers.","instruction":"將填料尺度分布對照最窄流道。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：流道設計包含填料分布影響。","instructionEn":"Compare filler-size distribution with narrow gaps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Flow paths account for filler distribution.","observation":"流道設計包含填料分布影響；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Flow paths account for filler distribution; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看平均粒徑會漏掉大顆粒堵塞。","failureEn":"Mean particle size misses large-particle blockage.","check":"流道設計包含填料分布影響。","checkEn":"Flow paths account for filler distribution.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-212-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"細間隙可能篩阻大顆粒填料。","textEn":"Narrow gaps can exclude larger fillers."},{"id":"pk-212-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看平均粒徑會漏掉大顆粒堵塞；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mean particle size misses large-particle blockage. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「比較填料尺度與間隙」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Compare filler scale and gaps\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["溫度圖與固化差異能互相檢查","曲線包含升溫與降溫方向","流道設計包含填料分布影響"],"optionsEn":["Temperature maps cross-check cure differences","Curves distinguish heating from cooling","Flow paths account for filler distribution"],"answer":2,"explanation":"細間隙可能篩阻大顆粒填料。本步要確認：流道設計包含填料分布影響；常見誤判是：只看平均粒徑會漏掉大顆粒堵塞。","explanationEn":"Narrow gaps can exclude larger fillers. Verify: Flow paths account for filler distribution. A common misinterpretation is: Mean particle size misses large-particle blockage."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-211"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-213","order":5,"sequence":213,"title":"判讀黏度與固化競爭","titleEn":"Interpret viscosity-cure competition","objective":"比較流動窗口與膠化趨勢，並能說明「流動完成需早於失去流動能力」。","objectiveEn":"Compare the flow window and gelation trend and explain: Filling must precede loss of flow.","instruction":"比較流動窗口與膠化趨勢。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：模型把填充與膠化分成不同事件。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Compare the flow window and gelation trend. Check evidence you create or obtain against: The model separates filling and gelation. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"模型把填充與膠化分成不同事件；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"The model separates filling and gelation; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"低初始黏度不能保證完整填充。","failureEn":"Low initial viscosity does not guarantee full filling.","check":"模型把填充與膠化分成不同事件。","checkEn":"The model separates filling and gelation.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-213-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"流動完成需早於失去流動能力。","textEn":"Filling must precede loss of flow."},{"id":"pk-213-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"低初始黏度不能保證完整填充；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Low initial viscosity does not guarantee full filling. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-213-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"填充與固化競爭可用 tfill/tgel 作教學比較；假設填充需 40 s、可流動窗口 60 s，比值 0.67，但不能把它單獨當量產安全餘裕。","textEn":"Use tfill/tgel as a teaching comparison; hypothetical 40 s fill and 60 s flow window give 0.67, not a standalone production safety margin."},{"id":"pk-213-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"黏度隨溫度和反應程度變化，升溫可能先降黏後快速固化。需看時間曲線、填料分離與狹窄間隙，不能只引用室溫黏度。","textEn":"Viscosity depends on temperature and conversion; heating may initially lower viscosity then accelerate cure. Inspect time histories, filler segregation and gaps rather than room-temperature viscosity alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀黏度與固化競爭」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret viscosity-cure competition\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["模型把填充與膠化分成不同事件","流動推論有可觀察形貌支持","各類晶粒的最薄覆蓋均被核對"],"optionsEn":["The model separates filling and gelation","Flow interpretations have observable shape evidence","Minimum cover is checked for every die type"],"answer":0,"explanation":"流動完成需早於失去流動能力。本步要確認：模型把填充與膠化分成不同事件；常見誤判是：低初始黏度不能保證完整填充。","explanationEn":"Filling must precede loss of flow. Verify: The model separates filling and gelation. A common misinterpretation is: Low initial viscosity does not guarantee full filling."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-212"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-214","order":6,"sequence":214,"title":"檢查模穴與密封面","titleEn":"Inspect cavity and sealing surfaces","objective":"核對異物、平整與密封接觸，並能說明「密封失效可造成漏料與真空異常」。","objectiveEn":"Check debris, flatness and sealing contact and explain: Seal faults cause leakage and vacuum errors.","instruction":"核對異物、平整與密封接觸。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異物與密封缺口均已處置。","instructionEn":"Check debris, flatness and sealing contact. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Debris and sealing gaps have dispositions.","observation":"異物與密封缺口均已處置；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Debris and sealing gaps have dispositions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"靠增加壓力無法修復受損密封。","failureEn":"Higher pressure cannot repair damaged seals.","check":"異物與密封缺口均已處置。","checkEn":"Debris and sealing gaps have dispositions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-214-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"密封失效可造成漏料與真空異常。","textEn":"Seal faults cause leakage and vacuum errors."},{"id":"pk-214-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"靠增加壓力無法修復受損密封；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Higher pressure cannot repair damaged seals. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查模穴與密封面」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect cavity and sealing surfaces\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["露出位置與核准剖面一致","異物與密封缺口均已處置","分類保留位置與界面資訊"],"optionsEn":["Exposure matches the approved section","Debris and sealing gaps have dispositions","Classification retains position and interface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"密封失效可造成漏料與真空異常。本步要確認：異物與密封缺口均已處置；常見誤判是：靠增加壓力無法修復受損密封。","explanationEn":"Seal faults cause leakage and vacuum errors. Verify: Debris and sealing gaps have dispositions. A common misinterpretation is: Higher pressure cannot repair damaged seals."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-213"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-215","order":7,"sequence":215,"title":"評估離型膜貼覆","titleEn":"Assess mold-release film coverage","objective":"比較褶皺與模穴角落貼合，並能說明「膜皺折可被複製到成品表面」。","objectiveEn":"Compare wrinkles and cavity-corner conformance and explain: Film wrinkles can print onto the package.","instruction":"比較褶皺與模穴角落貼合。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：表面限制區無未解決折痕。","instructionEn":"Compare wrinkles and cavity-corner conformance. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Critical surfaces lack unresolved creases.","observation":"表面限制區無未解決折痕；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Critical surfaces lack unresolved creases; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把膜紋當材料缺陷會誤診。","failureEn":"Film marks can be mistaken for material defects.","check":"表面限制區無未解決折痕。","checkEn":"Critical surfaces lack unresolved creases.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-215-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"膜皺折可被複製到成品表面。","textEn":"Film wrinkles can print onto the package."},{"id":"pk-215-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把膜紋當材料缺陷會誤診；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Film marks can be mistaken for material defects. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估離型膜貼覆」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess mold-release film coverage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["有線分支量測最小線距變化","疑似分層有位置與確認方法","表面限制區無未解決折痕"],"optionsEn":["Wirebond routes measure minimum-spacing changes","Suspected delamination has location and confirmation","Critical surfaces lack unresolved creases"],"answer":2,"explanation":"膜皺折可被複製到成品表面。本步要確認：表面限制區無未解決折痕；常見誤判是：把膜紋當材料缺陷會誤診。","explanationEn":"Film wrinkles can print onto the package. Verify: Critical surfaces lack unresolved creases. A common misinterpretation is: Film marks can be mistaken for material defects."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-214"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-216","order":8,"sequence":216,"title":"分析流動入口佈局","titleEn":"Analyze molding inlet layout","objective":"在晶粒布置上標出入料與障礙，並能說明「幾何障礙改變流動前緣」。","objectiveEn":"Map inlets and obstructions over die layout and explain: Obstructions change flow fronts.","instruction":"在晶粒布置上標出入料與障礙。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：慢流區與匯流區被標示。","instructionEn":"Map inlets and obstructions over die layout. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Slow-flow and merging regions are marked.","observation":"慢流區與匯流區被標示；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Slow-flow and merging regions are marked; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"均勻壓力不表示各區同步填滿。","failureEn":"Uniform pressure does not imply simultaneous filling.","check":"慢流區與匯流區被標示。","checkEn":"Slow-flow and merging regions are marked.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-216-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"幾何障礙改變流動前緣。","textEn":"Obstructions change flow fronts."},{"id":"pk-216-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"均勻壓力不表示各區同步填滿；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Uniform pressure does not imply simultaneous filling. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分析流動入口佈局」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Analyze molding inlet layout\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["慢流區與匯流區被標示","位移與旋轉均有空間分布","pk-234資料足以支持pk-202接續"],"optionsEn":["Slow-flow and merging regions are marked","Translation and rotation have spatial maps","pk-234 evidence supports continuation at pk-202"],"answer":0,"explanation":"幾何障礙改變流動前緣。本步要確認：慢流區與匯流區被標示；常見誤判是：均勻壓力不表示各區同步填滿。","explanationEn":"Obstructions change flow fronts. Verify: Slow-flow and merging regions are marked. A common misinterpretation is: Uniform pressure does not imply simultaneous filling."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-215"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-217","order":9,"sequence":217,"title":"規劃排氣路徑","titleEn":"Plan venting paths","objective":"追蹤最後填滿區到排氣口，並能說明「封閉流動前緣可能困住氣體」。","objectiveEn":"Trace last-fill regions toward vents and explain: Closed flow fronts can trap gas.","instruction":"追蹤最後填滿區到排氣口。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最後填充區保有排氣路徑。","instructionEn":"Trace last-fill regions toward vents. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Last-fill regions retain vent paths.","observation":"最後填充區保有排氣路徑；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Last-fill regions retain vent paths; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"排氣口早被覆蓋會困氣。","failureEn":"Early vent blockage traps gas.","check":"最後填充區保有排氣路徑。","checkEn":"Last-fill regions retain vent paths.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-217-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"封閉流動前緣可能困住氣體。","textEn":"Closed flow fronts can trap gas."},{"id":"pk-217-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"排氣口早被覆蓋會困氣；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Early vent blockage traps gas. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「規劃排氣路徑」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Plan venting paths\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["本例主路線接收pk-201重組資料","最後填充區保有排氣路徑","結論引用核准曲線或材料量測"],"optionsEn":["The main route receives pk-201 reconstitution data","Last-fill regions retain vent paths","Conclusions use qualified profiles or material measurements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"封閉流動前緣可能困住氣體。本步要確認：最後填充區保有排氣路徑；常見誤判是：排氣口早被覆蓋會困氣。","explanationEn":"Closed flow fronts can trap gas. Verify: Last-fill regions retain vent paths. A common misinterpretation is: Early vent blockage traps gas."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-216"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-218","order":10,"sequence":218,"title":"判讀抽真空歷程","titleEn":"Interpret cavity-vacuum history","objective":"比較抽氣曲線與保壓洩漏，並能說明「穩定真空需結合密封與逸氣狀態」。","objectiveEn":"Compare evacuation traces and leak behavior and explain: Stable vacuum depends on sealing and outgassing.","instruction":"比較抽氣曲線與保壓洩漏。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：異常曲線能區分慢抽與洩漏假設。","instructionEn":"Compare evacuation traces and leak behavior. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Abnormal traces distinguish slow pumping from leaks.","observation":"異常曲線能區分慢抽與洩漏假設；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Abnormal traces distinguish slow pumping from leaks; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看最低壓值會漏掉回升。","failureEn":"Minimum pressure alone misses rebound.","check":"異常曲線能區分慢抽與洩漏假設。","checkEn":"Abnormal traces distinguish slow pumping from leaks.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-218-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"穩定真空需結合密封與逸氣狀態。","textEn":"Stable vacuum depends on sealing and outgassing."},{"id":"pk-218-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看最低壓值會漏掉回升；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Minimum pressure alone misses rebound. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀抽真空歷程」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret cavity-vacuum history\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["熱歷程與裝夾方式共同記錄","實際材料與指定材料一致","異常曲線能區分慢抽與洩漏假設"],"optionsEn":["Thermal history and fixturing are recorded together","Actual and specified material agree","Abnormal traces distinguish slow pumping from leaks"],"answer":2,"explanation":"穩定真空需結合密封與逸氣狀態。本步要確認：異常曲線能區分慢抽與洩漏假設；常見誤判是：只看最低壓值會漏掉回升。","explanationEn":"Stable vacuum depends on sealing and outgassing. Verify: Abnormal traces distinguish slow pumping from leaks. A common misinterpretation is: Minimum pressure alone misses rebound."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-217"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-219","order":11,"sequence":219,"title":"判讀模封壓力歷程","titleEn":"Interpret molding-pressure history","objective":"標示填充、保持與卸壓階段，並能說明「壓力歷程影響流動與結構受力」。","objectiveEn":"Mark fill, hold and unload phases and explain: Pressure history affects flow and structural loading.","instruction":"標示填充、保持與卸壓階段。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：各階段對應正確物理事件。","instructionEn":"Mark fill, hold and unload phases. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Each phase matches its physical event.","observation":"各階段對應正確物理事件；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Each phase matches its physical event; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"整段用同一平均值會掩蓋瞬態。","failureEn":"One average hides transient loading.","check":"各階段對應正確物理事件。","checkEn":"Each phase matches its physical event.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-219-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"壓力歷程影響流動與結構受力。","textEn":"Pressure history affects flow and structural loading."},{"id":"pk-219-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"整段用同一平均值會掩蓋瞬態；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One average hides transient loading. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「判讀模封壓力歷程」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Interpret molding-pressure history\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["各階段對應正確物理事件","受力點避開未支持脆弱區","狀態判定含完整暴露紀錄"],"optionsEn":["Each phase matches its physical event","Load points avoid unsupported fragile regions","Material-state decisions include exposure history"],"answer":0,"explanation":"壓力歷程影響流動與結構受力。本步要確認：各階段對應正確物理事件；常見誤判是：整段用同一平均值會掩蓋瞬態。","explanationEn":"Pressure history affects flow and structural loading. Verify: Each phase matches its physical event. A common misinterpretation is: One average hides transient loading."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-218"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-220","order":12,"sequence":220,"title":"核對模具溫度均勻性","titleEn":"Verify mold-temperature uniformity","objective":"比較多區溫度與材料反應趨勢，並能說明「溫差可造成黏度和固化差異」。","objectiveEn":"Compare zone temperatures and material response and explain: Temperature gradients change viscosity and cure.","instruction":"比較多區溫度與材料反應趨勢。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：溫度圖與固化差異能互相檢查。","instructionEn":"Compare zone temperatures and material response. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Temperature maps cross-check cure differences.","observation":"溫度圖與固化差異能互相檢查；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Temperature maps cross-check cure differences; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"單區感測不能代表整片模封體。","failureEn":"One sensor cannot represent the entire molded body.","check":"溫度圖與固化差異能互相檢查。","checkEn":"Temperature maps cross-check cure differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-220-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"溫差可造成黏度和固化差異。","textEn":"Temperature gradients change viscosity and cure."},{"id":"pk-220-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"單區感測不能代表整片模封體；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"One sensor cannot represent the entire molded body. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對模具溫度均勻性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify mold-temperature uniformity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["流道設計包含填料分布影響","溫度圖與固化差異能互相檢查","缺陷位置能回指模具界面"],"optionsEn":["Flow paths account for filler distribution","Temperature maps cross-check cure differences","Defects map back to mold interfaces"],"answer":1,"explanation":"溫差可造成黏度和固化差異。本步要確認：溫度圖與固化差異能互相檢查；常見誤判是：單區感測不能代表整片模封體。","explanationEn":"Temperature gradients change viscosity and cure. Verify: Temperature maps cross-check cure differences. A common misinterpretation is: One sensor cannot represent the entire molded body."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-219"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-221","order":13,"sequence":221,"title":"追蹤填充前緣","titleEn":"Track the molding front","objective":"比較示意流動快慢與短射位置，並能說明「短射可揭露未填滿的路徑」。","objectiveEn":"Compare front progression with short-shot locations and explain: Short shots reveal incomplete flow paths.","instruction":"比較示意流動快慢與短射位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：流動推論有可觀察形貌支持。","instructionEn":"Compare front progression with short-shot locations. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Flow interpretations have observable shape evidence.","observation":"流動推論有可觀察形貌支持；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Flow interpretations have observable shape evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"外緣已滿不代表內部已填滿。","failureEn":"Filled edges do not prove filled interiors.","check":"流動推論有可觀察形貌支持。","checkEn":"Flow interpretations have observable shape evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-221-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"短射可揭露未填滿的路徑。","textEn":"Short shots reveal incomplete flow paths."},{"id":"pk-221-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"外緣已滿不代表內部已填滿；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Filled edges do not prove filled interiors. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「追蹤填充前緣」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Track the molding front\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["差值使用一致支承與座標","模型把填充與膠化分成不同事件","流動推論有可觀察形貌支持"],"optionsEn":["Differences use consistent support and coordinates","The model separates filling and gelation","Flow interpretations have observable shape evidence"],"answer":2,"explanation":"短射可揭露未填滿的路徑。本步要確認：流動推論有可觀察形貌支持；常見誤判是：外緣已滿不代表內部已填滿。","explanationEn":"Short shots reveal incomplete flow paths. Verify: Flow interpretations have observable shape evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Filled edges do not prove filled interiors."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-220"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-222","order":14,"sequence":222,"title":"分類模封空洞","titleEn":"Classify molding voids","objective":"區分孤立氣泡、界面空隙與未填充，並能說明「不同形態對應不同機制假設」。","objectiveEn":"Separate bubbles, interface gaps and unfilled regions and explain: Different shapes suggest different mechanisms.","instruction":"區分孤立氣泡、界面空隙與未填充。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：分類保留位置與界面資訊。","instructionEn":"Separate bubbles, interface gaps and unfilled regions. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Classification retains position and interface.","observation":"分類保留位置與界面資訊；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Classification retains position and interface; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"一律稱氣泡會掩蓋脫層或短射。","failureEn":"Calling everything bubbles hides delamination or short fill.","check":"分類保留位置與界面資訊。","checkEn":"Classification retains position and interface.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-222-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同形態對應不同機制假設。","textEn":"Different shapes suggest different mechanisms."},{"id":"pk-222-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"一律稱氣泡會掩蓋脫層或短射；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Calling everything bubbles hides delamination or short fill. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分類模封空洞」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Classify molding voids\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["分類保留位置與界面資訊","曲線包含升溫與降溫方向","異物與密封缺口均已處置"],"optionsEn":["Classification retains position and interface","Curves distinguish heating from cooling","Debris and sealing gaps have dispositions"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同形態對應不同機制假設。本步要確認：分類保留位置與界面資訊；常見誤判是：一律稱氣泡會掩蓋脫層或短射。","explanationEn":"Different shapes suggest different mechanisms. Verify: Classification retains position and interface. A common misinterpretation is: Calling everything bubbles hides delamination or short fill."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-221"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-223","order":15,"sequence":223,"title":"評估打線偏移替代分支","titleEn":"Assess wire-sweep alternative branch","objective":"僅對打線輸入比較封前封後線弧，並能說明「流動負載可移動細線」。","objectiveEn":"For wirebond inputs, compare loops around molding and explain: Flow loads can displace fine wires.","instruction":"僅對打線輸入比較封前封後線弧。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：有線分支量測最小線距變化。","instructionEn":"For wirebond inputs, compare loops around molding. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Wirebond routes measure minimum-spacing changes.","observation":"有線分支量測最小線距變化；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Wirebond routes measure minimum-spacing changes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"無線扇出產品不應虛構線弧檢查。","failureEn":"Wireless fan-out should not invent wire-loop checks.","check":"有線分支量測最小線距變化。","checkEn":"Wirebond routes measure minimum-spacing changes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-223-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"流動負載可移動細線。","textEn":"Flow loads can displace fine wires."},{"id":"pk-223-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"無線扇出產品不應虛構線弧檢查；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Wireless fan-out should not invent wire-loop checks. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估打線偏移替代分支」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess wire-sweep alternative branch\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["表面限制區無未解決折痕","有線分支量測最小線距變化","各類晶粒的最薄覆蓋均被核對"],"optionsEn":["Critical surfaces lack unresolved creases","Wirebond routes measure minimum-spacing changes","Minimum cover is checked for every die type"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流動負載可移動細線。本步要確認：有線分支量測最小線距變化；常見誤判是：無線扇出產品不應虛構線弧檢查。","explanationEn":"Flow loads can displace fine wires. Verify: Wirebond routes measure minimum-spacing changes. A common misinterpretation is: Wireless fan-out should not invent wire-loop checks."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-222"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-224","order":16,"sequence":224,"title":"量測模封晶粒位移","titleEn":"Measure mold-induced die shift","objective":"比較pk-201基準與模封後晶粒姿態，並能說明「模封流動與收縮可移動晶粒」。","objectiveEn":"Compare pk-201 baseline with post-mold die poses and explain: Mold flow and shrinkage can shift dies.","instruction":"比較pk-201基準與模封後晶粒姿態。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：位移與旋轉均有空間分布。","instructionEn":"Compare pk-201 baseline with post-mold die poses. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Translation and rotation have spatial maps.","observation":"位移與旋轉均有空間分布；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Translation and rotation have spatial maps; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只補全片平移不能修正局部轉角。","failureEn":"Global translation cannot fix local rotations.","check":"位移與旋轉均有空間分布。","checkEn":"Translation and rotation have spatial maps.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-224-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"模封流動與收縮可移動晶粒。","textEn":"Mold flow and shrinkage can shift dies."},{"id":"pk-224-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只補全片平移不能修正局部轉角；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Global translation cannot fix local rotations. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測模封晶粒位移」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure mold-induced die shift\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["露出位置與核准剖面一致","慢流區與匯流區被標示","位移與旋轉均有空間分布"],"optionsEn":["Exposure matches the approved section","Slow-flow and merging regions are marked","Translation and rotation have spatial maps"],"answer":2,"explanation":"模封流動與收縮可移動晶粒。本步要確認：位移與旋轉均有空間分布；常見誤判是：只補全片平移不能修正局部轉角。","explanationEn":"Mold flow and shrinkage can shift dies. Verify: Translation and rotation have spatial maps. A common misinterpretation is: Global translation cannot fix local rotations."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-223"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-225","order":17,"sequence":225,"title":"評估固化完成證據","titleEn":"Assess cure-completion evidence","objective":"區分經過加熱與材料轉化證據，並能說明「加熱時間不是唯一固化證據」。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish heating exposure from conversion evidence and explain: Heating time is not sole cure evidence.","instruction":"區分經過加熱與材料轉化證據。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：結論引用核准曲線或材料量測。","instructionEn":"Distinguish heating exposure from conversion evidence. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Conclusions use qualified profiles or material measurements.","observation":"結論引用核准曲線或材料量測；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Conclusions use qualified profiles or material measurements; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"表面變硬不等於全部固化完成。","failureEn":"Surface hardening does not prove complete cure.","check":"結論引用核准曲線或材料量測。","checkEn":"Conclusions use qualified profiles or material measurements.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-225-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"加熱時間不是唯一固化證據。","textEn":"Heating time is not sole cure evidence."},{"id":"pk-225-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"表面變硬不等於全部固化完成；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Surface hardening does not prove complete cure. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估固化完成證據」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess cure-completion evidence\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["結論引用核准曲線或材料量測","疑似分層有位置與確認方法","最後填充區保有排氣路徑"],"optionsEn":["Conclusions use qualified profiles or material measurements","Suspected delamination has location and confirmation","Last-fill regions retain vent paths"],"answer":0,"explanation":"加熱時間不是唯一固化證據。本步要確認：結論引用核准曲線或材料量測；常見誤判是：表面變硬不等於全部固化完成。","explanationEn":"Heating time is not sole cure evidence. Verify: Conclusions use qualified profiles or material measurements. A common misinterpretation is: Surface hardening does not prove complete cure."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-224"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-226","order":18,"sequence":226,"title":"規劃後固化支承","titleEn":"Plan post-mold-cure support","objective":"對照件溫歷程與支承限制，並能說明「後固化可能繼續收縮與變形」。","objectiveEn":"Compare part-temperature history and support constraints and explain: Post-cure may continue shrinkage and deformation.","instruction":"對照件溫歷程與支承限制。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：熱歷程與裝夾方式共同記錄。","instructionEn":"Compare part-temperature history and support constraints. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Thermal history and fixturing are recorded together.","observation":"熱歷程與裝夾方式共同記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Thermal history and fixturing are recorded together; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"不同支承的翹曲值不能直接混比。","failureEn":"Warpage under different supports is not directly comparable.","check":"熱歷程與裝夾方式共同記錄。","checkEn":"Thermal history and fixturing are recorded together.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-226-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"後固化可能繼續收縮與變形。","textEn":"Post-cure may continue shrinkage and deformation."},{"id":"pk-226-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"不同支承的翹曲值不能直接混比；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Warpage under different supports is not directly comparable. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「規劃後固化支承」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Plan post-mold-cure support\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["異常曲線能區分慢抽與洩漏假設","熱歷程與裝夾方式共同記錄","pk-234資料足以支持pk-202接續"],"optionsEn":["Abnormal traces distinguish slow pumping from leaks","Thermal history and fixturing are recorded together","pk-234 evidence supports continuation at pk-202"],"answer":1,"explanation":"後固化可能繼續收縮與變形。本步要確認：熱歷程與裝夾方式共同記錄；常見誤判是：不同支承的翹曲值不能直接混比。","explanationEn":"Post-cure may continue shrinkage and deformation. Verify: Thermal history and fixturing are recorded together. A common misinterpretation is: Warpage under different supports is not directly comparable."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-225"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-227","order":19,"sequence":227,"title":"檢查脫模受力區","titleEn":"Inspect demolding load zones","objective":"標出頂出或分離接觸位置，並能說明「脫模負載可造成邊角或界面損傷」。","objectiveEn":"Mark ejection and separation contacts and explain: Demolding loads can damage edges and interfaces.","instruction":"標出頂出或分離接觸位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：受力點避開未支持脆弱區。","instructionEn":"Mark ejection and separation contacts. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Load points avoid unsupported fragile regions.","observation":"受力點避開未支持脆弱區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Load points avoid unsupported fragile regions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"增大頂出力可能加劇裂損。","failureEn":"More ejection force may worsen cracking.","check":"受力點避開未支持脆弱區。","checkEn":"Load points avoid unsupported fragile regions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-227-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"脫模負載可造成邊角或界面損傷。","textEn":"Demolding loads can damage edges and interfaces."},{"id":"pk-227-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"增大頂出力可能加劇裂損；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"More ejection force may worsen cracking. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查脫模受力區」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect demolding load zones\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["本例主路線接收pk-201重組資料","各階段對應正確物理事件","受力點避開未支持脆弱區"],"optionsEn":["The main route receives pk-201 reconstitution data","Each phase matches its physical event","Load points avoid unsupported fragile regions"],"answer":2,"explanation":"脫模負載可造成邊角或界面損傷。本步要確認：受力點避開未支持脆弱區；常見誤判是：增大頂出力可能加劇裂損。","explanationEn":"Demolding loads can damage edges and interfaces. Verify: Load points avoid unsupported fragile regions. A common misinterpretation is: More ejection force may worsen cracking."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-226"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-228","order":20,"sequence":228,"title":"辨識溢料與披鋒","titleEn":"Identify flash and bleed","objective":"將多餘材料與密封位置比對，並能說明「披鋒可能反映密封或填充問題」。","objectiveEn":"Compare excess material with sealing locations and explain: Flash may reflect sealing or filling faults.","instruction":"將多餘材料與密封位置比對。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：缺陷位置能回指模具界面。","instructionEn":"Compare excess material with sealing locations. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Defects map back to mold interfaces.","observation":"缺陷位置能回指模具界面；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Defects map back to mold interfaces; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只修邊不追來源會反覆發生。","failureEn":"Trimming without diagnosis allows recurrence.","check":"缺陷位置能回指模具界面。","checkEn":"Defects map back to mold interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-228-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"披鋒可能反映密封或填充問題。","textEn":"Flash may reflect sealing or filling faults."},{"id":"pk-228-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只修邊不追來源會反覆發生；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Trimming without diagnosis allows recurrence. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「辨識溢料與披鋒」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Identify flash and bleed\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["缺陷位置能回指模具界面","實際材料與指定材料一致","溫度圖與固化差異能互相檢查"],"optionsEn":["Defects map back to mold interfaces","Actual and specified material agree","Temperature maps cross-check cure differences"],"answer":0,"explanation":"披鋒可能反映密封或填充問題。本步要確認：缺陷位置能回指模具界面；常見誤判是：只修邊不追來源會反覆發生。","explanationEn":"Flash may reflect sealing or filling faults. Verify: Defects map back to mold interfaces. A common misinterpretation is: Trimming without diagnosis allows recurrence."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-227"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-229","order":21,"sequence":229,"title":"量測室溫模封翹曲","titleEn":"Measure room-temperature warpage","objective":"採同一基準比較模封前後形貌，並能說明「複合結構收縮造成曲率變化」。","objectiveEn":"Compare pre/post-mold shape with one reference and explain: Composite shrinkage changes curvature.","instruction":"採同一基準比較模封前後形貌。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：差值使用一致支承與座標。","instructionEn":"Compare pre/post-mold shape with one reference. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Differences use consistent support and coordinates.","observation":"差值使用一致支承與座標；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Differences use consistent support and coordinates; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"正反面方向混用會顛倒曲率。","failureEn":"Mixed viewing sides invert curvature sign.","check":"差值使用一致支承與座標。","checkEn":"Differences use consistent support and coordinates.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-229-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"複合結構收縮造成曲率變化。","textEn":"Composite shrinkage changes curvature."},{"id":"pk-229-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"正反面方向混用會顛倒曲率；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mixed viewing sides invert curvature sign. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測室溫模封翹曲」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure room-temperature warpage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["流動推論有可觀察形貌支持","差值使用一致支承與座標","狀態判定含完整暴露紀錄"],"optionsEn":["Flow interpretations have observable shape evidence","Differences use consistent support and coordinates","Material-state decisions include exposure history"],"answer":1,"explanation":"複合結構收縮造成曲率變化。本步要確認：差值使用一致支承與座標；常見誤判是：正反面方向混用會顛倒曲率。","explanationEn":"Composite shrinkage changes curvature. Verify: Differences use consistent support and coordinates. A common misinterpretation is: Mixed viewing sides invert curvature sign."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-228"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-230","order":22,"sequence":230,"title":"量測熱態翹曲趨勢","titleEn":"Measure temperature-dependent warpage","objective":"沿教學溫度點追蹤曲率變化，並能說明「聚合物性質隨溫度變化」。","objectiveEn":"Track curvature across exercise temperature points and explain: Polymer properties vary with temperature.","instruction":"沿教學溫度點追蹤曲率變化。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：曲線包含升溫與降溫方向。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Track curvature across exercise temperature points. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Curves distinguish heating from cooling. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"曲線包含升溫與降溫方向；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Curves distinguish heating from cooling; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"室溫合格不保證後續熱站平坦。","failureEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not validate hot stations.","check":"曲線包含升溫與降溫方向。","checkEn":"Curves distinguish heating from cooling.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-230-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"聚合物性質隨溫度變化。","textEn":"Polymer properties vary with temperature."},{"id":"pk-230-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"室溫合格不保證後續熱站平坦；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not validate hot stations. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-230-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設室溫 bow=20 µm、熱態 bow=−30 µm，方向已翻轉；報最大絕對值 30 µm 會遺失翻轉訊息。符號與基準面必須一致。","textEn":"Hypothetical bow changes from +20 µm at room temperature to −30 µm hot, reversing direction; reporting only 30 µm maximum magnitude loses the reversal. Keep signs and reference planes consistent."},{"id":"pk-230-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"將升溫與降溫曲線疊合，檢查滯後、支承接觸與固化殘餘。材料跨 Tg 時模型可能需分段，不可只外推室溫彈性。","textEn":"Overlay heating and cooling curves for hysteresis, support contact and cure residuals. Crossing Tg may require piecewise models rather than room-temperature elastic extrapolation."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測熱態翹曲趨勢」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure temperature-dependent warpage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["流道設計包含填料分布影響","分類保留位置與界面資訊","曲線包含升溫與降溫方向"],"optionsEn":["Flow paths account for filler distribution","Classification retains position and interface","Curves distinguish heating from cooling"],"answer":2,"explanation":"聚合物性質隨溫度變化。本步要確認：曲線包含升溫與降溫方向；常見誤判是：室溫合格不保證後續熱站平坦。","explanationEn":"Polymer properties vary with temperature. Verify: Curves distinguish heating from cooling. A common misinterpretation is: Room-temperature flatness does not validate hot stations."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-229"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-231","order":23,"sequence":231,"title":"分配模封研磨預算","titleEn":"Allocate mold-grinding allowance","objective":"用最高晶粒與目標覆蓋厚度決定移除量，並能說明「研磨需保留所選結構的覆蓋需求」。","objectiveEn":"Use tallest die and cover target to budget removal and explain: Grinding preserves the selected cover requirement.","instruction":"用最高晶粒與目標覆蓋厚度決定移除量。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：各類晶粒的最薄覆蓋均被核對。","instructionEn":"Use tallest die and cover target to budget removal. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Minimum cover is checked for every die type.","observation":"各類晶粒的最薄覆蓋均被核對；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Minimum cover is checked for every die type; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"以平均晶粒高規劃可能磨傷最高晶粒。","failureEn":"Mean die height can expose the tallest die.","check":"各類晶粒的最薄覆蓋均被核對。","checkEn":"Minimum cover is checked for every die type.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-231-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"研磨需保留所選結構的覆蓋需求。","textEn":"Grinding preserves the selected cover requirement."},{"id":"pk-231-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"以平均晶粒高規劃可能磨傷最高晶粒；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mean die height can expose the tallest die. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「分配模封研磨預算」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Allocate mold-grinding allowance\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["各類晶粒的最薄覆蓋均被核對","模型把填充與膠化分成不同事件","有線分支量測最小線距變化"],"optionsEn":["Minimum cover is checked for every die type","The model separates filling and gelation","Wirebond routes measure minimum-spacing changes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"研磨需保留所選結構的覆蓋需求。本步要確認：各類晶粒的最薄覆蓋均被核對；常見誤判是：以平均晶粒高規劃可能磨傷最高晶粒。","explanationEn":"Grinding preserves the selected cover requirement. Verify: Minimum cover is checked for every die type. A common misinterpretation is: Mean die height can expose the tallest die."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-230"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-232","order":24,"sequence":232,"title":"檢查研磨露出界面","titleEn":"Inspect ground exposure interfaces","objective":"區分設計露背與意外磨穿，並能說明「露出是否合格取決於架構」。","objectiveEn":"Separate intended backside exposure from breakthrough and explain: Acceptable exposure depends on architecture.","instruction":"區分設計露背與意外磨穿。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：露出位置與核准剖面一致。","instructionEn":"Separate intended backside exposure from breakthrough. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Exposure matches the approved section.","observation":"露出位置與核准剖面一致；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Exposure matches the approved section; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"所有露矽不一定是缺陷或合格。","failureEn":"Exposed silicon is not automatically good or bad.","check":"露出位置與核准剖面一致。","checkEn":"Exposure matches the approved section.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-232-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"露出是否合格取決於架構。","textEn":"Acceptable exposure depends on architecture."},{"id":"pk-232-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"所有露矽不一定是缺陷或合格；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Exposed silicon is not automatically good or bad. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查研磨露出界面」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect ground exposure interfaces\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["位移與旋轉均有空間分布","露出位置與核准剖面一致","異物與密封缺口均已處置"],"optionsEn":["Translation and rotation have spatial maps","Exposure matches the approved section","Debris and sealing gaps have dispositions"],"answer":1,"explanation":"露出是否合格取決於架構。本步要確認：露出位置與核准剖面一致；常見誤判是：所有露矽不一定是缺陷或合格。","explanationEn":"Acceptable exposure depends on architecture. Verify: Exposure matches the approved section. A common misinterpretation is: Exposed silicon is not automatically good or bad."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-231"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-233","order":25,"sequence":233,"title":"檢查模封界面分層","titleEn":"Inspect molded-interface delamination","objective":"比較聲學訊號與界面剖面，並能說明「聲學異常需由界面結構解釋」。","objectiveEn":"Compare acoustic indications with interface sections and explain: Acoustic anomalies need interface interpretation.","instruction":"比較聲學訊號與界面剖面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：疑似分層有位置與確認方法。","instructionEn":"Compare acoustic indications with interface sections. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Suspected delamination has location and confirmation.","observation":"疑似分層有位置與確認方法；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Suspected delamination has location and confirmation; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"把所有反射當分層會過度報警。","failureEn":"Treating all reflections as delamination overcalls defects.","check":"疑似分層有位置與確認方法。","checkEn":"Suspected delamination has location and confirmation.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-233-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"聲學異常需由界面結構解釋。","textEn":"Acoustic anomalies need interface interpretation."},{"id":"pk-233-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"把所有反射當分層會過度報警；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Treating all reflections as delamination overcalls defects. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查模封界面分層」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect molded-interface delamination\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["表面限制區無未解決折痕","結論引用核准曲線或材料量測","疑似分層有位置與確認方法"],"optionsEn":["Critical surfaces lack unresolved creases","Conclusions use qualified profiles or material measurements","Suspected delamination has location and confirmation"],"answer":2,"explanation":"聲學異常需由界面結構解釋。本步要確認：疑似分層有位置與確認方法；常見誤判是：把所有反射當分層會過度報警。","explanationEn":"Acoustic anomalies need interface interpretation. Verify: Suspected delamination has location and confirmation. A common misinterpretation is: Treating all reflections as delamination overcalls defects."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-232"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-234","order":26,"sequence":234,"title":"交付模封放行與位移資料","titleEn":"Release molded body and shift data","objective":"提供形貌、界面與位移給解黏工站，並能說明「本路線回到m08後段再進RDL」。","objectiveEn":"Send shape, interface and shift data to debonding and explain: This route returns to late m08 before RDL.","instruction":"提供形貌、界面與位移給解黏工站。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：pk-234資料足以支持pk-202接續。","instructionEn":"Send shape, interface and shift data to debonding. Check evidence you create or obtain against: pk-234 evidence supports continuation at pk-202.","observation":"pk-234資料足以支持pk-202接續；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"pk-234 evidence supports continuation at pk-202; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"跳過解黏便進RDL會找不到焊墊面。","failureEn":"Skipping debonding leaves the pad surface inaccessible.","check":"pk-234資料足以支持pk-202接續。","checkEn":"pk-234 evidence supports continuation at pk-202.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-234-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"本路線回到m08後段再進RDL。","textEn":"This route returns to late m08 before RDL."},{"id":"pk-234-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"跳過解黏便進RDL會找不到焊墊面；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Skipping debonding leaves the pad surface inaccessible. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「交付模封放行與位移資料」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release molded body and shift data\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["pk-234資料足以支持pk-202接續","慢流區與匯流區被標示","熱歷程與裝夾方式共同記錄"],"optionsEn":["pk-234 evidence supports continuation at pk-202","Slow-flow and merging regions are marked","Thermal history and fixturing are recorded together"],"answer":0,"explanation":"本路線回到m08後段再進RDL。本步要確認：pk-234資料足以支持pk-202接續；常見誤判是：跳過解黏便進RDL會找不到焊墊面。","explanationEn":"This route returns to late m08 before RDL. Verify: pk-234 evidence supports continuation at pk-202. A common misinterpretation is: Skipping debonding leaves the pad surface inaccessible."},"sourceIds":["pk-besi-molding","pk-besi-moldline","pk-henkel-materials","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-233"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m10","order":10,"sequence":10,"title":"RDL介電、微影與銅電鍍","titleEn":"RDL dielectric, lithography and copper plating","description":"以26項獨立教學操作檢查RDL介電、微影與銅電鍍的材料、介面、量測和異常判讀。使用自行建立的示意模型，或您提供／由來源合法取得的量測資料；本課程未附逐工序實測表。門檻須明示為教學假設或來自合格材料文件。","descriptionEn":"Twenty-six distinct educational operations review materials, interfaces, metrology and diagnosis for rdl dielectric, lithography and copper plating. Use schematic models you create, or measurement data you supply or lawfully obtain from sources. No operation-specific measured tables are bundled. State limits as teaching assumptions or derive them from qualified material documents.","route":"採解黏後光成像介電層與銅半加成分支；其他材料與RDL先置有不同流程。","routeEn":"Uses post-debond photoimageable dielectric and semi-additive copper; other materials and RDL-first routes differ.","sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"steps":[{"id":"pk-235","order":1,"sequence":235,"title":"確認RDL工件與路線","titleEn":"Confirm RDL workpiece and route","objective":"採已解黏重組片與光成像介電層路線，並能說明「本例採銅半加成RDL概念流程」。","objectiveEn":"Use a debonded reconstituted wafer and photoimageable dielectric and explain: This example uses a semi-additive copper RDL concept.","instruction":"採已解黏重組片與光成像介電層路線。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：輸入含pk-208真實焊墊座標。","instructionEn":"Use a debonded reconstituted wafer and photoimageable dielectric. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Input includes actual pad coordinates from pk-208.","observation":"輸入含pk-208真實焊墊座標；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Input includes actual pad coordinates from pk-208; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"未解黏工件不能直接接入本路線。","failureEn":"An undebonded body cannot enter this route.","check":"輸入含pk-208真實焊墊座標。","checkEn":"Input includes actual pad coordinates from pk-208.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-235-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"本例採銅半加成RDL概念流程。","textEn":"This example uses a semi-additive copper RDL concept."},{"id":"pk-235-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"未解黏工件不能直接接入本路線；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"An undebonded body cannot enter this route. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「確認RDL工件與路線」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Confirm RDL workpiece and route\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["模型與量測適用性按區域核對","模型與檢查分開追蹤兩種結構","輸入含pk-208真實焊墊座標"],"optionsEn":["Model and measurement applicability are checked by region","Models and inspection track both structures separately","Input includes actual pad coordinates from pk-208"],"answer":2,"explanation":"本例採銅半加成RDL概念流程。本步要確認：輸入含pk-208真實焊墊座標；常見誤判是：未解黏工件不能直接接入本路線。","explanationEn":"This example uses a semi-additive copper RDL concept. Verify: Input includes actual pad coordinates from pk-208. A common misinterpretation is: An undebonded body cannot enter this route."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-208"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-236","order":2,"sequence":236,"title":"量測RDL表面地形","titleEn":"Measure RDL surface topography","objective":"比較矽與模封料交界台階，並能說明「界面台階影響塗膜與種子覆蓋」。","objectiveEn":"Compare steps between silicon and mold and explain: Interface steps affect coating and seed coverage.","instruction":"比較矽與模封料交界台階。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最高低地形均進入膜厚預算。","instructionEn":"Compare steps between silicon and mold. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Height extrema enter the film-thickness budget.","observation":"最高低地形均進入膜厚預算；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Height extrema enter the film-thickness budget; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只量晶粒中心會漏掉邊界台階。","failureEn":"Die-center readings miss boundary steps.","check":"最高低地形均進入膜厚預算。","checkEn":"Height extrema enter the film-thickness budget.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-236-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"界面台階影響塗膜與種子覆蓋。","textEn":"Interface steps affect coating and seed coverage."},{"id":"pk-236-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只量晶粒中心會漏掉邊界台階；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Die-center readings miss boundary steps. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測RDL表面地形」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure RDL surface topography\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最高低地形均進入膜厚預算","最不利位移下仍保有連接區","密度差異包含在量測抽樣中"],"optionsEn":["Height extrema enter the film-thickness budget","Overlap survives worst-case exercise displacement","Sampling includes pattern-density differences"],"answer":0,"explanation":"界面台階影響塗膜與種子覆蓋。本步要確認：最高低地形均進入膜厚預算；常見誤判是：只量晶粒中心會漏掉邊界台階。","explanationEn":"Interface steps affect coating and seed coverage. Verify: Height extrema enter the film-thickness budget. A common misinterpretation is: Die-center readings miss boundary steps."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-235"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-237","order":3,"sequence":237,"title":"建立晶粒位移補償圖","titleEn":"Build die-shift compensation maps","objective":"將實際焊墊位置對回RDL圖形，並能說明「局部位移可能超過全片剛體補償」。","objectiveEn":"Map actual pads to intended RDL features and explain: Local shifts may exceed global rigid correction.","instruction":"將實際焊墊位置對回RDL圖形。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：補償後所有接觸具有有效重疊。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Map actual pads to intended RDL features. Check evidence you create or obtain against: All contacts retain overlap after compensation. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"補償後所有接觸具有有效重疊；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"All contacts retain overlap after compensation; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"全片對準良好仍可有局部漏接。","failureEn":"Good global alignment can coexist with local misses.","check":"補償後所有接觸具有有效重疊。","checkEn":"All contacts retain overlap after compensation.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-237-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"局部位移可能超過全片剛體補償。","textEn":"Local shifts may exceed global rigid correction."},{"id":"pk-237-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"全片對準良好仍可有局部漏接；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Good global alignment can coexist with local misses. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-237-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"教學局部對準有 10 µm 整體平移加 ±2 µm 殘差；扣平移能移除偏置，卻不能把所有點誤差宣稱為零。","textEn":"A teaching alignment field with 10 µm translation and ±2 µm residuals allows removal of bias, not declaration of zero error at every point."},{"id":"pk-237-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"將重組晶粒地圖與 RDL 曝光座標統一，另查標記可視性與焦平面。補償只在模型和量測解析度允許範圍有效。","textEn":"Unify reconstructed-die and RDL exposure coordinates and separately check mark visibility and focal plane. Compensation works only within model and metrology resolution."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「建立晶粒位移補償圖」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Build die-shift compensation maps\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["窄線間區有完整清潔證據","補償後所有接觸具有有效重疊","通孔底與頂都符合示意幾何"],"optionsEn":["Narrow gaps have complete cleaning evidence","All contacts retain overlap after compensation","Via bottom and top meet exercise geometry"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部位移可能超過全片剛體補償。本步要確認：補償後所有接觸具有有效重疊；常見誤判是：全片對準良好仍可有局部漏接。","explanationEn":"Local shifts may exceed global rigid correction. Verify: All contacts retain overlap after compensation. A common misinterpretation is: Good global alignment can coexist with local misses."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-236"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-238","order":4,"sequence":238,"title":"比較介電材料適用性","titleEn":"Compare dielectric suitability","objective":"核對熱歷程、附著與圖形能力，並能說明「介電層同時是絕緣與機械界面」。","objectiveEn":"Check thermal history, adhesion and patterning capability and explain: Dielectric provides insulation and mechanical interfaces.","instruction":"核對熱歷程、附著與圖形能力。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：材料選擇同時滿足電性和機械需求。","instructionEn":"Check thermal history, adhesion and patterning capability. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Selection satisfies electrical and mechanical needs.","observation":"材料選擇同時滿足電性和機械需求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Selection satisfies electrical and mechanical needs; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看介電常數會漏掉加工失配。","failureEn":"Permittivity alone misses process incompatibility.","check":"材料選擇同時滿足電性和機械需求。","checkEn":"Selection satisfies electrical and mechanical needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-238-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"介電層同時是絕緣與機械界面。","textEn":"Dielectric provides insulation and mechanical interfaces."},{"id":"pk-238-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看介電常數會漏掉加工失配；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Permittivity alone misses process incompatibility. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「比較介電材料適用性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Compare dielectric suitability\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["底部可接觸性有確認證據","清除橋接後線寬仍符合示意規則","材料選擇同時滿足電性和機械需求"],"optionsEn":["Bottom accessibility has confirming evidence","Lines meet rules after bridge removal","Selection satisfies electrical and mechanical needs"],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電層同時是絕緣與機械界面。本步要確認：材料選擇同時滿足電性和機械需求；常見誤判是：只看介電常數會漏掉加工失配。","explanationEn":"Dielectric provides insulation and mechanical interfaces. Verify: Selection satisfies electrical and mechanical needs. A common misinterpretation is: Permittivity alone misses process incompatibility."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-237"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-239","order":5,"sequence":239,"title":"檢查介電前表面狀態","titleEn":"Inspect the pre-dielectric surface","objective":"分辨殘膠、顆粒及表面活化需求，並能說明「附著需要合適且穩定的表面」。","objectiveEn":"Separate adhesive residue, particles and activation needs and explain: Adhesion requires suitable stable surfaces.","instruction":"分辨殘膠、顆粒及表面活化需求。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：前處理不破壞露出焊墊。","instructionEn":"Separate adhesive residue, particles and activation needs. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Pretreatment preserves exposed pads.","observation":"前處理不破壞露出焊墊；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Pretreatment preserves exposed pads; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過度活化可能損傷聚合物或金屬。","failureEn":"Excess activation can damage polymers or metals.","check":"前處理不破壞露出焊墊。","checkEn":"Pretreatment preserves exposed pads.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-239-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"附著需要合適且穩定的表面。","textEn":"Adhesion requires suitable stable surfaces."},{"id":"pk-239-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過度活化可能損傷聚合物或金屬；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Excess activation can damage polymers or metals. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查介電前表面狀態」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect the pre-dielectric surface\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["前處理不破壞露出焊墊","底部清潔且金屬未被過度消耗","最弱截面而非僅平均值被記錄"],"optionsEn":["Pretreatment preserves exposed pads","Bottoms are clean without excessive metal loss","Weakest sections are recorded alongside averages"],"answer":0,"explanation":"附著需要合適且穩定的表面。本步要確認：前處理不破壞露出焊墊；常見誤判是：過度活化可能損傷聚合物或金屬。","explanationEn":"Adhesion requires suitable stable surfaces. Verify: Pretreatment preserves exposed pads. A common misinterpretation is: Excess activation can damage polymers or metals."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-238"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-240","order":6,"sequence":240,"title":"規劃介電塗佈流動","titleEn":"Plan dielectric coating flow","objective":"比較平面與台階附近的覆蓋，並能說明「旋塗或其他塗法有不同地形適應性」。","objectiveEn":"Compare coverage on planes and near steps and explain: Coating methods respond differently to topography.","instruction":"比較平面與台階附近的覆蓋。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：台階最薄處符合示意覆蓋要求。","instructionEn":"Compare coverage on planes and near steps. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Minimum step coverage meets exercise requirements.","observation":"台階最薄處符合示意覆蓋要求；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Minimum step coverage meets exercise requirements; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"全片平均厚度不能保證邊角絕緣。","failureEn":"Mean thickness cannot guarantee edge insulation.","check":"台階最薄處符合示意覆蓋要求。","checkEn":"Minimum step coverage meets exercise requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-240-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"旋塗或其他塗法有不同地形適應性。","textEn":"Coating methods respond differently to topography."},{"id":"pk-240-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"全片平均厚度不能保證邊角絕緣；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Mean thickness cannot guarantee edge insulation. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「規劃介電塗佈流動」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Plan dielectric coating flow\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["連通與隔離證據皆涵蓋關鍵網路","台階最薄處符合示意覆蓋要求","最終尺寸用固化後資料判定"],"optionsEn":["Continuity and isolation cover critical networks","Minimum step coverage meets exercise requirements","Final dimensions use post-cure data"],"answer":1,"explanation":"旋塗或其他塗法有不同地形適應性。本步要確認：台階最薄處符合示意覆蓋要求；常見誤判是：全片平均厚度不能保證邊角絕緣。","explanationEn":"Coating methods respond differently to topography. Verify: Minimum step coverage meets exercise requirements. A common misinterpretation is: Mean thickness cannot guarantee edge insulation."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-239"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-241","order":7,"sequence":241,"title":"檢查邊膠與背面污染","titleEn":"Inspect edge beads and backside contamination","objective":"標記邊緣堆積及背面附著物，並能說明「邊背污染會影響裝夾與後續曝光」。","objectiveEn":"Mark edge accumulation and backside deposits and explain: Edge/back contamination affects chucking and exposure.","instruction":"標記邊緣堆積及背面附著物。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：設備接觸區沒有未處置膜料。","instructionEn":"Mark edge accumulation and backside deposits. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Equipment contacts lack unresolved deposits.","observation":"設備接觸區沒有未處置膜料；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Equipment contacts lack unresolved deposits; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略背面污染可能引起對焦誤差。","failureEn":"Backside contamination can create focus errors.","check":"設備接觸區沒有未處置膜料。","checkEn":"Equipment contacts lack unresolved deposits.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-241-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"邊背污染會影響裝夾與後續曝光。","textEn":"Edge/back contamination affects chucking and exposure."},{"id":"pk-241-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略背面污染可能引起對焦誤差；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Backside contamination can create focus errors. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查邊膠與背面污染」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect edge beads and backside contamination\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["孔底與平面之間無未解釋斷點","跨界線段有專屬形貌或截面證據","設備接觸區沒有未處置膜料"],"optionsEn":["No unexplained breaks separate via bottom and plane","Crossing lines have dedicated imaging or sections","Equipment contacts lack unresolved deposits"],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊背污染會影響裝夾與後續曝光。本步要確認：設備接觸區沒有未處置膜料；常見誤判是：忽略背面污染可能引起對焦誤差。","explanationEn":"Edge/back contamination affects chucking and exposure. Verify: Equipment contacts lack unresolved deposits. A common misinterpretation is: Backside contamination can create focus errors."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-240"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-242","order":8,"sequence":242,"title":"核對介電預烤狀態","titleEn":"Review dielectric prebake condition","objective":"比較件溫與膜層收縮線索，並能說明「預烤改變溶劑含量和圖形反應」。","objectiveEn":"Compare part temperature and film-shrinkage evidence and explain: Prebake changes solvent content and pattern response.","instruction":"比較件溫與膜層收縮線索。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：預烤證據包含實際基板條件。","instructionEn":"Compare part temperature and film-shrinkage evidence. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Prebake evidence includes actual substrate conditions.","observation":"預烤證據包含實際基板條件；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Prebake evidence includes actual substrate conditions; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"設備設定相同不等於膜層状態相同。","failureEn":"Equal settings do not guarantee equal film state.","check":"預烤證據包含實際基板條件。","checkEn":"Prebake evidence includes actual substrate conditions.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-242-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"預烤改變溶劑含量和圖形反應。","textEn":"Prebake changes solvent content and pattern response."},{"id":"pk-242-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"設備設定相同不等於膜層状態相同；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Equal settings do not guarantee equal film state. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對介電預烤狀態」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review dielectric prebake condition\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["預烤證據包含實際基板條件","線高預算保留模穴高度裕量","未解決開短路不進入後續覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["Prebake evidence includes actual substrate conditions","Line-height budget preserves mold headroom","Unresolved faults do not proceed to overcoating"],"answer":0,"explanation":"預烤改變溶劑含量和圖形反應。本步要確認：預烤證據包含實際基板條件；常見誤判是：設備設定相同不等於膜層状態相同。","explanationEn":"Prebake changes solvent content and pattern response. Verify: Prebake evidence includes actual substrate conditions. A common misinterpretation is: Equal settings do not guarantee equal film state."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-241"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-243","order":9,"sequence":243,"title":"量測介電膜厚均勻性","titleEn":"Measure dielectric thickness uniformity","objective":"對晶粒上與模封區分開取樣，並能說明「不同下層材料可能造成量測差異」。","objectiveEn":"Sample die and mold regions separately and explain: Different underlying materials affect measurements.","instruction":"對晶粒上與模封區分開取樣。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：模型與量測適用性按區域核對。","instructionEn":"Sample die and mold regions separately. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Model and measurement applicability are checked by region.","observation":"模型與量測適用性按區域核對；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Model and measurement applicability are checked by region; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"不分基材的光學擬合可能偏誤。","failureEn":"Substrate-blind optical fits can be biased.","check":"模型與量測適用性按區域核對。","checkEn":"Model and measurement applicability are checked by region.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-243-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"不同下層材料可能造成量測差異。","textEn":"Different underlying materials affect measurements."},{"id":"pk-243-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"不分基材的光學擬合可能偏誤；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Substrate-blind optical fits can be biased. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測介電膜厚均勻性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure dielectric thickness uniformity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["輸入含pk-208真實焊墊座標","模型與量測適用性按區域核對","接觸包絡不因套刻而斷開"],"optionsEn":["Input includes actual pad coordinates from pk-208","Model and measurement applicability are checked by region","Overlay preserves contact envelopes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同下層材料可能造成量測差異。本步要確認：模型與量測適用性按區域核對；常見誤判是：不分基材的光學擬合可能偏誤。","explanationEn":"Different underlying materials affect measurements. Verify: Model and measurement applicability are checked by region. A common misinterpretation is: Substrate-blind optical fits can be biased."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-242"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-244","order":10,"sequence":244,"title":"對準介電通孔層","titleEn":"Align the dielectric-via layer","objective":"把通孔開口疊加真實焊墊，並能說明「接觸需要足夠的幾何重疊」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay vias on actual pads and explain: Contacts need sufficient geometric overlap.","instruction":"把通孔開口疊加真實焊墊。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最不利位移下仍保有連接區。","instructionEn":"Overlay vias on actual pads. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Overlap survives worst-case exercise displacement.","observation":"最不利位移下仍保有連接區；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Overlap survives worst-case exercise displacement; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只對理想地圖會漏接偏移晶粒。","failureEn":"Ideal-map alignment misses shifted dies.","check":"最不利位移下仍保有連接區。","checkEn":"Overlap survives worst-case exercise displacement.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-244-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"接觸需要足夠的幾何重疊。","textEn":"Contacts need sufficient geometric overlap."},{"id":"pk-244-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只對理想地圖會漏接偏移晶粒；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ideal-map alignment misses shifted dies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「對準介電通孔層」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Align the dielectric-via layer\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最窄截面與關鍵轉角均被檢查","最高低地形均進入膜厚預算","最不利位移下仍保有連接區"],"optionsEn":["Narrow sections and critical corners are checked","Height extrema enter the film-thickness budget","Overlap survives worst-case exercise displacement"],"answer":2,"explanation":"接觸需要足夠的幾何重疊。本步要確認：最不利位移下仍保有連接區；常見誤判是：只對理想地圖會漏接偏移晶粒。","explanationEn":"Contacts need sufficient geometric overlap. Verify: Overlap survives worst-case exercise displacement. A common misinterpretation is: Ideal-map alignment misses shifted dies."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-243"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-245","order":11,"sequence":245,"title":"評估通孔曝光窗口","titleEn":"Assess via-exposure window","objective":"比較開口深度方向的形狀，並能說明「曝光與材料反應決定側壁輪廓」。","objectiveEn":"Compare via shape through film depth and explain: Exposure and material response determine wall profile.","instruction":"比較開口深度方向的形狀。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：通孔底與頂都符合示意幾何。","instructionEn":"Compare via shape through film depth. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Via bottom and top meet exercise geometry.","observation":"通孔底與頂都符合示意幾何；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Via bottom and top meet exercise geometry; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"頂部尺寸合格可能仍有底部封閉。","failureEn":"Correct top size can hide a closed bottom.","check":"通孔底與頂都符合示意幾何。","checkEn":"Via bottom and top meet exercise geometry.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-245-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"曝光與材料反應決定側壁輪廓。","textEn":"Exposure and material response determine wall profile."},{"id":"pk-245-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"頂部尺寸合格可能仍有底部封閉；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Correct top size can hide a closed bottom. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「評估通孔曝光窗口」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Assess via-exposure window\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["通孔底與頂都符合示意幾何","模型與檢查分開追蹤兩種結構","補償後所有接觸具有有效重疊"],"optionsEn":["Via bottom and top meet exercise geometry","Models and inspection track both structures separately","All contacts retain overlap after compensation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"曝光與材料反應決定側壁輪廓。本步要確認：通孔底與頂都符合示意幾何；常見誤判是：頂部尺寸合格可能仍有底部封閉。","explanationEn":"Exposure and material response determine wall profile. Verify: Via bottom and top meet exercise geometry. A common misinterpretation is: Correct top size can hide a closed bottom."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-244"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-246","order":12,"sequence":246,"title":"檢查顯影通孔底部","titleEn":"Inspect developed via bottoms","objective":"辨識露墊面與殘留介電薄膜，並能說明「薄殘膜可阻斷電連接」。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish exposed pad from residual dielectric and explain: Thin residues can block electrical contact.","instruction":"辨識露墊面與殘留介電薄膜。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：底部可接觸性有確認證據。","instructionEn":"Distinguish exposed pad from residual dielectric. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Bottom accessibility has confirming evidence.","observation":"底部可接觸性有確認證據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Bottom accessibility has confirming evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"透明殘膜可能被誤認為清通。","failureEn":"Transparent residue can resemble an open via.","check":"底部可接觸性有確認證據。","checkEn":"Bottom accessibility has confirming evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-246-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"薄殘膜可阻斷電連接。","textEn":"Thin residues can block electrical contact."},{"id":"pk-246-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"透明殘膜可能被誤認為清通；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Transparent residue can resemble an open via. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查顯影通孔底部」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect developed via bottoms\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["材料選擇同時滿足電性和機械需求","底部可接觸性有確認證據","密度差異包含在量測抽樣中"],"optionsEn":["Selection satisfies electrical and mechanical needs","Bottom accessibility has confirming evidence","Sampling includes pattern-density differences"],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄殘膜可阻斷電連接。本步要確認：底部可接觸性有確認證據；常見誤判是：透明殘膜可能被誤認為清通。","explanationEn":"Thin residues can block electrical contact. Verify: Bottom accessibility has confirming evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Transparent residue can resemble an open via."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-245"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-247","order":13,"sequence":247,"title":"檢查通孔去殘膠","titleEn":"Inspect via descum","objective":"比較去除殘膜與焊墊保留，並能說明「清通與底層損傷必須同時控制」。","objectiveEn":"Compare residue removal and pad preservation and explain: Opening and underlying damage need joint control.","instruction":"比較去除殘膜與焊墊保留。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：底部清潔且金屬未被過度消耗。","instructionEn":"Compare residue removal and pad preservation. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Bottoms are clean without excessive metal loss.","observation":"底部清潔且金屬未被過度消耗；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Bottoms are clean without excessive metal loss; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只求清通可能損壞薄焊墊。","failureEn":"Opening alone can damage thin pads.","check":"底部清潔且金屬未被過度消耗。","checkEn":"Bottoms are clean without excessive metal loss.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-247-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"清通與底層損傷必須同時控制。","textEn":"Opening and underlying damage need joint control."},{"id":"pk-247-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只求清通可能損壞薄焊墊；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Opening alone can damage thin pads. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查通孔去殘膠」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect via descum\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["窄線間區有完整清潔證據","前處理不破壞露出焊墊","底部清潔且金屬未被過度消耗"],"optionsEn":["Narrow gaps have complete cleaning evidence","Pretreatment preserves exposed pads","Bottoms are clean without excessive metal loss"],"answer":2,"explanation":"清通與底層損傷必須同時控制。本步要確認：底部清潔且金屬未被過度消耗；常見誤判是：只求清通可能損壞薄焊墊。","explanationEn":"Opening and underlying damage need joint control. Verify: Bottoms are clean without excessive metal loss. A common misinterpretation is: Opening alone can damage thin pads."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-246"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-248","order":14,"sequence":248,"title":"驗證介電固化收縮","titleEn":"Verify dielectric cure shrinkage","objective":"量測固化前後膜厚與孔徑，並能說明「固化會改變幾何與殘留應力」。","objectiveEn":"Measure film thickness and via size across cure and explain: Cure changes geometry and residual stress.","instruction":"量測固化前後膜厚與孔徑。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最終尺寸用固化後資料判定。","instructionEn":"Measure film thickness and via size across cure. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Final dimensions use post-cure data.","observation":"最終尺寸用固化後資料判定；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Final dimensions use post-cure data; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"顯影後合格不保證固化後合格。","failureEn":"Post-develop acceptance does not guarantee post-cure acceptance.","check":"最終尺寸用固化後資料判定。","checkEn":"Final dimensions use post-cure data.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-248-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"固化會改變幾何與殘留應力。","textEn":"Cure changes geometry and residual stress."},{"id":"pk-248-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"顯影後合格不保證固化後合格；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Post-develop acceptance does not guarantee post-cure acceptance. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證介電固化收縮」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify dielectric cure shrinkage\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最終尺寸用固化後資料判定","清除橋接後線寬仍符合示意規則","台階最薄處符合示意覆蓋要求"],"optionsEn":["Final dimensions use post-cure data","Lines meet rules after bridge removal","Minimum step coverage meets exercise requirements"],"answer":0,"explanation":"固化會改變幾何與殘留應力。本步要確認：最終尺寸用固化後資料判定；常見誤判是：顯影後合格不保證固化後合格。","explanationEn":"Cure changes geometry and residual stress. Verify: Final dimensions use post-cure data. A common misinterpretation is: Post-develop acceptance does not guarantee post-cure acceptance."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-247"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-249","order":15,"sequence":249,"title":"檢查金屬阻障與種子層","titleEn":"Inspect barrier and seed layers","objective":"沿通孔側壁追蹤連續導電路徑，並能說明「後續電鍍依賴連續種子供電」。","objectiveEn":"Trace conductive coverage along via walls and explain: Later plating relies on continuous seed conduction.","instruction":"沿通孔側壁追蹤連續導電路徑。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：孔底與平面之間無未解釋斷點。","instructionEn":"Trace conductive coverage along via walls. Check evidence you create or obtain against: No unexplained breaks separate via bottom and plane.","observation":"孔底與平面之間無未解釋斷點；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"No unexplained breaks separate via bottom and plane; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平面片阻合格不保證孔內連通。","failureEn":"Good planar resistance does not prove via continuity.","check":"孔底與平面之間無未解釋斷點。","checkEn":"No unexplained breaks separate via bottom and plane.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-249-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"後續電鍍依賴連續種子供電。","textEn":"Later plating relies on continuous seed conduction."},{"id":"pk-249-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平面片阻合格不保證孔內連通；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Good planar resistance does not prove via continuity. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查金屬阻障與種子層」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect barrier and seed layers\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["設備接觸區沒有未處置膜料","孔底與平面之間無未解釋斷點","最弱截面而非僅平均值被記錄"],"optionsEn":["Equipment contacts lack unresolved deposits","No unexplained breaks separate via bottom and plane","Weakest sections are recorded alongside averages"],"answer":1,"explanation":"後續電鍍依賴連續種子供電。本步要確認：孔底與平面之間無未解釋斷點；常見誤判是：平面片阻合格不保證孔內連通。","explanationEn":"Later plating relies on continuous seed conduction. Verify: No unexplained breaks separate via bottom and plane. A common misinterpretation is: Good planar resistance does not prove via continuity."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-248"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-250","order":16,"sequence":250,"title":"核對RDL鍍銅光阻厚度","titleEn":"Review RDL plating-resist thickness","objective":"比較預期線高與光阻模穴高度，並能說明「鍍層越過模頂可形成側向長大」。","objectiveEn":"Compare intended line height and resist-mold depth and explain: Plating above the mold promotes lateral growth.","instruction":"比較預期線高與光阻模穴高度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：線高預算保留模穴高度裕量。","instructionEn":"Compare intended line height and resist-mold depth. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Line-height budget preserves mold headroom.","observation":"線高預算保留模穴高度裕量；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Line-height budget preserves mold headroom; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只驗線寬會漏掉過鍍橋接。","failureEn":"Width-only checks miss overplating bridges.","check":"線高預算保留模穴高度裕量。","checkEn":"Line-height budget preserves mold headroom.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-250-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"鍍層越過模頂可形成側向長大。","textEn":"Plating above the mold promotes lateral growth."},{"id":"pk-250-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只驗線寬會漏掉過鍍橋接；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Width-only checks miss overplating bridges. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「核對RDL鍍銅光阻厚度」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Review RDL plating-resist thickness\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["連通與隔離證據皆涵蓋關鍵網路","預烤證據包含實際基板條件","線高預算保留模穴高度裕量"],"optionsEn":["Continuity and isolation cover critical networks","Prebake evidence includes actual substrate conditions","Line-height budget preserves mold headroom"],"answer":2,"explanation":"鍍層越過模頂可形成側向長大。本步要確認：線高預算保留模穴高度裕量；常見誤判是：只驗線寬會漏掉過鍍橋接。","explanationEn":"Plating above the mold promotes lateral growth. Verify: Line-height budget preserves mold headroom. A common misinterpretation is: Width-only checks miss overplating bridges."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-249"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-251","order":17,"sequence":251,"title":"對準銅線光罩","titleEn":"Align the copper-line mask","objective":"將線路接觸區疊加通孔位置，並能說明「銅線與通孔需保持完整連接」。","objectiveEn":"Overlay line contacts with vias and explain: Copper lines must connect fully to vias.","instruction":"將線路接觸區疊加通孔位置。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：接觸包絡不因套刻而斷開。","instructionEn":"Overlay line contacts with vias. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Overlay preserves contact envelopes.","observation":"接觸包絡不因套刻而斷開；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Overlay preserves contact envelopes; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"線路整體偏移可形成系統性開路。","failureEn":"Global line shift can create systematic opens.","check":"接觸包絡不因套刻而斷開。","checkEn":"Overlay preserves contact envelopes.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-251-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"銅線與通孔需保持完整連接。","textEn":"Copper lines must connect fully to vias."},{"id":"pk-251-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"線路整體偏移可形成系統性開路；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Global line shift can create systematic opens. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「對準銅線光罩」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Align the copper-line mask\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["接觸包絡不因套刻而斷開","跨界線段有專屬形貌或截面證據","模型與量測適用性按區域核對"],"optionsEn":["Overlay preserves contact envelopes","Crossing lines have dedicated imaging or sections","Model and measurement applicability are checked by region"],"answer":0,"explanation":"銅線與通孔需保持完整連接。本步要確認：接觸包絡不因套刻而斷開；常見誤判是：線路整體偏移可形成系統性開路。","explanationEn":"Copper lines must connect fully to vias. Verify: Overlay preserves contact envelopes. A common misinterpretation is: Global line shift can create systematic opens."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-250"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-252","order":18,"sequence":252,"title":"檢查線路顯影形貌","titleEn":"Inspect developed routing patterns","objective":"辨識細線開口、頸縮與殘阻，並能說明「電鍍將繼承模穴的局部缺陷」。","objectiveEn":"Identify narrow openings, necking and resist residue and explain: Plating inherits local mold defects.","instruction":"辨識細線開口、頸縮與殘阻。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最窄截面與關鍵轉角均被檢查。","instructionEn":"Identify narrow openings, necking and resist residue. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Narrow sections and critical corners are checked.","observation":"最窄截面與關鍵轉角均被檢查；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Narrow sections and critical corners are checked; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平均線寬會掩蓋單點斷路風險。","failureEn":"Average width hides local break risk.","check":"最窄截面與關鍵轉角均被檢查。","checkEn":"Narrow sections and critical corners are checked.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-252-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"電鍍將繼承模穴的局部缺陷。","textEn":"Plating inherits local mold defects."},{"id":"pk-252-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平均線寬會掩蓋單點斷路風險；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Average width hides local break risk. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查線路顯影形貌」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect developed routing patterns\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最不利位移下仍保有連接區","最窄截面與關鍵轉角均被檢查","未解決開短路不進入後續覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["Overlap survives worst-case exercise displacement","Narrow sections and critical corners are checked","Unresolved faults do not proceed to overcoating"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電鍍將繼承模穴的局部缺陷。本步要確認：最窄截面與關鍵轉角均被檢查；常見誤判是：平均線寬會掩蓋單點斷路風險。","explanationEn":"Plating inherits local mold defects. Verify: Narrow sections and critical corners are checked. A common misinterpretation is: Average width hides local break risk."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-251"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-253","order":19,"sequence":253,"title":"模擬銅線與通孔共鍍","titleEn":"Simulate concurrent line and via plating","objective":"比較平面增厚與孔內填充，並能說明「線路增厚不表示孔內無空洞」。","objectiveEn":"Compare planar growth and via filling and explain: Line growth does not prove void-free vias.","instruction":"比較平面增厚與孔內填充。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：模型與檢查分開追蹤兩種結構。","instructionEn":"Compare planar growth and via filling. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Models and inspection track both structures separately.","observation":"模型與檢查分開追蹤兩種結構；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Models and inspection track both structures separately; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"以表面厚度推斷填孔完整會誤判。","failureEn":"Surface thickness cannot prove complete fill.","check":"模型與檢查分開追蹤兩種結構。","checkEn":"Models and inspection track both structures separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-253-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"線路增厚不表示孔內無空洞。","textEn":"Line growth does not prove void-free vias."},{"id":"pk-253-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"以表面厚度推斷填孔完整會誤判；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Surface thickness cannot prove complete fill. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「模擬銅線與通孔共鍍」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Simulate concurrent line and via plating\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["輸入含pk-208真實焊墊座標","通孔底與頂都符合示意幾何","模型與檢查分開追蹤兩種結構"],"optionsEn":["Input includes actual pad coordinates from pk-208","Via bottom and top meet exercise geometry","Models and inspection track both structures separately"],"answer":2,"explanation":"線路增厚不表示孔內無空洞。本步要確認：模型與檢查分開追蹤兩種結構；常見誤判是：以表面厚度推斷填孔完整會誤判。","explanationEn":"Line growth does not prove void-free vias. Verify: Models and inspection track both structures separately. A common misinterpretation is: Surface thickness cannot prove complete fill."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-252"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-254","order":20,"sequence":254,"title":"檢查局部電鍍均勻性","titleEn":"Inspect local plating uniformity","objective":"比較密集與稀疏線區的高度，並能說明「圖形密度可改變局部沉積」。","objectiveEn":"Compare dense and sparse routing heights and explain: Pattern density can change local deposition.","instruction":"比較密集與稀疏線區的高度。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：密度差異包含在量測抽樣中。","instructionEn":"Compare dense and sparse routing heights. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Sampling includes pattern-density differences.","observation":"密度差異包含在量測抽樣中；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Sampling includes pattern-density differences; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只在大銅墊量測會漏掉細線異常。","failureEn":"Large-pad measurements can miss fine-line anomalies.","check":"密度差異包含在量測抽樣中。","checkEn":"Sampling includes pattern-density differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-254-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"圖形密度可改變局部沉積。","textEn":"Pattern density can change local deposition."},{"id":"pk-254-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只在大銅墊量測會漏掉細線異常；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Large-pad measurements can miss fine-line anomalies. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查局部電鍍均勻性」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect local plating uniformity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["密度差異包含在量測抽樣中","最高低地形均進入膜厚預算","底部可接觸性有確認證據"],"optionsEn":["Sampling includes pattern-density differences","Height extrema enter the film-thickness budget","Bottom accessibility has confirming evidence"],"answer":0,"explanation":"圖形密度可改變局部沉積。本步要確認：密度差異包含在量測抽樣中；常見誤判是：只在大銅墊量測會漏掉細線異常。","explanationEn":"Pattern density can change local deposition. Verify: Sampling includes pattern-density differences. A common misinterpretation is: Large-pad measurements can miss fine-line anomalies."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-253"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-255","order":21,"sequence":255,"title":"驗證鍍後光阻剝除","titleEn":"Verify post-plate resist stripping","objective":"檢查線間與轉角殘阻，並能說明「殘阻會遮蔽後續種子蝕除」。","objectiveEn":"Inspect residue between lines and at corners and explain: Residue shields subsequent seed etching.","instruction":"檢查線間與轉角殘阻。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：窄線間區有完整清潔證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect residue between lines and at corners. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Narrow gaps have complete cleaning evidence.","observation":"窄線間區有完整清潔證據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Narrow gaps have complete cleaning evidence; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"平面目視合格不代表線間乾淨。","failureEn":"Planar visual acceptance does not prove clean gaps.","check":"窄線間區有完整清潔證據。","checkEn":"Narrow gaps have complete cleaning evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-255-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"殘阻會遮蔽後續種子蝕除。","textEn":"Residue shields subsequent seed etching."},{"id":"pk-255-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"平面目視合格不代表線間乾淨；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Planar visual acceptance does not prove clean gaps. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證鍍後光阻剝除」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify post-plate resist stripping\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["底部清潔且金屬未被過度消耗","窄線間區有完整清潔證據","補償後所有接觸具有有效重疊"],"optionsEn":["Bottoms are clean without excessive metal loss","Narrow gaps have complete cleaning evidence","All contacts retain overlap after compensation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘阻會遮蔽後續種子蝕除。本步要確認：窄線間區有完整清潔證據；常見誤判是：平面目視合格不代表線間乾淨。","explanationEn":"Residue shields subsequent seed etching. Verify: Narrow gaps have complete cleaning evidence. A common misinterpretation is: Planar visual acceptance does not prove clean gaps."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-254"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-256","order":22,"sequence":256,"title":"控制種子層蝕除邊界","titleEn":"Control seed-etch boundaries","objective":"比較線間導電膜與線側蝕量，並能說明「隔離完整性與線截面保留需平衡」。","objectiveEn":"Compare interline film and line undercut and explain: Isolation trades against retained line cross-section.","instruction":"比較線間導電膜與線側蝕量。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：清除橋接後線寬仍符合示意規則。","instructionEn":"Compare interline film and line undercut. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Lines meet rules after bridge removal.","observation":"清除橋接後線寬仍符合示意規則；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Lines meet rules after bridge removal; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"過蝕會使細線頸縮或斷裂。","failureEn":"Overetch necks or breaks fine lines.","check":"清除橋接後線寬仍符合示意規則。","checkEn":"Lines meet rules after bridge removal.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-256-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"隔離完整性與線截面保留需平衡。","textEn":"Isolation trades against retained line cross-section."},{"id":"pk-256-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"過蝕會使細線頸縮或斷裂；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Overetch necks or breaks fine lines. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「控制種子層蝕除邊界」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Control seed-etch boundaries\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["材料選擇同時滿足電性和機械需求","最終尺寸用固化後資料判定","清除橋接後線寬仍符合示意規則"],"optionsEn":["Selection satisfies electrical and mechanical needs","Final dimensions use post-cure data","Lines meet rules after bridge removal"],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔離完整性與線截面保留需平衡。本步要確認：清除橋接後線寬仍符合示意規則；常見誤判是：過蝕會使細線頸縮或斷裂。","explanationEn":"Isolation trades against retained line cross-section. Verify: Lines meet rules after bridge removal. A common misinterpretation is: Overetch necks or breaks fine lines."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-255"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-257","order":23,"sequence":257,"title":"量測RDL線寬線高","titleEn":"Measure RDL width and height","objective":"在直線、轉角及接點量測截面，並能說明「電阻與可靠度取決於實際截面」。","objectiveEn":"Measure sections at straights, corners and contacts and explain: Resistance and reliability depend on actual cross-section.","instruction":"在直線、轉角及接點量測截面。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：最弱截面而非僅平均值被記錄。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Measure sections at straights, corners and contacts. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Weakest sections are recorded alongside averages. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"最弱截面而非僅平均值被記錄；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Weakest sections are recorded alongside averages; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"忽略轉角凹陷會高估導電截面。","failureEn":"Ignoring corner recesses overstates conductive area.","check":"最弱截面而非僅平均值被記錄。","checkEn":"Weakest sections are recorded alongside averages.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-257-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"電阻與可靠度取決於實際截面。","textEn":"Resistance and reliability depend on actual cross-section."},{"id":"pk-257-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"忽略轉角凹陷會高估導電截面；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Ignoring corner recesses overstates conductive area. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."},{"id":"pk-257-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設銅線長 1 mm、寬 5 µm、高 3 µm、ρ=2×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，理想 R=ρL/(wt)=1.33 Ω；若高降至 2 µm，升至 2 Ω。","textEn":"A hypothetical copper line with L=1 mm, w=5 µm, t=3 µm and ρ=2×10⁻⁸ Ω·m has ideal R=1.33 Ω; reducing thickness to 2 µm increases it to 2 Ω."},{"id":"pk-257-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"直流矩形截面近似未含側壁角、表面粗糙、接點、電流擁擠或高頻集膚效應。應將截面量測與電性擬合互相核對。","textEn":"The DC rectangle approximation excludes taper, roughness, contacts, crowding and high-frequency skin effects; cross-check measured sections against electrical fits."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「量測RDL線寬線高」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Measure RDL width and height\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["最弱截面而非僅平均值被記錄","前處理不破壞露出焊墊","孔底與平面之間無未解釋斷點"],"optionsEn":["Weakest sections are recorded alongside averages","Pretreatment preserves exposed pads","No unexplained breaks separate via bottom and plane"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電阻與可靠度取決於實際截面。本步要確認：最弱截面而非僅平均值被記錄；常見誤判是：忽略轉角凹陷會高估導電截面。","explanationEn":"Resistance and reliability depend on actual cross-section. Verify: Weakest sections are recorded alongside averages. A common misinterpretation is: Ignoring corner recesses overstates conductive area."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-256"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-258","order":24,"sequence":258,"title":"驗證通孔與線路連通","titleEn":"Verify via and routing continuity","objective":"將菊鏈及隔離結構結果對回版圖，並能說明「通孔開路與線間短路需不同測試」。","objectiveEn":"Map chain and isolation results to layout and explain: Via opens and interline shorts need different tests.","instruction":"將菊鏈及隔離結構結果對回版圖。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：連通與隔離證據皆涵蓋關鍵網路。","instructionEn":"Map chain and isolation results to layout. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Continuity and isolation cover critical networks.","observation":"連通與隔離證據皆涵蓋關鍵網路；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Continuity and isolation cover critical networks; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"菊鏈合格不能排除不同鏈間短路。","failureEn":"A passing chain cannot exclude interchain shorts.","check":"連通與隔離證據皆涵蓋關鍵網路。","checkEn":"Continuity and isolation cover critical networks.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-258-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"通孔開路與線間短路需不同測試。","textEn":"Via opens and interline shorts need different tests."},{"id":"pk-258-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"菊鏈合格不能排除不同鏈間短路；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"A passing chain cannot exclude interchain shorts. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「驗證通孔與線路連通」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Verify via and routing continuity\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["線高預算保留模穴高度裕量","連通與隔離證據皆涵蓋關鍵網路","台階最薄處符合示意覆蓋要求"],"optionsEn":["Line-height budget preserves mold headroom","Continuity and isolation cover critical networks","Minimum step coverage meets exercise requirements"],"answer":1,"explanation":"通孔開路與線間短路需不同測試。本步要確認：連通與隔離證據皆涵蓋關鍵網路；常見誤判是：菊鏈合格不能排除不同鏈間短路。","explanationEn":"Via opens and interline shorts need different tests. Verify: Continuity and isolation cover critical networks. A common misinterpretation is: A passing chain cannot exclude interchain shorts."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-257"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-259","order":25,"sequence":259,"title":"檢查跨材料界面裂紋","titleEn":"Inspect cross-material interface cracking","objective":"沿矽與模封料邊界查看介電與銅層，並能說明「失配形變會集中在跨界位置」。","objectiveEn":"Inspect dielectric and copper across die-mold boundaries and explain: Mismatch deformation concentrates at boundaries.","instruction":"沿矽與模封料邊界查看介電與銅層。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：跨界線段有專屬形貌或截面證據。","instructionEn":"Inspect dielectric and copper across die-mold boundaries. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Crossing lines have dedicated imaging or sections.","observation":"跨界線段有專屬形貌或截面證據；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Crossing lines have dedicated imaging or sections; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"只看同材區會漏掉邊界失效。","failureEn":"Same-material inspection misses boundary failures.","check":"跨界線段有專屬形貌或截面證據。","checkEn":"Crossing lines have dedicated imaging or sections.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-259-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"失配形變會集中在跨界位置。","textEn":"Mismatch deformation concentrates at boundaries."},{"id":"pk-259-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"只看同材區會漏掉邊界失效；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Same-material inspection misses boundary failures. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「檢查跨材料界面裂紋」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Inspect cross-material interface cracking\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["設備接觸區沒有未處置膜料","接觸包絡不因套刻而斷開","跨界線段有專屬形貌或截面證據"],"optionsEn":["Equipment contacts lack unresolved deposits","Overlay preserves contact envelopes","Crossing lines have dedicated imaging or sections"],"answer":2,"explanation":"失配形變會集中在跨界位置。本步要確認：跨界線段有專屬形貌或截面證據；常見誤判是：只看同材區會漏掉邊界失效。","explanationEn":"Mismatch deformation concentrates at boundaries. Verify: Crossing lines have dedicated imaging or sections. A common misinterpretation is: Same-material inspection misses boundary failures."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-258"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-260","order":26,"sequence":260,"title":"放行RDL至下層或端接","titleEn":"Release RDL for next layer or terminals","objective":"整合幾何、電性與界面紀錄，並能說明「多層RDL須逐層保留對位與測試資訊」。","objectiveEn":"Combine geometric, electrical and interface records and explain: Multilayer RDL needs layerwise alignment and test records.","instruction":"整合幾何、電性與界面紀錄。以您自行建立或取得的證據逐項核對：未解決開短路不進入後續覆蓋。","instructionEn":"Combine geometric, electrical and interface records. Check evidence you create or obtain against: Unresolved faults do not proceed to overcoating.","observation":"未解決開短路不進入後續覆蓋；保留可重現判讀所需的原始圖像、量測或流程圖。","observationEn":"Unresolved faults do not proceed to overcoating; retain the original image, measurement or process map needed to reproduce the assessment.","failure":"提前覆蓋會使缺陷難以返工定位。","failureEn":"Premature covering makes faults difficult to locate or rework.","check":"未解決開短路不進入後續覆蓋。","checkEn":"Unresolved faults do not proceed to overcoating.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-260-k1","title":"本工序機制","titleEn":"Mechanism of this operation","text":"多層RDL須逐層保留對位與測試資訊。","textEn":"Multilayer RDL needs layerwise alignment and test records."},{"id":"pk-260-k2","title":"異常診斷與判讀邊界","titleEn":"Diagnosis and interpretation boundary","text":"提前覆蓋會使缺陷難以返工定位；應回查本步輸入證據，不能以猜測取代判定。","textEn":"Premature covering makes faults difficult to locate or rework. Recheck this operation's input evidence instead of substituting a guess."}],"quiz":{"question":"驗收「放行RDL至下層或端接」時，哪一項證據最直接對應本步目標？","questionEn":"When accepting \"Release RDL for next layer or terminals\", which evidence most directly addresses this operation?","options":["未解決開短路不進入後續覆蓋","預烤證據包含實際基板條件","最窄截面與關鍵轉角均被檢查"],"optionsEn":["Unresolved faults do not proceed to overcoating","Prebake evidence includes actual substrate conditions","Narrow sections and critical corners are checked"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多層RDL須逐層保留對位與測試資訊。本步要確認：未解決開短路不進入後續覆蓋；常見誤判是：提前覆蓋會使缺陷難以返工定位。","explanationEn":"Multilayer RDL needs layerwise alignment and test records. Verify: Unresolved faults do not proceed to overcoating. A common misinterpretation is: Premature covering makes faults difficult to locate or rework."},"sourceIds":["pk-suss-coating","pk-atotech-rdl","pk-atotech-semiconductor","pk-kla-inspection"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-259"],"learningMode":"conceptual-process-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-operation","sourceScope":"公開來源支持相關原理或設備功能；題目、步序和檢核為原創教學編排，未經原廠量產資格認證。","sourceScopeEn":"Public sources support related principles or tool functions. Tasks, sequencing and checks are authored educational work, not vendor-qualified production procedures.","photoId":"sputter-chamber","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察濺鍍設備的真空腔體與外部硬體；不能由照片推知 ALD/CVD 反應、膜厚、配方或本步結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe sputtering vacuum equipment and external hardware; the photograph does not establish ALD/CVD reactions, film thickness, recipes or step outcomes.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m11","title":"TSV 成孔、襯層、阻障與填孔","titleEn":"TSV formation, liner, barrier, and fill","description":"深孔的幾何、絕緣連續性與金屬覆蓋共同決定填孔與電性；入口外觀不能代替孔底證據。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Via geometry, dielectric continuity, and metal coverage jointly govern fill and electrical behavior; the entrance cannot establish bottom quality. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","order":11,"sequence":11,"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-261","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"TSV 深寬比核對","titleEn":"Check TSV aspect ratio","objective":"判斷「TSV 深寬比核對」是否滿足此具體條件：幾何位於已核准設備能力範圍。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check TSV aspect ratio meets this specific condition: Geometry falls within the approved tool capability.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：由剖面資料計算孔深與最小孔寬比。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Calculate depth divided by minimum width from cross sections. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：幾何位於已核准設備能力範圍；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Geometry falls within the approved tool capability. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"入口寬度代替最窄處會低估填孔難度。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Using entrance width hides the narrowest fill restriction. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"幾何位於已核准設備能力範圍；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Geometry falls within the approved tool capability. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-261-k1","title":"TSV 深寬比核對的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check TSV aspect ratio","text":"可檢驗條件為「幾何位於已核准設備能力範圍」。可藉由「由剖面資料計算孔深與最小孔寬比」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Geometry falls within the approved tool capability. Evidence can be developed through this action: Calculate depth divided by minimum width from cross sections. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-261-k2","title":"TSV 深寬比核對的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check TSV aspect ratio","text":"入口寬度代替最窄處會低估填孔難度。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Using entrance width hides the narrowest fill restriction. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-261-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"深寬比以指定寬度定義；假設孔深 50 µm、入口直徑 5 µm，AR=10。若底部縮成 3 µm，入口 AR 不能描述孔底覆蓋難度。","textEn":"Define aspect ratio using a stated width; hypothetical depth 50 µm and entrance diameter 5 µm give AR=10. A 3 µm bottom means entrance AR misses bottom coverage difficulty."},{"id":"pk-261-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"保留孔深、口徑、底徑、側壁角及扇貝紋。高 AR 所需襯層與種子覆蓋不能由平面膜厚直接推定。","textEn":"Retain depth, entrance and bottom diameters, sidewall angle and scallops. Planar film thickness does not establish high-AR liner or seed coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「TSV 深寬比核對」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check TSV aspect ratio?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","幾何位於已核准設備能力範圍","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：入口寬度代替最窄處會低估填孔難度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Geometry falls within the approved tool capability","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Using entrance width hides the narrowest fill restriction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「幾何位於已核准設備能力範圍」。入口寬度代替最窄處會低估填孔難度，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Geometry falls within the approved tool capability. Using entrance width hides the narrowest fill restriction, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":261,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-262","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"硬遮罩厚度分布","titleEn":"Map hard mask thickness","objective":"判斷「硬遮罩厚度分布」是否滿足此具體條件：各區域仍保有核准的遮罩餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map hard mask thickness meets this specific condition: Every region retains its approved mask allowance.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：疊合遮罩厚度圖與預期蝕刻損耗圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay mask thickness and predicted erosion maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各區域仍保有核准的遮罩餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Every region retains its approved mask allowance. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部遮罩耗盡可造成孔口擴張。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Local mask exhaustion can enlarge the via mouth. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各區域仍保有核准的遮罩餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Every region retains its approved mask allowance. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-262-k1","title":"硬遮罩厚度分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map hard mask thickness","text":"可檢驗條件為「各區域仍保有核准的遮罩餘量」。可藉由「疊合遮罩厚度圖與預期蝕刻損耗圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Every region retains its approved mask allowance. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay mask thickness and predicted erosion maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-262-k2","title":"硬遮罩厚度分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map hard mask thickness","text":"局部遮罩耗盡可造成孔口擴張。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Local mask exhaustion can enlarge the via mouth. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「硬遮罩厚度分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map hard mask thickness?","options":["忽略此失效線索：局部遮罩耗盡可造成孔口擴張。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各區域仍保有核准的遮罩餘量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Local mask exhaustion can enlarge the via mouth.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Every region retains its approved mask allowance","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「各區域仍保有核准的遮罩餘量」。局部遮罩耗盡可造成孔口擴張，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Every region retains its approved mask allowance. Local mask exhaustion can enlarge the via mouth, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":262,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-261"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-263","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"TSV 光阻開口殘留","titleEn":"Inspect TSV resist openings","objective":"判斷「TSV 光阻開口殘留」是否滿足此具體條件：孔口開放且無可辨識阻塞膜。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect TSV resist openings meets this specific condition: Openings are clear without detectable blocking film.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較顯影前後孔口影像與底部殘留訊號。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare opening images and residual-film signals. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔口開放且無可辨識阻塞膜；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Openings are clear without detectable blocking film. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"孔底殘膠會抑制起始蝕刻。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Residual resist inhibits initial etching. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔口開放且無可辨識阻塞膜；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Openings are clear without detectable blocking film. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-263-k1","title":"TSV 光阻開口殘留的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect TSV resist openings","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔口開放且無可辨識阻塞膜」。可藉由「比較顯影前後孔口影像與底部殘留訊號」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Openings are clear without detectable blocking film. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare opening images and residual-film signals. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-263-k2","title":"TSV 光阻開口殘留的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect TSV resist openings","text":"孔底殘膠會抑制起始蝕刻。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Residual resist inhibits initial etching. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「TSV 光阻開口殘留」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect TSV resist openings?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：孔底殘膠會抑制起始蝕刻。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","孔口開放且無可辨識阻塞膜"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Residual resist inhibits initial etching.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Openings are clear without detectable blocking film"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「孔口開放且無可辨識阻塞膜」。孔底殘膠會抑制起始蝕刻，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Openings are clear without detectable blocking film. Residual resist inhibits initial etching, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":263,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-262"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-264","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"成孔光罩套準","titleEn":"Check via-mask overlay","objective":"判斷「成孔光罩套準」是否滿足此具體條件：套準誤差未侵入設計保留區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check via-mask overlay meets this specific condition: Overlay errors do not enter design keep-out zones.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把孔位與禁佈區邊界共同套圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay via locations with keep-out boundaries. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：套準誤差未侵入設計保留區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Overlay errors do not enter design keep-out zones. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"孔位偏移可侵入元件或金屬。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Misplaced vias can intrude into devices or metal. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"套準誤差未侵入設計保留區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Overlay errors do not enter design keep-out zones. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-264-k1","title":"成孔光罩套準的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check via-mask overlay","text":"可檢驗條件為「套準誤差未侵入設計保留區」。可藉由「把孔位與禁佈區邊界共同套圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Overlay errors do not enter design keep-out zones. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay via locations with keep-out boundaries. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-264-k2","title":"成孔光罩套準的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check via-mask overlay","text":"孔位偏移可侵入元件或金屬。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Misplaced vias can intrude into devices or metal. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「成孔光罩套準」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check via-mask overlay?","options":["套準誤差未侵入設計保留區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：孔位偏移可侵入元件或金屬。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Overlay errors do not enter design keep-out zones","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Misplaced vias can intrude into devices or metal.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「套準誤差未侵入設計保留區」。孔位偏移可侵入元件或金屬，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Overlay errors do not enter design keep-out zones. Misplaced vias can intrude into devices or metal, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":264,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-263"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-265","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"深矽蝕刻剖面","titleEn":"Inspect deep silicon etch profile","objective":"判斷「深矽蝕刻剖面」是否滿足此具體條件：斜率符合選定填孔路線的規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect deep silicon etch profile meets this specific condition: Taper meets the selected fill route specification.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在模擬剖面量測側壁斜率。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure sidewall taper on simulated cross sections. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：斜率符合選定填孔路線的規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Taper meets the selected fill route specification. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"反入射輪廓可使上緣先封口。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Reentrant profiles can close at the top prematurely. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"斜率符合選定填孔路線的規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Taper meets the selected fill route specification. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-265-k1","title":"深矽蝕刻剖面的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect deep silicon etch profile","text":"可檢驗條件為「斜率符合選定填孔路線的規範」。可藉由「在模擬剖面量測側壁斜率」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Taper meets the selected fill route specification. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure sidewall taper on simulated cross sections. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-265-k2","title":"深矽蝕刻剖面的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect deep silicon etch profile","text":"反入射輪廓可使上緣先封口。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Reentrant profiles can close at the top prematurely. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「深矽蝕刻剖面」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect deep silicon etch profile?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","斜率符合選定填孔路線的規範","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：反入射輪廓可使上緣先封口。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Taper meets the selected fill route specification","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Reentrant profiles can close at the top prematurely."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「斜率符合選定填孔路線的規範」。反入射輪廓可使上緣先封口，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Taper meets the selected fill route specification. Reentrant profiles can close at the top prematurely, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":265,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-264"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-266","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"孔深均勻性","titleEn":"Map via-depth uniformity","objective":"判斷「孔深均勻性」是否滿足此具體條件：最深與最淺孔均在規格窗內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map via-depth uniformity meets this specific condition: Deepest and shallowest vias meet the specification window.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較中心中圈與邊緣孔深分布。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare center, middle, and edge depth distributions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：最深與最淺孔均在規格窗內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Deepest and shallowest vias meet the specification window. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只看平均孔深會漏掉邊緣異常。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Average depth can conceal edge excursions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最深與最淺孔均在規格窗內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Deepest and shallowest vias meet the specification window. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-266-k1","title":"孔深均勻性的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map via-depth uniformity","text":"可檢驗條件為「最深與最淺孔均在規格窗內」。可藉由「比較中心中圈與邊緣孔深分布」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Deepest and shallowest vias meet the specification window. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare center, middle, and edge depth distributions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-266-k2","title":"孔深均勻性的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map via-depth uniformity","text":"只看平均孔深會漏掉邊緣異常。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Average depth can conceal edge excursions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「孔深均勻性」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map via-depth uniformity?","options":["忽略此失效線索：只看平均孔深會漏掉邊緣異常。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最深與最淺孔均在規格窗內","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Average depth can conceal edge excursions.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Deepest and shallowest vias meet the specification window","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「最深與最淺孔均在規格窗內」。只看平均孔深會漏掉邊緣異常，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Deepest and shallowest vias meet the specification window. Average depth can conceal edge excursions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":266,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-265"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-267","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"側壁扇貝紋判讀","titleEn":"Assess sidewall scalloping","objective":"判斷「側壁扇貝紋判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：局部曲率未造成預測覆蓋中斷。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess sidewall scalloping meets this specific condition: Local curvature does not interrupt predicted coverage.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較側壁輪廓與襯層覆蓋模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare sidewall profiles with liner coverage models. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：局部曲率未造成預測覆蓋中斷；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Local curvature does not interrupt predicted coverage. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"尖銳凹槽會增加薄膜薄弱點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Sharp recesses create vulnerable coating regions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"局部曲率未造成預測覆蓋中斷；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Local curvature does not interrupt predicted coverage. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-267-k1","title":"側壁扇貝紋判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess sidewall scalloping","text":"可檢驗條件為「局部曲率未造成預測覆蓋中斷」。可藉由「比較側壁輪廓與襯層覆蓋模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Local curvature does not interrupt predicted coverage. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare sidewall profiles with liner coverage models. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-267-k2","title":"側壁扇貝紋判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess sidewall scalloping","text":"尖銳凹槽會增加薄膜薄弱點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Sharp recesses create vulnerable coating regions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「側壁扇貝紋判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess sidewall scalloping?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：尖銳凹槽會增加薄膜薄弱點。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","局部曲率未造成預測覆蓋中斷"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Sharp recesses create vulnerable coating regions.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Local curvature does not interrupt predicted coverage"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「局部曲率未造成預測覆蓋中斷」。尖銳凹槽會增加薄膜薄弱點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Local curvature does not interrupt predicted coverage. Sharp recesses create vulnerable coating regions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":267,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-266"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-268","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"孔底停止層判讀","titleEn":"Assess via-bottom stop layer","objective":"判斷「孔底停止層判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：停止層完整且孔底已到設計深度。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess via-bottom stop layer meets this specific condition: Stop layer is intact at the designed via depth.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：分辨孔底殘矽與停止層受損訊號。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Distinguish residual silicon from damaged stop layers. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：停止層完整且孔底已到設計深度；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Stop layer is intact at the designed via depth. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過蝕刻可損傷底部互連。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Overetch can damage underlying interconnects. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"停止層完整且孔底已到設計深度；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Stop layer is intact at the designed via depth. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-268-k1","title":"孔底停止層判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess via-bottom stop layer","text":"可檢驗條件為「停止層完整且孔底已到設計深度」。可藉由「分辨孔底殘矽與停止層受損訊號」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Stop layer is intact at the designed via depth. Evidence can be developed through this action: Distinguish residual silicon from damaged stop layers. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-268-k2","title":"孔底停止層判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess via-bottom stop layer","text":"過蝕刻可損傷底部互連。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Overetch can damage underlying interconnects. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「孔底停止層判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess via-bottom stop layer?","options":["停止層完整且孔底已到設計深度","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過蝕刻可損傷底部互連。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Stop layer is intact at the designed via depth","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Overetch can damage underlying interconnects.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「停止層完整且孔底已到設計深度」。過蝕刻可損傷底部互連，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Stop layer is intact at the designed via depth. Overetch can damage underlying interconnects, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":268,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-267"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-269","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"蝕刻側壁殘留清除驗證","titleEn":"Verify etch-residue removal","objective":"判斷「蝕刻側壁殘留清除驗證」是否滿足此具體條件：殘留降至核准門檻且輪廓未改變。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify etch-residue removal meets this specific condition: Residues meet approved limits without profile damage.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較清洗前後表面分析資料。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare surface-analysis data before and after cleaning. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：殘留降至核准門檻且輪廓未改變；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Residues meet approved limits without profile damage. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"殘留物可降低襯層附著。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Residues can weaken liner adhesion. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"殘留降至核准門檻且輪廓未改變；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Residues meet approved limits without profile damage. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-269-k1","title":"蝕刻側壁殘留清除驗證的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify etch-residue removal","text":"可檢驗條件為「殘留降至核准門檻且輪廓未改變」。可藉由「比較清洗前後表面分析資料」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Residues meet approved limits without profile damage. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare surface-analysis data before and after cleaning. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-269-k2","title":"蝕刻側壁殘留清除驗證的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify etch-residue removal","text":"殘留物可降低襯層附著。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Residues can weaken liner adhesion. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「蝕刻側壁殘留清除驗證」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify etch-residue removal?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","殘留降至核准門檻且輪廓未改變","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：殘留物可降低襯層附著。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Residues meet approved limits without profile damage","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Residues can weaken liner adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「殘留降至核准門檻且輪廓未改變」。殘留物可降低襯層附著，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Residues meet approved limits without profile damage. Residues can weaken liner adhesion, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":269,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-268"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-270","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"孔口缺口與崩裂","titleEn":"Inspect via-mouth notching and chips","objective":"判斷「孔口缺口與崩裂」是否滿足此具體條件：缺口與裂紋未越過允收界線。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect via-mouth notching and chips meets this specific condition: Notches and cracks remain within acceptance boundaries.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：放大孔口與遮罩交界影像。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect enlarged via-mouth and mask-edge images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified 