equirements. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"平均膜厚合格不代表底部連續。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Mean thickness does not establish bottom continuity. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最薄區仍符合絕緣設計要求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"The thinnest region meets insulation requirements. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-271-k1","title":"TSV 絕緣襯層覆蓋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess dielectric liner coverage","text":"可檢驗條件為「最薄區仍符合絕緣設計要求」。可藉由「讀取孔頂中段孔底膜厚資料」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: The thinnest region meets insulation requirements. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read liner thickness at top, middle, and bottom. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-271-k2","title":"TSV 絕緣襯層覆蓋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess dielectric liner coverage","text":"平均膜厚合格不代表底部連續。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Mean thickness does not establish bottom continuity. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「TSV 絕緣襯層覆蓋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess dielectric liner coverage?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：平均膜厚合格不代表底部連續。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最薄區仍符合絕緣設計要求"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Mean thickness does not establish bottom continuity.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","The thinnest region meets insulation requirements"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「最薄區仍符合絕緣設計要求」。平均膜厚合格不代表底部連續，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: The thinnest region meets insulation requirements. Mean thickness does not establish bottom continuity, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":271,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-270"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-272","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"襯層針孔電性篩選","titleEn":"Screen liner pinholes electrically","objective":"判斷「襯層針孔電性篩選」是否滿足此具體條件：漏電尾端未超過核准限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Screen liner pinholes electrically meets this specific condition: Leakage tails remain within approved limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對漏電分布與對照試片。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare leakage distributions with control coupons. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：漏電尾端未超過核准限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Leakage tails remain within approved limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"少量針孔可主導漏電尾端。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Sparse pinholes can dominate leakage tails. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"漏電尾端未超過核准限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Leakage tails remain within approved limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-272-k1","title":"襯層針孔電性篩選的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Screen liner pinholes electrically","text":"可檢驗條件為「漏電尾端未超過核准限制」。可藉由「比對漏電分布與對照試片」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Leakage tails remain within approved limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare leakage distributions with control coupons. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-272-k2","title":"襯層針孔電性篩選的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Screen liner pinholes electrically","text":"少量針孔可主導漏電尾端。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Sparse pinholes can dominate leakage tails. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「襯層針孔電性篩選」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Screen liner pinholes electrically?","options":["漏電尾端未超過核准限制","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：少量針孔可主導漏電尾端。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Leakage tails remain within approved limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Sparse pinholes can dominate leakage tails.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「漏電尾端未超過核准限制」。少量針孔可主導漏電尾端，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Leakage tails remain within approved limits. Sparse pinholes can dominate leakage tails, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":272,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-271"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-273","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"襯層薄膜應力","titleEn":"Evaluate liner film stress","objective":"判斷「襯層薄膜應力」是否滿足此具體條件：應力與翹曲符合整合預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate liner film stress meets this specific condition: Stress and bow remain within integration budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將晶圓曲率與膜厚共同代入模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Combine wafer curvature and film thickness in the model. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：應力與翹曲符合整合預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Stress and bow remain within integration budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"應力偏高可促進薄化後翹曲。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"High stress can promote bow after thinning. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"應力與翹曲符合整合預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Stress and bow remain within integration budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-273-k1","title":"襯層薄膜應力的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate liner film stress","text":"可檢驗條件為「應力與翹曲符合整合預算」。可藉由「將晶圓曲率與膜厚共同代入模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Stress and bow remain within integration budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Combine wafer curvature and film thickness in the model. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-273-k2","title":"襯層薄膜應力的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate liner film stress","text":"應力偏高可促進薄化後翹曲。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"High stress can promote bow after thinning. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「襯層薄膜應力」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate liner film stress?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","應力與翹曲符合整合預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：應力偏高可促進薄化後翹曲。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Stress and bow remain within integration budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: High stress can promote bow after thinning."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「應力與翹曲符合整合預算」。應力偏高可促進薄化後翹曲，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Stress and bow remain within integration budgets. High stress can promote bow after thinning, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":273,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-272"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-274","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"底部接觸開口支線","titleEn":"Evaluate via-last bottom-contact opening","objective":"判斷「底部接觸開口支線」是否滿足此具體條件：接觸區開啟而側壁絕緣保持。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate via-last bottom-contact opening meets this specific condition: Contact opens while sidewall insulation remains.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在 via-last 案例檢查孔底介電開口。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect bottom dielectric openings in a via-last case. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接觸區開啟而側壁絕緣保持；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact opens while sidewall insulation remains. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"側壁同步移除會增加短路風險。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Sidewall removal increases shorting risk. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接觸區開啟而側壁絕緣保持；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact opens while sidewall insulation remains. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-274-k1","title":"底部接觸開口支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate via-last bottom-contact opening","text":"可檢驗條件為「接觸區開啟而側壁絕緣保持」。可藉由「在 via-last 案例檢查孔底介電開口」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact opens while sidewall insulation remains. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect bottom dielectric openings in a via-last case. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-274-k2","title":"底部接觸開口支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate via-last bottom-contact opening","text":"側壁同步移除會增加短路風險。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Sidewall removal increases shorting risk. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「底部接觸開口支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate via-last bottom-contact opening?","options":["忽略此失效線索：側壁同步移除會增加短路風險。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","接觸區開啟而側壁絕緣保持","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Sidewall removal increases shorting risk.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Contact opens while sidewall insulation remains","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「接觸區開啟而側壁絕緣保持」。側壁同步移除會增加短路風險，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact opens while sidewall insulation remains. Sidewall removal increases shorting risk, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":274,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-273"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-275","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"金屬阻障層連續性","titleEn":"Check barrier continuity","objective":"判斷「金屬阻障層連續性」是否滿足此具體條件：孔底與轉角沒有阻障中斷。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check barrier continuity meets this specific condition: Barrier remains continuous at bottoms and corners.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：讀取截面成分圖與厚度圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Read cross-sectional composition and thickness maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔底與轉角沒有阻障中斷；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Barrier remains continuous at bottoms and corners. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"阻障破口可能允許銅擴散。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Barrier breaks can permit copper diffusion. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔底與轉角沒有阻障中斷；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Barrier remains continuous at bottoms and corners. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-275-k1","title":"金屬阻障層連續性的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check barrier continuity","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔底與轉角沒有阻障中斷」。可藉由「讀取截面成分圖與厚度圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Barrier remains continuous at bottoms and corners. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read cross-sectional composition and thickness maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-275-k2","title":"金屬阻障層連續性的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check barrier continuity","text":"阻障破口可能允許銅擴散。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Barrier breaks can permit copper diffusion. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「金屬阻障層連續性」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check barrier continuity?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：阻障破口可能允許銅擴散。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","孔底與轉角沒有阻障中斷"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Barrier breaks can permit copper diffusion.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Barrier remains continuous at bottoms and corners"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「孔底與轉角沒有阻障中斷」。阻障破口可能允許銅擴散，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Barrier remains continuous at bottoms and corners. Barrier breaks can permit copper diffusion, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":275,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-274"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-276","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"種子層孔底覆蓋","titleEn":"Check seed coverage at via bottoms","objective":"判斷「種子層孔底覆蓋」是否滿足此具體條件：種子形成可連續供電路徑。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check seed coverage at via bottoms meets this specific condition: Seed provides a continuous current path.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較孔底與平面種子導電性。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bottom and field seed conductivity. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：種子形成可連續供電路徑；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Seed provides a continuous current path. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"不連續種子可留下未鍍區。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Discontinuous seed can leave unplated regions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"種子形成可連續供電路徑；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Seed provides a continuous current path. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-276-k1","title":"種子層孔底覆蓋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check seed coverage at via bottoms","text":"可檢驗條件為「種子形成可連續供電路徑」。可藉由「比較孔底與平面種子導電性」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Seed provides a continuous current path. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bottom and field seed conductivity. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-276-k2","title":"種子層孔底覆蓋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check seed coverage at via bottoms","text":"不連續種子可留下未鍍區。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Discontinuous seed can leave unplated regions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「種子層孔底覆蓋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check seed coverage at via bottoms?","options":["種子形成可連續供電路徑","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：不連續種子可留下未鍍區。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Seed provides a continuous current path","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Discontinuous seed can leave unplated regions.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「種子形成可連續供電路徑」。不連續種子可留下未鍍區，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Seed provides a continuous current path. Discontinuous seed can leave unplated regions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":276,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-275"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-277","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"種子層片電阻分布","titleEn":"Map seed sheet resistance","objective":"判斷「種子層片電阻分布」是否滿足此具體條件：分布與連通性符合電鍍規劃。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map seed sheet resistance meets this specific condition: Distribution and continuity support the plating plan.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：套合片電阻圖與接點位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay sheet resistance and contact locations. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：分布與連通性符合電鍍規劃；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Distribution and continuity support the plating plan. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部高阻會扭曲電流分配。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Local high resistance distorts current distribution. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"分布與連通性符合電鍍規劃；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Distribution and continuity support the plating plan. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-277-k1","title":"種子層片電阻分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map seed sheet resistance","text":"可檢驗條件為「分布與連通性符合電鍍規劃」。可藉由「套合片電阻圖與接點位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Distribution and continuity support the plating plan. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay sheet resistance and contact locations. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-277-k2","title":"種子層片電阻分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map seed sheet resistance","text":"局部高阻會扭曲電流分配。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Local high resistance distorts current distribution. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「種子層片電阻分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map seed sheet resistance?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","分布與連通性符合電鍍規劃","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部高阻會扭曲電流分配。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Distribution and continuity support the plating plan","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Local high resistance distorts current distribution."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「分布與連通性符合電鍍規劃」。局部高阻會扭曲電流分配，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Distribution and continuity support the plating plan. Local high resistance distorts current distribution, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":277,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-276"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-278","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"鍍前潤濕模擬","titleEn":"Simulate preplating wetting","objective":"判斷「鍍前潤濕模擬」是否滿足此具體條件：孔腔完全潤濕且無滯留氣泡。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Simulate preplating wetting meets this specific condition: Via cavities are wetted without trapped bubbles.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：觀察透明孔模型中的氣泡排出。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Observe bubble release in a transparent via model. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔腔完全潤濕且無滯留氣泡；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Via cavities are wetted without trapped bubbles. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"困氣會阻擋局部金屬成核。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Trapped gas blocks local metal nucleation. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔腔完全潤濕且無滯留氣泡；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Via cavities are wetted without trapped bubbles. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-278-k1","title":"鍍前潤濕模擬的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Simulate preplating wetting","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔腔完全潤濕且無滯留氣泡」。可藉由「觀察透明孔模型中的氣泡排出」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Via cavities are wetted without trapped bubbles. Evidence can be developed through this action: Observe bubble release in a transparent via model. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-278-k2","title":"鍍前潤濕模擬的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Simulate preplating wetting","text":"困氣會阻擋局部金屬成核。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Trapped gas blocks local metal nucleation. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「鍍前潤濕模擬」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Simulate preplating wetting?","options":["忽略此失效線索：困氣會阻擋局部金屬成核。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","孔腔完全潤濕且無滯留氣泡","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Trapped gas blocks local metal nucleation.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Via cavities are wetted without trapped bubbles","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「孔腔完全潤濕且無滯留氣泡」。困氣會阻擋局部金屬成核，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Via cavities are wetted without trapped bubbles. Trapped gas blocks local metal nucleation, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":278,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-277"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-279","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"電鍍添加劑分析判讀","titleEn":"Interpret plating-additive monitoring","objective":"判斷「電鍍添加劑分析判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：各分析指標均保持受控。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret plating-additive monitoring meets this specific condition: Each analytical indicator remains controlled.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較槽液分析趨勢與核准控制窗。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bath-analysis trends with approved control windows. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各分析指標均保持受控；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Each analytical indicator remains controlled. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"補充量正常仍可能存在分析漂移。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Normal replenishment does not exclude analysis drift. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各分析指標均保持受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Each analytical indicator remains controlled. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-279-k1","title":"電鍍添加劑分析判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret plating-additive monitoring","text":"可檢驗條件為「各分析指標均保持受控」。可藉由「比較槽液分析趨勢與核准控制窗」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Each analytical indicator remains controlled. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bath-analysis trends with approved control windows. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-279-k2","title":"電鍍添加劑分析判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret plating-additive monitoring","text":"補充量正常仍可能存在分析漂移。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Normal replenishment does not exclude analysis drift. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「電鍍添加劑分析判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret plating-additive monitoring?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：補充量正常仍可能存在分析漂移。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各分析指標均保持受控"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Normal replenishment does not exclude analysis drift.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Each analytical indicator remains controlled"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「各分析指標均保持受控」。補充量正常仍可能存在分析漂移，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Each analytical indicator remains controlled. Normal replenishment does not exclude analysis drift, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":279,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-278"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-280","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"TSV 底向上填孔","titleEn":"Interpret bottom-up TSV filling","objective":"判斷「TSV 底向上填孔」是否滿足此具體條件：填孔前緣未在孔口提前閉合。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret bottom-up TSV filling meets this specific condition: Fill front avoids premature mouth closure.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較不同填孔進度的剖面序列。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare cross sections across fill progression. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：填孔前緣未在孔口提前閉合；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Fill front avoids premature mouth closure. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"入口先閉合會封住內部空隙。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Early mouth closure traps internal voids. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"填孔前緣未在孔口提前閉合；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Fill front avoids premature mouth closure. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-280-k1","title":"TSV 底向上填孔的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret bottom-up TSV filling","text":"可檢驗條件為「填孔前緣未在孔口提前閉合」。可藉由「比較不同填孔進度的剖面序列」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Fill front avoids premature mouth closure. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare cross sections across fill progression. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-280-k2","title":"TSV 底向上填孔的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret bottom-up TSV filling","text":"入口先閉合會封住內部空隙。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Early mouth closure traps internal voids. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-280-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"若孔口沉積速度大於內部填充，可能先封口困住 seam 或空洞。底向上填孔需以剖面時序證明，表面平坦不等於內部無缺陷。","textEn":"If mouth deposition outruns interior fill, early closure can trap seams or voids. Bottom-up filling requires time-resolved sections; a flat surface does not prove a sound interior."},{"id":"pk-280-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"比較不同填充時點的截面及鏈阻，區分種子不連續、潤濕不足與添加劑控制。不可僅因最終電阻偏高就任意調整鍍液。","textEn":"Compare sections and chain resistance at different fill stages, distinguishing seed discontinuity, wetting and additive control. High final resistance alone does not justify arbitrary bath changes."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「TSV 底向上填孔」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret bottom-up TSV filling?","options":["填孔前緣未在孔口提前閉合","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：入口先閉合會封住內部空隙。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Fill front avoids premature mouth closure","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Early mouth closure traps internal voids.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「填孔前緣未在孔口提前閉合」。入口先閉合會封住內部空隙，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Fill front avoids premature mouth closure. Early mouth closure traps internal voids, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":280,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-279"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-281","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"鍍銅過鍍層分布","titleEn":"Map copper overburden","objective":"判斷「鍍銅過鍍層分布」是否滿足此具體條件：過鍍可在核准移除預算內清除。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map copper overburden meets this specific condition: Overburden fits the approved removal budget.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將過鍍厚度圖傳入平坦化模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Feed overburden maps into the planarization model. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：過鍍可在核准移除預算內清除；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Overburden fits the approved removal budget. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"厚度不均會拉大拋光終點差異。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Uneven overburden spreads polishing endpoints. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"過鍍可在核准移除預算內清除；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Overburden fits the approved removal budget. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-281-k1","title":"鍍銅過鍍層分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map copper overburden","text":"可檢驗條件為「過鍍可在核准移除預算內清除」。可藉由「將過鍍厚度圖傳入平坦化模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Overburden fits the approved removal budget. Evidence can be developed through this action: Feed overburden maps into the planarization model. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-281-k2","title":"鍍銅過鍍層分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map copper overburden","text":"厚度不均會拉大拋光終點差異。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Uneven overburden spreads polishing endpoints. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「鍍銅過鍍層分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map copper overburden?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","過鍍可在核准移除預算內清除","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：厚度不均會拉大拋光終點差異。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Overburden fits the approved removal budget","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Uneven overburden spreads polishing endpoints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「過鍍可在核准移除預算內清除」。厚度不均會拉大拋光終點差異，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Overburden fits the approved removal budget. Uneven overburden spreads polishing endpoints, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":281,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-280"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-282","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"填孔空洞斷層檢測","titleEn":"Inspect filled-via voids by tomography","objective":"判斷「填孔空洞斷層檢測」是否滿足此具體條件：空洞尺寸位置符合允收規則。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect filled-via voids by tomography meets this specific condition: Void size and location meet acceptance rules.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤斷層切片中的低密度區。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Track low-density regions through tomographic slices. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：空洞尺寸位置符合允收規則；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Void size and location meet acceptance rules. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單張投影可把重疊結構誤判空洞。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"One projection can confuse overlap with voiding. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"空洞尺寸位置符合允收規則；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Void size and location meet acceptance rules. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-282-k1","title":"填孔空洞斷層檢測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect filled-via voids by tomography","text":"可檢驗條件為「空洞尺寸位置符合允收規則」。可藉由「追蹤斷層切片中的低密度區」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Void size and location meet acceptance rules. Evidence can be developed through this action: Track low-density regions through tomographic slices. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-282-k2","title":"填孔空洞斷層檢測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect filled-via voids by tomography","text":"單張投影可把重疊結構誤判空洞。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"One projection can confuse overlap with voiding. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「填孔空洞斷層檢測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect filled-via voids by tomography?","options":["忽略此失效線索：單張投影可把重疊結構誤判空洞。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","空洞尺寸位置符合允收規則","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: One projection can confuse overlap with voiding.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Void size and location meet acceptance rules","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「空洞尺寸位置符合允收規則」。單張投影可把重疊結構誤判空洞，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Void size and location meet acceptance rules. One projection can confuse overlap with voiding, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":282,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-281"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-283","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"填銅熱處理尺寸穩定","titleEn":"Assess filled-copper thermal stability","objective":"判斷「填銅熱處理尺寸穩定」是否滿足此具體條件：凸起與內應力位於整合限制內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess filled-copper thermal stability meets this specific condition: Protrusion and stress remain within integration limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較熱歷程前後表面凸起量。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare surface protrusion before and after thermal history. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：凸起與內應力位於整合限制內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Protrusion and stress remain within integration limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"銅與矽熱膨脹差可推升孔頂。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Copper-silicon expansion mismatch can raise via tops. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"凸起與內應力位於整合限制內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Protrusion and stress remain within integration limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-283-k1","title":"填銅熱處理尺寸穩定的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess filled-copper thermal stability","text":"可檢驗條件為「凸起與內應力位於整合限制內」。可藉由「比較熱歷程前後表面凸起量」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Protrusion and stress remain within integration limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare surface protrusion before and after thermal history. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-283-k2","title":"填銅熱處理尺寸穩定的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess filled-copper thermal stability","text":"銅與矽熱膨脹差可推升孔頂。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Copper-silicon expansion mismatch can raise via tops. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「填銅熱處理尺寸穩定」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess filled-copper thermal stability?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：銅與矽熱膨脹差可推升孔頂。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","凸起與內應力位於整合限制內"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Copper-silicon expansion mismatch can raise via tops.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Protrusion and stress remain within integration limits"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「凸起與內應力位於整合限制內」。銅與矽熱膨脹差可推升孔頂，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Protrusion and stress remain within integration limits. Copper-silicon expansion mismatch can raise via tops, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":283,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-282"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-284","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"TSV 銅 CMP 終點","titleEn":"Determine TSV copper CMP endpoint","objective":"判斷「TSV 銅 CMP 終點」是否滿足此具體條件：過鍍去除且停止層損失受控。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Determine TSV copper CMP endpoint meets this specific condition: Overburden clears while stop-layer loss stays controlled.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：同步讀取金屬移除與停止層訊號。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Read metal removal and stop-layer signals together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：過鍍去除且停止層損失受控；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Overburden clears while stop-layer loss stays controlled. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過拋光可產生凹陷與介電侵蝕。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Overpolish can produce dishing and dielectric erosion. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"過鍍去除且停止層損失受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Overburden clears while stop-layer loss stays controlled. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-284-k1","title":"TSV 銅 CMP 終點的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Determine TSV copper CMP endpoint","text":"可檢驗條件為「過鍍去除且停止層損失受控」。可藉由「同步讀取金屬移除與停止層訊號」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Overburden clears while stop-layer loss stays controlled. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read metal removal and stop-layer signals together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-284-k2","title":"TSV 銅 CMP 終點的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Determine TSV copper CMP endpoint","text":"過拋光可產生凹陷與介電侵蝕。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Overpolish can produce dishing and dielectric erosion. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「TSV 銅 CMP 終點」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Determine TSV copper CMP endpoint?","options":["過鍍去除且停止層損失受控","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過拋光可產生凹陷與介電侵蝕。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Overburden clears while stop-layer loss stays controlled","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Overpolish can produce dishing and dielectric erosion.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「過鍍去除且停止層損失受控」。過拋光可產生凹陷與介電侵蝕，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Overburden clears while stop-layer loss stays controlled. Overpolish can produce dishing and dielectric erosion, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":284,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-283"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-285","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"孔頂凹陷與侵蝕","titleEn":"Measure TSV dishing and erosion","objective":"判斷「孔頂凹陷與侵蝕」是否滿足此具體條件：局部與全域高度誤差均達標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure TSV dishing and erosion meets this specific condition: Local and global height errors meet requirements.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：跨越孔頂與鄰近介電區量測高度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure heights across via tops and neighboring dielectric. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：局部與全域高度誤差均達標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Local and global height errors meet requirements. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只量銅凹陷會漏看介電侵蝕。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Measuring copper alone misses dielectric erosion. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"局部與全域高度誤差均達標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Local and global height errors meet requirements. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-285-k1","title":"孔頂凹陷與侵蝕的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure TSV dishing and erosion","text":"可檢驗條件為「局部與全域高度誤差均達標」。可藉由「跨越孔頂與鄰近介電區量測高度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Local and global height errors meet requirements. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure heights across via tops and neighboring dielectric. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-285-k2","title":"孔頂凹陷與侵蝕的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure TSV dishing and erosion","text":"只量銅凹陷會漏看介電侵蝕。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Measuring copper alone misses dielectric erosion. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「孔頂凹陷與侵蝕」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure TSV dishing and erosion?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","局部與全域高度誤差均達標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只量銅凹陷會漏看介電侵蝕。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Local and global height errors meet requirements","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Measuring copper alone misses dielectric erosion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「局部與全域高度誤差均達標」。只量銅凹陷會漏看介電侵蝕，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Local and global height errors meet requirements. Measuring copper alone misses dielectric erosion, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":285,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-284"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-286","stageId":"pk-m11","title":"TSV 鏈結與隔離驗證","titleEn":"Verify TSV chains and isolation","objective":"判斷「TSV 鏈結與隔離驗證」是否滿足此具體條件：導通及隔離兩種證據同時合格。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify TSV chains and isolation meets this specific condition: Continuity and isolation evidence both pass.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：聯合判讀鏈結電阻與對矽漏電。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Interpret chain resistance and leakage to silicon together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：導通及隔離兩種證據同時合格；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Continuity and isolation evidence both pass. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"低鏈阻不能排除對基體漏電。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Low chain resistance does not exclude substrate leakage. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"導通及隔離兩種證據同時合格；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Continuity and isolation evidence both pass. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-286-k1","title":"TSV 鏈結與隔離驗證的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify TSV chains and isolation","text":"可檢驗條件為「導通及隔離兩種證據同時合格」。可藉由「聯合判讀鏈結電阻與對矽漏電」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Continuity and isolation evidence both pass. Evidence can be developed through this action: Interpret chain resistance and leakage to silicon together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-286-k2","title":"TSV 鏈結與隔離驗證的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify TSV chains and isolation","text":"低鏈阻不能排除對基體漏電。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Low chain resistance does not exclude substrate leakage. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「TSV 鏈結與隔離驗證」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify TSV chains and isolation?","options":["忽略此失效線索：低鏈阻不能排除對基體漏電。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","導通及隔離兩種證據同時合格","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Low chain resistance does not exclude substrate leakage.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Continuity and isolation evidence both pass","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「導通及隔離兩種證據同時合格」。低鏈阻不能排除對基體漏電，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Continuity and isolation evidence both pass. Low chain resistance does not exclude substrate leakage, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-lam-tsv","pkb-nordson-wafer"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":286,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-285"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"TSV 支線；依 via-middle、via-last 與中介層結構選用，並非所有封裝都有 TSV。","routeEn":"TSV branch: select for via-middle, via-last, or interposer structures; many packages have no TSVs.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m12","title":"TSV 顯露、背面鈍化與重布線","titleEn":"TSV reveal, backside passivation, and redistribution","description":"背磨控制厚度，選擇性顯露建立導通端點；機械支撐與後續介電完整性必須一起檢查。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Grinding sets thickness and selective reveal exposes contacts; mechanical support and subsequent dielectric integrity require joint checks. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","order":12,"sequence":12,"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-287","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"暫時載板平整度","titleEn":"Check temporary-carrier flatness","objective":"判斷「暫時載板平整度」是否滿足此具體條件：載板誤差不耗盡薄化公差。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check temporary-carrier flatness meets this specific condition: Carrier errors do not exhaust thinning tolerance.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較載板厚度及平面度地圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare carrier thickness and flatness maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：載板誤差不耗盡薄化公差；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Carrier errors do not exhaust thinning tolerance. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"載板楔角會轉移為晶圓厚度梯度。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Carrier wedge transfers into wafer thickness gradients. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"載板誤差不耗盡薄化公差；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Carrier errors do not exhaust thinning tolerance. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-287-k1","title":"暫時載板平整度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check temporary-carrier flatness","text":"可檢驗條件為「載板誤差不耗盡薄化公差」。可藉由「比較載板厚度及平面度地圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Carrier errors do not exhaust thinning tolerance. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare carrier thickness and flatness maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-287-k2","title":"暫時載板平整度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check temporary-carrier flatness","text":"載板楔角會轉移為晶圓厚度梯度。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Carrier wedge transfers into wafer thickness gradients. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「暫時載板平整度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check temporary-carrier flatness?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：載板楔角會轉移為晶圓厚度梯度。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","載板誤差不耗盡薄化公差"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Carrier wedge transfers into wafer thickness gradients.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Carrier errors do not exhaust thinning tolerance"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「載板誤差不耗盡薄化公差」。載板楔角會轉移為晶圓厚度梯度，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Carrier errors do not exhaust thinning tolerance. Carrier wedge transfers into wafer thickness gradients, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":287,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-288","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"前表面保護層覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect front-side protection","objective":"判斷「前表面保護層覆蓋」是否滿足此具體條件：凸塊完全受保護且無局部空腔。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect front-side protection meets this specific condition: Bumps are protected without local cavities.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把保護層剖面與最高凸塊疊合。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay protection cross sections with tallest bumps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：凸塊完全受保護且無局部空腔；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Bumps are protected without local cavities. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"凸塊上方支撐不足易壓傷。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Insufficient support above bumps permits damage. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"凸塊完全受保護且無局部空腔；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Bumps are protected without local cavities. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-288-k1","title":"前表面保護層覆蓋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect front-side protection","text":"可檢驗條件為「凸塊完全受保護且無局部空腔」。可藉由「把保護層剖面與最高凸塊疊合」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Bumps are protected without local cavities. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay protection cross sections with tallest bumps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-288-k2","title":"前表面保護層覆蓋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect front-side protection","text":"凸塊上方支撐不足易壓傷。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Insufficient support above bumps permits damage. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「前表面保護層覆蓋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect front-side protection?","options":["凸塊完全受保護且無局部空腔","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：凸塊上方支撐不足易壓傷。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Bumps are protected without local cavities","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Insufficient support above bumps permits damage.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「凸塊完全受保護且無局部空腔」。凸塊上方支撐不足易壓傷，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Bumps are protected without local cavities. Insufficient support above bumps permits damage, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":288,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-287"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-289","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"暫時黏著層均勻性","titleEn":"Map temporary-bond adhesive uniformity","objective":"判斷「暫時黏著層均勻性」是否滿足此具體條件：支撐層厚度與空洞均達標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map temporary-bond adhesive uniformity meets this specific condition: Support-layer thickness and voiding meet criteria.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測黏著層厚度及空洞區域。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure adhesive thickness and void regions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：支撐層厚度與空洞均達標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Support-layer thickness and voiding meet criteria. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"黏著層厚差會影響最終總厚度變異。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Bondline variation affects final thickness variation. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"支撐層厚度與空洞均達標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Support-layer thickness and voiding meet criteria. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-289-k1","title":"暫時黏著層均勻性的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map temporary-bond adhesive uniformity","text":"可檢驗條件為「支撐層厚度與空洞均達標」。可藉由「量測黏著層厚度及空洞區域」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Support-layer thickness and voiding meet criteria. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure adhesive thickness and void regions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-289-k2","title":"暫時黏著層均勻性的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map temporary-bond adhesive uniformity","text":"黏著層厚差會影響最終總厚度變異。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Bondline variation affects final thickness variation. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「暫時黏著層均勻性」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map temporary-bond adhesive uniformity?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","支撐層厚度與空洞均達標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：黏著層厚差會影響最終總厚度變異。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Support-layer thickness and voiding meet criteria","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Bondline variation affects final thickness variation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「支撐層厚度與空洞均達標」。黏著層厚差會影響最終總厚度變異，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Support-layer thickness and voiding meet criteria. Bondline variation affects final thickness variation, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":289,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-288"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-290","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"載板鍵合空洞","titleEn":"Inspect carrier-bond voids","objective":"判斷「載板鍵合空洞」是否滿足此具體條件：承載區無超出規則的未黏合區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect carrier-bond voids meets this specific condition: Load-bearing regions lack unacceptable unbonded areas.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：判讀紅外或聲學黏著介面影像。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Interpret infrared or acoustic bond-interface images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：承載區無超出規則的未黏合區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Load-bearing regions lack unacceptable unbonded areas. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"未黏區在背磨時可局部彎曲。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unbonded regions can flex during grinding. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"承載區無超出規則的未黏合區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Load-bearing regions lack unacceptable unbonded areas. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-290-k1","title":"載板鍵合空洞的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect carrier-bond voids","text":"可檢驗條件為「承載區無超出規則的未黏合區」。可藉由「判讀紅外或聲學黏著介面影像」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Load-bearing regions lack unacceptable unbonded areas. Evidence can be developed through this action: Interpret infrared or acoustic bond-interface images. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-290-k2","title":"載板鍵合空洞的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect carrier-bond voids","text":"未黏區在背磨時可局部彎曲。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unbonded regions can flex during grinding. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「載板鍵合空洞」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect carrier-bond voids?","options":["忽略此失效線索：未黏區在背磨時可局部彎曲。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","承載區無超出規則的未黏合區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Unbonded regions can flex during grinding.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Load-bearing regions lack unacceptable unbonded areas","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「承載區無超出規則的未黏合區」。未黏區在背磨時可局部彎曲，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Load-bearing regions lack unacceptable unbonded areas. Unbonded regions can flex during grinding, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":290,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-289"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-291","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"晶圓邊緣修整","titleEn":"Evaluate wafer-edge trimming","objective":"判斷「晶圓邊緣修整」是否滿足此具體條件：保留邊緣不形成脆弱刀口。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate wafer-edge trimming meets this specific condition: Remaining edge avoids a fragile knife shape.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較薄化前後邊緣幾何模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare edge geometry before and after thinning. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：保留邊緣不形成脆弱刀口；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Remaining edge avoids a fragile knife shape. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"尖薄邊緣易崩裂並傳播裂紋。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Sharp thin edges chip and propagate cracks. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"保留邊緣不形成脆弱刀口；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Remaining edge avoids a fragile knife shape. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-291-k1","title":"晶圓邊緣修整的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate wafer-edge trimming","text":"可檢驗條件為「保留邊緣不形成脆弱刀口」。可藉由「比較薄化前後邊緣幾何模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Remaining edge avoids a fragile knife shape. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare edge geometry before and after thinning. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-291-k2","title":"晶圓邊緣修整的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate wafer-edge trimming","text":"尖薄邊緣易崩裂並傳播裂紋。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Sharp thin edges chip and propagate cracks. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶圓邊緣修整」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate wafer-edge trimming?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：尖薄邊緣易崩裂並傳播裂紋。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","保留邊緣不形成脆弱刀口"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Sharp thin edges chip and propagate cracks.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Remaining edge avoids a fragile knife shape"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「保留邊緣不形成脆弱刀口」。尖薄邊緣易崩裂並傳播裂紋，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Remaining edge avoids a fragile knife shape. Sharp thin edges chip and propagate cracks, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":291,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-290"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-292","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"粗磨剩餘矽厚","titleEn":"Control silicon remaining after coarse grind","objective":"判斷「粗磨剩餘矽厚」是否滿足此具體條件：保留足夠後續精磨餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Control silicon remaining after coarse grind meets this specific condition: Sufficient allowance remains for fine grinding.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤厚度計訊號與移除量。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Track thickness-gauge signals and removal amount. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：保留足夠後續精磨餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Sufficient allowance remains for fine grinding. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"粗磨直接到終厚會保留深損傷。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Coarse grinding to final thickness retains deep damage. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"保留足夠後續精磨餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Sufficient allowance remains for fine grinding. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-292-k1","title":"粗磨剩餘矽厚的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Control silicon remaining after coarse grind","text":"可檢驗條件為「保留足夠後續精磨餘量」。可藉由「追蹤厚度計訊號與移除量」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Sufficient allowance remains for fine grinding. Evidence can be developed through this action: Track thickness-gauge signals and removal amount. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-292-k2","title":"粗磨剩餘矽厚的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Control silicon remaining after coarse grind","text":"粗磨直接到終厚會保留深損傷。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Coarse grinding to final thickness retains deep damage. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「粗磨剩餘矽厚」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Control silicon remaining after coarse grind?","options":["保留足夠後續精磨餘量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：粗磨直接到終厚會保留深損傷。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Sufficient allowance remains for fine grinding","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Coarse grinding to final thickness retains deep damage.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「保留足夠後續精磨餘量」。粗磨直接到終厚會保留深損傷，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Sufficient allowance remains for fine grinding. Coarse grinding to final thickness retains deep damage, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":292,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-291"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-293","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"精磨磨痕方向","titleEn":"Assess fine-grind marks","objective":"判斷「精磨磨痕方向」是否滿足此具體條件：磨痕及粗糙度符合後續移除能力。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess fine-grind marks meets this specific condition: Marks and roughness fit downstream removal capability.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較粗糙度地圖與磨痕分布。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare roughness maps with grind-mark patterns. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：磨痕及粗糙度符合後續移除能力；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Marks and roughness fit downstream removal capability. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部深痕可能超過應力消除深度。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Deep marks can exceed stress-relief removal depth. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"磨痕及粗糙度符合後續移除能力；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Marks and roughness fit downstream removal capability. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-293-k1","title":"精磨磨痕方向的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess fine-grind marks","text":"可檢驗條件為「磨痕及粗糙度符合後續移除能力」。可藉由「比較粗糙度地圖與磨痕分布」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Marks and roughness fit downstream removal capability. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare roughness maps with grind-mark patterns. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-293-k2","title":"精磨磨痕方向的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess fine-grind marks","text":"局部深痕可能超過應力消除深度。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Deep marks can exceed stress-relief removal depth. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「精磨磨痕方向」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess fine-grind marks?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","磨痕及粗糙度符合後續移除能力","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部深痕可能超過應力消除深度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Marks and roughness fit downstream removal capability","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Deep marks can exceed stress-relief removal depth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「磨痕及粗糙度符合後續移除能力」。局部深痕可能超過應力消除深度，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Marks and roughness fit downstream removal capability. Deep marks can exceed stress-relief removal depth, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":293,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-292"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-294","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"總厚度變異量測","titleEn":"Measure total thickness variation","objective":"判斷「總厚度變異量測」是否滿足此具體條件：最大與最小厚度均達標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure total thickness variation meets this specific condition: Maximum and minimum thicknesses meet limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：用共同座標比較多點厚度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare multipoint thicknesses in a common frame. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：最大與最小厚度均達標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Maximum and minimum thicknesses meet limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"中心單點合格不能代表全片。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A center-only pass does not represent the wafer. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最大與最小厚度均達標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Maximum and minimum thicknesses meet limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-294-k1","title":"總厚度變異量測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure total thickness variation","text":"可檢驗條件為「最大與最小厚度均達標」。可藉由「用共同座標比較多點厚度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Maximum and minimum thicknesses meet limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare multipoint thicknesses in a common frame. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-294-k2","title":"總厚度變異量測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure total thickness variation","text":"中心單點合格不能代表全片。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A center-only pass does not represent the wafer. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-294-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"背磨 TTV 若為 4 µm，而計畫 TSV 顯露窗口僅 3 µm，單一全片移除量可能無法同時滿足所有位置。這是幾何窗口衝突，不應以平均厚度掩蓋。","textEn":"If backside TTV is 4 µm but the authored reveal window is only 3 µm, one uniform removal may not satisfy every location. This geometric conflict cannot be hidden by mean thickness."},{"id":"pk-294-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"把剩餘矽厚地圖與 TSV 深度地圖配準，使用局部相對距離預測顯露，不以兩張圖各自平均值相減替代。","textEn":"Register remaining-silicon and TSV-depth maps and predict reveal from local differences rather than subtracting separate map averages."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「總厚度變異量測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure total thickness variation?","options":["忽略此失效線索：中心單點合格不能代表全片。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最大與最小厚度均達標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: A center-only pass does not represent the wafer.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Maximum and minimum thicknesses meet limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「最大與最小厚度均達標」。中心單點合格不能代表全片，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Maximum and minimum thicknesses meet limits. A center-only pass does not represent the wafer, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":294,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-293"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-295","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背磨損傷層消除","titleEn":"Evaluate grinding damage removal","objective":"判斷「背磨損傷層消除」是否滿足此具體條件：損傷訊號下降且剩餘厚度合格。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate grinding damage removal meets this specific condition: Damage decreases while remaining thickness passes.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較處理前後表面裂紋與強度資料。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare crack and strength data before and after treatment. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：損傷訊號下降且剩餘厚度合格；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Damage decreases while remaining thickness passes. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只降低粗糙度未必消除亞表面裂紋。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Lower roughness need not remove subsurface cracks. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"損傷訊號下降且剩餘厚度合格；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Damage decreases while remaining thickness passes. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-295-k1","title":"背磨損傷層消除的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate grinding damage removal","text":"可檢驗條件為「損傷訊號下降且剩餘厚度合格」。可藉由「比較處理前後表面裂紋與強度資料」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Damage decreases while remaining thickness passes. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare crack and strength data before and after treatment. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-295-k2","title":"背磨損傷層消除的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate grinding damage removal","text":"只降低粗糙度未必消除亞表面裂紋。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Lower roughness need not remove subsurface cracks. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背磨損傷層消除」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate grinding damage removal?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只降低粗糙度未必消除亞表面裂紋。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","損傷訊號下降且剩餘厚度合格"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Lower roughness need not remove subsurface cracks.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Damage decreases while remaining thickness passes"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「損傷訊號下降且剩餘厚度合格」。只降低粗糙度未必消除亞表面裂紋，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Damage decreases while remaining thickness passes. Lower roughness need not remove subsurface cracks, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":295,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-294"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-296","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"TSV 顯露終點模擬","titleEn":"Simulate TSV reveal endpoint","objective":"判斷「TSV 顯露終點模擬」是否滿足此具體條件：孔端露出但未超出支撐容許量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Simulate TSV reveal endpoint meets this specific condition: Tips are exposed within supported-height limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：讀取矽移除量與孔端高度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Read silicon removal and via-tip height together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔端露出但未超出支撐容許量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Tips are exposed within supported-height limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過度顯露會削弱孔端機械支撐。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Excessive reveal weakens mechanical tip support. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔端露出但未超出支撐容許量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Tips are exposed within supported-height limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-296-k1","title":"TSV 顯露終點模擬的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Simulate TSV reveal endpoint","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔端露出但未超出支撐容許量」。可藉由「讀取矽移除量與孔端高度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Tips are exposed within supported-height limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read silicon removal and via-tip height together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-296-k2","title":"TSV 顯露終點模擬的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Simulate TSV reveal endpoint","text":"過度顯露會削弱孔端機械支撐。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Excessive reveal weakens mechanical tip support. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「TSV 顯露終點模擬」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Simulate TSV reveal endpoint?","options":["孔端露出但未超出支撐容許量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過度顯露會削弱孔端機械支撐。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Tips are exposed within supported-height limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Excessive reveal weakens mechanical tip support.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「孔端露出但未超出支撐容許量」。過度顯露會削弱孔端機械支撐，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Tips are exposed within supported-height limits. Excessive reveal weakens mechanical tip support, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":296,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-295"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-297","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面顯露高度分布","titleEn":"Map backside reveal height","objective":"判斷「背面顯露高度分布」是否滿足此具體條件：最矮孔可接觸且最高孔不過凸。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map backside reveal height meets this specific condition: Shortest tips contact while tallest avoid excessive protrusion.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：建立全片 TSV 突出高度圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Map TSV protrusion heights across the wafer. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：最矮孔可接觸且最高孔不過凸；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Shortest tips contact while tallest avoid excessive protrusion. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"孔深差異會轉換成顯露高度差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Via-depth variation becomes reveal-height variation. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最矮孔可接觸且最高孔不過凸；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Shortest tips contact while tallest avoid excessive protrusion. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-297-k1","title":"背面顯露高度分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map backside reveal height","text":"可檢驗條件為「最矮孔可接觸且最高孔不過凸」。可藉由「建立全片 TSV 突出高度圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Shortest tips contact while tallest avoid excessive protrusion. Evidence can be developed through this action: Map TSV protrusion heights across the wafer. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-297-k2","title":"背面顯露高度分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map backside reveal height","text":"孔深差異會轉換成顯露高度差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Via-depth variation becomes reveal-height variation. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-297-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設露出高度 1、2、4 µm，平均 2.33 µm；若後段接觸模型容許 1–3 µm，4 µm 點可能有支承或鈍化風險。門檻僅為教學例。","textEn":"Hypothetical reveal heights 1, 2 and 4 µm average 2.33 µm; an authored downstream window of 1–3 µm flags the 4 µm point for support or passivation risk."},{"id":"pk-297-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"高度以鄰近矽或鈍化面為基準，分辨殘矽、銅突出和量測遮蔽。過度顯露不必然較好，需連同後續覆蓋評估。","textEn":"Reference height to nearby silicon or passivation and distinguish residual silicon, protruding copper and occlusion. More reveal is not automatically better; evaluate subsequent coverage."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面顯露高度分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map backside reveal height?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最矮孔可接觸且最高孔不過凸","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：孔深差異會轉換成顯露高度差。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Shortest tips contact while tallest avoid excessive protrusion","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Via-depth variation becomes reveal-height variation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「最矮孔可接觸且最高孔不過凸」。孔深差異會轉換成顯露高度差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Shortest tips contact while tallest avoid excessive protrusion. Via-depth variation becomes reveal-height variation, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":297,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-296"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-298","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面殘矽辨識","titleEn":"Identify residual backside silicon","objective":"判斷「背面殘矽辨識」是否滿足此具體條件：接觸區未殘留阻斷導通的矽。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Identify residual backside silicon meets this specific condition: Contact regions lack silicon blocking continuity.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：疊合元素分析與孔端影像。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay composition data with via-tip images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接觸區未殘留阻斷導通的矽；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact regions lack silicon blocking continuity. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"外觀露孔不代表金屬接觸完全開放。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Visible tips do not guarantee exposed metal contacts. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接觸區未殘留阻斷導通的矽；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact regions lack silicon blocking continuity. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-298-k1","title":"背面殘矽辨識的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Identify residual backside silicon","text":"可檢驗條件為「接觸區未殘留阻斷導通的矽」。可藉由「疊合元素分析與孔端影像」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact regions lack silicon blocking continuity. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay composition data with via-tip images. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-298-k2","title":"背面殘矽辨識的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Identify residual backside silicon","text":"外觀露孔不代表金屬接觸完全開放。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Visible tips do not guarantee exposed metal contacts. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面殘矽辨識」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Identify residual backside silicon?","options":["忽略此失效線索：外觀露孔不代表金屬接觸完全開放。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","接觸區未殘留阻斷導通的矽","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Visible tips do not guarantee exposed metal contacts.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Contact regions lack silicon blocking continuity","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「接觸區未殘留阻斷導通的矽」。外觀露孔不代表金屬接觸完全開放，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact regions lack silicon blocking continuity. Visible tips do not guarantee exposed metal contacts, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":298,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-297"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-299","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面介電鈍化","titleEn":"Evaluate backside dielectric passivation","objective":"判斷「背面介電鈍化」是否滿足此具體條件：矽表面連續隔離且無破口。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate backside dielectric passivation meets this specific condition: Silicon surface is continuously insulated.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較介電膜跨孔端的覆蓋。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare dielectric coverage around exposed tips. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：矽表面連續隔離且無破口；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Silicon surface is continuously insulated. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"孔根陰影區可能留下薄膜缺口。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Tip-base shadow regions can leave film gaps. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"矽表面連續隔離且無破口；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Silicon surface is continuously insulated. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-299-k1","title":"背面介電鈍化的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate backside dielectric passivation","text":"可檢驗條件為「矽表面連續隔離且無破口」。可藉由「比較介電膜跨孔端的覆蓋」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Silicon surface is continuously insulated. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare dielectric coverage around exposed tips. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-299-k2","title":"背面介電鈍化的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate backside dielectric passivation","text":"孔根陰影區可能留下薄膜缺口。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Tip-base shadow regions can leave film gaps. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面介電鈍化」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate backside dielectric passivation?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：孔根陰影區可能留下薄膜缺口。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","矽表面連續隔離且無破口"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Tip-base shadow regions can leave film gaps.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Silicon surface is continuously insulated"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「矽表面連續隔離且無破口」。孔根陰影區可能留下薄膜缺口，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Silicon surface is continuously insulated. Tip-base shadow regions can leave film gaps, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":299,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-298"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-300","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面介電開窗套準","titleEn":"Align backside dielectric openings","objective":"判斷「背面介電開窗套準」是否滿足此具體條件：開窗落在導電端面且保留隔離。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Align backside dielectric openings meets this specific condition: Openings reach contacts while preserving isolation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把開窗輪廓與孔端座標套圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay opening contours and via-tip coordinates. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：開窗落在導電端面且保留隔離；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Openings reach contacts while preserving isolation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"偏移開窗可能露出鄰近矽。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Shifted openings can expose adjacent silicon. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"開窗落在導電端面且保留隔離；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Openings reach contacts while preserving isolation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-300-k1","title":"背面介電開窗套準的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Align backside dielectric openings","text":"可檢驗條件為「開窗落在導電端面且保留隔離」。可藉由「把開窗輪廓與孔端座標套圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Openings reach contacts while preserving isolation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay opening contours and via-tip coordinates. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-300-k2","title":"背面介電開窗套準的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Align backside dielectric openings","text":"偏移開窗可能露出鄰近矽。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Shifted openings can expose adjacent silicon. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面介電開窗套準」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Align backside dielectric openings?","options":["開窗落在導電端面且保留隔離","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：偏移開窗可能露出鄰近矽。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Openings reach contacts while preserving isolation","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Shifted openings can expose adjacent silicon.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「開窗落在導電端面且保留隔離」。偏移開窗可能露出鄰近矽，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Openings reach contacts while preserving isolation. Shifted openings can expose adjacent silicon, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":300,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-299"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-301","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"孔端殘氧化物判讀","titleEn":"Assess oxide residue on via tips","objective":"判斷「孔端殘氧化物判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：殘膜受控且電阻符合接觸預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess oxide residue on via tips meets this specific condition: Residual film and resistance fit contact budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較表面分析與接觸電阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare surface analysis with contact resistance. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：殘膜受控且電阻符合接觸預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Residual film and resistance fit contact budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"氧化殘膜可使接觸電阻升高。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Oxide residue can increase contact resistance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"殘膜受控且電阻符合接觸預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Residual film and resistance fit contact budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-301-k1","title":"孔端殘氧化物判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess oxide residue on via tips","text":"可檢驗條件為「殘膜受控且電阻符合接觸預算」。可藉由「比較表面分析與接觸電阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Residual film and resistance fit contact budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare surface analysis with contact resistance. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-301-k2","title":"孔端殘氧化物判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess oxide residue on via tips","text":"氧化殘膜可使接觸電阻升高。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Oxide residue can increase contact resistance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「孔端殘氧化物判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess oxide residue on via tips?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","殘膜受控且電阻符合接觸預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：氧化殘膜可使接觸電阻升高。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Residual film and resistance fit contact budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Oxide residue can increase contact resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「殘膜受控且電阻符合接觸預算」。氧化殘膜可使接觸電阻升高，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Residual film and resistance fit contact budgets. Oxide residue can increase contact resistance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":301,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-300"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-302","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面阻障種子沉積","titleEn":"Assess backside barrier and seed deposition","objective":"判斷「背面阻障種子沉積」是否滿足此具體條件：導電層跨越台階仍保持連續。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess backside barrier and seed deposition meets this specific condition: Conductive film remains continuous across steps.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查跨越孔端台階的金屬覆蓋。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect metal coverage across via-tip steps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：導電層跨越台階仍保持連續；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Conductive film remains continuous across steps. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"台階遮蔽可造成金屬斷裂。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Step shadowing can break metal continuity. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"導電層跨越台階仍保持連續；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Conductive film remains continuous across steps. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-302-k1","title":"背面阻障種子沉積的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess backside barrier and seed deposition","text":"可檢驗條件為「導電層跨越台階仍保持連續」。可藉由「檢查跨越孔端台階的金屬覆蓋」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Conductive film remains continuous across steps. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect metal coverage across via-tip steps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-302-k2","title":"背面阻障種子沉積的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess backside barrier and seed deposition","text":"台階遮蔽可造成金屬斷裂。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Step shadowing can break metal continuity. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面阻障種子沉積」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess backside barrier and seed deposition?","options":["忽略此失效線索：台階遮蔽可造成金屬斷裂。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","導電層跨越台階仍保持連續","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Step shadowing can break metal continuity.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Conductive film remains continuous across steps","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「導電層跨越台階仍保持連續」。台階遮蔽可造成金屬斷裂，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Conductive film remains continuous across steps. Step shadowing can break metal continuity, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":302,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-301"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-303","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面 RDL 光阻模壁","titleEn":"Inspect backside RDL resist molds","objective":"判斷「背面 RDL 光阻模壁」是否滿足此具體條件：模腔可形成設計線寬與間距。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect backside RDL resist molds meets this specific condition: Mold cavities support designed width and spacing.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測開口底寬及模壁傾斜。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure opening bottom width and mold-wall slope. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：模腔可形成設計線寬與間距；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Mold cavities support designed width and spacing. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"模壁倒塌會導致橋接。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Collapsed resist walls can cause bridges. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"模腔可形成設計線寬與間距；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Mold cavities support designed width and spacing. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-303-k1","title":"背面 RDL 光阻模壁的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect backside RDL resist molds","text":"可檢驗條件為「模腔可形成設計線寬與間距」。可藉由「量測開口底寬及模壁傾斜」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Mold cavities support designed width and spacing. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure opening bottom width and mold-wall slope. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-303-k2","title":"背面 RDL 光阻模壁的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect backside RDL resist molds","text":"模壁倒塌會導致橋接。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Collapsed resist walls can cause bridges. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面 RDL 光阻模壁」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect backside RDL resist molds?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：模壁倒塌會導致橋接。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","模腔可形成設計線寬與間距"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Collapsed resist walls can cause bridges.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Mold cavities support designed width and spacing"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「模腔可形成設計線寬與間距」。模壁倒塌會導致橋接，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Mold cavities support designed width and spacing. Collapsed resist walls can cause bridges, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":303,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-302"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-304","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面 RDL 電鍍厚度","titleEn":"Map backside RDL plated thickness","objective":"判斷「背面 RDL 電鍍厚度」是否滿足此具體條件：圖形密度區域皆在厚度窗內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map backside RDL plated thickness meets this specific condition: All pattern-density regions meet thickness windows.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較寬線與窄線的金屬高度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare metal heights on wide and narrow traces. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：圖形密度區域皆在厚度窗內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All pattern-density regions meet thickness windows. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"密度效應會造成局部過鍍。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Pattern-density effects can cause local overplating. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"圖形密度區域皆在厚度窗內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All pattern-density regions meet thickness windows. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-304-k1","title":"背面 RDL 電鍍厚度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map backside RDL plated thickness","text":"可檢驗條件為「圖形密度區域皆在厚度窗內」。可藉由「比較寬線與窄線的金屬高度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All pattern-density regions meet thickness windows. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare metal heights on wide and narrow traces. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-304-k2","title":"背面 RDL 電鍍厚度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map backside RDL plated thickness","text":"密度效應會造成局部過鍍。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Pattern-density effects can cause local overplating. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面 RDL 電鍍厚度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map backside RDL plated thickness?","options":["圖形密度區域皆在厚度窗內","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：密度效應會造成局部過鍍。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["All pattern-density regions meet thickness windows","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Pattern-density effects can cause local overplating.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「圖形密度區域皆在厚度窗內」。密度效應會造成局部過鍍，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All pattern-density regions meet thickness windows. Pattern-density effects can cause local overplating, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":304,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-303"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-305","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面去光阻殘留","titleEn":"Inspect backside resist stripping","objective":"判斷「背面去光阻殘留」是否滿足此具體條件：線間清潔且金屬未明顯侵蝕。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect backside resist stripping meets this specific condition: Spaces are clean without excessive metal attack.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤線間殘膠與金屬表面變化。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Track intertrace residue and metal-surface changes. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：線間清潔且金屬未明顯侵蝕；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Spaces are clean without excessive metal attack. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"殘膠會遮蔽後續種子層去除。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Resist residue masks later seed removal. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"線間清潔且金屬未明顯侵蝕；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Spaces are clean without excessive metal attack. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-305-k1","title":"背面去光阻殘留的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect backside resist stripping","text":"可檢驗條件為「線間清潔且金屬未明顯侵蝕」。可藉由「追蹤線間殘膠與金屬表面變化」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Spaces are clean without excessive metal attack. Evidence can be developed through this action: Track intertrace residue and metal-surface changes. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-305-k2","title":"背面去光阻殘留的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect backside resist stripping","text":"殘膠會遮蔽後續種子層去除。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Resist residue masks later seed removal. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面去光阻殘留」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect backside resist stripping?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","線間清潔且金屬未明顯侵蝕","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：殘膠會遮蔽後續種子層去除。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Spaces are clean without excessive metal attack","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Resist residue masks later seed removal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「線間清潔且金屬未明顯侵蝕」。殘膠會遮蔽後續種子層去除，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Spaces are clean without excessive metal attack. Resist residue masks later seed removal, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":305,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-304"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-306","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面種子層隔離","titleEn":"Verify backside seed isolation","objective":"判斷「背面種子層隔離」是否滿足此具體條件：線間種子移除且細線保留。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify backside seed isolation meets this specific condition: Intertrace seed clears while fine traces remain.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將種子蝕刻影像與絕緣測試比對。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare seed-removal images with insulation tests. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：線間種子移除且細線保留；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Intertrace seed clears while fine traces remain. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過蝕刻會縮窄有效導線。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Overetch narrows effective conductor widths. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"線間種子移除且細線保留；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Intertrace seed clears while fine traces remain. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-306-k1","title":"背面種子層隔離的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify backside seed isolation","text":"可檢驗條件為「線間種子移除且細線保留」。可藉由「將種子蝕刻影像與絕緣測試比對」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Intertrace seed clears while fine traces remain. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare seed-removal images with insulation tests. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-306-k2","title":"背面種子層隔離的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify backside seed isolation","text":"過蝕刻會縮窄有效導線。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Overetch narrows effective conductor widths. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面種子層隔離」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify backside seed isolation?","options":["忽略此失效線索：過蝕刻會縮窄有效導線。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","線間種子移除且細線保留","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Overetch narrows effective conductor widths.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Intertrace seed clears while fine traces remain","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「線間種子移除且細線保留」。過蝕刻會縮窄有效導線，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Intertrace seed clears while fine traces remain. Overetch narrows effective conductor widths, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":306,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-305"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-307","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面 RDL 鏈阻","titleEn":"Measure backside RDL chain resistance","objective":"判斷「背面 RDL 鏈阻」是否滿足此具體條件：鏈阻與設計分布相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure backside RDL chain resistance meets this specific condition: Chain resistance agrees with design distributions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較四端量測與幾何預測。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare four-terminal measurements with geometry predictions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：鏈阻與設計分布相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Chain resistance agrees with design distributions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"高阻需區分線損與接點異常。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"High resistance requires separating trace and contact causes. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"鏈阻與設計分布相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Chain resistance agrees with design distributions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-307-k1","title":"背面 RDL 鏈阻的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure backside RDL chain resistance","text":"可檢驗條件為「鏈阻與設計分布相容」。可藉由「比較四端量測與幾何預測」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Chain resistance agrees with design distributions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare four-terminal measurements with geometry predictions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-307-k2","title":"背面 RDL 鏈阻的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure backside RDL chain resistance","text":"高阻需區分線損與接點異常。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"High resistance requires separating trace and contact causes. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面 RDL 鏈阻」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure backside RDL chain resistance?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：高阻需區分線損與接點異常。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","鏈阻與設計分布相容"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: High resistance requires separating trace and contact causes.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Chain resistance agrees with design distributions"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「鏈阻與設計分布相容」。高阻需區分線損與接點異常，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Chain resistance agrees with design distributions. High resistance requires separating trace and contact causes, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":307,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-306"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-308","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面保護層邊緣覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect backside protective-layer edges","objective":"判斷「背面保護層邊緣覆蓋」是否滿足此具體條件：金屬受保護且接點開放正確。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect backside protective-layer edges meets this specific condition: Metal is protected with correct contact openings.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查金屬角落與保護層邊界。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect metal corners and protective-layer boundaries. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：金屬受保護且接點開放正確；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Metal is protected with correct contact openings. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"角落裂縫可成為水分進入路徑。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Corner cracks can admit moisture. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"金屬受保護且接點開放正確；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Metal is protected with correct contact openings. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-308-k1","title":"背面保護層邊緣覆蓋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect backside protective-layer edges","text":"可檢驗條件為「金屬受保護且接點開放正確」。可藉由「檢查金屬角落與保護層邊界」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Metal is protected with correct contact openings. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect metal corners and protective-layer boundaries. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-308-k2","title":"背面保護層邊緣覆蓋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect backside protective-layer edges","text":"角落裂縫可成為水分進入路徑。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Corner cracks can admit moisture. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面保護層邊緣覆蓋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect backside protective-layer edges?","options":["金屬受保護且接點開放正確","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：角落裂縫可成為水分進入路徑。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Metal is protected with correct contact openings","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Corner cracks can admit moisture.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「金屬受保護且接點開放正確」。角落裂縫可成為水分進入路徑，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Metal is protected with correct contact openings. Corner cracks can admit moisture, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":308,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-307"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-309","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"背面焊墊金屬介面","titleEn":"Assess backside pad metallurgy","objective":"判斷「背面焊墊金屬介面」是否滿足此具體條件：層序與接合材料相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess backside pad metallurgy meets this specific condition: Layer sequence is compatible with bonding materials.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較焊墊層序與組裝介面要求。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare pad-layer sequence with assembly requirements. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：層序與接合材料相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Layer sequence is compatible with bonding materials. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"不相容表面可造成潤濕或擴散問題。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Incompatible finishes cause wetting or diffusion issues. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"層序與接合材料相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Layer sequence is compatible with bonding materials. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-309-k1","title":"背面焊墊金屬介面的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess backside pad metallurgy","text":"可檢驗條件為「層序與接合材料相容」。可藉由「比較焊墊層序與組裝介面要求」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Layer sequence is compatible with bonding materials. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare pad-layer sequence with assembly requirements. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-309-k2","title":"背面焊墊金屬介面的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess backside pad metallurgy","text":"不相容表面可造成潤濕或擴散問題。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Incompatible finishes cause wetting or diffusion issues. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面焊墊金屬介面」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess backside pad metallurgy?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","層序與接合材料相容","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：不相容表面可造成潤濕或擴散問題。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Layer sequence is compatible with bonding materials","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Incompatible finishes cause wetting or diffusion issues."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「層序與接合材料相容」。不相容表面可造成潤濕或擴散問題，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Layer sequence is compatible with bonding materials. Incompatible finishes cause wetting or diffusion issues, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":309,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-308"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-310","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"去黏方式支線選擇","titleEn":"Select carrier-debond branch","objective":"判斷「去黏方式支線選擇」是否滿足此具體條件：選用方法不超出晶圓材料限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Select carrier-debond branch meets this specific condition: Selected method respects wafer material limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：依材料相容性比較熱滑移與光解案例。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare thermal-slide and optical-release compatibility. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：選用方法不超出晶圓材料限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Selected method respects wafer material limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"照搬另一載板方法可損傷黏著介面。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Transferring another carrier method can damage interfaces. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"選用方法不超出晶圓材料限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Selected method respects wafer material limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-310-k1","title":"去黏方式支線選擇的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Select carrier-debond branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「選用方法不超出晶圓材料限制」。可藉由「依材料相容性比較熱滑移與光解案例」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Selected method respects wafer material limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare thermal-slide and optical-release compatibility. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-310-k2","title":"去黏方式支線選擇的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Select carrier-debond branch","text":"照搬另一載板方法可損傷黏著介面。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Transferring another carrier method can damage interfaces. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「去黏方式支線選擇」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Select carrier-debond branch?","options":["忽略此失效線索：照搬另一載板方法可損傷黏著介面。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","選用方法不超出晶圓材料限制","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Transferring another carrier method can damage interfaces.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Selected method respects wafer material limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「選用方法不超出晶圓材料限制」。照搬另一載板方法可損傷黏著介面，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Selected method respects wafer material limits. Transferring another carrier method can damage interfaces, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":310,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-309"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-311","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"去黏後清潔與翹曲","titleEn":"Inspect post-debond residue and bow","objective":"判斷「去黏後清潔與翹曲」是否滿足此具體條件：清潔度及自由形貌皆滿足搬運要求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect post-debond residue and bow meets this specific condition: Cleanliness and free shape meet handling requirements.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：聯合判讀殘膠影像及自由翹曲圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Review residual adhesive images and free-wafer bow. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：清潔度及自由形貌皆滿足搬運要求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cleanliness and free shape meet handling requirements. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"載板時平坦不表示去黏後平坦。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Flatness on a carrier does not prove free-wafer flatness. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"清潔度及自由形貌皆滿足搬運要求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cleanliness and free shape meet handling requirements. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-311-k1","title":"去黏後清潔與翹曲的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect post-debond residue and bow","text":"可檢驗條件為「清潔度及自由形貌皆滿足搬運要求」。可藉由「聯合判讀殘膠影像及自由翹曲圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cleanliness and free shape meet handling requirements. Evidence can be developed through this action: Review residual adhesive images and free-wafer bow. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-311-k2","title":"去黏後清潔與翹曲的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect post-debond residue and bow","text":"載板時平坦不表示去黏後平坦。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Flatness on a carrier does not prove free-wafer flatness. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「去黏後清潔與翹曲」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect post-debond residue and bow?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：載板時平坦不表示去黏後平坦。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","清潔度及自由形貌皆滿足搬運要求"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Flatness on a carrier does not prove free-wafer flatness.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cleanliness and free shape meet handling requirements"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「清潔度及自由形貌皆滿足搬運要求」。載板時平坦不表示去黏後平坦，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cleanliness and free shape meet handling requirements. Flatness on a carrier does not prove free-wafer flatness, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":311,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-310"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-312","stageId":"pk-m12","title":"薄晶圓轉移完整性","titleEn":"Verify thin-wafer transfer integrity","objective":"判斷「薄晶圓轉移完整性」是否滿足此具體條件：未新增裂紋或開路群聚。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify thin-wafer transfer integrity meets this specific condition: No new cracks or open-circuit clusters appear.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較轉移前後裂紋與電性座標圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare crack and electrical maps before and after transfer. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：未新增裂紋或開路群聚；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: No new cracks or open-circuit clusters appear. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部吸持載荷可誘發延遲破裂。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Localized pickup loads can initiate delayed fracture. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"未新增裂紋或開路群聚；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"No new cracks or open-circuit clusters appear. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-312-k1","title":"薄晶圓轉移完整性的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify thin-wafer transfer integrity","text":"可檢驗條件為「未新增裂紋或開路群聚」。可藉由「比較轉移前後裂紋與電性座標圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: No new cracks or open-circuit clusters appear. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare crack and electrical maps before and after transfer. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-312-k2","title":"薄晶圓轉移完整性的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify thin-wafer transfer integrity","text":"局部吸持載荷可誘發延遲破裂。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Localized pickup loads can initiate delayed fracture. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「薄晶圓轉移完整性」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify thin-wafer transfer integrity?","options":["未新增裂紋或開路群聚","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部吸持載荷可誘發延遲破裂。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["No new cracks or open-circuit clusters appear","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Localized pickup loads can initiate delayed fracture.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「未新增裂紋或開路群聚」。局部吸持載荷可誘發延遲破裂，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: No new cracks or open-circuit clusters appear. Localized pickup loads can initiate delayed fracture, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-disco-thin","pkb-lam-tsv"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":312,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-311"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"已填 TSV 晶圓的背面支線；載板、去黏方式與背面金屬順序依材料系統選用。","routeEn":"Backside branch for filled-TSV wafers; carrier, debond method, and backside metal sequence depend on the material system.","photoId":"wafers","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察晶圓外觀與整片／晶粒尺度的差異；照片不顯示奈米結構或本步量測結果。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe wafer appearance and wafer-versus-die scale; the photograph does not show nanoscale structures or this step’s measured results.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m13","title":"矽中介層與 2.5D 系統整合","titleEn":"Silicon interposers and 2.5D system integration","description":"中介層連接多顆晶粒；互連拓撲、機械變形與良品晶粒選擇共同影響組裝結果。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Interposers connect multiple dies; interconnect topology, deformation, and known-good-die selection jointly affect assembly. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","order":13,"sequence":13,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-313","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層晶粒腳位對映","titleEn":"Map die pins onto the interposer","objective":"判斷「中介層晶粒腳位對映」是否滿足此具體條件：電源地與訊號對映沒有衝突。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map die pins onto the interposer meets this specific condition: Power, ground, and signal mappings have no conflicts.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把晶粒焊墊網表與中介層接點逐一比對。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare die-pad netlists with interposer contacts. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：電源地與訊號對映沒有衝突；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Power, ground, and signal mappings have no conflicts. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"鏡射座標錯誤可對接到錯誤網路。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Mirrored coordinates can connect the wrong nets. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"電源地與訊號對映沒有衝突；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Power, ground, and signal mappings have no conflicts. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-313-k1","title":"中介層晶粒腳位對映的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map die pins onto the interposer","text":"可檢驗條件為「電源地與訊號對映沒有衝突」。可藉由「把晶粒焊墊網表與中介層接點逐一比對」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Power, ground, and signal mappings have no conflicts. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare die-pad netlists with interposer contacts. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-313-k2","title":"中介層晶粒腳位對映的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map die pins onto the interposer","text":"鏡射座標錯誤可對接到錯誤網路。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Mirrored coordinates can connect the wrong nets. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層晶粒腳位對映」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map die pins onto the interposer?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","電源地與訊號對映沒有衝突","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：鏡射座標錯誤可對接到錯誤網路。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Power, ground, and signal mappings have no conflicts","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Mirrored coordinates can connect the wrong nets."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「電源地與訊號對映沒有衝突」。鏡射座標錯誤可對接到錯誤網路，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Power, ground, and signal mappings have no conflicts. Mirrored coordinates can connect the wrong nets, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":313,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-314","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層尺寸與曝光邊界","titleEn":"Check interposer size and exposure boundaries","objective":"判斷「中介層尺寸與曝光邊界」是否滿足此具體條件：跨界互連有對應的套準驗證。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check interposer size and exposure boundaries meets this specific condition: Boundary-crossing interconnects have overlay verification.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：標記拼接邊界及跨界金屬路徑。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Mark stitching boundaries and crossing metal routes. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：跨界互連有對應的套準驗證；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Boundary-crossing interconnects have overlay verification. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"拼接偏移可能在長線形成頸縮。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Stitching offsets can neck long conductors. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"跨界互連有對應的套準驗證；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Boundary-crossing interconnects have overlay verification. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-314-k1","title":"中介層尺寸與曝光邊界的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check interposer size and exposure boundaries","text":"可檢驗條件為「跨界互連有對應的套準驗證」。可藉由「標記拼接邊界及跨界金屬路徑」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Boundary-crossing interconnects have overlay verification. Evidence can be developed through this action: Mark stitching boundaries and crossing metal routes. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-314-k2","title":"中介層尺寸與曝光邊界的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check interposer size and exposure boundaries","text":"拼接偏移可能在長線形成頸縮。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Stitching offsets can neck long conductors. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層尺寸與曝光邊界」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check interposer size and exposure boundaries?","options":["忽略此失效線索：拼接偏移可能在長線形成頸縮。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","跨界互連有對應的套準驗證","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Stitching offsets can neck long conductors.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Boundary-crossing interconnects have overlay verification","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「跨界互連有對應的套準驗證」。拼接偏移可能在長線形成頸縮，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Boundary-crossing interconnects have overlay verification. Stitching offsets can neck long conductors, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":314,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-313"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-315","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"介層金屬導通鏈","titleEn":"Test interposer metal chains","objective":"判斷「介層金屬導通鏈」是否滿足此具體條件：電阻隨長度變化符合結構模型。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Test interposer metal chains meets this specific condition: Resistance versus length agrees with structural models.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：對不同線長比較四端鏈阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare four-terminal chain resistance across lengths. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：電阻隨長度變化符合結構模型；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Resistance versus length agrees with structural models. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"截距異常可能來自接點而非線寬。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"An abnormal intercept may indicate contacts rather than width. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"電阻隨長度變化符合結構模型；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Resistance versus length agrees with structural models. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-315-k1","title":"介層金屬導通鏈的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Test interposer metal chains","text":"可檢驗條件為「電阻隨長度變化符合結構模型」。可藉由「對不同線長比較四端鏈阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Resistance versus length agrees with structural models. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare four-terminal chain resistance across lengths. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-315-k2","title":"介層金屬導通鏈的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Test interposer metal chains","text":"截距異常可能來自接點而非線寬。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"An abnormal intercept may indicate contacts rather than width. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介層金屬導通鏈」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Test interposer metal chains?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：截距異常可能來自接點而非線寬。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","電阻隨長度變化符合結構模型"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: An abnormal intercept may indicate contacts rather than width.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Resistance versus length agrees with structural models"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「電阻隨長度變化符合結構模型」。截距異常可能來自接點而非線寬，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Resistance versus length agrees with structural models. An abnormal intercept may indicate contacts rather than width, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":315,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-314"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-316","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層層間短路","titleEn":"Screen interposer interlayer shorts","objective":"判斷「中介層層間短路」是否滿足此具體條件：非相連網路保持規定隔離。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Screen interposer interlayer shorts meets this specific condition: Unconnected nets maintain specified isolation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較相鄰金屬層測試梳狀結構。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Evaluate comb structures between adjacent metal layers. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：非相連網路保持規定隔離；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Unconnected nets maintain specified isolation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"介電缺陷可在層間形成漏電。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Dielectric defects can create interlayer leakage. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"非相連網路保持規定隔離；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Unconnected nets maintain specified isolation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-316-k1","title":"中介層層間短路的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Screen interposer interlayer shorts","text":"可檢驗條件為「非相連網路保持規定隔離」。可藉由「比較相鄰金屬層測試梳狀結構」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Unconnected nets maintain specified isolation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Evaluate comb structures between adjacent metal layers. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-316-k2","title":"中介層層間短路的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Screen interposer interlayer shorts","text":"介電缺陷可在層間形成漏電。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Dielectric defects can create interlayer leakage. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層層間短路」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Screen interposer interlayer shorts?","options":["非相連網路保持規定隔離","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：介電缺陷可在層間形成漏電。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Unconnected nets maintain specified isolation","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Dielectric defects can create interlayer leakage.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「非相連網路保持規定隔離」。介電缺陷可在層間形成漏電，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Unconnected nets maintain specified isolation. Dielectric defects can create interlayer leakage, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":316,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-315"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-317","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層 TSV 端點對映","titleEn":"Map interposer TSV endpoints","objective":"判斷「中介層 TSV 端點對映」是否滿足此具體條件：端點及極性與設計資料一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map interposer TSV endpoints meets this specific condition: Endpoints and polarities match design data.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤上層網路穿越 TSV 到下層焊墊。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Trace upper nets through TSVs to lower pads. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：端點及極性與設計資料一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Endpoints and polarities match design data. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"僅查頂層可能漏掉底層換位。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Top-only review can miss backside swaps. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"端點及極性與設計資料一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Endpoints and polarities match design data. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-317-k1","title":"中介層 TSV 端點對映的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map interposer TSV endpoints","text":"可檢驗條件為「端點及極性與設計資料一致」。可藉由「追蹤上層網路穿越 TSV 到下層焊墊」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Endpoints and polarities match design data. Evidence can be developed through this action: Trace upper nets through TSVs to lower pads. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-317-k2","title":"中介層 TSV 端點對映的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map interposer TSV endpoints","text":"僅查頂層可能漏掉底層換位。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Top-only review can miss backside swaps. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層 TSV 端點對映」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map interposer TSV endpoints?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","端點及極性與設計資料一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：僅查頂層可能漏掉底層換位。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Endpoints and polarities match design data","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Top-only review can miss backside swaps."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「端點及極性與設計資料一致」。僅查頂層可能漏掉底層換位，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Endpoints and polarities match design data. Top-only review can miss backside swaps, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":317,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-316"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-318","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"介層微凸塊共平面度","titleEn":"Measure interposer microbump coplanarity","objective":"判斷「介層微凸塊共平面度」是否滿足此具體條件：局部共平面度符合接合行程預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure interposer microbump coplanarity meets this specific condition: Local coplanarity fits the bonding stroke budget.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較每顆晶粒區域的凸塊高度分布。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bump heights within each die footprint. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：局部共平面度符合接合行程預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Local coplanarity fits the bonding stroke budget. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"全片平均會掩蓋單顆晶粒區傾斜。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Wafer averages hide local footprint tilt. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"局部共平面度符合接合行程預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Local coplanarity fits the bonding stroke budget. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-318-k1","title":"介層微凸塊共平面度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure interposer microbump coplanarity","text":"可檢驗條件為「局部共平面度符合接合行程預算」。可藉由「比較每顆晶粒區域的凸塊高度分布」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Local coplanarity fits the bonding stroke budget. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bump heights within each die footprint. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-318-k2","title":"介層微凸塊共平面度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure interposer microbump coplanarity","text":"全片平均會掩蓋單顆晶粒區傾斜。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Wafer averages hide local footprint tilt. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介層微凸塊共平面度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure interposer microbump coplanarity?","options":["忽略此失效線索：全片平均會掩蓋單顆晶粒區傾斜。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","局部共平面度符合接合行程預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Wafer averages hide local footprint tilt.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Local coplanarity fits the bonding stroke budget","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「局部共平面度符合接合行程預算」。全片平均會掩蓋單顆晶粒區傾斜，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Local coplanarity fits the bonding stroke budget. Wafer averages hide local footprint tilt, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":318,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-317"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-319","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層切割道保護","titleEn":"Inspect interposer dicing streets","objective":"判斷「中介層切割道保護」是否滿足此具體條件：切割侵入量未接近有效互連。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect interposer dicing streets meets this specific condition: Cut encroachment avoids functional interconnects.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：疊合切割軌跡與金屬保護邊界。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay cutting paths and protected metal boundaries. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：切割侵入量未接近有效互連；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cut encroachment avoids functional interconnects. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"邊緣裂縫可沿介電層擴展。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Edge cracks can extend along dielectric layers. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"切割侵入量未接近有效互連；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cut encroachment avoids functional interconnects. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-319-k1","title":"中介層切割道保護的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect interposer dicing streets","text":"可檢驗條件為「切割侵入量未接近有效互連」。可藉由「疊合切割軌跡與金屬保護邊界」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cut encroachment avoids functional interconnects. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay cutting paths and protected metal boundaries. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-319-k2","title":"中介層切割道保護的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect interposer dicing streets","text":"邊緣裂縫可沿介電層擴展。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Edge cracks can extend along dielectric layers. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層切割道保護」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect interposer dicing streets?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：邊緣裂縫可沿介電層擴展。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","切割侵入量未接近有效互連"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Edge cracks can extend along dielectric layers.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cut encroachment avoids functional interconnects"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「切割侵入量未接近有效互連」。邊緣裂縫可沿介電層擴展，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cut encroachment avoids functional interconnects. Edge cracks can extend along dielectric layers, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":319,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-318"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-320","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層切割後邊緣","titleEn":"Inspect singulated interposer edges","objective":"判斷「中介層切割後邊緣」是否滿足此具體條件：崩角未越過核准保留區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect singulated interposer edges meets this specific condition: Chipping remains outside protected regions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測角落崩角及裂紋方向。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure corner chips and crack directions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：崩角未越過核准保留區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Chipping remains outside protected regions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只量崩角面積會漏看長裂紋。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Chip area alone can miss long cracks. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"崩角未越過核准保留區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Chipping remains outside protected regions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-320-k1","title":"中介層切割後邊緣的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect singulated interposer edges","text":"可檢驗條件為「崩角未越過核准保留區」。可藉由「量測角落崩角及裂紋方向」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Chipping remains outside protected regions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure corner chips and crack directions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-320-k2","title":"中介層切割後邊緣的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect singulated interposer edges","text":"只量崩角面積會漏看長裂紋。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Chip area alone can miss long cracks. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層切割後邊緣」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect singulated interposer edges?","options":["崩角未越過核准保留區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只量崩角面積會漏看長裂紋。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Chipping remains outside protected regions","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Chip area alone can miss long cracks.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「崩角未越過核准保留區」。只量崩角面積會漏看長裂紋，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Chipping remains outside protected regions. Chip area alone can miss long cracks, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":320,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-319"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-321","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層載台支撐","titleEn":"Evaluate interposer assembly support","objective":"判斷「中介層載台支撐」是否滿足此具體條件：放晶時局部撓度符合對位預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate interposer assembly support meets this specific condition: Local deflection fits placement alignment budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查支撐點與薄區變形模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect support positions and thin-region deformation. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：放晶時局部撓度符合對位預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Local deflection fits placement alignment budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"支撐空窗可導致放晶位置漂移。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unsupported spans can shift placement positions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"放晶時局部撓度符合對位預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Local deflection fits placement alignment budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-321-k1","title":"中介層載台支撐的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate interposer assembly support","text":"可檢驗條件為「放晶時局部撓度符合對位預算」。可藉由「檢查支撐點與薄區變形模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Local deflection fits placement alignment budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect support positions and thin-region deformation. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-321-k2","title":"中介層載台支撐的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate interposer assembly support","text":"支撐空窗可導致放晶位置漂移。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unsupported spans can shift placement positions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層載台支撐」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate interposer assembly support?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","放晶時局部撓度符合對位預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：支撐空窗可導致放晶位置漂移。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Local deflection fits placement alignment budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Unsupported spans can shift placement positions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「放晶時局部撓度符合對位預算」。支撐空窗可導致放晶位置漂移，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Local deflection fits placement alignment budgets. Unsupported spans can shift placement positions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":321,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-320"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-322","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"邏輯晶粒良品對位","titleEn":"Match known-good logic dies","objective":"判斷「邏輯晶粒良品對位」是否滿足此具體條件：只選取狀態有效的指定晶粒。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Match known-good logic dies meets this specific condition: Only specified dies with valid status are selected.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以晶圓座標與測試狀態核對取晶清單。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Match wafer coordinates and test states to pickup lists. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：只選取狀態有效的指定晶粒；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Only specified dies with valid status are selected. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"座標旋轉錯誤會取到鄰近失效晶粒。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Coordinate rotation errors select adjacent failing dies. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"只選取狀態有效的指定晶粒；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Only specified dies with valid status are selected. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-322-k1","title":"邏輯晶粒良品對位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Match known-good logic dies","text":"可檢驗條件為「只選取狀態有效的指定晶粒」。可藉由「以晶圓座標與測試狀態核對取晶清單」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Only specified dies with valid status are selected. Evidence can be developed through this action: Match wafer coordinates and test states to pickup lists. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-322-k2","title":"邏輯晶粒良品對位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Match known-good logic dies","text":"座標旋轉錯誤會取到鄰近失效晶粒。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Coordinate rotation errors select adjacent failing dies. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「邏輯晶粒良品對位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Match known-good logic dies?","options":["忽略此失效線索：座標旋轉錯誤會取到鄰近失效晶粒。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","只選取狀態有效的指定晶粒","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Coordinate rotation errors select adjacent failing dies.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Only specified dies with valid status are selected","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「只選取狀態有效的指定晶粒」。座標旋轉錯誤會取到鄰近失效晶粒，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Only specified dies with valid status are selected. Coordinate rotation errors select adjacent failing dies, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":322,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-321"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-323","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"記憶體堆疊入料匹配","titleEn":"Match incoming memory stacks","objective":"判斷「記憶體堆疊入料匹配」是否滿足此具體條件：電性介面與尺寸版本皆相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Match incoming memory stacks meets this specific condition: Electrical interfaces and geometry revisions are compatible.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對堆疊版本與介層介面需求。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare stack revisions with interposer interface requirements. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：電性介面與尺寸版本皆相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Electrical interfaces and geometry revisions are compatible. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"相同外形不保證介面版本一致。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Identical outlines do not establish interface compatibility. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"電性介面與尺寸版本皆相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Electrical interfaces and geometry revisions are compatible. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-323-k1","title":"記憶體堆疊入料匹配的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Match incoming memory stacks","text":"可檢驗條件為「電性介面與尺寸版本皆相容」。可藉由「比對堆疊版本與介層介面需求」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Electrical interfaces and geometry revisions are compatible. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare stack revisions with interposer interface requirements. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-323-k2","title":"記憶體堆疊入料匹配的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Match incoming memory stacks","text":"相同外形不保證介面版本一致。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Identical outlines do not establish interface compatibility. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記憶體堆疊入料匹配」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Match incoming memory stacks?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：相同外形不保證介面版本一致。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","電性介面與尺寸版本皆相容"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Identical outlines do not establish interface compatibility.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Electrical interfaces and geometry revisions are compatible"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「電性介面與尺寸版本皆相容」。相同外形不保證介面版本一致，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Electrical interfaces and geometry revisions are compatible. Identical outlines do not establish interface compatibility, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":323,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-322"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-324","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層助焊材圖形","titleEn":"Inspect interposer flux patterns","objective":"判斷「中介層助焊材圖形」是否滿足此具體條件：焊墊覆蓋足夠且禁沾區清潔。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect interposer flux patterns meets this specific condition: Pads have coverage while exclusion zones stay clean.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較轉印覆蓋與晶粒間禁沾區。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare transferred coverage and interdie exclusion zones. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：焊墊覆蓋足夠且禁沾區清潔；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Pads have coverage while exclusion zones stay clean. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過量助焊材可困在細間距縫隙。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Excess flux can become trapped in fine gaps. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"焊墊覆蓋足夠且禁沾區清潔；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Pads have coverage while exclusion zones stay clean. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-324-k1","title":"中介層助焊材圖形的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect interposer flux patterns","text":"可檢驗條件為「焊墊覆蓋足夠且禁沾區清潔」。可藉由「比較轉印覆蓋與晶粒間禁沾區」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Pads have coverage while exclusion zones stay clean. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare transferred coverage and interdie exclusion zones. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-324-k2","title":"中介層助焊材圖形的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect interposer flux patterns","text":"過量助焊材可困在細間距縫隙。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Excess flux can become trapped in fine gaps. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層助焊材圖形」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect interposer flux patterns?","options":["焊墊覆蓋足夠且禁沾區清潔","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過量助焊材可困在細間距縫隙。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Pads have coverage while exclusion zones stay clean","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Excess flux can become trapped in fine gaps.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「焊墊覆蓋足夠且禁沾區清潔」。過量助焊材可困在細間距縫隙，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Pads have coverage while exclusion zones stay clean. Excess flux can become trapped in fine gaps, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":324,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-323"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-325","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"第一顆邏輯晶粒放置","titleEn":"Place the first logic die virtually","objective":"判斷「第一顆邏輯晶粒放置」是否滿足此具體條件：各角落偏差均在核准範圍。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Place the first logic die virtually meets this specific condition: All corner offsets remain within approved limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以雙視野標記求解平移與轉角。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Solve translation and rotation from dual-field marks. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各角落偏差均在核准範圍；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All corner offsets remain within approved limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"中心對準仍可能有角度誤差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Center alignment can coexist with rotation error. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各角落偏差均在核准範圍；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All corner offsets remain within approved limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-325-k1","title":"第一顆邏輯晶粒放置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Place the first logic die virtually","text":"可檢驗條件為「各角落偏差均在核准範圍」。可藉由「以雙視野標記求解平移與轉角」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All corner offsets remain within approved limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Solve translation and rotation from dual-field marks. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-325-k2","title":"第一顆邏輯晶粒放置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Place the first logic die virtually","text":"中心對準仍可能有角度誤差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Center alignment can coexist with rotation error. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「第一顆邏輯晶粒放置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Place the first logic die virtually?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各角落偏差均在核准範圍","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：中心對準仍可能有角度誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","All corner offsets remain within approved limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Center alignment can coexist with rotation error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「各角落偏差均在核准範圍」。中心對準仍可能有角度誤差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All corner offsets remain within approved limits. Center alignment can coexist with rotation error, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":325,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-324"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-326","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"第二晶粒相對位置","titleEn":"Check relative position of neighboring dies","objective":"判斷「第二晶粒相對位置」是否滿足此具體條件：間隙滿足點膠與散熱結構需求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check relative position of neighboring dies meets this specific condition: Clearance supports dispense and thermal structures.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測兩晶粒間距及相互傾斜。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure interdie spacing and relative tilt. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：間隙滿足點膠與散熱結構需求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Clearance supports dispense and thermal structures. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"間距不足可阻斷後續充填流道。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Insufficient spacing can block underfill paths. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"間隙滿足點膠與散熱結構需求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Clearance supports dispense and thermal structures. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-326-k1","title":"第二晶粒相對位置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check relative position of neighboring dies","text":"可檢驗條件為「間隙滿足點膠與散熱結構需求」。可藉由「量測兩晶粒間距及相互傾斜」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Clearance supports dispense and thermal structures. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure interdie spacing and relative tilt. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-326-k2","title":"第二晶粒相對位置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check relative position of neighboring dies","text":"間距不足可阻斷後續充填流道。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Insufficient spacing can block underfill paths. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「第二晶粒相對位置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check relative position of neighboring dies?","options":["忽略此失效線索：間距不足可阻斷後續充填流道。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","間隙滿足點膠與散熱結構需求","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Insufficient spacing can block underfill paths.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Clearance supports dispense and thermal structures","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「間隙滿足點膠與散熱結構需求」。間距不足可阻斷後續充填流道，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Clearance supports dispense and thermal structures. Insufficient spacing can block underfill paths, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":326,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-325"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-327","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"記憶體堆疊放置","titleEn":"Place memory stacks virtually","objective":"判斷「記憶體堆疊放置」是否滿足此具體條件：堆疊位置及傾斜符合組裝規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Place memory stacks virtually meets this specific condition: Stack position and tilt meet assembly specifications.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對堆疊重心與支撐區域。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare stack centers of mass with support regions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：堆疊位置及傾斜符合組裝規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Stack position and tilt meet assembly specifications. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"較高堆疊易受工具偏載影響。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Tall stacks are sensitive to uneven tool loading. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"堆疊位置及傾斜符合組裝規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Stack position and tilt meet assembly specifications. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-327-k1","title":"記憶體堆疊放置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Place memory stacks virtually","text":"可檢驗條件為「堆疊位置及傾斜符合組裝規範」。可藉由「比對堆疊重心與支撐區域」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Stack position and tilt meet assembly specifications. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare stack centers of mass with support regions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-327-k2","title":"記憶體堆疊放置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Place memory stacks virtually","text":"較高堆疊易受工具偏載影響。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Tall stacks are sensitive to uneven tool loading. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記憶體堆疊放置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Place memory stacks virtually?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：較高堆疊易受工具偏載影響。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","堆疊位置及傾斜符合組裝規範"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Tall stacks are sensitive to uneven tool loading.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Stack position and tilt meet assembly specifications"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「堆疊位置及傾斜符合組裝規範」。較高堆疊易受工具偏載影響，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Stack position and tilt meet assembly specifications. Tall stacks are sensitive to uneven tool loading, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":327,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-326"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-328","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"多晶粒共同回焊支線","titleEn":"Evaluate a collective-reflow branch","objective":"判斷「多晶粒共同回焊支線」是否滿足此具體條件：所有接點皆進入合格的熱歷程窗。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate a collective-reflow branch meets this specific condition: All joints meet qualified thermal-history windows.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較多晶粒區的熱歷程與焊點收縮。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare thermal histories and joint collapse across dies. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：所有接點皆進入合格的熱歷程窗；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All joints meet qualified thermal-history windows. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"熱容量差異可造成局部未充分接合。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Thermal-mass differences can leave incomplete joints. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"所有接點皆進入合格的熱歷程窗；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All joints meet qualified thermal-history windows. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-328-k1","title":"多晶粒共同回焊支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate a collective-reflow branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「所有接點皆進入合格的熱歷程窗」。可藉由「比較多晶粒區的熱歷程與焊點收縮」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All joints meet qualified thermal-history windows. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare thermal histories and joint collapse across dies. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-328-k2","title":"多晶粒共同回焊支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate a collective-reflow branch","text":"熱容量差異可造成局部未充分接合。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Thermal-mass differences can leave incomplete joints. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「多晶粒共同回焊支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate a collective-reflow branch?","options":["所有接點皆進入合格的熱歷程窗","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：熱容量差異可造成局部未充分接合。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["All joints meet qualified thermal-history windows","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Thermal-mass differences can leave incomplete joints.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「所有接點皆進入合格的熱歷程窗」。熱容量差異可造成局部未充分接合，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All joints meet qualified thermal-history windows. Thermal-mass differences can leave incomplete joints, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":328,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-327"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-329","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"逐晶粒熱壓接合支線","titleEn":"Evaluate sequential thermocompression bonding","objective":"判斷「逐晶粒熱壓接合支線」是否滿足此具體條件：新接點合格且既有接點未劣化。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate sequential thermocompression bonding meets this specific condition: New joints pass without degrading existing joints.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤單顆熱壓對鄰近已接晶粒的影響。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Track local bonding effects on previously attached neighbors. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：新接點合格且既有接點未劣化；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: New joints pass without degrading existing joints. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"重複熱負載可能改變先前接點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Repeated thermal loads can alter earlier joints. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"新接點合格且既有接點未劣化；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"New joints pass without degrading existing joints. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-329-k1","title":"逐晶粒熱壓接合支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate sequential thermocompression bonding","text":"可檢驗條件為「新接點合格且既有接點未劣化」。可藉由「追蹤單顆熱壓對鄰近已接晶粒的影響」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: New joints pass without degrading existing joints. Evidence can be developed through this action: Track local bonding effects on previously attached neighbors. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-329-k2","title":"逐晶粒熱壓接合支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate sequential thermocompression bonding","text":"重複熱負載可能改變先前接點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Repeated thermal loads can alter earlier joints. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「逐晶粒熱壓接合支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate sequential thermocompression bonding?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","新接點合格且既有接點未劣化","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：重複熱負載可能改變先前接點。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","New joints pass without degrading existing joints","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Repeated thermal loads can alter earlier joints."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「新接點合格且既有接點未劣化」。重複熱負載可能改變先前接點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: New joints pass without degrading existing joints. Repeated thermal loads can alter earlier joints, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":329,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-328"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-330","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"互連塌陷高度","titleEn":"Measure interconnect collapse height","objective":"判斷「互連塌陷高度」是否滿足此具體條件：塌陷量與最終間隙均符合設計。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure interconnect collapse height meets this specific condition: Collapse and final gap both meet design requirements.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較接合前後間隙與凸塊高度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare gap and bump height before and after joining. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：塌陷量與最終間隙均符合設計；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Collapse and final gap both meet design requirements. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"塌陷不足與過度塌陷都有風險。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Both insufficient and excessive collapse are problematic. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"塌陷量與最終間隙均符合設計；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Collapse and final gap both meet design requirements. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-330-k1","title":"互連塌陷高度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure interconnect collapse height","text":"可檢驗條件為「塌陷量與最終間隙均符合設計」。可藉由「比較接合前後間隙與凸塊高度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Collapse and final gap both meet design requirements. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare gap and bump height before and after joining. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-330-k2","title":"互連塌陷高度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure interconnect collapse height","text":"塌陷不足與過度塌陷都有風險。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Both insufficient and excessive collapse are problematic. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「互連塌陷高度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure interconnect collapse height?","options":["忽略此失效線索：塌陷不足與過度塌陷都有風險。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","塌陷量與最終間隙均符合設計","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Both insufficient and excessive collapse are problematic.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Collapse and final gap both meet design requirements","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「塌陷量與最終間隙均符合設計」。塌陷不足與過度塌陷都有風險，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Collapse and final gap both meet design requirements. Both insufficient and excessive collapse are problematic, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":330,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-329"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-331","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層接合後翹曲","titleEn":"Map postbond interposer warpage","objective":"判斷「中介層接合後翹曲」是否滿足此具體條件：曲面變形未耗盡後續基板接合餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map postbond interposer warpage meets this specific condition: Deformation preserves downstream substrate bonding allowance.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在同一溫度基準比較接合前後曲面。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare prebond and postbond shapes at one temperature. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：曲面變形未耗盡後續基板接合餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Deformation preserves downstream substrate bonding allowance. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"不同量測溫度會混淆製程效應。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Different measurement temperatures confound process effects. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"曲面變形未耗盡後續基板接合餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Deformation preserves downstream substrate bonding allowance. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-331-k1","title":"中介層接合後翹曲的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map postbond interposer warpage","text":"可檢驗條件為「曲面變形未耗盡後續基板接合餘量」。可藉由「在同一溫度基準比較接合前後曲面」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Deformation preserves downstream substrate bonding allowance. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare prebond and postbond shapes at one temperature. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-331-k2","title":"中介層接合後翹曲的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map postbond interposer warpage","text":"不同量測溫度會混淆製程效應。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Different measurement temperatures confound process effects. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層接合後翹曲」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map postbond interposer warpage?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：不同量測溫度會混淆製程效應。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","曲面變形未耗盡後續基板接合餘量"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Different measurement temperatures confound process effects.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Deformation preserves downstream substrate bonding allowance"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「曲面變形未耗盡後續基板接合餘量」。不同量測溫度會混淆製程效應，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Deformation preserves downstream substrate bonding allowance. Different measurement temperatures confound process effects, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":331,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-330"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-332","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層充填流道","titleEn":"Inspect interposer underfill flow paths","objective":"判斷「中介層充填流道」是否滿足此具體條件：流道連通且未封住中央排氣路徑。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect interposer underfill flow paths meets this specific condition: Paths remain connected without trapping central air.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在模型追蹤多晶粒下方充填前緣。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Track underfill fronts beneath multiple dies. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：流道連通且未封住中央排氣路徑；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Paths remain connected without trapping central air. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"相向流前緣可包圍氣泡。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Opposing fronts can enclose bubbles. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"流道連通且未封住中央排氣路徑；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Paths remain connected without trapping central air. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-332-k1","title":"中介層充填流道的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect interposer underfill flow paths","text":"可檢驗條件為「流道連通且未封住中央排氣路徑」。可藉由「在模型追蹤多晶粒下方充填前緣」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Paths remain connected without trapping central air. Evidence can be developed through this action: Track underfill fronts beneath multiple dies. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-332-k2","title":"中介層充填流道的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect interposer underfill flow paths","text":"相向流前緣可包圍氣泡。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Opposing fronts can enclose bubbles. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層充填流道」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect interposer underfill flow paths?","options":["流道連通且未封住中央排氣路徑","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：相向流前緣可包圍氣泡。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Paths remain connected without trapping central air","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Opposing fronts can enclose bubbles.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「流道連通且未封住中央排氣路徑」。相向流前緣可包圍氣泡，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Paths remain connected without trapping central air. Opposing fronts can enclose bubbles, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":332,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-331"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-333","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"介層至基板凸塊檢查","titleEn":"Inspect interposer-to-substrate bumps","objective":"判斷「介層至基板凸塊檢查」是否滿足此具體條件：凸塊位置高度與焊墊相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect interposer-to-substrate bumps meets this specific condition: Bump position and height match substrate pads.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對底部凸塊地圖與基板焊墊。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bottom-bump maps with substrate pads. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：凸塊位置高度與焊墊相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Bump position and height match substrate pads. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"中介層頂部合格不等於底部合格。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A passing top interface does not establish bottom quality. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"凸塊位置高度與焊墊相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Bump position and height match substrate pads. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-333-k1","title":"介層至基板凸塊檢查的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect interposer-to-substrate bumps","text":"可檢驗條件為「凸塊位置高度與焊墊相容」。可藉由「比對底部凸塊地圖與基板焊墊」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Bump position and height match substrate pads. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bottom-bump maps with substrate pads. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-333-k2","title":"介層至基板凸塊檢查的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect interposer-to-substrate bumps","text":"中介層頂部合格不等於底部合格。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A passing top interface does not establish bottom quality. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介層至基板凸塊檢查」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect interposer-to-substrate bumps?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","凸塊位置高度與焊墊相容","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：中介層頂部合格不等於底部合格。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Bump position and height match substrate pads","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: A passing top interface does not establish bottom quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「凸塊位置高度與焊墊相容」。中介層頂部合格不等於底部合格，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Bump position and height match substrate pads. A passing top interface does not establish bottom quality, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":333,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-332"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-334","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"矽中介層基板放置","titleEn":"Place the silicon interposer on substrate","objective":"判斷「矽中介層基板放置」是否滿足此具體條件：各區域接點重疊符合接合需求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Place the silicon interposer on substrate meets this specific condition: Contact overlap meets bonding needs across regions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：模擬補償基板膨脹後的標記對準。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Simulate fiducial alignment with substrate expansion compensation. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各區域接點重疊符合接合需求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact overlap meets bonding needs across regions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"僅補償平移無法修正尺寸伸縮。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Translation correction cannot fix scale changes. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各區域接點重疊符合接合需求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact overlap meets bonding needs across regions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-334-k1","title":"矽中介層基板放置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Place the silicon interposer on substrate","text":"可檢驗條件為「各區域接點重疊符合接合需求」。可藉由「模擬補償基板膨脹後的標記對準」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact overlap meets bonding needs across regions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Simulate fiducial alignment with substrate expansion compensation. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-334-k2","title":"矽中介層基板放置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Place the silicon interposer on substrate","text":"僅補償平移無法修正尺寸伸縮。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Translation correction cannot fix scale changes. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「矽中介層基板放置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Place the silicon interposer on substrate?","options":["忽略此失效線索：僅補償平移無法修正尺寸伸縮。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各區域接點重疊符合接合需求","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Translation correction cannot fix scale changes.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Contact overlap meets bonding needs across regions","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「各區域接點重疊符合接合需求」。僅補償平移無法修正尺寸伸縮，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact overlap meets bonding needs across regions. Translation correction cannot fix scale changes, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":334,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-333"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-335","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"基板接合熱歷程","titleEn":"Verify substrate-attach thermal history","objective":"判斷「基板接合熱歷程」是否滿足此具體條件：焊點合格且晶粒不超過材料限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify substrate-attach thermal history meets this specific condition: Joints qualify without exceeding die material limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較晶粒頂面與底部焊點的模擬溫度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare die-top and bottom-joint temperatures. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：焊點合格且晶粒不超過材料限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Joints qualify without exceeding die material limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"底面達溫不能保證頂部材料安全。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Bottom temperature does not establish top-material compatibility. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"焊點合格且晶粒不超過材料限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Joints qualify without exceeding die material limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-335-k1","title":"基板接合熱歷程的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify substrate-attach thermal history","text":"可檢驗條件為「焊點合格且晶粒不超過材料限制」。可藉由「比較晶粒頂面與底部焊點的模擬溫度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Joints qualify without exceeding die material limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare die-top and bottom-joint temperatures. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-335-k2","title":"基板接合熱歷程的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify substrate-attach thermal history","text":"底面達溫不能保證頂部材料安全。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Bottom temperature does not establish top-material compatibility. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「基板接合熱歷程」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify substrate-attach thermal history?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：底面達溫不能保證頂部材料安全。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","焊點合格且晶粒不超過材料限制"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Bottom temperature does not establish top-material compatibility.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Joints qualify without exceeding die material limits"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「焊點合格且晶粒不超過材料限制」。底面達溫不能保證頂部材料安全，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Joints qualify without exceeding die material limits. Bottom temperature does not establish top-material compatibility, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":335,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-334"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-336","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"介層電源回路阻抗","titleEn":"Inspect interposer power-loop impedance","objective":"判斷「介層電源回路阻抗」是否滿足此具體條件：峰值與低頻壓降符合供電預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect interposer power-loop impedance meets this specific condition: Peaks and low-frequency drop fit power budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較電源與回流路徑的阻抗曲線。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare power and return-path impedance curves. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：峰值與低頻壓降符合供電預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Peaks and low-frequency drop fit power budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"良好直流電阻不代表高頻低阻抗。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Good DC resistance does not establish low high-frequency impedance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"峰值與低頻壓降符合供電預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Peaks and low-frequency drop fit power budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-336-k1","title":"介層電源回路阻抗的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect interposer power-loop impedance","text":"可檢驗條件為「峰值與低頻壓降符合供電預算」。可藉由「比較電源與回流路徑的阻抗曲線」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Peaks and low-frequency drop fit power budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare power and return-path impedance curves. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-336-k2","title":"介層電源回路阻抗的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect interposer power-loop impedance","text":"良好直流電阻不代表高頻低阻抗。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Good DC resistance does not establish low high-frequency impedance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-336-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設允許瞬態 droop 20 mV、負載階躍 10 A，目標阻抗量級 Ztarget=ΔV/ΔI=2 mΩ。它應附頻率範圍，不能只用 DC 電阻宣稱通過。","textEn":"For hypothetical droop 20 mV and load step 10 A, target impedance scale is 2 mΩ. Specify frequency range; DC resistance alone cannot establish compliance."},{"id":"pk-336-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"分開電阻壓降、封裝電感與去耦共振。將晶粒到基板再到穩壓器的回流路徑畫完整，避免只沿供電線看幾何。","textEn":"Separate resistive drop, package inductance and decoupling resonance. Draw the full return path from die through substrate to regulator rather than only supply geometry."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介層電源回路阻抗」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect interposer power-loop impedance?","options":["峰值與低頻壓降符合供電預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：良好直流電阻不代表高頻低阻抗。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Peaks and low-frequency drop fit power budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Good DC resistance does not establish low high-frequency impedance.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「峰值與低頻壓降符合供電預算」。良好直流電阻不代表高頻低阻抗，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Peaks and low-frequency drop fit power budgets. Good DC resistance does not establish low high-frequency impedance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":336,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-335"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-337","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"中介層訊號串擾","titleEn":"Evaluate interposer signal crosstalk","objective":"判斷「中介層訊號串擾」是否滿足此具體條件：耦合干擾未超過通道預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate interposer signal crosstalk meets this specific condition: Coupled interference stays within channel budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較相鄰通道的耦合響應。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare coupling responses between neighboring channels. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：耦合干擾未超過通道預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Coupled interference stays within channel budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只看單線損耗會漏掉相鄰干擾。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Single-line loss misses neighboring interference. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"耦合干擾未超過通道預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Coupled interference stays within channel budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-337-k1","title":"中介層訊號串擾的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate interposer signal crosstalk","text":"可檢驗條件為「耦合干擾未超過通道預算」。可藉由「比較相鄰通道的耦合響應」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Coupled interference stays within channel budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare coupling responses between neighboring channels. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-337-k2","title":"中介層訊號串擾的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate interposer signal crosstalk","text":"只看單線損耗會漏掉相鄰干擾。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Single-line loss misses neighboring interference. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-337-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"串擾同時取決於耦合長度、間距、回流面與邊沿速度。兩條同長線即使位元率相同，不同上升時間也可能有不同高頻耦合。","textEn":"Crosstalk depends on coupled length, spacing, reference planes and edge rate. Equal-length traces at the same data rate can couple differently with different rise times."},{"id":"pk-337-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"使用一致埠定義與終端比較近端/遠端串擾，保留激發與安靜受害線條件。不能只將更寬間距視為唯一改善方法。","textEn":"Compare near- and far-end crosstalk using consistent ports and terminations and state aggressor and quiet-victim conditions. Greater spacing is not the only possible improvement."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「中介層訊號串擾」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate interposer signal crosstalk?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","耦合干擾未超過通道預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只看單線損耗會漏掉相鄰干擾。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Coupled interference stays within channel budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Single-line loss misses neighboring interference."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「耦合干擾未超過通道預算」。只看單線損耗會漏掉相鄰干擾，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Coupled interference stays within channel budgets. Single-line loss misses neighboring interference, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":337,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-336"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-338","stageId":"pk-m13","title":"2.5D 整合缺陷關聯","titleEn":"Correlate 2.5D integration defects","objective":"判斷「2.5D 整合缺陷關聯」是否滿足此具體條件：缺陷定位有跨資料證據支持。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Correlate 2.5D integration defects meets this specific condition: Defect location is supported by multiple data types.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：疊合晶粒位置接合影像及失效網路。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay placement, joint images, and failing nets. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：缺陷定位有跨資料證據支持；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Defect location is supported by multiple data types. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只靠一張影像可能誤歸因。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A single image can support a false attribution. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"缺陷定位有跨資料證據支持；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Defect location is supported by multiple data types. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-338-k1","title":"2.5D 整合缺陷關聯的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Correlate 2.5D integration defects","text":"可檢驗條件為「缺陷定位有跨資料證據支持」。可藉由「疊合晶粒位置接合影像及失效網路」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Defect location is supported by multiple data types. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay placement, joint images, and failing nets. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-338-k2","title":"2.5D 整合缺陷關聯的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Correlate 2.5D integration defects","text":"只靠一張影像可能誤歸因。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A single image can support a false attribution. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「2.5D 整合缺陷關聯」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Correlate 2.5D integration defects?","options":["忽略此失效線索：只靠一張影像可能誤歸因。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","缺陷定位有跨資料證據支持","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: A single image can support a false attribution.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Defect location is supported by multiple data types","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「缺陷定位有跨資料證據支持」。只靠一張影像可能誤歸因，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Defect location is supported by multiple data types. A single image can support a false attribution, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-formfactor-kgd"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":338,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-337"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"矽中介層支線；RDL 中介層與局部矽橋是另類架構，需另選介面與製程。","routeEn":"Silicon-interposer branch; RDL interposers and local silicon bridges use different interfaces and flows.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m14","title":"有機與玻璃載板增層製作","titleEn":"Organic and glass substrate build-up","description":"增層介電、微孔與金屬圖形共同建立多層載板；粗糙度、附著與電損耗具有取捨。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Build-up dielectrics, microvias, and metal patterns form multilayer substrates; roughness, adhesion, and electrical loss trade off. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","order":14,"sequence":14,"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-339","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"載板芯材平面度","titleEn":"Map substrate-core flatness","objective":"判斷「載板芯材平面度」是否滿足此具體條件：幾何誤差在增層與搬運公差內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map substrate-core flatness meets this specific condition: Geometry fits build-up and handling tolerances.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較入料芯材的厚度及翹曲分布。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare incoming core thickness and warpage distributions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：幾何誤差在增層與搬運公差內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Geometry fits build-up and handling tolerances. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"芯材彎曲可累積為套準誤差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Core bow can accumulate into registration error. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"幾何誤差在增層與搬運公差內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Geometry fits build-up and handling tolerances. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-339-k1","title":"載板芯材平面度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map substrate-core flatness","text":"可檢驗條件為「幾何誤差在增層與搬運公差內」。可藉由「比較入料芯材的厚度及翹曲分布」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Geometry fits build-up and handling tolerances. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare incoming core thickness and warpage distributions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-339-k2","title":"載板芯材平面度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map substrate-core flatness","text":"芯材彎曲可累積為套準誤差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Core bow can accumulate into registration error. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「載板芯材平面度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map substrate-core flatness?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：芯材彎曲可累積為套準誤差。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","幾何誤差在增層與搬運公差內"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Core bow can accumulate into registration error.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Geometry fits build-up and handling tolerances"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「幾何誤差在增層與搬運公差內」。芯材彎曲可累積為套準誤差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Geometry fits build-up and handling tolerances. Core bow can accumulate into registration error, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":339,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-340","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"有機芯材含水判讀","titleEn":"Assess organic-core moisture","objective":"判斷「有機芯材含水判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：材料狀態符合核准壓合前要求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess organic-core moisture meets this specific condition: Material condition meets approved prelamination needs.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較材料調理紀錄與含水代理量測。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare conditioning records and moisture proxies. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：材料狀態符合核准壓合前要求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Material condition meets approved prelamination needs. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"受潮會改變尺寸與介電表現。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Moisture changes dimensions and dielectric behavior. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"材料狀態符合核准壓合前要求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Material condition meets approved prelamination needs. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-340-k1","title":"有機芯材含水判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess organic-core moisture","text":"可檢驗條件為「材料狀態符合核准壓合前要求」。可藉由「比較材料調理紀錄與含水代理量測」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Material condition meets approved prelamination needs. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare conditioning records and moisture proxies. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-340-k2","title":"有機芯材含水判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess organic-core moisture","text":"受潮會改變尺寸與介電表現。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Moisture changes dimensions and dielectric behavior. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「有機芯材含水判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess organic-core moisture?","options":["材料狀態符合核准壓合前要求","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：受潮會改變尺寸與介電表現。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Material condition meets approved prelamination needs","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Moisture changes dimensions and dielectric behavior.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「材料狀態符合核准壓合前要求」。受潮會改變尺寸與介電表現，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Material condition meets approved prelamination needs. Moisture changes dimensions and dielectric behavior, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":340,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-339"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-341","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"玻璃芯邊緣裂紋","titleEn":"Inspect glass-core edge cracks","objective":"判斷「玻璃芯邊緣裂紋」是否滿足此具體條件：裂紋未侵入機械保留區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect glass-core edge cracks meets this specific condition: Cracks do not enter protected mechanical regions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：用偏光與顯微影像定位邊緣缺陷。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Locate edge defects using polarized and microscopic images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：裂紋未侵入機械保留區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cracks do not enter protected mechanical regions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"細小邊裂可能於後續熱循環擴展。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Small edge cracks can grow during thermal cycling. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"裂紋未侵入機械保留區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cracks do not enter protected mechanical regions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-341-k1","title":"玻璃芯邊緣裂紋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect glass-core edge cracks","text":"可檢驗條件為「裂紋未侵入機械保留區」。可藉由「用偏光與顯微影像定位邊緣缺陷」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cracks do not enter protected mechanical regions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Locate edge defects using polarized and microscopic images. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-341-k2","title":"玻璃芯邊緣裂紋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect glass-core edge cracks","text":"細小邊裂可能於後續熱循環擴展。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Small edge cracks can grow during thermal cycling. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「玻璃芯邊緣裂紋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect glass-core edge cracks?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","裂紋未侵入機械保留區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：細小邊裂可能於後續熱循環擴展。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cracks do not enter protected mechanical regions","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Small edge cracks can grow during thermal cycling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「裂紋未侵入機械保留區」。細小邊裂可能於後續熱循環擴展，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cracks do not enter protected mechanical regions. Small edge cracks can grow during thermal cycling, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":341,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-340"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-342","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"有機芯通孔鑽孔支線","titleEn":"Inspect organic-core drilled holes","objective":"判斷「有機芯通孔鑽孔支線」是否滿足此具體條件：孔形及孔壁可接受後續金屬化。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect organic-core drilled holes meets this specific condition: Hole geometry supports subsequent metallization.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較孔壁粗糙與樹脂拖抹影像。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare hole-wall roughness and resin-smear images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔形及孔壁可接受後續金屬化；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Hole geometry supports subsequent metallization. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"樹脂拖抹會遮住內層銅接點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Resin smear can cover inner-layer copper contacts. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔形及孔壁可接受後續金屬化；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Hole geometry supports subsequent metallization. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-342-k1","title":"有機芯通孔鑽孔支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect organic-core drilled holes","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔形及孔壁可接受後續金屬化」。可藉由「比較孔壁粗糙與樹脂拖抹影像」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Hole geometry supports subsequent metallization. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare hole-wall roughness and resin-smear images. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-342-k2","title":"有機芯通孔鑽孔支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect organic-core drilled holes","text":"樹脂拖抹會遮住內層銅接點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Resin smear can cover inner-layer copper contacts. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「有機芯通孔鑽孔支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect organic-core drilled holes?","options":["忽略此失效線索：樹脂拖抹會遮住內層銅接點。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","孔形及孔壁可接受後續金屬化","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Resin smear can cover inner-layer copper contacts.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Hole geometry supports subsequent metallization","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「孔形及孔壁可接受後續金屬化」。樹脂拖抹會遮住內層銅接點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Hole geometry supports subsequent metallization. Resin smear can cover inner-layer copper contacts, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":342,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-341"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-343","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"玻璃通孔成孔支線","titleEn":"Inspect through-glass via formation","objective":"判斷「玻璃通孔成孔支線」是否滿足此具體條件：孔形及崩角符合金屬化能力。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect through-glass via formation meets this specific condition: Geometry and chipping fit metallization capability.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測玻璃孔錐度與出口崩角。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure glass-via taper and exit chipping. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.