:"Confirm: Residue is controlled without attacking inner contacts. Excess treatment can damage dielectric-copper interfaces, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":344,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-343"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-345","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"玻璃附著促進支線","titleEn":"Evaluate glass adhesion promotion","objective":"判斷「玻璃附著促進支線」是否滿足此具體條件：金屬附著經環境考驗仍達標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate glass adhesion promotion meets this specific condition: Metal adhesion passes after environmental exposure.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對處理前後附著試片結果。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare adhesion coupon results before and after treatment. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：金屬附著經環境考驗仍達標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Metal adhesion passes after environmental exposure. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"表面導電不等於金屬牢固附著。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Surface conductivity does not establish robust adhesion. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"金屬附著經環境考驗仍達標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Metal adhesion passes after environmental exposure. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-345-k1","title":"玻璃附著促進支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate glass adhesion promotion","text":"可檢驗條件為「金屬附著經環境考驗仍達標」。可藉由「比對處理前後附著試片結果」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Metal adhesion passes after environmental exposure. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare adhesion coupon results before and after treatment. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-345-k2","title":"玻璃附著促進支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate glass adhesion promotion","text":"表面導電不等於金屬牢固附著。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Surface conductivity does not establish robust adhesion. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「玻璃附著促進支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate glass adhesion promotion?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","金屬附著經環境考驗仍達標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：表面導電不等於金屬牢固附著。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Metal adhesion passes after environmental exposure","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Surface conductivity does not establish robust adhesion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「金屬附著經環境考驗仍達標」。表面導電不等於金屬牢固附著，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Metal adhesion passes after environmental exposure. Surface conductivity does not establish robust adhesion, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":345,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-344"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-346","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"化學銅種子覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect electroless copper seed coverage","objective":"判斷「化學銅種子覆蓋」是否滿足此具體條件：孔壁形成連通導電層。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect electroless copper seed coverage meets this specific condition: Via walls form a connected conductive film.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：查看孔壁及孔口種子連續性。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect seed continuity on via walls and mouths. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔壁形成連通導電層；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Via walls form a connected conductive film. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部種子缺口會形成電鍍空區。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Seed gaps cause unplated regions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔壁形成連通導電層；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Via walls form a connected conductive film. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-346-k1","title":"化學銅種子覆蓋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect electroless copper seed coverage","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔壁形成連通導電層」。可藉由「查看孔壁及孔口種子連續性」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Via walls form a connected conductive film. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect seed continuity on via walls and mouths. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-346-k2","title":"化學銅種子覆蓋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect electroless copper seed coverage","text":"局部種子缺口會形成電鍍空區。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Seed gaps cause unplated regions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「化學銅種子覆蓋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect electroless copper seed coverage?","options":["忽略此失效線索：局部種子缺口會形成電鍍空區。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","孔壁形成連通導電層","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Seed gaps cause unplated regions.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Via walls form a connected conductive film","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「孔壁形成連通導電層」。局部種子缺口會形成電鍍空區，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Via walls form a connected conductive film. Seed gaps cause unplated regions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":346,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-345"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-347","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"芯材通孔銅鍍層","titleEn":"Measure core through-hole copper","objective":"判斷「芯材通孔銅鍍層」是否滿足此具體條件：最薄孔壁符合可靠度設計要求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure core through-hole copper meets this specific condition: Thinnest wall meets reliability design requirements.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較孔口孔腰與孔底鍍層。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare copper at mouths, waists, and bottoms. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：最薄孔壁符合可靠度設計要求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Thinnest wall meets reliability design requirements. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"平面鍍層合格可能掩蓋孔腰不足。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Passing surface copper can hide a thin via waist. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最薄孔壁符合可靠度設計要求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Thinnest wall meets reliability design requirements. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-347-k1","title":"芯材通孔銅鍍層的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure core through-hole copper","text":"可檢驗條件為「最薄孔壁符合可靠度設計要求」。可藉由「比較孔口孔腰與孔底鍍層」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Thinnest wall meets reliability design requirements. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare copper at mouths, waists, and bottoms. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-347-k2","title":"芯材通孔銅鍍層的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure core through-hole copper","text":"平面鍍層合格可能掩蓋孔腰不足。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Passing surface copper can hide a thin via waist. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「芯材通孔銅鍍層」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure core through-hole copper?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：平面鍍層合格可能掩蓋孔腰不足。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最薄孔壁符合可靠度設計要求"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Passing surface copper can hide a thin via waist.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Thinnest wall meets reliability design requirements"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「最薄孔壁符合可靠度設計要求」。平面鍍層合格可能掩蓋孔腰不足，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Thinnest wall meets reliability design requirements. Passing surface copper can hide a thin via waist, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":347,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-346"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-348","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"芯材表面銅圖形","titleEn":"Inspect core copper patterns","objective":"判斷「芯材表面銅圖形」是否滿足此具體條件：連線正確且無線間銅殘留。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect core copper patterns meets this specific condition: Connections are correct without intertrace copper residue.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：疊合導線輪廓與設計網表。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay conductor contours and design netlists. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：連線正確且無線間銅殘留；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Connections are correct without intertrace copper residue. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部殘銅可形成高阻短路。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Residual copper can create resistive shorts. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"連線正確且無線間銅殘留；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Connections are correct without intertrace copper residue. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-348-k1","title":"芯材表面銅圖形的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect core copper patterns","text":"可檢驗條件為「連線正確且無線間銅殘留」。可藉由「疊合導線輪廓與設計網表」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Connections are correct without intertrace copper residue. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay conductor contours and design netlists. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-348-k2","title":"芯材表面銅圖形的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect core copper patterns","text":"局部殘銅可形成高阻短路。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Residual copper can create resistive shorts. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「芯材表面銅圖形」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect core copper patterns?","options":["連線正確且無線間銅殘留","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部殘銅可形成高阻短路。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Connections are correct without intertrace copper residue","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Residual copper can create resistive shorts.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「連線正確且無線間銅殘留」。局部殘銅可形成高阻短路，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Connections are correct without intertrace copper residue. Residual copper can create resistive shorts, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":348,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-347"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-349","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"增層膜貼合氣泡","titleEn":"Inspect build-up-film lamination bubbles","objective":"判斷「增層膜貼合氣泡」是否滿足此具體條件：台階周圍填實且無未黏合空區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect build-up-film lamination bubbles meets this specific condition: Steps are filled without unbonded cavities.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：沿導線台階觀察膜下氣泡。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect trapped bubbles near conductor steps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：台階周圍填實且無未黏合空區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Steps are filled without unbonded cavities. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"導線旁困氣可轉變成層間空洞。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Trapped air near traces becomes interlayer voids. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"台階周圍填實且無未黏合空區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Steps are filled without unbonded cavities. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-349-k1","title":"增層膜貼合氣泡的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect build-up-film lamination bubbles","text":"可檢驗條件為「台階周圍填實且無未黏合空區」。可藉由「沿導線台階觀察膜下氣泡」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Steps are filled without unbonded cavities. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect trapped bubbles near conductor steps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-349-k2","title":"增層膜貼合氣泡的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect build-up-film lamination bubbles","text":"導線旁困氣可轉變成層間空洞。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Trapped air near traces becomes interlayer voids. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「增層膜貼合氣泡」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect build-up-film lamination bubbles?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","台階周圍填實且無未黏合空區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：導線旁困氣可轉變成層間空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Steps are filled without unbonded cavities","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Trapped air near traces becomes interlayer voids."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「台階周圍填實且無未黏合空區」。導線旁困氣可轉變成層間空洞，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Steps are filled without unbonded cavities. Trapped air near traces becomes interlayer voids, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":349,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-348"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-350","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"增層介電厚度","titleEn":"Measure build-up dielectric thickness","objective":"判斷「增層介電厚度」是否滿足此具體條件：最薄區仍符合絕緣與阻抗要求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure build-up dielectric thickness meets this specific condition: Thinnest regions meet insulation and impedance needs.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較銅線頂部與線間介電厚度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare dielectric above traces and between traces. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：最薄區仍符合絕緣與阻抗要求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Thinnest regions meet insulation and impedance needs. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"名義膜厚不代表銅頂剩餘厚度。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Nominal film thickness is not the remaining thickness above copper. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最薄區仍符合絕緣與阻抗要求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Thinnest regions meet insulation and impedance needs. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-350-k1","title":"增層介電厚度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure build-up dielectric thickness","text":"可檢驗條件為「最薄區仍符合絕緣與阻抗要求」。可藉由「比較銅線頂部與線間介電厚度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Thinnest regions meet insulation and impedance needs. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare dielectric above traces and between traces. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-350-k2","title":"增層介電厚度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure build-up dielectric thickness","text":"名義膜厚不代表銅頂剩餘厚度。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Nominal film thickness is not the remaining thickness above copper. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-350-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"平行板近似 C=ε0εrA/t；假設 εr=4、A=1 mm²、t=20 µm，C≈1.77 pF；厚度減半則約 3.54 pF，邊緣效應尚未計入。","textEn":"Under C=ε0εrA/t, hypothetical εr=4, A=1 mm² and t=20 µm give about 1.77 pF; halving thickness gives 3.54 pF before fringing."},{"id":"pk-350-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"介電厚度同時影响阻抗、擊穿餘裕和雷射通孔可製造性。對圖面名目值應附局部厚度分布與吸濕條件，而非只檢平均。","textEn":"Dielectric thickness affects impedance, breakdown margin and laser-via manufacturability. Nominal drawings need local thickness distributions and moisture conditions, not averages alone."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「增層介電厚度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure build-up dielectric thickness?","options":["忽略此失效線索：名義膜厚不代表銅頂剩餘厚度。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最薄區仍符合絕緣與阻抗要求","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Nominal film thickness is not the remaining thickness above copper.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Thinnest regions meet insulation and impedance needs","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「最薄區仍符合絕緣與阻抗要求」。名義膜厚不代表銅頂剩餘厚度，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Thinnest regions meet insulation and impedance needs. Nominal film thickness is not the remaining thickness above copper, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":350,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-349"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-351","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"介電固化收縮","titleEn":"Evaluate dielectric cure shrinkage","objective":"判斷「介電固化收縮」是否滿足此具體條件：尺寸變化可被既定套準策略補償。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate dielectric cure shrinkage meets this specific condition: Dimensional change fits the registration strategy.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較壓合前後標記座標距離。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare fiducial distances before and after lamination. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：尺寸變化可被既定套準策略補償；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Dimensional change fits the registration strategy. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"各方向收縮不同不能以單一比例修正。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Anisotropic shrinkage resists one-factor scale correction. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"尺寸變化可被既定套準策略補償；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Dimensional change fits the registration strategy. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-351-k1","title":"介電固化收縮的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate dielectric cure shrinkage","text":"可檢驗條件為「尺寸變化可被既定套準策略補償」。可藉由「比較壓合前後標記座標距離」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Dimensional change fits the registration strategy. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare fiducial distances before and after lamination. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-351-k2","title":"介電固化收縮的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate dielectric cure shrinkage","text":"各方向收縮不同不能以單一比例修正。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Anisotropic shrinkage resists one-factor scale correction. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介電固化收縮」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate dielectric cure shrinkage?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：各方向收縮不同不能以單一比例修正。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","尺寸變化可被既定套準策略補償"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Anisotropic shrinkage resists one-factor scale correction.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Dimensional change fits the registration strategy"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「尺寸變化可被既定套準策略補償」。各方向收縮不同不能以單一比例修正，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Dimensional change fits the registration strategy. Anisotropic shrinkage resists one-factor scale correction, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":351,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-350"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-352","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"微孔雷射位置","titleEn":"Check laser microvia registration","objective":"判斷「微孔雷射位置」是否滿足此具體條件：孔中心保留足夠落墊邊界。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check laser microvia registration meets this specific condition: Centers retain sufficient capture-pad margin.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：疊合微孔中心與埋藏銅墊。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay microvia centers and buried capture pads. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔中心保留足夠落墊邊界；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Centers retain sufficient capture-pad margin. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"偏孔可在接點邊緣造成弱連接。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Offset vias create weak edge connections. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔中心保留足夠落墊邊界；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Centers retain sufficient capture-pad margin. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-352-k1","title":"微孔雷射位置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check laser microvia registration","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔中心保留足夠落墊邊界」。可藉由「疊合微孔中心與埋藏銅墊」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Centers retain sufficient capture-pad margin. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay microvia centers and buried capture pads. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-352-k2","title":"微孔雷射位置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check laser microvia registration","text":"偏孔可在接點邊緣造成弱連接。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Offset vias create weak edge connections. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「微孔雷射位置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check laser microvia registration?","options":["孔中心保留足夠落墊邊界","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：偏孔可在接點邊緣造成弱連接。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Centers retain sufficient capture-pad margin","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Offset vias create weak edge connections.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「孔中心保留足夠落墊邊界」。偏孔可在接點邊緣造成弱連接，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Centers retain sufficient capture-pad margin. Offset vias create weak edge connections, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":352,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-351"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-353","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"微孔底殘留","titleEn":"Inspect microvia-bottom residue","objective":"判斷「微孔底殘留」是否滿足此具體條件：目標銅墊有完整可金屬化表面。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect microvia-bottom residue meets this specific condition: Capture pads expose metallizable surfaces.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較孔底反射影像與剖面。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bottom reflectance images and cross sections. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：目標銅墊有完整可金屬化表面；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Capture pads expose metallizable surfaces. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"孔底殘膠可能造成間歇開路。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Bottom residue can produce intermittent opens. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"目標銅墊有完整可金屬化表面；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Capture pads expose metallizable surfaces. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-353-k1","title":"微孔底殘留的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect microvia-bottom residue","text":"可檢驗條件為「目標銅墊有完整可金屬化表面」。可藉由「比較孔底反射影像與剖面」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Capture pads expose metallizable surfaces. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bottom reflectance images and cross sections. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-353-k2","title":"微孔底殘留的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect microvia-bottom residue","text":"孔底殘膠可能造成間歇開路。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Bottom residue can produce intermittent opens. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「微孔底殘留」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect microvia-bottom residue?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","目標銅墊有完整可金屬化表面","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：孔底殘膠可能造成間歇開路。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Capture pads expose metallizable surfaces","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Bottom residue can produce intermittent opens."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「目標銅墊有完整可金屬化表面」。孔底殘膠可能造成間歇開路，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Capture pads expose metallizable surfaces. Bottom residue can produce intermittent opens, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":353,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-352"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-354","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"增層介電表面粗糙度","titleEn":"Assess build-up dielectric surface roughness","objective":"判斷「增層介電表面粗糙度」是否滿足此具體條件：粗糙度同時滿足附著及損耗目標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess build-up dielectric surface roughness meets this specific condition: Roughness meets adhesion and loss targets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較附著力與高頻損耗的對照資料。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare adhesion and high-frequency loss data. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：粗糙度同時滿足附著及損耗目標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Roughness meets adhesion and loss targets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單純提高粗糙度可能增加傳輸損耗。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Increasing roughness can increase transmission loss. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"粗糙度同時滿足附著及損耗目標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Roughness meets adhesion and loss targets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-354-k1","title":"增層介電表面粗糙度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess build-up dielectric surface roughness","text":"可檢驗條件為「粗糙度同時滿足附著及損耗目標」。可藉由「比較附著力與高頻損耗的對照資料」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Roughness meets adhesion and loss targets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare adhesion and high-frequency loss data. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-354-k2","title":"增層介電表面粗糙度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess build-up dielectric surface roughness","text":"單純提高粗糙度可能增加傳輸損耗。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Increasing roughness can increase transmission loss. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「增層介電表面粗糙度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess build-up dielectric surface roughness?","options":["忽略此失效線索：單純提高粗糙度可能增加傳輸損耗。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","粗糙度同時滿足附著及損耗目標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Increasing roughness can increase transmission loss.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Roughness meets adhesion and loss targets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「粗糙度同時滿足附著及損耗目標」。單純提高粗糙度可能增加傳輸損耗，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Roughness meets adhesion and loss targets. Increasing roughness can increase transmission loss, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":354,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-353"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-355","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"乾膜光阻貼合","titleEn":"Inspect dry-film resist lamination","objective":"判斷「乾膜光阻貼合」是否滿足此具體條件：光阻貼合完整且開孔區可圖形化。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect dry-film resist lamination meets this specific condition: Resist adheres and openings remain patternable.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查微孔附近光阻架橋與空氣夾入。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect resist tenting and trapped air near microvias. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：光阻貼合完整且開孔區可圖形化；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Resist adheres and openings remain patternable. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"光阻懸空可導致顯影形狀失真。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unsupported resist can distort developed shapes. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"光阻貼合完整且開孔區可圖形化；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Resist adheres and openings remain patternable. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-355-k1","title":"乾膜光阻貼合的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect dry-film resist lamination","text":"可檢驗條件為「光阻貼合完整且開孔區可圖形化」。可藉由「檢查微孔附近光阻架橋與空氣夾入」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Resist adheres and openings remain patternable. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect resist tenting and trapped air near microvias. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-355-k2","title":"乾膜光阻貼合的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect dry-film resist lamination","text":"光阻懸空可導致顯影形狀失真。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unsupported resist can distort developed shapes. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「乾膜光阻貼合」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect dry-film resist lamination?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：光阻懸空可導致顯影形狀失真。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","光阻貼合完整且開孔區可圖形化"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Unsupported resist can distort developed shapes.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Resist adheres and openings remain patternable"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「光阻貼合完整且開孔區可圖形化」。光阻懸空可導致顯影形狀失真，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Resist adheres and openings remain patternable. Unsupported resist can distort developed shapes, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":355,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-354"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-356","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"雷射直寫套準","titleEn":"Verify laser direct-imaging registration","objective":"判斷「雷射直寫套準」是否滿足此具體條件：局部殘差低於圖形套準容許量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify laser direct-imaging registration meets this specific condition: Local residuals meet pattern-registration allowance.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以分區標記修正面板尺寸變化。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Use regional fiducials to correct panel distortion. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：局部殘差低於圖形套準容許量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Local residuals meet pattern-registration allowance. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"全板剛體修正可能不足以補償變形。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Rigid correction can miss panel distortion. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"局部殘差低於圖形套準容許量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Local residuals meet pattern-registration allowance. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-356-k1","title":"雷射直寫套準的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify laser direct-imaging registration","text":"可檢驗條件為「局部殘差低於圖形套準容許量」。可藉由「以分區標記修正面板尺寸變化」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Local residuals meet pattern-registration allowance. Evidence can be developed through this action: Use regional fiducials to correct panel distortion. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-356-k2","title":"雷射直寫套準的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify laser direct-imaging registration","text":"全板剛體修正可能不足以補償變形。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Rigid correction can miss panel distortion. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「雷射直寫套準」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify laser direct-imaging registration?","options":["局部殘差低於圖形套準容許量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：全板剛體修正可能不足以補償變形。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Local residuals meet pattern-registration allowance","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Rigid correction can miss panel distortion.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「局部殘差低於圖形套準容許量」。全板剛體修正可能不足以補償變形，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Local residuals meet pattern-registration allowance. Rigid correction can miss panel distortion, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":356,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-355"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-357","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"細線光阻側壁","titleEn":"Inspect fine-line resist walls","objective":"判斷「細線光阻側壁」是否滿足此具體條件：光阻壁可分隔目標導線。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect fine-line resist walls meets this specific condition: Resist walls separate the intended conductors.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測底部開口及相鄰牆體完整性。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure bottom openings and neighboring wall integrity. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：光阻壁可分隔目標導線；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Resist walls separate the intended conductors. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過薄光阻牆容易在電鍍時失穩。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Thin resist walls can destabilize during plating. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"光阻壁可分隔目標導線；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Resist walls separate the intended conductors. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-357-k1","title":"細線光阻側壁的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect fine-line resist walls","text":"可檢驗條件為「光阻壁可分隔目標導線」。可藉由「量測底部開口及相鄰牆體完整性」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Resist walls separate the intended conductors. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure bottom openings and neighboring wall integrity. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-357-k2","title":"細線光阻側壁的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect fine-line resist walls","text":"過薄光阻牆容易在電鍍時失穩。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Thin resist walls can destabilize during plating. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「細線光阻側壁」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect fine-line resist walls?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","光阻壁可分隔目標導線","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過薄光阻牆容易在電鍍時失穩。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Resist walls separate the intended conductors","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Thin resist walls can destabilize during plating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「光阻壁可分隔目標導線」。過薄光阻牆容易在電鍍時失穩，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Resist walls separate the intended conductors. Thin resist walls can destabilize during plating, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":357,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-356"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-358","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"盲微孔填銅","titleEn":"Assess blind-microvia copper filling","objective":"判斷「盲微孔填銅」是否滿足此具體條件：孔內填實且表面凹陷受控。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess blind-microvia copper filling meets this specific condition: Vias fill while surface dimples remain controlled.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較孔底填充與上方鍍層成長。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bottom fill with top copper growth. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔內填實且表面凹陷受控；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Vias fill while surface dimples remain controlled. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"頂部先封閉會留下隱藏接縫。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Early top closure leaves hidden seams. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔內填實且表面凹陷受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Vias fill while surface dimples remain controlled. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-358-k1","title":"盲微孔填銅的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess blind-microvia copper filling","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔內填實且表面凹陷受控」。可藉由「比較孔底填充與上方鍍層成長」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Vias fill while surface dimples remain controlled. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bottom fill with top copper growth. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-358-k2","title":"盲微孔填銅的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess blind-microvia copper filling","text":"頂部先封閉會留下隱藏接縫。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Early top closure leaves hidden seams. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「盲微孔填銅」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess blind-microvia copper filling?","options":["忽略此失效線索：頂部先封閉會留下隱藏接縫。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","孔內填實且表面凹陷受控","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Early top closure leaves hidden seams.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Vias fill while surface dimples remain controlled","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「孔內填實且表面凹陷受控」。頂部先封閉會留下隱藏接縫，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Vias fill while surface dimples remain controlled. Early top closure leaves hidden seams, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":358,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-357"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-359","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"圖形電鍍線高","titleEn":"Map pattern-plated trace height","objective":"判斷「圖形電鍍線高」是否滿足此具體條件：不同密度線高都在規格範圍。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map pattern-plated trace height meets this specific condition: Trace heights pass across pattern densities.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較密集與孤立導線的高度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare dense and isolated trace heights. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：不同密度線高都在規格範圍；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Trace heights pass across pattern densities. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"電流集中可使孤立線過高。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Current crowding can overplate isolated lines. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"不同密度線高都在規格範圍；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Trace heights pass across pattern densities. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-359-k1","title":"圖形電鍍線高的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map pattern-plated trace height","text":"可檢驗條件為「不同密度線高都在規格範圍」。可藉由「比較密集與孤立導線的高度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Trace heights pass across pattern densities. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare dense and isolated trace heights. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-359-k2","title":"圖形電鍍線高的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map pattern-plated trace height","text":"電流集中可使孤立線過高。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Current crowding can overplate isolated lines. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「圖形電鍍線高」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map pattern-plated trace height?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：電流集中可使孤立線過高。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","不同密度線高都在規格範圍"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Current crowding can overplate isolated lines.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Trace heights pass across pattern densities"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「不同密度線高都在規格範圍」。電流集中可使孤立線過高，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Trace heights pass across pattern densities. Current crowding can overplate isolated lines, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":359,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-358"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-360","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"種子蝕刻側蝕","titleEn":"Measure seed-etch undercut","objective":"判斷「種子蝕刻側蝕」是否滿足此具體條件：底寬保留符合導通與附著需求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure seed-etch undercut meets this specific condition: Retained foot width supports conduction and adhesion.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較去種子前後導線底寬。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare trace-foot widths before and after seed removal. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：底寬保留符合導通與附著需求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Retained foot width supports conduction and adhesion. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過大側蝕會削弱細線支撐。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Excess undercut weakens fine-trace support. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"底寬保留符合導通與附著需求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Retained foot width supports conduction and adhesion. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-360-k1","title":"種子蝕刻側蝕的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure seed-etch undercut","text":"可檢驗條件為「底寬保留符合導通與附著需求」。可藉由「比較去種子前後導線底寬」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Retained foot width supports conduction and adhesion. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare trace-foot widths before and after seed removal. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-360-k2","title":"種子蝕刻側蝕的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure seed-etch undercut","text":"過大側蝕會削弱細線支撐。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Excess undercut weakens fine-trace support. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「種子蝕刻側蝕」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure seed-etch undercut?","options":["底寬保留符合導通與附著需求","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過大側蝕會削弱細線支撐。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Retained foot width supports conduction and adhesion","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Excess undercut weakens fine-trace support.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「底寬保留符合導通與附著需求」。過大側蝕會削弱細線支撐，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Retained foot width supports conduction and adhesion. Excess undercut weakens fine-trace support, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":360,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-359"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-361","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"增層微孔堆疊支線","titleEn":"Inspect stacked-microvia interfaces","objective":"判斷「增層微孔堆疊支線」是否滿足此具體條件：上下微孔介面接觸連續。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect stacked-microvia interfaces meets this specific condition: Stacked-via interfaces maintain continuous contact.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在堆疊孔截面追蹤界面接觸。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Trace interface contact in stacked-via cross sections. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：上下微孔介面接觸連續；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Stacked-via interfaces maintain continuous contact. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"介面凹陷可成為疲勞弱點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Interface dimples can become fatigue weak points. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"上下微孔介面接觸連續；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Stacked-via interfaces maintain continuous contact. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-361-k1","title":"增層微孔堆疊支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect stacked-microvia interfaces","text":"可檢驗條件為「上下微孔介面接觸連續」。可藉由「在堆疊孔截面追蹤界面接觸」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Stacked-via interfaces maintain continuous contact. Evidence can be developed through this action: Trace interface contact in stacked-via cross sections. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-361-k2","title":"增層微孔堆疊支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect stacked-microvia interfaces","text":"介面凹陷可成為疲勞弱點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Interface dimples can become fatigue weak points. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-361-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"三層堆疊微孔的偏移可以累積。假設每層確定向同側偏 3 µm，總偏 9 µm；只有獨立隨機偏差才可另作 RSS 模型。","textEn":"Offsets in three stacked microvias may accumulate. Three hypothetical deterministic 3 µm same-direction offsets total 9 µm; RSS requires a separate independent-random model."},{"id":"pk-361-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"檢查上下接墊捕捉區、介面裂紋與熱循環累積應變。錯列孔與堆疊孔有不同佈線和力學代價，不以單一面積指標決策。","textEn":"Inspect capture pads, interface cracks and cyclic strain. Staggered and stacked vias have different routing and mechanical tradeoffs; area alone is insufficient."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「增層微孔堆疊支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect stacked-microvia interfaces?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","上下微孔介面接觸連續","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：介面凹陷可成為疲勞弱點。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Stacked-via interfaces maintain continuous contact","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Interface dimples can become fatigue weak points."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「上下微孔介面接觸連續」。介面凹陷可成為疲勞弱點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Stacked-via interfaces maintain continuous contact. Interface dimples can become fatigue weak points, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":361,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-360"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-362","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"防焊層開口","titleEn":"Inspect solder-mask openings","objective":"判斷「防焊層開口」是否滿足此具體條件：開口保留所選焊墊定義方式。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect solder-mask openings meets this specific condition: Openings preserve the chosen pad-definition scheme.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對防焊邊界與焊墊設計。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare mask boundaries and pad designs. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：開口保留所選焊墊定義方式；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Openings preserve the chosen pad-definition scheme. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"開口偏移可改變有效潤濕面積。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Misregistration changes effective wettable area. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"開口保留所選焊墊定義方式；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Openings preserve the chosen pad-definition scheme. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-362-k1","title":"防焊層開口的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect solder-mask openings","text":"可檢驗條件為「開口保留所選焊墊定義方式」。可藉由「比對防焊邊界與焊墊設計」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Openings preserve the chosen pad-definition scheme. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare mask boundaries and pad designs. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-362-k2","title":"防焊層開口的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect solder-mask openings","text":"開口偏移可改變有效潤濕面積。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Misregistration changes effective wettable area. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「防焊層開口」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect solder-mask openings?","options":["忽略此失效線索：開口偏移可改變有效潤濕面積。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","開口保留所選焊墊定義方式","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Misregistration changes effective wettable area.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Openings preserve the chosen pad-definition scheme","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「開口保留所選焊墊定義方式」。開口偏移可改變有效潤濕面積，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Openings preserve the chosen pad-definition scheme. Misregistration changes effective wettable area, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":362,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-361"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-363","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"表面處理可焊性","titleEn":"Assess final-finish solderability","objective":"判斷「表面處理可焊性」是否滿足此具體條件：表面處理與接合合金相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess final-finish solderability meets this specific condition: Finish is compatible with the joining alloy.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較表面成分與潤濕試片。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare finish composition and wetting coupons. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：表面處理與接合合金相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Finish is compatible with the joining alloy. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部污染可造成不潤濕。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Local contamination can cause nonwetting. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"表面處理與接合合金相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Finish is compatible with the joining alloy. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-363-k1","title":"表面處理可焊性的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess final-finish solderability","text":"可檢驗條件為「表面處理與接合合金相容」。可藉由「比較表面成分與潤濕試片」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Finish is compatible with the joining alloy. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare finish composition and wetting coupons. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-363-k2","title":"表面處理可焊性的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess final-finish solderability","text":"局部污染可造成不潤濕。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Local contamination can cause nonwetting. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「表面處理可焊性」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess final-finish solderability?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部污染可造成不潤濕。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","表面處理與接合合金相容"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Local contamination can cause nonwetting.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Finish is compatible with the joining alloy"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「表面處理與接合合金相容」。局部污染可造成不潤濕，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Finish is compatible with the joining alloy. Local contamination can cause nonwetting, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":363,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-362"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-364","stageId":"pk-m14","title":"載板電測與尺寸放行","titleEn":"Release substrate electrical and dimensional data","objective":"判斷「載板電測與尺寸放行」是否滿足此具體條件：電性與尺寸兩項均符合組裝介面。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Release substrate electrical and dimensional data meets this specific condition: Electrical and dimensional results meet assembly interfaces.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：聯合判讀開短路結果與焊墊位置圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Review continuity tests and pad-coordinate maps together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：電性與尺寸兩項均符合組裝介面；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Electrical and dimensional results meet assembly interfaces. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"僅電測合格不保證可正確貼裝。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Electrical passing alone does not establish mountability. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"電性與尺寸兩項均符合組裝介面；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Electrical and dimensional results meet assembly interfaces. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-364-k1","title":"載板電測與尺寸放行的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Release substrate electrical and dimensional data","text":"可檢驗條件為「電性與尺寸兩項均符合組裝介面」。可藉由「聯合判讀開短路結果與焊墊位置圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Electrical and dimensional results meet assembly interfaces. Evidence can be developed through this action: Review continuity tests and pad-coordinate maps together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-364-k2","title":"載板電測與尺寸放行的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Release substrate electrical and dimensional data","text":"僅電測合格不保證可正確貼裝。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Electrical passing alone does not establish mountability. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「載板電測與尺寸放行」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Release substrate electrical and dimensional data?","options":["電性與尺寸兩項均符合組裝介面","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：僅電測合格不保證可正確貼裝。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Electrical and dimensional results meet assembly interfaces","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Electrical passing alone does not establish mountability.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「電性與尺寸兩項均符合組裝介面」。僅電測合格不保證可正確貼裝，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Electrical and dimensional results meet assembly interfaces. Electrical passing alone does not establish mountability, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-dupont-substrate","pkb-atotech-glass","pkb-atotech-sap"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":364,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-363"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"有機芯或玻璃芯支線；玻璃通孔與有機鑽孔各用其合格路線，不可互換製程參數。","routeEn":"Organic-core or glass-core branch; glass vias and organic drilling use separately qualified routes.","photoId":"bga-inside","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察 BGA 封裝內的晶粒及周邊互連；不將這張傳統封裝內部照片當作扇出、RDL、HBM 或 CPO 實拍。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a die and surrounding interconnects in a BGA package; this conventional package interior is not a fan-out, RDL, HBM or CPO process photograph.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m15","title":"混合鍵合與直接接合對準","titleEn":"Hybrid bonding and direct-bond alignment","description":"混合鍵合同時依靠介電與金屬介面；顆粒、局部平坦度、銅高度差與對位都必須受控。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Hybrid bonding combines dielectric and metal interfaces; particles, local flatness, copper height, and alignment must all be controlled. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","order":15,"sequence":15,"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-365","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"鍵合路線幾何匹配","titleEn":"Match geometry to a bonding route","objective":"判斷「鍵合路線幾何匹配」是否滿足此具體條件：所選路線能容納尺寸與良品分布。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Match geometry to a bonding route meets this specific condition: The selected route accommodates geometry and good-die distribution.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較晶粒尺寸與晶圓良率分布案例。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare die-size and wafer-yield cases. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：所選路線能容納尺寸與良品分布；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: The selected route accommodates geometry and good-die distribution. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"相同流程不適合所有異尺寸晶粒。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"One flow does not suit all unequal die sizes. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"所選路線能容納尺寸與良品分布；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"The selected route accommodates geometry and good-die distribution. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-365-k1","title":"鍵合路線幾何匹配的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Match geometry to a bonding route","text":"可檢驗條件為「所選路線能容納尺寸與良品分布」。可藉由「比較晶粒尺寸與晶圓良率分布案例」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: The selected route accommodates geometry and good-die distribution. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare die-size and wafer-yield cases. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-365-k2","title":"鍵合路線幾何匹配的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Match geometry to a bonding route","text":"相同流程不適合所有異尺寸晶粒。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"One flow does not suit all unequal die sizes. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「鍵合路線幾何匹配」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Match geometry to a bonding route?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","所選路線能容納尺寸與良品分布","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：相同流程不適合所有異尺寸晶粒。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","The selected route accommodates geometry and good-die distribution","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: One flow does not suit all unequal die sizes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「所選路線能容納尺寸與良品分布」。相同流程不適合所有異尺寸晶粒，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: The selected route accommodates geometry and good-die distribution. One flow does not suit all unequal die sizes, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":365,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-366","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"混合鍵合層序核對","titleEn":"Check hybrid-bond layer sequence","objective":"判斷「混合鍵合層序核對」是否滿足此具體條件：材料配對與層序符合核准介面。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check hybrid-bond layer sequence meets this specific condition: Materials and layers match the approved interface.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對兩側銅墊與介電層剖面。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare copper-pad and dielectric cross sections on both sides. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：材料配對與層序符合核准介面；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Materials and layers match the approved interface. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"金屬相接不能補救介電不相容。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Metal contact cannot remedy incompatible dielectric bonding. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"材料配對與層序符合核准介面；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Materials and layers match the approved interface. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-366-k1","title":"混合鍵合層序核對的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check hybrid-bond layer sequence","text":"可檢驗條件為「材料配對與層序符合核准介面」。可藉由「比對兩側銅墊與介電層剖面」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Materials and layers match the approved interface. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare copper-pad and dielectric cross sections on both sides. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-366-k2","title":"混合鍵合層序核對的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check hybrid-bond layer sequence","text":"金屬相接不能補救介電不相容。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Metal contact cannot remedy incompatible dielectric bonding. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「混合鍵合層序核對」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check hybrid-bond layer sequence?","options":["忽略此失效線索：金屬相接不能補救介電不相容。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","材料配對與層序符合核准介面","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Metal contact cannot remedy incompatible dielectric bonding.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Materials and layers match the approved interface","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「材料配對與層序符合核准介面」。金屬相接不能補救介電不相容，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Materials and layers match the approved interface. Metal contact cannot remedy incompatible dielectric bonding, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":366,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-365"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-367","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"CMP 局部平坦度","titleEn":"Measure local CMP flatness","objective":"判斷「CMP 局部平坦度」是否滿足此具體條件：局部起伏符合接合表面規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure local CMP flatness meets this specific condition: Local topography meets bonding-surface criteria.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在銅墊群與介電區量測形貌。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure topography across pad groups and dielectric regions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：局部起伏符合接合表面規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Local topography meets bonding-surface criteria. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"整片平坦仍可能有局部凹凸。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Global flatness can hide local topography. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"局部起伏符合接合表面規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Local topography meets bonding-surface criteria. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-367-k1","title":"CMP 局部平坦度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure local CMP flatness","text":"可檢驗條件為「局部起伏符合接合表面規範」。可藉由「在銅墊群與介電區量測形貌」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Local topography meets bonding-surface criteria. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure topography across pad groups and dielectric regions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-367-k2","title":"CMP 局部平坦度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure local CMP flatness","text":"整片平坦仍可能有局部凹凸。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Global flatness can hide local topography. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CMP 局部平坦度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure local CMP flatness?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：整片平坦仍可能有局部凹凸。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","局部起伏符合接合表面規範"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Global flatness can hide local topography.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Local topography meets bonding-surface criteria"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「局部起伏符合接合表面規範」。整片平坦仍可能有局部凹凸，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Local topography meets bonding-surface criteria. Global flatness can hide local topography, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":367,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-366"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-368","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"銅墊凹入深度","titleEn":"Measure copper-pad recess","objective":"判斷「銅墊凹入深度」是否滿足此具體條件：高度差符合所選熱歷程設計。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure copper-pad recess meets this specific condition: Height difference fits the selected thermal-history design.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較銅與相鄰介電表面高度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare copper and neighboring dielectric heights. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：高度差符合所選熱歷程設計；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Height difference fits the selected thermal-history design. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"凹入太深可能無法形成金屬接觸。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Excess recess can prevent metal contact. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"高度差符合所選熱歷程設計；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Height difference fits the selected thermal-history design. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-368-k1","title":"銅墊凹入深度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure copper-pad recess","text":"可檢驗條件為「高度差符合所選熱歷程設計」。可藉由「比較銅與相鄰介電表面高度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Height difference fits the selected thermal-history design. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare copper and neighboring dielectric heights. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-368-k2","title":"銅墊凹入深度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure copper-pad recess","text":"凹入太深可能無法形成金屬接觸。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Excess recess can prevent metal contact. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-368-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設接墊中心凹陷 3 nm、邊緣 1 nm，單一中心值會漏掉形狀。凹陷應連同介電侵蝕與粗糙度報告，且不同尺度需獨立量測。","textEn":"A hypothetical pad with 3 nm center and 1 nm edge recess cannot be described by center depth alone. Report dielectric erosion and roughness separately with scale-appropriate measurements."},{"id":"pk-368-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"不能以增加熱量任意補救所有凹陷：過度熱負載可能影響已完成元件。先確定形貌、Cu 微結構和允許熱預算，再做合格試片研究。","textEn":"Extra heating is not a universal recess remedy; excessive thermal load can affect finished devices. Establish topography, copper microstructure and thermal budget before qualified coupon studies."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「銅墊凹入深度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure copper-pad recess?","options":["高度差符合所選熱歷程設計","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：凹入太深可能無法形成金屬接觸。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Height difference fits the selected thermal-history design","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Excess recess can prevent metal contact.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「高度差符合所選熱歷程設計」。凹入太深可能無法形成金屬接觸，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Height difference fits the selected thermal-history design. Excess recess can prevent metal contact, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":368,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-367"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-369","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"鍵合介電表面粗糙度","titleEn":"Measure bonding-dielectric roughness","objective":"判斷「鍵合介電表面粗糙度」是否滿足此具體條件：粗糙度與局部缺陷均受控。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure bonding-dielectric roughness meets this specific condition: Roughness and local defects are controlled.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較不同掃描範圍的表面統計。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare surface statistics at multiple scan scales. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：粗糙度與局部缺陷均受控；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Roughness and local defects are controlled. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只看單一均方根值會漏掉顆粒。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A single RMS value can miss particles. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"粗糙度與局部缺陷均受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Roughness and local defects are controlled. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-369-k1","title":"鍵合介電表面粗糙度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure bonding-dielectric roughness","text":"可檢驗條件為「粗糙度與局部缺陷均受控」。可藉由「比較不同掃描範圍的表面統計」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Roughness and local defects are controlled. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare surface statistics at multiple scan scales. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-369-k2","title":"鍵合介電表面粗糙度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure bonding-dielectric roughness","text":"只看單一均方根值會漏掉顆粒。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A single RMS value can miss particles. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「鍵合介電表面粗糙度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure bonding-dielectric roughness?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","粗糙度與局部缺陷均受控","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只看單一均方根值會漏掉顆粒。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Roughness and local defects are controlled","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: A single RMS value can miss particles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「粗糙度與局部缺陷均受控」。只看單一均方根值會漏掉顆粒，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Roughness and local defects are controlled. A single RMS value can miss particles, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":369,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-368"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-370","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"銅墊腐蝕檢查","titleEn":"Inspect copper-pad corrosion","objective":"判斷「銅墊腐蝕檢查」是否滿足此具體條件：銅墊無超出規則的腐蝕區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect copper-pad corrosion meets this specific condition: Pads lack corrosion beyond acceptance rules.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：對照表面影像與元素訊號。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare surface images and elemental signals. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：銅墊無超出規則的腐蝕區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Pads lack corrosion beyond acceptance rules. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"腐蝕可使墊面凹入且增加接觸阻抗。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Corrosion recesses pads and raises contact impedance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"銅墊無超出規則的腐蝕區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Pads lack corrosion beyond acceptance rules. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-370-k1","title":"銅墊腐蝕檢查的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect copper-pad corrosion","text":"可檢驗條件為「銅墊無超出規則的腐蝕區」。可藉由「對照表面影像與元素訊號」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Pads lack corrosion beyond acceptance rules. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare surface images and elemental signals. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-370-k2","title":"銅墊腐蝕檢查的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect copper-pad corrosion","text":"腐蝕可使墊面凹入且增加接觸阻抗。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Corrosion recesses pads and raises contact impedance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「銅墊腐蝕檢查」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect copper-pad corrosion?","options":["忽略此失效線索：腐蝕可使墊面凹入且增加接觸阻抗。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","銅墊無超出規則的腐蝕區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Corrosion recesses pads and raises contact impedance.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Pads lack corrosion beyond acceptance rules","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「銅墊無超出規則的腐蝕區」。腐蝕可使墊面凹入且增加接觸阻抗，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Pads lack corrosion beyond acceptance rules. Corrosion recesses pads and raises contact impedance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":370,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-369"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-371","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"晶粒切割污染路徑","titleEn":"Map singulation contamination paths","objective":"判斷「晶粒切割污染路徑」是否滿足此具體條件：切割污染未進入有效接合區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map singulation contamination paths meets this specific condition: Singulation contamination stays outside active bond areas.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較保護前後接合面的顆粒地圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bonding-surface particle maps across protection cases. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：切割污染未進入有效接合區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Singulation contamination stays outside active bond areas. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"切割邊緣潔淨不代表面內潔淨。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Clean edges do not establish a clean bonding face. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"切割污染未進入有效接合區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Singulation contamination stays outside active bond areas. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-371-k1","title":"晶粒切割污染路徑的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map singulation contamination paths","text":"可檢驗條件為「切割污染未進入有效接合區」。可藉由「比較保護前後接合面的顆粒地圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Singulation contamination stays outside active bond areas. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bonding-surface particle maps across protection cases. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-371-k2","title":"晶粒切割污染路徑的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map singulation contamination paths","text":"切割邊緣潔淨不代表面內潔淨。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Clean edges do not establish a clean bonding face. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒切割污染路徑」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map singulation contamination paths?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：切割邊緣潔淨不代表面內潔淨。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","切割污染未進入有效接合區"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Clean edges do not establish a clean bonding face.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Singulation contamination stays outside active bond areas"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「切割污染未進入有效接合區」。切割邊緣潔淨不代表面內潔淨，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Singulation contamination stays outside active bond areas. Clean edges do not establish a clean bonding face, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":371,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-370"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-372","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"接合面清洗驗證","titleEn":"Verify bonding-surface cleaning","objective":"判斷「接合面清洗驗證」是否滿足此具體條件：兩種污染指標均符合接合規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify bonding-surface cleaning meets this specific condition: Both contamination indicators meet bonding criteria.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對顆粒數與有機殘留訊號。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare particle counts and organic-residue signals. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：兩種污染指標均符合接合規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Both contamination indicators meet bonding criteria. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"去除顆粒後仍可能殘留有機物。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Particle removal can leave organic residues. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"兩種污染指標均符合接合規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Both contamination indicators meet bonding criteria. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-372-k1","title":"接合面清洗驗證的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify bonding-surface cleaning","text":"可檢驗條件為「兩種污染指標均符合接合規範」。可藉由「比對顆粒數與有機殘留訊號」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Both contamination indicators meet bonding criteria. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare particle counts and organic-residue signals. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-372-k2","title":"接合面清洗驗證的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify bonding-surface cleaning","text":"去除顆粒後仍可能殘留有機物。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Particle removal can leave organic residues. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「接合面清洗驗證」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify bonding-surface cleaning?","options":["兩種污染指標均符合接合規範","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：去除顆粒後仍可能殘留有機物。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Both contamination indicators meet bonding criteria","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Particle removal can leave organic residues.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「兩種污染指標均符合接合規範」。去除顆粒後仍可能殘留有機物，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Both contamination indicators meet bonding criteria. Particle removal can leave organic residues, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":372,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-371"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-373","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"表面活化狀態","titleEn":"Assess surface activation state","objective":"判斷「表面活化狀態」是否滿足此具體條件：表面狀態落在核准活化窗口。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess surface activation state meets this specific condition: Surface state lies in the approved activation window.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較接觸角與參考接合強度資料。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare contact angle and reference bond-strength data. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：表面狀態落在核准活化窗口；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Surface state lies in the approved activation window. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"低接觸角單獨不能證明接合強度。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Low contact angle alone does not prove bond strength. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"表面狀態落在核准活化窗口；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Surface state lies in the approved activation window. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-373-k1","title":"表面活化狀態的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess surface activation state","text":"可檢驗條件為「表面狀態落在核准活化窗口」。可藉由「比較接觸角與參考接合強度資料」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Surface state lies in the approved activation window. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare contact angle and reference bond-strength data. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-373-k2","title":"表面活化狀態的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess surface activation state","text":"低接觸角單獨不能證明接合強度。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Low contact angle alone does not prove bond strength. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「表面活化狀態」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess surface activation state?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","表面狀態落在核准活化窗口","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：低接觸角單獨不能證明接合強度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Surface state lies in the approved activation window","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Low contact angle alone does not prove bond strength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「表面狀態落在核准活化窗口」。低接觸角單獨不能證明接合強度，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Surface state lies in the approved activation window. Low contact angle alone does not prove bond strength, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":373,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-372"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-374","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"活化後等待時間","titleEn":"Evaluate postactivation queue time","objective":"判斷「活化後等待時間」是否滿足此具體條件：等候未超出已驗證可接合時窗。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate postactivation queue time meets this specific condition: Queue time stays within the validated bonding window.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將等待時間與顆粒及表面狀態對照。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Correlate queue time with particles and surface state. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：等候未超出已驗證可接合時窗；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Queue time stays within the validated bonding window. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"等待造成再污染或表面狀態改變。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Waiting permits contamination or surface-state change. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"等候未超出已驗證可接合時窗；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Queue time stays within the validated bonding window. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-374-k1","title":"活化後等待時間的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate postactivation queue time","text":"可檢驗條件為「等候未超出已驗證可接合時窗」。可藉由「將等待時間與顆粒及表面狀態對照」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Queue time stays within the validated bonding window. Evidence can be developed through this action: Correlate queue time with particles and surface state. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-374-k2","title":"活化後等待時間的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate postactivation queue time","text":"等待造成再污染或表面狀態改變。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Waiting permits contamination or surface-state change. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「活化後等待時間」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate postactivation queue time?","options":["忽略此失效線索：等待造成再污染或表面狀態改變。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","等候未超出已驗證可接合時窗","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Waiting permits contamination or surface-state change.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Queue time stays within the validated bonding window","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「等候未超出已驗證可接合時窗」。等待造成再污染或表面狀態改變，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Queue time stays within the validated bonding window. Waiting permits contamination or surface-state change, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":374,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-373"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-375","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"晶粒背面吸持","titleEn":"Evaluate backside die pickup","objective":"判斷「晶粒背面吸持」是否滿足此具體條件：取晶不接觸接合面且形變受控。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate backside die pickup meets this specific condition: Pickup avoids the bonding face and controls deformation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查吸持區與薄晶粒撓度模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect pickup regions and thin-die deflection models. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：取晶不接觸接合面且形變受控；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Pickup avoids the bonding face and controls deformation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部吸持會使薄晶粒彎曲。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Localized suction can bend thin dies. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"取晶不接觸接合面且形變受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Pickup avoids the bonding face and controls deformation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-375-k1","title":"晶粒背面吸持的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate backside die pickup","text":"可檢驗條件為「取晶不接觸接合面且形變受控」。可藉由「檢查吸持區與薄晶粒撓度模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Pickup avoids the bonding face and controls deformation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect pickup regions and thin-die deflection models. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-375-k2","title":"晶粒背面吸持的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate backside die pickup","text":"局部吸持會使薄晶粒彎曲。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Localized suction can bend thin dies. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒背面吸持」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate backside die pickup?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部吸持會使薄晶粒彎曲。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","取晶不接觸接合面且形變受控"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Localized suction can bend thin dies.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Pickup avoids the bonding face and controls deformation"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「取晶不接觸接合面且形變受控」。局部吸持會使薄晶粒彎曲，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Pickup avoids the bonding face and controls deformation. Localized suction can bend thin dies, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":375,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-374"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-376","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"晶粒工具潔淨度","titleEn":"Inspect bonding-tool cleanliness","objective":"判斷「晶粒工具潔淨度」是否滿足此具體條件：工具未引入可辨識接合區污染。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect bonding-tool cleanliness meets this specific condition: Tools introduce no detectable bond-area contamination.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對工具接觸印痕與污染轉移圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare tool imprints and contamination-transfer maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：工具未引入可辨識接合區污染；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Tools introduce no detectable bond-area contamination. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"清洗過的晶粒可能被工具再污染。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Cleaned dies can be recontaminated by tools. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"工具未引入可辨識接合區污染；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Tools introduce no detectable bond-area contamination. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-376-k1","title":"晶粒工具潔淨度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect bonding-tool cleanliness","text":"可檢驗條件為「工具未引入可辨識接合區污染」。可藉由「比對工具接觸印痕與污染轉移圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Tools introduce no detectable bond-area contamination. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare tool imprints and contamination-transfer maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-376-k2","title":"晶粒工具潔淨度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect bonding-tool cleanliness","text":"清洗過的晶粒可能被工具再污染。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Cleaned dies can be recontaminated by tools. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒工具潔淨度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect bonding-tool cleanliness?","options":["工具未引入可辨識接合區污染","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：清洗過的晶粒可能被工具再污染。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Tools introduce no detectable bond-area contamination","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Cleaned dies can be recontaminated by tools.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「工具未引入可辨識接合區污染」。清洗過的晶粒可能被工具再污染，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Tools introduce no detectable bond-area contamination. Cleaned dies can be recontaminated by tools, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":376,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-375"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-377","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"對位標記辨識","titleEn":"Validate alignment-mark recognition","objective":"判斷「對位標記辨識」是否滿足此具體條件：中心估計穩定且可重複。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Validate alignment-mark recognition meets this specific condition: Center estimates remain stable and repeatable.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在不同照明下比較標記中心估計。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare mark-center estimates under varied illumination. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：中心估計穩定且可重複；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Center estimates remain stable and repeatable. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"不對稱反光會偏移視覺中心。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Asymmetric reflections bias the optical center. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"中心估計穩定且可重複；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Center estimates remain stable and repeatable. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-377-k1","title":"對位標記辨識的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Validate alignment-mark recognition","text":"可檢驗條件為「中心估計穩定且可重複」。可藉由「在不同照明下比較標記中心估計」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Center estimates remain stable and repeatable. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare mark-center estimates under varied illumination. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-377-k2","title":"對位標記辨識的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Validate alignment-mark recognition","text":"不對稱反光會偏移視覺中心。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Asymmetric reflections bias the optical center. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「對位標記辨識」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Validate alignment-mark recognition?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","中心估計穩定且可重複","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：不對稱反光會偏移視覺中心。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Center estimates remain stable and repeatable","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Asymmetric reflections bias the optical center."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「中心估計穩定且可重複」。不對稱反光會偏移視覺中心，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Center estimates remain stable and repeatable. Asymmetric reflections bias the optical center, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":377,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-376"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-378","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"座標鏡射與轉換","titleEn":"Verify bonding coordinate transforms","objective":"判斷「座標鏡射與轉換」是否滿足此具體條件：各角落對映與設計座標一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify bonding coordinate transforms meets this specific condition: Corner mappings match design coordinates.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把上下相機座標轉為共同接合座標。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Transform upper and lower camera data to one bond frame. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各角落對映與設計座標一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Corner mappings match design coordinates. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"少一次鏡射會造成系統性反向偏移。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Missing a mirror transform causes systematic reversed offsets. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各角落對映與設計座標一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Corner mappings match design coordinates. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-378-k1","title":"座標鏡射與轉換的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify bonding coordinate transforms","text":"可檢驗條件為「各角落對映與設計座標一致」。可藉由「把上下相機座標轉為共同接合座標」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Corner mappings match design coordinates. Evidence can be developed through this action: Transform upper and lower camera data to one bond frame. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-378-k2","title":"座標鏡射與轉換的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify bonding coordinate transforms","text":"少一次鏡射會造成系統性反向偏移。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Missing a mirror transform causes systematic reversed offsets. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「座標鏡射與轉換」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify bonding coordinate transforms?","options":["忽略此失效線索：少一次鏡射會造成系統性反向偏移。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各角落對映與設計座標一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Missing a mirror transform causes systematic reversed offsets.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Corner mappings match design coordinates","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「各角落對映與設計座標一致」。少一次鏡射會造成系統性反向偏移，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Corner mappings match design coordinates. Missing a mirror transform causes systematic reversed offsets, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":378,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-377"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-379","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"晶粒尺度與正交誤差","titleEn":"Separate die scale and orthogonality error","objective":"判斷「晶粒尺度與正交誤差」是否滿足此具體條件：尺度及正交分量分別有量測證據。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Separate die scale and orthogonality error meets this specific condition: Scale and orthogonality components are independently measured.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：擬合多標記座標的仿射殘差。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Fit affine residuals from multiple fiducials. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：尺度及正交分量分別有量測證據；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Scale and orthogonality components are independently measured. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"剛體對位不能修正晶粒尺度誤差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Rigid alignment cannot correct die-scale error. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"尺度及正交分量分別有量測證據；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Scale and orthogonality components are independently measured. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-379-k1","title":"晶粒尺度與正交誤差的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Separate die scale and orthogonality error","text":"可檢驗條件為「尺度及正交分量分別有量測證據」。可藉由「擬合多標記座標的仿射殘差」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Scale and orthogonality components are independently measured. Evidence can be developed through this action: Fit affine residuals from multiple fiducials. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-379-k2","title":"晶粒尺度與正交誤差的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Separate die scale and orthogonality error","text":"剛體對位不能修正晶粒尺度誤差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Rigid alignment cannot correct die-scale error. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-379-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設晶粒邊長 10 mm、倍率差 2 ppm，跨晶粒尺度差 20 nm；加上旋轉和正交誤差後，角落可能是最差位置。","textEn":"A hypothetical 10 mm die with 2 ppm scale mismatch has 20 nm dimensional difference; rotation and orthogonality can make corners worst-case."},{"id":"pk-379-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"先擬合可校正的仿射項，再看剩餘非線性場。對位規格需說明單軸、向量、最大值或分位數，不可互換。","textEn":"Fit correctable affine terms first, then inspect nonlinear residuals. Specify whether overlay limits are single-axis, vector, maximum or percentile; these are not interchangeable."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒尺度與正交誤差」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Separate die scale and orthogonality error?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：剛體對位不能修正晶粒尺度誤差。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","尺度及正交分量分別有量測證據"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Rigid alignment cannot correct die-scale error.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Scale and orthogonality components are independently measured"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「尺度及正交分量分別有量測證據」。剛體對位不能修正晶粒尺度誤差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Scale and orthogonality components are independently measured. Rigid alignment cannot correct die-scale error, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":379,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-378"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-380","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"接合頭傾斜校正","titleEn":"Assess bond-head tilt correction","objective":"判斷「接合頭傾斜校正」是否滿足此具體條件：接觸順序符合計畫且傾斜受控。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess bond-head tilt correction meets this specific condition: Contact order follows the plan with controlled tilt.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較多角落接近曲線與間隙。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare corner approach curves and gaps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接觸順序符合計畫且傾斜受控；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact order follows the plan with controlled tilt. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單邊先壓實可能導致側向滑移。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Early one-sided contact can induce lateral slip. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接觸順序符合計畫且傾斜受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact order follows the plan with controlled tilt. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-380-k1","title":"接合頭傾斜校正的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess bond-head tilt correction","text":"可檢驗條件為「接觸順序符合計畫且傾斜受控」。可藉由「比較多角落接近曲線與間隙」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact order follows the plan with controlled tilt. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare corner approach curves and gaps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-380-k2","title":"接合頭傾斜校正的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess bond-head tilt correction","text":"單邊先壓實可能導致側向滑移。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Early one-sided contact can induce lateral slip. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「接合頭傾斜校正」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess bond-head tilt correction?","options":["接觸順序符合計畫且傾斜受控","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：單邊先壓實可能導致側向滑移。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Contact order follows the plan with controlled tilt","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Early one-sided contact can induce lateral slip.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「接觸順序符合計畫且傾斜受控」。單邊先壓實可能導致側向滑移，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact order follows the plan with controlled tilt. Early one-sided contact can induce lateral slip, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":380,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-379"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-381","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"接觸瞬間位移","titleEn":"Measure placement shift at contact","objective":"判斷「接觸瞬間位移」是否滿足此具體條件：接觸造成的位移在對位預算內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure placement shift at contact meets this specific condition: Contact-induced shift stays within alignment budget.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較接觸前後原位標記位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare in-situ marks before and after contact. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接觸造成的位移在對位預算內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact-induced shift stays within alignment budget. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"自由空間對準不等於接觸後對準。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Free-space alignment does not prove postcontact alignment. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接觸造成的位移在對位預算內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact-induced shift stays within alignment budget. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-381-k1","title":"接觸瞬間位移的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure placement shift at contact","text":"可檢驗條件為「接觸造成的位移在對位預算內」。可藉由「比較接觸前後原位標記位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact-induced shift stays within alignment budget. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare in-situ marks before and after contact. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-381-k2","title":"接觸瞬間位移的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure placement shift at contact","text":"自由空間對準不等於接觸後對準。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Free-space alignment does not prove postcontact alignment. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「接觸瞬間位移」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure placement shift at contact?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","接觸造成的位移在對位預算內","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：自由空間對準不等於接觸後對準。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Contact-induced shift stays within alignment budget","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Free-space alignment does not prove postcontact alignment."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「接觸造成的位移在對位預算內」。自由空間對準不等於接觸後對準，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact-induced shift stays within alignment budget. Free-space alignment does not prove postcontact alignment, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":381,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-380"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-382","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"介電預接合波前","titleEn":"Observe dielectric prebond propagation","objective":"判斷「介電預接合波前」是否滿足此具體條件：前緣連續且未包圍大面積未接區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Observe dielectric prebond propagation meets this specific condition: Fronts remain continuous without enclosing large unbonded areas.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤紅外影像中的接合前緣。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Track bonding fronts in infrared image sequences. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：前緣連續且未包圍大面積未接區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Fronts remain continuous without enclosing large unbonded areas. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"前緣分叉可能圍住顆粒或氣體。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Split fronts can trap particles or gas. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"前緣連續且未包圍大面積未接區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Fronts remain continuous without enclosing large unbonded areas. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-382-k1","title":"介電預接合波前的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Observe dielectric prebond propagation","text":"可檢驗條件為「前緣連續且未包圍大面積未接區」。可藉由「追蹤紅外影像中的接合前緣」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Fronts remain continuous without enclosing large unbonded areas. Evidence can be developed through this action: Track bonding fronts in infrared image sequences. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-382-k2","title":"介電預接合波前的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Observe dielectric prebond propagation","text":"前緣分叉可能圍住顆粒或氣體。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Split fronts can trap particles or gas. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介電預接合波前」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Observe dielectric prebond propagation?","options":["忽略此失效線索：前緣分叉可能圍住顆粒或氣體。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","前緣連續且未包圍大面積未接區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Split fronts can trap particles or gas.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Fronts remain continuous without enclosing large unbonded areas","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「前緣連續且未包圍大面積未接區」。前緣分叉可能圍住顆粒或氣體，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Fronts remain continuous without enclosing large unbonded areas. Split fronts can trap particles or gas, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":382,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-381"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-383","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"集合轉移載板支線","titleEn":"Assess a collective-transfer carrier branch","objective":"判斷「集合轉移載板支線」是否滿足此具體條件：兩段誤差的合成值仍符合介面。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess a collective-transfer carrier branch meets this specific condition: Combined errors meet interface requirements.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：累加放晶及晶圓鍵合套準誤差。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Combine placement and wafer-bond overlay errors. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：兩段誤差的合成值仍符合介面；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Combined errors meet interface requirements. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"各段個別合格不保證總誤差合格。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Each stage passing does not guarantee total overlay passes. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"兩段誤差的合成值仍符合介面；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Combined errors meet interface requirements. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-383-k1","title":"集合轉移載板支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess a collective-transfer carrier branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「兩段誤差的合成值仍符合介面」。可藉由「累加放晶及晶圓鍵合套準誤差」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Combined errors meet interface requirements. Evidence can be developed through this action: Combine placement and wafer-bond overlay errors. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-383-k2","title":"集合轉移載板支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess a collective-transfer carrier branch","text":"各段個別合格不保證總誤差合格。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Each stage passing does not guarantee total overlay passes. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「集合轉移載板支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess a collective-transfer carrier branch?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：各段個別合格不保證總誤差合格。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","兩段誤差的合成值仍符合介面"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Each stage passing does not guarantee total overlay passes.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Combined errors meet interface requirements"],"answer":3,"explanati