nomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"批次首尾晶粒可能經歷不同等待。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"First and last dies can experience different queue times. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各晶粒清潔與等待時間均受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Each die has controlled cleanliness and queue time. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-384-k1","title":"直接放晶支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess direct die-placement bonding","text":"可檢驗條件為「各晶粒清潔與等待時間均受控」。可藉由「比較逐晶粒活化搬運與接觸紀錄」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Each die has controlled cleanliness and queue time. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare activation, transfer, and contact records per die. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-384-k2","title":"直接放晶支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess direct die-placement bonding","text":"批次首尾晶粒可能經歷不同等待。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"First and last dies can experience different queue times. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「直接放晶支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess direct die-placement bonding?","options":["各晶粒清潔與等待時間均受控","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：批次首尾晶粒可能經歷不同等待。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Each die has controlled cleanliness and queue time","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: First and last dies can experience different queue times.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「各晶粒清潔與等待時間均受控」。批次首尾晶粒可能經歷不同等待，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Each die has controlled cleanliness and queue time. First and last dies can experience different queue times, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":384,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-383"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-385","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"晶圓對晶圓配對支線","titleEn":"Assess wafer-to-wafer pairing","objective":"判斷「晶圓對晶圓配對支線」是否滿足此具體條件：有效重疊與預期良品配對一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess wafer-to-wafer pairing meets this specific condition: Effective overlap matches expected good-die pairs.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：疊合上下晶圓良品圖與旋轉標記。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay good-die maps and rotation marks. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：有效重疊與預期良品配對一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Effective overlap matches expected good-die pairs. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只用平均良率會忽略空間相關缺陷。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Mean yield misses spatially correlated defects. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"有效重疊與預期良品配對一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Effective overlap matches expected good-die pairs. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-385-k1","title":"晶圓對晶圓配對支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess wafer-to-wafer pairing","text":"可檢驗條件為「有效重疊與預期良品配對一致」。可藉由「疊合上下晶圓良品圖與旋轉標記」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Effective overlap matches expected good-die pairs. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay good-die maps and rotation marks. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-385-k2","title":"晶圓對晶圓配對支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess wafer-to-wafer pairing","text":"只用平均良率會忽略空間相關缺陷。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Mean yield misses spatially correlated defects. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶圓對晶圓配對支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess wafer-to-wafer pairing?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","有效重疊與預期良品配對一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只用平均良率會忽略空間相關缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Effective overlap matches expected good-die pairs","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Mean yield misses spatially correlated defects."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「有效重疊與預期良品配對一致」。只用平均良率會忽略空間相關缺陷，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Effective overlap matches expected good-die pairs. Mean yield misses spatially correlated defects, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":385,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-384"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-386","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"鍵合後熱處理判讀","titleEn":"Assess postbond thermal treatment","objective":"判斷「鍵合後熱處理判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：金屬接觸改善且介電未劣化。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess postbond thermal treatment meets this specific condition: Metal contact improves without dielectric degradation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較熱歷程前後鏈阻及界面影像。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare chain resistance and interfaces across thermal history. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：金屬接觸改善且介電未劣化；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Metal contact improves without dielectric degradation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"提高溫度不能無限制補償表面缺陷。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Higher temperature cannot indefinitely compensate surface defects. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"金屬接觸改善且介電未劣化；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Metal contact improves without dielectric degradation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-386-k1","title":"鍵合後熱處理判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess postbond thermal treatment","text":"可檢驗條件為「金屬接觸改善且介電未劣化」。可藉由「比較熱歷程前後鏈阻及界面影像」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Metal contact improves without dielectric degradation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare chain resistance and interfaces across thermal history. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-386-k2","title":"鍵合後熱處理判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess postbond thermal treatment","text":"提高溫度不能無限制補償表面缺陷。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Higher temperature cannot indefinitely compensate surface defects. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「鍵合後熱處理判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess postbond thermal treatment?","options":["忽略此失效線索：提高溫度不能無限制補償表面缺陷。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","金屬接觸改善且介電未劣化","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Higher temperature cannot indefinitely compensate surface defects.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Metal contact improves without dielectric degradation","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「金屬接觸改善且介電未劣化」。提高溫度不能無限制補償表面缺陷，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Metal contact improves without dielectric degradation. Higher temperature cannot indefinitely compensate surface defects, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":386,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-385"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-387","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"鍵合空洞定位","titleEn":"Locate hybrid-bond voids","objective":"判斷「鍵合空洞定位」是否滿足此具體條件：空洞位置及尺寸可追溯到介面。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Locate hybrid-bond voids meets this specific condition: Void position and size are traceable to the interface.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把原位對準與接合影像共同定位。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Co-register alignment data and bond images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：空洞位置及尺寸可追溯到介面；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Void position and size are traceable to the interface. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"影像亮暗變化不全等同空洞。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Image contrast changes are not always voids. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"空洞位置及尺寸可追溯到介面；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Void position and size are traceable to the interface. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-387-k1","title":"鍵合空洞定位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Locate hybrid-bond voids","text":"可檢驗條件為「空洞位置及尺寸可追溯到介面」。可藉由「把原位對準與接合影像共同定位」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Void position and size are traceable to the interface. Evidence can be developed through this action: Co-register alignment data and bond images. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-387-k2","title":"鍵合空洞定位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Locate hybrid-bond voids","text":"影像亮暗變化不全等同空洞。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Image contrast changes are not always voids. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「鍵合空洞定位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Locate hybrid-bond voids?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：影像亮暗變化不全等同空洞。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","空洞位置及尺寸可追溯到介面"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Image contrast changes are not always voids.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Void position and size are traceable to the interface"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「空洞位置及尺寸可追溯到介面」。影像亮暗變化不全等同空洞，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Void position and size are traceable to the interface. Image contrast changes are not always voids, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":387,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-386"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-388","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"銅接點鏈阻分離","titleEn":"Separate copper-contact chain resistance","objective":"判斷「銅接點鏈阻分離」是否滿足此具體條件：接點電阻分布符合介面預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Separate copper-contact chain resistance meets this specific condition: Contact resistance distribution fits the interface budget.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：利用不同接點數鏈結分離線阻及接點阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Use varied contact-count chains to separate line and contact resistance. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接點電阻分布符合介面預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact resistance distribution fits the interface budget. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"長導線電阻可掩蓋個別接點異常。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Long-line resistance can mask contact anomalies. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接點電阻分布符合介面預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact resistance distribution fits the interface budget. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-388-k1","title":"銅接點鏈阻分離的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Separate copper-contact chain resistance","text":"可檢驗條件為「接點電阻分布符合介面預算」。可藉由「利用不同接點數鏈結分離線阻及接點阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact resistance distribution fits the interface budget. Evidence can be developed through this action: Use varied contact-count chains to separate line and contact resistance. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-388-k2","title":"銅接點鏈阻分離的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Separate copper-contact chain resistance","text":"長導線電阻可掩蓋個別接點異常。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Long-line resistance can mask contact anomalies. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「銅接點鏈阻分離」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Separate copper-contact chain resistance?","options":["接點電阻分布符合介面預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：長導線電阻可掩蓋個別接點異常。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Contact resistance distribution fits the interface budget","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Long-line resistance can mask contact anomalies.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「接點電阻分布符合介面預算」。長導線電阻可掩蓋個別接點異常，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact resistance distribution fits the interface budget. Long-line resistance can mask contact anomalies, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":388,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-387"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-389","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"接合強度與破面","titleEn":"Interpret bond strength and fracture surfaces","objective":"判斷「接合強度與破面」是否滿足此具體條件：破壞模式符合已核准接合評估。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret bond strength and fracture surfaces meets this specific condition: Failure mode agrees with the qualified bond evaluation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把破壞載荷與破面位置共同判讀。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Interpret failure load with fracture location. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：破壞模式符合已核准接合評估；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Failure mode agrees with the qualified bond evaluation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"高載荷也可能伴隨不期望材料破壞。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"High load can coexist with undesirable material fracture. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"破壞模式符合已核准接合評估；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Failure mode agrees with the qualified bond evaluation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-389-k1","title":"接合強度與破面的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret bond strength and fracture surfaces","text":"可檢驗條件為「破壞模式符合已核准接合評估」。可藉由「把破壞載荷與破面位置共同判讀」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Failure mode agrees with the qualified bond evaluation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Interpret failure load with fracture location. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-389-k2","title":"接合強度與破面的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret bond strength and fracture surfaces","text":"高載荷也可能伴隨不期望材料破壞。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"High load can coexist with undesirable material fracture. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「接合強度與破面」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret bond strength and fracture surfaces?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","破壞模式符合已核准接合評估","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：高載荷也可能伴隨不期望材料破壞。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Failure mode agrees with the qualified bond evaluation","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: High load can coexist with undesirable material fracture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「破壞模式符合已核准接合評估」。高載荷也可能伴隨不期望材料破壞，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Failure mode agrees with the qualified bond evaluation. High load can coexist with undesirable material fracture, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":389,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-388"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-390","stageId":"pk-m15","title":"混合鍵合證據放行","titleEn":"Release hybrid-bond evidence","objective":"判斷「混合鍵合證據放行」是否滿足此具體條件：所有介面證據達標且可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Release hybrid-bond evidence meets this specific condition: All interface evidence meets criteria and is traceable.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：聯合檢視空洞對位電性與強度記錄。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Review void, overlay, electrical, and strength records together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：所有介面證據達標且可追溯；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All interface evidence meets criteria and is traceable. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單獨電性通過不能保證長期接合可靠。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Electrical passing alone does not prove durable bonding. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"所有介面證據達標且可追溯；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All interface evidence meets criteria and is traceable. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-390-k1","title":"混合鍵合證據放行的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Release hybrid-bond evidence","text":"可檢驗條件為「所有介面證據達標且可追溯」。可藉由「聯合檢視空洞對位電性與強度記錄」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All interface evidence meets criteria and is traceable. Evidence can be developed through this action: Review void, overlay, electrical, and strength records together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-390-k2","title":"混合鍵合證據放行的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Release hybrid-bond evidence","text":"單獨電性通過不能保證長期接合可靠。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Electrical passing alone does not prove durable bonding. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「混合鍵合證據放行」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Release hybrid-bond evidence?","options":["忽略此失效線索：單獨電性通過不能保證長期接合可靠。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","所有介面證據達標且可追溯","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Electrical passing alone does not prove durable bonding.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","All interface evidence meets criteria and is traceable","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「所有介面證據達標且可追溯」。單獨電性通過不能保證長期接合可靠，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All interface evidence meets criteria and is traceable. Electrical passing alone does not prove durable bonding, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-evg-hybrid","pkb-besi-hybrid","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":390,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-389"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"晶圓對晶圓、直接晶粒對晶圓及集合轉移為替代支線；混合鍵合不能視為微凸塊回焊。","routeEn":"Wafer-to-wafer, direct die-to-wafer, and collective transfer are alternative branches; hybrid bonding is not microbump reflow.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m16","title":"HBM 與晶粒堆疊組裝","titleEn":"HBM and chiplet stack assembly","description":"堆疊放大單層缺陷的成本，必須維持晶粒譜系、逐層幾何與測試可達性。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Stacking magnifies the cost of individual defects and requires die genealogy, layer geometry, and test access. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","order":16,"sequence":16,"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-391","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"HBM 基底晶粒驗證","titleEn":"Verify an HBM base die","objective":"判斷「HBM 基底晶粒驗證」是否滿足此具體條件：基底狀態及介面版本皆有效。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify an HBM base die meets this specific condition: Base status and interface revision are valid.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：核對基底晶粒測試記錄與堆疊版本。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Match base-die test records and stack revisions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：基底狀態及介面版本皆有效；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Base status and interface revision are valid. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"基底失效會使上層良品晶粒一同損失。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A failing base wastes otherwise good upper dies. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"基底狀態及介面版本皆有效；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Base status and interface revision are valid. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-391-k1","title":"HBM 基底晶粒驗證的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify an HBM base die","text":"可檢驗條件為「基底狀態及介面版本皆有效」。可藉由「核對基底晶粒測試記錄與堆疊版本」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Base status and interface revision are valid. Evidence can be developed through this action: Match base-die test records and stack revisions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-391-k2","title":"HBM 基底晶粒驗證的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify an HBM base die","text":"基底失效會使上層良品晶粒一同損失。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A failing base wastes otherwise good upper dies. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「HBM 基底晶粒驗證」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify an HBM base die?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：基底失效會使上層良品晶粒一同損失。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","基底狀態及介面版本皆有效"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: A failing base wastes otherwise good upper dies.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Base status and interface revision are valid"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「基底狀態及介面版本皆有效」。基底失效會使上層良品晶粒一同損失，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Base status and interface revision are valid. A failing base wastes otherwise good upper dies, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":391,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-392","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"記憶體晶粒分檔","titleEn":"Bin memory dies for stacking","objective":"判斷「記憶體晶粒分檔」是否滿足此具體條件：選用晶粒符合堆疊目標分檔。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Bin memory dies for stacking meets this specific condition: Selected dies meet the target stack bin.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較功能測試與速度分檔資料。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare functional results and speed-bin data. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：選用晶粒符合堆疊目標分檔；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Selected dies meet the target stack bin. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"不同速度分檔混入會限制整體性能。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Mixed speed bins can limit stack performance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"選用晶粒符合堆疊目標分檔；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Selected dies meet the target stack bin. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-392-k1","title":"記憶體晶粒分檔的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Bin memory dies for stacking","text":"可檢驗條件為「選用晶粒符合堆疊目標分檔」。可藉由「比較功能測試與速度分檔資料」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Selected dies meet the target stack bin. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare functional results and speed-bin data. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-392-k2","title":"記憶體晶粒分檔的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Bin memory dies for stacking","text":"不同速度分檔混入會限制整體性能。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Mixed speed bins can limit stack performance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記憶體晶粒分檔」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Bin memory dies for stacking?","options":["選用晶粒符合堆疊目標分檔","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：不同速度分檔混入會限制整體性能。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Selected dies meet the target stack bin","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Mixed speed bins can limit stack performance.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「選用晶粒符合堆疊目標分檔」。不同速度分檔混入會限制整體性能，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Selected dies meet the target stack bin. Mixed speed bins can limit stack performance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":392,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-391"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-393","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊層序核對","titleEn":"Verify stack layer order","objective":"判斷「堆疊層序核對」是否滿足此具體條件：每層朝向與通道對應正確。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify stack layer order meets this specific condition: Every layer has correct orientation and channel mapping.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以晶粒識別與接面朝向建立層序圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Build a layer map from die identity and face orientation. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：每層朝向與通道對應正確；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Every layer has correct orientation and channel mapping. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"層序錯置可能無法在後段修復。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Incorrect ordering may be irreparable downstream. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"每層朝向與通道對應正確；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Every layer has correct orientation and channel mapping. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-393-k1","title":"堆疊層序核對的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify stack layer order","text":"可檢驗條件為「每層朝向與通道對應正確」。可藉由「以晶粒識別與接面朝向建立層序圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Every layer has correct orientation and channel mapping. Evidence can be developed through this action: Build a layer map from die identity and face orientation. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-393-k2","title":"堆疊層序核對的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify stack layer order","text":"層序錯置可能無法在後段修復。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Incorrect ordering may be irreparable downstream. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊層序核對」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify stack layer order?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","每層朝向與通道對應正確","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：層序錯置可能無法在後段修復。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Every layer has correct orientation and channel mapping","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Incorrect ordering may be irreparable downstream."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「每層朝向與通道對應正確」。層序錯置可能無法在後段修復，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Every layer has correct orientation and channel mapping. Incorrect ordering may be irreparable downstream, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":393,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-392"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-394","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"薄晶粒厚度分布","titleEn":"Map thinned-die thickness","objective":"判斷「薄晶粒厚度分布」是否滿足此具體條件：累計厚度與楔角保留堆疊餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map thinned-die thickness meets this specific condition: Accumulated thickness and wedge preserve stack allowance.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較每顆晶粒厚度及局部楔角。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare individual die thickness and wedge. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：累計厚度與楔角保留堆疊餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Accumulated thickness and wedge preserve stack allowance. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"微小楔角可逐層累積成傾斜。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Small wedges can accumulate into stack tilt. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"累計厚度與楔角保留堆疊餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Accumulated thickness and wedge preserve stack allowance. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-394-k1","title":"薄晶粒厚度分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map thinned-die thickness","text":"可檢驗條件為「累計厚度與楔角保留堆疊餘量」。可藉由「比較每顆晶粒厚度及局部楔角」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Accumulated thickness and wedge preserve stack allowance. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare individual die thickness and wedge. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-394-k2","title":"薄晶粒厚度分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map thinned-die thickness","text":"微小楔角可逐層累積成傾斜。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Small wedges can accumulate into stack tilt. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「薄晶粒厚度分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map thinned-die thickness?","options":["忽略此失效線索：微小楔角可逐層累積成傾斜。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","累計厚度與楔角保留堆疊餘量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Small wedges can accumulate into stack tilt.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Accumulated thickness and wedge preserve stack allowance","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「累計厚度與楔角保留堆疊餘量」。微小楔角可逐層累積成傾斜，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Accumulated thickness and wedge preserve stack allowance. Small wedges can accumulate into stack tilt, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":394,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-393"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-395","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"晶粒邊緣機械完整性","titleEn":"Inspect stack-die edge integrity","objective":"判斷「晶粒邊緣機械完整性」是否滿足此具體條件：裂紋未靠近有效互連區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect stack-die edge integrity meets this specific condition: Cracks remain away from functional interconnects.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤崩角位置與 TSV 保留區。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Relate edge chips to TSV keep-out regions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：裂紋未靠近有效互連區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cracks remain away from functional interconnects. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"邊裂可在堆疊載荷下擴展。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Edge cracks can extend under stacking loads. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"裂紋未靠近有效互連區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cracks remain away from functional interconnects. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-395-k1","title":"晶粒邊緣機械完整性的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect stack-die edge integrity","text":"可檢驗條件為「裂紋未靠近有效互連區」。可藉由「追蹤崩角位置與 TSV 保留區」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cracks remain away from functional interconnects. Evidence can be developed through this action: Relate edge chips to TSV keep-out regions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-395-k2","title":"晶粒邊緣機械完整性的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect stack-die edge integrity","text":"邊裂可在堆疊載荷下擴展。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Edge cracks can extend under stacking loads. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒邊緣機械完整性」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect stack-die edge integrity?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：邊裂可在堆疊載荷下擴展。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","裂紋未靠近有效互連區"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Edge cracks can extend under stacking loads.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cracks remain away from functional interconnects"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「裂紋未靠近有效互連區」。邊裂可在堆疊載荷下擴展，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cracks remain away from functional interconnects. Edge cracks can extend under stacking loads, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":395,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-394"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-396","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"背面接點共平面度","titleEn":"Inspect backside stack-contact coplanarity","objective":"判斷「背面接點共平面度」是否滿足此具體條件：接點高度落在鍵合可補償範圍。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect backside stack-contact coplanarity meets this specific condition: Contact heights fit bonding compensation capability.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較單顆晶粒背面接點高度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare backside contact heights per die. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接點高度落在鍵合可補償範圍；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact heights fit bonding compensation capability. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"晶粒總厚度合格仍可能有局部墊差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Passing die thickness can hide local pad-height variation. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接點高度落在鍵合可補償範圍；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact heights fit bonding compensation capability. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-396-k1","title":"背面接點共平面度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect backside stack-contact coplanarity","text":"可檢驗條件為「接點高度落在鍵合可補償範圍」。可藉由「比較單顆晶粒背面接點高度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact heights fit bonding compensation capability. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare backside contact heights per die. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-396-k2","title":"背面接點共平面度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect backside stack-contact coplanarity","text":"晶粒總厚度合格仍可能有局部墊差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Passing die thickness can hide local pad-height variation. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「背面接點共平面度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect backside stack-contact coplanarity?","options":["接點高度落在鍵合可補償範圍","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：晶粒總厚度合格仍可能有局部墊差。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Contact heights fit bonding compensation capability","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Passing die thickness can hide local pad-height variation.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「接點高度落在鍵合可補償範圍」。晶粒總厚度合格仍可能有局部墊差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact heights fit bonding compensation capability. Passing die thickness can hide local pad-height variation, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":396,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-395"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-397","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"微凸塊體積分布","titleEn":"Map stack microbump volume","objective":"判斷「微凸塊體積分布」是否滿足此具體條件：體積與高度分布符合接合需求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map stack microbump volume meets this specific condition: Volume and height distributions fit joining needs.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：由三維影像估計凸塊體積。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Estimate bump volume from three-dimensional images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：體積與高度分布符合接合需求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Volume and height distributions fit joining needs. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"僅看直徑無法識別不同體積。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Diameter alone cannot establish equal volume. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"體積與高度分布符合接合需求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Volume and height distributions fit joining needs. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-397-k1","title":"微凸塊體積分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map stack microbump volume","text":"可檢驗條件為「體積與高度分布符合接合需求」。可藉由「由三維影像估計凸塊體積」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Volume and height distributions fit joining needs. Evidence can be developed through this action: Estimate bump volume from three-dimensional images. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-397-k2","title":"微凸塊體積分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map stack microbump volume","text":"僅看直徑無法識別不同體積。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Diameter alone cannot establish equal volume. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「微凸塊體積分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map stack microbump volume?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","體積與高度分布符合接合需求","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：僅看直徑無法識別不同體積。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Volume and height distributions fit joining needs","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Diameter alone cannot establish equal volume."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「體積與高度分布符合接合需求」。僅看直徑無法識別不同體積，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Volume and height distributions fit joining needs. Diameter alone cannot establish equal volume, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":397,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-396"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-398","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"非導電膜支線","titleEn":"Inspect a nonconductive-film branch","objective":"判斷「非導電膜支線」是否滿足此具體條件：膜可填隙且不妨礙金屬接觸。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect a nonconductive-film branch meets this specific condition: Film fills gaps without preventing metal contact.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較膜厚與凸塊穿透接合模擬。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare film thickness and bump-penetration simulations. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：膜可填隙且不妨礙金屬接觸；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Film fills gaps without preventing metal contact. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"膜殘留於接點可造成高阻。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Film trapped at contacts can cause high resistance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"膜可填隙且不妨礙金屬接觸；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Film fills gaps without preventing metal contact. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-398-k1","title":"非導電膜支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect a nonconductive-film branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「膜可填隙且不妨礙金屬接觸」。可藉由「比較膜厚與凸塊穿透接合模擬」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Film fills gaps without preventing metal contact. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare film thickness and bump-penetration simulations. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-398-k2","title":"非導電膜支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect a nonconductive-film branch","text":"膜殘留於接點可造成高阻。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Film trapped at contacts can cause high resistance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「非導電膜支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect a nonconductive-film branch?","options":["忽略此失效線索：膜殘留於接點可造成高阻。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","膜可填隙且不妨礙金屬接觸","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Film trapped at contacts can cause high resistance.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Film fills gaps without preventing metal contact","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「膜可填隙且不妨礙金屬接觸」。膜殘留於接點可造成高阻，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Film fills gaps without preventing metal contact. Film trapped at contacts can cause high resistance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":398,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-397"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-399","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"非導電膠支線","titleEn":"Inspect a nonconductive-paste branch","objective":"判斷「非導電膠支線」是否滿足此具體條件：膠流未封住排氣且接點乾淨。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect a nonconductive-paste branch meets this specific condition: Flow preserves venting and clean contacts.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：觀察壓合時膠流與排氣路徑。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Observe paste flow and venting during simulated compression. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：膠流未封住排氣且接點乾淨；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Flow preserves venting and clean contacts. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部膠量過多可困氣或推移晶粒。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Excess paste can trap air or shift dies. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"膠流未封住排氣且接點乾淨；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Flow preserves venting and clean contacts. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-399-k1","title":"非導電膠支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect a nonconductive-paste branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「膠流未封住排氣且接點乾淨」。可藉由「觀察壓合時膠流與排氣路徑」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Flow preserves venting and clean contacts. Evidence can be developed through this action: Observe paste flow and venting during simulated compression. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-399-k2","title":"非導電膠支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect a nonconductive-paste branch","text":"局部膠量過多可困氣或推移晶粒。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Excess paste can trap air or shift dies. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「非導電膠支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect a nonconductive-paste branch?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部膠量過多可困氣或推移晶粒。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","膠流未封住排氣且接點乾淨"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Excess paste can trap air or shift dies.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Flow preserves venting and clean contacts"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「膠流未封住排氣且接點乾淨」。局部膠量過多可困氣或推移晶粒，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Flow preserves venting and clean contacts. Excess paste can trap air or shift dies, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":399,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-398"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-400","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"薄晶粒取放載荷","titleEn":"Assess thin-die pickup loading","objective":"判斷「薄晶粒取放載荷」是否滿足此具體條件：模擬拉應力低於核准設計限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess thin-die pickup loading meets this specific condition: Simulated tensile stress stays within approved design limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較多點支撐與局部頂針撓曲。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare distributed support and localized ejector deflection. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：模擬拉應力低於核准設計限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Simulated tensile stress stays within approved design limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單點頂起容易誘發薄晶粒裂紋。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Point lifting can crack thin dies. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"模擬拉應力低於核准設計限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Simulated tensile stress stays within approved design limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-400-k1","title":"薄晶粒取放載荷的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess thin-die pickup loading","text":"可檢驗條件為「模擬拉應力低於核准設計限制」。可藉由「比較多點支撐與局部頂針撓曲」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Simulated tensile stress stays within approved design limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare distributed support and localized ejector deflection. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-400-k2","title":"薄晶粒取放載荷的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess thin-die pickup loading","text":"單點頂起容易誘發薄晶粒裂紋。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Point lifting can crack thin dies. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「薄晶粒取放載荷」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess thin-die pickup loading?","options":["模擬拉應力低於核准設計限制","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：單點頂起容易誘發薄晶粒裂紋。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Simulated tensile stress stays within approved design limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Point lifting can crack thin dies.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「模擬拉應力低於核准設計限制」。單點頂起容易誘發薄晶粒裂紋，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Simulated tensile stress stays within approved design limits. Point lifting can crack thin dies, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":400,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-399"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-401","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"首層記憶體對位","titleEn":"Align the first memory layer","objective":"判斷「首層記憶體對位」是否滿足此具體條件：各角落接點重疊符合規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Align the first memory layer meets this specific condition: Corner contact overlap meets specifications.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把首層標記與基底接點套準。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Align first-layer marks to base contacts. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各角落接點重疊符合規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Corner contact overlap meets specifications. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"首層系統偏移會影響全部上層。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"First-layer systematic offset affects all upper layers. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各角落接點重疊符合規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Corner contact overlap meets specifications. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-401-k1","title":"首層記憶體對位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Align the first memory layer","text":"可檢驗條件為「各角落接點重疊符合規範」。可藉由「把首層標記與基底接點套準」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Corner contact overlap meets specifications. Evidence can be developed through this action: Align first-layer marks to base contacts. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-401-k2","title":"首層記憶體對位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Align the first memory layer","text":"首層系統偏移會影響全部上層。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"First-layer systematic offset affects all upper layers. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「首層記憶體對位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Align the first memory layer?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各角落接點重疊符合規範","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：首層系統偏移會影響全部上層。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Corner contact overlap meets specifications","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: First-layer systematic offset affects all upper layers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「各角落接點重疊符合規範」。首層系統偏移會影響全部上層，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Corner contact overlap meets specifications. First-layer systematic offset affects all upper layers, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":401,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-400"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-402","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"熱壓接合位移曲線","titleEn":"Interpret thermocompression displacement curves","objective":"判斷「熱壓接合位移曲線」是否滿足此具體條件：位移變化與預期接觸事件一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret thermocompression displacement curves meets this specific condition: Displacement changes match expected contact events.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較壓合位移及接點高度變化。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare compression displacement and contact-height changes. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：位移變化與預期接觸事件一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Displacement changes match expected contact events. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"載具順應性可能誤當焊點塌陷。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Fixture compliance can be mistaken for joint collapse. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"位移變化與預期接觸事件一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Displacement changes match expected contact events. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-402-k1","title":"熱壓接合位移曲線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret thermocompression displacement curves","text":"可檢驗條件為「位移變化與預期接觸事件一致」。可藉由「比較壓合位移及接點高度變化」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Displacement changes match expected contact events. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare compression displacement and contact-height changes. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-402-k2","title":"熱壓接合位移曲線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret thermocompression displacement curves","text":"載具順應性可能誤當焊點塌陷。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Fixture compliance can be mistaken for joint collapse. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「熱壓接合位移曲線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret thermocompression displacement curves?","options":["忽略此失效線索：載具順應性可能誤當焊點塌陷。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","位移變化與預期接觸事件一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Fixture compliance can be mistaken for joint collapse.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Displacement changes match expected contact events","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「位移變化與預期接觸事件一致」。載具順應性可能誤當焊點塌陷，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Displacement changes match expected contact events. Fixture compliance can be mistaken for joint collapse, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":402,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-401"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-403","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"局部熱歷程梯度","titleEn":"Assess local bonding thermal gradients","objective":"判斷「局部熱歷程梯度」是否滿足此具體條件：全部接點經歷合格熱歷程。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess local bonding thermal gradients meets this specific condition: All contacts experience a qualified thermal history.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較晶粒中心與四角溫度軌跡。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare center and corner temperature histories. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：全部接點經歷合格熱歷程；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All contacts experience a qualified thermal history. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"中央達溫不能代表角落接合充分。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Center temperature does not establish corner joining. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"全部接點經歷合格熱歷程；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All contacts experience a qualified thermal history. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-403-k1","title":"局部熱歷程梯度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess local bonding thermal gradients","text":"可檢驗條件為「全部接點經歷合格熱歷程」。可藉由「比較晶粒中心與四角溫度軌跡」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All contacts experience a qualified thermal history. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare center and corner temperature histories. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-403-k2","title":"局部熱歷程梯度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess local bonding thermal gradients","text":"中央達溫不能代表角落接合充分。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Center temperature does not establish corner joining. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「局部熱歷程梯度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess local bonding thermal gradients?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：中央達溫不能代表角落接合充分。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","全部接點經歷合格熱歷程"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Center temperature does not establish corner joining.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","All contacts experience a qualified thermal history"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「全部接點經歷合格熱歷程」。中央達溫不能代表角落接合充分，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All contacts experience a qualified thermal history. Center temperature does not establish corner joining, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":403,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-402"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-404","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊層間間隙","titleEn":"Measure interlayer gaps","objective":"判斷「堆疊層間間隙」是否滿足此具體條件：間隙與填膠層設計相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure interlayer gaps meets this specific condition: Gaps agree with adhesive-layer design.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：由側視量測分離各層間距。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Resolve individual interlayer gaps from side views. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：間隙與填膠層設計相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Gaps agree with adhesive-layer design. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"平均堆疊高度可能掩蓋局部薄間隙。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Average stack height can conceal thin local gaps. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"間隙與填膠層設計相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Gaps agree with adhesive-layer design. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-404-k1","title":"堆疊層間間隙的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure interlayer gaps","text":"可檢驗條件為「間隙與填膠層設計相容」。可藉由「由側視量測分離各層間距」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Gaps agree with adhesive-layer design. Evidence can be developed through this action: Resolve individual interlayer gaps from side views. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-404-k2","title":"堆疊層間間隙的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure interlayer gaps","text":"平均堆疊高度可能掩蓋局部薄間隙。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Average stack height can conceal thin local gaps. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊層間間隙」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure interlayer gaps?","options":["間隙與填膠層設計相容","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：平均堆疊高度可能掩蓋局部薄間隙。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Gaps agree with adhesive-layer design","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Average stack height can conceal thin local gaps.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「間隙與填膠層設計相容」。平均堆疊高度可能掩蓋局部薄間隙，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Gaps agree with adhesive-layer design. Average stack height can conceal thin local gaps, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":404,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-403"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-405","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"層間傾斜累積","titleEn":"Track cumulative stack tilt","objective":"判斷「層間傾斜累積」是否滿足此具體條件：累積傾斜未超過下一層對位預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Track cumulative stack tilt meets this specific condition: Cumulative tilt fits next-layer alignment budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：逐層擬合頂面傾斜向量。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Fit top-surface tilt vectors after each layer. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：累積傾斜未超過下一層對位預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cumulative tilt fits next-layer alignment budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"相同方向小偏差可逐層累積。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Small same-direction errors accumulate layer by layer. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"累積傾斜未超過下一層對位預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cumulative tilt fits next-layer alignment budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-405-k1","title":"層間傾斜累積的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Track cumulative stack tilt","text":"可檢驗條件為「累積傾斜未超過下一層對位預算」。可藉由「逐層擬合頂面傾斜向量」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cumulative tilt fits next-layer alignment budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Fit top-surface tilt vectors after each layer. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-405-k2","title":"層間傾斜累積的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Track cumulative stack tilt","text":"相同方向小偏差可逐層累積。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Small same-direction errors accumulate layer by layer. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-405-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設每層厚度差造成 0.02° 同向傾斜，八層最壞累積 0.16°；在 5 mm 跨距對應約 14 µm 高差。實際須以逐層量測確認是否同向。","textEn":"Eight hypothetical layers each tilted 0.02° in the same direction accumulate 0.16° worst case, corresponding to about 14 µm over 5 mm. Layer measurements must establish whether tilts align."},{"id":"pk-405-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"將角度、局部間隙和接點共平面分開檢查。頂層平面不能單獨證明每層內部接合完整，需結合電測與非破壞影像。","textEn":"Inspect angle, local gap and contact coplanarity separately. A flat top does not prove every internal interface is sound; combine electrical and nondestructive evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「層間傾斜累積」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Track cumulative stack tilt?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","累積傾斜未超過下一層對位預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：相同方向小偏差可逐層累積。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cumulative tilt fits next-layer alignment budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Small same-direction errors accumulate layer by layer."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「累積傾斜未超過下一層對位預算」。相同方向小偏差可逐層累積，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cumulative tilt fits next-layer alignment budgets. Small same-direction errors accumulate layer by layer, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":405,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-404"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-406","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"層間連通抽測","titleEn":"Sample interlayer continuity","objective":"判斷「層間連通抽測」是否滿足此具體條件：新增電阻與預期接點數一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Sample interlayer continuity meets this specific condition: Added resistance agrees with expected contact count.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較新加層前後測試鏈電阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare test-chain resistance before and after adding a layer. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：新增電阻與預期接點數一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Added resistance agrees with expected contact count. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"總阻增加異常可能定位新層接點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Abnormal resistance increment can identify new-layer contacts. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"新增電阻與預期接點數一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Added resistance agrees with expected contact count. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-406-k1","title":"層間連通抽測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Sample interlayer continuity","text":"可檢驗條件為「新增電阻與預期接點數一致」。可藉由「比較新加層前後測試鏈電阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Added resistance agrees with expected contact count. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare test-chain resistance before and after adding a layer. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-406-k2","title":"層間連通抽測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Sample interlayer continuity","text":"總阻增加異常可能定位新層接點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Abnormal resistance increment can identify new-layer contacts. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「層間連通抽測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Sample interlayer continuity?","options":["忽略此失效線索：總阻增加異常可能定位新層接點。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","新增電阻與預期接點數一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Abnormal resistance increment can identify new-layer contacts.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Added resistance agrees with expected contact count","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「新增電阻與預期接點數一致」。總阻增加異常可能定位新層接點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Added resistance agrees with expected contact count. Abnormal resistance increment can identify new-layer contacts, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":406,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-405"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-407","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊內部空洞","titleEn":"Inspect internal stack voids","objective":"判斷「堆疊內部空洞」是否滿足此具體條件：異常可定位至特定層間介面。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect internal stack voids meets this specific condition: Anomalies can be assigned to a specific interface.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較不同焦深的聲學或斷層影像。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare acoustic or tomographic images at multiple depths. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：異常可定位至特定層間介面；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Anomalies can be assigned to a specific interface. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"重疊回波容易混淆缺陷深度。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Overlapping echoes can confuse defect depth. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"異常可定位至特定層間介面；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Anomalies can be assigned to a specific interface. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-407-k1","title":"堆疊內部空洞的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect internal stack voids","text":"可檢驗條件為「異常可定位至特定層間介面」。可藉由「比較不同焦深的聲學或斷層影像」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Anomalies can be assigned to a specific interface. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare acoustic or tomographic images at multiple depths. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-407-k2","title":"堆疊內部空洞的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect internal stack voids","text":"重疊回波容易混淆缺陷深度。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Overlapping echoes can confuse defect depth. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊內部空洞」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect internal stack voids?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：重疊回波容易混淆缺陷深度。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","異常可定位至特定層間介面"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Overlapping echoes can confuse defect depth.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Anomalies can be assigned to a specific interface"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「異常可定位至特定層間介面」。重疊回波容易混淆缺陷深度，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Anomalies can be assigned to a specific interface. Overlapping echoes can confuse defect depth, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":407,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-406"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-408","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"上層晶粒偏移","titleEn":"Measure upper-layer displacement","objective":"判斷「上層晶粒偏移」是否滿足此具體條件：每層相對與絕對偏移皆達標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure upper-layer displacement meets this specific condition: Relative and absolute layer offsets meet limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以基底座標比較各層角落位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare layer corners in the base coordinate frame. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：每層相對與絕對偏移皆達標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Relative and absolute layer offsets meet limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"僅逐層比對可漏掉總體漂移。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Adjacent-layer checks can miss total drift. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"每層相對與絕對偏移皆達標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Relative and absolute layer offsets meet limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-408-k1","title":"上層晶粒偏移的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure upper-layer displacement","text":"可檢驗條件為「每層相對與絕對偏移皆達標」。可藉由「以基底座標比較各層角落位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Relative and absolute layer offsets meet limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare layer corners in the base coordinate frame. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-408-k2","title":"上層晶粒偏移的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure upper-layer displacement","text":"僅逐層比對可漏掉總體漂移。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Adjacent-layer checks can miss total drift. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「上層晶粒偏移」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure upper-layer displacement?","options":["每層相對與絕對偏移皆達標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：僅逐層比對可漏掉總體漂移。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Relative and absolute layer offsets meet limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Adjacent-layer checks can miss total drift.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「每層相對與絕對偏移皆達標」。僅逐層比對可漏掉總體漂移，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Relative and absolute layer offsets meet limits. Adjacent-layer checks can miss total drift, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":408,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-407"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-409","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"上蓋晶粒支線","titleEn":"Evaluate a top-cap die branch","objective":"判斷「上蓋晶粒支線」是否滿足此具體條件：上蓋接觸不造成局部集中載荷。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate a top-cap die branch meets this specific condition: Cap contact avoids concentrated local loads.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較上蓋平整度與機械支撐面。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare cap flatness and mechanical support surfaces. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：上蓋接觸不造成局部集中載荷；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cap contact avoids concentrated local loads. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"凸起缺陷可把載荷傳入記憶體薄晶粒。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Protrusions can transfer load into thin memory dies. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"上蓋接觸不造成局部集中載荷；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cap contact avoids concentrated local loads. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-409-k1","title":"上蓋晶粒支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate a top-cap die branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「上蓋接觸不造成局部集中載荷」。可藉由「比較上蓋平整度與機械支撐面」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cap contact avoids concentrated local loads. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare cap flatness and mechanical support surfaces. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-409-k2","title":"上蓋晶粒支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate a top-cap die branch","text":"凸起缺陷可把載荷傳入記憶體薄晶粒。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Protrusions can transfer load into thin memory dies. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「上蓋晶粒支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate a top-cap die branch?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","上蓋接觸不造成局部集中載荷","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：凸起缺陷可把載荷傳入記憶體薄晶粒。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cap contact avoids concentrated local loads","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Protrusions can transfer load into thin memory dies."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「上蓋接觸不造成局部集中載荷」。凸起缺陷可把載荷傳入記憶體薄晶粒，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cap contact avoids concentrated local loads. Protrusions can transfer load into thin memory dies, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":409,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-408"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-410","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊封膠流動","titleEn":"Evaluate stack molding flow","objective":"判斷「堆疊封膠流動」是否滿足此具體條件：流動可填滿狹縫且晶粒位移受控。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate stack molding flow meets this specific condition: Flow fills gaps with controlled die displacement.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：觀察狹縫填膠前緣與模流壓力。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Observe gap-filling fronts and mold-flow pressure. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：流動可填滿狹縫且晶粒位移受控；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Flow fills gaps with controlled die displacement. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"高速流前緣可能推移或困氣。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Fast flow fronts can displace dies or trap air. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"流動可填滿狹縫且晶粒位移受控；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Flow fills gaps with controlled die displacement. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-410-k1","title":"堆疊封膠流動的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate stack molding flow","text":"可檢驗條件為「流動可填滿狹縫且晶粒位移受控」。可藉由「觀察狹縫填膠前緣與模流壓力」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Flow fills gaps with controlled die displacement. Evidence can be developed through this action: Observe gap-filling fronts and mold-flow pressure. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-410-k2","title":"堆疊封膠流動的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate stack molding flow","text":"高速流前緣可能推移或困氣。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Fast flow fronts can displace dies or trap air. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊封膠流動」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate stack molding flow?","options":["忽略此失效線索：高速流前緣可能推移或困氣。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","流動可填滿狹縫且晶粒位移受控","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Fast flow fronts can displace dies or trap air.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Flow fills gaps with controlled die displacement","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「流動可填滿狹縫且晶粒位移受控」。高速流前緣可能推移或困氣，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Flow fills gaps with controlled die displacement. Fast flow fronts can displace dies or trap air, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":410,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-409"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-411","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊固化形變","titleEn":"Assess stack cure deformation","objective":"判斷「堆疊固化形變」是否滿足此具體條件：收縮未造成不可接受翹曲。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess stack cure deformation meets this specific condition: Shrinkage does not produce unacceptable warpage.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較固化前後層序與外形。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare layer alignment and shape before and after cure. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：收縮未造成不可接受翹曲；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Shrinkage does not produce unacceptable warpage. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"固化收縮可改變層間剪應力。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Cure shrinkage changes interlayer shear stress. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"收縮未造成不可接受翹曲；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Shrinkage does not produce unacceptable warpage. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-411-k1","title":"堆疊固化形變的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess stack cure deformation","text":"可檢驗條件為「收縮未造成不可接受翹曲」。可藉由「比較固化前後層序與外形」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Shrinkage does not produce unacceptable warpage. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare layer alignment and shape before and after cure. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-411-k2","title":"堆疊固化形變的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess stack cure deformation","text":"固化收縮可改變層間剪應力。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Cure shrinkage changes interlayer shear stress. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊固化形變」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess stack cure deformation?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：固化收縮可改變層間剪應力。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","收縮未造成不可接受翹曲"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Cure shrinkage changes interlayer shear stress.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Shrinkage does not produce unacceptable warpage"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「收縮未造成不可接受翹曲」。固化收縮可改變層間剪應力，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Shrinkage does not produce unacceptable warpage. Cure shrinkage changes interlayer shear stress, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":411,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-410"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-412","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊切割邊界","titleEn":"Inspect stack singulation boundaries","objective":"判斷「堆疊切割邊界」是否滿足此具體條件：切割面無跨層延伸裂縫。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect stack singulation boundaries meets this specific condition: Cut faces lack cracks propagating across layers.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤切割面穿越不同材料位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Trace cuts through different materials. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：切割面無跨層延伸裂縫；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cut faces lack cracks propagating across layers. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"材料硬度差可能使裂紋偏折。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Hardness differences can deflect cracks. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"切割面無跨層延伸裂縫；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cut faces lack cracks propagating across layers. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-412-k1","title":"堆疊切割邊界的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect stack singulation boundaries","text":"可檢驗條件為「切割面無跨層延伸裂縫」。可藉由「追蹤切割面穿越不同材料位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cut faces lack cracks propagating across layers. Evidence can be developed through this action: Trace cuts through different materials. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-412-k2","title":"堆疊切割邊界的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect stack singulation boundaries","text":"材料硬度差可能使裂紋偏折。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Hardness differences can deflect cracks. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊切割邊界」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect stack singulation boundaries?","options":["切割面無跨層延伸裂縫","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：材料硬度差可能使裂紋偏折。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Cut faces lack cracks propagating across layers","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Hardness differences can deflect cracks.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「切割面無跨層延伸裂縫」。材料硬度差可能使裂紋偏折，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cut faces lack cracks propagating across layers. Hardness differences can deflect cracks, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":412,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-411"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-413","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"完整堆疊電測","titleEn":"Test a completed stack","objective":"判斷「完整堆疊電測」是否滿足此具體條件：所有目標層均有可追溯測試結果。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Test a completed stack meets this specific condition: Every target layer has traceable test results.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：聯合讀取基底控制與上層記憶體測試。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Read base-control and upper-memory tests together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：所有目標層均有可追溯測試結果；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Every target layer has traceable test results. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只測基底功能會漏掉上層記憶體失效。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Base-only testing misses upper-memory faults. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"所有目標層均有可追溯測試結果；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Every target layer has traceable test results. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-413-k1","title":"完整堆疊電測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Test a completed stack","text":"可檢驗條件為「所有目標層均有可追溯測試結果」。可藉由「聯合讀取基底控制與上層記憶體測試」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Every target layer has traceable test results. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read base-control and upper-memory tests together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-413-k2","title":"完整堆疊電測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Test a completed stack","text":"只測基底功能會漏掉上層記憶體失效。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Base-only testing misses upper-memory faults. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「完整堆疊電測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Test a completed stack?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","所有目標層均有可追溯測試結果","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只測基底功能會漏掉上層記憶體失效。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Every target layer has traceable test results","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Base-only testing misses upper-memory faults."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「所有目標層均有可追溯測試結果」。只測基底功能會漏掉上層記憶體失效，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Every target layer has traceable test results. Base-only testing misses upper-memory faults, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":413,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-412"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-414","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"冗餘通道修復驗證","titleEn":"Verify redundant-channel repair","objective":"判斷「冗餘通道修復驗證」是否滿足此具體條件：修復後功能合格且映射可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify redundant-channel repair meets this specific condition: Function passes with a traceable repair map.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較修復對映前後的故障位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare fault maps before and after repair mapping. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：修復後功能合格且映射可追溯；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Function passes with a traceable repair map. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"未保存映射會使後段診斷失真。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Missing repair maps distort downstream diagnosis. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"修復後功能合格且映射可追溯；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Function passes with a traceable repair map. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-414-k1","title":"冗餘通道修復驗證的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify redundant-channel repair","text":"可檢驗條件為「修復後功能合格且映射可追溯」。可藉由「比較修復對映前後的故障位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Function passes with a traceable repair map. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare fault maps before and after repair mapping. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-414-k2","title":"冗餘通道修復驗證的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify redundant-channel repair","text":"未保存映射會使後段診斷失真。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Missing repair maps distort downstream diagnosis. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「冗餘通道修復驗證」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify redundant-channel repair?","options":["忽略此失效線索：未保存映射會使後段診斷失真。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","修復後功能合格且映射可追溯","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Missing repair maps distort downstream diagnosis.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Function passes with a traceable repair map","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「修復後功能合格且映射可追溯」。未保存映射會使後段診斷失真，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Function passes with a traceable repair map. Missing repair maps distort downstream diagnosis, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":414,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-413"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-415","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊散熱路徑","titleEn":"Evaluate stack thermal paths","objective":"判斷「堆疊散熱路徑」是否滿足此具體條件：最高溫層符合設計限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate stack thermal paths meets this specific condition: The hottest layer meets design limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較各層功耗與通往散熱面的熱阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare layer power with resistance to cooling surfaces. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：最高溫層符合設計限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: The hottest layer meets design limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只看上表面溫度會低估內層熱點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Top-surface temperature can underestimate internal hotspots. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最高溫層符合設計限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"The hottest layer meets design limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-415-k1","title":"堆疊散熱路徑的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate stack thermal paths","text":"可檢驗條件為「最高溫層符合設計限制」。可藉由「比較各層功耗與通往散熱面的熱阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: The hottest layer meets design limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare layer power with resistance to cooling surfaces. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-415-k2","title":"堆疊散熱路徑的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate stack thermal paths","text":"只看上表面溫度會低估內層熱點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Top-surface temperature can underestimate internal hotspots. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-415-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設八層各發熱 1 W、頂面為唯一熱出口，最底層熱流須穿過更多界面。不能用 8 W 乘單一晶粒熱阻來保證每層結溫。","textEn":"For eight hypothetical 1 W layers with only top cooling, lower layers traverse more interfaces. Multiplying 8 W by one die's resistance does not establish all junction temperatures."},{"id":"pk-415-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"建立逐層熱阻與發熱節點，另列側向擴散和 TSV 熱通道。空間上不均勻的記憶體活動需要非均勻功率輸入。","textEn":"Build per-layer resistance and source nodes, including spreading and TSV thermal paths. Nonuniform memory activity requires nonuniform power inputs."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊散熱路徑」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate stack thermal paths?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只看上表面溫度會低估內層熱點。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最高溫層符合設計限制"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Top-surface temperature can underestimate internal hotspots.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","The hottest layer meets design limits"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「最高溫層符合設計限制」。只看上表面溫度會低估內層熱點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: The hottest layer meets design limits. Top-surface temperature can underestimate internal hotspots, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic","v9deep-thermal-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":415,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-414"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-416","stageId":"pk-m16","title":"堆疊良品移交","titleEn":"Transfer known-good stacks","objective":"判斷「堆疊良品移交」是否滿足此具體條件：移交記錄完整且對應實體識別。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Transfer known-good stacks meets this specific condition: Handoff records match physical identifiers.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：封存晶粒譜系修復圖與整疊測試結果。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Archive die genealogy, repair maps, and stack results. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：移交記錄完整且對應實體識別；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Handoff records match physical identifiers. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"混批或識別失配會破壞良品可信度。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Lot mixing or ID mismatch invalidates good-stack evidence. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"移交記錄完整且對應實體識別；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Handoff records match physical identifiers. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-416-k1","title":"堆疊良品移交的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Transfer known-good stacks","text":"可檢驗條件為「移交記錄完整且對應實體識別」。可藉由「封存晶粒譜系修復圖與整疊測試結果」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Handoff records match physical identifiers. Evidence can be developed through this action: Archive die genealogy, repair maps, and stack results. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-416-k2","title":"堆疊良品移交的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Transfer known-good stacks","text":"混批或識別失配會破壞良品可信度。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Lot mixing or ID mismatch invalidates good-stack evidence. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「堆疊良品移交」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Transfer known-good stacks?","options":["移交記錄完整且對應實體識別","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：混批或識別失配會破壞良品可信度。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Handoff records match physical identifiers","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Lot mixing or ID mismatch invalidates good-stack evidence.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「移交記錄完整且對應實體識別」。混批或識別失配會破壞良品可信度，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Handoff records match physical identifiers. Lot mixing or ID mismatch invalidates good-stack evidence, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-kgd","pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-tsmc-soic"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":416,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-415"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依產品採微凸塊熱壓、回焊或混合鍵合；本模組比較支線，不宣稱任何供應商固定堆疊配方。","routeEn":"Products may use microbump thermocompression, reflow, or hybrid bonding; these are alternatives, not a supplier recipe.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m17","title":"底部填膠、上蓋與散熱整合","titleEn":"Underfill, lid, and thermal integration","description":"膠材承擔熱機械應力轉移，導熱介面承擔熱流；兩者功能不同，必須共同評估翹曲與熱阻。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Adhesives transfer thermomechanical stress while thermal interfaces carry heat; their different functions require joint warpage and thermal-resistance evaluation. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","order":17,"sequence":17,"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-417","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"充填間隙流阻","titleEn":"Evaluate underfill gap-flow resistance","objective":"判斷「充填間隙流阻」是否滿足此具體條件：預期流動能在已驗證作業窗內完成。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate underfill gap-flow resistance meets this specific condition: Predicted flow completes within the validated working window.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較不同晶粒間隙的充填時間模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare fill-time models for different die gaps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：預期流動能在已驗證作業窗內完成；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Predicted flow completes within the validated working window. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"間隙變小會顯著增加流動阻力。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Smaller gaps substantially increase flow resistance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"預期流動能在已驗證作業窗內完成；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Predicted flow completes within the validated working window. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-417-k1","title":"充填間隙流阻的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate underfill gap-flow resistance","text":"可檢驗條件為「預期流動能在已驗證作業窗內完成」。可藉由「比較不同晶粒間隙的充填時間模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Predicted flow completes within the validated working window. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare fill-time models for different die gaps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-417-k2","title":"充填間隙流阻的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate underfill gap-flow resistance","text":"間隙變小會顯著增加流動阻力。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Smaller gaps substantially increase flow resistance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-417-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"狹縫毛細填充的簡化模型常有時間隨流長平方增加的趨勢；路長由 5 增至 10 mm，其他假設不變時時間量級可增四倍。真實填料與固化會偏離。","textEn":"Simplified slit-capillary models often give fill time scaling with length squared; increasing 5 to 10 mm can quadruple time if assumptions hold. Fillers and curing cause deviations."},{"id":"pk-417-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"先檢查表面潤濕、間隙一致性和排氣路徑，再比較黏度。兩個入口相遇可能困氣，填滿外緣不能證明內部無空洞。","textEn":"Check wetting, gap uniformity and venting before comparing viscosity. Converging fronts can trap gas; a filled edge does not prove a void-free interior."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「充填間隙流阻」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate underfill gap-flow resistance?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","預期流動能在已驗證作業窗內完成","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：間隙變小會顯著增加流動阻力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Predicted flow completes within the validated working window","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Smaller gaps substantially increase flow resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「預期流動能在已驗證作業窗內完成」。間隙變小會顯著增加流動阻力，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Predicted flow completes within the validated working window. Smaller gaps substantially increase flow resistance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":417,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-418","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"填膠材料可用狀態","titleEn":"Check underfill material working state","objective":"判斷「填膠材料可用狀態」是否滿足此具體條件：材料狀態符合供應商核准要求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check underfill material working state meets this specific condition: Material condition meets approved supplier requirements.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對儲存解凍及可使用時間紀錄。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare storage, thaw, and working-time records. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：材料狀態符合供應商核准要求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Material condition meets approved supplier requirements. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"外觀正常仍可能已超出可用時間。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Normal appearance can conceal expired working time. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"材料狀態符合供應商核准要求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Material condition meets approved supplier requirements. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-418-k1","title":"填膠材料可用狀態的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check underfill material working state","text":"可檢驗條件為「材料狀態符合供應商核准要求」。可藉由「比對儲存解凍及可使用時間紀錄」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Material condition meets approved supplier requirements. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare storage, thaw, and working-time records. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-418-k2","title":"填膠材料可用狀態的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check underfill material working state","text":"外觀正常仍可能已超出可用時間。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Normal appearance can conceal expired working time. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「填膠材料可用狀態」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check underfill material working state?","options":["忽略此失效線索：外觀正常仍可能已超出可用時間。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","材料狀態符合供應商核准要求","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Normal appearance can conceal expired working time.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Material condition meets approved supplier requirements","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「材料狀態符合供應商核准要求」。外觀正常仍可能已超出可用時間，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Material condition meets approved supplier requirements. Normal appearance can conceal expired working time, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":418,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-417"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-419","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"填膠黏度溫度關係","titleEn":"Interpret underfill viscosity versus temperature","objective":"判斷「填膠黏度溫度關係」是否滿足此具體條件：使用黏度對應實際溫度及剪切條件。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret underfill viscosity versus temperature meets this specific condition: Viscosity matches actual temperature and shear conditions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：讀取材料流變曲線並與模型匹配。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Match material rheology curves to the model. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：使用黏度對應實際溫度及剪切條件；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Viscosity matches actual temperature and shear conditions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"常溫單點黏度不能代表充填流動。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"One room-temperature viscosity cannot represent filling. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"使用黏度對應實際溫度及剪切條件；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Viscosity matches actual temperature and shear conditions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-419-k1","title":"填膠黏度溫度關係的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret underfill viscosity versus temperature","text":"可檢驗條件為「使用黏度對應實際溫度及剪切條件」。可藉由「讀取材料流變曲線並與模型匹配」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Viscosity matches actual temperature and shear conditions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Match material rheology curves to the model. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-419-k2","title":"填膠黏度溫度關係的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret underfill viscosity versus temperature","text":"常溫單點黏度不能代表充填流動。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"One room-temperature viscosity cannot represent filling. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「填膠黏度溫度關係」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret underfill viscosity versus temperature?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：常溫單點黏度不能代表充填流動。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","使用黏度對應實際溫度及剪切條件"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: One room-temperature viscosity cannot represent filling.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Viscosity matches actual temperature and shear conditions"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「使用黏度對應實際溫度及剪切條件」。常溫單點黏度不能代表充填流動，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Viscosity matches actual temperature and shear conditions. One room-temperature viscosity cannot represent filling, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":419,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-418"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-420","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"焊點殘留與潤濕","titleEn":"Assess joint residue and underfill wetting","objective":"判斷「焊點殘留與潤濕」是否滿足此具體條件：流前緣連續且無污染引起的停滯。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess joint residue and underfill wetting meets this specific condition: Fronts remain continuous without contamination-induced arrest.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較清潔狀態下的潤濕前緣。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare wetting fronts for different cleanliness states. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：流前緣連續且無污染引起的停滯；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Fronts remain continuous without contamination-induced arrest. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"助焊殘留可使局部拒膠。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Flux residue can locally inhibit wetting. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"流前緣連續且無污染引起的停滯；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Fronts remain continuous without contamination-induced arrest. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-420-k1","title":"焊點殘留與潤濕的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess joint residue and underfill wetting","text":"可檢驗條件為「流前緣連續且無污染引起的停滯」。可藉由「比較清潔狀態下的潤濕前緣」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Fronts remain continuous without contamination-induced arrest. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare wetting fronts for different cleanliness states. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-420-k2","title":"焊點殘留與潤濕的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess joint residue and underfill wetting","text":"助焊殘留可使局部拒膠。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Flux residue can locally inhibit wetting. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊點殘留與潤濕」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess joint residue and underfill wetting?","options":["流前緣連續且無污染引起的停滯","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：助焊殘留可使局部拒膠。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Fronts remain continuous without contamination-induced arrest","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Flux residue can locally inhibit wetting.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「流前緣連續且無污染引起的停滯」。助焊殘留可使局部拒膠，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Fronts remain continuous without contamination-induced arrest. Flux residue can locally inhibit wetting, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":420,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-419"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-421","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"填膠點位設計","titleEn":"Plan underfill dispense locations","objective":"判斷「填膠點位設計」是否滿足此具體條件：點位保留連續排氣出口。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Plan underfill dispense locations meets this specific condition: Dispense locations preserve continuous vent outlets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：模擬不同邊緣點位的排氣路徑。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Simulate venting for alternative edge dispense locations. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：點位保留連續排氣出口；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Dispense locations preserve continuous vent outlets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"多邊同時點膠可包圍未排出的氣體。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Simultaneous multiedge dispensing can enclose air. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"點位保留連續排氣出口；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Dispense locations preserve continuous vent outlets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-421-k1","title":"填膠點位設計的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Plan underfill dispense locations","text":"可檢驗條件為「點位保留連續排氣出口」。可藉由「模擬不同邊緣點位的排氣路徑」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Dispense locations preserve continuous vent outlets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Simulate venting for alternative edge dispense locations. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-421-k2","title":"填膠點位設計的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Plan underfill dispense locations","text":"多邊同時點膠可包圍未排出的氣體。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Simultaneous multiedge dispensing can enclose air. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「填膠點位設計」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Plan underfill dispense locations?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","點位保留連續排氣出口","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：多邊同時點膠可包圍未排出的氣體。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Dispense locations preserve continuous vent outlets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Simultaneous multiedge dispensing can enclose air."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「點位保留連續排氣出口」。多邊同時點膠可包圍未排出的氣體，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Dispense locations preserve continuous vent outlets. Simultaneous multiedge dispensing can enclose air, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":421,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-420"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-422","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"點膠質量校準","titleEn":"Calibrate dispensed underfill mass","objective":"判斷「點膠質量校準」是否滿足此具體條件：兩種估計在量測不確定度內一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Calibrate dispensed underfill mass meets this specific condition: Estimates agree within measurement uncertainty.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較重量與光學體積估計。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare mass with optical volume estimates. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：兩種估計在量測不確定度內一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Estimates agree within measurement uncertainty. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"針頭拉絲會使重量與落點不一致。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Needle stringing can separate dispensed mass from intended placement. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"兩種估計在量測不確定度內一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Estimates agree within measurement uncertainty. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-422-k1","title":"點膠質量校準的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Calibrate dispensed underfill mass","text":"可檢驗條件為「兩種估計在量測不確定度內一致」。可藉由「比較重量與光學體積估計」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Estimates agree within measurement uncertainty. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare mass with optical volume estimates. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-422-k2","title":"點膠質量校準的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Calibrate dispensed underfill mass","text":"針頭拉絲會使重量與落點不一致。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Needle stringing can separate dispensed mass from intended placement. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「點膠質量校準」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Calibrate dispensed underfill mass?","options":["忽略此失效線索：針頭拉絲會使重量與落點不一致。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","兩種估計在量測不確定度內一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Needle stringing can separate dispensed mass from intended placement.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Estimates agree within measurement uncertainty","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「兩種估計在量測不確定度內一致」。針頭拉絲會使重量與落點不一致，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Estimates agree within measurement uncertainty. Needle stringing can separate dispensed mass from intended placement, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":422,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-421"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-423","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"晶粒邊緣膠前緣","titleEn":"Track the die-edge underfill front","objective":"判斷「晶粒邊緣膠前緣」是否滿足此具體條件：前緣到達遠端且未留未填區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Track the die-edge underfill front meets this specific condition: Front reaches the far side without unfilled regions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：讀取透明模型的時間序列。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Read time-series images from the transparent model. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：前緣到達遠端且未留未填區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Front reaches the far side without unfilled regions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"可見邊緣濕潤不代表底部已充滿。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Visible edge wetting does not prove complete bottom filling. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"前緣到達遠端且未留未填區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Front reaches the far side without unfilled regions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-423-k1","title":"晶粒邊緣膠前緣的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Track the die-edge underfill front","text":"可檢驗條件為「前緣到達遠端且未留未填區」。可藉由「讀取透明模型的時間序列」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Front reaches the far side without unfilled regions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read time-series images from the transparent model. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-423-k2","title":"晶粒邊緣膠前緣的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Track the die-edge underfill front","text":"可見邊緣濕潤不代表底部已充滿。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Visible edge wetting does not prove complete bottom filling. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒邊緣膠前緣」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Track the die-edge underfill front?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：可見邊緣濕潤不代表底部已充滿。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","前緣到達遠端且未留未填區"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Visible edge wetting does not prove complete bottom filling.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Front reaches the far side without unfilled regions"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「前緣到達遠端且未留未填區」。可見邊緣濕潤不代表底部已充滿，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Front reaches the far side without unfilled regions. Visible edge wetting does not prove complete bottom filling, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":423,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-422"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-424","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"充填膠圓角","titleEn":"Measure underfill fillets","objective":"判斷「充填膠圓角」是否滿足此具體條件：圓角不侵入接點或光學保留區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure underfill fillets meets this specific condition: Fillets avoid contact and optical keep-out regions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測四邊膠圓角高度與延伸距離。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure fillet height and extension on all sides. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：圓角不侵入接點或光學保留區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Fillets avoid contact and optical keep-out regions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過大圓角可增加局部剛性或污染。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Excessive fillets can increase stiffness or contaminate adjacent regions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"圓角不侵入接點或光學保留區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Fillets avoid contact and optical keep-out regions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-424-k1","title":"充填膠圓角的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure underfill fillets","text":"可檢驗條件為「圓角不侵入接點或光學保留區」。可藉由「量測四邊膠圓角高度與延伸距離」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Fillets avoid contact and optical keep-out regions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure fillet height and extension on all sides. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-424-k2","title":"充填膠圓角的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure underfill fillets","text":"過大圓角可增加局部剛性或污染。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Excessive fillets can increase stiffness or contaminate adjacent regions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「充填膠圓角」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure underfill fillets?","options":["圓角不侵入接點或光學保留區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過大圓角可增加局部剛性或污染。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Fillets avoid contact and optical keep-out regions","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Excessive fillets can increase stiffness or contaminate adjacent regions.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「圓角不侵入接點或光學保留區」。過大圓角可增加局部剛性或污染，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Fillets avoid contact and optical keep-out regions. Excessive fillets can increase stiffness or contaminate adjacent regions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":424,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-423"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-425","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"固化反應程度","titleEn":"Assess underfill cure state","objective":"判斷「固化反應程度」是否滿足此具體條件：反應程度與核准固化狀態一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess underfill cure state meets this specific condition: Cure state agrees with the qualified reference.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較殘餘反應熱與參考樣本。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare residual reaction heat with reference samples. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：反應程度與核准固化狀態一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cure state agrees with the qualified reference. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"爐內溫度紀錄不能直接證明膠體固化。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Oven temperature records alone do not prove adhesive cure. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"反應程度與核准固化狀態一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cure state agrees with the qualified reference. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-425-k1","title":"固化反應程度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess underfill cure state","text":"可檢驗條件為「反應程度與核准固化狀態一致」。可藉由「比較殘餘反應熱與參考樣本」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cure state agrees with the qualified reference. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare residual reaction heat with reference samples. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-425-k2","title":"固化反應程度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess underfill cure state","text":"爐內溫度紀錄不能直接證明膠體固化。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Oven temperature records alone do not prove adhesive cure. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「固化反應程度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess underfill cure state?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","反應程度與核准固化狀態一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：爐內溫度紀錄不能直接證明膠體固化。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cure state agrees with the qualified reference","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Oven temperature records alone do not prove adhesive cure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「反應程度與核准固化狀態一致」。爐內溫度紀錄不能直接證明膠體固化，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cure state agrees with the qualified reference. Oven temperature records alone do not prove adhesive cure, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":425,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-424"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-426","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"填膠玻璃轉移行為","titleEn":"Interpret underfill glass transition","objective":"判斷「填膠玻璃轉移行為」是否滿足此具體條件：模型涵蓋轉移區前後的材料變化。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret underfill glass transition meets this specific condition: Models cover material changes across the transition.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較模數隨溫度曲線與使用範圍。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare modulus-temperature curves with service range. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：模型涵蓋轉移區前後的材料變化；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Models cover material changes across the transition. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單一常數模數可低估溫度依賴應力。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Constant modulus can underestimate temperature-dependent stress. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"模型涵蓋轉移區前後的材料變化；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Models cover material changes across the transition. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-426-k1","title":"填膠玻璃轉移行為的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret underfill glass transition","text":"可檢驗條件為「模型涵蓋轉移區前後的材料變化」。可藉由「比較模數隨溫度曲線與使用範圍」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Models cover material changes across the transition. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare modulus-temperature curves with service range. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-426-k2","title":"填膠玻璃轉移行為的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret underfill glass transition","text":"單一常數模數可低估溫度依賴應力。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Constant modulus can underestimate temperature-dependent stress. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「填膠玻璃轉移行為」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret underfill glass transition?","options":["忽略此失效線索：單一常數模數可低估溫度依賴應力。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","模型涵蓋轉移區前後的材料變化","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Constant modulus can underestimate temperature-dependent stress.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Models cover material changes across the transition","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「模型涵蓋轉移區前後的材料變化」。單一常數模數可低估溫度依賴應力，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Models cover material changes across the transition. Constant modulus can underestimate temperature-dependent stress, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":426,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-425"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-427","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"填膠空洞聲學檢查","titleEn":"Inspect underfill voids acoustically","objective":"判斷「填膠空洞聲學檢查」是否滿足此具體條件：空洞位置與面積符合允收規則。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect underfill voids acoustically meets this specific condition: Void location and area meet acceptance rules.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：判讀不同焦深的介面回波。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Interpret interface echoes at multiple focal depths. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：空洞位置與面積符合允收規則；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Void location and area meet acceptance rules. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"反射差異需先排除幾何與耦合因素。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Contrast requires excluding geometry and coupling effects. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"空洞位置與面積符合允收規則；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Void location and area meet acceptance rules. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-427-k1","title":"填膠空洞聲學檢查的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect underfill voids acoustically","text":"可檢驗條件為「空洞位置與面積符合允收規則」。可藉由「判讀不同焦深的介面回波」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Void location and area meet acceptance rules. Evidence can be developed through this action: Interpret interface echoes at multiple focal depths. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-427-k2","title":"填膠空洞聲學檢查的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect underfill voids acoustically","text":"反射差異需先排除幾何與耦合因素。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Contrast requires excluding geometry and coupling effects. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「填膠空洞聲學檢查」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect underfill voids acoustically?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：反射差異需先排除幾何與耦合因素。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","空洞位置與面積符合允收規則"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Contrast requires excluding geometry and coupling effects.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Void location and area meet acceptance rules"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「空洞位置與面積符合允收規則」。反射差異需先排除幾何與耦合因素，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Void location and area meet acceptance rules. Contrast requires excluding geometry and coupling effects, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":427,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-426"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-428","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"晶粒角落應力","titleEn":"Evaluate die-corner stress","objective":"判斷「晶粒角落應力」是否滿足此具體條件：設計指標對網格細化已穩定。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate die-corner stress meets this specific condition: Design indicators stabilize with mesh refinement.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較角落網格收斂後的應力指標。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare converged stress measures near die corners. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：設計指標對網格細化已穩定；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Design indicators stabilize with mesh refinement. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"奇異點峰值不能直接當材料失效值。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Singular peak stress cannot directly represent material failure. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"設計指標對網格細化已穩定；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Design indicators stabilize with mesh refinement. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-428-k1","title":"晶粒角落應力的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate die-corner stress","text":"可檢驗條件為「設計指標對網格細化已穩定」。可藉由「比較角落網格收斂後的應力指標」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Design indicators stabilize with mesh refinement. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare converged stress measures near die corners. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-428-k2","title":"晶粒角落應力的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate die-corner stress","text":"奇異點峰值不能直接當材料失效值。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Singular peak stress cannot directly represent material failure. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒角落應力」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate die-corner stress?","options":["設計指標對網格細化已穩定","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：奇異點峰值不能直接當材料失效值。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Design indicators stabilize with mesh refinement","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Singular peak stress cannot directly represent material failure.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「設計指標對網格細化已穩定」。奇異點峰值不能直接當材料失效值，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Design indicators stabilize with mesh refinement. Singular peak stress cannot directly represent material failure, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":428,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-427"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-429","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"上蓋接觸面平整度","titleEn":"Measure lid contact-face flatness","objective":"判斷「上蓋接觸面平整度」是否滿足此具體條件：接觸面幾何允許目標介面厚度。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure lid contact-face flatness meets this specific condition: Contact geometry permits the target bondline thickness.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較上蓋內表面與晶粒高度圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare lid inner surface and die-height maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接觸面幾何允許目標介面厚度；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Contact geometry permits the target bondline thickness. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"上蓋外表面平坦不代表內面平坦。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Flat outer surfaces do not establish inner-face flatness. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接觸面幾何允許目標介面厚度；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Contact geometry permits the target bondline thickness. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-429-k1","title":"上蓋接觸面平整度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure lid contact-face flatness","text":"可檢驗條件為「接觸面幾何允許目標介面厚度」。可藉由「比較上蓋內表面與晶粒高度圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Contact geometry permits the target bondline thickness. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare lid inner surface and die-height maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-429-k2","title":"上蓋接觸面平整度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure lid contact-face flatness","text":"上蓋外表面平坦不代表內面平坦。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Flat outer surfaces do not establish inner-face flatness. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「上蓋接觸面平整度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure lid contact-face flatness?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","接觸面幾何允許目標介面厚度","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：上蓋外表面平坦不代表內面平坦。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Contact geometry permits the target bondline thickness","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Flat outer surfaces do not establish inner-face flatness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「接觸面幾何允許目標介面厚度」。上蓋外表面平坦不代表內面平坦，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Contact geometry permits the target bondline thickness. Flat outer surfaces do not establish inner-face flatness, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":429,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-428"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-430","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"多晶粒高度補償","titleEn":"Plan multi-die height compensation","objective":"判斷「多晶粒高度補償」是否滿足此具體條件：各晶粒可在容許厚度內接觸導熱層。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Plan multi-die height compensation meets this specific condition: All dies contact thermal layers within allowed thickness.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較不同晶粒頂面與上蓋台階。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare die tops and lid pedestal heights. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各晶粒可在容許厚度內接觸導熱層；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All dies contact thermal layers within allowed thickness. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"最高晶粒可能承受過多裝配載荷。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"The tallest die can carry excessive assembly load. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各晶粒可在容許厚度內接觸導熱層；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All dies contact thermal layers within allowed thickness. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-430-k1","title":"多晶粒高度補償的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Plan multi-die height compensation","text":"可檢驗條件為「各晶粒可在容許厚度內接觸導熱層」。可藉由「比較不同晶粒頂面與上蓋台階」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All dies contact thermal layers within allowed thickness. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare die tops and lid pedestal heights. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-430-k2","title":"多晶粒高度補償的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Plan multi-die height compensation","text":"最高晶粒可能承受過多裝配載荷。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"The tallest die can carry excessive assembly load. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「多晶粒高度補償」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Plan multi-die height compensation?","options":["忽略此失效線索：最高晶粒可能承受過多裝配載荷。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各晶粒可在容許厚度內接觸導熱層","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: The tallest die can carry excessive assembly load.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","All dies contact thermal layers within allowed thickness","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「各晶粒可在容許厚度內接觸導熱層」。最高晶粒可能承受過多裝配載荷，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All dies contact thermal layers within allowed thickness. The tallest die can carry excessive assembly load, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":430,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-429"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-431","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"導熱介面材料選擇","titleEn":"Compare thermal-interface material branches","objective":"判斷「導熱介面材料選擇」是否滿足此具體條件：材料兼顧熱阻與封裝應變需求。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Compare thermal-interface material branches meets this specific condition: Material meets thermal resistance and strain needs.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較接觸熱阻及機械順應性。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare contact resistance and mechanical compliance. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：材料兼顧熱阻與封裝應變需求；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Material meets thermal resistance and strain needs. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"高本體導熱率不保證低接觸熱阻。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"High bulk conductivity does not ensure low contact resistance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"材料兼顧熱阻與封裝應變需求；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Material meets thermal resistance and strain needs. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-431-k1","title":"導熱介面材料選擇的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Compare thermal-interface material branches","text":"可檢驗條件為「材料兼顧熱阻與封裝應變需求」。可藉由「比較接觸熱阻及機械順應性」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Material meets thermal resistance and strain needs. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare contact resistance and mechanical compliance. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-431-k2","title":"導熱介面材料選擇的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Compare thermal-interface material branches","text":"高本體導熱率不保證低接觸熱阻。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"High bulk conductivity does not ensure low contact resistance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「導熱介面材料選擇」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Compare thermal-interface material branches?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：高本體導熱率不保證低接觸熱阻。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","材料兼顧熱阻與封裝應變需求"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: High bulk conductivity does not ensure low contact resistance.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Material meets thermal resistance and strain needs"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「材料兼顧熱阻與封裝應變需求」。高本體導熱率不保證低接觸熱阻，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Material meets thermal resistance and strain needs. High bulk conductivity does not ensure low contact resistance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":431,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-430"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-432","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"導熱層塗佈覆蓋","titleEn":"Inspect thermal-interface coverage","objective":"判斷「導熱層塗佈覆蓋」是否滿足此具體條件：目標熱區連續覆蓋且不污染保留區。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect thermal-interface coverage meets this specific condition: Hot regions are covered without contaminating keep-outs.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較塗佈圖形與實際發熱區。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare deposited patterns with heat-producing regions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：目標熱區連續覆蓋且不污染保留區；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Hot regions are covered without contaminating keep-outs. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只看總塗佈量會漏掉熱點缺膠。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Total deposited mass can hide uncovered hotspots. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"目標熱區連續覆蓋且不污染保留區；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Hot regions are covered without contaminating keep-outs. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-432-k1","title":"導熱層塗佈覆蓋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect thermal-interface coverage","text":"可檢驗條件為「目標熱區連續覆蓋且不污染保留區」。可藉由「比較塗佈圖形與實際發熱區」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Hot regions are covered without contaminating keep-outs. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare deposited patterns with heat-producing regions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-432-k2","title":"導熱層塗佈覆蓋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect thermal-interface coverage","text":"只看總塗佈量會漏掉熱點缺膠。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Total deposited mass can hide uncovered hotspots. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「導熱層塗佈覆蓋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect thermal-interface coverage?","options":["目標熱區連續覆蓋且不污染保留區","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只看總塗佈量會漏掉熱點缺膠。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Hot regions are covered without contaminating keep-outs","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Total deposited mass can hide uncovered hotspots.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「目標熱區連續覆蓋且不污染保留區」。只看總塗佈量會漏掉熱點缺膠，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Hot regions are covered without contaminating keep-outs. Total deposited mass can hide uncovered hotspots, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":432,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-431"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-433","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"導熱層厚度控制","titleEn":"Control thermal-interface thickness","objective":"判斷「導熱層厚度控制」是否滿足此具體條件：厚度與接觸壓力均在材料工作窗內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Control thermal-interface thickness meets this specific condition: Thickness and pressure meet material operating windows.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以支撐幾何推算壓合後厚度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Infer compressed thickness from support geometry. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：厚度與接觸壓力均在材料工作窗內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Thickness and pressure meet material operating windows. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過薄層可能無法吸收翹曲間隙。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"An overly thin layer may not accommodate warpage gaps. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"厚度與接觸壓力均在材料工作窗內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Thickness and pressure meet material operating windows. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-433-k1","title":"導熱層厚度控制的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Control thermal-interface thickness","text":"可檢驗條件為「厚度與接觸壓力均在材料工作窗內」。可藉由「以支撐幾何推算壓合後厚度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Thickness and pressure meet material operating windows. Evidence can be developed through this action: Infer compressed thickness from support geometry. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-433-k2","title":"導熱層厚度控制的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Control thermal-interface thickness","text":"過薄層可能無法吸收翹曲間隙。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"An overly thin layer may not accommodate warpage gaps. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-433-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設 TIM 厚 50 µm、k=5 W/(m·K)、面積 100 mm²，塊材 R=0.1 K/W；50 W 對應 5 K，未計兩面接觸熱阻。","textEn":"For hypothetical TIM thickness 50 µm, k=5 W/(m·K) and area 100 mm², bulk R=0.1 K/W; 50 W gives 5 K before contact resistance."},{"id":"pk-433-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"減薄可以降低塊材項，但若不足以填補翹曲而形成乾接觸，總熱阻反而可能上升。將厚度、覆蓋率、壓力與熱測結果共同判讀。","textEn":"Thinning lowers bulk resistance, but insufficient gap filling under warpage can increase total resistance. Interpret thickness, coverage, pressure and thermal data together."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「導熱層厚度控制」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Control thermal-interface thickness?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","厚度與接觸壓力均在材料工作窗內","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過薄層可能無法吸收翹曲間隙。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Thickness and pressure meet material operating windows","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: An overly thin layer may not accommodate warpage gaps."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「厚度與接觸壓力均在材料工作窗內」。過薄層可能無法吸收翹曲間隙，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Thickness and pressure meet material operating windows. An overly thin layer may not accommodate warpage gaps, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization","v9deep-thermal-contact"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":433,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-432"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-434","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"上蓋膠路點膠","titleEn":"Inspect lid-adhesive dispense paths","objective":"判斷「上蓋膠路點膠」是否滿足此具體條件：膠路符合結構需求且未封堵必要排氣。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect lid-adhesive dispense paths meets this specific condition: Paths meet structural needs without blocking required vents.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查膠路連續性與排氣設計。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect adhesive-path continuity and vent design. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：膠路符合結構需求且未封堵必要排氣；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Paths meet structural needs without blocking required vents. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"連續封閉膠環未必適合所有封裝。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A closed adhesive ring is not suitable for every package. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"膠路符合結構需求且未封堵必要排氣；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Paths meet structural needs without blocking required vents. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-434-k1","title":"上蓋膠路點膠的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect lid-adhesive dispense paths","text":"可檢驗條件為「膠路符合結構需求且未封堵必要排氣」。可藉由「檢查膠路連續性與排氣設計」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Paths meet structural needs without blocking required vents. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect adhesive-path continuity and vent design. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-434-k2","title":"上蓋膠路點膠的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect lid-adhesive dispense paths","text":"連續封閉膠環未必適合所有封裝。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A closed adhesive ring is not suitable for every package. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「上蓋膠路點膠」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect lid-adhesive dispense paths?","options":["忽略此失效線索：連續封閉膠環未必適合所有封裝。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","膠路符合結構需求且未封堵必要排氣","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: A closed adhesive ring is not suitable for every package.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Paths meet structural needs without blocking required vents","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「膠路符合結構需求且未封堵必要排氣」。連續封閉膠環未必適合所有封裝，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Paths meet structural needs without blocking required vents. A closed adhesive ring is not suitable for every package, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":434,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-433"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-435","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"補強環放置","titleEn":"Place a stiffener ring virtually","objective":"判斷「補強環放置」是否滿足此具體條件：對位及接觸不干涉焊墊與元件。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Place a stiffener ring virtually meets this specific condition: Alignment and contact avoid pads and components.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較補強環與基板邊界位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare stiffener positions with substrate boundaries. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：對位及接觸不干涉焊墊與元件；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Alignment and contact avoid pads and components. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"偏移補強環可改變局部翹曲約束。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Shifted stiffeners alter local warpage constraints. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"對位及接觸不干涉焊墊與元件；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Alignment and contact avoid pads and components. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-435-k1","title":"補強環放置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Place a stiffener ring virtually","text":"可檢驗條件為「對位及接觸不干涉焊墊與元件」。可藉由「比較補強環與基板邊界位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Alignment and contact avoid pads and components. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare stiffener positions with substrate boundaries. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-435-k2","title":"補強環放置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Place a stiffener ring virtually","text":"偏移補強環可改變局部翹曲約束。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Shifted stiffeners alter local warpage constraints. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「補強環放置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Place a stiffener ring virtually?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：偏移補強環可改變局部翹曲約束。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","對位及接觸不干涉焊墊與元件"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Shifted stiffeners alter local warpage constraints.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Alignment and contact avoid pads and components"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「對位及接觸不干涉焊墊與元件」。偏移補強環可改變局部翹曲約束，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Alignment and contact avoid pads and components. Shifted stiffeners alter local warpage constraints, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":435,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-434"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-436","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"上蓋壓合載荷分布","titleEn":"Assess lid-attach load distribution","objective":"判斷「上蓋壓合載荷分布」是否滿足此具體條件：局部壓力不超過核准機械限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess lid-attach load distribution meets this specific condition: Local pressure remains within approved mechanical limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較載荷圖與晶粒支撐點。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare load maps and die support locations. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：局部壓力不超過核准機械限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Local pressure remains within approved mechanical limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"總載荷合格仍可能有局部過壓。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Acceptable total load can hide local overpressure. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"局部壓力不超過核准機械限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Local pressure remains within approved mechanical limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-436-k1","title":"上蓋壓合載荷分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess lid-attach load distribution","text":"可檢驗條件為「局部壓力不超過核准機械限制」。可藉由「比較載荷圖與晶粒支撐點」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Local pressure remains within approved mechanical limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare load maps and die support locations. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-436-k2","title":"上蓋壓合載荷分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess lid-attach load distribution","text":"總載荷合格仍可能有局部過壓。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Acceptable total load can hide local overpressure. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「上蓋壓合載荷分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess lid-attach load distribution?","options":["局部壓力不超過核准機械限制","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：總載荷合格仍可能有局部過壓。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Local pressure remains within approved mechanical limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Acceptable total load can hide local overpressure.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「局部壓力不超過核准機械限制」。總載荷合格仍可能有局部過壓，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Local pressure remains within approved mechanical limits. Acceptable total load can hide local overpressure, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":436,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-435"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-437","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"上蓋固化後翹曲","titleEn":"Map postcure package warpage","objective":"判斷「上蓋固化後翹曲」是否滿足此具體條件：整體翹曲保留板級組裝餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map postcure package warpage meets this specific condition: Package warpage preserves board-assembly allowance.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在共同溫度下量測上蓋與基板曲面。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure lid and substrate shape at a common temperature. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：整體翹曲保留板級組裝餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Package warpage preserves board-assembly allowance. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"固化收縮可使上蓋與基板相互拉彎。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Cure shrinkage can bow lid and substrate together. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"整體翹曲保留板級組裝餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Package warpage preserves board-assembly allowance. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-437-k1","title":"上蓋固化後翹曲的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map postcure package warpage","text":"可檢驗條件為「整體翹曲保留板級組裝餘量」。可藉由「在共同溫度下量測上蓋與基板曲面」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Package warpage preserves board-assembly allowance. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure lid and substrate shape at a common temperature. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-437-k2","title":"上蓋固化後翹曲的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map postcure package warpage","text":"固化收縮可使上蓋與基板相互拉彎。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Cure shrinkage can bow lid and substrate together. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「上蓋固化後翹曲」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map postcure package warpage?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","整體翹曲保留板級組裝餘量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：固化收縮可使上蓋與基板相互拉彎。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Package warpage preserves board-assembly allowance","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Cure shrinkage can bow lid and substrate together."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「整體翹曲保留板級組裝餘量」。固化收縮可使上蓋與基板相互拉彎，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Package warpage preserves board-assembly allowance. Cure shrinkage can bow lid and substrate together, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":437,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-436"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-438","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"介面泵出支線","titleEn":"Assess thermal-interface pump-out","objective":"判斷「介面泵出支線」是否滿足此具體條件：邊界遷移與熱阻變化符合耐久目標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess thermal-interface pump-out meets this specific condition: Migration and resistance change meet durability targets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較熱循環前後材料邊界與熱阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare material edges and thermal resistance after cycling. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：邊界遷移與熱阻變化符合耐久目標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Migration and resistance change meet durability targets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"初始熱阻低仍可能有長期材料泵出。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Low initial resistance does not exclude long-term pump-out. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"邊界遷移與熱阻變化符合耐久目標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Migration and resistance change meet durability targets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-438-k1","title":"介面泵出支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess thermal-interface pump-out","text":"可檢驗條件為「邊界遷移與熱阻變化符合耐久目標」。可藉由「比較熱循環前後材料邊界與熱阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Migration and resistance change meet durability targets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare material edges and thermal resistance after cycling. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-438-k2","title":"介面泵出支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess thermal-interface pump-out","text":"初始熱阻低仍可能有長期材料泵出。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Low initial resistance does not exclude long-term pump-out. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介面泵出支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess thermal-interface pump-out?","options":["忽略此失效線索：初始熱阻低仍可能有長期材料泵出。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","邊界遷移與熱阻變化符合耐久目標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Low initial resistance does not exclude long-term pump-out.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Migration and resistance change meet durability targets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「邊界遷移與熱阻變化符合耐久目標」。初始熱阻低仍可能有長期材料泵出，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Migration and resistance change meet durability targets. Low initial resistance does not exclude long-term pump-out, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":438,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-437"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-439","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"封裝熱阻量測","titleEn":"Measure package thermal resistance","objective":"判斷「封裝熱阻量測」是否滿足此具體條件：測試邊界及功耗定義完整可重現。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure package thermal resistance meets this specific condition: Boundary conditions and power definitions are reproducible.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：用已校正溫感與功耗計算溫升。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Calculate temperature rise using calibrated sensors and power. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：測試邊界及功耗定義完整可重現；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Boundary conditions and power definitions are reproducible. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"未定義冷卻邊界無法比較熱阻。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Undefined cooling boundaries invalidate thermal comparisons. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"測試邊界及功耗定義完整可重現；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Boundary conditions and power definitions are reproducible. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-439-k1","title":"封裝熱阻量測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure package thermal resistance","text":"可檢驗條件為「測試邊界及功耗定義完整可重現」。可藉由「用已校正溫感與功耗計算溫升」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Boundary conditions and power definitions are reproducible. Evidence can be developed through this action: Calculate temperature rise using calibrated sensors and power. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-439-k2","title":"封裝熱阻量測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure package thermal resistance","text":"未定義冷卻邊界無法比較熱阻。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Undefined cooling boundaries invalidate thermal comparisons. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「封裝熱阻量測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure package thermal resistance?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：未定義冷卻邊界無法比較熱阻。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","測試邊界及功耗定義完整可重現"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Undefined cooling boundaries invalidate thermal comparisons.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Boundary conditions and power definitions are reproducible"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「測試邊界及功耗定義完整可重現」。未定義冷卻邊界無法比較熱阻，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Boundary conditions and power definitions are reproducible. Undefined cooling boundaries invalidate thermal comparisons, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":439,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-438"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-440","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"瞬態熱路分析","titleEn":"Interpret transient thermal paths","objective":"判斷「瞬態熱路分析」是否滿足此具體條件：主要時間常數與模型界面一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret transient thermal paths meets this specific condition: Major time constants agree with modeled interfaces.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較熱階躍響應與結構模型。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare thermal-step responses with structure models. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：主要時間常數與模型界面一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Major time constants agree with modeled interfaces. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單一穩態值可能掩蓋介面分層。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A steady-state value can hide interface separation. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"主要時間常數與模型界面一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Major time constants agree with modeled interfaces. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-440-k1","title":"瞬態熱路分析的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret transient thermal paths","text":"可檢驗條件為「主要時間常數與模型界面一致」。可藉由「比較熱階躍響應與結構模型」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Major time constants agree with modeled interfaces. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare thermal-step responses with structure models. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-440-k2","title":"瞬態熱路分析的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret transient thermal paths","text":"單一穩態值可能掩蓋介面分層。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A steady-state value can hide interface separation. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「瞬態熱路分析」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret transient thermal paths?","options":["主要時間常數與模型界面一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：單一穩態值可能掩蓋介面分層。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Major time constants agree with modeled interfaces","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: A steady-state value can hide interface separation.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「主要時間常數與模型界面一致」。單一穩態值可能掩蓋介面分層，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Major time constants agree with modeled interfaces. A steady-state value can hide interface separation, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":440,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-439"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-441","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"液冷冷板支線","titleEn":"Assess a liquid-cold-plate branch","objective":"判斷「液冷冷板支線」是否滿足此具體條件：熱與機械介面均滿足系統規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess a liquid-cold-plate branch meets this specific condition: Thermal and mechanical interfaces meet system criteria.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對接觸壓力流量及洩漏測試紀錄。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare contact pressure, flow, and leak-test records. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：熱與機械介面均滿足系統規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Thermal and mechanical interfaces meet system criteria. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"增加流量不能補救不良固體接觸。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Increasing flow cannot remedy poor solid contact. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"熱與機械介面均滿足系統規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Thermal and mechanical interfaces meet system criteria. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-441-k1","title":"液冷冷板支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess a liquid-cold-plate branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「熱與機械介面均滿足系統規範」。可藉由「比對接觸壓力流量及洩漏測試紀錄」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Thermal and mechanical interfaces meet system criteria. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare contact pressure, flow, and leak-test records. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-441-k2","title":"液冷冷板支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess a liquid-cold-plate branch","text":"增加流量不能補救不良固體接觸。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Increasing flow cannot remedy poor solid contact. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「液冷冷板支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess a liquid-cold-plate branch?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","熱與機械介面均滿足系統規範","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：增加流量不能補救不良固體接觸。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Thermal and mechanical interfaces meet system criteria","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Increasing flow cannot remedy poor solid contact."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「熱與機械介面均滿足系統規範」。增加流量不能補救不良固體接觸，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Thermal and mechanical interfaces meet system criteria. Increasing flow cannot remedy poor solid contact, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":441,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-440"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-442","stageId":"pk-m17","title":"熱機耦合介面放行","titleEn":"Release coupled thermal-mechanical interfaces","objective":"判斷「熱機耦合介面放行」是否滿足此具體條件：三者均達標且使用相同樣品識別。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Release coupled thermal-mechanical interfaces meets this specific condition: All pass with consistent specimen identity.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：同時檢視熱阻翹曲與介面完整性。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Review thermal resistance, bow, and interface integrity together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：三者均達標且使用相同樣品識別；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All pass with consistent specimen identity. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"混用不同樣品資料會形成虛假通過。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Mixing specimens can produce a false combined pass. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"三者均達標且使用相同樣品識別；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All pass with consistent specimen identity. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-442-k1","title":"熱機耦合介面放行的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Release coupled thermal-mechanical interfaces","text":"可檢驗條件為「三者均達標且使用相同樣品識別」。可藉由「同時檢視熱阻翹曲與介面完整性」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All pass with consistent specimen identity. Evidence can be developed through this action: Review thermal resistance, bow, and interface integrity together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-442-k2","title":"熱機耦合介面放行的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Release coupled thermal-mechanical interfaces","text":"混用不同樣品資料會形成虛假通過。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Mixing specimens can produce a false combined pass. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「熱機耦合介面放行」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Release coupled thermal-mechanical interfaces?","options":["忽略此失效線索：混用不同樣品資料會形成虛假通過。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","三者均達標且使用相同樣品識別","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Mixing specimens can produce a false combined pass.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","All pass with consistent specimen identity","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「三者均達標且使用相同樣品識別」。混用不同樣品資料會形成虛假通過，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All pass with consistent specimen identity. Mixing specimens can produce a false combined pass, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-henkel-underfill","pkb-henkel-lid","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":442,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-441"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依封裝選毛細充填、模封充填或預施膠；有蓋、無蓋及液冷介面是替代結構。","routeEn":"Select capillary, molded, or preapplied underfill; lidded, lidless, and liquid-cooled interfaces are alternative structures.","photoId":"bga-section","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察封裝截面、基板與外部焊球；它不是 TSV／HBM／混合鍵合的專屬截面，也不能判定內部空洞。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe a package cross section, substrate and external balls; it is not a TSV/HBM/hybrid-bond cross section and cannot establish internal voiding.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m18","title":"植球、基板組裝與外觀終檢","titleEn":"Ball attach, substrate assembly, and final inspection","description":"對外焊球的數量、共平面度與潤濕品質連接封裝與板級製造，必須區分封裝缺陷與後續貼板缺陷。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Ball count, coplanarity, and wetting connect package and board assembly; package defects must be distinguished from later board-attach defects. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","order":18,"sequence":18,"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-443","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"基板焊墊清潔度","titleEn":"Inspect substrate-pad cleanliness","objective":"判斷「基板焊墊清潔度」是否滿足此具體條件：可焊表面無阻礙潤濕的污染。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect substrate-pad cleanliness meets this specific condition: Solderable surfaces lack wetting-blocking contamination.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較焊墊表面影像與污染指標。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare pad images and contamination indicators. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：可焊表面無阻礙潤濕的污染；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Solderable surfaces lack wetting-blocking contamination. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"外觀明亮不一定代表無有機殘留。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Bright appearance does not exclude organic residue. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"可焊表面無阻礙潤濕的污染；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Solderable surfaces lack wetting-blocking contamination. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-443-k1","title":"基板焊墊清潔度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect substrate-pad cleanliness","text":"可檢驗條件為「可焊表面無阻礙潤濕的污染」。可藉由「比較焊墊表面影像與污染指標」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Solderable surfaces lack wetting-blocking contamination. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare pad images and contamination indicators. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-443-k2","title":"基板焊墊清潔度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect substrate-pad cleanliness","text":"外觀明亮不一定代表無有機殘留。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Bright appearance does not exclude organic residue. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「基板焊墊清潔度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect substrate-pad cleanliness?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：外觀明亮不一定代表無有機殘留。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","可焊表面無阻礙潤濕的污染"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Bright appearance does not exclude organic residue.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Solderable surfaces lack wetting-blocking contamination"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「可焊表面無阻礙潤濕的污染」。外觀明亮不一定代表無有機殘留，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Solderable surfaces lack wetting-blocking contamination. Bright appearance does not exclude organic residue, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":443,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-444","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"植球焊墊定義","titleEn":"Verify ball-pad definition","objective":"判斷「植球焊墊定義」是否滿足此具體條件：焊墊形態與設計資料一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify ball-pad definition meets this specific condition: Pad geometry matches the design definition.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：區分防焊定義與非防焊定義焊墊。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Distinguish solder-mask-defined and nonsolder-mask-defined pads. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：焊墊形態與設計資料一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Pad geometry matches the design definition. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"使用錯誤焊墊模型會誤估應力。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Wrong pad models misestimate stress. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"焊墊形態與設計資料一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Pad geometry matches the design definition. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-444-k1","title":"植球焊墊定義的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify ball-pad definition","text":"可檢驗條件為「焊墊形態與設計資料一致」。可藉由「區分防焊定義與非防焊定義焊墊」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Pad geometry matches the design definition. Evidence can be developed through this action: Distinguish solder-mask-defined and nonsolder-mask-defined pads. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-444-k2","title":"植球焊墊定義的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify ball-pad definition","text":"使用錯誤焊墊模型會誤估應力。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Wrong pad models misestimate stress. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「植球焊墊定義」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify ball-pad definition?","options":["焊墊形態與設計資料一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：使用錯誤焊墊模型會誤估應力。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Pad geometry matches the design definition","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Wrong pad models misestimate stress.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「焊墊形態與設計資料一致」。使用錯誤焊墊模型會誤估應力，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Pad geometry matches the design definition. Wrong pad models misestimate stress, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":444,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-443"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-445","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球合金版本","titleEn":"Verify solder-ball alloy revision","objective":"判斷「焊球合金版本」是否滿足此具體條件：合金版本與核准熱歷程相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify solder-ball alloy revision meets this specific condition: Alloy revision matches the qualified thermal history.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：核對球材識別與接合材料清單。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Match ball identity to joining material lists. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：合金版本與核准熱歷程相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Alloy revision matches the qualified thermal history. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"外形相同的合金可能有不同接合需求。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Identical ball geometry can hide different joining needs. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"合金版本與核准熱歷程相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Alloy revision matches the qualified thermal history. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-445-k1","title":"焊球合金版本的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify solder-ball alloy revision","text":"可檢驗條件為「合金版本與核准熱歷程相容」。可藉由「核對球材識別與接合材料清單」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Alloy revision matches the qualified thermal history. Evidence can be developed through this action: Match ball identity to joining material lists. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-445-k2","title":"焊球合金版本的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify solder-ball alloy revision","text":"外形相同的合金可能有不同接合需求。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Identical ball geometry can hide different joining needs. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球合金版本」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify solder-ball alloy revision?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","合金版本與核准熱歷程相容","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：外形相同的合金可能有不同接合需求。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Alloy revision matches the qualified thermal history","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Identical ball geometry can hide different joining needs."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「合金版本與核准熱歷程相容」。外形相同的合金可能有不同接合需求，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Alloy revision matches the qualified thermal history. Identical ball geometry can hide different joining needs, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":445,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-444"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-446","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球尺寸分布","titleEn":"Measure solder-ball size distribution","objective":"判斷「焊球尺寸分布」是否滿足此具體條件：尺寸尾端符合規定的批次限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure solder-ball size distribution meets this specific condition: Distribution tails meet lot limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較抽樣直徑與體積統計。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare sampled diameter and volume statistics. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：尺寸尾端符合規定的批次限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Distribution tails meet lot limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只報平均直徑會漏掉過大過小球。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Mean diameter hides oversized and undersized balls. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"尺寸尾端符合規定的批次限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Distribution tails meet lot limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-446-k1","title":"焊球尺寸分布的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure solder-ball size distribution","text":"可檢驗條件為「尺寸尾端符合規定的批次限制」。可藉由「比較抽樣直徑與體積統計」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Distribution tails meet lot limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare sampled diameter and volume statistics. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-446-k2","title":"焊球尺寸分布的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure solder-ball size distribution","text":"只報平均直徑會漏掉過大過小球。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Mean diameter hides oversized and undersized balls. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球尺寸分布」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure solder-ball size distribution?","options":["忽略此失效線索：只報平均直徑會漏掉過大過小球。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","尺寸尾端符合規定的批次限制","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Mean diameter hides oversized and undersized balls.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Distribution tails meet lot limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「尺寸尾端符合規定的批次限制」。只報平均直徑會漏掉過大過小球，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Distribution tails meet lot limits. Mean diameter hides oversized and undersized balls, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":446,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-445"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-447","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"助焊劑塗佈厚度","titleEn":"Inspect flux-coating thickness","objective":"判斷「助焊劑塗佈厚度」是否滿足此具體條件：每個焊墊覆蓋量在核准窗內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect flux-coating thickness meets this specific condition: Coverage per pad remains within approved windows.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：量測印刷或轉印後膜厚地圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure printed or transferred flux-thickness maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：每個焊墊覆蓋量在核准窗內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Coverage per pad remains within approved windows. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部缺膠可造成球材暫時固定不足。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Insufficient flux can weaken temporary ball retention. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"每個焊墊覆蓋量在核准窗內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Coverage per pad remains within approved windows. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-447-k1","title":"助焊劑塗佈厚度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect flux-coating thickness","text":"可檢驗條件為「每個焊墊覆蓋量在核准窗內」。可藉由「量測印刷或轉印後膜厚地圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Coverage per pad remains within approved windows. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure printed or transferred flux-thickness maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-447-k2","title":"助焊劑塗佈厚度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect flux-coating thickness","text":"局部缺膠可造成球材暫時固定不足。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Insufficient flux can weaken temporary ball retention. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「助焊劑塗佈厚度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect flux-coating thickness?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：局部缺膠可造成球材暫時固定不足。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","每個焊墊覆蓋量在核准窗內"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Insufficient flux can weaken temporary ball retention.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Coverage per pad remains within approved windows"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「每個焊墊覆蓋量在核准窗內」。局部缺膠可造成球材暫時固定不足，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Coverage per pad remains within approved windows. Insufficient flux can weaken temporary ball retention, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":447,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-446"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-448","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"植球模板孔位","titleEn":"Verify ball-placement stencil apertures","objective":"判斷「植球模板孔位」是否滿足此具體條件：孔位與避讓區對應正確。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify ball-placement stencil apertures meets this specific condition: Apertures and exclusion zones map correctly.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將模板孔座標與基板焊墊重疊。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay stencil apertures with substrate pads. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：孔位與避讓區對應正確；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Apertures and exclusion zones map correctly. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"模板方向反置會造成系統性漏球。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Reversed stencils cause systematic missing balls. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"孔位與避讓區對應正確；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Apertures and exclusion zones map correctly. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-448-k1","title":"植球模板孔位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify ball-placement stencil apertures","text":"可檢驗條件為「孔位與避讓區對應正確」。可藉由「將模板孔座標與基板焊墊重疊」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Apertures and exclusion zones map correctly. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay stencil apertures with substrate pads. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-448-k2","title":"植球模板孔位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify ball-placement stencil apertures","text":"模板方向反置會造成系統性漏球。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Reversed stencils cause systematic missing balls. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「植球模板孔位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify ball-placement stencil apertures?","options":["孔位與避讓區對應正確","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：模板方向反置會造成系統性漏球。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Apertures and exclusion zones map correctly","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Reversed stencils cause systematic missing balls.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「孔位與避讓區對應正確」。模板方向反置會造成系統性漏球，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Apertures and exclusion zones map correctly. Reversed stencils cause systematic missing balls, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":448,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-447"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-449","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"單球落位","titleEn":"Inspect individual ball seating","objective":"判斷「單球落位」是否滿足此具體條件：每個指定焊墊恰有一顆球。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect individual ball seating meets this specific condition: Each specified pad carries exactly one ball.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：觀察每個孔位的球數與偏心。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect ball count and eccentricity at each site. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：每個指定焊墊恰有一顆球；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Each specified pad carries exactly one ball. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"雙球或偏球可能在回焊後橋接。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Double or off-center balls can bridge after reflow. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"每個指定焊墊恰有一顆球；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Each specified pad carries exactly one ball. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-449-k1","title":"單球落位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect individual ball seating","text":"可檢驗條件為「每個指定焊墊恰有一顆球」。可藉由「觀察每個孔位的球數與偏心」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Each specified pad carries exactly one ball. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect ball count and eccentricity at each site. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-449-k2","title":"單球落位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect individual ball seating","text":"雙球或偏球可能在回焊後橋接。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Double or off-center balls can bridge after reflow. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「單球落位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect individual ball seating?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","每個指定焊墊恰有一顆球","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：雙球或偏球可能在回焊後橋接。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Each specified pad carries exactly one ball","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Double or off-center balls can bridge after reflow."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「每個指定焊墊恰有一顆球」。雙球或偏球可能在回焊後橋接，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Each specified pad carries exactly one ball. Double or off-center balls can bridge after reflow, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":449,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-448"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-450","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"植球後漏球檢測","titleEn":"Detect missing balls after placement","objective":"判斷「植球後漏球檢測」是否滿足此具體條件：所有應植位置都有可辨識球體。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Detect missing balls after placement meets this specific condition: Every populated position contains a detectable ball.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對實際球圖與設計球圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare actual and designed ball maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：所有應植位置都有可辨識球體；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Every populated position contains a detectable ball. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"設計空位不可被誤判成漏球。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Intentional vacancies must not be labeled missing balls. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"所有應植位置都有可辨識球體；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Every populated position contains a detectable ball. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-450-k1","title":"植球後漏球檢測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Detect missing balls after placement","text":"可檢驗條件為「所有應植位置都有可辨識球體」。可藉由「比對實際球圖與設計球圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Every populated position contains a detectable ball. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare actual and designed ball maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-450-k2","title":"植球後漏球檢測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Detect missing balls after placement","text":"設計空位不可被誤判成漏球。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Intentional vacancies must not be labeled missing balls. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「植球後漏球檢測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Detect missing balls after placement?","options":["忽略此失效線索：設計空位不可被誤判成漏球。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","所有應植位置都有可辨識球體","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Intentional vacancies must not be labeled missing balls.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Every populated position contains a detectable ball","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「所有應植位置都有可辨識球體」。設計空位不可被誤判成漏球，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Every populated position contains a detectable ball. Intentional vacancies must not be labeled missing balls, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":450,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-449"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-451","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球暫固定搬運","titleEn":"Evaluate ball retention during transfer","objective":"判斷「焊球暫固定搬運」是否滿足此具體條件：球體未滑移或脫落。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate ball retention during transfer meets this specific condition: Balls neither slip nor detach.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較搬運前後球心座標。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare ball centers before and after transfer. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：球體未滑移或脫落；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Balls neither slip nor detach. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"搬運振動可能改變未回焊球位。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Transfer vibration can move unreflowed balls. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"球體未滑移或脫落；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Balls neither slip nor detach. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-451-k1","title":"焊球暫固定搬運的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate ball retention during transfer","text":"可檢驗條件為「球體未滑移或脫落」。可藉由「比較搬運前後球心座標」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Balls neither slip nor detach. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare ball centers before and after transfer. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-451-k2","title":"焊球暫固定搬運的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate ball retention during transfer","text":"搬運振動可能改變未回焊球位。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Transfer vibration can move unreflowed balls. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球暫固定搬運」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate ball retention during transfer?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：搬運振動可能改變未回焊球位。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","球體未滑移或脫落"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Transfer vibration can move unreflowed balls.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Balls neither slip nor detach"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「球體未滑移或脫落」。搬運振動可能改變未回焊球位，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Balls neither slip nor detach. Transfer vibration can move unreflowed balls, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":451,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-450"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-452","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"回焊熱電偶位置","titleEn":"Plan reflow temperature sensing","objective":"判斷「回焊熱電偶位置」是否滿足此具體條件：最冷及最熱位置都有量測代表。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Plan reflow temperature sensing meets this specific condition: Cold and hot locations are represented.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：選取熱容量差異最大的監測位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Select monitoring locations with contrasting thermal mass. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：最冷及最熱位置都有量測代表；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cold and hot locations are represented. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只放中央感測器會漏掉邊緣差異。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Center-only sensing misses edge differences. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最冷及最熱位置都有量測代表；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cold and hot locations are represented. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-452-k1","title":"回焊熱電偶位置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Plan reflow temperature sensing","text":"可檢驗條件為「最冷及最熱位置都有量測代表」。可藉由「選取熱容量差異最大的監測位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cold and hot locations are represented. Evidence can be developed through this action: Select monitoring locations with contrasting thermal mass. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-452-k2","title":"回焊熱電偶位置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Plan reflow temperature sensing","text":"只放中央感測器會漏掉邊緣差異。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Center-only sensing misses edge differences. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「回焊熱電偶位置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Plan reflow temperature sensing?","options":["最冷及最熱位置都有量測代表","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只放中央感測器會漏掉邊緣差異。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Cold and hot locations are represented","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Center-only sensing misses edge differences.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「最冷及最熱位置都有量測代表」。只放中央感測器會漏掉邊緣差異，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cold and hot locations are represented. Center-only sensing misses edge differences, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":452,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-451"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-453","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"回焊熱歷程核對","titleEn":"Verify ball-attach reflow history","objective":"判斷「回焊熱歷程核對」是否滿足此具體條件：接點與封裝材料限制同時滿足。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify ball-attach reflow history meets this specific condition: Joint and package material limits both pass.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將球材與封裝限制共同套用到溫度曲線。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Apply alloy and package limits to temperature histories. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：接點與封裝材料限制同時滿足；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Joint and package material limits both pass. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"焊料達成接合不代表封裝未受熱傷害。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Joined solder does not prove an undamaged package. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"接點與封裝材料限制同時滿足；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Joint and package material limits both pass. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-453-k1","title":"回焊熱歷程核對的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify ball-attach reflow history","text":"可檢驗條件為「接點與封裝材料限制同時滿足」。可藉由「將球材與封裝限制共同套用到溫度曲線」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Joint and package material limits both pass. Evidence can be developed through this action: Apply alloy and package limits to temperature histories. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-453-k2","title":"回焊熱歷程核對的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify ball-attach reflow history","text":"焊料達成接合不代表封裝未受熱傷害。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Joined solder does not prove an undamaged package. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「回焊熱歷程核對」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify ball-attach reflow history?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","接點與封裝材料限制同時滿足","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：焊料達成接合不代表封裝未受熱傷害。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Joint and package material limits both pass","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Joined solder does not prove an undamaged package."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「接點與封裝材料限制同時滿足」。焊料達成接合不代表封裝未受熱傷害，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Joint and package material limits both pass. Joined solder does not prove an undamaged package, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":453,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-452"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-454","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"回焊時翹曲","titleEn":"Assess warpage during reflow","objective":"判斷「回焊時翹曲」是否滿足此具體條件：高溫接觸幾何仍符合接合預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess warpage during reflow meets this specific condition: Hot contact geometry still fits joining budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較加熱與冷卻中的共平面度。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare coplanarity during heating and cooling. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：高溫接觸幾何仍符合接合預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Hot contact geometry still fits joining budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"室溫平坦不能排除高溫翹曲。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not exclude hot warpage. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"高溫接觸幾何仍符合接合預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Hot contact geometry still fits joining budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-454-k1","title":"回焊時翹曲的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess warpage during reflow","text":"可檢驗條件為「高溫接觸幾何仍符合接合預算」。可藉由「比較加熱與冷卻中的共平面度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Hot contact geometry still fits joining budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare coplanarity during heating and cooling. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-454-k2","title":"回焊時翹曲的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess warpage during reflow","text":"室溫平坦不能排除高溫翹曲。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not exclude hot warpage. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-454-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設室溫焊球共平面差 20 µm，回焊熱態基板又增加 40 µm 局部翹曲，不能只用室溫 20 µm 判斷所有焊點接觸。方向不同時須用實際形貌疊合。","textEn":"A hypothetical 20 µm room-temperature coplanarity spread plus 40 µm hot substrate distortion cannot be assessed from the room value alone; differing directions require actual shape registration."},{"id":"pk-454-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"將焊球塌陷、基板熱態形狀與助焊劑作用時間同步比較。焊點開路可源於動態脫離，不一定是原始漏球。","textEn":"Compare ball collapse, hot substrate shape and flux timing together. An open can arise from dynamic separation rather than an initially missing ball."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「回焊時翹曲」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess warpage during reflow?","options":["忽略此失效線索：室溫平坦不能排除高溫翹曲。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","高溫接觸幾何仍符合接合預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Room-temperature flatness does not exclude hot warpage.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Hot contact geometry still fits joining budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「高溫接觸幾何仍符合接合預算」。室溫平坦不能排除高溫翹曲，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Hot contact geometry still fits joining budgets. Room-temperature flatness does not exclude hot warpage, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":454,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-453"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-455","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球自對準判讀","titleEn":"Interpret solder-ball self-alignment","objective":"判斷「焊球自對準判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：球心偏差收斂且未發生鄰球接觸。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret solder-ball self-alignment meets this specific condition: Offsets converge without contacting adjacent balls.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較回焊前後球心與焊墊中心。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare ball and pad centers before and after reflow. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：球心偏差收斂且未發生鄰球接觸；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Offsets converge without contacting adjacent balls. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"表面張力不能修正任意大的初始偏位。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Surface tension cannot correct arbitrary initial offsets. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"球心偏差收斂且未發生鄰球接觸；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Offsets converge without contacting adjacent balls. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-455-k1","title":"焊球自對準判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret solder-ball self-alignment","text":"可檢驗條件為「球心偏差收斂且未發生鄰球接觸」。可藉由「比較回焊前後球心與焊墊中心」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Offsets converge without contacting adjacent balls. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare ball and pad centers before and after reflow. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-455-k2","title":"焊球自對準判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret solder-ball self-alignment","text":"表面張力不能修正任意大的初始偏位。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Surface tension cannot correct arbitrary initial offsets. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球自對準判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret solder-ball self-alignment?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：表面張力不能修正任意大的初始偏位。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","球心偏差收斂且未發生鄰球接觸"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Surface tension cannot correct arbitrary initial offsets.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Offsets converge without contacting adjacent balls"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「球心偏差收斂且未發生鄰球接觸」。表面張力不能修正任意大的初始偏位，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Offsets converge without contacting adjacent balls. Surface tension cannot correct arbitrary initial offsets, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":455,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-454"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-456","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"潤濕角與球高","titleEn":"Measure wetting shape and ball height","objective":"判斷「潤濕角與球高」是否滿足此具體條件：幾何與核准焊墊及球體組合相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure wetting shape and ball height meets this specific condition: Geometry matches the qualified pad-ball combination.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：由側視輪廓量測球高與接觸區。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure ball height and contact region from profiles. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：幾何與核准焊墊及球體組合相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Geometry matches the qualified pad-ball combination. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"球高異常可能來自體積或潤濕差異。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Height anomalies can reflect volume or wetting differences. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"幾何與核准焊墊及球體組合相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Geometry matches the qualified pad-ball combination. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-456-k1","title":"潤濕角與球高的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure wetting shape and ball height","text":"可檢驗條件為「幾何與核准焊墊及球體組合相容」。可藉由「由側視輪廓量測球高與接觸區」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Geometry matches the qualified pad-ball combination. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure ball height and contact region from profiles. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-456-k2","title":"潤濕角與球高的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure wetting shape and ball height","text":"球高異常可能來自體積或潤濕差異。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Height anomalies can reflect volume or wetting differences. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「潤濕角與球高」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure wetting shape and ball height?","options":["幾何與核准焊墊及球體組合相容","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：球高異常可能來自體積或潤濕差異。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Geometry matches the qualified pad-ball combination","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Height anomalies can reflect volume or wetting differences.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「幾何與核准焊墊及球體組合相容」。球高異常可能來自體積或潤濕差異，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Geometry matches the qualified pad-ball combination. Height anomalies can reflect volume or wetting differences, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":456,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-455"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-457","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球橋接判讀","titleEn":"Inspect solder-ball bridges","objective":"判斷「焊球橋接判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：不同網路焊球保持分離。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect solder-ball bridges meets this specific condition: Balls on different nets remain separate.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較相鄰球之間的三維分離。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect three-dimensional separation between neighbors. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：不同網路焊球保持分離；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Balls on different nets remain separate. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"二維投影重疊不一定是真實橋接。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Projection overlap is not always a physical bridge. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"不同網路焊球保持分離；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Balls on different nets remain separate. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-457-k1","title":"焊球橋接判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect solder-ball bridges","text":"可檢驗條件為「不同網路焊球保持分離」。可藉由「比較相鄰球之間的三維分離」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Balls on different nets remain separate. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect three-dimensional separation between neighbors. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-457-k2","title":"焊球橋接判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect solder-ball bridges","text":"二維投影重疊不一定是真實橋接。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Projection overlap is not always a physical bridge. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球橋接判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect solder-ball bridges?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","不同網路焊球保持分離","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：二維投影重疊不一定是真實橋接。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Balls on different nets remain separate","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Projection overlap is not always a physical bridge."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「不同網路焊球保持分離」。二維投影重疊不一定是真實橋接，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Balls on different nets remain separate. Projection overlap is not always a physical bridge, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":457,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-456"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-458","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球空洞分析","titleEn":"Assess solder-ball voids","objective":"判斷「焊球空洞分析」是否滿足此具體條件：採用與規格相符的空洞定義。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess solder-ball voids meets this specific condition: Void metrics use the definition required by specification.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：分離投影面積與三維空洞體積。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Separate projected area from three-dimensional void volume. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：採用與規格相符的空洞定義；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Void metrics use the definition required by specification. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"混用面積率與體積率會誤判。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Mixing area and volume fractions misclassifies voiding. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"採用與規格相符的空洞定義；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Void metrics use the definition required by specification. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-458-k1","title":"焊球空洞分析的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess solder-ball voids","text":"可檢驗條件為「採用與規格相符的空洞定義」。可藉由「分離投影面積與三維空洞體積」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Void metrics use the definition required by specification. Evidence can be developed through this action: Separate projected area from three-dimensional void volume. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-458-k2","title":"焊球空洞分析的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess solder-ball voids","text":"混用面積率與體積率會誤判。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Mixing area and volume fractions misclassifies voiding. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球空洞分析」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess solder-ball voids?","options":["忽略此失效線索：混用面積率與體積率會誤判。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","採用與規格相符的空洞定義","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Mixing area and volume fractions misclassifies voiding.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Void metrics use the definition required by specification","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「採用與規格相符的空洞定義」。混用面積率與體積率會誤判，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Void metrics use the definition required by specification. Mixing area and volume fractions misclassifies voiding, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":458,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-457"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-459","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"回焊殘留清潔","titleEn":"Verify postreflow residue cleaning","objective":"判斷「回焊殘留清潔」是否滿足此具體條件：清潔後無超規殘留或侵蝕。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify postreflow residue cleaning meets this specific condition: No out-of-limit residue or attack remains.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查球根與防焊邊界殘留。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect residue around ball roots and mask edges. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：清潔後無超規殘留或侵蝕；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: No out-of-limit residue or attack remains. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"球頂潔淨可能掩蓋球根殘留。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Clean ball tops can hide residues at their bases. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"清潔後無超規殘留或侵蝕；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"No out-of-limit residue or attack remains. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-459-k1","title":"回焊殘留清潔的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify postreflow residue cleaning","text":"可檢驗條件為「清潔後無超規殘留或侵蝕」。可藉由「檢查球根與防焊邊界殘留」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: No out-of-limit residue or attack remains. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect residue around ball roots and mask edges. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-459-k2","title":"回焊殘留清潔的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify postreflow residue cleaning","text":"球頂潔淨可能掩蓋球根殘留。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Clean ball tops can hide residues at their bases. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「回焊殘留清潔」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify postreflow residue cleaning?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：球頂潔淨可能掩蓋球根殘留。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","清潔後無超規殘留或侵蝕"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Clean ball tops can hide residues at their bases.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","No out-of-limit residue or attack remains"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「清潔後無超規殘留或侵蝕」。球頂潔淨可能掩蓋球根殘留，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: No out-of-limit residue or attack remains. Clean ball tops can hide residues at their bases, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":459,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-458"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-460","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球共平面度","titleEn":"Measure final ball coplanarity","objective":"判斷「焊球共平面度」是否滿足此具體條件：所有端點符合組裝共平面規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure final ball coplanarity meets this specific condition: All terminals meet assembly coplanarity criteria.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：擬合基準平面後量測各球最低點。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Measure ball lowest points against a fitted reference plane. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：所有端點符合組裝共平面規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: All terminals meet assembly coplanarity criteria. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"基準平面選錯會系統性低估偏差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Wrong reference planes systematically understate variation. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"所有端點符合組裝共平面規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"All terminals meet assembly coplanarity criteria. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-460-k1","title":"焊球共平面度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure final ball coplanarity","text":"可檢驗條件為「所有端點符合組裝共平面規範」。可藉由「擬合基準平面後量測各球最低點」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: All terminals meet assembly coplanarity criteria. Evidence can be developed through this action: Measure ball lowest points against a fitted reference plane. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-460-k2","title":"焊球共平面度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure final ball coplanarity","text":"基準平面選錯會系統性低估偏差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Wrong reference planes systematically understate variation. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球共平面度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure final ball coplanarity?","options":["所有端點符合組裝共平面規範","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：基準平面選錯會系統性低估偏差。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["All terminals meet assembly coplanarity criteria","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Wrong reference planes systematically understate variation.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「所有端點符合組裝共平面規範」。基準平面選錯會系統性低估偏差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: All terminals meet assembly coplanarity criteria. Wrong reference planes systematically understate variation, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":460,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-459"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-461","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"焊球剪切破面","titleEn":"Interpret ball-shear fracture surfaces","objective":"判斷「焊球剪切破面」是否滿足此具體條件：破壞模式及載荷均符合評估規則。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret ball-shear fracture surfaces meets this specific condition: Failure mode and load both meet evaluation rules.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：聯合比較剪切載荷與界面破面。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare shear load and interface fracture surfaces. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：破壞模式及載荷均符合評估規則；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Failure mode and load both meet evaluation rules. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"高剪力仍可能伴隨脆性介面破壞。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"High force can coexist with brittle interface fracture. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"破壞模式及載荷均符合評估規則；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Failure mode and load both meet evaluation rules. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-461-k1","title":"焊球剪切破面的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret ball-shear fracture surfaces","text":"可檢驗條件為「破壞模式及載荷均符合評估規則」。可藉由「聯合比較剪切載荷與界面破面」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Failure mode and load both meet evaluation rules. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare shear load and interface fracture surfaces. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-461-k2","title":"焊球剪切破面的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret ball-shear fracture surfaces","text":"高剪力仍可能伴隨脆性介面破壞。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"High force can coexist with brittle interface fracture. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊球剪切破面」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret ball-shear fracture surfaces?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","破壞模式及載荷均符合評估規則","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：高剪力仍可能伴隨脆性介面破壞。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Failure mode and load both meet evaluation rules","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: High force can coexist with brittle interface fracture."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「破壞模式及載荷均符合評估規則」。高剪力仍可能伴隨脆性介面破壞，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Failure mode and load both meet evaluation rules. High force can coexist with brittle interface fracture, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":461,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-460"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-462","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"封裝外形尺寸","titleEn":"Verify package outline dimensions","objective":"判斷「封裝外形尺寸」是否滿足此具體條件：外形及高度滿足系統裝配限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify package outline dimensions meets this specific condition: Outline and height meet system assembly limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較外形高度與圖面公差。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare outline and height with drawing tolerances. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：外形及高度滿足系統裝配限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Outline and height meet system assembly limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"局部毛邊可超出整體外形平均值。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Local flash can exceed average outline dimensions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"外形及高度滿足系統裝配限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Outline and height meet system assembly limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-462-k1","title":"封裝外形尺寸的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify package outline dimensions","text":"可檢驗條件為「外形及高度滿足系統裝配限制」。可藉由「比較外形高度與圖面公差」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Outline and height meet system assembly limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare outline and height with drawing tolerances. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-462-k2","title":"封裝外形尺寸的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify package outline dimensions","text":"局部毛邊可超出整體外形平均值。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Local flash can exceed average outline dimensions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「封裝外形尺寸」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify package outline dimensions?","options":["忽略此失效線索：局部毛邊可超出整體外形平均值。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","外形及高度滿足系統裝配限制","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Local flash can exceed average outline dimensions.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Outline and height meet system assembly limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「外形及高度滿足系統裝配限制」。局部毛邊可超出整體外形平均值，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Outline and height meet system assembly limits. Local flash can exceed average outline dimensions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":462,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-461"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-463","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"基板去框分離","titleEn":"Assess substrate singulation","objective":"判斷「基板去框分離」是否滿足此具體條件：無超規裂紋毛邊及焊球損傷。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess substrate singulation meets this specific condition: No unacceptable cracks, burrs, or ball damage.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查分離面與焊球鄰近區域。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect singulated edges and nearby ball regions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：無超規裂紋毛邊及焊球損傷；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: No unacceptable cracks, burrs, or ball damage. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"分離應力可能傳入內部接點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Singulation stress can reach internal joints. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"無超規裂紋毛邊及焊球損傷；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"No unacceptable cracks, burrs, or ball damage. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-463-k1","title":"基板去框分離的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess substrate singulation","text":"可檢驗條件為「無超規裂紋毛邊及焊球損傷」。可藉由「檢查分離面與焊球鄰近區域」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: No unacceptable cracks, burrs, or ball damage. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect singulated edges and nearby ball regions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-463-k2","title":"基板去框分離的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess substrate singulation","text":"分離應力可能傳入內部接點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Singulation stress can reach internal joints. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「基板去框分離」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess substrate singulation?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：分離應力可能傳入內部接點。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","無超規裂紋毛邊及焊球損傷"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Singulation stress can reach internal joints.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","No unacceptable cracks, burrs, or ball damage"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「無超規裂紋毛邊及焊球損傷」。分離應力可能傳入內部接點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: No unacceptable cracks, burrs, or ball damage. Singulation stress can reach internal joints, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":463,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-462"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-464","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"頂面標記辨識","titleEn":"Validate package marking readability","objective":"判斷「頂面標記辨識」是否滿足此具體條件：標記清晰且識別內容完全一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Validate package marking readability meets this specific condition: Marks are readable and match product identity.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對光學讀碼與實際產品識別。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare optical decoding and actual product identity. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：標記清晰且識別內容完全一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Marks are readable and match product identity. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"可讀取的錯誤標記仍屬追溯失效。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Readable but incorrect marks still break traceability. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"標記清晰且識別內容完全一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Marks are readable and match product identity. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-464-k1","title":"頂面標記辨識的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Validate package marking readability","text":"可檢驗條件為「標記清晰且識別內容完全一致」。可藉由「比對光學讀碼與實際產品識別」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Marks are readable and match product identity. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare optical decoding and actual product identity. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-464-k2","title":"頂面標記辨識的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Validate package marking readability","text":"可讀取的錯誤標記仍屬追溯失效。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Readable but incorrect marks still break traceability. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「頂面標記辨識」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Validate package marking readability?","options":["標記清晰且識別內容完全一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：可讀取的錯誤標記仍屬追溯失效。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Marks are readable and match product identity","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Readable but incorrect marks still break traceability.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「標記清晰且識別內容完全一致」。可讀取的錯誤標記仍屬追溯失效，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Marks are readable and match product identity. Readable but incorrect marks still break traceability, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":464,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-463"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-465","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"封裝表面異物","titleEn":"Inspect package surface foreign material","objective":"判斷「封裝表面異物」是否滿足此具體條件：異物及刮痕依各自規則判讀。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect package surface foreign material meets this specific condition: Foreign matter and scratches use their own criteria.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：區分刮痕纖維與材料原有紋理。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Distinguish scratches, fibers, and native texture. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：異物及刮痕依各自規則判讀；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Foreign matter and scratches use their own criteria. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"把原有紋理當異物會增加誤判。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Native texture mistaken for debris increases false calls. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"異物及刮痕依各自規則判讀；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Foreign matter and scratches use their own criteria. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-465-k1","title":"封裝表面異物的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect package surface foreign material","text":"可檢驗條件為「異物及刮痕依各自規則判讀」。可藉由「區分刮痕纖維與材料原有紋理」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Foreign matter and scratches use their own criteria. Evidence can be developed through this action: Distinguish scratches, fibers, and native texture. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-465-k2","title":"封裝表面異物的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect package surface foreign material","text":"把原有紋理當異物會增加誤判。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Native texture mistaken for debris increases false calls. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「封裝表面異物」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect package surface foreign material?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","異物及刮痕依各自規則判讀","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：把原有紋理當異物會增加誤判。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Foreign matter and scratches use their own criteria","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Native texture mistaken for debris increases false calls."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「異物及刮痕依各自規則判讀」。把原有紋理當異物會增加誤判，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Foreign matter and scratches use their own criteria. Native texture mistaken for debris increases false calls, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":465,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-464"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-466","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"托盤接觸與方向","titleEn":"Verify tray support and orientation","objective":"判斷「托盤接觸與方向」是否滿足此具體條件：托盤不對焊球施加不當載荷。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify tray support and orientation meets this specific condition: Trays avoid inappropriate ball loading.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查支撐點與球體避讓。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Inspect tray supports and ball clearance. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：托盤不對焊球施加不當載荷；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Trays avoid inappropriate ball loading. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"方向錯誤可使焊球承受機械壓力。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Wrong orientation can place load on solder balls. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"托盤不對焊球施加不當載荷；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Trays avoid inappropriate ball loading. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-466-k1","title":"托盤接觸與方向的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify tray support and orientation","text":"可檢驗條件為「托盤不對焊球施加不當載荷」。可藉由「檢查支撐點與球體避讓」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Trays avoid inappropriate ball loading. Evidence can be developed through this action: Inspect tray supports and ball clearance. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-466-k2","title":"托盤接觸與方向的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify tray support and orientation","text":"方向錯誤可使焊球承受機械壓力。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Wrong orientation can place load on solder balls. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「托盤接觸與方向」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify tray support and orientation?","options":["忽略此失效線索：方向錯誤可使焊球承受機械壓力。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","托盤不對焊球施加不當載荷","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Wrong orientation can place load on solder balls.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Trays avoid inappropriate ball loading","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「托盤不對焊球施加不當載荷」。方向錯誤可使焊球承受機械壓力，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Trays avoid inappropriate ball loading. Wrong orientation can place load on solder balls, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":466,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-465"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-467","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"防潮包裝狀態","titleEn":"Verify moisture-protective packing state","objective":"判斷「防潮包裝狀態」是否滿足此具體條件：記錄與所選防潮分類相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify moisture-protective packing state meets this specific condition: Records agree with the selected moisture classification.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：核對乾燥劑指示卡封口與曝露紀錄。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Check desiccant, indicator, seal, and exposure records. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：記錄與所選防潮分類相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Records agree with the selected moisture classification. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"封袋完整不代表封袋前曝露合格。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"An intact bag does not prove acceptable prior exposure. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"記錄與所選防潮分類相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Records agree with the selected moisture classification. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-467-k1","title":"防潮包裝狀態的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify moisture-protective packing state","text":"可檢驗條件為「記錄與所選防潮分類相容」。可藉由「核對乾燥劑指示卡封口與曝露紀錄」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Records agree with the selected moisture classification. Evidence can be developed through this action: Check desiccant, indicator, seal, and exposure records. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-467-k2","title":"防潮包裝狀態的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify moisture-protective packing state","text":"封袋完整不代表封袋前曝露合格。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"An intact bag does not prove acceptable prior exposure. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「防潮包裝狀態」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify moisture-protective packing state?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：封袋完整不代表封袋前曝露合格。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","記錄與所選防潮分類相容"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: An intact bag does not prove acceptable prior exposure.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Records agree with the selected moisture classification"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「記錄與所選防潮分類相容」。封袋完整不代表封袋前曝露合格，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Records agree with the selected moisture classification. An intact bag does not prove acceptable prior exposure, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":467,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-466"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-468","stageId":"pk-m18","title":"外觀電性關聯終檢","titleEn":"Correlate final appearance and electrical defects","objective":"判斷「外觀電性關聯終檢」是否滿足此具體條件：缺陷與腳位對應可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Correlate final appearance and electrical defects meets this specific condition: Defects and pin mappings are traceable.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將缺球偏球與失效腳位共同套圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Overlay missing or shifted balls with failing pins. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：缺陷與腳位對應可追溯；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Defects and pin mappings are traceable. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"外觀正常不能排除隱藏開路。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Normal appearance does not exclude hidden opens. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"缺陷與腳位對應可追溯；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Defects and pin mappings are traceable. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-468-k1","title":"外觀電性關聯終檢的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Correlate final appearance and electrical defects","text":"可檢驗條件為「缺陷與腳位對應可追溯」。可藉由「將缺球偏球與失效腳位共同套圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Defects and pin mappings are traceable. Evidence can be developed through this action: Overlay missing or shifted balls with failing pins. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-468-k2","title":"外觀電性關聯終檢的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Correlate final appearance and electrical defects","text":"外觀正常不能排除隱藏開路。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Normal appearance does not exclude hidden opens. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「外觀電性關聯終檢」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Correlate final appearance and electrical defects?","options":["缺陷與腳位對應可追溯","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：外觀正常不能排除隱藏開路。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Defects and pin mappings are traceable","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Normal appearance does not exclude hidden opens.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「缺陷與腳位對應可追溯」。外觀正常不能排除隱藏開路，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Defects and pin mappings are traceable. Normal appearance does not exclude hidden opens, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-nordson-axi","pkb-nordson-wafer","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":468,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-467"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"BGA 對外焊球支線；LGA、裸晶模組與光學連接器採其他端接形式。","routeEn":"External BGA solder-ball branch; LGA, bare-die modules, and optical connectors use other terminations.","photoId":"bga-balls","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察電路板上封裝元件的位置及外觀；這是頂視圖，焊球位於底部不可見，無法由此判定接合品質。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe the package on a circuit board; this is a top view, so underside balls are not visible and joint quality cannot be inferred.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m19","title":"封裝可靠度與失效分析","titleEn":"Package reliability and failure analysis","description":"加速應力必須連結到使用失效機制；測試時間、失效定義與樣本分母不完整時，不能宣稱壽命。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Accelerated stress must connect to service failure mechanisms; lifetime claims require complete duration, failure definitions, and sample denominators. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","order":19,"sequence":19,"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-469","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"使用任務剖面","titleEn":"Build a service mission profile","objective":"判斷「使用任務剖面」是否滿足此具體條件：任務載荷與預期失效機制有對應。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Build a service mission profile meets this specific condition: Mission loads map to expected failure mechanisms.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將溫度功率濕度與開關循環分開建模。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Model temperature, power, humidity, and switching cycles separately. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：任務載荷與預期失效機制有對應；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Mission loads map to expected failure mechanisms. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"用單一最高溫度代表全壽命會失真。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"One maximum temperature misrepresents lifetime exposure. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"任務載荷與預期失效機制有對應；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Mission loads map to expected failure mechanisms. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-469-k1","title":"使用任務剖面的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Build a service mission profile","text":"可檢驗條件為「任務載荷與預期失效機制有對應」。可藉由「將溫度功率濕度與開關循環分開建模」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Mission loads map to expected failure mechanisms. Evidence can be developed through this action: Model temperature, power, humidity, and switching cycles separately. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-469-k2","title":"使用任務剖面的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Build a service mission profile","text":"用單一最高溫度代表全壽命會失真。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"One maximum temperature misrepresents lifetime exposure. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「使用任務剖面」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Build a service mission profile?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","任務載荷與預期失效機制有對應","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：用單一最高溫度代表全壽命會失真。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Mission loads map to expected failure mechanisms","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: One maximum temperature misrepresents lifetime exposure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「任務載荷與預期失效機制有對應」。用單一最高溫度代表全壽命會失真，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Mission loads map to expected failure mechanisms. One maximum temperature misrepresents lifetime exposure, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":469,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-470","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"可靠度抽樣矩陣","titleEn":"Construct a reliability sampling matrix","objective":"判斷「可靠度抽樣矩陣」是否滿足此具體條件：樣本來源與試驗分母完整。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Construct a reliability sampling matrix meets this specific condition: Sample origins and test denominators are complete.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：分配批次製程角落與對照樣本。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Allocate lots, process corners, and control specimens. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：樣本來源與試驗分母完整；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Sample origins and test denominators are complete. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只挑外觀最佳樣本會造成選樣偏差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Selecting only best-looking units creates sampling bias. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"樣本來源與試驗分母完整；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Sample origins and test denominators are complete. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-470-k1","title":"可靠度抽樣矩陣的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Construct a reliability sampling matrix","text":"可檢驗條件為「樣本來源與試驗分母完整」。可藉由「分配批次製程角落與對照樣本」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Sample origins and test denominators are complete. Evidence can be developed through this action: Allocate lots, process corners, and control specimens. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-470-k2","title":"可靠度抽樣矩陣的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Construct a reliability sampling matrix","text":"只挑外觀最佳樣本會造成選樣偏差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Selecting only best-looking units creates sampling bias. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「可靠度抽樣矩陣」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Construct a reliability sampling matrix?","options":["忽略此失效線索：只挑外觀最佳樣本會造成選樣偏差。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","樣本來源與試驗分母完整","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Selecting only best-looking units creates sampling bias.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Sample origins and test denominators are complete","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「樣本來源與試驗分母完整」。只挑外觀最佳樣本會造成選樣偏差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Sample origins and test denominators are complete. Selecting only best-looking units creates sampling bias, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":470,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-469"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-471","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"應力前基準電測","titleEn":"Establish prestress electrical baselines","objective":"判斷「應力前基準電測」是否滿足此具體條件：基準值及量測條件可重現。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Establish prestress electrical baselines meets this specific condition: Baseline values and conditions are reproducible.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：保存每顆樣本的初始參數向量。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Save each sample's initial parameter vector. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：基準值及量測條件可重現；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Baseline values and conditions are reproducible. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"僅保存通過標記無法分析後續漂移。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Pass-only records cannot support drift analysis. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"基準值及量測條件可重現；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Baseline values and conditions are reproducible. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-471-k1","title":"應力前基準電測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Establish prestress electrical baselines","text":"可檢驗條件為「基準值及量測條件可重現」。可藉由「保存每顆樣本的初始參數向量」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Baseline values and conditions are reproducible. Evidence can be developed through this action: Save each sample's initial parameter vector. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-471-k2","title":"應力前基準電測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Establish prestress electrical baselines","text":"僅保存通過標記無法分析後續漂移。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Pass-only records cannot support drift analysis. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「應力前基準電測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Establish prestress electrical baselines?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：僅保存通過標記無法分析後續漂移。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","基準值及量測條件可重現"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Pass-only records cannot support drift analysis.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Baseline values and conditions are reproducible"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「基準值及量測條件可重現」。僅保存通過標記無法分析後續漂移，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Baseline values and conditions are reproducible. Pass-only records cannot support drift analysis, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":471,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-470"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-472","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"應力前聲學影像","titleEn":"Establish prestress acoustic images","objective":"判斷「應力前聲學影像」是否滿足此具體條件：影像深度座標與樣本識別完整。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Establish prestress acoustic images meets this specific condition: Depth coordinates and sample identities are complete.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以固定介面深度保存初始影像。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Store baseline images at fixed interface depths. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：影像深度座標與樣本識別完整；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Depth coordinates and sample identities are complete. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"無基準影像易把原有特徵誤當新裂紋。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Without baselines, native features may appear to be new cracks. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"影像深度座標與樣本識別完整；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Depth coordinates and sample identities are complete. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-472-k1","title":"應力前聲學影像的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Establish prestress acoustic images","text":"可檢驗條件為「影像深度座標與樣本識別完整」。可藉由「以固定介面深度保存初始影像」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Depth coordinates and sample identities are complete. Evidence can be developed through this action: Store baseline images at fixed interface depths. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-472-k2","title":"應力前聲學影像的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Establish prestress acoustic images","text":"無基準影像易把原有特徵誤當新裂紋。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Without baselines, native features may appear to be new cracks. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「應力前聲學影像」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Establish prestress acoustic images?","options":["影像深度座標與樣本識別完整","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：無基準影像易把原有特徵誤當新裂紋。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Depth coordinates and sample identities are complete","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Without baselines, native features may appear to be new cracks.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「影像深度座標與樣本識別完整」。無基準影像易把原有特徵誤當新裂紋，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Depth coordinates and sample identities are complete. Without baselines, native features may appear to be new cracks, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":472,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-471"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-473","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"濕敏預處理支線","titleEn":"Assess moisture-preconditioning branch","objective":"判斷「濕敏預處理支線」是否滿足此具體條件：歷程符合選定分類與試驗計畫。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess moisture-preconditioning branch meets this specific condition: History matches the selected classification and test plan.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：核對吸濕曝露與回焊模擬紀錄。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Review moisture exposure and reflow-simulation records. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：歷程符合選定分類與試驗計畫；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: History matches the selected classification and test plan. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"不同預處理條件不可直接合併比較。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Different preconditioning conditions cannot be pooled blindly. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"歷程符合選定分類與試驗計畫；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"History matches the selected classification and test plan. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-473-k1","title":"濕敏預處理支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess moisture-preconditioning branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「歷程符合選定分類與試驗計畫」。可藉由「核對吸濕曝露與回焊模擬紀錄」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: History matches the selected classification and test plan. Evidence can be developed through this action: Review moisture exposure and reflow-simulation records. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-473-k2","title":"濕敏預處理支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess moisture-preconditioning branch","text":"不同預處理條件不可直接合併比較。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Different preconditioning conditions cannot be pooled blindly. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「濕敏預處理支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess moisture-preconditioning branch?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","歷程符合選定分類與試驗計畫","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：不同預處理條件不可直接合併比較。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","History matches the selected classification and test plan","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Different preconditioning conditions cannot be pooled blindly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「歷程符合選定分類與試驗計畫」。不同預處理條件不可直接合併比較，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: History matches the selected classification and test plan. Different preconditioning conditions cannot be pooled blindly, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":473,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-472"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-474","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"溫度循環負載","titleEn":"Interpret temperature-cycling loads","objective":"判斷「溫度循環負載」是否滿足此具體條件：樣本達成計畫的循環與停留定義。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret temperature-cycling loads meets this specific condition: Specimens meet planned cycle and dwell definitions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較樣本實際溫度與箱體設定。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare specimen temperatures with chamber settings. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：樣本達成計畫的循環與停留定義；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Specimens meet planned cycle and dwell definitions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"箱溫達標不等於樣品已達溫。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Chamber temperature does not prove specimen equilibration. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"樣本達成計畫的循環與停留定義；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Specimens meet planned cycle and dwell definitions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-474-k1","title":"溫度循環負載的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret temperature-cycling loads","text":"可檢驗條件為「樣本達成計畫的循環與停留定義」。可藉由「比較樣本實際溫度與箱體設定」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Specimens meet planned cycle and dwell definitions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare specimen temperatures with chamber settings. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-474-k2","title":"溫度循環負載的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret temperature-cycling loads","text":"箱溫達標不等於樣品已達溫。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Chamber temperature does not prove specimen equilibration. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-474-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"溫度循環需記錄上下限、升降速率、停留、轉移與試件實際溫度；相同循環數不代表相同損傷。教學例不指定通用合格週期。","textEn":"Thermal cycling requires limits, ramp rates, dwells, transfer and actual specimen temperatures; equal cycle counts do not imply equal damage. No universal qualification cycle is specified here."},{"id":"pk-474-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"先確認使用任務是否由焊點疲勞、介面分層或脆性裂紋主導，再安排中間檢查。停機後才量測可能漏掉熱態間歇開路。","textEn":"Determine whether the mission is dominated by solder fatigue, delamination or brittle cracking and schedule intermediate checks. Post-test measurements may miss hot intermittent opens."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「溫度循環負載」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret temperature-cycling loads?","options":["忽略此失效線索：箱溫達標不等於樣品已達溫。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","樣本達成計畫的循環與停留定義","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Chamber temperature does not prove specimen equilibration.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Specimens meet planned cycle and dwell definitions","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「樣本達成計畫的循環與停留定義」。箱溫達標不等於樣品已達溫，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Specimens meet planned cycle and dwell definitions. Chamber temperature does not prove specimen equilibration, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":474,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-473"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-475","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"功率循環熱梯度","titleEn":"Interpret power-cycling gradients","objective":"判斷「功率循環熱梯度」是否滿足此具體條件：熱梯度與任務機制具有關聯。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret power-cycling gradients meets this specific condition: Thermal gradients relate to the mission mechanism.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：讀取通電加熱期間晶粒與基板溫差。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Read die-substrate differences during powered heating. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：熱梯度與任務機制具有關聯；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Thermal gradients relate to the mission mechanism. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"功率循環不能等同均溫箱體循環。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Power cycling is not equivalent to uniform chamber cycling. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"熱梯度與任務機制具有關聯；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Thermal gradients relate to the mission mechanism. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-475-k1","title":"功率循環熱梯度的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret power-cycling gradients","text":"可檢驗條件為「熱梯度與任務機制具有關聯」。可藉由「讀取通電加熱期間晶粒與基板溫差」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Thermal gradients relate to the mission mechanism. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read die-substrate differences during powered heating. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-475-k2","title":"功率循環熱梯度的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret power-cycling gradients","text":"功率循環不能等同均溫箱體循環。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Power cycling is not equivalent to uniform chamber cycling. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「功率循環熱梯度」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret power-cycling gradients?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：功率循環不能等同均溫箱體循環。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","熱梯度與任務機制具有關聯"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Power cycling is not equivalent to uniform chamber cycling.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Thermal gradients relate to the mission mechanism"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「熱梯度與任務機制具有關聯」。功率循環不能等同均溫箱體循環，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Thermal gradients relate to the mission mechanism. Power cycling is not equivalent to uniform chamber cycling, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":475,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-474"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-476","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"高溫儲存漂移","titleEn":"Assess high-temperature storage drift","objective":"判斷「高溫儲存漂移」是否滿足此具體條件：漂移依預定失效定義判定。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess high-temperature storage drift meets this specific condition: Drift is judged against predefined failure definitions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較無偏壓老化前後接點電阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare contact resistance before and after unbiased aging. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：漂移依預定失效定義判定；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Drift is judged against predefined failure definitions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"無偏壓結果不能代表帶電遷移風險。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unbiased results do not represent biased migration risk. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"漂移依預定失效定義判定；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Drift is judged against predefined failure definitions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-476-k1","title":"高溫儲存漂移的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess high-temperature storage drift","text":"可檢驗條件為「漂移依預定失效定義判定」。可藉由「比較無偏壓老化前後接點電阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Drift is judged against predefined failure definitions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare contact resistance before and after unbiased aging. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-476-k2","title":"高溫儲存漂移的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess high-temperature storage drift","text":"無偏壓結果不能代表帶電遷移風險。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unbiased results do not represent biased migration risk. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「高溫儲存漂移」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess high-temperature storage drift?","options":["漂移依預定失效定義判定","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：無偏壓結果不能代表帶電遷移風險。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Drift is judged against predefined failure definitions","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Unbiased results do not represent biased migration risk.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「漂移依預定失效定義判定」。無偏壓結果不能代表帶電遷移風險，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanati