ical and thermal stress match the qualified test. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只記箱溫會漏掉自發熱效應。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Chamber temperature alone misses self-heating. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"電熱應力符合已核准的操作試驗；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Electrical and thermal stress match the qualified test. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-477-k1","title":"高溫操作壽命支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess high-temperature operating-life branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「電熱應力符合已核准的操作試驗」。可藉由「核對偏壓功耗與實際接面溫度」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Electrical and thermal stress match the qualified test. Evidence can be developed through this action: Verify bias, power, and actual junction temperature. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-477-k2","title":"高溫操作壽命支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess high-temperature operating-life branch","text":"只記箱溫會漏掉自發熱效應。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Chamber temperature alone misses self-heating. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「高溫操作壽命支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess high-temperature operating-life branch?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","電熱應力符合已核准的操作試驗","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只記箱溫會漏掉自發熱效應。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Electrical and thermal stress match the qualified test","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Chamber temperature alone misses self-heating."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「電熱應力符合已核准的操作試驗」。只記箱溫會漏掉自發熱效應，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Electrical and thermal stress match the qualified test. Chamber temperature alone misses self-heating, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":477,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-476"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-478","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"溫濕偏壓失效","titleEn":"Assess temperature-humidity-bias failures","objective":"判斷「溫濕偏壓失效」是否滿足此具體條件：漏電及功能依計畫讀取點完整。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess temperature-humidity-bias failures meets this specific condition: Leakage and function are recorded at planned readouts.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較漏電隨時間與偏壓極性。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare leakage over time and bias polarity. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：漏電及功能依計畫讀取點完整；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Leakage and function are recorded at planned readouts. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"離箱乾燥可能暫時掩蓋濕氣失效。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Drying outside the chamber can temporarily hide moisture failures. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"漏電及功能依計畫讀取點完整；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Leakage and function are recorded at planned readouts. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-478-k1","title":"溫濕偏壓失效的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess temperature-humidity-bias failures","text":"可檢驗條件為「漏電及功能依計畫讀取點完整」。可藉由「比較漏電隨時間與偏壓極性」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Leakage and function are recorded at planned readouts. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare leakage over time and bias polarity. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-478-k2","title":"溫濕偏壓失效的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess temperature-humidity-bias failures","text":"離箱乾燥可能暫時掩蓋濕氣失效。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Drying outside the chamber can temporarily hide moisture failures. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「溫濕偏壓失效」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess temperature-humidity-bias failures?","options":["忽略此失效線索：離箱乾燥可能暫時掩蓋濕氣失效。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","漏電及功能依計畫讀取點完整","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Drying outside the chamber can temporarily hide moisture failures.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Leakage and function are recorded at planned readouts","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「漏電及功能依計畫讀取點完整」。離箱乾燥可能暫時掩蓋濕氣失效，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Leakage and function are recorded at planned readouts. Drying outside the chamber can temporarily hide moisture failures, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":478,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-477"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-479","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"加速濕熱支線","titleEn":"Assess accelerated humidity-test branch","objective":"判斷「加速濕熱支線」是否滿足此具體條件：試驗機制與目標使用環境可合理連結。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess accelerated humidity-test branch meets this specific condition: Test mechanisms can reasonably connect to target service.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：檢查壓力濕度溫度與材料相容性。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Check pressure, humidity, temperature, and material compatibility. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：試驗機制與目標使用環境可合理連結；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Test mechanisms can reasonably connect to target service. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過激條件可能產生非使用失效機制。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Excessive stress can create irrelevant failure mechanisms. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"試驗機制與目標使用環境可合理連結；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Test mechanisms can reasonably connect to target service. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-479-k1","title":"加速濕熱支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess accelerated humidity-test branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「試驗機制與目標使用環境可合理連結」。可藉由「檢查壓力濕度溫度與材料相容性」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Test mechanisms can reasonably connect to target service. Evidence can be developed through this action: Check pressure, humidity, temperature, and material compatibility. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-479-k2","title":"加速濕熱支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess accelerated humidity-test branch","text":"過激條件可能產生非使用失效機制。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Excessive stress can create irrelevant failure mechanisms. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「加速濕熱支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess accelerated humidity-test branch?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：過激條件可能產生非使用失效機制。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","試驗機制與目標使用環境可合理連結"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Excessive stress can create irrelevant failure mechanisms.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Test mechanisms can reasonably connect to target service"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「試驗機制與目標使用環境可合理連結」。過激條件可能產生非使用失效機制，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Test mechanisms can reasonably connect to target service. Excessive stress can create irrelevant failure mechanisms, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":479,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-478"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-480","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"導體電遷移評估","titleEn":"Assess conductor electromigration","objective":"判斷「導體電遷移評估」是否滿足此具體條件：失效判據與受測導體截面明確。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess conductor electromigration meets this specific condition: Failure criteria and conductor cross sections are explicit.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較電流密度溫度與電阻時間曲線。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare current density, temperature, and resistance history. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：失效判據與受測導體截面明確；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Failure criteria and conductor cross sections are explicit. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"不計電流擁擠會低估局部應力。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Ignoring current crowding underestimates local stress. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"失效判據與受測導體截面明確；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Failure criteria and conductor cross sections are explicit. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-480-k1","title":"導體電遷移評估的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess conductor electromigration","text":"可檢驗條件為「失效判據與受測導體截面明確」。可藉由「比較電流密度溫度與電阻時間曲線」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Failure criteria and conductor cross sections are explicit. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare current density, temperature, and resistance history. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-480-k2","title":"導體電遷移評估的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess conductor electromigration","text":"不計電流擁擠會低估局部應力。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Ignoring current crowding underestimates local stress. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「導體電遷移評估」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess conductor electromigration?","options":["失效判據與受測導體截面明確","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：不計電流擁擠會低估局部應力。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Failure criteria and conductor cross sections are explicit","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Ignoring current crowding underestimates local stress.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「失效判據與受測導體截面明確」。不計電流擁擠會低估局部應力，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Failure criteria and conductor cross sections are explicit. Ignoring current crowding underestimates local stress, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":480,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-479"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-481","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"介電時間依賴失效","titleEn":"Assess time-dependent dielectric failure","objective":"判斷「介電時間依賴失效」是否滿足此具體條件：介電受力與電極幾何均可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess time-dependent dielectric failure meets this specific condition: Dielectric stress and electrode geometry are traceable.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：分析偏壓下漏電與失效時間。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Analyze leakage and failure times under bias. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：介電受力與電極幾何均可追溯；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Dielectric stress and electrode geometry are traceable. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"接觸短路不能誤歸為介電崩潰。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Contact shorts must not be mislabeled dielectric breakdown. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"介電受力與電極幾何均可追溯；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Dielectric stress and electrode geometry are traceable. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-481-k1","title":"介電時間依賴失效的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess time-dependent dielectric failure","text":"可檢驗條件為「介電受力與電極幾何均可追溯」。可藉由「分析偏壓下漏電與失效時間」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Dielectric stress and electrode geometry are traceable. Evidence can be developed through this action: Analyze leakage and failure times under bias. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-481-k2","title":"介電時間依賴失效的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess time-dependent dielectric failure","text":"接觸短路不能誤歸為介電崩潰。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Contact shorts must not be mislabeled dielectric breakdown. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「介電時間依賴失效」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess time-dependent dielectric failure?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","介電受力與電極幾何均可追溯","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：接觸短路不能誤歸為介電崩潰。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Dielectric stress and electrode geometry are traceable","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Contact shorts must not be mislabeled dielectric breakdown."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「介電受力與電極幾何均可追溯」。接觸短路不能誤歸為介電崩潰，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Dielectric stress and electrode geometry are traceable. Contact shorts must not be mislabeled dielectric breakdown, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":481,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-480"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-482","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"板級彎曲支線","titleEn":"Assess board-level bend branch","objective":"判斷「板級彎曲支線」是否滿足此具體條件：失效事件具有同步應變證據。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess board-level bend branch meets this specific condition: Failures have synchronized strain evidence.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比對板應變與封裝接點開路事件。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare board strain with joint-open events. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：失效事件具有同步應變證據；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Failures have synchronized strain evidence. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"機台位移不能直接代表封裝附近應變。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Machine travel does not directly represent local board strain. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"失效事件具有同步應變證據；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Failures have synchronized strain evidence. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-482-k1","title":"板級彎曲支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess board-level bend branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「失效事件具有同步應變證據」。可藉由「比對板應變與封裝接點開路事件」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Failures have synchronized strain evidence. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare board strain with joint-open events. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-482-k2","title":"板級彎曲支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess board-level bend branch","text":"機台位移不能直接代表封裝附近應變。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Machine travel does not directly represent local board strain. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「板級彎曲支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess board-level bend branch?","options":["忽略此失效線索：機台位移不能直接代表封裝附近應變。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","失效事件具有同步應變證據","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Machine travel does not directly represent local board strain.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Failures have synchronized strain evidence","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「失效事件具有同步應變證據」。機台位移不能直接代表封裝附近應變，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Failures have synchronized strain evidence. Machine travel does not directly represent local board strain, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":482,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-481"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-483","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"板級跌落支線","titleEn":"Assess board-level drop branch","objective":"判斷「板級跌落支線」是否滿足此具體條件：瞬斷事件與實際衝擊時間對得上。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess board-level drop branch meets this specific condition: Transient opens align with measured impact timing.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：同步讀取加速度與高速導通資料。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Read acceleration and high-speed continuity together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：瞬斷事件與實際衝擊時間對得上；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Transient opens align with measured impact timing. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"事後直流量測可能漏掉短暫斷路。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Posttest DC measurements can miss transient opens. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"瞬斷事件與實際衝擊時間對得上；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Transient opens align with measured impact timing. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-483-k1","title":"板級跌落支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess board-level drop branch","text":"可檢驗條件為「瞬斷事件與實際衝擊時間對得上」。可藉由「同步讀取加速度與高速導通資料」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Transient opens align with measured impact timing. Evidence can be developed through this action: Read acceleration and high-speed continuity together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-483-k2","title":"板級跌落支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess board-level drop branch","text":"事後直流量測可能漏掉短暫斷路。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Posttest DC measurements can miss transient opens. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「板級跌落支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess board-level drop branch?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：事後直流量測可能漏掉短暫斷路。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","瞬斷事件與實際衝擊時間對得上"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Posttest DC measurements can miss transient opens.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Transient opens align with measured impact timing"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「瞬斷事件與實際衝擊時間對得上」。事後直流量測可能漏掉短暫斷路，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Transient opens align with measured impact timing. Posttest DC measurements can miss transient opens, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":483,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-482"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-484","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"機械振動共振","titleEn":"Assess vibration resonance","objective":"判斷「機械振動共振」是否滿足此具體條件：樣本負載可與夾具影響分離。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess vibration resonance meets this specific condition: Specimen loads can be separated from fixture effects.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較加速度傳遞率與夾具模態。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare acceleration transmissibility and fixture modes. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：樣本負載可與夾具影響分離；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Specimen loads can be separated from fixture effects. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"夾具共振可能被誤判為產品弱點。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Fixture resonance can be mistaken for a product weakness. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"樣本負載可與夾具影響分離；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Specimen loads can be separated from fixture effects. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-484-k1","title":"機械振動共振的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess vibration resonance","text":"可檢驗條件為「樣本負載可與夾具影響分離」。可藉由「比較加速度傳遞率與夾具模態」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Specimen loads can be separated from fixture effects. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare acceleration transmissibility and fixture modes. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-484-k2","title":"機械振動共振的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess vibration resonance","text":"夾具共振可能被誤判為產品弱點。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Fixture resonance can be mistaken for a product weakness. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「機械振動共振」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess vibration resonance?","options":["樣本負載可與夾具影響分離","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：夾具共振可能被誤判為產品弱點。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Specimen loads can be separated from fixture effects","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Fixture resonance can be mistaken for a product weakness.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「樣本負載可與夾具影響分離」。夾具共振可能被誤判為產品弱點，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Specimen loads can be separated from fixture effects. Fixture resonance can be mistaken for a product weakness, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":484,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-483"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-485","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"焊接界面老化","titleEn":"Assess solder-interface aging","objective":"判斷「焊接界面老化」是否滿足此具體條件：組織變化與機械結果有一致證據。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess solder-interface aging meets this specific condition: Microstructural changes agree with mechanical evidence.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較介金屬層形貌及破面變化。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare intermetallic morphology and fracture changes. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：組織變化與機械結果有一致證據；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Microstructural changes agree with mechanical evidence. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單一層厚數值不能代表全部脆化風險。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"One layer thickness cannot represent all embrittlement risks. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"組織變化與機械結果有一致證據；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Microstructural changes agree with mechanical evidence. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-485-k1","title":"焊接界面老化的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess solder-interface aging","text":"可檢驗條件為「組織變化與機械結果有一致證據」。可藉由「比較介金屬層形貌及破面變化」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Microstructural changes agree with mechanical evidence. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare intermetallic morphology and fracture changes. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-485-k2","title":"焊接界面老化的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess solder-interface aging","text":"單一層厚數值不能代表全部脆化風險。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"One layer thickness cannot represent all embrittlement risks. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「焊接界面老化」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess solder-interface aging?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","組織變化與機械結果有一致證據","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：單一層厚數值不能代表全部脆化風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Microstructural changes agree with mechanical evidence","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: One layer thickness cannot represent all embrittlement risks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「組織變化與機械結果有一致證據」。單一層厚數值不能代表全部脆化風險，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Microstructural changes agree with mechanical evidence. One layer thickness cannot represent all embrittlement risks, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":485,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-484"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-486","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"非破壞電性定位","titleEn":"Localize faults electrically before sectioning","objective":"判斷「非破壞電性定位」是否滿足此具體條件：失效定位保留多個可能原因。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Localize faults electrically before sectioning meets this specific condition: Localization retains plausible competing causes.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：用網路對映比較開路與短路位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare open and short locations through net mapping. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：失效定位保留多個可能原因；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Localization retains plausible competing causes. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"過早鎖定單一原因會誤導切片。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Premature commitment to one cause misdirects sectioning. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"失效定位保留多個可能原因；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Localization retains plausible competing causes. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-486-k1","title":"非破壞電性定位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Localize faults electrically before sectioning","text":"可檢驗條件為「失效定位保留多個可能原因」。可藉由「用網路對映比較開路與短路位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Localization retains plausible competing causes. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare open and short locations through net mapping. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-486-k2","title":"非破壞電性定位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Localize faults electrically before sectioning","text":"過早鎖定單一原因會誤導切片。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Premature commitment to one cause misdirects sectioning. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「非破壞電性定位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Localize faults electrically before sectioning?","options":["忽略此失效線索：過早鎖定單一原因會誤導切片。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","失效定位保留多個可能原因","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Premature commitment to one cause misdirects sectioning.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Localization retains plausible competing causes","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「失效定位保留多個可能原因」。過早鎖定單一原因會誤導切片，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Localization retains plausible competing causes. Premature commitment to one cause misdirects sectioning, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":486,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-485"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-487","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"時間域反射定位","titleEn":"Localize discontinuities with reflectometry","objective":"判斷「時間域反射定位」是否滿足此具體條件：異常延遲與候選界面距離一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Localize discontinuities with reflectometry meets this specific condition: Anomaly delay agrees with candidate interface distance.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較故障與良品反射波形。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare failing and good-unit reflection traces. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：異常延遲與候選界面距離一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Anomaly delay agrees with candidate interface distance. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"治具反射未去除會產生虛假定位。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unremoved fixture reflections create false localization. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"異常延遲與候選界面距離一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Anomaly delay agrees with candidate interface distance. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-487-k1","title":"時間域反射定位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Localize discontinuities with reflectometry","text":"可檢驗條件為「異常延遲與候選界面距離一致」。可藉由「比較故障與良品反射波形」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Anomaly delay agrees with candidate interface distance. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare failing and good-unit reflection traces. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-487-k2","title":"時間域反射定位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Localize discontinuities with reflectometry","text":"治具反射未去除會產生虛假定位。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unremoved fixture reflections create false localization. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「時間域反射定位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Localize discontinuities with reflectometry?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：治具反射未去除會產生虛假定位。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","異常延遲與候選界面距離一致"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Unremoved fixture reflections create false localization.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Anomaly delay agrees with candidate interface distance"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「異常延遲與候選界面距離一致」。治具反射未去除會產生虛假定位，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Anomaly delay agrees with candidate interface distance. Unremoved fixture reflections create false localization, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":487,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-486"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-488","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"三維 X 光追蹤","titleEn":"Track defects with three-dimensional X-ray","objective":"判斷「三維 X 光追蹤」是否滿足此具體條件：缺陷在相鄰切片有連續證據。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Track defects with three-dimensional X-ray meets this specific condition: Defects have coherent evidence across adjacent slices.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：沿互連方向追蹤疑似空隙或裂縫。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Trace suspected voids or cracks along interconnects. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：缺陷在相鄰切片有連續證據；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Defects have coherent evidence across adjacent slices. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"重建偽影不可當成真實裂紋。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Reconstruction artifacts must not be treated as cracks. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"缺陷在相鄰切片有連續證據；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Defects have coherent evidence across adjacent slices. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-488-k1","title":"三維 X 光追蹤的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Track defects with three-dimensional X-ray","text":"可檢驗條件為「缺陷在相鄰切片有連續證據」。可藉由「沿互連方向追蹤疑似空隙或裂縫」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Defects have coherent evidence across adjacent slices. Evidence can be developed through this action: Trace suspected voids or cracks along interconnects. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-488-k2","title":"三維 X 光追蹤的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Track defects with three-dimensional X-ray","text":"重建偽影不可當成真實裂紋。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Reconstruction artifacts must not be treated as cracks. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「三維 X 光追蹤」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Track defects with three-dimensional X-ray?","options":["缺陷在相鄰切片有連續證據","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：重建偽影不可當成真實裂紋。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Defects have coherent evidence across adjacent slices","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Reconstruction artifacts must not be treated as cracks.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「缺陷在相鄰切片有連續證據」。重建偽影不可當成真實裂紋，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Defects have coherent evidence across adjacent slices. Reconstruction artifacts must not be treated as cracks, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":488,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-487"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-489","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"聲學分層定位","titleEn":"Localize delamination acoustically","objective":"判斷「聲學分層定位」是否滿足此具體條件：分層介面定位有聲程依據。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Localize delamination acoustically meets this specific condition: Delamination location is supported by acoustic path lengths.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把回波時間與材料層序對照。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare echo timing with the material stack. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：分層介面定位有聲程依據；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Delamination location is supported by acoustic path lengths. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"反射相位改變需排除材料差異。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Phase changes require excluding material differences. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"分層介面定位有聲程依據；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Delamination location is supported by acoustic path lengths. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-489-k1","title":"聲學分層定位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Localize delamination acoustically","text":"可檢驗條件為「分層介面定位有聲程依據」。可藉由「把回波時間與材料層序對照」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Delamination location is supported by acoustic path lengths. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare echo timing with the material stack. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-489-k2","title":"聲學分層定位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Localize delamination acoustically","text":"反射相位改變需排除材料差異。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Phase changes require excluding material differences. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「聲學分層定位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Localize delamination acoustically?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","分層介面定位有聲程依據","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：反射相位改變需排除材料差異。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Delamination location is supported by acoustic path lengths","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Phase changes require excluding material differences."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「分層介面定位有聲程依據」。反射相位改變需排除材料差異，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Delamination location is supported by acoustic path lengths. Phase changes require excluding material differences, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":489,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-488"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-490","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"截面製樣定位","titleEn":"Plan a failure-analysis cross section","objective":"判斷「截面製樣定位」是否滿足此具體條件：截面穿過疑似缺陷且有方向記錄。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Plan a failure-analysis cross section meets this specific condition: Section crosses the suspected defect with recorded orientation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以電性與非破壞影像決定截面位置。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Choose section location using electrical and nondestructive data. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：截面穿過疑似缺陷且有方向記錄；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Section crosses the suspected defect with recorded orientation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"盲目切片可能錯過微小失效區。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unguided sectioning can miss small failure regions. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"截面穿過疑似缺陷且有方向記錄；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Section crosses the suspected defect with recorded orientation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-490-k1","title":"截面製樣定位的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Plan a failure-analysis cross section","text":"可檢驗條件為「截面穿過疑似缺陷且有方向記錄」。可藉由「以電性與非破壞影像決定截面位置」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Section crosses the suspected defect with recorded orientation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Choose section location using electrical and nondestructive data. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-490-k2","title":"截面製樣定位的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Plan a failure-analysis cross section","text":"盲目切片可能錯過微小失效區。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unguided sectioning can miss small failure regions. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「截面製樣定位」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Plan a failure-analysis cross section?","options":["忽略此失效線索：盲目切片可能錯過微小失效區。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","截面穿過疑似缺陷且有方向記錄","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Unguided sectioning can miss small failure regions.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Section crosses the suspected defect with recorded orientation","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「截面穿過疑似缺陷且有方向記錄」。盲目切片可能錯過微小失效區，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Section crosses the suspected defect with recorded orientation. Unguided sectioning can miss small failure regions, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":490,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-489"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-491","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"截面 SEM 與元素判讀","titleEn":"Interpret cross-sectional SEM and composition","objective":"判斷「截面 SEM 與元素判讀」是否滿足此具體條件：成分與幾何證據支持相同假說。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Interpret cross-sectional SEM and composition meets this specific condition: Composition and geometry support the same hypothesis.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：共同檢視形貌與元素分布。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Review morphology and elemental distributions together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：成分與幾何證據支持相同假說；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Composition and geometry support the same hypothesis. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"研磨拖抹可能看似材料橋接。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Polishing smear can resemble a material bridge. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"成分與幾何證據支持相同假說；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Composition and geometry support the same hypothesis. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-491-k1","title":"截面 SEM 與元素判讀的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Interpret cross-sectional SEM and composition","text":"可檢驗條件為「成分與幾何證據支持相同假說」。可藉由「共同檢視形貌與元素分布」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Composition and geometry support the same hypothesis. Evidence can be developed through this action: Review morphology and elemental distributions together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-491-k2","title":"截面 SEM 與元素判讀的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Interpret cross-sectional SEM and composition","text":"研磨拖抹可能看似材料橋接。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Polishing smear can resemble a material bridge. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「截面 SEM 與元素判讀」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Interpret cross-sectional SEM and composition?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：研磨拖抹可能看似材料橋接。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","成分與幾何證據支持相同假說"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Polishing smear can resemble a material bridge.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Composition and geometry support the same hypothesis"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「成分與幾何證據支持相同假說」。研磨拖抹可能看似材料橋接，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Composition and geometry support the same hypothesis. Polishing smear can resemble a material bridge, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":491,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-490"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-492","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"FIB 局部介面分析","titleEn":"Assess targeted FIB interface analysis","objective":"判斷「FIB 局部介面分析」是否滿足此具體條件：製樣位置及加工影響有記錄。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess targeted FIB interface analysis meets this specific condition: Section location and preparation effects are recorded.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較局部薄片與原始缺陷座標。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare targeted sections with original defect coordinates. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：製樣位置及加工影響有記錄；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Section location and preparation effects are recorded. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"離子加工再沉積可能製造假缺陷。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Ion-beam redeposition can create apparent defects. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"製樣位置及加工影響有記錄；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Section location and preparation effects are recorded. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-492-k1","title":"FIB 局部介面分析的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess targeted FIB interface analysis","text":"可檢驗條件為「製樣位置及加工影響有記錄」。可藉由「比較局部薄片與原始缺陷座標」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Section location and preparation effects are recorded. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare targeted sections with original defect coordinates. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-492-k2","title":"FIB 局部介面分析的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess targeted FIB interface analysis","text":"離子加工再沉積可能製造假缺陷。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Ion-beam redeposition can create apparent defects. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「FIB 局部介面分析」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess targeted FIB interface analysis?","options":["製樣位置及加工影響有記錄","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：離子加工再沉積可能製造假缺陷。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Section location and preparation effects are recorded","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Ion-beam redeposition can create apparent defects.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「製樣位置及加工影響有記錄」。離子加工再沉積可能製造假缺陷，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Section location and preparation effects are recorded. Ion-beam redeposition can create apparent defects, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":492,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-491"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-493","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"壽命模型適用性","titleEn":"Check lifetime-model applicability","objective":"判斷「壽命模型適用性」是否滿足此具體條件：外推範圍與信賴限制完整揭露。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Check lifetime-model applicability meets this specific condition: Extrapolation scope and confidence limits are explicit.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把失效機制與加速模型假設逐項對照。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Match mechanisms against acceleration-model assumptions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：外推範圍與信賴限制完整揭露；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Extrapolation scope and confidence limits are explicit. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"跨機制套用加速因子會產生虛假壽命。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Cross-mechanism acceleration factors produce false lifetime estimates. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"外推範圍與信賴限制完整揭露；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Extrapolation scope and confidence limits are explicit. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-493-k1","title":"壽命模型適用性的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Check lifetime-model applicability","text":"可檢驗條件為「外推範圍與信賴限制完整揭露」。可藉由「把失效機制與加速模型假設逐項對照」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Extrapolation scope and confidence limits are explicit. Evidence can be developed through this action: Match mechanisms against acceleration-model assumptions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-493-k2","title":"壽命模型適用性的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Check lifetime-model applicability","text":"跨機制套用加速因子會產生虛假壽命。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Cross-mechanism acceleration factors produce false lifetime estimates. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-493-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"簡化疲勞模型若 N∝(Δε)^−m，假設 m=2、應變範圍加倍，預測壽命為 1/4；這是教學敏感度，不是未校準材料的真實壽命。","textEn":"For a simplified fatigue model N∝(Δε)^−m with hypothetical m=2, doubling strain range predicts one-quarter life. This is sensitivity analysis, not life data for an uncalibrated material."},{"id":"pk-493-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"加速模型需用同失效機制、相容應力範圍與實驗資料校正。不同溫度下材料黏彈性或破壞位置改變，可能使同一模型失效。","textEn":"Calibrate acceleration models with matching failure mechanisms, compatible stress ranges and experiments. Temperature-dependent viscoelasticity or changed fracture location can invalidate one model."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「壽命模型適用性」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Check lifetime-model applicability?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","外推範圍與信賴限制完整揭露","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：跨機制套用加速因子會產生虛假壽命。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Extrapolation scope and confidence limits are explicit","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Cross-mechanism acceleration factors produce false lifetime estimates."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「外推範圍與信賴限制完整揭露」。跨機制套用加速因子會產生虛假壽命，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Extrapolation scope and confidence limits are explicit. Cross-mechanism acceleration factors produce false lifetime estimates, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":493,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-492"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-494","stageId":"pk-m19","title":"失效原因與改善驗證","titleEn":"Verify corrective-action causality","objective":"判斷「失效原因與改善驗證」是否滿足此具體條件：改善效果可重現且未引入新失效。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify corrective-action causality meets this specific condition: Improvement repeats without introducing new failures.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：用對照批次確認改善前後相同失效機制。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Use controlled lots to compare the same failure mechanism. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：改善效果可重現且未引入新失效；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Improvement repeats without introducing new failures. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"良率上升本身不能證明根因已消除。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Yield improvement alone does not prove root-cause removal. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"改善效果可重現且未引入新失效；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Improvement repeats without introducing new failures. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-494-k1","title":"失效原因與改善驗證的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify corrective-action causality","text":"可檢驗條件為「改善效果可重現且未引入新失效」。可藉由「用對照批次確認改善前後相同失效機制」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Improvement repeats without introducing new failures. Evidence can be developed through this action: Use controlled lots to compare the same failure mechanism. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-494-k2","title":"失效原因與改善驗證的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify corrective-action causality","text":"良率上升本身不能證明根因已消除。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Yield improvement alone does not prove root-cause removal. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「失效原因與改善驗證」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify corrective-action causality?","options":["忽略此失效線索：良率上升本身不能證明根因已消除。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","改善效果可重現且未引入新失效","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Yield improvement alone does not prove root-cause removal.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Improvement repeats without introducing new failures","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「改善效果可重現且未引入新失效」。良率上升本身不能證明根因已消除，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Improvement repeats without introducing new failures. Yield improvement alone does not prove root-cause removal, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-ti-reliability","pkb-ti-qualification","pkb-amkor-failure","pkb-amkor-characterization"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":494,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-493"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"可靠度評估為抽樣與破壞性分析支線，並非所有成品都依次接受所有應力試驗；條件依適用規格訂定。","routeEn":"Reliability uses sampling and destructive-analysis branches; not every unit receives every stress test, and conditions follow the applicable specification.","photoId":"sem-microscope","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察掃描式電子顯微鏡設備；這是設備照片，不是本步缺陷、截面或尺寸的 SEM 影像。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe scanning-electron-microscope hardware; this is an equipment photograph, not a micrograph of this step’s defects, section or dimensions.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]},{"id":"pk-m20","title":"終測、系統驗證與良率移交","titleEn":"Final test, system validation, and yield handoff","description":"終測判斷當下功能，系統驗證判斷介面與任務行為；兩者均不等同完整壽命認證。本模組為 26 個可分支的判讀作業，課程順序不代表量產配方。網站提供原創示意模型；本模組未隨附逐步實測資料或商用允收門檻。","descriptionEn":"Final test assesses present function and system validation assesses interfaces and mission behavior; neither alone establishes full lifetime qualification. These 26 branching interpretation exercises are a learning sequence, not a production recipe. The site supplies original schematic models, not per-step measured datasets or commercial acceptance limits.","route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","order":20,"sequence":20,"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"steps":[{"id":"pk-495","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"終測治具接點校驗","titleEn":"Validate final-test fixture contacts","objective":"判斷「終測治具接點校驗」是否滿足此具體條件：治具接觸變異小於測試判定餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Validate final-test fixture contacts meets this specific condition: Fixture variability stays below decision margin.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較參考樣本重複插拔的接觸電阻。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare contact resistance across reference-unit insertions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：治具接觸變異小於測試判定餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Fixture variability stays below decision margin. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"治具高阻可被誤判成封裝開路。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Fixture resistance can mimic package opens. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"治具接觸變異小於測試判定餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Fixture variability stays below decision margin. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-495-k1","title":"終測治具接點校驗的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Validate final-test fixture contacts","text":"可檢驗條件為「治具接觸變異小於測試判定餘量」。可藉由「比較參考樣本重複插拔的接觸電阻」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Fixture variability stays below decision margin. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare contact resistance across reference-unit insertions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-495-k2","title":"終測治具接點校驗的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Validate final-test fixture contacts","text":"治具高阻可被誤判成封裝開路。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Fixture resistance can mimic package opens. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「終測治具接點校驗」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Validate final-test fixture contacts?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：治具高阻可被誤判成封裝開路。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","治具接觸變異小於測試判定餘量"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Fixture resistance can mimic package opens.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Fixture variability stays below decision margin"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「治具接觸變異小於測試判定餘量」。治具高阻可被誤判成封裝開路，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Fixture variability stays below decision margin. Fixture resistance can mimic package opens, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":495,"order":1,"localOrder":1,"prerequisiteIds":[],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-496","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"電源與地腳短路篩選","titleEn":"Screen power-ground shorts","objective":"判斷「電源與地腳短路篩選」是否滿足此具體條件：供電網路無非預期低阻路徑。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Screen power-ground shorts meets this specific condition: Power nets have no unintended low-resistance paths.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在功能上電前判讀受限量測的電阻圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Review constrained resistance maps before functional power-up. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：供電網路無非預期低阻路徑；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Power nets have no unintended low-resistance paths. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"直接功能上電可能掩蓋初始短路來源。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Immediate functional powering can obscure initial short origins. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"供電網路無非預期低阻路徑；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Power nets have no unintended low-resistance paths. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-496-k1","title":"電源與地腳短路篩選的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Screen power-ground shorts","text":"可檢驗條件為「供電網路無非預期低阻路徑」。可藉由「在功能上電前判讀受限量測的電阻圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Power nets have no unintended low-resistance paths. Evidence can be developed through this action: Review constrained resistance maps before functional power-up. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-496-k2","title":"電源與地腳短路篩選的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Screen power-ground shorts","text":"直接功能上電可能掩蓋初始短路來源。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Immediate functional powering can obscure initial short origins. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「電源與地腳短路篩選」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Screen power-ground shorts?","options":["供電網路無非預期低阻路徑","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：直接功能上電可能掩蓋初始短路來源。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Power nets have no unintended low-resistance paths","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Immediate functional powering can obscure initial short origins.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「供電網路無非預期低阻路徑」。直接功能上電可能掩蓋初始短路來源，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Power nets have no unintended low-resistance paths. Immediate functional powering can obscure initial short origins, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":496,"order":2,"localOrder":2,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-495"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-497","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"腳位導通覆蓋","titleEn":"Verify pin-continuity coverage","objective":"判斷「腳位導通覆蓋」是否滿足此具體條件：每種必要腳位有對應量測策略。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Verify pin-continuity coverage meets this specific condition: Every required pin class has a measurement strategy.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將測試項目覆蓋到每個設計腳位。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Map test items to every designed pin. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：每種必要腳位有對應量測策略；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Every required pin class has a measurement strategy. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"共用電源腳需要避免虛假的覆蓋宣稱。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Shared power pins require avoiding false coverage claims. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"每種必要腳位有對應量測策略；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Every required pin class has a measurement strategy. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-497-k1","title":"腳位導通覆蓋的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Verify pin-continuity coverage","text":"可檢驗條件為「每種必要腳位有對應量測策略」。可藉由「將測試項目覆蓋到每個設計腳位」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Every required pin class has a measurement strategy. Evidence can be developed through this action: Map test items to every designed pin. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-497-k2","title":"腳位導通覆蓋的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Verify pin-continuity coverage","text":"共用電源腳需要避免虛假的覆蓋宣稱。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Shared power pins require avoiding false coverage claims. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「腳位導通覆蓋」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Verify pin-continuity coverage?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","每種必要腳位有對應量測策略","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：共用電源腳需要避免虛假的覆蓋宣稱。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Every required pin class has a measurement strategy","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Shared power pins require avoiding false coverage claims."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「每種必要腳位有對應量測策略」。共用電源腳需要避免虛假的覆蓋宣稱，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Every required pin class has a measurement strategy. Shared power pins require avoiding false coverage claims, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":497,"order":3,"localOrder":3,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-496"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-498","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"漏電與待機電流","titleEn":"Assess leakage and standby current","objective":"判斷「漏電與待機電流」是否滿足此具體條件：測試狀態明確且尾端分布達標。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess leakage and standby current meets this specific condition: Test states are explicit and distribution tails pass.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較電壓溫度條件下的電流分布。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare currents across voltage and temperature conditions. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：測試狀態明確且尾端分布達標；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Test states are explicit and distribution tails pass. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"未固定邏輯狀態會混入動態電流。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Uncontrolled logic states mix in dynamic current. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"測試狀態明確且尾端分布達標；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Test states are explicit and distribution tails pass. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-498-k1","title":"漏電與待機電流的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess leakage and standby current","text":"可檢驗條件為「測試狀態明確且尾端分布達標」。可藉由「比較電壓溫度條件下的電流分布」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Test states are explicit and distribution tails pass. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare currents across voltage and temperature conditions. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-498-k2","title":"漏電與待機電流的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess leakage and standby current","text":"未固定邏輯狀態會混入動態電流。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Uncontrolled logic states mix in dynamic current. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「漏電與待機電流」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess leakage and standby current?","options":["忽略此失效線索：未固定邏輯狀態會混入動態電流。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","測試狀態明確且尾端分布達標","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Uncontrolled logic states mix in dynamic current.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Test states are explicit and distribution tails pass","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「測試狀態明確且尾端分布達標」。未固定邏輯狀態會混入動態電流，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Test states are explicit and distribution tails pass. Uncontrolled logic states mix in dynamic current, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":498,"order":4,"localOrder":4,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-497"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-499","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"掃描鏈測試對映","titleEn":"Map scan-chain failures","objective":"判斷「掃描鏈測試對映」是否滿足此具體條件：失效位址與測試版本可追溯。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map scan-chain failures meets this specific condition: Failing addresses and test revisions are traceable.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將掃描失效位置對映到實體晶粒。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Map scan failures to physical dies. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：失效位址與測試版本可追溯；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Failing addresses and test revisions are traceable. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"錯用測試版本可能造成全面假失敗。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Wrong test revisions can cause widespread false failures. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"失效位址與測試版本可追溯；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Failing addresses and test revisions are traceable. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-499-k1","title":"掃描鏈測試對映的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map scan-chain failures","text":"可檢驗條件為「失效位址與測試版本可追溯」。可藉由「將掃描失效位置對映到實體晶粒」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Failing addresses and test revisions are traceable. Evidence can be developed through this action: Map scan failures to physical dies. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-499-k2","title":"掃描鏈測試對映的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map scan-chain failures","text":"錯用測試版本可能造成全面假失敗。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Wrong test revisions can cause widespread false failures. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「掃描鏈測試對映」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map scan-chain failures?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：錯用測試版本可能造成全面假失敗。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","失效位址與測試版本可追溯"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Wrong test revisions can cause widespread false failures.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Failing addresses and test revisions are traceable"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「失效位址與測試版本可追溯」。錯用測試版本可能造成全面假失敗，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Failing addresses and test revisions are traceable. Wrong test revisions can cause widespread false failures, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":499,"order":5,"localOrder":5,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-498"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-500","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"記憶體功能圖樣","titleEn":"Assess memory functional patterns","objective":"判斷「記憶體功能圖樣」是否滿足此具體條件：目標故障類別都有可追溯測試。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess memory functional patterns meets this specific condition: Target fault classes have traceable tests.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較位址資料及保持類測試的覆蓋。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare address, data, and retention-test coverage. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：目標故障類別都有可追溯測試；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Target fault classes have traceable tests. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單一讀寫圖樣不能覆蓋所有記憶體故障。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"One read-write pattern cannot cover all memory faults. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"目標故障類別都有可追溯測試；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Target fault classes have traceable tests. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-500-k1","title":"記憶體功能圖樣的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess memory functional patterns","text":"可檢驗條件為「目標故障類別都有可追溯測試」。可藉由「比較位址資料及保持類測試的覆蓋」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Target fault classes have traceable tests. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare address, data, and retention-test coverage. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-500-k2","title":"記憶體功能圖樣的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess memory functional patterns","text":"單一讀寫圖樣不能覆蓋所有記憶體故障。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"One read-write pattern cannot cover all memory faults. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「記憶體功能圖樣」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess memory functional patterns?","options":["目標故障類別都有可追溯測試","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：單一讀寫圖樣不能覆蓋所有記憶體故障。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Target fault classes have traceable tests","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: One read-write pattern cannot cover all memory faults.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「目標故障類別都有可追溯測試」。單一讀寫圖樣不能覆蓋所有記憶體故障，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Target fault classes have traceable tests. One read-write pattern cannot cover all memory faults, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":500,"order":6,"localOrder":6,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-499"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-501","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"晶粒間鏈路訓練","titleEn":"Validate die-to-die link training","objective":"判斷「晶粒間鏈路訓練」是否滿足此具體條件：所有必要通道在允許補償內收斂。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Validate die-to-die link training meets this specific condition: Required lanes converge within allowed compensation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：追蹤每條通道訓練結果與補償量。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Track training results and compensation per lane. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：所有必要通道在允許補償內收斂；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Required lanes converge within allowed compensation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"訓練成功仍可能只有很小時序餘量。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Successful training can retain little timing margin. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"所有必要通道在允許補償內收斂；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Required lanes converge within allowed compensation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-501-k1","title":"晶粒間鏈路訓練的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Validate die-to-die link training","text":"可檢驗條件為「所有必要通道在允許補償內收斂」。可藉由「追蹤每條通道訓練結果與補償量」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Required lanes converge within allowed compensation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Track training results and compensation per lane. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-501-k2","title":"晶粒間鏈路訓練的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Validate die-to-die link training","text":"訓練成功仍可能只有很小時序餘量。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Successful training can retain little timing margin. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「晶粒間鏈路訓練」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Validate die-to-die link training?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","所有必要通道在允許補償內收斂","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：訓練成功仍可能只有很小時序餘量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Required lanes converge within allowed compensation","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Successful training can retain little timing margin."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「所有必要通道在允許補償內收斂」。訓練成功仍可能只有很小時序餘量，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Required lanes converge within allowed compensation. Successful training can retain little timing margin, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":501,"order":7,"localOrder":7,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-500"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-502","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"高速眼圖量測","titleEn":"Measure high-speed eye diagrams","objective":"判斷「高速眼圖量測」是否滿足此具體條件：採用指定參考平面與測試負載。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure high-speed eye diagrams meets this specific condition: Specified reference planes and loads are used.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較去嵌入前後的眼高與眼寬。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare eye height and width before and after de-embedding. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：採用指定參考平面與測試負載；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Specified reference planes and loads are used. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"治具損耗未分離會低估封裝性能。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unseparated fixture loss can understate package performance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"採用指定參考平面與測試負載；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Specified reference planes and loads are used. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-502-k1","title":"高速眼圖量測的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure high-speed eye diagrams","text":"可檢驗條件為「採用指定參考平面與測試負載」。可藉由「比較去嵌入前後的眼高與眼寬」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Specified reference planes and loads are used. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare eye height and width before and after de-embedding. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-502-k2","title":"高速眼圖量測的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure high-speed eye diagrams","text":"治具損耗未分離會低估封裝性能。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unseparated fixture loss can understate package performance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「高速眼圖量測」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure high-speed eye diagrams?","options":["忽略此失效線索：治具損耗未分離會低估封裝性能。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","採用指定參考平面與測試負載","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Unseparated fixture loss can understate package performance.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Specified reference planes and loads are used","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「採用指定參考平面與測試負載」。治具損耗未分離會低估封裝性能，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Specified reference planes and loads are used. Unseparated fixture loss can understate package performance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":502,"order":8,"localOrder":8,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-501"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-503","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"誤碼率與觀察時間","titleEn":"Assess bit error rate and observation duration","objective":"判斷「誤碼率與觀察時間」是否滿足此具體條件：報告包含位元分母與信賴限制。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess bit error rate and observation duration meets this specific condition: Reports include bit-count denominator and confidence limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：將錯誤數除以實際觀察位元數。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Divide error count by actually observed bit count. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：報告包含位元分母與信賴限制；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Reports include bit-count denominator and confidence limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"零錯誤不代表真實誤碼率為零。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Zero observed errors do not establish zero true BER. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"報告包含位元分母與信賴限制；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Reports include bit-count denominator and confidence limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-503-k1","title":"誤碼率與觀察時間的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess bit error rate and observation duration","text":"可檢驗條件為「報告包含位元分母與信賴限制」。可藉由「將錯誤數除以實際觀察位元數」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Reports include bit-count denominator and confidence limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Divide error count by actually observed bit count. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-503-k2","title":"誤碼率與觀察時間的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess bit error rate and observation duration","text":"零錯誤不代表真實誤碼率為零。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Zero observed errors do not establish zero true BER. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-503-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設有效觀測 10^12 bits 且零錯誤，在獨立稀有錯誤模型下 95% BER 上限約 3×10⁻¹²；不是 BER=0。若錯誤群聚，需另看 burst 統計。","textEn":"With hypothetical 10^12 observed bits and zero errors, an independent rare-error model gives approximately 3×10⁻¹² at 95% confidence, not BER=0. Bursts require separate statistics."},{"id":"pk-503-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"記錄碼型、速率、等化、FEC 前後、溫度和供電條件。相同平均 BER 的鏈路可能有不同突發錯誤長度和系統影響。","textEn":"Record pattern, rate, equalization, pre/post-FEC status, temperature and voltage. Equal average BER can conceal different burst lengths and system impact."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「誤碼率與觀察時間」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess bit error rate and observation duration?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：零錯誤不代表真實誤碼率為零。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","報告包含位元分母與信賴限制"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Zero observed errors do not establish zero true BER.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Reports include bit-count denominator and confidence limits"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「報告包含位元分母與信賴限制」。零錯誤不代表真實誤碼率為零，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Reports include bit-count denominator and confidence limits. Zero observed errors do not establish zero true BER, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":503,"order":9,"localOrder":9,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-502"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-504","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"供電瞬變響應","titleEn":"Measure power-delivery transients","objective":"判斷「供電瞬變響應」是否滿足此具體條件：壓降及振鈴在供電容限內。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure power-delivery transients meets this specific condition: Droop and ringing remain within supply tolerances.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較負載階躍與晶粒端電壓波形。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare load steps and die-side voltage waveforms. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：壓降及振鈴在供電容限內；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Droop and ringing remain within supply tolerances. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"電源端穩定不代表晶粒端穩定。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A stable source does not establish stable die-side voltage. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"壓降及振鈴在供電容限內；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Droop and ringing remain within supply tolerances. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-504-k1","title":"供電瞬變響應的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure power-delivery transients","text":"可檢驗條件為「壓降及振鈴在供電容限內」。可藉由「比較負載階躍與晶粒端電壓波形」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Droop and ringing remain within supply tolerances. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare load steps and die-side voltage waveforms. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-504-k2","title":"供電瞬變響應的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure power-delivery transients","text":"電源端穩定不代表晶粒端穩定。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A stable source does not establish stable die-side voltage. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「供電瞬變響應」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure power-delivery transients?","options":["壓降及振鈴在供電容限內","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：電源端穩定不代表晶粒端穩定。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Droop and ringing remain within supply tolerances","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: A stable source does not establish stable die-side voltage.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「壓降及振鈴在供電容限內」。電源端穩定不代表晶粒端穩定，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Droop and ringing remain within supply tolerances. A stable source does not establish stable die-side voltage, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":504,"order":10,"localOrder":10,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-503"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-505","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"溫度電壓性能邊界","titleEn":"Map performance across temperature and voltage","objective":"判斷「溫度電壓性能邊界」是否滿足此具體條件：功能及餘量覆蓋產品指定範圍。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Map performance across temperature and voltage meets this specific condition: Function and margin cover specified product ranges.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以一致測試版本比較條件矩陣。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare a condition matrix using one test revision. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：功能及餘量覆蓋產品指定範圍；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Function and margin cover specified product ranges. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只在典型條件通過不能代表全範圍。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Typical-condition passing does not cover the full range. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"功能及餘量覆蓋產品指定範圍；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Function and margin cover specified product ranges. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-505-k1","title":"溫度電壓性能邊界的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Map performance across temperature and voltage","text":"可檢驗條件為「功能及餘量覆蓋產品指定範圍」。可藉由「以一致測試版本比較條件矩陣」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Function and margin cover specified product ranges. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare a condition matrix using one test revision. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-505-k2","title":"溫度電壓性能邊界的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Map performance across temperature and voltage","text":"只在典型條件通過不能代表全範圍。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Typical-condition passing does not cover the full range. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「溫度電壓性能邊界」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Map performance across temperature and voltage?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","功能及餘量覆蓋產品指定範圍","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只在典型條件通過不能代表全範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Function and margin cover specified product ranges","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Typical-condition passing does not cover the full range."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「功能及餘量覆蓋產品指定範圍」。只在典型條件通過不能代表全範圍，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Function and margin cover specified product ranges. Typical-condition passing does not cover the full range, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":505,"order":11,"localOrder":11,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-504"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-506","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"系統工作負載熱點","titleEn":"Locate workload-driven system hotspots","objective":"判斷「系統工作負載熱點」是否滿足此具體條件：最高熱點與散熱設計限制相容。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Locate workload-driven system hotspots meets this specific condition: Hottest regions meet thermal design limits.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較多種代表工作負載的功耗地圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare power maps for representative workloads. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：最高熱點與散熱設計限制相容；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Hottest regions meet thermal design limits. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"總功耗相同不代表熱點相同。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Equal total power does not imply equal hotspots. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最高熱點與散熱設計限制相容；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Hottest regions meet thermal design limits. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-506-k1","title":"系統工作負載熱點的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Locate workload-driven system hotspots","text":"可檢驗條件為「最高熱點與散熱設計限制相容」。可藉由「比較多種代表工作負載的功耗地圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Hottest regions meet thermal design limits. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare power maps for representative workloads. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-506-k2","title":"系統工作負載熱點的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Locate workload-driven system hotspots","text":"總功耗相同不代表熱點相同。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Equal total power does not imply equal hotspots. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「系統工作負載熱點」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Locate workload-driven system hotspots?","options":["忽略此失效線索：總功耗相同不代表熱點相同。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","最高熱點與散熱設計限制相容","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Equal total power does not imply equal hotspots.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Hottest regions meet thermal design limits","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「最高熱點與散熱設計限制相容」。總功耗相同不代表熱點相同，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Hottest regions meet thermal design limits. Equal total power does not imply equal hotspots, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":506,"order":12,"localOrder":12,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-505"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-507","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"系統級間歇故障","titleEn":"Diagnose intermittent system faults","objective":"判斷「系統級間歇故障」是否滿足此具體條件：故障具有時間一致的診斷證據。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Diagnose intermittent system faults meets this specific condition: Faults have time-consistent diagnostic evidence.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：同步比對溫度鏈路錯誤與電源事件。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Correlate temperature, link errors, and supply events. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：故障具有時間一致的診斷證據；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Faults have time-consistent diagnostic evidence. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"未同步的紀錄可能造成假相關。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unsynchronized logs can produce spurious correlations. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"故障具有時間一致的診斷證據；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Faults have time-consistent diagnostic evidence. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-507-k1","title":"系統級間歇故障的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Diagnose intermittent system faults","text":"可檢驗條件為「故障具有時間一致的診斷證據」。可藉由「同步比對溫度鏈路錯誤與電源事件」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Faults have time-consistent diagnostic evidence. Evidence can be developed through this action: Correlate temperature, link errors, and supply events. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-507-k2","title":"系統級間歇故障的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Diagnose intermittent system faults","text":"未同步的紀錄可能造成假相關。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unsynchronized logs can produce spurious correlations. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「系統級間歇故障」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Diagnose intermittent system faults?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：未同步的紀錄可能造成假相關。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","故障具有時間一致的診斷證據"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Unsynchronized logs can produce spurious correlations.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Faults have time-consistent diagnostic evidence"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「故障具有時間一致的診斷證據」。未同步的紀錄可能造成假相關，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Faults have time-consistent diagnostic evidence. Unsynchronized logs can produce spurious correlations, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":507,"order":13,"localOrder":13,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-506"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-508","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 光纖端面檢查","titleEn":"Inspect CPO fiber end faces","objective":"判斷「CPO 光纖端面檢查」是否滿足此具體條件：端面狀態符合連接器驗收規則。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect CPO fiber end faces meets this specific condition: End faces meet connector acceptance rules.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在模擬影像中分類刮痕及污染。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Classify scratches and contamination in simulated images. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：端面狀態符合連接器驗收規則；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: End faces meet connector acceptance rules. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"污染可能同時影響損耗與反射。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Contamination can affect both loss and reflection. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"端面狀態符合連接器驗收規則；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"End faces meet connector acceptance rules. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-508-k1","title":"CPO 光纖端面檢查的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect CPO fiber end faces","text":"可檢驗條件為「端面狀態符合連接器驗收規則」。可藉由「在模擬影像中分類刮痕及污染」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: End faces meet connector acceptance rules. Evidence can be developed through this action: Classify scratches and contamination in simulated images. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-508-k2","title":"CPO 光纖端面檢查的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect CPO fiber end faces","text":"污染可能同時影響損耗與反射。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Contamination can affect both loss and reflection. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 光纖端面檢查」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect CPO fiber end faces?","options":["端面狀態符合連接器驗收規則","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：污染可能同時影響損耗與反射。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["End faces meet connector acceptance rules","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Contamination can affect both loss and reflection.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「端面狀態符合連接器驗收規則」。污染可能同時影響損耗與反射，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: End faces meet connector acceptance rules. Contamination can affect both loss and reflection, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":508,"order":14,"localOrder":14,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-507"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-509","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 光耦合位置","titleEn":"Evaluate CPO optical coupling alignment","objective":"判斷「CPO 光耦合位置」是否滿足此具體條件：耦合位置有足夠裝配誤差餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate CPO optical coupling alignment meets this specific condition: Coupling location retains assembly-error margin.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較橫向軸向位移與耦合功率地圖。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare lateral and axial offsets with coupling-power maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：耦合位置有足夠裝配誤差餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Coupling location retains assembly-error margin. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只找最高點可能忽略極窄容差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Peak-only alignment can overlook narrow tolerance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"耦合位置有足夠裝配誤差餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Coupling location retains assembly-error margin. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-509-k1","title":"CPO 光耦合位置的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate CPO optical coupling alignment","text":"可檢驗條件為「耦合位置有足夠裝配誤差餘量」。可藉由「比較橫向軸向位移與耦合功率地圖」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Coupling location retains assembly-error margin. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare lateral and axial offsets with coupling-power maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-509-k2","title":"CPO 光耦合位置的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate CPO optical coupling alignment","text":"只找最高點可能忽略極窄容差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Peak-only alignment can overlook narrow tolerance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 光耦合位置」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate CPO optical coupling alignment?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","耦合位置有足夠裝配誤差餘量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：只找最高點可能忽略極窄容差。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Coupling location retains assembly-error margin","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Peak-only alignment can overlook narrow tolerance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「耦合位置有足夠裝配誤差餘量」。只找最高點可能忽略極窄容差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Coupling location retains assembly-error margin. Peak-only alignment can overlook narrow tolerance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":509,"order":15,"localOrder":15,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-508"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-510","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 固化位移","titleEn":"Measure CPO adhesive-cure shift","objective":"判斷「CPO 固化位移」是否滿足此具體條件：固化位移與功率變化符合介面預算。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure CPO adhesive-cure shift meets this specific condition: Cure shift and power change meet interface budgets.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較固定前後光功率與對位標記。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare optical power and alignment marks before and after fixation. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：固化位移與功率變化符合介面預算；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Cure shift and power change meet interface budgets. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"初始最佳對位不保證固化後最佳。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Optimal initial alignment need not remain optimal after cure. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"固化位移與功率變化符合介面預算；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Cure shift and power change meet interface budgets. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-510-k1","title":"CPO 固化位移的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure CPO adhesive-cure shift","text":"可檢驗條件為「固化位移與功率變化符合介面預算」。可藉由「比較固定前後光功率與對位標記」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Cure shift and power change meet interface budgets. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare optical power and alignment marks before and after fixation. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-510-k2","title":"CPO 固化位移的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure CPO adhesive-cure shift","text":"初始最佳對位不保證固化後最佳。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Optimal initial alignment need not remain optimal after cure. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 固化位移」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure CPO adhesive-cure shift?","options":["忽略此失效線索：初始最佳對位不保證固化後最佳。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","固化位移與功率變化符合介面預算","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Optimal initial alignment need not remain optimal after cure.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Cure shift and power change meet interface budgets","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「固化位移與功率變化符合介面預算」。初始最佳對位不保證固化後最佳，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Cure shift and power change meet interface budgets. Optimal initial alignment need not remain optimal after cure, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":510,"order":16,"localOrder":16,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-509"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-511","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 插入損耗校準","titleEn":"Calibrate CPO insertion loss","objective":"判斷「CPO 插入損耗校準」是否滿足此具體條件：連接器及線纜參考面定義一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Calibrate CPO insertion loss meets this specific condition: Connector and cable reference planes are consistent.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較參考路徑與待測路徑光功率。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare reference-path and device-path optical power. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：連接器及線纜參考面定義一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Connector and cable reference planes are consistent. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"未扣除治具損耗會誤估元件損耗。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unaccounted fixture loss biases device loss estimates. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"連接器及線纜參考面定義一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Connector and cable reference planes are consistent. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-511-k1","title":"CPO 插入損耗校準的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Calibrate CPO insertion loss","text":"可檢驗條件為「連接器及線纜參考面定義一致」。可藉由「比較參考路徑與待測路徑光功率」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Connector and cable reference planes are consistent. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare reference-path and device-path optical power. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-511-k2","title":"CPO 插入損耗校準的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Calibrate CPO insertion loss","text":"未扣除治具損耗會誤估元件損耗。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unaccounted fixture loss biases device loss estimates. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 插入損耗校準」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Calibrate CPO insertion loss?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：未扣除治具損耗會誤估元件損耗。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","連接器及線纜參考面定義一致"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Unaccounted fixture loss biases device loss estimates.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Connector and cable reference planes are consistent"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「連接器及線纜參考面定義一致」。未扣除治具損耗會誤估元件損耗，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Connector and cable reference planes are consistent. Unaccounted fixture loss biases device loss estimates, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":511,"order":17,"localOrder":17,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-510"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-512","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 波長與偏振支線","titleEn":"Evaluate wavelength and polarization response","objective":"判斷「CPO 波長與偏振支線」是否滿足此具體條件：最差波長與偏振仍符合規範。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate wavelength and polarization response meets this specific condition: Worst-case wavelength and polarization meet criteria.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：在規定範圍比較光功率響應。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare optical responses over the specified ranges. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：最差波長與偏振仍符合規範；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Worst-case wavelength and polarization meet criteria. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"單一波長功率合格不能代表全頻帶。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Single-wavelength passing does not establish full-band performance. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"最差波長與偏振仍符合規範；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Worst-case wavelength and polarization meet criteria. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-512-k1","title":"CPO 波長與偏振支線的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate wavelength and polarization response","text":"可檢驗條件為「最差波長與偏振仍符合規範」。可藉由「在規定範圍比較光功率響應」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Worst-case wavelength and polarization meet criteria. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare optical responses over the specified ranges. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-512-k2","title":"CPO 波長與偏振支線的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate wavelength and polarization response","text":"單一波長功率合格不能代表全頻帶。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Single-wavelength passing does not establish full-band performance. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 波長與偏振支線」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate wavelength and polarization response?","options":["最差波長與偏振仍符合規範","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：單一波長功率合格不能代表全頻帶。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Worst-case wavelength and polarization meet criteria","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Single-wavelength passing does not establish full-band performance.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「最差波長與偏振仍符合規範」。單一波長功率合格不能代表全頻帶，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Worst-case wavelength and polarization meet criteria. Single-wavelength passing does not establish full-band performance, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":512,"order":18,"localOrder":18,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-511"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-513","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 光電頻率響應","titleEn":"Measure CPO electro-optic response","objective":"判斷「CPO 光電頻率響應」是否滿足此具體條件：量測涵蓋所需頻帶與動態範圍。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Measure CPO electro-optic response meets this specific condition: Measurements cover required bandwidth and dynamic range.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以校正參考面比較幅相頻率曲線。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare magnitude and phase against calibrated reference planes. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：量測涵蓋所需頻帶與動態範圍；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Measurements cover required bandwidth and dynamic range. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"光功率穩定不能證明高速頻寬合格。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Stable optical power does not prove high-speed bandwidth. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"量測涵蓋所需頻帶與動態範圍；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Measurements cover required bandwidth and dynamic range. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-513-k1","title":"CPO 光電頻率響應的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Measure CPO electro-optic response","text":"可檢驗條件為「量測涵蓋所需頻帶與動態範圍」。可藉由「以校正參考面比較幅相頻率曲線」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Measurements cover required bandwidth and dynamic range. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare magnitude and phase against calibrated reference planes. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-513-k2","title":"CPO 光電頻率響應的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Measure CPO electro-optic response","text":"光功率穩定不能證明高速頻寬合格。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Stable optical power does not prove high-speed bandwidth. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 光電頻率響應」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Measure CPO electro-optic response?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","量測涵蓋所需頻帶與動態範圍","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：光功率穩定不能證明高速頻寬合格。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Measurements cover required bandwidth and dynamic range","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Stable optical power does not prove high-speed bandwidth."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「量測涵蓋所需頻帶與動態範圍」。光功率穩定不能證明高速頻寬合格，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Measurements cover required bandwidth and dynamic range. Stable optical power does not prove high-speed bandwidth, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":513,"order":19,"localOrder":19,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-512"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-514","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 光鏈路誤碼","titleEn":"Evaluate CPO optical-link errors","objective":"判斷「CPO 光鏈路誤碼」是否滿足此具體條件：指定接收條件下誤碼證據完整。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Evaluate CPO optical-link errors meets this specific condition: Error evidence is complete at specified receiver conditions.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：同步記錄光衰減與錯誤位元。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Record optical attenuation and bit errors together. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：指定接收條件下誤碼證據完整；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Error evidence is complete at specified receiver conditions. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"只量平均光功率無法識別時序錯誤。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Average optical power cannot identify timing errors. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"指定接收條件下誤碼證據完整；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Error evidence is complete at specified receiver conditions. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-514-k1","title":"CPO 光鏈路誤碼的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Evaluate CPO optical-link errors","text":"可檢驗條件為「指定接收條件下誤碼證據完整」。可藉由「同步記錄光衰減與錯誤位元」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Error evidence is complete at specified receiver conditions. Evidence can be developed through this action: Record optical attenuation and bit errors together. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-514-k2","title":"CPO 光鏈路誤碼的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Evaluate CPO optical-link errors","text":"只量平均光功率無法識別時序錯誤。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Average optical power cannot identify timing errors. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 光鏈路誤碼」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Evaluate CPO optical-link errors?","options":["忽略此失效線索：只量平均光功率無法識別時序錯誤。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","指定接收條件下誤碼證據完整","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Average optical power cannot identify timing errors.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Error evidence is complete at specified receiver conditions","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「指定接收條件下誤碼證據完整」。只量平均光功率無法識別時序錯誤，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Error evidence is complete at specified receiver conditions. Average optical power cannot identify timing errors, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":514,"order":20,"localOrder":20,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-513"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-515","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 溫漂與熱串擾","titleEn":"Assess CPO thermal drift and crosstalk","objective":"判斷「CPO 溫漂與熱串擾」是否滿足此具體條件：補償範圍涵蓋最差熱耦合狀態。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess CPO thermal drift and crosstalk meets this specific condition: Compensation covers worst thermal-coupling states.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：切換鄰近電子負載並追蹤光譜位移。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。 進階練習：依下方工程算例重算一次，將所用單位、假設及無法由現有資料判定的項目寫入筆記。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Switch neighboring electrical loads and track spectral shifts. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing. Advanced exercise: reproduce the worked example below and record units, assumptions and conclusions unsupported by the available data.","observation":"觀察重點：補償範圍涵蓋最差熱耦合狀態；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Compensation covers worst thermal-coupling states. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"固定環境溫度仍可能有局部熱漂移。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Fixed ambient temperature can coexist with local thermal drift. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"補償範圍涵蓋最差熱耦合狀態；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Compensation covers worst thermal-coupling states. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-515-k1","title":"CPO 溫漂與熱串擾的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess CPO thermal drift and crosstalk","text":"可檢驗條件為「補償範圍涵蓋最差熱耦合狀態」。可藉由「切換鄰近電子負載並追蹤光譜位移」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Compensation covers worst thermal-coupling states. Evidence can be developed through this action: Switch neighboring electrical loads and track spectral shifts. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-515-k2","title":"CPO 溫漂與熱串擾的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess CPO thermal drift and crosstalk","text":"固定環境溫度仍可能有局部熱漂移。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Fixed ambient temperature can coexist with local thermal drift. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."},{"id":"pk-515-v9-k3","title":"工程算例與模型邊界","titleEn":"Engineering example and model boundary","text":"假設波導有效熱光係數 1.8×10⁻⁴/K、長 1 mm、λ=1.55 µm，均勻 1 K 溫升造成固定幾何相位約 0.730 rad。局部熱點則須沿路徑積分。","textEn":"For hypothetical effective thermo-optic coefficient 1.8×10⁻⁴/K, length 1 mm and λ=1.55 µm, uniform 1 K rise gives fixed-geometry phase about 0.730 rad. Local hotspots require path integration."},{"id":"pk-515-v9-k4","title":"進階判據與診斷策略","titleEn":"Advanced criteria and diagnostic strategy","text":"分別量測本地加熱效率、鄰近串擾和封裝背景漂移，建立工作點相關的耦合矩陣。只校正單顆相位器不能保證多通道共同運作時穩定。","textEn":"Measure local efficiency, neighboring crosstalk and package drift separately and build an operating-point-dependent matrix. Calibrating one phase shifter does not guarantee stability during joint operation."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 溫漂與熱串擾」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess CPO thermal drift and crosstalk?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：固定環境溫度仍可能有局部熱漂移。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","補償範圍涵蓋最差熱耦合狀態"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Fixed ambient temperature can coexist with local thermal drift.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Compensation covers worst thermal-coupling states"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「補償範圍涵蓋最差熱耦合狀態」。固定環境溫度仍可能有局部熱漂移，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Compensation covers worst thermal-coupling states. Fixed ambient temperature can coexist with local thermal drift, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo","v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":20,"sequence":515,"order":21,"localOrder":21,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-514"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"pk-516","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"CPO 光纖應變釋放","titleEn":"Inspect CPO fiber strain relief","objective":"判斷「CPO 光纖應變釋放」是否滿足此具體條件：機械擾動未耗盡光耦合餘量。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Inspect CPO fiber strain relief meets this specific condition: Mechanical disturbance preserves coupling margin.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較彎曲與拉力模型對耦合點位移。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare bend and pull models at coupling points. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：機械擾動未耗盡光耦合餘量；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Mechanical disturbance preserves coupling margin. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"封裝固定不等於光纖接頭無受力。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"A fixed package does not mean an unloaded fiber joint. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"機械擾動未耗盡光耦合餘量；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Mechanical disturbance preserves coupling margin. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-516-k1","title":"CPO 光纖應變釋放的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Inspect CPO fiber strain relief","text":"可檢驗條件為「機械擾動未耗盡光耦合餘量」。可藉由「比較彎曲與拉力模型對耦合點位移」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Mechanical disturbance preserves coupling margin. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare bend and pull models at coupling points. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-516-k2","title":"CPO 光纖應變釋放的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Inspect CPO fiber strain relief","text":"封裝固定不等於光纖接頭無受力。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"A fixed package does not mean an unloaded fiber joint. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「CPO 光纖應變釋放」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Inspect CPO fiber strain relief?","options":["機械擾動未耗盡光耦合餘量","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：封裝固定不等於光纖接頭無受力。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Mechanical disturbance preserves coupling margin","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: A fixed package does not mean an unloaded fiber joint.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「機械擾動未耗盡光耦合餘量」。封裝固定不等於光纖接頭無受力，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Mechanical disturbance preserves coupling margin. A fixed package does not mean an unloaded fiber joint, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":516,"order":22,"localOrder":22,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-515"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":true,"route":"CPO 光學支線；只用於具有光纖／光子元件的封裝。","routeEn":"CPO optical branch; only for packages containing fiber or photonic components.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-517","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"多通道良率分解","titleEn":"Decompose multi-channel yield","objective":"判斷「多通道良率分解」是否滿足此具體條件：各良率分母與重測規則明確。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Decompose multi-channel yield meets this specific condition: Denominators and retest rules are explicit.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：把單晶粒堆疊封裝及通道良率分開計算。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Separate die, stack, package, and channel yields. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：各良率分母與重測規則明確；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Denominators and retest rules are explicit. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"直接相乘相關良率可能產生偏差。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Multiplying correlated yields can bias estimates. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"各良率分母與重測規則明確；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Denominators and retest rules are explicit. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-517-k1","title":"多通道良率分解的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Decompose multi-channel yield","text":"可檢驗條件為「各良率分母與重測規則明確」。可藉由「把單晶粒堆疊封裝及通道良率分開計算」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Denominators and retest rules are explicit. Evidence can be developed through this action: Separate die, stack, package, and channel yields. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-517-k2","title":"多通道良率分解的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Decompose multi-channel yield","text":"直接相乘相關良率可能產生偏差。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Multiplying correlated yields can bias estimates. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「多通道良率分解」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Decompose multi-channel yield?","options":["以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","各良率分母與重測規則明確","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：直接相乘相關良率可能產生偏差。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Denominators and retest rules are explicit","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Multiplying correlated yields can bias estimates."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應確認「各良率分母與重測規則明確」。直接相乘相關良率可能產生偏差，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Denominators and retest rules are explicit. Multiplying correlated yields can bias estimates, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":517,"order":23,"localOrder":23,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-516"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-518","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"測試再現性與誤判","titleEn":"Assess test repeatability and false calls","objective":"判斷「測試再現性與誤判」是否滿足此具體條件：量測變異與產品變異可分離。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Assess test repeatability and false calls meets this specific condition: Measurement variation separates from product variation.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：比較跨治具與跨時間的同樣本量測。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Compare identical samples across fixtures and times. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：量測變異與產品變異可分離；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Measurement variation separates from product variation. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"無限制重測會把真失效洗成通過。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Unlimited retest can turn real failures into apparent passes. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"量測變異與產品變異可分離；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Measurement variation separates from product variation. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-518-k1","title":"測試再現性與誤判的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Assess test repeatability and false calls","text":"可檢驗條件為「量測變異與產品變異可分離」。可藉由「比較跨治具與跨時間的同樣本量測」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Measurement variation separates from product variation. Evidence can be developed through this action: Compare identical samples across fixtures and times. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-518-k2","title":"測試再現性與誤判的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Assess test repeatability and false calls","text":"無限制重測會把真失效洗成通過。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Unlimited retest can turn real failures into apparent passes. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「測試再現性與誤判」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Assess test repeatability and false calls?","options":["忽略此失效線索：無限制重測會把真失效洗成通過。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","量測變異與產品變異可分離","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。"],"optionsEn":["Ignore this failure clue: Unlimited retest can turn real failures into apparent passes.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Measurement variation separates from product variation","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應確認「量測變異與產品變異可分離」。無限制重測會把真失效洗成通過，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Measurement variation separates from product variation. Unlimited retest can turn real failures into apparent passes, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":518,"order":24,"localOrder":24,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-517"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-519","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"良率異常批次隔離","titleEn":"Isolate anomalous yield lots","objective":"判斷「良率異常批次隔離」是否滿足此具體條件：隔離範圍有可追溯資料支持。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Isolate anomalous yield lots meets this specific condition: Containment scope has traceable data support.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：以失效腳位空間圖定位共同製程因素。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Use spatial failing-pin maps to locate shared process factors. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：隔離範圍有可追溯資料支持；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Containment scope has traceable data support. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"僅按總良率隔離可能漏掉局部失效群。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Total-yield containment can miss localized clusters. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"隔離範圍有可追溯資料支持；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Containment scope has traceable data support. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-519-k1","title":"良率異常批次隔離的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Isolate anomalous yield lots","text":"可檢驗條件為「隔離範圍有可追溯資料支持」。可藉由「以失效腳位空間圖定位共同製程因素」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Containment scope has traceable data support. Evidence can be developed through this action: Use spatial failing-pin maps to locate shared process factors. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-519-k2","title":"良率異常批次隔離的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Isolate anomalous yield lots","text":"僅按總良率隔離可能漏掉局部失效群。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Total-yield containment can miss localized clusters. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「良率異常批次隔離」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Isolate anomalous yield lots?","options":["只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：僅按總良率隔離可能漏掉局部失效群。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。","隔離範圍有可追溯資料支持"],"optionsEn":["Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Total-yield containment can miss localized clusters.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average.","Containment scope has traceable data support"],"answer":3,"explanation":"應確認「隔離範圍有可追溯資料支持」。僅按總良率隔離可能漏掉局部失效群，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Containment scope has traceable data support. Total-yield containment can miss localized clusters, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":519,"order":25,"localOrder":25,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-518"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"},{"id":"pk-520","stageId":"pk-m20","title":"產品測試與譜系移交","titleEn":"Handoff product test and genealogy","objective":"判斷「產品測試與譜系移交」是否滿足此具體條件：交付狀態與所有識別資料一致。","objectiveEn":"Determine whether Handoff product test and genealogy meets this specific condition: Delivery status agrees with all identifiers.","instruction":"以示意模型練習，並在需要量測時使用你自行提供或從所列來源取得的可用資料：封存材料版本晶粒來源測試與修復對映。保存資料來源與樣本識別；依有來源的設計或材料規範判讀。缺少資料或門檻時標記待驗證。","instructionEn":"Practice with the schematic model and, where measurements are needed, use data you supply or obtain from the listed sources: Archive material revisions, die origins, tests, and repair maps. Preserve provenance and specimen identity, and use documented design or material criteria. Mark the result unverified when data or limits are missing.","observation":"觀察重點：交付狀態與所有識別資料一致；保留局部異常，勿只抄錄平均結果。","observationEn":"Observable evidence: Delivery status agrees with all identifiers. Retain local anomalies instead of reporting only averages.","failure":"測試通過不能替代缺失的可靠度資格。應先回看此步的原始資料及對照樣本，不能用後段通過結果直接排除此原因。","failureEn":"Test passing cannot replace missing reliability qualification. Revisit raw data and controls for this step; a later passing result alone does not exclude this cause.","check":"交付狀態與所有識別資料一致；提交與判斷相符的圖、曲線或紀錄。","checkEn":"Delivery status agrees with all identifiers. Submit the image, curve, or record supporting the judgment.","knowledge":[{"id":"pk-520-k1","title":"產品測試與譜系移交的驗證依據","titleEn":"Evidence for Handoff product test and genealogy","text":"可檢驗條件為「交付狀態與所有識別資料一致」。可藉由「封存材料版本晶粒來源測試與修復對映」建立證據；資料須自行提供或查證取得，完成動作與結果合格是兩個不同問題。","textEn":"The testable condition is: Delivery status agrees with all identifiers. Evidence can be developed through this action: Archive material revisions, die origins, tests, and repair maps. Supply or verify the data; performing an action and obtaining an acceptable result are separate questions."},{"id":"pk-520-k2","title":"產品測試與譜系移交的失效線索","titleEn":"Failure clues for Handoff product test and genealogy","text":"測試通過不能替代缺失的可靠度資格。將此線索與本步量測位置、材料狀態及前後差異交叉比對，保留其他合理原因直到證據足夠。","textEn":"Test passing cannot replace missing reliability qualification. Cross-check this clue against measurement location, material state, and before-and-after differences; retain alternative explanations until the evidence distinguishes them."}],"quiz":{"question":"完成「產品測試與譜系移交」時，哪項證據最直接支持通過？","questionEn":"Which evidence most directly supports passing Handoff product test and genealogy?","options":["交付狀態與所有識別資料一致","只完成操作或讀入影像，尚未檢查其是否符合判準。","忽略此失效線索：測試通過不能替代缺失的可靠度資格。","以全批平均值取代這一步所需的局部或個別證據。"],"optionsEn":["Delivery status agrees with all identifiers","Complete the action or load the image without checking the criterion.","Ignore this failure clue: Test passing cannot replace missing reliability qualification.","Replace the required local or individual evidence with a lot average."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應確認「交付狀態與所有識別資料一致」。測試通過不能替代缺失的可靠度資格，因此僅完成操作或忽略局部異常不能作為通過依據。","explanationEn":"Confirm: Delivery status agrees with all identifiers. Test passing cannot replace missing reliability qualification, so performing the action or ignoring local anomalies cannot establish a pass."},"sourceIds":["pkb-formfactor-packaging","pkb-amkor-characterization","pkb-keysight-optical","pkb-keysight-cpo"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":10,"sequence":520,"order":26,"localOrder":26,"prerequisiteIds":["pk-519"],"prerequisiteMeaning":"learning-sequence","optionalBranch":false,"route":"依邏輯、記憶體或 CPO 產品選測試支線；光學步驟只適用含光子元件的組件。","routeEn":"Select logic, memory, or CPO testing branches; optical steps apply only to photonic assemblies.","photoId":"probe-station","photoNote":"本步代表性真實照片（同模組可能共用）。可觀察探針台的定位與量測硬體；照片不包含待測電路的 I-V 曲線、測試條件或良率。","photoNoteEn":"Representative real photograph for this step (may be shared within the module). Observe probe-station positioning and measurement hardware; no DUT I–V curves, test conditions or yield data are shown.","photoEvidence":"representative-equipment-or-structure"}]}],"stepCount":520,"estimatedMinutes":6510,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","curriculumVersion":2,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/packaging-flow.svg","enrichmentVersion":9,"subcategory":"pkg-integration","subcategoryTitle":"封裝整合總覽","subcategoryTitleEn":"Package integration overview","photoId":"v9-quilt-array"},{"id":"silicon-photonics","title":"矽光子與 CPO 光引擎","titleEn":"Silicon Photonics and CPO Optical Engines","category":"packaging","summary":"48 項循序任務：由波導、光源與調變器進入光纖封裝、IL/PDL、熱串擾矩陣、應力相位、製程公差、N−1 備援與端到端 BER 驗收，含可手算的自訂工程案例。","summaryEn":"Forty-eight sequential tasks connect waveguides, sources and modulators with fiber packaging, IL/PDL, thermal-crosstalk matrices, stress-induced phase, process tolerance, N−1 redundancy and end-to-end BER acceptance, with reproducible authored examples.","scope":"矽光子與 CPO 共同設計的原創教學；24 項基礎任務後新增 24 項定量設計審查。算例不是商用 PDK 或原廠實測，外部研究依其公開測試條件引用。","scopeEn":"Authored silicon-photonics and CPO co-design teaching, preserving 24 foundational tasks and appending 24 quantitative reviews. Examples are not commercial PDK values or vendor measurements; cited research retains its published test conditions.","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging","v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl","v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress","v9-media-aim-talk","v9-media-ozen","v10-video-ea6d9da34f55"],"diagram":{"type":"photonics","labels":["光源","調變器","波導","耦合","偵測器"],"labelsEn":["Source","Modulator","Waveguide","Coupler","Detector"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"depth":4,"stages":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01","order":1,"title":"鏈路規格","titleEn":"Link specification","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-01","order":1,"title":"分辨光與電介面","titleEn":"Distinguish optical and electrical interfaces","objective":"完成「分辨光與電介面」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish optical and electrical interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"光傳輸搬運資訊，驅動、接收與控制仍需電子電路。","textEn":"Optical transmission carries information while drivers, receivers and control remain electronic."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在系統圖區分光路、電路與控制路徑。","textEn":"Separate optical, electrical and control paths in the system diagram."}],"check":"在系統圖區分光路、電路與控制路徑。","checkEn":"Separate optical, electrical and control paths in the system diagram.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分辨光與電介面」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish optical and electrical interfaces?","options":["光傳輸搬運資訊，驅動、接收與控制仍需電子電路。","鏈路可用性同時取決於光功率、頻寬和雜訊。","靠近運算晶片可縮短電連接，但提高熱與維修整合要求。"],"optionsEn":["Optical transmission carries information while drivers, receivers and control remain electronic.","Link viability depends jointly on optical power, bandwidth and noise.","Placing optics near compute shortens electrical links but increases thermal and service integration demands."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光傳輸搬運資訊，驅動、接收與控制仍需電子電路。","explanationEn":"Optical transmission carries information while drivers, receivers and control remain electronic."},"prerequisiteIds":[],"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"把雷射、調變器、光纖、偵測器、驅動器和控制器放到同一圖，以不同線型標光訊號、電資料及電源，追蹤一個位元。","instructionEn":"Place laser, modulator, fiber, detector, driver and controller in one diagram; use separate line styles for optical data, electrical data and power, and trace one bit.","failure":"把熱調諧控制線當成高速資料線，會混淆頻寬需求。","failureEn":"Treating a thermal-control line as the high-speed data path confuses bandwidth requirements.","observation":"光傳輸搬運資訊，驅動、接收與控制仍需電子電路。 在系統圖區分光路、電路與控制路徑。","observationEn":"Optical transmission carries information while drivers, receivers and control remain electronic. Separate optical, electrical and control paths in the system diagram.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-02","order":2,"title":"建立功率與頻寬預算","titleEn":"Build power and bandwidth budgets","objective":"完成「建立功率與頻寬預算」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build power and bandwidth budgets.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"鏈路可用性同時取決於光功率、頻寬和雜訊。","textEn":"Link viability depends jointly on optical power, bandwidth and noise."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列出輸出功率、損耗及接收端需求，統一單位。","textEn":"List source power, losses and receiver needs with consistent units."}],"check":"列出輸出功率、損耗及接收端需求，統一單位。","checkEn":"List source power, losses and receiver needs with consistent units.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立功率與頻寬預算」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build power and bandwidth budgets?","options":["靠近運算晶片可縮短電連接，但提高熱與維修整合要求。","光傳輸搬運資訊，驅動、接收與控制仍需電子電路。","鏈路可用性同時取決於光功率、頻寬和雜訊。"],"optionsEn":["Placing optics near compute shortens electrical links but increases thermal and service integration demands.","Optical transmission carries information while drivers, receivers and control remain electronic.","Link viability depends jointly on optical power, bandwidth and noise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鏈路可用性同時取決於光功率、頻寬和雜訊。","explanationEn":"Link viability depends jointly on optical power, bandwidth and noise."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s01-01"],"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"分列光功率、電頻寬及雜訊三張預算表，為每列指定參考面、單位和測試條件，再找出共同瓶頸。","instructionEn":"Create separate optical-power, electrical-bandwidth and noise budgets, specifying reference planes, units and conditions before identifying joint bottlenecks.","failure":"只有光功率餘裕不能證明接收器頻寬或 BER 達標。","failureEn":"Optical power margin alone does not establish receiver bandwidth or BER.","observation":"鏈路可用性同時取決於光功率、頻寬和雜訊。 列出輸出功率、損耗及接收端需求，統一單位。","observationEn":"Link viability depends jointly on optical power, bandwidth and noise. List source power, losses and receiver needs with consistent units.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-03","order":3,"title":"比較 CPO 與可插拔","titleEn":"Compare CPO and pluggables","objective":"完成「比較 CPO 與可插拔」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare cpo and pluggables.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"靠近運算晶片可縮短電連接，但提高熱與維修整合要求。","textEn":"Placing optics near compute shortens electrical links but increases thermal and service integration demands."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s01-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比较兩種架構的熱源位置和替換界面。","textEn":"Compare heat-source locations and replacement interfaces."}],"check":"比较兩種架構的熱源位置和替換界面。","checkEn":"Compare heat-source locations and replacement interfaces.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較 CPO 與可插拔」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare cpo and pluggables?","options":["鏈路可用性同時取決於光功率、頻寬和雜訊。","靠近運算晶片可縮短電連接，但提高熱與維修整合要求。","光傳輸搬運資訊，驅動、接收與控制仍需電子電路。"],"optionsEn":["Link viability depends jointly on optical power, bandwidth and noise.","Placing optics near compute shortens electrical links but increases thermal and service integration demands.","Optical transmission carries information while drivers, receivers and control remain electronic."],"answer":1,"explanation":"靠近運算晶片可縮短電連接，但提高熱與維修整合要求。","explanationEn":"Placing optics near compute shortens electrical links but increases thermal and service integration demands."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s01-02"],"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"畫交換晶片至光引擎的電路徑，分別比較可插拔與 CPO 的線長、冷卻、維修和測試接近性，列出選型依據。","instructionEn":"Draw electrical paths from switch to optics and compare pluggable and CPO length, cooling, service and test access, recording selection criteria.","failure":"電連接縮短並不自動降低包含雷射與調諧的所有系統功耗。","failureEn":"Shorter electrical links do not automatically reduce all system power including lasers and tuning.","observation":"靠近運算晶片可縮短電連接，但提高熱與維修整合要求。 比较兩種架構的熱源位置和替換界面。","observationEn":"Placing optics near compute shortens electrical links but increases thermal and service integration demands. Compare heat-source locations and replacement interfaces.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02","order":2,"title":"波導與模態","titleEn":"Waveguides and modes","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-01","order":1,"title":"理解折射率導光","titleEn":"Understand index guiding","objective":"完成「理解折射率導光」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand index guiding.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"高低折射率結構可束縛光場，但模態分布需滿足波動方程。","textEn":"Index contrast can confine light, while mode profiles must satisfy wave equations."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"標出核心、包覆層及消逝場。","textEn":"Label core, cladding and evanescent field."}],"check":"標出核心、包覆層及消逝場。","checkEn":"Label core, cladding and evanescent field.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解折射率導光」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand index guiding?","options":["有效折射率描述相位傳播，群折射率描述波包延遲。","彎曲輻射與側壁散射是不同損耗機制。","高低折射率結構可束縛光場，但模態分布需滿足波動方程。"],"optionsEn":["Effective index describes phase propagation; group index describes pulse delay.","Bend radiation and sidewall scattering are distinct loss mechanisms.","Index contrast can confine light, while mode profiles must satisfy wave equations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高低折射率結構可束縛光場，但模態分布需滿足波動方程。","explanationEn":"Index contrast can confine light, while mode profiles must satisfy wave equations."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s01-03"],"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"畫核心與上下包覆層剖面，標出折射率與場分布，將模態束縛和單純幾何光線反射分開討論。","instructionEn":"Draw core and claddings with indices and field profiles, distinguishing modal confinement from simple ray reflection.","failure":"只用核心折射率不能決定有效折射率或單模條件。","failureEn":"Core index alone does not determine effective index or single-mode operation.","observation":"高低折射率結構可束縛光場，但模態分布需滿足波動方程。 標出核心、包覆層及消逝場。","observationEn":"Index contrast can confine light, while mode profiles must satisfy wave equations. Label core, cladding and evanescent field.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-02","order":2,"title":"區分有效與群折射率","titleEn":"Distinguish effective and group index","objective":"完成「區分有效與群折射率」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for distinguish effective and group index.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"有效折射率描述相位傳播，群折射率描述波包延遲。","textEn":"Effective index describes phase propagation; group index describes pulse delay."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"說明相位計算與延遲計算應選不同折射率。","textEn":"Choose the appropriate index for phase and delay calculations."}],"check":"說明相位計算與延遲計算應選不同折射率。","checkEn":"Choose the appropriate index for phase and delay calculations.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「區分有效與群折射率」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains distinguish effective and group index?","options":["高低折射率結構可束縛光場，但模態分布需滿足波動方程。","有效折射率描述相位傳播，群折射率描述波包延遲。","彎曲輻射與側壁散射是不同損耗機制。"],"optionsEn":["Index contrast can confine light, while mode profiles must satisfy wave equations.","Effective index describes phase propagation; group index describes pulse delay.","Bend radiation and sidewall scattering are distinct loss mechanisms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"有效折射率描述相位傳播，群折射率描述波包延遲。","explanationEn":"Effective index describes phase propagation; group index describes pulse delay."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s02-01"],"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"將相位延遲使用的 neff 與群延遲使用的 ng 分開，建立長度、波長和頻率導數的單位表，勿把兩者任意互換。","instructionEn":"Separate neff for phase from ng for group delay and tabulate length, wavelength and frequency-derivative units without interchanging the indices.","failure":"以 neff 直接代替 ng 可能錯估群延遲與共振自由頻譜範圍。","failureEn":"Substituting neff for ng can misestimate group delay and free spectral range.","observation":"有效折射率描述相位傳播，群折射率描述波包延遲。 說明相位計算與延遲計算應選不同折射率。","observationEn":"Effective index describes phase propagation; group index describes pulse delay. Choose the appropriate index for phase and delay calculations.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-03","order":3,"title":"分析彎曲與粗糙損耗","titleEn":"Analyze bend and roughness loss","objective":"完成「分析彎曲與粗糙損耗」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze bend and roughness loss.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"彎曲輻射與側壁散射是不同損耗機制。","textEn":"Bend radiation and sidewall scattering are distinct loss mechanisms."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s02-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為兩種損耗各提出一項可比較量測。","textEn":"Propose a comparative measurement for each loss mechanism."}],"check":"為兩種損耗各提出一項可比較量測。","checkEn":"Propose a comparative measurement for each loss mechanism.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析彎曲與粗糙損耗」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze bend and roughness loss?","options":["彎曲輻射與側壁散射是不同損耗機制。","高低折射率結構可束縛光場，但模態分布需滿足波動方程。","有效折射率描述相位傳播，群折射率描述波包延遲。"],"optionsEn":["Bend radiation and sidewall scattering are distinct loss mechanisms.","Index contrast can confine light, while mode profiles must satisfy wave equations.","Effective index describes phase propagation; group index describes pulse delay."],"answer":0,"explanation":"彎曲輻射與側壁散射是不同損耗機制。","explanationEn":"Bend radiation and sidewall scattering are distinct loss mechanisms."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s02-02"],"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"比較直線、彎曲和粗糙側壁三種結構，在相同波長及耦合器條件下拆分損耗，記錄哪些參數尚未量測。","instructionEn":"Compare straight, bent and rough-wall structures at matching wavelength and couplers, separating losses and recording unmeasured parameters.","failure":"把端到端損耗全歸因側壁粗糙會忽略耦合與彎曲損耗。","failureEn":"Attributing all end-to-end loss to sidewall roughness ignores coupling and bends.","observation":"彎曲輻射與側壁散射是不同損耗機制。 為兩種損耗各提出一項可比較量測。","observationEn":"Bend radiation and sidewall scattering are distinct loss mechanisms. Propose a comparative measurement for each loss mechanism.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03","order":3,"title":"光源與耦合","titleEn":"Sources and coupling","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-01","order":1,"title":"辨識光源整合方式","titleEn":"Identify source integration options","objective":"完成「辨識光源整合方式」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for identify source integration options.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"矽本身不是高效率直接能隙發光材料，光源常需其他材料或外部整合。","textEn":"Silicon is not an efficient direct-bandgap emitter, so sources often need other materials or external integration."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較外部光源與異質整合的介面需求。","textEn":"Compare interface needs for external and heterogeneous sources."}],"check":"比較外部光源與異質整合的介面需求。","checkEn":"Compare interface needs for external and heterogeneous sources.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「辨識光源整合方式」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains identify source integration options?","options":["邊緣與光柵耦合在方向、頻譜及封裝可及性上不同。","矽本身不是高效率直接能隙發光材料，光源常需其他材料或外部整合。","兩個光場的空間重疊影響耦合效率，位置與角度誤差會降低重疊。"],"optionsEn":["Edge and grating coupling differ in direction, spectrum and packaging access.","Silicon is not an efficient direct-bandgap emitter, so sources often need other materials or external integration.","Spatial overlap of two fields affects coupling; position and angle errors reduce overlap."],"answer":1,"explanation":"矽本身不是高效率直接能隙發光材料，光源常需其他材料或外部整合。","explanationEn":"Silicon is not an efficient direct-bandgap emitter, so sources often need other materials or external integration."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s02-03"],"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"分別畫外接光源、異質接合雷射與研究性單片整合的電熱光邊界，列出替換、冷卻和反射管理需求。","instructionEn":"Draw electro-thermal-optical boundaries for external, bonded and research monolithic lasers, listing replacement, cooling and reflection needs.","failure":"材料整合方式不同，不能直接共用某平台的壽命與產率數字。","failureEn":"Different integration routes cannot directly share one platform's lifetime and yield.","observation":"矽本身不是高效率直接能隙發光材料，光源常需其他材料或外部整合。 比較外部光源與異質整合的介面需求。","observationEn":"Silicon is not an efficient direct-bandgap emitter, so sources often need other materials or external integration. Compare interface needs for external and heterogeneous sources.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-02","order":2,"title":"理解模態匹配","titleEn":"Understand mode matching","objective":"完成「理解模態匹配」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand mode matching.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"兩個光場的空間重疊影響耦合效率，位置與角度誤差會降低重疊。","textEn":"Spatial overlap of two fields affects coupling; position and angle errors reduce overlap."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在模擬圖調整偏移並觀察定性耦合變化。","textEn":"Vary offset in a simulation and observe qualitative coupling changes."}],"check":"在模擬圖調整偏移並觀察定性耦合變化。","checkEn":"Vary offset in a simulation and observe qualitative coupling changes.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解模態匹配」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand mode matching?","options":["兩個光場的空間重疊影響耦合效率，位置與角度誤差會降低重疊。","邊緣與光柵耦合在方向、頻譜及封裝可及性上不同。","矽本身不是高效率直接能隙發光材料，光源常需其他材料或外部整合。"],"optionsEn":["Spatial overlap of two fields affects coupling; position and angle errors reduce overlap.","Edge and grating coupling differ in direction, spectrum and packaging access.","Silicon is not an efficient direct-bandgap emitter, so sources often need other materials or external integration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩個光場的空間重疊影響耦合效率，位置與角度誤差會降低重疊。","explanationEn":"Spatial overlap of two fields affects coupling; position and angle errors reduce overlap."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s03-01"],"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"畫光纖與波導的歸一化模場，改變尺寸和位置，區分模式形狀不匹配與對位誤差，追蹤功率守恆。","instructionEn":"Draw normalized fiber and waveguide modes, vary size and position, distinguish shape mismatch from misalignment and track power conservation.","failure":"兩個模態中心重合不保證形狀或偏振匹配。","failureEn":"Coincident mode centers do not guarantee matching shape or polarization.","observation":"兩個光場的空間重疊影響耦合效率，位置與角度誤差會降低重疊。 在模擬圖調整偏移並觀察定性耦合變化。","observationEn":"Spatial overlap of two fields affects coupling; position and angle errors reduce overlap. Vary offset in a simulation and observe qualitative coupling changes.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-03","order":3,"title":"比較邊緣與光柵耦合","titleEn":"Compare edge and grating coupling","objective":"完成「比較邊緣與光柵耦合」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for compare edge and grating coupling.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"邊緣與光柵耦合在方向、頻譜及封裝可及性上不同。","textEn":"Edge and grating coupling differ in direction, spectrum and packaging access."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s03-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出兩種入射方向並註記量測介面。","textEn":"Draw incidence directions and measurement interfaces for both."}],"check":"畫出兩種入射方向並註記量測介面。","checkEn":"Draw incidence directions and measurement interfaces for both.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「比較邊緣與光柵耦合」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains compare edge and grating coupling?","options":["矽本身不是高效率直接能隙發光材料，光源常需其他材料或外部整合。","兩個光場的空間重疊影響耦合效率，位置與角度誤差會降低重疊。","邊緣與光柵耦合在方向、頻譜及封裝可及性上不同。"],"optionsEn":["Silicon is not an efficient direct-bandgap emitter, so sources often need other materials or external integration.","Spatial overlap of two fields affects coupling; position and angle errors reduce overlap.","Edge and grating coupling differ in direction, spectrum and packaging access."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣與光柵耦合在方向、頻譜及封裝可及性上不同。","explanationEn":"Edge and grating coupling differ in direction, spectrum and packaging access."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s03-02"],"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"用剖面比較端面耦合與表面光柵的光纖方向、可測試性、頻寬和偏振需求，列出每種的封裝限制。","instructionEn":"Compare fiber direction, test access, bandwidth and polarization for edge and surface-grating coupling and list packaging constraints.","failure":"不能把某一光柵的最佳波長性能視為整個波段性能。","failureEn":"A grating's best-wavelength result does not establish full-band performance.","observation":"邊緣與光柵耦合在方向、頻譜及封裝可及性上不同。 畫出兩種入射方向並註記量測介面。","observationEn":"Edge and grating coupling differ in direction, spectrum and packaging access. Draw incidence directions and measurement interfaces for both.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04","order":4,"title":"調變與偵測","titleEn":"Modulation and detection","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-01","order":1,"title":"理解相位調變","titleEn":"Understand phase modulation","objective":"完成「理解相位調變」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand phase modulation.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"折射率或有效光程改變會改變相位，可經干涉轉成強度變化。","textEn":"Changing index or optical path changes phase, which interference can convert to intensity."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用 MZI 方塊圖標出兩臂相位差。","textEn":"Mark arm phase difference in an MZI diagram."}],"check":"用 MZI 方塊圖標出兩臂相位差。","checkEn":"Mark arm phase difference in an MZI diagram.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解相位調變」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand phase modulation?","options":["折射率或有效光程改變會改變相位，可經干涉轉成強度變化。","微環在整圈相位符合條件時產生共振，溫度與幾何會改變共振位置。","光電流取決於入射功率與響應度，接收性能亦受雜訊和頻寬限制。"],"optionsEn":["Changing index or optical path changes phase, which interference can convert to intensity.","A ring resonates when round-trip phase meets the condition; temperature and geometry shift resonance.","Photocurrent depends on optical power and responsivity; noise and bandwidth also limit reception."],"answer":0,"explanation":"折射率或有效光程改變會改變相位，可經干涉轉成強度變化。","explanationEn":"Changing index or optical path changes phase, which interference can convert to intensity."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s03-03"],"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"畫兩臂干涉器並標相位和振幅，將相位調變如何轉成強度變化的機制逐一說明，再檢查偏壓點。","instructionEn":"Draw interferometer arms with phase and amplitude, explain conversion from phase to intensity and inspect the bias point.","failure":"單臂相位變化不直接等於輸出強度線性變化，工作點很重要。","failureEn":"Single-arm phase change is not directly linear intensity change; bias matters.","observation":"折射率或有效光程改變會改變相位，可經干涉轉成強度變化。 用 MZI 方塊圖標出兩臂相位差。","observationEn":"Changing index or optical path changes phase, which interference can convert to intensity. Mark arm phase difference in an MZI diagram.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-02","order":2,"title":"理解微環共振","titleEn":"Understand ring resonance","objective":"完成「理解微環共振」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand ring resonance.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"微環在整圈相位符合條件時產生共振，溫度與幾何會改變共振位置。","textEn":"A ring resonates when round-trip phase meets the condition; temperature and geometry shift resonance."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較兩個溫度下的示意共振譜。","textEn":"Compare schematic resonance spectra at two temperatures."}],"check":"比較兩個溫度下的示意共振譜。","checkEn":"Compare schematic resonance spectra at two temperatures.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解微環共振」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand ring resonance?","options":["光電流取決於入射功率與響應度，接收性能亦受雜訊和頻寬限制。","折射率或有效光程改變會改變相位，可經干涉轉成強度變化。","微環在整圈相位符合條件時產生共振，溫度與幾何會改變共振位置。"],"optionsEn":["Photocurrent depends on optical power and responsivity; noise and bandwidth also limit reception.","Changing index or optical path changes phase, which interference can convert to intensity.","A ring resonates when round-trip phase meets the condition; temperature and geometry shift resonance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"微環在整圈相位符合條件時產生共振，溫度與幾何會改變共振位置。","explanationEn":"A ring resonates when round-trip phase meets the condition; temperature and geometry shift resonance."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s04-01"],"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"從 round-trip 相位畫出環形共振條件，標自由頻譜範圍、線寬與耦合，思考溫漂如何移動共振。","instructionEn":"Build the ring resonance condition from round-trip phase, mark FSR, linewidth and coupling and consider thermal resonance shifts.","failure":"只看高 Q 不足以判斷資料頻寬、調諧需求與製程容差。","failureEn":"High Q alone does not establish data bandwidth, tuning needs or process tolerance.","observation":"微環在整圈相位符合條件時產生共振，溫度與幾何會改變共振位置。 比較兩個溫度下的示意共振譜。","observationEn":"A ring resonates when round-trip phase meets the condition; temperature and geometry shift resonance. Compare schematic resonance spectra at two temperatures.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-03","order":3,"title":"理解光電偵測","titleEn":"Understand photodetection","objective":"完成「理解光電偵測」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand photodetection.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"光電流取決於入射功率與響應度，接收性能亦受雜訊和頻寬限制。","textEn":"Photocurrent depends on optical power and responsivity; noise and bandwidth also limit reception."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s04-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"檢查功率乘以 A/W 是否得到電流單位。","textEn":"Check that power multiplied by A/W yields current."}],"check":"檢查功率乘以 A/W 是否得到電流單位。","checkEn":"Check that power multiplied by A/W yields current.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解光電偵測」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand photodetection?","options":["微環在整圈相位符合條件時產生共振，溫度與幾何會改變共振位置。","光電流取決於入射功率與響應度，接收性能亦受雜訊和頻寬限制。","折射率或有效光程改變會改變相位，可經干涉轉成強度變化。"],"optionsEn":["A ring resonates when round-trip phase meets the condition; temperature and geometry shift resonance.","Photocurrent depends on optical power and responsivity; noise and bandwidth also limit reception.","Changing index or optical path changes phase, which interference can convert to intensity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光電流取決於入射功率與響應度，接收性能亦受雜訊和頻寬限制。","explanationEn":"Photocurrent depends on optical power and responsivity; noise and bandwidth also limit reception."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s04-02"],"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"把入射光功率、響應度、光電流和暗電流接成量測鏈，再列出接收電路的頻寬與飽和限制。","instructionEn":"Connect incident power, responsivity, photocurrent and dark current in a measurement chain, then list receiver bandwidth and saturation limits.","failure":"高直流響應度不保證高速接收雜訊低或不飽和。","failureEn":"High DC responsivity does not guarantee low high-speed noise or freedom from saturation.","observation":"光電流取決於入射功率與響應度，接收性能亦受雜訊和頻寬限制。 檢查功率乘以 A/W 是否得到電流單位。","observationEn":"Photocurrent depends on optical power and responsivity; noise and bandwidth also limit reception. Check that power multiplied by A/W yields current.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05","order":5,"title":"製程與公差","titleEn":"Fabrication and tolerances","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-01","order":1,"title":"建立光子製程模組","titleEn":"Map photonic process modules","objective":"完成「建立光子製程模組」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map photonic process modules.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"波導、摻雜區、金屬及光學材料需以相容流程整合。","textEn":"Waveguides, doped regions, metals and optical materials need compatible integration."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"建立模組相依圖並標出熱預算衝突。","textEn":"Build dependencies and mark thermal-budget conflicts."}],"check":"建立模組相依圖並標出熱預算衝突。","checkEn":"Build dependencies and mark thermal-budget conflicts.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立光子製程模組」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map photonic process modules?","options":["線寬與厚度變異會改變模態及有效折射率。","晶圓級光測有助在封裝前篩選元件，但耦合誤差會影響量測。","波導、摻雜區、金屬及光學材料需以相容流程整合。"],"optionsEn":["Width and thickness variations change modes and effective index.","Wafer-level optical tests screen devices before packaging, but coupling error affects measurement.","Waveguides, doped regions, metals and optical materials need compatible integration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"波導、摻雜區、金屬及光學材料需以相容流程整合。","explanationEn":"Waveguides, doped regions, metals and optical materials need compatible integration."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s04-03"],"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"以波導、摻雜、鍺偵測器、金屬和鈍化畫模組依賴，標出共用及可選步驟，不自行拼接不同 PDK 的規則。","instructionEn":"Map dependencies among waveguides, doping, germanium detectors, metal and passivation, distinguishing shared and optional steps without mixing PDK rules.","failure":"把不同代工平台的單項最佳數字合併會產生不存在的流程。","failureEn":"Combining best numbers from different foundries creates a nonexistent flow.","observation":"波導、摻雜區、金屬及光學材料需以相容流程整合。 建立模組相依圖並標出熱預算衝突。","observationEn":"Waveguides, doped regions, metals and optical materials need compatible integration. Build dependencies and mark thermal-budget conflicts.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-02","order":2,"title":"追蹤幾何敏感度","titleEn":"Track geometry sensitivity","objective":"完成「追蹤幾何敏感度」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for track geometry sensitivity.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"線寬與厚度變異會改變模態及有效折射率。","textEn":"Width and thickness variations change modes and effective index."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"對兩個幾何參數作小擾動比較並記錄假設。","textEn":"Compare small perturbations in two geometric parameters with stated assumptions."}],"check":"對兩個幾何參數作小擾動比較並記錄假設。","checkEn":"Compare small perturbations in two geometric parameters with stated assumptions.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「追蹤幾何敏感度」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains track geometry sensitivity?","options":["波導、摻雜區、金屬及光學材料需以相容流程整合。","線寬與厚度變異會改變模態及有效折射率。","晶圓級光測有助在封裝前篩選元件，但耦合誤差會影響量測。"],"optionsEn":["Waveguides, doped regions, metals and optical materials need compatible integration.","Width and thickness variations change modes and effective index.","Wafer-level optical tests screen devices before packaging, but coupling error affects measurement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"線寬與厚度變異會改變模態及有效折射率。","explanationEn":"Width and thickness variations change modes and effective index."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s05-01"],"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"挑選寬度與厚度兩個參數，各做正負小擾動並記錄 neff 或共振偏移，檢查導數符號與線性範圍。","instructionEn":"Perturb width and thickness positively and negatively and record neff or resonance shifts, checking derivative signs and linear range.","failure":"幾何參數常相關，不能未查證就以獨立蒙地卡羅替代實際角落。","failureEn":"Geometry can be correlated and cannot automatically be replaced by independent Monte Carlo samples.","observation":"線寬與厚度變異會改變模態及有效折射率。 對兩個幾何參數作小擾動比較並記錄假設。","observationEn":"Width and thickness variations change modes and effective index. Compare small perturbations in two geometric parameters with stated assumptions.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-03","order":3,"title":"規劃晶圓光測","titleEn":"Plan wafer-level optical tests","objective":"完成「規劃晶圓光測」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan wafer-level optical tests.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"晶圓級光測有助在封裝前篩選元件，但耦合誤差會影響量測。","textEn":"Wafer-level optical tests screen devices before packaging, but coupling error affects measurement."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s05-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"把元件損耗與量測耦合損耗分開。","textEn":"Separate device loss from measurement coupling loss."}],"check":"把元件損耗與量測耦合損耗分開。","checkEn":"Separate device loss from measurement coupling loss.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃晶圓光測」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan wafer-level optical tests?","options":["晶圓級光測有助在封裝前篩選元件，但耦合誤差會影響量測。","波導、摻雜區、金屬及光學材料需以相容流程整合。","線寬與厚度變異會改變模態及有效折射率。"],"optionsEn":["Wafer-level optical tests screen devices before packaging, but coupling error affects measurement.","Waveguides, doped regions, metals and optical materials need compatible integration.","Width and thickness variations change modes and effective index."],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶圓級光測有助在封裝前篩選元件，但耦合誤差會影響量測。","explanationEn":"Wafer-level optical tests screen devices before packaging, but coupling error affects measurement."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s05-02"],"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"規劃晶圓位置、參考波導、偏振、溫度和接觸順序，讓同一晶粒的多種光測能追溯至相同座標。","instructionEn":"Plan wafer sites, reference waveguides, polarization, temperature and probing order so measurements on one die share traceable coordinates.","failure":"參考耦合器漂移可能看起來像整片波導損耗惡化。","failureEn":"Reference-coupler drift can look like wafer-wide propagation degradation.","observation":"晶圓級光測有助在封裝前篩選元件，但耦合誤差會影響量測。 把元件損耗與量測耦合損耗分開。","observationEn":"Wafer-level optical tests screen devices before packaging, but coupling error affects measurement. Separate device loss from measurement coupling loss.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06","order":6,"title":"熱機光共同設計","titleEn":"Thermomechanical optical co-design","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-01","order":1,"title":"建立熱漂移模型","titleEn":"Build a thermal-drift model","objective":"完成「建立熱漂移模型」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for build a thermal-drift model.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"溫度經熱光效應與膨脹改變光程，兩種貢獻可同時存在。","textEn":"Temperature changes optical path through thermo-optic response and expansion."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在相位模型分別標出折射率及長度項。","textEn":"Mark index and length contributions separately in a phase model."}],"check":"在相位模型分別標出折射率及長度項。","checkEn":"Mark index and length contributions separately in a phase model.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立熱漂移模型」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains build a thermal-drift model?","options":["調諧需要感測、致動與控制，致動範圍和延遲限制可補償的漂移。","溫度經熱光效應與膨脹改變光程，兩種貢獻可同時存在。","應力可改變折射率張量，材料方向與偏振需一併考慮。"],"optionsEn":["Tuning needs sensing, actuation and control; range and delay limit compensated drift.","Temperature changes optical path through thermo-optic response and expansion.","Stress can alter the refractive-index tensor; material orientation and polarization matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溫度經熱光效應與膨脹改變光程，兩種貢獻可同時存在。","explanationEn":"Temperature changes optical path through thermo-optic response and expansion."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s05-03"],"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"沿光路分段記錄溫度，先以有效熱光係數計算相位，再分開加上幾何膨脹與熱機應力項。","instructionEn":"Record temperature along path segments, compute phase using effective thermo-optic coefficients and separately add expansion and thermomechanical stress.","failure":"材料本體熱光係數與有效模態係數不能無條件互換。","failureEn":"Bulk material and effective modal thermo-optic coefficients are not interchangeable.","observation":"溫度經熱光效應與膨脹改變光程，兩種貢獻可同時存在。 在相位模型分別標出折射率及長度項。","observationEn":"Temperature changes optical path through thermo-optic response and expansion. Mark index and length contributions separately in a phase model.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-02","order":2,"title":"理解應力光學效應","titleEn":"Understand stress-optic effects","objective":"完成「理解應力光學效應」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for understand stress-optic effects.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"應力可改變折射率張量，材料方向與偏振需一併考慮。","textEn":"Stress can alter the refractive-index tensor; material orientation and polarization matter."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"列出應力到光學模型需要傳遞的量。","textEn":"List quantities transferred from stress to optical models."}],"check":"列出應力到光學模型需要傳遞的量。","checkEn":"List quantities transferred from stress to optical models.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「理解應力光學效應」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains understand stress-optic effects?","options":["應力可改變折射率張量，材料方向與偏振需一併考慮。","調諧需要感測、致動與控制，致動範圍和延遲限制可補償的漂移。","溫度經熱光效應與膨脹改變光程，兩種貢獻可同時存在。"],"optionsEn":["Stress can alter the refractive-index tensor; material orientation and polarization matter.","Tuning needs sensing, actuation and control; range and delay limit compensated drift.","Temperature changes optical path through thermo-optic response and expansion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"應力可改變折射率張量，材料方向與偏振需一併考慮。","explanationEn":"Stress can alter the refractive-index tensor; material orientation and polarization matter."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s06-01"],"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"把封裝應力張量與波導方向對應，區分軸向應變造成的路徑變長和光彈性造成的折射率改變。","instructionEn":"Map the package stress tensor to waveguide orientation, separating geometric strain from photoelastic index change.","failure":"最大等效應力不含足夠方向資訊來決定所有偏振相位。","failureEn":"Maximum equivalent stress lacks enough directional information to determine all polarization phases.","observation":"應力可改變折射率張量，材料方向與偏振需一併考慮。 列出應力到光學模型需要傳遞的量。","observationEn":"Stress can alter the refractive-index tensor; material orientation and polarization matter. List quantities transferred from stress to optical models.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-03","order":3,"title":"規劃閉迴路調諧","titleEn":"Plan closed-loop tuning","objective":"完成「規劃閉迴路調諧」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan closed-loop tuning.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"調諧需要感測、致動與控制，致動範圍和延遲限制可補償的漂移。","textEn":"Tuning needs sensing, actuation and control; range and delay limit compensated drift."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s06-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"畫出含飽和與延遲的概念控制回路。","textEn":"Draw a conceptual loop with saturation and delay."}],"check":"畫出含飽和與延遲的概念控制回路。","checkEn":"Draw a conceptual loop with saturation and delay.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「規劃閉迴路調諧」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan closed-loop tuning?","options":["溫度經熱光效應與膨脹改變光程，兩種貢獻可同時存在。","應力可改變折射率張量，材料方向與偏振需一併考慮。","調諧需要感測、致動與控制，致動範圍和延遲限制可補償的漂移。"],"optionsEn":["Temperature changes optical path through thermo-optic response and expansion.","Stress can alter the refractive-index tensor; material orientation and polarization matter.","Tuning needs sensing, actuation and control; range and delay limit compensated drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"調諧需要感測、致動與控制，致動範圍和延遲限制可補償的漂移。","explanationEn":"Tuning needs sensing, actuation and control; range and delay limit compensated drift."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s06-02"],"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"畫感測、控制器與加熱器回路，標示取樣、熱延遲、功率上限和故障處理，再模擬一個溫度擾動。","instructionEn":"Draw sensor, controller and heater loops with sampling, thermal delay, power limits and fault handling, then simulate a temperature disturbance.","failure":"控制器積分持續增長但加熱器已飽和時，不能宣稱鎖定成功。","failureEn":"A growing integrator with a saturated heater does not indicate successful lock.","observation":"調諧需要感測、致動與控制，致動範圍和延遲限制可補償的漂移。 畫出含飽和與延遲的概念控制回路。","observationEn":"Tuning needs sensing, actuation and control; range and delay limit compensated drift. Draw a conceptual loop with saturation and delay.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07","order":7,"title":"封裝與光纖","titleEn":"Packaging and fibers","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-01","order":1,"title":"建立六自由度對位","titleEn":"Map six-degree alignment","objective":"完成「建立六自由度對位」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for map six-degree alignment.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"三個平移和三個旋轉自由度可能影響光纖與晶片耦合。","textEn":"Three translations and three rotations can affect fiber-to-chip coupling."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"在原創模型標出六個自由度。","textEn":"Mark all six degrees on an original model."}],"check":"在原創模型標出六個自由度。","checkEn":"Mark all six degrees on an original model.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「建立六自由度對位」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains map six-degree alignment?","options":["三個平移和三個旋轉自由度可能影響光纖與晶片耦合。","固化收縮及材料熱膨脹可使對位在固定後改變。","光纖端面污染與機械損傷會增加鏈路損耗。"],"optionsEn":["Three translations and three rotations can affect fiber-to-chip coupling.","Cure shrinkage and thermal expansion can shift alignment after attachment.","Fiber-face contamination and mechanical damage can increase link loss."],"answer":0,"explanation":"三個平移和三個旋轉自由度可能影響光纖與晶片耦合。","explanationEn":"Three translations and three rotations can affect fiber-to-chip coupling."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s06-03"],"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"在光纖端面建立 XYZ 和三轉角，先掃描平移再檢查轉角耦合，保存峰值與容差曲面而不只最佳座標。","instructionEn":"Define XYZ and three rotations at the fiber face, scan translation and then angular coupling, retaining peak and tolerance surfaces rather than one coordinate.","failure":"對位最佳點可能非常窄，單次成功不能代表裝配產率。","failureEn":"An alignment peak may be narrow; one success does not establish assembly yield.","observation":"三個平移和三個旋轉自由度可能影響光纖與晶片耦合。 在原創模型標出六個自由度。","observationEn":"Three translations and three rotations can affect fiber-to-chip coupling. Mark all six degrees on an original model.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-02","order":2,"title":"分析黏著固化漂移","titleEn":"Analyze adhesive curing drift","objective":"完成「分析黏著固化漂移」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for analyze adhesive curing drift.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"固化收縮及材料熱膨脹可使對位在固定後改變。","textEn":"Cure shrinkage and thermal expansion can shift alignment after attachment."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"比較固定前、固定後及熱循環後的檢查點。","textEn":"Compare checks before attachment, after attachment and after thermal cycling."}],"check":"比較固定前、固定後及熱循環後的檢查點。","checkEn":"Compare checks before attachment, after attachment and after thermal cycling.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「分析黏著固化漂移」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains analyze adhesive curing drift?","options":["光纖端面污染與機械損傷會增加鏈路損耗。","三個平移和三個旋轉自由度可能影響光纖與晶片耦合。","固化收縮及材料熱膨脹可使對位在固定後改變。"],"optionsEn":["Fiber-face contamination and mechanical damage can increase link loss.","Three translations and three rotations can affect fiber-to-chip coupling.","Cure shrinkage and thermal expansion can shift alignment after attachment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固化收縮及材料熱膨脹可使對位在固定後改變。","explanationEn":"Cure shrinkage and thermal expansion can shift alignment after attachment."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s07-01"],"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"設置固化前、固化後夾持、解夾和降溫後四個檢查點，追蹤位置與光功率以分辨收縮和夾具回彈。","instructionEn":"Use before-cure, clamped-after-cure, released and cooled checkpoints to track position and power and distinguish shrinkage from fixture springback.","failure":"固化時光功率正常不代表解夾後保持相同耦合。","failureEn":"Good power while curing does not guarantee equal coupling after clamp release.","observation":"固化收縮及材料熱膨脹可使對位在固定後改變。 比較固定前、固定後及熱循環後的檢查點。","observationEn":"Cure shrinkage and thermal expansion can shift alignment after attachment. Compare checks before attachment, after attachment and after thermal cycling.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-03","order":3,"title":"設計維修與潔淨介面","titleEn":"Plan service and cleanliness interfaces","objective":"完成「設計維修與潔淨介面」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for plan service and cleanliness interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"光纖端面污染與機械損傷會增加鏈路損耗。","textEn":"Fiber-face contamination and mechanical damage can increase link loss."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s07-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"為教學接頭建立目視與損耗紀錄欄位。","textEn":"Create visual-inspection and loss-record fields for teaching connectors."}],"check":"為教學接頭建立目視與損耗紀錄欄位。","checkEn":"Create visual-inspection and loss-record fields for teaching connectors.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「設計維修與潔淨介面」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains plan service and cleanliness interfaces?","options":["固化收縮及材料熱膨脹可使對位在固定後改變。","光纖端面污染與機械損傷會增加鏈路損耗。","三個平移和三個旋轉自由度可能影響光纖與晶片耦合。"],"optionsEn":["Cure shrinkage and thermal expansion can shift alignment after attachment.","Fiber-face contamination and mechanical damage can increase link loss.","Three translations and three rotations can affect fiber-to-chip coupling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光纖端面污染與機械損傷會增加鏈路損耗。","explanationEn":"Fiber-face contamination and mechanical damage can increase link loss."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s07-02"],"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"畫可維修光介面的工具空間、彎曲半徑與應變釋放，再建立清潔、檢視和重新校正的驗證表。","instructionEn":"Draw service-tool access, bend radius and strain relief, then create cleanliness, inspection and recalibration checks.","failure":"只保護連接器而忽略纖維拉力可能使端點再次偏移。","failureEn":"Protecting only the connector while ignoring fiber tension can shift the endpoint.","observation":"光纖端面污染與機械損傷會增加鏈路損耗。 為教學接頭建立目視與損耗紀錄欄位。","observationEn":"Fiber-face contamination and mechanical damage can increase link loss. Create visual-inspection and loss-record fields for teaching connectors.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08","order":8,"title":"鏈路驗證","titleEn":"Link verification","steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-01","order":1,"title":"加總光損耗","titleEn":"Add optical losses","objective":"完成「加總光損耗」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for add optical losses.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-01-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"以 dB 表示的串聯損耗可相加，線性功率比例則相乘。","textEn":"Series losses add in dB and multiply as linear power ratios."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-01-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"用兩種表示法計算同一示意鏈路並核對。","textEn":"Calculate one illustrative link in both forms and compare."}],"check":"用兩種表示法計算同一示意鏈路並核對。","checkEn":"Calculate one illustrative link in both forms and compare.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「加總光損耗」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains add optical losses?","options":["眼圖提供時序與幅度品質線索，誤碼率需帶有測試長度和條件。","光學功能、封裝穩定與可靠度需分別驗證後再整合判讀。","以 dB 表示的串聯損耗可相加，線性功率比例則相乘。"],"optionsEn":["An eye diagram indicates timing and amplitude quality; error-rate results need test length and conditions.","Optical function, package stability and reliability need separate validation before integration.","Series losses add in dB and multiply as linear power ratios."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以 dB 表示的串聯損耗可相加，線性功率比例則相乘。","explanationEn":"Series losses add in dB and multiply as linear power ratios."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s07-03"],"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"將每個耦合、波導、分光和接頭損耗放在同一參考面預算，分別標量測與教學假設，再計最差餘裕。","instructionEn":"Budget couplers, guides, splitters and connectors at common reference planes, label measurements versus assumptions and calculate worst margin.","failure":"dB 可相加，但 dBm 是絕對功率，不能把多個 dBm 損耗直接相加。","failureEn":"Losses in dB add, whereas dBm denotes absolute power and cannot be summed as losses.","observation":"以 dB 表示的串聯損耗可相加，線性功率比例則相乘。 用兩種表示法計算同一示意鏈路並核對。","observationEn":"Series losses add in dB and multiply as linear power ratios. Calculate one illustrative link in both forms and compare.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-02","order":2,"title":"解讀眼圖與誤碼","titleEn":"Interpret eye diagrams and errors","objective":"完成「解讀眼圖與誤碼」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for interpret eye diagrams and errors.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-02-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"眼圖提供時序與幅度品質線索，誤碼率需帶有測試長度和條件。","textEn":"An eye diagram indicates timing and amplitude quality; error-rate results need test length and conditions."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-02-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"註記資料率、觀測位元數與環境條件。","textEn":"Record data rate, observed bit count and environmental conditions."}],"check":"註記資料率、觀測位元數與環境條件。","checkEn":"Record data rate, observed bit count and environmental conditions.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「解讀眼圖與誤碼」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains interpret eye diagrams and errors?","options":["以 dB 表示的串聯損耗可相加，線性功率比例則相乘。","眼圖提供時序與幅度品質線索，誤碼率需帶有測試長度和條件。","光學功能、封裝穩定與可靠度需分別驗證後再整合判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Series losses add in dB and multiply as linear power ratios.","An eye diagram indicates timing and amplitude quality; error-rate results need test length and conditions.","Optical function, package stability and reliability need separate validation before integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"眼圖提供時序與幅度品質線索，誤碼率需帶有測試長度和條件。","explanationEn":"An eye diagram indicates timing and amplitude quality; error-rate results need test length and conditions."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s08-01"],"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"同時保存眼圖量測條件、錯誤計數和位元數，區分 FEC 前後結果，檢查是否有突發或間歇故障。","instructionEn":"Save eye-diagram conditions, error counts and bit counts, distinguish pre/post-FEC results and inspect burst or intermittent faults.","failure":"眼圖張開不能單獨證明指定信賴度的低 BER。","failureEn":"An open eye alone does not establish low BER at a stated confidence.","observation":"眼圖提供時序與幅度品質線索，誤碼率需帶有測試長度和條件。 註記資料率、觀測位元數與環境條件。","observationEn":"An eye diagram indicates timing and amplitude quality; error-rate results need test length and conditions. Record data rate, observed bit count and environmental conditions.","enrichmentVersion":9},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-03","order":3,"title":"提交整合證據","titleEn":"Submit integration evidence","objective":"完成「提交整合證據」的概念模型與工程檢核。","objectiveEn":"Build and review the conceptual model for submit integration evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-03-k1","title":"核心原理","titleEn":"Core principle","text":"光學功能、封裝穩定與可靠度需分別驗證後再整合判讀。","textEn":"Optical function, package stability and reliability need separate validation before integration."},{"id":"silicon-photonics-s08-03-k2","title":"總工程師檢核","titleEn":"Chief engineer review","text":"交付功率預算、對位紀錄與熱漂移假設。","textEn":"Deliver power budget, alignment record and thermal-drift assumptions."}],"check":"交付功率預算、對位紀錄與熱漂移假設。","checkEn":"Deliver power budget, alignment record and thermal-drift assumptions.","sourceIds":["intel-photonics","intel-packaging"],"simulationOnly":true,"quiz":{"question":"哪個敘述最直接說明「提交整合證據」的核心原理？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains submit integration evidence?","options":["光學功能、封裝穩定與可靠度需分別驗證後再整合判讀。","以 dB 表示的串聯損耗可相加，線性功率比例則相乘。","眼圖提供時序與幅度品質線索，誤碼率需帶有測試長度和條件。"],"optionsEn":["Optical function, package stability and reliability need separate validation before integration.","Series losses add in dB and multiply as linear power ratios.","An eye diagram indicates timing and amplitude quality; error-rate results need test length and conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光學功能、封裝穩定與可靠度需分別驗證後再整合判讀。","explanationEn":"Optical function, package stability and reliability need separate validation before integration."},"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s08-02"],"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":20,"instruction":"整合光路、熱模型、對位容差、量測原檔和未解議題，以需求編號對應每一份證據，請同學重算一項預算。","instructionEn":"Combine optical routes, thermal models, alignment tolerances, raw data and open issues, map evidence to requirement IDs and ask a peer to reproduce a budget.","failure":"把缺少量測的項目標為已驗證，會使系統交付失去可追溯性。","failureEn":"Marking unmeasured items verified destroys handoff traceability.","observation":"光學功能、封裝穩定與可靠度需分別驗證後再整合判讀。 交付功率預算、對位紀錄與熱漂移假設。","observationEn":"Optical function, package stability and reliability need separate validation before integration. Deliver power budget, alignment record and thermal-drift assumptions.","enrichmentVersion":9}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-stage09","order":9,"sequence":9,"title":"光學量測與系統能量","titleEn":"Optical metrology and system energy","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-025","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-s08-03"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"分離鏈路參考面與插入損耗","titleEn":"Separate reference planes and insertion loss","objective":"報告 6.02 dB 並保留參考面、波長和偏振。","objectiveEn":"Report 6.02 dB with reference planes, wavelength and polarization.","instruction":"畫出雷射、光纖、PIC 與功率計，各接頭編號。讓旁路與 DUT 共用參考面，列出尚未去嵌的項目。","instructionEn":"Draw laser, fiber, PIC and meter, numbering connectors. Give bypass and DUT common reference planes and list unremoved terms.","observation":"假設參考功率 1.00 mW，輸出 0.25 mW，IL=10 log10(1/0.25)=6.02 dB；此值仍包含未去嵌耦合器。","observationEn":"With hypothetical reference 1.00 mW and output 0.25 mW, IL=10 log10(1/0.25)=6.02 dB; unremoved coupler loss remains included.","failure":"重新插拔參考線後未重校正，會把治具漂移當元件變化。","failureEn":"Reconnecting without rereferencing makes fixture drift appear to be device change.","check":"報告 6.02 dB 並保留參考面、波長和偏振。","checkEn":"Report 6.02 dB with reference planes, wavelength and polarization.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-025-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"損耗附波長、偏振與參考面；端到端數字不能冒充波導本身損耗。","textEn":"Loss requires wavelength, polarization and reference planes; end-to-end loss is not waveguide loss alone.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-025-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設參考功率 1.00 mW，輸出 0.25 mW，IL=10 log10(1/0.25)=6.02 dB；此值仍包含未去嵌耦合器。 驗收：報告 6.02 dB 並保留參考面、波長和偏振。","textEn":"With hypothetical reference 1.00 mW and output 0.25 mW, IL=10 log10(1/0.25)=6.02 dB; unremoved coupler loss remains included. Acceptance: Report 6.02 dB with reference planes, wavelength and polarization."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「分離鏈路參考面與插入損耗」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Separate reference planes and insertion loss\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["報告 6.02 dB 並保留參考面、波長和偏振。","把 6.02 dB 全部指派為波導傳播損耗。","僅有輸出功率便能比較不同量測。"],"optionsEn":["Report 6.02 dB with reference planes, wavelength and polarization.","Assign all 6.02 dB to waveguide propagation.","Output power alone suffices to compare different measurements."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設參考功率 1.00 mW，輸出 0.25 mW，IL=10 log10(1/0.25)=6.02 dB；此值仍包含未去嵌耦合器。 重新插拔參考線後未重校正，會把治具漂移當元件變化。","explanationEn":"With hypothetical reference 1.00 mW and output 0.25 mW, IL=10 log10(1/0.25)=6.02 dB; unremoved coupler loss remains included. Reconnecting without rereferencing makes fixture drift appear to be device change."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-026","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-025"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"以切回法拆出傳播損耗","titleEn":"Extract propagation loss by cutback","objective":"分別報告 α、C、殘差與彎曲數。","objectiveEn":"Report α, C, residuals and bend counts separately.","instruction":"用三個長度資料擬合直線，檢查殘差。加入具有不同彎曲數的樣本，辨識額外幾何損耗。","instructionEn":"Fit three lengths and inspect residuals. Add a sample with a different bend count and identify added geometric loss.","observation":"假設 1、2、3 cm 對應 3.4、3.8、4.2 dB，α=0.4 dB/cm、C=3.0 dB；只有兩端等效時才能以 C/2 分配單端耦合。","observationEn":"Hypothetical 1, 2, 3 cm structures at 3.4, 3.8, 4.2 dB give α=0.4 dB/cm and C=3.0 dB; C/2 applies to one coupler only if the ends are equivalent.","failure":"長波導有額外交叉時，斜率不再只含傳播損耗。","failureEn":"Extra crossings on longer paths contaminate the propagation slope.","check":"分別報告 α、C、殘差與彎曲數。","checkEn":"Report α, C, residuals and bend counts separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-026-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"同型耦合器搭配不同長度波導，可擬合 IL=αL+C；斜率和截距代表不同機制。","textEn":"Matched couplers with different waveguide lengths can fit IL=αL+C; slope and intercept represent different mechanisms.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-026-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 1、2、3 cm 對應 3.4、3.8、4.2 dB，α=0.4 dB/cm、C=3.0 dB；只有兩端等效時才能以 C/2 分配單端耦合。 驗收：分別報告 α、C、殘差與彎曲數。","textEn":"Hypothetical 1, 2, 3 cm structures at 3.4, 3.8, 4.2 dB give α=0.4 dB/cm and C=3.0 dB; C/2 applies to one coupler only if the ends are equivalent. Acceptance: Report α, C, residuals and bend counts separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「以切回法拆出傳播損耗」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Extract propagation loss by cutback\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["直接以 4.2/3=1.4 dB/cm 當傳播損耗。","分別報告 α、C、殘差與彎曲數。","長度不同即可忽略耦合器差異。"],"optionsEn":["Use 4.2/3=1.4 dB/cm as propagation loss.","Report α, C, residuals and bend counts separately.","Different lengths justify ignoring coupler differences."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設 1、2、3 cm 對應 3.4、3.8、4.2 dB，α=0.4 dB/cm、C=3.0 dB；只有兩端等效時才能以 C/2 分配單端耦合。 長波導有額外交叉時，斜率不再只含傳播損耗。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical 1, 2, 3 cm structures at 3.4, 3.8, 4.2 dB give α=0.4 dB/cm and C=3.0 dB; C/2 applies to one coupler only if the ends are equivalent. Extra crossings on longer paths contaminate the propagation slope."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-027","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-026"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"把偏振依賴納入餘裕","titleEn":"Include polarization dependence in margin","objective":"報告極值、2.04 dB 與重複量測漂移。","objectiveEn":"Report extrema, 2.04 dB and repeatability drift.","instruction":"固定波長和對位，掃描偏振並記錄極值與重複性，再以最差狀態建立預算。","instructionEn":"Fix wavelength and alignment, scan polarization and record extrema and repeatability, then budget the worst state.","observation":"假設 Pmax=0.8 mW、Pmin=0.5 mW，PDL=2.04 dB；只量 TE 不能證明已找到所有偏振極值。","observationEn":"Hypothetical Pmax=0.8 mW and Pmin=0.5 mW give PDL=2.04 dB; TE alone does not establish extrema over all polarizations.","failure":"偏振掃描時的溫漂可能被誤算入 PDL。","failureEn":"Thermal drift during polarization scanning can contaminate PDL.","check":"報告極值、2.04 dB 與重複量測漂移。","checkEn":"Report extrema, 2.04 dB and repeatability drift.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-027-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"PDL=10 log10(Pmax/Pmin) 量化隨偏振改變的傳輸差異，與插入損耗定義不同。","textEn":"PDL=10 log10(Pmax/Pmin) measures variation over polarization and differs from insertion loss.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-027-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 Pmax=0.8 mW、Pmin=0.5 mW，PDL=2.04 dB；只量 TE 不能證明已找到所有偏振極值。 驗收：報告極值、2.04 dB 與重複量測漂移。","textEn":"Hypothetical Pmax=0.8 mW and Pmin=0.5 mW give PDL=2.04 dB; TE alone does not establish extrema over all polarizations. Acceptance: Report extrema, 2.04 dB and repeatability drift."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「把偏振依賴納入餘裕」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Include polarization dependence in margin\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["將功率相減後標為 0.3 dB。","最佳 TE 點代表所有偏振皆合格。","報告極值、2.04 dB 與重複量測漂移。"],"optionsEn":["Subtract powers and label the result 0.3 dB.","The best TE point proves every polarization passes.","Report extrema, 2.04 dB and repeatability drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設 Pmax=0.8 mW、Pmin=0.5 mW，PDL=2.04 dB；只量 TE 不能證明已找到所有偏振極值。 偏振掃描時的溫漂可能被誤算入 PDL。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical Pmax=0.8 mW and Pmin=0.5 mW give PDL=2.04 dB; TE alone does not establish extrema over all polarizations. Thermal drift during polarization scanning can contaminate PDL."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-028","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-027"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"校準光纖對位容差盆地","titleEn":"Calibrate the fiber-alignment tolerance basin","objective":"提交等高線、搜尋間隔與重複定位誤差。","objectiveEn":"Submit contours, scan spacing and repositioning error.","instruction":"在峰值附近做 X/Y 網格掃描，將功率轉為額外損耗，畫出 1 dB 等高線，再掃描俯仰角。","instructionEn":"Scan an X/Y grid around the peak, convert to excess loss, draw the 1 dB contour and then sweep pitch angle.","observation":"假設峰值 1 mW，1 dB 邊界為 0.794 mW；0.75 mW 則是 1.25 dB 額外損耗，已超過此自訂窗口。","observationEn":"For a hypothetical 1 mW peak, the 1 dB boundary is 0.794 mW; 0.75 mW is 1.25 dB excess loss, outside that authored window.","failure":"只保存峰值會掩蓋非常窄的裝配容差。","failureEn":"Saving only the peak hides a narrow assembly tolerance.","check":"提交等高線、搜尋間隔與重複定位誤差。","checkEn":"Submit contours, scan spacing and repositioning error.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-028-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"最高光功率只是一點；封裝需要 X、Y、角度和溫度共同限制的可接受區域。","textEn":"Peak power is one point; packaging requires acceptable regions jointly constrained by X, Y, angle and temperature.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-028-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設峰值 1 mW，1 dB 邊界為 0.794 mW；0.75 mW 則是 1.25 dB 額外損耗，已超過此自訂窗口。 驗收：提交等高線、搜尋間隔與重複定位誤差。","textEn":"For a hypothetical 1 mW peak, the 1 dB boundary is 0.794 mW; 0.75 mW is 1.25 dB excess loss, outside that authored window. Acceptance: Submit contours, scan spacing and repositioning error."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「校準光纖對位容差盆地」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Calibrate the fiber-alignment tolerance basin\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["提交等高線、搜尋間隔與重複定位誤差。","0.75 mW 位於 1 dB 容差內。","峰值最高必然代表量產窗口最寬。"],"optionsEn":["Submit contours, scan spacing and repositioning error.","0.75 mW is inside the 1 dB tolerance.","The highest peak guarantees the widest production window."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設峰值 1 mW，1 dB 邊界為 0.794 mW；0.75 mW 則是 1.25 dB 額外損耗，已超過此自訂窗口。 只保存峰值會掩蓋非常窄的裝配容差。","explanationEn":"For a hypothetical 1 mW peak, the 1 dB boundary is 0.794 mW; 0.75 mW is 1.25 dB excess loss, outside that authored window. Saving only the peak hides a narrow assembly tolerance."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-029","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-028"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"區分光功率與接收器靈敏度","titleEn":"Distinguish power from receiver sensitivity","objective":"在一致條件下算出 3 dB 並列未分配餘裕。","objectiveEn":"Obtain 3 dB under matching conditions and list unallocated margins.","instruction":"用同一格式列發射功率、總損耗與接收靈敏度，另列老化與不確定度餘裕。","instructionEn":"Tabulate launch power, total loss and sensitivity for matching conditions, then separately allocate aging and uncertainty margin.","observation":"假設均為平均功率：+2 dBm 減 8 dB 得 −6 dBm，靈敏度 −9 dBm，原始餘裕 3 dB。","observationEn":"Assuming average power throughout, +2 dBm minus 8 dB gives −6 dBm; sensitivity −9 dBm yields 3 dB raw margin.","failure":"混用 PAM4 OMA 和 NRZ 平均功率，可能算出沒有意義的餘裕。","failureEn":"Mixing PAM4 OMA with NRZ average power can create meaningless margin.","check":"在一致條件下算出 3 dB 並列未分配餘裕。","checkEn":"Obtain 3 dB under matching conditions and list unallocated margins.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-029-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"靈敏度附資料格式、速率、誤碼門檻及 FEC 條件；平均功率不能與 OMA 直接混用。","textEn":"Sensitivity depends on format, rate, BER and FEC; average power cannot be interchanged directly with OMA.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-029-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設均為平均功率：+2 dBm 減 8 dB 得 −6 dBm，靈敏度 −9 dBm，原始餘裕 3 dB。 驗收：在一致條件下算出 3 dB 並列未分配餘裕。","textEn":"Assuming average power throughout, +2 dBm minus 8 dB gives −6 dBm; sensitivity −9 dBm yields 3 dB raw margin. Acceptance: Obtain 3 dB under matching conditions and list unallocated margins."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「區分光功率與接收器靈敏度」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Distinguish power from receiver sensitivity\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["不同調變格式可直接共用靈敏度。","在一致條件下算出 3 dB 並列未分配餘裕。","接收功率非零即證明誤碼合格。"],"optionsEn":["Different formats can directly share sensitivity values.","Obtain 3 dB under matching conditions and list unallocated margins.","Nonzero received power proves acceptable BER."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設均為平均功率：+2 dBm 減 8 dB 得 −6 dBm，靈敏度 −9 dBm，原始餘裕 3 dB。 混用 PAM4 OMA 和 NRZ 平均功率，可能算出沒有意義的餘裕。","explanationEn":"Assuming average power throughout, +2 dBm minus 8 dB gives −6 dBm; sensitivity −9 dBm yields 3 dB raw margin. Mixing PAM4 OMA with NRZ average power can create meaningless margin."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-030","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-029"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"分拆系統每位元能量","titleEn":"Separate system energy per bit","objective":"用同一功耗邊界比較 10 與 40 pJ/bit。","objectiveEn":"Compare 10 and 40 pJ/bit using the same power boundary.","instruction":"建立能量樹並列滿載及待機功耗，使用有效吞吐量重算，而非只用標示線路速率。","instructionEn":"Build a power tree with active and idle consumption and recalculate using payload throughput rather than only rated line rate.","observation":"假設 4 W、400 Gb/s 有效吞吐，為 10 pJ/bit；若吞吐降至 100 Gb/s 而功率不變，為 40 pJ/bit。","observationEn":"Hypothetical 4 W at 400 Gb/s payload gives 10 pJ/bit; at 100 Gb/s with unchanged power it gives 40 pJ/bit.","failure":"只計調變器漏掉持續運作的光源與熱控制。","failureEn":"Counting only the modulator omits continuous laser and thermal-control power.","check":"用同一功耗邊界比較 10 與 40 pJ/bit。","checkEn":"Compare 10 and 40 pJ/bit using the same power boundary.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-030-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"Ebit=P/B 的範圍應說明是否含雷射、驅動、接收、DSP、TEC 和調諧。","textEn":"Ebit=P/B must state whether laser, driver, receiver, DSP, TEC and tuning are included.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-pdl"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-030-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 4 W、400 Gb/s 有效吞吐，為 10 pJ/bit；若吞吐降至 100 Gb/s 而功率不變，為 40 pJ/bit。 驗收：用同一功耗邊界比較 10 與 40 pJ/bit。","textEn":"Hypothetical 4 W at 400 Gb/s payload gives 10 pJ/bit; at 100 Gb/s with unchanged power it gives 40 pJ/bit. Acceptance: Compare 10 and 40 pJ/bit using the same power boundary."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「分拆系統每位元能量」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Separate system energy per bit\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["低負載的每位元能量一定保持不變。","忽略雷射仍能稱為全系統功耗。","用同一功耗邊界比較 10 與 40 pJ/bit。"],"optionsEn":["Energy per bit must remain constant at low load.","Omitting the laser still yields full-system power.","Compare 10 and 40 pJ/bit using the same power boundary."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設 4 W、400 Gb/s 有效吞吐，為 10 pJ/bit；若吞吐降至 100 Gb/s 而功率不變，為 40 pJ/bit。 只計調變器漏掉持續運作的光源與熱控制。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical 4 W at 400 Gb/s payload gives 10 pJ/bit; at 100 Gb/s with unchanged power it gives 40 pJ/bit. Counting only the modulator omits continuous laser and thermal-control power."}}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-stage10","order":10,"sequence":10,"title":"熱、機械與光學耦合","titleEn":"Thermal, mechanical and optical coupling","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-031","order":1,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-030"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"從溫度場積分光學相位","titleEn":"Integrate phase from a temperature field","objective":"算出 0.730 rad 並註記固定幾何近似。","objectiveEn":"Obtain 0.730 rad and state the fixed-geometry approximation.","instruction":"把光路分成三段，列長度與溫升，用有效熱光係數相加，再另列熱膨脹項。","instructionEn":"Divide the path into three sections, tabulate lengths and temperature rises, sum using an effective thermo-optic coefficient and retain expansion separately.","observation":"假設 L=1 mm、λ=1.55 µm、dneff/dT=1.8×10⁻⁴/K、ΔT=1 K，固定幾何得 Δφ=0.730 rad；此係數不是通用 PDK 值。","observationEn":"Hypothetical L=1 mm, λ=1.55 µm, dneff/dT=1.8×10⁻⁴/K and ΔT=1 K give Δφ=0.730 rad at fixed geometry; the coefficient is not universal PDK data.","failure":"核心材料係數不等於有效模態係數，後者含包覆層與模場比例。","failureEn":"The core-material coefficient differs from the effective modal coefficient, which includes cladding and confinement.","check":"算出 0.730 rad 並註記固定幾何近似。","checkEn":"Obtain 0.730 rad and state the fixed-geometry approximation.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-031-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"φ=(2π/λ)∫neff(s,T,σ)ds；非均勻熱點須沿光路積分，不能只讀封裝平均溫度。","textEn":"φ=(2π/λ)∫neff(s,T,σ)ds; nonuniform hotspots require path integration, not package-average temperature.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-031-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 L=1 mm、λ=1.55 µm、dneff/dT=1.8×10⁻⁴/K、ΔT=1 K，固定幾何得 Δφ=0.730 rad；此係數不是通用 PDK 值。 驗收：算出 0.730 rad 並註記固定幾何近似。","textEn":"Hypothetical L=1 mm, λ=1.55 µm, dneff/dT=1.8×10⁻⁴/K and ΔT=1 K give Δφ=0.730 rad at fixed geometry; the coefficient is not universal PDK data. Acceptance: Obtain 0.730 rad and state the fixed-geometry approximation."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「從溫度場積分光學相位」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Integrate phase from a temperature field\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["算出 0.730 rad 並註記固定幾何近似。","只需用封裝平均溫度便能保證局部相位。","mm 與 µm 可不換算直接相除。"],"optionsEn":["Obtain 0.730 rad and state the fixed-geometry approximation.","Package-average temperature guarantees local phase.","Divide mm by µm without unit conversion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設 L=1 mm、λ=1.55 µm、dneff/dT=1.8×10⁻⁴/K、ΔT=1 K，固定幾何得 Δφ=0.730 rad；此係數不是通用 PDK 值。 核心材料係數不等於有效模態係數，後者含包覆層與模場比例。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical L=1 mm, λ=1.55 µm, dneff/dT=1.8×10⁻⁴/K and ΔT=1 K give Δφ=0.730 rad at fixed geometry; the coefficient is not universal PDK data. The core-material coefficient differs from the effective modal coefficient, which includes cladding and confinement."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-032","order":2,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-031"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"建立加熱器熱串擾矩陣","titleEn":"Build a heater thermal-crosstalk matrix","objective":"保留非對角項並驗證 1.2 rad 聯合響應。","objectiveEn":"Retain off-diagonal terms and verify the 1.2 rad joint response.","instruction":"一次擾動一個加熱器，記錄所有監測相位；用未參與擬合的雙加熱器組合驗證。","instructionEn":"Perturb one heater at a time and record all phases; validate using joint heater combinations excluded from fitting.","observation":"假設 H=[[0.10,0.02],[0.02,0.10]] rad/mW，各輸入 10 mW，兩個相位均改變 1.2 rad，而非 1.0。","observationEn":"For hypothetical H=[[0.10,0.02],[0.02,0.10]] rad/mW and 10 mW on each heater, both phases shift 1.2 rad, not 1.0.","failure":"單加熱器校正而忽略鄰居，會在同時工作時失準。","failureEn":"Calibration that ignores neighbors fails during simultaneous operation.","check":"保留非對角項並驗證 1.2 rad 聯合響應。","checkEn":"Retain off-diagonal terms and verify the 1.2 rad joint response.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-032-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"小訊號 Δφ=HΔP；對角項是本地效率，非對角項是熱串擾，適用於指定工作點附近。","textEn":"Small-signal Δφ=HΔP has local efficiency on the diagonal and crosstalk off diagonal, valid near a stated operating point.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-032-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 H=[[0.10,0.02],[0.02,0.10]] rad/mW，各輸入 10 mW，兩個相位均改變 1.2 rad，而非 1.0。 驗收：保留非對角項並驗證 1.2 rad 聯合響應。","textEn":"For hypothetical H=[[0.10,0.02],[0.02,0.10]] rad/mW and 10 mW on each heater, both phases shift 1.2 rad, not 1.0. Acceptance: Retain off-diagonal terms and verify the 1.2 rad joint response."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「建立加熱器熱串擾矩陣」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Build a heater thermal-crosstalk matrix\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["非對角項都只是雜訊，可歸零。","保留非對角項並驗證 1.2 rad 聯合響應。","單獨校正即可免除聯合驗證。"],"optionsEn":["All off-diagonal terms are noise and may be zeroed.","Retain off-diagonal terms and verify the 1.2 rad joint response.","Independent calibration eliminates joint verification."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設 H=[[0.10,0.02],[0.02,0.10]] rad/mW，各輸入 10 mW，兩個相位均改變 1.2 rad，而非 1.0。 單加熱器校正而忽略鄰居，會在同時工作時失準。","explanationEn":"For hypothetical H=[[0.10,0.02],[0.02,0.10]] rad/mW and 10 mW on each heater, both phases shift 1.2 rad, not 1.0. Calibration that ignores neighbors fails during simultaneous operation."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-033","order":3,"sequence":33,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-032"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"檢查調諧解的功率可行性","titleEn":"Check tuning-power feasibility","objective":"標示不可行，再以功率約束重新求解。","objectiveEn":"Flag infeasibility and solve again under power constraints.","instruction":"用上一個 H 解目標 [1,0] rad，檢查功率上下限。若不可行，修改預偏壓或允許的共同相位再求解。","instructionEn":"Solve the previous H for target [1,0] rad and inspect power limits. If infeasible, change bias or permitted common phase and solve again.","observation":"解為 P1=10.417 mW、P2=−2.083 mW；零偏壓不能直接實現。共同相位能否調整取決於系統功能。","observationEn":"The solution is P1=10.417 mW and P2=−2.083 mW, infeasible at zero bias. Whether common phase may change depends on the system.","failure":"把負值截為零而不重算，會留下第二通道相位誤差。","failureEn":"Clipping a negative value without recomputation leaves phase error on the second channel.","check":"標示不可行，再以功率約束重新求解。","checkEn":"Flag infeasibility and solve again under power constraints.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-033-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"矩陣可逆不等於物理可實現；加熱器通常不能從零偏壓提供負熱功率。","textEn":"Invertibility does not ensure physical feasibility; a heater generally cannot supply negative heat from zero bias.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-033-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"解為 P1=10.417 mW、P2=−2.083 mW；零偏壓不能直接實現。共同相位能否調整取決於系統功能。 驗收：標示不可行，再以功率約束重新求解。","textEn":"The solution is P1=10.417 mW and P2=−2.083 mW, infeasible at zero bias. Whether common phase may change depends on the system. Acceptance: Flag infeasibility and solve again under power constraints."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「檢查調諧解的功率可行性」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Check tuning-power feasibility\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["負值截零仍可宣稱精確達成原目標。","可逆矩陣表示所有目標都能實現。","標示不可行，再以功率約束重新求解。"],"optionsEn":["Clipping negative power still exactly achieves the target.","An invertible matrix makes every target realizable.","Flag infeasibility and solve again under power constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"解為 P1=10.417 mW、P2=−2.083 mW；零偏壓不能直接實現。共同相位能否調整取決於系統功能。 把負值截為零而不重算，會留下第二通道相位誤差。","explanationEn":"The solution is P1=10.417 mW and P2=−2.083 mW, infeasible at zero bias. Whether common phase may change depends on the system. Clipping a negative value without recomputation leaves phase error on the second channel."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-034","order":4,"sequence":34,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-033"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"分離熱效率與動態響應","titleEn":"Separate thermal efficiency and dynamics","objective":"同報 Pπ、τ、殘差與取樣率。","objectiveEn":"Report Pπ, τ, residuals and sampling rate together.","instruction":"施加小功率階躍，擬合 φ(t)=φ∞(1−exp(−t/τ))，檢查早期與尾端殘差，再比較設計。","instructionEn":"Apply a small power step, fit φ(t)=φ∞(1−exp(−t/τ)), inspect early and late residuals and compare designs.","observation":"假設 τ=20 µs，f3dB≈1/(2πτ)=7.96 kHz；達到 95% 約需 3τ=60 µs。","observationEn":"For hypothetical τ=20 µs, f3dB≈1/(2πτ)=7.96 kHz and 95% settling takes about 3τ=60 µs.","failure":"只由 Pπ 推斷閉迴路頻寬會漏掉熱延遲與感測延遲。","failureEn":"Inferring closed-loop bandwidth from Pπ alone omits thermal and sensing delays.","check":"同報 Pπ、τ、殘差與取樣率。","checkEn":"Report Pπ, τ, residuals and sampling rate together.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-034-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"熱隔離同時改變熱阻與熱容，低 Pπ 不代表快速；單極點近似需以殘差驗證。","textEn":"Thermal isolation changes resistance and capacitance; low Pπ does not imply speed, and a single pole requires residual checks.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-034-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 τ=20 µs，f3dB≈1/(2πτ)=7.96 kHz；達到 95% 約需 3τ=60 µs。 驗收：同報 Pπ、τ、殘差與取樣率。","textEn":"For hypothetical τ=20 µs, f3dB≈1/(2πτ)=7.96 kHz and 95% settling takes about 3τ=60 µs. Acceptance: Report Pπ, τ, residuals and sampling rate together."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「分離熱效率與動態響應」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Separate thermal efficiency and dynamics\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["同報 Pπ、τ、殘差與取樣率。","20 µs 對應 50 MHz 的 3 dB 頻寬。","耗電最少的加熱器必定反應最快。"],"optionsEn":["Report Pπ, τ, residuals and sampling rate together.","20 µs corresponds to 50 MHz 3 dB bandwidth.","The least-power heater always responds fastest."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設 τ=20 µs，f3dB≈1/(2πτ)=7.96 kHz；達到 95% 約需 3τ=60 µs。 只由 Pπ 推斷閉迴路頻寬會漏掉熱延遲與感測延遲。","explanationEn":"For hypothetical τ=20 µs, f3dB≈1/(2πτ)=7.96 kHz and 95% settling takes about 3τ=60 µs. Inferring closed-loop bandwidth from Pπ alone omits thermal and sensing delays."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-035","order":5,"sequence":35,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-034"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"連接結構應變與光路變化","titleEn":"Connect structural strain and optical-path change","objective":"分列應變積分與應力光學項。","objectiveEn":"Separate the strain integral from the photoelastic term.","instruction":"熱場輸入結構場後，擷取沿波導應變並保留方向及約束條件；先算純幾何相位項。","instructionEn":"Map thermal results into structural analysis, extract along-waveguide strain with orientation and constraints, and compute geometric phase first.","observation":"假設 L=1 mm、軸向應變 100 µε，ΔL=0.1 µm；neff=2.4、λ=1.55 µm，純幾何 Δφ=0.973 rad，未含應力光學。","observationEn":"Hypothetical L=1 mm and axial strain 100 µε give ΔL=0.1 µm; neff=2.4 and λ=1.55 µm give geometric Δφ=0.973 rad before photoelastic effects.","failure":"von Mises 應力缺乏方向資訊，不能直接唯一決定 TE/TM 折射率。","failureEn":"Von Mises stress lacks directional information and cannot uniquely determine TE/TM index changes.","check":"分列應變積分與應力光學項。","checkEn":"Separate the strain integral from the photoelastic term.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-035-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"熱應力改變幾何與折射率，需分開建模再由模態求解或校正靈敏度合成。","textEn":"Thermal stress changes geometry and index; model them separately and combine through modal solutions or calibrated sensitivities.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-035-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 L=1 mm、軸向應變 100 µε，ΔL=0.1 µm；neff=2.4、λ=1.55 µm，純幾何 Δφ=0.973 rad，未含應力光學。 驗收：分列應變積分與應力光學項。","textEn":"Hypothetical L=1 mm and axial strain 100 µε give ΔL=0.1 µm; neff=2.4 and λ=1.55 µm give geometric Δφ=0.973 rad before photoelastic effects. Acceptance: Separate the strain integral from the photoelastic term."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「連接結構應變與光路變化」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Connect structural strain and optical-path change\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["最大 von Mises 值能唯一決定 TE/TM 相位。","分列應變積分與應力光學項。","0.1 µm 幾何位移對所有波長都可忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Maximum von Mises stress uniquely determines TE/TM phase.","Separate the strain integral from the photoelastic term.","A 0.1 µm geometric shift is negligible at every wavelength."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設 L=1 mm、軸向應變 100 µε，ΔL=0.1 µm；neff=2.4、λ=1.55 µm，純幾何 Δφ=0.973 rad，未含應力光學。 von Mises 應力缺乏方向資訊，不能直接唯一決定 TE/TM 折射率。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical L=1 mm and axial strain 100 µε give ΔL=0.1 µm; neff=2.4 and λ=1.55 µm give geometric Δφ=0.973 rad before photoelastic effects. Von Mises stress lacks directional information and cannot uniquely determine TE/TM index changes."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-036","order":6,"sequence":36,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-035"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"比較散熱材料的完整介面","titleEn":"Compare complete cooling-material interfaces","objective":"分列 0.025 與 0.10 K/W 並保留機械比較。","objectiveEn":"Report 0.025 and 0.10 K/W separately and retain mechanical comparison.","instruction":"列兩個等厚層的 t/(kA)，加上兩面接觸熱阻，再另表比較膨脹失配與電隔離。","instructionEn":"Calculate t/(kA) for two equal-thickness layers, add both contacts and separately compare expansion mismatch and electrical isolation.","observation":"假設 A=100 mm²、t=0.5 mm、k=200 W/(m·K)，Rbulk=0.025 K/W；兩面接觸合計 0.10 K/W，總值 0.125 K/W。","observationEn":"For hypothetical A=100 mm², t=0.5 mm and k=200 W/(m·K), Rbulk=0.025 K/W; contacts totaling 0.10 K/W give 0.125 K/W overall.","failure":"忽略介面與翹曲，會高估塊材導熱率帶來的改善。","failureEn":"Ignoring interfaces and warpage overstates improvements from bulk conductivity.","check":"分列 0.025 與 0.10 K/W 並保留機械比較。","checkEn":"Report 0.025 and 0.10 K/W separately and retain mechanical comparison.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-036-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"Cu、W、AlN 等材料還須比較膨脹、剛性、厚度、絕緣需求與接觸熱阻，不能只排名塊材 k。","textEn":"Cu, W and AlN also require comparison of expansion, stiffness, thickness, insulation and contact resistance rather than bulk k alone.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-heater-platform","v9deep-thermal-contact","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-036-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 A=100 mm²、t=0.5 mm、k=200 W/(m·K)，Rbulk=0.025 K/W；兩面接觸合計 0.10 K/W，總值 0.125 K/W。 驗收：分列 0.025 與 0.10 K/W 並保留機械比較。","textEn":"For hypothetical A=100 mm², t=0.5 mm and k=200 W/(m·K), Rbulk=0.025 K/W; contacts totaling 0.10 K/W give 0.125 K/W overall. Acceptance: Report 0.025 and 0.10 K/W separately and retain mechanical comparison."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「比較散熱材料的完整介面」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Compare complete cooling-material interfaces\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["總熱阻就是 0.025 K/W。","最大 k 永遠代表最佳 CPO 基板。","分列 0.025 與 0.10 K/W 並保留機械比較。"],"optionsEn":["Total resistance is 0.025 K/W.","The largest k always identifies the best CPO substrate.","Report 0.025 and 0.10 K/W separately and retain mechanical comparison."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設 A=100 mm²、t=0.5 mm、k=200 W/(m·K)，Rbulk=0.025 K/W；兩面接觸合計 0.10 K/W，總值 0.125 K/W。 忽略介面與翹曲，會高估塊材導熱率帶來的改善。","explanationEn":"For hypothetical A=100 mm², t=0.5 mm and k=200 W/(m·K), Rbulk=0.025 K/W; contacts totaling 0.10 K/W give 0.125 K/W overall. Ignoring interfaces and warpage overstates improvements from bulk conductivity."}}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-stage11","order":11,"sequence":11,"title":"封裝公差、統計與故障備援","titleEn":"Packaging tolerance, statistics and fault redundancy","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-037","order":1,"sequence":37,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-036"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"建立固化位移預算","titleEn":"Budget cure-induced displacement","objective":"分列偏置和隨機項，對照對位容差。","objectiveEn":"Separate bias and random terms and compare with alignment tolerance.","instruction":"在固化前、固化後夾持、解夾及熱平衡後各量 XYZ 和功率，找出主導時段。","instructionEn":"Measure XYZ and power before cure, after cure while clamped, after release and at thermal equilibrium to identify dominant intervals.","observation":"假設三個同向位移 0.2、0.3、0.4 µm，最壞和 0.9 µm；只有獨立零均值隨機項可用 RSS=0.539 µm 作標準差估計。","observationEn":"Three hypothetical same-direction shifts 0.2, 0.3 and 0.4 µm sum to 0.9 µm worst case; RSS=0.539 µm is a standard-deviation estimate only for independent zero-mean random terms.","failure":"將確定性收縮也 RSS 會低估系統偏差。","failureEn":"Applying RSS to deterministic shrinkage underestimates systematic bias.","check":"分列偏置和隨機項，對照對位容差。","checkEn":"Separate bias and random terms and compare with alignment tolerance.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-037-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"光纖受固化收縮、解夾和冷卻共同影響；自由收縮率不直接等於端點位移。","textEn":"Fiber position depends on cure shrinkage, clamp release and cooling; free shrinkage is not endpoint displacement.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-037-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設三個同向位移 0.2、0.3、0.4 µm，最壞和 0.9 µm；只有獨立零均值隨機項可用 RSS=0.539 µm 作標準差估計。 驗收：分列偏置和隨機項，對照對位容差。","textEn":"Three hypothetical same-direction shifts 0.2, 0.3 and 0.4 µm sum to 0.9 µm worst case; RSS=0.539 µm is a standard-deviation estimate only for independent zero-mean random terms. Acceptance: Separate bias and random terms and compare with alignment tolerance."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「建立固化位移預算」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Budget cure-induced displacement\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["分列偏置和隨機項，對照對位容差。","所有誤差均可直接 RSS。","夾持時合格便可省略解夾量測。"],"optionsEn":["Separate bias and random terms and compare with alignment tolerance.","Every error can automatically be combined by RSS.","Passing while clamped removes the need for release measurements."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設三個同向位移 0.2、0.3、0.4 µm，最壞和 0.9 µm；只有獨立零均值隨機項可用 RSS=0.539 µm 作標準差估計。 將確定性收縮也 RSS 會低估系統偏差。","explanationEn":"Three hypothetical same-direction shifts 0.2, 0.3 and 0.4 µm sum to 0.9 µm worst case; RSS=0.539 µm is a standard-deviation estimate only for independent zero-mean random terms. Applying RSS to deterministic shrinkage underestimates systematic bias."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-038","order":2,"sequence":38,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-037"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"辨識量測雜訊與長期漂移","titleEn":"Distinguish noise from long-term drift","objective":"分列隨機、校正及重新接線項。","objectiveEn":"Separate random, calibration and reconnection terms.","instruction":"同裝置先短時重複，再跨重新接線和溫度循環量測，保存完整時間序列。","instructionEn":"Repeat over short intervals, then across reconnections and thermal cycles, preserving the full time series.","observation":"假設單次 σ=0.04 dB，16 次平均標準誤 0.01 dB；0.15 dB 校正偏移不會因此消失。","observationEn":"With hypothetical single-reading σ=0.04 dB, 16 averages give standard error 0.01 dB; a 0.15 dB calibration offset remains.","failure":"只報平均後散布會漏掉再接線與校正不確定度。","failureEn":"Reporting only averaged scatter omits reconnection and calibration uncertainty.","check":"分列隨機、校正及重新接線項。","checkEn":"Separate random, calibration and reconnection terms.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-038-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"短時間平均降低獨立隨機噪聲，但不能消除校正偏置或長時間漂移。","textEn":"Short averaging reduces independent random noise but not calibration bias or long-term drift.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-038-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設單次 σ=0.04 dB，16 次平均標準誤 0.01 dB；0.15 dB 校正偏移不會因此消失。 驗收：分列隨機、校正及重新接線項。","textEn":"With hypothetical single-reading σ=0.04 dB, 16 averages give standard error 0.01 dB; a 0.15 dB calibration offset remains. Acceptance: Separate random, calibration and reconnection terms."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「辨識量測雜訊與長期漂移」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Distinguish noise from long-term drift\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["16 次平均會把所有偏差降低四倍。","分列隨機、校正及重新接線項。","最佳一次結果最能代表長期穩定度。"],"optionsEn":["Sixteen averages reduce every bias fourfold.","Separate random, calibration and reconnection terms.","The best reading best represents long-term stability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設單次 σ=0.04 dB，16 次平均標準誤 0.01 dB；0.15 dB 校正偏移不會因此消失。 只報平均後散布會漏掉再接線與校正不確定度。","explanationEn":"With hypothetical single-reading σ=0.04 dB, 16 averages give standard error 0.01 dB; a 0.15 dB calibration offset remains. Reporting only averaged scatter omits reconnection and calibration uncertainty."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-039","order":3,"sequence":39,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-038"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"把製程角落轉為相位餘裕","titleEn":"Translate process corners into phase margin","objective":"列擾動範圍並以第二次模態求解檢查。","objectiveEn":"State perturbation range and check with a second modal solution.","instruction":"建立寬度、高度對 neff 的 Jacobian，驗證符號，再比較相關角落和隨機變動。","instructionEn":"Build a width/height Jacobian for neff, verify signs and compare correlated corners with random variation.","observation":"假設 dneff/dw=0.001/nm、Δw=2 nm，Δneff=0.002；L=100 µm、λ=1.55 µm 得 Δφ=0.811 rad。","observationEn":"Hypothetical dneff/dw=0.001/nm and Δw=2 nm give Δneff=0.002; L=100 µm and λ=1.55 µm give Δφ=0.811 rad.","failure":"大幅外推線性導數可能跨過模態轉換區。","failureEn":"Extrapolating a derivative too far may cross a modal transition.","check":"列擾動範圍並以第二次模態求解檢查。","checkEn":"State perturbation range and check with a second modal solution.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-039-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"局部靈敏度只適用小擾動；幾何參數可能相關，不能隨意當獨立變數抽樣。","textEn":"Local sensitivities apply to small perturbations; geometric variables may be correlated rather than independent.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-039-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 dneff/dw=0.001/nm、Δw=2 nm，Δneff=0.002；L=100 µm、λ=1.55 µm 得 Δφ=0.811 rad。 驗收：列擾動範圍並以第二次模態求解檢查。","textEn":"Hypothetical dneff/dw=0.001/nm and Δw=2 nm give Δneff=0.002; L=100 µm and λ=1.55 µm give Δφ=0.811 rad. Acceptance: State perturbation range and check with a second modal solution."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「把製程角落轉為相位餘裕」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Translate process corners into phase margin\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["任意大幾何變化都能共用同一線性係數。","平均尺寸合格即可排除角落失效。","列擾動範圍並以第二次模態求解檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Arbitrarily large changes share one linear derivative.","Passing average dimensions rules out corner failure.","State perturbation range and check with a second modal solution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設 dneff/dw=0.001/nm、Δw=2 nm，Δneff=0.002；L=100 µm、λ=1.55 µm 得 Δφ=0.811 rad。 大幅外推線性導數可能跨過模態轉換區。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical dneff/dw=0.001/nm and Δw=2 nm give Δneff=0.002; L=100 µm and λ=1.55 µm give Δφ=0.811 rad. Extrapolating a derivative too far may cross a modal transition."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-040","order":4,"sequence":40,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-039"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"拆分多通道與共同原因良率","titleEn":"Separate channel and common-cause yield","objective":"明示獨立假設並分析共用元件。","objectiveEn":"State independence assumptions and analyze shared elements.","instruction":"畫通道和共用元件樹，標單通道缺陷與共因，先算獨立基準再加入共因敏感度。","instructionEn":"Draw channels and shared components, label individual and common faults, calculate an independent baseline then analyze common causes.","observation":"假設 16 通道各 99% 且獨立，全過為 0.99^16=85.15%；另有獨立 98% 光源良率時總值 83.44%。","observationEn":"For 16 hypothetical independent 99% channels, all-pass yield is 0.99^16=85.15%; a separate independent 98% laser yield gives 83.44%.","failure":"用 99% 當整顆封裝良率，會高估全部通道同時成功的機率。","failureEn":"Using 99% as whole-package yield overstates simultaneous success.","check":"明示獨立假設並分析共用元件。","checkEn":"State independence assumptions and analyze shared elements.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-040-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"全部通道合格與單通道良率不同；共用光源和污染可造成相關失效。","textEn":"All-channel pass differs from per-channel yield; shared lasers and contamination can correlate failures.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-040-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 16 通道各 99% 且獨立，全過為 0.99^16=85.15%；另有獨立 98% 光源良率時總值 83.44%。 驗收：明示獨立假設並分析共用元件。","textEn":"For 16 hypothetical independent 99% channels, all-pass yield is 0.99^16=85.15%; a separate independent 98% laser yield gives 83.44%. Acceptance: State independence assumptions and analyze shared elements."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「拆分多通道與共同原因良率」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Separate channel and common-cause yield\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["明示獨立假設並分析共用元件。","整顆 16 通道良率仍必為 99%。","共用光源故障只影響一個通道。"],"optionsEn":["State independence assumptions and analyze shared elements.","The 16-channel package must still yield 99%.","A shared-laser fault affects only one channel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設 16 通道各 99% 且獨立，全過為 0.99^16=85.15%；另有獨立 98% 光源良率時總值 83.44%。 用 99% 當整顆封裝良率，會高估全部通道同時成功的機率。","explanationEn":"For 16 hypothetical independent 99% channels, all-pass yield is 0.99^16=85.15%; a separate independent 98% laser yield gives 83.44%. Using 99% as whole-package yield overstates simultaneous success."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-041","order":5,"sequence":41,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-040"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"用零錯誤測試建立 BER 上限","titleEn":"Bound BER after a zero-error test","objective":"提交錯誤數、位元數、時間及信賴假設。","objectiveEn":"Submit errors, bits, time and confidence assumptions.","instruction":"列目標 BER、有效位元數與測試時間，另檢查突發錯誤或 FEC 是否使簡化假設失效。","instructionEn":"List target BER, effective bits and duration, then assess whether bursts or FEC invalidate the simplified assumptions.","observation":"假設 100 Gb/s、10 s 零錯誤，N=10^12，上限約 3×10⁻¹²；要約 10⁻¹² 需 30 s。","observationEn":"At a hypothetical 100 Gb/s for 10 s with zero errors, N=10^12 and the bound is about 3×10⁻¹²; about 30 s is needed for 10⁻¹².","failure":"只報零錯誤會隱藏有限樣本與相關性問題。","failureEn":"Reporting only zero errors hides finite sampling and correlation.","check":"提交錯誤數、位元數、時間及信賴假設。","checkEn":"Submit errors, bits, time and confidence assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-041-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"零錯誤不是 BER=0；獨立稀有錯誤下，95% 單側上限近似 3/N。","textEn":"Zero errors do not mean BER=0; for independent rare errors the one-sided 95% bound is approximately 3/N.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-041-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 100 Gb/s、10 s 零錯誤，N=10^12，上限約 3×10⁻¹²；要約 10⁻¹² 需 30 s。 驗收：提交錯誤數、位元數、時間及信賴假設。","textEn":"At a hypothetical 100 Gb/s for 10 s with zero errors, N=10^12 and the bound is about 3×10⁻¹²; about 30 s is needed for 10⁻¹². Acceptance: Submit errors, bits, time and confidence assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「用零錯誤測試建立 BER 上限」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Bound BER after a zero-error test\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["零錯誤證明永久無錯。","提交錯誤數、位元數、時間及信賴假設。","10 s 已證明 10⁻¹² 的 95% 上限。"],"optionsEn":["Zero observed errors prove permanent error-free operation.","Submit errors, bits, time and confidence assumptions.","Ten seconds establishes a 10⁻¹² bound at 95%."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設 100 Gb/s、10 s 零錯誤，N=10^12，上限約 3×10⁻¹²；要約 10⁻¹² 需 30 s。 只報零錯誤會隱藏有限樣本與相關性問題。","explanationEn":"At a hypothetical 100 Gb/s for 10 s with zero errors, N=10^12 and the bound is about 3×10⁻¹²; about 30 s is needed for 10⁻¹². Reporting only zero errors hides finite sampling and correlation."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-042","order":6,"sequence":42,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-041"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"注入 N−1 光路故障","titleEn":"Inject N−1 optical-route faults","objective":"逐故障提交備援路與剩餘餘裕。","objectiveEn":"Submit the backup route and residual margin for each fault.","instruction":"在原創圖逐一刪除鏈路或開關，重新求路並加總損耗、延遲與調諧功率。","instructionEn":"Remove each defined link or switch from an original graph, reroute and sum loss, delay and tuning power.","observation":"假設主路 5 dB、備援 7 dB、預算 8 dB，備援餘裕只剩 1 dB；兩路共用唯一雷射便無法容忍其故障。","observationEn":"With hypothetical primary 5 dB, backup 7 dB and budget 8 dB, backup margin is 1 dB; one shared laser prevents tolerance of that laser's failure.","failure":"畫兩條線卻不找共用失效點，不能證明 N−1。","failureEn":"Two lines without shared-fault analysis do not establish N−1.","check":"逐故障提交備援路與剩餘餘裕。","checkEn":"Submit the backup route and residual margin for each fault.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-042-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"N−1 是指定元件集合中任一單一故障後仍達功能；必須列明集合及共用元件。","textEn":"N−1 means preserving function after one fault in a defined component set; specify that set and shared elements.","sourceIds":["v9deep-cpo-interface","v9deep-thermal-array"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-042-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設主路 5 dB、備援 7 dB、預算 8 dB，備援餘裕只剩 1 dB；兩路共用唯一雷射便無法容忍其故障。 驗收：逐故障提交備援路與剩餘餘裕。","textEn":"With hypothetical primary 5 dB, backup 7 dB and budget 8 dB, backup margin is 1 dB; one shared laser prevents tolerance of that laser's failure. Acceptance: Submit the backup route and residual margin for each fault."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「注入 N−1 光路故障」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Inject N−1 optical-route faults\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["兩路必然可容忍任何單一故障。","只需幾何連通，不需損耗預算。","逐故障提交備援路與剩餘餘裕。"],"optionsEn":["Two routes necessarily tolerate any single failure.","Connectivity alone suffices without loss budgeting.","Submit the backup route and residual margin for each fault."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設主路 5 dB、備援 7 dB、預算 8 dB，備援餘裕只剩 1 dB；兩路共用唯一雷射便無法容忍其故障。 畫兩條線卻不找共用失效點，不能證明 N−1。","explanationEn":"With hypothetical primary 5 dB, backup 7 dB and budget 8 dB, backup margin is 1 dB; one shared laser prevents tolerance of that laser's failure. Two lines without shared-fault analysis do not establish N−1."}}]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-stage12","order":12,"sequence":12,"title":"控制、驗證與工程交付","titleEn":"Control, verification and engineering handoff","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-043","order":1,"sequence":43,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-042"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"檢查控制飽和與恢復","titleEn":"Check controller saturation and recovery","objective":"驗證飽和告警和故障解除後恢復。","objectiveEn":"Verify saturation warning and recovery after fault removal.","instruction":"模擬可恢復漂移後再超出調諧範圍，記錄命令、誤差和飽和旗標，實作 anti-windup。","instructionEn":"Simulate recoverable drift followed by an out-of-range disturbance, log command, error and saturation, and implement anti-windup.","observation":"假設上限 20 mW、需求 24 mW，應標示 4 mW 不足；裁切命令不能等同光學鎖定。","observationEn":"For hypothetical limit 20 mW and demand 24 mW, report a 4 mW shortfall; command clipping is not optical lock.","failure":"光纖脫耦時持續加熱無法恢復耦合，只會升溫。","failureEn":"Heating after fiber decoupling may increase temperature without restoring coupling.","check":"驗證飽和告警和故障解除後恢復。","checkEn":"Verify saturation warning and recovery after fault removal.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-043-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"控制器需區分熱漂移、感測雜訊、脫耦與致動飽和，並防止積分累積。","textEn":"Control must distinguish thermal drift, sensor noise, decoupling and actuator saturation and prevent integrator windup.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-043-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設上限 20 mW、需求 24 mW，應標示 4 mW 不足；裁切命令不能等同光學鎖定。 驗收：驗證飽和告警和故障解除後恢復。","textEn":"For hypothetical limit 20 mW and demand 24 mW, report a 4 mW shortfall; command clipping is not optical lock. Acceptance: Verify saturation warning and recovery after fault removal."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「檢查控制飽和與恢復」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Check controller saturation and recovery\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["驗證飽和告警和故障解除後恢復。","所有低光功率都應靠加熱修正。","發出命令就表示誤差消失。"],"optionsEn":["Verify saturation warning and recovery after fault removal.","Every low-power event should be corrected by heating.","Issuing a command proves error has vanished."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設上限 20 mW、需求 24 mW，應標示 4 mW 不足；裁切命令不能等同光學鎖定。 光纖脫耦時持續加熱無法恢復耦合，只會升溫。","explanationEn":"For hypothetical limit 20 mW and demand 24 mW, report a 4 mW shortfall; command clipping is not optical lock. Heating after fiber decoupling may increase temperature without restoring coupling."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-044","order":2,"sequence":44,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-043"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"建立多物理場收斂證據","titleEn":"Establish multiphysics convergence evidence","objective":"分列數值誤差與參數敏感度。","objectiveEn":"Separate numerical error and parameter sensitivity.","instruction":"在熱點、黏著層和波導加密，監測同一相位輸出，再獨立掃描接觸熱阻與材料係數。","instructionEn":"Refine hotspots, adhesive and waveguides while monitoring one phase output, then independently sweep contact resistance and material coefficients.","observation":"假設網格輸出 0.80、0.86、0.87 rad，最後差約 1.16%；材料不確定度若達 ±0.10 rad，仍是主要限制。","observationEn":"Hypothetical mesh results 0.80, 0.86 and 0.87 rad differ by about 1.16% in the final pair; material uncertainty of ±0.10 rad remains dominant.","failure":"平滑彩圖不是網格收斂證據。","failureEn":"Smooth contours are not convergence evidence.","check":"分列數值誤差與參數敏感度。","checkEn":"Separate numerical error and parameter sensitivity.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-044-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"網格、時間步與材料不確定度是不同問題；數值收斂不能證明材料模型正確。","textEn":"Mesh, time-step and material uncertainty are different issues; numerical convergence does not validate materials.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-044-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設網格輸出 0.80、0.86、0.87 rad，最後差約 1.16%；材料不確定度若達 ±0.10 rad，仍是主要限制。 驗收：分列數值誤差與參數敏感度。","textEn":"Hypothetical mesh results 0.80, 0.86 and 0.87 rad differ by about 1.16% in the final pair; material uncertainty of ±0.10 rad remains dominant. Acceptance: Separate numerical error and parameter sensitivity."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「建立多物理場收斂證據」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Establish multiphysics convergence evidence\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["兩個網格相近便證明所有材料假設正確。","分列數值誤差與參數敏感度。","彩圖可取代能量平衡檢查。"],"optionsEn":["Similar meshes validate every material assumption.","Separate numerical error and parameter sensitivity.","Contours replace energy-balance checks."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設網格輸出 0.80、0.86、0.87 rad，最後差約 1.16%；材料不確定度若達 ±0.10 rad，仍是主要限制。 平滑彩圖不是網格收斂證據。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical mesh results 0.80, 0.86 and 0.87 rad differ by about 1.16% in the final pair; material uncertainty of ±0.10 rad remains dominant. Smooth contours are not convergence evidence."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-045","order":3,"sequence":45,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-044"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"規劃維修介面與再校正","titleEn":"Plan service interfaces and recalibration","objective":"同參考面提交前後差與重校正紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Submit before/after change and recalibration records at common reference planes.","instruction":"固定參考面量拆裝前後損耗，保留端面影像與插拔次數，設定需重新對位的條件。","instructionEn":"Measure loss at fixed reference planes before and after service, retain end-face images and mating counts, and define realignment conditions.","observation":"假設 IL 從 4.0 變 4.7 dB，增加 0.7 dB；若自訂恢復界限 0.5 dB，應查污染、角度及參考漂移。","observationEn":"Hypothetical IL rising from 4.0 to 4.7 dB adds 0.7 dB; an authored 0.5 dB restoration limit requires investigation of contamination, angle and reference drift.","failure":"前後不同參考線會混入治具差異。","failureEn":"Different reference paths mix fixture changes into service degradation.","check":"同參考面提交前後差與重校正紀錄。","checkEn":"Submit before/after change and recalibration records at common reference planes.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-045-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"可維修需要可達性、潔淨度、重定位與校正恢復；可插拔不等於無損重接。","textEn":"Serviceability requires access, cleanliness, repositioning and recalibration; pluggability is not lossless reconnection.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-045-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 IL 從 4.0 變 4.7 dB，增加 0.7 dB；若自訂恢復界限 0.5 dB，應查污染、角度及參考漂移。 驗收：同參考面提交前後差與重校正紀錄。","textEn":"Hypothetical IL rising from 4.0 to 4.7 dB adds 0.7 dB; an authored 0.5 dB restoration limit requires investigation of contamination, angle and reference drift. Acceptance: Submit before/after change and recalibration records at common reference planes."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「規劃維修介面與再校正」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Plan service interfaces and recalibration\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["接頭插回便表示性能完全恢復。","0.7 dB 可不對照預算直接忽略。","同參考面提交前後差與重校正紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["Reinsertion proves full performance restoration.","Ignore 0.7 dB without checking the budget.","Submit before/after change and recalibration records at common reference planes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設 IL 從 4.0 變 4.7 dB，增加 0.7 dB；若自訂恢復界限 0.5 dB，應查污染、角度及參考漂移。 前後不同參考線會混入治具差異。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical IL rising from 4.0 to 4.7 dB adds 0.7 dB; an authored 0.5 dB restoration limit requires investigation of contamination, angle and reference drift. Different reference paths mix fixture changes into service degradation."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-046","order":4,"sequence":46,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-045"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"分離研究平台與產品資格","titleEn":"Distinguish research platforms and product qualification","objective":"分列已證實、教學推算和尚待驗證。","objectiveEn":"Separate demonstrated facts, teaching calculations and unverified requirements.","instruction":"讀一份官方 CPO 研究，分列已展示結構、條件與缺少的壽命或批次資料，對照設計需求。","instructionEn":"Read an official CPO study, separate demonstrated structures and conditions from missing lifetime or lot data, and compare requirements.","observation":"教學審查：室溫 8 顆樣本不能證明高溫壽命、濕熱、機械衝擊和供應變動已驗證。","observationEn":"Teaching review: eight room-temperature samples do not establish high-temperature life, humidity, shock or supply-variation qualification.","failure":"把研究最小節距當成所有供應商通用規格會產生不實承諾。","failureEn":"Treating research minimum pitch as a universal specification creates unsupported promises.","check":"分列已證實、教學推算和尚待驗證。","checkEn":"Separate demonstrated facts, teaching calculations and unverified requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-046-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"論文展示、PDK、工程樣品與量產資格屬不同證據層級，最佳點不能取代跨批次能力。","textEn":"Papers, PDKs, engineering samples and qualification are different evidence levels; a best point does not establish across-lot capability.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-046-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學審查：室溫 8 顆樣本不能證明高溫壽命、濕熱、機械衝擊和供應變動已驗證。 驗收：分列已證實、教學推算和尚待驗證。","textEn":"Teaching review: eight room-temperature samples do not establish high-temperature life, humidity, shock or supply-variation qualification. Acceptance: Separate demonstrated facts, teaching calculations and unverified requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「分離研究平台與產品資格」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Distinguish research platforms and product qualification\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["分列已證實、教學推算和尚待驗證。","研究試片等同完整量產資格。","最佳樣本代表完整良率分布。"],"optionsEn":["Separate demonstrated facts, teaching calculations and unverified requirements.","A research vehicle equals full production qualification.","The best sample represents the whole yield distribution."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學審查：室溫 8 顆樣本不能證明高溫壽命、濕熱、機械衝擊和供應變動已驗證。 把研究最小節距當成所有供應商通用規格會產生不實承諾。","explanationEn":"Teaching review: eight room-temperature samples do not establish high-temperature life, humidity, shock or supply-variation qualification. Treating research minimum pitch as a universal specification creates unsupported promises."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-047","order":5,"sequence":47,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-046"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"編寫光引擎驗收矩陣","titleEn":"Write an optical-engine acceptance matrix","objective":"每列可追溯，主路備援與溫度角落分開驗收。","objectiveEn":"Make every row traceable and accept primary, backup and temperature corners separately.","instruction":"為功率、速率、BER、溫度、能量和維修建列，每列附原始檔、校正版本及責任人。","instructionEn":"Create rows for power, rate, BER, temperature, energy and service, each with raw files, calibration version and owner.","observation":"若主路餘裕 3 dB、備援 1 dB，需分成兩組工作條件，不能用主路結果覆蓋備援。","observationEn":"If primary margin is 3 dB and backup 1 dB, accept them under separate conditions rather than extending primary evidence to backup.","failure":"只有通過/失敗而沒有條件，無法重現判定。","failureEn":"Pass/fail without conditions cannot be reproduced.","check":"每列可追溯，主路備援與溫度角落分開驗收。","checkEn":"Make every row traceable and accept primary, backup and temperature corners separately.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-047-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"需求、介面、方法、條件、門檻與證據應逐列對應，避免光功率掩蓋頻寬或可靠度缺口。","textEn":"Link requirements, interfaces, methods, conditions, limits and evidence row by row so power does not hide bandwidth or reliability gaps.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-047-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"若主路餘裕 3 dB、備援 1 dB，需分成兩組工作條件，不能用主路結果覆蓋備援。 驗收：每列可追溯，主路備援與溫度角落分開驗收。","textEn":"If primary margin is 3 dB and backup 1 dB, accept them under separate conditions rather than extending primary evidence to backup. Acceptance: Make every row traceable and accept primary, backup and temperature corners separately."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「編寫光引擎驗收矩陣」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Write an optical-engine acceptance matrix\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["主路通過免測備援。","每列可追溯，主路備援與溫度角落分開驗收。","課程完成百分比就是驗收矩陣。"],"optionsEn":["Primary success removes backup testing.","Make every row traceable and accept primary, backup and temperature corners separately.","A completion percentage is an acceptance matrix."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若主路餘裕 3 dB、備援 1 dB，需分成兩組工作條件，不能用主路結果覆蓋備援。 只有通過/失敗而沒有條件，無法重現判定。","explanationEn":"If primary margin is 3 dB and backup 1 dB, accept them under separate conditions rather than extending primary evidence to backup. Pass/fail without conditions cannot be reproduced."}},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-048","order":6,"sequence":48,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"],"prerequisiteIds":["silicon-photonics-v9-047"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"交付可重現 CPO 設計審查","titleEn":"Deliver a reproducible CPO review","objective":"另一人能重算損耗及相位並指出適用邊界。","objectiveEn":"A peer can reproduce loss and phase and identify validity limits.","instruction":"封存光路、CSV、損耗表、熱矩陣、故障案例與軟體版本，讓同學重算兩個例題。","instructionEn":"Archive routes, CSV, loss tables, thermal matrices, fault cases and software versions, and have a peer reproduce two examples.","observation":"最小封包包含有單位輸入、公式、假設、輸出圖、來源 URL 與未解議題；模擬不得標為量產實測。","observationEn":"A minimal package includes inputs with units, formulas, assumptions, plots, source URLs and open issues; simulation must not be labeled production measurement.","failure":"只有示意圖而缺單位和參考面，無法稽核。","failureEn":"Schematics without units or reference planes are unauditable.","check":"另一人能重算損耗及相位並指出適用邊界。","checkEn":"A peer can reproduce loss and phase and identify validity limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-048-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"交付應讓他人以相同輸入重算，並區分預測、教學算例和實測。","textEn":"Handoff should enable recomputation from identical inputs and distinguish predictions, examples and measurements.","sourceIds":["v9deep-thermal-array","v9deep-cpo-interface"]},{"id":"silicon-photonics-v9-048-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"最小封包包含有單位輸入、公式、假設、輸出圖、來源 URL 與未解議題；模擬不得標為量產實測。 驗收：另一人能重算損耗及相位並指出適用邊界。","textEn":"A minimal package includes inputs with units, formulas, assumptions, plots, source URLs and open issues; simulation must not be labeled production measurement. Acceptance: A peer can reproduce loss and phase and identify validity limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「交付可重現 CPO 設計審查」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Deliver a reproducible CPO review\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["教學數據可改標為原廠量產資料。","只交渲染圖片，不需數值輸入。","另一人能重算損耗及相位並指出適用邊界。"],"optionsEn":["Teaching data can be relabeled vendor production data.","Rendered images suffice without numeric inputs.","A peer can reproduce loss and phase and identify validity limits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"最小封包包含有單位輸入、公式、假設、輸出圖、來源 URL 與未解議題；模擬不得標為量產實測。 只有示意圖而缺單位和參考面，無法稽核。","explanationEn":"A minimal package includes inputs with units, formulas, assumptions, plots, source URLs and open issues; simulation must not be labeled production measurement. Schematics without units or reference planes are unauditable."}}]}],"stepCount":48,"estimatedMinutes":1080,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"status":"guided","kind":"course","enrichmentVersion":9,"subcategory":"pkg-systems","subcategoryTitle":"CPO 與系統整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"CPO and systems integration","photoId":"v9-photonic-assembly"},{"id":"a106","title":"晶圓對晶圓混合接合","titleEn":"Wafer-to-wafer hybrid bonding","category":"packaging","kind":"course","summary":"36 項任務深入 W2W 混合接合：保留原 12 步，再以配對良率、二維對位、CMP 形貌、污染統計、熱機相容、Kelvin 電阻、串鏈與資格證據完成設計審查。","summaryEn":"Thirty-six W2W hybrid-bonding tasks preserve the original twelve and add pairing yield, 2D overlay, CMP topography, contamination statistics, thermomechanical compatibility, Kelvin resistance, chains and qualification evidence.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-evg","v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w","v9deep-thermal-stress","v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v9-media-3363c0f741d8","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":36,"estimatedMinutes":840,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"diagram":{"type":"package","labels":["晶圓配對","表面整備","對位","混合接合","可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Wafer pairing","Surface preparation","Alignment","Hybrid bond","Reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a106-stage01","order":1,"title":"界面與版圖","titleEn":"Interface and layout","description":"先界定成對晶圓、接點與驗證結構。","descriptionEn":"Define the paired wafers, contacts and verification structures.","steps":[{"id":"a106-v6-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-evg","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"界定混合接合的兩種功能","titleEn":"Define the two functions of hybrid bonding","objective":"區別介電層支撐與金屬導通。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish dielectric attachment from metal conduction.","instruction":"畫出兩片面對面的截面，將介電層接觸與銅接墊接觸分色。追蹤一條訊號跨越界面的路徑，指出哪些位置負責支撐、哪些位置必須導通。","instructionEn":"Draw face-to-face sections and color dielectric and copper contacts separately. Trace one signal across the interface, identifying mechanical attachment and required electrical continuity.","observation":"整片看似貼合，並不表示每個銅接點已導通。","observationEn":"Apparent full-area attachment does not prove continuity through every copper contact.","failure":"若把介電層畫成導線，重新檢查電流路徑與材料標記。","failureEn":"If dielectric is drawn as a wire, revisit the current path and material labels.","check":"分別指定機械接合與電性接點的驗證方法。","checkEn":"Assign separate verification approaches to attachment and electrical contacts.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-01-k1","title":"雙重界面","titleEn":"A dual interface","text":"混合接合把介電層連接與嵌入金屬互連結合在同一界面。","textEn":"Hybrid bonding combines dielectric attachment and embedded metal interconnects at one interface."},{"id":"a106-v6-01-k2","title":"功能分驗","titleEn":"Separate functional evidence","text":"機械完整與電性導通互相關聯，但不能互相替代驗證。","textEn":"Mechanical integrity and electrical continuity are related but need separate evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"看見整片沒有分離，能證明什麼？","questionEn":"What does observing that the wafers remain attached establish?","options":["提供機械貼合的部分證據，仍須電性驗證。","介電貼合強度已足以代表所有接觸電阻。","只要外圓重合，就證明每一接墊的隔離合格。"],"optionsEn":["It provides some attachment evidence; electrical verification remains necessary.","Dielectric attachment strength fully represents every contact resistance.","Overlapping outlines prove isolation of every pad."],"answer":0,"explanation":"提供機械貼合的部分證據，仍須電性驗證。 混合接合把介電層連接與嵌入金屬互連結合在同一界面。","explanationEn":"It provides some attachment evidence; electrical verification remains necessary. Hybrid bonding combines dielectric attachment and embedded metal interconnects at one interface."}},{"id":"a106-v6-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-evg","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-01"],"title":"核對成對晶圓的版圖與方位","titleEn":"Check paired layouts and orientation","objective":"避免面對面翻轉造成接點配對錯誤。","objectiveEn":"Prevent contact mismatches caused by face-to-face reversal.","instruction":"在透明紙或繪圖軟體畫兩片含不對稱記號的晶圓。將上片翻面，逐一對應接墊與方向標記，再比較旋轉與鏡射的差異。","instructionEn":"Draw two wafers with asymmetric marks on transparent sheets or in drawing software. Flip the upper wafer and match pads and orientation marks, comparing rotation with reflection.","observation":"對稱圖案可能掩蓋翻面錯誤，因此保留不對稱檢查點。","observationEn":"Symmetric patterns can hide a reversal error, so retain an asymmetric check.","failure":"只對齊外圓卻錯配接墊時，應回到座標轉換，而非微調所有接點。","failureEn":"If wafer outlines align but pads mismatch, revisit coordinate transforms rather than adjust every contact.","check":"用三個非共線標記驗證方向，並說明翻面後的接點對應。","checkEn":"Verify orientation with three non-collinear marks and explain pad correspondence after flipping.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-02-k1","title":"座標轉換","titleEn":"Coordinate transformation","text":"面對面接合需要一致的翻面、旋轉與位移定義。","textEn":"Face-to-face bonding needs consistent definitions of reflection, rotation and translation."},{"id":"a106-v6-02-k2","title":"不對稱標記","titleEn":"Asymmetric marks","text":"不對稱資訊能區分看似相同的錯誤方位。","textEn":"Asymmetric information distinguishes otherwise similar incorrect orientations."}],"quiz":{"question":"外圓重合但不對稱標記相反，優先檢查什麼？","questionEn":"Outlines overlap but asymmetric marks reverse. What should be checked first?","options":["只調整同一平移量，不檢查是否鏡射。","翻面與座標對應規則。","只看晶圓外圓，因為圖案方位不影響接點對應。"],"optionsEn":["Apply one translation without checking for reflection.","The flip and coordinate-mapping rules.","Inspect the wafer outline only, assuming pattern orientation cannot affect matching."],"answer":1,"explanation":"翻面與座標對應規則。 面對面接合需要一致的翻面、旋轉與位移定義。","explanationEn":"The flip and coordinate-mapping rules. Face-to-face bonding needs consistent definitions of reflection, rotation and translation."}},{"id":"a106-v6-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-02"],"title":"比較接墊尺寸與容許偏移","titleEn":"Compare pad size and overlay allowance","objective":"理解接觸重疊與相鄰間距的共同限制。","objectiveEn":"Understand joint limits from contact overlap and neighbor spacing.","instruction":"畫一組等尺寸接墊與一組上下不同尺寸接墊，逐次平移上層透明圖。記錄何時重疊不足或接近鄰點；所有尺寸自行假設，不能套用為製造規格。","instructionEn":"Draw equal-size and unequal-size pad pairs and translate the upper overlay. Record loss of overlap or approach to a neighbor; label all dimensions hypothetical, not manufacturing specifications.","observation":"增加接墊大小可改善部分重疊，但也會改變相鄰間距。","observationEn":"Enlarging a pad can improve overlap while changing neighbor clearance.","failure":"只最大化重疊而忽略鄰近接點，可能隱藏短路或介電風險。","failureEn":"Maximizing overlap while ignoring neighbors can conceal shorting or dielectric risk.","check":"同時呈現重疊與間距兩項判據，並指出適用的偏移方向。","checkEn":"Show both overlap and clearance criteria and identify the displacement directions considered.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-03-k1","title":"版圖容差","titleEn":"Layout tolerance","text":"接墊形狀與相對尺寸會改變對位誤差的容忍度。","textEn":"Pad geometry and relative size affect tolerance to alignment error."},{"id":"a106-v6-03-k2","title":"局部代價","titleEn":"Local trade-off","text":"幾何上的改良須連同鄰點間距和電性一起評估。","textEn":"A geometric improvement must be assessed with neighbor spacing and electrical behavior."}],"quiz":{"question":"為何不能無限制放大所有接墊？","questionEn":"Why not enlarge every pad without limit?","options":["接墊加大只會改善重疊，不影響鄰近間距。","只要銅面積增加，就不需考慮介電隔離。","重疊改善可能消耗鄰點間距。"],"optionsEn":["Enlarging pads improves overlap without affecting neighbor spacing.","More copper area removes the need to consider dielectric isolation.","Improved overlap can consume neighbor clearance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重疊改善可能消耗鄰點間距。 接墊形狀與相對尺寸會改變對位誤差的容忍度。","explanationEn":"Improved overlap can consume neighbor clearance. Pad geometry and relative size affect tolerance to alignment error."}},{"id":"a106-v6-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-03"],"title":"配置串鏈與隔離測試結構","titleEn":"Plan chain and isolation test structures","objective":"讓開路與相鄰漏電能被分開發現。","objectiveEn":"Make opens and neighbor leakage separately observable.","instruction":"在示意版圖串接多個跨界面接點，另畫相鄰但不相連的導體。預測單一開路、接觸電阻增加及鄰點短路，各會改變哪項測試結果。","instructionEn":"Chain multiple cross-interface contacts in a schematic and draw separate adjacent conductors. Predict which measurements change for an open, higher contact resistance or a neighbor short.","observation":"串鏈只顯示累積路徑，未必能定位單一異常接點。","observationEn":"A chain exposes a cumulative path but may not localize one defective contact.","failure":"把低串鏈電阻當作隔離合格會漏掉另一種故障；保留獨立隔離判據。","failureEn":"Treating low chain resistance as proof of isolation misses another failure class; retain a separate criterion.","check":"建立故障、測試結構與可見現象的三欄對照。","checkEn":"Map each fault to a test structure and observable response.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-04-k1","title":"可觀測性","titleEn":"Observability","text":"測試結構必須讓想找的失效改變可讀取的量。","textEn":"A test structure must make the targeted failure affect an observable quantity."},{"id":"a106-v6-04-k2","title":"累積與定位","titleEn":"Aggregation and localization","text":"整條串鏈的結果與單一接點的結果具有不同解析度。","textEn":"Whole-chain and individual-contact results have different diagnostic resolution."}],"quiz":{"question":"串鏈可導通，還需要哪類補充證據？","questionEn":"A chain conducts. What complementary evidence is still useful?","options":["相鄰導體的隔離與漏電檢查。","只重複同一串鏈讀值，不需要不同測試結構。","只檢查機械接合強度便能排除相鄰短路。"],"optionsEn":["Isolation and leakage checks between neighboring conductors.","Repeat the same chain reading; different test structures are unnecessary.","Mechanical bond strength alone rules out neighbor shorts."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相鄰導體的隔離與漏電檢查。 測試結構必須讓想找的失效改變可讀取的量。","explanationEn":"Isolation and leakage checks between neighboring conductors. A test structure must make the targeted failure affect an observable quantity."}}]},{"id":"a106-stage02","order":2,"title":"表面與對位","titleEn":"Surface and alignment","description":"區分表面幾何、表面狀態與面內對位的限制。","descriptionEn":"Separate limits from surface geometry, surface condition and in-plane alignment.","steps":[{"id":"a106-v6-05","order":1,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-04"],"title":"判讀 CMP 後的銅凹陷與介電平坦度","titleEn":"Interpret copper recess and dielectric flatness","objective":"分開比較銅高度與介電面形貌。","objectiveEn":"Compare copper height separately from dielectric topography.","instruction":"畫出銅突出、合適凹陷及過深凹陷三種假想截面，標出首先接觸的位置。比較它們對介電貼合與後續金屬連接的影響，不設定通用奈米公差。","instructionEn":"Draw hypothetical protruding, appropriately recessed and deeply recessed copper sections. Mark first-contact locations and compare dielectric attachment and later metal connection without assigning universal nanometer tolerances.","observation":"全片平均平坦仍可能掩蓋某些接墊的局部高度問題。","observationEn":"Good average flatness can still hide local pad-height problems.","failure":"把所有材料畫成完全齊平，可能遺失研究流程所需的受控凹陷；回查來源路線。","failureEn":"Drawing every material perfectly flush can erase the controlled recess required by the referenced route; review its assumptions.","check":"說明三種截面的不同風險，且將量產公差保留為待查規格。","checkEn":"Explain the distinct risks and leave production tolerances as requirements to obtain.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-05-k1","title":"受控形貌","titleEn":"Controlled topography","text":"接合前形貌須同時配合介電接觸及後續銅連接。","textEn":"Prebond topography must accommodate both dielectric contact and subsequent copper connection."},{"id":"a106-v6-05-k2","title":"局部高度","titleEn":"Local height","text":"銅凹陷相對於鄰近介電面定義，不能只看晶圓平均厚度。","textEn":"Copper recess is relative to nearby dielectric, not merely average wafer thickness."}],"quiz":{"question":"銅凹陷應相對於哪個基準判讀？","questionEn":"What reference defines copper recess?","options":["整片晶圓背面的平均平面。","相鄰介電表面。","尚未拋光前的總銅沉積厚度。"],"optionsEn":["The average plane of the wafer backside.","The adjacent dielectric surface.","Total copper thickness before polishing."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相鄰介電表面。 接合前形貌須同時配合介電接觸及後續銅連接。","explanationEn":"The adjacent dielectric surface. Prebond topography must accommodate both dielectric contact and subsequent copper connection."}},{"id":"a106-v6-06","order":2,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-evg","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-05"],"title":"追溯清潔、活化與等待時間","titleEn":"Trace cleaning, activation and waiting","objective":"將表面狀態與後續接合條件連接。","objectiveEn":"Connect surface condition to subsequent bonding conditions.","instruction":"建立清潔、表面活化、等待與接合的時間線，為兩條假設路徑標記暴露及搬運點。比較粒子控制與活化目的，不推定兩者可互相取代。","instructionEn":"Build timelines for cleaning, activation, waiting and bonding, marking exposure and handling in two hypothetical routes. Compare particle control with activation without treating them as interchangeable.","observation":"兩片幾何相同的表面，仍可能因狀態或污染不同而表現不同。","observationEn":"Geometrically similar surfaces can behave differently because of condition or contamination.","failure":"缺少交接時間紀錄時，不能把不良全歸因於對位。","failureEn":"Without handoff timing records, do not attribute all failures to overlay.","check":"時間線包含每次表面暴露與可追溯的狀態紀錄。","checkEn":"Include each exposure and a traceable surface-condition record.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-06-k1","title":"表面功能","titleEn":"Surface functionality","text":"介電層直接接合依賴適當的表面狀態，不只是兩片相碰。","textEn":"Direct dielectric bonding depends on suitable surface condition, not merely physical contact."},{"id":"a106-v6-06-k2","title":"交接窗口","titleEn":"Handoff window","text":"等待和搬運也是流程條件，應與清潔及活化一起記錄。","textEn":"Waiting and handling are process conditions that belong with cleaning and activation records."}],"quiz":{"question":"活化後延長等待，為何仍需重新核對接合條件？","questionEn":"Why review bonding conditions after a longer post-activation wait?","options":["只要對位精度相同，表面暴露時間就不影響判定。","等待越久必然接合越強，不需檢查表面狀態。","表面狀態和暴露歷程可能改變。"],"optionsEn":["Equal overlay accuracy makes surface-exposure time irrelevant.","A longer wait always strengthens bonding without checking surface condition.","Surface condition and exposure history may change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面狀態和暴露歷程可能改變。 介電層直接接合依賴適當的表面狀態，不只是兩片相碰。","explanationEn":"Surface condition and exposure history may change. Direct dielectric bonding depends on suitable surface condition, not merely physical contact."}},{"id":"a106-v6-07","order":3,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-06"],"title":"分離平移、旋轉與變形誤差","titleEn":"Separate translation, rotation and distortion","objective":"用多位置標記判斷對位誤差模式。","objectiveEn":"Diagnose overlay-error patterns from multiple marks.","instruction":"在中心與四個外圍位置畫誤差箭頭，分別建立同向、繞中心旋轉及局部不規則三個案例。嘗試以一個平移修正各案例，觀察哪些殘差無法消除。","instructionEn":"Draw overlay vectors at the center and four outer positions for translation, rotation and irregular local distortion. Apply one translation correction to each and identify residuals it cannot remove.","observation":"中心對好仍可能在邊緣有旋轉或形變殘差。","observationEn":"Good center alignment can coexist with rotational or distortion residuals at the edge.","failure":"只用單一標記決定全片合格會忽略誤差模式；增加空間取樣。","failureEn":"One-mark acceptance overlooks error structure; add spatial sampling.","check":"將每種誤差對應到可修正部分與待調查部分。","checkEn":"Distinguish correctable components from residuals requiring investigation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-07-k1","title":"誤差場","titleEn":"Error field","text":"對位是一個空間分布，不只是單一偏移值。","textEn":"Overlay is a spatial field, not just one offset."},{"id":"a106-v6-07-k2","title":"剛體限制","titleEn":"Rigid-body limits","text":"平移與旋轉不能完全補償所有局部變形。","textEn":"Translation and rotation cannot fully compensate every local distortion."}],"quiz":{"question":"平移後中心已對齊但邊緣仍繞中心偏轉，較像哪種誤差？","questionEn":"Translation fixes the center but edge vectors remain rotational. What does this suggest?","options":["仍有旋轉分量。","單純固定方向的平移，中心結果足以代表全片。","一定是所有接墊同等加寬，無需檢查對位模型。"],"optionsEn":["A remaining rotational component.","Pure fixed-direction translation, with center results representing the entire wafer.","Every pad must have widened equally, requiring no alignment-model review."],"answer":0,"explanation":"仍有旋轉分量。 對位是一個空間分布，不只是單一偏移值。","explanationEn":"A remaining rotational component. Overlay is a spatial field, not just one offset."}},{"id":"a106-v6-08","order":4,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-evg","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-07"],"title":"規劃接合前的雙面放行","titleEn":"Plan a two-surface prebond review","objective":"防止只檢查其中一片晶圓。","objectiveEn":"Avoid checking only one member of the wafer pair.","instruction":"為上下晶圓各建一張表，列出身分、方位、形貌、污染與等待歷程。挑選一項缺失資料，討論它如何影響整對晶圓的放行，而非以另一片的結果補值。","instructionEn":"Make separate records for wafer identity, orientation, topography, contamination and waiting history. Remove one item and explain how that affects pair release rather than substituting the other wafer’s result.","observation":"接合是成對事件，單片合格不等於配對與界面均合格。","observationEn":"Bonding is a paired event; one acceptable wafer does not prove a valid pair or interface.","failure":"批次或方位配對錯誤不能靠後段退火修正。","failureEn":"Annealing cannot repair an incorrect lot or orientation pairing.","check":"放行表可從接合批次追溯到兩片來料及各自量測。","checkEn":"Trace the bonded lot to both incoming wafers and their individual measurements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-08-k1","title":"配對追溯","titleEn":"Pair traceability","text":"兩側輸入共同決定接合界面品質。","textEn":"Both inputs jointly determine interface quality."},{"id":"a106-v6-08-k2","title":"缺值處理","titleEn":"Handling missing evidence","text":"另一片的好結果不能補足本片缺少的證據。","textEn":"A good result from one wafer cannot fill an evidence gap for the other."}],"quiz":{"question":"上片形貌合格、下片未量測，正確結論為何？","questionEn":"The upper wafer passes topography checks but the lower is unmeasured. What follows?","options":["下片可沿用上片結果，因為兩片目標規格相同。","整對晶圓仍待驗證。","對位設備型號相同，就不需要下片形貌證據。"],"optionsEn":["The lower wafer can inherit the upper result because target specifications match.","The pair remains unverified.","The same aligner model removes the need for lower-wafer topography evidence."],"answer":1,"explanation":"整對晶圓仍待驗證。 兩側輸入共同決定接合界面品質。","explanationEn":"The pair remains unverified. Both inputs jointly determine interface quality."}}]},{"id":"a106-stage03","order":3,"title":"接合與驗證","titleEn":"Bonding and verification","description":"結合機械、空洞與電性證據，避免只用外觀判定接合成功。","descriptionEn":"Combine mechanical, void and electrical evidence rather than judge a bond by appearance.","steps":[{"id":"a106-v6-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-08"],"title":"觀察接合波與未接合區域","titleEn":"Observe the bond wave and unbonded regions","objective":"把接觸傳播與空洞證據連結。","objectiveEn":"Relate contact propagation to void evidence.","instruction":"在原創示意圖畫出由起始接觸點擴展的接合前緣，再加入一個粒子與一個局部形貌障礙。預測可能留下的未接合區，與來源影像中的觀察方法比較。","instructionEn":"Draw an original bond front spreading from initial contact, then add one particle and one local topographic obstacle. Predict unbonded regions and compare the observation approach with referenced imagery.","observation":"前緣通過與界面完全無空洞是不同判斷。","observationEn":"Passage of a bond front is not the same conclusion as a void-free interface.","failure":"若只保存最終外觀，可能缺少判斷缺陷起源的時間資訊。","failureEn":"Keeping only the final appearance may lose timing needed to diagnose defect origins.","check":"標記預測區域、可檢查的方法及不能由示意圖證明的部分。","checkEn":"Mark predicted regions, an inspection approach and what the schematic cannot prove.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-09-k1","title":"接觸傳播","titleEn":"Contact propagation","text":"表面接觸可沿界面擴展，局部障礙會影響完整貼合。","textEn":"Contact can propagate along the interface, while local obstacles affect complete attachment."},{"id":"a106-v6-09-k2","title":"空洞定位","titleEn":"Void localization","text":"缺陷位置需與前處理和形貌紀錄交叉比較。","textEn":"Defect locations should be compared with preparation and topography records."}],"quiz":{"question":"模型顯示接合前緣已到邊緣，仍需檢查什麼？","questionEn":"The modeled bond front reaches the edge. What still needs checking?","options":["只需確認接觸前緣速度，無需檢查內部區域。","只量測外圓厚度，就可取代界面檢查。","界面內是否殘留未接合區。"],"optionsEn":["Only bond-front speed needs checking, not interior regions.","Edge thickness alone replaces interface inspection.","Whether unbonded regions remain inside the interface."],"answer":2,"explanation":"界面內是否殘留未接合區。 表面接觸可沿界面擴展，局部障礙會影響完整貼合。","explanationEn":"Whether unbonded regions remain inside the interface. Contact can propagate along the interface, while local obstacles affect complete attachment."}},{"id":"a106-v6-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-evg","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-09"],"title":"判讀退火對介電層與銅連接的作用","titleEn":"Interpret annealing of dielectric and copper bonds","objective":"區分初始貼合與後續接合強化。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish initial attachment from subsequent bond strengthening.","instruction":"用前後兩張截面圖標出預接合與退火後狀態，分別追蹤介電界面及銅接點。列出需向實際製程取得的熱預算與材料相容性資料，不填入通用溫度配方。","instructionEn":"Compare prebond and post-anneal sections, following dielectric interfaces and copper contacts separately. List thermal-budget and compatibility information needed from the actual process without inventing a universal temperature recipe.","observation":"某條研究路線的可用條件不代表所有介電材料與金屬堆疊皆適用。","observationEn":"Conditions demonstrated for one research route do not apply automatically to every dielectric and metal stack.","failure":"用提高溫度補償未知污染，可能增加其他損害而未處理根因。","failureEn":"Raising temperature to compensate for unknown contamination may add damage without addressing the cause.","check":"說明退火前後需要不同證據，並保留產品熱限制。","checkEn":"Explain the evidence needed before and after annealing and retain product thermal constraints.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-10-k1","title":"接合演變","titleEn":"Bond evolution","text":"初始貼合與永久介電、金屬接合的形成是不同階段。","textEn":"Initial attachment and development of permanent dielectric and metal bonds are distinct stages."},{"id":"a106-v6-10-k2","title":"熱預算相容性","titleEn":"Thermal-budget compatibility","text":"接合條件須與先前完成的元件和互連相容。","textEn":"Bonding conditions must remain compatible with existing devices and interconnects."}],"quiz":{"question":"能否把研究文章中的退火條件直接當所有產品配方？","questionEn":"Can an article’s anneal condition become the recipe for every product?","options":["不能，材料、堆疊與熱預算需分別核對。","能，只要研究和產品使用相同晶圓直徑。","能，所有既有互連對接合熱歷程的承受能力相同。"],"optionsEn":["No; materials, stacks and thermal budgets need separate review.","Yes, if research and product wafer diameters match.","Yes; all existing interconnects tolerate the same bonding thermal history."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不能，材料、堆疊與熱預算需分別核對。 初始貼合與永久介電、金屬接合的形成是不同階段。","explanationEn":"No; materials, stacks and thermal budgets need separate review. Initial attachment and development of permanent dielectric and metal bonds are distinct stages."}},{"id":"a106-v6-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-10"],"title":"交叉判讀空洞、串鏈與接點電阻","titleEn":"Cross-check voids, chains and contact resistance","objective":"避免單一測試掩蓋不同失效模式。","objectiveEn":"Avoid allowing one test to conceal other failure modes.","instruction":"製作四個紙上案例：外觀正常但串鏈開路、可導通但局部空洞、阻值偏高及各項一致。為每例選擇下一個能縮小原因範圍的量測，而非立即重工。","instructionEn":"Create paper cases with a normal appearance but open chain, conduction with local voids, elevated resistance and consistent results. Choose the next discriminating measurement before proposing rework.","observation":"不同證據可能互補，也可能揭露取樣範圍不一致。","observationEn":"Different evidence can complement itself or reveal inconsistent sampling coverage.","failure":"若把測到一條好串鏈擴大成整片合格，需回查測試覆蓋率。","failureEn":"If one good chain becomes a claim about the entire wafer, revisit coverage.","check":"每個異常結論均指出測試覆蓋範圍及尚未排除的原因。","checkEn":"State test coverage and remaining possible causes for every abnormal conclusion.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-11-k1","title":"多物理驗證","titleEn":"Multiphysics verification","text":"機械界面與電性路徑需要交叉驗證，才能縮小失效原因。","textEn":"Mechanical interface and electrical-path evidence must be combined to narrow causes."},{"id":"a106-v6-11-k2","title":"取樣覆蓋","titleEn":"Sampling coverage","text":"局部良好結果不等於未量測區域已被證明良好。","textEn":"A good local result does not establish the condition of unmeasured regions."}],"quiz":{"question":"一條串鏈正常但附近影像有空洞，最佳解讀是什麼？","questionEn":"One chain passes but nearby imaging shows a void. What is the best interpretation?","options":["串鏈導通已足以排除所有機械界面缺陷。","兩種測試覆蓋與失效敏感性不同，需交叉定位。","有局部空洞便可認定整片每個接點都開路。"],"optionsEn":["Chain continuity rules out every mechanical-interface defect.","Coverage and failure sensitivity differ; correlate their locations.","One local void proves every wafer contact is open."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩種測試覆蓋與失效敏感性不同，需交叉定位。 機械界面與電性路徑需要交叉驗證，才能縮小失效原因。","explanationEn":"Coverage and failure sensitivity differ; correlate their locations. Mechanical interface and electrical-path evidence must be combined to narrow causes."}},{"id":"a106-v6-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-11"],"title":"建立接合批次的可靠度與交接表","titleEn":"Build a bond-lot reliability handoff","objective":"將製程條件、初始結果與後續變化連在一起。","objectiveEn":"Link process conditions, initial results and later changes.","instruction":"把配對識別、對位地圖、形貌、接合紀錄及初始電性放入一張交接表。再加入假設的應力前後結果，區分初始缺陷和隨時間出現的劣化。","instructionEn":"Combine pairing, overlay, topography, bond history and initial electrical results in a handoff sheet. Add hypothetical before-and-after stress results to distinguish initial defects from later degradation.","observation":"初始可導通不代表經應力後仍維持相同表現。","observationEn":"Initial continuity does not guarantee unchanged behavior after stress.","failure":"沒有初始基線便難以判斷變化；先補足基線與樣本對應。","failureEn":"Without a baseline, change is hard to judge; restore baseline and sample correspondence.","check":"為放行、複查與後續可靠度驗證各列出條件，不宣稱教學模型已證明量產可靠度。","checkEn":"Define release, review and later reliability conditions without claiming that the teaching model proves production reliability.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v6-12-k1","title":"基線比較","titleEn":"Baseline comparison","text":"可靠度觀察需要把同一樣本的初始與後續證據連接。","textEn":"Reliability observations need a link between the same sample’s initial and later evidence."},{"id":"a106-v6-12-k2","title":"工程交接","titleEn":"Engineering handoff","text":"後段薄化、互連與測試需知道接合界面的限制與未解問題。","textEn":"Later thinning, interconnect and test operations need interface limits and unresolved issues."}],"quiz":{"question":"為何保留應力測試前的電性基線？","questionEn":"Why retain electrical results from before a stress test?","options":["用基線直接代替所有應力後量測。","只比較不同批次的最終平均值，不追蹤同一樣本。","用來識別後續變化，而不只看最終數字。"],"optionsEn":["Substitute the baseline for every post-stress measurement.","Compare only final averages from different lots without tracking the same sample.","To identify change rather than view only a final number."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用來識別後續變化，而不只看最終數字。 可靠度觀察需要把同一樣本的初始與後續證據連接。","explanationEn":"To identify change rather than view only a final number. Reliability observations need a link between the same sample’s initial and later evidence."}}]},{"id":"a106-v9-stage04","order":4,"sequence":4,"title":"配對良率與二維對位","titleEn":"Pairing yield and two-dimensional overlay","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"a106-v9-013","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v6-12"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"比較整片配對與良品晶粒組合","titleEn":"Compare wafer pairing and known-good-die assembly","objective":"同報地圖交集與獨立模型，指出兩者差異。","objectiveEn":"Report both map intersection and the independence model, explaining differences.","instruction":"畫兩張 4×4 良率地圖，對位後計算共同良品，再思考 D2W 可重配的範圍和限制。","instructionEn":"Draw two 4×4 yield maps, align them and count jointly good positions, then assess D2W remapping possibilities and constraints.","observation":"假設上下片每位置良率 90% 且獨立、接合存活率 98%，共同良品率=0.9²×0.98=79.38%；有空間相關時不能直接套用。","observationEn":"Assuming independent 90% die yield on each wafer and 98% bond survival gives 0.9²×0.98=79.38%; spatial correlation invalidates direct use.","failure":"忽略上下晶圓地圖相關性會使成本估算失真。","failureEn":"Ignoring cross-wafer map correlation distorts cost estimates.","check":"同報地圖交集與獨立模型，指出兩者差異。","checkEn":"Report both map intersection and the independence model, explaining differences.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-013-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"W2W 同時接合整片對應位置；D2W 可挑選晶粒，但增加切割、搬運與放置負擔。","textEn":"W2W bonds corresponding wafer positions together; D2W can select dies but adds singulation, handling and placement burdens.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a106-v9-013-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設上下片每位置良率 90% 且獨立、接合存活率 98%，共同良品率=0.9²×0.98=79.38%；有空間相關時不能直接套用。 驗收：同報地圖交集與獨立模型，指出兩者差異。","textEn":"Assuming independent 90% die yield on each wafer and 98% bond survival gives 0.9²×0.98=79.38%; spatial correlation invalidates direct use. Acceptance: Report both map intersection and the independence model, explaining differences."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「比較整片配對與良品晶粒組合」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Compare wafer pairing and known-good-die assembly\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["同報地圖交集與獨立模型，指出兩者差異。","90% 與 90% 配對後必為 90%。","D2W 挑良品不會增加任何搬運風險。"],"optionsEn":["Report both map intersection and the independence model, explaining differences.","Pairing two 90% wafers necessarily yields 90%.","D2W selection adds no handling risks."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設上下片每位置良率 90% 且獨立、接合存活率 98%，共同良品率=0.9²×0.98=79.38%；有空間相關時不能直接套用。 忽略上下晶圓地圖相關性會使成本估算失真。","explanationEn":"Assuming independent 90% die yield on each wafer and 98% bond survival gives 0.9²×0.98=79.38%; spatial correlation invalidates direct use. Ignoring cross-wafer map correlation distorts cost estimates."}},{"id":"a106-v9-014","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-013"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"將對位誤差表示為向量","titleEn":"Represent overlay as a vector","objective":"同報向量圖、偏置及半徑分布。","objectiveEn":"Report the vector map, bias and radial distribution.","instruction":"將各測點 dx、dy 畫成向量場，算 r=√(dx²+dy²)，區分平均偏置與殘差。","instructionEn":"Plot dx and dy as a vector field, calculate r=√(dx²+dy²), and separate mean bias from residuals.","observation":"假設 dx=30 nm、dy=40 nm，r=50 nm；兩個方向都小於 45 nm，仍不符合自訂 r≤45 nm。","observationEn":"Hypothetical dx=30 nm and dy=40 nm give r=50 nm; both axes are below 45 nm but fail an authored radial limit r≤45 nm.","failure":"只看平均向量接近零會掩蓋正負誤差相消。","failureEn":"A near-zero mean vector can hide cancellation of positive and negative errors.","check":"同報向量圖、偏置及半徑分布。","checkEn":"Report the vector map, bias and radial distribution.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-014-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"X/Y 誤差與徑向誤差有不同統計分布，不能把單軸門檻直接當二維半徑門檻。","textEn":"X/Y errors and radial error have different distributions; a one-axis limit is not a two-dimensional radial limit.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a106-v9-014-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 dx=30 nm、dy=40 nm，r=50 nm；兩個方向都小於 45 nm，仍不符合自訂 r≤45 nm。 驗收：同報向量圖、偏置及半徑分布。","textEn":"Hypothetical dx=30 nm and dy=40 nm give r=50 nm; both axes are below 45 nm but fail an authored radial limit r≤45 nm. Acceptance: Report the vector map, bias and radial distribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「將對位誤差表示為向量」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Represent overlay as a vector\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["兩軸各小於 45 nm 就保證半徑小於 45 nm。","同報向量圖、偏置及半徑分布。","平均零等於每點零誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Both axes below 45 nm guarantee radius below 45 nm.","Report the vector map, bias and radial distribution.","Zero mean implies zero error at every point."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設 dx=30 nm、dy=40 nm，r=50 nm；兩個方向都小於 45 nm，仍不符合自訂 r≤45 nm。 只看平均向量接近零會掩蓋正負誤差相消。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical dx=30 nm and dy=40 nm give r=50 nm; both axes are below 45 nm but fail an authored radial limit r≤45 nm. A near-zero mean vector can hide cancellation of positive and negative errors."}},{"id":"a106-v9-015","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-014"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"拆出旋轉造成的邊緣位移","titleEn":"Separate rotation-induced edge displacement","objective":"保留 θ 的弧度單位與邊緣預測值。","objectiveEn":"Retain θ in radians and predicted edge displacement.","instruction":"以中心和邊緣對位標記擬合旋轉，將剛體旋轉從向量場扣除再看局部殘差。","instructionEn":"Fit rotation using center and edge marks, subtract rigid rotation and inspect local residuals.","observation":"假設半徑 100 mm、旋轉 1 µrad，邊緣位移 100 nm；中心標記幾乎不動不能證明全片合格。","observationEn":"At hypothetical radius 100 mm and rotation 1 µrad, edge shift is 100 nm; a nearly fixed center does not prove whole-wafer compliance.","failure":"僅用中心標記校正會漏掉角度誤差。","failureEn":"Center-only alignment misses rotational error.","check":"保留 θ 的弧度單位與邊緣預測值。","checkEn":"Retain θ in radians and predicted edge displacement.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-015-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"小旋轉造成的切向位移約 rθ，距中心越遠越敏感。","textEn":"A small rotation causes tangential displacement approximately rθ, increasing away from the center.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a106-v9-015-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設半徑 100 mm、旋轉 1 µrad，邊緣位移 100 nm；中心標記幾乎不動不能證明全片合格。 驗收：保留 θ 的弧度單位與邊緣預測值。","textEn":"At hypothetical radius 100 mm and rotation 1 µrad, edge shift is 100 nm; a nearly fixed center does not prove whole-wafer compliance. Acceptance: Retain θ in radians and predicted edge displacement."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「拆出旋轉造成的邊緣位移」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Separate rotation-induced edge displacement\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["1 µrad 在所有半徑造成同樣位移。","中心對準即可免查邊緣。","保留 θ 的弧度單位與邊緣預測值。"],"optionsEn":["1 µrad produces equal displacement at every radius.","Center alignment removes the need to check edges.","Retain θ in radians and predicted edge displacement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設半徑 100 mm、旋轉 1 µrad，邊緣位移 100 nm；中心標記幾乎不動不能證明全片合格。 僅用中心標記校正會漏掉角度誤差。","explanationEn":"At hypothetical radius 100 mm and rotation 1 µrad, edge shift is 100 nm; a nearly fixed center does not prove whole-wafer compliance. Center-only alignment misses rotational error."}},{"id":"a106-v9-016","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-015"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"區別倍率與局部變形","titleEn":"Distinguish scale error from local distortion","objective":"提交擬合係數與扣除後殘差。","objectiveEn":"Submit fitted coefficients and post-fit residuals.","instruction":"擬合平移、旋轉、倍率及正交項，再畫剩餘向量，保留未被模型描述的高階形變。","instructionEn":"Fit translation, rotation, scale and orthogonality, then plot residual vectors and retain higher-order distortion outside the model.","observation":"假設倍率差 1 ppm、r=100 mm，徑向差 100 nm；與 1 µrad 旋轉量級相同但方向不同。","observationEn":"A hypothetical 1 ppm scale mismatch at r=100 mm gives 100 nm radial error, comparable in magnitude to 1 µrad rotation but different in direction.","failure":"只報全片 RMS 無法區分可校正的倍率與局部缺陷。","failureEn":"Whole-wafer RMS alone cannot distinguish correctable scale from local defects.","check":"提交擬合係數與扣除後殘差。","checkEn":"Submit fitted coefficients and post-fit residuals.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-016-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"倍率誤差產生隨半徑增加的徑向位移；局部非線性變形無法靠一個平移完全修正。","textEn":"Scale error produces radial displacement increasing with radius; local nonlinear distortion cannot be removed by one translation.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a106-v9-016-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設倍率差 1 ppm、r=100 mm，徑向差 100 nm；與 1 µrad 旋轉量級相同但方向不同。 驗收：提交擬合係數與扣除後殘差。","textEn":"A hypothetical 1 ppm scale mismatch at r=100 mm gives 100 nm radial error, comparable in magnitude to 1 µrad rotation but different in direction. Acceptance: Submit fitted coefficients and post-fit residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「區別倍率與局部變形」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Distinguish scale error from local distortion\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["提交擬合係數與扣除後殘差。","調一個平移量能消除全片倍率差。","徑向與切向向量代表同一誤差機制。"],"optionsEn":["Submit fitted coefficients and post-fit residuals.","One translation removes wafer-scale mismatch.","Radial and tangential vectors indicate the same mechanism."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設倍率差 1 ppm、r=100 mm，徑向差 100 nm；與 1 µrad 旋轉量級相同但方向不同。 只報全片 RMS 無法區分可校正的倍率與局部缺陷。","explanationEn":"A hypothetical 1 ppm scale mismatch at r=100 mm gives 100 nm radial error, comparable in magnitude to 1 µrad rotation but different in direction. Whole-wafer RMS alone cannot distinguish correctable scale from local defects."}},{"id":"a106-v9-017","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-016"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"計算接墊重疊與對位窗口","titleEn":"Calculate pad overlap and overlay window","objective":"報告 72% 並列仍需接觸電阻驗證。","objectiveEn":"Report 72% and retain contact-resistance verification.","instruction":"以兩個等大方形接墊作教學模型，逐次改變 dx、dy，計算重疊比例並標明模型不是原廠版圖。","instructionEn":"Use two equal square pads as a teaching model, sweep dx and dy, calculate overlap fraction and identify the layout as authored.","observation":"假設邊長 1 µm、dx=0.2 µm、dy=0.1 µm，重疊=(1−0.2)(1−0.1)=0.72 µm²，即 72%。","observationEn":"Hypothetical 1 µm squares with dx=0.2 µm and dy=0.1 µm overlap by (1−0.2)(1−0.1)=0.72 µm², or 72%.","failure":"以圓形接墊套用方形面積公式會得到錯誤窗口。","failureEn":"Applying the square formula to round pads gives an incorrect window.","check":"報告 72% 並列仍需接觸電阻驗證。","checkEn":"Report 72% and retain contact-resistance verification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-017-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"重疊面積影響接觸機會，但電阻還受界面品質影響；幾何重疊不是完整電性驗證。","textEn":"Overlap affects contact opportunity, but resistance also depends on interface quality; geometry alone is not electrical validation.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a106-v9-017-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設邊長 1 µm、dx=0.2 µm、dy=0.1 µm，重疊=(1−0.2)(1−0.1)=0.72 µm²，即 72%。 驗收：報告 72% 並列仍需接觸電阻驗證。","textEn":"Hypothetical 1 µm squares with dx=0.2 µm and dy=0.1 µm overlap by (1−0.2)(1−0.1)=0.72 µm², or 72%. Acceptance: Report 72% and retain contact-resistance verification."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「計算接墊重疊與對位窗口」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Calculate pad overlap and overlay window\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["72% 重疊必然代表 72% 電性良率。","報告 72% 並列仍需接觸電阻驗證。","接墊放大可無限改善而沒有鄰點代價。"],"optionsEn":["72% overlap necessarily means 72% electrical yield.","Report 72% and retain contact-resistance verification.","Unlimited pad enlargement has no neighboring-pad penalty."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設邊長 1 µm、dx=0.2 µm、dy=0.1 µm，重疊=(1−0.2)(1−0.1)=0.72 µm²，即 72%。 以圓形接墊套用方形面積公式會得到錯誤窗口。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical 1 µm squares with dx=0.2 µm and dy=0.1 µm overlap by (1−0.2)(1−0.1)=0.72 µm², or 72%. Applying the square formula to round pads gives an incorrect window."}},{"id":"a106-v9-018","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-017"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"同時計算鄰點淨間距","titleEn":"Calculate neighboring-pad clearance","objective":"同圖標重疊和 0.7 µm 淨間距，另列電場評估。","objectiveEn":"Mark overlap and 0.7 µm clearance together and retain electric-field assessment.","instruction":"畫三個相鄰方形接墊，沿最危險方向平移上層，計算對目標與鄰點的間距。","instructionEn":"Draw three adjacent square pads, translate the upper layer in the critical direction and compute intended and neighbor clearances.","observation":"假設節距 2 µm、等寬 1 µm、偏移 0.3 µm，簡化同向幾何的鄰點最小邊距=2−1−0.3=0.7 µm。","observationEn":"For hypothetical 2 µm pitch, 1 µm equal widths and 0.3 µm shift, simplified directional neighbor clearance is 2−1−0.3=0.7 µm.","failure":"只最大化重疊可能消耗介電隔離餘裕。","failureEn":"Maximizing overlap alone can consume dielectric isolation margin.","check":"同圖標重疊和 0.7 µm 淨間距，另列電場評估。","checkEn":"Mark overlap and 0.7 µm clearance together and retain electric-field assessment.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-018-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"提升重疊和保留鄰近隔離是相互競爭的幾何需求，不能只檢查正確配對接點。","textEn":"Improving overlap competes with neighboring isolation; checking only intended pairs is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a106-v9-018-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設節距 2 µm、等寬 1 µm、偏移 0.3 µm，簡化同向幾何的鄰點最小邊距=2−1−0.3=0.7 µm。 驗收：同圖標重疊和 0.7 µm 淨間距，另列電場評估。","textEn":"For hypothetical 2 µm pitch, 1 µm equal widths and 0.3 µm shift, simplified directional neighbor clearance is 2−1−0.3=0.7 µm. Acceptance: Mark overlap and 0.7 µm clearance together and retain electric-field assessment."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「同時計算鄰點淨間距」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Calculate neighboring-pad clearance\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["只看目標重疊即可排除相鄰漏電。","0.7 µm 幾何間距直接證明所有電壓都安全。","同圖標重疊和 0.7 µm 淨間距，另列電場評估。"],"optionsEn":["Intended overlap alone rules out neighbor leakage.","A 0.7 µm gap guarantees isolation at every voltage.","Mark overlap and 0.7 µm clearance together and retain electric-field assessment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設節距 2 µm、等寬 1 µm、偏移 0.3 µm，簡化同向幾何的鄰點最小邊距=2−1−0.3=0.7 µm。 只最大化重疊可能消耗介電隔離餘裕。","explanationEn":"For hypothetical 2 µm pitch, 1 µm equal widths and 0.3 µm shift, simplified directional neighbor clearance is 2−1−0.3=0.7 µm. Maximizing overlap alone can consume dielectric isolation margin."}}]},{"id":"a106-v9-stage05","order":5,"sequence":5,"title":"表面形貌、污染與接合波","titleEn":"Topography, contamination and bond waves","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"a106-v9-019","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-018"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"區分粗糙度、凹陷與全片翹曲","titleEn":"Distinguish roughness, recess and wafer bow","objective":"為三種尺度各指定獨立指標與量測方法。","objectiveEn":"Assign independent metrics and methods to all three scales.","instruction":"為 AFM、輪廓或全片形貌各畫量測視窗，標明濾波及基準面，避免先濾掉欲檢查訊號。","instructionEn":"Draw measurement windows for AFM, profiling and wafer shape, specifying filters and reference planes without filtering away the target signal.","observation":"教學例：1 µm 視窗的 0.2 nm RMS 與全片 20 µm bow 可同時存在；兩者不矛盾，也不能互相替代。","observationEn":"Teaching example: 0.2 nm RMS over a 1 µm window can coexist with 20 µm whole-wafer bow; neither contradicts nor replaces the other.","failure":"小區域很平不代表整片能無缺陷接觸。","failureEn":"A locally smooth area does not guarantee defect-free whole-wafer contact.","check":"為三種尺度各指定獨立指標與量測方法。","checkEn":"Assign independent metrics and methods to all three scales.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-019-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"奈米級表面粗糙、局部 Cu 凹陷與全片翹曲分属不同空間尺度，單一 RMS 不能同時描述。","textEn":"Nanoscale roughness, local Cu recess and wafer bow occur at different spatial scales; one RMS cannot describe them all.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"]},{"id":"a106-v9-019-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學例：1 µm 視窗的 0.2 nm RMS 與全片 20 µm bow 可同時存在；兩者不矛盾，也不能互相替代。 驗收：為三種尺度各指定獨立指標與量測方法。","textEn":"Teaching example: 0.2 nm RMS over a 1 µm window can coexist with 20 µm whole-wafer bow; neither contradicts nor replaces the other. Acceptance: Assign independent metrics and methods to all three scales."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「區分粗糙度、凹陷與全片翹曲」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Distinguish roughness, recess and wafer bow\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["為三種尺度各指定獨立指標與量測方法。","AFM RMS 合格即證明全片翹曲合格。","去除所有低頻成分後仍可直接量 bow。"],"optionsEn":["Assign independent metrics and methods to all three scales.","Passing AFM RMS proves whole-wafer bow compliance.","Bow remains directly measurable after removing all low-frequency content."],"answer":0,"explanation":"教學例：1 µm 視窗的 0.2 nm RMS 與全片 20 µm bow 可同時存在；兩者不矛盾，也不能互相替代。 小區域很平不代表整片能無缺陷接觸。","explanationEn":"Teaching example: 0.2 nm RMS over a 1 µm window can coexist with 20 µm whole-wafer bow; neither contradicts nor replaces the other. A locally smooth area does not guarantee defect-free whole-wafer contact."}},{"id":"a106-v9-020","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-019"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"建立銅凹陷分布而非單點值","titleEn":"Map copper recess rather than one point","objective":"呈現分布和最差點，門檻標為教學假設。","objectiveEn":"Show distribution and worst point, labeling the threshold hypothetical.","instruction":"對稀疏與密集接墊各取中心和邊緣掃描，保存原始剖面、平面扣除方法及異常值。","instructionEn":"Scan center and edge of sparse and dense pads and retain raw profiles, plane-removal method and outliers.","observation":"假設凹陷量 2、3、4 nm，平均 3 nm 不代表每點都是 3；若自訂窗口 2–3.5 nm，4 nm 點仍不符合。","observationEn":"Hypothetical recess values 2, 3 and 4 nm average 3 nm, but a 4 nm point fails an authored 2–3.5 nm window.","failure":"只以平均値放行會遮蔽局部過度凹陷。","failureEn":"Acceptance by average hides excessive local recess.","check":"呈現分布和最差點，門檻標為教學假設。","checkEn":"Show distribution and worst point, labeling the threshold hypothetical.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-020-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"凹陷是 Cu 相對周圍介電層的高度差，需一致基準面、材料辨識和掃描位置。","textEn":"Recess is copper height relative to surrounding dielectric and requires a consistent plane, material identification and scan location.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"]},{"id":"a106-v9-020-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設凹陷量 2、3、4 nm，平均 3 nm 不代表每點都是 3；若自訂窗口 2–3.5 nm，4 nm 點仍不符合。 驗收：呈現分布和最差點，門檻標為教學假設。","textEn":"Hypothetical recess values 2, 3 and 4 nm average 3 nm, but a 4 nm point fails an authored 2–3.5 nm window. Acceptance: Show distribution and worst point, labeling the threshold hypothetical."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「建立銅凹陷分布而非單點值」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Map copper recess rather than one point\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["平均 3 nm 即代表所有點合格。","呈現分布和最差點，門檻標為教學假設。","凹陷可忽略介電基準直接讀絕對高度。"],"optionsEn":["A 3 nm average means every point passes.","Show distribution and worst point, labeling the threshold hypothetical.","Recess can be read as absolute height without a dielectric reference."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設凹陷量 2、3、4 nm，平均 3 nm 不代表每點都是 3；若自訂窗口 2–3.5 nm，4 nm 點仍不符合。 只以平均値放行會遮蔽局部過度凹陷。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical recess values 2, 3 and 4 nm average 3 nm, but a 4 nm point fails an authored 2–3.5 nm window. Acceptance by average hides excessive local recess."}},{"id":"a106-v9-021","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-020"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"檢查圖形密度與 CMP 差異","titleEn":"Inspect pattern-density effects on CMP","objective":"提出有前後量測與副作用檢查的 dummy 試驗。","objectiveEn":"Propose a dummy-layout experiment with before/after data and side-effect checks.","instruction":"畫出相同晶粒內的稀疏、密集及 dummy 區，將高度差與密度圖疊合，控制量測尺度。","instructionEn":"Map sparse, dense and dummy regions on one die, overlay height differences and density, and control measurement scale.","observation":"教學假設兩區金屬密度 20% 和 60%，即使全片平均膜厚相同，也不能推定局部接墊高度相同。","observationEn":"Hypothetical 20% and 60% metal-density regions can share wafer-average thickness yet have different local pad heights.","failure":"增加 dummy 而不檢查電容、隔離和對位標記，可能引入其他問題。","failureEn":"Adding dummy metal without checking capacitance, isolation and marks may introduce other problems.","check":"提出有前後量測與副作用檢查的 dummy 試驗。","checkEn":"Propose a dummy-layout experiment with before/after data and side-effect checks.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-021-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"局部金屬密度與特徵尺寸改變拋光接觸條件，可能造成凹陷與侵蝕的不同趨勢。","textEn":"Local metal density and feature size change polishing contact conditions and can affect dishing and erosion differently.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"]},{"id":"a106-v9-021-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學假設兩區金屬密度 20% 和 60%，即使全片平均膜厚相同，也不能推定局部接墊高度相同。 驗收：提出有前後量測與副作用檢查的 dummy 試驗。","textEn":"Hypothetical 20% and 60% metal-density regions can share wafer-average thickness yet have different local pad heights. Acceptance: Propose a dummy-layout experiment with before/after data and side-effect checks."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「檢查圖形密度與 CMP 差異」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Inspect pattern-density effects on CMP\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["全片平均厚度等於局部平坦度。","dummy 只改機械性，永遠不影響電性。","提出有前後量測與副作用檢查的 dummy 試驗。"],"optionsEn":["Wafer-average thickness equals local planarity.","Dummy metal affects mechanics only and never electrical behavior.","Propose a dummy-layout experiment with before/after data and side-effect checks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學假設兩區金屬密度 20% 和 60%，即使全片平均膜厚相同，也不能推定局部接墊高度相同。 增加 dummy 而不檢查電容、隔離和對位標記，可能引入其他問題。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical 20% and 60% metal-density regions can share wafer-average thickness yet have different local pad heights. Adding dummy metal without checking capacitance, isolation and marks may introduce other problems."}},{"id":"a106-v9-022","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-021"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"從污染密度估算無缺陷機率","titleEn":"Estimate defect-free probability from contamination","objective":"標出獨立、均勻、致命比例三項假設。","objectiveEn":"State independence, uniformity and fatal-fraction assumptions.","instruction":"選定有效接合面積，換算顆粒密度單位，再對密度與有效致命比例做敏感度分析。","instructionEn":"Choose effective bond area, convert particle-density units and sweep density and effective fatal fraction.","observation":"假設 D=0.01/mm²、A=100 mm²，P0=e⁻¹=36.79%；這不是所有顆粒皆致命的實測結論，只是模型假設。","observationEn":"Hypothetical D=0.01/mm² and A=100 mm² give P0=e⁻¹=36.79%; fatality of every particle is an assumed model, not measured evidence.","failure":"把顆粒計數直接轉電性良率而不辨粒徑位置，會過度簡化。","failureEn":"Converting particle count directly to electrical yield ignores size and location.","check":"標出獨立、均勻、致命比例三項假設。","checkEn":"State independence, uniformity and fatal-fraction assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-022-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"簡化 Poisson 模型 P0=exp(−DA) 假設缺陷獨立且均勻；群聚污染需用空間地圖檢查。","textEn":"The simplified Poisson model P0=exp(−DA) assumes independent uniform defects; clusters require spatial-map checks.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"]},{"id":"a106-v9-022-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 D=0.01/mm²、A=100 mm²，P0=e⁻¹=36.79%；這不是所有顆粒皆致命的實測結論，只是模型假設。 驗收：標出獨立、均勻、致命比例三項假設。","textEn":"Hypothetical D=0.01/mm² and A=100 mm² give P0=e⁻¹=36.79%; fatality of every particle is an assumed model, not measured evidence. Acceptance: State independence, uniformity and fatal-fraction assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「從污染密度估算無缺陷機率」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Estimate defect-free probability from contamination\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["標出獨立、均勻、致命比例三項假設。","P0=36.79% 是所有實際產品的已知良率。","群聚污染可不看地圖直接用同一模型。"],"optionsEn":["State independence, uniformity and fatal-fraction assumptions.","36.79% is established yield for every actual product.","Clustered contamination needs no map-based check."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設 D=0.01/mm²、A=100 mm²，P0=e⁻¹=36.79%；這不是所有顆粒皆致命的實測結論，只是模型假設。 把顆粒計數直接轉電性良率而不辨粒徑位置，會過度簡化。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical D=0.01/mm² and A=100 mm² give P0=e⁻¹=36.79%; fatality of every particle is an assumed model, not measured evidence. Converting particle count directly to electrical yield ignores size and location."}},{"id":"a106-v9-023","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-022"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"規劃表面等待時間實驗","titleEn":"Design a surface queue-time experiment","objective":"提交隨機化表、混淆因子與量測指標。","objectiveEn":"Submit randomization, confounders and response metrics.","instruction":"設短、中、長三組自訂等待時間，隨機化量測順序，記錄濕度、載具、清潔批次及接合後缺陷。","instructionEn":"Choose short, medium and long authored delays, randomize measurement order and log humidity, carriers, cleaning lot and post-bond defects.","observation":"教學設計每組 5 試片共 15 片，只是比較計畫；不能在未量測前宣稱已找到製程窗口。","observationEn":"A teaching design of five coupons per delay uses 15 samples; it is an experiment plan, not evidence of a validated process window.","failure":"把長等待組全放在同一天，可能將日期差誤認為等待效應。","failureEn":"Running all long-delay samples on one day confounds delay with day effects.","check":"提交隨機化表、混淆因子與量測指標。","checkEn":"Submit randomization, confounders and response metrics.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-023-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"清潔或活化後的表面會隨環境與等待時間演變；時間、搬運和批次必須分開控制。","textEn":"Surfaces evolve after cleaning or activation with environment and delay; time, handling and lot must be controlled separately.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"]},{"id":"a106-v9-023-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學設計每組 5 試片共 15 片，只是比較計畫；不能在未量測前宣稱已找到製程窗口。 驗收：提交隨機化表、混淆因子與量測指標。","textEn":"A teaching design of five coupons per delay uses 15 samples; it is an experiment plan, not evidence of a validated process window. Acceptance: Submit randomization, confounders and response metrics."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「規劃表面等待時間實驗」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Design a surface queue-time experiment\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["未取得結果即可宣稱最短等待時間已合格。","提交隨機化表、混淆因子與量測指標。","等待組與批次完全重合不影響推論。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest delay can be declared qualified before data exist.","Submit randomization, confounders and response metrics.","Perfect confounding of delay and lot does not affect inference."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學設計每組 5 試片共 15 片，只是比較計畫；不能在未量測前宣稱已找到製程窗口。 把長等待組全放在同一天，可能將日期差誤認為等待效應。","explanationEn":"A teaching design of five coupons per delay uses 15 samples; it is an experiment plan, not evidence of a validated process window. Running all long-delay samples on one day confounds delay with day effects."}},{"id":"a106-v9-024","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-023"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"判讀接合波前與未接合區域","titleEn":"Interpret bond-wave fronts and unbonded regions","objective":"聯合波前、空洞圖與電性結果判讀。","objectiveEn":"Interpret fronts, void maps and electrical results together.","instruction":"在原創時序圖標接觸起點、波前和邊緣排氣，將最終空洞位置與前段形貌疊合。","instructionEn":"Mark initiation, fronts and edge venting on an original time sequence, then overlay final voids with pre-bond shape.","observation":"教學例：同樣 2 s 完成的兩片，一片中央空洞、一片無可見空洞；相同總時間不能證明相同品質。","observationEn":"Teaching example: two wafers finish in 2 s, but one has a central void and the other no visible void; equal duration does not prove equal quality.","failure":"把波前到邊緣視為所有接點已導通，混淆機械接觸與電連接。","failureEn":"A front reaching the edge does not establish electrical continuity at every contact.","check":"聯合波前、空洞圖與電性結果判讀。","checkEn":"Interpret fronts, void maps and electrical results together.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-024-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"波前傳播受局部間隙、氣體逸出、表面能與形狀影響，波速不是唯一品質指標。","textEn":"Bond-wave propagation depends on gap, gas escape, surface energy and shape; speed alone is not quality.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v6-hybrid-evg"]},{"id":"a106-v9-024-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學例：同樣 2 s 完成的兩片，一片中央空洞、一片無可見空洞；相同總時間不能證明相同品質。 驗收：聯合波前、空洞圖與電性結果判讀。","textEn":"Teaching example: two wafers finish in 2 s, but one has a central void and the other no visible void; equal duration does not prove equal quality. Acceptance: Interpret fronts, void maps and electrical results together."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「判讀接合波前與未接合區域」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Interpret bond-wave fronts and unbonded regions\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["接合波快就代表接觸電阻一定低。","波前到邊緣即可省略電測。","聯合波前、空洞圖與電性結果判讀。"],"optionsEn":["A fast bond wave guarantees low contact resistance.","A front reaching the edge eliminates electrical tests.","Interpret fronts, void maps and electrical results together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學例：同樣 2 s 完成的兩片，一片中央空洞、一片無可見空洞；相同總時間不能證明相同品質。 把波前到邊緣視為所有接點已導通，混淆機械接觸與電連接。","explanationEn":"Teaching example: two wafers finish in 2 s, but one has a central void and the other no visible void; equal duration does not prove equal quality. A front reaching the edge does not establish electrical continuity at every contact."}}]},{"id":"a106-v9-stage06","order":6,"sequence":6,"title":"熱機相容與電性去嵌","titleEn":"Thermomechanical compatibility and electrical de-embedding","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"a106-v9-025","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-024"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"估算熱膨脹與銅凹陷閉合","titleEn":"Estimate expansion and recess closure","objective":"報告 1 nm 量級及自由膨脹假設的限制。","objectiveEn":"Report the 1 nm scale and limitations of free expansion.","instruction":"畫銅、介電與基板剖面，先算自由膨脹，再列出拘束、微結構和蠕變所需證據。","instructionEn":"Draw copper, dielectric and substrate, calculate free expansion and list evidence needed for constraint, microstructure and creep.","observation":"假設 Δα=10 ppm/K、h=1 µm、ΔT=100 K，差動伸長約 1 nm；不能因此保證任何 1 nm 凹陷皆完成接合。","observationEn":"Hypothetical Δα=10 ppm/K, h=1 µm and ΔT=100 K give about 1 nm differential expansion, not proof that every 1 nm recess bonds.","failure":"直接把自由膨脹等同界面接觸，會漏掉拘束與表面狀態。","failureEn":"Equating free expansion with interface contact ignores constraint and surface state.","check":"報告 1 nm 量級及自由膨脹假設的限制。","checkEn":"Report the 1 nm scale and limitations of free expansion.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-025-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"Δh≈Δα·h·ΔT 是自由膨脹的尺度估計；嵌入銅受拘束且可能塑性變形，不能當通用退火配方。","textEn":"Δh≈Δα·h·ΔT estimates free-expansion scale; embedded copper is constrained and may deform plastically, so it is not a general annealing recipe.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"a106-v9-025-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 Δα=10 ppm/K、h=1 µm、ΔT=100 K，差動伸長約 1 nm；不能因此保證任何 1 nm 凹陷皆完成接合。 驗收：報告 1 nm 量級及自由膨脹假設的限制。","textEn":"Hypothetical Δα=10 ppm/K, h=1 µm and ΔT=100 K give about 1 nm differential expansion, not proof that every 1 nm recess bonds. Acceptance: Report the 1 nm scale and limitations of free expansion."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「估算熱膨脹與銅凹陷閉合」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Estimate expansion and recess closure\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["報告 1 nm 量級及自由膨脹假設的限制。","只憑此公式即可指定量產退火溫度。","所有材料都可忽略拘束自由膨脹。"],"optionsEn":["Report the 1 nm scale and limitations of free expansion.","This formula alone sets a production anneal temperature.","All materials expand freely without constraint."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設 Δα=10 ppm/K、h=1 µm、ΔT=100 K，差動伸長約 1 nm；不能因此保證任何 1 nm 凹陷皆完成接合。 直接把自由膨脹等同界面接觸，會漏掉拘束與表面狀態。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical Δα=10 ppm/K, h=1 µm and ΔT=100 K give about 1 nm differential expansion, not proof that every 1 nm recess bonds. Equating free expansion with interface contact ignores constraint and surface state."}},{"id":"a106-v9-026","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-025"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"建立熱歷程與材料相容性表","titleEn":"Build a thermal-history compatibility table","objective":"交付分層相容性表並標出需要實驗的界面。","objectiveEn":"Deliver a layer-by-layer table and flag interfaces requiring experiments.","instruction":"逐層列材料、既往熱歷程及尚未驗證的變化，分開升溫、停留和冷卻資料。","instructionEn":"List materials, prior thermal histories and unverified changes layer by layer, separating ramp, dwell and cooldown data.","observation":"教學例：兩個方案峰值相同但停留 10 和 100 min，擴散或反應程度一般不能假設相同；不自行替代原廠材料規格。","observationEn":"Teaching example: equal peaks with 10 versus 100 min dwell need not have equal diffusion or reaction; vendor material limits cannot be replaced by this example.","failure":"只核峰值溫度會忽略時間依賴與累積歷程。","failureEn":"Checking only the peak ignores time dependence and accumulated history.","check":"交付分層相容性表並標出需要實驗的界面。","checkEn":"Deliver a layer-by-layer table and flag interfaces requiring experiments.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-026-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"後接合熱處理同時影響金屬、介電、既有 BEOL 和元件；最高溫度不是唯一負載。","textEn":"Post-bond heating affects metal, dielectric, existing BEOL and devices; peak temperature is not the only load.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"a106-v9-026-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學例：兩個方案峰值相同但停留 10 和 100 min，擴散或反應程度一般不能假設相同；不自行替代原廠材料規格。 驗收：交付分層相容性表並標出需要實驗的界面。","textEn":"Teaching example: equal peaks with 10 versus 100 min dwell need not have equal diffusion or reaction; vendor material limits cannot be replaced by this example. Acceptance: Deliver a layer-by-layer table and flag interfaces requiring experiments."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「建立熱歷程與材料相容性表」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Build a thermal-history compatibility table\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["峰值相同就代表任意停留時間等效。","交付分層相容性表並標出需要實驗的界面。","接合成功即可忽略原有元件特性漂移。"],"optionsEn":["Equal peaks make all dwell times equivalent.","Deliver a layer-by-layer table and flag interfaces requiring experiments.","Successful attachment makes prior device drift irrelevant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學例：兩個方案峰值相同但停留 10 和 100 min，擴散或反應程度一般不能假設相同；不自行替代原廠材料規格。 只核峰值溫度會忽略時間依賴與累積歷程。","explanationEn":"Teaching example: equal peaks with 10 versus 100 min dwell need not have equal diffusion or reaction; vendor material limits cannot be replaced by this example. Checking only the peak ignores time dependence and accumulated history."}},{"id":"a106-v9-027","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-026"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"辨識破壞位置與接合能量","titleEn":"Identify fracture location and bond-energy evidence","objective":"提交荷重曲線、幾何及破面分類。","objectiveEn":"Submit load curves, geometry and fracture classification.","instruction":"畫裂紋路徑並記錄界面、介電或矽內破壞，對比相同幾何的試片，不混用剪切力與界面能。","instructionEn":"Map crack paths and identify interface, dielectric or silicon fracture, comparing identical geometries without mixing shear force and interface energy.","observation":"假設兩試片都在 20 N 破裂，一片界面分離、一片矽破裂；相同力不代表相同界面韌性。","observationEn":"Two hypothetical coupons fracture at 20 N, one at the interface and one in silicon; equal force does not imply equal interfacial toughness.","failure":"不記錄破面而只排列最大荷重，可能誤判改善方向。","failureEn":"Ranking peak load without fracture surfaces can misidentify improvement.","check":"提交荷重曲線、幾何及破面分類。","checkEn":"Submit load curves, geometry and fracture classification.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-027-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"機械測試數字只有配合幾何、載入方式與破面位置才可比較；高載荷可能由試片本體破裂決定。","textEn":"Mechanical values require geometry, loading and fracture location for comparison; high load may reflect substrate fracture rather than interface strength.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"a106-v9-027-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設兩試片都在 20 N 破裂，一片界面分離、一片矽破裂；相同力不代表相同界面韌性。 驗收：提交荷重曲線、幾何及破面分類。","textEn":"Two hypothetical coupons fracture at 20 N, one at the interface and one in silicon; equal force does not imply equal interfacial toughness. Acceptance: Submit load curves, geometry and fracture classification."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「辨識破壞位置與接合能量」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Identify fracture location and bond-energy evidence\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["相同破壞力必然代表相同界面接合能。","矽本體破裂便能精確求出所有界面韌性。","提交荷重曲線、幾何及破面分類。"],"optionsEn":["Equal fracture force implies equal bond energy.","Silicon fracture precisely determines every interface toughness.","Submit load curves, geometry and fracture classification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設兩試片都在 20 N 破裂，一片界面分離、一片矽破裂；相同力不代表相同界面韌性。 不記錄破面而只排列最大荷重，可能誤判改善方向。","explanationEn":"Two hypothetical coupons fracture at 20 N, one at the interface and one in silicon; equal force does not imply equal interfacial toughness. Ranking peak load without fracture surfaces can misidentify improvement."}},{"id":"a106-v9-028","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-027"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"以四端結構分離接點電阻","titleEn":"Separate contact resistance with four terminals","objective":"列單位、端點、反向電流檢查及不確定度。","objectiveEn":"List units, terminals, current-reversal check and uncertainty.","instruction":"畫電流端與高阻抗感測端，檢查電壓是否跨欲測接點，再改變電流方向檢查偏置。","instructionEn":"Draw current and high-impedance voltage terminals, verify the measured span and reverse current to check offset.","observation":"假設 I=10 mA、ΔV=50 µV，R=5 mΩ；若量測偏置 10 µV 未扣除，誤差相當於 1 mΩ。","observationEn":"Hypothetical I=10 mA and ΔV=50 µV give R=5 mΩ; an unremoved 10 µV offset corresponds to 1 mΩ error.","failure":"毫伏與微伏混用會造成千倍錯誤。","failureEn":"Confusing millivolts and microvolts creates a thousandfold error.","check":"列單位、端點、反向電流檢查及不確定度。","checkEn":"List units, terminals, current-reversal check and uncertainty.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-028-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"四端量測將施加電流與感測電壓分開以降低導線電阻影響，但仍需正確結構和寄生修正。","textEn":"Four-terminal measurement separates current and voltage paths to reduce lead resistance, but still requires valid structures and parasitic correction.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"a106-v9-028-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 I=10 mA、ΔV=50 µV，R=5 mΩ；若量測偏置 10 µV 未扣除，誤差相當於 1 mΩ。 驗收：列單位、端點、反向電流檢查及不確定度。","textEn":"Hypothetical I=10 mA and ΔV=50 µV give R=5 mΩ; an unremoved 10 µV offset corresponds to 1 mΩ error. Acceptance: List units, terminals, current-reversal check and uncertainty."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「以四端結構分離接點電阻」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Separate contact resistance with four terminals\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["列單位、端點、反向電流檢查及不確定度。","四端法能自動消除所有偏置與版圖寄生。","50 µV 除以 10 mA 等於 5 Ω。"],"optionsEn":["List units, terminals, current-reversal check and uncertainty.","Four terminals automatically remove all offsets and layout parasitics.","50 µV divided by 10 mA is 5 Ω."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設 I=10 mA、ΔV=50 µV，R=5 mΩ；若量測偏置 10 µV 未扣除，誤差相當於 1 mΩ。 毫伏與微伏混用會造成千倍錯誤。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical I=10 mA and ΔV=50 µV give R=5 mΩ; an unremoved 10 µV offset corresponds to 1 mΩ error. Confusing millivolts and microvolts creates a thousandfold error."}},{"id":"a106-v9-029","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-028"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"從串鏈回推平均接點的限制","titleEn":"Understand limits of chain-derived contact averages","objective":"報告基線、接點數、平均與定位限制。","objectiveEn":"Report baseline, count, average and localization limits.","instruction":"列串鏈總電阻、參考走線和接點數，計算平均並設計不同長度鏈以檢查比例關係。","instructionEn":"List total resistance, reference wiring and contact count, calculate the average and use different chain lengths to test scaling.","observation":"假設 100 接點總 1.5 Ω、走線基線 1.0 Ω，平均接點 5 mΩ；可能仍混有少數高阻與多數低阻。","observationEn":"A hypothetical 100-contact chain at 1.5 Ω with 1.0 Ω wiring gives mean contact resistance 5 mΩ; high-resistance outliers may remain.","failure":"把平均值當每個接點精確值會遮蔽尾端分布。","failureEn":"Treating the mean as each exact contact value hides distribution tails.","check":"報告基線、接點數、平均與定位限制。","checkEn":"Report baseline, count, average and localization limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-029-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"串鏈含走線、轉接與大量接點；扣除基線後可估平均，但不能定位單一高阻接點。","textEn":"Chains include wiring, transitions and many contacts; baseline subtraction estimates an average but cannot locate one high-resistance contact.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"a106-v9-029-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 100 接點總 1.5 Ω、走線基線 1.0 Ω，平均接點 5 mΩ；可能仍混有少數高阻與多數低阻。 驗收：報告基線、接點數、平均與定位限制。","textEn":"A hypothetical 100-contact chain at 1.5 Ω with 1.0 Ω wiring gives mean contact resistance 5 mΩ; high-resistance outliers may remain. Acceptance: Report baseline, count, average and localization limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「從串鏈回推平均接點的限制」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Understand limits of chain-derived contact averages\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["平均 5 mΩ 證明每個接點都是 5 mΩ。","報告基線、接點數、平均與定位限制。","可不扣走線直接除以接點數。"],"optionsEn":["A 5 mΩ average proves every contact is 5 mΩ.","Report baseline, count, average and localization limits.","Divide by contact count without removing wiring resistance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設 100 接點總 1.5 Ω、走線基線 1.0 Ω，平均接點 5 mΩ；可能仍混有少數高阻與多數低阻。 把平均值當每個接點精確值會遮蔽尾端分布。","explanationEn":"A hypothetical 100-contact chain at 1.5 Ω with 1.0 Ω wiring gives mean contact resistance 5 mΩ; high-resistance outliers may remain. Treating the mean as each exact contact value hides distribution tails."}},{"id":"a106-v9-030","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-029"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"區分導通與介電隔離失效","titleEn":"Distinguish continuity from dielectric-isolation failure","objective":"分列導通、漏電與可靠度證據。","objectiveEn":"Separate continuity, leakage and reliability evidence.","instruction":"建立串鏈與梳狀隔離結構對照表，逐一預測開路、橋接及介電缺陷改變哪項測試。","instructionEn":"Map chain and comb-isolation structures and predict responses to opens, bridges and dielectric defects.","observation":"假設 1 V 下漏電 1 nA，等效靜態阻值 1 GΩ；這不等於已知擊穿電壓或時間依賴壽命。","observationEn":"Hypothetical leakage 1 nA at 1 V gives static equivalent resistance 1 GΩ, not breakdown voltage or time-dependent lifetime.","failure":"單一低壓漏電合格不能排除高場長時間劣化。","failureEn":"Passing one low-voltage leakage test does not exclude long-term high-field degradation.","check":"分列導通、漏電與可靠度證據。","checkEn":"Separate continuity, leakage and reliability evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-030-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"接點低電阻和鄰近接點低漏電是不同驗證目標，必須有獨立結構與電壓條件。","textEn":"Low contact resistance and low neighbor leakage are separate targets requiring separate structures and voltage conditions.","sourceIds":["v6-hybrid-imec","v9deep-thermal-stress"]},{"id":"a106-v9-030-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 1 V 下漏電 1 nA，等效靜態阻值 1 GΩ；這不等於已知擊穿電壓或時間依賴壽命。 驗收：分列導通、漏電與可靠度證據。","textEn":"Hypothetical leakage 1 nA at 1 V gives static equivalent resistance 1 GΩ, not breakdown voltage or time-dependent lifetime. Acceptance: Separate continuity, leakage and reliability evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「區分導通與介電隔離失效」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Distinguish continuity from dielectric-isolation failure\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["串鏈導通便能排除鄰點短路。","1 GΩ 靜態值可證明所有電壓無擊穿。","分列導通、漏電與可靠度證據。"],"optionsEn":["Chain continuity rules out neighbor shorts.","A static 1 GΩ value proves no breakdown at any voltage.","Separate continuity, leakage and reliability evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設 1 V 下漏電 1 nA，等效靜態阻值 1 GΩ；這不等於已知擊穿電壓或時間依賴壽命。 單一低壓漏電合格不能排除高場長時間劣化。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical leakage 1 nA at 1 V gives static equivalent resistance 1 GΩ, not breakdown voltage or time-dependent lifetime. Passing one low-voltage leakage test does not exclude long-term high-field degradation."}}]},{"id":"a106-v9-stage07","order":7,"sequence":7,"title":"統計、根因與資格交付","titleEn":"Statistics, root cause and qualification handoff","description":"六項原創工程推算與判讀任務。算例皆為明示假設，需保留單位、參考面、模型範圍與驗收證據。","descriptionEn":"Six authored calculation and interpretation tasks. Examples are explicitly hypothetical; retain units, reference planes, model limits and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"],"enrichmentVersion":9,"steps":[{"id":"a106-v9-031","order":1,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-030"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"從接點失效率推算串鏈存活","titleEn":"Estimate chain survival from contact failures","objective":"保留獨立模型與群聚診斷的差異。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish the independence model from cluster diagnosis.","instruction":"掃描接點數 N 與單接點失效率 q，計算 (1−q)^N，再比較故障位置地圖。","instructionEn":"Sweep contact count N and failure probability q, calculate (1−q)^N and compare fault-location maps.","observation":"假設 q=0.001、N=1000，串鏈存活約 36.77%；單接點 99.9% 並不表示千接點鏈也是 99.9%。","observationEn":"Hypothetical q=0.001 and N=1000 give about 36.77% chain survival; 99.9% per contact is not 99.9% per thousand-contact chain.","failure":"將群聚缺陷視為獨立，會錯估不同鏈長的結果。","failureEn":"Treating clustered defects as independent misestimates chain-length effects.","check":"保留獨立模型與群聚診斷的差異。","checkEn":"Distinguish the independence model from cluster diagnosis.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-031-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"獨立接點存活相乘，長串鏈放大低機率缺陷；真實缺陷可能群聚，需另驗證。","textEn":"Independent contact survival multiplies and long chains amplify rare defects; real clustering requires separate validation.","sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"]},{"id":"a106-v9-031-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 q=0.001、N=1000，串鏈存活約 36.77%；單接點 99.9% 並不表示千接點鏈也是 99.9%。 驗收：保留獨立模型與群聚診斷的差異。","textEn":"Hypothetical q=0.001 and N=1000 give about 36.77% chain survival; 99.9% per contact is not 99.9% per thousand-contact chain. Acceptance: Distinguish the independence model from cluster diagnosis."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「從接點失效率推算串鏈存活」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Estimate chain survival from contact failures\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["保留獨立模型與群聚診斷的差異。","1000 接點鏈必然仍有 99.9% 良率。","長串鏈無法放大稀有接點缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Distinguish the independence model from cluster diagnosis.","A 1000-contact chain must still yield 99.9%.","Long chains do not amplify rare contact defects."],"answer":0,"explanation":"假設 q=0.001、N=1000，串鏈存活約 36.77%；單接點 99.9% 並不表示千接點鏈也是 99.9%。 將群聚缺陷視為獨立，會錯估不同鏈長的結果。","explanationEn":"Hypothetical q=0.001 and N=1000 give about 36.77% chain survival; 99.9% per contact is not 99.9% per thousand-contact chain. Treating clustered defects as independent misestimates chain-length effects."}},{"id":"a106-v9-032","order":2,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-031"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"量化零失效樣本的信賴界限","titleEn":"Quantify confidence after zero sample failures","objective":"明示樣本單位、數量、信賴度與相關性限制。","objectiveEn":"State sampling unit, count, confidence and correlation limits.","instruction":"分別以晶圓、晶粒或接點作抽樣單位，檢查是否同批相關，再計算可支持的上限。","instructionEn":"Choose wafer, die or contact as the sampling unit, inspect within-lot correlation and calculate the supported bound.","observation":"假設 300 個獨立試片零失效，95% 上限約 1%；不能宣稱失效率已低於 1 ppm。","observationEn":"With hypothetical 300 independent failure-free coupons, the approximate 95% upper bound is 1%, not evidence below 1 ppm.","failure":"把同片大量接點當完全獨立試片，可能誇大樣本資訊。","failureEn":"Treating many contacts on one wafer as independent coupons can exaggerate information.","check":"明示樣本單位、數量、信賴度與相關性限制。","checkEn":"State sampling unit, count, confidence and correlation limits.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-032-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"零失效只能界定上限；獨立二項模型下，95% 失效率上限約 3/n，樣本單位要明確。","textEn":"Zero failures only bounds the rate; under independent Bernoulli sampling the 95% upper bound is about 3/n and the sampling unit must be clear.","sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"]},{"id":"a106-v9-032-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"假設 300 個獨立試片零失效，95% 上限約 1%；不能宣稱失效率已低於 1 ppm。 驗收：明示樣本單位、數量、信賴度與相關性限制。","textEn":"With hypothetical 300 independent failure-free coupons, the approximate 95% upper bound is 1%, not evidence below 1 ppm. Acceptance: State sampling unit, count, confidence and correlation limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「量化零失效樣本的信賴界限」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Quantify confidence after zero sample failures\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["300 個零失效已證明小於 1 ppm。","明示樣本單位、數量、信賴度與相關性限制。","所有同片接點必然統計獨立。"],"optionsEn":["Three hundred zero-failure samples prove below 1 ppm.","State sampling unit, count, confidence and correlation limits.","All contacts on one wafer are necessarily independent."],"answer":1,"explanation":"假設 300 個獨立試片零失效，95% 上限約 1%；不能宣稱失效率已低於 1 ppm。 把同片大量接點當完全獨立試片，可能誇大樣本資訊。","explanationEn":"With hypothetical 300 independent failure-free coupons, the approximate 95% upper bound is 1%, not evidence below 1 ppm. Treating many contacts on one wafer as independent coupons can exaggerate information."}},{"id":"a106-v9-033","order":3,"sequence":33,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-032"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"整合上下片及接合後地圖","titleEn":"Merge upper, lower and post-bond maps","objective":"提交座標轉換與三標記殘差。","objectiveEn":"Submit transforms and three-mark residuals.","instruction":"以三個非共線且不對稱標記驗證轉換，疊合前段顆粒、對位殘差、空洞及電性地圖。","instructionEn":"Verify transforms with three asymmetric non-collinear marks and overlay particles, overlay residuals, voids and electrical maps.","observation":"教學例：上片圖左側缺陷經鏡射後可能對應成品右側；若直接疊圖，會錯誤宣稱缺陷不相關。","observationEn":"Teaching example: a defect on the upper map's left may become the assembled right after reflection; direct overlay could falsely suggest no correlation.","failure":"地圖方向錯誤會破壞根因分析而不易從圓形外觀察覺。","failureEn":"Wrong map orientation undermines root-cause analysis while wafer outlines still look correct.","check":"提交座標轉換與三標記殘差。","checkEn":"Submit transforms and three-mark residuals.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-033-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"晶圓面對面接合涉及鏡射、旋轉和座標原點；不同量測圖必須先轉為同一實體位置。","textEn":"Face-to-face bonding introduces reflection, rotation and origins; maps must be transformed to common physical coordinates.","sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"]},{"id":"a106-v9-033-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學例：上片圖左側缺陷經鏡射後可能對應成品右側；若直接疊圖，會錯誤宣稱缺陷不相關。 驗收：提交座標轉換與三標記殘差。","textEn":"Teaching example: a defect on the upper map's left may become the assembled right after reflection; direct overlay could falsely suggest no correlation. Acceptance: Submit transforms and three-mark residuals."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「整合上下片及接合後地圖」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Merge upper, lower and post-bond maps\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["圓形晶圓重合即代表所有座標正確。","鏡射可永遠以旋轉取代。","提交座標轉換與三標記殘差。"],"optionsEn":["Overlapping circles prove coordinate correctness.","Reflection can always be replaced by rotation.","Submit transforms and three-mark residuals."],"answer":2,"explanation":"教學例：上片圖左側缺陷經鏡射後可能對應成品右側；若直接疊圖，會錯誤宣稱缺陷不相關。 地圖方向錯誤會破壞根因分析而不易從圓形外觀察覺。","explanationEn":"Teaching example: a defect on the upper map's left may become the assembled right after reflection; direct overlay could falsely suggest no correlation. Wrong map orientation undermines root-cause analysis while wafer outlines still look correct."}},{"id":"a106-v9-034","order":4,"sequence":34,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-033"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"建立空洞與高阻的競爭假說","titleEn":"Build competing hypotheses for voids and high resistance","objective":"提交假說、辨識試驗及預期結果表。","objectiveEn":"Submit hypotheses, discriminating tests and expected results.","instruction":"列至少三個假說，為每個指定可支持及可否證的量測，先安排非破壞定位再選截面。","instructionEn":"List at least three hypotheses and supporting and falsifying measurements, using nondestructive localization before sectioning.","observation":"若空洞圖與高阻位置不重合，先查座標與檢測解析度，再考慮無可見空洞的電性機制。","observationEn":"If void and high-resistance maps do not coincide, first check coordinates and resolution before proposing electrically defective but visually bonded interfaces.","failure":"看到空洞就直接歸因清洗不足，會忽略形貌和困氣。","failureEn":"Attributing every void to poor cleaning ignores topography and trapped gas.","check":"提交假說、辨識試驗及預期結果表。","checkEn":"Submit hypotheses, discriminating tests and expected results.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-034-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"相同高阻可由未接合、污染、氧化或幾何錯位造成；單一影像通常不足以唯一決定根因。","textEn":"High resistance can arise from nonbonding, contamination, oxide or misalignment; one image rarely identifies a unique cause.","sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"]},{"id":"a106-v9-034-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"若空洞圖與高阻位置不重合，先查座標與檢測解析度，再考慮無可見空洞的電性機制。 驗收：提交假說、辨識試驗及預期結果表。","textEn":"If void and high-resistance maps do not coincide, first check coordinates and resolution before proposing electrically defective but visually bonded interfaces. Acceptance: Submit hypotheses, discriminating tests and expected results."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「建立空洞與高阻的競爭假說」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Build competing hypotheses for voids and high resistance\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["提交假說、辨識試驗及預期結果表。","任何空洞都只能由清洗不足造成。","沒有可見空洞必然表示電性完美。"],"optionsEn":["Submit hypotheses, discriminating tests and expected results.","Every void is caused only by poor cleaning.","No visible void guarantees perfect electrical behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若空洞圖與高阻位置不重合，先查座標與檢測解析度，再考慮無可見空洞的電性機制。 看到空洞就直接歸因清洗不足，會忽略形貌和困氣。","explanationEn":"If void and high-resistance maps do not coincide, first check coordinates and resolution before proposing electrically defective but visually bonded interfaces. Attributing every void to poor cleaning ignores topography and trapped gas."}},{"id":"a106-v9-035","order":5,"sequence":35,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-034"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"分離加速試驗與使用壽命","titleEn":"Separate accelerated testing and service life","objective":"交付任務、機制、試驗與壽命推論界限。","objectiveEn":"Deliver mission, mechanism, test and limits of life inference.","instruction":"先定使用任務與失效判據，再選溫循、濕熱或電性應力；保留應力前後電阻、漏電和影像。","instructionEn":"Define mission and failure criterion before selecting cycling, humidity or electrical stress, retaining before/after resistance, leakage and images.","observation":"教學例：試片經 1000 次某溫循無失效，只能報該條件下的觀察；沒有模型與任務剖面不能換算十年壽命。","observationEn":"Teaching example: survival of 1000 cycles supports that observation only; ten-year life cannot be inferred without a model and mission profile.","failure":"以通過某次試驗宣稱所有環境永久可靠，是超出證據的推論。","failureEn":"Claiming permanent reliability in every environment from one test exceeds evidence.","check":"交付任務、機制、試驗與壽命推論界限。","checkEn":"Deliver mission, mechanism, test and limits of life inference.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-035-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"加速模型依賴失效機制；改變應力後若機制改變，單一加速因子便不適用。","textEn":"Acceleration models depend on failure mechanisms; one factor fails if stress changes the mechanism.","sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"]},{"id":"a106-v9-035-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"教學例：試片經 1000 次某溫循無失效，只能報該條件下的觀察；沒有模型與任務剖面不能換算十年壽命。 驗收：交付任務、機制、試驗與壽命推論界限。","textEn":"Teaching example: survival of 1000 cycles supports that observation only; ten-year life cannot be inferred without a model and mission profile. Acceptance: Deliver mission, mechanism, test and limits of life inference."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「分離加速試驗與使用壽命」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Separate accelerated testing and service life\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["1000 次任何溫循都等同十年使用。","交付任務、機制、試驗與壽命推論界限。","只要無失效就不需保留應力條件。"],"optionsEn":["Any 1000 thermal cycles equal ten years of service.","Deliver mission, mechanism, test and limits of life inference.","No failures removes the need to retain stress conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"教學例：試片經 1000 次某溫循無失效，只能報該條件下的觀察；沒有模型與任務剖面不能換算十年壽命。 以通過某次試驗宣稱所有環境永久可靠，是超出證據的推論。","explanationEn":"Teaching example: survival of 1000 cycles supports that observation only; ten-year life cannot be inferred without a model and mission profile. Claiming permanent reliability in every environment from one test exceeds evidence."}},{"id":"a106-v9-036","order":6,"sequence":36,"estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"learningMode":"quantitative-design-review","evidenceStatus":"authored-educational-example","enrichmentVersion":9,"sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"],"prerequisiteIds":["a106-v9-035"],"sourceScope":"來源支持相關公開原理與研究背景；數值、判據、步序及選擇題為原創教學編排，並非原廠量產參數。","sourceScopeEn":"Sources support public principles and research context; numbers, criteria, sequence and quizzes are authored teaching work, not vendor production parameters.","title":"交付 W2W 資格證據封包","titleEn":"Deliver a W2W qualification-evidence package","objective":"另一人可重算例題並區分研究事實與未驗需求。","objectiveEn":"A peer can recompute examples and distinguish research facts from unverified requirements.","instruction":"整合上下片身份、旅行單、形貌、對位、機械與電性結果，逐需求列合格、未驗與不適用。","instructionEn":"Combine wafer identities, travelers, topography, overlay, mechanical and electrical results and mark each requirement passed, untested or inapplicable.","observation":"官方 2026 年 200 nm W2W 研究展示是有日期和試片範圍的里程碑；本課 1 µm 方墊算例不能被標為該流程複製。","observationEn":"The official 2026 200 nm W2W study is a dated test-vehicle milestone; this course's 1 µm square-pad examples are not reproductions of that flow.","failure":"把不同世代研究數字混成一份虛構量產配方會失去來源可追溯性。","failureEn":"Combining different research generations into a fictional production recipe destroys traceability.","check":"另一人可重算例題並區分研究事實與未驗需求。","checkEn":"A peer can recompute examples and distinguish research facts from unverified requirements.","knowledge":[{"id":"a106-v9-036-k1","title":"機制、公式與適用範圍","titleEn":"Mechanism, equation and validity","text":"研究節距紀錄、教學模擬與供應商資格需分開標示；交付應可追溯至晶圓、版圖與量測版本。","textEn":"Research pitch records, teaching simulations and supplier qualification must be separately labeled and traceable to wafers, layouts and measurement versions.","sourceIds":["v9deep-w2w-2026","pkb-tsmc-soic","v6-hybrid-imec"]},{"id":"a106-v9-036-k2","title":"原創算例與判讀","titleEn":"Authored worked example and interpretation","text":"官方 2026 年 200 nm W2W 研究展示是有日期和試片範圍的里程碑；本課 1 µm 方墊算例不能被標為該流程複製。 驗收：另一人可重算例題並區分研究事實與未驗需求。","textEn":"The official 2026 200 nm W2W study is a dated test-vehicle milestone; this course's 1 µm square-pad examples are not reproductions of that flow. Acceptance: A peer can recompute examples and distinguish research facts from unverified requirements."}],"quiz":{"question":"檢查「交付 W2W 資格證據封包」時，哪個判斷有完整工程依據？","questionEn":"When reviewing \"Deliver a W2W qualification-evidence package\", which conclusion is supported?","options":["課程完成即可代表原廠製造資格。","不同研究平台數字可直接混成共用配方。","另一人可重算例題並區分研究事實與未驗需求。"],"optionsEn":["Course completion grants vendor manufacturing qualification.","Numbers from different research platforms form one shared recipe.","A peer can recompute examples and distinguish research facts from unverified requirements."],"answer":2,"explanation":"官方 2026 年 200 nm W2W 研究展示是有日期和試片範圍的里程碑；本課 1 µm 方墊算例不能被標為該流程複製。 把不同世代研究數字混成一份虛構量產配方會失去來源可追溯性。","explanationEn":"The official 2026 200 nm W2W study is a dated test-vehicle milestone; this course's 1 µm square-pad examples are not reproductions of that flow. Combining different research generations into a fictional production recipe destroys traceability."}}]}],"scope":"公開原理的 36 項教學任務，包含自訂幾何、試算與實驗規劃；保留原 12 項進度 ID。研究里程碑、教學數字與量產資格明確區分，不提供專有配方。","scopeEn":"Thirty-six educational tasks in public principles with authored geometry, calculations and experiment plans, preserving the first twelve progress IDs. Research milestones, teaching numbers and production qualification remain distinct; no proprietary recipes are provided.","curriculumVersion":6,"enrichmentVersion":9,"subcategory":"pkg-joining","subcategoryTitle":"凸塊與精密接合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bumps and precision bonding","photoId":"v8-wafer"},{"id":"a103","title":"銅柱微凸塊製作","titleEn":"Copper-pillar microbump fabrication","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入凸塊共面性、電流密度與界面可靠度。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore bump coplanarity, current density and interface reliability, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["互連幾何與來料","圖形與金屬生長","界面與封裝互動","量測與可靠度放行"],"labelsEn":["Interconnect geometry and input","Patterning and metal growth","Interfaces and package interaction","Metrology and reliability release"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a103-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"互連幾何與來料","titleEn":"Interconnect geometry and input","description":"針對互連幾何與來料完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for interconnect geometry and input, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a103-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"焊墊與凸塊座標｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pad and bump coordinates | mechanism and design","objective":"針對焊墊與凸塊座標，把「焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pad and bump coordinates, turn \"Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「焊墊與凸塊座標」的模型：焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pad and bump coordinates: Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊墊與凸塊座標的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pad and bump coordinates, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-01-k1","title":"焊墊與凸塊座標：機制","titleEn":"Pad and bump coordinates: mechanism","text":"焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。","textEn":"Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。 必須排除的錯判：以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊墊與凸塊座標」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pad and bump coordinates — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。","以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊","初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長"],"optionsEn":["Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area.","Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap","Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life"],"answer":0,"explanation":"焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。 疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。 因此不能採用「以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊」。","explanationEn":"Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area. Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. Therefore reject: Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap."}},{"id":"a103-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-01"],"title":"焊墊與凸塊座標｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pad and bump coordinates | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對焊墊與凸塊座標，把「焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pad and bump coordinates, turn \"Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。 將「以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊墊與凸塊座標的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pad and bump coordinates: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-02-k1","title":"焊墊與凸塊座標：機制","titleEn":"Pad and bump coordinates: mechanism","text":"焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。","textEn":"Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。 必須排除的錯判：以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊墊與凸塊座標」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pad and bump coordinates — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長","疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。","以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊"],"optionsEn":["Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life","Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals.","Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap"],"answer":1,"explanation":"焊墊開口、凸塊中心與封裝對位誤差須同一座標系，局部偏心會縮小有效接合面。 疊合設計輪廓與量測中心，分開平移、旋轉與非線性殘差。 因此不能採用「以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊」。","explanationEn":"Pad openings, pillar centers and assembly overlay need one coordinate system; local eccentricity reduces useful contact area. Overlay design contours and measured centers; separate translation, rotation and nonlinear residuals. Therefore reject: Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap."}},{"id":"a103-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-02"],"title":"種子層連續性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Seed continuity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對種子層連續性，把「開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed continuity, turn \"A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「種子層連續性」的模型：開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for seed continuity: A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子層連續性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for seed continuity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-03-k1","title":"種子層連續性：機制","titleEn":"Seed continuity: mechanism","text":"開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。","textEn":"A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。 必須排除的錯判：僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. Misinterpretation to reject: Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子層連續性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed continuity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通","總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查","開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。"],"optionsEn":["Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity","Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks","A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。 以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。 因此不能採用「僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通」。","explanationEn":"A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography. Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. Therefore reject: Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity."}},{"id":"a103-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-03"],"title":"種子層連續性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Seed continuity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對種子層連續性，把「開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed continuity, turn \"A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。 將「僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子層連續性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for seed continuity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-04-k1","title":"種子層連續性：機制","titleEn":"Seed continuity: mechanism","text":"開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。","textEn":"A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。 必須排除的錯判：僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. Misinterpretation to reject: Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子層連續性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed continuity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。","僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通","總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查"],"optionsEn":["Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors.","Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity","Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"開路種子層使局部電位與沉積量失控；名義厚度相同不保證跨地形導通。 以片電阻地圖配合截面查看孔邊覆蓋，將探針接觸異常另列。 因此不能採用「僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通」。","explanationEn":"A discontinuous seed disrupts local potential and deposition; identical nominal thickness does not guarantee continuity over topography. Combine sheet-resistance maps with cross-sections at aperture edges and isolate probe-contact errors. Therefore reject: Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity."}},{"id":"a103-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-04"],"title":"光阻孔洞與側壁｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Resist apertures and sidewalls | mechanism and design","objective":"針對光阻孔洞與側壁，把「孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resist apertures and sidewalls, turn \"Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「光阻孔洞與側壁」的模型：孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for resist apertures and sidewalls: Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光阻孔洞與側壁的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for resist apertures and sidewalls, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-05-k1","title":"光阻孔洞與側壁：機制","titleEn":"Resist apertures and sidewalls: mechanism","text":"孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。","textEn":"Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。 必須排除的錯判：頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光阻孔洞與側壁」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resist apertures and sidewalls — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕","孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。","頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes","Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation.","Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。 比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。 因此不能採用「頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留」。","explanationEn":"Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation. Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. Therefore reject: Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base."}},{"id":"a103-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-05"],"title":"光阻孔洞與側壁｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Resist apertures and sidewalls | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對光阻孔洞與側壁，把「孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resist apertures and sidewalls, turn \"Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。 將「頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光阻孔洞與側壁的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for resist apertures and sidewalls: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-06-k1","title":"光阻孔洞與側壁：機制","titleEn":"Resist apertures and sidewalls: mechanism","text":"孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。","textEn":"Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。 必須排除的錯判：頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光阻孔洞與側壁」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resist apertures and sidewalls — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留","絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕","比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base","Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes","Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔徑、側壁角與光阻厚度共同決定柱的截面與可成長高度；顯影殘留可阻斷底部成核。 比較俯視孔徑、底部開口與截面角度，不把頂口尺寸當作柱底尺寸。 因此不能採用「頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留」。","explanationEn":"Aperture size, sidewall angle and resist thickness jointly constrain pillar shape and height; developer residue can obstruct nucleation. Compare top-view diameter, bottom opening and cross-section angle; the top opening is not the base diameter. Therefore reject: Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base."}}]},{"id":"a103-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"圖形與金屬生長","titleEn":"Patterning and metal growth","description":"針對圖形與金屬生長完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for patterning and metal growth, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a103-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-06"],"title":"電荷與高度預算｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Charge and height budget | mechanism and design","objective":"針對電荷與高度預算，把「法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For charge and height budget, turn \"Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「電荷與高度預算」的模型：法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for charge and height budget: Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電荷與高度預算的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for charge and height budget, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-07-k1","title":"電荷與高度預算：機制","titleEn":"Charge and height budget: mechanism","text":"法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。","textEn":"Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。 必須排除的錯判：總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電荷與高度預算」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For charge and height budget — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。","總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高","兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率"],"optionsEn":["Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current.","Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar","Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。 固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。 因此不能採用「總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高」。","explanationEn":"Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current. Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. Therefore reject: Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar."}},{"id":"a103-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-07"],"title":"電荷與高度預算｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Charge and height budget | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對電荷與高度預算，把「法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For charge and height budget, turn \"Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。 將「總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電荷與高度預算的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for charge and height budget: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-08-k1","title":"電荷與高度預算：機制","titleEn":"Charge and height budget: mechanism","text":"法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。","textEn":"Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。 必須排除的錯判：總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電荷與高度預算」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For charge and height budget — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率","固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。","總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高"],"optionsEn":["Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance","Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals.","Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar"],"answer":1,"explanation":"法拉第關係把總電荷連到理想沉積質量，實際高度還受電流效率、有效面積及邊緣電流影響。 固定圖形密度比較電荷與高度斜率，檢查中心至邊緣殘差。 因此不能採用「總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高」。","explanationEn":"Faraday's relation links charge to ideal deposited mass; actual height also depends on current efficiency, active area and edge current. Compare charge–height slopes at fixed pattern density and inspect center-to-edge residuals. Therefore reject: Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar."}},{"id":"a103-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-08"],"title":"圖形密度與共面性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pattern density and coplanarity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對圖形密度與共面性，把「高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pattern density and coplanarity, turn \"Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「圖形密度與共面性」的模型：高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pattern density and coplanarity: Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均柱高相同就能同時接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付圖形密度與共面性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pattern density and coplanarity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-09-k1","title":"圖形密度與共面性：機制","titleEn":"Pattern density and coplanarity: mechanism","text":"高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。","textEn":"Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。 必須排除的錯判：平均柱高相同就能同時接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圖形密度與共面性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pattern density and coplanarity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均柱高相同就能同時接觸","最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面","高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact","Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface","Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。 繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。 因此不能採用「平均柱高相同就能同時接觸」。","explanationEn":"Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales. Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. Therefore reject: Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact."}},{"id":"a103-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-09"],"title":"圖形密度與共面性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pattern density and coplanarity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對圖形密度與共面性，把「高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pattern density and coplanarity, turn \"Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。 將「平均柱高相同就能同時接觸」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均柱高相同就能同時接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付圖形密度與共面性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pattern density and coplanarity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-10-k1","title":"圖形密度與共面性：機制","titleEn":"Pattern density and coplanarity: mechanism","text":"高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。","textEn":"Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。 必須排除的錯判：平均柱高相同就能同時接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圖形密度與共面性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pattern density and coplanarity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。","平均柱高相同就能同時接觸","最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面"],"optionsEn":["Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements.","Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact","Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"高低圖形密度區分配不同局部電流；共面性須以單晶粒接觸面與全片高度分布分別定義。 繪製柱高直方圖並依圖形密度分組，報告最大最小差與重複量測。 因此不能採用「平均柱高相同就能同時接觸」。","explanationEn":"Dense and sparse patterns redistribute local current; define coplanarity at both die-contact and wafer-distribution scales. Plot pillar-height histograms grouped by pattern density, reporting range and repeat measurements. Therefore reject: Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact."}},{"id":"a103-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-10"],"title":"銅微結構｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Copper microstructure | mechanism and design","objective":"針對銅微結構，把「晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For copper microstructure, turn \"Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「銅微結構」的模型：晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for copper microstructure: Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅微結構的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for copper microstructure, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-11-k1","title":"銅微結構：機制","titleEn":"Copper microstructure: mechanism","text":"晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。","textEn":"Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。 必須排除的錯判：初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅微結構」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For copper microstructure — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移","晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。","初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長"],"optionsEn":["Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration","Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement.","Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。 將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。 因此不能採用「初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長」。","explanationEn":"Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement. Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. Therefore reject: Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life."}},{"id":"a103-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-11"],"title":"銅微結構｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Copper microstructure | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對銅微結構，把「晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For copper microstructure, turn \"Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。 將「初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅微結構的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for copper microstructure: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-12-k1","title":"銅微結構：機制","titleEn":"Copper microstructure: mechanism","text":"晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。","textEn":"Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。 必須排除的錯判：初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅微結構」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For copper microstructure — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長","通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移","將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life","Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration","Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒與雜質影響延展、電阻與後續熱循環；室溫電阻正常並不排除脆化界面。 將電阻、截面與熱處理前後微結構配對，保持樣本位置可追溯。 因此不能採用「初始電阻低就代表疲勞壽命長」。","explanationEn":"Grains and impurities affect ductility, resistance and thermal cycling; normal room-temperature resistance does not exclude embrittlement. Pair resistance, cross-section and pre/post-thermal microstructure with traceable sampling positions. Therefore reject: Assuming low initial resistance proves long fatigue life."}}]},{"id":"a103-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"界面與封裝互動","titleEn":"Interfaces and package interaction","description":"針對界面與封裝互動完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for interfaces and package interaction, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a103-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-12"],"title":"阻障與焊料帽｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Barrier and solder cap | mechanism and design","objective":"針對阻障與焊料帽，把「阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For barrier and solder cap, turn \"Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「阻障與焊料帽」的模型：阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for barrier and solder cap: Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付阻障與焊料帽的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for barrier and solder cap, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-13-k1","title":"阻障與焊料帽：機制","titleEn":"Barrier and solder cap: mechanism","text":"阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。","textEn":"Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。 必須排除的錯判：總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. Misinterpretation to reject: Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「阻障與焊料帽」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For barrier and solder cap — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。","總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查","各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功"],"optionsEn":["Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers.","Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks","Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly"],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。 量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。 因此不能採用「總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查」。","explanationEn":"Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers. Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. Therefore reject: Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks."}},{"id":"a103-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-13"],"title":"阻障與焊料帽｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Barrier and solder cap | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對阻障與焊料帽，把「阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For barrier and solder cap, turn \"Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。 將「總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付阻障與焊料帽的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for barrier and solder cap: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-14-k1","title":"阻障與焊料帽：機制","titleEn":"Barrier and solder cap: mechanism","text":"阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。","textEn":"Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。 必須排除的錯判：總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. Misinterpretation to reject: Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「阻障與焊料帽」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For barrier and solder cap — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功","量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。","總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查"],"optionsEn":["Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly","Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder.","Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"阻障層與焊料帽在接合中參與擴散與反應；只報總凸塊高會掩蓋各層厚度不足。 量測分層截面及帽體積，將金屬間化合物與未反應焊料分開。 因此不能採用「總凸塊高度能代替各層組成檢查」。","explanationEn":"Barrier and solder cap participate in diffusion and reaction; reporting total bump height hides deficient individual layers. Measure layer-resolved cross-sections and cap volume; distinguish intermetallic from remaining solder. Therefore reject: Using total bump height instead of layer-composition checks."}},{"id":"a103-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-14"],"title":"去種子層與側蝕｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Seed removal and undercut | mechanism and design","objective":"針對去種子層與側蝕，把「移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed removal and undercut, turn \"Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「去種子層與側蝕」的模型：移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for seed removal and undercut: Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付去種子層與側蝕的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for seed removal and undercut, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-15-k1","title":"去種子層與側蝕：機制","titleEn":"Seed removal and undercut: mechanism","text":"移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。","textEn":"Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。 必須排除的錯判：絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「去種子層與側蝕」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed removal and undercut — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕","以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊","移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes","Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap","Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。 配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。 因此不能採用「絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕」。","explanationEn":"Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria. Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. Therefore reject: Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes."}},{"id":"a103-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-15"],"title":"去種子層與側蝕｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Seed removal and undercut | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對去種子層與側蝕，把「移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed removal and undercut, turn \"Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。 將「絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付去種子層與側蝕的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for seed removal and undercut: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-16-k1","title":"去種子層與側蝕：機制","titleEn":"Seed removal and undercut: mechanism","text":"移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。","textEn":"Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。 必須排除的錯判：絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「去種子層與側蝕」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed removal and undercut — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。","絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕","以全片平均偏移代表每顆凸塊重疊"],"optionsEn":["Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions.","Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes","Using mean wafer offset to represent every bump overlap"],"answer":0,"explanation":"移除導通背景需避免柱底側蝕；短路消失與機械根部完整是兩個不同驗收條件。 配對絕緣測試與柱根截面，在大間距和密集區各取樣。 因此不能採用「絕緣通過即可忽略柱根側蝕」。","explanationEn":"Removing the conductive background must limit base undercut; eliminating shorts and preserving the mechanical root are separate criteria. Pair isolation tests with pillar-root cross-sections in both sparse and dense regions. Therefore reject: Ignoring base undercut after isolation passes."}},{"id":"a103-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-16"],"title":"電阻與電流密度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Resistance and current density | mechanism and design","objective":"針對電阻與電流密度，把「柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resistance and current density, turn \"R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「電阻與電流密度」的模型：柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設銅柱直徑 20 μm、長 40 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m：R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ。10 mA 對應 J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m²；忽略接觸、尺寸效應與溫升，不能據此宣稱安全電流。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for resistance and current density: R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For an illustrative 20 μm diameter, 40 μm long Cu pillar with ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ. At 10 mA, J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m². Contact resistance, size effects and heating are omitted, so this does not establish a safe current. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電阻與電流密度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for resistance and current density, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-17-k1","title":"電阻與電流密度：機制","titleEn":"Resistance and current density: mechanism","text":"柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。","textEn":"R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。 必須排除的錯判：兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. Misinterpretation to reject: Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設銅柱直徑 20 μm、長 40 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m：R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ。10 mA 對應 J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m²；忽略接觸、尺寸效應與溫升，不能據此宣稱安全電流。","textEn":"For an illustrative 20 μm diameter, 40 μm long Cu pillar with ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ. At 10 mA, J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m². Contact resistance, size effects and heating are omitted, so this does not establish a safe current."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電阻與電流密度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resistance and current density — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通","柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。","兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率"],"optionsEn":["Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity","R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average.","Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。 做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。 因此不能採用「兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率」。","explanationEn":"R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average. Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. Therefore reject: Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance."}},{"id":"a103-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-17"],"title":"電阻與電流密度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Resistance and current density | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對電阻與電流密度，把「柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resistance and current density, turn \"R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。 將「兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設銅柱直徑 20 μm、長 40 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m：R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ。10 mA 對應 J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m²；忽略接觸、尺寸效應與溫升，不能據此宣稱安全電流。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. Challenge the hypothesis \"Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For an illustrative 20 μm diameter, 40 μm long Cu pillar with ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ. At 10 mA, J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m². Contact resistance, size effects and heating are omitted, so this does not establish a safe current. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電阻與電流密度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for resistance and current density: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-18-k1","title":"電阻與電流密度：機制","titleEn":"Resistance and current density: mechanism","text":"柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。","textEn":"R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。 必須排除的錯判：兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. Misinterpretation to reject: Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設銅柱直徑 20 μm、長 40 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m：R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ。10 mA 對應 J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m²；忽略接觸、尺寸效應與溫升，不能據此宣稱安全電流。","textEn":"For an illustrative 20 μm diameter, 40 μm long Cu pillar with ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R=ρL/A≈2.16 mΩ. At 10 mA, J≈3.18×10⁷ A/m². Contact resistance, size effects and heating are omitted, so this does not establish a safe current."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電阻與電流密度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resistance and current density — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率","僅用中心種子厚度證明全片電鍍連通","做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。"],"optionsEn":["Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance","Using center seed thickness alone to prove plating continuity","Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term."],"answer":2,"explanation":"柱身 R=ρL/A 只描述幾何導體；量測電阻還含接觸與引線，局部狹頸的 J 高於平均。 做四端與兩端比較，將幾何推算值同實測差額列成未知界面項。 因此不能採用「兩端電阻可直接反推純銅電阻率」。","explanationEn":"R=ρL/A describes the pillar body only; measured resistance includes contacts and leads, while a neck has higher J than the average. Compare four- and two-terminal results and record excess measured resistance as an unresolved interface term. Therefore reject: Directly inferring pure-Cu resistivity from two-terminal resistance."}}]},{"id":"a103-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"量測與可靠度放行","titleEn":"Metrology and reliability release","description":"針對量測與可靠度放行完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for metrology and reliability release, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a103-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-18"],"title":"剪切測試的破壞位置｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Shear-test failure locus | mechanism and design","objective":"針對剪切測試的破壞位置，把「剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For shear-test failure locus, turn \"Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「剪切測試的破壞位置」的模型：剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for shear-test failure locus: Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付剪切測試的破壞位置的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for shear-test failure locus, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-19-k1","title":"剪切測試的破壞位置：機制","titleEn":"Shear-test failure locus: mechanism","text":"剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。","textEn":"Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。 必須排除的錯判：最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剪切測試的破壞位置」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For shear-test failure locus — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。","最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面","頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留"],"optionsEn":["Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading.","Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface","Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base"],"answer":0,"explanation":"剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。 標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。 因此不能採用「最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面」。","explanationEn":"Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading. Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. Therefore reject: Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface."}},{"id":"a103-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-19"],"title":"剪切測試的破壞位置｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Shear-test failure locus | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對剪切測試的破壞位置，把「剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For shear-test failure locus, turn \"Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。 將「最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付剪切測試的破壞位置的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for shear-test failure locus: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-20-k1","title":"剪切測試的破壞位置：機制","titleEn":"Shear-test failure locus: mechanism","text":"剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。","textEn":"Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。 必須排除的錯判：最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剪切測試的破壞位置」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For shear-test failure locus — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["頂口尺寸合格即代表柱底無殘留","標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。","最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a correct top opening proves a residue-free base","Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone.","Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"剪切力需連同工具高度、加載方向與破面位置解讀；高峰值也可能來自不相關結構受力。 標示破面在柱身、焊料或焊墊，對照相同幾何的樣本而非只比牛頓數。 因此不能採用「最高剪切力必定代表最佳接合界面」。","explanationEn":"Interpret shear force with tool height, loading direction and fracture locus; a high peak can include unrelated structural loading. Locate fracture in pillar, solder or pad, comparing matched geometry rather than force alone. Therefore reject: Assuming the highest shear force identifies the best interface."}},{"id":"a103-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-20"],"title":"電遷移與溫升分辨｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Separate electromigration and heating | mechanism and design","objective":"針對電遷移與溫升分辨，把「阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For separate electromigration and heating, turn \"Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「電遷移與溫升分辨」的模型：阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for separate electromigration and heating: Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電遷移與溫升分辨的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for separate electromigration and heating, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-21-k1","title":"電遷移與溫升分辨：機制","titleEn":"Separate electromigration and heating: mechanism","text":"阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。","textEn":"Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。 必須排除的錯判：通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電遷移與溫升分辨」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For separate electromigration and heating — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移","總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高","阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。"],"optionsEn":["Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration","Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar","Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。 比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。 因此不能採用「通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移」。","explanationEn":"Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history. Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. Therefore reject: Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration."}},{"id":"a103-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-21"],"title":"電遷移與溫升分辨｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Separate electromigration and heating | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對電遷移與溫升分辨，把「阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For separate electromigration and heating, turn \"Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。 將「通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電遷移與溫升分辨的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for separate electromigration and heating: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-22-k1","title":"電遷移與溫升分辨：機制","titleEn":"Separate electromigration and heating: mechanism","text":"阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。","textEn":"Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。 必須排除的錯判：通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電遷移與溫升分辨」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For separate electromigration and heating — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。","通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移","總電荷相同必有相同每顆柱高"],"optionsEn":["Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift.","Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration","Assuming equal total charge gives equal height at every pillar"],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻值漂移可能由溫度可逆變化或不可逆空洞引起，必須同時保留電流極性與溫度歷程。 比較冷卻後阻值恢復與失效端位置，先排除量測接點飄移。 因此不能採用「通電中電阻上升只能是電遷移」。","explanationEn":"Resistance drift can reflect reversible heating or irreversible voiding; preserve current polarity and thermal history. Compare resistance recovery after cooling and failure location, first excluding probe drift. Therefore reject: Treating every powered resistance rise as electromigration."}},{"id":"a103-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-22"],"title":"組裝交接與抽樣｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Assembly handoff and sampling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對組裝交接與抽樣，把「後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For assembly handoff and sampling, turn \"Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「組裝交接與抽樣」的模型：後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for assembly handoff and sampling: Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付組裝交接與抽樣的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for assembly handoff and sampling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-23-k1","title":"組裝交接與抽樣：機制","titleEn":"Assembly handoff and sampling: mechanism","text":"後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。","textEn":"Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。 必須排除的錯判：各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「組裝交接與抽樣」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For assembly handoff and sampling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均柱高相同就能同時接觸","後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。","各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact","Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success.","Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly"],"answer":1,"explanation":"後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。 交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。 因此不能採用「各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功」。","explanationEn":"Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success. Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. Therefore reject: Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly."}},{"id":"a103-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"],"prerequisiteIds":["a103-v9-23"],"title":"組裝交接與抽樣｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Assembly handoff and sampling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對組裝交接與抽樣，把「後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For assembly handoff and sampling, turn \"Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。 將「各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付組裝交接與抽樣的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for assembly handoff and sampling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a103-v9-24-k1","title":"組裝交接與抽樣：機制","titleEn":"Assembly handoff and sampling: mechanism","text":"後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。","textEn":"Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]},{"id":"a103-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。 必須排除的錯判：各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-asebump"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「組裝交接與抽樣」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For assembly handoff and sampling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功","平均柱高相同就能同時接觸","交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly","Assuming equal mean pillar height ensures simultaneous contact","Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"後段需要柱高、偏心、帽體積與污染的聯合分布；單一合格率不能表示多條件共同成功率。 交付可追溯晶粒地圖及不確定度，挑選邊緣條件樣本進行接合驗證。 因此不能採用「各項各自合格就保證所有凸塊組裝成功」。","explanationEn":"Assembly needs joint distributions of height, eccentricity, cap volume and contamination; one yield does not represent joint success. Deliver traceable die maps with uncertainty and include edge-condition samples in bonding validation. Therefore reject: Assuming individual parameter passes guarantee all-bump assembly."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-joining","subcategoryTitle":"凸塊與精密接合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bumps and precision bonding","photoId":"v9-quilt-solder"},{"id":"a104","title":"熱壓接合","titleEn":"Thermocompression bonding","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入力—熱—位移耦合與接合後界面。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore force–temperature–displacement coupling and bonded interfaces, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["接觸設計","熱機控制","界面形成","可靠度與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Contact design","Thermomechanical control","Interface formation","Reliability and verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a104-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"接觸設計","titleEn":"Contact design","description":"針對接觸設計完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for contact design, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a104-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"接合堆疊剖面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Bond-stack cross-section | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接合堆疊剖面，把「上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bond-stack cross-section, turn \"Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接合堆疊剖面」的模型：上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for bond-stack cross-section: Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合堆疊剖面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for bond-stack cross-section, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-01-k1","title":"接合堆疊剖面：機制","titleEn":"Bond-stack cross-section: mechanism","text":"上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。","textEn":"Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。 必須排除的錯判：工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合堆疊剖面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bond-stack cross-section — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。","工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲","Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量"],"optionsEn":["Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes.","Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage","Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression"],"answer":0,"explanation":"上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。 畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。 因此不能採用「工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲」。","explanationEn":"Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes. Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. Therefore reject: Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage."}},{"id":"a104-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-01"],"title":"接合堆疊剖面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Bond-stack cross-section | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接合堆疊剖面，把「上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bond-stack cross-section, turn \"Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。 將「工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合堆疊剖面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for bond-stack cross-section: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-02-k1","title":"接合堆疊剖面：機制","titleEn":"Bond-stack cross-section: mechanism","text":"上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。","textEn":"Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。 必須排除的錯判：工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合堆疊剖面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bond-stack cross-section — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量","畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。","工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲"],"optionsEn":["Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression","Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations.","Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"上晶粒、接合點、下基板與工具各有剛性和熱膨脹，邊界不能簡化成兩個完全平板。 畫受力與熱流兩張圖，標明受約束及自由伸長位置。 因此不能採用「工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲」。","explanationEn":"Die, joints, substrate and tools have distinct stiffness and expansion; the boundary is not simply two rigid planes. Draw separate load and heat-flow diagrams, identifying constrained and free-expansion locations. Therefore reject: Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage."}},{"id":"a104-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-02"],"title":"已知良品與面向｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Known-good die and orientation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對已知良品與面向，把「接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good die and orientation, turn \"Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「已知良品與面向」的模型：接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for known-good die and orientation: Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付已知良品與面向的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for known-good die and orientation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-03-k1","title":"已知良品與面向：機制","titleEn":"Known-good die and orientation: mechanism","text":"接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。","textEn":"Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。 必須排除的錯判：晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「已知良品與面向」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good die and orientation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查","高電阻一律表示加熱不足","接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。"],"optionsEn":["Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers","Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating","Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens."],"answer":2,"explanation":"接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。 以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。 因此不能採用「晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查」。","explanationEn":"Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens. Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. Therefore reject: Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers."}},{"id":"a104-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-03"],"title":"已知良品與面向｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Known-good die and orientation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對已知良品與面向，把「接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good die and orientation, turn \"Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。 將「晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付已知良品與面向的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for known-good die and orientation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-04-k1","title":"已知良品與面向：機制","titleEn":"Known-good die and orientation: mechanism","text":"接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。","textEn":"Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。 必須排除的錯判：晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「已知良品與面向」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good die and orientation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。","晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查","高電阻一律表示加熱不足"],"optionsEn":["Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone.","Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers","Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接合後難以接近的節點須在前段建立電性與面向追溯，鏡像坐標錯誤可造成規則性開路。 以非對稱標記驗證旋轉與翻面，對照良品地圖而非僅辨識條碼。 因此不能採用「晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查」。","explanationEn":"Nodes inaccessible after bonding need pre-bond electrical and orientation traceability; mirrored coordinates can produce systematic opens. Verify rotation and flipping with asymmetric marks and compare known-good-die maps, not barcodes alone. Therefore reject: Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers."}},{"id":"a104-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-04"],"title":"接觸壓力分布｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Contact-pressure distribution | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接觸壓力分布，把「總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For contact-pressure distribution, turn \"Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接觸壓力分布」的模型：總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for contact-pressure distribution: Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接觸壓力分布的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for contact-pressure distribution, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-05-k1","title":"接觸壓力分布：機制","titleEn":"Contact-pressure distribution: mechanism","text":"總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。","textEn":"Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。 必須排除的錯判：固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸壓力分布」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For contact-pressure distribution — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["增加壓力總能消除所有空洞","總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。","固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓"],"optionsEn":["Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids","Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open.","Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure"],"answer":1,"explanation":"總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。 將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。 因此不能採用「固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓」。","explanationEn":"Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open. Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. Therefore reject: Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure."}},{"id":"a104-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-05"],"title":"接觸壓力分布｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Contact-pressure distribution | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接觸壓力分布，把「總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For contact-pressure distribution, turn \"Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。 將「固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接觸壓力分布的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for contact-pressure distribution: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-06-k1","title":"接觸壓力分布：機制","titleEn":"Contact-pressure distribution: mechanism","text":"總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。","textEn":"Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。 必須排除的錯判：固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸壓力分布」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For contact-pressure distribution — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓","增加壓力總能消除所有空洞","將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure","Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids","Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites."],"answer":2,"explanation":"總力除以名義面積只是平均；少數高凸塊先承載會造成局部過載與其餘接點未接觸。 將柱高分布與接觸順序連結，檢查高低點的破面與電阻。 因此不能採用「固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓」。","explanationEn":"Force divided by nominal area is only an average; tall bumps can overload while other joints remain open. Link bump-height distribution to contact order and inspect fracture/resistance at high and low sites. Therefore reject: Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure."}}]},{"id":"a104-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"熱機控制","titleEn":"Thermomechanical control","description":"針對熱機控制完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for thermomechanical control, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a104-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-06"],"title":"溫度讀值與界面溫度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Sensor versus interface temperature | mechanism and design","objective":"針對溫度讀值與界面溫度，把「工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sensor versus interface temperature, turn \"Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「溫度讀值與界面溫度」的模型：工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for sensor versus interface temperature: Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付溫度讀值與界面溫度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for sensor versus interface temperature, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-07-k1","title":"溫度讀值與界面溫度：機制","titleEn":"Sensor versus interface temperature: mechanism","text":"工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。","textEn":"Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。 必須排除的錯判：工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度讀值與界面溫度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sensor versus interface temperature — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。","工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步","反應層越厚接合必越好"],"optionsEn":["Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories.","Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized","Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding"],"answer":0,"explanation":"工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。 比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。 因此不能採用「工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步」。","explanationEn":"Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories. Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. Therefore reject: Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized."}},{"id":"a104-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-07"],"title":"溫度讀值與界面溫度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Sensor versus interface temperature | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對溫度讀值與界面溫度，把「工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sensor versus interface temperature, turn \"Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。 將「工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付溫度讀值與界面溫度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for sensor versus interface temperature: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-08-k1","title":"溫度讀值與界面溫度：機制","titleEn":"Sensor versus interface temperature: mechanism","text":"工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。","textEn":"Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。 必須排除的錯判：工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度讀值與界面溫度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sensor versus interface temperature — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["反應層越厚接合必越好","比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。","工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding","Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty.","Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized"],"answer":1,"explanation":"工具感測溫度與接合界面有熱阻、熱容量和延遲；相同設定不保證不同堆疊的相同熱歷程。 比較見證件的界面溫度與工具曲線，記錄校正位置和誤差。 因此不能採用「工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步」。","explanationEn":"Tool sensors and bond interfaces differ through thermal resistance, capacity and delay; identical settings need not yield identical histories. Compare witness-interface and tool-temperature traces with calibration location and uncertainty. Therefore reject: Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized."}},{"id":"a104-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-08"],"title":"熱膨脹對位｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal overlay | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱膨脹對位，把「不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal overlay, turn \"CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱膨脹對位」的模型：不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal overlay: CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱膨脹對位的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal overlay, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-09-k1","title":"熱膨脹對位：機制","titleEn":"Thermal overlay: mechanism","text":"不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。","textEn":"CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。 必須排除的錯判：熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱膨脹對位」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal overlay — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量","熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測","不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。"],"optionsEn":["Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation","Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass","CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。 在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。 因此不能採用「熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量」。","explanationEn":"CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment. Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. Therefore reject: Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation."}},{"id":"a104-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-09"],"title":"熱膨脹對位｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal overlay | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱膨脹對位，把「不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal overlay, turn \"CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。 將「熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱膨脹對位的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal overlay: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-10-k1","title":"熱膨脹對位：機制","titleEn":"Thermal overlay: mechanism","text":"不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。","textEn":"CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。 必須排除的錯判：熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱膨脹對位」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal overlay — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。","熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量","熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測"],"optionsEn":["Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift.","Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation","Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同 CTE 的晶粒與基板加熱後產生位置依賴偏移；室溫對位不能直接當熱態對位。 在中心、邊緣畫位移向量，檢查比例性伸縮與工具漂移是否可分。 因此不能採用「熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量」。","explanationEn":"CTE mismatch produces position-dependent displacement on heating; room-temperature alignment is not hot alignment. Map displacement vectors at center and edge, separating scale change from tool drift. Therefore reject: Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation."}},{"id":"a104-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-10"],"title":"位移回授與壓縮｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Displacement feedback and compression | mechanism and design","objective":"針對位移回授與壓縮，把「量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For displacement feedback and compression, turn \"Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「位移回授與壓縮」的模型：量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for displacement feedback and compression: Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付位移回授與壓縮的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for displacement feedback and compression, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-11-k1","title":"位移回授與壓縮：機制","titleEn":"Displacement feedback and compression: mechanism","text":"量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。","textEn":"Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。 必須排除的錯判：Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「位移回授與壓縮」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For displacement feedback and compression — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致","量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。","Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance","Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression.","Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression"],"answer":1,"explanation":"量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。 以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。 因此不能採用「Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量」。","explanationEn":"Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression. Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. Therefore reject: Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression."}},{"id":"a104-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-11"],"title":"位移回授與壓縮｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Displacement feedback and compression | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對位移回授與壓縮，把「量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For displacement feedback and compression, turn \"Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。 將「Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付位移回授與壓縮的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for displacement feedback and compression: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-12-k1","title":"位移回授與壓縮：機制","titleEn":"Displacement feedback and compression: mechanism","text":"量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。","textEn":"Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。 必須排除的錯判：Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「位移回授與壓縮」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For displacement feedback and compression — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量","菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致","以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression","Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance","Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量到的 Z 位移含工具、基板與接點變形，不能全部算成焊料壓縮。 以空載與剛性參考比較回授，再同接合後間隙截面交叉驗證。 因此不能採用「Z 回授位移就是每顆焊點壓縮量」。","explanationEn":"Measured Z motion includes tool, substrate and joint compliance; it is not all solder compression. Use unloaded and rigid references, then cross-check against post-bond gap sections. Therefore reject: Equating Z feedback with each joint's compression."}}]},{"id":"a104-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"界面形成","titleEn":"Interface formation","description":"針對界面形成完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for interface formation, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a104-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-12"],"title":"氧化與潤濕證據｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Oxide and wetting evidence | mechanism and design","objective":"針對氧化與潤濕證據，把「未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For oxide and wetting evidence, turn \"Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「氧化與潤濕證據」的模型：未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for oxide and wetting evidence: Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：高電阻一律表示加熱不足。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付氧化與潤濕證據的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for oxide and wetting evidence, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-13-k1","title":"氧化與潤濕證據：機制","titleEn":"Oxide and wetting evidence: mechanism","text":"未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。","textEn":"Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。 必須排除的錯判：高電阻一律表示加熱不足。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氧化與潤濕證據」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For oxide and wetting evidence — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。","高電阻一律表示加熱不足","相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定"],"optionsEn":["Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them.","Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating","Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools"],"answer":0,"explanation":"未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。 比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。 因此不能採用「高電阻一律表示加熱不足」。","explanationEn":"Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them. Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. Therefore reject: Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating."}},{"id":"a104-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-13"],"title":"氧化與潤濕證據｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Oxide and wetting evidence | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對氧化與潤濕證據，把「未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For oxide and wetting evidence, turn \"Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。 將「高電阻一律表示加熱不足」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. Challenge the hypothesis \"Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：高電阻一律表示加熱不足。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付氧化與潤濕證據的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for oxide and wetting evidence: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-14-k1","title":"氧化與潤濕證據：機制","titleEn":"Oxide and wetting evidence: mechanism","text":"未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。","textEn":"Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。 必須排除的錯判：高電阻一律表示加熱不足。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「氧化與潤濕證據」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For oxide and wetting evidence — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定","比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。","高電阻一律表示加熱不足"],"optionsEn":["Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools","Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section.","Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating"],"answer":1,"explanation":"未潤濕、污染與接觸不足可呈相似高電阻，需界面化學或形貌證據才能分辨。 比較接合面、開路位置與良品對照，避免只用一张低倍率截面。 因此不能採用「高電阻一律表示加熱不足」。","explanationEn":"Nonwetting, contamination and inadequate contact can all give high resistance; interface chemistry or morphology is needed to distinguish them. Compare bond faces, open-site maps and good controls rather than one low-magnification section. Therefore reject: Attributing every high resistance to insufficient heating."}},{"id":"a104-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-14"],"title":"聚合物流動與排氣｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Polymer flow and venting | mechanism and design","objective":"針對聚合物流動與排氣，把「非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For polymer flow and venting, turn \"Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「聚合物流動與排氣」的模型：非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for polymer flow and venting: Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：增加壓力總能消除所有空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付聚合物流動與排氣的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for polymer flow and venting, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-15-k1","title":"聚合物流動與排氣：機制","titleEn":"Polymer flow and venting: mechanism","text":"非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。","textEn":"Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。 必須排除的錯判：增加壓力總能消除所有空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「聚合物流動與排氣」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For polymer flow and venting — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["增加壓力總能消除所有空洞","工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲","非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids","Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage","Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。 將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。 因此不能採用「增加壓力總能消除所有空洞」。","explanationEn":"Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths. Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. Therefore reject: Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids."}},{"id":"a104-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-15"],"title":"聚合物流動與排氣｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Polymer flow and venting | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對聚合物流動與排氣，把「非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For polymer flow and venting, turn \"Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。 將「增加壓力總能消除所有空洞」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：增加壓力總能消除所有空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付聚合物流動與排氣的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for polymer flow and venting: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-16-k1","title":"聚合物流動與排氣：機制","titleEn":"Polymer flow and venting: mechanism","text":"非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。","textEn":"Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。 必須排除的錯判：增加壓力總能消除所有空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「聚合物流動與排氣」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For polymer flow and venting — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。","增加壓力總能消除所有空洞","工具平行即可消除堆疊的翹曲"],"optionsEn":["Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information.","Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids","Assuming parallel tools eliminate stack warpage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"非導電膜或膠的流動、固化與氣體排出競爭，間隙閉合過快可能封住逃逸路徑。 將空洞位置同流動前沿和邊緣排氣路徑對照，加入材料批次資訊。 因此不能採用「增加壓力總能消除所有空洞」。","explanationEn":"Polymer flow, curing and gas escape compete; fast gap closure can trap escape paths. Compare void locations with fronts and edge vent paths while retaining material-lot information. Therefore reject: Assuming greater pressure always removes all voids."}},{"id":"a104-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-16"],"title":"界面反應與脆層｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interface reaction and brittle layers | mechanism and design","objective":"針對界面反應與脆層，把「反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface reaction and brittle layers, turn \"Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「界面反應與脆層」的模型：反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：教學假設接觸總力 20 N、有效承載面積 4 mm²，平均壓力為 5 MPa；若只有四分之一面積先接觸，局部平均可達 20 MPa。這不是設備力或溫度配方，實際須由變形與接觸分析界定。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interface reaction and brittle layers: Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: An illustrative 20 N on 4 mm² gives a 5 MPa average pressure. If only one quarter initially touches, its average can reach 20 MPa. This is not a tool force or temperature recipe; deformation/contact analysis determines the actual distribution. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：反應層越厚接合必越好。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付界面反應與脆層的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interface reaction and brittle layers, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-17-k1","title":"界面反應與脆層：機制","titleEn":"Interface reaction and brittle layers: mechanism","text":"反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。","textEn":"Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。 必須排除的錯判：反應層越厚接合必越好。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"教學假設接觸總力 20 N、有效承載面積 4 mm²，平均壓力為 5 MPa；若只有四分之一面積先接觸，局部平均可達 20 MPa。這不是設備力或溫度配方，實際須由變形與接觸分析界定。","textEn":"An illustrative 20 N on 4 mm² gives a 5 MPa average pressure. If only one quarter initially touches, its average can reach 20 MPa. This is not a tool force or temperature recipe; deformation/contact analysis determines the actual distribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「界面反應與脆層」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface reaction and brittle layers — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查","反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。","反應層越厚接合必越好"],"optionsEn":["Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers","Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable.","Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding"],"answer":1,"explanation":"反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。 把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。 因此不能採用「反應層越厚接合必越好」。","explanationEn":"Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable. Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. Therefore reject: Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding."}},{"id":"a104-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-17"],"title":"界面反應與脆層｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interface reaction and brittle layers | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對界面反應與脆層，把「反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface reaction and brittle layers, turn \"Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。 將「反應層越厚接合必越好」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：教學假設接觸總力 20 N、有效承載面積 4 mm²，平均壓力為 5 MPa；若只有四分之一面積先接觸，局部平均可達 20 MPa。這不是設備力或溫度配方，實際須由變形與接觸分析界定。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: An illustrative 20 N on 4 mm² gives a 5 MPa average pressure. If only one quarter initially touches, its average can reach 20 MPa. This is not a tool force or temperature recipe; deformation/contact analysis determines the actual distribution. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：反應層越厚接合必越好。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付界面反應與脆層的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interface reaction and brittle layers: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-18-k1","title":"界面反應與脆層：機制","titleEn":"Interface reaction and brittle layers: mechanism","text":"反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。","textEn":"Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。 必須排除的錯判：反應層越厚接合必越好。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"教學假設接觸總力 20 N、有效承載面積 4 mm²，平均壓力為 5 MPa；若只有四分之一面積先接觸，局部平均可達 20 MPa。這不是設備力或溫度配方，實際須由變形與接觸分析界定。","textEn":"An illustrative 20 N on 4 mm² gives a 5 MPa average pressure. If only one quarter initially touches, its average can reach 20 MPa. This is not a tool force or temperature recipe; deformation/contact analysis determines the actual distribution."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「界面反應與脆層」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface reaction and brittle layers — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["反應層越厚接合必越好","晶粒料號相同即可省略翻面座標檢查","把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding","Skipping flip-coordinate checks for identical part numbers","Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging."],"answer":2,"explanation":"反應層形成有助於接合，但其厚度、形貌與應力集中需共同評估，並非越厚越可靠。 把界面層厚度分布、裂紋路徑及電性配對，區分初始與老化後。 因此不能採用「反應層越厚接合必越好」。","explanationEn":"Reaction layers enable bonding, but thickness, morphology and stress concentration must be assessed together; thicker is not automatically more reliable. Pair layer-thickness distributions, crack paths and electrical data before and after aging. Therefore reject: Assuming thicker reaction layers always improve bonding."}}]},{"id":"a104-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"可靠度與驗證","titleEn":"Reliability and verification","description":"針對可靠度與驗證完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for reliability and verification, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a104-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-18"],"title":"冷卻殘餘應力｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Residual stress during cooling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對冷卻殘餘應力，把「卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For residual stress during cooling, turn \"Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「冷卻殘餘應力」的模型：卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for residual stress during cooling: Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付冷卻殘餘應力的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for residual stress during cooling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-19-k1","title":"冷卻殘餘應力：機制","titleEn":"Residual stress during cooling: mechanism","text":"卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。","textEn":"Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。 必須排除的錯判：熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「冷卻殘餘應力」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For residual stress during cooling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。","熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測","固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓"],"optionsEn":["Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling.","Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass","Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure"],"answer":0,"explanation":"卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。 比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。 因此不能採用「熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測」。","explanationEn":"Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling. Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. Therefore reject: Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass."}},{"id":"a104-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-19"],"title":"冷卻殘餘應力｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Residual stress during cooling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對冷卻殘餘應力，把「卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For residual stress during cooling, turn \"Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。 將「熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付冷卻殘餘應力的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for residual stress during cooling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-20-k1","title":"冷卻殘餘應力：機制","titleEn":"Residual stress during cooling: mechanism","text":"卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。","textEn":"Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。 必須排除的錯判：熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「冷卻殘餘應力」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For residual stress during cooling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["固定總力可保證各凸塊同壓","比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。","熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測"],"optionsEn":["Assuming constant total force guarantees equal bump pressure","Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports.","Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass"],"answer":1,"explanation":"卸載與冷卻順序改變約束狀態，熱態良好接觸可能在降溫後轉為裂紋。 比較熱態、冷態翹曲及開路分布，先固定相同量測支撐條件。 因此不能採用「熱態電性通過即可省略冷態重測」。","explanationEn":"Unloading and cooling alter constraints; good hot contact can become cracked after cooling. Compare hot/cold warpage and open maps with consistent measurement supports. Therefore reject: Skipping cold retest after a hot electrical pass."}},{"id":"a104-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-20"],"title":"鏈路電測與局部定位｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Chain testing and localization | mechanism and design","objective":"針對鏈路電測與局部定位，把「菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chain testing and localization, turn \"Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「鏈路電測與局部定位」的模型：菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for chain testing and localization: Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付鏈路電測與局部定位的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for chain testing and localization, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-21-k1","title":"鏈路電測與局部定位：機制","titleEn":"Chain testing and localization: mechanism","text":"菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。","textEn":"Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。 必須排除的錯判：菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鏈路電測與局部定位」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chain testing and localization — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致","工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步","菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance","Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized","Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。 先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。 因此不能採用「菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致」。","explanationEn":"Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces. Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. Therefore reject: Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance."}},{"id":"a104-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-21"],"title":"鏈路電測與局部定位｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Chain testing and localization | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對鏈路電測與局部定位，把「菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chain testing and localization, turn \"Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。 將「菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付鏈路電測與局部定位的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for chain testing and localization: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-22-k1","title":"鏈路電測與局部定位：機制","titleEn":"Chain testing and localization: mechanism","text":"菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。","textEn":"Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。 必須排除的錯判：菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鏈路電測與局部定位」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chain testing and localization — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。","菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致","工具達設定溫度代表所有界面已同步"],"optionsEn":["Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions.","Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance","Assuming a tool setpoint means every interface is synchronized"],"answer":0,"explanation":"菊鍊能放大連接失效但只给總阻值，局部 Kelvin 結構有助分離接點與路線。 先量鏈路再定位异常段，将量測底噪和重复性列入判定。 因此不能採用「菊鍊合格證明每接點阻值完全一致」。","explanationEn":"Daisy chains expose interconnect failures but return aggregate resistance; local Kelvin structures help separate joints and traces. Measure chains, localize anomalous segments and include instrument floor and repeatability in decisions. Therefore reject: Assuming a passing chain proves identical joint resistance."}},{"id":"a104-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-22"],"title":"接合窗口的轉移限制｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Limits of process-window transfer | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接合窗口的轉移限制，把「工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For limits of process-window transfer, turn \"Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接合窗口的轉移限制」的模型：工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for limits of process-window transfer: Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合窗口的轉移限制的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for limits of process-window transfer, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-23-k1","title":"接合窗口的轉移限制：機制","titleEn":"Limits of process-window transfer: mechanism","text":"工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。","textEn":"Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。 必須排除的錯判：相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. Misinterpretation to reject: Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合窗口的轉移限制」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For limits of process-window transfer — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量","工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。","相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定"],"optionsEn":["Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation","Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses.","Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools"],"answer":1,"explanation":"工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。 列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。 因此不能採用「相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定」。","explanationEn":"Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses. Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. Therefore reject: Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools."}},{"id":"a104-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a104-v9-23"],"title":"接合窗口的轉移限制｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Limits of process-window transfer | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接合窗口的轉移限制，把「工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For limits of process-window transfer, turn \"Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。 將「相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. Challenge the hypothesis \"Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合窗口的轉移限制的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for limits of process-window transfer: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a104-v9-24-k1","title":"接合窗口的轉移限制：機制","titleEn":"Limits of process-window transfer: mechanism","text":"工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。","textEn":"Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a104-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。 必須排除的錯判：相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. Misinterpretation to reject: Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besitcb","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合窗口的轉移限制」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For limits of process-window transfer — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定","熱偏移是一個可全片共用的平移量","列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。"],"optionsEn":["Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools","Treating thermal displacement as one uniform translation","Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"工具、材料、晶粒尺寸與間距變更會改變接觸和熱歷程，舊窗口須用見證件重新建立。 列變更矩陣與保留條件，至少含幾何、電性、界面和熱循環證據。 因此不能採用「相同型號設備可直接共用全部設定」。","explanationEn":"Tool, material, die-size and pitch changes alter contact and thermal histories; qualify transferred windows using witnesses. Document changes and holds using geometric, electrical, interface and thermal-cycle evidence. Therefore reject: Transferring every setting unchanged between nominally identical tools."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-joining","subcategoryTitle":"凸塊與精密接合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bumps and precision bonding","photoId":"v9-quilt-solder"},{"id":"a105","title":"直接銅對銅接合","titleEn":"Direct copper-to-copper bonding","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d","v9-media-3363c0f741d8","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入銅表面形貌、接觸形成與界面電阻。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore copper topography, contact formation and interface resistance, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["表面與界面設計","接觸形成","電性與力學證據","整合與壽命"],"labelsEn":["Surface and interface design","Contact formation","Electrical and mechanical evidence","Integration and lifetime"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a105-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"表面與界面設計","titleEn":"Surface and interface design","description":"針對表面與界面設計完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for surface and interface design, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a105-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"銅與介電界面區分｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Separate Cu and dielectric interfaces | mechanism and design","objective":"針對銅與介電界面區分，把「直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For separate cu and dielectric interfaces, turn \"Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「銅與介電界面區分」的模型：直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for separate cu and dielectric interfaces: Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅與介電界面區分的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for separate cu and dielectric interfaces, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-01-k1","title":"銅與介電界面區分：機制","titleEn":"Separate Cu and dielectric interfaces: mechanism","text":"直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。","textEn":"Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。 必須排除的錯判：所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅與介電界面區分」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For separate cu and dielectric interfaces — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。","所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面","提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻"],"optionsEn":["Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding.","Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface","Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit"],"answer":0,"explanation":"直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。 畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。 因此不能採用「所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面」。","explanationEn":"Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding. Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. Therefore reject: Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface."}},{"id":"a105-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-01"],"title":"銅與介電界面區分｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Separate Cu and dielectric interfaces | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對銅與介電界面區分，把「直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For separate cu and dielectric interfaces, turn \"Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。 將「所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅與介電界面區分的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for separate cu and dielectric interfaces: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-02-k1","title":"銅與介電界面區分：機制","titleEn":"Separate Cu and dielectric interfaces: mechanism","text":"直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。","textEn":"Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。 必須排除的錯判：所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅與介電界面區分」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For separate cu and dielectric interfaces — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻","畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。","所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面"],"optionsEn":["Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit","Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths.","Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"直接銅接合的承載與導電區必須明確界定，不能把混合接合的介電質支撐默認套入。 畫有無介電支撐兩種剖面，標出接觸應力和電流路徑。 因此不能採用「所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面」。","explanationEn":"Define the load-bearing and conductive regions explicitly; do not silently import dielectric support from hybrid bonding. Draw sections with and without dielectric support and mark contact stress and current paths. Therefore reject: Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface."}},{"id":"a105-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-02"],"title":"表面氧化與等待時間｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Oxidation and queue time | mechanism and design","objective":"針對表面氧化與等待時間，把「表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For oxidation and queue time, turn \"Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「表面氧化與等待時間」的模型：表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for oxidation and queue time: Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付表面氧化與等待時間的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for oxidation and queue time, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-03-k1","title":"表面氧化與等待時間：機制","titleEn":"Oxidation and queue time: mechanism","text":"表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。","textEn":"Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。 必須排除的錯判：清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「表面氧化與等待時間」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For oxidation and queue time — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變","一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面","表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely","Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface","Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。 將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。 因此不能採用「清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變」。","explanationEn":"Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry. Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. Therefore reject: Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely."}},{"id":"a105-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-03"],"title":"表面氧化與等待時間｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Oxidation and queue time | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對表面氧化與等待時間，把「表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For oxidation and queue time, turn \"Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。 將「清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付表面氧化與等待時間的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for oxidation and queue time: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-04-k1","title":"表面氧化與等待時間：機制","titleEn":"Oxidation and queue time: mechanism","text":"表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。","textEn":"Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。 必須排除的錯判：清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「表面氧化與等待時間」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For oxidation and queue time — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。","清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變","一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面"],"optionsEn":["Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics.","Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely","Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面狀態會隨清潔後暴露環境改變，等待時間是整合變數而不是行政記錄。 將批次、暴露與接合電阻关联，必要時用表面分析區分氧化和有機物。 因此不能採用「清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變」。","explanationEn":"Surface state changes with exposure after preparation; queue time is an integration variable, not merely a log entry. Correlate lot, exposure and resistance, using surface analysis to distinguish oxides from organics. Therefore reject: Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely."}},{"id":"a105-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-04"],"title":"粗糙度頻譜｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Roughness spectrum | mechanism and design","objective":"針對粗糙度頻譜，把「相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For roughness spectrum, turn \"Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「粗糙度頻譜」的模型：相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for roughness spectrum: Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付粗糙度頻譜的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for roughness spectrum, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-05-k1","title":"粗糙度頻譜：機制","titleEn":"Roughness spectrum: mechanism","text":"相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。","textEn":"Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。 必須排除的錯判：相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粗糙度頻譜」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For roughness spectrum — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生","相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。","相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積"],"optionsEn":["Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic","Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage.","Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area"],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。 比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。 因此不能採用「相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積」。","explanationEn":"Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage. Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. Therefore reject: Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area."}},{"id":"a105-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-05"],"title":"粗糙度頻譜｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Roughness spectrum | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對粗糙度頻譜，把「相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For roughness spectrum, turn \"Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。 將「相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付粗糙度頻譜的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for roughness spectrum: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-06-k1","title":"粗糙度頻譜：機制","titleEn":"Roughness spectrum: mechanism","text":"相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。","textEn":"Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。 必須排除的錯判：相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粗糙度頻譜」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For roughness spectrum — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積","四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生","比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area","Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic","Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相同 RMS 粗糙度可能來自不同空間波長；接觸面積還受起伏尺度與翹曲控制。 比較掃描尺寸、濾波條件與高度分布，避免把不同量測帶寬直接合併。 因此不能採用「相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積」。","explanationEn":"Equal RMS roughness can contain different spatial wavelengths; contact area also depends on waviness and warpage. Compare scan size, filtering and height distributions rather than merging different measurement bandwidths. Therefore reject: Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area."}}]},{"id":"a105-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"接觸形成","titleEn":"Contact formation","description":"針對接觸形成完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for contact formation, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a105-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-06"],"title":"銅凹陷與突出｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cu recess and protrusion | mechanism and design","objective":"針對銅凹陷與突出，把「金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cu recess and protrusion, turn \"Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「銅凹陷與突出」的模型：金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cu recess and protrusion: Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅凹陷與突出的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cu recess and protrusion, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-07-k1","title":"銅凹陷與突出：機制","titleEn":"Cu recess and protrusion: mechanism","text":"金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。","textEn":"Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。 必須排除的錯判：全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅凹陷與突出」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cu recess and protrusion — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。","全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷","聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙"],"optionsEn":["Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact.","Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small","Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps"],"answer":0,"explanation":"金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。 以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。 因此不能採用「全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷」。","explanationEn":"Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact. Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. Therefore reject: Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small."}},{"id":"a105-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-07"],"title":"銅凹陷與突出｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cu recess and protrusion | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對銅凹陷與突出，把「金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cu recess and protrusion, turn \"Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。 將「全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅凹陷與突出的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cu recess and protrusion: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-08-k1","title":"銅凹陷與突出：機制","titleEn":"Cu recess and protrusion: mechanism","text":"金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。","textEn":"Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。 必須排除的錯判：全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅凹陷與突出」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cu recess and protrusion — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙","以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。","全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷"],"optionsEn":["Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps","Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane.","Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small"],"answer":1,"explanation":"金屬相對周邊的高度決定最先接觸區和局部承壓，平均平坦不保證每個焊墊足夠接觸。 以跨焊墊線掃描量相對高度，記錄相鄰介電質作基準的方法。 因此不能採用「全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷」。","explanationEn":"Metal height relative to surroundings determines initial contact and local load; mean flatness does not guarantee all-pad contact. Measure cross-pad height relative to adjacent dielectric and document the reference plane. Therefore reject: Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small."}},{"id":"a105-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-08"],"title":"重疊面積預算｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Overlap-area budget | mechanism and design","objective":"針對重疊面積預算，把「對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overlap-area budget, turn \"Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「重疊面積預算」的模型：對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for overlap-area budget: Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付重疊面積預算的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for overlap-area budget, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-09-k1","title":"重疊面積預算：機制","titleEn":"Overlap-area budget: mechanism","text":"對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。","textEn":"Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。 必須排除的錯判：中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重疊面積預算」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overlap-area budget — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊","把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度","對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。"],"optionsEn":["Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment","Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength","Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。 由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。 因此不能採用「中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊」。","explanationEn":"Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center. Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. Therefore reject: Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment."}},{"id":"a105-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-09"],"title":"重疊面積預算｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Overlap-area budget | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對重疊面積預算，把「對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overlap-area budget, turn \"Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。 將「中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付重疊面積預算的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for overlap-area budget: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-10-k1","title":"重疊面積預算：機制","titleEn":"Overlap-area budget: mechanism","text":"對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。","textEn":"Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。 必須排除的錯判：中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重疊面積預算」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overlap-area budget — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。","中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊","把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度"],"optionsEn":["Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners.","Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment","Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength"],"answer":0,"explanation":"對位誤差減少有效電接觸面積並提高局部電流擁擠，旋轉誤差在遠離中心處更大。 由實測向量計算每顆焊墊交集面積，比較中心與角落。 因此不能採用「中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊」。","explanationEn":"Overlay reduces conducting area and increases crowding; rotational error grows farther from the center. Calculate pad-intersection areas from measured vectors and compare center and corners. Therefore reject: Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment."}},{"id":"a105-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-10"],"title":"真實接觸與塑性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Real contact and plasticity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對真實接觸與塑性，把「粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For real contact and plasticity, turn \"Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「真實接觸與塑性」的模型：粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for real contact and plasticity: Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付真實接觸與塑性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for real contact and plasticity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-11-k1","title":"真實接觸與塑性：機制","titleEn":"Real contact and plasticity: mechanism","text":"粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。","textEn":"Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。 必須排除的錯判：提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「真實接觸與塑性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For real contact and plasticity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合","粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。","提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes","Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions.","Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit"],"answer":1,"explanation":"粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。 比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。 因此不能採用「提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻」。","explanationEn":"Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions. Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. Therefore reject: Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit."}},{"id":"a105-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-11"],"title":"真實接觸與塑性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Real contact and plasticity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對真實接觸與塑性，把「粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For real contact and plasticity, turn \"Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。 將「提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付真實接觸與塑性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for real contact and plasticity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-12-k1","title":"真實接觸與塑性：機制","titleEn":"Real contact and plasticity: mechanism","text":"粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。","textEn":"Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。 必須排除的錯判：提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「真實接觸與塑性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For real contact and plasticity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻","分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合","比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit","Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes","Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粗糙峰先接觸，局部塑性及擴散會改變界面；名義壓力不足以描述接觸演化。 比較載入前後形貌、接觸電阻與殘餘印痕，用同幾何對照件。 因此不能採用「提高名義壓力必定線性降低接觸電阻」。","explanationEn":"Asperities touch first; local plasticity and diffusion evolve the interface, beyond nominal-pressure descriptions. Compare pre/post-load topography, resistance and residual impressions using matched geometries. Therefore reject: Assuming pressure reduces contact resistance linearly without limit."}}]},{"id":"a105-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"電性與力學證據","titleEn":"Electrical and mechanical evidence","description":"針對電性與力學證據完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for electrical and mechanical evidence, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a105-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-12"],"title":"晶粒取向與界面遷移｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Grain orientation and interface migration | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶粒取向與界面遷移，把「銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For grain orientation and interface migration, turn \"Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶粒取向與界面遷移」的模型：銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for grain orientation and interface migration: Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒取向與界面遷移的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for grain orientation and interface migration, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-13-k1","title":"晶粒取向與界面遷移：機制","titleEn":"Grain orientation and interface migration: mechanism","text":"銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。","textEn":"Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。 必須排除的錯判：一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒取向與界面遷移」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For grain orientation and interface migration — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。","一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面","設備流程完成即代表界面已合格"],"optionsEn":["Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity.","Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface","Equating completed processing with a qualified interface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。 用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。 因此不能採用「一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面」。","explanationEn":"Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity. Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. Therefore reject: Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface."}},{"id":"a105-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-13"],"title":"晶粒取向與界面遷移｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Grain orientation and interface migration | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶粒取向與界面遷移，把「銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For grain orientation and interface migration, turn \"Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。 將「一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒取向與界面遷移的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for grain orientation and interface migration: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-14-k1","title":"晶粒取向與界面遷移：機制","titleEn":"Grain orientation and interface migration: mechanism","text":"銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。","textEn":"Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。 必須排除的錯判：一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒取向與界面遷移」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For grain orientation and interface migration — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["設備流程完成即代表界面已合格","用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。","一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面"],"optionsEn":["Equating completed processing with a qualified interface","Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias.","Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"銅晶粒的取向和界面遷移會影響接合演化，初始接觸消失不等於所有區域皆連續。 用多位置截面或取向分析對照電性，標注取樣偏差。 因此不能採用「一張無接縫截面足以代表整片界面」。","explanationEn":"Grain orientation and boundary migration affect bond evolution; a locally vanished seam does not prove full-area continuity. Compare multisite sections or orientation analysis with electrical data and note sampling bias. Therefore reject: Using one seam-free section to certify the whole interface."}},{"id":"a105-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-14"],"title":"Kelvin 接觸電阻｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Kelvin contact resistance | mechanism and design","objective":"針對Kelvin 接觸電阻，把「四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For kelvin contact resistance, turn \"Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「Kelvin 接觸電阻」的模型：四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for kelvin contact resistance: Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Kelvin 接觸電阻的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for kelvin contact resistance, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-15-k1","title":"Kelvin 接觸電阻：機制","titleEn":"Kelvin contact resistance: mechanism","text":"四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。","textEn":"Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。 必須排除的錯判：四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Kelvin 接觸電阻」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For kelvin contact resistance — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生","所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面","四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic","Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface","Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。 比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。 因此不能採用「四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生」。","explanationEn":"Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates. Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. Therefore reject: Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic."}},{"id":"a105-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-15"],"title":"Kelvin 接觸電阻｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Kelvin contact resistance | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對Kelvin 接觸電阻，把「四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For kelvin contact resistance, turn \"Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。 將「四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Kelvin 接觸電阻的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for kelvin contact resistance: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-16-k1","title":"Kelvin 接觸電阻：機制","titleEn":"Kelvin contact resistance: mechanism","text":"四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。","textEn":"Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。 必須排除的錯判：四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Kelvin 接觸電阻」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For kelvin contact resistance — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。","四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生","所有無焊料接合都具有相同混合界面"],"optionsEn":["Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution.","Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic","Treating every solderless bond as the same hybrid interface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"四端結構能減少引線影響，但電流擁擠與幾何展開仍可能混入界面估算。 比较不同接點尺寸的 R×面積趨勢，檢查是否存在固定串聯項。 因此不能採用「四端量測自動排除所有幾何寄生」。","explanationEn":"Four-terminal structures reduce lead effects, but current spreading and geometry can still enter interface estimates. Compare R×area across contact sizes and check for a fixed series contribution. Therefore reject: Assuming four-terminal measurement removes every geometric parasitic."}},{"id":"a105-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-16"],"title":"空洞與偵測極限｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Voids and detection limits | mechanism and design","objective":"針對空洞與偵測極限，把「聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For voids and detection limits, turn \"Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「空洞與偵測極限」的模型：聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設總接點電阻 12 mΩ，四端量得銅體與走線為 7±1 mΩ，界面差值估計 5 mΩ；若總值不確定度為 1 mΩ 且獨立，差值標準不確定度為 √2≈1.41 mΩ。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for voids and detection limits: Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: Assume total resistance 12 mΩ and four-terminal body/trace contribution 7±1 mΩ. The inferred interface contribution is 5 mΩ; with independent 1 mΩ total uncertainty, its standard uncertainty is √2≈1.41 mΩ. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空洞與偵測極限的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for voids and detection limits, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-17-k1","title":"空洞與偵測極限：機制","titleEn":"Voids and detection limits: mechanism","text":"聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。","textEn":"Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。 必須排除的錯判：聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設總接點電阻 12 mΩ，四端量得銅體與走線為 7±1 mΩ，界面差值估計 5 mΩ；若總值不確定度為 1 mΩ 且獨立，差值標準不確定度為 √2≈1.41 mΩ。","textEn":"Assume total resistance 12 mΩ and four-terminal body/trace contribution 7±1 mΩ. The inferred interface contribution is 5 mΩ; with independent 1 mΩ total uncertainty, its standard uncertainty is √2≈1.41 mΩ."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空洞與偵測極限」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For voids and detection limits — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變","聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。","聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely","Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity.","Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。 對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。 因此不能採用「聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙」。","explanationEn":"Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity. Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. Therefore reject: Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps."}},{"id":"a105-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-17"],"title":"空洞與偵測極限｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Voids and detection limits | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對空洞與偵測極限，把「聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For voids and detection limits, turn \"Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。 將「聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設總接點電阻 12 mΩ，四端量得銅體與走線為 7±1 mΩ，界面差值估計 5 mΩ；若總值不確定度為 1 mΩ 且獨立，差值標準不確定度為 √2≈1.41 mΩ。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: Assume total resistance 12 mΩ and four-terminal body/trace contribution 7±1 mΩ. The inferred interface contribution is 5 mΩ; with independent 1 mΩ total uncertainty, its standard uncertainty is √2≈1.41 mΩ. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空洞與偵測極限的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for voids and detection limits: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-18-k1","title":"空洞與偵測極限：機制","titleEn":"Voids and detection limits: mechanism","text":"聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。","textEn":"Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。 必須排除的錯判：聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設總接點電阻 12 mΩ，四端量得銅體與走線為 7±1 mΩ，界面差值估計 5 mΩ；若總值不確定度為 1 mΩ 且獨立，差值標準不確定度為 √2≈1.41 mΩ。","textEn":"Assume total resistance 12 mΩ and four-terminal body/trace contribution 7±1 mΩ. The inferred interface contribution is 5 mΩ; with independent 1 mΩ total uncertainty, its standard uncertainty is √2≈1.41 mΩ."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空洞與偵測極限」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For voids and detection limits — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙","清潔完成後表面狀態會永久不變","對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。"],"optionsEn":["Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps","Assuming a prepared surface remains unchanged indefinitely","Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"聲學、截面與電性看到不同空洞尺度；沒有檢出只代表低於當次方法的靈敏度。 對照方法的解析度、掃描範圍與埋深，設計已知缺陷見證件。 因此不能採用「聲學無異常可排除奈米界面空隙」。","explanationEn":"Acoustic, cross-section and electrical methods respond to different void scales; nondetection is limited by sensitivity. Compare resolution, coverage and depth sensitivity using known-defect witnesses. Therefore reject: Using a clean acoustic image to exclude nanoscale interface gaps."}}]},{"id":"a105-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合與壽命","titleEn":"Integration and lifetime","description":"針對整合與壽命完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for integration and lifetime, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a105-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-18"],"title":"界面強度與能量｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interface strength and energy | mechanism and design","objective":"針對界面強度與能量，把「拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface strength and energy, turn \"Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「界面強度與能量」的模型：拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interface strength and energy: Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付界面強度與能量的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interface strength and energy, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-19-k1","title":"界面強度與能量：機制","titleEn":"Interface strength and energy: mechanism","text":"拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。","textEn":"Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。 必須排除的錯判：把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「界面強度與能量」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface strength and energy — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。","把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度","相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積"],"optionsEn":["Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information.","Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength","Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area"],"answer":0,"explanation":"拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。 標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。 因此不能採用「把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度」。","explanationEn":"Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information. Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. Therefore reject: Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength."}},{"id":"a105-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-19"],"title":"界面強度與能量｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interface strength and energy | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對界面強度與能量，把「拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface strength and energy, turn \"Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。 將「把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付界面強度與能量的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interface strength and energy: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-20-k1","title":"界面強度與能量：機制","titleEn":"Interface strength and energy: mechanism","text":"拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。","textEn":"Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。 必須排除的錯判：把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「界面強度與能量」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface strength and energy — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同 RMS 值代表相同真實接觸面積","標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。","把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal RMS roughness with equal real contact area","Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images.","Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength"],"answer":1,"explanation":"拉力或剪力峰值依試片幾何，界面斷裂能須考慮裂紋路徑與模式混合。 標記裂紋是否留在界面，報告載入方向、面積和破面影像。 因此不能採用「把不同試片的峰值力當成材料固有強度」。","explanationEn":"Peak tensile/shear loads depend on specimen geometry; fracture energy also requires crack-path and mode-mix information. Identify whether cracks stay at the interface and report direction, area and fracture images. Therefore reject: Treating peak forces from different specimens as intrinsic material strength."}},{"id":"a105-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-20"],"title":"熱循環與電流耦合｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal cycling and current coupling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱循環與電流耦合，把「熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal cycling and current coupling, turn \"Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱循環與電流耦合」的模型：熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal cycling and current coupling: Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱循環與電流耦合的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal cycling and current coupling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-21-k1","title":"熱循環與電流耦合：機制","titleEn":"Thermal cycling and current coupling: mechanism","text":"熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。","textEn":"Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。 必須排除的錯判：分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱循環與電流耦合」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal cycling and current coupling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合","全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷","熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes","Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small","Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。 先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。 因此不能採用「分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合」。","explanationEn":"Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled. Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. Therefore reject: Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes."}},{"id":"a105-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-21"],"title":"熱循環與電流耦合｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal cycling and current coupling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱循環與電流耦合，把「熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal cycling and current coupling, turn \"Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。 將「分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱循環與電流耦合的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal cycling and current coupling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-22-k1","title":"熱循環與電流耦合：機制","titleEn":"Thermal cycling and current coupling: mechanism","text":"熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。","textEn":"Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。 必須排除的錯判：分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱循環與電流耦合」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal cycling and current coupling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。","分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合","全片翹曲小即可不量局部銅凹陷"],"optionsEn":["Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order.","Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes","Ignoring local Cu recess when wafer warpage is small"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱失配可先降低有效面積，再由電流集中加劇發熱；機械與電性退化不是獨立事件。 先後量測冷態電阻、通電溫升與裂紋，保留試驗順序。 因此不能採用「分開通過機械和電性測試就可忽略耦合」。","explanationEn":"Thermal mismatch can reduce area before current crowding increases heating; mechanical and electrical degradation are coupled. Measure cold resistance, powered temperature rise and cracking while preserving test order. Therefore reject: Ignoring coupling after separate mechanical and electrical passes."}},{"id":"a105-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-22"],"title":"接合界面交接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interface qualification handoff | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接合界面交接，把「可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface qualification handoff, turn \"Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接合界面交接」的模型：可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interface qualification handoff: Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：設備流程完成即代表界面已合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating completed processing with a qualified interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合界面交接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interface qualification handoff, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-23-k1","title":"接合界面交接：機制","titleEn":"Interface qualification handoff: mechanism","text":"可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。","textEn":"Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。 必須排除的錯判：設備流程完成即代表界面已合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating completed processing with a qualified interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合界面交接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface qualification handoff — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊","可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。","設備流程完成即代表界面已合格"],"optionsEn":["Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment","Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle.","Equating completed processing with a qualified interface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。 建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。 因此不能採用「設備流程完成即代表界面已合格」。","explanationEn":"Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle. Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. Therefore reject: Equating completed processing with a qualified interface."}},{"id":"a105-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a105-v9-23"],"title":"接合界面交接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interface qualification handoff | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接合界面交接，把「可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface qualification handoff, turn \"Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。 將「設備流程完成即代表界面已合格」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating completed processing with a qualified interface\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：設備流程完成即代表界面已合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating completed processing with a qualified interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合界面交接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interface qualification handoff: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a105-v9-24-k1","title":"接合界面交接：機制","titleEn":"Interface qualification handoff: mechanism","text":"可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。","textEn":"Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a105-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。 必須排除的錯判：設備流程完成即代表界面已合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating completed processing with a qualified interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besipub","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合界面交接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface qualification handoff — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["設備流程完成即代表界面已合格","中心對位合格即可推論四角重疊","建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Equating completed processing with a qualified interface","Inferring corner overlap from a passing center alignment","Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可接受條件須同時包含面積覆蓋、阻值分布、強度及後續熱預算，不只設備顯示完成。 建立批次證據包並列出未覆蓋的面積或應力範圍。 因此不能採用「設備流程完成即代表界面已合格」。","explanationEn":"Acceptance combines coverage, resistance distribution, strength and downstream thermal budget, not a completed tool cycle. Assemble lot evidence and declare untested area or stress ranges. Therefore reject: Equating completed processing with a qualified interface."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-joining","subcategoryTitle":"凸塊與精密接合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bumps and precision bonding","photoId":"v9-quilt-solder"},{"id":"a107","title":"晶粒對晶圓混合接合","titleEn":"Die-to-wafer hybrid bonding","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w","v9-media-3363c0f741d8","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入已知良品、局部對位與混合介面。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore known-good die, local overlay and hybrid interfaces, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["晶粒輸入","表面準備","精密貼合","良率證據"],"labelsEn":["Die inputs","Surface preparation","Precision bonding","Yield evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a107-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"晶粒輸入","titleEn":"Die inputs","description":"針對晶粒輸入完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for die inputs, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a107-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"已知良品置信度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Known-good-die confidence | mechanism and design","objective":"針對已知良品置信度，把「測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good-die confidence, turn \"Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「已知良品置信度」的模型：測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for known-good-die confidence: Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：把前測通過當成永久良品。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating a pretest pass as permanently good. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付已知良品置信度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for known-good-die confidence, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-01-k1","title":"已知良品置信度：機制","titleEn":"Known-good-die confidence: mechanism","text":"測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。","textEn":"Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。 必須排除的錯判：把前測通過當成永久良品。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating a pretest pass as permanently good. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「已知良品置信度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good-die confidence — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。","把前測通過當成永久良品","所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加"],"optionsEn":["Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free.","Treating a pretest pass as permanently good","Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。 比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。 因此不能採用「把前測通過當成永久良品」。","explanationEn":"Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free. Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. Therefore reject: Treating a pretest pass as permanently good."}},{"id":"a107-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-01"],"title":"已知良品置信度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Known-good-die confidence | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對已知良品置信度，把「測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good-die confidence, turn \"Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。 將「把前測通過當成永久良品」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating a pretest pass as permanently good\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：把前測通過當成永久良品。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating a pretest pass as permanently good. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付已知良品置信度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for known-good-die confidence: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-02-k1","title":"已知良品置信度：機制","titleEn":"Known-good-die confidence: mechanism","text":"測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。","textEn":"Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。 必須排除的錯判：把前測通過當成永久良品。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating a pretest pass as permanently good. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「已知良品置信度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good-die confidence — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加","比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。","把前測通過當成永久良品"],"optionsEn":["Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation","Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data.","Treating a pretest pass as permanently good"],"answer":1,"explanation":"測試覆蓋率與逃逸率決定選片可信度，通過並非零缺陷。 比較前測、接合後測與失效定位。 因此不能採用「把前測通過當成永久良品」。","explanationEn":"Test coverage and escapes determine selection confidence; passing is not defect-free. Compare pre-bond, post-bond and localization data. Therefore reject: Treating a pretest pass as permanently good."}},{"id":"a107-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-02"],"title":"切割後表面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Post-singulation surfaces | mechanism and design","objective":"針對切割後表面，把「切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For post-singulation surfaces, turn \"Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「切割後表面」的模型：切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for post-singulation surfaces: Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare particle and void maps spatially. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare particle and void maps spatially. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付切割後表面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for post-singulation surfaces, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-03-k1","title":"切割後表面：機制","titleEn":"Post-singulation surfaces: mechanism","text":"切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。","textEn":"Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。 必須排除的錯判：顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare particle and void maps spatially. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「切割後表面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For post-singulation surfaces — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險","只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整","切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk","Inferring bond completeness from final position","Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。 對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。 因此不能採用「顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險」。","explanationEn":"Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately. Compare particle and void maps spatially. Therefore reject: Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk."}},{"id":"a107-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-03"],"title":"切割後表面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Post-singulation surfaces | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對切割後表面，把「切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For post-singulation surfaces, turn \"Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。 將「顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare particle and void maps spatially. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare particle and void maps spatially. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付切割後表面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for post-singulation surfaces: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-04-k1","title":"切割後表面：機制","titleEn":"Post-singulation surfaces: mechanism","text":"切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。","textEn":"Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。 必須排除的錯判：顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare particle and void maps spatially. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「切割後表面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For post-singulation surfaces — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。","顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險","只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整"],"optionsEn":["Compare particle and void maps spatially.","Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk","Inferring bond completeness from final position"],"answer":0,"explanation":"切割顆粒可成為接合空洞起點，晶粒邊緣與中心須分開採樣。 對照顆粒圖與空洞圖的空間相關。 因此不能採用「顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險」。","explanationEn":"Dicing particles can initiate voids; sample edges and centers separately. Compare particle and void maps spatially. Therefore reject: Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk."}},{"id":"a107-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-04"],"title":"活化與等待｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Activation and queue time | mechanism and design","objective":"針對活化與等待，把「表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For activation and queue time, turn \"Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「活化與等待」的模型：表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for activation and queue time: Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring storage with identical activation settings. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付活化與等待的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for activation and queue time, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-05-k1","title":"活化與等待：機制","titleEn":"Activation and queue time: mechanism","text":"表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。","textEn":"Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。 必須排除的錯判：活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring storage with identical activation settings. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「活化與等待」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For activation and queue time — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["開路只能由晶粒對位造成","表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。","活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every open to die misalignment","Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history.","Ignoring storage with identical activation settings"],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。 記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。 因此不能採用「活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境」。","explanationEn":"Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history. Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. Therefore reject: Ignoring storage with identical activation settings."}},{"id":"a107-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-05"],"title":"活化與等待｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Activation and queue time | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對活化與等待，把「表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For activation and queue time, turn \"Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。 將「活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring storage with identical activation settings\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring storage with identical activation settings. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付活化與等待的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for activation and queue time: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-06-k1","title":"活化與等待：機制","titleEn":"Activation and queue time: mechanism","text":"表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。","textEn":"Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。 必須排除的錯判：活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring storage with identical activation settings. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「活化與等待」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For activation and queue time — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境","開路只能由晶粒對位造成","記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring storage with identical activation settings","Attributing every open to die misalignment","Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面化學會隨保存環境演化，活化效果須連到實際等待歷程。 記錄活化到貼合時間及見證接合。 因此不能採用「活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境」。","explanationEn":"Surface chemistry evolves during storage; activation must be linked to queue history. Record activation-to-bond delay and witness results. Therefore reject: Ignoring storage with identical activation settings."}}]},{"id":"a107-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"表面準備","titleEn":"Surface preparation","description":"針對表面準備完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for surface preparation, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a107-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-06"],"title":"局部銅凹陷｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Local Cu recess | mechanism and design","objective":"針對局部銅凹陷，把「單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For local cu recess, turn \"Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「局部銅凹陷」的模型：單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for local cu recess: Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean height to rule out local noncontact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付局部銅凹陷的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for local cu recess, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-07-k1","title":"局部銅凹陷：機制","titleEn":"Local Cu recess: mechanism","text":"單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。","textEn":"Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。 必須排除的錯判：平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean height to rule out local noncontact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「局部銅凹陷」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For local cu recess — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。","平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸","銅接通就證明全部介電質接合"],"optionsEn":["Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails.","Using mean height to rule out local noncontact","Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding"],"answer":0,"explanation":"單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。 量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。 因此不能採用「平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸」。","explanationEn":"Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails. Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. Therefore reject: Using mean height to rule out local noncontact."}},{"id":"a107-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-07"],"title":"局部銅凹陷｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Local Cu recess | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對局部銅凹陷，把「單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For local cu recess, turn \"Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。 將「平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using mean height to rule out local noncontact\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean height to rule out local noncontact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付局部銅凹陷的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for local cu recess: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-08-k1","title":"局部銅凹陷：機制","titleEn":"Local Cu recess: mechanism","text":"單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。","textEn":"Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。 必須排除的錯判：平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean height to rule out local noncontact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「局部銅凹陷」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For local cu recess — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["銅接通就證明全部介電質接合","量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。","平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸"],"optionsEn":["Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding","Measure pad-relative height at center and corners.","Using mean height to rule out local noncontact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"單顆晶粒的焊墊高度分布影響接觸，晶圓平均不能替代逐顆尾端風險。 量中心和四角焊墊的相對高度。 因此不能採用「平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸」。","explanationEn":"Per-die pad-height distribution controls contact; wafer means hide die-level tails. Measure pad-relative height at center and corners. Therefore reject: Using mean height to rule out local noncontact."}},{"id":"a107-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-08"],"title":"翻面與座標｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Flip and coordinates | mechanism and design","objective":"針對翻面與座標，把「翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For flip and coordinates, turn \"Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「翻面與座標」的模型：翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for flip and coordinates: Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付翻面與座標的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for flip and coordinates, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-09-k1","title":"翻面與座標：機制","titleEn":"Flip and coordinates: mechanism","text":"翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。","textEn":"Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。 必須排除的錯判：翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「翻面與座標」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For flip and coordinates — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度","接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換","翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation","Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable","Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。 模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。 因此不能採用「翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度」。","explanationEn":"Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks. Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. Therefore reject: Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation."}},{"id":"a107-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-09"],"title":"翻面與座標｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Flip and coordinates | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對翻面與座標，把「翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For flip and coordinates, turn \"Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。 將「翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付翻面與座標的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for flip and coordinates: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-10-k1","title":"翻面與座標：機制","titleEn":"Flip and coordinates: mechanism","text":"翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。","textEn":"Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。 必須排除的錯判：翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「翻面與座標」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For flip and coordinates — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。","翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度","接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換"],"optionsEn":["Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly.","Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation","Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"翻面改變座標手性，旋轉補償須以非對稱標記驗證。 模擬一個非對稱 pad 圖的翻轉。 因此不能採用「翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度」。","explanationEn":"Flipping changes handedness; validate rotation using asymmetric marks. Transform an asymmetric pad map explicitly. Therefore reject: Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation."}},{"id":"a107-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-10"],"title":"誤差分解｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Overlay decomposition | mechanism and design","objective":"針對誤差分解，把「拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overlay decomposition, turn \"Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「誤差分解」的模型：拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for overlay decomposition: Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付誤差分解的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for overlay decomposition, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-11-k1","title":"誤差分解：機制","titleEn":"Overlay decomposition: mechanism","text":"拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。","textEn":"Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。 必須排除的錯判：所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. Misinterpretation to reject: Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「誤差分解」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overlay decomposition — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率","拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。","所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加"],"optionsEn":["Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield","Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors.","Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。 作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。 因此不能採用「所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加」。","explanationEn":"Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors. Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. Therefore reject: Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation."}},{"id":"a107-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-11"],"title":"誤差分解｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Overlay decomposition | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對誤差分解，把「拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overlay decomposition, turn \"Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。 將「所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. Challenge the hypothesis \"Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付誤差分解的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for overlay decomposition: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-12-k1","title":"誤差分解：機制","titleEn":"Overlay decomposition: mechanism","text":"拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。","textEn":"Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。 必須排除的錯判：所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. Misinterpretation to reject: Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「誤差分解」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overlay decomposition — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加","晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率","作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。"],"optionsEn":["Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation","Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield","Use repeat placements and time-series control charts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"拾取、相機、平台與熱漂移的誤差須分解系統項和隨機項。 作重複放置和時間序列控制圖。 因此不能採用「所有誤差都可用 RSS 相加」。","explanationEn":"Separate systematic and random pickup, camera, stage and thermal errors. Use repeat placements and time-series control charts. Therefore reject: Combining all errors by RSS regardless of correlation."}}]},{"id":"a107-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"精密貼合","titleEn":"Precision bonding","description":"針對精密貼合完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for precision bonding, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a107-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-12"],"title":"接合波與局部接觸｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Bond-wave contact | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接合波與局部接觸，把「接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bond-wave contact, turn \"Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接合波與局部接觸」的模型：接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for bond-wave contact: Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring bond completeness from final position. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合波與局部接觸的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for bond-wave contact, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-13-k1","title":"接合波與局部接觸：機制","titleEn":"Bond-wave contact: mechanism","text":"接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。","textEn":"Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。 必須排除的錯判：只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring bond completeness from final position. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合波與局部接觸」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bond-wave contact — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。","只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整","初始良率即可代表產品壽命"],"optionsEn":["Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact.","Inferring bond completeness from final position","Treating initial yield as product lifetime"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。 比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。 因此不能採用「只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整」。","explanationEn":"Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact. Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. Therefore reject: Inferring bond completeness from final position."}},{"id":"a107-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-13"],"title":"接合波與局部接觸｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Bond-wave contact | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接合波與局部接觸，把「接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bond-wave contact, turn \"Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。 將「只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring bond completeness from final position\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring bond completeness from final position. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合波與局部接觸的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for bond-wave contact: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-14-k1","title":"接合波與局部接觸：機制","titleEn":"Bond-wave contact: mechanism","text":"接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。","textEn":"Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。 必須排除的錯判：只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring bond completeness from final position. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合波與局部接觸」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bond-wave contact — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["初始良率即可代表產品壽命","比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。","只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整"],"optionsEn":["Treating initial yield as product lifetime","Compare void shapes with contact initiation points.","Inferring bond completeness from final position"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸從局部展開時會受翹曲與顆粒阻擋，表面潔淨度和力學不可分開。 比較空洞形狀與接觸起點。 因此不能採用「只看最終位置即可判斷接合完整」。","explanationEn":"Propagating contact is obstructed by warp and particles; cleanliness and mechanics interact. Compare void shapes with contact initiation points. Therefore reject: Inferring bond completeness from final position."}},{"id":"a107-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-14"],"title":"銅接點電性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cu-joint electrical behavior | mechanism and design","objective":"針對銅接點電性，把「電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cu-joint electrical behavior, turn \"Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「銅接點電性」的模型：電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cu-joint electrical behavior: Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：開路只能由晶粒對位造成。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing every open to die misalignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅接點電性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cu-joint electrical behavior, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-15-k1","title":"銅接點電性：機制","titleEn":"Cu-joint electrical behavior: mechanism","text":"電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。","textEn":"Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。 必須排除的錯判：開路只能由晶粒對位造成。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing every open to die misalignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅接點電性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cu-joint electrical behavior — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["開路只能由晶粒對位造成","把前測通過當成永久良品","電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every open to die misalignment","Treating a pretest pass as permanently good","Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。 把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。 因此不能採用「開路只能由晶粒對位造成」。","explanationEn":"Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps. Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. Therefore reject: Attributing every open to die misalignment."}},{"id":"a107-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-15"],"title":"銅接點電性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cu-joint electrical behavior | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對銅接點電性，把「電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cu-joint electrical behavior, turn \"Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。 將「開路只能由晶粒對位造成」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. Challenge the hypothesis \"Attributing every open to die misalignment\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：開路只能由晶粒對位造成。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing every open to die misalignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付銅接點電性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cu-joint electrical behavior: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-16-k1","title":"銅接點電性：機制","titleEn":"Cu-joint electrical behavior: mechanism","text":"電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。","textEn":"Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。 必須排除的錯判：開路只能由晶粒對位造成。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing every open to die misalignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「銅接點電性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cu-joint electrical behavior — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。","開路只能由晶粒對位造成","把前測通過當成永久良品"],"optionsEn":["Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites.","Attributing every open to die misalignment","Treating a pretest pass as permanently good"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電性開路可能來自錯位、空洞或銅接觸不足，須對應局部圖。 把 Kelvin 點、菊鍊與影像對位。 因此不能採用「開路只能由晶粒對位造成」。","explanationEn":"Opens may reflect overlay, voids or insufficient Cu contact; correlate local maps. Register Kelvin, chain and imaging sites. Therefore reject: Attributing every open to die misalignment."}},{"id":"a107-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-16"],"title":"介電質界面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Dielectric interface | mechanism and design","objective":"針對介電質界面，把「介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For dielectric interface, turn \"Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「介電質界面」的模型：介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設 20 顆晶粒各自良率 0.99 且獨立，全數良好機率 0.99²⁰≈0.818。若每顆選片後為 0.999，則≈0.980；這只算晶粒，不含接合相關缺陷。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for dielectric interface: Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For 20 independent dies at 0.99 yield, all-good probability is 0.99²⁰≈0.818; at 0.999 after selection it is≈0.980. Bonding and correlated defects are excluded. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：銅接通就證明全部介電質接合。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付介電質界面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for dielectric interface, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-17-k1","title":"介電質界面：機制","titleEn":"Dielectric interface: mechanism","text":"介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。","textEn":"Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。 必須排除的錯判：銅接通就證明全部介電質接合。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. Misinterpretation to reject: Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設 20 顆晶粒各自良率 0.99 且獨立，全數良好機率 0.99²⁰≈0.818。若每顆選片後為 0.999，則≈0.980；這只算晶粒，不含接合相關缺陷。","textEn":"For 20 independent dies at 0.99 yield, all-good probability is 0.99²⁰≈0.818; at 0.999 after selection it is≈0.980. Bonding and correlated defects are excluded."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「介電質界面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For dielectric interface — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險","介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。","銅接通就證明全部介電質接合"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk","Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions.","Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding"],"answer":1,"explanation":"介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。 對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。 因此不能採用「銅接通就證明全部介電質接合」。","explanationEn":"Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions. Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. Therefore reject: Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding."}},{"id":"a107-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-17"],"title":"介電質界面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Dielectric interface | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對介電質界面，把「介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For dielectric interface, turn \"Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。 將「銅接通就證明全部介電質接合」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設 20 顆晶粒各自良率 0.99 且獨立，全數良好機率 0.99²⁰≈0.818。若每顆選片後為 0.999，則≈0.980；這只算晶粒，不含接合相關缺陷。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For 20 independent dies at 0.99 yield, all-good probability is 0.99²⁰≈0.818; at 0.999 after selection it is≈0.980. Bonding and correlated defects are excluded. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：銅接通就證明全部介電質接合。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付介電質界面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for dielectric interface: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-18-k1","title":"介電質界面：機制","titleEn":"Dielectric interface: mechanism","text":"介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。","textEn":"Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。 必須排除的錯判：銅接通就證明全部介電質接合。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. Misinterpretation to reject: Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設 20 顆晶粒各自良率 0.99 且獨立，全數良好機率 0.99²⁰≈0.818。若每顆選片後為 0.999，則≈0.980；這只算晶粒，不含接合相關缺陷。","textEn":"For 20 independent dies at 0.99 yield, all-good probability is 0.99²⁰≈0.818; at 0.999 after selection it is≈0.980. Bonding and correlated defects are excluded."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「介電質界面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For dielectric interface — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["銅接通就證明全部介電質接合","顆粒總數相同就有相同接合風險","對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。"],"optionsEn":["Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding","Equating equal particle counts with equal bonding risk","Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電質接合提供支撐，銅電性合格仍可能存在未接合區。 對照聲學、裂紋與電性採樣。 因此不能採用「銅接通就證明全部介電質接合」。","explanationEn":"Dielectric bonding supports the stack; passing Cu conductivity may coexist with unbonded regions. Compare acoustic, crack and electrical sampling. Therefore reject: Using Cu continuity to prove complete dielectric bonding."}}]},{"id":"a107-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"良率證據","titleEn":"Yield evidence","description":"針對良率證據完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for yield evidence, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a107-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-18"],"title":"修補與不可逆點｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Rework and irreversible points | mechanism and design","objective":"針對修補與不可逆點，把「選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rework and irreversible points, turn \"Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「修補與不可逆點」的模型：選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for rework and irreversible points: Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付修補與不可逆點的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for rework and irreversible points, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-19-k1","title":"修補與不可逆點：機制","titleEn":"Rework and irreversible points: mechanism","text":"選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。","textEn":"Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。 必須排除的錯判：接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「修補與不可逆點」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rework and irreversible points — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。","接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換","活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境"],"optionsEn":["Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first.","Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable","Ignoring storage with identical activation settings"],"answer":0,"explanation":"選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。 畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。 因此不能採用「接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換」。","explanationEn":"Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first. Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. Therefore reject: Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable."}},{"id":"a107-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-19"],"title":"修補與不可逆點｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Rework and irreversible points | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對修補與不可逆點，把「選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rework and irreversible points, turn \"Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。 將「接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付修補與不可逆點的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for rework and irreversible points: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-20-k1","title":"修補與不可逆點：機制","titleEn":"Rework and irreversible points: mechanism","text":"選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。","textEn":"Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。 必須排除的錯判：接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「修補與不可逆點」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rework and irreversible points — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["活化條件相同即可忽略保存環境","畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。","接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring storage with identical activation settings","Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes.","Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable"],"answer":1,"explanation":"選片改善來料良率，但已成形界面可能難以修補，需先定義保留點。 畫出可重測、可更換與不可逆節點。 因此不能採用「接合後任意晶粒都可無損更換」。","explanationEn":"Selection improves input yield, but formed interfaces may be hard to rework; define hold points first. Map retest, replacement and irreversible nodes. Therefore reject: Assuming every bonded die is nondestructively replaceable."}},{"id":"a107-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-20"],"title":"堆疊良率模型｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Stack-yield model | mechanism and design","objective":"針對堆疊良率模型，把「獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stack-yield model, turn \"Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「堆疊良率模型」的模型：獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for stack-yield model: Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付堆疊良率模型的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for stack-yield model, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-21-k1","title":"堆疊良率模型：機制","titleEn":"Stack-yield model: mechanism","text":"獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。","textEn":"Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。 必須排除的錯判：晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堆疊良率模型」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stack-yield model — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率","平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸","獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。"],"optionsEn":["Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield","Using mean height to rule out local noncontact","Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。 比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。 因此不能採用「晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率」。","explanationEn":"Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation. Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. Therefore reject: Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield."}},{"id":"a107-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-21"],"title":"堆疊良率模型｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Stack-yield model | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對堆疊良率模型，把「獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stack-yield model, turn \"Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。 將「晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付堆疊良率模型的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for stack-yield model: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-22-k1","title":"堆疊良率模型：機制","titleEn":"Stack-yield model: mechanism","text":"獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。","textEn":"Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。 必須排除的錯判：晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「堆疊良率模型」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stack-yield model — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。","晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率","平均高度合格即排除局部未接觸"],"optionsEn":["Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures.","Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield","Using mean height to rule out local noncontact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"獨立乘法模型是起點，共因顆粒或翹曲會使缺陷相關。 比較獨立預測與晶圓群聚失效。 因此不能採用「晶粒良率乘積必精確等於組裝良率」。","explanationEn":"Independent yield multiplication is a starting model; particles and warp introduce correlation. Compare independent predictions with clustered wafer failures. Therefore reject: Equating the die-yield product with exact assembly yield."}},{"id":"a107-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-22"],"title":"熱與資料交接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal and data handoff | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱與資料交接，把「後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal and data handoff, turn \"Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱與資料交接」的模型：後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal and data handoff: Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始良率即可代表產品壽命。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating initial yield as product lifetime. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱與資料交接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal and data handoff, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-23-k1","title":"熱與資料交接：機制","titleEn":"Thermal and data handoff: mechanism","text":"後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。","textEn":"Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。 必須排除的錯判：初始良率即可代表產品壽命。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating initial yield as product lifetime. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱與資料交接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal and data handoff — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度","後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。","初始良率即可代表產品壽命"],"optionsEn":["Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation","Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history.","Treating initial yield as product lifetime"],"answer":1,"explanation":"後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。 提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。 因此不能採用「初始良率即可代表產品壽命」。","explanationEn":"Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history. Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. Therefore reject: Treating initial yield as product lifetime."}},{"id":"a107-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"],"prerequisiteIds":["a107-v9-23"],"title":"熱與資料交接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal and data handoff | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱與資料交接，把「後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal and data handoff, turn \"Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。 將「初始良率即可代表產品壽命」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating initial yield as product lifetime\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始良率即可代表產品壽命。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating initial yield as product lifetime. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱與資料交接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal and data handoff: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a107-v9-24-k1","title":"熱與資料交接：機制","titleEn":"Thermal and data handoff: mechanism","text":"後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。","textEn":"Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]},{"id":"a107-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。 必須排除的錯判：初始良率即可代表產品壽命。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating initial yield as product lifetime. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-imecd2w"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱與資料交接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal and data handoff — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["初始良率即可代表產品壽命","翻面等同平面旋轉 180 度","提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Treating initial yield as product lifetime","Equating a flip with a 180-degree planar rotation","Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges."],"answer":2,"explanation":"後續熱循環可改變應力和電阻，需保留逐顆幾何及材料履歷。 提交前後測配對資料及未驗證熱範圍。 因此不能採用「初始良率即可代表產品壽命」。","explanationEn":"Later thermal cycles alter stress and resistance; retain per-die geometry and material history. Submit paired tests and unverified thermal ranges. Therefore reject: Treating initial yield as product lifetime."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-joining","subcategoryTitle":"凸塊與精密接合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bumps and precision bonding","photoId":"v9-quilt-3d"},{"id":"a108","title":"晶粒對晶粒堆疊","titleEn":"Die-to-die stacking","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub","v9-media-76504c18d14b","v9-media-3363c0f741d8","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入堆疊拓撲、累積誤差與可測性。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore stack topology, accumulated error and testability, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["堆疊定義","層間組裝","跨層驗證","熱與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Stack definition","Interlayer assembly","Cross-layer verification","Thermal and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a108-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"堆疊定義","titleEn":"Stack definition","description":"針對堆疊定義完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for stack definition, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a108-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"面向與拓撲｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Orientation and topology | mechanism and design","objective":"針對面向與拓撲，把「面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For orientation and topology, turn \"Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「面向與拓撲」的模型：面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫每層訊號、電源和背面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for orientation and topology: Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫每層訊號、電源和背面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Reusing one net map for every orientation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付面向與拓撲的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for orientation and topology, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-01-k1","title":"面向與拓撲：機制","titleEn":"Orientation and topology: mechanism","text":"面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。","textEn":"Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫每層訊號、電源和背面。 必須排除的錯判：所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. Misinterpretation to reject: Reusing one net map for every orientation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「面向與拓撲」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For orientation and topology — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。","所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖","每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移"],"optionsEn":["Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads.","Reusing one net map for every orientation","Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small"],"answer":0,"explanation":"面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。 畫每層訊號、電源和背面。 因此不能採用「所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖」。","explanationEn":"Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads. Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. Therefore reject: Reusing one net map for every orientation."}},{"id":"a108-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-01"],"title":"面向與拓撲｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Orientation and topology | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對面向與拓撲，把「面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For orientation and topology, turn \"Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫每層訊號、電源和背面。 將「所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. Challenge the hypothesis \"Reusing one net map for every orientation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫每層訊號、電源和背面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Reusing one net map for every orientation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付面向與拓撲的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for orientation and topology: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-02-k1","title":"面向與拓撲：機制","titleEn":"Orientation and topology: mechanism","text":"面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。","textEn":"Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫每層訊號、電源和背面。 必須排除的錯判：所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. Misinterpretation to reject: Reusing one net map for every orientation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「面向與拓撲」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For orientation and topology — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移","畫每層訊號、電源和背面。","所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small","Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer.","Reusing one net map for every orientation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"面對面與背對面堆疊改變 TSV 需求和可用電極。 畫每層訊號、電源和背面。 因此不能採用「所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖」。","explanationEn":"Face-to-face versus back-to-face changes TSV needs and accessible pads. Draw signals, supplies and backsides for every layer. Therefore reject: Reusing one net map for every orientation."}},{"id":"a108-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-02"],"title":"層間接口契約｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interlayer interface contract | mechanism and design","objective":"針對層間接口契約，把「尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interlayer interface contract, turn \"Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「層間接口契約」的模型：尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interlayer interface contract: Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Create an interface table agreed by both layers. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Create an interface table agreed by both layers. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：幾何能接合即表示電路相容。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層間接口契約的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interlayer interface contract, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-03-k1","title":"層間接口契約：機制","titleEn":"Interlayer interface contract: mechanism","text":"尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。","textEn":"Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。 必須排除的錯判：幾何能接合即表示電路相容。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Create an interface table agreed by both layers. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層間接口契約」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interlayer interface contract — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["幾何能接合即表示電路相容","最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面","尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。"],"optionsEn":["Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility","Using top-layer images for every buried interface","Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。 列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。 因此不能採用「幾何能接合即表示電路相容」。","explanationEn":"Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible. Create an interface table agreed by both layers. Therefore reject: Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility."}},{"id":"a108-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-03"],"title":"層間接口契約｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interlayer interface contract | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對層間接口契約，把「尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interlayer interface contract, turn \"Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。 將「幾何能接合即表示電路相容」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Create an interface table agreed by both layers. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Create an interface table agreed by both layers. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：幾何能接合即表示電路相容。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層間接口契約的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interlayer interface contract: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-04-k1","title":"層間接口契約：機制","titleEn":"Interlayer interface contract: mechanism","text":"尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。","textEn":"Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。 必須排除的錯判：幾何能接合即表示電路相容。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Create an interface table agreed by both layers. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層間接口契約」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interlayer interface contract — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。","幾何能接合即表示電路相容","最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面"],"optionsEn":["Create an interface table agreed by both layers.","Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility","Using top-layer images for every buried interface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"尺寸、電壓、時序和熱負荷須同時相容。 列上下層雙方簽認的接口表。 因此不能採用「幾何能接合即表示電路相容」。","explanationEn":"Dimensions, voltage, timing and thermal load must all be compatible. Create an interface table agreed by both layers. Therefore reject: Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility."}},{"id":"a108-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-04"],"title":"厚度堆積｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thickness accumulation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對厚度堆積，把「隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thickness accumulation, turn \"Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「厚度堆積」的模型：隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thickness accumulation: Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：全部厚度公差都可平方和開根。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付厚度堆積的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thickness accumulation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-05-k1","title":"厚度堆積：機制","titleEn":"Thickness accumulation: mechanism","text":"隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。","textEn":"Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。 必須排除的錯判：全部厚度公差都可平方和開根。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. Misinterpretation to reject: Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「厚度堆積」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thickness accumulation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流","隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。","全部厚度公差都可平方和開根"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents","Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently.","Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。 區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。 因此不能採用「全部厚度公差都可平方和開根」。","explanationEn":"Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently. Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. Therefore reject: Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance."}},{"id":"a108-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-05"],"title":"厚度堆積｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thickness accumulation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對厚度堆積，把「隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thickness accumulation, turn \"Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。 將「全部厚度公差都可平方和開根」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：全部厚度公差都可平方和開根。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付厚度堆積的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thickness accumulation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-06-k1","title":"厚度堆積：機制","titleEn":"Thickness accumulation: mechanism","text":"隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。","textEn":"Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。 必須排除的錯判：全部厚度公差都可平方和開根。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. Misinterpretation to reject: Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「厚度堆積」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thickness accumulation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["全部厚度公差都可平方和開根","所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流","區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。"],"optionsEn":["Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance","Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents","Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隨機與系統厚度誤差累積方式不同。 區分同機台偏差與逐片變異。 因此不能採用「全部厚度公差都可平方和開根」。","explanationEn":"Random and systematic thickness errors accumulate differently. Separate tool bias from wafer-to-wafer variation. Therefore reject: Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance."}}]},{"id":"a108-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"層間組裝","titleEn":"Interlayer assembly","description":"針對層間組裝完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for interlayer assembly, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a108-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-06"],"title":"已知良品序列｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Known-good-die sequence | mechanism and design","objective":"針對已知良品序列，把「昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good-die sequence, turn \"Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「已知良品序列」的模型：昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for known-good-die sequence: Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最終測試即可取代全部中間測試。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Replacing every intermediate test with final testing. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付已知良品序列的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for known-good-die sequence, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-07-k1","title":"已知良品序列：機制","titleEn":"Known-good-die sequence: mechanism","text":"昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。","textEn":"Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。 必須排除的錯判：最終測試即可取代全部中間測試。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. Misinterpretation to reject: Replacing every intermediate test with final testing. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「已知良品序列」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good-die sequence — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。","最終測試即可取代全部中間測試","邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常"],"optionsEn":["Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work.","Replacing every intermediate test with final testing","Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality"],"answer":0,"explanation":"昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。 計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。 因此不能採用「最終測試即可取代全部中間測試」。","explanationEn":"Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work. Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. Therefore reject: Replacing every intermediate test with final testing."}},{"id":"a108-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-07"],"title":"已知良品序列｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Known-good-die sequence | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對已知良品序列，把「昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good-die sequence, turn \"Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。 將「最終測試即可取代全部中間測試」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. Challenge the hypothesis \"Replacing every intermediate test with final testing\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最終測試即可取代全部中間測試。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Replacing every intermediate test with final testing. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付已知良品序列的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for known-good-die sequence: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-08-k1","title":"已知良品序列：機制","titleEn":"Known-good-die sequence: mechanism","text":"昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。","textEn":"Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。 必須排除的錯判：最終測試即可取代全部中間測試。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. Misinterpretation to reject: Replacing every intermediate test with final testing. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「已知良品序列」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good-die sequence — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常","計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。","最終測試即可取代全部中間測試"],"optionsEn":["Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality","Compare hold-point cost and escape risk.","Replacing every intermediate test with final testing"],"answer":1,"explanation":"昂貴上層疊入前的測試可以避免浪費後續工序。 計算各保留點的成本與逃逸風險。 因此不能採用「最終測試即可取代全部中間測試」。","explanationEn":"Testing before adding costly layers avoids wasted downstream work. Compare hold-point cost and escape risk. Therefore reject: Replacing every intermediate test with final testing."}},{"id":"a108-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-08"],"title":"拾取支撐｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pickup support | mechanism and design","objective":"針對拾取支撐，把「薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pickup support, turn \"Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「拾取支撐」的模型：薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pickup support: Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare center support and overhanging edges. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare center support and overhanging edges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating average suction with equal bending risk. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付拾取支撐的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pickup support, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-09-k1","title":"拾取支撐：機制","titleEn":"Pickup support: mechanism","text":"薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。","textEn":"Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。 必須排除的錯判：平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare center support and overhanging edges. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating average suction with equal bending risk. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「拾取支撐」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pickup support — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險","總功耗相同便有相同最高溫","薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Equating average suction with equal bending risk","Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature","Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。 比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。 因此不能採用「平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險」。","explanationEn":"Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths. Compare center support and overhanging edges. Therefore reject: Equating average suction with equal bending risk."}},{"id":"a108-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-09"],"title":"拾取支撐｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pickup support | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對拾取支撐，把「薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pickup support, turn \"Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。 將「平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare center support and overhanging edges. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating average suction with equal bending risk\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare center support and overhanging edges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating average suction with equal bending risk. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付拾取支撐的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pickup support: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-10-k1","title":"拾取支撐：機制","titleEn":"Pickup support: mechanism","text":"薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。","textEn":"Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。 必須排除的錯判：平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare center support and overhanging edges. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating average suction with equal bending risk. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「拾取支撐」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pickup support — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。","平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險","總功耗相同便有相同最高溫"],"optionsEn":["Compare center support and overhanging edges.","Equating average suction with equal bending risk","Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature"],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄晶粒的彎曲和表面損傷取決於吸附與頂針受力路徑。 比較中心支撐與邊缘懸空的示意。 因此不能採用「平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險」。","explanationEn":"Thin-die bending and damage depend on suction/ejector load paths. Compare center support and overhanging edges. Therefore reject: Equating average suction with equal bending risk."}},{"id":"a108-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-10"],"title":"逐層對位｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Layer-by-layer overlay | mechanism and design","objective":"針對逐層對位，把「相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For layer-by-layer overlay, turn \"Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「逐層對位」的模型：相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for layer-by-layer overlay: Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付逐層對位的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for layer-by-layer overlay, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-11-k1","title":"逐層對位：機制","titleEn":"Layer-by-layer overlay: mechanism","text":"相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。","textEn":"Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。 必須排除的錯判：每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「逐層對位」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For layer-by-layer overlay — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力","相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。","每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress","Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum.","Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small"],"answer":1,"explanation":"相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。 同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。 因此不能採用「每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移」。","explanationEn":"Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum. Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. Therefore reject: Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small."}},{"id":"a108-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-11"],"title":"逐層對位｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Layer-by-layer overlay | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對逐層對位，把「相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For layer-by-layer overlay, turn \"Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。 將「每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付逐層對位的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for layer-by-layer overlay: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-12-k1","title":"逐層對位：機制","titleEn":"Layer-by-layer overlay: mechanism","text":"相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。","textEn":"Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。 必須排除的錯判：每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「逐層對位」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For layer-by-layer overlay — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移","加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力","同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small","Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress","Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相對每層對準不保證對共同基準的累積誤差小。 同時繪相鄰誤差與全堆疊基準誤差。 因此不能採用「每層偏移小就不用量整體漂移」。","explanationEn":"Good adjacent-layer overlay need not ensure small error to a common datum. Plot adjacent-layer and common-datum errors. Therefore reject: Ignoring global drift when individual shifts are small."}}]},{"id":"a108-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"跨層驗證","titleEn":"Cross-layer verification","description":"針對跨層驗證完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for cross-layer verification, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a108-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-12"],"title":"接合界面抽樣｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interface sampling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接合界面抽樣，把「埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface sampling, turn \"Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接合界面抽樣」的模型：埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「列每一界面的可測量與盲區。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interface sampling: Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"列每一界面的可測量與盲區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using top-layer images for every buried interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合界面抽樣的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interface sampling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-13-k1","title":"接合界面抽樣：機制","titleEn":"Interface sampling: mechanism","text":"埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。","textEn":"Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列每一界面的可測量與盲區。 必須排除的錯判：最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. Misinterpretation to reject: Using top-layer images for every buried interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合界面抽樣」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface sampling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。","最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面","先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效"],"optionsEn":["Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures.","Using top-layer images for every buried interface","Grinding first before electrical localization"],"answer":0,"explanation":"埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。 列每一界面的可測量與盲區。 因此不能採用「最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面」。","explanationEn":"Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures. List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. Therefore reject: Using top-layer images for every buried interface."}},{"id":"a108-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-13"],"title":"接合界面抽樣｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interface sampling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接合界面抽樣，把「埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface sampling, turn \"Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：列每一界面的可測量與盲區。 將「最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using top-layer images for every buried interface\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"列每一界面的可測量與盲區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using top-layer images for every buried interface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接合界面抽樣的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interface sampling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-14-k1","title":"接合界面抽樣：機制","titleEn":"Interface sampling: mechanism","text":"埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。","textEn":"Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列每一界面的可測量與盲區。 必須排除的錯判：最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. Misinterpretation to reject: Using top-layer images for every buried interface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接合界面抽樣」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface sampling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效","列每一界面的可測量與盲區。","最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面"],"optionsEn":["Grinding first before electrical localization","List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface.","Using top-layer images for every buried interface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"埋藏層的取樣可接近性隨堆疊改變，須預留見證結構。 列每一界面的可測量與盲區。 因此不能採用「最上層影像可代表所有埋藏界面」。","explanationEn":"Buried-interface access changes during stacking; reserve witness structures. List measurable quantities and blind spots per interface. Therefore reject: Using top-layer images for every buried interface."}},{"id":"a108-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-14"],"title":"跨層供電｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Vertical power delivery | mechanism and design","objective":"針對跨層供電，把「多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For vertical power delivery, turn \"Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「跨層供電」的模型：多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for vertical power delivery: Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付跨層供電的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for vertical power delivery, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-15-k1","title":"跨層供電：機制","titleEn":"Vertical power delivery: mechanism","text":"多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。","textEn":"Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。 必須排除的錯判：所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨層供電」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For vertical power delivery — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流","所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖","多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents","Reusing one net map for every orientation","Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。 依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。 因此不能採用「所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流」。","explanationEn":"Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading. Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. Therefore reject: Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents."}},{"id":"a108-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-15"],"title":"跨層供電｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Vertical power delivery | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對跨層供電，把「多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For vertical power delivery, turn \"Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。 將「所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付跨層供電的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for vertical power delivery: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-16-k1","title":"跨層供電：機制","titleEn":"Vertical power delivery: mechanism","text":"多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。","textEn":"Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。 必須排除的錯判：所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨層供電」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For vertical power delivery — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。","所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流","所有堆疊方向可共用同一接線圖"],"optionsEn":["Draw a vertical current tree from layer power.","Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents","Reusing one net map for every orientation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多層電流匯流造成不同 TSV 和接點電流負載。 依每層功耗畫垂直電流樹。 因此不能採用「所有層用電相同即各 TSV 同電流」。","explanationEn":"Summed layer currents impose unequal TSV and joint loading. Draw a vertical current tree from layer power. Therefore reject: Assuming equal layer power gives equal TSV currents."}},{"id":"a108-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-16"],"title":"測試存取｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Test access | mechanism and design","objective":"針對測試存取，把「埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For test access, turn \"Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「測試存取」的模型：埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設 8 層厚度各 50±1 μm，獨立標準差的總厚不確定度 √8≈2.83 μm；若每層有同向 1 μm 系統偏差，總偏差為 8 μm，不能用 RSS 消除。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for test access: Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: Eight illustrative 50±1 μm layers give √8≈2.83 μm total standard uncertainty if independent. A same-sign 1 μm systematic bias per layer instead adds to 8 μm. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付測試存取的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for test access, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-17-k1","title":"測試存取：機制","titleEn":"Test access: mechanism","text":"埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。","textEn":"Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。 必須排除的錯判：邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設 8 層厚度各 50±1 μm，獨立標準差的總厚不確定度 √8≈2.83 μm；若每層有同向 1 μm 系統偏差，總偏差為 8 μm，不能用 RSS 消除。","textEn":"Eight illustrative 50±1 μm layers give √8≈2.83 μm total standard uncertainty if independent. A same-sign 1 μm systematic bias per layer instead adds to 8 μm."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試存取」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For test access — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["幾何能接合即表示電路相容","埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。","邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常"],"optionsEn":["Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility","Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality.","Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality"],"answer":1,"explanation":"埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。 比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。 因此不能採用「邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常」。","explanationEn":"Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality. Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. Therefore reject: Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality."}},{"id":"a108-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-17"],"title":"測試存取｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Test access | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對測試存取，把「埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For test access, turn \"Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。 將「邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設 8 層厚度各 50±1 μm，獨立標準差的總厚不確定度 √8≈2.83 μm；若每層有同向 1 μm 系統偏差，總偏差為 8 μm，不能用 RSS 消除。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: Eight illustrative 50±1 μm layers give √8≈2.83 μm total standard uncertainty if independent. A same-sign 1 μm systematic bias per layer instead adds to 8 μm. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付測試存取的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for test access: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-18-k1","title":"測試存取：機制","titleEn":"Test access: mechanism","text":"埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。","textEn":"Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。 必須排除的錯判：邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設 8 層厚度各 50±1 μm，獨立標準差的總厚不確定度 √8≈2.83 μm；若每層有同向 1 μm 系統偏差，總偏差為 8 μm，不能用 RSS 消除。","textEn":"Eight illustrative 50±1 μm layers give √8≈2.83 μm total standard uncertainty if independent. A same-sign 1 μm systematic bias per layer instead adds to 8 μm."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試存取」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For test access — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常","幾何能接合即表示電路相容","比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。"],"optionsEn":["Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality","Equating mechanical mating with circuit compatibility","Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"埋藏邏輯需設計可觀測和可控制路徑，邊界測試不等於完整功能測試。 比較連通測試、記憶體測試與功能測試覆蓋。 因此不能採用「邊界鏈路通過即所有邏輯功能正常」。","explanationEn":"Buried logic needs observable and controllable paths; boundary testing is not full functionality. Compare continuity, memory and functional coverage. Therefore reject: Equating boundary-chain success with all logic functionality."}}]},{"id":"a108-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"熱與可靠度","titleEn":"Thermal and reliability","description":"針對熱與可靠度完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for thermal and reliability, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a108-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-18"],"title":"熱源與熱阻｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Heat sources and resistances | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱源與熱阻，把「熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For heat sources and resistances, turn \"Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱源與熱阻」的模型：熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for heat sources and resistances: Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總功耗相同便有相同最高溫。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱源與熱阻的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for heat sources and resistances, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-19-k1","title":"熱源與熱阻：機制","titleEn":"Heat sources and resistances: mechanism","text":"熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。","textEn":"Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。 必須排除的錯判：總功耗相同便有相同最高溫。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱源與熱阻」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For heat sources and resistances — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。","總功耗相同便有相同最高溫","全部厚度公差都可平方和開根"],"optionsEn":["Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots.","Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature","Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。 在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。 因此不能採用「總功耗相同便有相同最高溫」。","explanationEn":"Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots. Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. Therefore reject: Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature."}},{"id":"a108-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-19"],"title":"熱源與熱阻｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Heat sources and resistances | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱源與熱阻，把「熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For heat sources and resistances, turn \"Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。 將「總功耗相同便有相同最高溫」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總功耗相同便有相同最高溫。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱源與熱阻的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for heat sources and resistances: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-20-k1","title":"熱源與熱阻：機制","titleEn":"Heat sources and resistances: mechanism","text":"熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。","textEn":"Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。 必須排除的錯判：總功耗相同便有相同最高溫。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱源與熱阻」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For heat sources and resistances — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["全部厚度公差都可平方和開根","在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。","總功耗相同便有相同最高溫"],"optionsEn":["Applying RSS to every thickness tolerance","Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power.","Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature"],"answer":1,"explanation":"熱源位置改變每層溫度；只有總功耗無法決定熱點。 在同總功耗下交換上、下層熱源。 因此不能採用「總功耗相同便有相同最高溫」。","explanationEn":"Heat-source location changes layer temperatures; total power alone cannot locate hotspots. Swap top/bottom sources at equal total power. Therefore reject: Assuming equal total power yields equal peak temperature."}},{"id":"a108-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-20"],"title":"層間應力｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interlayer stress | mechanism and design","objective":"針對層間應力，把「材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interlayer stress, turn \"Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「層間應力」的模型：材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interlayer stress: Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層間應力的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interlayer stress, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-21-k1","title":"層間應力：機制","titleEn":"Interlayer stress: mechanism","text":"材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。","textEn":"Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。 必須排除的錯判：加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層間應力」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interlayer stress — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力","最終測試即可取代全部中間測試","材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress","Replacing every intermediate test with final testing","Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。 比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。 因此不能採用「加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力」。","explanationEn":"Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear. Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. Therefore reject: Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress."}},{"id":"a108-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-21"],"title":"層間應力｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interlayer stress | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對層間應力，把「材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interlayer stress, turn \"Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。 將「加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層間應力的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interlayer stress: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-22-k1","title":"層間應力：機制","titleEn":"Interlayer stress: mechanism","text":"材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。","textEn":"Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。 必須排除的錯判：加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層間應力」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interlayer stress — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。","加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力","最終測試即可取代全部中間測試"],"optionsEn":["Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage.","Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress","Replacing every intermediate test with final testing"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料不對稱及厚度差產生曲率和界面剪應力。 比較對稱與不對稱堆疊的翹曲圖。 因此不能採用「加厚最上層總能降低所有界面應力」。","explanationEn":"Material asymmetry and thickness differences generate curvature and interface shear. Compare symmetric and asymmetric stack warpage. Therefore reject: Assuming a thicker top layer lowers every interface stress."}},{"id":"a108-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-22"],"title":"失效拆解順序｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Failure-analysis order | mechanism and design","objective":"針對失效拆解順序，把「破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For failure-analysis order, turn \"Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「失效拆解順序」的模型：破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「制定先後順序及保留對照片。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for failure-analysis order: Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Plan analysis order and retained controls. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"制定先後順序及保留對照片。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plan analysis order and retained controls. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Grinding first before electrical localization. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付失效拆解順序的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for failure-analysis order, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-23-k1","title":"失效拆解順序：機制","titleEn":"Failure-analysis order: mechanism","text":"破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。","textEn":"Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"制定先後順序及保留對照片。 必須排除的錯判：先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plan analysis order and retained controls. Misinterpretation to reject: Grinding first before electrical localization. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「失效拆解順序」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For failure-analysis order — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險","破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。","先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效"],"optionsEn":["Equating average suction with equal bending risk","Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first.","Grinding first before electrical localization"],"answer":1,"explanation":"破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。 制定先後順序及保留對照片。 因此不能採用「先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效」。","explanationEn":"Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first. Plan analysis order and retained controls. Therefore reject: Grinding first before electrical localization."}},{"id":"a108-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"],"prerequisiteIds":["a108-v9-23"],"title":"失效拆解順序｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Failure-analysis order | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對失效拆解順序，把「破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For failure-analysis order, turn \"Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：制定先後順序及保留對照片。 將「先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Plan analysis order and retained controls. Challenge the hypothesis \"Grinding first before electrical localization\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"制定先後順序及保留對照片。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plan analysis order and retained controls. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Grinding first before electrical localization. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付失效拆解順序的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for failure-analysis order: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a108-v9-24-k1","title":"失效拆解順序：機制","titleEn":"Failure-analysis order: mechanism","text":"破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。","textEn":"Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]},{"id":"a108-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"制定先後順序及保留對照片。 必須排除的錯判：先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plan analysis order and retained controls. Misinterpretation to reject: Grinding first before electrical localization. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-besipub"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「失效拆解順序」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For failure-analysis order — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效","平均吸力相同即有相同彎曲風險","制定先後順序及保留對照片。"],"optionsEn":["Grinding first before electrical localization","Equating average suction with equal bending risk","Plan analysis order and retained controls."],"answer":2,"explanation":"破壞性拆解會消除某些證據，應先電測和非破壞定位。 制定先後順序及保留對照片。 因此不能採用「先研磨到可見裂紋再作電測最有效」。","explanationEn":"Destructive sectioning removes evidence; localize electrically and nondestructively first. Plan analysis order and retained controls. Therefore reject: Grinding first before electrical localization."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-joining","subcategoryTitle":"凸塊與精密接合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bumps and precision bonding","photoId":"v9-quilt-3d"},{"id":"a109","title":"晶圓暫時接合與解接合","titleEn":"Temporary wafer bonding and debonding","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入載板支撐、黏著窗口與低損傷解接合。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore carrier support, adhesion window and low-damage release, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["材料與路徑","暫時接合","背面加工","解接合與清潔"],"labelsEn":["Materials and routes","Temporary bonding","Backside processing","Debond and cleaning"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a109-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"材料與路徑","titleEn":"Materials and routes","description":"針對材料與路徑完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for materials and routes, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a109-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"載板材料選擇｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Carrier selection | mechanism and design","objective":"針對載板材料選擇，把「透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier selection, turn \"Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「載板材料選擇」的模型：透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for carrier selection: Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板材料選擇的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for carrier selection, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-01-k1","title":"載板材料選擇：機制","titleEn":"Carrier selection: mechanism","text":"透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。","textEn":"Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。 必須排除的錯判：玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板材料選擇」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier selection — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。","玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長","加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability.","Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength","Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release"],"answer":0,"explanation":"透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。 按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。 因此不能採用「玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長」。","explanationEn":"Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability. Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. Therefore reject: Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength."}},{"id":"a109-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-01"],"title":"載板材料選擇｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Carrier selection | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對載板材料選擇，把「透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier selection, turn \"Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。 將「玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板材料選擇的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for carrier selection: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-02-k1","title":"載板材料選擇：機制","titleEn":"Carrier selection: mechanism","text":"透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。","textEn":"Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。 必須排除的錯判：玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板材料選擇」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier selection — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好","按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。","玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長"],"optionsEn":["Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release","Build a material matrix against processing and release needs.","Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength"],"answer":1,"explanation":"透明度、CTE、剛性和清潔相容性決定載板用途。 按加工與釋放需求建立材料矩陣。 因此不能採用「玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長」。","explanationEn":"Transparency, CTE, stiffness and cleaning compatibility determine carrier suitability. Build a material matrix against processing and release needs. Therefore reject: Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength."}},{"id":"a109-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-02"],"title":"釋放路徑比較｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Release-route comparison | mechanism and design","objective":"針對釋放路徑比較，把「熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For release-route comparison, turn \"Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「釋放路徑比較」的模型：熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for release-route comparison: Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各種解接合只差光源名稱。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付釋放路徑比較的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for release-route comparison, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-03-k1","title":"釋放路徑比較：機制","titleEn":"Release-route comparison: mechanism","text":"熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。","textEn":"Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。 必須排除的錯判：各種解接合只差光源名稱。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「釋放路徑比較」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For release-route comparison — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各種解接合只差光源名稱","外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容","熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。"],"optionsEn":["Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels","Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof","Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。 把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。 因此不能採用「各種解接合只差光源名稱」。","explanationEn":"Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries. Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. Therefore reject: Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels."}},{"id":"a109-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-03"],"title":"釋放路徑比較｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Release-route comparison | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對釋放路徑比較，把「熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For release-route comparison, turn \"Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。 將「各種解接合只差光源名稱」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各種解接合只差光源名稱。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付釋放路徑比較的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for release-route comparison: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-04-k1","title":"釋放路徑比較：機制","titleEn":"Release-route comparison: mechanism","text":"熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。","textEn":"Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。 必須排除的錯判：各種解接合只差光源名稱。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「釋放路徑比較」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For release-route comparison — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。","各種解接合只差光源名稱","外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容"],"optionsEn":["Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section.","Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels","Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof"],"answer":0,"explanation":"熱滑移、UV 與 IR 釋放的作用層和設備邊界不同。 把吸收層、透明路徑和支撐面標到剖面。 因此不能採用「各種解接合只差光源名稱」。","explanationEn":"Thermal-slide, UV and IR release act at different layers and boundaries. Mark absorbers, optical paths and supports in section. Therefore reject: Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels."}},{"id":"a109-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-04"],"title":"膠層厚度地圖｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Adhesive thickness map | mechanism and design","objective":"針對膠層厚度地圖，把「膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For adhesive thickness map, turn \"Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「膠層厚度地圖」的模型：膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for adhesive thickness map: Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膠層厚度地圖的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for adhesive thickness map, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-05-k1","title":"膠層厚度地圖：機制","titleEn":"Adhesive thickness map: mechanism","text":"膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。","textEn":"Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。 必須排除的錯判：總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膠層厚度地圖」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For adhesive thickness map — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["厚度減半僅讓剛性減半","膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。","總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻"],"optionsEn":["Assuming half thickness means half stiffness","Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors.","Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。 分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。 因此不能採用「總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻」。","explanationEn":"Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors. Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. Therefore reject: Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness."}},{"id":"a109-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-05"],"title":"膠層厚度地圖｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Adhesive thickness map | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對膠層厚度地圖，把「膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For adhesive thickness map, turn \"Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。 將「總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膠層厚度地圖的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for adhesive thickness map: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-06-k1","title":"膠層厚度地圖：機制","titleEn":"Adhesive thickness map: mechanism","text":"膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。","textEn":"Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。 必須排除的錯判：總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膠層厚度地圖」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For adhesive thickness map — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻","厚度減半僅讓剛性減半","分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness","Assuming half thickness means half stiffness","Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"膠層厚度變化會轉成加工支撐和厚度誤差。 分開量載板、膠層與晶圓厚度。 因此不能採用「總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻」。","explanationEn":"Adhesive variations become support and processing-thickness errors. Measure carrier, adhesive and wafer thickness separately. Therefore reject: Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness."}}]},{"id":"a109-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"暫時接合","titleEn":"Temporary bonding","description":"針對暫時接合完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for temporary bonding, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a109-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-06"],"title":"空洞與氣泡｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Voids and bubbles | mechanism and design","objective":"針對空洞與氣泡，把「未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For voids and bubbles, turn \"Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「空洞與氣泡」的模型：未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for voids and bubbles: Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming small voids never matter downstream. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空洞與氣泡的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for voids and bubbles, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-07-k1","title":"空洞與氣泡：機制","titleEn":"Voids and bubbles: mechanism","text":"未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。","textEn":"Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。 必須排除的錯判：小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming small voids never matter downstream. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空洞與氣泡」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For voids and bubbles — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。","小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響","只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐"],"optionsEn":["Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation.","Assuming small voids never matter downstream","Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled"],"answer":0,"explanation":"未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。 將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。 因此不能採用「小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響」。","explanationEn":"Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation. Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. Therefore reject: Assuming small voids never matter downstream."}},{"id":"a109-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-07"],"title":"空洞與氣泡｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Voids and bubbles | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對空洞與氣泡，把「未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For voids and bubbles, turn \"Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。 將「小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming small voids never matter downstream\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming small voids never matter downstream. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空洞與氣泡的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for voids and bubbles: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-08-k1","title":"空洞與氣泡：機制","titleEn":"Voids and bubbles: mechanism","text":"未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。","textEn":"Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。 必須排除的錯判：小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming small voids never matter downstream. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空洞與氣泡」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For voids and bubbles — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐","將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。","小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled","Register void and post-thinning thickness maps.","Assuming small voids never matter downstream"],"answer":1,"explanation":"未接合空洞降低局部剛性，背面載荷可放大變形。 將空洞圖與薄化後厚度圖配準。 因此不能採用「小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響」。","explanationEn":"Bond voids reduce local stiffness, amplifying backside-load deformation. Register void and post-thinning thickness maps. Therefore reject: Assuming small voids never matter downstream."}},{"id":"a109-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-08"],"title":"邊緣封閉｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Edge coverage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對邊緣封閉，把「邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For edge coverage, turn \"Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「邊緣封閉」的模型：邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for edge coverage: Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只測中心接合強度即可代表整片。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using center bond strength to represent the wafer. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付邊緣封閉的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for edge coverage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-09-k1","title":"邊緣封閉：機制","titleEn":"Edge coverage: mechanism","text":"邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。","textEn":"Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。 必須排除的錯判：只測中心接合強度即可代表整片。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. Misinterpretation to reject: Using center bond strength to represent the wafer. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「邊緣封閉」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For edge coverage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只測中心接合強度即可代表整片","肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測","邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。"],"optionsEn":["Using center bond strength to represent the wafer","Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface","Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。 檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。 因此不能採用「只測中心接合強度即可代表整片」。","explanationEn":"Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration. Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. Therefore reject: Using center bond strength to represent the wafer."}},{"id":"a109-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-09"],"title":"邊緣封閉｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Edge coverage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對邊緣封閉，把「邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For edge coverage, turn \"Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。 將「只測中心接合強度即可代表整片」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using center bond strength to represent the wafer\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只測中心接合強度即可代表整片。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using center bond strength to represent the wafer. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付邊緣封閉的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for edge coverage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-10-k1","title":"邊緣封閉：機制","titleEn":"Edge coverage: mechanism","text":"邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。","textEn":"Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。 必須排除的錯判：只測中心接合強度即可代表整片。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. Misinterpretation to reject: Using center bond strength to represent the wafer. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「邊緣封閉」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For edge coverage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。","只測中心接合強度即可代表整片","肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測"],"optionsEn":["Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones.","Using center bond strength to represent the wafer","Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface"],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣缺膠可能成為液體入侵及應力起點。 檢查圓周覆蓋及邊緣排除區。 因此不能採用「只測中心接合強度即可代表整片」。","explanationEn":"Edge adhesive gaps can admit fluids and initiate stress concentration. Inspect circumferential coverage and exclusion zones. Therefore reject: Using center bond strength to represent the wafer."}},{"id":"a109-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-10"],"title":"熱预算相容性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal-budget compatibility | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱预算相容性，把「暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal-budget compatibility, turn \"Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱预算相容性」的模型：暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal-budget compatibility: Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱预算相容性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal-budget compatibility, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-11-k1","title":"熱预算相容性：機制","titleEn":"Thermal-budget compatibility: mechanism","text":"暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。","textEn":"Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。 必須排除的錯判：加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱预算相容性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal-budget compatibility — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["每次清潔後載板等同全新","暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。","加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Treating every cleaned carrier as new","Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability.","Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release"],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。 比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。 因此不能採用「加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好」。","explanationEn":"Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability. Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. Therefore reject: Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release."}},{"id":"a109-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-11"],"title":"熱预算相容性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal-budget compatibility | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱预算相容性，把「暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal-budget compatibility, turn \"Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。 將「加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱预算相容性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal-budget compatibility: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-12-k1","title":"熱预算相容性：機制","titleEn":"Thermal-budget compatibility: mechanism","text":"暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。","textEn":"Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。 必須排除的錯判：加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱预算相容性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal-budget compatibility — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好","每次清潔後載板等同全新","比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release","Treating every cleaned carrier as new","Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"暫時膠需承受加工歷程又保留釋放能力。 比較加工前後的剪切、滑移和殘膠。 因此不能採用「加工時黏得越強解接合一定越好」。","explanationEn":"Temporary adhesive must survive processing while retaining releasability. Compare shear, slip and residue before/after processing. Therefore reject: Assuming stronger process adhesion always improves release."}}]},{"id":"a109-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"背面加工","titleEn":"Backside processing","description":"針對背面加工完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for backside processing, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a109-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-12"],"title":"化學與真空相容性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Chemical and vacuum compatibility | mechanism and design","objective":"針對化學與真空相容性，把「溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chemical and vacuum compatibility, turn \"Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「化學與真空相容性」的模型：溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for chemical and vacuum compatibility: Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付化學與真空相容性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for chemical and vacuum compatibility, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-13-k1","title":"化學與真空相容性：機制","titleEn":"Chemical and vacuum compatibility: mechanism","text":"溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。","textEn":"Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。 必須排除的錯判：外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. Misinterpretation to reject: Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「化學與真空相容性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chemical and vacuum compatibility — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。","外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容","沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功"],"optionsEn":["Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks.","Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof","Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke"],"answer":0,"explanation":"溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。 用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。 因此不能採用「外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容」。","explanationEn":"Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks. Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. Therefore reject: Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof."}},{"id":"a109-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-13"],"title":"化學與真空相容性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Chemical and vacuum compatibility | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對化學與真空相容性，把「溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chemical and vacuum compatibility, turn \"Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。 將「外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付化學與真空相容性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for chemical and vacuum compatibility: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-14-k1","title":"化學與真空相容性：機制","titleEn":"Chemical and vacuum compatibility: mechanism","text":"溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。","textEn":"Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。 必須排除的錯判：外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. Misinterpretation to reject: Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「化學與真空相容性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chemical and vacuum compatibility — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功","用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。","外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容"],"optionsEn":["Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke","Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination.","Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof"],"answer":1,"explanation":"溶脹、揮發和污染可能改變支撐而非直接可見裂紋。 用見證件比質量、厚度和污染。 因此不能採用「外觀無裂紋即證明材料相容」。","explanationEn":"Swelling, outgassing and contamination can change support without visible cracks. Compare witness mass, thickness and contamination. Therefore reject: Using crack-free appearance as compatibility proof."}},{"id":"a109-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-14"],"title":"薄片應力｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thin-wafer stress | mechanism and design","objective":"針對薄片應力，把「薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thin-wafer stress, turn \"Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「薄片應力」的模型：薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thin-wafer stress: Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare support needs when thickness halves. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare support needs when thickness halves. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：厚度減半僅讓剛性減半。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming half thickness means half stiffness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付薄片應力的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thin-wafer stress, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-15-k1","title":"薄片應力：機制","titleEn":"Thin-wafer stress: mechanism","text":"薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。","textEn":"Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。 必須排除的錯判：厚度減半僅讓剛性減半。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare support needs when thickness halves. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming half thickness means half stiffness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄片應力」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thin-wafer stress — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["厚度減半僅讓剛性減半","玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長","薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming half thickness means half stiffness","Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength","Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。 比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。 因此不能採用「厚度減半僅讓剛性減半」。","explanationEn":"Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed. Compare support needs when thickness halves. Therefore reject: Assuming half thickness means half stiffness."}},{"id":"a109-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-15"],"title":"薄片應力｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thin-wafer stress | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對薄片應力，把「薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thin-wafer stress, turn \"Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。 將「厚度減半僅讓剛性減半」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare support needs when thickness halves. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming half thickness means half stiffness\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare support needs when thickness halves. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：厚度減半僅讓剛性減半。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming half thickness means half stiffness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付薄片應力的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thin-wafer stress: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-16-k1","title":"薄片應力：機制","titleEn":"Thin-wafer stress: mechanism","text":"薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。","textEn":"Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。 必須排除的錯判：厚度減半僅讓剛性減半。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare support needs when thickness halves. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming half thickness means half stiffness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄片應力」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thin-wafer stress — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。","厚度減半僅讓剛性減半","玻璃載板可自動相容所有雷射波長"],"optionsEn":["Compare support needs when thickness halves.","Assuming half thickness means half stiffness","Assuming glass is compatible with every laser wavelength"],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄片彎曲剛性近似隨厚度三次方下降。 比較厚度減半時支撐需求的變化。 因此不能採用「厚度減半僅讓剛性減半」。","explanationEn":"Thin-plate bending stiffness approximately scales with thickness cubed. Compare support needs when thickness halves. Therefore reject: Assuming half thickness means half stiffness."}},{"id":"a109-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-16"],"title":"解接合支撐｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Release support | mechanism and design","objective":"針對解接合支撐，把「釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For release support, turn \"Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「解接合支撐」的模型：釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫解接合前中後三種支撐。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設兩材料 Δα=5 ppm/K、長 100 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差異伸長 ΔL=ΔαLΔT=50 μm；黏著拘束會把其中部分轉為應力，不能把此數直接視為實際滑移。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for release support: Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw supports before, during and after release. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For Δα=5 ppm/K, L=100 mm and ΔT=100 K, free differential expansion is 50 μm. Adhesive constraints convert part into stress; this is not the actual slip. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"畫解接合前中後三種支撐。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw supports before, during and after release. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付解接合支撐的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for release support, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-17-k1","title":"解接合支撐：機制","titleEn":"Release support: mechanism","text":"釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。","textEn":"Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫解接合前中後三種支撐。 必須排除的錯判：只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw supports before, during and after release. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設兩材料 Δα=5 ppm/K、長 100 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差異伸長 ΔL=ΔαLΔT=50 μm；黏著拘束會把其中部分轉為應力，不能把此數直接視為實際滑移。","textEn":"For Δα=5 ppm/K, L=100 mm and ΔT=100 K, free differential expansion is 50 μm. Adhesive constraints convert part into stress; this is not the actual slip."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「解接合支撐」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For release support — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各種解接合只差光源名稱","釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。","只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐"],"optionsEn":["Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels","Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans.","Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled"],"answer":1,"explanation":"釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。 畫解接合前中後三種支撐。 因此不能採用「只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐」。","explanationEn":"Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans. Draw supports before, during and after release. Therefore reject: Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled."}},{"id":"a109-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-17"],"title":"解接合支撐｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Release support | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對解接合支撐，把「釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For release support, turn \"Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫解接合前中後三種支撐。 將「只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設兩材料 Δα=5 ppm/K、長 100 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差異伸長 ΔL=ΔαLΔT=50 μm；黏著拘束會把其中部分轉為應力，不能把此數直接視為實際滑移。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw supports before, during and after release. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For Δα=5 ppm/K, L=100 mm and ΔT=100 K, free differential expansion is 50 μm. Adhesive constraints convert part into stress; this is not the actual slip. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"畫解接合前中後三種支撐。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw supports before, during and after release. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付解接合支撐的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for release support: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-18-k1","title":"解接合支撐：機制","titleEn":"Release support: mechanism","text":"釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。","textEn":"Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫解接合前中後三種支撐。 必須排除的錯判：只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw supports before, during and after release. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設兩材料 Δα=5 ppm/K、長 100 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差異伸長 ΔL=ΔαLΔT=50 μm；黏著拘束會把其中部分轉為應力，不能把此數直接視為實際滑移。","textEn":"For Δα=5 ppm/K, L=100 mm and ΔT=100 K, free differential expansion is 50 μm. Adhesive constraints convert part into stress; this is not the actual slip."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「解接合支撐」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For release support — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐","各種解接合只差光源名稱","畫解接合前中後三種支撐。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled","Treating release routes as interchangeable light-source labels","Draw supports before, during and after release."],"answer":2,"explanation":"釋放瞬間載荷路徑改變，應避免自由薄片懸空。 畫解接合前中後三種支撐。 因此不能採用「只控制釋放能量即可忽略接收支撐」。","explanationEn":"Release abruptly changes load paths; avoid unsupported thin-wafer spans. Draw supports before, during and after release. Therefore reject: Ignoring receiving support when release energy is controlled."}}]},{"id":"a109-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"解接合與清潔","titleEn":"Debond and cleaning","description":"針對解接合與清潔完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for debond and cleaning, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a109-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-18"],"title":"殘膠判定｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Residue assessment | mechanism and design","objective":"針對殘膠判定，把「殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For residue assessment, turn \"Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「殘膠判定」的模型：殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for residue assessment: Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付殘膠判定的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for residue assessment, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-19-k1","title":"殘膠判定：機制","titleEn":"Residue assessment: mechanism","text":"殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。","textEn":"Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。 必須排除的錯判：肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「殘膠判定」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For residue assessment — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。","肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測","總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻"],"optionsEn":["Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness.","Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface","Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。 比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。 因此不能採用「肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測」。","explanationEn":"Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness. Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. Therefore reject: Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface."}},{"id":"a109-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-19"],"title":"殘膠判定｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Residue assessment | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對殘膠判定，把「殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For residue assessment, turn \"Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。 將「肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付殘膠判定的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for residue assessment: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-20-k1","title":"殘膠判定：機制","titleEn":"Residue assessment: mechanism","text":"殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。","textEn":"Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。 必須排除的錯判：肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「殘膠判定」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For residue assessment — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總厚度均勻即可證明膠層均勻","比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。","肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測"],"optionsEn":["Inferring uniform adhesive from uniform total thickness","Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses.","Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface"],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘膠可影響後段接合與量測，透明外觀不等於潔淨。 比較接觸角、表面分析和後段見證片。 因此不能採用「肉眼透明即可免除殘留檢測」。","explanationEn":"Residue affects later bonding and metrology; optical transparency is not cleanliness. Compare contact angle, surface analysis and downstream witnesses. Therefore reject: Skipping residue checks for a transparent surface."}},{"id":"a109-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-20"],"title":"載板再用｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Carrier reuse | mechanism and design","objective":"針對載板再用，把「重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier reuse, turn \"Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「載板再用」的模型：重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for carrier reuse: Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每次清潔後載板等同全新。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating every cleaned carrier as new. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板再用的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for carrier reuse, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-21-k1","title":"載板再用：機制","titleEn":"Carrier reuse: mechanism","text":"重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。","textEn":"Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。 必須排除的錯判：每次清潔後載板等同全新。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating every cleaned carrier as new. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板再用」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier reuse — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["每次清潔後載板等同全新","小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響","重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。"],"optionsEn":["Treating every cleaned carrier as new","Assuming small voids never matter downstream","Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。 以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。 因此不能採用「每次清潔後載板等同全新」。","explanationEn":"Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp. Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. Therefore reject: Treating every cleaned carrier as new."}},{"id":"a109-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-21"],"title":"載板再用｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Carrier reuse | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對載板再用，把「重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier reuse, turn \"Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。 將「每次清潔後載板等同全新」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating every cleaned carrier as new\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每次清潔後載板等同全新。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating every cleaned carrier as new. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板再用的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for carrier reuse: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-22-k1","title":"載板再用：機制","titleEn":"Carrier reuse: mechanism","text":"重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。","textEn":"Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。 必須排除的錯判：每次清潔後載板等同全新。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating every cleaned carrier as new. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板再用」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier reuse — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。","每次清潔後載板等同全新","小空洞在所有後續步驟都無影響"],"optionsEn":["Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle.","Treating every cleaned carrier as new","Assuming small voids never matter downstream"],"answer":0,"explanation":"重複清潔可能累積表面損傷、邊緣缺陷或翹曲。 以循環次數追蹤平坦度與缺陷。 因此不能採用「每次清潔後載板等同全新」。","explanationEn":"Repeated cleaning can accumulate surface damage, edge defects or warp. Track flatness and defects by reuse cycle. Therefore reject: Treating every cleaned carrier as new."}},{"id":"a109-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-22"],"title":"完整轉移證據｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Transfer evidence | mechanism and design","objective":"針對完整轉移證據，把「薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For transfer evidence, turn \"Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「完整轉移證據」的模型：薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for transfer evidence: Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付完整轉移證據的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for transfer evidence, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-23-k1","title":"完整轉移證據：機制","titleEn":"Transfer evidence: mechanism","text":"薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。","textEn":"Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。 必須排除的錯判：沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. Misinterpretation to reject: Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「完整轉移證據」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For transfer evidence — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只測中心接合強度即可代表整片","薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。","沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功"],"optionsEn":["Using center bond strength to represent the wafer","Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes.","Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke"],"answer":1,"explanation":"薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。 提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。 因此不能採用「沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功」。","explanationEn":"Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes. Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. Therefore reject: Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke."}},{"id":"a109-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"],"prerequisiteIds":["a109-v9-23"],"title":"完整轉移證據｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Transfer evidence | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對完整轉移證據，把「薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For transfer evidence, turn \"Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。 將「沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. Challenge the hypothesis \"Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付完整轉移證據的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for transfer evidence: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a109-v9-24-k1","title":"完整轉移證據：機制","titleEn":"Transfer evidence: mechanism","text":"薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。","textEn":"Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]},{"id":"a109-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。 必須排除的錯判：沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. Misinterpretation to reject: Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-evgtemp","v9a-corningcarrier"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「完整轉移證據」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For transfer evidence — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功","只測中心接合強度即可代表整片","提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。"],"optionsEn":["Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke","Using center bond strength to represent the wafer","Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points."],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄片無破裂、表面可接合和厚度合格是不同結果。 提供三類資料與後段驗證保留點。 因此不能採用「沒有破片即表示暫時接合全程成功」。","explanationEn":"Intact transfer, bondable surfaces and correct thickness are distinct outcomes. Deliver all three evidence types and downstream hold points. Therefore reject: Calling the process successful solely because no wafer broke."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-handling","subcategoryTitle":"薄化、切割與晶粒搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thinning, dicing and die handling","photoId":"v8-wafer"},{"id":"a110","title":"晶圓薄化與背面研磨","titleEn":"Wafer thinning and backside grinding","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入薄化幾何、次表面損傷與薄片支撐。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore thinning geometry, subsurface damage and thin-wafer support, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["厚度需求","研磨與支撐","損傷去除","背面驗收"],"labelsEn":["Thickness requirements","Grinding and support","Damage removal","Backside acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a110-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"厚度需求","titleEn":"Thickness requirements","description":"針對厚度需求完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for thickness requirements, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a110-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"最終厚度分配｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Final-thickness allocation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對最終厚度分配，把「目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For final-thickness allocation, turn \"Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「最終厚度分配」的模型：目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for final-thickness allocation: Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付最終厚度分配的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for final-thickness allocation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-01-k1","title":"最終厚度分配：機制","titleEn":"Final-thickness allocation: mechanism","text":"目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。","textEn":"Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。 必須排除的錯判：研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「最終厚度分配」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For final-thickness allocation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。","研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度","高解析讀值等同高準確度"],"optionsEn":["Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances.","Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness","Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。 畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。 因此不能採用「研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度」。","explanationEn":"Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances. Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. Therefore reject: Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness."}},{"id":"a110-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-01"],"title":"最終厚度分配｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Final-thickness allocation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對最終厚度分配，把「目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For final-thickness allocation, turn \"Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。 將「研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付最終厚度分配的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for final-thickness allocation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-02-k1","title":"最終厚度分配：機制","titleEn":"Final-thickness allocation: mechanism","text":"目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。","textEn":"Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。 必須排除的錯判：研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「最終厚度分配」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For final-thickness allocation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["高解析讀值等同高準確度","畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。","研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度"],"optionsEn":["Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy","Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall.","Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"目標厚度須扣除後續應力釋放和露出加工留量。 畫厚度預算的逐站瀑布圖。 因此不能採用「研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度」。","explanationEn":"Final thickness must reserve later stress-relief and reveal allowances. Draw a station-by-station thickness waterfall. Therefore reject: Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness."}},{"id":"a110-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-02"],"title":"TTV 與翹曲｜機制與設計","titleEn":"TTV versus warpage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對TTV 與翹曲，把「總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For ttv versus warpage, turn \"Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「TTV 與翹曲」的模型：總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for ttv versus warpage: Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：單面高度圖可直接當 TTV。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating a one-sided height map as TTV. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付TTV 與翹曲的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for ttv versus warpage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-03-k1","title":"TTV 與翹曲：機制","titleEn":"TTV versus warpage: mechanism","text":"總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。","textEn":"Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。 必須排除的錯判：單面高度圖可直接當 TTV。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating a one-sided height map as TTV. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「TTV 與翹曲」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For ttv versus warpage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["單面高度圖可直接當 TTV","中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋","總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。"],"optionsEn":["Treating a one-sided height map as TTV","Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass","Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands."],"answer":2,"explanation":"總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。 比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。 因此不能採用「單面高度圖可直接當 TTV」。","explanationEn":"Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands. Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. Therefore reject: Treating a one-sided height map as TTV."}},{"id":"a110-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-03"],"title":"TTV 與翹曲｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"TTV versus warpage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對TTV 與翹曲，把「總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For ttv versus warpage, turn \"Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。 將「單面高度圖可直接當 TTV」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating a one-sided height map as TTV\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：單面高度圖可直接當 TTV。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating a one-sided height map as TTV. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付TTV 與翹曲的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for ttv versus warpage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-04-k1","title":"TTV 與翹曲：機制","titleEn":"TTV versus warpage: mechanism","text":"總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。","textEn":"Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。 必須排除的錯判：單面高度圖可直接當 TTV。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating a one-sided height map as TTV. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「TTV 與翹曲」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For ttv versus warpage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。","單面高度圖可直接當 TTV","中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements.","Treating a one-sided height map as TTV","Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"總厚度變異與自由形狀翹曲是不同量。 比較夾持與自由狀態雙面量測。 因此不能採用「單面高度圖可直接當 TTV」。","explanationEn":"Total-thickness variation and free-shape warpage are different measurands. Compare clamped and free-state two-sided measurements. Therefore reject: Treating a one-sided height map as TTV."}},{"id":"a110-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-04"],"title":"正面保護｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Frontside protection | mechanism and design","objective":"針對正面保護，把「保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For frontside protection, turn \"Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「正面保護」的模型：保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for frontside protection: Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付正面保護的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for frontside protection, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-05-k1","title":"正面保護：機制","titleEn":"Frontside protection: mechanism","text":"保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。","textEn":"Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。 必須排除的錯判：保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「正面保護」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For frontside protection — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何","保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。","保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力"],"optionsEn":["Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry","Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face.","Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。 比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。 因此不能採用「保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力」。","explanationEn":"Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face. Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. Therefore reject: Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading."}},{"id":"a110-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-05"],"title":"正面保護｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Frontside protection | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對正面保護，把「保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For frontside protection, turn \"Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。 將「保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付正面保護的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for frontside protection: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-06-k1","title":"正面保護：機制","titleEn":"Frontside protection: mechanism","text":"保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。","textEn":"Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。 必須排除的錯判：保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「正面保護」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For frontside protection — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力","應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何","比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading","Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry","Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保護層需承擔局部凸塊地形且避免污染功能面。 比較凸塊周圍支撐和剝離後表面。 因此不能採用「保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力」。","explanationEn":"Protection must accommodate bump topography without contaminating the functional face. Compare support near bumps and post-peel surfaces. Therefore reject: Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading."}}]},{"id":"a110-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"研磨與支撐","titleEn":"Grinding and support","description":"針對研磨與支撐完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for grinding and support, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a110-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-06"],"title":"粗磨與細磨｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Coarse and fine grinding | mechanism and design","objective":"針對粗磨與細磨，把「移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For coarse and fine grinding, turn \"Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「粗磨與細磨」的模型：移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for coarse and fine grinding: Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare removal per station with damage sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare removal per station with damage sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付粗磨與細磨的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for coarse and fine grinding, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-07-k1","title":"粗磨與細磨：機制","titleEn":"Coarse and fine grinding: mechanism","text":"移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。","textEn":"Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。 必須排除的錯判：最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare removal per station with damage sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粗磨與細磨」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For coarse and fine grinding — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。","最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋","厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度"],"optionsEn":["Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage.","Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks","Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick"],"answer":0,"explanation":"移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。 對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。 因此不能採用「最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage. Compare removal per station with damage sections. Therefore reject: Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks."}},{"id":"a110-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-07"],"title":"粗磨與細磨｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Coarse and fine grinding | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對粗磨與細磨，把「移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For coarse and fine grinding, turn \"Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。 將「最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare removal per station with damage sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare removal per station with damage sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付粗磨與細磨的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for coarse and fine grinding: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-08-k1","title":"粗磨與細磨：機制","titleEn":"Coarse and fine grinding: mechanism","text":"移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。","textEn":"Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。 必須排除的錯判：最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare removal per station with damage sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粗磨與細磨」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For coarse and fine grinding — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度","對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。","最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick","Compare removal per station with damage sections.","Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"移除效率和損傷深度互相牽制，細磨不保證去除全部粗磨損傷。 對照逐站移除量與截面損傷。 因此不能採用「最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Removal rate trades against damage depth; fine grinding need not remove all coarse damage. Compare removal per station with damage sections. Therefore reject: Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks."}},{"id":"a110-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-08"],"title":"載荷與輪痕｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Loads and wheel marks | mechanism and design","objective":"針對載荷與輪痕，把「輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For loads and wheel marks, turn \"Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「載荷與輪痕」的模型：輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for loads and wheel marks: Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal bending strength in every direction. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載荷與輪痕的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for loads and wheel marks, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-09-k1","title":"載荷與輪痕：機制","titleEn":"Loads and wheel marks: mechanism","text":"輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。","textEn":"Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。 必須排除的錯判：所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal bending strength in every direction. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載荷與輪痕」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For loads and wheel marks — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同","最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度","輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal bending strength in every direction","Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability","Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。 按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。 因此不能採用「所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同」。","explanationEn":"Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress. Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. Therefore reject: Assuming equal bending strength in every direction."}},{"id":"a110-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-09"],"title":"載荷與輪痕｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Loads and wheel marks | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對載荷與輪痕，把「輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For loads and wheel marks, turn \"Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。 將「所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal bending strength in every direction\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal bending strength in every direction. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載荷與輪痕的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for loads and wheel marks: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-10-k1","title":"載荷與輪痕：機制","titleEn":"Loads and wheel marks: mechanism","text":"輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。","textEn":"Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。 必須排除的錯判：所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal bending strength in every direction. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載荷與輪痕」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For loads and wheel marks — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。","所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同","最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Compare radial and tangential strength sampling.","Assuming equal bending strength in every direction","Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"輪痕方向與局部負載可留下應力各向異性。 按徑向和切向取樣比較強度。 因此不能採用「所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同」。","explanationEn":"Wheel-mark direction and local loads can create anisotropic stress. Compare radial and tangential strength sampling. Therefore reject: Assuming equal bending strength in every direction."}},{"id":"a110-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-10"],"title":"厚度量測基準｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thickness reference | mechanism and design","objective":"針對厚度量測基準，把「透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thickness reference, turn \"Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「厚度量測基準」的模型：透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thickness reference: Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：高解析讀值等同高準確度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付厚度量測基準的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thickness reference, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-11-k1","title":"厚度量測基準：機制","titleEn":"Thickness reference: mechanism","text":"透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。","textEn":"Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。 必須排除的錯判：高解析讀值等同高準確度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「厚度量測基準」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thickness reference — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷","透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。","高解析讀值等同高準確度"],"optionsEn":["Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage","Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings.","Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy"],"answer":1,"explanation":"透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。 用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。 因此不能採用「高解析讀值等同高準確度」。","explanationEn":"Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings. Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. Therefore reject: Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy."}},{"id":"a110-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-11"],"title":"厚度量測基準｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thickness reference | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對厚度量測基準，把「透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thickness reference, turn \"Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。 將「高解析讀值等同高準確度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：高解析讀值等同高準確度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付厚度量測基準的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thickness reference: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-12-k1","title":"厚度量測基準：機制","titleEn":"Thickness reference: mechanism","text":"透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。","textEn":"Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。 必須排除的錯判：高解析讀值等同高準確度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「厚度量測基準」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thickness reference — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["高解析讀值等同高準確度","晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷","用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。"],"optionsEn":["Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy","Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage","Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method."],"answer":2,"explanation":"透明保護層、背面反射與探頭校正會影響厚度讀值。 用可追溯標準片與另一方法交叉校核。 因此不能採用「高解析讀值等同高準確度」。","explanationEn":"Transparent protection, backside reflections and probe calibration affect readings. Cross-check with traceable standards and a second method. Therefore reject: Equating high readout resolution with high accuracy."}}]},{"id":"a110-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"損傷去除","titleEn":"Damage removal","description":"針對損傷去除完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for damage removal, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a110-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-12"],"title":"邊緣缺口｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Edge chipping | mechanism and design","objective":"針對邊緣缺口，把「邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For edge chipping, turn \"Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「邊緣缺口」的模型：邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for edge chipping: Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付邊緣缺口的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for edge chipping, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-13-k1","title":"邊緣缺口：機制","titleEn":"Edge chipping: mechanism","text":"邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。","textEn":"Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。 必須排除的錯判：中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「邊緣缺口」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For edge chipping — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。","中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋","所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格"],"optionsEn":["Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges.","Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass","Using one backside specification for all thin wafers"],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。 保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。 因此不能採用「中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges. Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. Therefore reject: Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass."}},{"id":"a110-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-13"],"title":"邊緣缺口｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Edge chipping | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對邊緣缺口，把「邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For edge chipping, turn \"Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。 將「中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付邊緣缺口的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for edge chipping: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-14-k1","title":"邊緣缺口：機制","titleEn":"Edge chipping: mechanism","text":"邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。","textEn":"Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。 必須排除的錯判：中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「邊緣缺口」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For edge chipping — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格","保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。","中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Using one backside specification for all thin wafers","Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions.","Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass"],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊緣裂紋受後續搬運彎曲放大，中心強度不能代表邊緣。 保留圓周缺陷圖與搬運方向。 因此不能採用「中心厚度合格可忽略邊緣裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Edge flaws are amplified by handling bending; center strength does not represent edges. Retain circumferential defect maps and handling directions. Therefore reject: Ignoring edge cracks after a center-thickness pass."}},{"id":"a110-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-14"],"title":"應力釋放｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Stress relief | mechanism and design","objective":"針對應力釋放，把「移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stress relief, turn \"Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「應力釋放」的模型：移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for stress relief: Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付應力釋放的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for stress relief, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-15-k1","title":"應力釋放：機制","titleEn":"Stress relief: mechanism","text":"移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。","textEn":"Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。 必須排除的錯判：應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「應力釋放」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stress relief — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何","研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度","移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry","Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness","Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。 比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。 因此不能採用「應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何」。","explanationEn":"Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry. Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. Therefore reject: Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry."}},{"id":"a110-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-15"],"title":"應力釋放｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Stress relief | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對應力釋放，把「移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stress relief, turn \"Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。 將「應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付應力釋放的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for stress relief: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-16-k1","title":"應力釋放：機制","titleEn":"Stress relief: mechanism","text":"移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。","textEn":"Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。 必須排除的錯判：應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「應力釋放」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stress relief — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。","應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何","研磨終點就是最終封裝厚度"],"optionsEn":["Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions.","Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry","Equating the grinding endpoint with final package thickness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"移除受損表面可提高強度但同時改變厚度和背面化學。 比較前後曲率、厚度與強度分布。 因此不能採用「應力釋放只改機械性能不改幾何」。","explanationEn":"Removing damaged material can improve strength while changing thickness and chemistry. Compare curvature, thickness and strength distributions. Therefore reject: Assuming stress relief changes mechanics but not geometry."}},{"id":"a110-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-16"],"title":"周邊保留環｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Retained peripheral ring | mechanism and design","objective":"針對周邊保留環，把「保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For retained peripheral ring, turn \"A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「周邊保留環」的模型：保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：同材料薄片在小撓度板模型下 D∝t³。厚度由 100 μm 降至 50 μm，彎曲剛性為原來 1/8；實際破壞還受裂紋、支撐與殘應力控制。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for retained peripheral ring: A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For the same material under small-deflection plate theory, D∝t³. Reducing 100 μm to 50 μm gives one eighth the stiffness; fracture also depends on flaws, support and residual stress. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付周邊保留環的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for retained peripheral ring, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-17-k1","title":"周邊保留環：機制","titleEn":"Retained peripheral ring: mechanism","text":"保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。","textEn":"A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。 必須排除的錯判：厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"同材料薄片在小撓度板模型下 D∝t³。厚度由 100 μm 降至 50 μm，彎曲剛性為原來 1/8；實際破壞還受裂紋、支撐與殘應力控制。","textEn":"For the same material under small-deflection plate theory, D∝t³. Reducing 100 μm to 50 μm gives one eighth the stiffness; fracture also depends on flaws, support and residual stress."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「周邊保留環」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For retained peripheral ring — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["單面高度圖可直接當 TTV","保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。","厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度"],"optionsEn":["Treating a one-sided height map as TTV","A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow.","Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。 畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。 因此不能採用「厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度」。","explanationEn":"A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow. Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. Therefore reject: Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick."}},{"id":"a110-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-17"],"title":"周邊保留環｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Retained peripheral ring | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對周邊保留環，把「保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For retained peripheral ring, turn \"A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。 將「厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：同材料薄片在小撓度板模型下 D∝t³。厚度由 100 μm 降至 50 μm，彎曲剛性為原來 1/8；實際破壞還受裂紋、支撐與殘應力控制。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For the same material under small-deflection plate theory, D∝t³. Reducing 100 μm to 50 μm gives one eighth the stiffness; fracture also depends on flaws, support and residual stress. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付周邊保留環的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for retained peripheral ring: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-18-k1","title":"周邊保留環：機制","titleEn":"Retained peripheral ring: mechanism","text":"保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。","textEn":"A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。 必須排除的錯判：厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"同材料薄片在小撓度板模型下 D∝t³。厚度由 100 μm 降至 50 μm，彎曲剛性為原來 1/8；實際破壞還受裂紋、支撐與殘應力控制。","textEn":"For the same material under small-deflection plate theory, D∝t³. Reducing 100 μm to 50 μm gives one eighth the stiffness; fracture also depends on flaws, support and residual stress."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「周邊保留環」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For retained peripheral ring — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度","單面高度圖可直接當 TTV","畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。"],"optionsEn":["Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick","Treating a one-sided height map as TTV","Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保留周邊厚環可增加薄片搬運剛性，但會改變後續分離路徑。 畫薄區、過渡區及厚環的受力。 因此不能採用「厚環支撐等同全片均勻厚度」。","explanationEn":"A thick peripheral ring improves handling stiffness but changes separation flow. Draw loads in thin, transition and ring regions. Therefore reject: Treating ring-supported wafers as uniformly thick."}}]},{"id":"a110-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"背面驗收","titleEn":"Backside acceptance","description":"針對背面驗收完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for backside acceptance, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a110-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-18"],"title":"破裂統計｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Fracture statistics | mechanism and design","objective":"針對破裂統計，把「脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fracture statistics, turn \"Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「破裂統計」的模型：脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for fracture statistics: Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付破裂統計的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for fracture statistics, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-19-k1","title":"破裂統計：機制","titleEn":"Fracture statistics: mechanism","text":"脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。","textEn":"Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。 必須排除的錯判：最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. Misinterpretation to reject: Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破裂統計」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fracture statistics — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。","最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度","保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力"],"optionsEn":["Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail.","Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability","Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading"],"answer":0,"explanation":"脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。 比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。 因此不能採用「最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度」。","explanationEn":"Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail. Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. Therefore reject: Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability."}},{"id":"a110-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-19"],"title":"破裂統計｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Fracture statistics | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對破裂統計，把「脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fracture statistics, turn \"Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。 將「最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付破裂統計的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for fracture statistics: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-20-k1","title":"破裂統計：機制","titleEn":"Fracture statistics: mechanism","text":"脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。","textEn":"Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。 必須排除的錯判：最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. Misinterpretation to reject: Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「破裂統計」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fracture statistics — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["保護膜厚即可保證所有凸塊不受力","比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。","最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Assuming film thickness prevents every bump from loading","Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry.","Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"脆性強度由缺陷分布控制，平均值不足以描述低端失效。 比較相同測試幾何下的分位數與樣本量。 因此不能採用「最高強度樣本可代表整批可靠度」。","explanationEn":"Brittle strength depends on flaw distribution; means hide the weak tail. Compare quantiles and sample sizes at identical test geometry. Therefore reject: Using the strongest sample to represent lot reliability."}},{"id":"a110-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-20"],"title":"薄片轉移｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thin-wafer transfer | mechanism and design","objective":"針對薄片轉移，把「真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thin-wafer transfer, turn \"Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「薄片轉移」的模型：真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thin-wafer transfer: Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付薄片轉移的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thin-wafer transfer, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-21-k1","title":"薄片轉移：機制","titleEn":"Thin-wafer transfer: mechanism","text":"真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。","textEn":"Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。 必須排除的錯判：晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄片轉移」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thin-wafer transfer — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷","最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋","真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage","Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks","Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans."],"answer":2,"explanation":"真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。 逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。 因此不能採用「晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷」。","explanationEn":"Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans. Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. Therefore reject: Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage."}},{"id":"a110-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-21"],"title":"薄片轉移｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thin-wafer transfer | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對薄片轉移，把「真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thin-wafer transfer, turn \"Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。 將「晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付薄片轉移的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thin-wafer transfer: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-22-k1","title":"薄片轉移：機制","titleEn":"Thin-wafer transfer: mechanism","text":"真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。","textEn":"Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。 必須排除的錯判：晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄片轉移」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thin-wafer transfer — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。","晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷","最後表面光滑就無次表面裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station.","Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage","Equating smooth surfaces with no subsurface cracks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"真空夾持、載板和膜框切換改變支撐跨距。 逐站標出跨距及厚度最薄處。 因此不能採用「晶圓未破就表示沒有潛在搬運損傷」。","explanationEn":"Vacuum chucks, carriers and frames change unsupported spans. Mark spans and thinnest locations at each station. Therefore reject: Assuming unbroken wafers have no latent handling damage."}},{"id":"a110-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-22"],"title":"後段交接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Downstream handoff | mechanism and design","objective":"針對後段交接，把「TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For downstream handoff, turn \"TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「後段交接」的模型：TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按下站功能分別列接受條件。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for downstream handoff: TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Define acceptance by the next station's function. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按下站功能分別列接受條件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define acceptance by the next station's function. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one backside specification for all thin wafers. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付後段交接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for downstream handoff, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-23-k1","title":"後段交接：機制","titleEn":"Downstream handoff: mechanism","text":"TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。","textEn":"TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按下站功能分別列接受條件。 必須排除的錯判：所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define acceptance by the next station's function. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one backside specification for all thin wafers. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「後段交接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For downstream handoff — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同","TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。","所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal bending strength in every direction","TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements.","Using one backside specification for all thin wafers"],"answer":1,"explanation":"TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。 按下站功能分別列接受條件。 因此不能採用「所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格」。","explanationEn":"TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements. Define acceptance by the next station's function. Therefore reject: Using one backside specification for all thin wafers."}},{"id":"a110-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a110-v9-23"],"title":"後段交接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Downstream handoff | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對後段交接，把「TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For downstream handoff, turn \"TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按下站功能分別列接受條件。 將「所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Define acceptance by the next station's function. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using one backside specification for all thin wafers\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按下站功能分別列接受條件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define acceptance by the next station's function. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one backside specification for all thin wafers. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付後段交接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for downstream handoff: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a110-v9-24-k1","title":"後段交接：機制","titleEn":"Downstream handoff: mechanism","text":"TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。","textEn":"TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a110-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按下站功能分別列接受條件。 必須排除的錯判：所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define acceptance by the next station's function. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one backside specification for all thin wafers. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「後段交接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For downstream handoff — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格","所有方向的彎曲強度可視為相同","按下站功能分別列接受條件。"],"optionsEn":["Using one backside specification for all thin wafers","Assuming equal bending strength in every direction","Define acceptance by the next station's function."],"answer":2,"explanation":"TSV、光學或背金屬用途對背面粗糙度和殘留有不同要求。 按下站功能分別列接受條件。 因此不能採用「所有薄晶圓可用一套背面規格」。","explanationEn":"TSV, optical and backside-metal uses impose different roughness/residue requirements. Define acceptance by the next station's function. Therefore reject: Using one backside specification for all thin wafers."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-handling","subcategoryTitle":"薄化、切割與晶粒搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thinning, dicing and die handling","photoId":"v8-wafer"},{"id":"a111","title":"雷射隱形切割","titleEn":"Laser stealth dicing","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入內部改質層、裂紋傳播與薄晶粒強度。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore internal modified layers, crack propagation and thin-die strength, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["材料與路徑","內部改質","分離與邊緣","驗證與整合"],"labelsEn":["Material and path","Internal modification","Separation and edges","Validation and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a111-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"材料與路徑","titleEn":"Material and path","description":"針對材料與路徑完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for material and path, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a111-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"光穿透條件｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Optical penetration | mechanism and design","objective":"針對光穿透條件，把「焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For optical penetration, turn \"The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「光穿透條件」的模型：焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for optical penetration: The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one optical path for every wafer material. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光穿透條件的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for optical penetration, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-01-k1","title":"光穿透條件：機制","titleEn":"Optical penetration: mechanism","text":"焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。","textEn":"The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。 必須排除的錯判：所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one optical path for every wafer material. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光穿透條件」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For optical penetration — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。","所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路","表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗"],"optionsEn":["The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth.","Using one optical path for every wafer material","Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。 畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。 因此不能採用「所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路」。","explanationEn":"The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth. Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. Therefore reject: Using one optical path for every wafer material."}},{"id":"a111-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-01"],"title":"光穿透條件｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Optical penetration | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對光穿透條件，把「焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For optical penetration, turn \"The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。 將「所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using one optical path for every wafer material\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one optical path for every wafer material. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光穿透條件的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for optical penetration: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-02-k1","title":"光穿透條件：機制","titleEn":"Optical penetration: mechanism","text":"焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。","textEn":"The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。 必須排除的錯判：所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one optical path for every wafer material. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光穿透條件」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For optical penetration — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗","畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。","所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路"],"optionsEn":["Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification","Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction.","Using one optical path for every wafer material"],"answer":1,"explanation":"焦點須位於材料內部，入射面與材料吸收決定可達深度。 畫光路及表面膜層，辨認遮擋。 因此不能採用「所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路」。","explanationEn":"The focus must lie inside the material; entry surface and absorption limit depth. Draw the optical path and films, identifying obstruction. Therefore reject: Using one optical path for every wafer material."}},{"id":"a111-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-02"],"title":"街道與功能區｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Streets and active areas | mechanism and design","objective":"針對街道與功能區，把「改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For streets and active areas, turn \"Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「街道與功能區」的模型：改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for streets and active areas: Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：街道中心對準就無需保護餘量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付街道與功能區的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for streets and active areas, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-03-k1","title":"街道與功能區：機制","titleEn":"Streets and active areas: mechanism","text":"改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。","textEn":"Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。 必須排除的錯判：街道中心對準就無需保護餘量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. Misinterpretation to reject: Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「街道與功能區」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For streets and active areas — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["街道中心對準就無需保護餘量","交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度","改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。"],"optionsEn":["Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment","Assuming order never affects thin-die strength","Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。 疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。 因此不能採用「街道中心對準就無需保護餘量」。","explanationEn":"Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs. Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. Therefore reject: Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment."}},{"id":"a111-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-03"],"title":"街道與功能區｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Streets and active areas | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對街道與功能區，把「改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For streets and active areas, turn \"Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。 將「街道中心對準就無需保護餘量」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. Challenge the hypothesis \"Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：街道中心對準就無需保護餘量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付街道與功能區的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for streets and active areas: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-04-k1","title":"街道與功能區：機制","titleEn":"Streets and active areas: mechanism","text":"改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。","textEn":"Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。 必須排除的錯判：街道中心對準就無需保護餘量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. Misinterpretation to reject: Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「街道與功能區」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For streets and active areas — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。","街道中心對準就無需保護餘量","交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度"],"optionsEn":["Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error.","Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment","Assuming order never affects thin-die strength"],"answer":0,"explanation":"改質和裂開區必須留在電路保護邊界外。 疊合街道、密封環及定位誤差。 因此不能採用「街道中心對準就無需保護餘量」。","explanationEn":"Modification and fracture zones must remain outside circuit keep-outs. Overlay streets, seal rings and positioning error. Therefore reject: Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment."}},{"id":"a111-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-04"],"title":"厚度與焦深｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thickness and focal depth | mechanism and design","objective":"針對厚度與焦深，把「厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thickness and focal depth, turn \"Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「厚度與焦深」的模型：厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thickness and focal depth: Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Register thickness maps and focal references. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register thickness maps and focal references. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付厚度與焦深的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thickness and focal depth, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-05-k1","title":"厚度與焦深：機制","titleEn":"Thickness and focal depth: mechanism","text":"厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。","textEn":"Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。 必須排除的錯判：名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register thickness maps and focal references. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「厚度與焦深」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thickness and focal depth — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同","厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。","名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖"],"optionsEn":["Equating frame expansion with equal street forces","Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside.","Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。 將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。 因此不能採用「名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖」。","explanationEn":"Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside. Register thickness maps and focal references. Therefore reject: Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness."}},{"id":"a111-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-05"],"title":"厚度與焦深｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thickness and focal depth | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對厚度與焦深，把「厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thickness and focal depth, turn \"Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。 將「名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Register thickness maps and focal references. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register thickness maps and focal references. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付厚度與焦深的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thickness and focal depth: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-06-k1","title":"厚度與焦深：機制","titleEn":"Thickness and focal depth: mechanism","text":"厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。","textEn":"Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。 必須排除的錯判：名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register thickness maps and focal references. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「厚度與焦深」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thickness and focal depth — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖","擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同","將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。"],"optionsEn":["Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness","Equating frame expansion with equal street forces","Register thickness maps and focal references."],"answer":2,"explanation":"厚度變化改變內部焦點位置相對背面的距離。 將厚度地圖與焦點基準配準。 因此不能採用「名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖」。","explanationEn":"Thickness variation changes focus distance from the backside. Register thickness maps and focal references. Therefore reject: Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness."}}]},{"id":"a111-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"內部改質","titleEn":"Internal modification","description":"針對內部改質完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for internal modification, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a111-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-06"],"title":"改質層概念｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Modified-layer concept | mechanism and design","objective":"針對改質層概念，把「局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For modified-layer concept, turn \"Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「改質層概念」的模型：局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for modified-layer concept: Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：隱形切割等同表面燒蝕。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付改質層概念的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for modified-layer concept, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-07-k1","title":"改質層概念：機制","titleEn":"Modified-layer concept: mechanism","text":"局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。","textEn":"Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。 必須排除的錯判：隱形切割等同表面燒蝕。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「改質層概念」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For modified-layer concept — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。","隱形切割等同表面燒蝕","無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench.","Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation","Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。 用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。 因此不能採用「隱形切割等同表面燒蝕」。","explanationEn":"Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench. Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. Therefore reject: Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation."}},{"id":"a111-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-07"],"title":"改質層概念｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Modified-layer concept | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對改質層概念，把「局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For modified-layer concept, turn \"Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。 將「隱形切割等同表面燒蝕」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：隱形切割等同表面燒蝕。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付改質層概念的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for modified-layer concept: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-08-k1","title":"改質層概念：機制","titleEn":"Modified-layer concept: mechanism","text":"局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。","textEn":"Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。 必須排除的錯判：隱形切割等同表面燒蝕。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「改質層概念」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For modified-layer concept — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋","用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。","隱形切割等同表面燒蝕"],"optionsEn":["Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks","Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section.","Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部材料改變形成裂開起始，並非以表面燒蝕切出完整溝槽。 用截面區分表面去除和內部改質。 因此不能採用「隱形切割等同表面燒蝕」。","explanationEn":"Local modification initiates fracture rather than ablating a full surface trench. Distinguish surface removal and internal modification in section. Therefore reject: Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation."}},{"id":"a111-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-08"],"title":"晶向與裂紋｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Orientation and cracks | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶向與裂紋，把「裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For orientation and cracks, turn \"Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶向與裂紋」的模型：裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較正交街道邊緣形貌。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for orientation and cracks: Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較正交街道邊緣形貌。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶向與裂紋的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for orientation and cracks, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-09-k1","title":"晶向與裂紋：機制","titleEn":"Orientation and cracks: mechanism","text":"裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。","textEn":"Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較正交街道邊緣形貌。 必須排除的錯判：裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶向與裂紋」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For orientation and cracks — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線","無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測","裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly","Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust","Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory."],"answer":2,"explanation":"裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。 比較正交街道邊緣形貌。 因此不能採用「裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線」。","explanationEn":"Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory. Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. Therefore reject: Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly."}},{"id":"a111-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-09"],"title":"晶向與裂紋｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Orientation and cracks | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶向與裂紋，把「裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For orientation and cracks, turn \"Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較正交街道邊緣形貌。 將「裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較正交街道邊緣形貌。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶向與裂紋的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for orientation and cracks: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-10-k1","title":"晶向與裂紋：機制","titleEn":"Orientation and cracks: mechanism","text":"裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。","textEn":"Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較正交街道邊緣形貌。 必須排除的錯判：裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶向與裂紋」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For orientation and cracks — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較正交街道邊緣形貌。","裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線","無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測"],"optionsEn":["Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets.","Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly","Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust"],"answer":0,"explanation":"裂紋路徑會受晶向和應力狀態影響，不能僅依光束軌跡預測。 比較正交街道邊緣形貌。 因此不能採用「裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線」。","explanationEn":"Cracks depend on crystal orientation and stress, not just beam trajectory. Compare edge morphology along orthogonal streets. Therefore reject: Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly."}},{"id":"a111-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-10"],"title":"改質連續性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Modification continuity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對改質連續性，把「不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For modification continuity, turn \"Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「改質連續性」的模型：不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for modification continuity: Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付改質連續性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for modification continuity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-11-k1","title":"改質連續性：機制","titleEn":"Modification continuity: mechanism","text":"不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。","textEn":"Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。 必須排除的錯判：表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「改質連續性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For modification continuity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["機械分離成功即電性一定不變","不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。","表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗"],"optionsEn":["Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior","Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection.","Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。 以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。 因此不能採用「表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗」。","explanationEn":"Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection. Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. Therefore reject: Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification."}},{"id":"a111-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-11"],"title":"改質連續性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Modification continuity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對改質連續性，把「不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For modification continuity, turn \"Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。 將「表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付改質連續性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for modification continuity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-12-k1","title":"改質連續性：機制","titleEn":"Modification continuity: mechanism","text":"不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。","textEn":"Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。 必須排除的錯判：表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「改質連續性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For modification continuity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗","機械分離成功即電性一定不變","以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。"],"optionsEn":["Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification","Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior","Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不連續弱化區可能造成未分離或偏折裂紋。 以分離後未斷區反推改質連續性。 因此不能採用「表面看不見痕跡即表示改質失敗」。","explanationEn":"Discontinuous weakening can cause incomplete separation or deflection. Use unseparated segments to evaluate continuity. Therefore reject: Treating invisible surface marks as failed modification."}}]},{"id":"a111-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"分離與邊緣","titleEn":"Separation and edges","description":"針對分離與邊緣完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for separation and edges, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a111-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-12"],"title":"研磨前後順序｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Grinding order | mechanism and design","objective":"針對研磨前後順序，把「SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For grinding order, turn \"SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「研磨前後順序」的模型：SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for grinding order: SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming order never affects thin-die strength. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付研磨前後順序的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for grinding order, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-13-k1","title":"研磨前後順序：機制","titleEn":"Grinding order: mechanism","text":"SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。","textEn":"SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。 必須排除的錯判：交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming order never affects thin-die strength. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「研磨前後順序」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For grinding order — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。","交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度","已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片"],"optionsEn":["SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order.","Assuming order never affects thin-die strength","Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die"],"answer":0,"explanation":"SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。 比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。 因此不能採用「交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度」。","explanationEn":"SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order. Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. Therefore reject: Assuming order never affects thin-die strength."}},{"id":"a111-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-13"],"title":"研磨前後順序｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Grinding order | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對研磨前後順序，把「SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For grinding order, turn \"SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。 將「交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming order never affects thin-die strength\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming order never affects thin-die strength. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付研磨前後順序的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for grinding order: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-14-k1","title":"研磨前後順序：機制","titleEn":"Grinding order: mechanism","text":"SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。","textEn":"SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。 必須排除的錯判：交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming order never affects thin-die strength. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「研磨前後順序」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For grinding order — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片","比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。","交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度"],"optionsEn":["Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die","Compare thin-first and thin-later flows.","Assuming order never affects thin-die strength"],"answer":1,"explanation":"SDBG 的加工順序使研磨和裂紋發展共同影響最後邊緣。 比較先薄化與後薄化兩條流程。 因此不能採用「交換順序不影響薄晶粒強度」。","explanationEn":"SDBG couples grinding and crack evolution through process order. Compare thin-first and thin-later flows. Therefore reject: Assuming order never affects thin-die strength."}},{"id":"a111-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-14"],"title":"膜框擴張｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Tape expansion | mechanism and design","objective":"針對膜框擴張，把「膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tape expansion, turn \"Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「膜框擴張」的模型：膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for tape expansion: Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating frame expansion with equal street forces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膜框擴張的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for tape expansion, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-15-k1","title":"膜框擴張：機制","titleEn":"Tape expansion: mechanism","text":"膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。","textEn":"Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。 必須排除的錯判：擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating frame expansion with equal street forces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膜框擴張」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tape expansion — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同","所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路","膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。"],"optionsEn":["Equating frame expansion with equal street forces","Using one optical path for every wafer material","Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。 量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。 因此不能採用「擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同」。","explanationEn":"Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation. Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. Therefore reject: Equating frame expansion with equal street forces."}},{"id":"a111-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-15"],"title":"膜框擴張｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Tape expansion | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對膜框擴張，把「膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tape expansion, turn \"Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。 將「擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating frame expansion with equal street forces\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating frame expansion with equal street forces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膜框擴張的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for tape expansion: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-16-k1","title":"膜框擴張：機制","titleEn":"Tape expansion: mechanism","text":"膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。","textEn":"Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。 必須排除的錯判：擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating frame expansion with equal street forces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膜框擴張」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tape expansion — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。","擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同","所有晶圓材料都可共用同一光路"],"optionsEn":["Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation.","Equating frame expansion with equal street forces","Using one optical path for every wafer material"],"answer":0,"explanation":"膜框擴張把載荷傳入街道，非均勻張力可造成不同分離量。 量中心與邊緣晶粒間隙和旋轉。 因此不能採用「擴張距離相同即每條街道受力相同」。","explanationEn":"Tape expansion loads streets; uneven tension causes uneven separation. Measure center/edge die gaps and rotation. Therefore reject: Equating frame expansion with equal street forces."}},{"id":"a111-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-16"],"title":"崩邊與裂紋深度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Chipping and crack depth | mechanism and design","objective":"針對崩邊與裂紋深度，把「邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chipping and crack depth, turn \"Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「崩邊與裂紋深度」的模型：邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設街道寬 40 μm、對準誤差界限 ±3 μm、受影響區寬 12 μm，單側理想幾何餘量為 (40−12)/2−3=11 μm；還未包含裂紋偏折和保護區。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for chipping and crack depth: Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For a hypothetical 40 μm street, ±3 μm alignment bound and 12 μm affected zone, one-sided geometric margin is (40−12)/2−3=11 μm before crack deviation and keep-outs. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付崩邊與裂紋深度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for chipping and crack depth, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-17-k1","title":"崩邊與裂紋深度：機制","titleEn":"Chipping and crack depth: mechanism","text":"邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。","textEn":"Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。 必須排除的錯判：無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設街道寬 40 μm、對準誤差界限 ±3 μm、受影響區寬 12 μm，單側理想幾何餘量為 (40−12)/2−3=11 μm；還未包含裂紋偏折和保護區。","textEn":"For a hypothetical 40 μm street, ±3 μm alignment bound and 12 μm affected zone, one-sided geometric margin is (40−12)/2−3=11 μm before crack deviation and keep-outs."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「崩邊與裂紋深度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chipping and crack depth — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["街道中心對準就無需保護餘量","邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。","無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment","Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength.","Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。 結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。 因此不能採用「無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength. Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. Therefore reject: Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks."}},{"id":"a111-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-17"],"title":"崩邊與裂紋深度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Chipping and crack depth | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對崩邊與裂紋深度，把「邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chipping and crack depth, turn \"Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。 將「無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設街道寬 40 μm、對準誤差界限 ±3 μm、受影響區寬 12 μm，單側理想幾何餘量為 (40−12)/2−3=11 μm；還未包含裂紋偏折和保護區。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For a hypothetical 40 μm street, ±3 μm alignment bound and 12 μm affected zone, one-sided geometric margin is (40−12)/2−3=11 μm before crack deviation and keep-outs. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付崩邊與裂紋深度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for chipping and crack depth: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-18-k1","title":"崩邊與裂紋深度：機制","titleEn":"Chipping and crack depth: mechanism","text":"邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。","textEn":"Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。 必須排除的錯判：無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設街道寬 40 μm、對準誤差界限 ±3 μm、受影響區寬 12 μm，單側理想幾何餘量為 (40−12)/2−3=11 μm；還未包含裂紋偏折和保護區。","textEn":"For a hypothetical 40 μm street, ±3 μm alignment bound and 12 μm affected zone, one-sided geometric margin is (40−12)/2−3=11 μm before crack deviation and keep-outs."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「崩邊與裂紋深度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chipping and crack depth — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋","街道中心對準就無需保護餘量","結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。"],"optionsEn":["Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks","Omitting keep-out margin after center alignment","Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣外觀只顯示表面，次表面裂紋仍可能控制抗折強度。 結合邊緣影像和匹配方向彎曲試驗。 因此不能採用「無可見崩邊即無潛在裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Edge appearance shows the surface; subsurface cracks may control strength. Combine edge images with direction-matched bend tests. Therefore reject: Equating no visible chipping with no latent cracks."}}]},{"id":"a111-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗證與整合","titleEn":"Validation and integration","description":"針對驗證與整合完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for validation and integration, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a111-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-18"],"title":"粒子與拾取｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Particles and pickup | mechanism and design","objective":"針對粒子與拾取，把「分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For particles and pickup, turn \"Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「粒子與拾取」的模型：分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for particles and pickup: Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付粒子與拾取的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for particles and pickup, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-19-k1","title":"粒子與拾取：機制","titleEn":"Particles and pickup: mechanism","text":"分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。","textEn":"Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。 必須排除的錯判：無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粒子與拾取」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For particles and pickup — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。","無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測","名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖"],"optionsEn":["Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding.","Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust","Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。 比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。 因此不能採用「無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測」。","explanationEn":"Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding. Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. Therefore reject: Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust."}},{"id":"a111-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-19"],"title":"粒子與拾取｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Particles and pickup | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對粒子與拾取，把「分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For particles and pickup, turn \"Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。 將「無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付粒子與拾取的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for particles and pickup: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-20-k1","title":"粒子與拾取：機制","titleEn":"Particles and pickup: mechanism","text":"分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。","textEn":"Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。 必須排除的錯判：無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「粒子與拾取」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For particles and pickup — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["名義厚度相同便可省略全片地圖","比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。","無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測"],"optionsEn":["Skipping wafer maps at equal nominal thickness","Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup.","Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分離後顆粒與膜黏著會影響後續高潔淨接合。 比較拾取前後顆粒和晶粒面向。 因此不能採用「無鋸屑就可省略顆粒檢測」。","explanationEn":"Post-separation particles and tape adhesion affect clean bonding. Compare particles and orientation before/after pickup. Therefore reject: Skipping particle inspection because there is no sawdust."}},{"id":"a111-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-20"],"title":"電性保護｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Electrical protection | mechanism and design","objective":"針對電性保護，把「切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For electrical protection, turn \"Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「電性保護」的模型：切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for electrical protection: Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：機械分離成功即電性一定不變。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電性保護的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for electrical protection, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-21-k1","title":"電性保護：機制","titleEn":"Electrical protection: mechanism","text":"切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。","textEn":"Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。 必須排除的錯判：機械分離成功即電性一定不變。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電性保護」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For electrical protection — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["機械分離成功即電性一定不變","隱形切割等同表面燒蝕","切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior","Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation","Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects."],"answer":2,"explanation":"切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。 配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。 因此不能採用「機械分離成功即電性一定不變」。","explanationEn":"Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects. Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. Therefore reject: Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior."}},{"id":"a111-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-21"],"title":"電性保護｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Electrical protection | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對電性保護，把「切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For electrical protection, turn \"Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。 將「機械分離成功即電性一定不變」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：機械分離成功即電性一定不變。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電性保護的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for electrical protection: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-22-k1","title":"電性保護：機制","titleEn":"Electrical protection: mechanism","text":"切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。","textEn":"Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。 必須排除的錯判：機械分離成功即電性一定不變。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電性保護」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For electrical protection — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。","機械分離成功即電性一定不變","隱形切割等同表面燒蝕"],"optionsEn":["Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations.","Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior","Equating stealth dicing with surface ablation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"切割傷害可能接近密封環或引發後續應力敏感缺陷。 配對切割前後電性及邊緣位置。 因此不能採用「機械分離成功即電性一定不變」。","explanationEn":"Dicing damage may approach seal rings or trigger stress-sensitive defects. Pair pre/post electrical data with edge locations. Therefore reject: Assuming successful separation preserves electrical behavior."}},{"id":"a111-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-22"],"title":"路徑驗收｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Route qualification | mechanism and design","objective":"針對路徑驗收，把「材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For route qualification, turn \"Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「路徑驗收」的模型：材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立變更矩陣和見證片組。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for route qualification: Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Build a change matrix and witness set. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立變更矩陣和見證片組。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build a change matrix and witness set. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付路徑驗收的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for route qualification, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-23-k1","title":"路徑驗收：機制","titleEn":"Route qualification: mechanism","text":"材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。","textEn":"Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立變更矩陣和見證片組。 必須排除的錯判：已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build a change matrix and witness set. Misinterpretation to reject: Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「路徑驗收」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For route qualification — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線","材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。","已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片"],"optionsEn":["Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly","Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation.","Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。 建立變更矩陣和見證片組。 因此不能採用「已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片」。","explanationEn":"Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation. Build a change matrix and witness set. Therefore reject: Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die."}},{"id":"a111-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a111-v9-23"],"title":"路徑驗收｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Route qualification | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對路徑驗收，把「材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For route qualification, turn \"Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立變更矩陣和見證片組。 將「已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Build a change matrix and witness set. Challenge the hypothesis \"Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立變更矩陣和見證片組。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build a change matrix and witness set. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付路徑驗收的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for route qualification: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a111-v9-24-k1","title":"路徑驗收：機制","titleEn":"Route qualification: mechanism","text":"材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。","textEn":"Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]},{"id":"a111-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立變更矩陣和見證片組。 必須排除的錯判：已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build a change matrix and witness set. Misinterpretation to reject: Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-dbg"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「路徑驗收」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For route qualification — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片","裂紋永遠完全沿雷射掃描線","建立變更矩陣和見證片組。"],"optionsEn":["Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die","Assuming cracks follow the scan line exactly","Build a change matrix and witness set."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料、膜層和厚度改變需重新確認透光與裂開邊界。 建立變更矩陣和見證片組。 因此不能採用「已驗證矽流程可直接套用所有複合晶片」。","explanationEn":"Material, film and thickness changes require new optical/fracture validation. Build a change matrix and witness set. Therefore reject: Transferring a qualified silicon flow to every composite die."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-handling","subcategoryTitle":"薄化、切割與晶粒搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thinning, dicing and die handling","photoId":"v8-wafer"},{"id":"a112","title":"電漿晶圓切割","titleEn":"Plasma wafer dicing","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入遮罩、深蝕刻及膜框熱邊界。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore masking, deep etch and frame thermal boundaries, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["分離設計","遮罩與載台","蝕刻行為","邊緣與良率"],"labelsEn":["Singulation design","Mask and chuck","Etch behavior","Edges and yield"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a112-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"分離設計","titleEn":"Singulation design","description":"針對分離設計完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for singulation design, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a112-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"街道版圖｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Street layout | mechanism and design","objective":"針對街道版圖，把「遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For street layout, turn \"Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「街道版圖」的模型：遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「列街道逐層材料。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for street layout: Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: List the layer stack in each street. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"列街道逐層材料。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List the layer stack in each street. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming Si etching removes every street material. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付街道版圖的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for street layout, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-01-k1","title":"街道版圖：機制","titleEn":"Street layout: mechanism","text":"遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。","textEn":"Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列街道逐層材料。 必須排除的錯判：矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List the layer stack in each street. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming Si etching removes every street material. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「街道版圖」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For street layout — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。","矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料","垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑"],"optionsEn":["Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon.","Assuming Si etching removes every street material","Equating vertical walls with smooth walls"],"answer":0,"explanation":"遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。 列街道逐層材料。 因此不能採用「矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料」。","explanationEn":"Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon. List the layer stack in each street. Therefore reject: Assuming Si etching removes every street material."}},{"id":"a112-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-01"],"title":"街道版圖｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Street layout | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對街道版圖，把「遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For street layout, turn \"Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：列街道逐層材料。 將「矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: List the layer stack in each street. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming Si etching removes every street material\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"列街道逐層材料。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List the layer stack in each street. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming Si etching removes every street material. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付街道版圖的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for street layout: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-02-k1","title":"街道版圖：機制","titleEn":"Street layout: mechanism","text":"遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。","textEn":"Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列街道逐層材料。 必須排除的錯判：矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List the layer stack in each street. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming Si etching removes every street material. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「街道版圖」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For street layout — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑","列街道逐層材料。","矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料"],"optionsEn":["Equating vertical walls with smooth walls","List the layer stack in each street.","Assuming Si etching removes every street material"],"answer":1,"explanation":"遮罩開口需避開金屬與功能層，街道並非只有矽。 列街道逐層材料。 因此不能採用「矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料」。","explanationEn":"Mask openings must accommodate metals and functional films; streets are not pure silicon. List the layer stack in each street. Therefore reject: Assuming Si etching removes every street material."}},{"id":"a112-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-02"],"title":"圖形密度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pattern density | mechanism and design","objective":"針對圖形密度，把「開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pattern density, turn \"Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「圖形密度」的模型：開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pattern density: Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal width with equal etch rate. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付圖形密度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pattern density, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-03-k1","title":"圖形密度：機制","titleEn":"Pattern density: mechanism","text":"開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。","textEn":"Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。 必須排除的錯判：相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal width with equal etch rate. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圖形密度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pattern density — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率","速率只由總加工時間決定","開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal width with equal etch rate","Assuming etch depth depends only on time","Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。 比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。 因此不能採用「相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率」。","explanationEn":"Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load. Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. Therefore reject: Equating equal width with equal etch rate."}},{"id":"a112-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-03"],"title":"圖形密度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pattern density | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對圖形密度，把「開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pattern density, turn \"Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。 將「相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating equal width with equal etch rate\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal width with equal etch rate. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付圖形密度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pattern density: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-04-k1","title":"圖形密度：機制","titleEn":"Pattern density: mechanism","text":"開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。","textEn":"Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。 必須排除的錯判：相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal width with equal etch rate. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圖形密度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pattern density — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。","相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率","速率只由總加工時間決定"],"optionsEn":["Compare depth for sparse and dense streets.","Equating equal width with equal etch rate","Assuming etch depth depends only on time"],"answer":0,"explanation":"開口面積比影響反應物供應與總熱負荷。 比較稀疏與密集街道的深度。 因此不能採用「相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率」。","explanationEn":"Open-area fraction affects reactant supply and heat load. Compare depth for sparse and dense streets. Therefore reject: Equating equal width with equal etch rate."}},{"id":"a112-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-04"],"title":"遮罩預算｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Mask budget | mechanism and design","objective":"針對遮罩預算，把「遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mask budget, turn \"Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「遮罩預算」的模型：遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for mask budget: Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付遮罩預算的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for mask budget, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-05-k1","title":"遮罩預算：機制","titleEn":"Mask budget: mechanism","text":"遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。","textEn":"Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。 必須排除的錯判：平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遮罩預算」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mask budget — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開","遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。","平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活"],"optionsEn":["Equating mean depth with complete singulation","Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity.","Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere"],"answer":1,"explanation":"遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。 用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。 因此不能採用「平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活」。","explanationEn":"Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity. Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. Therefore reject: Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere."}},{"id":"a112-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-05"],"title":"遮罩預算｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Mask budget | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對遮罩預算，把「遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mask budget, turn \"Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。 將「平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付遮罩預算的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for mask budget: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-06-k1","title":"遮罩預算：機制","titleEn":"Mask budget: mechanism","text":"遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。","textEn":"Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。 必須排除的錯判：平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遮罩預算」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mask budget — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活","平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開","用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。"],"optionsEn":["Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere","Equating mean depth with complete singulation","Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"遮罩選擇比須保留過蝕與非均勻性餘量。 用最慢區深度和最大遮罩損失估算。 因此不能採用「平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活」。","explanationEn":"Mask selectivity needs margin for overetch and nonuniformity. Use slowest-site depth and greatest mask loss. Therefore reject: Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere."}}]},{"id":"a112-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"遮罩與載台","titleEn":"Mask and chuck","description":"針對遮罩與載台完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for mask and chuck, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a112-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-06"],"title":"膜框相容性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Tape-frame compatibility | mechanism and design","objective":"針對膜框相容性，把「膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tape-frame compatibility, turn \"Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「膜框相容性」的模型：膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for tape-frame compatibility: Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating chamber fit with material compatibility. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膜框相容性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for tape-frame compatibility, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-07-k1","title":"膜框相容性：機制","titleEn":"Tape-frame compatibility: mechanism","text":"膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。","textEn":"Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。 必須排除的錯判：膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating chamber fit with material compatibility. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膜框相容性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tape-frame compatibility — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。","膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容","非機械切割就不會傷害電路"],"optionsEn":["Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility.","Equating chamber fit with material compatibility","Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits"],"answer":0,"explanation":"膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。 對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。 因此不能採用「膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容」。","explanationEn":"Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility. Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. Therefore reject: Equating chamber fit with material compatibility."}},{"id":"a112-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-07"],"title":"膜框相容性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Tape-frame compatibility | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對膜框相容性，把「膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tape-frame compatibility, turn \"Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。 將「膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating chamber fit with material compatibility\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating chamber fit with material compatibility. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膜框相容性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for tape-frame compatibility: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-08-k1","title":"膜框相容性：機制","titleEn":"Tape-frame compatibility: mechanism","text":"膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。","textEn":"Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。 必須排除的錯判：膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating chamber fit with material compatibility. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膜框相容性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tape-frame compatibility — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["非機械切割就不會傷害電路","對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。","膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容"],"optionsEn":["Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits","Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination.","Equating chamber fit with material compatibility"],"answer":1,"explanation":"膜材揮發、耐熱與夾持決定能否承受真空加工。 對照見證膜的外觀、黏力及污染。 因此不能採用「膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容」。","explanationEn":"Tape outgassing, heat resistance and clamping govern vacuum compatibility. Check witness-film appearance, adhesion and contamination. Therefore reject: Equating chamber fit with material compatibility."}},{"id":"a112-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-08"],"title":"散熱接觸｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal contact | mechanism and design","objective":"針對散熱接觸，把「薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal contact, turn \"Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「散熱接觸」的模型：薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal contact: Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付散熱接觸的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal contact, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-09-k1","title":"散熱接觸：機制","titleEn":"Thermal contact: mechanism","text":"薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。","textEn":"Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。 必須排除的錯判：載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「散熱接觸」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal contact — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度","裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留","薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。"],"optionsEn":["Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location","Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough","Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。 比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。 因此不能採用「載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度」。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature. Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. Therefore reject: Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location."}},{"id":"a112-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-09"],"title":"散熱接觸｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal contact | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對散熱接觸，把「薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal contact, turn \"Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。 將「載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付散熱接觸的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal contact: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-10-k1","title":"散熱接觸：機制","titleEn":"Thermal contact: mechanism","text":"薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。","textEn":"Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。 必須排除的錯判：載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「散熱接觸」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal contact — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。","載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度","裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留"],"optionsEn":["Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration.","Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location","Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough"],"answer":0,"explanation":"薄晶圓與膜框的接觸熱阻影響局部溫度。 比較熱見證與邊緣變色位置。 因此不能採用「載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度」。","explanationEn":"Contact resistance between thin wafer and frame affects local temperature. Compare thermal witnesses and edge discoloration. Therefore reject: Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location."}},{"id":"a112-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-10"],"title":"側壁循環｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Sidewall cycles | mechanism and design","objective":"針對側壁循環，把「交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sidewall cycles, turn \"Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「側壁循環」的模型：交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for sidewall cycles: Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating vertical walls with smooth walls. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付側壁循環的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for sidewall cycles, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-11-k1","title":"側壁循環：機制","titleEn":"Sidewall cycles: mechanism","text":"交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。","textEn":"Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。 必須排除的錯判：垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating vertical walls with smooth walls. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側壁循環」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sidewall cycles — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強","交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。","垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑"],"optionsEn":["Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die","Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle.","Equating vertical walls with smooth walls"],"answer":1,"explanation":"交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。 量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。 因此不能採用「垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑」。","explanationEn":"Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle. Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. Therefore reject: Equating vertical walls with smooth walls."}},{"id":"a112-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-11"],"title":"側壁循環｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Sidewall cycles | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對側壁循環，把「交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sidewall cycles, turn \"Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。 將「垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating vertical walls with smooth walls\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating vertical walls with smooth walls. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付側壁循環的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for sidewall cycles: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-12-k1","title":"側壁循環：機制","titleEn":"Sidewall cycles: mechanism","text":"交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。","textEn":"Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。 必須排除的錯判：垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating vertical walls with smooth walls. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側壁循環」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sidewall cycles — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑","電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強","量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。"],"optionsEn":["Equating vertical walls with smooth walls","Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die","Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude."],"answer":2,"explanation":"交替移除和保護形成深溝，循環紋路與側壁角要分開評估。 量上中下寬度和紋路幅度。 因此不能採用「垂直側壁即可保證表面平滑」。","explanationEn":"Alternating removal and protection forms trenches; assess scallops separately from wall angle. Measure top/mid/bottom width and scallop amplitude. Therefore reject: Equating vertical walls with smooth walls."}}]},{"id":"a112-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"蝕刻行為","titleEn":"Etch behavior","description":"針對蝕刻行為完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for etch behavior, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a112-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-12"],"title":"深寬比效應｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Aspect-ratio effects | mechanism and design","objective":"針對深寬比效應，把「深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For aspect-ratio effects, turn \"Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「深寬比效應」的模型：深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for aspect-ratio effects: Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare depth curves across opening widths. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare depth curves across opening widths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：速率只由總加工時間決定。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming etch depth depends only on time. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付深寬比效應的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for aspect-ratio effects, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-13-k1","title":"深寬比效應：機制","titleEn":"Aspect-ratio effects: mechanism","text":"深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。","textEn":"Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。 必須排除的錯判：速率只由總加工時間決定。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare depth curves across opening widths. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming etch depth depends only on time. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「深寬比效應」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For aspect-ratio effects — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。","速率只由總加工時間決定","只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本"],"optionsEn":["Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces.","Assuming etch depth depends only on time","Comparing cost using chamber time alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。 比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。 因此不能採用「速率只由總加工時間決定」。","explanationEn":"Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces. Compare depth curves across opening widths. Therefore reject: Assuming etch depth depends only on time."}},{"id":"a112-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-13"],"title":"深寬比效應｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Aspect-ratio effects | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對深寬比效應，把「深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For aspect-ratio effects, turn \"Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。 將「速率只由總加工時間決定」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare depth curves across opening widths. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming etch depth depends only on time\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare depth curves across opening widths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：速率只由總加工時間決定。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming etch depth depends only on time. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付深寬比效應的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for aspect-ratio effects: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-14-k1","title":"深寬比效應：機制","titleEn":"Aspect-ratio effects: mechanism","text":"深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。","textEn":"Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。 必須排除的錯判：速率只由總加工時間決定。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare depth curves across opening widths. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming etch depth depends only on time. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「深寬比效應」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For aspect-ratio effects — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本","比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。","速率只由總加工時間決定"],"optionsEn":["Comparing cost using chamber time alone","Compare depth curves across opening widths.","Assuming etch depth depends only on time"],"answer":1,"explanation":"深溝的傳輸限制使底部反應與表面不同。 比較不同開口寬度的深度曲線。 因此不能採用「速率只由總加工時間決定」。","explanationEn":"Transport limitations make deep-trench bottoms differ from surfaces. Compare depth curves across opening widths. Therefore reject: Assuming etch depth depends only on time."}},{"id":"a112-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-14"],"title":"穿透終點｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Breakthrough endpoint | mechanism and design","objective":"針對穿透終點，把「最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For breakthrough endpoint, turn \"Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「穿透終點」的模型：最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for breakthrough endpoint: Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating mean depth with complete singulation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付穿透終點的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for breakthrough endpoint, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-15-k1","title":"穿透終點：機制","titleEn":"Breakthrough endpoint: mechanism","text":"最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。","textEn":"Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。 必須排除的錯判：平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating mean depth with complete singulation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「穿透終點」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For breakthrough endpoint — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開","矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料","最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。"],"optionsEn":["Equating mean depth with complete singulation","Assuming Si etching removes every street material","Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached."],"answer":2,"explanation":"最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。 定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。 因此不能採用「平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開」。","explanationEn":"Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached. Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. Therefore reject: Equating mean depth with complete singulation."}},{"id":"a112-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-15"],"title":"穿透終點｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Breakthrough endpoint | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對穿透終點，把「最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For breakthrough endpoint, turn \"Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。 將「平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating mean depth with complete singulation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating mean depth with complete singulation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付穿透終點的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for breakthrough endpoint: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-16-k1","title":"穿透終點：機制","titleEn":"Breakthrough endpoint: mechanism","text":"最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。","textEn":"Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。 必須排除的錯判：平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating mean depth with complete singulation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「穿透終點」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For breakthrough endpoint — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。","平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開","矽可蝕刻就能直接穿透全部街道材料"],"optionsEn":["Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk.","Equating mean depth with complete singulation","Assuming Si etching removes every street material"],"answer":0,"explanation":"最先穿透處暴露膜框，最慢處仍未分離。 定義最早、最晚終點和過蝕風險。 因此不能採用「平均深度達厚度就表示全部切開」。","explanationEn":"Early breakthrough exposes tape while slow sites remain attached. Define earliest/latest endpoints and overetch risk. Therefore reject: Equating mean depth with complete singulation."}},{"id":"a112-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-16"],"title":"充電與電路｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Charging and circuits | mechanism and design","objective":"針對充電與電路，把「電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For charging and circuits, turn \"Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「充電與電路」的模型：電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用匹配電路作前後電性比較。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設晶圓厚 50 μm、街道開口 10 μm，名義深寬比為 5。若遮罩消耗 2 μm、矽移除 50 μm，表觀選擇比為 25；不能用它預測不同圖形負載。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for charging and circuits: Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare matched circuits before and after processing. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: A hypothetical 50 μm wafer and 10 μm opening give aspect ratio 5. Removing 50 μm Si with 2 μm mask loss gives apparent selectivity 25, not a prediction for different pattern loading. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"用匹配電路作前後電性比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare matched circuits before and after processing. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：非機械切割就不會傷害電路。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付充電與電路的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for charging and circuits, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-17-k1","title":"充電與電路：機制","titleEn":"Charging and circuits: mechanism","text":"電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。","textEn":"Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用匹配電路作前後電性比較。 必須排除的錯判：非機械切割就不會傷害電路。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare matched circuits before and after processing. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設晶圓厚 50 μm、街道開口 10 μm，名義深寬比為 5。若遮罩消耗 2 μm、矽移除 50 μm，表觀選擇比為 25；不能用它預測不同圖形負載。","textEn":"A hypothetical 50 μm wafer and 10 μm opening give aspect ratio 5. Removing 50 μm Si with 2 μm mask loss gives apparent selectivity 25, not a prediction for different pattern loading."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「充電與電路」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For charging and circuits — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率","電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。","非機械切割就不會傷害電路"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal width with equal etch rate","Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks.","Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。 用匹配電路作前後電性比較。 因此不能採用「非機械切割就不會傷害電路」。","explanationEn":"Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks. Compare matched circuits before and after processing. Therefore reject: Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits."}},{"id":"a112-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-17"],"title":"充電與電路｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Charging and circuits | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對充電與電路，把「電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For charging and circuits, turn \"Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用匹配電路作前後電性比較。 將「非機械切割就不會傷害電路」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設晶圓厚 50 μm、街道開口 10 μm，名義深寬比為 5。若遮罩消耗 2 μm、矽移除 50 μm，表觀選擇比為 25；不能用它預測不同圖形負載。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare matched circuits before and after processing. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: A hypothetical 50 μm wafer and 10 μm opening give aspect ratio 5. Removing 50 μm Si with 2 μm mask loss gives apparent selectivity 25, not a prediction for different pattern loading. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"用匹配電路作前後電性比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare matched circuits before and after processing. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：非機械切割就不會傷害電路。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付充電與電路的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for charging and circuits: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-18-k1","title":"充電與電路：機制","titleEn":"Charging and circuits: mechanism","text":"電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。","textEn":"Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用匹配電路作前後電性比較。 必須排除的錯判：非機械切割就不會傷害電路。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare matched circuits before and after processing. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設晶圓厚 50 μm、街道開口 10 μm，名義深寬比為 5。若遮罩消耗 2 μm、矽移除 50 μm，表觀選擇比為 25；不能用它預測不同圖形負載。","textEn":"A hypothetical 50 μm wafer and 10 μm opening give aspect ratio 5. Removing 50 μm Si with 2 μm mask loss gives apparent selectivity 25, not a prediction for different pattern loading."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「充電與電路」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For charging and circuits — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["非機械切割就不會傷害電路","相同線寬必有相同蝕刻速率","用匹配電路作前後電性比較。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits","Equating equal width with equal etch rate","Compare matched circuits before and after processing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電漿環境可影響暴露結構，分離良率需搭配電性檢查。 用匹配電路作前後電性比較。 因此不能採用「非機械切割就不會傷害電路」。","explanationEn":"Plasma exposure can affect structures; singulation yield needs electrical checks. Compare matched circuits before and after processing. Therefore reject: Assuming nonmechanical dicing cannot damage circuits."}}]},{"id":"a112-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"邊緣與良率","titleEn":"Edges and yield","description":"針對邊緣與良率完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for edges and yield, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a112-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-18"],"title":"側壁殘留｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Sidewall residues | mechanism and design","objective":"針對側壁殘留，把「殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sidewall residues, turn \"Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「側壁殘留」的模型：殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for sidewall residues: Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付側壁殘留的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for sidewall residues, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-19-k1","title":"側壁殘留：機制","titleEn":"Sidewall residues: mechanism","text":"殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。","textEn":"Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。 必須排除的錯判：裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側壁殘留」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sidewall residues — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。","裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留","平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活"],"optionsEn":["Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding.","Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough","Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere"],"answer":0,"explanation":"殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。 以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。 因此不能採用「裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留」。","explanationEn":"Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding. Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. Therefore reject: Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough."}},{"id":"a112-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-19"],"title":"側壁殘留｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Sidewall residues | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對側壁殘留，把「殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sidewall residues, turn \"Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。 將「裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付側壁殘留的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for sidewall residues: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-20-k1","title":"側壁殘留：機制","titleEn":"Sidewall residues: mechanism","text":"殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。","textEn":"Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。 必須排除的錯判：裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側壁殘留」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sidewall residues — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均選擇比可確保所有位置遮罩存活","以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。","裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留"],"optionsEn":["Using mean selectivity to guarantee mask survival everywhere","Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses.","Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough"],"answer":1,"explanation":"殘留聚合物或遮罩可影響黏著和後續接合。 以表面分析和接合見證交叉比較。 因此不能採用「裂縫已開通即可忽略側壁殘留」。","explanationEn":"Polymer or mask residue affects adhesion and downstream bonding. Cross-check surface analysis and bonding witnesses. Therefore reject: Ignoring residue after trench breakthrough."}},{"id":"a112-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-20"],"title":"晶粒強度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Die strength | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶粒強度，把「去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die strength, turn \"Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶粒強度」的模型：去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for die strength: Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒強度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for die strength, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-21-k1","title":"晶粒強度：機制","titleEn":"Die strength: mechanism","text":"去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。","textEn":"Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。 必須排除的錯判：電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒強度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die strength — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強","膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容","去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die","Equating chamber fit with material compatibility","Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。 保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。 因此不能採用「電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強」。","explanationEn":"Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls. Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. Therefore reject: Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die."}},{"id":"a112-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-21"],"title":"晶粒強度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Die strength | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶粒強度，把「去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die strength, turn \"Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。 將「電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒強度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for die strength: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-22-k1","title":"晶粒強度：機制","titleEn":"Die strength: mechanism","text":"去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。","textEn":"Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。 必須排除的錯判：電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒強度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die strength — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。","電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強","膜框能入腔就代表材料已相容"],"optionsEn":["Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched.","Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die","Equating chamber fit with material compatibility"],"answer":0,"explanation":"去除材料可減少鋸切類損傷，但強度仍受缺陷與側壁形貌控制。 保持試片厚度與加載方向一致。 因此不能採用「電漿切割必定讓所有晶粒同等強」。","explanationEn":"Material removal avoids some saw damage, but strength still depends on flaws and sidewalls. Keep specimen thickness and loading direction matched. Therefore reject: Assuming plasma dicing gives identical strength to every die."}},{"id":"a112-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-22"],"title":"良率與節拍｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Yield and throughput | mechanism and design","objective":"針對良率與節拍，把「整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For yield and throughput, turn \"Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「良率與節拍」的模型：整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for yield and throughput: Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Comparing cost using chamber time alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良率與節拍的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for yield and throughput, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-23-k1","title":"良率與節拍：機制","titleEn":"Yield and throughput: mechanism","text":"整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。","textEn":"Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。 必須排除的錯判：只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. Misinterpretation to reject: Comparing cost using chamber time alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良率與節拍」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For yield and throughput — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度","整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。","只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本"],"optionsEn":["Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location","Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time.","Comparing cost using chamber time alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。 計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。 因此不能採用「只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本」。","explanationEn":"Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time. Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. Therefore reject: Comparing cost using chamber time alone."}},{"id":"a112-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"],"prerequisiteIds":["a112-v9-23"],"title":"良率與節拍｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Yield and throughput | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對良率與節拍，把「整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For yield and throughput, turn \"Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。 將「只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. Challenge the hypothesis \"Comparing cost using chamber time alone\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Comparing cost using chamber time alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良率與節拍的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for yield and throughput: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a112-v9-24-k1","title":"良率與節拍：機制","titleEn":"Yield and throughput: mechanism","text":"整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。","textEn":"Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]},{"id":"a112-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。 必須排除的錯判：只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. Misinterpretation to reject: Comparing cost using chamber time alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-sptsdice","v8b-drie"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良率與節拍」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For yield and throughput — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本","載台溫度就是晶圓所有位置溫度","計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。"],"optionsEn":["Comparing cost using chamber time alone","Equating chuck temperature with every wafer location","Calculate full-route time and cost per good die."],"answer":2,"explanation":"整片並行分離的節拍優势需扣除遮罩與清潔工序。 計算完整路徑時間與每良品成本。 因此不能採用「只比較腔體時間即可比較工法成本」。","explanationEn":"Parallel singulation benefits must include masking and cleaning time. Calculate full-route time and cost per good die. Therefore reject: Comparing cost using chamber time alone."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-handling","subcategoryTitle":"薄化、切割與晶粒搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thinning, dicing and die handling","photoId":"v8-drie-failure"},{"id":"a113","title":"晶粒拾取與精密放置","titleEn":"Die picking and precision placement","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb","v9-media-3363c0f741d8","v9-media-pi-video-library","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入薄晶粒取放、座標轉換與受力保護。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore thin-die handling, coordinate transforms and load protection, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["晶粒輸入","拾取受力","定位放置","檢測交接"],"labelsEn":["Die input","Pickup loading","Positioning","Inspection handoff"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a113-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"晶粒輸入","titleEn":"Die input","description":"針對晶粒輸入完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for die input, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a113-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"晶粒地圖身分｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Die-map identity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶粒地圖身分，把「晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die-map identity, turn \"Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶粒地圖身分」的模型：晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「核對原點、列行與缺口方向。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for die-map identity: Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Check origin, row/column and notch direction. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"核對原點、列行與缺口方向。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check origin, row/column and notch direction. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒地圖身分的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for die-map identity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-01-k1","title":"晶粒地圖身分：機制","titleEn":"Die-map identity: mechanism","text":"晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。","textEn":"Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"核對原點、列行與缺口方向。 必須排除的錯判：地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check origin, row/column and notch direction. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒地圖身分」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die-map identity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。","地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同","膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面"],"optionsEn":["Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs.","Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates","Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。 核對原點、列行與缺口方向。 因此不能採用「地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同」。","explanationEn":"Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs. Check origin, row/column and notch direction. Therefore reject: Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates."}},{"id":"a113-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-01"],"title":"晶粒地圖身分｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Die-map identity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶粒地圖身分，把「晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die-map identity, turn \"Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：核對原點、列行與缺口方向。 將「地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Check origin, row/column and notch direction. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"核對原點、列行與缺口方向。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check origin, row/column and notch direction. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒地圖身分的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for die-map identity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-02-k1","title":"晶粒地圖身分：機制","titleEn":"Die-map identity: mechanism","text":"晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。","textEn":"Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"核對原點、列行與缺口方向。 必須排除的錯判：地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check origin, row/column and notch direction. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒地圖身分」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die-map identity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面","核對原點、列行與缺口方向。","地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同"],"optionsEn":["Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces","Check origin, row/column and notch direction.","Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶粒座標需連結測試結果與取放紀錄以避免錯選。 核對原點、列行與缺口方向。 因此不能採用「地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同」。","explanationEn":"Die coordinates must link test results to placement logs. Check origin, row/column and notch direction. Therefore reject: Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates."}},{"id":"a113-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-02"],"title":"膜黏著分布｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Tape adhesion distribution | mechanism and design","objective":"針對膜黏著分布，把「黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tape adhesion distribution, turn \"Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「膜黏著分布」的模型：黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for tape adhesion distribution: Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring storage history for identical tape type. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膜黏著分布的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for tape adhesion distribution, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-03-k1","title":"膜黏著分布：機制","titleEn":"Tape adhesion distribution: mechanism","text":"黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。","textEn":"Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。 必須排除的錯判：膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring storage history for identical tape type. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膜黏著分布」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tape adhesion distribution — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程","影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差","黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring storage history for identical tape type","Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias","Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history."],"answer":2,"explanation":"黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。 比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。 因此不能採用「膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程」。","explanationEn":"Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history. Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. Therefore reject: Ignoring storage history for identical tape type."}},{"id":"a113-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-03"],"title":"膜黏著分布｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Tape adhesion distribution | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對膜黏著分布，把「黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tape adhesion distribution, turn \"Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。 將「膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring storage history for identical tape type\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring storage history for identical tape type. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付膜黏著分布的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for tape adhesion distribution: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-04-k1","title":"膜黏著分布：機制","titleEn":"Tape adhesion distribution: mechanism","text":"黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。","textEn":"Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。 必須排除的錯判：膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring storage history for identical tape type. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「膜黏著分布」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tape adhesion distribution — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。","膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程","影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差"],"optionsEn":["Compare force traces for matched pickup sites.","Ignoring storage history for identical tape type","Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias"],"answer":0,"explanation":"黏著力和剝離速度、溫度、照射歷程相關。 比較同位置重複拾取的力曲線。 因此不能採用「膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程」。","explanationEn":"Adhesion depends on peel rate, temperature and exposure history. Compare force traces for matched pickup sites. Therefore reject: Ignoring storage history for identical tape type."}},{"id":"a113-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-04"],"title":"頂針受力｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Ejector loading | mechanism and design","objective":"針對頂針受力，把「頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For ejector loading, turn \"Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「頂針受力」的模型：頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for ejector loading: Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總頂力小就不會局部破裂。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming small total force excludes local fracture. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付頂針受力的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for ejector loading, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-05-k1","title":"頂針受力：機制","titleEn":"Ejector loading: mechanism","text":"頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。","textEn":"Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。 必須排除的錯判：總頂力小就不會局部破裂。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming small total force excludes local fracture. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「頂針受力」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For ejector loading — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["兩點對準可以證明全片無變形","頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。","總頂力小就不會局部破裂"],"optionsEn":["Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation","Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies.","Assuming small total force excludes local fracture"],"answer":1,"explanation":"頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。 畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。 因此不能採用「總頂力小就不會局部破裂」。","explanationEn":"Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies. Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. Therefore reject: Assuming small total force excludes local fracture."}},{"id":"a113-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-05"],"title":"頂針受力｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Ejector loading | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對頂針受力，把「頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For ejector loading, turn \"Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。 將「總頂力小就不會局部破裂」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming small total force excludes local fracture\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總頂力小就不會局部破裂。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming small total force excludes local fracture. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付頂針受力的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for ejector loading: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-06-k1","title":"頂針受力：機制","titleEn":"Ejector loading: mechanism","text":"頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。","textEn":"Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。 必須排除的錯判：總頂力小就不會局部破裂。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming small total force excludes local fracture. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「頂針受力」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For ejector loading — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總頂力小就不會局部破裂","兩點對準可以證明全片無變形","畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming small total force excludes local fracture","Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation","Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans."],"answer":2,"explanation":"頂針集中載荷可能使薄晶粒局部彎曲或裂開。 畫針位、吸嘴支撐與懸空區。 因此不能採用「總頂力小就不會局部破裂」。","explanationEn":"Concentrated ejector loading can bend or crack thin dies. Draw pin sites, nozzle support and free spans. Therefore reject: Assuming small total force excludes local fracture."}}]},{"id":"a113-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"拾取受力","titleEn":"Pickup loading","description":"針對拾取受力完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for pickup loading, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a113-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-06"],"title":"吸嘴接觸｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Nozzle contact | mechanism and design","objective":"針對吸嘴接觸，把「吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For nozzle contact, turn \"Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「吸嘴接觸」的模型：吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for nozzle contact: Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付吸嘴接觸的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for nozzle contact, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-07-k1","title":"吸嘴接觸：機制","titleEn":"Nozzle contact: mechanism","text":"吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。","textEn":"Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。 必須排除的錯判：吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吸嘴接觸」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For nozzle contact — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。","吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置","開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行"],"optionsEn":["Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support.","Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient","Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day"],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。 將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。 因此不能採用「吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置」。","explanationEn":"Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support. Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. Therefore reject: Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient."}},{"id":"a113-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-07"],"title":"吸嘴接觸｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Nozzle contact | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對吸嘴接觸，把「吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For nozzle contact, turn \"Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。 將「吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付吸嘴接觸的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for nozzle contact: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-08-k1","title":"吸嘴接觸：機制","titleEn":"Nozzle contact: mechanism","text":"吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。","textEn":"Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。 必須排除的錯判：吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吸嘴接觸」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For nozzle contact — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行","將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。","吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置"],"optionsEn":["Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day","Overlay contact footprints on device layouts.","Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient"],"answer":1,"explanation":"吸嘴需避開敏感結構並提供足夠平面支撐。 將接觸輪廓疊到元件版圖。 因此不能採用「吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置」。","explanationEn":"Nozzles must avoid sensitive structures while providing planar support. Overlay contact footprints on device layouts. Therefore reject: Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient."}},{"id":"a113-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-08"],"title":"拾取與剝離｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pickup and peeling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對拾取與剝離，把「同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pickup and peeling, turn \"Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「拾取與剝離」的模型：同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pickup and peeling: Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Align displacement, force and high-speed images. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Align displacement, force and high-speed images. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating final travel with identical stress history. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付拾取與剝離的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pickup and peeling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-09-k1","title":"拾取與剝離：機制","titleEn":"Pickup and peeling: mechanism","text":"同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。","textEn":"Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。 必須排除的錯判：最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Align displacement, force and high-speed images. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating final travel with identical stress history. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「拾取與剝離」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pickup and peeling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程","相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑","同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。"],"optionsEn":["Equating final travel with identical stress history","Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip","Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。 對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。 因此不能採用「最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程」。","explanationEn":"Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load. Align displacement, force and high-speed images. Therefore reject: Equating final travel with identical stress history."}},{"id":"a113-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-09"],"title":"拾取與剝離｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pickup and peeling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對拾取與剝離，把「同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pickup and peeling, turn \"Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。 將「最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Align displacement, force and high-speed images. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating final travel with identical stress history\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Align displacement, force and high-speed images. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating final travel with identical stress history. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付拾取與剝離的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pickup and peeling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-10-k1","title":"拾取與剝離：機制","titleEn":"Pickup and peeling: mechanism","text":"同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。","textEn":"Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。 必須排除的錯判：最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Align displacement, force and high-speed images. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating final travel with identical stress history. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「拾取與剝離」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pickup and peeling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。","最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程","相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑"],"optionsEn":["Align displacement, force and high-speed images.","Equating final travel with identical stress history","Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步移動的時間差改變剝離角及瞬間負載。 對齊位移、力和高速影像時間軸。 因此不能採用「最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程」。","explanationEn":"Motion timing changes peel angle and transient load. Align displacement, force and high-speed images. Therefore reject: Equating final travel with identical stress history."}},{"id":"a113-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-10"],"title":"顆粒轉移｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Particle transfer | mechanism and design","objective":"針對顆粒轉移，把「吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For particle transfer, turn \"Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「顆粒轉移」的模型：吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for particle transfer: Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付顆粒轉移的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for particle transfer, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-11-k1","title":"顆粒轉移：機制","titleEn":"Particle transfer: mechanism","text":"吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。","textEn":"Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。 必須排除的錯判：膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「顆粒轉移」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For particle transfer — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差","吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。","膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面"],"optionsEn":["Using 3σ while omitting mean bias","Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces.","Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces"],"answer":1,"explanation":"吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。 區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。 因此不能採用「膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面」。","explanationEn":"Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces. Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. Therefore reject: Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces."}},{"id":"a113-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-11"],"title":"顆粒轉移｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Particle transfer | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對顆粒轉移，把「吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For particle transfer, turn \"Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。 將「膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付顆粒轉移的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for particle transfer: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-12-k1","title":"顆粒轉移：機制","titleEn":"Particle transfer: mechanism","text":"吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。","textEn":"Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。 必須排除的錯判：膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「顆粒轉移」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For particle transfer — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面","只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差","區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces","Using 3σ while omitting mean bias","Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸嘴和膜都可能將顆粒帶到功能面。 區分拾取前缺陷與拾取後新增點。 因此不能採用「膜上顆粒不會進入接合介面」。","explanationEn":"Nozzles and tape can transfer particles to functional surfaces. Separate pre-existing from pickup-added particles. Therefore reject: Assuming tape particles cannot reach bond interfaces."}}]},{"id":"a113-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"定位放置","titleEn":"Positioning","description":"針對定位放置完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for positioning, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a113-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-12"],"title":"視覺標記｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Vision fiducials | mechanism and design","objective":"針對視覺標記，把「反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For vision fiducials, turn \"Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「視覺標記」的模型：反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較不同光照下的座標漂移。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for vision fiducials: Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較不同光照下的座標漂移。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付視覺標記的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for vision fiducials, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-13-k1","title":"視覺標記：機制","titleEn":"Vision fiducials: mechanism","text":"反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。","textEn":"Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較不同光照下的座標漂移。 必須排除的錯判：影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺標記」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For vision fiducials — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。","影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差","放置良率等於最終接合良率"],"optionsEn":["Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers.","Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias","Equating placement yield with final bonding yield"],"answer":0,"explanation":"反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。 比較不同光照下的座標漂移。 因此不能採用「影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差」。","explanationEn":"Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers. Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. Therefore reject: Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias."}},{"id":"a113-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-13"],"title":"視覺標記｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Vision fiducials | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對視覺標記，把「反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For vision fiducials, turn \"Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較不同光照下的座標漂移。 將「影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較不同光照下的座標漂移。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付視覺標記的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for vision fiducials: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-14-k1","title":"視覺標記：機制","titleEn":"Vision fiducials: mechanism","text":"反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。","textEn":"Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較不同光照下的座標漂移。 必須排除的錯判：影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「視覺標記」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For vision fiducials — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["放置良率等於最終接合良率","比較不同光照下的座標漂移。","影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差"],"optionsEn":["Equating placement yield with final bonding yield","Compare coordinate drift under different illumination.","Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias"],"answer":1,"explanation":"反光與遮擋使幾何中心不等於標記識別中心。 比較不同光照下的座標漂移。 因此不能採用「影像解析度高即可消除識別偏差」。","explanationEn":"Reflections and occlusion shift detected fiducial centers. Compare coordinate drift under different illumination. Therefore reject: Assuming high image resolution eliminates recognition bias."}},{"id":"a113-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-14"],"title":"剛體轉換｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Rigid transforms | mechanism and design","objective":"針對剛體轉換，把「平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rigid transforms, turn \"Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「剛體轉換」的模型：平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for rigid transforms: Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩點對準可以證明全片無變形。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付剛體轉換的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for rigid transforms, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-15-k1","title":"剛體轉換：機制","titleEn":"Rigid transforms: mechanism","text":"平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。","textEn":"Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。 必須排除的錯判：兩點對準可以證明全片無變形。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. Misinterpretation to reject: Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剛體轉換」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rigid transforms — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["兩點對準可以證明全片無變形","地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同","平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。"],"optionsEn":["Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation","Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates","Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。 以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。 因此不能採用「兩點對準可以證明全片無變形」。","explanationEn":"Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more. Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. Therefore reject: Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation."}},{"id":"a113-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-15"],"title":"剛體轉換｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Rigid transforms | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對剛體轉換，把「平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rigid transforms, turn \"Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。 將「兩點對準可以證明全片無變形」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩點對準可以證明全片無變形。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付剛體轉換的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for rigid transforms: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-16-k1","title":"剛體轉換：機制","titleEn":"Rigid transforms: mechanism","text":"平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。","textEn":"Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。 必須排除的錯判：兩點對準可以證明全片無變形。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. Misinterpretation to reject: Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剛體轉換」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rigid transforms — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。","兩點對準可以證明全片無變形","地圖尺寸相同就表示座標定義相同"],"optionsEn":["Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks.","Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation","Equating equal map dimensions with equal coordinates"],"answer":0,"explanation":"平移旋轉可描述剛體，但翹曲與縮放需額外模型。 以至少三個非共線標記檢查殘差。 因此不能採用「兩點對準可以證明全片無變形」。","explanationEn":"Translation/rotation describe rigid bodies; warp and scaling require more. Check residuals using at least three noncollinear marks. Therefore reject: Using two-point alignment to prove no deformation."}},{"id":"a113-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-16"],"title":"熱漂移校正｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal drift calibration | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱漂移校正，把「相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal drift calibration, turn \"Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱漂移校正」的模型：相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設平台、視覺、取放的獨立標準差為 0.4、0.3、0.5 μm，RSS≈0.707 μm；若另有 1 μm 固定偏差，須先校正，不可把它當可平均掉的隨機值。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal drift calibration: Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Interleave fixed references through long runs. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: Independent illustrative stage, vision and placement standard deviations of 0.4, 0.3 and 0.5 μm give RSS≈0.707 μm. A separate 1 μm fixed bias requires calibration, not averaging. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Interleave fixed references through long runs. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱漂移校正的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal drift calibration, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-17-k1","title":"熱漂移校正：機制","titleEn":"Thermal drift calibration: mechanism","text":"相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。","textEn":"Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。 必須排除的錯判：開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Interleave fixed references through long runs. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設平台、視覺、取放的獨立標準差為 0.4、0.3、0.5 μm，RSS≈0.707 μm；若另有 1 μm 固定偏差，須先校正，不可把它當可平均掉的隨機值。","textEn":"Independent illustrative stage, vision and placement standard deviations of 0.4, 0.3 and 0.5 μm give RSS≈0.707 μm. A separate 1 μm fixed bias requires calibration, not averaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱漂移校正」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal drift calibration — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程","相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。","開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring storage history for identical tape type","Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime.","Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day"],"answer":1,"explanation":"相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。 用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。 因此不能採用「開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行」。","explanationEn":"Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime. Interleave fixed references through long runs. Therefore reject: Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day."}},{"id":"a113-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-17"],"title":"熱漂移校正｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal drift calibration | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱漂移校正，把「相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal drift calibration, turn \"Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。 將「開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設平台、視覺、取放的獨立標準差為 0.4、0.3、0.5 μm，RSS≈0.707 μm；若另有 1 μm 固定偏差，須先校正，不可把它當可平均掉的隨機值。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Interleave fixed references through long runs. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: Independent illustrative stage, vision and placement standard deviations of 0.4, 0.3 and 0.5 μm give RSS≈0.707 μm. A separate 1 μm fixed bias requires calibration, not averaging. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Interleave fixed references through long runs. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱漂移校正的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal drift calibration: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-18-k1","title":"熱漂移校正：機制","titleEn":"Thermal drift calibration: mechanism","text":"相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。","textEn":"Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。 必須排除的錯判：開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Interleave fixed references through long runs. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設平台、視覺、取放的獨立標準差為 0.4、0.3、0.5 μm，RSS≈0.707 μm；若另有 1 μm 固定偏差，須先校正，不可把它當可平均掉的隨機值。","textEn":"Independent illustrative stage, vision and placement standard deviations of 0.4, 0.3 and 0.5 μm give RSS≈0.707 μm. A separate 1 μm fixed bias requires calibration, not averaging."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱漂移校正」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal drift calibration — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行","膜料號相同即可忽略保存歷程","用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day","Ignoring storage history for identical tape type","Interleave fixed references through long runs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相機與平台熱漂移會隨運轉時間變化。 用固定參考點穿插量測長時間序列。 因此不能採用「開機時校正足以涵蓋全天運行」。","explanationEn":"Camera/stage drift can evolve with runtime. Interleave fixed references through long runs. Therefore reject: Assuming startup calibration covers the whole day."}}]},{"id":"a113-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"檢測交接","titleEn":"Inspection handoff","description":"針對檢測交接完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for inspection handoff, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a113-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-18"],"title":"放置接觸｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Placement contact | mechanism and design","objective":"針對放置接觸，把「接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For placement contact, turn \"Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「放置接觸」的模型：接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for placement contact: Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare precontact and post-unload position. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare precontact and post-unload position. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付放置接觸的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for placement contact, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-19-k1","title":"放置接觸：機制","titleEn":"Placement contact: mechanism","text":"接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。","textEn":"Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。 必須排除的錯判：相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare precontact and post-unload position. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「放置接觸」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For placement contact — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。","相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑","總頂力小就不會局部破裂"],"optionsEn":["Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip.","Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip","Assuming small total force excludes local fracture"],"answer":0,"explanation":"接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。 比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。 因此不能採用「相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑」。","explanationEn":"Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip. Compare precontact and post-unload position. Therefore reject: Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip."}},{"id":"a113-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-19"],"title":"放置接觸｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Placement contact | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對放置接觸，把「接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For placement contact, turn \"Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。 將「相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare precontact and post-unload position. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare precontact and post-unload position. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付放置接觸的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for placement contact: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-20-k1","title":"放置接觸：機制","titleEn":"Placement contact: mechanism","text":"接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。","textEn":"Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。 必須排除的錯判：相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare precontact and post-unload position. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「放置接觸」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For placement contact — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總頂力小就不會局部破裂","比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。","相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑"],"optionsEn":["Assuming small total force excludes local fracture","Compare precontact and post-unload position.","Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip"],"answer":1,"explanation":"接觸速度和基板順應性決定反彈與滑移風險。 比較接觸前與卸載後晶粒位置。 因此不能採用「相機看到到位即可判斷卸載後不滑」。","explanationEn":"Contact speed and substrate compliance govern rebound and slip. Compare precontact and post-unload position. Therefore reject: Assuming visual arrival guarantees no post-unload slip."}},{"id":"a113-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-20"],"title":"放置精度統計｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Placement statistics | mechanism and design","objective":"針對放置精度統計，把「重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For placement statistics, turn \"Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「放置精度統計」的模型：重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for placement statistics: Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using 3σ while omitting mean bias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付放置精度統計的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for placement statistics, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-21-k1","title":"放置精度統計：機制","titleEn":"Placement statistics: mechanism","text":"重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。","textEn":"Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。 必須排除的錯判：只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Using 3σ while omitting mean bias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「放置精度統計」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For placement statistics — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差","吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置","重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。"],"optionsEn":["Using 3σ while omitting mean bias","Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient","Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。 分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。 因此不能採用「只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差」。","explanationEn":"Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails. Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. Therefore reject: Using 3σ while omitting mean bias."}},{"id":"a113-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-21"],"title":"放置精度統計｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Placement statistics | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對放置精度統計，把「重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For placement statistics, turn \"Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。 將「只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using 3σ while omitting mean bias\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using 3σ while omitting mean bias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付放置精度統計的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for placement statistics: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-22-k1","title":"放置精度統計：機制","titleEn":"Placement statistics: mechanism","text":"重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。","textEn":"Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。 必須排除的錯判：只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Using 3σ while omitting mean bias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「放置精度統計」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For placement statistics — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。","只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差","吸力足夠即可忽略接觸位置"],"optionsEn":["Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately.","Using 3σ while omitting mean bias","Ignoring contact position when suction is sufficient"],"answer":0,"explanation":"重複精度與絕對準確度不同，尾端樣本須保留。 分開偏差、標準差及最壞殘差。 因此不能採用「只報 3σ 即可隱去平均偏差」。","explanationEn":"Repeatability differs from absolute accuracy; retain distribution tails. Report bias, standard deviation and worst residual separately. Therefore reject: Using 3σ while omitting mean bias."}},{"id":"a113-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-22"],"title":"後段可接合性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Downstream bondability | mechanism and design","objective":"針對後段可接合性，把「精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For downstream bondability, turn \"Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「後段可接合性」的模型：精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for downstream bondability: Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：放置良率等於最終接合良率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating placement yield with final bonding yield. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付後段可接合性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for downstream bondability, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-23-k1","title":"後段可接合性：機制","titleEn":"Downstream bondability: mechanism","text":"精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。","textEn":"Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。 必須排除的錯判：放置良率等於最終接合良率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating placement yield with final bonding yield. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「後段可接合性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For downstream bondability — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程","精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。","放置良率等於最終接合良率"],"optionsEn":["Equating final travel with identical stress history","Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation.","Equating placement yield with final bonding yield"],"answer":1,"explanation":"精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。 交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。 因此不能採用「放置良率等於最終接合良率」。","explanationEn":"Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation. Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. Therefore reject: Equating placement yield with final bonding yield."}},{"id":"a113-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"],"prerequisiteIds":["a113-v9-23"],"title":"後段可接合性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Downstream bondability | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對後段可接合性，把「精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For downstream bondability, turn \"Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。 將「放置良率等於最終接合良率」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating placement yield with final bonding yield\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：放置良率等於最終接合良率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating placement yield with final bonding yield. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付後段可接合性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for downstream bondability: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a113-v9-24-k1","title":"後段可接合性：機制","titleEn":"Downstream bondability: mechanism","text":"精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。","textEn":"Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]},{"id":"a113-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。 必須排除的錯判：放置良率等於最終接合良率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating placement yield with final bonding yield. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-besihyb","v9a-besitcb"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「後段可接合性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For downstream bondability — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["放置良率等於最終接合良率","最終位移相同就具有相同應力歷程","交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。"],"optionsEn":["Equating placement yield with final bonding yield","Equating final travel with identical stress history","Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"精準位置、無裂紋與潔淨表面需共同驗證。 交付逐顆座標、缺陷與來源追溯。 因此不能採用「放置良率等於最終接合良率」。","explanationEn":"Position accuracy, crack absence and cleanliness need joint validation. Deliver per-die coordinates, defects and source traceability. Therefore reject: Equating placement yield with final bonding yield."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-handling","subcategoryTitle":"薄化、切割與晶粒搬運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Thinning, dicing and die handling","photoId":"v9-quilt-array"},{"id":"a114","title":"底部填膠流動控制","titleEn":"Underfill flow control","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入毛細流動、填料與固化應力。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore capillary flow, fillers and cure stress, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["間隙與潤濕","流動與排氣","固化與應力","檢測可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Gap and wetting","Flow and venting","Cure and stress","Inspection and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a114-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"間隙與潤濕","titleEn":"Gap and wetting","description":"針對間隙與潤濕完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for gap and wetting, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a114-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"間隙幾何｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Gap geometry | mechanism and design","objective":"針對間隙幾何，把「局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For gap geometry, turn \"Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「間隙幾何」的模型：局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫最窄通道及流動分岔。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for gap geometry: Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map narrowest channels and flow splits. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫最窄通道及流動分岔。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map narrowest channels and flow splits. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean gap to predict every fill time. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付間隙幾何的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for gap geometry, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-01-k1","title":"間隙幾何：機制","titleEn":"Gap geometry: mechanism","text":"局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。","textEn":"Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫最窄通道及流動分岔。 必須排除的錯判：平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map narrowest channels and flow splits. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean gap to predict every fill time. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「間隙幾何」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For gap geometry — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。","平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間","四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞"],"optionsEn":["Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance.","Using mean gap to predict every fill time","Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。 畫最窄通道及流動分岔。 因此不能採用「平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間」。","explanationEn":"Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance. Map narrowest channels and flow splits. Therefore reject: Using mean gap to predict every fill time."}},{"id":"a114-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-01"],"title":"間隙幾何｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Gap geometry | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對間隙幾何，把「局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For gap geometry, turn \"Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫最窄通道及流動分岔。 將「平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map narrowest channels and flow splits. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using mean gap to predict every fill time\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫最窄通道及流動分岔。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map narrowest channels and flow splits. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean gap to predict every fill time. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付間隙幾何的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for gap geometry: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-02-k1","title":"間隙幾何：機制","titleEn":"Gap geometry: mechanism","text":"局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。","textEn":"Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫最窄通道及流動分岔。 必須排除的錯判：平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map narrowest channels and flow splits. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean gap to predict every fill time. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「間隙幾何」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For gap geometry — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞","畫最窄通道及流動分岔。","平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間"],"optionsEn":["Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids","Map narrowest channels and flow splits.","Using mean gap to predict every fill time"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部間隙和凸塊障礙控制流動阻力。 畫最窄通道及流動分岔。 因此不能採用「平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間」。","explanationEn":"Local gaps and bump obstacles control flow resistance. Map narrowest channels and flow splits. Therefore reject: Using mean gap to predict every fill time."}},{"id":"a114-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-02"],"title":"接觸角與表面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Contact angle and surface | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接觸角與表面，把「潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For contact angle and surface, turn \"Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接觸角與表面」的模型：潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for contact angle and surface: Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Applying handbook contact angles to every surface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接觸角與表面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for contact angle and surface, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-03-k1","title":"接觸角與表面：機制","titleEn":"Contact angle and surface: mechanism","text":"潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。","textEn":"Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。 必須排除的錯判：材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. Misinterpretation to reject: Applying handbook contact angles to every surface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸角與表面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For contact angle and surface — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面","看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿","潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["Applying handbook contact angles to every surface","Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill","Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。 以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。 因此不能採用「材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面」。","explanationEn":"Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness. Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. Therefore reject: Applying handbook contact angles to every surface."}},{"id":"a114-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-03"],"title":"接觸角與表面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Contact angle and surface | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接觸角與表面，把「潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For contact angle and surface, turn \"Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。 將「材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. Challenge the hypothesis \"Applying handbook contact angles to every surface\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Applying handbook contact angles to every surface. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接觸角與表面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for contact angle and surface: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-04-k1","title":"接觸角與表面：機制","titleEn":"Contact angle and surface: mechanism","text":"潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。","textEn":"Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。 必須排除的錯判：材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. Misinterpretation to reject: Applying handbook contact angles to every surface. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸角與表面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For contact angle and surface — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。","材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面","看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿"],"optionsEn":["Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history.","Applying handbook contact angles to every surface","Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill"],"answer":0,"explanation":"潤濕取決於實際表面污染和粗糙度。 以相同清潔歷程見證片量測。 因此不能採用「材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面」。","explanationEn":"Wetting depends on actual contamination and roughness. Measure witnesses with matched cleaning history. Therefore reject: Applying handbook contact angles to every surface."}},{"id":"a114-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-04"],"title":"黏度與時間｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Viscosity and time | mechanism and design","objective":"針對黏度與時間，把「材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For viscosity and time, turn \"Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「黏度與時間」的模型：材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較使用前後流變曲線。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for viscosity and time: Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare rheology before and during use. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較使用前後流變曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare rheology before and during use. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付黏度與時間的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for viscosity and time, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-05-k1","title":"黏度與時間：機制","titleEn":"Viscosity and time: mechanism","text":"材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。","textEn":"Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較使用前後流變曲線。 必須排除的錯判：一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare rheology before and during use. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏度與時間」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For viscosity and time — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力","材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。","一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠"],"optionsEn":["Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress","Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time.","Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。 比較使用前後流變曲線。 因此不能採用「一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠」。","explanationEn":"Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time. Compare rheology before and during use. Therefore reject: Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill."}},{"id":"a114-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-05"],"title":"黏度與時間｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Viscosity and time | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對黏度與時間，把「材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For viscosity and time, turn \"Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較使用前後流變曲線。 將「一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare rheology before and during use. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較使用前後流變曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare rheology before and during use. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付黏度與時間的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for viscosity and time: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-06-k1","title":"黏度與時間：機制","titleEn":"Viscosity and time: mechanism","text":"材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。","textEn":"Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較使用前後流變曲線。 必須排除的錯判：一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare rheology before and during use. Misinterpretation to reject: Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏度與時間」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For viscosity and time — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠","固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力","比較使用前後流變曲線。"],"optionsEn":["Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill","Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress","Compare rheology before and during use."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料黏度可能隨溫度及固化時間改變。 比較使用前後流變曲線。 因此不能採用「一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠」。","explanationEn":"Viscosity may change with temperature and cure time. Compare rheology before and during use. Therefore reject: Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill."}}]},{"id":"a114-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"流動與排氣","titleEn":"Flow and venting","description":"針對流動與排氣完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for flow and venting, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a114-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-06"],"title":"毛細尺度模型｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Capillary scaling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對毛細尺度模型，把「理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For capillary scaling, turn \"Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「毛細尺度模型」的模型：理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for capillary scaling: Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Plot L² against t and inspect departures. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plot L² against t and inspect departures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：流長加倍只需兩倍時間。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付毛細尺度模型的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for capillary scaling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-07-k1","title":"毛細尺度模型：機制","titleEn":"Capillary scaling: mechanism","text":"理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。","textEn":"Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。 必須排除的錯判：流長加倍只需兩倍時間。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plot L² against t and inspect departures. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「毛細尺度模型」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For capillary scaling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。","流長加倍只需兩倍時間","Tg 越高便無條件越可靠"],"optionsEn":["Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment.","Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time","Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable"],"answer":0,"explanation":"理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。 繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。 因此不能採用「流長加倍只需兩倍時間」。","explanationEn":"Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment. Plot L² against t and inspect departures. Therefore reject: Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time."}},{"id":"a114-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-07"],"title":"毛細尺度模型｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Capillary scaling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對毛細尺度模型，把「理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For capillary scaling, turn \"Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。 將「流長加倍只需兩倍時間」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Plot L² against t and inspect departures. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plot L² against t and inspect departures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：流長加倍只需兩倍時間。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付毛細尺度模型的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for capillary scaling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-08-k1","title":"毛細尺度模型：機制","titleEn":"Capillary scaling: mechanism","text":"理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。","textEn":"Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。 必須排除的錯判：流長加倍只需兩倍時間。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plot L² against t and inspect departures. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「毛細尺度模型」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For capillary scaling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["Tg 越高便無條件越可靠","繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。","流長加倍只需兩倍時間"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable","Plot L² against t and inspect departures.","Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time"],"answer":1,"explanation":"理想流長平方隨時間成長，幾何和流變改變時須重新檢查。 繪 L² 對 t 並檢查曲線偏離。 因此不能採用「流長加倍只需兩倍時間」。","explanationEn":"Ideal squared flow length grows with time; geometry/rheology changes require reassessment. Plot L² against t and inspect departures. Therefore reject: Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time."}},{"id":"a114-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-08"],"title":"填料與篩分｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Fillers and filtration | mechanism and design","objective":"針對填料與篩分，把「粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fillers and filtration, turn \"Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「填料與篩分」的模型：粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for fillers and filtration: Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付填料與篩分的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for fillers and filtration, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-09-k1","title":"填料與篩分：機制","titleEn":"Fillers and filtration: mechanism","text":"粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。","textEn":"Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。 必須排除的錯判：總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「填料與篩分」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fillers and filtration — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析","相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度","粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation","Equating equal void area with equal reliability","Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。 比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。 因此不能採用「總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析」。","explanationEn":"Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration. Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. Therefore reject: Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation."}},{"id":"a114-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-09"],"title":"填料與篩分｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Fillers and filtration | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對填料與篩分，把「粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fillers and filtration, turn \"Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。 將「總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付填料與篩分的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for fillers and filtration: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-10-k1","title":"填料與篩分：機制","titleEn":"Fillers and filtration: mechanism","text":"粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。","textEn":"Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。 必須排除的錯判：總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「填料與篩分」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fillers and filtration — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。","總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析","相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions.","Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation","Equating equal void area with equal reliability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"粒徑相對間隙過大會堵塞或造成局部濃度變化。 比較入口出口及窄隙填料分布。 因此不能採用「總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析」。","explanationEn":"Large particles relative to gaps can clog or change local concentration. Compare filler distributions at inlet, outlet and constrictions. Therefore reject: Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation."}},{"id":"a114-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-10"],"title":"流前沿相遇｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Meeting fronts | mechanism and design","objective":"針對流前沿相遇，把「兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For meeting fronts, turn \"Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「流前沿相遇」的模型：兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for meeting fronts: Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw front time sequences and vent paths. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw front time sequences and vent paths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付流前沿相遇的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for meeting fronts, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-11-k1","title":"流前沿相遇：機制","titleEn":"Meeting fronts: mechanism","text":"兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。","textEn":"Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。 必須排除的錯判：四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw front time sequences and vent paths. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「流前沿相遇」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For meeting fronts — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態","兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。","四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞"],"optionsEn":["Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior","Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling.","Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids"],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。 畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。 因此不能採用「四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞」。","explanationEn":"Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling. Draw front time sequences and vent paths. Therefore reject: Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids."}},{"id":"a114-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-11"],"title":"流前沿相遇｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Meeting fronts | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對流前沿相遇，把「兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For meeting fronts, turn \"Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。 將「四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw front time sequences and vent paths. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw front time sequences and vent paths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付流前沿相遇的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for meeting fronts: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-12-k1","title":"流前沿相遇：機制","titleEn":"Meeting fronts: mechanism","text":"兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。","textEn":"Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。 必須排除的錯判：四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw front time sequences and vent paths. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「流前沿相遇」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For meeting fronts — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞","初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態","畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids","Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior","Draw front time sequences and vent paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"兩個前沿合流可能圍困空氣，增加出膠點並不必然更快更完整。 畫前沿時間序列與排氣路徑。 因此不能採用「四邊同時出膠總比單邊更無空洞」。","explanationEn":"Meeting fronts can trap air; extra dispense sites do not guarantee better filling. Draw front time sequences and vent paths. Therefore reject: Assuming four-sided dispensing always eliminates voids."}}]},{"id":"a114-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"固化與應力","titleEn":"Cure and stress","description":"針對固化與應力完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for cure and stress, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a114-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-12"],"title":"焊點與通道｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Joints and channels | mechanism and design","objective":"針對焊點與通道，把「陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For joints and channels, turn \"Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「焊點與通道」的模型：陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較沿列與斜向流動示意。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for joints and channels: Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較沿列與斜向流動示意。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊點與通道的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for joints and channels, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-13-k1","title":"焊點與通道：機制","titleEn":"Joints and channels: mechanism","text":"陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。","textEn":"Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較沿列與斜向流動示意。 必須排除的錯判：看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. Misinterpretation to reject: Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊點與通道」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For joints and channels — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。","看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿","填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求"],"optionsEn":["Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions.","Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill","Assuming filled and cured meets every package need"],"answer":0,"explanation":"陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。 比較沿列與斜向流動示意。 因此不能採用「看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿」。","explanationEn":"Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions. Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. Therefore reject: Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill."}},{"id":"a114-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-13"],"title":"焊點與通道｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Joints and channels | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對焊點與通道，把「陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For joints and channels, turn \"Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較沿列與斜向流動示意。 將「看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較沿列與斜向流動示意。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊點與通道的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for joints and channels: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-14-k1","title":"焊點與通道：機制","titleEn":"Joints and channels: mechanism","text":"陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。","textEn":"Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較沿列與斜向流動示意。 必須排除的錯判：看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. Misinterpretation to reject: Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊點與通道」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For joints and channels — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求","比較沿列與斜向流動示意。","看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿"],"optionsEn":["Assuming filled and cured meets every package need","Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow.","Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill"],"answer":1,"explanation":"陣列方向改變流阻與毛細旁路，流量不均可繞過密集區。 比較沿列與斜向流動示意。 因此不能採用「看到遠端出膠即可證明中間已填滿」。","explanationEn":"Array direction alters resistance and bypass paths; flow can skip dense regions. Compare row-aligned and diagonal flow. Therefore reject: Using far-edge arrival as proof of complete internal fill."}},{"id":"a114-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-14"],"title":"固化收縮｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對固化收縮，把「固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cure shrinkage, turn \"Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「固化收縮」的模型：固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cure shrinkage: Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固化收縮的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cure shrinkage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-15-k1","title":"固化收縮：機制","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage: mechanism","text":"固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。","textEn":"Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。 必須排除的錯判：固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固化收縮」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cure shrinkage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力","平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間","固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress","Using mean gap to predict every fill time","Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。 比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。 因此不能採用「固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力」。","explanationEn":"Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress. Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. Therefore reject: Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress."}},{"id":"a114-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-15"],"title":"固化收縮｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對固化收縮，把「固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cure shrinkage, turn \"Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。 將「固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固化收縮的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cure shrinkage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-16-k1","title":"固化收縮：機制","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage: mechanism","text":"固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。","textEn":"Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。 必須排除的錯判：固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固化收縮」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cure shrinkage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。","固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力","平均間隙足以預測所有填充時間"],"optionsEn":["Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation.","Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress","Using mean gap to predict every fill time"],"answer":0,"explanation":"固化增加模數並帶來收縮，拘束條件決定殘餘應力。 比較自由收縮與接合堆疊變形。 因此不能採用「固化收縮只會改體積不會改應力」。","explanationEn":"Cure increases modulus and introduces shrinkage; constraints set residual stress. Compare free shrinkage and bonded-stack deformation. Therefore reject: Assuming cure shrinkage changes volume but not stress."}},{"id":"a114-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-16"],"title":"Tg 與 CTE｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Tg and CTE | mechanism and design","objective":"針對Tg 與 CTE，把「玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tg and cte, turn \"Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「Tg 與 CTE」的模型：玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：在平行板、牛頓流體且忽略重力的教學尺度模型中 L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ；流長加倍需約四倍時間，黏度加倍需約兩倍時間。真實凸塊和填料會改變此關係。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for tg and cte: Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Overlay material curves and operating range. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For a Newtonian liquid between parallel plates, neglecting gravity, L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ: doubling length takes about four times as long and doubling viscosity twice as long. Bumps and fillers modify the relation. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay material curves and operating range. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：Tg 越高便無條件越可靠。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Tg 與 CTE的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for tg and cte, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-17-k1","title":"Tg 與 CTE：機制","titleEn":"Tg and CTE: mechanism","text":"玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。","textEn":"Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。 必須排除的錯判：Tg 越高便無條件越可靠。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay material curves and operating range. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"在平行板、牛頓流體且忽略重力的教學尺度模型中 L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ；流長加倍需約四倍時間，黏度加倍需約兩倍時間。真實凸塊和填料會改變此關係。","textEn":"For a Newtonian liquid between parallel plates, neglecting gravity, L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ: doubling length takes about four times as long and doubling viscosity twice as long. Bumps and fillers modify the relation."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Tg 與 CTE」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tg and cte — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面","玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。","Tg 越高便無條件越可靠"],"optionsEn":["Applying handbook contact angles to every surface","Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures.","Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable"],"answer":1,"explanation":"玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。 把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。 因此不能採用「Tg 越高便無條件越可靠」。","explanationEn":"Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures. Overlay material curves and operating range. Therefore reject: Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable."}},{"id":"a114-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-17"],"title":"Tg 與 CTE｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Tg and CTE | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對Tg 與 CTE，把「玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tg and cte, turn \"Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。 將「Tg 越高便無條件越可靠」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：在平行板、牛頓流體且忽略重力的教學尺度模型中 L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ；流長加倍需約四倍時間，黏度加倍需約兩倍時間。真實凸塊和填料會改變此關係。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Overlay material curves and operating range. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For a Newtonian liquid between parallel plates, neglecting gravity, L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ: doubling length takes about four times as long and doubling viscosity twice as long. Bumps and fillers modify the relation. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Overlay material curves and operating range. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：Tg 越高便無條件越可靠。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Tg 與 CTE的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for tg and cte: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-18-k1","title":"Tg 與 CTE：機制","titleEn":"Tg and CTE: mechanism","text":"玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。","textEn":"Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。 必須排除的錯判：Tg 越高便無條件越可靠。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Overlay material curves and operating range. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"在平行板、牛頓流體且忽略重力的教學尺度模型中 L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ；流長加倍需約四倍時間，黏度加倍需約兩倍時間。真實凸塊和填料會改變此關係。","textEn":"For a Newtonian liquid between parallel plates, neglecting gravity, L²∝hγcosθ·t/μ: doubling length takes about four times as long and doubling viscosity twice as long. Bumps and fillers modify the relation."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Tg 與 CTE」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tg and cte — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["Tg 越高便無條件越可靠","材料手冊接觸角適用所有表面","把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable","Applying handbook contact angles to every surface","Overlay material curves and operating range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"玻璃轉移附近模數和膨脹行為改變，不能用單一常數跨全溫域。 把材料曲線與使用溫度範圍疊合。 因此不能採用「Tg 越高便無條件越可靠」。","explanationEn":"Modulus and expansion change near glass transition; one constant may not span temperatures. Overlay material curves and operating range. Therefore reject: Assuming higher Tg is unconditionally more reliable."}}]},{"id":"a114-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"檢測可靠度","titleEn":"Inspection and reliability","description":"針對檢測可靠度完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for inspection and reliability, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a114-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-18"],"title":"空洞量測｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Void metrology | mechanism and design","objective":"針對空洞量測，把「空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For void metrology, turn \"Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「空洞量測」的模型：空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for void metrology: Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal void area with equal reliability. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空洞量測的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for void metrology, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-19-k1","title":"空洞量測：機制","titleEn":"Void metrology: mechanism","text":"空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。","textEn":"Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。 必須排除的錯判：相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal void area with equal reliability. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空洞量測」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For void metrology — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。","相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度","一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠"],"optionsEn":["Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area.","Equating equal void area with equal reliability","Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill"],"answer":0,"explanation":"空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。 配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。 因此不能採用「相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度」。","explanationEn":"Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area. Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. Therefore reject: Equating equal void area with equal reliability."}},{"id":"a114-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-19"],"title":"空洞量測｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Void metrology | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對空洞量測，把「空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For void metrology, turn \"Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。 將「相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating equal void area with equal reliability\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal void area with equal reliability. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空洞量測的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for void metrology: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-20-k1","title":"空洞量測：機制","titleEn":"Void metrology: mechanism","text":"空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。","textEn":"Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。 必須排除的錯判：相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal void area with equal reliability. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空洞量測」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For void metrology — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["一次室溫黏度可代表整段填膠","配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。","相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Using one room-temperature viscosity for the whole fill","Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations.","Equating equal void area with equal reliability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"空洞位置和連通性常比總面積更能反映風險。 配對聲學圖、截面和焊點位置。 因此不能採用「相同空洞面積必有相同可靠度」。","explanationEn":"Void location/connectivity can matter more than total area. Pair acoustic maps, sections and joint locations. Therefore reject: Equating equal void area with equal reliability."}},{"id":"a114-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-20"],"title":"吸濕與界面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces | mechanism and design","objective":"針對吸濕與界面，把「吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For moisture and interfaces, turn \"Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「吸濕與界面」的模型：吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for moisture and interfaces: Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付吸濕與界面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for moisture and interfaces, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-21-k1","title":"吸濕與界面：機制","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces: mechanism","text":"吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。","textEn":"Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。 必須排除的錯判：初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. Misinterpretation to reject: Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吸濕與界面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For moisture and interfaces — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態","流長加倍只需兩倍時間","吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。"],"optionsEn":["Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior","Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time","Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。 比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。 因此不能採用「初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態」。","explanationEn":"Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating. Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. Therefore reject: Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior."}},{"id":"a114-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-21"],"title":"吸濕與界面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對吸濕與界面，把「吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For moisture and interfaces, turn \"Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。 將「初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付吸濕與界面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for moisture and interfaces: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-22-k1","title":"吸濕與界面：機制","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces: mechanism","text":"吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。","textEn":"Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。 必須排除的錯判：初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. Misinterpretation to reject: Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吸濕與界面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For moisture and interfaces — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。","初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態","流長加倍只需兩倍時間"],"optionsEn":["Compare dry controls with conditioned samples.","Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior","Assuming twice the flow length takes twice the time"],"answer":0,"explanation":"吸濕膨脹與黏著下降可能在後續熱歷程中顯現。 比較乾燥對照與受濕樣本。 因此不能採用「初始黏著強度能代表受濕後狀態」。","explanationEn":"Hygroscopic expansion and adhesion loss may appear during later heating. Compare dry controls with conditioned samples. Therefore reject: Using initial adhesion for moisture-conditioned behavior."}},{"id":"a114-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-22"],"title":"返修與驗收｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Rework and acceptance | mechanism and design","objective":"針對返修與驗收，把「可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rework and acceptance, turn \"Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「返修與驗收」的模型：可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for rework and acceptance: Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming filled and cured meets every package need. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付返修與驗收的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for rework and acceptance, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-23-k1","title":"返修與驗收：機制","titleEn":"Rework and acceptance: mechanism","text":"可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。","textEn":"Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。 必須排除的錯判：填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming filled and cured meets every package need. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「返修與驗收」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rework and acceptance — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析","可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。","填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation","Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off.","Assuming filled and cured meets every package need"],"answer":1,"explanation":"可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。 按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。 因此不能採用「填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求」。","explanationEn":"Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off. Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. Therefore reject: Assuming filled and cured meets every package need."}},{"id":"a114-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a114-v9-23"],"title":"返修與驗收｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Rework and acceptance | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對返修與驗收，把「可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rework and acceptance, turn \"Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。 將「填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming filled and cured meets every package need\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming filled and cured meets every package need. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付返修與驗收的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for rework and acceptance: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a114-v9-24-k1","title":"返修與驗收：機制","titleEn":"Rework and acceptance: mechanism","text":"可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。","textEn":"Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a114-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。 必須排除的錯判：填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming filled and cured meets every package need. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-henkel","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「返修與驗收」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rework and acceptance — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求","總填料比例相同就不會有局部偏析","按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming filled and cured meets every package need","Assuming equal bulk filler fraction excludes segregation","Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可返修性、熱導及機械保護之間有權衡。 按產品邊界列雙重驗收條件。 因此不能採用「填滿且固化即滿足所有封裝需求」。","explanationEn":"Reworkability, thermal conduction and mechanical protection trade off. Define paired acceptance criteria for product boundaries. Therefore reject: Assuming filled and cured meets every package need."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-encapsulation","subcategoryTitle":"封膠、扇出與異質整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Encapsulation, fan-out and heterogeneous integration","photoId":"bga-section"},{"id":"a115","title":"模封材料與翹曲控制","titleEn":"Molding compounds and warpage control","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入模封收縮、材料非線性與翹曲。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore mold shrinkage, material nonlinearity and warpage, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["材料表徵","流動與固化","翹曲耦合","可靠度放行"],"labelsEn":["Material characterization","Flow and curing","Warpage coupling","Reliability release"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a115-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"材料表徵","titleEn":"Material characterization","description":"針對材料表徵完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for material characterization, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a115-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"材料組成｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Material composition | mechanism and design","objective":"針對材料組成，把「樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For material composition, turn \"Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「材料組成」的模型：樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將材料批次連到實測曲線。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for material composition: Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Link material lots to measured curves. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將材料批次連到實測曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Link material lots to measured curves. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同填料百分比必有相同模數。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating filler percentage with modulus. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付材料組成的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for material composition, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-01-k1","title":"材料組成：機制","titleEn":"Material composition: mechanism","text":"樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。","textEn":"Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將材料批次連到實測曲線。 必須排除的錯判：相同填料百分比必有相同模數。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Link material lots to measured curves. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating filler percentage with modulus. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「材料組成」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For material composition — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。","相同填料百分比必有相同模數","所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述"],"optionsEn":["Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics.","Equating filler percentage with modulus","Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT"],"answer":0,"explanation":"樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。 將材料批次連到實測曲線。 因此不能採用「相同填料百分比必有相同模數」。","explanationEn":"Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics. Link material lots to measured curves. Therefore reject: Equating filler percentage with modulus."}},{"id":"a115-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-01"],"title":"材料組成｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Material composition | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對材料組成，把「樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For material composition, turn \"Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將材料批次連到實測曲線。 將「相同填料百分比必有相同模數」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Link material lots to measured curves. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating filler percentage with modulus\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將材料批次連到實測曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Link material lots to measured curves. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同填料百分比必有相同模數。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating filler percentage with modulus. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付材料組成的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for material composition: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-02-k1","title":"材料組成：機制","titleEn":"Material composition: mechanism","text":"樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。","textEn":"Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將材料批次連到實測曲線。 必須排除的錯判：相同填料百分比必有相同模數。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Link material lots to measured curves. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating filler percentage with modulus. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「材料組成」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For material composition — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述","將材料批次連到實測曲線。","相同填料百分比必有相同模數"],"optionsEn":["Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT","Link material lots to measured curves.","Equating filler percentage with modulus"],"answer":1,"explanation":"樹脂、填料及界面決定流動與熱機性質。 將材料批次連到實測曲線。 因此不能採用「相同填料百分比必有相同模數」。","explanationEn":"Resin, fillers and interfaces determine flow and thermomechanics. Link material lots to measured curves. Therefore reject: Equating filler percentage with modulus."}},{"id":"a115-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-02"],"title":"Tg 分段模型｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Piecewise Tg model | mechanism and design","objective":"針對Tg 分段模型，把「Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For piecewise tg model, turn \"CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「Tg 分段模型」的模型：Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for piecewise tg model: CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：室溫模數可代表整段固化。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Tg 分段模型的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for piecewise tg model, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-03-k1","title":"Tg 分段模型：機制","titleEn":"Piecewise Tg model: mechanism","text":"Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。","textEn":"CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。 必須排除的錯判：室溫模數可代表整段固化。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. Misinterpretation to reject: Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Tg 分段模型」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For piecewise tg model — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["室溫模數可代表整段固化","總厚度相同必有相同翹曲","Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。"],"optionsEn":["Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing","Equating total thickness with warpage","CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。 以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。 因此不能採用「室溫模數可代表整段固化」。","explanationEn":"CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature. Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. Therefore reject: Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing."}},{"id":"a115-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-03"],"title":"Tg 分段模型｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Piecewise Tg model | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對Tg 分段模型，把「Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For piecewise tg model, turn \"CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。 將「室溫模數可代表整段固化」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：室溫模數可代表整段固化。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Tg 分段模型的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for piecewise tg model: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-04-k1","title":"Tg 分段模型：機制","titleEn":"Piecewise Tg model: mechanism","text":"Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。","textEn":"CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。 必須排除的錯判：室溫模數可代表整段固化。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. Misinterpretation to reject: Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Tg 分段模型」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For piecewise tg model — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。","室溫模數可代表整段固化","總厚度相同必有相同翹曲"],"optionsEn":["Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value.","Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing","Equating total thickness with warpage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Tg 附近的 CTE 和模數變化影響冷卻曲率。 以分段曲線取代單一室溫值。 因此不能採用「室溫模數可代表整段固化」。","explanationEn":"CTE/modulus changes near Tg affect cooling curvature. Use piecewise curves instead of one room-temperature value. Therefore reject: Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing."}},{"id":"a115-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-04"],"title":"固化參考態｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cure reference state | mechanism and design","objective":"針對固化參考態，把「應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cure reference state, turn \"The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「固化參考態」的模型：應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cure reference state: The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最高溫度必是零應力參考。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming peak temperature is stress-free. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固化參考態的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cure reference state, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-05-k1","title":"固化參考態：機制","titleEn":"Cure reference state: mechanism","text":"應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。","textEn":"The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。 必須排除的錯判：最高溫度必是零應力參考。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming peak temperature is stress-free. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固化參考態」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cure reference state — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只需室溫翹曲驗收","應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。","最高溫度必是零應力參考"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying warpage at room temperature only","The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature.","Assuming peak temperature is stress-free"],"answer":1,"explanation":"應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。 追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。 因此不能採用「最高溫度必是零應力參考」。","explanationEn":"The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature. Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. Therefore reject: Assuming peak temperature is stress-free."}},{"id":"a115-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-05"],"title":"固化參考態｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cure reference state | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對固化參考態，把「應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cure reference state, turn \"The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。 將「最高溫度必是零應力參考」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming peak temperature is stress-free\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最高溫度必是零應力參考。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming peak temperature is stress-free. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固化參考態的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cure reference state: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-06-k1","title":"固化參考態：機制","titleEn":"Cure reference state: mechanism","text":"應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。","textEn":"The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。 必須排除的錯判：最高溫度必是零應力參考。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming peak temperature is stress-free. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固化參考態」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cure reference state — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["最高溫度必是零應力參考","只需室溫翹曲驗收","追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming peak temperature is stress-free","Qualifying warpage at room temperature only","Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應力自由態並不一定是最高加工溫度。 追蹤凝膠、收縮與拘束開始。 因此不能採用「最高溫度必是零應力參考」。","explanationEn":"The stress-free state is not necessarily peak process temperature. Track gelation, shrinkage and constraint onset. Therefore reject: Assuming peak temperature is stress-free."}}]},{"id":"a115-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"流動與固化","titleEn":"Flow and curing","description":"針對流動與固化完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for flow and curing, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a115-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-06"],"title":"流動前沿｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Flow fronts | mechanism and design","objective":"針對流動前沿，把「晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For flow fronts, turn \"Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「流動前沿」的模型：晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for flow fronts: Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Relate front maps to defect positions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Relate front maps to defect positions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：充滿模具即表示內部無空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating a full mold with void-free interiors. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付流動前沿的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for flow fronts, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-07-k1","title":"流動前沿：機制","titleEn":"Flow fronts: mechanism","text":"晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。","textEn":"Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。 必須排除的錯判：充滿模具即表示內部無空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Relate front maps to defect positions. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating a full mold with void-free interiors. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「流動前沿」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For flow fronts — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。","充滿模具即表示內部無空洞","相同終溫必有相同殘應力"],"optionsEn":["Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids.","Equating a full mold with void-free interiors","Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。 把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。 因此不能採用「充滿模具即表示內部無空洞」。","explanationEn":"Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids. Relate front maps to defect positions. Therefore reject: Equating a full mold with void-free interiors."}},{"id":"a115-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-07"],"title":"流動前沿｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Flow fronts | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對流動前沿，把「晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For flow fronts, turn \"Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。 將「充滿模具即表示內部無空洞」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Relate front maps to defect positions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating a full mold with void-free interiors\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Relate front maps to defect positions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：充滿模具即表示內部無空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating a full mold with void-free interiors. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付流動前沿的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for flow fronts: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-08-k1","title":"流動前沿：機制","titleEn":"Flow fronts: mechanism","text":"晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。","textEn":"Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。 必須排除的錯判：充滿模具即表示內部無空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Relate front maps to defect positions. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating a full mold with void-free interiors. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「流動前沿」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For flow fronts — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同終溫必有相同殘應力","把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。","充滿模具即表示內部無空洞"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress","Relate front maps to defect positions.","Equating a full mold with void-free interiors"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶粒與高低台階改變前沿，可能留下焊線掃移或空洞。 把前沿圖與缺陷位置相連。 因此不能採用「充滿模具即表示內部無空洞」。","explanationEn":"Dies and steps alter fronts, causing wire sweep or voids. Relate front maps to defect positions. Therefore reject: Equating a full mold with void-free interiors."}},{"id":"a115-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-08"],"title":"填料偏析｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Filler segregation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對填料偏析，把「局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For filler segregation, turn \"Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「填料偏析」的模型：局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「沿流向和厚度比較截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for filler segregation: Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare sections along flow and through thickness. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"沿流向和厚度比較截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare sections along flow and through thickness. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付填料偏析的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for filler segregation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-09-k1","title":"填料偏析：機制","titleEn":"Filler segregation: mechanism","text":"局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。","textEn":"Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"沿流向和厚度比較截面。 必須排除的錯判：整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare sections along flow and through thickness. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「填料偏析」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For filler segregation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差","夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦","局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation","Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness","Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。 沿流向和厚度比較截面。 因此不能採用「整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差」。","explanationEn":"Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform. Compare sections along flow and through thickness. Therefore reject: Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation."}},{"id":"a115-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-09"],"title":"填料偏析｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Filler segregation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對填料偏析，把「局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For filler segregation, turn \"Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：沿流向和厚度比較截面。 將「整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare sections along flow and through thickness. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"沿流向和厚度比較截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare sections along flow and through thickness. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付填料偏析的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for filler segregation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-10-k1","title":"填料偏析：機制","titleEn":"Filler segregation: mechanism","text":"局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。","textEn":"Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"沿流向和厚度比較截面。 必須排除的錯判：整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare sections along flow and through thickness. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「填料偏析」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For filler segregation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["沿流向和厚度比較截面。","整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差","夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦"],"optionsEn":["Compare sections along flow and through thickness.","Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation","Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部填料變化使 CTE 和模數不均。 沿流向和厚度比較截面。 因此不能採用「整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差」。","explanationEn":"Local filler variation makes CTE/modulus nonuniform. Compare sections along flow and through thickness. Therefore reject: Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation."}},{"id":"a115-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-10"],"title":"固化收縮｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對固化收縮，把「化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cure shrinkage, turn \"Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「固化收縮」的模型：化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「分離等溫固化與降溫變形。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cure shrinkage: Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"分離等溫固化與降溫變形。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固化收縮的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cure shrinkage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-11-k1","title":"固化收縮：機制","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage: mechanism","text":"化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。","textEn":"Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分離等溫固化與降溫變形。 必須排除的錯判：所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. Misinterpretation to reject: Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固化收縮」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cure shrinkage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分層只能歸因於材料黏度","化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。","所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述"],"optionsEn":["Attributing delamination only to viscosity","Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals.","Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT"],"answer":1,"explanation":"化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。 分離等溫固化與降溫變形。 因此不能採用「所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述」。","explanationEn":"Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals. Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. Therefore reject: Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT."}},{"id":"a115-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-11"],"title":"固化收縮｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對固化收縮，把「化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cure shrinkage, turn \"Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：分離等溫固化與降溫變形。 將「所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"分離等溫固化與降溫變形。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固化收縮的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cure shrinkage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-12-k1","title":"固化收縮：機制","titleEn":"Cure shrinkage: mechanism","text":"化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。","textEn":"Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分離等溫固化與降溫變形。 必須排除的錯判：所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. Misinterpretation to reject: Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固化收縮」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cure shrinkage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述","分層只能歸因於材料黏度","分離等溫固化與降溫變形。"],"optionsEn":["Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT","Attributing delamination only to viscosity","Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"化學收縮與熱收縮可作用於不同時間段。 分離等溫固化與降溫變形。 因此不能採用「所有收縮都可用 CTE·ΔT 描述」。","explanationEn":"Chemical and thermal shrinkage occur over different intervals. Separate isothermal-cure and cooling deformation. Therefore reject: Describing all shrinkage with CTE·ΔT."}}]},{"id":"a115-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"翹曲耦合","titleEn":"Warpage coupling","description":"針對翹曲耦合完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for warpage coupling, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a115-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-12"],"title":"層合不對稱｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Laminate asymmetry | mechanism and design","objective":"針對層合不對稱，把「材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For laminate asymmetry, turn \"Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「層合不對稱」的模型：材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for laminate asymmetry: Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總厚度相同必有相同翹曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating total thickness with warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層合不對稱的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for laminate asymmetry, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-13-k1","title":"層合不對稱：機制","titleEn":"Laminate asymmetry: mechanism","text":"材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。","textEn":"Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。 必須排除的錯判：總厚度相同必有相同翹曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating total thickness with warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層合不對稱」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For laminate asymmetry — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。","總厚度相同必有相同翹曲","擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確"],"optionsEn":["Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness.","Equating total thickness with warpage","Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。 比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。 因此不能採用「總厚度相同必有相同翹曲」。","explanationEn":"Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness. Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. Therefore reject: Equating total thickness with warpage."}},{"id":"a115-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-13"],"title":"層合不對稱｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Laminate asymmetry | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對層合不對稱，把「材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For laminate asymmetry, turn \"Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。 將「總厚度相同必有相同翹曲」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating total thickness with warpage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總厚度相同必有相同翹曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating total thickness with warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層合不對稱的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for laminate asymmetry: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-14-k1","title":"層合不對稱：機制","titleEn":"Laminate asymmetry: mechanism","text":"材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。","textEn":"Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。 必須排除的錯判：總厚度相同必有相同翹曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating total thickness with warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層合不對稱」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For laminate asymmetry — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確","比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。","總厚度相同必有相同翹曲"],"optionsEn":["Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties","Compare symmetric and offset-die sections.","Equating total thickness with warpage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料和厚度不對稱形成彎矩，總厚度相同亦可不同曲率。 比較上下對稱及偏置晶粒截面。 因此不能採用「總厚度相同必有相同翹曲」。","explanationEn":"Material/thickness asymmetry forms bending moments even at equal total thickness. Compare symmetric and offset-die sections. Therefore reject: Equating total thickness with warpage."}},{"id":"a115-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-14"],"title":"溫度依賴翹曲｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Temperature-dependent warp | mechanism and design","objective":"針對溫度依賴翹曲，把「室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For temperature-dependent warp, turn \"Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「溫度依賴翹曲」的模型：室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for temperature-dependent warp: Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只需室溫翹曲驗收。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Qualifying warpage at room temperature only. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付溫度依賴翹曲的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for temperature-dependent warp, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-15-k1","title":"溫度依賴翹曲：機制","titleEn":"Temperature-dependent warp: mechanism","text":"室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。","textEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。 必須排除的錯判：只需室溫翹曲驗收。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. Misinterpretation to reject: Qualifying warpage at room temperature only. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度依賴翹曲」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For temperature-dependent warp — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只需室溫翹曲驗收","相同填料百分比必有相同模數","室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying warpage at room temperature only","Equating filler percentage with modulus","Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。 量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。 因此不能採用「只需室溫翹曲驗收」。","explanationEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness. Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. Therefore reject: Qualifying warpage at room temperature only."}},{"id":"a115-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-15"],"title":"溫度依賴翹曲｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Temperature-dependent warp | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對溫度依賴翹曲，把「室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For temperature-dependent warp, turn \"Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。 將「只需室溫翹曲驗收」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. Challenge the hypothesis \"Qualifying warpage at room temperature only\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只需室溫翹曲驗收。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Qualifying warpage at room temperature only. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付溫度依賴翹曲的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for temperature-dependent warp: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-16-k1","title":"溫度依賴翹曲：機制","titleEn":"Temperature-dependent warp: mechanism","text":"室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。","textEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。 必須排除的錯判：只需室溫翹曲驗收。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. Misinterpretation to reject: Qualifying warpage at room temperature only. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度依賴翹曲」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For temperature-dependent warp — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。","只需室溫翹曲驗收","相同填料百分比必有相同模數"],"optionsEn":["Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports.","Qualifying warpage at room temperature only","Equating filler percentage with modulus"],"answer":0,"explanation":"室溫平坦不保證接合或回流溫度平坦。 量同一支撐條件的升降溫曲線。 因此不能採用「只需室溫翹曲驗收」。","explanationEn":"Room-temperature flatness does not ensure hot flatness. Measure heating/cooling curves with matched supports. Therefore reject: Qualifying warpage at room temperature only."}},{"id":"a115-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-16"],"title":"黏彈鬆弛｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Viscoelastic relaxation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對黏彈鬆弛，把「時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For viscoelastic relaxation, turn \"Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「黏彈鬆弛」的模型：時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較不同保溫時間的變形。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設自由材料 CTE 差 10 ppm/K、ΔT=100 K，失配應變為 0.001=0.1%。這不是封裝應力；要計算應力還需模數、泊松比、幾何、固化參考態及鬆弛。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for viscoelastic relaxation: Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare deformation at different dwell durations. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: A hypothetical CTE difference of 10 ppm/K over 100 K gives mismatch strain 0.001=0.1%. Stress also needs modulus, Poisson ratio, geometry, cure reference state and relaxation. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"比較不同保溫時間的變形。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare deformation at different dwell durations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同終溫必有相同殘應力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付黏彈鬆弛的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for viscoelastic relaxation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-17-k1","title":"黏彈鬆弛：機制","titleEn":"Viscoelastic relaxation: mechanism","text":"時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。","textEn":"Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較不同保溫時間的變形。 必須排除的錯判：相同終溫必有相同殘應力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare deformation at different dwell durations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設自由材料 CTE 差 10 ppm/K、ΔT=100 K，失配應變為 0.001=0.1%。這不是封裝應力；要計算應力還需模數、泊松比、幾何、固化參考態及鬆弛。","textEn":"A hypothetical CTE difference of 10 ppm/K over 100 K gives mismatch strain 0.001=0.1%. Stress also needs modulus, Poisson ratio, geometry, cure reference state and relaxation."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏彈鬆弛」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For viscoelastic relaxation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["室溫模數可代表整段固化","時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。","相同終溫必有相同殘應力"],"optionsEn":["Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing","Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits.","Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。 比較不同保溫時間的變形。 因此不能採用「相同終溫必有相同殘應力」。","explanationEn":"Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits. Compare deformation at different dwell durations. Therefore reject: Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress."}},{"id":"a115-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-17"],"title":"黏彈鬆弛｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Viscoelastic relaxation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對黏彈鬆弛，把「時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For viscoelastic relaxation, turn \"Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較不同保溫時間的變形。 將「相同終溫必有相同殘應力」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設自由材料 CTE 差 10 ppm/K、ΔT=100 K，失配應變為 0.001=0.1%。這不是封裝應力；要計算應力還需模數、泊松比、幾何、固化參考態及鬆弛。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare deformation at different dwell durations. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: A hypothetical CTE difference of 10 ppm/K over 100 K gives mismatch strain 0.001=0.1%. Stress also needs modulus, Poisson ratio, geometry, cure reference state and relaxation. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"比較不同保溫時間的變形。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare deformation at different dwell durations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同終溫必有相同殘應力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付黏彈鬆弛的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for viscoelastic relaxation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-18-k1","title":"黏彈鬆弛：機制","titleEn":"Viscoelastic relaxation: mechanism","text":"時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。","textEn":"Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較不同保溫時間的變形。 必須排除的錯判：相同終溫必有相同殘應力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare deformation at different dwell durations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設自由材料 CTE 差 10 ppm/K、ΔT=100 K，失配應變為 0.001=0.1%。這不是封裝應力；要計算應力還需模數、泊松比、幾何、固化參考態及鬆弛。","textEn":"A hypothetical CTE difference of 10 ppm/K over 100 K gives mismatch strain 0.001=0.1%. Stress also needs modulus, Poisson ratio, geometry, cure reference state and relaxation."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「黏彈鬆弛」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For viscoelastic relaxation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同終溫必有相同殘應力","室溫模數可代表整段固化","比較不同保溫時間的變形。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress","Using room-temperature modulus throughout curing","Compare deformation at different dwell durations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間與溫度影響應力鬆弛，瞬間彈性模型有適用限。 比較不同保溫時間的變形。 因此不能採用「相同終溫必有相同殘應力」。","explanationEn":"Time and temperature govern relaxation; instantaneous elasticity has limits. Compare deformation at different dwell durations. Therefore reject: Assuming equal final temperature gives equal residual stress."}}]},{"id":"a115-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"可靠度放行","titleEn":"Reliability release","description":"針對可靠度放行完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for reliability release, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a115-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-18"],"title":"量測支撐｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Measurement support | mechanism and design","objective":"針對量測支撐，把「夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For measurement support, turn \"Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「量測支撐」的模型：夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for measurement support: Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付量測支撐的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for measurement support, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-19-k1","title":"量測支撐：機制","titleEn":"Measurement support: mechanism","text":"夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。","textEn":"Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。 必須排除的錯判：夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測支撐」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For measurement support — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。","夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦","最高溫度必是零應力參考"],"optionsEn":["Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape.","Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness","Assuming peak temperature is stress-free"],"answer":0,"explanation":"夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。 記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。 因此不能採用「夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦」。","explanationEn":"Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape. Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. Therefore reject: Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness."}},{"id":"a115-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-19"],"title":"量測支撐｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Measurement support | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對量測支撐，把「夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For measurement support, turn \"Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。 將「夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付量測支撐的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for measurement support: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-20-k1","title":"量測支撐：機制","titleEn":"Measurement support: mechanism","text":"夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。","textEn":"Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。 必須排除的錯判：夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測支撐」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For measurement support — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["最高溫度必是零應力參考","記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。","夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦"],"optionsEn":["Assuming peak temperature is stress-free","Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force.","Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness"],"answer":1,"explanation":"夾持會壓平樣品並改變所量形状。 記錄重力方向、支點和接觸力。 因此不能採用「夾持後平坦即證明自由狀態平坦」。","explanationEn":"Clamping can flatten samples and change measured shape. Record gravity orientation, supports and contact force. Therefore reject: Inferring free flatness from clamped flatness."}},{"id":"a115-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-20"],"title":"分層與吸濕｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Delamination and moisture | mechanism and design","objective":"針對分層與吸濕，把「水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For delamination and moisture, turn \"Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「分層與吸濕」的模型：水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for delamination and moisture: Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：分層只能歸因於材料黏度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing delamination only to viscosity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付分層與吸濕的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for delamination and moisture, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-21-k1","title":"分層與吸濕：機制","titleEn":"Delamination and moisture: mechanism","text":"水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。","textEn":"Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。 必須排除的錯判：分層只能歸因於材料黏度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing delamination only to viscosity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分層與吸濕」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For delamination and moisture — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分層只能歸因於材料黏度","充滿模具即表示內部無空洞","水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。"],"optionsEn":["Attributing delamination only to viscosity","Equating a full mold with void-free interiors","Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination."],"answer":2,"explanation":"水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。 配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。 因此不能採用「分層只能歸因於材料黏度」。","explanationEn":"Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination. Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. Therefore reject: Attributing delamination only to viscosity."}},{"id":"a115-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-21"],"title":"分層與吸濕｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Delamination and moisture | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對分層與吸濕，把「水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For delamination and moisture, turn \"Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。 將「分層只能歸因於材料黏度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. Challenge the hypothesis \"Attributing delamination only to viscosity\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：分層只能歸因於材料黏度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing delamination only to viscosity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付分層與吸濕的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for delamination and moisture: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-22-k1","title":"分層與吸濕：機制","titleEn":"Delamination and moisture: mechanism","text":"水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。","textEn":"Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。 必須排除的錯判：分層只能歸因於材料黏度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing delamination only to viscosity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分層與吸濕」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For delamination and moisture — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。","分層只能歸因於材料黏度","充滿模具即表示內部無空洞"],"optionsEn":["Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces.","Attributing delamination only to viscosity","Equating a full mold with void-free interiors"],"answer":0,"explanation":"水分、界面黏著及熱失配可共同引發分層。 配對受濕歷程、聲學圖和破面。 因此不能採用「分層只能歸因於材料黏度」。","explanationEn":"Moisture, adhesion and thermal mismatch can jointly cause delamination. Pair moisture history, acoustic maps and fracture faces. Therefore reject: Attributing delamination only to viscosity."}},{"id":"a115-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-22"],"title":"模型校準與交接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Model calibration and handoff | mechanism and design","objective":"針對模型校準與交接，把「模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For model calibration and handoff, turn \"Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「模型校準與交接」的模型：模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for model calibration and handoff: Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付模型校準與交接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for model calibration and handoff, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-23-k1","title":"模型校準與交接：機制","titleEn":"Model calibration and handoff: mechanism","text":"模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。","textEn":"Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。 必須排除的錯判：擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型校準與交接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For model calibration and handoff — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差","模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。","擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確"],"optionsEn":["Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation","Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability.","Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties"],"answer":1,"explanation":"模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。 保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。 因此不能採用「擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確」。","explanationEn":"Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability. Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. Therefore reject: Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties."}},{"id":"a115-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"],"prerequisiteIds":["a115-v9-23"],"title":"模型校準與交接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Model calibration and handoff | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對模型校準與交接，把「模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For model calibration and handoff, turn \"Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。 將「擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付模型校準與交接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for model calibration and handoff: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a115-v9-24-k1","title":"模型校準與交接：機制","titleEn":"Model calibration and handoff: mechanism","text":"模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。","textEn":"Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]},{"id":"a115-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。 必須排除的錯判：擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","pkb-henkel-underfill"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型校準與交接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For model calibration and handoff — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確","整批配方相同就不可能局部翹曲差","保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。"],"optionsEn":["Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties","Assuming one formulation excludes local warp variation","Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模型需用獨立條件驗證，擬合一條曲線不足以預測新堆疊。 保留一種厚度或溫度歷程作盲測。 因此不能採用「擬合誤差小即證明所有物性正確」。","explanationEn":"Validate on independent conditions; fitting one curve cannot establish transferability. Hold out a thickness or thermal history for validation. Therefore reject: Treating low fit error as proof of correct material properties."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-encapsulation","subcategoryTitle":"封膠、扇出與異質整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Encapsulation, fan-out and heterogeneous integration","photoId":"bga-section"},{"id":"a116","title":"扇出型晶圓級封裝","titleEn":"Fan-out wafer-level packaging","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入重組晶圓、晶粒位移與 RDL 互連。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore reconstituted wafers, die shift and rdl interconnect, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["架構選擇","重組與模封","RDL 建構","封裝驗證"],"labelsEn":["Architecture selection","Reconstitution and molding","RDL construction","Package validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a116-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"架構選擇","titleEn":"Architecture selection","description":"針對架構選擇完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for architecture selection, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a116-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"Chip-first 與 chip-last｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Chip-first and chip-last | mechanism and design","objective":"針對Chip-first 與 chip-last，把「先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chip-first and chip-last, turn \"Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「Chip-first 與 chip-last」的模型：先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for chip-first and chip-last: Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map material/test handoffs for both routes. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map material/test handoffs for both routes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating the routes as renamed identical risks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Chip-first 與 chip-last的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for chip-first and chip-last, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-01-k1","title":"Chip-first 與 chip-last：機制","titleEn":"Chip-first and chip-last: mechanism","text":"先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。","textEn":"Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。 必須排除的錯判：兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map material/test handoffs for both routes. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating the routes as renamed identical risks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Chip-first 與 chip-last」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chip-first and chip-last — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。","兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險","平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲"],"optionsEn":["Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points.","Treating the routes as renamed identical risks","Using mean die density to describe warpage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。 畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。 因此不能採用「兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險」。","explanationEn":"Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points. Map material/test handoffs for both routes. Therefore reject: Treating the routes as renamed identical risks."}},{"id":"a116-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-01"],"title":"Chip-first 與 chip-last｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Chip-first and chip-last | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對Chip-first 與 chip-last，把「先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For chip-first and chip-last, turn \"Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。 將「兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map material/test handoffs for both routes. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating the routes as renamed identical risks\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map material/test handoffs for both routes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating the routes as renamed identical risks. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Chip-first 與 chip-last的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for chip-first and chip-last: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-02-k1","title":"Chip-first 與 chip-last：機制","titleEn":"Chip-first and chip-last: mechanism","text":"先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。","textEn":"Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。 必須排除的錯判：兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map material/test handoffs for both routes. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating the routes as renamed identical risks. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Chip-first 與 chip-last」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For chip-first and chip-last — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲","畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。","兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險"],"optionsEn":["Using mean die density to describe warpage","Map material/test handoffs for both routes.","Treating the routes as renamed identical risks"],"answer":1,"explanation":"先放晶粒或先做 RDL 改變對位、已知良品與返修節點。 畫兩路徑的材料與測試交接。 因此不能採用「兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險」。","explanationEn":"Die-first versus RDL-first changes overlay, screening and rework points. Map material/test handoffs for both routes. Therefore reject: Treating the routes as renamed identical risks."}},{"id":"a116-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-02"],"title":"扇出面積配置｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Fan-out area allocation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對扇出面積配置，把「晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fan-out area allocation, turn \"Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「扇出面積配置」的模型：晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for fan-out area allocation: Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：扇出面積只影響 I/O 數。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付扇出面積配置的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for fan-out area allocation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-03-k1","title":"扇出面積配置：機制","titleEn":"Fan-out area allocation: mechanism","text":"晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。","textEn":"Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。 必須排除的錯判：扇出面積只影響 I/O 數。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「扇出面積配置」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fan-out area allocation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["扇出面積只影響 I/O 數","可見金屬即等於可可靠接線","晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count","Equating visible metal with reliable contact","Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。 標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。 因此不能採用「扇出面積只影響 I/O 數」。","explanationEn":"Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics. Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. Therefore reject: Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count."}},{"id":"a116-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-03"],"title":"扇出面積配置｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Fan-out area allocation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對扇出面積配置，把「晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fan-out area allocation, turn \"Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。 將「扇出面積只影響 I/O 數」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：扇出面積只影響 I/O 數。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付扇出面積配置的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for fan-out area allocation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-04-k1","title":"扇出面積配置：機制","titleEn":"Fan-out area allocation: mechanism","text":"晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。","textEn":"Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。 必須排除的錯判：扇出面積只影響 I/O 數。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「扇出面積配置」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fan-out area allocation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。","扇出面積只影響 I/O 數","可見金屬即等於可可靠接線"],"optionsEn":["Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs.","Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count","Equating visible metal with reliable contact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒外增加配線區同時改變封裝尺寸與機械邊界。 標出晶粒、RDL、焊球和保護區。 因此不能採用「扇出面積只影響 I/O 數」。","explanationEn":"Extra routing beyond die edges changes package size and mechanics. Mark die, RDL, balls and keep-outs. Therefore reject: Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count."}},{"id":"a116-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-04"],"title":"良品與重組地圖｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Good-die and reconstitution map | mechanism and design","objective":"針對良品與重組地圖，把「來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For good-die and reconstitution map, turn \"Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「良品與重組地圖」的模型：來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for good-die and reconstitution map: Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：重組後只保留封裝編號即可。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良品與重組地圖的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for good-die and reconstitution map, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-05-k1","title":"良品與重組地圖：機制","titleEn":"Good-die and reconstitution map: mechanism","text":"來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。","textEn":"Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。 必須排除的錯判：重組後只保留封裝編號即可。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. Misinterpretation to reject: Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良品與重組地圖」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For good-die and reconstitution map — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線","來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。","重組後只保留封裝編號即可"],"optionsEn":["Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment","Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability.","Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution"],"answer":1,"explanation":"來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。 驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。 因此不能採用「重組後只保留封裝編號即可」。","explanationEn":"Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability. Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. Therefore reject: Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution."}},{"id":"a116-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-05"],"title":"良品與重組地圖｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Good-die and reconstitution map | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對良品與重組地圖，把「來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For good-die and reconstitution map, turn \"Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。 將「重組後只保留封裝編號即可」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. Challenge the hypothesis \"Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：重組後只保留封裝編號即可。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良品與重組地圖的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for good-die and reconstitution map: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-06-k1","title":"良品與重組地圖：機制","titleEn":"Good-die and reconstitution map: mechanism","text":"來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。","textEn":"Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。 必須排除的錯判：重組後只保留封裝編號即可。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. Misinterpretation to reject: Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良品與重組地圖」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For good-die and reconstitution map — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["重組後只保留封裝編號即可","對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線","驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。"],"optionsEn":["Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution","Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment","Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping."],"answer":2,"explanation":"來源晶圓與重組位置需一對一可追溯。 驗證翻轉、旋轉與批次映射。 因此不能採用「重組後只保留封裝編號即可」。","explanationEn":"Source wafer and reconstituted position need one-to-one traceability. Verify flip, rotation and lot mapping. Therefore reject: Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution."}}]},{"id":"a116-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"重組與模封","titleEn":"Reconstitution and molding","description":"針對重組與模封完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for reconstitution and molding, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a116-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-06"],"title":"載板與膠層｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Carrier and adhesive | mechanism and design","objective":"針對載板與膠層，把「載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier and adhesive, turn \"Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「載板與膠層」的模型：載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較模封前後逐顆位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for carrier and adhesive: Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare per-die positions before/after molding. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較模封前後逐顆位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare per-die positions before/after molding. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始放置精準就不會後續位移。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板與膠層的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for carrier and adhesive, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-07-k1","title":"載板與膠層：機制","titleEn":"Carrier and adhesive: mechanism","text":"載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。","textEn":"Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較模封前後逐顆位置。 必須排除的錯判：初始放置精準就不會後續位移。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare per-die positions before/after molding. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板與膠層」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier and adhesive — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。","初始放置精準就不會後續位移","RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環"],"optionsEn":["Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift.","Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift","Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。 比較模封前後逐顆位置。 因此不能採用「初始放置精準就不會後續位移」。","explanationEn":"Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift. Compare per-die positions before/after molding. Therefore reject: Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift."}},{"id":"a116-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-07"],"title":"載板與膠層｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Carrier and adhesive | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對載板與膠層，把「載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier and adhesive, turn \"Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較模封前後逐顆位置。 將「初始放置精準就不會後續位移」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare per-die positions before/after molding. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較模封前後逐顆位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare per-die positions before/after molding. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：初始放置精準就不會後續位移。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板與膠層的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for carrier and adhesive: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-08-k1","title":"載板與膠層：機制","titleEn":"Carrier and adhesive: mechanism","text":"載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。","textEn":"Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較模封前後逐顆位置。 必須排除的錯判：初始放置精準就不會後續位移。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare per-die positions before/after molding. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板與膠層」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier and adhesive — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環","比較模封前後逐顆位置。","初始放置精準就不會後續位移"],"optionsEn":["Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes","Compare per-die positions before/after molding.","Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift"],"answer":1,"explanation":"載板 CTE 和黏著改變模封後晶粒位移。 比較模封前後逐顆位置。 因此不能採用「初始放置精準就不會後續位移」。","explanationEn":"Carrier CTE and adhesion affect post-mold die shift. Compare per-die positions before/after molding. Therefore reject: Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift."}},{"id":"a116-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-08"],"title":"模封流動｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Mold flow | mechanism and design","objective":"針對模封流動，把「流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mold flow, turn \"Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「模封流動」的模型：流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「依流向分組分析位移向量。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for mold flow: Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Group displacement vectors by flow direction. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"依流向分組分析位移向量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Group displacement vectors by flow direction. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：位移是純平移不需量旋轉。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating shift as translation only. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付模封流動的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for mold flow, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-09-k1","title":"模封流動：機制","titleEn":"Mold flow: mechanism","text":"流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。","textEn":"Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"依流向分組分析位移向量。 必須排除的錯判：位移是純平移不需量旋轉。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Group displacement vectors by flow direction. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating shift as translation only. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模封流動」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mold flow — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["位移是純平移不需量旋轉","球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸","流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。"],"optionsEn":["Treating shift as translation only","Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact","Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies."],"answer":2,"explanation":"流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。 依流向分組分析位移向量。 因此不能採用「位移是純平移不需量旋轉」。","explanationEn":"Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies. Group displacement vectors by flow direction. Therefore reject: Treating shift as translation only."}},{"id":"a116-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-09"],"title":"模封流動｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Mold flow | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對模封流動，把「流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mold flow, turn \"Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：依流向分組分析位移向量。 將「位移是純平移不需量旋轉」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Group displacement vectors by flow direction. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating shift as translation only\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"依流向分組分析位移向量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Group displacement vectors by flow direction. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：位移是純平移不需量旋轉。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating shift as translation only. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付模封流動的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for mold flow: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-10-k1","title":"模封流動：機制","titleEn":"Mold flow: mechanism","text":"流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。","textEn":"Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"依流向分組分析位移向量。 必須排除的錯判：位移是純平移不需量旋轉。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Group displacement vectors by flow direction. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating shift as translation only. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模封流動」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mold flow — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["依流向分組分析位移向量。","位移是純平移不需量旋轉","球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸"],"optionsEn":["Group displacement vectors by flow direction.","Treating shift as translation only","Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"流動載荷和固化收縮可能造成平移與旋轉。 依流向分組分析位移向量。 因此不能採用「位移是純平移不需量旋轉」。","explanationEn":"Flow loading and cure shrinkage can translate/rotate dies. Group displacement vectors by flow direction. Therefore reject: Treating shift as translation only."}},{"id":"a116-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-10"],"title":"重組翹曲｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Reconstituted warpage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對重組翹曲，把「晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reconstituted warpage, turn \"Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「重組翹曲」的模型：晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for reconstituted warpage: Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean die density to describe warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付重組翹曲的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for reconstituted warpage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-11-k1","title":"重組翹曲：機制","titleEn":"Reconstituted warpage: mechanism","text":"晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。","textEn":"Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。 必須排除的錯判：平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean die density to describe warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重組翹曲」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reconstituted warpage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率","晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。","平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲"],"optionsEn":["Equating package failure rate with die failure rate","Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature.","Using mean die density to describe warpage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。 比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。 因此不能採用「平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲」。","explanationEn":"Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature. Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. Therefore reject: Using mean die density to describe warpage."}},{"id":"a116-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-11"],"title":"重組翹曲｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Reconstituted warpage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對重組翹曲，把「晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reconstituted warpage, turn \"Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。 將「平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using mean die density to describe warpage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean die density to describe warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付重組翹曲的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for reconstituted warpage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-12-k1","title":"重組翹曲：機制","titleEn":"Reconstituted warpage: mechanism","text":"晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。","textEn":"Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。 必須排除的錯判：平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean die density to describe warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「重組翹曲」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reconstituted warpage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲","封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率","比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。"],"optionsEn":["Using mean die density to describe warpage","Equating package failure rate with die failure rate","Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒與模封材料分布形成非均勻剛性和曲率。 比較熱態與室溫全片形狀。 因此不能採用「平均晶粒密度足以描述翹曲」。","explanationEn":"Die/mold distribution creates nonuniform stiffness and curvature. Compare hot and room-temperature wafer shapes. Therefore reject: Using mean die density to describe warpage."}}]},{"id":"a116-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"RDL 建構","titleEn":"RDL construction","description":"針對RDL 建構完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for rdl construction, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a116-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-12"],"title":"露墊與表面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pad exposure and surface | mechanism and design","objective":"針對露墊與表面，把「露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pad exposure and surface, turn \"Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「露墊與表面」的模型：露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pad exposure and surface: Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair pad sections with contact resistance. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair pad sections with contact resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：可見金屬即等於可可靠接線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating visible metal with reliable contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付露墊與表面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pad exposure and surface, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-13-k1","title":"露墊與表面：機制","titleEn":"Pad exposure and surface: mechanism","text":"露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。","textEn":"Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。 必須排除的錯判：可見金屬即等於可可靠接線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair pad sections with contact resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating visible metal with reliable contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「露墊與表面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pad exposure and surface — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。","可見金屬即等於可可靠接線","每片加工費較低就一定更便宜"],"optionsEn":["Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage.","Equating visible metal with reliable contact","Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost"],"answer":0,"explanation":"露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。 配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。 因此不能採用「可見金屬即等於可可靠接線」。","explanationEn":"Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage. Pair pad sections with contact resistance. Therefore reject: Equating visible metal with reliable contact."}},{"id":"a116-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-13"],"title":"露墊與表面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pad exposure and surface | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對露墊與表面，把「露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pad exposure and surface, turn \"Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。 將「可見金屬即等於可可靠接線」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair pad sections with contact resistance. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating visible metal with reliable contact\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair pad sections with contact resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：可見金屬即等於可可靠接線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating visible metal with reliable contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付露墊與表面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pad exposure and surface: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-14-k1","title":"露墊與表面：機制","titleEn":"Pad exposure and surface: mechanism","text":"露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。","textEn":"Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。 必須排除的錯判：可見金屬即等於可可靠接線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair pad sections with contact resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating visible metal with reliable contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「露墊與表面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pad exposure and surface — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["每片加工費較低就一定更便宜","配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。","可見金屬即等於可可靠接線"],"optionsEn":["Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost","Pair pad sections with contact resistance.","Equating visible metal with reliable contact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"露墊、台階與殘膠決定 RDL 接觸和覆蓋。 配對露墊截面與接觸電阻。 因此不能採用「可見金屬即等於可可靠接線」。","explanationEn":"Pad exposure, steps and residue determine RDL contact/coverage. Pair pad sections with contact resistance. Therefore reject: Equating visible metal with reliable contact."}},{"id":"a116-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-14"],"title":"自適應對位｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Adaptive alignment | mechanism and design","objective":"針對自適應對位，把「以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For adaptive alignment, turn \"Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「自適應對位」的模型：以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for adaptive alignment: Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付自適應對位的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for adaptive alignment, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-15-k1","title":"自適應對位：機制","titleEn":"Adaptive alignment: mechanism","text":"以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。","textEn":"Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。 必須排除的錯判：對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. Misinterpretation to reject: Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「自適應對位」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For adaptive alignment — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線","兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險","以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。"],"optionsEn":["Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment","Treating the routes as renamed identical risks","Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。 比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。 因此不能採用「對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線」。","explanationEn":"Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules. Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. Therefore reject: Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment."}},{"id":"a116-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-15"],"title":"自適應對位｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Adaptive alignment | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對自適應對位，把「以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For adaptive alignment, turn \"Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。 將「對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付自適應對位的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for adaptive alignment: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-16-k1","title":"自適應對位：機制","titleEn":"Adaptive alignment: mechanism","text":"以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。","textEn":"Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。 必須排除的錯判：對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. Misinterpretation to reject: Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「自適應對位」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For adaptive alignment — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。","對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線","兩路徑只改步驟名稱不改風險"],"optionsEn":["Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation.","Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment","Treating the routes as renamed identical risks"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以實際晶粒位置調整圖形需保留線間距及過孔規則。 比較調整前後 DRC 與捕捉餘量。 因此不能採用「對位修正可以無限制拉伸配線」。","explanationEn":"Adapting patterns to die locations must preserve spacing and via rules. Compare DRC and capture margin before/after adaptation. Therefore reject: Allowing unlimited routing stretch for alignment."}},{"id":"a116-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-16"],"title":"跨材料 RDL｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cross-material RDL | mechanism and design","objective":"針對跨材料 RDL，把「銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cross-material rdl, turn \"Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「跨材料 RDL」的模型：銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設重組後晶粒平移 4 μm，而 RDL 捕捉墊可允許 ±6 μm；留給曝光、熱變形與量測不確定度的合計餘量只剩 2 μm，不可把各站公差各自都設為 6 μm。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cross-material rdl: Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Locate cracks relative to die edges. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: If illustrative die shift is 4 μm and the RDL capture allowance is ±6 μm, only 2 μm remains for exposure, thermal deformation and measurement uncertainty—not 6 μm at every station. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Locate cracks relative to die edges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付跨材料 RDL的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cross-material rdl, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-17-k1","title":"跨材料 RDL：機制","titleEn":"Cross-material RDL: mechanism","text":"銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。","textEn":"Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。 必須排除的錯判：RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Locate cracks relative to die edges. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設重組後晶粒平移 4 μm，而 RDL 捕捉墊可允許 ±6 μm；留給曝光、熱變形與量測不確定度的合計餘量只剩 2 μm，不可把各站公差各自都設為 6 μm。","textEn":"If illustrative die shift is 4 μm and the RDL capture allowance is ±6 μm, only 2 μm remains for exposure, thermal deformation and measurement uncertainty—not 6 μm at every station."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨材料 RDL」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cross-material rdl — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["扇出面積只影響 I/O 數","銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。","RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環"],"optionsEn":["Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count","Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain.","Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。 定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。 因此不能採用「RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環」。","explanationEn":"Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain. Locate cracks relative to die edges. Therefore reject: Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes."}},{"id":"a116-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-17"],"title":"跨材料 RDL｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cross-material RDL | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對跨材料 RDL，把「銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cross-material rdl, turn \"Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。 將「RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設重組後晶粒平移 4 μm，而 RDL 捕捉墊可允許 ±6 μm；留給曝光、熱變形與量測不確定度的合計餘量只剩 2 μm，不可把各站公差各自都設為 6 μm。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Locate cracks relative to die edges. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: If illustrative die shift is 4 μm and the RDL capture allowance is ±6 μm, only 2 μm remains for exposure, thermal deformation and measurement uncertainty—not 6 μm at every station. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Locate cracks relative to die edges. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付跨材料 RDL的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cross-material rdl: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-18-k1","title":"跨材料 RDL：機制","titleEn":"Cross-material RDL: mechanism","text":"銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。","textEn":"Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。 必須排除的錯判：RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Locate cracks relative to die edges. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設重組後晶粒平移 4 μm，而 RDL 捕捉墊可允許 ±6 μm；留給曝光、熱變形與量測不確定度的合計餘量只剩 2 μm，不可把各站公差各自都設為 6 μm。","textEn":"If illustrative die shift is 4 μm and the RDL capture allowance is ±6 μm, only 2 μm remains for exposure, thermal deformation and measurement uncertainty—not 6 μm at every station."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨材料 RDL」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cross-material rdl — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環","扇出面積只影響 I/O 數","定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。"],"optionsEn":["Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes","Assuming fan-out area affects only I/O count","Locate cracks relative to die edges."],"answer":2,"explanation":"銅線跨越矽與模封邊界時承受局部失配應變。 定位裂紋與晶粒邊緣的關係。 因此不能採用「RDL 直流導通便不需熱循環」。","explanationEn":"Cu lines crossing Si/mold boundaries experience local mismatch strain. Locate cracks relative to die edges. Therefore reject: Skipping thermal cycling after RDL continuity passes."}}]},{"id":"a116-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"封裝驗證","titleEn":"Package validation","description":"針對封裝驗證完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for package validation, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a116-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-18"],"title":"焊球與板連接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Balls and board connection | mechanism and design","objective":"針對焊球與板連接，把「封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For balls and board connection, turn \"Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「焊球與板連接」的模型：封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for balls and board connection: Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊球與板連接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for balls and board connection, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-19-k1","title":"焊球與板連接：機制","titleEn":"Balls and board connection: mechanism","text":"封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。","textEn":"Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。 必須排除的錯判：球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊球與板連接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For balls and board connection — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。","球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸","重組後只保留封裝編號即可"],"optionsEn":["Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact.","Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact","Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution"],"answer":0,"explanation":"封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。 做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。 因此不能採用「球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸」。","explanationEn":"Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact. Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. Therefore reject: Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact."}},{"id":"a116-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-19"],"title":"焊球與板連接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Balls and board connection | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對焊球與板連接，把「封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For balls and board connection, turn \"Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。 將「球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊球與板連接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for balls and board connection: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-20-k1","title":"焊球與板連接：機制","titleEn":"Balls and board connection: mechanism","text":"封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。","textEn":"Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。 必須排除的錯判：球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊球與板連接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For balls and board connection — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["重組後只保留封裝編號即可","做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。","球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸"],"optionsEn":["Keeping only final package IDs after reconstitution","Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections.","Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"封裝翹曲、球高和板變形共同決定接觸。 做熱態共面性與接合截面比較。 因此不能採用「球徑一致即可保證全部焊點接觸」。","explanationEn":"Package warp, ball height and board deformation jointly determine contact. Compare hot coplanarity and bond sections. Therefore reject: Using equal ball diameter to guarantee all joints contact."}},{"id":"a116-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-20"],"title":"端到端測試｜機制與設計","titleEn":"End-to-end tests | mechanism and design","objective":"針對端到端測試，把「晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For end-to-end tests, turn \"Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「端到端測試」的模型：晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立各測試結構和故障對照表。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for end-to-end tests: Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map test structures to failure classes. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立各測試結構和故障對照表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map test structures to failure classes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating package failure rate with die failure rate. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付端到端測試的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for end-to-end tests, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-21-k1","title":"端到端測試：機制","titleEn":"End-to-end tests: mechanism","text":"晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。","textEn":"Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立各測試結構和故障對照表。 必須排除的錯判：封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map test structures to failure classes. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating package failure rate with die failure rate. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「端到端測試」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For end-to-end tests — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率","初始放置精準就不會後續位移","晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。"],"optionsEn":["Equating package failure rate with die failure rate","Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift","Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。 建立各測試結構和故障對照表。 因此不能採用「封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率」。","explanationEn":"Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses. Map test structures to failure classes. Therefore reject: Equating package failure rate with die failure rate."}},{"id":"a116-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-21"],"title":"端到端測試｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"End-to-end tests | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對端到端測試，把「晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For end-to-end tests, turn \"Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立各測試結構和故障對照表。 將「封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map test structures to failure classes. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating package failure rate with die failure rate\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立各測試結構和故障對照表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map test structures to failure classes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating package failure rate with die failure rate. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付端到端測試的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for end-to-end tests: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-22-k1","title":"端到端測試：機制","titleEn":"End-to-end tests: mechanism","text":"晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。","textEn":"Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立各測試結構和故障對照表。 必須排除的錯判：封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map test structures to failure classes. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating package failure rate with die failure rate. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「端到端測試」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For end-to-end tests — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["建立各測試結構和故障對照表。","封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率","初始放置精準就不會後續位移"],"optionsEn":["Map test structures to failure classes.","Equating package failure rate with die failure rate","Assuming accurate initial placement prevents later shift"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒、RDL 與板接口需分層定位以免誤判良率來源。 建立各測試結構和故障對照表。 因此不能採用「封裝總失效率可直接當晶粒失效率」。","explanationEn":"Localize die, RDL and board interfaces separately to identify yield losses. Map test structures to failure classes. Therefore reject: Equating package failure rate with die failure rate."}},{"id":"a116-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-22"],"title":"良率與成本｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Yield and cost | mechanism and design","objective":"針對良率與成本，把「良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For yield and cost, turn \"Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「良率與成本」的模型：良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for yield and cost: Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare routes at equal package functionality. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare routes at equal package functionality. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每片加工費較低就一定更便宜。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良率與成本的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for yield and cost, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-23-k1","title":"良率與成本：機制","titleEn":"Yield and cost: mechanism","text":"良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。","textEn":"Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。 必須排除的錯判：每片加工費較低就一定更便宜。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare routes at equal package functionality. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良率與成本」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For yield and cost — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["位移是純平移不需量旋轉","良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。","每片加工費較低就一定更便宜"],"optionsEn":["Treating shift as translation only","Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package.","Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost"],"answer":1,"explanation":"良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。 比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。 因此不能採用「每片加工費較低就一定更便宜」。","explanationEn":"Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package. Compare routes at equal package functionality. Therefore reject: Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost."}},{"id":"a116-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"],"prerequisiteIds":["a116-v9-23"],"title":"良率與成本｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Yield and cost | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對良率與成本，把「良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For yield and cost, turn \"Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。 將「每片加工費較低就一定更便宜」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare routes at equal package functionality. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare routes at equal package functionality. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每片加工費較低就一定更便宜。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良率與成本的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for yield and cost: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a116-v9-24-k1","title":"良率與成本：機制","titleEn":"Yield and cost: mechanism","text":"良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。","textEn":"Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]},{"id":"a116-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。 必須排除的錯判：每片加工費較低就一定更便宜。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare routes at equal package functionality. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imecfan","v9a-asefan"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良率與成本」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For yield and cost — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["每片加工費較低就一定更便宜","位移是純平移不需量旋轉","比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。"],"optionsEn":["Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost","Treating shift as translation only","Compare routes at equal package functionality."],"answer":2,"explanation":"良率、可用面積和重組損失決定每良品成本。 比較相同封裝功能下兩路徑成本。 因此不能採用「每片加工費較低就一定更便宜」。","explanationEn":"Yield, usable area and reconstitution loss set cost per good package. Compare routes at equal package functionality. Therefore reject: Equating lower wafer processing cost with lower unit cost."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-encapsulation","subcategoryTitle":"封膠、扇出與異質整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Encapsulation, fan-out and heterogeneous integration","photoId":"v9-quilt-array"},{"id":"a117","title":"扇出型面板級封裝","titleEn":"Fan-out panel-level packaging","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入大面積均勻性、面板變形與拼接對位。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore large-area uniformity, panel distortion and stitching, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["面板布局","重組與搬運","大面積圖形","良率與可靠度"],"labelsEn":["Panel layout","Reconstitution and handling","Large-area patterning","Yield and reliability"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a117-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"面板布局","titleEn":"Panel layout","description":"針對面板布局完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for panel layout, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a117-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"格式與設備邊界｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Format and tool boundaries | mechanism and design","objective":"針對格式與設備邊界，把「面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For format and tool boundaries, turn \"Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「格式與設備邊界」的模型：面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立所有站點有效處理面積表。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for format and tool boundaries: Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: List effective process areas at every station. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立所有站點有效處理面積表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List effective process areas at every station. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：單一設備可容納就代表整線可用。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付格式與設備邊界的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for format and tool boundaries, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-01-k1","title":"格式與設備邊界：機制","titleEn":"Format and tool boundaries: mechanism","text":"面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。","textEn":"Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立所有站點有效處理面積表。 必須排除的錯判：單一設備可容納就代表整線可用。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List effective process areas at every station. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「格式與設備邊界」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For format and tool boundaries — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。","單一設備可容納就代表整線可用","只採樣中心即可代表面板"],"optionsEn":["Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection.","Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility","Sampling only the center to represent a panel"],"answer":0,"explanation":"面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。 建立所有站點有效處理面積表。 因此不能採用「單一設備可容納就代表整線可用」。","explanationEn":"Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection. List effective process areas at every station. Therefore reject: Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility."}},{"id":"a117-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-01"],"title":"格式與設備邊界｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Format and tool boundaries | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對格式與設備邊界，把「面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For format and tool boundaries, turn \"Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立所有站點有效處理面積表。 將「單一設備可容納就代表整線可用」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: List effective process areas at every station. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立所有站點有效處理面積表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List effective process areas at every station. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：單一設備可容納就代表整線可用。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付格式與設備邊界的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for format and tool boundaries: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-02-k1","title":"格式與設備邊界：機制","titleEn":"Format and tool boundaries: mechanism","text":"面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。","textEn":"Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立所有站點有效處理面積表。 必須排除的錯判：單一設備可容納就代表整線可用。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List effective process areas at every station. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「格式與設備邊界」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For format and tool boundaries — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只採樣中心即可代表面板","建立所有站點有效處理面積表。","單一設備可容納就代表整線可用"],"optionsEn":["Sampling only the center to represent a panel","List effective process areas at every station.","Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility"],"answer":1,"explanation":"面板尺寸須同曝光、鍍膜、搬運和檢測設備相容。 建立所有站點有效處理面積表。 因此不能採用「單一設備可容納就代表整線可用」。","explanationEn":"Panel size must fit patterning, deposition, handling and inspection. List effective process areas at every station. Therefore reject: Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility."}},{"id":"a117-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-02"],"title":"邊緣與利用率｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Edges and utilization | mechanism and design","objective":"針對邊緣與利用率，把「邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For edges and utilization, turn \"Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「邊緣與利用率」的模型：邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for edges and utilization: Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總面積除單位面積就是實際產量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using area division as actual output. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付邊緣與利用率的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for edges and utilization, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-03-k1","title":"邊緣與利用率：機制","titleEn":"Edges and utilization: mechanism","text":"邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。","textEn":"Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。 必須排除的錯判：總面積除單位面積就是實際產量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. Misinterpretation to reject: Using area division as actual output. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「邊緣與利用率」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For edges and utilization — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總面積除單位面積就是實際產量","每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題","邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。"],"optionsEn":["Using area division as actual output","Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects","Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。 用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。 因此不能採用「總面積除單位面積就是實際產量」。","explanationEn":"Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization. Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. Therefore reject: Using area division as actual output."}},{"id":"a117-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-03"],"title":"邊緣與利用率｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Edges and utilization | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對邊緣與利用率，把「邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For edges and utilization, turn \"Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。 將「總面積除單位面積就是實際產量」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using area division as actual output\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總面積除單位面積就是實際產量。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using area division as actual output. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付邊緣與利用率的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for edges and utilization: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-04-k1","title":"邊緣與利用率：機制","titleEn":"Edges and utilization: mechanism","text":"邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。","textEn":"Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。 必須排除的錯判：總面積除單位面積就是實際產量。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. Misinterpretation to reject: Using area division as actual output. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「邊緣與利用率」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For edges and utilization — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。","總面積除單位面積就是實際產量","每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題"],"optionsEn":["Count grid placements rather than divide area alone.","Using area division as actual output","Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects"],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣排除、街道和測試區降低幾何利用率。 用實際格點配置計數而非只除面積。 因此不能採用「總面積除單位面積就是實際產量」。","explanationEn":"Edge exclusions, streets and test zones reduce utilization. Count grid placements rather than divide area alone. Therefore reject: Using area division as actual output."}},{"id":"a117-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-04"],"title":"晶粒分布｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Die distribution | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶粒分布，把「不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die distribution, turn \"Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶粒分布」的模型：不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for die distribution: Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare central, edge and corner layouts. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare central, edge and corner layouts. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同平均密度即可消除局部差異。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal mean density removes local differences. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒分布的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for die distribution, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-05-k1","title":"晶粒分布：機制","titleEn":"Die distribution: mechanism","text":"不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。","textEn":"Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。 必須排除的錯判：相同平均密度即可消除局部差異。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare central, edge and corner layouts. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal mean density removes local differences. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒分布」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die distribution — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區","不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。","相同平均密度即可消除局部差異"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes","Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional.","Assuming equal mean density removes local differences"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。 比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。 因此不能採用「相同平均密度即可消除局部差異」。","explanationEn":"Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional. Compare central, edge and corner layouts. Therefore reject: Assuming equal mean density removes local differences."}},{"id":"a117-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-05"],"title":"晶粒分布｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Die distribution | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶粒分布，把「不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die distribution, turn \"Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。 將「相同平均密度即可消除局部差異」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare central, edge and corner layouts. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming equal mean density removes local differences\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare central, edge and corner layouts. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同平均密度即可消除局部差異。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming equal mean density removes local differences. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒分布的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for die distribution: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-06-k1","title":"晶粒分布：機制","titleEn":"Die distribution: mechanism","text":"不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。","textEn":"Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。 必須排除的錯判：相同平均密度即可消除局部差異。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare central, edge and corner layouts. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming equal mean density removes local differences. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒分布」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die distribution — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同平均密度即可消除局部差異","平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區","比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal mean density removes local differences","Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes","Compare central, edge and corner layouts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不均勻晶粒密度使模封流動和剛性有方向性。 比較中央、邊緣與角落配置。 因此不能採用「相同平均密度即可消除局部差異」。","explanationEn":"Uneven die density makes mold flow and stiffness directional. Compare central, edge and corner layouts. Therefore reject: Assuming equal mean density removes local differences."}}]},{"id":"a117-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"重組與搬運","titleEn":"Reconstitution and handling","description":"針對重組與搬運完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for reconstitution and handling, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a117-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-06"],"title":"搬運撓曲｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Handling sag | mechanism and design","objective":"針對搬運撓曲，把「大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For handling sag, turn \"Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「搬運撓曲」的模型：大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫吸盤間距與懸空區。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for handling sag: Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫吸盤間距與懸空區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付搬運撓曲的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for handling sag, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-07-k1","title":"搬運撓曲：機制","titleEn":"Handling sag: mechanism","text":"大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。","textEn":"Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫吸盤間距與懸空區。 必須排除的錯判：量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. Misinterpretation to reject: Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「搬運撓曲」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For handling sag — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。","量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲","縮放全圖不會改變電性規則"],"optionsEn":["Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support.","Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag","Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules"],"answer":0,"explanation":"大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。 畫吸盤間距與懸空區。 因此不能採用「量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲」。","explanationEn":"Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support. Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. Therefore reject: Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag."}},{"id":"a117-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-07"],"title":"搬運撓曲｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Handling sag | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對搬運撓曲，把「大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For handling sag, turn \"Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫吸盤間距與懸空區。 將「量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫吸盤間距與懸空區。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付搬運撓曲的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for handling sag: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-08-k1","title":"搬運撓曲：機制","titleEn":"Handling sag: mechanism","text":"大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。","textEn":"Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫吸盤間距與懸空區。 必須排除的錯判：量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. Misinterpretation to reject: Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「搬運撓曲」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For handling sag — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["縮放全圖不會改變電性規則","畫吸盤間距與懸空區。","量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲"],"optionsEn":["Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules","Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans.","Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag"],"answer":1,"explanation":"大跨距使重力撓曲增加，取放時形狀不同於量測平台。 畫吸盤間距與懸空區。 因此不能採用「量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲」。","explanationEn":"Large spans increase sag; handling shape differs from metrology support. Draw suction spacing and unsupported spans. Therefore reject: Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag."}},{"id":"a117-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-08"],"title":"熱變形場｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal distortion field | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱變形場，把「長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal distortion field, turn \"Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱變形場」的模型：長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal distortion field: Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱變形場的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal distortion field, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-09-k1","title":"熱變形場：機制","titleEn":"Thermal distortion field: mechanism","text":"長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。","textEn":"Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。 必須排除的錯判：一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. Misinterpretation to reject: Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱變形場」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal distortion field — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形","面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格","長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。"],"optionsEn":["Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation","Inferring package warpage from panel warpage","Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。 擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。 因此不能採用「一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形」。","explanationEn":"Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales. Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. Therefore reject: Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation."}},{"id":"a117-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-09"],"title":"熱變形場｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal distortion field | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱變形場，把「長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal distortion field, turn \"Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。 將「一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. Challenge the hypothesis \"Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱變形場的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal distortion field: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-10-k1","title":"熱變形場：機制","titleEn":"Thermal distortion field: mechanism","text":"長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。","textEn":"Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。 必須排除的錯判：一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. Misinterpretation to reject: Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱變形場」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal distortion field — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。","一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形","面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格"],"optionsEn":["Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields.","Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation","Inferring package warpage from panel warpage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"長尺度下小 CTE 差亦造成顯著非剛體位移。 擬合平移旋轉後再看殘差場。 因此不能採用「一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形」。","explanationEn":"Small CTE differences create substantial nonrigid displacement over large scales. Fit rigid motion, then inspect residual fields. Therefore reject: Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation."}},{"id":"a117-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-10"],"title":"模封角落｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Mold corners | mechanism and design","objective":"針對模封角落，把「矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mold corners, turn \"Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「模封角落」的模型：矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for mold corners: Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Track corner voids and warpage separately. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Track corner voids and warpage separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只採樣中心即可代表面板。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Sampling only the center to represent a panel. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付模封角落的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for mold corners, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-11-k1","title":"模封角落：機制","titleEn":"Mold corners: mechanism","text":"矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。","textEn":"Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。 必須排除的錯判：只採樣中心即可代表面板。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Track corner voids and warpage separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Sampling only the center to represent a panel. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模封角落」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mold corners — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同總良率代表同樣成熟度","矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。","只採樣中心即可代表面板"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity","Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers.","Sampling only the center to represent a panel"],"answer":1,"explanation":"矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。 單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。 因此不能採用「只採樣中心即可代表面板」。","explanationEn":"Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers. Track corner voids and warpage separately. Therefore reject: Sampling only the center to represent a panel."}},{"id":"a117-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-11"],"title":"模封角落｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Mold corners | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對模封角落，把「矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mold corners, turn \"Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。 將「只採樣中心即可代表面板」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Track corner voids and warpage separately. Challenge the hypothesis \"Sampling only the center to represent a panel\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Track corner voids and warpage separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只採樣中心即可代表面板。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Sampling only the center to represent a panel. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付模封角落的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for mold corners: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-12-k1","title":"模封角落：機制","titleEn":"Mold corners: mechanism","text":"矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。","textEn":"Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。 必須排除的錯判：只採樣中心即可代表面板。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Track corner voids and warpage separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Sampling only the center to represent a panel. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模封角落」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mold corners — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只採樣中心即可代表面板","相同總良率代表同樣成熟度","單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。"],"optionsEn":["Sampling only the center to represent a panel","Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity","Track corner voids and warpage separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"矩形角落的流動和應力邊界不同於中央。 單獨統計四角空洞和翹曲。 因此不能採用「只採樣中心即可代表面板」。","explanationEn":"Rectangular corners have different flow/stress boundaries from centers. Track corner voids and warpage separately. Therefore reject: Sampling only the center to represent a panel."}}]},{"id":"a117-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"大面積圖形","titleEn":"Large-area patterning","description":"針對大面積圖形完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for large-area patterning, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a117-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-12"],"title":"曝光拼接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Exposure stitching | mechanism and design","objective":"針對曝光拼接，把「曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For exposure stitching, turn \"Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「曝光拼接」的模型：曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for exposure stitching: Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付曝光拼接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for exposure stitching, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-13-k1","title":"曝光拼接：機制","titleEn":"Exposure stitching: mechanism","text":"曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。","textEn":"Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。 必須排除的錯判：每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曝光拼接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For exposure stitching — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。","每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題","面板越大成本必單調下降"],"optionsEn":["Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control.","Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects","Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost"],"answer":0,"explanation":"曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。 跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。 因此不能採用「每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題」。","explanationEn":"Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control. Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. Therefore reject: Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects."}},{"id":"a117-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-13"],"title":"曝光拼接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Exposure stitching | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對曝光拼接，把「曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For exposure stitching, turn \"Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。 將「每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付曝光拼接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for exposure stitching: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-14-k1","title":"曝光拼接：機制","titleEn":"Exposure stitching: mechanism","text":"曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。","textEn":"Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。 必須排除的錯判：每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「曝光拼接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For exposure stitching — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["面板越大成本必單調下降","跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。","每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題"],"optionsEn":["Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost","Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams.","Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects"],"answer":1,"explanation":"曝光場接縫需控制位置、尺度和線段連續性。 跨接縫設計線阻與套刻見證。 因此不能採用「每場內 DRC 通過便無拼接問題」。","explanationEn":"Field seams need position, scale and conductor continuity control. Use resistance and overlay witnesses across seams. Therefore reject: Assuming within-field DRC excludes stitching defects."}},{"id":"a117-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-14"],"title":"RDL 厚度均勻｜機制與設計","titleEn":"RDL thickness uniformity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對RDL 厚度均勻，把「鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rdl thickness uniformity, turn \"Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「RDL 厚度均勻」的模型：鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for rdl thickness uniformity: Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map thickness and group by current paths. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map thickness and group by current paths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付RDL 厚度均勻的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for rdl thickness uniformity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-15-k1","title":"RDL 厚度均勻：機制","titleEn":"RDL thickness uniformity: mechanism","text":"鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。","textEn":"Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。 必須排除的錯判：平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map thickness and group by current paths. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「RDL 厚度均勻」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rdl thickness uniformity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區","單一設備可容納就代表整線可用","鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes","Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility","Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。 繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。 因此不能採用「平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區」。","explanationEn":"Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas. Map thickness and group by current paths. Therefore reject: Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes."}},{"id":"a117-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-15"],"title":"RDL 厚度均勻｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"RDL thickness uniformity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對RDL 厚度均勻，把「鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rdl thickness uniformity, turn \"Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。 將「平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map thickness and group by current paths. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map thickness and group by current paths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付RDL 厚度均勻的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for rdl thickness uniformity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-16-k1","title":"RDL 厚度均勻：機制","titleEn":"RDL thickness uniformity: mechanism","text":"鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。","textEn":"Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。 必須排除的錯判：平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map thickness and group by current paths. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「RDL 厚度均勻」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rdl thickness uniformity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。","平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區","單一設備可容納就代表整線可用"],"optionsEn":["Map thickness and group by current paths.","Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes","Equating one tool's capacity with line compatibility"],"answer":0,"explanation":"鍍液流場和電流分配在大面積可能不均。 繪厚度地圖並按電流路徑分組。 因此不能採用「平均鍍厚符合即可忽略邊緣薄區」。","explanationEn":"Flow and current distribution can be nonuniform over large areas. Map thickness and group by current paths. Therefore reject: Ignoring thin edges after mean thickness passes."}},{"id":"a117-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-16"],"title":"圖形伸縮補償｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pattern-scale compensation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對圖形伸縮補償，把「尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pattern-scale compensation, turn \"Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「圖形伸縮補償」的模型：尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設 500×500 mm 面板四邊各排除 10 mm，可用面積 480²=230400 mm²；20×20 mm 封裝忽略街道時最多 24²=576 個。加街道、測試區及良率後數量必降。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pattern-scale compensation: Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For an illustrative 500×500 mm panel with 10 mm excluded edges, usable area is 480²=230400 mm²; 20×20 mm packages fit at most 24²=576 before streets, test zones and yield. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：縮放全圖不會改變電性規則。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付圖形伸縮補償的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pattern-scale compensation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-17-k1","title":"圖形伸縮補償：機制","titleEn":"Pattern-scale compensation: mechanism","text":"尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。","textEn":"Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。 必須排除的錯判：縮放全圖不會改變電性規則。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設 500×500 mm 面板四邊各排除 10 mm，可用面積 480²=230400 mm²；20×20 mm 封裝忽略街道時最多 24²=576 個。加街道、測試區及良率後數量必降。","textEn":"For an illustrative 500×500 mm panel with 10 mm excluded edges, usable area is 480²=230400 mm²; 20×20 mm packages fit at most 24²=576 before streets, test zones and yield."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圖形伸縮補償」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pattern-scale compensation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總面積除單位面積就是實際產量","尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。","縮放全圖不會改變電性規則"],"optionsEn":["Using area division as actual output","Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin.","Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules"],"answer":1,"explanation":"尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。 檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。 因此不能採用「縮放全圖不會改變電性規則」。","explanationEn":"Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin. Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. Therefore reject: Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules."}},{"id":"a117-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-17"],"title":"圖形伸縮補償｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pattern-scale compensation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對圖形伸縮補償，把「尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pattern-scale compensation, turn \"Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。 將「縮放全圖不會改變電性規則」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設 500×500 mm 面板四邊各排除 10 mm，可用面積 480²=230400 mm²；20×20 mm 封裝忽略街道時最多 24²=576 個。加街道、測試區及良率後數量必降。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For an illustrative 500×500 mm panel with 10 mm excluded edges, usable area is 480²=230400 mm²; 20×20 mm packages fit at most 24²=576 before streets, test zones and yield. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：縮放全圖不會改變電性規則。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付圖形伸縮補償的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pattern-scale compensation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-18-k1","title":"圖形伸縮補償：機制","titleEn":"Pattern-scale compensation: mechanism","text":"尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。","textEn":"Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。 必須排除的錯判：縮放全圖不會改變電性規則。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設 500×500 mm 面板四邊各排除 10 mm，可用面積 480²=230400 mm²；20×20 mm 封裝忽略街道時最多 24²=576 個。加街道、測試區及良率後數量必降。","textEn":"For an illustrative 500×500 mm panel with 10 mm excluded edges, usable area is 480²=230400 mm²; 20×20 mm packages fit at most 24²=576 before streets, test zones and yield."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「圖形伸縮補償」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pattern-scale compensation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["縮放全圖不會改變電性規則","總面積除單位面積就是實際產量","檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules","Using area division as actual output","Check spacing and via overlap after compensation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"尺寸補償須保留局部設計規則及連接捕捉餘量。 檢查補償前後線距與過孔重疊。 因此不能採用「縮放全圖不會改變電性規則」。","explanationEn":"Scale compensation must preserve local rules and capture margin. Check spacing and via overlap after compensation. Therefore reject: Assuming global scaling never changes electrical rules."}}]},{"id":"a117-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"良率與可靠度","titleEn":"Yield and reliability","description":"針對良率與可靠度完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for yield and reliability, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a117-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-18"],"title":"分割與殘應力｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Singulation and residual stress | mechanism and design","objective":"針對分割與殘應力，把「分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For singulation and residual stress, turn \"Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「分割與殘應力」的模型：分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for singulation and residual stress: Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring package warpage from panel warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付分割與殘應力的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for singulation and residual stress, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-19-k1","title":"分割與殘應力：機制","titleEn":"Singulation and residual stress: mechanism","text":"分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。","textEn":"Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。 必須排除的錯判：面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring package warpage from panel warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分割與殘應力」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For singulation and residual stress — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。","面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格","相同平均密度即可消除局部差異"],"optionsEn":["Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape.","Inferring package warpage from panel warpage","Assuming equal mean density removes local differences"],"answer":0,"explanation":"分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。 比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。 因此不能採用「面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格」。","explanationEn":"Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape. Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. Therefore reject: Inferring package warpage from panel warpage."}},{"id":"a117-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-19"],"title":"分割與殘應力｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Singulation and residual stress | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對分割與殘應力，把「分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For singulation and residual stress, turn \"Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。 將「面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring package warpage from panel warpage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring package warpage from panel warpage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付分割與殘應力的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for singulation and residual stress: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-20-k1","title":"分割與殘應力：機制","titleEn":"Singulation and residual stress: mechanism","text":"分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。","textEn":"Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。 必須排除的錯判：面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring package warpage from panel warpage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分割與殘應力」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For singulation and residual stress — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同平均密度即可消除局部差異","比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。","面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming equal mean density removes local differences","Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation.","Inferring package warpage from panel warpage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分割釋放面板應力，單顆封裝形狀可能改變。 比較分割前後曲率與接點電性。 因此不能採用「面板翹曲合格就保證單顆翹曲合格」。","explanationEn":"Singulation releases panel stress and can change package shape. Compare curvature/electrical data before and after singulation. Therefore reject: Inferring package warpage from panel warpage."}},{"id":"a117-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-20"],"title":"空間良率｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Spatial yield | mechanism and design","objective":"針對空間良率，把「邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For spatial yield, turn \"Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「空間良率」的模型：邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for spatial yield: Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Cross-map position, station and failure class. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Cross-map position, station and failure class. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同總良率代表同樣成熟度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空間良率的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for spatial yield, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-21-k1","title":"空間良率：機制","titleEn":"Spatial yield: mechanism","text":"邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。","textEn":"Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。 必須排除的錯判：相同總良率代表同樣成熟度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Cross-map position, station and failure class. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空間良率」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For spatial yield — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["相同總良率代表同樣成熟度","量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲","邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。"],"optionsEn":["Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity","Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag","Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。 建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。 因此不能採用「相同總良率代表同樣成熟度」。","explanationEn":"Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages. Cross-map position, station and failure class. Therefore reject: Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity."}},{"id":"a117-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-21"],"title":"空間良率｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Spatial yield | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對空間良率，把「邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For spatial yield, turn \"Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。 將「相同總良率代表同樣成熟度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Cross-map position, station and failure class. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Cross-map position, station and failure class. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：相同總良率代表同樣成熟度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付空間良率的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for spatial yield: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-22-k1","title":"空間良率：機制","titleEn":"Spatial yield: mechanism","text":"邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。","textEn":"Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。 必須排除的錯判：相同總良率代表同樣成熟度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Cross-map position, station and failure class. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「空間良率」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For spatial yield — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。","相同總良率代表同樣成熟度","量測時平坦即可證明搬運不彎曲"],"optionsEn":["Cross-map position, station and failure class.","Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity","Using flat metrology to prove no handling sag"],"answer":0,"explanation":"邊緣群聚失效代表系統機制，不宜只報全板平均。 建立位置、站點與失效類型交叉圖。 因此不能採用「相同總良率代表同樣成熟度」。","explanationEn":"Edge-clustered failures indicate systematic mechanisms hidden by averages. Cross-map position, station and failure class. Therefore reject: Equating equal total yield with equal process maturity."}},{"id":"a117-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-22"],"title":"規模化經濟｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Scale economics | mechanism and design","objective":"針對規模化經濟，把「面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For scale economics, turn \"Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「規模化經濟」的模型：面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較每良品成本及尾端風險。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for scale economics: Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較每良品成本及尾端風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：面板越大成本必單調下降。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付規模化經濟的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for scale economics, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-23-k1","title":"規模化經濟：機制","titleEn":"Scale economics: mechanism","text":"面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。","textEn":"Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較每良品成本及尾端風險。 必須排除的錯判：面板越大成本必單調下降。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規模化經濟」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For scale economics — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形","面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。","面板越大成本必單調下降"],"optionsEn":["Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation","Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs.","Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost"],"answer":1,"explanation":"面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。 比較每良品成本及尾端風險。 因此不能採用「面板越大成本必單調下降」。","explanationEn":"Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs. Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. Therefore reject: Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost."}},{"id":"a117-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"],"prerequisiteIds":["a117-v9-23"],"title":"規模化經濟｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Scale economics | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對規模化經濟，把「面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For scale economics, turn \"Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較每良品成本及尾端風險。 將「面板越大成本必單調下降」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較每良品成本及尾端風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：面板越大成本必單調下降。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付規模化經濟的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for scale economics: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a117-v9-24-k1","title":"規模化經濟：機制","titleEn":"Scale economics: mechanism","text":"面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。","textEn":"Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]},{"id":"a117-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較每良品成本及尾端風險。 必須排除的錯判：面板越大成本必單調下降。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asefan","v9a-asepanel"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規模化經濟」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For scale economics — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["面板越大成本必單調下降","一個全域平移可修正全部熱變形","比較每良品成本及尾端風險。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost","Correcting all thermal distortion with one translation","Compare cost per good unit and tail risks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"面積增加需扣除設備、搬運損失和修補成本。 比較每良品成本及尾端風險。 因此不能採用「面板越大成本必單調下降」。","explanationEn":"Larger area must account for tool, handling and rework costs. Compare cost per good unit and tail risks. Therefore reject: Assuming larger panels always lower unit cost."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-encapsulation","subcategoryTitle":"封膠、扇出與異質整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Encapsulation, fan-out and heterogeneous integration","photoId":"v8-wafer"},{"id":"a118","title":"重佈線層微影與電鍍","titleEn":"Redistribution-layer lithography and plating","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入細線 RDL、過孔連通與跨材料可靠度。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore fine rdl, via continuity and cross-material reliability, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["介面與版圖","微影與種子","電鍍與蝕除","電性與壽命"],"labelsEn":["Interfaces and layout","Lithography and seed","Plating and etchback","Electrical and lifetime"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a118-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"介面與版圖","titleEn":"Interfaces and layout","description":"針對介面與版圖完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for interfaces and layout, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a118-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"互連功能分層｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interconnect function layers | mechanism and design","objective":"針對互連功能分層，把「電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interconnect function layers, turn \"Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「互連功能分層」的模型：電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「標每層網路及回流面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interconnect function layers: Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Mark networks and return planes per layer. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"標每層網路及回流面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark networks and return planes per layer. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最小線寬可用於所有電源線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using minimum width for all power traces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付互連功能分層的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interconnect function layers, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-01-k1","title":"互連功能分層：機制","titleEn":"Interconnect function layers: mechanism","text":"電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。","textEn":"Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標每層網路及回流面。 必須排除的錯判：最小線寬可用於所有電源線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark networks and return planes per layer. Misinterpretation to reject: Using minimum width for all power traces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「互連功能分層」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interconnect function layers — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。","最小線寬可用於所有電源線","中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界"],"optionsEn":["Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents.","Using minimum width for all power traces","Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。 標每層網路及回流面。 因此不能採用「最小線寬可用於所有電源線」。","explanationEn":"Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents. Mark networks and return planes per layer. Therefore reject: Using minimum width for all power traces."}},{"id":"a118-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-01"],"title":"互連功能分層｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interconnect function layers | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對互連功能分層，把「電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interconnect function layers, turn \"Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：標每層網路及回流面。 將「最小線寬可用於所有電源線」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Mark networks and return planes per layer. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using minimum width for all power traces\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"標每層網路及回流面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark networks and return planes per layer. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最小線寬可用於所有電源線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using minimum width for all power traces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付互連功能分層的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interconnect function layers: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-02-k1","title":"互連功能分層：機制","titleEn":"Interconnect function layers: mechanism","text":"電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。","textEn":"Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標每層網路及回流面。 必須排除的錯判：最小線寬可用於所有電源線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark networks and return planes per layer. Misinterpretation to reject: Using minimum width for all power traces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「互連功能分層」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interconnect function layers — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界","標每層網路及回流面。","最小線寬可用於所有電源線"],"optionsEn":["Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin","Mark networks and return planes per layer.","Using minimum width for all power traces"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電源與訊號線有不同寬度、阻抗和電流需求。 標每層網路及回流面。 因此不能採用「最小線寬可用於所有電源線」。","explanationEn":"Power and signal traces need different widths, impedances and currents. Mark networks and return planes per layer. Therefore reject: Using minimum width for all power traces."}},{"id":"a118-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-02"],"title":"介電層與固化｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Dielectric and cure | mechanism and design","objective":"針對介電層與固化，把「介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For dielectric and cure, turn \"Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「介電層與固化」的模型：介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for dielectric and cure: Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：介電層只需看擊穿電壓。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付介電層與固化的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for dielectric and cure, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-03-k1","title":"介電層與固化：機制","titleEn":"Dielectric and cure: mechanism","text":"介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。","textEn":"Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。 必須排除的錯判：介電層只需看擊穿電壓。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「介電層與固化」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For dielectric and cure — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["介電層只需看擊穿電壓","電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面","介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。"],"optionsEn":["Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage","Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass","Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。 配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。 因此不能採用「介電層只需看擊穿電壓」。","explanationEn":"Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion. Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. Therefore reject: Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage."}},{"id":"a118-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-03"],"title":"介電層與固化｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Dielectric and cure | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對介電層與固化，把「介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For dielectric and cure, turn \"Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。 將「介電層只需看擊穿電壓」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：介電層只需看擊穿電壓。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付介電層與固化的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for dielectric and cure: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-04-k1","title":"介電層與固化：機制","titleEn":"Dielectric and cure: mechanism","text":"介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。","textEn":"Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。 必須排除的錯判：介電層只需看擊穿電壓。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「介電層與固化」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For dielectric and cure — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。","介電層只需看擊穿電壓","電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面"],"optionsEn":["Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses.","Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage","Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"介電層的厚度、吸濕和固化影響電容與附著。 配對厚度、漏電及剝離見證。 因此不能採用「介電層只需看擊穿電壓」。","explanationEn":"Thickness, moisture and cure affect capacitance and adhesion. Pair thickness, leakage and adhesion witnesses. Therefore reject: Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage."}},{"id":"a118-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-04"],"title":"過孔開口｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Via openings | mechanism and design","objective":"針對過孔開口，把「底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via openings, turn \"Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「過孔開口」的模型：底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for via openings: Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付過孔開口的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for via openings, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-05-k1","title":"過孔開口：機制","titleEn":"Via openings: mechanism","text":"底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。","textEn":"Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。 必須排除的錯判：頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「過孔開口」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via openings — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性","底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。","頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨"],"optionsEn":["Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film","Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity.","Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom"],"answer":1,"explanation":"底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。 比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。 因此不能採用「頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨」。","explanationEn":"Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity. Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. Therefore reject: Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom."}},{"id":"a118-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-05"],"title":"過孔開口｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Via openings | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對過孔開口，把「底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via openings, turn \"Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。 將「頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付過孔開口的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for via openings: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-06-k1","title":"過孔開口：機制","titleEn":"Via openings: mechanism","text":"底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。","textEn":"Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。 必須排除的錯判：頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「過孔開口」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via openings — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨","所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性","比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom","Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film","Compare top dimensions with bottom sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"底部殘留和側壁形狀決定金屬連通。 比較頂部尺寸與孔底截面。 因此不能採用「頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨」。","explanationEn":"Bottom residue and wall profile determine metal continuity. Compare top dimensions with bottom sections. Therefore reject: Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom."}}]},{"id":"a118-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"微影與種子","titleEn":"Lithography and seed","description":"針對微影與種子完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for lithography and seed, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a118-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-06"],"title":"種子覆蓋｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Seed coverage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對種子覆蓋，把「台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed coverage, turn \"Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「種子覆蓋」的模型：台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for seed coverage: Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子覆蓋的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for seed coverage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-07-k1","title":"種子覆蓋：機制","titleEn":"Seed coverage: mechanism","text":"台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。","textEn":"Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。 必須排除的錯判：平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子覆蓋」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed coverage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。","平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋","絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄"],"optionsEn":["Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth.","Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage","Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。 以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。 因此不能採用「平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋」。","explanationEn":"Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth. Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. Therefore reject: Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage."}},{"id":"a118-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-07"],"title":"種子覆蓋｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Seed coverage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對種子覆蓋，把「台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed coverage, turn \"Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。 將「平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子覆蓋的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for seed coverage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-08-k1","title":"種子覆蓋：機制","titleEn":"Seed coverage: mechanism","text":"台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。","textEn":"Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。 必須排除的錯判：平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子覆蓋」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed coverage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄","以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。","平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes","Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections.","Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"台階和孔壁需連續導電層才能均勻成長。 以片阻加截面檢查覆蓋。 因此不能採用「平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋」。","explanationEn":"Steps and via walls need continuous seed for uniform growth. Use sheet resistance plus coverage sections. Therefore reject: Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage."}},{"id":"a118-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-08"],"title":"光阻解析｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Resist resolution | mechanism and design","objective":"針對光阻解析，把「線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resist resolution, turn \"Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「光阻解析」的模型：線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「在密集與孤立線測底寬。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for resist resolution: Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"在密集與孤立線測底寬。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：頂部線寬可代表整個截面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using top width for the whole cross-section. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光阻解析的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for resist resolution, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-09-k1","title":"光阻解析：機制","titleEn":"Resist resolution: mechanism","text":"線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。","textEn":"Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在密集與孤立線測底寬。 必須排除的錯判：頂部線寬可代表整個截面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. Misinterpretation to reject: Using top width for the whole cross-section. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光阻解析」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resist resolution — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["頂部線寬可代表整個截面","名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值","線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。"],"optionsEn":["Using top width for the whole cross-section","Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone","Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。 在密集與孤立線測底寬。 因此不能採用「頂部線寬可代表整個截面」。","explanationEn":"Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation. Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. Therefore reject: Using top width for the whole cross-section."}},{"id":"a118-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-09"],"title":"光阻解析｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Resist resolution | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對光阻解析，把「線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resist resolution, turn \"Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：在密集與孤立線測底寬。 將「頂部線寬可代表整個截面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using top width for the whole cross-section\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"在密集與孤立線測底寬。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：頂部線寬可代表整個截面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using top width for the whole cross-section. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光阻解析的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for resist resolution: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-10-k1","title":"光阻解析：機制","titleEn":"Resist resolution: mechanism","text":"線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。","textEn":"Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在密集與孤立線測底寬。 必須排除的錯判：頂部線寬可代表整個截面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. Misinterpretation to reject: Using top width for the whole cross-section. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光阻解析」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resist resolution — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["在密集與孤立線測底寬。","頂部線寬可代表整個截面","名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值"],"optionsEn":["Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines.","Using top width for the whole cross-section","Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"線寬、厚度和側壁角共同限制細線成形。 在密集與孤立線測底寬。 因此不能採用「頂部線寬可代表整個截面」。","explanationEn":"Width, thickness and wall angle jointly limit trace formation. Measure bottom widths in dense/isolated lines. Therefore reject: Using top width for the whole cross-section."}},{"id":"a118-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-10"],"title":"對位捕捉｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Overlay capture | mechanism and design","objective":"針對對位捕捉，把「過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overlay capture, turn \"Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「對位捕捉」的模型：過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for overlay capture: Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付對位捕捉的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for overlay capture, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-11-k1","title":"對位捕捉：機制","titleEn":"Overlay capture: mechanism","text":"過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。","textEn":"Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。 必須排除的錯判：中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「對位捕捉」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overlay capture — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段","過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。","中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass","Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors.","Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin"],"answer":1,"explanation":"過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。 將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。 因此不能採用「中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界」。","explanationEn":"Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors. Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. Therefore reject: Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin."}},{"id":"a118-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-11"],"title":"對位捕捉｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Overlay capture | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對對位捕捉，把「過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overlay capture, turn \"Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。 將「中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付對位捕捉的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for overlay capture: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-12-k1","title":"對位捕捉：機制","titleEn":"Overlay capture: mechanism","text":"過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。","textEn":"Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。 必須排除的錯判：中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「對位捕捉」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overlay capture — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界","直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段","將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin","Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass","Correlate overlap-area maps and opens."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過孔与下層墊的重疊須包含製程偏移和量測誤差。 將重疊面積地圖和開路相配。 因此不能採用「中心偏差合格就必有足夠邊界」。","explanationEn":"Via-pad overlap must include process and metrology errors. Correlate overlap-area maps and opens. Therefore reject: Assuming acceptable center error guarantees edge margin."}}]},{"id":"a118-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"電鍍與蝕除","titleEn":"Plating and etchback","description":"針對電鍍與蝕除完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for plating and etchback, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a118-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-12"],"title":"電鍍線形｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Plated profile | mechanism and design","objective":"針對電鍍線形，把「電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For plated profile, turn \"Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「電鍍線形」的模型：電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量線頂、底及彎角截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for plated profile: Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure top, bottom and bend sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量線頂、底及彎角截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure top, bottom and bend sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電鍍線形的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for plated profile, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-13-k1","title":"電鍍線形：機制","titleEn":"Plated profile: mechanism","text":"電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。","textEn":"Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量線頂、底及彎角截面。 必須排除的錯判：電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure top, bottom and bend sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電鍍線形」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For plated profile — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。","電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面","一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則"],"optionsEn":["Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions.","Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass","Freezing all rules after one electrical pass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。 量線頂、底及彎角截面。 因此不能採用「電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面」。","explanationEn":"Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions. Measure top, bottom and bend sections. Therefore reject: Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass."}},{"id":"a118-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-13"],"title":"電鍍線形｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Plated profile | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對電鍍線形，把「電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For plated profile, turn \"Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量線頂、底及彎角截面。 將「電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure top, bottom and bend sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量線頂、底及彎角截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure top, bottom and bend sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電鍍線形的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for plated profile: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-14-k1","title":"電鍍線形：機制","titleEn":"Plated profile: mechanism","text":"電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。","textEn":"Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量線頂、底及彎角截面。 必須排除的錯判：電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure top, bottom and bend sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電鍍線形」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For plated profile — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則","量線頂、底及彎角截面。","電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面"],"optionsEn":["Freezing all rules after one electrical pass","Measure top, bottom and bend sections.","Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電流擁擠可使線頂與邊緣過厚，平均厚度不能代表最窄截面。 量線頂、底及彎角截面。 因此不能採用「電鍍總量可直接推得最小線截面」。","explanationEn":"Crowding can overplate tops/edges; mean thickness hides constrictions. Measure top, bottom and bend sections. Therefore reject: Inferring minimum cross-section from total plated mass."}},{"id":"a118-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-14"],"title":"雜質與延展｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Impurities and ductility | mechanism and design","objective":"針對雜質與延展，把「細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For impurities and ductility, turn \"Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「雜質與延展」的模型：細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for impurities and ductility: Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付雜質與延展的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for impurities and ductility, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-15-k1","title":"雜質與延展：機制","titleEn":"Impurities and ductility: mechanism","text":"細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。","textEn":"Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。 必須排除的錯判：所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. Misinterpretation to reject: Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雜質與延展」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For impurities and ductility — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性","最小線寬可用於所有電源線","細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。"],"optionsEn":["Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film","Using minimum width for all power traces","Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。 比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。 因此不能採用「所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性」。","explanationEn":"Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits. Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. Therefore reject: Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film."}},{"id":"a118-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-15"],"title":"雜質與延展｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Impurities and ductility | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對雜質與延展，把「細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For impurities and ductility, turn \"Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。 將「所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付雜質與延展的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for impurities and ductility: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-16-k1","title":"雜質與延展：機制","titleEn":"Impurities and ductility: mechanism","text":"細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。","textEn":"Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。 必須排除的錯判：所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. Misinterpretation to reject: Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雜質與延展」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For impurities and ductility — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。","所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性","最小線寬可用於所有電源線"],"optionsEn":["Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal.","Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film","Using minimum width for all power traces"],"answer":0,"explanation":"細銅線的微結構影響裂紋敏感性，需驗證實際沉積材料。 比較退火前後晶粒與拉伸見證。 因此不能採用「所有銅沉積都可用塊材延展性」。","explanationEn":"Fine-Cu microstructure affects crack sensitivity; validate actual deposits. Compare grains and tensile witnesses before/after anneal. Therefore reject: Using bulk ductility for every deposited Cu film."}},{"id":"a118-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-16"],"title":"去種子側蝕｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Seed-etch undercut | mechanism and design","objective":"針對去種子側蝕，把「清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed-etch undercut, turn \"Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「去種子側蝕」的模型：清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「同時量絕緣與根部線寬。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設銅線 L=2 mm、w=5 μm、t=3 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈2.27 Ω。若線寬減少 10% 而其餘不變，R 增加約 11.1%；不含接點與尺寸效應。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for seed-etch undercut: Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure isolation and root width together. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For L=2 mm, w=5 μm, t=3 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R≈2.27 Ω. A 10% width reduction raises R by about 11.1%, excluding contacts and size effects. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"同時量絕緣與根部線寬。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure isolation and root width together. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付去種子側蝕的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for seed-etch undercut, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-17-k1","title":"去種子側蝕：機制","titleEn":"Seed-etch undercut: mechanism","text":"清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。","textEn":"Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"同時量絕緣與根部線寬。 必須排除的錯判：絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure isolation and root width together. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設銅線 L=2 mm、w=5 μm、t=3 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈2.27 Ω。若線寬減少 10% 而其餘不變，R 增加約 11.1%；不含接點與尺寸效應。","textEn":"For L=2 mm, w=5 μm, t=3 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R≈2.27 Ω. A 10% width reduction raises R by about 11.1%, excluding contacts and size effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「去種子側蝕」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed-etch undercut — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["介電層只需看擊穿電壓","清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。","絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄"],"optionsEn":["Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage","Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots.","Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。 同時量絕緣與根部線寬。 因此不能採用「絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄」。","explanationEn":"Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots. Measure isolation and root width together. Therefore reject: Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes."}},{"id":"a118-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-17"],"title":"去種子側蝕｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Seed-etch undercut | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對去種子側蝕，把「清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed-etch undercut, turn \"Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：同時量絕緣與根部線寬。 將「絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設銅線 L=2 mm、w=5 μm、t=3 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈2.27 Ω。若線寬減少 10% 而其餘不變，R 增加約 11.1%；不含接點與尺寸效應。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure isolation and root width together. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For L=2 mm, w=5 μm, t=3 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R≈2.27 Ω. A 10% width reduction raises R by about 11.1%, excluding contacts and size effects. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"同時量絕緣與根部線寬。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure isolation and root width together. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付去種子側蝕的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for seed-etch undercut: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-18-k1","title":"去種子側蝕：機制","titleEn":"Seed-etch undercut: mechanism","text":"清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。","textEn":"Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"同時量絕緣與根部線寬。 必須排除的錯判：絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure isolation and root width together. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設銅線 L=2 mm、w=5 μm、t=3 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈2.27 Ω。若線寬減少 10% 而其餘不變，R 增加約 11.1%；不含接點與尺寸效應。","textEn":"For L=2 mm, w=5 μm, t=3 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m, R≈2.27 Ω. A 10% width reduction raises R by about 11.1%, excluding contacts and size effects."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「去種子側蝕」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed-etch undercut — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄","介電層只需看擊穿電壓","同時量絕緣與根部線寬。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes","Assessing dielectric only by breakdown voltage","Measure isolation and root width together."],"answer":2,"explanation":"清除種子防短路時會縮小細線根部。 同時量絕緣與根部線寬。 因此不能採用「絕緣通過便可忽略線根變窄」。","explanationEn":"Seed removal prevents shorts but can narrow trace roots. Measure isolation and root width together. Therefore reject: Ignoring root narrowing after isolation passes."}}]},{"id":"a118-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"電性與壽命","titleEn":"Electrical and lifetime","description":"針對電性與壽命完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for electrical and lifetime, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a118-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-18"],"title":"電阻與尺寸｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Resistance and dimensions | mechanism and design","objective":"針對電阻與尺寸，把「電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resistance and dimensions, turn \"Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「電阻與尺寸」的模型：電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以四端線阻配合截面重建。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for resistance and dimensions: Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以四端線阻配合截面重建。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電阻與尺寸的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for resistance and dimensions, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-19-k1","title":"電阻與尺寸：機制","titleEn":"Resistance and dimensions: mechanism","text":"電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。","textEn":"Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以四端線阻配合截面重建。 必須排除的錯判：名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電阻與尺寸」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resistance and dimensions — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。","名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值","頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨"],"optionsEn":["Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width.","Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone","Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。 以四端線阻配合截面重建。 因此不能採用「名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值」。","explanationEn":"Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width. Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. Therefore reject: Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone."}},{"id":"a118-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-19"],"title":"電阻與尺寸｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Resistance and dimensions | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對電阻與尺寸，把「電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resistance and dimensions, turn \"Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以四端線阻配合截面重建。 將「名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以四端線阻配合截面重建。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電阻與尺寸的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for resistance and dimensions: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-20-k1","title":"電阻與尺寸：機制","titleEn":"Resistance and dimensions: mechanism","text":"電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。","textEn":"Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以四端線阻配合截面重建。 必須排除的錯判：名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電阻與尺寸」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resistance and dimensions — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["頂視過孔打開即底部必潔淨","以四端線阻配合截面重建。","名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值"],"optionsEn":["Assuming a visible opening has a clean bottom","Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections.","Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電阻受截面最小值與接點影響，不只設計線寬。 以四端線阻配合截面重建。 因此不能採用「名義線寬即可準確計算全線阻值」。","explanationEn":"Resistance depends on constrictions and contacts, not just design width. Combine four-terminal trace resistance and sections. Therefore reject: Calculating exact resistance from nominal width alone."}},{"id":"a118-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-20"],"title":"跨界面應變｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cross-interface strain | mechanism and design","objective":"針對跨界面應變，把「RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cross-interface strain, turn \"RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「跨界面應變」的模型：RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cross-interface strain: RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付跨界面應變的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cross-interface strain, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-21-k1","title":"跨界面應變：機制","titleEn":"Cross-interface strain: mechanism","text":"RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。","textEn":"RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。 必須排除的錯判：直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨界面應變」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cross-interface strain — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段","平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋","RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass","Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage","RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。 按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。 因此不能採用「直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段」。","explanationEn":"RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain. Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. Therefore reject: Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass."}},{"id":"a118-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-21"],"title":"跨界面應變｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cross-interface strain | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對跨界面應變，把「RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cross-interface strain, turn \"RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。 將「直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付跨界面應變的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cross-interface strain: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-22-k1","title":"跨界面應變：機制","titleEn":"Cross-interface strain: mechanism","text":"RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。","textEn":"RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。 必須排除的錯判：直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨界面應變」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cross-interface strain — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。","直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段","平面厚度足夠即可證明孔壁覆蓋"],"optionsEn":["Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends.","Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass","Using planar thickness to prove sidewall coverage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"RDL 跨越不同 CTE 材料時局部應变較高。 按晶粒邊界和彎角定位裂紋。 因此不能採用「直線區無裂紋即可忽略跨界面段」。","explanationEn":"RDL crossing dissimilar-CTE materials can have elevated local strain. Locate cracks by die boundaries and bends. Therefore reject: Ignoring interface crossings after straight traces pass."}},{"id":"a118-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-22"],"title":"可靠度與設計回饋｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Reliability and design feedback | mechanism and design","objective":"針對可靠度與設計回饋，把「線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reliability and design feedback, turn \"Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「可靠度與設計回饋」的模型：線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for reliability and design feedback: Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map failures back to layout rules. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map failures back to layout rules. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Freezing all rules after one electrical pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付可靠度與設計回饋的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for reliability and design feedback, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-23-k1","title":"可靠度與設計回饋：機制","titleEn":"Reliability and design feedback: mechanism","text":"線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。","textEn":"Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。 必須排除的錯判：一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map failures back to layout rules. Misinterpretation to reject: Freezing all rules after one electrical pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可靠度與設計回饋」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reliability and design feedback — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["頂部線寬可代表整個截面","線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。","一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則"],"optionsEn":["Using top width for the whole cross-section","Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules.","Freezing all rules after one electrical pass"],"answer":1,"explanation":"線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。 建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。 因此不能採用「一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則」。","explanationEn":"Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules. Map failures back to layout rules. Therefore reject: Freezing all rules after one electrical pass."}},{"id":"a118-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"],"prerequisiteIds":["a118-v9-23"],"title":"可靠度與設計回饋｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Reliability and design feedback | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對可靠度與設計回饋，把「線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reliability and design feedback, turn \"Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。 將「一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map failures back to layout rules. Challenge the hypothesis \"Freezing all rules after one electrical pass\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map failures back to layout rules. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Freezing all rules after one electrical pass. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付可靠度與設計回饋的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for reliability and design feedback: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a118-v9-24-k1","title":"可靠度與設計回饋：機制","titleEn":"Reliability and design feedback: mechanism","text":"線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。","textEn":"Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]},{"id":"a118-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。 必須排除的錯判：一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map failures back to layout rules. Misinterpretation to reject: Freezing all rules after one electrical pass. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechrdl","v9a-imecpdk"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可靠度與設計回饋」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reliability and design feedback — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則","頂部線寬可代表整個截面","建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。"],"optionsEn":["Freezing all rules after one electrical pass","Using top width for the whole cross-section","Map failures back to layout rules."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線距、過孔冗餘和熱循環資料需回饋設計規則。 建立失效位置對版圖規則的對照。 因此不能採用「一次電測合格即可凍結所有設計規則」。","explanationEn":"Spacing, via redundancy and cycling results must inform design rules. Map failures back to layout rules. Therefore reject: Freezing all rules after one electrical pass."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-encapsulation","subcategoryTitle":"封膠、扇出與異質整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Encapsulation, fan-out and heterogeneous integration","photoId":"v9-quilt-solder"},{"id":"a119","title":"嵌入式晶粒封裝","titleEn":"Embedded-die packaging","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入嵌入深度、雷射接點與層合可靠度。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore embedding depth, laser contacts and laminate reliability, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["嵌入架構","放置與層合","接點形成","驗證與熱路徑"],"labelsEn":["Embedding architecture","Placement and lamination","Contact formation","Verification and thermal paths"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a119-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"嵌入架構","titleEn":"Embedding architecture","description":"針對嵌入架構完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for embedding architecture, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a119-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"腔體與層疊｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cavity and stackup | mechanism and design","objective":"針對腔體與層疊，把「腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cavity and stackup, turn \"Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「腔體與層疊」的模型：腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「列最壞組合的幾何界限。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cavity and stackup: Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: List worst-case geometry combinations. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"列最壞組合的幾何界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List worst-case geometry combinations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：名義腔深較大就不需公差分析。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付腔體與層疊的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cavity and stackup, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-01-k1","title":"腔體與層疊：機制","titleEn":"Cavity and stackup: mechanism","text":"腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。","textEn":"Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列最壞組合的幾何界限。 必須排除的錯判：名義腔深較大就不需公差分析。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List worst-case geometry combinations. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「腔體與層疊」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cavity and stackup — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。","名義腔深較大就不需公差分析","降低總壓力必能解決所有破片"],"optionsEn":["Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness.","Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger","Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture"],"answer":0,"explanation":"腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。 列最壞組合的幾何界限。 因此不能採用「名義腔深較大就不需公差分析」。","explanationEn":"Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness. List worst-case geometry combinations. Therefore reject: Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger."}},{"id":"a119-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-01"],"title":"腔體與層疊｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cavity and stackup | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對腔體與層疊，把「腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cavity and stackup, turn \"Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：列最壞組合的幾何界限。 將「名義腔深較大就不需公差分析」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: List worst-case geometry combinations. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"列最壞組合的幾何界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List worst-case geometry combinations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：名義腔深較大就不需公差分析。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付腔體與層疊的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cavity and stackup: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-02-k1","title":"腔體與層疊：機制","titleEn":"Cavity and stackup: mechanism","text":"腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。","textEn":"Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列最壞組合的幾何界限。 必須排除的錯判：名義腔深較大就不需公差分析。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List worst-case geometry combinations. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「腔體與層疊」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cavity and stackup — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["降低總壓力必能解決所有破片","列最壞組合的幾何界限。","名義腔深較大就不需公差分析"],"optionsEn":["Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture","List worst-case geometry combinations.","Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger"],"answer":1,"explanation":"腔深與晶粒厚度決定上方介電質及平坦度。 列最壞組合的幾何界限。 因此不能採用「名義腔深較大就不需公差分析」。","explanationEn":"Cavity depth and die thickness set cover dielectric and flatness. List worst-case geometry combinations. Therefore reject: Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger."}},{"id":"a119-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-02"],"title":"晶粒良品｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Known-good embedded die | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶粒良品，把「嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good embedded die, turn \"Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶粒良品」的模型：嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for known-good embedded die: Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：嵌入前測試可全由終測取代。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒良品的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for known-good embedded die, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-03-k1","title":"晶粒良品：機制","titleEn":"Known-good embedded die: mechanism","text":"嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。","textEn":"Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。 必須排除的錯判：嵌入前測試可全由終測取代。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. Misinterpretation to reject: Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒良品」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good embedded die — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["嵌入前測試可全由終測取代","外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊","嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。"],"optionsEn":["Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests","Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad","Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost."],"answer":2,"explanation":"嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。 比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。 因此不能採用「嵌入前測試可全由終測取代」。","explanationEn":"Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost. Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. Therefore reject: Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests."}},{"id":"a119-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-03"],"title":"晶粒良品｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Known-good embedded die | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶粒良品，把「嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For known-good embedded die, turn \"Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。 將「嵌入前測試可全由終測取代」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. Challenge the hypothesis \"Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：嵌入前測試可全由終測取代。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒良品的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for known-good embedded die: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-04-k1","title":"晶粒良品：機制","titleEn":"Known-good embedded die: mechanism","text":"嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。","textEn":"Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。 必須排除的錯判：嵌入前測試可全由終測取代。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. Misinterpretation to reject: Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒良品」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For known-good embedded die — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。","嵌入前測試可全由終測取代","外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊"],"optionsEn":["Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk.","Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests","Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad"],"answer":0,"explanation":"嵌入後返修受限，前測覆蓋影響整板成本。 比較前測投入與報廢層板風險。 因此不能採用「嵌入前測試可全由終測取代」。","explanationEn":"Limited rework makes pretest coverage important to board cost. Compare screening effort and laminate scrap risk. Therefore reject: Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests."}},{"id":"a119-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-04"],"title":"焊墊金屬相容｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pad metallurgy | mechanism and design","objective":"針對焊墊金屬相容，把「晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pad metallurgy, turn \"Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「焊墊金屬相容」的模型：晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pad metallurgy: Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw pad thickness and protection sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw pad thickness and protection sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊墊金屬相容的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pad metallurgy, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-05-k1","title":"焊墊金屬相容：機制","titleEn":"Pad metallurgy: mechanism","text":"晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。","textEn":"Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。 必須排除的錯判：任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw pad thickness and protection sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊墊金屬相容」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pad metallurgy — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔開得越深連接必越可靠","晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。","任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接"],"optionsEn":["Assuming deeper openings always improve contact","Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization.","Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged"],"answer":1,"explanation":"晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。 畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。 因此不能採用「任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接」。","explanationEn":"Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization. Draw pad thickness and protection sections. Therefore reject: Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged."}},{"id":"a119-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-05"],"title":"焊墊金屬相容｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pad metallurgy | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對焊墊金屬相容，把「晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pad metallurgy, turn \"Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。 將「任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw pad thickness and protection sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw pad thickness and protection sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付焊墊金屬相容的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pad metallurgy: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-06-k1","title":"焊墊金屬相容：機制","titleEn":"Pad metallurgy: mechanism","text":"晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。","textEn":"Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。 必須排除的錯判：任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw pad thickness and protection sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「焊墊金屬相容」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pad metallurgy — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接","孔開得越深連接必越可靠","畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。"],"optionsEn":["Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged","Assuming deeper openings always improve contact","Draw pad thickness and protection sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒墊需承受後續雷射開孔及金屬化。 畫焊墊厚度與保護層剖面。 因此不能採用「任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接」。","explanationEn":"Die pads must tolerate laser opening and metallization. Draw pad thickness and protection sections. Therefore reject: Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged."}}]},{"id":"a119-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"放置與層合","titleEn":"Placement and lamination","description":"針對放置與層合完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for placement and lamination, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a119-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-06"],"title":"固定與位移｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Fixation and shift | mechanism and design","objective":"針對固定與位移，把「層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fixation and shift, turn \"Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「固定與位移」的模型：層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for fixation and shift: Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare fiducials before/after lamination. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare fiducials before/after lamination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：放置精度就是最終嵌入精度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating placement with final embedding accuracy. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固定與位移的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for fixation and shift, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-07-k1","title":"固定與位移：機制","titleEn":"Fixation and shift: mechanism","text":"層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。","textEn":"Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。 必須排除的錯判：放置精度就是最終嵌入精度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare fiducials before/after lamination. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating placement with final embedding accuracy. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固定與位移」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fixation and shift — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。","放置精度就是最終嵌入精度","表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通"],"optionsEn":["Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies.","Equating placement with final embedding accuracy","Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact"],"answer":0,"explanation":"層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。 比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。 因此不能採用「放置精度就是最終嵌入精度」。","explanationEn":"Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies. Compare fiducials before/after lamination. Therefore reject: Equating placement with final embedding accuracy."}},{"id":"a119-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-07"],"title":"固定與位移｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Fixation and shift | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對固定與位移，把「層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For fixation and shift, turn \"Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。 將「放置精度就是最終嵌入精度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare fiducials before/after lamination. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating placement with final embedding accuracy\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare fiducials before/after lamination. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：放置精度就是最終嵌入精度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating placement with final embedding accuracy. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付固定與位移的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for fixation and shift: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-08-k1","title":"固定與位移：機制","titleEn":"Fixation and shift: mechanism","text":"層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。","textEn":"Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。 必須排除的錯判：放置精度就是最終嵌入精度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare fiducials before/after lamination. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating placement with final embedding accuracy. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「固定與位移」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For fixation and shift — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通","比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。","放置精度就是最終嵌入精度"],"optionsEn":["Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact","Compare fiducials before/after lamination.","Equating placement with final embedding accuracy"],"answer":1,"explanation":"層壓流動和壓力會讓晶粒平移或傾斜。 比對層壓前後 fiducial 位置。 因此不能採用「放置精度就是最終嵌入精度」。","explanationEn":"Lamination flow/pressure can shift or tilt dies. Compare fiducials before/after lamination. Therefore reject: Equating placement with final embedding accuracy."}},{"id":"a119-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-08"],"title":"樹脂填充｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Resin filling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對樹脂填充，把「晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resin filling, turn \"Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「樹脂填充」的模型：晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「取晶粒角落和中央截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for resin filling: Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Section corners and centers. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"取晶粒角落和中央截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Section corners and centers. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：板表面平整即內部無空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring no internal voids from a flat board. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付樹脂填充的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for resin filling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-09-k1","title":"樹脂填充：機制","titleEn":"Resin filling: mechanism","text":"晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。","textEn":"Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"取晶粒角落和中央截面。 必須排除的錯判：板表面平整即內部無空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Section corners and centers. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring no internal voids from a flat board. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樹脂填充」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resin filling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["板表面平整即內部無空洞","互連短就必定結溫較低","晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。"],"optionsEn":["Inferring no internal voids from a flat board","Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature","Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。 取晶粒角落和中央截面。 因此不能採用「板表面平整即內部無空洞」。","explanationEn":"Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids. Section corners and centers. Therefore reject: Inferring no internal voids from a flat board."}},{"id":"a119-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-09"],"title":"樹脂填充｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Resin filling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對樹脂填充，把「晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For resin filling, turn \"Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：取晶粒角落和中央截面。 將「板表面平整即內部無空洞」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Section corners and centers. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring no internal voids from a flat board\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"取晶粒角落和中央截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Section corners and centers. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：板表面平整即內部無空洞。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring no internal voids from a flat board. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付樹脂填充的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for resin filling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-10-k1","title":"樹脂填充：機制","titleEn":"Resin filling: mechanism","text":"晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。","textEn":"Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"取晶粒角落和中央截面。 必須排除的錯判：板表面平整即內部無空洞。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Section corners and centers. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring no internal voids from a flat board. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樹脂填充」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For resin filling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["取晶粒角落和中央截面。","板表面平整即內部無空洞","互連短就必定結溫較低"],"optionsEn":["Section corners and centers.","Inferring no internal voids from a flat board","Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒周圍狹縫可能形成樹脂不足與氣泡。 取晶粒角落和中央截面。 因此不能採用「板表面平整即內部無空洞」。","explanationEn":"Narrow die-edge gaps can cause resin starvation and voids. Section corners and centers. Therefore reject: Inferring no internal voids from a flat board."}},{"id":"a119-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-10"],"title":"層壓應力｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Lamination stress | mechanism and design","objective":"針對層壓應力，把「不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For lamination stress, turn \"Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「層壓應力」的模型：不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for lamination stress: Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：降低總壓力必能解決所有破片。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層壓應力的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for lamination stress, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-11-k1","title":"層壓應力：機制","titleEn":"Lamination stress: mechanism","text":"不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。","textEn":"Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。 必須排除的錯判：降低總壓力必能解決所有破片。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層壓應力」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For lamination stress — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["層壓後密封就不再吸濕","不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。","降低總壓力必能解決所有破片"],"optionsEn":["Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake","Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads.","Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。 連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。 因此不能採用「降低總壓力必能解決所有破片」。","explanationEn":"Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads. Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. Therefore reject: Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture."}},{"id":"a119-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-11"],"title":"層壓應力｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Lamination stress | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對層壓應力，把「不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For lamination stress, turn \"Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。 將「降低總壓力必能解決所有破片」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：降低總壓力必能解決所有破片。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層壓應力的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for lamination stress: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-12-k1","title":"層壓應力：機制","titleEn":"Lamination stress: mechanism","text":"不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。","textEn":"Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。 必須排除的錯判：降低總壓力必能解決所有破片。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層壓應力」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For lamination stress — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["降低總壓力必能解決所有破片","層壓後密封就不再吸濕","連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture","Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake","Relate support, cavities and fracture sites."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不均勻壓力可能使晶粒彎曲，總壓力不能代表局部負載。 連結支撐、腔體與破裂位置。 因此不能採用「降低總壓力必能解決所有破片」。","explanationEn":"Uneven pressure can bend dies; total pressure hides local loads. Relate support, cavities and fracture sites. Therefore reject: Assuming lower pressure solves every fracture."}}]},{"id":"a119-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"接點形成","titleEn":"Contact formation","description":"針對接點形成完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for contact formation, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a119-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-12"],"title":"開孔對位｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Via-to-pad alignment | mechanism and design","objective":"針對開孔對位，把「埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via-to-pad alignment, turn \"Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「開孔對位」的模型：埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for via-to-pad alignment: Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付開孔對位的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for via-to-pad alignment, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-13-k1","title":"開孔對位：機制","titleEn":"Via-to-pad alignment: mechanism","text":"埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。","textEn":"Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。 必須排除的錯判：外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. Misinterpretation to reject: Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「開孔對位」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via-to-pad alignment — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。","外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊","看到內部需要先研磨整板"],"optionsEn":["Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion.","Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad","Grinding the board before localization"],"answer":0,"explanation":"埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。 保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。 因此不能採用「外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊」。","explanationEn":"Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion. Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. Therefore reject: Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad."}},{"id":"a119-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-13"],"title":"開孔對位｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Via-to-pad alignment | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對開孔對位，把「埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via-to-pad alignment, turn \"Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。 將「外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付開孔對位的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for via-to-pad alignment: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-14-k1","title":"開孔對位：機制","titleEn":"Via-to-pad alignment: mechanism","text":"埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。","textEn":"Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。 必須排除的錯判：外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. Misinterpretation to reject: Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「開孔對位」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via-to-pad alignment — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["看到內部需要先研磨整板","保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。","外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊"],"optionsEn":["Grinding the board before localization","Retain local residuals and capture boundaries.","Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad"],"answer":1,"explanation":"埋藏焊墊的位置需從可見標記和層壓變形推定。 保留局部對位殘差與捕捉邊界。 因此不能採用「外框標記對準即可保證所有埋藏墊」。","explanationEn":"Buried pad locations depend on visible references and laminate distortion. Retain local residuals and capture boundaries. Therefore reject: Using frame alignment to guarantee every buried pad."}},{"id":"a119-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-14"],"title":"孔底損傷｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Via-bottom damage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對孔底損傷，把「開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via-bottom damage, turn \"Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「孔底損傷」的模型：開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for via-bottom damage: Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔開得越深連接必越可靠。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming deeper openings always improve contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔底損傷的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for via-bottom damage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-15-k1","title":"孔底損傷：機制","titleEn":"Via-bottom damage: mechanism","text":"開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。","textEn":"Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。 必須排除的錯判：孔開得越深連接必越可靠。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming deeper openings always improve contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔底損傷」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via-bottom damage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔開得越深連接必越可靠","名義腔深較大就不需公差分析","開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming deeper openings always improve contact","Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger","Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。 比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。 因此不能採用「孔開得越深連接必越可靠」。","explanationEn":"Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal. Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. Therefore reject: Assuming deeper openings always improve contact."}},{"id":"a119-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-15"],"title":"孔底損傷｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Via-bottom damage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對孔底損傷，把「開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via-bottom damage, turn \"Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。 將「孔開得越深連接必越可靠」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming deeper openings always improve contact\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔開得越深連接必越可靠。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming deeper openings always improve contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔底損傷的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for via-bottom damage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-16-k1","title":"孔底損傷：機制","titleEn":"Via-bottom damage: mechanism","text":"開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。","textEn":"Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。 必須排除的錯判：孔開得越深連接必越可靠。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming deeper openings always improve contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔底損傷」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via-bottom damage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。","孔開得越深連接必越可靠","名義腔深較大就不需公差分析"],"optionsEn":["Compare bottom sections and contact resistance.","Assuming deeper openings always improve contact","Skipping tolerances when nominal cavity depth is larger"],"answer":0,"explanation":"開孔需露出焊墊又避免薄墊受損。 比較孔底截面和接觸電阻。 因此不能採用「孔開得越深連接必越可靠」。","explanationEn":"Opening must expose pads without damaging thin metal. Compare bottom sections and contact resistance. Therefore reject: Assuming deeper openings always improve contact."}},{"id":"a119-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-16"],"title":"金屬化連續｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Metallization continuity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對金屬化連續，把「孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For metallization continuity, turn \"Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「金屬化連續」的模型：孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設晶粒厚 100±5 μm、腔深 120±4 μm，名義上方餘隙 20 μm；若公差為界限，最小餘隙 11 μm、最大 29 μm。RSS 只適用已知統計模型，不能替代最壞界限。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for metallization continuity: Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For a 100±5 μm die in a 120±4 μm cavity, nominal clearance is 20 μm and bounded extremes are 11–29 μm. RSS requires a statistical model and cannot replace worst-case bounds. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付金屬化連續的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for metallization continuity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-17-k1","title":"金屬化連續：機制","titleEn":"Metallization continuity: mechanism","text":"孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。","textEn":"Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。 必須排除的錯判：表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. Misinterpretation to reject: Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設晶粒厚 100±5 μm、腔深 120±4 μm，名義上方餘隙 20 μm；若公差為界限，最小餘隙 11 μm、最大 29 μm。RSS 只適用已知統計模型，不能替代最壞界限。","textEn":"For a 100±5 μm die in a 120±4 μm cavity, nominal clearance is 20 μm and bounded extremes are 11–29 μm. RSS requires a statistical model and cannot replace worst-case bounds."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「金屬化連續」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For metallization continuity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["嵌入前測試可全由終測取代","孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。","表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通"],"optionsEn":["Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests","Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection.","Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。 用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。 因此不能採用「表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通」。","explanationEn":"Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection. Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. Therefore reject: Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact."}},{"id":"a119-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-17"],"title":"金屬化連續｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Metallization continuity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對金屬化連續，把「孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For metallization continuity, turn \"Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。 將「表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設晶粒厚 100±5 μm、腔深 120±4 μm，名義上方餘隙 20 μm；若公差為界限，最小餘隙 11 μm、最大 29 μm。RSS 只適用已知統計模型，不能替代最壞界限。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For a 100±5 μm die in a 120±4 μm cavity, nominal clearance is 20 μm and bounded extremes are 11–29 μm. RSS requires a statistical model and cannot replace worst-case bounds. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付金屬化連續的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for metallization continuity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-18-k1","title":"金屬化連續：機制","titleEn":"Metallization continuity: mechanism","text":"孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。","textEn":"Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。 必須排除的錯判：表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. Misinterpretation to reject: Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設晶粒厚 100±5 μm、腔深 120±4 μm，名義上方餘隙 20 μm；若公差為界限，最小餘隙 11 μm、最大 29 μm。RSS 只適用已知統計模型，不能替代最壞界限。","textEn":"For a 100±5 μm die in a 120±4 μm cavity, nominal clearance is 20 μm and bounded extremes are 11–29 μm. RSS requires a statistical model and cannot replace worst-case bounds."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「金屬化連續」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For metallization continuity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通","嵌入前測試可全由終測取代","用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。"],"optionsEn":["Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact","Replacing pre-embedding tests with final tests","Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔壁與焊墊的連續覆蓋決定垂直接點。 用鏈路加局部截面定位不連續。 因此不能採用「表面銅厚足夠即可保證孔底連通」。","explanationEn":"Continuous wall-to-pad coverage determines vertical connection. Use chains and local sections to locate discontinuity. Therefore reject: Using surface Cu thickness to prove bottom contact."}}]},{"id":"a119-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗證與熱路徑","titleEn":"Verification and thermal paths","description":"針對驗證與熱路徑完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for verification and thermal paths, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a119-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-18"],"title":"熱流路徑｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal paths | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱流路徑，把「嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal paths, turn \"Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱流路徑」的模型：嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal paths: Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：互連短就必定結溫較低。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱流路徑的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal paths, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-19-k1","title":"熱流路徑：機制","titleEn":"Thermal paths: mechanism","text":"嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。","textEn":"Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。 必須排除的錯判：互連短就必定結溫較低。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱流路徑」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal paths — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。","互連短就必定結溫較低","任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接"],"optionsEn":["Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths.","Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature","Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged"],"answer":0,"explanation":"嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。 比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。 因此不能採用「互連短就必定結溫較低」。","explanationEn":"Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths. Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. Therefore reject: Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature."}},{"id":"a119-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-19"],"title":"熱流路徑｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal paths | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱流路徑，把「嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal paths, turn \"Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。 將「互連短就必定結溫較低」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：互連短就必定結溫較低。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱流路徑的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal paths: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-20-k1","title":"熱流路徑：機制","titleEn":"Thermal paths: mechanism","text":"嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。","textEn":"Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。 必須排除的錯判：互連短就必定結溫較低。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱流路徑」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal paths — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["任何原晶粒墊都可直接雷射連接","比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。","互連短就必定結溫較低"],"optionsEn":["Laser-contacting any original die pad unchanged","Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes.","Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature"],"answer":1,"explanation":"嵌入介電質可能增加熱阻，電路縮短不代表散熱改善。 比較晶粒到板面與銅平面的熱網路。 因此不能採用「互連短就必定結溫較低」。","explanationEn":"Embedding dielectric may increase thermal resistance despite shorter electrical paths. Compare thermal networks to board surfaces and Cu planes. Therefore reject: Assuming shorter interconnect guarantees lower junction temperature."}},{"id":"a119-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-20"],"title":"水分與界面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces | mechanism and design","objective":"針對水分與界面，把「晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For moisture and interfaces, turn \"Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「水分與界面」的模型：晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照受濕後聲學與電性。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for moisture and interfaces: Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"對照受濕後聲學與電性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：層壓後密封就不再吸濕。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付水分與界面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for moisture and interfaces, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-21-k1","title":"水分與界面：機制","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces: mechanism","text":"晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。","textEn":"Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照受濕後聲學與電性。 必須排除的錯判：層壓後密封就不再吸濕。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水分與界面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For moisture and interfaces — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["層壓後密封就不再吸濕","放置精度就是最終嵌入精度","晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake","Equating placement with final embedding accuracy","Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。 對照受濕後聲學與電性。 因此不能採用「層壓後密封就不再吸濕」。","explanationEn":"Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths. Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. Therefore reject: Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake."}},{"id":"a119-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-21"],"title":"水分與界面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對水分與界面，把「晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For moisture and interfaces, turn \"Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照受濕後聲學與電性。 將「層壓後密封就不再吸濕」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"對照受濕後聲學與電性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：層壓後密封就不再吸濕。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付水分與界面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for moisture and interfaces: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-22-k1","title":"水分與界面：機制","titleEn":"Moisture and interfaces: mechanism","text":"晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。","textEn":"Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照受濕後聲學與電性。 必須排除的錯判：層壓後密封就不再吸濕。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水分與界面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For moisture and interfaces — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["對照受濕後聲學與電性。","層壓後密封就不再吸濕","放置精度就是最終嵌入精度"],"optionsEn":["Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results.","Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake","Equating placement with final embedding accuracy"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒—樹脂界面可能成為吸濕分層路徑。 對照受濕後聲學與電性。 因此不能採用「層壓後密封就不再吸濕」。","explanationEn":"Die–resin interfaces can become moisture-delamination paths. Compare conditioned acoustic/electrical results. Therefore reject: Assuming lamination prevents all moisture uptake."}},{"id":"a119-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-22"],"title":"測試與失效拆解｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Testing and failure analysis | mechanism and design","objective":"針對測試與失效拆解，把「埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For testing and failure analysis, turn \"Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「測試與失效拆解」的模型：埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for testing and failure analysis: Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Localize nets before destructive sectioning. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Localize nets before destructive sectioning. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：看到內部需要先研磨整板。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Grinding the board before localization. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付測試與失效拆解的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for testing and failure analysis, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-23-k1","title":"測試與失效拆解：機制","titleEn":"Testing and failure analysis: mechanism","text":"埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。","textEn":"Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。 必須排除的錯判：看到內部需要先研磨整板。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Localize nets before destructive sectioning. Misinterpretation to reject: Grinding the board before localization. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試與失效拆解」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For testing and failure analysis — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["板表面平整即內部無空洞","埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。","看到內部需要先研磨整板"],"optionsEn":["Inferring no internal voids from a flat board","Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence.","Grinding the board before localization"],"answer":1,"explanation":"埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。 先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。 因此不能採用「看到內部需要先研磨整板」。","explanationEn":"Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence. Localize nets before destructive sectioning. Therefore reject: Grinding the board before localization."}},{"id":"a119-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a119-v9-23"],"title":"測試與失效拆解｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Testing and failure analysis | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對測試與失效拆解，把「埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For testing and failure analysis, turn \"Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。 將「看到內部需要先研磨整板」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Localize nets before destructive sectioning. Challenge the hypothesis \"Grinding the board before localization\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Localize nets before destructive sectioning. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：看到內部需要先研磨整板。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Grinding the board before localization. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付測試與失效拆解的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for testing and failure analysis: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a119-v9-24-k1","title":"測試與失效拆解：機制","titleEn":"Testing and failure analysis: mechanism","text":"埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。","textEn":"Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a119-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。 必須排除的錯判：看到內部需要先研磨整板。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Localize nets before destructive sectioning. Misinterpretation to reject: Grinding the board before localization. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asevip","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試與失效拆解」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For testing and failure analysis — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["看到內部需要先研磨整板","板表面平整即內部無空洞","先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。"],"optionsEn":["Grinding the board before localization","Inferring no internal voids from a flat board","Localize nets before destructive sectioning."],"answer":2,"explanation":"埋藏元件需要設計測試節點及保留非破壞證據。 先定位網路再決定破壞性截面。 因此不能採用「看到內部需要先研磨整板」。","explanationEn":"Buried components need test access and retained nondestructive evidence. Localize nets before destructive sectioning. Therefore reject: Grinding the board before localization."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-encapsulation","subcategoryTitle":"封膠、扇出與異質整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Encapsulation, fan-out and heterogeneous integration","photoId":"bga-section"},{"id":"a120","title":"系統級封裝異質整合","titleEn":"System-in-package heterogeneous integration","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip","v3-media-698d26511517","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入功能分割、異質接口與系統驗證。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore functional partitioning, heterogeneous interfaces and system validation, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["系統分工","封裝架構","跨域整合","測試與供應鏈"],"labelsEn":["System partition","Package architecture","Cross-domain integration","Test and supply chain"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a120-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"系統分工","titleEn":"System partition","description":"針對系統分工完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for system partition, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a120-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"功能需求樹｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Functional requirement tree | mechanism and design","objective":"針對功能需求樹，把「系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For functional requirement tree, turn \"System performance must become measurable module interfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「功能需求樹」的模型：系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for functional requirement tree: System performance must become measurable module interfaces. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：把功能元件放一起即成完整系統。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating colocated components with a complete system. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付功能需求樹的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for functional requirement tree, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-01-k1","title":"功能需求樹：機制","titleEn":"Functional requirement tree: mechanism","text":"系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。","textEn":"System performance must become measurable module interfaces.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。 必須排除的錯判：把功能元件放一起即成完整系統。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating colocated components with a complete system. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「功能需求樹」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For functional requirement tree — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。","把功能元件放一起即成完整系統","各元件單獨熱測通過即可"],"optionsEn":["System performance must become measurable module interfaces.","Equating colocated components with a complete system","Relying only on individual thermal passes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。 把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。 因此不能採用「把功能元件放一起即成完整系統」。","explanationEn":"System performance must become measurable module interfaces. Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. Therefore reject: Equating colocated components with a complete system."}},{"id":"a120-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-01"],"title":"功能需求樹｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Functional requirement tree | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對功能需求樹，把「系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For functional requirement tree, turn \"System performance must become measurable module interfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。 將「把功能元件放一起即成完整系統」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating colocated components with a complete system\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：把功能元件放一起即成完整系統。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating colocated components with a complete system. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付功能需求樹的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for functional requirement tree: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-02-k1","title":"功能需求樹：機制","titleEn":"Functional requirement tree: mechanism","text":"系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。","textEn":"System performance must become measurable module interfaces.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。 必須排除的錯判：把功能元件放一起即成完整系統。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating colocated components with a complete system. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「功能需求樹」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For functional requirement tree — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各元件單獨熱測通過即可","把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。","把功能元件放一起即成完整系統"],"optionsEn":["Relying only on individual thermal passes","Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components.","Equating colocated components with a complete system"],"answer":1,"explanation":"系統性能需拆成可量測的模組接口。 把頻寬、延遲、功耗連到各元件。 因此不能採用「把功能元件放一起即成完整系統」。","explanationEn":"System performance must become measurable module interfaces. Allocate bandwidth, latency and power to components. Therefore reject: Equating colocated components with a complete system."}},{"id":"a120-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-02"],"title":"晶粒技術分工｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Die technology partition | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶粒技術分工，把「不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die technology partition, turn \"Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶粒技術分工」的模型：不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for die technology partition: Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：分割越多一定越省成本。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒技術分工的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for die technology partition, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-03-k1","title":"晶粒技術分工：機制","titleEn":"Die technology partition: mechanism","text":"不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。","textEn":"Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。 必須排除的錯判：分割越多一定越省成本。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒技術分工」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die technology partition — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分割越多一定越省成本","金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合","不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost","Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling","Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。 比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。 因此不能採用「分割越多一定越省成本」。","explanationEn":"Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs. Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. Therefore reject: Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost."}},{"id":"a120-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-03"],"title":"晶粒技術分工｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Die technology partition | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶粒技術分工，把「不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die technology partition, turn \"Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。 將「分割越多一定越省成本」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：分割越多一定越省成本。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒技術分工的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for die technology partition: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-04-k1","title":"晶粒技術分工：機制","titleEn":"Die technology partition: mechanism","text":"不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。","textEn":"Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。 必須排除的錯判：分割越多一定越省成本。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒技術分工」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die technology partition — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。","分割越多一定越省成本","金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合"],"optionsEn":["Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets.","Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost","Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同製程的優勢須抵銷封裝接口成本。 比較單晶片與多晶粒的完整預算。 因此不能採用「分割越多一定越省成本」。","explanationEn":"Process-node benefits must offset packaging-interface costs. Compare complete monolithic and multichip budgets. Therefore reject: Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost."}},{"id":"a120-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-04"],"title":"接口契約｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Interface contracts | mechanism and design","objective":"針對接口契約，把「電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface contracts, turn \"Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「接口契約」的模型：電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「列雙方責任和版本。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for interface contracts: Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: List ownership and versions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"列雙方責任和版本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List ownership and versions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：協定名稱相同即保證互通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接口契約的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for interface contracts, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-05-k1","title":"接口契約：機制","titleEn":"Interface contracts: mechanism","text":"電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。","textEn":"Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列雙方責任和版本。 必須排除的錯判：協定名稱相同即保證互通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List ownership and versions. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接口契約」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface contracts — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["元件全固定好就不需應力分析","電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。","協定名稱相同即保證互通"],"optionsEn":["Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation","Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree.","Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。 列雙方責任和版本。 因此不能採用「協定名稱相同即保證互通」。","explanationEn":"Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree. List ownership and versions. Therefore reject: Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability."}},{"id":"a120-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-05"],"title":"接口契約｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Interface contracts | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對接口契約，把「電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For interface contracts, turn \"Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：列雙方責任和版本。 將「協定名稱相同即保證互通」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: List ownership and versions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"列雙方責任和版本。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"List ownership and versions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：協定名稱相同即保證互通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付接口契約的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for interface contracts: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-06-k1","title":"接口契約：機制","titleEn":"Interface contracts: mechanism","text":"電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。","textEn":"Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列雙方責任和版本。 必須排除的錯判：協定名稱相同即保證互通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"List ownership and versions. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接口契約」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For interface contracts — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["協定名稱相同即保證互通","元件全固定好就不需應力分析","列雙方責任和版本。"],"optionsEn":["Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability","Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation","List ownership and versions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電壓、時序、阻抗、協定和測試要求都需一致。 列雙方責任和版本。 因此不能採用「協定名稱相同即保證互通」。","explanationEn":"Voltage, timing, impedance, protocol and test contracts must agree. List ownership and versions. Therefore reject: Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability."}}]},{"id":"a120-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"封裝架構","titleEn":"Package architecture","description":"針對封裝架構完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for package architecture, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a120-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-06"],"title":"封裝拓撲｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Package topology | mechanism and design","objective":"針對封裝拓撲，把「2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For package topology, turn \"2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「封裝拓撲」的模型：2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for package topology: 2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最短連線總是最好的架構。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付封裝拓撲的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for package topology, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-07-k1","title":"封裝拓撲：機制","titleEn":"Package topology: mechanism","text":"2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。","textEn":"2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。 必須排除的錯判：最短連線總是最好的架構。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「封裝拓撲」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For package topology — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。","最短連線總是最好的架構","系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格"],"optionsEn":["2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability.","Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture","Equating successful boot with all interface qualification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。 畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。 因此不能採用「最短連線總是最好的架構」。","explanationEn":"2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability. Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. Therefore reject: Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture."}},{"id":"a120-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-07"],"title":"封裝拓撲｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Package topology | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對封裝拓撲，把「2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For package topology, turn \"2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。 將「最短連線總是最好的架構」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最短連線總是最好的架構。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付封裝拓撲的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for package topology: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-08-k1","title":"封裝拓撲：機制","titleEn":"Package topology: mechanism","text":"2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。","textEn":"2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。 必須排除的錯判：最短連線總是最好的架構。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「封裝拓撲」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For package topology — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格","畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。","最短連線總是最好的架構"],"optionsEn":["Equating successful boot with all interface qualification","Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology.","Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture"],"answer":1,"explanation":"2D、2.5D、3D 改變連線長度、散熱及可測性。 畫三種拓撲的電熱路徑。 因此不能採用「最短連線總是最好的架構」。","explanationEn":"2D/2.5D/3D change links, cooling and testability. Draw electrical/thermal paths for each topology. Therefore reject: Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture."}},{"id":"a120-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-08"],"title":"被動元件配置｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Passive placement | mechanism and design","objective":"針對被動元件配置，把「去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For passive placement, turn \"Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「被動元件配置」的模型：去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for passive placement: Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Mark closed power and RF current loops. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark closed power and RF current loops. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付被動元件配置的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for passive placement, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-09-k1","title":"被動元件配置：機制","titleEn":"Passive placement: mechanism","text":"去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。","textEn":"Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。 必須排除的錯判：電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark closed power and RF current loops. Misinterpretation to reject: Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「被動元件配置」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For passive placement — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好","只看最終良率就能比較生產成本","去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。"],"optionsEn":["Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center","Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone","Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space."],"answer":2,"explanation":"去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。 標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。 因此不能採用「電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好」。","explanationEn":"Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space. Mark closed power and RF current loops. Therefore reject: Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center."}},{"id":"a120-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-09"],"title":"被動元件配置｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Passive placement | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對被動元件配置，把「去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For passive placement, turn \"Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。 將「電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Mark closed power and RF current loops. Challenge the hypothesis \"Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark closed power and RF current loops. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付被動元件配置的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for passive placement: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-10-k1","title":"被動元件配置：機制","titleEn":"Passive placement: mechanism","text":"去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。","textEn":"Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。 必須排除的錯判：電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark closed power and RF current loops. Misinterpretation to reject: Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「被動元件配置」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For passive placement — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。","電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好","只看最終良率就能比較生產成本"],"optionsEn":["Mark closed power and RF current loops.","Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center","Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"去耦、濾波和匹配元件需按回路而非空位配置。 標出電源與射頻電流閉合路徑。 因此不能採用「電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好」。","explanationEn":"Place decoupling/filtering/matching components by loops, not free space. Mark closed power and RF current loops. Therefore reject: Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center."}},{"id":"a120-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-10"],"title":"熱源共存｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Coexisting heat sources | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱源共存，把「高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For coexisting heat sources, turn \"High-power components warm sensitive neighbors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱源共存」的模型：高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for coexisting heat sources: High-power components warm sensitive neighbors. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各元件單獨熱測通過即可。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Relying only on individual thermal passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱源共存的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for coexisting heat sources, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-11-k1","title":"熱源共存：機制","titleEn":"Coexisting heat sources: mechanism","text":"高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。","textEn":"High-power components warm sensitive neighbors.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。 必須排除的錯判：各元件單獨熱測通過即可。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. Misinterpretation to reject: Relying only on individual thermal passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱源共存」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For coexisting heat sources — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證","高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。","各元件單獨熱測通過即可"],"optionsEn":["Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification","High-power components warm sensitive neighbors.","Relying only on individual thermal passes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。 比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。 因此不能採用「各元件單獨熱測通過即可」。","explanationEn":"High-power components warm sensitive neighbors. Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. Therefore reject: Relying only on individual thermal passes."}},{"id":"a120-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-11"],"title":"熱源共存｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Coexisting heat sources | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱源共存，把「高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For coexisting heat sources, turn \"High-power components warm sensitive neighbors.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。 將「各元件單獨熱測通過即可」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. Challenge the hypothesis \"Relying only on individual thermal passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各元件單獨熱測通過即可。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Relying only on individual thermal passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱源共存的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for coexisting heat sources: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-12-k1","title":"熱源共存：機制","titleEn":"Coexisting heat sources: mechanism","text":"高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。","textEn":"High-power components warm sensitive neighbors.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。 必須排除的錯判：各元件單獨熱測通過即可。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. Misinterpretation to reject: Relying only on individual thermal passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱源共存」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For coexisting heat sources — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各元件單獨熱測通過即可","韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證","比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。"],"optionsEn":["Relying only on individual thermal passes","Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification","Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高功耗元件會升高鄰近敏感元件溫度。 比較局部熱源開關的交叉溫升。 因此不能採用「各元件單獨熱測通過即可」。","explanationEn":"High-power components warm sensitive neighbors. Compare cross-heating with individual sources toggled. Therefore reject: Relying only on individual thermal passes."}}]},{"id":"a120-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"跨域整合","titleEn":"Cross-domain integration","description":"針對跨域整合完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for cross-domain integration, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a120-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-12"],"title":"射頻隔離｜機制與設計","titleEn":"RF isolation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對射頻隔離，把「共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rf isolation, turn \"Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「射頻隔離」的模型：共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for rf isolation: Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付射頻隔離的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for rf isolation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-13-k1","title":"射頻隔離：機制","titleEn":"RF isolation: mechanism","text":"共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。","textEn":"Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。 必須排除的錯判：金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「射頻隔離」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rf isolation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。","金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合","各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳"],"optionsEn":["Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference.","Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling","Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system"],"answer":0,"explanation":"共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。 畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。 因此不能採用「金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合」。","explanationEn":"Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference. Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. Therefore reject: Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling."}},{"id":"a120-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-13"],"title":"射頻隔離｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"RF isolation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對射頻隔離，把「共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For rf isolation, turn \"Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。 將「金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付射頻隔離的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for rf isolation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-14-k1","title":"射頻隔離：機制","titleEn":"RF isolation: mechanism","text":"共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。","textEn":"Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。 必須排除的錯判：金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「射頻隔離」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For rf isolation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳","畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。","金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合"],"optionsEn":["Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system","Draw desired signals and unintended coupling.","Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling"],"answer":1,"explanation":"共用電源、地和基材都可能耦合干擾。 畫有意信號與非預期耦合路徑。 因此不能採用「金屬罩能消除全部電源耦合」。","explanationEn":"Shared power, grounds and substrates can couple interference. Draw desired signals and unintended coupling. Therefore reject: Assuming a shield eliminates all power coupling."}},{"id":"a120-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-14"],"title":"機械堆疊｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Mechanical stackup | mechanism and design","objective":"針對機械堆疊，把「材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mechanical stackup, turn \"Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「機械堆疊」的模型：材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for mechanical stackup: Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：元件全固定好就不需應力分析。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付機械堆疊的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for mechanical stackup, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-15-k1","title":"機械堆疊：機制","titleEn":"Mechanical stackup: mechanism","text":"材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。","textEn":"Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。 必須排除的錯判：元件全固定好就不需應力分析。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「機械堆疊」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mechanical stackup — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["元件全固定好就不需應力分析","把功能元件放一起即成完整系統","材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。"],"optionsEn":["Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation","Equating colocated components with a complete system","Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。 比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。 因此不能採用「元件全固定好就不需應力分析」。","explanationEn":"Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity. Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. Therefore reject: Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation."}},{"id":"a120-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-15"],"title":"機械堆疊｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Mechanical stackup | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對機械堆疊，把「材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mechanical stackup, turn \"Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。 將「元件全固定好就不需應力分析」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：元件全固定好就不需應力分析。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付機械堆疊的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for mechanical stackup: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-16-k1","title":"機械堆疊：機制","titleEn":"Mechanical stackup: mechanism","text":"材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。","textEn":"Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。 必須排除的錯判：元件全固定好就不需應力分析。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「機械堆疊」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mechanical stackup — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。","元件全固定好就不需應力分析","把功能元件放一起即成完整系統"],"optionsEn":["Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces.","Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation","Equating colocated components with a complete system"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料失配和元件高度決定局部應力及共面性。 比較關鍵界面的熱機邊界。 因此不能採用「元件全固定好就不需應力分析」。","explanationEn":"Material mismatch and component height set stress/coplanarity. Compare thermomechanical boundaries at key interfaces. Therefore reject: Skipping stress analysis after mechanical fixation."}},{"id":"a120-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-16"],"title":"測試可觀測性｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Test observability | mechanism and design","objective":"針對測試可觀測性，把「每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For test observability, turn \"Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「測試可觀測性」的模型：每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把測試點對照失效類型。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設三子模組獨立良率 0.98、0.99、0.97，且組裝良率 0.95，粗估總良率乘積≈0.894。此模型不含相關缺陷、返修與篩選，可作比較基準而非產量承諾。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for test observability: Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Map test points to failures. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: Illustrative independent module yields 0.98, 0.99, 0.97 and assembly yield 0.95 multiply to≈0.894, excluding correlations, rework and screening. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"把測試點對照失效類型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map test points to failures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating successful boot with all interface qualification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付測試可觀測性的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for test observability, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-17-k1","title":"測試可觀測性：機制","titleEn":"Test observability: mechanism","text":"每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。","textEn":"Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把測試點對照失效類型。 必須排除的錯判：系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map test points to failures. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating successful boot with all interface qualification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設三子模組獨立良率 0.98、0.99、0.97，且組裝良率 0.95，粗估總良率乘積≈0.894。此模型不含相關缺陷、返修與篩選，可作比較基準而非產量承諾。","textEn":"Illustrative independent module yields 0.98, 0.99, 0.97 and assembly yield 0.95 multiply to≈0.894, excluding correlations, rework and screening."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試可觀測性」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For test observability — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分割越多一定越省成本","每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。","系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost","Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs.","Equating successful boot with all interface qualification"],"answer":1,"explanation":"每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。 把測試點對照失效類型。 因此不能採用「系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格」。","explanationEn":"Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs. Map test points to failures. Therefore reject: Equating successful boot with all interface qualification."}},{"id":"a120-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-17"],"title":"測試可觀測性｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Test observability | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對測試可觀測性，把「每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For test observability, turn \"Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把測試點對照失效類型。 將「系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設三子模組獨立良率 0.98、0.99、0.97，且組裝良率 0.95，粗估總良率乘積≈0.894。此模型不含相關缺陷、返修與篩選，可作比較基準而非產量承諾。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Map test points to failures. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating successful boot with all interface qualification\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: Illustrative independent module yields 0.98, 0.99, 0.97 and assembly yield 0.95 multiply to≈0.894, excluding correlations, rework and screening. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"把測試點對照失效類型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Map test points to failures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating successful boot with all interface qualification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付測試可觀測性的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for test observability: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-18-k1","title":"測試可觀測性：機制","titleEn":"Test observability: mechanism","text":"每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。","textEn":"Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把測試點對照失效類型。 必須排除的錯判：系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Map test points to failures. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating successful boot with all interface qualification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設三子模組獨立良率 0.98、0.99、0.97，且組裝良率 0.95，粗估總良率乘積≈0.894。此模型不含相關缺陷、返修與篩選，可作比較基準而非產量承諾。","textEn":"Illustrative independent module yields 0.98, 0.99, 0.97 and assembly yield 0.95 multiply to≈0.894, excluding correlations, rework and screening."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測試可觀測性」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For test observability — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格","分割越多一定越省成本","把測試點對照失效類型。"],"optionsEn":["Equating successful boot with all interface qualification","Assuming more partitioning always lowers cost","Map test points to failures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每項功能需可控制輸入和可觀察輸出。 把測試點對照失效類型。 因此不能採用「系統啟動成功等於全部接口合格」。","explanationEn":"Each function needs controllable inputs and observable outputs. Map test points to failures. Therefore reject: Equating successful boot with all interface qualification."}}]},{"id":"a120-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"測試與供應鏈","titleEn":"Test and supply chain","description":"針對測試與供應鏈完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for test and supply chain, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a120-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-18"],"title":"良率與返修｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Yield and rework | mechanism and design","objective":"針對良率與返修，把「昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For yield and rework, turn \"Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「良率與返修」的模型：昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for yield and rework: Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只看最終良率就能比較生產成本。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良率與返修的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for yield and rework, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-19-k1","title":"良率與返修：機制","titleEn":"Yield and rework: mechanism","text":"昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。","textEn":"Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。 必須排除的錯判：只看最終良率就能比較生產成本。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. Misinterpretation to reject: Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良率與返修」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For yield and rework — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。","只看最終良率就能比較生產成本","協定名稱相同即保證互通"],"optionsEn":["Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost.","Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone","Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability"],"answer":0,"explanation":"昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。 比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。 因此不能採用「只看最終良率就能比較生產成本」。","explanationEn":"Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost. Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. Therefore reject: Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone."}},{"id":"a120-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-19"],"title":"良率與返修｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Yield and rework | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對良率與返修，把「昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For yield and rework, turn \"Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。 將「只看最終良率就能比較生產成本」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. Challenge the hypothesis \"Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只看最終良率就能比較生產成本。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付良率與返修的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for yield and rework: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-20-k1","title":"良率與返修：機制","titleEn":"Yield and rework: mechanism","text":"昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。","textEn":"Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。 必須排除的錯判：只看最終良率就能比較生產成本。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. Misinterpretation to reject: Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「良率與返修」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For yield and rework — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["協定名稱相同即保證互通","比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。","只看最終良率就能比較生產成本"],"optionsEn":["Equating a shared protocol name with interoperability","Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches.","Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"昂貴模組的組装順序會影響報廢成本。 比較早測、晚測及可返修分支。 因此不能採用「只看最終良率就能比較生產成本」。","explanationEn":"Assembly order of expensive modules changes scrap cost. Compare early tests, late tests and rework branches. Therefore reject: Comparing manufacturing cost from final yield alone."}},{"id":"a120-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-20"],"title":"版本與來源｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Versions and provenance | mechanism and design","objective":"針對版本與來源，把「晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For versions and provenance, turn \"Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「版本與來源」的模型：晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for versions and provenance: Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付版本與來源的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for versions and provenance, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-21-k1","title":"版本與來源：機制","titleEn":"Versions and provenance: mechanism","text":"晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。","textEn":"Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。 必須排除的錯判：韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「版本與來源」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For versions and provenance — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證","最短連線總是最好的架構","晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification","Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture","Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。 建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。 因此不能採用「韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證」。","explanationEn":"Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability. Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. Therefore reject: Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification."}},{"id":"a120-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-21"],"title":"版本與來源｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Versions and provenance | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對版本與來源，把「晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For versions and provenance, turn \"Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。 將「韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付版本與來源的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for versions and provenance: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-22-k1","title":"版本與來源：機制","titleEn":"Versions and provenance: mechanism","text":"晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。","textEn":"Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。 必須排除的錯判：韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「版本與來源」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For versions and provenance — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。","韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證","最短連線總是最好的架構"],"optionsEn":["Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables.","Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification","Assuming shortest links always give the best architecture"],"answer":0,"explanation":"晶粒、基板和韌體版本須一起追溯。 建立可重現的 BOM 和接口版本表。 因此不能採用「韌體升級不會影響封裝驗證」。","explanationEn":"Die, substrate and firmware versions need joint traceability. Build reproducible BOM and interface version tables. Therefore reject: Assuming firmware changes never affect package qualification."}},{"id":"a120-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-22"],"title":"系統接受測試｜機制與設計","titleEn":"System acceptance | mechanism and design","objective":"針對系統接受測試，把「電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For system acceptance, turn \"Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「系統接受測試」的模型：電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for system acceptance: Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付系統接受測試的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for system acceptance, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-23-k1","title":"系統接受測試：機制","titleEn":"System acceptance: mechanism","text":"電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。","textEn":"Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。 必須排除的錯判：各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「系統接受測試」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For system acceptance — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好","電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。","各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳"],"optionsEn":["Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center","Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload.","Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。 提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。 因此不能採用「各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳」。","explanationEn":"Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload. Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. Therefore reject: Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system."}},{"id":"a120-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"],"prerequisiteIds":["a120-v9-23"],"title":"系統接受測試｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"System acceptance | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對系統接受測試，把「電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For system acceptance, turn \"Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。 將「各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付系統接受測試的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for system acceptance: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a120-v9-24-k1","title":"系統接受測試：機制","titleEn":"System acceptance: mechanism","text":"電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。","textEn":"Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]},{"id":"a120-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。 必須排除的錯判：各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-asesip","v9a-asevip"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「系統接受測試」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For system acceptance — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳","電容越靠近外觀上的晶粒中心越好","提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system","Placing capacitors by visual proximity to die center","Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電、熱、機械及軟體證據需對應同一工作負載。 提交代表和邊界情境驗證矩陣。 因此不能採用「各領域各自最佳即保證系統最佳」。","explanationEn":"Electrical, thermal, mechanical and software evidence must share a workload. Submit representative and boundary-scenario matrices. Therefore reject: Assuming independently optimized domains guarantee the best system."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-encapsulation","subcategoryTitle":"封膠、扇出與異質整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Encapsulation, fan-out and heterogeneous integration","photoId":"v9-quilt-array"},{"id":"a121","title":"矽穿孔蝕刻與絕緣","titleEn":"Through-silicon-via etching and insulation","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入TSV 孔形、絕緣覆蓋與漏電。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore tsv geometry, insulation coverage and leakage, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["孔洞架構","深矽蝕刻","絕緣界面","測試交接"],"labelsEn":["Via architecture","Deep silicon etch","Insulating interfaces","Test handoff"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a121-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"孔洞架構","titleEn":"Via architecture","description":"針對孔洞架構完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for via architecture, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a121-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"Via-first/middle/last｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Via-first/middle/last | mechanism and design","objective":"針對Via-first/middle/last，把「形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via-first/middle/last, turn \"Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「Via-first/middle/last」的模型：形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for via-first/middle/last: Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Giving every TSV the same thermal budget. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Via-first/middle/last的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for via-first/middle/last, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-01-k1","title":"Via-first/middle/last：機制","titleEn":"Via-first/middle/last: mechanism","text":"形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。","textEn":"Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。 必須排除的錯判：所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Giving every TSV the same thermal budget. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Via-first/middle/last」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via-first/middle/last — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。","所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算","平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點"],"optionsEn":["Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection.","Giving every TSV the same thermal budget","Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots"],"answer":0,"explanation":"形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。 畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。 因此不能採用「所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算」。","explanationEn":"Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection. Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. Therefore reject: Giving every TSV the same thermal budget."}},{"id":"a121-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-01"],"title":"Via-first/middle/last｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Via-first/middle/last | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對Via-first/middle/last，把「形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For via-first/middle/last, turn \"Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。 將「所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. Challenge the hypothesis \"Giving every TSV the same thermal budget\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Giving every TSV the same thermal budget. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付Via-first/middle/last的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for via-first/middle/last: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-02-k1","title":"Via-first/middle/last：機制","titleEn":"Via-first/middle/last: mechanism","text":"形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。","textEn":"Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。 必須排除的錯判：所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Giving every TSV the same thermal budget. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「Via-first/middle/last」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For via-first/middle/last — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點","畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。","所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算"],"optionsEn":["Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots","Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces.","Giving every TSV the same thermal budget"],"answer":1,"explanation":"形成時點決定可用熱預算與保護的既有結構。 畫三條整合路徑和不可逆界面。 因此不能採用「所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算」。","explanationEn":"Insertion timing determines thermal budget and structures needing protection. Draw three integration routes and irreversible interfaces. Therefore reject: Giving every TSV the same thermal budget."}},{"id":"a121-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-02"],"title":"孔徑與深度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Diameter and depth | mechanism and design","objective":"針對孔徑與深度，把「深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For diameter and depth, turn \"Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「孔徑與深度」的模型：深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量上中下直徑而非只量入口。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for diameter and depth: Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量上中下直徑而非只量入口。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔徑與深度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for diameter and depth, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-03-k1","title":"孔徑與深度：機制","titleEn":"Diameter and depth: mechanism","text":"深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。","textEn":"Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量上中下直徑而非只量入口。 必須排除的錯判：入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. Misinterpretation to reject: Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔徑與深度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For diameter and depth — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV","孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證","深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。"],"optionsEn":["Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter","Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes","Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。 量上中下直徑而非只量入口。 因此不能採用「入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV」。","explanationEn":"Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling. Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. Therefore reject: Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter."}},{"id":"a121-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-03"],"title":"孔徑與深度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Diameter and depth | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對孔徑與深度，把「深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For diameter and depth, turn \"Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量上中下直徑而非只量入口。 將「入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. Challenge the hypothesis \"Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量上中下直徑而非只量入口。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔徑與深度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for diameter and depth: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-04-k1","title":"孔徑與深度：機制","titleEn":"Diameter and depth: mechanism","text":"深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。","textEn":"Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量上中下直徑而非只量入口。 必須排除的錯判：入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. Misinterpretation to reject: Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔徑與深度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For diameter and depth — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["量上中下直徑而非只量入口。","入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV","孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證"],"optionsEn":["Measure top/middle/bottom diameter.","Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter","Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"深寬比影響傳輸、側壁覆蓋和後續填充。 量上中下直徑而非只量入口。 因此不能採用「入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV」。","explanationEn":"Aspect ratio affects transport, coating and filling. Measure top/middle/bottom diameter. Therefore reject: Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter."}},{"id":"a121-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-04"],"title":"遮罩與保護區｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Mask and keep-outs | mechanism and design","objective":"針對遮罩與保護區，把「遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mask and keep-outs, turn \"Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「遮罩與保護區」的模型：遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for mask and keep-outs: Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付遮罩與保護區的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for mask and keep-outs, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-05-k1","title":"遮罩與保護區：機制","titleEn":"Mask and keep-outs: mechanism","text":"遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。","textEn":"Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。 必須排除的錯判：孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遮罩與保護區」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mask and keep-outs — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質","遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。","孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮"],"optionsEn":["Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties","Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices.","Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。 估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。 因此不能採用「孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮」。","explanationEn":"Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices. Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. Therefore reject: Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes."}},{"id":"a121-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-05"],"title":"遮罩與保護區｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Mask and keep-outs | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對遮罩與保護區，把「遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For mask and keep-outs, turn \"Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。 將「孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付遮罩與保護區的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for mask and keep-outs: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-06-k1","title":"遮罩與保護區：機制","titleEn":"Mask and keep-outs: mechanism","text":"遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。","textEn":"Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。 必須排除的錯判：孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「遮罩與保護區」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For mask and keep-outs — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮","共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質","估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes","Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties","Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds."],"answer":2,"explanation":"遮罩要承受深蝕刻且保護附近元件。 估最壞遮罩消耗和對位界限。 因此不能採用「孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮」。","explanationEn":"Masks must survive deep etch while protecting nearby devices. Estimate worst mask loss and overlay bounds. Therefore reject: Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes."}}]},{"id":"a121-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"深矽蝕刻","titleEn":"Deep silicon etch","description":"針對深矽蝕刻完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for deep silicon etch, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a121-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-06"],"title":"深度負載｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Depth loading | mechanism and design","objective":"針對深度負載，把「孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For depth loading, turn \"Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「深度負載」的模型：孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按孔群密度比較深度圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for depth loading: Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare depth maps by via density. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按孔群密度比較深度圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare depth maps by via density. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：固定時間可保證每孔同深。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付深度負載的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for depth loading, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-07-k1","title":"深度負載：機制","titleEn":"Depth loading: mechanism","text":"孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。","textEn":"Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按孔群密度比較深度圖。 必須排除的錯判：固定時間可保證每孔同深。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare depth maps by via density. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「深度負載」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For depth loading — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。","固定時間可保證每孔同深","低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命"],"optionsEn":["Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences.","Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth","Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。 按孔群密度比較深度圖。 因此不能採用「固定時間可保證每孔同深」。","explanationEn":"Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences. Compare depth maps by via density. Therefore reject: Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth."}},{"id":"a121-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-07"],"title":"深度負載｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Depth loading | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對深度負載，把「孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For depth loading, turn \"Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按孔群密度比較深度圖。 將「固定時間可保證每孔同深」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare depth maps by via density. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按孔群密度比較深度圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare depth maps by via density. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：固定時間可保證每孔同深。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付深度負載的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for depth loading: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-08-k1","title":"深度負載：機制","titleEn":"Depth loading: mechanism","text":"孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。","textEn":"Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按孔群密度比較深度圖。 必須排除的錯判：固定時間可保證每孔同深。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare depth maps by via density. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「深度負載」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For depth loading — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命","按孔群密度比較深度圖。","固定時間可保證每孔同深"],"optionsEn":["Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage","Compare depth maps by via density.","Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔密度與深寬比使不同區域蝕刻速率不同。 按孔群密度比較深度圖。 因此不能採用「固定時間可保證每孔同深」。","explanationEn":"Via density and aspect ratio cause spatial etch-rate differences. Compare depth maps by via density. Therefore reject: Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth."}},{"id":"a121-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-08"],"title":"側壁紋路｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Sidewall scallops | mechanism and design","objective":"針對側壁紋路，把「週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sidewall scallops, turn \"Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「側壁紋路」的模型：週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for sidewall scallops: Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付側壁紋路的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for sidewall scallops, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-09-k1","title":"側壁紋路：機制","titleEn":"Sidewall scallops: mechanism","text":"週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。","textEn":"Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。 必須排除的錯判：平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側壁紋路」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sidewall scallops — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻","TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值","週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation","Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value","Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration."],"answer":2,"explanation":"週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。 將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。 因此不能採用「平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻」。","explanationEn":"Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration. Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. Therefore reject: Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation."}},{"id":"a121-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-09"],"title":"側壁紋路｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Sidewall scallops | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對側壁紋路，把「週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For sidewall scallops, turn \"Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。 將「平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付側壁紋路的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for sidewall scallops: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-10-k1","title":"側壁紋路：機制","titleEn":"Sidewall scallops: mechanism","text":"週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。","textEn":"Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。 必須排除的錯判：平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「側壁紋路」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For sidewall scallops — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。","平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻","TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值"],"optionsEn":["Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections.","Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation","Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value"],"answer":0,"explanation":"週期紋路增加有效表面和局部電場集中。 將紋路幅度同後續覆蓋截面對照。 因此不能採用「平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻」。","explanationEn":"Cyclic scallops increase surface area and field concentration. Compare scallop amplitude with coating sections. Therefore reject: Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation."}},{"id":"a121-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-10"],"title":"孔底與轉角｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Bottom and corners | mechanism and design","objective":"針對孔底與轉角，把「孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bottom and corners, turn \"Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「孔底與轉角」的模型：孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for bottom and corners: Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔底與轉角的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for bottom and corners, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-11-k1","title":"孔底與轉角：機制","titleEn":"Bottom and corners: mechanism","text":"孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。","textEn":"Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。 必須排除的錯判：平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. Misinterpretation to reject: Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔底與轉角」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bottom and corners — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區","孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。","平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點"],"optionsEn":["Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes","Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields.","Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。 檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。 因此不能採用「平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點」。","explanationEn":"Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields. Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. Therefore reject: Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots."}},{"id":"a121-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-11"],"title":"孔底與轉角｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Bottom and corners | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對孔底與轉角，把「孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bottom and corners, turn \"Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。 將「平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔底與轉角的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for bottom and corners: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-12-k1","title":"孔底與轉角：機制","titleEn":"Bottom and corners: mechanism","text":"孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。","textEn":"Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。 必須排除的錯判：平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. Misinterpretation to reject: Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔底與轉角」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bottom and corners — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點","孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區","檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。"],"optionsEn":["Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots","Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes","Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔底轉角影響沉積連續與局部場強。 檢查最薄絕緣處而非平均厚度。 因此不能採用「平均膜厚可排除所有擊穿弱點」。","explanationEn":"Bottom corners affect coating continuity and local fields. Inspect thinnest insulation, not the mean. Therefore reject: Using average thickness to exclude breakdown weak spots."}}]},{"id":"a121-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"絕緣界面","titleEn":"Insulating interfaces","description":"針對絕緣界面完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for insulating interfaces, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a121-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-12"],"title":"清潔與表面｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Cleaning and surface | mechanism and design","objective":"針對清潔與表面，把「蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cleaning and surface, turn \"Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「清潔與表面」的模型：蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「配對清潔見證與漏電分布。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for cleaning and surface: Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"配對清潔見證與漏電分布。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付清潔與表面的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for cleaning and surface, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-13-k1","title":"清潔與表面：機制","titleEn":"Cleaning and surface: mechanism","text":"蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。","textEn":"Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對清潔見證與漏電分布。 必須排除的錯判：孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「清潔與表面」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cleaning and surface — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。","孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證","孔深達標即表示可直接填銅"],"optionsEn":["Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces.","Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes","Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu"],"answer":0,"explanation":"蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。 配對清潔見證與漏電分布。 因此不能採用「孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證」。","explanationEn":"Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces. Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. Therefore reject: Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes."}},{"id":"a121-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-13"],"title":"清潔與表面｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Cleaning and surface | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對清潔與表面，把「蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For cleaning and surface, turn \"Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：配對清潔見證與漏電分布。 將「孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"配對清潔見證與漏電分布。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付清潔與表面的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for cleaning and surface: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-14-k1","title":"清潔與表面：機制","titleEn":"Cleaning and surface: mechanism","text":"蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。","textEn":"Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"配對清潔見證與漏電分布。 必須排除的錯判：孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「清潔與表面」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For cleaning and surface — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔深達標即表示可直接填銅","配對清潔見證與漏電分布。","孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證"],"optionsEn":["Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu","Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions.","Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"蝕刻殘留與表面損傷改變介電質界面。 配對清潔見證與漏電分布。 因此不能採用「孔洞幾何合格即不需表面驗證」。","explanationEn":"Etch residue and damage change dielectric interfaces. Pair cleaning witnesses and leakage distributions. Therefore reject: Skipping surface qualification after geometry passes."}},{"id":"a121-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-14"],"title":"絕緣覆蓋｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Insulation coverage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對絕緣覆蓋，把「共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For insulation coverage, turn \"Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「絕緣覆蓋」的模型：共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for insulation coverage: Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付絕緣覆蓋的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for insulation coverage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-15-k1","title":"絕緣覆蓋：機制","titleEn":"Insulation coverage: mechanism","text":"共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。","textEn":"Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。 必須排除的錯判：共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕緣覆蓋」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For insulation coverage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質","所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算","共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。"],"optionsEn":["Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties","Giving every TSV the same thermal budget","Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。 截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。 因此不能採用「共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質」。","explanationEn":"Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias. Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. Therefore reject: Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties."}},{"id":"a121-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-15"],"title":"絕緣覆蓋｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Insulation coverage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對絕緣覆蓋，把「共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For insulation coverage, turn \"Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。 將「共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付絕緣覆蓋的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for insulation coverage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-16-k1","title":"絕緣覆蓋：機制","titleEn":"Insulation coverage: mechanism","text":"共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。","textEn":"Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。 必須排除的錯判：共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕緣覆蓋」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For insulation coverage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。","共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質","所有 TSV 都可用相同熱預算"],"optionsEn":["Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically.","Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties","Giving every TSV the same thermal budget"],"answer":0,"explanation":"共形膜在深孔仍可能有厚度與材料品質梯度。 截面取孔頂、中、底並驗證電性。 因此不能採用「共形沉積名稱即保證全孔相同性質」。","explanationEn":"Conformal films can still vary in thickness/quality down deep vias. Sample top/middle/bottom and verify electrically. Therefore reject: Treating a conformal-process label as proof of uniform properties."}},{"id":"a121-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-16"],"title":"漏電與擊穿｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Leakage and breakdown | mechanism and design","objective":"針對漏電與擊穿，把「漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For leakage and breakdown, turn \"Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「漏電與擊穿」的模型：漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設孔深 50 μm、直徑 5 μm，深寬比 10。理想同軸近似 C≈2π εL/ln(b/a)，a 為導體半徑、b 為外側半徑；真正 TSV 還含半導體耗盡與頻率依賴。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for leakage and breakdown: Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: A 50 μm deep, 5 μm diameter illustrative via has aspect ratio 10. Ideal coaxial C≈2π εL/ln(b/a), with conductor radius a and outer radius b; real TSVs add semiconductor depletion and frequency dependence. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付漏電與擊穿的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for leakage and breakdown, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-17-k1","title":"漏電與擊穿：機制","titleEn":"Leakage and breakdown: mechanism","text":"漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。","textEn":"Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。 必須排除的錯判：低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設孔深 50 μm、直徑 5 μm，深寬比 10。理想同軸近似 C≈2π εL/ln(b/a)，a 為導體半徑、b 為外側半徑；真正 TSV 還含半導體耗盡與頻率依賴。","textEn":"A 50 μm deep, 5 μm diameter illustrative via has aspect ratio 10. Ideal coaxial C≈2π εL/ln(b/a), with conductor radius a and outer radius b; real TSVs add semiconductor depletion and frequency dependence."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漏電與擊穿」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For leakage and breakdown — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV","漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。","低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命"],"optionsEn":["Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter","Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct.","Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage"],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。 規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。 因此不能採用「低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命」。","explanationEn":"Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct. Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. Therefore reject: Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage."}},{"id":"a121-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-17"],"title":"漏電與擊穿｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Leakage and breakdown | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對漏電與擊穿，把「漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For leakage and breakdown, turn \"Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。 將「低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設孔深 50 μm、直徑 5 μm，深寬比 10。理想同軸近似 C≈2π εL/ln(b/a)，a 為導體半徑、b 為外側半徑；真正 TSV 還含半導體耗盡與頻率依賴。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: A 50 μm deep, 5 μm diameter illustrative via has aspect ratio 10. Ideal coaxial C≈2π εL/ln(b/a), with conductor radius a and outer radius b; real TSVs add semiconductor depletion and frequency dependence. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付漏電與擊穿的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for leakage and breakdown: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-18-k1","title":"漏電與擊穿：機制","titleEn":"Leakage and breakdown: mechanism","text":"漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。","textEn":"Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。 必須排除的錯判：低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設孔深 50 μm、直徑 5 μm，深寬比 10。理想同軸近似 C≈2π εL/ln(b/a)，a 為導體半徑、b 為外側半徑；真正 TSV 還含半導體耗盡與頻率依賴。","textEn":"A 50 μm deep, 5 μm diameter illustrative via has aspect ratio 10. Ideal coaxial C≈2π εL/ln(b/a), with conductor radius a and outer radius b; real TSVs add semiconductor depletion and frequency dependence."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漏電與擊穿」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For leakage and breakdown — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命","入口孔徑足以描述整個 TSV","規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。"],"optionsEn":["Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage","Describing a TSV only by its entrance diameter","Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses."],"answer":2,"explanation":"漏電、擊穿及時間退化是不同測量。 規劃電壓、溫度及時間的分離見證。 因此不能採用「低初始漏電即可預測無限壽命」。","explanationEn":"Leakage, breakdown and time-dependent degradation are distinct. Plan separate voltage, temperature and time witnesses. Therefore reject: Inferring unlimited life from low initial leakage."}}]},{"id":"a121-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"測試交接","titleEn":"Test handoff","description":"針對測試交接完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for test handoff, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a121-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-18"],"title":"電容與基板｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Capacitance and substrate | mechanism and design","objective":"針對電容與基板，把「TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For capacitance and substrate, turn \"TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「電容與基板」的模型：TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for capacitance and substrate: TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電容與基板的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for capacitance and substrate, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-19-k1","title":"電容與基板：機制","titleEn":"Capacitance and substrate: mechanism","text":"TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。","textEn":"TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。 必須排除的錯判：TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電容與基板」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For capacitance and substrate — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。","TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值","孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮"],"optionsEn":["TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency.","Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value","Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。 比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。 因此不能採用「TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值」。","explanationEn":"TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency. Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. Therefore reject: Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value."}},{"id":"a121-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-19"],"title":"電容與基板｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Capacitance and substrate | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對電容與基板，把「TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For capacitance and substrate, turn \"TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。 將「TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付電容與基板的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for capacitance and substrate: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-20-k1","title":"電容與基板：機制","titleEn":"Capacitance and substrate: mechanism","text":"TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。","textEn":"TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。 必須排除的錯判：TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電容與基板」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For capacitance and substrate — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔位對準就可忽略遮罩退縮","比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。","TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring mask retreat after alignment passes","Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity.","Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value"],"answer":1,"explanation":"TSV—矽系統可能具有偏壓和頻率依賴。 比較 C–V、頻率與基板電阻率。 因此不能採用「TSV 電容永遠是固定平行板值」。","explanationEn":"TSV–silicon behavior may depend on bias and frequency. Compare C–V, frequency and substrate resistivity. Therefore reject: Treating TSV capacitance as a fixed parallel-plate value."}},{"id":"a121-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-20"],"title":"應力保護區｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Stress keep-out zone | mechanism and design","objective":"針對應力保護區，把「填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stress keep-out zone, turn \"Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「應力保護區」的模型：填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for stress keep-out zone: Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare nearby and remote witness devices. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare nearby and remote witness devices. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付應力保護區的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for stress keep-out zone, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-21-k1","title":"應力保護區：機制","titleEn":"Stress keep-out zone: mechanism","text":"填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。","textEn":"Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。 必須排除的錯判：孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare nearby and remote witness devices. Misinterpretation to reject: Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「應力保護區」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stress keep-out zone — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區","固定時間可保證每孔同深","填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。"],"optionsEn":["Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes","Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth","Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early."],"answer":2,"explanation":"填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。 比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。 因此不能採用「孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區」。","explanationEn":"Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early. Compare nearby and remote witness devices. Therefore reject: Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes."}},{"id":"a121-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-21"],"title":"應力保護區｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Stress keep-out zone | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對應力保護區，把「填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stress keep-out zone, turn \"Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。 將「孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare nearby and remote witness devices. Challenge the hypothesis \"Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare nearby and remote witness devices. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付應力保護區的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for stress keep-out zone: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-22-k1","title":"應力保護區：機制","titleEn":"Stress keep-out zone: mechanism","text":"填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。","textEn":"Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。 必須排除的錯判：孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare nearby and remote witness devices. Misinterpretation to reject: Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「應力保護區」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stress keep-out zone — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。","孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區","固定時間可保證每孔同深"],"optionsEn":["Compare nearby and remote witness devices.","Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes","Assuming fixed time ensures equal depth"],"answer":0,"explanation":"填銅後熱失配可影響周邊元件，孔洞設計須提前保留區。 比較鄰近與遠端見證元件。 因此不能採用「孔外絕緣良好即可取消應力保護區」。","explanationEn":"Post-fill mismatch can affect nearby devices; reserve space early. Compare nearby and remote witness devices. Therefore reject: Removing stress keep-outs after insulation passes."}},{"id":"a121-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-22"],"title":"金屬化交接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Metallization handoff | mechanism and design","objective":"針對金屬化交接，把「填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For metallization handoff, turn \"Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「金屬化交接」的模型：填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for metallization handoff: Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔深達標即表示可直接填銅。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付金屬化交接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for metallization handoff, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-23-k1","title":"金屬化交接：機制","titleEn":"Metallization handoff: mechanism","text":"填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。","textEn":"Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。 必須排除的錯判：孔深達標即表示可直接填銅。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「金屬化交接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For metallization handoff — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻","填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。","孔深達標即表示可直接填銅"],"optionsEn":["Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation","Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation.","Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu"],"answer":1,"explanation":"填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。 提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。 因此不能採用「孔深達標即表示可直接填銅」。","explanationEn":"Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation. Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. Therefore reject: Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu."}},{"id":"a121-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"],"prerequisiteIds":["a121-v9-23"],"title":"金屬化交接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Metallization handoff | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對金屬化交接，把「填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For metallization handoff, turn \"Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。 將「孔深達標即表示可直接填銅」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔深達標即表示可直接填銅。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付金屬化交接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for metallization handoff: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a121-v9-24-k1","title":"金屬化交接：機制","titleEn":"Metallization handoff: mechanism","text":"填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。","textEn":"Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]},{"id":"a121-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。 必須排除的錯判：孔深達標即表示可直接填銅。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v8b-drie","v9a-imec3d"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「金屬化交接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For metallization handoff — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔深達標即表示可直接填銅","平均側壁角垂直即絕緣必均勻","提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu","Assuming vertical mean angle ensures uniform insulation","Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps."],"answer":2,"explanation":"填充需要可覆蓋孔形、潔淨表面及已驗證絕緣。 提交孔形與漏電共同地圖。 因此不能採用「孔深達標即表示可直接填銅」。","explanationEn":"Filling requires coatable geometry, clean surfaces and qualified insulation. Deliver paired geometry/leakage maps. Therefore reject: Assuming target depth alone makes vias ready for Cu."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-vias","subcategoryTitle":"穿孔與金屬互連","subcategoryTitleEn":"Through vias and metal interconnects","photoId":"v8-drie-failure"},{"id":"a122","title":"矽穿孔金屬填充","titleEn":"Through-silicon-via metal filling","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入阻障種子、成長前沿與空洞。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore barrier/seed, growth fronts and voids, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["材料與孔形","阻障與種子","金屬填充","應力與電性"],"labelsEn":["Materials and geometry","Barrier and seed","Metal filling","Stress and electrical"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a122-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"材料與孔形","titleEn":"Materials and geometry","description":"針對材料與孔形完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for materials and geometry, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a122-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"導體選擇｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Conductor selection | mechanism and design","objective":"針對導體選擇，把「Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For conductor selection, turn \"Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「導體選擇」的模型：Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for conductor selection: Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare resistance and stress objectives. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare resistance and stress objectives. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming lowest resistivity is always best. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付導體選擇的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for conductor selection, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-01-k1","title":"導體選擇：機制","titleEn":"Conductor selection: mechanism","text":"Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。","textEn":"Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。 必須排除的錯判：最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare resistance and stress objectives. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming lowest resistivity is always best. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導體選擇」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For conductor selection — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。","最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇","總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌"],"optionsEn":["Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch.","Assuming lowest resistivity is always best","Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。 比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。 因此不能採用「最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇」。","explanationEn":"Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch. Compare resistance and stress objectives. Therefore reject: Assuming lowest resistivity is always best."}},{"id":"a122-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-01"],"title":"導體選擇｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Conductor selection | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對導體選擇，把「Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For conductor selection, turn \"Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。 將「最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare resistance and stress objectives. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming lowest resistivity is always best\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare resistance and stress objectives. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming lowest resistivity is always best. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付導體選擇的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for conductor selection: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-02-k1","title":"導體選擇：機制","titleEn":"Conductor selection: mechanism","text":"Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。","textEn":"Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。 必須排除的錯判：最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare resistance and stress objectives. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming lowest resistivity is always best. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導體選擇」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For conductor selection — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌","比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。","最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇"],"optionsEn":["Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology","Compare resistance and stress objectives.","Assuming lowest resistivity is always best"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Cu 與 W 的電阻、成膜方式和热失配不同。 比較電阻與應力的雙目標表。 因此不能採用「最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇」。","explanationEn":"Cu and W differ in resistivity, deposition and thermal mismatch. Compare resistance and stress objectives. Therefore reject: Assuming lowest resistivity is always best."}},{"id":"a122-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-02"],"title":"孔形來料｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Incoming geometry | mechanism and design","objective":"針對孔形來料，把「再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For incoming geometry, turn \"Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「孔形來料」的模型：再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量孔口收縮及全深度截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for incoming geometry: Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量孔口收縮及全深度截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔形來料的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for incoming geometry, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-03-k1","title":"孔形來料：機制","titleEn":"Incoming geometry: mechanism","text":"再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。","textEn":"Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量孔口收縮及全深度截面。 必須排除的錯判：孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔形來料」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For incoming geometry — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿","流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同","再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill","Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport","Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids."],"answer":2,"explanation":"再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。 量孔口收縮及全深度截面。 因此不能採用「孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿」。","explanationEn":"Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids. Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. Therefore reject: Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill."}},{"id":"a122-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-03"],"title":"孔形來料｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Incoming geometry | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對孔形來料，把「再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For incoming geometry, turn \"Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量孔口收縮及全深度截面。 將「孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量孔口收縮及全深度截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔形來料的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for incoming geometry: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-04-k1","title":"孔形來料：機制","titleEn":"Incoming geometry: mechanism","text":"再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。","textEn":"Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量孔口收縮及全深度截面。 必須排除的錯判：孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔形來料」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For incoming geometry — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["量孔口收縮及全深度截面。","孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿","流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同"],"optionsEn":["Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile.","Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill","Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport"],"answer":0,"explanation":"再入形孔口可能先封閉而困住內部空洞。 量孔口收縮及全深度截面。 因此不能採用「孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿」。","explanationEn":"Reentrant mouths can close early and trap voids. Measure mouth constriction and full-depth profile. Therefore reject: Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill."}},{"id":"a122-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-04"],"title":"擴散阻障｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Diffusion barrier | mechanism and design","objective":"針對擴散阻障，把「阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For diffusion barrier, turn \"Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「擴散阻障」的模型：阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for diffusion barrier: Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付擴散阻障的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for diffusion barrier, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-05-k1","title":"擴散阻障：機制","titleEn":"Diffusion barrier: mechanism","text":"阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。","textEn":"Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。 必須排除的錯判：阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「擴散阻障」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For diffusion barrier — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化","阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。","阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free","Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact.","Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost"],"answer":1,"explanation":"阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。 比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。 因此不能採用「阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度」。","explanationEn":"Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact. Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. Therefore reject: Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost."}},{"id":"a122-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-05"],"title":"擴散阻障｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Diffusion barrier | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對擴散阻障，把「阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For diffusion barrier, turn \"Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。 將「阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付擴散阻障的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for diffusion barrier: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-06-k1","title":"擴散阻障：機制","titleEn":"Diffusion barrier: mechanism","text":"阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。","textEn":"Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。 必須排除的錯判：阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「擴散阻障」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For diffusion barrier — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度","表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化","比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost","Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free","Compare continuity, thickness and resistance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"阻障需阻擋金屬進入介電質或矽，同時維持接觸。 比較連續性、厚度和接觸電阻。 因此不能採用「阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度」。","explanationEn":"Barriers must block metal diffusion while preserving contact. Compare continuity, thickness and resistance. Therefore reject: Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost."}}]},{"id":"a122-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"阻障與種子","titleEn":"Barrier and seed","description":"針對阻障與種子完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for barrier and seed, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a122-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-06"],"title":"種子連通｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Seed connectivity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對種子連通，把「深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed connectivity, turn \"Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「種子連通」的模型：深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for seed connectivity: Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面種子導通即孔底也連通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子連通的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for seed connectivity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-07-k1","title":"種子連通：機制","titleEn":"Seed connectivity: mechanism","text":"深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。","textEn":"Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。 必須排除的錯判：表面種子導通即孔底也連通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子連通」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed connectivity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。","表面種子導通即孔底也連通","銅填滿後幾何永遠固定"],"optionsEn":["Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating.","Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity","Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。 將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。 因此不能採用「表面種子導通即孔底也連通」。","explanationEn":"Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating. Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. Therefore reject: Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity."}},{"id":"a122-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-07"],"title":"種子連通｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Seed connectivity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對種子連通，把「深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed connectivity, turn \"Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。 將「表面種子導通即孔底也連通」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面種子導通即孔底也連通。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子連通的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for seed connectivity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-08-k1","title":"種子連通：機制","titleEn":"Seed connectivity: mechanism","text":"深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。","textEn":"Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。 必須排除的錯判：表面種子導通即孔底也連通。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子連通」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed connectivity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["銅填滿後幾何永遠固定","將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。","表面種子導通即孔底也連通"],"optionsEn":["Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes","Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections.","Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"深孔種子不連續會使局部無法電鍍。 將片阻和孔底截面合併判讀。 因此不能採用「表面種子導通即孔底也連通」。","explanationEn":"Discontinuous deep seed prevents local plating. Combine sheet resistance and bottom sections. Therefore reject: Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity."}},{"id":"a122-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-08"],"title":"潤濕與氣泡｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Wetting and bubbles | mechanism and design","objective":"針對潤濕與氣泡，把「被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For wetting and bubbles, turn \"Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「潤濕與氣泡」的模型：被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較空洞形狀和分布高度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for wetting and bubbles: Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare void shape and height distribution. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較空洞形狀和分布高度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare void shape and height distribution. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing every void to low plating current. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付潤濕與氣泡的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for wetting and bubbles, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-09-k1","title":"潤濕與氣泡：機制","titleEn":"Wetting and bubbles: mechanism","text":"被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。","textEn":"Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較空洞形狀和分布高度。 必須排除的錯判：所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare void shape and height distribution. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing every void to low plating current. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潤濕與氣泡」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For wetting and bubbles — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成","低電阻即可免除空洞檢測","被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every void to low plating current","Skipping void inspection after low resistance","Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids."],"answer":2,"explanation":"被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。 比較空洞形狀和分布高度。 因此不能採用「所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成」。","explanationEn":"Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids. Compare void shape and height distribution. Therefore reject: Attributing every void to low plating current."}},{"id":"a122-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-09"],"title":"潤濕與氣泡｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Wetting and bubbles | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對潤濕與氣泡，把「被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For wetting and bubbles, turn \"Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較空洞形狀和分布高度。 將「所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare void shape and height distribution. Challenge the hypothesis \"Attributing every void to low plating current\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較空洞形狀和分布高度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare void shape and height distribution. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Attributing every void to low plating current. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付潤濕與氣泡的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for wetting and bubbles: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-10-k1","title":"潤濕與氣泡：機制","titleEn":"Wetting and bubbles: mechanism","text":"被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。","textEn":"Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較空洞形狀和分布高度。 必須排除的錯判：所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare void shape and height distribution. Misinterpretation to reject: Attributing every void to low plating current. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潤濕與氣泡」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For wetting and bubbles — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較空洞形狀和分布高度。","所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成","低電阻即可免除空洞檢測"],"optionsEn":["Compare void shape and height distribution.","Attributing every void to low plating current","Skipping void inspection after low resistance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"被困氣體阻斷局部沉積，與後期封口空洞有不同位置特徵。 比較空洞形狀和分布高度。 因此不能採用「所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成」。","explanationEn":"Trapped gas blocks deposition and differs from late pinch-off voids. Compare void shape and height distribution. Therefore reject: Attributing every void to low plating current."}},{"id":"a122-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-10"],"title":"底部優先成長｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Bottom-up growth | mechanism and design","objective":"針對底部優先成長，把「填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bottom-up growth, turn \"Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「底部優先成長」的模型：填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for bottom-up growth: Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付底部優先成長的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for bottom-up growth, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-11-k1","title":"底部優先成長：機制","titleEn":"Bottom-up growth: mechanism","text":"填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。","textEn":"Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。 必須排除的錯判：總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「底部優先成長」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bottom-up growth — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性","填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。","總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌"],"optionsEn":["Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics","Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter.","Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology"],"answer":1,"explanation":"填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。 重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。 因此不能採用「總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌」。","explanationEn":"Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter. Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. Therefore reject: Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology."}},{"id":"a122-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-11"],"title":"底部優先成長｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Bottom-up growth | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對底部優先成長，把「填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bottom-up growth, turn \"Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。 將「總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付底部優先成長的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for bottom-up growth: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-12-k1","title":"底部優先成長：機制","titleEn":"Bottom-up growth: mechanism","text":"填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。","textEn":"Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。 必須排除的錯判：總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「底部優先成長」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bottom-up growth — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌","空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性","重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。"],"optionsEn":["Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology","Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics","Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"填充前沿需要避免上部提前封口，局部成長速度是關鍵。 重建多個中間截面的前沿演化。 因此不能採用「總沉積量相同即可保證相同填充形貌」。","explanationEn":"Growth fronts must avoid early mouth closure; local rates matter. Reconstruct fronts from intermediate sections. Therefore reject: Equating total deposited mass with fill morphology."}}]},{"id":"a122-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"金屬填充","titleEn":"Metal filling","description":"針對金屬填充完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for metal filling, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a122-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-12"],"title":"傳質與圖形｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Transport and pattern | mechanism and design","objective":"針對傳質與圖形，把「孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For transport and pattern, turn \"Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「傳質與圖形」的模型：孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按密度區比較空洞與厚度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for transport and pattern: Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare voids/thickness by density region. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按密度區比較空洞與厚度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare voids/thickness by density region. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付傳質與圖形的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for transport and pattern, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-13-k1","title":"傳質與圖形：機制","titleEn":"Transport and pattern: mechanism","text":"孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。","textEn":"Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按密度區比較空洞與厚度。 必須排除的錯判：流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare voids/thickness by density region. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「傳質與圖形」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For transport and pattern — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。","流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同","只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質"],"optionsEn":["Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply.","Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport","Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。 按密度區比較空洞與厚度。 因此不能採用「流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同」。","explanationEn":"Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply. Compare voids/thickness by density region. Therefore reject: Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport."}},{"id":"a122-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-13"],"title":"傳質與圖形｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Transport and pattern | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對傳質與圖形，把「孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For transport and pattern, turn \"Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按密度區比較空洞與厚度。 將「流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare voids/thickness by density region. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按密度區比較空洞與厚度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare voids/thickness by density region. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付傳質與圖形的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for transport and pattern: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-14-k1","title":"傳質與圖形：機制","titleEn":"Transport and pattern: mechanism","text":"孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。","textEn":"Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按密度區比較空洞與厚度。 必須排除的錯判：流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare voids/thickness by density region. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「傳質與圖形」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For transport and pattern — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質","按密度區比較空洞與厚度。","流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同"],"optionsEn":["Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends","Compare voids/thickness by density region.","Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔密度、流場和深度影響有效反應物供應。 按密度區比較空洞與厚度。 因此不能採用「流場均勻就代表所有孔內傳質相同」。","explanationEn":"Density, flow and depth affect reactant supply. Compare voids/thickness by density region. Therefore reject: Equating uniform bulk flow with equal in-via transport."}},{"id":"a122-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-14"],"title":"過鍍與平坦化｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Overburden and planarization | mechanism and design","objective":"針對過鍍與平坦化，把「表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overburden and planarization, turn \"Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「過鍍與平坦化」的模型：表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for overburden and planarization: Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Budget removal, dishing and residue. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Budget removal, dishing and residue. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付過鍍與平坦化的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for overburden and planarization, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-15-k1","title":"過鍍與平坦化：機制","titleEn":"Overburden and planarization: mechanism","text":"表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。","textEn":"Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。 必須排除的錯判：表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Budget removal, dishing and residue. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「過鍍與平坦化」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overburden and planarization — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化","最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇","表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free","Assuming lowest resistivity is always best","Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。 列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。 因此不能採用「表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化」。","explanationEn":"Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste. Budget removal, dishing and residue. Therefore reject: Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free."}},{"id":"a122-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-15"],"title":"過鍍與平坦化｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Overburden and planarization | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對過鍍與平坦化，把「表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For overburden and planarization, turn \"Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。 將「表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Budget removal, dishing and residue. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Budget removal, dishing and residue. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付過鍍與平坦化的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for overburden and planarization: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-16-k1","title":"過鍍與平坦化：機制","titleEn":"Overburden and planarization: mechanism","text":"表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。","textEn":"Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。 必須排除的錯判：表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Budget removal, dishing and residue. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「過鍍與平坦化」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For overburden and planarization — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。","表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化","最低電阻材料必是每種 TSV 最佳選擇"],"optionsEn":["Budget removal, dishing and residue.","Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free","Assuming lowest resistivity is always best"],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面金屬留量須足夠平坦化又限制應力與材料耗損。 列去除量、凹陷和殘留預算。 因此不能採用「表面越厚越容易且無風險平坦化」。","explanationEn":"Overburden must enable planarization while limiting stress/waste. Budget removal, dishing and residue. Therefore reject: Assuming thicker overburden makes planarization risk-free."}},{"id":"a122-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-16"],"title":"熱處理與突出｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal treatment and protrusion | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱處理與突出，把「金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal treatment and protrusion, turn \"Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱處理與突出」的模型：金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量熱前後高度與周邊應變。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設直徑 5 μm、長 50 μm 的理想銅 TSV，ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈43.3 mΩ。截面有效面積若因空洞減少 20%，均勻模型 R 增至約54.1 mΩ；真實空洞還有電流集中。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal treatment and protrusion: Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: An ideal 5 μm diameter, 50 μm long Cu TSV at ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m has R≈43.3 mΩ. A uniform 20% area loss gives≈54.1 mΩ, before real void current crowding. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"量熱前後高度與周邊應變。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：銅填滿後幾何永遠固定。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱處理與突出的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal treatment and protrusion, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-17-k1","title":"熱處理與突出：機制","titleEn":"Thermal treatment and protrusion: mechanism","text":"金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。","textEn":"Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量熱前後高度與周邊應變。 必須排除的錯判：銅填滿後幾何永遠固定。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設直徑 5 μm、長 50 μm 的理想銅 TSV，ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈43.3 mΩ。截面有效面積若因空洞減少 20%，均勻模型 R 增至約54.1 mΩ；真實空洞還有電流集中。","textEn":"An ideal 5 μm diameter, 50 μm long Cu TSV at ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m has R≈43.3 mΩ. A uniform 20% area loss gives≈54.1 mΩ, before real void current crowding."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱處理與突出」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal treatment and protrusion — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿","金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。","銅填滿後幾何永遠固定"],"optionsEn":["Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill","Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution.","Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。 量熱前後高度與周邊應變。 因此不能採用「銅填滿後幾何永遠固定」。","explanationEn":"Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution. Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. Therefore reject: Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes."}},{"id":"a122-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-17"],"title":"熱處理與突出｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal treatment and protrusion | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱處理與突出，把「金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal treatment and protrusion, turn \"Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量熱前後高度與周邊應變。 將「銅填滿後幾何永遠固定」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設直徑 5 μm、長 50 μm 的理想銅 TSV，ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈43.3 mΩ。截面有效面積若因空洞減少 20%，均勻模型 R 增至約54.1 mΩ；真實空洞還有電流集中。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: An ideal 5 μm diameter, 50 μm long Cu TSV at ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m has R≈43.3 mΩ. A uniform 20% area loss gives≈54.1 mΩ, before real void current crowding. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"量熱前後高度與周邊應變。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：銅填滿後幾何永遠固定。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱處理與突出的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal treatment and protrusion: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-18-k1","title":"熱處理與突出：機制","titleEn":"Thermal treatment and protrusion: mechanism","text":"金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。","textEn":"Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量熱前後高度與周邊應變。 必須排除的錯判：銅填滿後幾何永遠固定。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設直徑 5 μm、長 50 μm 的理想銅 TSV，ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m，R≈43.3 mΩ。截面有效面積若因空洞減少 20%，均勻模型 R 增至約54.1 mΩ；真實空洞還有電流集中。","textEn":"An ideal 5 μm diameter, 50 μm long Cu TSV at ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ω·m has R≈43.3 mΩ. A uniform 20% area loss gives≈54.1 mΩ, before real void current crowding."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱處理與突出」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal treatment and protrusion — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["銅填滿後幾何永遠固定","孔口越窄越容易無空洞填滿","量熱前後高度與周邊應變。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes","Assuming narrower mouths facilitate void-free fill","Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain."],"answer":2,"explanation":"金屬微結構和 CTE 失配可使 TSV 突出或應力重分布。 量熱前後高度與周邊應變。 因此不能採用「銅填滿後幾何永遠固定」。","explanationEn":"Microstructure and CTE mismatch can cause protrusion or stress redistribution. Measure pre/post-thermal height and nearby strain. Therefore reject: Assuming filled Cu geometry never changes."}}]},{"id":"a122-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"應力與電性","titleEn":"Stress and electrical","description":"針對應力與電性完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for stress and electrical, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a122-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-18"],"title":"四端電測｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Four-terminal testing | mechanism and design","objective":"針對四端電測，把「實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For four-terminal testing, turn \"Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「四端電測」的模型：實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for four-terminal testing: Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：低電阻即可免除空洞檢測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping void inspection after low resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付四端電測的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for four-terminal testing, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-19-k1","title":"四端電測：機制","titleEn":"Four-terminal testing: mechanism","text":"實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。","textEn":"Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。 必須排除的錯判：低電阻即可免除空洞檢測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping void inspection after low resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「四端電測」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For four-terminal testing — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。","低電阻即可免除空洞檢測","阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度"],"optionsEn":["Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids.","Skipping void inspection after low resistance","Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost"],"answer":0,"explanation":"實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。 將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。 因此不能採用「低電阻即可免除空洞檢測」。","explanationEn":"Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids. Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. Therefore reject: Skipping void inspection after low resistance."}},{"id":"a122-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-19"],"title":"四端電測｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Four-terminal testing | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對四端電測，把「實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For four-terminal testing, turn \"Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。 將「低電阻即可免除空洞檢測」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. Challenge the hypothesis \"Skipping void inspection after low resistance\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：低電阻即可免除空洞檢測。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Skipping void inspection after low resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付四端電測的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for four-terminal testing: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-20-k1","title":"四端電測：機制","titleEn":"Four-terminal testing: mechanism","text":"實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。","textEn":"Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。 必須排除的錯判：低電阻即可免除空洞檢測。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. Misinterpretation to reject: Skipping void inspection after low resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「四端電測」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For four-terminal testing — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["阻障越厚越能無代價提高可靠度","將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。","低電阻即可免除空洞檢測"],"optionsEn":["Assuming thicker barriers improve reliability without cost","Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images.","Skipping void inspection after low resistance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"實測電阻包含端點與有效截面，低阻並不排除小空洞。 將 Kelvin 結果和非破壞影像對照。 因此不能採用「低電阻即可免除空洞檢測」。","explanationEn":"Resistance includes terminations/area; low resistance does not exclude small voids. Compare Kelvin results and nondestructive images. Therefore reject: Skipping void inspection after low resistance."}},{"id":"a122-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-20"],"title":"熱機耦合｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermomechanical coupling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱機耦合，把「局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermomechanical coupling, turn \"Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱機耦合」的模型：局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermomechanical coupling: Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱機耦合的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermomechanical coupling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-21-k1","title":"熱機耦合：機制","titleEn":"Thermomechanical coupling: mechanism","text":"局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。","textEn":"Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。 必須排除的錯判：空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱機耦合」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermomechanical coupling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性","表面種子導通即孔底也連通","局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics","Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity","Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。 對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。 因此不能採用「空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性」。","explanationEn":"Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress. Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. Therefore reject: Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics."}},{"id":"a122-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-21"],"title":"熱機耦合｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermomechanical coupling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱機耦合，把「局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermomechanical coupling, turn \"Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。 將「空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱機耦合的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermomechanical coupling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-22-k1","title":"熱機耦合：機制","titleEn":"Thermomechanical coupling: mechanism","text":"局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。","textEn":"Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。 必須排除的錯判：空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱機耦合」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermomechanical coupling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。","空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性","表面種子導通即孔底也連通"],"optionsEn":["Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations.","Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics","Inferring bottom continuity from surface conductivity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"局部空洞和剛性梯度使應力集中。 對照裂紋、空洞及熱循環位置。 因此不能採用「空洞只影響電阻不影響機械性」。","explanationEn":"Voids and stiffness gradients concentrate stress. Correlate cracks, voids and cycling locations. Therefore reject: Assuming voids affect resistance but not mechanics."}},{"id":"a122-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-22"],"title":"放行與露出｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Release to reveal | mechanism and design","objective":"針對放行與露出，把「填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For release to reveal, turn \"Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「放行與露出」的模型：填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for release to reveal: Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付放行與露出的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for release to reveal, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-23-k1","title":"放行與露出：機制","titleEn":"Release to reveal: mechanism","text":"填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。","textEn":"Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。 必須排除的錯判：只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. Misinterpretation to reject: Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「放行與露出」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For release to reveal — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成","填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。","只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質"],"optionsEn":["Attributing every void to low plating current","Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region.","Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends"],"answer":1,"explanation":"填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。 交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。 因此不能採用「只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質」。","explanationEn":"Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region. Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. Therefore reject: Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends."}},{"id":"a122-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a122-v9-23"],"title":"放行與露出｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Release to reveal | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對放行與露出，把「填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For release to reveal, turn \"Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。 將「只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付放行與露出的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for release to reveal: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a122-v9-24-k1","title":"放行與露出：機制","titleEn":"Release to reveal: mechanism","text":"填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。","textEn":"Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a122-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。 必須排除的錯判：只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. Misinterpretation to reject: Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["pk-atotech-semiconductor","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「放行與露出」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For release to reveal — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質","所有空洞都由電鍍電流過小造成","交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。"],"optionsEn":["Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends","Attributing every void to low plating current","Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds."],"answer":2,"explanation":"填充驗收需包含孔口、孔底及將被露出的區域。 交付深度對位圖與缺陷界限。 因此不能採用「只截孔中部即可代表露出端品質」。","explanationEn":"Qualify mouth, bottom and future reveal region. Deliver depth-registered maps and defect bounds. Therefore reject: Using only mid-via sections to qualify reveal ends."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-vias","subcategoryTitle":"穿孔與金屬互連","subcategoryTitleEn":"Through vias and metal interconnects","photoId":"v9-quilt-solder"},{"id":"a123","title":"矽穿孔背面露出","titleEn":"Through-silicon-via backside reveal","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入薄化終點、選擇比與露出均勻性。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore thinning endpoint, selectivity and reveal uniformity, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["深度與支撐","接近 TSV","選擇性露出","背面連接"],"labelsEn":["Depth and support","Approach TSVs","Selective reveal","Backside connection"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a123-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"深度與支撐","titleEn":"Depth and support","description":"針對深度與支撐完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for depth and support, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a123-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"深度座標｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Depth coordinates | mechanism and design","objective":"針對深度座標，把「TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For depth coordinates, turn \"TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「深度座標」的模型：TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「統一圖面和量測零點。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for depth coordinates: TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Unify design and metrology zero references. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"統一圖面和量測零點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Unify design and metrology zero references. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Subtracting depths without checking datums. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付深度座標的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for depth coordinates, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-01-k1","title":"深度座標：機制","titleEn":"Depth coordinates: mechanism","text":"TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。","textEn":"TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"統一圖面和量測零點。 必須排除的錯判：兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Unify design and metrology zero references. Misinterpretation to reject: Subtracting depths without checking datums. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「深度座標」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For depth coordinates — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。","兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準","高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比"],"optionsEn":["TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum.","Subtracting depths without checking datums","Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。 統一圖面和量測零點。 因此不能採用「兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準」。","explanationEn":"TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum. Unify design and metrology zero references. Therefore reject: Subtracting depths without checking datums."}},{"id":"a123-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-01"],"title":"深度座標｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Depth coordinates | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對深度座標，把「TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For depth coordinates, turn \"TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：統一圖面和量測零點。 將「兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Unify design and metrology zero references. Challenge the hypothesis \"Subtracting depths without checking datums\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"統一圖面和量測零點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Unify design and metrology zero references. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Subtracting depths without checking datums. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付深度座標的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for depth coordinates: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-02-k1","title":"深度座標：機制","titleEn":"Depth coordinates: mechanism","text":"TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。","textEn":"TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"統一圖面和量測零點。 必須排除的錯判：兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Unify design and metrology zero references. Misinterpretation to reject: Subtracting depths without checking datums. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「深度座標」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For depth coordinates — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比","統一圖面和量測零點。","兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準"],"optionsEn":["Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity","Unify design and metrology zero references.","Subtracting depths without checking datums"],"answer":1,"explanation":"TSV 深度與背面厚度必須共用原始正面基準。 統一圖面和量測零點。 因此不能採用「兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準」。","explanationEn":"TSV depth and backside thickness need a common frontside datum. Unify design and metrology zero references. Therefore reject: Subtracting depths without checking datums."}},{"id":"a123-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-02"],"title":"來料 TTV｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Incoming TTV | mechanism and design","objective":"針對來料 TTV，把「全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For incoming ttv, turn \"Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「來料 TTV」的模型：全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for incoming ttv: Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Register TTV and via-depth maps. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register TTV and via-depth maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付來料 TTV的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for incoming ttv, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-03-k1","title":"來料 TTV：機制","titleEn":"Incoming TTV: mechanism","text":"全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。","textEn":"Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。 必須排除的錯判：平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register TTV and via-depth maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「來料 TTV」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For incoming ttv — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出","全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成","全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。"],"optionsEn":["Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal","Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal","Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites."],"answer":2,"explanation":"全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。 將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。 因此不能採用「平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出」。","explanationEn":"Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites. Register TTV and via-depth maps. Therefore reject: Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal."}},{"id":"a123-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-03"],"title":"來料 TTV｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Incoming TTV | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對來料 TTV，把「全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For incoming ttv, turn \"Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。 將「平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Register TTV and via-depth maps. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Register TTV and via-depth maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付來料 TTV的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for incoming ttv: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-04-k1","title":"來料 TTV：機制","titleEn":"Incoming TTV: mechanism","text":"全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。","textEn":"Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。 必須排除的錯判：平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Register TTV and via-depth maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「來料 TTV」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For incoming ttv — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。","平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出","全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成"],"optionsEn":["Register TTV and via-depth maps.","Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal","Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal"],"answer":0,"explanation":"全片厚度分布決定最早和最晚露出區。 將 TTV 與 TSV 深度地圖配準。 因此不能採用「平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出」。","explanationEn":"Thickness distribution determines earliest/latest reveal sites. Register TTV and via-depth maps. Therefore reject: Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal."}},{"id":"a123-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-04"],"title":"載板支撐｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Carrier support | mechanism and design","objective":"針對載板支撐，把「背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier support, turn \"Frontside support carries backside loads without shift.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「載板支撐」的模型：背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for carrier support: Frontside support carries backside loads without shift. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：載板剛性高即可忽略膠層。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板支撐的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for carrier support, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-05-k1","title":"載板支撐：機制","titleEn":"Carrier support: mechanism","text":"背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。","textEn":"Frontside support carries backside loads without shift.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。 必須排除的錯判：載板剛性高即可忽略膠層。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板支撐」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier support — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均突出高度可代表所有接點","背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。","載板剛性高即可忽略膠層"],"optionsEn":["Using mean protrusion for every contact","Frontside support carries backside loads without shift.","Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff"],"answer":1,"explanation":"背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。 檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。 因此不能採用「載板剛性高即可忽略膠層」。","explanationEn":"Frontside support carries backside loads without shift. Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. Therefore reject: Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff."}},{"id":"a123-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-05"],"title":"載板支撐｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Carrier support | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對載板支撐，把「背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For carrier support, turn \"Frontside support carries backside loads without shift.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。 將「載板剛性高即可忽略膠層」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：載板剛性高即可忽略膠層。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付載板支撐的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for carrier support: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-06-k1","title":"載板支撐：機制","titleEn":"Carrier support: mechanism","text":"背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。","textEn":"Frontside support carries backside loads without shift.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。 必須排除的錯判：載板剛性高即可忽略膠層。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「載板支撐」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For carrier support — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["載板剛性高即可忽略膠層","平均突出高度可代表所有接點","檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff","Using mean protrusion for every contact","Inspect adhesive voids and displacement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"背面加工載荷需由前側支撐承受且避免位移。 檢查膠層空洞及前後位移。 因此不能採用「載板剛性高即可忽略膠層」。","explanationEn":"Frontside support carries backside loads without shift. Inspect adhesive voids and displacement. Therefore reject: Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff."}}]},{"id":"a123-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"接近 TSV","titleEn":"Approach TSVs","description":"針對接近 TSV完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for approach tsvs, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a123-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-06"],"title":"研磨接近｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Grinding approach | mechanism and design","objective":"針對研磨接近，把「大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For grinding approach, turn \"Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「研磨接近」的模型：大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立最壞厚度與停止界限。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for grinding approach: Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立最壞厚度與停止界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付研磨接近的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for grinding approach, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-07-k1","title":"研磨接近：機制","titleEn":"Grinding approach: mechanism","text":"大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。","textEn":"Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立最壞厚度與停止界限。 必須排除的錯判：只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. Misinterpretation to reject: Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「研磨接近」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For grinding approach — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。","只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV","金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣"],"optionsEn":["Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal.","Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone","Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation"],"answer":0,"explanation":"大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。 建立最壞厚度與停止界限。 因此不能採用「只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV」。","explanationEn":"Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal. Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. Therefore reject: Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone."}},{"id":"a123-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-07"],"title":"研磨接近｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Grinding approach | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對研磨接近，把「大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For grinding approach, turn \"Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立最壞厚度與停止界限。 將「只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. Challenge the hypothesis \"Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立最壞厚度與停止界限。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付研磨接近的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for grinding approach: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-08-k1","title":"研磨接近：機制","titleEn":"Grinding approach: mechanism","text":"大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。","textEn":"Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立最壞厚度與停止界限。 必須排除的錯判：只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. Misinterpretation to reject: Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「研磨接近」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For grinding approach — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣","建立最壞厚度與停止界限。","只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV"],"optionsEn":["Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation","Define worst thickness and stop boundaries.","Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone"],"answer":1,"explanation":"大量移除應在碰到敏感金屬前保留可控餘量。 建立最壞厚度與停止界限。 因此不能採用「只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV」。","explanationEn":"Bulk removal needs controllable allowance before sensitive metal. Define worst thickness and stop boundaries. Therefore reject: Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone."}},{"id":"a123-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-08"],"title":"損傷層去除｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Damage removal | mechanism and design","objective":"針對損傷層去除，把「背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For damage removal, turn \"Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「損傷層去除」的模型：背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for damage removal: Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：露出金屬後損傷自然不重要。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付損傷層去除的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for damage removal, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-09-k1","title":"損傷層去除：機制","titleEn":"Damage removal: mechanism","text":"背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。","textEn":"Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。 必須排除的錯判：露出金屬後損傷自然不重要。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「損傷層去除」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For damage removal — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["露出金屬後損傷自然不重要","露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸","背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure","Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape","Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength."],"answer":2,"explanation":"背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。 比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。 因此不能採用「露出金屬後損傷自然不重要」。","explanationEn":"Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength. Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. Therefore reject: Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure."}},{"id":"a123-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-09"],"title":"損傷層去除｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Damage removal | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對損傷層去除，把「背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For damage removal, turn \"Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。 將「露出金屬後損傷自然不重要」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：露出金屬後損傷自然不重要。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付損傷層去除的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for damage removal: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-10-k1","title":"損傷層去除：機制","titleEn":"Damage removal: mechanism","text":"背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。","textEn":"Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。 必須排除的錯判：露出金屬後損傷自然不重要。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「損傷層去除」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For damage removal — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。","露出金屬後損傷自然不重要","露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸"],"optionsEn":["Compare damage depth and remaining allowance.","Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure","Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape"],"answer":0,"explanation":"背面損傷影響後續蝕刻均勻與機械強度。 比较損傷深度與剩餘留量。 因此不能採用「露出金屬後損傷自然不重要」。","explanationEn":"Backside damage affects etch uniformity and strength. Compare damage depth and remaining allowance. Therefore reject: Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure."}},{"id":"a123-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-10"],"title":"選擇比｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Selectivity | mechanism and design","objective":"針對選擇比，把「矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For selectivity, turn \"Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「選擇比」的模型：矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以見證層量實際選擇比。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for selectivity: Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure selectivity on witness layers. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以見證層量實際選擇比。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure selectivity on witness layers. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付選擇比的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for selectivity, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-11-k1","title":"選擇比：機制","titleEn":"Selectivity: mechanism","text":"矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。","textEn":"Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以見證層量實際選擇比。 必須排除的錯判：高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure selectivity on witness layers. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「選擇比」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For selectivity — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面","矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。","高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比"],"optionsEn":["Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back","Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window.","Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity"],"answer":1,"explanation":"矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。 以見證層量實際選擇比。 因此不能採用「高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比」。","explanationEn":"Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window. Measure selectivity on witness layers. Therefore reject: Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity."}},{"id":"a123-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-11"],"title":"選擇比｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Selectivity | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對選擇比，把「矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For selectivity, turn \"Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以見證層量實際選擇比。 將「高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure selectivity on witness layers. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以見證層量實際選擇比。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure selectivity on witness layers. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付選擇比的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for selectivity: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-12-k1","title":"選擇比：機制","titleEn":"Selectivity: mechanism","text":"矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。","textEn":"Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以見證層量實際選擇比。 必須排除的錯判：高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure selectivity on witness layers. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「選擇比」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For selectivity — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比","正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面","以見證層量實際選擇比。"],"optionsEn":["Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity","Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back","Measure selectivity on witness layers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"矽、介電質和金屬的相對移除速率決定窗口。 以見證層量實際選擇比。 因此不能採用「高矽蝕刻速率就是高選擇比」。","explanationEn":"Relative Si/dielectric/metal removal rates define the window. Measure selectivity on witness layers. Therefore reject: Equating fast Si removal with high selectivity."}}]},{"id":"a123-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"選擇性露出","titleEn":"Selective reveal","description":"針對選擇性露出完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for selective reveal, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a123-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-12"],"title":"終點感測｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Endpoint sensing | mechanism and design","objective":"針對終點感測，把「全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For endpoint sensing, turn \"Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「終點感測」的模型：全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「以局部量測核對全域終點。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for endpoint sensing: Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Check global endpoints against local measurements. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"以局部量測核對全域終點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check global endpoints against local measurements. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付終點感測的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for endpoint sensing, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-13-k1","title":"終點感測：機制","titleEn":"Endpoint sensing: mechanism","text":"全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。","textEn":"Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以局部量測核對全域終點。 必須排除的錯判：全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check global endpoints against local measurements. Misinterpretation to reject: Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「終點感測」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For endpoint sensing — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。","全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成","看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格"],"optionsEn":["Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias.","Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal","Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible"],"answer":0,"explanation":"全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。 以局部量測核對全域終點。 因此不能採用「全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成」。","explanationEn":"Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias. Check global endpoints against local measurements. Therefore reject: Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal."}},{"id":"a123-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-13"],"title":"終點感測｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Endpoint sensing | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對終點感測，把「全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For endpoint sensing, turn \"Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：以局部量測核對全域終點。 將「全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Check global endpoints against local measurements. Challenge the hypothesis \"Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"以局部量測核對全域終點。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check global endpoints against local measurements. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付終點感測的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for endpoint sensing: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-14-k1","title":"終點感測：機制","titleEn":"Endpoint sensing: mechanism","text":"全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。","textEn":"Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"以局部量測核對全域終點。 必須排除的錯判：全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check global endpoints against local measurements. Misinterpretation to reject: Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「終點感測」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For endpoint sensing — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格","以局部量測核對全域終點。","全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible","Check global endpoints against local measurements.","Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal"],"answer":1,"explanation":"全域訊號可能先反映大面積區而非最晚孔。 以局部量測核對全域終點。 因此不能採用「全域終點一出現即可停止且全部完成」。","explanationEn":"Global signals may reflect large regions rather than last vias. Check global endpoints against local measurements. Therefore reject: Stopping at first global endpoint as complete reveal."}},{"id":"a123-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-14"],"title":"突出高度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Protrusion height | mechanism and design","objective":"針對突出高度，把「露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For protrusion height, turn \"Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「突出高度」的模型：露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for protrusion height: Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure regional height relative to support planes. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure regional height relative to support planes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均突出高度可代表所有接點。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean protrusion for every contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付突出高度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for protrusion height, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-15-k1","title":"突出高度：機制","titleEn":"Protrusion height: mechanism","text":"露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。","textEn":"Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。 必須排除的錯判：平均突出高度可代表所有接點。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure regional height relative to support planes. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean protrusion for every contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「突出高度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For protrusion height — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均突出高度可代表所有接點","兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準","露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。"],"optionsEn":["Using mean protrusion for every contact","Subtracting depths without checking datums","Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。 量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。 因此不能採用「平均突出高度可代表所有接點」。","explanationEn":"Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact. Measure regional height relative to support planes. Therefore reject: Using mean protrusion for every contact."}},{"id":"a123-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-15"],"title":"突出高度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Protrusion height | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對突出高度，把「露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For protrusion height, turn \"Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。 將「平均突出高度可代表所有接點」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure regional height relative to support planes. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using mean protrusion for every contact\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure regional height relative to support planes. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：平均突出高度可代表所有接點。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using mean protrusion for every contact. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付突出高度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for protrusion height: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-16-k1","title":"突出高度：機制","titleEn":"Protrusion height: mechanism","text":"露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。","textEn":"Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。 必須排除的錯判：平均突出高度可代表所有接點。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure regional height relative to support planes. Misinterpretation to reject: Using mean protrusion for every contact. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「突出高度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For protrusion height — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。","平均突出高度可代表所有接點","兩個深度數值相減不需檢查基準"],"optionsEn":["Measure regional height relative to support planes.","Using mean protrusion for every contact","Subtracting depths without checking datums"],"answer":0,"explanation":"露出高度分布影響後續介電質覆蓋與接觸。 量每區高度與支撐面相對關係。 因此不能採用「平均突出高度可代表所有接點」。","explanationEn":"Protrusion distribution affects later dielectric coverage/contact. Measure regional height relative to support planes. Therefore reject: Using mean protrusion for every contact."}},{"id":"a123-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-16"],"title":"絕緣保存｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Insulation preservation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對絕緣保存，把「側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For insulation preservation, turn \"Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「絕緣保存」的模型：側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「對照漏電與露出端截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設最深未露出 TSV 上方還有 3 μm 矽，最快區已露出；若理想矽對保護層選擇比 30，額外移除 3 μm 矽對應 0.1 μm 保護層消耗，仍須另加非均勻與量測餘量。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for insulation preservation: Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: If the latest TSV has 3 μm Si remaining while another is exposed, ideal selectivity 30 implies 0.1 μm protective-layer loss during completion, before nonuniformity and metrology margins. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"對照漏電與露出端截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付絕緣保存的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for insulation preservation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-17-k1","title":"絕緣保存：機制","titleEn":"Insulation preservation: mechanism","text":"側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。","textEn":"Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照漏電與露出端截面。 必須排除的錯判：金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設最深未露出 TSV 上方還有 3 μm 矽，最快區已露出；若理想矽對保護層選擇比 30，額外移除 3 μm 矽對應 0.1 μm 保護層消耗，仍須另加非均勻與量測餘量。","textEn":"If the latest TSV has 3 μm Si remaining while another is exposed, ideal selectivity 30 implies 0.1 μm protective-layer loss during completion, before nonuniformity and metrology margins."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕緣保存」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For insulation preservation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出","側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。","金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣"],"optionsEn":["Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal","Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal.","Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation"],"answer":1,"explanation":"側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。 對照漏電與露出端截面。 因此不能採用「金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣」。","explanationEn":"Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal. Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. Therefore reject: Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation."}},{"id":"a123-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-17"],"title":"絕緣保存｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Insulation preservation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對絕緣保存，把「側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For insulation preservation, turn \"Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：對照漏電與露出端截面。 將「金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設最深未露出 TSV 上方還有 3 μm 矽，最快區已露出；若理想矽對保護層選擇比 30，額外移除 3 μm 矽對應 0.1 μm 保護層消耗，仍須另加非均勻與量測餘量。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: If the latest TSV has 3 μm Si remaining while another is exposed, ideal selectivity 30 implies 0.1 μm protective-layer loss during completion, before nonuniformity and metrology margins. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"對照漏電與露出端截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付絕緣保存的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for insulation preservation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-18-k1","title":"絕緣保存：機制","titleEn":"Insulation preservation: mechanism","text":"側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。","textEn":"Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"對照漏電與露出端截面。 必須排除的錯判：金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設最深未露出 TSV 上方還有 3 μm 矽，最快區已露出；若理想矽對保護層選擇比 30，額外移除 3 μm 矽對應 0.1 μm 保護層消耗，仍須另加非均勻與量測餘量。","textEn":"If the latest TSV has 3 μm Si remaining while another is exposed, ideal selectivity 30 implies 0.1 μm protective-layer loss during completion, before nonuniformity and metrology margins."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕緣保存」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For insulation preservation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣","平均厚度達標即所有 TSV 同步露出","對照漏電與露出端截面。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation","Equating mean thickness with simultaneous reveal","Compare leakage and revealed-end sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"側壁絕緣在露出時仍需隔離金屬與矽。 對照漏電與露出端截面。 因此不能採用「金屬露出後不再需要側壁絕緣」。","explanationEn":"Sidewall insulation must retain metal–Si isolation during reveal. Compare leakage and revealed-end sections. Therefore reject: Assuming exposed metal no longer needs sidewall insulation."}}]},{"id":"a123-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"背面連接","titleEn":"Backside connection","description":"針對背面連接完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for backside connection, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a123-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-18"],"title":"污染與氧化｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Contamination and oxidation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對污染與氧化，把「暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For contamination and oxidation, turn \"Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「污染與氧化」的模型：暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for contamination and oxidation: Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Pair queue history and contact resistance. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair queue history and contact resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付污染與氧化的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for contamination and oxidation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-19-k1","title":"污染與氧化：機制","titleEn":"Contamination and oxidation: mechanism","text":"暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。","textEn":"Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。 必須排除的錯判：露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair queue history and contact resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「污染與氧化」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For contamination and oxidation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。","露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸","載板剛性高即可忽略膠層"],"optionsEn":["Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue.","Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape","Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff"],"answer":0,"explanation":"暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。 把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。 因此不能採用「露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸」。","explanationEn":"Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue. Pair queue history and contact resistance. Therefore reject: Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape."}},{"id":"a123-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-19"],"title":"污染與氧化｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Contamination and oxidation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對污染與氧化，把「暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For contamination and oxidation, turn \"Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。 將「露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Pair queue history and contact resistance. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Pair queue history and contact resistance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付污染與氧化的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for contamination and oxidation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-20-k1","title":"污染與氧化：機制","titleEn":"Contamination and oxidation: mechanism","text":"暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。","textEn":"Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。 必須排除的錯判：露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Pair queue history and contact resistance. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「污染與氧化」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For contamination and oxidation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["載板剛性高即可忽略膠層","把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。","露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring adhesive because the carrier is stiff","Pair queue history and contact resistance.","Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape"],"answer":1,"explanation":"暴露金屬可能再氧化或受殘留污染。 把等待歷程與接觸電阻配對。 因此不能採用「露出形貌良好就一定可低阻接觸」。","explanationEn":"Exposed metal can oxidize or retain residue. Pair queue history and contact resistance. Therefore reject: Inferring low-resistance contact from good shape."}},{"id":"a123-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-20"],"title":"背面 RDL｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Backside RDL | mechanism and design","objective":"針對背面 RDL，把「新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For backside rdl, turn \"Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「背面 RDL」的模型：新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for backside rdl: Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付背面 RDL的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for backside rdl, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-21-k1","title":"背面 RDL：機制","titleEn":"Backside RDL: mechanism","text":"新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。","textEn":"Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。 必須排除的錯判：正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. Misinterpretation to reject: Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「背面 RDL」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For backside rdl — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面","只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV","新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。"],"optionsEn":["Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back","Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone","Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。 核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。 因此不能採用「正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面」。","explanationEn":"Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height. Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. Therefore reject: Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back."}},{"id":"a123-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-21"],"title":"背面 RDL｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Backside RDL | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對背面 RDL，把「新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For backside rdl, turn \"Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。 將「正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付背面 RDL的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for backside rdl: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-22-k1","title":"背面 RDL：機制","titleEn":"Backside RDL: mechanism","text":"新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。","textEn":"Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。 必須排除的錯判：正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. Misinterpretation to reject: Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「背面 RDL」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For backside rdl — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。","正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面","只依固定研磨時間就可安全到 TSV"],"optionsEn":["Check backside mirroring and pad overlap.","Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back","Reaching TSVs safely by fixed grinding time alone"],"answer":0,"explanation":"新配線需捕捉實際 TSV 位置和高度。 核對背面坐標鏡像及焊墊重疊。 因此不能採用「正面座標可不轉換直接使用背面」。","explanationEn":"Backside routing must capture actual TSV position/height. Check backside mirroring and pad overlap. Therefore reject: Using frontside coordinates unchanged on the back."}},{"id":"a123-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-22"],"title":"露出驗收｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Reveal acceptance | mechanism and design","objective":"針對露出驗收，把「露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reveal acceptance, turn \"Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「露出驗收」的模型：露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立逐區幾何電性對照。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for reveal acceptance: Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立逐區幾何電性對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付露出驗收的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for reveal acceptance, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-23-k1","title":"露出驗收：機制","titleEn":"Reveal acceptance: mechanism","text":"露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。","textEn":"Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立逐區幾何電性對照。 必須排除的錯判：看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. Misinterpretation to reject: Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「露出驗收」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reveal acceptance — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["露出金屬後損傷自然不重要","露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。","看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure","Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence.","Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible"],"answer":1,"explanation":"露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。 建立逐區幾何電性對照。 因此不能採用「看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格」。","explanationEn":"Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence. Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. Therefore reject: Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible."}},{"id":"a123-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"],"prerequisiteIds":["a123-v9-23"],"title":"露出驗收｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Reveal acceptance | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對露出驗收，把「露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reveal acceptance, turn \"Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立逐區幾何電性對照。 將「看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. Challenge the hypothesis \"Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立逐區幾何電性對照。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付露出驗收的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for reveal acceptance: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a123-v9-24-k1","title":"露出驗收：機制","titleEn":"Reveal acceptance: mechanism","text":"露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。","textEn":"Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]},{"id":"a123-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立逐區幾何電性對照。 必須排除的錯判：看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. Misinterpretation to reject: Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-disco","v9a-imecback"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「露出驗收」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reveal acceptance — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格","露出金屬後損傷自然不重要","建立逐區幾何電性對照。"],"optionsEn":["Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible","Assuming damage ceases to matter after metal exposure","Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons."],"answer":2,"explanation":"露出完整、低漏電和良好接觸需三重證據。 建立逐區幾何電性對照。 因此不能採用「看到每個 TSV 即代表露出合格」。","explanationEn":"Complete reveal, low leakage and good contact need separate evidence. Build regional geometry/electrical comparisons. Therefore reject: Qualifying reveal solely because every TSV is visible."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-vias","subcategoryTitle":"穿孔與金屬互連","subcategoryTitleEn":"Through vias and metal interconnects","photoId":"v8-wafer"},{"id":"a124","title":"玻璃穿孔製作","titleEn":"Through-glass-via fabrication","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v9at-intel-glass"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入玻璃孔洞、裂紋與金屬化。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore glass vias, cracking and metallization, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["玻璃與孔設計","成孔與邊緣","金屬化","電熱機驗證"],"labelsEn":["Glass and via design","Hole formation and edges","Metallization","Multiphysics validation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a124-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"玻璃與孔設計","titleEn":"Glass and via design","description":"針對玻璃與孔設計完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for glass and via design, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a124-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"玻璃組成｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Glass composition | mechanism and design","objective":"針對玻璃組成，把「玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For glass composition, turn \"CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「玻璃組成」的模型：玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「指定材料牌號和量測頻率。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for glass composition: CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Specify material grade and measurement frequency. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"指定材料牌號和量測頻率。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Specify material grade and measurement frequency. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating all glass as one material. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付玻璃組成的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for glass composition, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-01-k1","title":"玻璃組成：機制","titleEn":"Glass composition: mechanism","text":"玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。","textEn":"CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"指定材料牌號和量測頻率。 必須排除的錯判：所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Specify material grade and measurement frequency. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating all glass as one material. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「玻璃組成」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For glass composition — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。","所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質","表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢"],"optionsEn":["CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing.","Treating all glass as one material","Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion"],"answer":0,"explanation":"玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。 指定材料牌號和量測頻率。 因此不能採用「所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質」。","explanationEn":"CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing. Specify material grade and measurement frequency. Therefore reject: Treating all glass as one material."}},{"id":"a124-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-01"],"title":"玻璃組成｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Glass composition | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對玻璃組成，把「玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For glass composition, turn \"CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：指定材料牌號和量測頻率。 將「所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Specify material grade and measurement frequency. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating all glass as one material\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"指定材料牌號和量測頻率。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Specify material grade and measurement frequency. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating all glass as one material. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付玻璃組成的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for glass composition: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-02-k1","title":"玻璃組成：機制","titleEn":"Glass composition: mechanism","text":"玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。","textEn":"CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"指定材料牌號和量測頻率。 必須排除的錯判：所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Specify material grade and measurement frequency. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating all glass as one material. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「玻璃組成」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For glass composition — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢","指定材料牌號和量測頻率。","所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質"],"optionsEn":["Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion","Specify material grade and measurement frequency.","Treating all glass as one material"],"answer":1,"explanation":"玻璃的 CTE、介電損耗和強度依組成及加工而異。 指定材料牌號和量測頻率。 因此不能採用「所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質」。","explanationEn":"CTE, dielectric loss and strength depend on composition/processing. Specify material grade and measurement frequency. Therefore reject: Treating all glass as one material."}},{"id":"a124-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-02"],"title":"通孔與盲孔｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Through and blind vias | mechanism and design","objective":"針對通孔與盲孔，把「孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For through and blind vias, turn \"Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「通孔與盲孔」的模型：孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for through and blind vias: Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付通孔與盲孔的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for through and blind vias, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-03-k1","title":"通孔與盲孔：機制","titleEn":"Through and blind vias: mechanism","text":"孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。","textEn":"Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。 必須排除的錯判：盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. Misinterpretation to reject: Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通孔與盲孔」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For through and blind vias — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設","雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連","孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias","Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces","Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。 畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。 因此不能採用「盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設」。","explanationEn":"Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting. Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. Therefore reject: Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias."}},{"id":"a124-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-03"],"title":"通孔與盲孔｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Through and blind vias | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對通孔與盲孔，把「孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For through and blind vias, turn \"Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。 將「盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付通孔與盲孔的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for through and blind vias: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-04-k1","title":"通孔與盲孔：機制","titleEn":"Through and blind vias: mechanism","text":"孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。","textEn":"Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。 必須排除的錯判：盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. Misinterpretation to reject: Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通孔與盲孔」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For through and blind vias — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。","盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設","雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連"],"optionsEn":["Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections.","Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias","Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔類型決定成孔、金屬化及排氣路徑。 畫孔口、孔底和對外連通。 因此不能採用「盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設」。","explanationEn":"Via type changes drilling, metallization and venting. Draw mouths, bottoms and vent connections. Therefore reject: Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias."}},{"id":"a124-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-04"],"title":"孔形與錐度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Profile and taper | mechanism and design","objective":"針對孔形與錐度，把「錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For profile and taper, turn \"Taper changes coating and current-carrying area.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「孔形與錐度」的模型：錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for profile and taper: Taper changes coating and current-carrying area. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure both diameters and wall roughness. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure both diameters and wall roughness. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：入口直徑就是最小導體截面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔形與錐度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for profile and taper, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-05-k1","title":"孔形與錐度：機制","titleEn":"Profile and taper: mechanism","text":"錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。","textEn":"Taper changes coating and current-carrying area.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。 必須排除的錯判：入口直徑就是最小導體截面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure both diameters and wall roughness. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔形與錐度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For profile and taper — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算","錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。","入口直徑就是最小導體截面"],"optionsEn":["Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via","Taper changes coating and current-carrying area.","Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area"],"answer":1,"explanation":"錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。 量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。 因此不能採用「入口直徑就是最小導體截面」。","explanationEn":"Taper changes coating and current-carrying area. Measure both diameters and wall roughness. Therefore reject: Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area."}},{"id":"a124-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-05"],"title":"孔形與錐度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Profile and taper | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對孔形與錐度，把「錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For profile and taper, turn \"Taper changes coating and current-carrying area.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。 將「入口直徑就是最小導體截面」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure both diameters and wall roughness. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure both diameters and wall roughness. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：入口直徑就是最小導體截面。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔形與錐度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for profile and taper: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-06-k1","title":"孔形與錐度：機制","titleEn":"Profile and taper: mechanism","text":"錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。","textEn":"Taper changes coating and current-carrying area.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。 必須排除的錯判：入口直徑就是最小導體截面。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure both diameters and wall roughness. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔形與錐度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For profile and taper — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["入口直徑就是最小導體截面","鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算","量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。"],"optionsEn":["Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area","Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via","Measure both diameters and wall roughness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"錐度改變金屬覆蓋和局部電流面積。 量上下直徑和壁面粗糙度。 因此不能採用「入口直徑就是最小導體截面」。","explanationEn":"Taper changes coating and current-carrying area. Measure both diameters and wall roughness. Therefore reject: Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area."}}]},{"id":"a124-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"成孔與邊緣","titleEn":"Hole formation and edges","description":"針對成孔與邊緣完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for hole formation and edges, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a124-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-06"],"title":"成孔裂紋｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Hole-formation cracks | mechanism and design","objective":"針對成孔裂紋，把「脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For hole-formation cracks, turn \"Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「成孔裂紋」的模型：脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for hole-formation cracks: Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付成孔裂紋的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for hole-formation cracks, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-07-k1","title":"成孔裂紋：機制","titleEn":"Hole-formation cracks: mechanism","text":"脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。","textEn":"Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。 必須排除的錯判：孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「成孔裂紋」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For hole-formation cracks — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。","孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋","玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險"],"optionsEn":["Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling.","Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes","Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk"],"answer":0,"explanation":"脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。 比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。 因此不能採用「孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling. Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. Therefore reject: Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes."}},{"id":"a124-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-07"],"title":"成孔裂紋｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Hole-formation cracks | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對成孔裂紋，把「脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For hole-formation cracks, turn \"Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。 將「孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付成孔裂紋的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for hole-formation cracks: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-08-k1","title":"成孔裂紋：機制","titleEn":"Hole-formation cracks: mechanism","text":"脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。","textEn":"Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。 必須排除的錯判：孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「成孔裂紋」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For hole-formation cracks — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險","比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。","孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk","Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling.","Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"脆性玻璃的微裂紋可能在熱循環後成長。 比較成孔前後偏光與截面證據。 因此不能採用「孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋」。","explanationEn":"Glass microcracks may grow during thermal cycling. Compare polariscopic/section evidence before and after drilling. Therefore reject: Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes."}},{"id":"a124-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-08"],"title":"孔間距與強度｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Pitch and strength | mechanism and design","objective":"針對孔間距與強度，把「孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pitch and strength, turn \"Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「孔間距與強度」的模型：孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for pitch and strength: Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using single-hole strength for all arrays. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔間距與強度的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for pitch and strength, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-09-k1","title":"孔間距與強度：機制","titleEn":"Pitch and strength: mechanism","text":"孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。","textEn":"Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。 必須排除的錯判：單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Using single-hole strength for all arrays. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔間距與強度」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pitch and strength — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列","低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗","孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。"],"optionsEn":["Using single-hole strength for all arrays","Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance","Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。 比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。 因此不能採用「單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列」。","explanationEn":"Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter. Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. Therefore reject: Using single-hole strength for all arrays."}},{"id":"a124-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-09"],"title":"孔間距與強度｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Pitch and strength | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對孔間距與強度，把「孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For pitch and strength, turn \"Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。 將「單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using single-hole strength for all arrays\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using single-hole strength for all arrays. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付孔間距與強度的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for pitch and strength: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-10-k1","title":"孔間距與強度：機制","titleEn":"Pitch and strength: mechanism","text":"孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。","textEn":"Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。 必須排除的錯判：單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Using single-hole strength for all arrays. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔間距與強度」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For pitch and strength — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。","單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列","低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗"],"optionsEn":["Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses.","Using single-hole strength for all arrays","Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔群降低承載截面，邊距和排列影響破裂。 比較單孔和密集陣列見證片。 因此不能採用「單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列」。","explanationEn":"Via arrays reduce load-bearing area; edge distances/layout matter. Compare isolated-hole and dense-array witnesses. Therefore reject: Using single-hole strength for all arrays."}},{"id":"a124-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-10"],"title":"表面附著｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Surface adhesion | mechanism and design","objective":"針對表面附著，把「玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For surface adhesion, turn \"Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「表面附著」的模型：玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for surface adhesion: Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付表面附著的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for surface adhesion, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-11-k1","title":"表面附著：機制","titleEn":"Surface adhesion: mechanism","text":"玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。","textEn":"Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。 必須排除的錯判：表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「表面附著」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For surface adhesion — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身","玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。","表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢"],"optionsEn":["Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias","Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding.","Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion"],"answer":1,"explanation":"玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。 測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。 因此不能採用「表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢」。","explanationEn":"Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding. Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. Therefore reject: Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion."}},{"id":"a124-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-11"],"title":"表面附著｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Surface adhesion | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對表面附著，把「玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For surface adhesion, turn \"Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。 將「表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付表面附著的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for surface adhesion: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-12-k1","title":"表面附著：機制","titleEn":"Surface adhesion: mechanism","text":"玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。","textEn":"Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。 必須排除的錯判：表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「表面附著」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For surface adhesion — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢","量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身","測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion","Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias","Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"玻璃—金屬附著需驗證，低粗糙表面不自動等於高黏著。 測剝離並定位實際破壞界面。 因此不能採用「表面越平滑金屬必黏得越牢」。","explanationEn":"Glass–metal adhesion needs validation; smoothness does not ensure bonding. Measure peel and locate fracture interfaces. Therefore reject: Assuming smoother glass always improves adhesion."}}]},{"id":"a124-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"金屬化","titleEn":"Metallization","description":"針對金屬化完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for metallization, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a124-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-12"],"title":"種子覆蓋｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Seed coverage | mechanism and design","objective":"針對種子覆蓋，把「高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed coverage, turn \"High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「種子覆蓋」的模型：高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「檢查入口、中央和出口截面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for seed coverage: High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"檢查入口、中央和出口截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子覆蓋的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for seed coverage, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-13-k1","title":"種子覆蓋：機制","titleEn":"Seed coverage: mechanism","text":"高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。","textEn":"High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查入口、中央和出口截面。 必須排除的錯判：雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子覆蓋」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed coverage — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。","雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連","只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板"],"optionsEn":["High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating.","Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces","Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。 檢查入口、中央和出口截面。 因此不能採用「雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連」。","explanationEn":"High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating. Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. Therefore reject: Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces."}},{"id":"a124-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-13"],"title":"種子覆蓋｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Seed coverage | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對種子覆蓋，把「高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For seed coverage, turn \"High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：檢查入口、中央和出口截面。 將「雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"檢查入口、中央和出口截面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付種子覆蓋的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for seed coverage: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-14-k1","title":"種子覆蓋：機制","titleEn":"Seed coverage: mechanism","text":"高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。","textEn":"High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查入口、中央和出口截面。 必須排除的錯判：雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「種子覆蓋」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For seed coverage — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板","檢查入口、中央和出口截面。","雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連"],"optionsEn":["Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance","Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections.","Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高深寬比孔壁的連續性決定後續鍍層。 檢查入口、中央和出口截面。 因此不能採用「雙面表面有種子即可證明孔壁相連」。","explanationEn":"High-aspect wall continuity determines subsequent plating. Inspect entrance, middle and exit sections. Therefore reject: Inferring wall continuity from seeded faces."}},{"id":"a124-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-14"],"title":"實心與鍍壁｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Solid versus shell vias | mechanism and design","objective":"針對實心與鍍壁，把「實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For solid versus shell vias, turn \"Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「實心與鍍壁」的模型：實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for solid versus shell vias: Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付實心與鍍壁的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for solid versus shell vias, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-15-k1","title":"實心與鍍壁：機制","titleEn":"Solid versus shell vias: mechanism","text":"實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。","textEn":"Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。 必須排除的錯判：鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「實心與鍍壁」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For solid versus shell vias — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算","所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質","實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。"],"optionsEn":["Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via","Treating all glass as one material","Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically."],"answer":2,"explanation":"實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。 分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。 因此不能採用「鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算」。","explanationEn":"Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically. Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. Therefore reject: Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via."}},{"id":"a124-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-15"],"title":"實心與鍍壁｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Solid versus shell vias | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對實心與鍍壁，把「實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For solid versus shell vias, turn \"Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。 將「鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. Challenge the hypothesis \"Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付實心與鍍壁的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for solid versus shell vias: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-16-k1","title":"實心與鍍壁：機制","titleEn":"Solid versus shell vias: mechanism","text":"實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。","textEn":"Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。 必須排除的錯判：鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. Misinterpretation to reject: Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「實心與鍍壁」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For solid versus shell vias — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。","鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算","所有玻璃具有相同介電與熱性質"],"optionsEn":["Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately.","Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via","Treating all glass as one material"],"answer":0,"explanation":"實心和鍍壁導體的電、熱、機械行為不同。 分別計算導電截面和金屬體積。 因此不能採用「鍍壁孔電阻可按實心孔算」。","explanationEn":"Solid and shell conductors differ electrically, thermally and mechanically. Calculate conducting area and metal volume separately. Therefore reject: Calculating shell-via resistance as a solid via."}},{"id":"a124-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-16"],"title":"熱失配｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Thermal mismatch | mechanism and design","objective":"針對熱失配，把「銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal mismatch, turn \"Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「熱失配」的模型：銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設玻璃厚 300 μm、孔徑 50 μm，深寬比 6；若金屬只鍍成 5 μm 厚圓筒，導體面積 π(25²−20²)≈707 μm²，不可用實心孔面積 1963 μm² 計算電阻。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for thermal mismatch: Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: For 300 μm glass and 50 μm vias, aspect ratio is 6. A 5 μm plated shell has area π(25²−20²)≈707 μm², not the 1963 μm² area of a solid via. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱失配的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for thermal mismatch, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-17-k1","title":"熱失配：機制","titleEn":"Thermal mismatch: mechanism","text":"銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。","textEn":"Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。 必須排除的錯判：玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設玻璃厚 300 μm、孔徑 50 μm，深寬比 6；若金屬只鍍成 5 μm 厚圓筒，導體面積 π(25²−20²)≈707 μm²，不可用實心孔面積 1963 μm² 計算電阻。","textEn":"For 300 μm glass and 50 μm vias, aspect ratio is 6. A 5 μm plated shell has area π(25²−20²)≈707 μm², not the 1963 μm² area of a solid via."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱失配」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal mismatch — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設","銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。","玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險"],"optionsEn":["Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias","Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress.","Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk"],"answer":1,"explanation":"銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。 比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。 因此不能採用「玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險」。","explanationEn":"Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress. Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. Therefore reject: Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk."}},{"id":"a124-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-17"],"title":"熱失配｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Thermal mismatch | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對熱失配，把「銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For thermal mismatch, turn \"Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。 將「玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設玻璃厚 300 μm、孔徑 50 μm，深寬比 6；若金屬只鍍成 5 μm 厚圓筒，導體面積 π(25²−20²)≈707 μm²，不可用實心孔面積 1963 μm² 計算電阻。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: For 300 μm glass and 50 μm vias, aspect ratio is 6. A 5 μm plated shell has area π(25²−20²)≈707 μm², not the 1963 μm² area of a solid via. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付熱失配的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for thermal mismatch: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-18-k1","title":"熱失配：機制","titleEn":"Thermal mismatch: mechanism","text":"銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。","textEn":"Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。 必須排除的錯判：玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設玻璃厚 300 μm、孔徑 50 μm，深寬比 6；若金屬只鍍成 5 μm 厚圓筒，導體面積 π(25²−20²)≈707 μm²，不可用實心孔面積 1963 μm² 計算電阻。","textEn":"For 300 μm glass and 50 μm vias, aspect ratio is 6. A 5 μm plated shell has area π(25²−20²)≈707 μm², not the 1963 μm² area of a solid via."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱失配」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For thermal mismatch — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險","盲孔可直接沿用通孔的填充假設","比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。"],"optionsEn":["Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk","Using through-via fill assumptions for blind vias","Compare crack orientation before/after cycling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"銅與玻璃膨脹差可集中孔邊應力。 比較溫度循環前後裂紋方位。 因此不能採用「玻璃絕緣就表示沒有熱機風險」。","explanationEn":"Cu–glass expansion mismatch can concentrate rim stress. Compare crack orientation before/after cycling. Therefore reject: Equating insulation with no thermomechanical risk."}}]},{"id":"a124-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"電熱機驗證","titleEn":"Multiphysics validation","description":"針對電熱機驗證完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for multiphysics validation, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a124-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-18"],"title":"高頻寄生｜機制與設計","titleEn":"High-frequency parasitics | mechanism and design","objective":"針對高頻寄生，把「TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For high-frequency parasitics, turn \"Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「高頻寄生」的模型：TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for high-frequency parasitics: Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付高頻寄生的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for high-frequency parasitics, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-19-k1","title":"高頻寄生：機制","titleEn":"High-frequency parasitics: mechanism","text":"TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。","textEn":"Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。 必須排除的錯判：低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高頻寄生」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For high-frequency parasitics — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。","低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗","入口直徑就是最小導體截面"],"optionsEn":["Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling.","Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance","Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area"],"answer":0,"explanation":"TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。 畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。 因此不能採用「低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗」。","explanationEn":"Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling. Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. Therefore reject: Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance."}},{"id":"a124-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-19"],"title":"高頻寄生｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"High-frequency parasitics | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對高頻寄生，把「TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For high-frequency parasitics, turn \"Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。 將「低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. Challenge the hypothesis \"Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付高頻寄生的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for high-frequency parasitics: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-20-k1","title":"高頻寄生：機制","titleEn":"High-frequency parasitics: mechanism","text":"TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。","textEn":"Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。 必須排除的錯判：低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. Misinterpretation to reject: Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高頻寄生」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For high-frequency parasitics — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["入口直徑就是最小導體截面","畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。","低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗"],"optionsEn":["Treating entrance diameter as minimum conducting area","Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models.","Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"TGV 周圍回流結構決定電感和耦合。 畫信號和地孔回路並建雙埠模型。 因此不能採用「低直流電阻即可保證高頻低損耗」。","explanationEn":"Return structures around TGVs set inductance/coupling. Draw signal/ground loops and two-port models. Therefore reject: Inferring low RF loss from low DC resistance."}},{"id":"a124-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-20"],"title":"量測去嵌入｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Measurement de-embedding | mechanism and design","objective":"針對量測去嵌入，把「探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For measurement de-embedding, turn \"Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「量測去嵌入」的模型：探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「使用直通和開短路見證比較。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for measurement de-embedding: Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare thru/open/short witnesses. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"使用直通和開短路見證比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thru/open/short witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付量測去嵌入的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for measurement de-embedding, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-21-k1","title":"量測去嵌入：機制","titleEn":"Measurement de-embedding: mechanism","text":"探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。","textEn":"Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"使用直通和開短路見證比較。 必須排除的錯判：量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thru/open/short witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測去嵌入」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For measurement de-embedding — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身","孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋","探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。"],"optionsEn":["Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias","Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes","Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。 使用直通和開短路見證比較。 因此不能採用「量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身」。","explanationEn":"Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior. Compare thru/open/short witnesses. Therefore reject: Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias."}},{"id":"a124-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-21"],"title":"量測去嵌入｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Measurement de-embedding | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對量測去嵌入，把「探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For measurement de-embedding, turn \"Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：使用直通和開短路見證比較。 將「量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare thru/open/short witnesses. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"使用直通和開短路見證比較。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare thru/open/short witnesses. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付量測去嵌入的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for measurement de-embedding: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-22-k1","title":"量測去嵌入：機制","titleEn":"Measurement de-embedding: mechanism","text":"探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。","textEn":"Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"使用直通和開短路見證比較。 必須排除的錯判：量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare thru/open/short witnesses. Misinterpretation to reject: Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測去嵌入」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For measurement de-embedding — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["使用直通和開短路見證比較。","量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身","孔可導通就可忽略玻璃微裂紋"],"optionsEn":["Compare thru/open/short witnesses.","Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias","Ignoring glass microcracks after via continuity passes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"探針墊和走線會混入 TGV 的量測。 使用直通和開短路見證比較。 因此不能採用「量到的 S 參數全屬於孔洞本身」。","explanationEn":"Probe pads/traces contaminate measured TGV behavior. Compare thru/open/short witnesses. Therefore reject: Assigning measured S-parameters entirely to vias."}},{"id":"a124-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-22"],"title":"整合放行｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Integration release | mechanism and design","objective":"針對整合放行，把「電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For integration release, turn \"Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「整合放行」的模型：電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「保存孔群位置和失效類型。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for integration release: Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Retain array location and failure class. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"保存孔群位置和失效類型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Retain array location and failure class. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付整合放行的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for integration release, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-23-k1","title":"整合放行：機制","titleEn":"Integration release: mechanism","text":"電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。","textEn":"Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保存孔群位置和失效類型。 必須排除的錯判：只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Retain array location and failure class. Misinterpretation to reject: Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「整合放行」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For integration release — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列","電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。","只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板"],"optionsEn":["Using single-hole strength for all arrays","Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together.","Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。 保存孔群位置和失效類型。 因此不能採用「只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板」。","explanationEn":"Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together. Retain array location and failure class. Therefore reject: Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance."}},{"id":"a124-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"],"prerequisiteIds":["a124-v9-23"],"title":"整合放行｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Integration release | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對整合放行，把「電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For integration release, turn \"Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：保存孔群位置和失效類型。 將「只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Retain array location and failure class. Challenge the hypothesis \"Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"保存孔群位置和失效類型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Retain array location and failure class. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付整合放行的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for integration release: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a124-v9-24-k1","title":"整合放行：機制","titleEn":"Integration release: mechanism","text":"電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。","textEn":"Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]},{"id":"a124-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"保存孔群位置和失效類型。 必須排除的錯判：只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Retain array location and failure class. Misinterpretation to reject: Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-corningtgv","v9a-atotechmulti"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「整合放行」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For integration release — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板","單孔強度足以代表所有孔陣列","保存孔群位置和失效類型。"],"optionsEn":["Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance","Using single-hole strength for all arrays","Retain array location and failure class."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電連通、裂紋與玻璃處理良率須共同驗證。 保存孔群位置和失效類型。 因此不能採用「只要 TGV 電阻低即可做大面積基板」。","explanationEn":"Qualify continuity, cracks and handling yield together. Retain array location and failure class. Therefore reject: Scaling substrates based only on low TGV resistance."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-vias","subcategoryTitle":"穿孔與金屬互連","subcategoryTitleEn":"Through vias and metal interconnects","photoId":"v8-micro-pillars"},{"id":"a125","title":"矽中介層佈線","titleEn":"Silicon-interposer routing","category":"packaging","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":960,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack","v3-media-698d26511517","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"summary":"以 12 個技術單元、24 步分析與驗證深入矽中介層布線、TSV 與回流路徑。逐一建立剖面、測試見證、失效判別和可審查的驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Twelve technical units and 24 analysis/verification steps explore silicon interposer routing, tsvs and return paths, building sections, test witnesses, failure discrimination and reviewable acceptance evidence.","scope":"公開工程原理與原創教學推理；數值是明示假設的算例，不是生產配方或供應商規格。各單元先建立物理模型，再設計能區分失效機制的量測。24 步是學習工作包，完整量產需經授權設備、材料及產品資格驗證。","scopeEn":"Public engineering principles and original educational reasoning. Numbers are explicitly hypothetical examples, not production recipes or supplier specifications. Each unit builds a physical model then measurements that discriminate failure mechanisms. The 24 steps are learning work packages; production requires qualified equipment, materials and product validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["接口與架構","高密度布線","垂直連通","簽核與整合"],"labelsEn":["Interfaces and architecture","Dense routing","Vertical connection","Signoff and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a125-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"接口與架構","titleEn":"Interfaces and architecture","description":"針對接口與架構完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for interfaces and architecture, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a125-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"被動與主動中介層｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Passive and active interposers | mechanism and design","objective":"針對被動與主動中介層，把「是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For passive and active interposers, turn \"Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「被動與主動中介層」的模型：是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for passive and active interposers: Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Mark passive wiring and active functions. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark passive wiring and active functions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有矽中介層都只是無源連線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating all silicon interposers as passive. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付被動與主動中介層的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for passive and active interposers, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-01-k1","title":"被動與主動中介層：機制","titleEn":"Passive and active interposers: mechanism","text":"是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。","textEn":"Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-01-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。 必須排除的錯判：所有矽中介層都只是無源連線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark passive wiring and active functions. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating all silicon interposers as passive. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「被動與主動中介層」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For passive and active interposers — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。","所有矽中介層都只是無源連線","線長相同即傳輸行為相同"],"optionsEn":["Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements.","Treating all silicon interposers as passive","Equating length with transmission behavior"],"answer":0,"explanation":"是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。 標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。 因此不能採用「所有矽中介層都只是無源連線」。","explanationEn":"Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements. Mark passive wiring and active functions. Therefore reject: Treating all silicon interposers as passive."}},{"id":"a125-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-01"],"title":"被動與主動中介層｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Passive and active interposers | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對被動與主動中介層，把「是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For passive and active interposers, turn \"Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。 將「所有矽中介層都只是無源連線」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Mark passive wiring and active functions. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating all silicon interposers as passive\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Mark passive wiring and active functions. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：所有矽中介層都只是無源連線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating all silicon interposers as passive. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付被動與主動中介層的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for passive and active interposers: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-02-k1","title":"被動與主動中介層：機制","titleEn":"Passive and active interposers: mechanism","text":"是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。","textEn":"Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-02-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。 必須排除的錯判：所有矽中介層都只是無源連線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Mark passive wiring and active functions. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating all silicon interposers as passive. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「被動與主動中介層」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For passive and active interposers — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["線長相同即傳輸行為相同","標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。","所有矽中介層都只是無源連線"],"optionsEn":["Equating length with transmission behavior","Mark passive wiring and active functions.","Treating all silicon interposers as passive"],"answer":1,"explanation":"是否含主動電路改變供電、測試和熱需求。 標出被動線路及主動功能邊界。 因此不能採用「所有矽中介層都只是無源連線」。","explanationEn":"Active circuitry changes power, testing and thermal requirements. Mark passive wiring and active functions. Therefore reject: Treating all silicon interposers as passive."}},{"id":"a125-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-02"],"title":"晶粒邊界分配｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Die shoreline allocation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對晶粒邊界分配，把「I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die shoreline allocation, turn \"I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「晶粒邊界分配」的模型：I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「按實際節距計算可用連接數。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for die shoreline allocation: I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Count usable connections at actual pitch. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"按實際節距計算可用連接數。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Count usable connections at actual pitch. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating geometric positions with signal count. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒邊界分配的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for die shoreline allocation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-03-k1","title":"晶粒邊界分配：機制","titleEn":"Die shoreline allocation: mechanism","text":"I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。","textEn":"I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-03-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按實際節距計算可用連接數。 必須排除的錯判：幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Count usable connections at actual pitch. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating geometric positions with signal count. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒邊界分配」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die shoreline allocation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數","地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置","I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。"],"optionsEn":["Equating geometric positions with signal count","Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space","I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。 按實際節距計算可用連接數。 因此不能採用「幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數」。","explanationEn":"I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy. Count usable connections at actual pitch. Therefore reject: Equating geometric positions with signal count."}},{"id":"a125-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-03"],"title":"晶粒邊界分配｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Die shoreline allocation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對晶粒邊界分配，把「I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For die shoreline allocation, turn \"I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：按實際節距計算可用連接數。 將「幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Count usable connections at actual pitch. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating geometric positions with signal count\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"按實際節距計算可用連接數。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Count usable connections at actual pitch. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating geometric positions with signal count. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付晶粒邊界分配的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for die shoreline allocation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-04-k1","title":"晶粒邊界分配：機制","titleEn":"Die shoreline allocation: mechanism","text":"I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。","textEn":"I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-04-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"按實際節距計算可用連接數。 必須排除的錯判：幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Count usable connections at actual pitch. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating geometric positions with signal count. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「晶粒邊界分配」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For die shoreline allocation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["按實際節距計算可用連接數。","幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數","地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置"],"optionsEn":["Count usable connections at actual pitch.","Equating geometric positions with signal count","Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space"],"answer":0,"explanation":"I/O 位置須同回流、電源與冗餘共享邊界。 按實際節距計算可用連接數。 因此不能採用「幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數」。","explanationEn":"I/O shares shoreline with returns, power and redundancy. Count usable connections at actual pitch. Therefore reject: Equating geometric positions with signal count."}},{"id":"a125-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-04"],"title":"層疊規劃｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Stackup planning | mechanism and design","objective":"針對層疊規劃，把「配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stackup planning, turn \"Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「層疊規劃」的模型：配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫每層介電厚度及回流。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for stackup planning: Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫每層介電厚度及回流。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層疊規劃的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for stackup planning, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-05-k1","title":"層疊規劃：機制","titleEn":"Stackup planning: mechanism","text":"配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。","textEn":"Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-05-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫每層介電厚度及回流。 必須排除的錯判：增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層疊規劃」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stackup planning — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景","配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。","增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線"],"optionsEn":["Treating silicon as a perfect insulator","Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance.","Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost"],"answer":1,"explanation":"配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。 畫每層介電厚度及回流。 因此不能採用「增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線」。","explanationEn":"Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance. Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. Therefore reject: Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost."}},{"id":"a125-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-05"],"title":"層疊規劃｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Stackup planning | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對層疊規劃，把「配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For stackup planning, turn \"Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫每層介電厚度及回流。 將「增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫每層介電厚度及回流。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付層疊規劃的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for stackup planning: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-06-k1","title":"層疊規劃：機制","titleEn":"Stackup planning: mechanism","text":"配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。","textEn":"Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-06-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫每層介電厚度及回流。 必須排除的錯判：增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層疊規劃」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For stackup planning — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線","矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景","畫每層介電厚度及回流。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost","Treating silicon as a perfect insulator","Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"配線層與參考平面決定路由和阻抗。 畫每層介電厚度及回流。 因此不能採用「增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線」。","explanationEn":"Routing layers and reference planes determine routes/impedance. Draw dielectric thickness and returns by layer. Therefore reject: Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost."}}]},{"id":"a125-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"高密度布線","titleEn":"Dense routing","description":"針對高密度布線完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for dense routing, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a125-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-06"],"title":"線寬與損耗｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Width and loss | mechanism and design","objective":"針對線寬與損耗，把「細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For width and loss, turn \"Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「線寬與損耗」的模型：細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for width and loss: Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare RC and area for two widths. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare RC and area for two widths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最細線寬總最節能。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付線寬與損耗的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for width and loss, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-07-k1","title":"線寬與損耗：機制","titleEn":"Width and loss: mechanism","text":"細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。","textEn":"Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-07-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。 必須排除的錯判：最細線寬總最節能。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare RC and area for two widths. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「線寬與損耗」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For width and loss — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。","最細線寬總最節能","信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力"],"optionsEn":["Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter.","Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient","Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes"],"answer":0,"explanation":"細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。 比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。 因此不能採用「最細線寬總最節能」。","explanationEn":"Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter. Compare RC and area for two widths. Therefore reject: Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient."}},{"id":"a125-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-07"],"title":"線寬與損耗｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Width and loss | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對線寬與損耗，把「細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For width and loss, turn \"Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。 將「最細線寬總最節能」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare RC and area for two widths. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare RC and area for two widths. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：最細線寬總最節能。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付線寬與損耗的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for width and loss: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-08-k1","title":"線寬與損耗：機制","titleEn":"Width and loss: mechanism","text":"細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。","textEn":"Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-08-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。 必須排除的錯判：最細線寬總最節能。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare RC and area for two widths. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「線寬與損耗」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For width and loss — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力","比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。","最細線寬總最節能"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes","Compare RC and area for two widths.","Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient"],"answer":1,"explanation":"細線降低擁塞但增加電阻，截面與金屬品質都重要。 比較兩種線寬的 RC 和面積。 因此不能採用「最細線寬總最節能」。","explanationEn":"Fine lines ease congestion but raise resistance; geometry and material matter. Compare RC and area for two widths. Therefore reject: Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient."}},{"id":"a125-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-08"],"title":"差分與回流｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Differential and return paths | mechanism and design","objective":"針對差分與回流，把「差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For differential and return paths, turn \"Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「差分與回流」的模型：差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「畫換層和地孔連接。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for differential and return paths: Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Draw transitions and ground-via connections. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"畫換層和地孔連接。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw transitions and ground-via connections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：差分訊號完全不需地參考。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming differential signals need no ground reference. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付差分與回流的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for differential and return paths, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-09-k1","title":"差分與回流：機制","titleEn":"Differential and return paths: mechanism","text":"差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。","textEn":"Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-09-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫換層和地孔連接。 必須排除的錯判：差分訊號完全不需地參考。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw transitions and ground-via connections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming differential signals need no ground reference. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「差分與回流」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For differential and return paths — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["差分訊號完全不需地參考","接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性","差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。"],"optionsEn":["Assuming differential signals need no ground reference","Treating seams as drawing-only issues","Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control."],"answer":2,"explanation":"差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。 畫換層和地孔連接。 因此不能採用「差分訊號完全不需地參考」。","explanationEn":"Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control. Draw transitions and ground-via connections. Therefore reject: Assuming differential signals need no ground reference."}},{"id":"a125-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-09"],"title":"差分與回流｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Differential and return paths | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對差分與回流，把「差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For differential and return paths, turn \"Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：畫換層和地孔連接。 將「差分訊號完全不需地參考」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Draw transitions and ground-via connections. Challenge the hypothesis \"Assuming differential signals need no ground reference\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"畫換層和地孔連接。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Draw transitions and ground-via connections. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：差分訊號完全不需地參考。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Assuming differential signals need no ground reference. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付差分與回流的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for differential and return paths: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-10-k1","title":"差分與回流：機制","titleEn":"Differential and return paths: mechanism","text":"差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。","textEn":"Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-10-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"畫換層和地孔連接。 必須排除的錯判：差分訊號完全不需地參考。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Draw transitions and ground-via connections. Misinterpretation to reject: Assuming differential signals need no ground reference. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「差分與回流」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For differential and return paths — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["畫換層和地孔連接。","差分訊號完全不需地參考","接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性"],"optionsEn":["Draw transitions and ground-via connections.","Assuming differential signals need no ground reference","Treating seams as drawing-only issues"],"answer":0,"explanation":"差分對仍需要定義共模回流和不平衡。 畫換層和地孔連接。 因此不能採用「差分訊號完全不需地參考」。","explanationEn":"Differential pairs still need common-mode returns and imbalance control. Draw transitions and ground-via connections. Therefore reject: Assuming differential signals need no ground reference."}},{"id":"a125-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-10"],"title":"彎折和過孔｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Bends and vias | mechanism and design","objective":"針對彎折和過孔，把「局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bends and vias, turn \"Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「彎折和過孔」的模型：局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較直線與過孔測試結構。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for bends and vias: Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare straight and via test structures. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較直線與過孔測試結構。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare straight and via test structures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：線長相同即傳輸行為相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating length with transmission behavior. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付彎折和過孔的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for bends and vias, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-11-k1","title":"彎折和過孔：機制","titleEn":"Bends and vias: mechanism","text":"局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。","textEn":"Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-11-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較直線與過孔測試結構。 必須排除的錯判：線長相同即傳輸行為相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare straight and via test structures. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating length with transmission behavior. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彎折和過孔」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bends and vias — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效","局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。","線長相同即傳輸行為相同"],"optionsEn":["Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure","Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion.","Equating length with transmission behavior"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。 比較直線與過孔測試結構。 因此不能採用「線長相同即傳輸行為相同」。","explanationEn":"Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion. Compare straight and via test structures. Therefore reject: Equating length with transmission behavior."}},{"id":"a125-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-11"],"title":"彎折和過孔｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Bends and vias | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對彎折和過孔，把「局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For bends and vias, turn \"Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較直線與過孔測試結構。 將「線長相同即傳輸行為相同」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare straight and via test structures. Challenge the hypothesis \"Equating length with transmission behavior\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較直線與過孔測試結構。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare straight and via test structures. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：線長相同即傳輸行為相同。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Equating length with transmission behavior. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付彎折和過孔的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for bends and vias: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-12-k1","title":"彎折和過孔：機制","titleEn":"Bends and vias: mechanism","text":"局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。","textEn":"Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-12-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較直線與過孔測試結構。 必須排除的錯判：線長相同即傳輸行為相同。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare straight and via test structures. Misinterpretation to reject: Equating length with transmission behavior. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彎折和過孔」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For bends and vias — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["線長相同即傳輸行為相同","導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效","比較直線與過孔測試結構。"],"optionsEn":["Equating length with transmission behavior","Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure","Compare straight and via test structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部不連續會造成反射和模式轉換。 比較直線與過孔測試結構。 因此不能採用「線長相同即傳輸行為相同」。","explanationEn":"Local discontinuities cause reflections/mode conversion. Compare straight and via test structures. Therefore reject: Equating length with transmission behavior."}}]},{"id":"a125-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"垂直連通","titleEn":"Vertical connection","description":"針對垂直連通完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for vertical connection, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a125-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-12"],"title":"TSV 分配｜機制與設計","titleEn":"TSV allocation | mechanism and design","objective":"針對TSV 分配，把「訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tsv allocation, turn \"Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「TSV 分配」的模型：訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for tsv allocation: Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Build TSV net and current-density maps. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build TSV net and current-density maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付TSV 分配的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for tsv allocation, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-13-k1","title":"TSV 分配：機制","titleEn":"TSV allocation: mechanism","text":"訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。","textEn":"Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-13-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。 必須排除的錯判：地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build TSV net and current-density maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「TSV 分配」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tsv allocation — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。","地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置","各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格"],"optionsEn":["Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops.","Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space","Treating separate simulations as system qualification"],"answer":0,"explanation":"訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。 建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。 因此不能採用「地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置」。","explanationEn":"Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops. Build TSV net and current-density maps. Therefore reject: Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space."}},{"id":"a125-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-13"],"title":"TSV 分配｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"TSV allocation | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對TSV 分配，把「訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For tsv allocation, turn \"Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。 將「地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Build TSV net and current-density maps. Challenge the hypothesis \"Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Build TSV net and current-density maps. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付TSV 分配的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for tsv allocation: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-14-k1","title":"TSV 分配：機制","titleEn":"TSV allocation: mechanism","text":"訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。","textEn":"Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-14-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。 必須排除的錯判：地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Build TSV net and current-density maps. Misinterpretation to reject: Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「TSV 分配」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For tsv allocation — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格","建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。","地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置"],"optionsEn":["Treating separate simulations as system qualification","Build TSV net and current-density maps.","Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space"],"answer":1,"explanation":"訊號、電源與地 TSV 的位置共同决定回路。 建立 TSV 網路與電流密度圖。 因此不能採用「地 TSV 可只按剩餘空間放置」。","explanationEn":"Signal, power and ground TSV locations jointly define loops. Build TSV net and current-density maps. Therefore reject: Placing ground TSVs only in leftover space."}},{"id":"a125-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-14"],"title":"矽基板耦合｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Silicon substrate coupling | mechanism and design","objective":"針對矽基板耦合，把「矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For silicon substrate coupling, turn \"Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「矽基板耦合」的模型：矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for silicon substrate coupling: Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating silicon as a perfect insulator. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付矽基板耦合的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for silicon substrate coupling, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-15-k1","title":"矽基板耦合：機制","titleEn":"Silicon substrate coupling: mechanism","text":"矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。","textEn":"Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-15-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。 必須排除的錯判：矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating silicon as a perfect insulator. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「矽基板耦合」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For silicon substrate coupling — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景","所有矽中介層都只是無源連線","矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。"],"optionsEn":["Treating silicon as a perfect insulator","Treating all silicon interposers as passive","Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk."],"answer":2,"explanation":"矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。 比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。 因此不能採用「矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景」。","explanationEn":"Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk. Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. Therefore reject: Treating silicon as a perfect insulator."}},{"id":"a125-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-15"],"title":"矽基板耦合｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Silicon substrate coupling | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對矽基板耦合，把「矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For silicon substrate coupling, turn \"Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。 將「矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating silicon as a perfect insulator\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating silicon as a perfect insulator. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付矽基板耦合的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for silicon substrate coupling: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-16-k1","title":"矽基板耦合：機制","titleEn":"Silicon substrate coupling: mechanism","text":"矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。","textEn":"Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-16-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。 必須排除的錯判：矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating silicon as a perfect insulator. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「矽基板耦合」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For silicon substrate coupling — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。","矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景","所有矽中介層都只是無源連線"],"optionsEn":["Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models.","Treating silicon as a perfect insulator","Treating all silicon interposers as passive"],"answer":0,"explanation":"矽電阻率和偏壓影響損耗與串擾。 比較基板模型與絕緣理想模型。 因此不能採用「矽中介層可視為完全絕緣背景」。","explanationEn":"Silicon resistivity/bias affect loss and crosstalk. Compare substrate-aware and ideal-insulator models. Therefore reject: Treating silicon as a perfect insulator."}},{"id":"a125-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-16"],"title":"供電降壓｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Power drop | mechanism and design","objective":"針對供電降壓，把「高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For power drop, turn \"Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「供電降壓」的模型：高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。 原創算例：假設可用邊長 10 mm、I/O 節距 50 μm、單列配置，理想最多 200 個位置；若每四位置需一個回流地，訊號位置上限約 150，還不含電源和保留區。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Build the model for power drop: Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement. Original example: A 10 mm shoreline at 50 μm pitch permits an ideal 200 positions in one row. If one of every four is ground, signals are at most about 150 before power/keep-outs. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付供電降壓的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for power drop, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-17-k1","title":"供電降壓：機制","titleEn":"Power drop: mechanism","text":"高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。","textEn":"Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-17-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。 必須排除的錯判：信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-17-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設可用邊長 10 mm、I/O 節距 50 μm、單列配置，理想最多 200 個位置；若每四位置需一個回流地，訊號位置上限約 150，還不含電源和保留區。","textEn":"A 10 mm shoreline at 50 μm pitch permits an ideal 200 positions in one row. If one of every four is ground, signals are at most about 150 before power/keep-outs."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「供電降壓」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For power drop — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數","高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。","信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力"],"optionsEn":["Equating geometric positions with signal count","Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section.","Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。 計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。 因此不能採用「信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力」。","explanationEn":"Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section. Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. Therefore reject: Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes."}},{"id":"a125-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-17"],"title":"供電降壓｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Power drop | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對供電降壓，把「高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For power drop, turn \"Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。 將「信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。 原創算例：假設可用邊長 10 mm、I/O 節距 50 μm、單列配置，理想最多 200 個位置；若每四位置需一個回流地，訊號位置上限約 150，還不含電源和保留區。 請重算一次，將一項輸入改變 10%，並指出此近似與本單元證據的關係。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. Challenge the hypothesis \"Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition. Original example: A 10 mm shoreline at 50 μm pitch permits an ideal 200 positions in one row. If one of every four is ground, signals are at most about 150 before power/keep-outs. Recalculate, vary one input by 10%, and relate the approximation to this unit’s evidence.","observation":"計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付供電降壓的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for power drop: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-18-k1","title":"供電降壓：機制","titleEn":"Power drop: mechanism","text":"高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。","textEn":"Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-18-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。 必須排除的錯判：信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. Misinterpretation to reject: Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-18-k3","title":"明示假設的量化算例","titleEn":"Quantitative example with explicit assumptions","text":"假設可用邊長 10 mm、I/O 節距 50 μm、單列配置，理想最多 200 個位置；若每四位置需一個回流地，訊號位置上限約 150，還不含電源和保留區。","textEn":"A 10 mm shoreline at 50 μm pitch permits an ideal 200 positions in one row. If one of every four is ground, signals are at most about 150 before power/keep-outs."}],"quiz":{"question":"在「供電降壓」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For power drop — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力","幾何位置數等於全部可用訊號數","計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes","Equating geometric positions with signal count","Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"高密度訊號布線不可侵占必要供電截面。 計算最遠節點 IR drop 和回路電感。 因此不能採用「信號 DRC 通過即可忽略供電能力」。","explanationEn":"Dense signal routes must preserve power cross-section. Calculate far-node IR drop and loop inductance. Therefore reject: Ignoring power capacity after signal DRC passes."}}]},{"id":"a125-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"簽核與整合","titleEn":"Signoff and integration","description":"針對簽核與整合完成三個專屬技術單元；每個單元包含物理分析與量測診斷兩步。","descriptionEn":"Three dedicated units for signoff and integration, each with physical analysis and measurement diagnosis.","steps":[{"id":"a125-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-18"],"title":"光罩與拼接｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Reticle and stitching | mechanism and design","objective":"針對光罩與拼接，把「大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reticle and stitching, turn \"Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「光罩與拼接」的模型：大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for reticle and stitching: Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating seams as drawing-only issues. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光罩與拼接的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for reticle and stitching, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-19-k1","title":"光罩與拼接：機制","titleEn":"Reticle and stitching: mechanism","text":"大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。","textEn":"Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-19-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。 必須排除的錯判：接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating seams as drawing-only issues. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光罩與拼接」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reticle and stitching — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。","接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性","增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線"],"optionsEn":["Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks.","Treating seams as drawing-only issues","Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost"],"answer":0,"explanation":"大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。 在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。 因此不能採用「接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性」。","explanationEn":"Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks. Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. Therefore reject: Treating seams as drawing-only issues."}},{"id":"a125-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-19"],"title":"光罩與拼接｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Reticle and stitching | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對光罩與拼接，把「大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For reticle and stitching, turn \"Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。 將「接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating seams as drawing-only issues\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating seams as drawing-only issues. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付光罩與拼接的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for reticle and stitching: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-20-k1","title":"光罩與拼接：機制","titleEn":"Reticle and stitching: mechanism","text":"大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。","textEn":"Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-20-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。 必須排除的錯判：接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating seams as drawing-only issues. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「光罩與拼接」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For reticle and stitching — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["增加金屬層總能無代價解決布線","在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。","接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性"],"optionsEn":["Assuming extra metal layers solve routing without cost","Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams.","Treating seams as drawing-only issues"],"answer":1,"explanation":"大尺寸中介層可能需跨曝光場連線驗證。 在接縫放置電阻與套刻見證。 因此不能採用「接縫只是圖面問題不影響電性」。","explanationEn":"Large interposers may require cross-field continuity checks. Put resistance/overlay witnesses at seams. Therefore reject: Treating seams as drawing-only issues."}},{"id":"a125-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-20"],"title":"製造測試｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Manufacturing test | mechanism and design","objective":"針對製造測試，把「短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For manufacturing test, turn \"Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「製造測試」的模型：短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for manufacturing test: Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付製造測試的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for manufacturing test, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-21-k1","title":"製造測試：機制","titleEn":"Manufacturing test: mechanism","text":"短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。","textEn":"Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-21-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。 必須排除的錯判：導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. Misinterpretation to reject: Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「製造測試」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For manufacturing test — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效","最細線寬總最節能","短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。"],"optionsEn":["Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure","Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient","Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。 比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。 因此不能採用「導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效」。","explanationEn":"Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures. Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. Therefore reject: Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure."}},{"id":"a125-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-21"],"title":"製造測試｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Manufacturing test | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對製造測試，把「短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For manufacturing test, turn \"Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。 將「導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. Challenge the hypothesis \"Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付製造測試的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for manufacturing test: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-22-k1","title":"製造測試：機制","titleEn":"Manufacturing test: mechanism","text":"短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。","textEn":"Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-22-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。 必須排除的錯判：導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. Misinterpretation to reject: Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「製造測試」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For manufacturing test — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。","導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效","最細線寬總最節能"],"optionsEn":["Compare chains, combs and RF coupons.","Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure","Assuming minimum width is always most energy-efficient"],"answer":0,"explanation":"短路、開路及寄生偏離需要不同測試結構。 比較菊鍊、梳齒和 RF coupon。 因此不能採用「導通測試即可覆蓋全部互連失效」。","explanationEn":"Shorts, opens and parasitic deviations need different structures. Compare chains, combs and RF coupons. Therefore reject: Using continuity to cover every interconnect failure."}},{"id":"a125-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-22"],"title":"共同簽核｜機制與設計","titleEn":"Co-signoff | mechanism and design","objective":"針對共同簽核，把「中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For co-signoff, turn \"Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"本步先建立「共同簽核」的模型：中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。 在剖面或資料表中標出控制量、受影響量和交接介面；提出一組只改一項條件的比較，寫出預測方向。用「檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。」規劃模型將如何被推翻；不要把畫得合理當作已經實測。","instructionEn":"Build the model for co-signoff: Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes. Mark controlled quantities, responses and handoff interfaces in a section or data table. Compare two cases changing one condition and predict direction. Use this evidence plan: Check versions and double-counted interfaces. State how the model could be falsified; a plausible drawing is not a measurement.","observation":"檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check versions and double-counted interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating separate simulations as system qualification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付共同簽核的剖面或因果圖、兩組條件比較及一項可否定預測的量測；標出單位、基準與前後站接口。","checkEn":"Submit a section/causal diagram for co-signoff, a two-case comparison and one falsifying measurement; include units, datums and upstream/downstream interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-23-k1","title":"共同簽核：機制","titleEn":"Co-signoff: mechanism","text":"中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。","textEn":"Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-23-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。 必須排除的錯判：各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check versions and double-counted interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating separate simulations as system qualification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共同簽核」的機制與設計中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For co-signoff — mechanism and design — which decision or action is justified?","options":["差分訊號完全不需地參考","中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。","各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格"],"optionsEn":["Assuming differential signals need no ground reference","Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes.","Treating separate simulations as system qualification"],"answer":1,"explanation":"中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。 檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。 因此不能採用「各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格」。","explanationEn":"Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes. Check versions and double-counted interfaces. Therefore reject: Treating separate simulations as system qualification."}},{"id":"a125-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"],"prerequisiteIds":["a125-v9-23"],"title":"共同簽核｜證據與診斷","titleEn":"Co-signoff | evidence and diagnosis","objective":"針對共同簽核，把「中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。」轉成可驗證的工程判定，明確列出適用範圍與未知量。","objectiveEn":"For co-signoff, turn \"Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes.\" into a testable engineering decision with explicit bounds and unknowns.","instruction":"以先前模型進行證據審查：檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。 將「各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格」當作待否定假說，另提出一項可能造成相同表象的混淆因素。安排對照樣本、座標和重複量測，分開記錄觀察值與機制推論；指出哪個結果會讓你暫停放行。","instructionEn":"Review the preceding model with evidence: Check versions and double-counted interfaces. Challenge the hypothesis \"Treating separate simulations as system qualification\" and name another mechanism that could give the same appearance. Plan controls, sampling coordinates and repeated measurements; separate observations from inference and identify a hold condition.","observation":"檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。 請分開列出符合預測與不符合預測的位置或樣本。","observationEn":"Check versions and double-counted interfaces. Report locations or samples agreeing and disagreeing with the prediction separately.","failure":"避免：各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格。先檢查是否混用基準、忽略局部差異或超出模型範圍，再以本單元量測區分機制。","failureEn":"Avoid: Treating separate simulations as system qualification. Check for mixed references, missed local variation or extrapolation before using this unit’s measurements to distinguish mechanisms.","check":"交付共同簽核的證據表：原始觀察、兩個競爭假說、對照方法、不確定度與接受／暫緩條件；至少一項證據須獨立於主要讀值。","checkEn":"Submit evidence for co-signoff: observations, two competing hypotheses, controls, uncertainty and accept/hold criteria, including one observation independent of the main reading.","knowledge":[{"id":"a125-v9-24-k1","title":"共同簽核：機制","titleEn":"Co-signoff: mechanism","text":"中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。","textEn":"Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]},{"id":"a125-v9-24-k2","title":"量測與錯判分辨","titleEn":"Measurement and discrimination","text":"檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。 必須排除的錯判：各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格。量測解析度、重複性與系統偏差分別列示；不同方法看到的範圍不可默認相同。","textEn":"Check versions and double-counted interfaces. Misinterpretation to reject: Treating separate simulations as system qualification. Report resolution, repeatability and systematic bias separately; different methods do not automatically cover the same domain.","sourceIds":["v9a-imec3d","v9a-intelpack"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共同簽核」的證據與診斷中，哪一項判斷或行動有充分依據？","questionEn":"For co-signoff — evidence and diagnosis — which decision or action is justified?","options":["各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格","差分訊號完全不需地參考","檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。"],"optionsEn":["Treating separate simulations as system qualification","Assuming differential signals need no ground reference","Check versions and double-counted interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中介層、晶粒及封裝模型需相同端口與參考面。 檢查模型版本及重複計算界面。 因此不能採用「各自模擬合格可直接視為整機合格」。","explanationEn":"Interposer, die and package models need consistent ports/reference planes. Check versions and double-counted interfaces. Therefore reject: Treating separate simulations as system qualification."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-substrates","subcategoryTitle":"中介層與封裝基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interposers and package substrates","photoId":"v9-quilt-array"},{"id":"a126","title":"有機中介層製作","titleEn":"Organic-interposer fabrication","category":"packaging","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 步深入有機中介層 RDL、回流與機械順應性；每個技術單元分為建模與證據驗證，包含可重算的教學算例、失效辨識及相關工法。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 steps examine organic-interposer rdl, returns and mechanical compliance. Each technical unit separates modeling from evidence validation, with reproducible teaching examples, failure diagnosis and related methods.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"公開資料支持的原理與工程判讀課；24 步是學習拆解，不是工廠完整 SOP。數值均為明示假設的教學例；實際材料、設備、驗收門檻須依專案規格。有機中介層不是單一材料或通用製程；公開 CoWoS-R 案例僅示範架構，尺寸與可靠度資料不得外推全部供應商。","scopeEn":"A principles and engineering-interpretation course grounded in public material. The 24 steps are an educational decomposition, not a complete factory SOP. Numbers are labeled hypothetical; actual materials, equipment and acceptance limits require project specifications. Organic interposers are not one material or universal process; public CoWoS-R examples illustrate architecture, not universal geometry or reliability.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["架構與層疊","介電與佈線","翹曲與介面","整合與驗收"],"labelsEn":["Architecture and stack-up","Dielectrics and routing","Warpage and interfaces","Integration and acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a126-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"架構與層疊","titleEn":"Architecture and stack-up","description":"本階段處理架構與層疊：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address architecture and stack-up through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a126-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"劃分晶粒與中介層","titleEn":"Partition dies and interposer","objective":"建立「劃分晶粒與中介層」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for partition dies and interposer: An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「劃分晶粒與中介層」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for partition dies and interposer actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition.","check":"交付「劃分晶粒與中介層」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for partition dies and interposer, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-01-k1","title":"劃分晶粒與中介層：機制","titleEn":"Partition dies and interposer: mechanism","text":"中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。","textEn":"An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-01-k2","title":"劃分晶粒與中介層：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Partition dies and interposer: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「劃分晶粒與中介層」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for partition dies and interposer?","options":["RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。 畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。","explanationEn":"An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition. Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels."}},{"id":"a126-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-01"],"title":"劃分晶粒與中介層：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Partition dies and interposer: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「劃分晶粒與中介層」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the partition dies and interposer model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「劃分晶粒與中介層」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for partition dies and interposer actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition.","check":"交付「劃分晶粒與中介層」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for partition dies and interposer: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-02-k1","title":"劃分晶粒與中介層：機制","titleEn":"Partition dies and interposer: mechanism","text":"中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。","textEn":"An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-02-k2","title":"劃分晶粒與中介層：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Partition dies and interposer: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「劃分晶粒與中介層：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for partition dies and interposer: challenge and acceptance?","options":["有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。"],"optionsEn":["Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels."],"answer":2,"explanation":"中介層把高密度晶粒互連轉接到較大尺度封裝，需定義兩端焊墊。 畫出晶粒、RDL、C4 及基板的層次。","explanationEn":"An interposer translates dense die connections to package scale; both pad interfaces need definition. Draw die, RDL, C4 and substrate levels."}},{"id":"a126-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-02"],"title":"設定層疊與回流","titleEn":"Set stack-up and returns","objective":"建立「設定層疊與回流」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for set stack-up and returns: Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。標每層信號與接地用途。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Label signal and ground roles for each layer. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：標每層信號與接地用途。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Label signal and ground roles for each layer. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「設定層疊與回流」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for set stack-up and returns actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer.","check":"交付「設定層疊與回流」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for set stack-up and returns, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-03-k1","title":"設定層疊與回流：機制","titleEn":"Set stack-up and returns: mechanism","text":"每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。","textEn":"Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-03-k2","title":"設定層疊與回流：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Set stack-up and returns: evidence and interpretation","text":"標每層信號與接地用途。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Label signal and ground roles for each layer. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設定層疊與回流」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for set stack-up and returns?","options":["每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性"],"optionsEn":["Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。 標每層信號與接地用途。","explanationEn":"Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer. Label signal and ground roles for each layer."}},{"id":"a126-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-03"],"title":"設定層疊與回流：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Set stack-up and returns: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「設定層疊與回流」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the set stack-up and returns model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。標每層信號與接地用途。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Label signal and ground roles for each layer. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：標每層信號與接地用途。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Label signal and ground roles for each layer. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「設定層疊與回流」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for set stack-up and returns actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer.","check":"交付「設定層疊與回流」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for set stack-up and returns: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-04-k1","title":"設定層疊與回流：機制","titleEn":"Set stack-up and returns: mechanism","text":"每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。","textEn":"Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-04-k2","title":"設定層疊與回流：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Set stack-up and returns: evidence and interpretation","text":"標每層信號與接地用途。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Label signal and ground roles for each layer. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設定層疊與回流：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for set stack-up and returns: challenge and acceptance?","options":["RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","標每層信號與接地用途。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Label signal and ground roles for each layer.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"每條高速訊號需要連續回流，不能只有信號層而無參考。 標每層信號與接地用途。","explanationEn":"Every fast signal needs a continuous return, not only a signal layer. Label signal and ground roles for each layer."}},{"id":"a126-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-04"],"title":"分配逃線區域","titleEn":"Allocate escape routing","objective":"建立「分配逃線區域」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for allocate escape routing: Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「分配逃線區域」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for allocate escape routing actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability.","check":"交付「分配逃線區域」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for allocate escape routing, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-05-k1","title":"分配逃線區域：機制","titleEn":"Allocate escape routing: mechanism","text":"焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。","textEn":"Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-05-k2","title":"分配逃線區域：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Allocate escape routing: evidence and interpretation","text":"選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分配逃線區域」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for allocate escape routing?","options":["有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。"],"optionsEn":["Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。 選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。","explanationEn":"Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability. Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge."}},{"id":"a126-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-05"],"title":"分配逃線區域：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Allocate escape routing: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「分配逃線區域」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the allocate escape routing model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「分配逃線區域」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for allocate escape routing actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability.","check":"交付「分配逃線區域」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for allocate escape routing: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-06-k1","title":"分配逃線區域：機制","titleEn":"Allocate escape routing: mechanism","text":"焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。","textEn":"Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-06-k2","title":"分配逃線區域：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Allocate escape routing: evidence and interpretation","text":"選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分配逃線區域：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for allocate escape routing: challenge and acceptance?","options":["選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性"],"optionsEn":["Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"焊墊陣列、過孔與線距共同限制可佈線性。 選一個晶粒角落完整逃線至中介層邊緣。","explanationEn":"Pad arrays, vias and spacing jointly limit routability. Route one die corner fully to the interposer edge."}}]},{"id":"a126-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"介電與佈線","titleEn":"Dielectrics and routing","description":"本階段處理介電與佈線：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address dielectrics and routing through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a126-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-06"],"title":"選擇介電材料","titleEn":"Select dielectric materials","objective":"建立「選擇介電材料」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for select dielectric materials: Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。建立電性與機械性能雙表。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：建立電性與機械性能雙表。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「選擇介電材料」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for select dielectric materials actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables.","check":"交付「選擇介電材料」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for select dielectric materials, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-07-k1","title":"選擇介電材料：機制","titleEn":"Select dielectric materials: mechanism","text":"介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。","textEn":"Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-07-k2","title":"選擇介電材料：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Select dielectric materials: evidence and interpretation","text":"建立電性與機械性能雙表。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「選擇介電材料」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for select dielectric materials?","options":["RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。 建立電性與機械性能雙表。","explanationEn":"Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables. Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables."}},{"id":"a126-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-07"],"title":"選擇介電材料：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Select dielectric materials: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「選擇介電材料」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the select dielectric materials model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。建立電性與機械性能雙表。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：建立電性與機械性能雙表。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「選擇介電材料」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for select dielectric materials actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables.","check":"交付「選擇介電材料」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for select dielectric materials: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-08-k1","title":"選擇介電材料：機制","titleEn":"Select dielectric materials: mechanism","text":"介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。","textEn":"Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-08-k2","title":"選擇介電材料：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Select dielectric materials: evidence and interpretation","text":"建立電性與機械性能雙表。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「選擇介電材料：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for select dielectric materials: challenge and acceptance?","options":["有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","建立電性與機械性能雙表。"],"optionsEn":["Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables."],"answer":2,"explanation":"介電常數、損耗、吸濕與 CTE 是不同設計變數。 建立電性與機械性能雙表。","explanationEn":"Permittivity, loss, moisture uptake and CTE are distinct variables. Build separate electrical and mechanical property tables."}},{"id":"a126-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-08"],"title":"估算銅線電阻","titleEn":"Estimate copper resistance","objective":"建立「估算銅線電阻」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for estimate copper resistance: Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。\n\n假設銅線長 5 mm、寬 10 μm、厚 5 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm，R=ρL/(wt)=1.7 Ω；0.1 A 時 DC 壓降 0.17 V。窄線溫升、接點及 AC 效應尚未計入。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.\n\nFor hypothetical copper length 5 mm, width 10 μm, thickness 5 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm, R=1.7 Ω; at 0.1 A DC drop is 0.17 V. Heating, contacts and AC effects are excluded.","observation":"觀察焦點：重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「估算銅線電阻」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for estimate copper resistance actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing.","check":"交付「估算銅線電阻」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for estimate copper resistance, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-09-k1","title":"估算銅線電阻：機制","titleEn":"Estimate copper resistance: mechanism","text":"窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。","textEn":"Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-09-k2","title":"估算銅線電阻：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Estimate copper resistance: evidence and interpretation","text":"重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-09-k3","title":"自訂算例與模型界限","titleEn":"Hypothetical worked example and model boundary","text":"假設銅線長 5 mm、寬 10 μm、厚 5 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm，R=ρL/(wt)=1.7 Ω；0.1 A 時 DC 壓降 0.17 V。窄線溫升、接點及 AC 效應尚未計入。 有機中介層不是單一材料或通用製程；公開 CoWoS-R 案例僅示範架構，尺寸與可靠度資料不得外推全部供應商。","textEn":"For hypothetical copper length 5 mm, width 10 μm, thickness 5 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm, R=1.7 Ω; at 0.1 A DC drop is 0.17 V. Heating, contacts and AC effects are excluded. Organic interposers are not one material or universal process; public CoWoS-R examples illustrate architecture, not universal geometry or reliability.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「估算銅線電阻」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for estimate copper resistance?","options":["窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性"],"optionsEn":["Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。 重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。","explanationEn":"Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing. Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness."}},{"id":"a126-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-09"],"title":"估算銅線電阻：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Estimate copper resistance: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「估算銅線電阻」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the estimate copper resistance model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。\n\n假設銅線長 5 mm、寬 10 μm、厚 5 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm，R=ρL/(wt)=1.7 Ω；0.1 A 時 DC 壓降 0.17 V。窄線溫升、接點及 AC 效應尚未計入。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.\n\nFor hypothetical copper length 5 mm, width 10 μm, thickness 5 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm, R=1.7 Ω; at 0.1 A DC drop is 0.17 V. Heating, contacts and AC effects are excluded.","observation":"觀察焦點：重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「估算銅線電阻」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for estimate copper resistance actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing.","check":"交付「估算銅線電阻」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for estimate copper resistance: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-10-k1","title":"估算銅線電阻：機制","titleEn":"Estimate copper resistance: mechanism","text":"窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。","textEn":"Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-10-k2","title":"估算銅線電阻：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Estimate copper resistance: evidence and interpretation","text":"重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-10-k3","title":"自訂算例與模型界限","titleEn":"Hypothetical worked example and model boundary","text":"假設銅線長 5 mm、寬 10 μm、厚 5 μm、ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm，R=ρL/(wt)=1.7 Ω；0.1 A 時 DC 壓降 0.17 V。窄線溫升、接點及 AC 效應尚未計入。 有機中介層不是單一材料或通用製程；公開 CoWoS-R 案例僅示範架構，尺寸與可靠度資料不得外推全部供應商。","textEn":"For hypothetical copper length 5 mm, width 10 μm, thickness 5 μm and ρ=1.7×10⁻⁸ Ωm, R=1.7 Ω; at 0.1 A DC drop is 0.17 V. Heating, contacts and AC effects are excluded. Organic interposers are not one material or universal process; public CoWoS-R examples illustrate architecture, not universal geometry or reliability.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「估算銅線電阻：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for estimate copper resistance: challenge and acceptance?","options":["RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"窄長 RDL 可有顯著 DC 壓降，即使晶粒間距看似很短。 重算 1.7 Ω 範例並將厚度加倍。","explanationEn":"Long narrow RDL can create appreciable DC drop despite short die spacing. Recalculate 1.7 Ω and double thickness."}},{"id":"a126-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-10"],"title":"檢查過孔轉接","titleEn":"Check via transitions","objective":"建立「檢查過孔轉接」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for check via transitions: Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Trace signal and return transitions in a section. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Trace signal and return transitions in a section. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「檢查過孔轉接」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for check via transitions actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity.","check":"交付「檢查過孔轉接」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for check via transitions, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-11-k1","title":"檢查過孔轉接：機制","titleEn":"Check via transitions: mechanism","text":"過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。","textEn":"Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-11-k2","title":"檢查過孔轉接：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Check via transitions: evidence and interpretation","text":"用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Trace signal and return transitions in a section. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「檢查過孔轉接」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for check via transitions?","options":["有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。"],"optionsEn":["Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。 用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。","explanationEn":"Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity. Trace signal and return transitions in a section."}},{"id":"a126-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-11"],"title":"檢查過孔轉接：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Check via transitions: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「檢查過孔轉接」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the check via transitions model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Trace signal and return transitions in a section. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Trace signal and return transitions in a section. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「檢查過孔轉接」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for check via transitions actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity.","check":"交付「檢查過孔轉接」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for check via transitions: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-12-k1","title":"檢查過孔轉接：機制","titleEn":"Check via transitions: mechanism","text":"過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。","textEn":"Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-12-k2","title":"檢查過孔轉接：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Check via transitions: evidence and interpretation","text":"用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Trace signal and return transitions in a section. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「檢查過孔轉接：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for check via transitions: challenge and acceptance?","options":["用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性"],"optionsEn":["Trace signal and return transitions in a section.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"過孔電感、焊墊電容及回流中斷形成聯合不連續。 用剖面追蹤信號及回流換層。","explanationEn":"Via inductance, pad capacitance and return interruption form a combined discontinuity. Trace signal and return transitions in a section."}}]},{"id":"a126-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"翹曲與介面","titleEn":"Warpage and interfaces","description":"本階段處理翹曲與介面：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address warpage and interfaces through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a126-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-12"],"title":"分析順應性","titleEn":"Analyze compliance","objective":"建立「分析順應性」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for analyze compliance: Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「分析順應性」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for analyze compliance actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation.","check":"交付「分析順應性」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for analyze compliance, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-13-k1","title":"分析順應性：機制","titleEn":"Analyze compliance: mechanism","text":"聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。","textEn":"Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-13-k2","title":"分析順應性：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Analyze compliance: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分析順應性」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for analyze compliance?","options":["RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。 比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。","explanationEn":"Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation. Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers."}},{"id":"a126-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-13"],"title":"分析順應性：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Analyze compliance: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「分析順應性」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the analyze compliance model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「分析順應性」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for analyze compliance actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation.","check":"交付「分析順應性」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for analyze compliance: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-14-k1","title":"分析順應性：機制","titleEn":"Analyze compliance: mechanism","text":"聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。","textEn":"Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-14-k2","title":"分析順應性：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Analyze compliance: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分析順應性：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for analyze compliance: challenge and acceptance?","options":["有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。"],"optionsEn":["Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"聚合物可分散某些應力，但也帶來蠕變和翹曲變化。 比較剛性與順應中介層的受力路徑。","explanationEn":"Polymers redistribute some stress but introduce creep and warpage variation. Compare load paths in rigid and compliant interposers."}},{"id":"a126-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-14"],"title":"控制銅分布平衡","titleEn":"Balance copper distribution","objective":"建立「控制銅分布平衡」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for balance copper distribution: Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「控制銅分布平衡」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for balance copper distribution actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments.","check":"交付「控制銅分布平衡」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for balance copper distribution, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-15-k1","title":"控制銅分布平衡：機制","titleEn":"Balance copper distribution: mechanism","text":"不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。","textEn":"Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-15-k2","title":"控制銅分布平衡：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Balance copper distribution: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制銅分布平衡」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for balance copper distribution?","options":["不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性"],"optionsEn":["Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。 比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。","explanationEn":"Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments. Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane."}},{"id":"a126-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-15"],"title":"控制銅分布平衡：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Balance copper distribution: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「控制銅分布平衡」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the balance copper distribution model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「控制銅分布平衡」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for balance copper distribution actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments.","check":"交付「控制銅分布平衡」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for balance copper distribution: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-16-k1","title":"控制銅分布平衡：機制","titleEn":"Balance copper distribution: mechanism","text":"不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。","textEn":"Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-16-k2","title":"控制銅分布平衡：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Balance copper distribution: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制銅分布平衡：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for balance copper distribution: challenge and acceptance?","options":["RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力"],"optionsEn":["Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不對稱金屬密度可改變熱膨脹彎矩。 比較兩層銅覆蓋率及中性面。","explanationEn":"Asymmetric metal density can change thermal bending moments. Compare copper coverage and the neutral plane."}},{"id":"a126-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-16"],"title":"判讀 C4 接點應變","titleEn":"Interpret C4 strain","objective":"建立「判讀 C4 接點應變」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：中介層柔性與底填會重新分配 C4 應變，不能只看 CTE 差值。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for interpret c4 strain: Interposer compliance and underfill redistribute C4 strain; CTE difference alone is insufficient.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。標出角落接點及約束。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Mark corner joints and constraints. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：標出角落接點及約束。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Mark corner joints and constraints. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「判讀 C4 接點應變」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到中介層柔性與底填會重新分配 C4 應變，不能只看 CTE 差值。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for interpret c4 strain actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Interposer compliance and underfill redistribute C4 strain; CTE difference alone is insufficient.","check":"交付「判讀 C4 接點應變」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for interpret c4 strain, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-17-k1","title":"判讀 C4 接點應變：機制","titleEn":"Interpret C4 strain: mechanism","text":"中介層柔性與底填會重新分配 C4 應變，不能只看 CTE 差值。","textEn":"Interposer compliance and underfill redistribute C4 strain; CTE difference alone is insufficient.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-17-k2","title":"判讀 C4 接點應變：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Interpret C4 strain: evidence and interpretation","text":"標出角落接點及約束。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Mark corner joints and constraints. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「判讀 C4 接點應變」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for interpret c4 strain?","options":["有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","中介層柔性與底填會重新分配 C4 應變，不能只看 CTE 差值。"],"optionsEn":["Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed 