 local warpage.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress"],"answer":1,"explanation":"電性菊鏈、熱循環及界面影像提供互補資訊。 配準失效位置與局部翹曲。","explanationEn":"Daisy chains, thermal cycling and interface images provide complementary evidence. Register failure locations with local warpage."}},{"id":"a126-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-22"],"title":"完成中介層交接","titleEn":"Complete interposer handoff","objective":"建立「完成中介層交接」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for complete interposer handoff: Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力。本步先檢查「完成中介層交接」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress. First check whether evidence for complete interposer handoff actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range.","check":"交付「完成中介層交接」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for complete interposer handoff, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-23-k1","title":"完成中介層交接：機制","titleEn":"Complete interposer handoff: mechanism","text":"交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。","textEn":"Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-23-k2","title":"完成中介層交接：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Complete interposer handoff: evidence and interpretation","text":"列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「完成中介層交接」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for complete interposer handoff?","options":["有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性","交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity","Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range."],"answer":2,"explanation":"交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。 列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。","explanationEn":"Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range. List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams."}},{"id":"a126-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"],"prerequisiteIds":["a126-v9-23"],"title":"完成中介層交接：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Complete interposer handoff: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「完成中介層交接」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the complete interposer handoff model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性。本步先檢查「完成中介層交接」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity. First check whether evidence for complete interposer handoff actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range.","check":"交付「完成中介層交接」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for complete interposer handoff: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a126-v9-24-k1","title":"完成中介層交接：機制","titleEn":"Complete interposer handoff: mechanism","text":"交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。","textEn":"Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]},{"id":"a126-v9-24-k2","title":"完成中介層交接：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Complete interposer handoff: evidence and interpretation","text":"列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["pkb-tsmc-cowos","v9at-tsmc-organic","v9at-ti-pdn"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「完成中介層交接：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for complete interposer handoff: challenge and acceptance?","options":["列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。","有機材料柔軟所以沒有熱應力","RDL 線距夠小就保證高速訊號完整性"],"optionsEn":["List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams.","Organic compliance eliminates all thermal stress","Fine RDL spacing guarantees high-speed integrity"],"answer":0,"explanation":"交付需層疊、焊墊圖、材料版本、模型與驗證範圍。 列明不能由公開架構圖推定的製造參數。","explanationEn":"Handoff needs stack-up, pad map, material version, models and validation range. List manufacturing parameters not inferable from public architecture diagrams."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-substrates","subcategoryTitle":"中介層與封裝基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interposers and package substrates","photoId":"bga-section"},{"id":"a127","title":"玻璃核心封裝基板","titleEn":"Glass-core package substrates","category":"packaging","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 步深入玻璃核心平整度、TGV 與脆裂風險；每個技術單元分為建模與證據驗證，包含可重算的教學算例、失效辨識及相關工法。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 steps examine glass-core flatness, tgvs and brittle-fracture risk. Each technical unit separates modeling from evidence validation, with reproducible teaching examples, failure diagnosis and related methods.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"公開資料支持的原理與工程判讀課；24 步是學習拆解，不是工廠完整 SOP。數值均為明示假設的教學例；實際材料、設備、驗收門檻須依專案規格。公開測試載具展示不能等同所有玻璃核心方案已量產；材料組成、TGV 幾何與電性需個別驗證。","scopeEn":"A principles and engineering-interpretation course grounded in public material. The 24 steps are an educational decomposition, not a complete factory SOP. Numbers are labeled hypothetical; actual materials, equipment and acceptance limits require project specifications. A public test-vehicle demonstration does not establish production status for every glass-core solution; composition, TGV geometry and electrical behavior require validation.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["玻璃核心角色","TGV 與金屬化","翹曲與缺陷","整合與證據"],"labelsEn":["Glass-core role","TGV and metallization","Warpage and defects","Integration and evidence"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a127-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"玻璃核心角色","titleEn":"Glass-core role","description":"本階段處理玻璃核心角色：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address glass-core role through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a127-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"定義核心與增層","titleEn":"Define core and build-up","objective":"建立「定義核心與增層」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for define core and build-up: The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。將核心和增層分色標示。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Color core and build-up separately. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：將核心和增層分色標示。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Color core and build-up separately. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「定義核心與增層」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for define core and build-up actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing.","check":"交付「定義核心與增層」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for define core and build-up, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-01-k1","title":"定義核心與增層：機制","titleEn":"Define core and build-up: mechanism","text":"核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。","textEn":"The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-01-k2","title":"定義核心與增層：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Define core and build-up: evidence and interpretation","text":"將核心和增層分色標示。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Color core and build-up separately. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「定義核心與增層」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for define core and build-up?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。 將核心和增層分色標示。","explanationEn":"The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing. Color core and build-up separately."}},{"id":"a127-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-01"],"title":"定義核心與增層：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Define core and build-up: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「定義核心與增層」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the define core and build-up model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。將核心和增層分色標示。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Color core and build-up separately. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：將核心和增層分色標示。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Color core and build-up separately. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「定義核心與增層」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for define core and build-up actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing.","check":"交付「定義核心與增層」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for define core and build-up: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-02-k1","title":"定義核心與增層：機制","titleEn":"Define core and build-up: mechanism","text":"核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。","textEn":"The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-02-k2","title":"定義核心與增層：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Define core and build-up: evidence and interpretation","text":"將核心和增層分色標示。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Color core and build-up separately. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「定義核心與增層：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for define core and build-up: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","將核心和增層分色標示。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Color core and build-up separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核心負責機械支撐及穿通，外側增層負責細密佈線。 將核心和增層分色標示。","explanationEn":"The core supports mechanics and through-connections; outer build-up handles fine routing. Color core and build-up separately."}},{"id":"a127-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-02"],"title":"比較玻璃材料族","titleEn":"Compare glass families","objective":"建立「比較玻璃材料族」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for compare glass families: Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Avoid using one glass value for every formulation. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Avoid using one glass value for every formulation. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「比較玻璃材料族」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for compare glass families actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition.","check":"交付「比較玻璃材料族」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for compare glass families, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-03-k1","title":"比較玻璃材料族：機制","titleEn":"Compare glass families: mechanism","text":"玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。","textEn":"Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-03-k2","title":"比較玻璃材料族：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Compare glass families: evidence and interpretation","text":"不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Avoid using one glass value for every formulation. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「比較玻璃材料族」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for compare glass families?","options":["玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。 不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。","explanationEn":"Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition. Avoid using one glass value for every formulation."}},{"id":"a127-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-03"],"title":"比較玻璃材料族：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Compare glass families: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「比較玻璃材料族」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the compare glass families model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Avoid using one glass value for every formulation. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Avoid using one glass value for every formulation. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「比較玻璃材料族」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for compare glass families actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition.","check":"交付「比較玻璃材料族」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for compare glass families: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-04-k1","title":"比較玻璃材料族：機制","titleEn":"Compare glass families: mechanism","text":"玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。","textEn":"Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-04-k2","title":"比較玻璃材料族：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Compare glass families: evidence and interpretation","text":"不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Avoid using one glass value for every formulation. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「比較玻璃材料族：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for compare glass families: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Avoid using one glass value for every formulation.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"玻璃的 CTE、損耗、強度及加工性隨組成變化。 不以單一玻璃數值代表所有配方。","explanationEn":"Glass CTE, loss, strength and machinability vary with composition. Avoid using one glass value for every formulation."}},{"id":"a127-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-04"],"title":"建立平整度基準","titleEn":"Establish flatness baseline","objective":"建立「建立平整度基準」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for establish flatness baseline: Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。記錄量測溫度與參考平面。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Record measurement temperature and reference plane. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：記錄量測溫度與參考平面。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Record measurement temperature and reference plane. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「建立平整度基準」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for establish flatness baseline actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands.","check":"交付「建立平整度基準」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for establish flatness baseline, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-05-k1","title":"建立平整度基準：機制","titleEn":"Establish flatness baseline: mechanism","text":"室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。","textEn":"Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-05-k2","title":"建立平整度基準：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Establish flatness baseline: evidence and interpretation","text":"記錄量測溫度與參考平面。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Record measurement temperature and reference plane. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「建立平整度基準」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for establish flatness baseline?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands."],"answer":2,"explanation":"室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。 記錄量測溫度與參考平面。","explanationEn":"Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands. Record measurement temperature and reference plane."}},{"id":"a127-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-05"],"title":"建立平整度基準：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Establish flatness baseline: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「建立平整度基準」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the establish flatness baseline model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。記錄量測溫度與參考平面。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Record measurement temperature and reference plane. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：記錄量測溫度與參考平面。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Record measurement temperature and reference plane. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「建立平整度基準」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for establish flatness baseline actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands.","check":"交付「建立平整度基準」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for establish flatness baseline: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-06-k1","title":"建立平整度基準：機制","titleEn":"Establish flatness baseline: mechanism","text":"室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。","textEn":"Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-06-k2","title":"建立平整度基準：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Establish flatness baseline: evidence and interpretation","text":"記錄量測溫度與參考平面。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Record measurement temperature and reference plane. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「建立平整度基準：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for establish flatness baseline: challenge and acceptance?","options":["記錄量測溫度與參考平面。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Record measurement temperature and reference plane.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"室溫平整度和熱態翹曲是不同量，量測尺度也不同。 記錄量測溫度與參考平面。","explanationEn":"Room-temperature flatness and hot warpage are different measurands. Record measurement temperature and reference plane."}}]},{"id":"a127-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"TGV 與金屬化","titleEn":"TGV and metallization","description":"本階段處理TGV 與金屬化：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address tgv and metallization through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a127-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-06"],"title":"規劃 TGV 幾何","titleEn":"Plan TGV geometry","objective":"建立「規劃 TGV 幾何」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for plan tgv geometry: Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「規劃 TGV 幾何」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for plan tgv geometry actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength.","check":"交付「規劃 TGV 幾何」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for plan tgv geometry, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-07-k1","title":"規劃 TGV 幾何：機制","titleEn":"Plan TGV geometry: mechanism","text":"孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。","textEn":"Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-07-k2","title":"規劃 TGV 幾何：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Plan TGV geometry: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規劃 TGV 幾何」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for plan tgv geometry?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。 畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。","explanationEn":"Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength. Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance."}},{"id":"a127-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-07"],"title":"規劃 TGV 幾何：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Plan TGV geometry: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「規劃 TGV 幾何」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the plan tgv geometry model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「規劃 TGV 幾何」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for plan tgv geometry actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength.","check":"交付「規劃 TGV 幾何」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for plan tgv geometry: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-08-k1","title":"規劃 TGV 幾何：機制","titleEn":"Plan TGV geometry: mechanism","text":"孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。","textEn":"Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-08-k2","title":"規劃 TGV 幾何：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Plan TGV geometry: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規劃 TGV 幾何：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for plan tgv geometry: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"孔徑、錐度及間距同時限制金屬化與結構強度。 畫出最薄玻璃壁與孔口。","explanationEn":"Diameter, taper and pitch jointly constrain metallization and strength. Draw the thinnest glass web and via entrance."}},{"id":"a127-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-08"],"title":"檢查孔壁損傷","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall damage","objective":"建立「檢查孔壁損傷」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for inspect sidewall damage: Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「檢查孔壁損傷」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for inspect sidewall damage actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads.","check":"交付「檢查孔壁損傷」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for inspect sidewall damage, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-09-k1","title":"檢查孔壁損傷：機制","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall damage: mechanism","text":"加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。","textEn":"Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-09-k2","title":"檢查孔壁損傷：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall damage: evidence and interpretation","text":"區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「檢查孔壁損傷」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for inspect sidewall damage?","options":["加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。 區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。","explanationEn":"Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads. Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips."}},{"id":"a127-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-09"],"title":"檢查孔壁損傷：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall damage: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「檢查孔壁損傷」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the inspect sidewall damage model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「檢查孔壁損傷」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for inspect sidewall damage actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads.","check":"交付「檢查孔壁損傷」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for inspect sidewall damage: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-10-k1","title":"檢查孔壁損傷：機制","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall damage: mechanism","text":"加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。","textEn":"Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-10-k2","title":"檢查孔壁損傷：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Inspect sidewall damage: evidence and interpretation","text":"區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「檢查孔壁損傷：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for inspect sidewall damage: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"加工微裂可能在後續熱或机械負荷下延伸。 區分表面粗糙與裂紋尖端。","explanationEn":"Process microcracks can grow under later thermal or mechanical loads. Distinguish surface roughness from crack tips."}},{"id":"a127-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-10"],"title":"設計金屬化界面","titleEn":"Design metallization interfaces","objective":"建立「設計金屬化界面」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for design metallization interfaces: Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「設計金屬化界面」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for design metallization interfaces actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer.","check":"交付「設計金屬化界面」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for design metallization interfaces, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-11-k1","title":"設計金屬化界面：機制","titleEn":"Design metallization interfaces: mechanism","text":"附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。","textEn":"Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-11-k2","title":"設計金屬化界面：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Design metallization interfaces: evidence and interpretation","text":"將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設計金屬化界面」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for design metallization interfaces?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。 將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。","explanationEn":"Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer. Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately."}},{"id":"a127-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-11"],"title":"設計金屬化界面：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Design metallization interfaces: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「設計金屬化界面」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the design metallization interfaces model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「設計金屬化界面」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for design metallization interfaces actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer.","check":"交付「設計金屬化界面」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for design metallization interfaces: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-12-k1","title":"設計金屬化界面：機制","titleEn":"Design metallization interfaces: mechanism","text":"附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。","textEn":"Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-12-k2","title":"設計金屬化界面：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Design metallization interfaces: evidence and interpretation","text":"將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設計金屬化界面：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for design metallization interfaces: challenge and acceptance?","options":["將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"附著層與銅的界面完整性影響電阻與應力傳遞。 將電氣連續與機械附著分別驗證。","explanationEn":"Adhesion-layer and copper integrity affect resistance and stress transfer. Verify electrical continuity and mechanical adhesion separately."}}]},{"id":"a127-v9-stage03","order":3,"title":"翹曲與缺陷","titleEn":"Warpage and defects","description":"本階段處理翹曲與缺陷：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address warpage and defects through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a127-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-12"],"title":"估算熱失配","titleEn":"Estimate thermal mismatch","objective":"建立「估算熱失配」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for estimate thermal mismatch: Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。\n\n假設玻璃與銅的 CTE 差 12 ppm/K、跨距 10 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差位移為 12 μm；實際應力仍取決於約束、彈性與裂紋缺陷，不能直接由位移得到破壞強度。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.\n\nFor assumed glass-copper CTE difference 12 ppm/K, span 10 mm and ΔT=100 K, free mismatch is 12 μm. Actual stress depends on constraint, elasticity and flaws; displacement is not fracture strength.","observation":"觀察焦點：重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「估算熱失配」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for estimate thermal mismatch actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally.","check":"交付「估算熱失配」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for estimate thermal mismatch, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-13-k1","title":"估算熱失配：機制","titleEn":"Estimate thermal mismatch: mechanism","text":"玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。","textEn":"Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-13-k2","title":"估算熱失配：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Estimate thermal mismatch: evidence and interpretation","text":"重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-13-k3","title":"自訂算例與模型界限","titleEn":"Hypothetical worked example and model boundary","text":"假設玻璃與銅的 CTE 差 12 ppm/K、跨距 10 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差位移為 12 μm；實際應力仍取決於約束、彈性與裂紋缺陷，不能直接由位移得到破壞強度。 公開測試載具展示不能等同所有玻璃核心方案已量產；材料組成、TGV 幾何與電性需個別驗證。","textEn":"For assumed glass-copper CTE difference 12 ppm/K, span 10 mm and ΔT=100 K, free mismatch is 12 μm. Actual stress depends on constraint, elasticity and flaws; displacement is not fracture strength. A public test-vehicle demonstration does not establish production status for every glass-core solution; composition, TGV geometry and electrical behavior require validation.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「估算熱失配」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for estimate thermal mismatch?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。 重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。","explanationEn":"Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally. Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening."}},{"id":"a127-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-13"],"title":"估算熱失配：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Estimate thermal mismatch: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「估算熱失配」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the estimate thermal mismatch model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。\n\n假設玻璃與銅的 CTE 差 12 ppm/K、跨距 10 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差位移為 12 μm；實際應力仍取決於約束、彈性與裂紋缺陷，不能直接由位移得到破壞強度。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.\n\nFor assumed glass-copper CTE difference 12 ppm/K, span 10 mm and ΔT=100 K, free mismatch is 12 μm. Actual stress depends on constraint, elasticity and flaws; displacement is not fracture strength.","observation":"觀察焦點：重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「估算熱失配」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for estimate thermal mismatch actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally.","check":"交付「估算熱失配」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for estimate thermal mismatch: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-14-k1","title":"估算熱失配：機制","titleEn":"Estimate thermal mismatch: mechanism","text":"玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。","textEn":"Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-14-k2","title":"估算熱失配：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Estimate thermal mismatch: evidence and interpretation","text":"重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-14-k3","title":"自訂算例與模型界限","titleEn":"Hypothetical worked example and model boundary","text":"假設玻璃與銅的 CTE 差 12 ppm/K、跨距 10 mm、ΔT=100 K，自由差位移為 12 μm；實際應力仍取決於約束、彈性與裂紋缺陷，不能直接由位移得到破壞強度。 公開測試載具展示不能等同所有玻璃核心方案已量產；材料組成、TGV 幾何與電性需個別驗證。","textEn":"For assumed glass-copper CTE difference 12 ppm/K, span 10 mm and ΔT=100 K, free mismatch is 12 μm. Actual stress depends on constraint, elasticity and flaws; displacement is not fracture strength. A public test-vehicle demonstration does not establish production status for every glass-core solution; composition, TGV geometry and electrical behavior require validation.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「估算熱失配：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for estimate thermal mismatch: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening."],"answer":2,"explanation":"玻璃和銅膨脹不同會在孔口及端面形成局部負荷。 重算 12 μm 差位移並說明不是裂紋張開量。","explanationEn":"Glass-copper mismatch loads via entrances and ends locally. Recalculate 12 μm mismatch and explain why it is not crack opening."}},{"id":"a127-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-14"],"title":"管理邊缘缺陷","titleEn":"Manage edge flaws","objective":"建立「管理邊缘缺陷」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for manage edge flaws: Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Mark supports and potential tensile regions. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Mark supports and potential tensile regions. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「管理邊缘缺陷」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for manage edge flaws actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact.","check":"交付「管理邊缘缺陷」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for manage edge flaws, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-15-k1","title":"管理邊缘缺陷：機制","titleEn":"Manage edge flaws: mechanism","text":"脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。","textEn":"Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-15-k2","title":"管理邊缘缺陷：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Manage edge flaws: evidence and interpretation","text":"標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Mark supports and potential tensile regions. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「管理邊缘缺陷」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for manage edge flaws?","options":["脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。 標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。","explanationEn":"Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact. Mark supports and potential tensile regions."}},{"id":"a127-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-15"],"title":"管理邊缘缺陷：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Manage edge flaws: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「管理邊缘缺陷」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the manage edge flaws model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Mark supports and potential tensile regions. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Mark supports and potential tensile regions. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「管理邊缘缺陷」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for manage edge flaws actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact.","check":"交付「管理邊缘缺陷」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for manage edge flaws: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-16-k1","title":"管理邊缘缺陷：機制","titleEn":"Manage edge flaws: mechanism","text":"脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。","textEn":"Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-16-k2","title":"管理邊缘缺陷：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Manage edge flaws: evidence and interpretation","text":"標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Mark supports and potential tensile regions. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「管理邊缘缺陷：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for manage edge flaws: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Mark supports and potential tensile regions.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"脆性核心對切割邊緣與搬運接觸敏感。 標出搬運支撐點與可能拉應力區。","explanationEn":"Brittle cores are sensitive to diced edges and handling contact. Mark supports and potential tensile regions."}},{"id":"a127-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-16"],"title":"觀察熱態翹曲","titleEn":"Observe hot warpage","objective":"建立「觀察熱態翹曲」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：疊層金屬密度和聚合物固化會影響整包變形。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for observe hot warpage: Metal distribution and polymer cure affect package warpage.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。比較升溫與降溫曲線是否遲滯。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Compare heating and cooling curves for hysteresis. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較升溫與降溫曲線是否遲滯。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare heating and cooling curves for hysteresis. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「觀察熱態翹曲」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到疊層金屬密度和聚合物固化會影響整包變形。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for observe hot warpage actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Metal distribution and polymer cure affect package warpage.","check":"交付「觀察熱態翹曲」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for observe hot warpage, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-17-k1","title":"觀察熱態翹曲：機制","titleEn":"Observe hot warpage: mechanism","text":"疊層金屬密度和聚合物固化會影響整包變形。","textEn":"Metal distribution and polymer cure affect package warpage.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-17-k2","title":"觀察熱態翹曲：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Observe hot warpage: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較升溫與降溫曲線是否遲滯。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare heating and cooling curves for hysteresis. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「觀察熱態翹曲」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for observe hot warpage?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","疊層金屬密度和聚合物固化會影響整包變形。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Metal distribution and polymer cure affect package warpage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"疊層金屬密度和聚合物固化會影響整包變形。 比較升溫與降溫曲線是否遲滯。","explanationEn":"Metal distribution and polymer cure affect package warpage. Compare heating and cooling curves for hysteresis."}},{"id":"a127-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-17"],"title":"觀察熱態翹曲：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Observe hot warpage: challenge and acceptance","objectiv