ons distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「觀察熱態翹曲：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for observe hot warpage: challenge and acceptance?","options":["比較升溫與降溫曲線是否遲滯。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Compare heating and cooling curves for hysteresis.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"疊層金屬密度和聚合物固化會影響整包變形。 比較升溫與降溫曲線是否遲滯。","explanationEn":"Metal distribution and polymer cure affect package warpage. Compare heating and cooling curves for hysteresis."}}]},{"id":"a127-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"整合與證據","titleEn":"Integration and evidence","description":"本階段處理整合與證據：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address integration and evidence through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a127-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-18"],"title":"驗證電氣互連","titleEn":"Validate electrical interconnects","objective":"建立「驗證電氣互連」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for validate electrical interconnects: Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「驗證電氣互連」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for validate electrical interconnects actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance.","check":"交付「驗證電氣互連」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for validate electrical interconnects, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-19-k1","title":"驗證電氣互連：機制","titleEn":"Validate electrical interconnects: mechanism","text":"TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。","textEn":"Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-19-k2","title":"驗證電氣互連：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Validate electrical interconnects: evidence and interpretation","text":"將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「驗證電氣互連」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for validate electrical interconnects?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。 將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。","explanationEn":"Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance. Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately."}},{"id":"a127-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-19"],"title":"驗證電氣互連：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Validate electrical interconnects: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「驗證電氣互連」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the validate electrical interconnects model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「驗證電氣互連」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for validate electrical interconnects actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance.","check":"交付「驗證電氣互連」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for validate electrical interconnects: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-20-k1","title":"驗證電氣互連：機制","titleEn":"Validate electrical interconnects: mechanism","text":"TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。","textEn":"Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-20-k2","title":"驗證電氣互連：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Validate electrical interconnects: evidence and interpretation","text":"將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「驗證電氣互連：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for validate electrical interconnects: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"TGV 的 DC 電阻合格不保證高速轉接阻抗合格。 將菊鏈與高頻量測分開規劃。","explanationEn":"Passing TGV DC resistance does not qualify high-speed transition impedance. Plan daisy-chain and high-frequency tests separately."}},{"id":"a127-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-20"],"title":"安排破壞與非破壞對照","titleEn":"Pair destructive and nondestructive checks","objective":"建立「安排破壞與非破壞對照」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for pair destructive and nondestructive checks: CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「安排破壞與非破壞對照」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for pair destructive and nondestructive checks actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation.","check":"交付「安排破壞與非破壞對照」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for pair destructive and nondestructive checks, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-21-k1","title":"安排破壞與非破壞對照：機制","titleEn":"Pair destructive and nondestructive checks: mechanism","text":"CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。","textEn":"CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-21-k2","title":"安排破壞與非破壞對照：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Pair destructive and nondestructive checks: evidence and interpretation","text":"用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「安排破壞與非破壞對照」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for pair destructive and nondestructive checks?","options":["CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。 用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。","explanationEn":"CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation. Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates."}},{"id":"a127-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-21"],"title":"安排破壞與非破壞對照：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Pair destructive and nondestructive checks: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「安排破壞與非破壞對照」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the pair destructive and nondestructive checks model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「安排破壞與非破壞對照」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for pair destructive and nondestructive checks actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation.","check":"交付「安排破壞與非破壞對照」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for pair destructive and nondestructive checks: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-22-k1","title":"安排破壞與非破壞對照：機制","titleEn":"Pair destructive and nondestructive checks: mechanism","text":"CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。","textEn":"CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-22-k2","title":"安排破壞與非破壞對照：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Pair destructive and nondestructive checks: evidence and interpretation","text":"用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「安排破壞與非破壞對照：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for pair destructive and nondestructive checks: challenge and acceptance?","options":["玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋"],"optionsEn":["A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates.","Flat glass cannot crack"],"answer":1,"explanation":"CT 或光學影像的檢出限須由已知缺陷或截面驗證。 用相同座標核對孔壁缺陷。","explanationEn":"CT/optical detection limits need known defects or section validation. Check via-wall defects at registered coordinates."}},{"id":"a127-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-22"],"title":"評估研究成熟度","titleEn":"Assess research maturity","objective":"建立「評估研究成熟度」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for assess research maturity: Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋。本步先檢查「評估研究成熟度」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Flat glass cannot crack. First check whether evidence for assess research maturity actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones.","check":"交付「評估研究成熟度」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for assess research maturity, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-23-k1","title":"評估研究成熟度：機制","titleEn":"Assess research maturity: mechanism","text":"功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。","textEn":"Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-23-k2","title":"評估研究成熟度：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Assess research maturity: evidence and interpretation","text":"用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「評估研究成熟度」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for assess research maturity?","options":["玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃","功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。"],"optionsEn":["Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass","Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones."],"answer":2,"explanation":"功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。 用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。","explanationEn":"Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones. Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence."}},{"id":"a127-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"],"prerequisiteIds":["a127-v9-23"],"title":"評估研究成熟度：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Assess research maturity: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「評估研究成熟度」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the assess research maturity model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃。本步先檢查「評估研究成熟度」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass. First check whether evidence for assess research maturity actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones.","check":"交付「評估研究成熟度」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for assess research maturity: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a127-v9-24-k1","title":"評估研究成熟度：機制","titleEn":"Assess research maturity: mechanism","text":"功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。","textEn":"Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]},{"id":"a127-v9-24-k2","title":"評估研究成熟度：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Assess research maturity: evidence and interpretation","text":"用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-intel-glass","v9at-intel-glass-brief"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「評估研究成熟度：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for assess research maturity: challenge and acceptance?","options":["用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。","玻璃平整就不會產生裂紋","玻璃核心代表全部介電層都是玻璃"],"optionsEn":["Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence.","Flat glass cannot crack","A glass core means every dielectric layer is glass"],"answer":0,"explanation":"功能測試載具、可靠度驗證與量產資格是不同里程碑。 用公開證據標註已證明與仍待證明事項。","explanationEn":"Functional vehicles, reliability validation and production qualification are distinct milestones. Label demonstrated and unresolved claims from public evidence."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-substrates","subcategoryTitle":"中介層與封裝基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interposers and package substrates","photoId":"bga-section"},{"id":"a128","title":"ABF 增層封裝基板","titleEn":"ABF build-up package substrates","category":"packaging","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 步深入ABF 介電增層、微孔、銅附著與高頻損耗；每個技術單元分為建模與證據驗證，包含可重算的教學算例、失效辨識及相關工法。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 steps examine abf build-up dielectric, microvias, copper adhesion and rf loss. Each technical unit separates modeling from evidence validation, with reproducible teaching examples, failure diagnosis and related methods.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si","v9-media-5b703d7dcca3","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"公開資料支持的原理與工程判讀課；24 步是學習拆解，不是工廠完整 SOP。數值均為明示假設的教學例；實際材料、設備、驗收門檻須依專案規格。ABF 是材料系列商標，不是一種固定通用配方；固化、粗化及製程條件需依供應商版本與專業設備規範。","scopeEn":"A principles and engineering-interpretation course grounded in public material. The 24 steps are an educational decomposition, not a complete factory SOP. Numbers are labeled hypothetical; actual materials, equipment and acceptance limits require project specifications. ABF is a branded material family, not one universal recipe; cure, roughening and process conditions require vendor-version and equipment specifications.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["材料與層疊","成孔與導體","表面與電性","可靠度與交付"],"labelsEn":["Materials and stack-up","Vias and conductors","Surfaces and electrical behavior","Reliability and handoff"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a128-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"材料與層疊","titleEn":"Materials and stack-up","description":"本階段處理材料與層疊：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address materials and stack-up through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a128-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"辨識 ABF 功能","titleEn":"Identify ABF function","objective":"建立「辨識 ABF 功能」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for identify abf function: ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「辨識 ABF 功能」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for identify abf function actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts.","check":"交付「辨識 ABF 功能」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for identify abf function, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-01-k1","title":"辨識 ABF 功能：機制","titleEn":"Identify ABF function: mechanism","text":"ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。","textEn":"ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-01-k2","title":"辨識 ABF 功能：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Identify ABF function: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「辨識 ABF 功能」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for identify abf function?","options":["粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料"],"optionsEn":["More roughening always improves RF performance","ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts.","ABF is conductive copper foil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。 畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。","explanationEn":"ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts. Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers."}},{"id":"a128-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-01"],"title":"辨識 ABF 功能：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Identify ABF function: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「辨識 ABF 功能」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the identify abf function model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「辨識 ABF 功能」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for identify abf function actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts.","check":"交付「辨識 ABF 功能」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for identify abf function: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-02-k1","title":"辨識 ABF 功能：機制","titleEn":"Identify ABF function: mechanism","text":"ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。","textEn":"ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-02-k2","title":"辨識 ABF 功能：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Identify ABF function: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「辨識 ABF 功能：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for identify abf function: challenge and acceptance?","options":["ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。"],"optionsEn":["ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance","Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"ABF 提供層間絕緣和細線基底，銅才承擔主要導電。 畫銅線與介電層而不混為一層。","explanationEn":"ABF provides interlayer insulation and a routing foundation; copper conducts. Draw copper and dielectric as separate layers."}},{"id":"a128-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-02"],"title":"選擇材料等級","titleEn":"Select material grade","objective":"建立「選擇材料等級」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for select material grade: Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。記錄材料版號與資料表條件。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Record grade/version and datasheet conditions. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：記錄材料版號與資料表條件。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Record grade/version and datasheet conditions. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「選擇材料等級」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for select material grade actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade.","check":"交付「選擇材料等級」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for select material grade, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-03-k1","title":"選擇材料等級：機制","titleEn":"Select material grade: mechanism","text":"介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。","textEn":"Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-03-k2","title":"選擇材料等級：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Select material grade: evidence and interpretation","text":"記錄材料版號與資料表條件。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Record grade/version and datasheet conditions. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「選擇材料等級」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for select material grade?","options":["介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade.","ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。 記錄材料版號與資料表條件。","explanationEn":"Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade. Record grade/version and datasheet conditions."}},{"id":"a128-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-03"],"title":"選擇材料等級：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Select material grade: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「選擇材料等級」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the select material grade model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。記錄材料版號與資料表條件。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Record grade/version and datasheet conditions. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：記錄材料版號與資料表條件。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Record grade/version and datasheet conditions. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「選擇材料等級」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for select material grade actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade.","check":"交付「選擇材料等級」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for select material grade: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-04-k1","title":"選擇材料等級：機制","titleEn":"Select material grade: mechanism","text":"介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。","textEn":"Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-04-k2","title":"選擇材料等級：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Select material grade: evidence and interpretation","text":"記錄材料版號與資料表條件。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Record grade/version and datasheet conditions. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「選擇材料等級：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for select material grade: challenge and acceptance?","options":["粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","記錄材料版號與資料表條件。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料"],"optionsEn":["More roughening always improves RF performance","Record grade/version and datasheet conditions.","ABF is conductive copper foil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"介電、熱機與加工性能會隨產品等級改變。 記錄材料版號與資料表條件。","explanationEn":"Dielectric, thermomechanical and process properties vary by grade. Record grade/version and datasheet conditions."}},{"id":"a128-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-04"],"title":"設計對稱層疊","titleEn":"Design symmetric stack-up","objective":"建立「設計對稱層疊」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for design symmetric stack-up: Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「設計對稱層疊」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for design symmetric stack-up actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending.","check":"交付「設計對稱層疊」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for design symmetric stack-up, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-05-k1","title":"設計對稱層疊：機制","titleEn":"Design symmetric stack-up: mechanism","text":"上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。","textEn":"Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-05-k2","title":"設計對稱層疊：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Design symmetric stack-up: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設計對稱層疊」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for design symmetric stack-up?","options":["ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。"],"optionsEn":["ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance","Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending."],"answer":2,"explanation":"上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。 比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。","explanationEn":"Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending. Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage."}},{"id":"a128-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-05"],"title":"設計對稱層疊：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Design symmetric stack-up: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「設計對稱層疊」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the design symmetric stack-up model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「設計對稱層疊」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for design symmetric stack-up actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending.","check":"交付「設計對稱層疊」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for design symmetric stack-up: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-06-k1","title":"設計對稱層疊：機制","titleEn":"Design symmetric stack-up: mechanism","text":"上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。","textEn":"Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-06-k2","title":"設計對稱層疊：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Design symmetric stack-up: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「設計對稱層疊：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for design symmetric stack-up: challenge and acceptance?","options":["比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage.","ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"上下層數及銅分布影響固化後彎矩。 比較對稱與單側增層的翹曲方向。","explanationEn":"Top/bottom layers and copper distribution affect post-cure bending. Compare symmetric and one-sided build-up warpage."}}]},{"id":"a128-v9-stage02","order":2,"title":"成孔與導體","titleEn":"Vias and conductors","description":"本階段處理成孔與導體：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address vias and conductors through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a128-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-06"],"title":"理解層壓界面","titleEn":"Understand lamination interfaces","objective":"建立「理解層壓界面」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：未填滿的凹陷及夾氣會形成局部絕緣和附著缺陷。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for understand lamination interfaces: Unfilled recesses and trapped gas create local insulation/adhesion defects.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。用截面區分厚度不均與空洞。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Distinguish thickness variation from voids in sections. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：用截面區分厚度不均與空洞。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Distinguish thickness variation from voids in sections. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「理解層壓界面」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到未填滿的凹陷及夾氣會形成局部絕緣和附著缺陷。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for understand lamination interfaces actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Unfilled recesses and trapped gas create local insulation/adhesion defects.","check":"交付「理解層壓界面」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for understand lamination interfaces, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-07-k1","title":"理解層壓界面：機制","titleEn":"Understand lamination interfaces: mechanism","text":"未填滿的凹陷及夾氣會形成局部絕緣和附