bel simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：用截面區分厚度不均與空洞。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Distinguish thickness variation from voids in sections. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「理解層壓界面」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到未填滿的凹陷及夾氣會形成局部絕緣和附著缺陷。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for understand lamination interfaces actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Unfilled recesses and trapped gas create local insulation/adhesion defects.","check":"交付「理解層壓界面」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for understand lamination interfaces: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-08-k1","title":"理解層壓界面：機制","titleEn":"Understand lamination interfaces: mechanism","text":"未填滿的凹陷及夾氣會形成局部絕緣和附著缺陷。","textEn":"Unfilled recesses and trapped gas create local insulation/adhesion defects.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-08-k2","title":"理解層壓界面：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Understand lamination interfaces: evidence and interpretation","text":"用截面區分厚度不均與空洞。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Distinguish thickness variation from voids in sections. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「理解層壓界面：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for understand lamination interfaces: challenge and acceptance?","options":["ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","用截面區分厚度不均與空洞。"],"optionsEn":["ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance","Distinguish thickness variation from voids in sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"未填滿的凹陷及夾氣會形成局部絕緣和附著缺陷。 用截面區分厚度不均與空洞。","explanationEn":"Unfilled recesses and trapped gas create local insulation/adhesion defects. Distinguish thickness variation from voids in sections."}},{"id":"a128-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-08"],"title":"規劃微孔連接","titleEn":"Plan microvia connections","objective":"建立「規劃微孔連接」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for plan microvia connections: Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Label the metal layers connected by each via. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Label the metal layers connected by each via. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「規劃微孔連接」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for plan microvia connections actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity.","check":"交付「規劃微孔連接」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for plan microvia connections, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-09-k1","title":"規劃微孔連接：機制","titleEn":"Plan microvia connections: mechanism","text":"孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。","textEn":"Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-09-k2","title":"規劃微孔連接：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Plan microvia connections: evidence and interpretation","text":"標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Label the metal layers connected by each via. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規劃微孔連接」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for plan microvia connections?","options":["孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity.","ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。 標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。","explanationEn":"Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity. Label the metal layers connected by each via."}},{"id":"a128-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-09"],"title":"規劃微孔連接：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Plan microvia connections: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「規劃微孔連接」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the plan microvia connections model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Label the metal layers connected by each via. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Label the metal layers connected by each via. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「規劃微孔連接」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for plan microvia connections actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity.","check":"交付「規劃微孔連接」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for plan microvia connections: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-10-k1","title":"規劃微孔連接：機制","titleEn":"Plan microvia connections: mechanism","text":"孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。","textEn":"Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-10-k2","title":"規劃微孔連接：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Plan microvia connections: evidence and interpretation","text":"標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Label the metal layers connected by each via. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「規劃微孔連接：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for plan microvia connections: challenge and acceptance?","options":["粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料"],"optionsEn":["More roughening always improves RF performance","Label the metal layers connected by each via.","ABF is conductive copper foil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔底焊墊、孔壁及孔口幾何共同影響電鍍連續性。 標示每個微孔對接的金屬層。","explanationEn":"Bottom pad, wall and entrance geometry jointly affect plating continuity. Label the metal layers connected by each via."}},{"id":"a128-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-10"],"title":"管理除膠與表面","titleEn":"Manage residue and surface condition","objective":"建立「管理除膠與表面」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：殘膠會阻礙電接觸；粗化與低損耗要求可能衝突。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for manage residue and surface condition: Residue blocks contact; roughening and low loss may conflict.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。比較附著需求與表面粗糙指標。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Compare adhesion needs with roughness metrics. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較附著需求與表面粗糙指標。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare adhesion needs with roughness metrics. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「管理除膠與表面」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到殘膠會阻礙電接觸；粗化與低損耗要求可能衝突。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for manage residue and surface condition actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Residue blocks contact; roughening and low loss may conflict.","check":"交付「管理除膠與表面」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for manage residue and surface condition, including 