所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for control seed and plating actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Seed continuity and local current distribution govern via-wall and trace formation.","check":"交付「控制種子與電鍍」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for control seed and plating, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-13-k1","title":"控制種子與電鍍：機制","titleEn":"Control seed and plating: mechanism","text":"種子連續性及局部電流分布決定孔壁與線路形成。","textEn":"Seed continuity and local current distribution govern via-wall and trace formation.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-13-k2","title":"控制種子與電鍍：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Control seed and plating: evidence and interpretation","text":"用孔口、孔中及孔底三處驗證。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Check via entrance, middle and bottom. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制種子與電鍍」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for control seed and plating?","options":["粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","種子連續性及局部電流分布決定孔壁與線路形成。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料"],"optionsEn":["More roughening always improves RF performance","Seed continuity and local current distribution govern via-wall and trace formation.","ABF is conductive copper foil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"種子連續性及局部電流分布決定孔壁與線路形成。 用孔口、孔中及孔底三處驗證。","explanationEn":"Seed continuity and local current distribution govern via-wall and trace formation. Check via entrance, middle and bottom."}},{"id":"a128-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-13"],"title":"控制種子與電鍍：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Control seed and plating: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「控制種子與電鍍」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the control seed and plating model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。用孔口、孔中及孔底三處驗證。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Check via entrance, middle and bottom. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：用孔口、孔中及孔底三處驗證。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Check via entrance, middle and bottom. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「控制種子與電鍍」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到種子連續性及局部電流分布決定孔壁與線路形成。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for control seed and plating actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Seed continuity and local current distribution govern via-wall and trace formation.","check":"交付「控制種子與電鍍」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for control seed and plating: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-14-k1","title":"控制種子與電鍍：機制","titleEn":"Control seed and plating: mechanism","text":"種子連續性及局部電流分布決定孔壁與線路形成。","textEn":"Seed continuity and local current distribution govern via-wall and trace formation.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-14-k2","title":"控制種子與電鍍：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Control seed and plating: evidence and interpretation","text":"用孔口、孔中及孔底三處驗證。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Check via entrance, middle and bottom. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制種子與電鍍：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for control seed and plating: challenge and acceptance?","options":["ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","用孔口、孔中及孔底三處驗證。"],"optionsEn":["ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance","Check via entrance, middle and bottom."],"answer":2,"explanation":"種子連續性及局部電流分布決定孔壁與線路形成。 用孔口、孔中及孔底三處驗證。","explanationEn":"Seed continuity and local current distribution govern via-wall and trace formation. Check via entrance, middle and bottom."}},{"id":"a128-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-14"],"title":"檢查細線形貌","titleEn":"Inspect fine-line geometry","objective":"建立「檢查細線形貌」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for inspect fine-line geometry: Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。同時量線頂與線底寬度。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Measure top and bottom trace widths. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：同時量線頂與線底寬度。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Measure top and bottom trace widths. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「檢查細線形貌」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for inspect fine-line geometry actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts.","check":"交付「檢查細線形貌」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for inspect fine-line geometry, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-15-k1","title":"檢查細線形貌：機制","titleEn":"Inspect fine-line geometry: mechanism","text":"線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。","textEn":"Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-15-k2","title":"檢查細線形貌：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Inspect fine-line geometry: evidence and interpretation","text":"同時量線頂與線底寬度。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Measure top and bottom trace widths. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「檢查細線形貌」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for inspect fine-line geometry?","options":["線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts.","ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。 同時量線頂與線底寬度。","explanationEn":"Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts. Measure top and bottom trace widths."}},{"id":"a128-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-15"],"title":"檢查細線形貌：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Inspect fine-line geometry: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「檢查細線形貌」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the inspect fine-line geometry model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。同時量線頂與線底寬度。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Measure top and bottom trace widths. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：同時量線頂與線底寬度。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Measure top and bottom trace widths. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「檢查細線形貌」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for inspect fine-line geometry actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts.","check":"交付「檢查細線形貌」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for inspect fine-line geometry: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-16-k1","title":"檢查細線形貌：機制","titleEn":"Inspect fine-line geometry: mechanism","text":"線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。","textEn":"Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-16-k2","title":"檢查細線形貌：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Inspect fine-line geometry: evidence and interpretation","text":"同時量線頂與線底寬度。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Measure top and bottom trace widths. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「檢查細線形貌：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for inspect fine-line geometry: challenge and acceptance?","options":["粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","同時量線頂與線底寬度。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料"],"optionsEn":["More roughening always improves RF performance","Measure top and bottom trace widths.","ABF is conductive copper foil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"線寬、截面與間距偏差會影響阻抗、電阻及短路風險。 同時量線頂與線底寬度。","explanationEn":"Width, section and gap errors affect impedance, resistance and shorts. Measure top and bottom trace widths."}},{"id":"a128-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-16"],"title":"估算介電電容","titleEn":"Estimate dielectric capacitance","objective":"建立「估算介電電容」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for estimate dielectric capacitance: Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。\n\n假設平行板面積 1 mm²、間距 20 μm、εr=3.5，C=ε0εrA/d≈1.55 pF；介電厚度 ±10% 對 C 產生約相反方向 10% 一階變化，邊緣場未計。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.\n\nFor area 1 mm², spacing 20 μm and εr=3.5, C≈1.55 pF. Thickness ±10% produces approximately opposite ±10% first-order capacitance change, excluding fringing.","observation":"觀察焦點：重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「估算介電電容」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for estimate dielectric capacitance actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling.","check":"交付「估算介電電容」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for estimate dielectric capacitance, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-17-k1","title":"估算介電電容：機制","titleEn":"Estimate dielectric capacitance: mechanism","text":"電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。","textEn":"Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-17-k2","title":"估算介電電容：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Estimate dielectric capacitance: evidence and interpretation","text":"重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-17-k3","title":"自訂算例與模型界限","titleEn":"Hypothetical worked example and model boundary","text":"假設平行板面積 1 mm²、間距 20 μm、εr=3.5，C=ε0εrA/d≈1.55 pF；介電厚度 ±10% 對 C 產生約相反方向 10% 一階變化，邊緣場未計。 ABF 是材料系列商標，不是一種固定通用配方；固化、粗化及製程條件需依供應商版本與專業設備規範。","textEn":"For area 1 mm², spacing 20 μm and εr=3.5, C≈1.55 pF. Thickness ±10% produces approximately opposite ±10% first-order capacitance change, excluding fringing. ABF is a branded material family, not one universal recipe; cure, roughening and process conditions require vendor-version and equipment specifications.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「估算介電電容」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for estimate dielectric capacitance?","options":["ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。"],"optionsEn":["ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance","Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling."],"answer":2,"explanation":"電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。 重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。","explanationEn":"Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling. Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance."}},{"id":"a128-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-17"],"title":"估算介電電容：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Estimate dielectric capacitance: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「估算介電電容」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the estimate dielectric capacitance model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。\n\n假設平行板面積 1 mm²、間距 20 μm、εr=3.5，C=ε0εrA/d≈1.55 pF；介電厚度 ±10% 對 C 產生約相反方向 10% 一階變化，邊緣場未計。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.\n\nFor area 1 mm², spacing 20 μm and εr=3.5, C≈1.55 pF. Thickness ±10% produces approximately opposite ±10% first-order capacitance change, excluding fringing.","observation":"觀察焦點：重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「估算介電電容」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for estimate dielectric capacitance actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling.","check":"交付「估算介電電容」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for estimate dielectric capacitance: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-18-k1","title":"估算介電電容：機制","titleEn":"Estimate dielectric capacitance: mechanism","text":"電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。","textEn":"Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-18-k2","title":"估算介電電容：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Estimate dielectric capacitance: evidence and interpretation","text":"重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-18-k3","title":"自訂算例與模型界限","titleEn":"Hypothetical worked example and model boundary","text":"假設平行板面積 1 mm²、間距 20 μm、εr=3.5，C=ε0εrA/d≈1.55 pF；介電厚度 ±10% 對 C 產生約相反方向 10% 一階變化，邊緣場未計。 ABF 是材料系列商標，不是一種固定通用配方；固化、粗化及製程條件需依供應商版本與專業設備規範。","textEn":"For area 1 mm², spacing 20 μm and εr=3.5, C≈1.55 pF. Thickness ±10% produces approximately opposite ±10% first-order capacitance change, excluding fringing. ABF is a branded material family, not one universal recipe; cure, roughening and process conditions require vendor-version and equipment specifications.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「估算介電電容：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for estimate dielectric capacitance: challenge and acceptance?","options":["重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance.","ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"電容取決於厚度及介電常數，局部薄區可能增加耦合。 重算 1.55 pF 與厚度容差。","explanationEn":"Capacitance depends on thickness and permittivity; thin regions can increase coupling. Recalculate 1.55 pF with thickness tolerance."}}]},{"id":"a128-v9-stage04","order":4,"title":"可靠度與交付","titleEn":"Reliability and handoff","description":"本階段處理可靠度與交付：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address reliability and handoff through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a128-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-18"],"title":"衡量粗糙與高頻損耗","titleEn":"Assess roughness and RF loss","objective":"建立「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for assess roughness and rf loss: Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for assess roughness and rf loss actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient.","check":"交付「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for assess roughness and rf loss, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-19-k1","title":"衡量粗糙與高頻損耗：機制","titleEn":"Assess roughness and RF loss: mechanism","text":"導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。","textEn":"Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-19-k2","title":"衡量粗糙與高頻損耗：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Assess roughness and RF loss: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for assess roughness and rf loss?","options":["粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料"],"optionsEn":["More roughening always improves RF performance","Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient.","ABF is conductive copper foil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。 比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。","explanationEn":"Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient. Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss."}},{"id":"a128-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-19"],"title":"衡量粗糙與高頻損耗：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Assess roughness and RF loss: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the assess roughness and rf loss model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for assess roughness and rf loss actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient.","check":"交付「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for assess roughness and rf loss: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-20-k1","title":"衡量粗糙與高頻損耗：機制","titleEn":"Assess roughness and RF loss: mechanism","text":"導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。","textEn":"Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-20-k2","title":"衡量粗糙與高頻損耗：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Assess roughness and RF loss: evidence and interpretation","text":"比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「衡量粗糙與高頻損耗：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for assess roughness and rf loss: challenge and acceptance?","options":["ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。"],"optionsEn":["ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance","Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"導體粗糙可增加高頻損耗，不能只用 DC 電阻排名。 比較 DC 與高頻插損的排序。","explanationEn":"Conductor roughness can increase RF loss; DC resistance alone is insufficient. Compare rankings by DC resistance and RF insertion loss."}},{"id":"a128-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-20"],"title":"追蹤濕熱可靠度","titleEn":"Track moisture/thermal reliability","objective":"建立「追蹤濕熱可靠度」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for track moisture/thermal reliability: Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「追蹤濕熱可靠度」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for track moisture/thermal reliability actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact.","check":"交付「追蹤濕熱可靠度」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for track moisture/thermal reliability, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-21-k1","title":"追蹤濕熱可靠度：機制","titleEn":"Track moisture/thermal reliability: mechanism","text":"介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。","textEn":"Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-21-k2","title":"追蹤濕熱可靠度：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Track moisture/thermal reliability: evidence and interpretation","text":"把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「追蹤濕熱可靠度」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for track moisture/thermal reliability?","options":["介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好"],"optionsEn":["Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact.","ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。 把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。","explanationEn":"Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact. Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time."}},{"id":"a128-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-21"],"title":"追蹤濕熱可靠度：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Track moisture/thermal reliability: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「追蹤濕熱可靠度」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the track moisture/thermal reliability model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「追蹤濕熱可靠度」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for track moisture/thermal reliability actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact.","check":"交付「追蹤濕熱可靠度」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for track moisture/thermal reliability: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-22-k1","title":"追蹤濕熱可靠度：機制","titleEn":"Track moisture/thermal reliability: mechanism","text":"介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。","textEn":"Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-22-k2","title":"追蹤濕熱可靠度：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Track moisture/thermal reliability: evidence and interpretation","text":"把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「追蹤濕熱可靠度：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for track moisture/thermal reliability: challenge and acceptance?","options":["粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料"],"optionsEn":["More roughening always improves RF performance","Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time.","ABF is conductive copper foil"],"answer":1,"explanation":"介電吸濕、微孔疲勞與界面剝離可能交互作用。 把電阻、絕緣及影像按時間配準。","explanationEn":"Moisture uptake, via fatigue and delamination can interact. Register resistance, isolation and imaging over time."}},{"id":"a128-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-22"],"title":"交付基板製造證據","titleEn":"Deliver substrate evidence","objective":"建立「交付基板製造證據」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for deliver substrate evidence: Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. List checks required after a material revision. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: List checks required after a material revision. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：ABF 是導電銅箔材料。本步先檢查「交付基板製造證據」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: ABF is conductive copper foil. First check whether evidence for deliver substrate evidence actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability.","check":"交付「交付基板製造證據」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for deliver substrate evidence, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-23-k1","title":"交付基板製造證據：機制","titleEn":"Deliver substrate evidence: mechanism","text":"材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。","textEn":"Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-23-k2","title":"交付基板製造證據：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Deliver substrate evidence: evidence and interpretation","text":"列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"List checks required after a material revision. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「交付基板製造證據」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for deliver substrate evidence?","options":["ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好","材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。"],"optionsEn":["ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance","Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。 列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。","explanationEn":"Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability. List checks required after a material revision."}},{"id":"a128-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"],"prerequisiteIds":["a128-v9-23"],"title":"交付基板製造證據：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Deliver substrate evidence: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「交付基板製造證據」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the deliver substrate evidence model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. List checks required after a material revision. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: List checks required after a material revision. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好。本步先檢查「交付基板製造證據」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: More roughening always improves RF performance. First check whether evidence for deliver substrate evidence actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability.","check":"交付「交付基板製造證據」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for deliver substrate evidence: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a128-v9-24-k1","title":"交付基板製造證據：機制","titleEn":"Deliver substrate evidence: mechanism","text":"材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。","textEn":"Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]},{"id":"a128-v9-24-k2","title":"交付基板製造證據：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Deliver substrate evidence: evidence and interpretation","text":"列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"List checks required after a material revision. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9at-ajinomoto-abf","v9at-ajinomoto-history","v9at-ti-si"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「交付基板製造證據：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for deliver substrate evidence: challenge and acceptance?","options":["列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。","ABF 是導電銅箔材料","粗化越強，高頻性能一定越好"],"optionsEn":["List checks required after a material revision.","ABF is conductive copper foil","More roughening always improves RF performance"],"answer":0,"explanation":"材料批次、微孔良率與層疊模型需能互相追溯。 列出因材料換版必須重驗的項目。","explanationEn":"Material lot, via yield and stack-up model need traceability. List checks required after a material revision."}}]}],"subcategory":"pkg-substrates","subcategoryTitle":"中介層與封裝基板","subcategoryTitleEn":"Interposers and package substrates","photoId":"bga-section"},{"id":"a129","title":"嵌入式互連橋整合","titleEn":"Embedded interconnect-bridge integration","category":"packaging","kind":"course","summary":"以四階段、24 步深入嵌入式矽橋局部細密互連與封裝邊界；每個技術單元分為建模與證據驗證，包含可重算的教學算例、失效辨識及相關工法。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 steps examine embedded silicon-bridge fine interconnects and package boundaries. Each technical unit separates modeling from evidence validation, with reproducible teaching examples, failure diagnosis and related methods.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib","v9-media-76504c18d14b","v10-media-14f744acab6a"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":720,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"scope":"公開資料支持的原理與工程判讀課；24 步是學習拆解，不是工廠完整 SOP。數值均為明示假設的教學例；實際材料、設備、驗收門檻須依專案規格。本課以公開 EMIB 架構說明局部桥接；不同世代的供電、TSV 及互連能力須看原始資料，不能混稱所有橋接方案相同。","scopeEn":"A principles and engineering-interpretation course grounded in public material. The 24 steps are an educational decomposition, not a complete factory SOP. Numbers are labeled hypothetical; actual materials, equipment and acceptance limits require project specifications. Public EMIB architecture illustrates local bridges; power, TSV and interconnect capabilities vary by generation and must not be conflated.","diagram":{"type":"packaging","labels":["局部橋接架構","焊墊與對準","電熱機路徑","測試與整合"],"labelsEn":["Local bridge architecture","Pads and alignment","Electrical thermal mechanical paths","Test and integration"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a129-v9-stage01","order":1,"title":"局部橋接架構","titleEn":"Local bridge architecture","description":"本階段處理局部橋接架構：依序完成三個技術單元的模型與獨立驗證，將物理主張連到可觀察資料。","descriptionEn":"Address local bridge architecture through three technical units, each with a model and independent verification linking physical claims to observable evidence.","steps":[{"id":"a129-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"比較局部與全面中介層","titleEn":"Compare local and full interposers","objective":"建立「比較局部與全面中介層」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for compare local and full interposers: A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：矽橋等於覆蓋整包的矽中介層。本步先檢查「比較局部與全面中介層」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A silicon bridge equals a full-package silicon interposer. First check whether evidence for compare local and full interposers actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed.","check":"交付「比較局部與全面中介層」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for compare local and full interposers, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a129-v9-01-k1","title":"比較局部與全面中介層：機制","titleEn":"Compare local and full interposers: mechanism","text":"局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。","textEn":"A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]},{"id":"a129-v9-01-k2","title":"比較局部與全面中介層：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Compare local and full interposers: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「比較局部與全面中介層」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for compare local and full interposers?","options":["所有橋接世代都完全沒有 TSV","局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。","矽橋等於覆蓋整包的矽中介層"],"optionsEn":["Every bridge generation is entirely TSV-free","A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed.","A silicon bridge equals a full-package silicon interposer"],"answer":1,"explanation":"局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。 畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。","explanationEn":"A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed. Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate."}},{"id":"a129-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"],"prerequisiteIds":["a129-v9-01"],"title":"比較局部與全面中介層：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Compare local and full interposers: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「比較局部與全面中介層」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the compare local and full interposers model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.","observation":"觀察焦點：畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：所有橋接世代都完全沒有 TSV。本步先檢查「比較局部與全面中介層」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Every bridge generation is entirely TSV-free. First check whether evidence for compare local and full interposers actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed.","check":"交付「比較局部與全面中介層」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for compare local and full interposers: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a129-v9-02-k1","title":"比較局部與全面中介層：機制","titleEn":"Compare local and full interposers: mechanism","text":"局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。","textEn":"A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]},{"id":"a129-v9-02-k2","title":"比較局部與全面中介層：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Compare local and full interposers: evidence and interpretation","text":"畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「比較局部與全面中介層：反證與驗收」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for compare local and full interposers: challenge and acceptance?","options":["矽橋等於覆蓋整包的矽中介層","所有橋接世代都完全沒有 TSV","畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。"],"optionsEn":["A silicon bridge equals a full-package silicon interposer","Every bridge generation is entirely TSV-free","Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部橋只在需要高密度連線處配置矽互連。 畫兩晶粒間的橋及其餘有機基板。","explanationEn":"A local bridge places silicon routing only where dense links are needed. Draw a bridge between two dies and the surrounding substrate."}},{"id":"a129-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"],"prerequisiteIds":["a129-v9-02"],"title":"分配晶粒邊緣頻寬","titleEn":"Allocate shoreline bandwidth","objective":"建立「分配晶粒邊緣頻寬」的可檢驗工程模型，說明：可用邊緣長與焊墊配置限制資料通道，不只看矽面積。","objectiveEn":"Build a testable engineering model for allocate shoreline bandwidth: Available edge length and pad layout limit lanes, not only silicon area.","instruction":"先在工程筆記畫出本單元的系統邊界、材料或訊號路徑。驗算 80 個接點的幾何例。 把操作前後的預測分開記錄，標示量綱、固定條件與一項待量測輸入；引用原始來源的適用條件，不把示意圖當實測。\n\n假設晶粒邊緣長 4 mm、單列有效接點間距 50 μm，幾何上限為 80 個接點；若保留 20% 給接地與備援，剩 64 個資料接點。這不是任何 EMIB 產品規格。","instructionEn":"Sketch this unit’s system boundary and material or signal path. Check the 80-site geometric example. Record before/after predictions separately, with dimensions, controlled conditions and one input requiring measurement. Respect source validity conditions and distinguish a schematic from measured evidence.\n\nFor a hypothetical 4 mm edge and 50 μm single-row effective pitch, the geometric limit is 80 sites; reserving 20% for ground/spares leaves 64 data sites. This is not an EMIB specification.","observation":"觀察焦點：驗算 80 個接點的幾何例。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Check the 80-site geometric example. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：矽橋等於覆蓋整包的矽中介層。本步先檢查「分配晶粒邊緣頻寬」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到可用邊緣長與焊墊配置限制資料通道，不只看矽面積。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: A silicon bridge equals a full-package silicon interposer. First check whether evidence for allocate shoreline bandwidth actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Available edge length and pad layout limit lanes, not only silicon area.","check":"交付「分配晶粒邊緣頻寬」模型與比較圖，至少包含本步指定的操作、預測方向、量測單位及未驗證假設。","checkEn":"Submit the model and comparison for allocate shoreline bandwidth, including the specified action, predicted direction, units and an unvalidated assumption.","knowledge":[{"id":"a129-v9-03-k1","title":"分配晶粒邊緣頻寬：機制","titleEn":"Allocate shoreline bandwidth: mechanism","text":"可用邊緣長與焊墊配置限制資料通道，不只看矽面積。","textEn":"Available edge length and pad layout limit lanes, not only silicon area.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]},{"id":"a129-v9-03-k2","title":"分配晶粒邊緣頻寬：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Allocate shoreline bandwidth: evidence and interpretation","text":"驗算 80 個接點的幾何例。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Check the 80-site geometric example. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]},{"id":"a129-v9-03-k3","title":"自訂算例與模型界限","titleEn":"Hypothetical worked example and model boundary","text":"假設晶粒邊緣長 4 mm、單列有效接點間距 50 μm，幾何上限為 80 個接點；若保留 20% 給接地與備援，剩 64 個資料接點。這不是任何 EMIB 產品規格。 本課以公開 EMIB 架構說明局部桥接；不同世代的供電、TSV 及互連能力須看原始資料，不能混稱所有橋接方案相同。","textEn":"For a hypothetical 4 mm edge and 50 μm single-row effective pitch, the geometric limit is 80 sites; reserving 20% for ground/spares leaves 64 data sites. This is not an EMIB specification. Public EMIB architecture illustrates local bridges; power, TSV and interconnect capabilities vary by generation and must not be conflated.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「分配晶粒邊緣頻寬」中，哪個處理方式或主張有物理依據？","questionEn":"Which approach or claim is physically justified for allocate shoreline bandwidth?","options":["可用邊緣長與焊墊配置限制資料通道，不只看矽面積。","矽橋等於覆蓋整包的矽中介層","所有橋接世代都完全沒有 TSV"],"optionsEn":["Available edge length and pad layout limit lanes, not only silicon area.","A silicon bridge equals a full-package silicon interposer","Every bridge generation is entirely TSV-free"],"answer":0,"explanation":"可用邊緣長與焊墊配置限制資料通道，不只看矽面積。 驗算 80 個接點的幾何例。","explanationEn":"Available edge length and pad layout limit lanes, not only silicon area. Check the 80-site geometric example."}},{"id":"a129-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"],"prerequisiteIds":["a129-v9-03"],"title":"分配晶粒邊緣頻寬：反證與驗收","titleEn":"Allocate shoreline bandwidth: challenge and acceptance","objective":"以獨立證據檢驗「分配晶粒邊緣頻寬」的模型，辨別真實效應與量測或模型誤差。","objectiveEn":"Test the allocate shoreline bandwidth model with independent evidence and separate physical effects from measurement or model error.","instruction":"沿用上一步模型，但先寫下什麼結果會推翻它。驗算 80 個接點的幾何例。 加入一組對照或重複量測，改變一個會造成混淆的條件，將觀察分為支持、矛盾及仍不足。若只有模擬資料，清楚標成模擬，並指定下一項實物驗證。\n\n假設晶粒邊緣長 4 mm、單列有效接點間距 50 μm，幾何上限為 80 個接點；若保留 20% 給接地與備援，剩 64 個資料接點。這不是任何 EMIB 產品規格。","instructionEn":"Use the previous model, first specifying what result would refute it. Check the 80-site geometric example. Add a control or repeated measurement, vary one confounder, and classify observations as supporting, conflicting or insufficient. Label simulated data explicitly and specify the next physical validation.\n\nFor a hypothetical 4 mm edge and 50 μm single-row effective pitch, the geometric limit is 80 sites; reserving 20% for ground/spares leaves 64 data sites. This is not an EMIB specification.","observation":"觀察焦點：驗算 80 個接點的幾何例。 只有在控制條件一致且差異大於量測不確定度時，才把差異歸於所討論的機制。","observationEn":"Observation focus: Check the 80-site geometric example. Attribute differences to the mechanism only with matched controls and differences distinguishable from measurement uncertainty.","failure":"需排除的錯判：所有橋接世代都完全沒有 TSV。本步先檢查「分配晶粒邊緣頻寬」的證據是否真的支持機制；若不支持，回到可用邊緣長與焊墊配置限制資料通道，不只看矽面積。所指出的物理限制。","failureEn":"Misinterpretation to reject: Every bridge generation is entirely TSV-free. First check whether evidence for allocate shoreline bandwidth actually supports the mechanism. If not, revisit the physical constraint: Available edge length and pad layout limit lanes, not only silicon area.","check":"交付「分配晶粒邊緣頻寬」的驗收紀錄：包含指定觀察、誤差來源、能支持的結論與一項應暫緩放行的結果。","checkEn":"Submit acceptance evidence for allocate shoreline bandwidth: the specified observation, error sources, supported conclusion and one hold condition.","knowledge":[{"id":"a129-v9-04-k1","title":"分配晶粒邊緣頻寬：機制","titleEn":"Allocate shoreline bandwidth: mechanism","text":"可用邊緣長與焊墊配置限制資料通道，不只看矽面積。","textEn":"Available edge length and pad layout limit lanes, not only silicon area.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel-emib"]},{"id":"a129-v9-04-k2","title":"分配晶粒邊緣頻寬：證據與判讀","titleEn":"Allocate shoreline bandwidth: evidence and interpretation","text":"驗算 80 個接點的幾何例。 記錄原始觀察和推論之間的區別。","textEn":"Check the 80-site geometric example. Keep raw observations distinct from inference.","sourceIds":["v9a-intelpack","v9at-intel